{
  "chapter.63A7B1E69BE2C38A.title": "I · A Light Among Ruins",
  "chapter.63A7B1E69BE2C38A.chapter_subtitle": [
    "You wake beside a ruin of Heliodor with empty hands. A compass is waiting for you, and so is an Atlas."
  ],
  "quest.3C1A37141ABD78D8.title": "Waking among ruins",
  "quest.3C1A37141ABD78D8.quest_desc": [
    "Shelter by the ruin",
    "",
    "Use the pedestal at the heart of the ruin to take the Heliodor Compass, then pick a nearby site with water, wood and room to grow.",
    "",
    "Tuff cut by machines, copper veins gone dark, gardens that kept growing with nobody to tend them. Whoever lived here left all at once."
  ],
  "quest.3AC9E31D78B2BCB0.title": "Somewhere to begin",
  "quest.3AC9E31D78B2BCB0.quest_desc": [
    "Shelter by the ruin",
    "",
    "Craft a crafting table. Before spending materials, check a recipe's uses in the recipe viewer.",
    "",
    "The ruin kept its stones, not its tools. Whatever Heliodor knew, you start again from wood."
  ],
  "quest.153F660992CE9BA3.title": "Read the stone",
  "quest.153F660992CE9BA3.quest_desc": [
    "Shelter by the ruin",
    "",
    "Make a stone pickaxe. Check the block overlay before mining an unfamiliar ore: tool tier matters.",
    "",
    "The ruin's tuff was cut with machines, not chisels. Some day you will need that kind of precision too."
  ],
  "quest.0CA82678D5DFA3E8.title": "A recipe worth keeping",
  "quest.0CA82678D5DFA3E8.quest_desc": [
    "Small useful habits",
    "",
    "Bookmark a recipe you plan to make next in the recipe viewer (its keys are listed in Controls) and remove finished ones so the list stays useful.",
    "",
    "A short list of what comes next: that is how Heliodor's workshops started every morning."
  ],
  "quest.2742A6E0D4B75C80.title": "A shelf for tomorrow",
  "quest.2742A6E0D4B75C80.quest_desc": [
    "Shelter by the ruin",
    "",
    "Make a chest. Keep your next project's materials apart, and try the sorting and matching-deposit controls on ordinary items.",
    "",
    "Among the loose pages, a copper seal with a golden A: 'Council inventory. Everything is recorded.' Somebody here counted everything."
  ],
  "quest.216E7E97E831A00C.title": "Heat with a purpose",
  "quest.216E7E97E831A00C.quest_desc": [
    "Shelter by the ruin",
    "",
    "Build a furnace and smelt or cook a useful batch; prepare the inputs before lighting it.",
    "",
    "Supply, transform, collect: Heliodor ran whole cities on that pattern, fed by the sun instead of coal."
  ],
  "quest.73220D1B896D7CD9.title": "The edge of the dark",
  "quest.73220D1B896D7CD9.quest_desc": [
    "Shelter by the ruin",
    "",
    "Prepare eight torches and light the path between your entrance, water and workshop before you go underground.",
    "",
    "A loose page carries a blessing, signed with a single letter: 'May the light find you at home. —B.'"
  ],
  "quest.4FC6DEBD8FEED1C0.title": "A return address",
  "quest.4FC6DEBD8FEED1C0.quest_desc": [
    "Small useful habits",
    "",
    "Place and use a bed once you can get wool safely; keep the respawn space clear and tell your companions where it is.",
    "",
    "In the ruin, nobody switched the lights off. Whoever lived there meant to come back that same night."
  ],
  "quest.34262755FE4ACAB3.title": "The Atlas listens",
  "quest.34262755FE4ACAB3.quest_desc": [
    "A light answers",
    "",
    "Click the task to open the Atlas, pick The Atlas Awakens and deliver a book and a copper ingot. The Living Atlas itself waits in the Signal Tower: the compass leads there.",
    "",
    "In the Atlas Courtyard the cover warms up. A voice pushes through the static: '…make room for… &kthose&r who… have not arrived.'"
  ],
  "quest.744122ED817C45E5.title": "Carry the river",
  "quest.744122ED817C45E5.quest_desc": [
    "J.'s notes · Garden and table",
    "",
    "Smelt iron for a bucket and bring water to a small farm beside your shelter.",
    "",
    "Heliodor's gardens still drink from channels nobody tends. Water was the first thing its people learned to move."
  ],
  "quest.4E81EB4CAA1D1D13.title": "The patient part",
  "quest.4E81EB4CAA1D1D13.quest_desc": [
    "J.'s notes · Garden and table",
    "",
    "Harvest three wheat and replant before you leave; keep seeds apart from food.",
    "",
    "A note in careful green ink: 'Sow extra. Someone hungry always turns up. —J.'"
  ],
  "quest.0DDC984DEA3CAD80.title": "A kitchen tool",
  "quest.0DDC984DEA3CAD80.quest_desc": [
    "J.'s notes · Garden and table",
    "",
    "Make a flint knife and check its uses: Farmer's Delight knives work on the cutting board and gather certain ingredients.",
    "",
    "The ruin's kitchens were built for crowds. Whoever ran them fed far more people than ever lived here."
  ],
  "quest.1EE8E17F9022A402.title": "A different kind of crafting",
  "quest.1EE8E17F9022A402.quest_desc": [
    "J.'s notes · Garden and table",
    "",
    "Place a cutting board, put an ingredient on it and use the tool its recipe shows.",
    "",
    "In Heliodor even a kitchen board was a small machine: something goes in, one gesture, something useful comes out."
  ],
  "quest.7CD0636D9B7DDA5E.title": "Four places at the table",
  "quest.7CD0636D9B7DDA5E.quest_desc": [
    "J.'s notes · Garden and table",
    "",
    "Prepare four bowls. Some meals give the bowl back, so count them when you plan a batch.",
    "",
    "The ruin's tables are laid for more guests than chairs. J. wrote underneath: 'A kitchen is measured by who it can welcome.'"
  ],
  "quest.7022698D6AF61048.title": "Food before distance",
  "quest.7022698D6AF61048.quest_desc": [
    "J.'s notes · Garden and table",
    "",
    "Bake three bread for a short survey and watch saturation as well as hunger. Keep a reserve at home.",
    "",
    "J.'s packing lists always start with bread, 'for whoever gets lost'."
  ],
  "quest.5E980BB86AE535DF.title": "A table for those returning",
  "quest.5E980BB86AE535DF.quest_desc": [
    "J.'s notes · Garden and table",
    "",
    "Open the Atlas, select A Table for Travellers, check what is missing and choose Deliver.",
    "",
    "J. always kept a place set for strangers. The Atlas answers the delivery with one clear word through the noise: '…welcome.'"
  ],
  "quest.4C7F73BE72A73BFA.title": "A home to come back to",
  "quest.4C7F73BE72A73BFA.quest_desc": [
    "Shelter by the ruin",
    "",
    "Deliver a white bed, a campfire, two lanterns and four bread to Habitation Module in the Atlas. Set it in its place in the Ark, with the controller there: /sethome marks your one home and /home brings you back to it from anywhere.",
    "",
    "J.'s note, under a drawn doorway: 'Wherever the road ends, there has to be a door that opens from the inside.'"
  ],
  "quest.0E2E2C08C06F343B.title": "Metal that remembers weather",
  "quest.0E2E2C08C06F343B.quest_desc": [
    "T.'s notes · Measure the horizon",
    "",
    "Smelt four copper ingots and keep them with the glass for the lens.",
    "",
    "Every instrument in the ruin has a copper frame gone green. Someone designed them to be repaired, not replaced."
  ],
  "quest.27B833739C94F3B1.title": "A window small enough to carry",
  "quest.27B833739C94F3B1.quest_desc": [
    "T.'s notes · Measure the horizon",
    "",
    "Smelt four glass, taking sand from a small, safe patch rather than undermining your shelter.",
    "",
    "Heliodor built with glass so the light could reach everything. It was what its people loved most."
  ],
  "quest.7D9F3FDD50B52514.title": "A borrowed horizon",
  "quest.7D9F3FDD50B52514.quest_desc": [
    "T.'s notes · Measure the horizon",
    "",
    "Open the Atlas, select Assemble the Lens and deliver the listed materials to receive the raw lens once. Keep it for the first signal.",
    "",
    "Beside the sketch, in a small, precise hand: 'Measure before believing. —T.'"
  ],
  "quest.67D63EA89ED72879.title": "Mark the ordinary",
  "quest.67D63EA89ED72879.quest_desc": [
    "Small useful habits",
    "",
    "Find the map's controls and mark your shelter with a practical name.",
    "",
    "The Atlas remembers a world that no longer matches yours. Your own map is the one that tells the truth today."
  ],
  "quest.078C1FA519669777.title": "Leave with a question",
  "quest.078C1FA519669777.quest_desc": [
    "T.'s notes · Measure the horizon",
    "",
    "Prepare three paper for field notes, and pack food, a pickaxe and light with room left for samples.",
    "",
    "The compass will not send you far. Heliodor's traces are close, if you know how to look."
  ],
  "quest.42845362110B95B7.title": "Two accounts of one place",
  "quest.42845362110B95B7.quest_desc": [
    "T.'s notes · Measure the horizon",
    "",
    "Take a short walk and compare a nearby landmark with your map, then open Field Survey in the Atlas and deliver its materials (paper and an ordinary compass) to receive your survey notes.",
    "",
    "What the villagers remember and what the Atlas remembers do not match. Somebody has to write it down again."
  ],
  "quest.5625EFC0A0C376CF.title": "The expedition ends at home",
  "quest.5625EFC0A0C376CF.quest_desc": [
    "Small useful habits",
    "",
    "Back home, restock food and torches before storing the rest, try matching-deposit and note one material you were missing.",
    "",
    "Every trip in J.'s notes ends the same way: 'Back home. Nobody lost.'"
  ],
  "quest.762B0B9FB46F552F.title": "One light answers",
  "quest.762B0B9FB46F552F.quest_desc": [
    "A light answers",
    "",
    "Open First Signal in the Atlas and deliver the listed materials. Bring the Signal Ember, from the Signal Tower, as well. Once, your team receives a signal core and two of Terra's calibration frames: the core builds a survey station, and one frame builds the metallurgic infuser that copies the rest.",
    "",
    "Far away, a light answers. Through the static, a voice: '…can you &khear&r… us? We are still… here.'"
  ],
  "quest.258FF615C9AD9711.title": "A workshop with a destination",
  "quest.258FF615C9AD9711.quest_desc": [
    "A light answers",
    "",
    "When every project of this act is delivered, choose Advance in the Atlas to open the next one; if it takes too long, choose Refresh before retrying.",
    "",
    "The voice has gone quiet. Once you advance, the compass will turn toward a workshop that sank with its tools inside."
  ],
  "quest.2E22D95F3AC6BE45.title": "A place your compass remembers",
  "quest.2E22D95F3AC6BE45.quest_desc": [
    "A light answers",
    "",
    "Build a survey station from the signal core, copper, smooth stone and glass. Use an ordinary compass on it to mark the spot without spending the compass (it points here within this dimension); an empty hand opens your team's Atlas.",
    "",
    "Heliodor had a station like this in every square. The Heliodor Compass follows the Atlas; this one brings you home."
  ],
  "image.5FA9913813897189.title": "&#E8DCB5Shelter by the ruin",
  "image.59D6720CE929BFC4.title": "&#E8DCB5J.'s notes\\nGarden and table",
  "image.5B66BE95D53E20EF.title": "&#E8DCB5T.'s notes\\nMeasure the horizon",
  "image.0DEB76F601E735E0.title": "&#E8DCB5A light answers",
  "image.64856A838DF0F3F2.title": "I · A Light Among Ruins",
  "chapter.0F7AE2DC86CB6F50.title": "II · The Lost Crafts",
  "chapter.0F7AE2DC86CB6F50.chapter_subtitle": [
    "A workshop the earth swallowed keeps Heliodor's crafts: measuring, powering, growing and feeding. Someone once brought them to one bench."
  ],
  "quest.048D2E6A70144A24.title": "Four benches, one workshop",
  "quest.048D2E6A70144A24.quest_desc": [
    "The Sunken Workshop",
    "",
    "Four benches, four crafts: work them in any order. Only a delivery in the Atlas moves your team's story; everything else is practice.",
    "",
    "The signal led to a workshop the earth swallowed. Four benches, four crafts, and one name scratched into every one: Terra."
  ],
  "quest.1C29DD1E3979A642.title": "Let water do the turning",
  "quest.1C29DD1E3979A642.quest_desc": [
    "Terra · Measure and shape",
    "",
    "Craft a Create water wheel from planks around a shaft, and use its Ponder scene to set it in flowing water.",
    "",
    "Terra's first note starts with a stream, not a furnace: 'Borrow a force before you make one.'"
  ],
  "quest.505AD15489797C5A.title": "An iron ingot, made flat",
  "quest.505AD15489797C5A.quest_desc": [
    "Terra · Measure and shape",
    "",
    "Connect a mechanical press to rotation with a depot under its head, as Ponder shows, and press iron ingots into iron sheets.",
    "",
    "In the Sunken Workshop the presses still stand in a row, rusted mid-stroke."
  ],
  "quest.24DF7B8F88C1FCB9.title": "Read the strain",
  "quest.24DF7B8F88C1FCB9.quest_desc": [
    "Terra · Measure and shape",
    "",
    "Make Engineer's Goggles (glass, string and a gold plate from your press), wear them and compare a machine's speed and stress before adding another.",
    "",
    "Terra crossed out 'make it turn faster' and wrote 'measure first'. Somebody above her kept asking for more."
  ],
  "quest.5C34E7D93BAD4D93.title": "Wire without a factory",
  "quest.5C34E7D93BAD4D93.quest_desc": [
    "Terra · Measure and shape",
    "",
    "With Immersive Engineering's hammer turn a copper ingot into a plate, then use its wirecutters to make copper wire for your first connections.",
    "",
    "A hand route for when the machines are gone. Terra always left one."
  ],
  "quest.5F676C980602FEFF.title": "A Measure of Iron",
  "quest.5F676C980602FEFF.quest_desc": [
    "Terra · Measure and shape",
    "",
    "Build a Mekanism metallurgic infuser with one frame from First Signal, then infuse a raw lens with redstone to copy the frame. Deliver the copy to Precision Bench in the Atlas and keep the infuser running: every later frame comes from it.",
    "",
    "Terra's standard joins hand tools and machines in one measure. The same frame holds Heliodor's lens in its solar heating plates."
  ],
  "quest.1AF624DC63ABDC33.title": "A small electrical beginning",
  "quest.1AF624DC63ABDC33.quest_desc": [
    "Power with a purpose",
    "",
    "Build an Actually Additions coal generator (iron casings with black quartz, iron and wooden rods) and keep fuel nearby.",
    "",
    "A soot-stained page: 'Coal, for now. Until the sun. —T.'"
  ],
  "quest.4E94D46197FC6BC3.title": "A beam with a job",
  "quest.4E94D46197FC6BC3.quest_desc": [
    "Power with a purpose",
    "",
    "Build an Atomic Reconstructor (iron casing, iron and redstone), power it and test it with one redstone dust where drops are easy to recover.",
    "",
    "Heliodor shaped matter with light long before it tried to shape anything bigger."
  ],
  "quest.5525FEC32B117FD6.title": "Redstone remembers another shape",
  "quest.5525FEC32B117FD6.quest_desc": [
    "Power with a purpose",
    "",
    "Beam redstone dust into ordinary Restonia crystals (40 energy each). Keep two, with an iron casing and two Create andesite alloys, for an energy coupler.",
    "",
    "The crystals hum at the same pitch as the Atlas. Terra noticed too; her margin only says: 'Why?'"
  ],
  "quest.5281CA2BAADED9DF.title": "A Crystal Connection",
  "quest.5281CA2BAADED9DF.quest_desc": [
    "Power with a purpose",
    "",
    "Craft an energy coupler from two Restonia crystals, an iron casing and two andesite alloys, and deliver it to Crystal Grid in the Atlas. Your generator and reconstructor stay installed.",
    "",
    "With the coupler, Heliodor turned rotation into current. Every generator coil it built asks for one."
  ],
  "quest.13D42DB7A4E29182.title": "Write a first working spell",
  "quest.13D42DB7A4E29182.quest_desc": [
    "A workshop that grows",
    "",
    "Make a novice spell book from a book and a spare iron shovel, pickaxe, axe and sword, then try a utility spell somewhere safe.",
    "",
    "Beside Terra's machines, someone kept a quieter shelf of prayers and spells, signed with a single letter: B."
  ],
  "quest.1751AC5350F46D6C.title": "Keep a source-gem reserve",
  "quest.1751AC5350F46D6C.quest_desc": [
    "A workshop that grows",
    "",
    "Make Ars source gems by imbuing amethyst or lapis in an imbuement chamber (archwood planks and gold). The living matrix needs two.",
    "",
    "B. wrote that magic is tended, not squeezed. The workshop's gem beds were never emptied."
  ],
  "quest.0D777B65AE7AD4C0.title": "A crop with workshop uses",
  "quest.0D777B65AE7AD4C0.quest_desc": [
    "A workshop that grows",
    "",
    "At an Enchanting Apparatus (diamond, gold and sourcestone), a seed with four source gems makes magebloom seeds; the listed Source cost is zero. Grow a bed and craft the blooms into fibers: keep two.",
    "",
    "A flower grown to be woven into machines. Heliodor never quite saw a line between the two."
  ],
  "quest.7A2C3D602817EC20.title": "The living workshop",
  "quest.7A2C3D602817EC20.quest_desc": [
    "A workshop that grows",
    "",
    "Craft a living matrix (two magebloom fibers, two source gems and a new calibration frame) and deliver it to Living Workshop in the Atlas after Precision Bench.",
    "",
    "Terra's measurements drawn over B.'s garden bed: the only page in the workshop signed by both."
  ],
  "quest.60274F8FAAB2F834.title": "The kitchen keeps working",
  "quest.60274F8FAAB2F834.quest_desc": [
    "J. · Provision the journey",
    "",
    "Build a Farmer's Delight cooking pot (iron, bricks, a water bucket and a wooden shovel), set it over heat and cook a batch from nearby crops.",
    "",
    "J.'s list puts a cooking pot before any second machine. A workshop runs on whoever feeds it."
  ],
  "quest.53F96B4513813835.title": "Use the catch",
  "quest.53F96B4513813835.quest_desc": [
    "J. · Provision the journey",
    "",
    "Fillet a catch with an Aquaculture knife and cook the fillets on a campfire, in a furnace or in a smoker. Save some for rations.",
    "",
    "The workshop's canal still has fish. J. stocked it himself, the note says, 'for the long shifts'."
  ],
  "quest.7B649EF9ED27AC7F.title": "Pack a real travelling meal",
  "quest.7B649EF9ED27AC7F.quest_desc": [
    "J. · Provision the journey",
    "",
    "Two vegetable soups and two cooked Aquaculture fish fillets make one pack of Travel Rations; the soup takes carrot, potato, beetroot and leafy-green tags.",
    "",
    "J. packed these for workers who were not allowed to go home. The note does not say who gave that order."
  ],
  "quest.774DD93299251487.title": "The travelling pantry",
  "quest.774DD93299251487.quest_desc": [
    "J. · Provision the journey",
    "",
    "Open the Atlas and deliver one pack of Travel Rations to Travelling Pantry. No pot, rod or other equipment is taken.",
    "",
    "J.'s note ends with a correction: 'Count the people who come back, not the crates that leave.'"
  ],
  "quest.7ECAF177C9C78440.title": "The traveller's module",
  "quest.7ECAF177C9C78440.quest_desc": [
    "J. · Provision the journey",
    "",
    "Deliver two packs of Travel Rations, a compass, four empty maps and a spyglass to Exploration Module in the Atlas. In its place in the Ark, waystones stop charging your team experience and /rtp opens, once an hour.",
    "",
    "A faded map in the Sunken Workshop, signed —T.: 'Roads were measured in days, not in lives. Travel light and come back.'"
  ],
  "quest.3E9B76FA05037B25.title": "Can the next person repeat it?",
  "quest.3E9B76FA05037B25.quest_desc": [
    "Terra · Measure and shape",
    "",
    "Optional: press a second iron ingot, label the press's input and output, and leave a note on what to check if rotation stops.",
    "",
    "Terra wrote every procedure 'for the next one'. She never expected to be the one missing."
  ],
  "quest.453C69E2CF5980E2.title": "Leave the bed ready",
  "quest.453C69E2CF5980E2.quest_desc": [
    "A workshop that grows",
    "",
    "Optional: harvest a small magebloom batch, process some fibers and leave the bed planted, with seeds and spare fibers stored apart.",
    "",
    "B.'s rule for any garden: leave it ready for someone else's hands."
  ],
  "quest.069839E9FD2685EE.title": "The room in the records",
  "quest.069839E9FD2685EE.quest_desc": [
    "The Sunken Workshop",
    "",
    "With the four projects delivered, bring three paper and one copper ingot to the Atlas and deliver Workshop Archive. Bring Terra's Blueprint, from the Sunken Workshop's vault, as well. The Atlas hands you Terra's Arm, which lengthens your reach while worn.",
    "",
    "The Sunken Workshop agrees at last: no craft ever replaced the others. And through the static, for the first time, the voice says its own name: '…&kTe&rrra.'"
  ],
  "quest.3D2B82152F596665.title": "A workshop worth connecting",
  "quest.3D2B82152F596665.quest_desc": [
    "The Sunken Workshop",
    "",
    "Optional: choose one supply worth improving (sheets, crystals, fibers or provisions) and keep the other benches working. When the act is complete, choose Advance in the Atlas.",
    "",
    "Terra's workshop fed routes she never drew. The next pages follow where everything went."
  ],
  "image.03FB4B88054E9EEE.title": "&#E8DCB5Terra\\nMeasure and shape",
  "image.53449E341176BD4D.title": "&#E8DCB5Power with a purpose\\n ",
  "image.7A2F67C2142D529E.title": "&#E8DCB5A workshop that\\ngrows",
  "image.7FA32DD3E4117588.title": "&#E8DCB5J.\\nProvision the\\njourney",
  "image.581C3012B6280B80.title": "II · The Lost Crafts",
  "chapter.778667D17CE889F6.title": "III · Routes of Exchange",
  "chapter.778667D17CE889F6.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Under a broken glass dome a garden still blooms. Heliodor's routes started here and led to a capital no map shows."
  ],
  "quest.37439F67D72711CE.title": "The silence between workshops",
  "quest.37439F67D72711CE.quest_desc": [
    "The Greenhouse Dome",
    "",
    "Five projects rebuild Heliodor's routes: signal, nursery, power, logistics and hands. Each is a delivery in the Atlas, and the materials come first.",
    "",
    "Under the Greenhouse Dome, Juan's trees still flower. His ledgers show food leaving here for every city, and above all for one: Solsticio."
  ],
  "quest.6B801E1DFD8835ED.title": "Presses from the fallen sky",
  "quest.6B801E1DFD8835ED.quest_desc": [
    "A shared language",
    "",
    "Break a meteorite's mysterious cube without Silk Touch to get the four AE2 presses (a charged meteorite compass points to one), then print and assemble two logic processors in a powered Inscriber.",
    "",
    "Heliodor's routes spoke a language of circuits. The presses fell from the sky; Terra only learned to read them."
  ],
  "quest.67715DD11D530227.title": "A board takes several benches",
  "quest.67715DD11D530227.quest_desc": [
    "A shared language",
    "",
    "Assemble a PneumaticCraft PCB from an unassembled board, two capacitors and two transistors, following its guide for plastic, UV exposure, etching acid and pressures. The Amadron PCB blueprint costs eight emeralds.",
    "",
    "Every route in Juan's ledgers has a board like this at each end, so either side could repair it."
  ],
  "quest.34E8C304216AA748.title": "A blue signal",
  "quest.34E8C304216AA748.quest_desc": [
    "A shared language",
    "",
    "Beam lapis into ordinary Palis crystals at the Atomic Reconstructor (40 energy each). Two go into a routing matrix, with two logic processors, a PCB and a calibration frame.",
    "",
    "Blue was the colour of Heliodor's routes. On the old maps, every blue line ends at the same blank spot."
  ],
  "quest.3E5FB620D650D35E.title": "Budget the first crystal",
  "quest.3E5FB620D650D35E.quest_desc": [
    "Juan · Supplies that return",
    "",
    "Four inferium around an infusion crystal make one prudentium; the crystal costs a diamond, four prosperity shards and four inferium. Budget eight additional inferium for two prudentium.",
    "",
    "Juan grew essences the way he grew wheat: planted, counted, never all at once."
  ],
  "quest.6FF1C6BDC6CF1D6A.title": "Wax from an ordinary hive",
  "quest.6FF1C6BDC6CF1D6A.quest_desc": [
    "Juan · Supplies that return",
    "",
    "Process ordinary Minecraft honeycomb into wax in a basic Productive Bees centrifuge (iron and a grindstone). Two wax, no special breeding.",
    "",
    "The Greenhouse Dome still hums. Juan's bees outlived everyone who kept them."
  ],
  "quest.7E5DA638A8AF99BA.title": "The old garden contributes",
  "quest.7E5DA638A8AF99BA.quest_desc": [
    "Juan · Supplies that return",
    "",
    "Make another living matrix (a calibration frame, two source gems and two magebloom fibers): the act II one was consumed. With two prudentium and two wax it becomes a propagation core.",
    "",
    "Juan's notes grow into B.'s garden bed: the two of them planned this greenhouse together."
  ],
  "quest.1AAAAA6B2E1E4563.title": "Osmium learns a signal",
  "quest.1AAAAA6B2E1E4563.quest_desc": [
    "Terra · Power in many places",
    "",
    "Infuse an osmium ingot with 20 redstone infusion in a powered Metallurgic Infuser to make a basic control circuit. A power regulator needs two.",
    "",
    "A small generator is enough. Heliodor spread its power thin on purpose, so no single failure could take everything."
  ],
  "quest.597D8746CE914B5A.title": "Steel without a giant furnace",
  "quest.597D8746CE914B5A.quest_desc": [
    "Terra · Power in many places",
    "",
    "Hammer a steel ingot into an Immersive Engineering steel plate; Mekanism's carbon infusion (enriched iron, steel dust, then smelting) is an early route to the ingot. Keep two plates.",
    "",
    "The dome's frame is steel under copper. It held the glass up for years after the people were gone."
  ],
  "quest.5D719D69593E262A.title": "A coupling, not a power plant",
  "quest.5D719D69593E262A.quest_desc": [
    "Terra · Power in many places",
    "",
    "Rebuild an energy coupler (two Restonia crystals, an iron casing and two andesite alloys). With two circuits and two steel plates it makes a power regulator.",
    "",
    "The same coupling Terra drew in the Sunken Workshop, now feeding a whole greenhouse."
  ],
  "quest.16E8D490AF70ABCE.title": "Read the tree before the shelf",
  "quest.16E8D490AF70ABCE.quest_desc": [
    "Measure before moving",
    "",
    "Squeeze a Menril log for 1000 mB of resin, dry it in a Drying Basin into a crystallized Menril block, and craft the block into nine chunks. Keep two.",
    "",
    "Juan planted Menril along every route, so the roads themselves could keep count."
  ],
  "quest.4D75C5943C18E96B.title": "Bake the logic",
  "quest.4D75C5943C18E96B.quest_desc": [
    "Measure before moving",
    "",
    "Craft four raw LaserIO logic chips from a quartz block, clay balls, gold nuggets and redstone, and smelt them into finished chips. The sensor needs two.",
    "",
    "Clay and gold, baked like bread. Some of Heliodor's best ideas came out of its kitchens."
  ],
  "quest.601DDFCEB1D5FEA2.title": "A second matrix has a job",
  "quest.601DDFCEB1D5FEA2.quest_desc": [
    "Measure before moving",
    "",
    "Make another routing matrix (two logic processors, a PCB, two Palis crystals and a calibration frame): the first went to A Shared Language. With two Menril chunks and two finished chips it makes an inventory sensor.",
    "",
    "A route that knows when it is full needs nobody shouting at it. Juan's ledgers say that took years to learn."
  ],
  "quest.7C4CA98F4865E101.title": "Paper tells the hands",
  "quest.7C4CA98F4865E101.quest_desc": [
    "A workshop within reach",
    "",
    "Craft six blank Modular Routers modules from paper, gold nuggets and redstone; keep two for the handling core and configure the rest for real jobs.",
    "",
    "In Heliodor, instructions were written on paper first, and only then given to a machine."
  ],
  "quest.130D7A6D79505C81.title": "Five careful passes",
  "quest.130D7A6D79505C81.quest_desc": [
    "A workshop within reach",
    "",
    "Start a Create precision mechanism with a gold plate, then deploy a small cogwheel, a large cogwheel and an iron nugget in order, five times (deployers need brass hands; see Ponder). The result is probabilistic: keep spare inputs.",
    "",
    "Terra's hand shows in every Heliodor mechanism: patient, repeatable, never quite trusting luck."
  ],
  "quest.4634B9599F78810B.title": "A regulator for the hands",
  "quest.4634B9599F78810B.quest_desc": [
    "A workshop within reach",
    "",
    "Make a second power regulator (two basic circuits, two steel plates and an energy coupler); the first was delivered. With two blank modules and a precision mechanism it makes a handling core.",
    "",
    "Hands that pass a part along and keep their tools: Juan's crews worked that way, from dome to dome."
  ],
  "quest.2BF5828C4002A4BD.title": "Label the destination",
  "quest.2BF5828C4002A4BD.quest_desc": [
    "A shared language",
    "",
    "Optional: pick one workshop input, label its source, destination and spare stock, and send a small batch its receiver can recognise unaided.",
    "",
    "Every crate in Juan's ledgers carries a destination. The ones bound for Solsticio carry a golden seal as well."
  ],
  "quest.2D2C52A913E6718A.title": "Leave another harvest possible",
  "quest.2D2C52A913E6718A.quest_desc": [
    "Juan · Supplies that return",
    "",
    "Optional: harvest one crop batch and one ordinary hive batch, and keep back what each needs to produce again.",
    "",
    "Juan never shipped his last seed. 'The city can wait a week,' he wrote. 'The field cannot wait a year.'"
  ],
  "quest.7601671FE64DE066.title": "Watch a whole batch",
  "quest.7601671FE64DE066.quest_desc": [
    "Terra · Power in many places",
    "",
    "Optional: run a small infuser batch and compare its energy buffer before and after; keep spare fuel or a second source.",
    "",
    "Heliodor's glass roofs once caught the sun for machines like these. None of them ever ran on a single source."
  ],
  "quest.758AAF75374D9805.title": "Stop before overflow",
  "quest.758AAF75374D9805.quest_desc": [
    "Measure before moving",
    "",
    "Optional: with Integrated Dynamics and Integrated Tunnels, or LaserIO, read a buffer and stop insertion at a small threshold, then watch it resume.",
    "",
    "Every pipe in the greenhouse has a valve Juan could close by hand. He never trusted a store that could not say 'enough'."
  ],
  "quest.2011CCEBA6EF8242.title": "Thirty-two arrive together",
  "quest.2011CCEBA6EF8242.quest_desc": [
    "A workshop within reach",
    "",
    "Optional: move 32 ordinary items between containers with configured Modular Routers modules or a Create setup, and account for all of them at the other end.",
    "",
    "Juan counted crews the way he counted crates: everyone who left had to arrive."
  ],
  "quest.17BBD680007901AB.title": "A Shared Language",
  "quest.17BBD680007901AB.quest_desc": [
    "A shared language",
    "",
    "Deliver one routing matrix to A Shared Language in the Atlas. It also gives you an Altar of Peace, which keeps hostile creatures from spawning around it.",
    "",
    "Different benches agree on a destination again. The Atlas voice, clearer now: 'Terra here. If you &kcan&r read this… the routes… still work.'"
  ],
  "quest.075794DD2C2DFAA0.title": "Seeds of Continuity",
  "quest.075794DD2C2DFAA0.quest_desc": [
    "Juan · Supplies that return",
    "",
    "Deliver one propagation core to Seeds of Continuity in the Atlas. Bring the Mother Seed, from the Dome Greenhouse, as well. It gives you an Altar of Growth: crops around it grow much faster and yield more.",
    "",
    "Juan designed that altar to feed a Heliodor that never stopped growing. His greenhouse fed multitudes; now it can feed you."
  ],
  "quest.55E5576006404510.title": "Power without a Monolith",
  "quest.55E5576006404510.quest_desc": [
    "Terra · Power in many places",
    "",
    "Deliver one power regulator to Power without a Monolith in the Atlas. Bring the Heliodor Crucible, from the Foundry Under the Lava, as well. Regulators are also what Create's advanced solar heating plates, energisers and motors ask for.",
    "",
    "Terra's drawing leaves room for many small suns instead of one great one. Someone wrote 'inefficient' across it, in gold ink."
  ],
  "quest.27A67154B0D96862.title": "When the Shelf is Full",
  "quest.27A67154B0D96862.quest_desc": [
    "Measure before moving",
    "",
    "Deliver one inventory sensor to When the Shelf is Full in the Atlas.",
    "",
    "A full shelf can warn before it jams. Juan's routes did; the orders from Solsticio never waited for the answer."
  ],
  "quest.6C696AA48D00D512.title": "Small Hands, Large Workshops",
  "quest.6C696AA48D00D512.quest_desc": [
    "A workshop within reach",
    "",
    "Deliver one handling core to Small Hands, Large Workshops in the Atlas. It gives you an Altar of Levelling, which flattens or repairs the ground around it with the land's own blocks, free of materials.",
    "",
    "Heliodor levelled its terraces with this altar and planted every one. The fields went on; the people did not."
  ],
  "quest.1C41DFAC2A66054B.title": "A module that breathes",
  "quest.1C41DFAC2A66054B.quest_desc": [
    "A workshop within reach",
    "",
    "Deliver one propagation core, eight moss blocks and four glistering melon slices to Nature Module in the Atlas. In its place in the Ark it gives your whole team Regeneration and half the hunger, anywhere, and a bookmarked compass marks your garden.",
    "",
    "Juan kept the greenhouse air warm through Heliodor's worst winter. He never asked the plants to grow faster; he asked them to last."
  ],
  "quest.6542C13CC523B0E9.title": "Routes of Exchange",
  "quest.6542C13CC523B0E9.quest_desc": [
    "The Greenhouse Dome",
    "",
    "After the five projects, deliver three paper and one copper ingot to Exchange Route in the Atlas to close the act. Bring the Route Seal, from the Viaduct, as well.",
    "",
    "Every route ends at Solsticio, the capital, and Solsticio is on no map. Terra's voice: 'Look up. The city &mfell&r… did not fall. It is &kstill&r… here.'"
  ],
  "image.1DB295BCFB482280.title": "&#E8DCB5A shared language\\n ",
  "image.1338180D935C206D.title": "&#E8DCB5Juan\\nSupplies that return",
  "image.6927ADE174034DB6.title": "&#E8DCB5Terra\\nPower in many places",
  "image.7C0FD0C7A3DDAD7A.title": "&#E8DCB5Measure before\\nmoving",
  "image.66F68AD0DC228920.title": "&#E8DCB5A workshop within\\nreach",
  "image.15CF12312DD272BC.title": "III · Routes of Exchange",
  "chapter.5EDFD33D3A393061.title": "IV · Voices of the Atlas",
  "chapter.5EDFD33D3A393061.chapter_subtitle": [
    "From an observatory on a cliff, Heliodor watched the sky. In the Temple of the Sacred Light it tried to seize it. In the Aether, the Sun Spirit stopped it."
  ],
  "quest.4C15458A9B706E5B.title": "The missing witnesses",
  "quest.4C15458A9B706E5B.quest_desc": [
    "The Observatory · The witnesses",
    "",
    "Four routes lead to this act's Atlas projects, and a fifth ends at the Sun Spirit; arrivals in other worlds are recorded on their own when your team gets there.",
    "",
    "The Cliffside Observatory still points at the same patch of sky. Its log ends on a single line: 'The light answered.'"
  ],
  "quest.2D6ECC29EBA13A7E.title": "Aether: a witnessed arrival",
  "quest.2D6ECC29EBA13A7E.quest_desc": [
    "Journeys recorded by the team",
    "",
    "Reach the Aether with anyone on your team; arriving, logging in or respawning there counts, even in an earlier act. Clicking this task does nothing: the server records the journey.",
    "",
    "The Observatory's telescope pointed here. Heliodor went up to ask the sky a question."
  ],
  "quest.7FC45742FF7B3AC7.title": "Twilight Forest: a witnessed arrival",
  "quest.7FC45742FF7B3AC7.quest_desc": [
    "Journeys recorded by the team",
    "",
    "Reach the Twilight Forest with anyone on your team; arriving, logging in or respawning there counts, even in an earlier act. The server records it and there is nothing to deliver.",
    "",
    "Heliodor's gardeners called this forest the rehearsal: a world where the light never quite arrives. Juan kept a sanctuary here."
  ],
  "quest.5F8D676F685B8FCE.title": "Bumblezone: a witnessed arrival",
  "quest.5F8D676F685B8FCE.quest_desc": [
    "Journeys recorded by the team",
    "",
    "Reach the Bumblezone with anyone on your team; arriving, logging in or respawning there counts, even in an earlier act. The server records it and there is nothing to claim.",
    "",
    "Juan's bees came from here. Heliodor signed a treaty with them, and the bees still keep their side."
  ],
  "quest.04C25D07C0D4FB2A.title": "A crystal tuned to listening",
  "quest.04C25D07C0D4FB2A.quest_desc": [
    "Listen to the fragments",
    "",
    "Make Spirit Fire (drop datura and light it with flint and steel), turn four diamonds into four spirit-attuned gems in it, and craft the gems 2×2 into one spirit-attuned crystal.",
    "",
    "The Observatory listened as well as looked. Its crystals still catch voices nobody is speaking."
  ],
  "quest.3BF05DF763333CD9.title": "Two fragments of testimony",
  "quest.3BF05DF763333CD9.quest_desc": [
    "Listen to the fragments",
    "",
    "Make Malum's crude scythe (three iron ingots, one refined soulstone and two wooden rods) and kill a witch with it for arcane spirits. Keep two for each spectral lens.",
    "",
    "Every spirit the scythe frees carries a scrap of something it saw. Heliodor's scraps all end in the same flash."
  ],
  "quest.470125DBFA02EAFD.title": "A patient shutter",
  "quest.470125DBFA02EAFD.quest_desc": [
    "Listen to the fragments",
    "",
    "Prepare one Create precision mechanism for the spectral lens; its assembly can fail, so budget a few attempts.",
    "",
    "The Observatory's shutter opened for one second a night. Terra built it; the order to open it wider came from someone else."
  ],
  "quest.4066B5E1E0D6EF29.title": "The familiar frame",
  "quest.4066B5E1E0D6EF29.quest_desc": [
    "Listen to the fragments",
    "",
    "Craft a calibration frame from two iron sheets, two copper wires and a raw lens; the spectral lens consumes it.",
    "",
    "Terra's frame again, the same measure as in the first workshop. She built everything to fit together. That was the problem."
  ],
  "quest.599BBE74166CEC6E.title": "Assemble the spectral lens",
  "quest.599BBE74166CEC6E.quest_desc": [
    "Listen to the fragments",
    "",
    "Combine a spirit-attuned crystal, two arcane spirits, a precision mechanism and a calibration frame into one spectral lens. Plan two lenses: the archive takes one and the containment seal another.",
    "",
    "Through the lens the static thins. You can hear several voices now, and one of them is giving orders."
  ],
  "quest.3A81D7FB202BC1EF.title": "A route with a return",
  "quest.3A81D7FB202BC1EF.quest_desc": [
    "Compare distant skies",
    "",
    "Optional: the Aether portal is a glowstone frame lit with water; the Twilight Forest opens when you throw a diamond into a 2×2 pool ringed with flowers (lightning strikes, so stand back). Pack food and mark the way home.",
    "",
    "The Observatory's charts mark both doors. Heliodor never went through one without a way back."
  ],
  "quest.72D8C6025B573FA7.title": "Light above the clouds",
  "quest.72D8C6025B573FA7.quest_desc": [
    "Compare distant skies",
    "",
    "Mine ambrosium ore in the Aether for two ambrosium shards, and keep them apart from your expedition supplies.",
    "",
    "The Aether's light is not the sun's. Heliodor noticed first, and wanted it."
  ],
  "quest.63A78566481EFF47.title": "A forest worked into metal",
  "quest.63A78566481EFF47.quest_desc": [
    "Compare distant skies",
    "",
    "Craft raw ironwood from liveroot, raw iron and a gold nugget, and smelt it into two ironwood ingots.",
    "",
    "Juan's sanctuary in the forest kept samples of everything, labelled with the place and the date. The last label has no date."
  ],
  "quest.00A91663CFB48B49.title": "Food for the record and the road",
  "quest.00A91663CFB48B49.quest_desc": [
    "Compare distant skies",
    "",
    "Make a spare pack of Travel Rations (two vegetable soups and two cooked fish fillets); the horizon chart consumes one, along with survey notes, which can be crafted again. Bring separate food to eat.",
    "",
    "Juan packed rations for the Observatory's night crews. The last order asked for double, 'for the ceremony'."
  ],
  "quest.3DD3BA9CAD0FBB51.title": "Two skies on one page",
  "quest.3DD3BA9CAD0FBB51.quest_desc": [
    "Compare distant skies",
    "",
    "Craft a horizon chart from two ambrosium shards, two ironwood ingots, survey notes and Travel Rations. Before delivering it, check that your team has arrived in both the Aether and the Twilight Forest.",
    "",
    "On one page, two skies that disagree about the colour of morning. The Observatory kept both."
  ],
  "quest.589D6D9B175C666C.title": "Enter as a guest",
  "quest.589D6D9B175C666C.quest_desc": [
    "Juan · A living agreement",
    "",
    "Optional: throw an ender pearl at a beehive or bee nest to enter the Bumblezone. Mark where you left and learn the way back first; hitting bees or taking honey carelessly brings Wrath.",
    "",
    "Juan's treaty had one clause: take nothing you cannot give back."
  ],
  "quest.72A9A7677DB57D63.title": "Carry a little of the meadow",
  "quest.72A9A7677DB57D63.quest_desc": [
    "Juan · A living agreement",
    "",
    "Gather two pollen puffs from pollen piles in the Bumblezone, using a tool without Silk Touch.",
    "",
    "Pollen from the treaty meadow. Juan's bees still remember the smell of the greenhouse."
  ],
  "quest.10D4D0C6845BF1A4.title": "Wax from the treaty hives",
  "quest.10D4D0C6845BF1A4.quest_desc": [
    "Juan · A living agreement",
    "",
    "Prepare two Productive Bees wax: ordinary honeycomb goes through the centrifuge, with no special breeding needed.",
    "",
    "The treaty was sealed in wax: Juan's way of saying it could be melted and made again."
  ],
  "quest.155E722412CD338B.title": "Two living supports",
  "quest.155E722412CD338B.quest_desc": [
    "Juan · A living agreement",
    "",
    "Prepare two living matrices, each from two magebloom fibers, two source gems and a calibration frame.",
    "",
    "Terra's frame, Juan's fibers, B.'s gems: the three of them still hold together in one object."
  ],
  "quest.780224C0B0190A32.title": "A small agreement",
  "quest.780224C0B0190A32.quest_desc": [
    "Juan · A living agreement",
    "",
    "Combine two pollen puffs, two Productive Bees wax and two living matrices into one ecosystem capsule.",
    "",
    "A whole meadow's agreement, small enough to carry. Heliodor's Altar of Renewal was built around one of these."
  ],
  "quest.7201D80B58E95944.title": "A dark edge for the vessel",
  "quest.7201D80B58E95944.quest_desc": [
    "The Temple · What was sealed",
    "",
    "Mine EvilCraft dark ore for two dark gems; check the tool tier and the Origins of Darkness guide first.",
    "",
    "The Temple of the Sacred Light is ringed with dark stone. Its builders knew the light needed a boundary."
  ],
  "quest.13E112503294DBB6.title": "Steel with a remembered purpose",
  "quest.13E112503294DBB6.quest_desc": [
    "The Temple · What was sealed",
    "",
    "At Malum's Spirit Altar, an iron ingot, four refined soulstone, three wicked, one earthen and one arcane spirit make one soul-stained steel ingot. For two, gather eight refined soulstone, six wicked, two earthen and two arcane spirits.",
    "",
    "B. was Bodhi, the temple's priest. He forged the sanctuary's seals from this steel, and he was the one who said no."
  ],
  "quest.26ECD64E96DE924C.title": "A second listening glass",
  "quest.26ECD64E96DE924C.quest_desc": [
    "The Temple · What was sealed",
    "",
    "Craft a second spectral lens for the containment seal, with the same crystal, spirits, mechanism and frame.",
    "",
    "One lens for the archive, one for the seal. Bodhi's note: 'Whatever you listen to, you must also be able to close.'"
  ],
  "quest.7DB1A841D53C017A.title": "Keep the silence legible",
  "quest.7DB1A841D53C017A.quest_desc": [
    "The Temple · What was sealed",
    "",
    "Optional: set the archive's materials apart from the seal's and check which lens each one consumes.",
    "",
    "In the temple, one line of testimony stays unreadable. Bodhi left it that way on purpose: some gaps should not be filled with a convenient answer."
  ],
  "quest.429BA86EC20C7A84.title": "Close the vessel gently",
  "quest.429BA86EC20C7A84.quest_desc": [
    "The Temple · What was sealed",
    "",
    "Craft one containment seal from two dark gems, two soul-stained steel ingots and a spectral lens; reactor rods for thorium fission ask for one as well.",
    "",
    "The seal is Bodhi's answer to the temple's machine: not a cage for the light, a boundary around it."
  ],
  "quest.4BC3DA06CD2E169A.title": "Voices in the Glass",
  "quest.4BC3DA06CD2E169A.quest_desc": [
    "Listen to the fragments",
    "",
    "Open the Atlas and deliver one spectral lens to Voices in the Glass; keep the second lens for the seal. Bring the Eyepiece of Voices (Cliff Observatory), the Forest Testimony (Sanctuary) and the Sacred Flame (Temple) as well. Reinforced energisers and motors also take a spectral lens.",
    "",
    "The Observatory's crystal plays back a council session. A woman's voice, calm and certain: 'We will not worship the light. We will &mown&r… hold it.' The others call her Aurelia."
  ],
  "quest.6F61C77D6FFCC3F3.title": "Above and Beyond the Canopy",
  "quest.6F61C77D6FFCC3F3.quest_desc": [
    "Compare distant skies",
    "",
    "Once your team has arrived in the Aether and the Twilight Forest, deliver one horizon chart to Above and Beyond the Canopy in the Atlas. It gives you an Altar of Repose, a small chest that slowly mends the gear inside.",
    "",
    "The Observatory's last chart marks a point above the Aether's clouds, circled in gold: where the light came from."
  ],
  "quest.3329AFECCED6CAAD.title": "The Pollinators Agreement",
  "quest.3329AFECCED6CAAD.quest_desc": [
    "Juan · A living agreement",
    "",
    "Once your team has arrived in the Bumblezone, deliver one ecosystem capsule to The Pollinators Agreement in the Atlas. It gives you an Altar of Renewal, which grows the trees and flowers of its biome around it, with a dye garden that makes every colour.",
    "",
    "Juan's treaty still holds: the bees kept working after the witnesses left. Some promises outlive the people who made them."
  ],
  "quest.09ED3CB7AB982A11.title": "A Vessel for Restless Memory",
  "quest.09ED3CB7AB982A11.quest_desc": [
    "The Temple · What was sealed",
    "",
    "After Voices in the Glass, deliver one containment seal to A Vessel for Restless Memory in the Atlas. It gives you an Altar of Time: hostile creatures around it move in slow motion and drop far more.",
    "",
    "In the Temple of the Sacred Light the memory opens. Aurelia's council fused the sacred light with Terra's machines to build a god that would obey. Bodhi warned them; the crater is what his warning looked like."
  ],
  "quest.0E407D24B1E4BA07.title": "The Sun Spirit",
  "quest.0E407D24B1E4BA07.quest_desc": [
    "The Aether · The Sun Spirit",
    "",
    "Defeat a Sun Spirit in one of the Aether's gold dungeons; the compass leads there after the silver dungeon. Only its own ice crystals, struck back at it, can wound it. The first one your team defeats drops the Heart of Heliodor, and the server records it.",
    "",
    "It did not destroy Heliodor: it stopped it, and kept the Heart so no one could try again. Bodhi, through the noise: 'It was never &mtheirs&r… never anyone's to take.'"
  ],
  "quest.2BAA7A0AC06298AA.title": "A Clear Voice",
  "quest.2BAA7A0AC06298AA.quest_desc": [
    "The Aether · The Sun Spirit",
    "",
    "Deliver the Heart of Heliodor to A Clear Voice in the Atlas. Bring the Sun Key, from the Sun Antechamber, as well. Only your team's own Heart counts, the one your Sun Spirit dropped. The Atlas keeps it; you will need it again in Solsticio.",
    "",
    "The crystal settles into the Atlas like a key into a lock, and the noise falls away. Terra, whole for the first time: 'There you are. We have always been able to hear you.'"
  ],
  "quest.4BCEABDD4D9E618C.title": "Mana that overflows",
  "quest.4BCEABDD4D9E618C.quest_desc": [
    "The Temple · What was sealed",
    "",
    "Deliver one spectral lens, sixteen amethyst shards and sixteen lapis lazuli to Arcane Module in the Atlas. In its place in the Ark your team's maximum mana and its regeneration rise by half, in every magic that shows them.",
    "",
    "Bodhi never trusted a power that had to be taken. 'Let it overflow,' he wrote, 'and nobody has to fight over the cup.'"
  ],
  "quest.360D23E7AD32EF6E.title": "The Atlas keeps their voices",
  "quest.360D23E7AD32EF6E.quest_desc": [
    "The Observatory · The witnesses",
    "",
    "With the five projects recorded, the Heart among them, deliver three paper and one copper ingot to The Voices of the Atlas, then choose Advance.",
    "",
    "The temple's last page, read aloud at last: the fusion did not destroy Heliodor, because the Sun Spirit stopped it first and froze everyone inside the light. Terra: 'Now you know what we did. Help us leave without doing it again.'"
  ],
  "image.5D3B686B381AC801.title": "&#E8DCB5Listen to the\\nfragments",
  "image.5A3B25ECD442E8FD.title": "&#E8DCB5Compare distant\\nskies",
  "image.29EE397B163A9AB6.title": "&#E8DCB5Juan\\nA living agreement",
  "image.4D895E524719B78E.title": "&#E8DCB5The Temple\\nWhat was sealed",
  "image.4B16CD2CA0C39EE9.title": "IV · Voices of the Atlas",
  "chapter.068A1E3F716693DD.title": "V · The Ark",
  "chapter.068A1E3F716693DD.chapter_subtitle": [
    "With the Heart of Heliodor in the Atlas, the voice arrives whole: they are alive, inside the light. Build the Ark that opens the way without repeating the fusion."
  ],
  "quest.6E93F29B79991680.title": "A whole voice",
  "quest.6E93F29B79991680.quest_desc": [
    "Terra · The Ark's plan",
    "",
    "Three projects prepare the Ark's plan; its six modules, their batches and the activation follow in V · The Activation. Only deliveries in the Atlas record them.",
    "",
    "With the Heart in the Atlas, Terra's voice arrives whole: 'We are alive, inside the light. We call it the Entrelumen. Build the Ark, and this time do not try to own what you open.'"
  ],
  "quest.7B041D8C096D588D.title": "Two alloys for the bypass",
  "quest.7B041D8C096D588D.quest_desc": [
    "A network that recovers",
    "",
    "Make two Mekanism atomic alloys in the Metallurgic Infuser: infused alloy with 20 diamond infusion gives reinforced alloy, and reinforced alloy with 40 refined-obsidian infusion gives atomic alloy.",
    "",
    "Terra designed the Ark's bus with a second path around every part. The fusion machine had none."
  ],
  "quest.3B42EB9382C43AAF.title": "A second path for the order",
  "quest.3B42EB9382C43AAF.quest_desc": [
    "A network that recovers",
    "",
    "Prepare two PneumaticCraft printed circuit boards: an Empty PCB from the Pressure Chamber, exposed in a UV Light Box and etched, then assembled with two capacitors and two transistors.",
    "",
    "The boards that ran Juan's routes now carry the Ark's orders. Nothing in it is new, and that is the point."
  ],
  "quest.616121CD1220D7F0.title": "Keep the hands at work",
  "quest.616121CD1220D7F0.quest_desc": [
    "A network that recovers",
    "",
    "Set aside two handling cores for the bus, each from two blank router modules, a precision mechanism and a power regulator.",
    "",
    "Hands that pass a part on and keep their tools. Terra wants the Ark built by many hands, never by one machine."
  ],
  "quest.6C6D77098E537A3C.title": "Know what the buffer holds",
  "quest.6C6D77098E537A3C.quest_desc": [
    "A network that recovers",
    "",
    "Add one inventory sensor to the bus recipe: Menril chunks, LaserIO logic chips and a routing matrix, as in act III.",
    "",
    "The fusion drew power until nothing was left. The Ark has to know when it is full, and stop."
  ],
  "quest.765DEE642FC97F72.title": "A bus with a way around",
  "quest.765DEE642FC97F72.quest_desc": [
    "A network that recovers",
    "",
    "In a crafting grid combine two atomic alloys, two printed circuit boards, two handling cores and one inventory sensor: seven slots make one Ark Connection Bus. Modern Industrialization's nuclear reactor and Ad Astra's NASA workbench ask for one too.",
    "",
    "The Ark's spine. Terra: 'If one route fails, the others carry it. That is all I wanted from the start.'"
  ],
  "quest.612B6CF528DB5881.title": "Field note: empty, refill, resume",
  "quest.612B6CF528DB5881.quest_desc": [
    "Optional field notes · self-reported",
    "",
    "Optional, self-reported: label one input buffer, note its count, cut its supply and let a small job draw it down; restore it and check that the next batch finishes once.",
    "",
    "A pause that can be resumed is what Heliodor lacked. The fusion had only one speed."
  ],
  "quest.7A6A246A99FABD76.title": "A Network that Recovers",
  "quest.7A6A246A99FABD76.quest_desc": [
    "A network that recovers",
    "",
    "Deliver one Ark Connection Bus to A Network That Recovers in the Atlas.",
    "",
    "The first piece of the Ark is a way around failure. Terra, quietly: 'Aurelia asked me for a god. For you, I am building a door.'"
  ],
  "quest.6A0476FB91872873.title": "Metal from an open sky",
  "quest.6A0476FB91872873.quest_desc": [
    "Juan · A reserve that grows back",
    "",
    "Make two Nature's Aura sky ingots at a flower-decorated Offering Table, using a Spirit of Calling crafted from Overworld and Nether aura bottles, a diamond, infused iron and tainted gold. Infused iron gives one ingot; tainted gold gives two.",
    "",
    "Juan grew metal under the open sky long before the council wanted the sky itself."
  ],
  "quest.1CCC9F83FE8B9B51.title": "A harvest with a ceiling",
  "quest.1CCC9F83FE8B9B51.quest_desc": [
    "Juan · A reserve that grows back",
    "",
    "Prepare two imperium essences: four tertium around an infusion crystal make one, and each lower tier also takes four, so two imperium cost eight tertium, or 128 inferium.",
    "",
    "Juan's fear, even now inside the light, is running out. A reserve that grows back is his part of the Ark."
  ],
  "quest.60C09916BD96526A.title": "Carry the habitat forward",
  "quest.60C09916BD96526A.quest_desc": [
    "Juan · A reserve that grows back",
    "",
    "Set aside two ecosystem capsules, each from two pollen puffs, two Productive Bees wax and two living matrices, as in act IV.",
    "",
    "The treaty meadow, carried into the Ark. Juan wants the bees to come along."
  ],
  "quest.409935D6C0EBDC29.title": "Leave the nursery growing",
  "quest.409935D6C0EBDC29.quest_desc": [
    "Juan · A reserve that grows back",
    "",
    "Add two propagation cores (prudentium, wax and a living matrix each), budgeted apart from the imperium and capsules.",
    "",
    "The greenhouse recipe again, doubled. Juan's nursery is the one part of Heliodor that never stopped."
  ],
  "quest.6F3334D0429BBA36.title": "The reserve's engine",
  "quest.6F3334D0429BBA36.quest_desc": [
    "Juan · A reserve that grows back",
    "",
    "Combine two sky ingots, two imperium essences, two ecosystem capsules and two propagation cores in a crafting grid. Eight slots make one renewal engine; Modern Industrialization's quantum circuits need one too.",
    "",
    "Juan's rule, built into a machine: take only what can grow back."
  ],
  "quest.5DE0AEDC6388B1EE.title": "Field note: take one, grow one",
  "quest.5DE0AEDC6388B1EE.quest_desc": [
    "Optional field notes · self-reported",
    "",
    "Optional, self-reported: take one bounded batch from your crops, your hive and your aura route, and let each recover before repeating.",
    "",
    "Juan asks the question he has asked for years inside the light: will there be enough tomorrow?"
  ],
  "quest.0FA172F312611EF8.title": "Renewable Horizons",
  "quest.0FA172F312611EF8.quest_desc": [
    "Juan · A reserve that grows back",
    "",
    "Deliver one renewal engine to Renewable Horizons in the Atlas.",
    "",
    "Juan, from inside the Entrelumen: 'Take only what can grow back before the next person needs it. I have fed a whole city on that rule.'"
  ],
  "quest.2BA2EF5E6E24A403.title": "Two meals before departure",
  "quest.2BA2EF5E6E24A403.quest_desc": [
    "Aurelia · A place to return to",
    "",
    "Cook two Farmer's Delight fish stews in a cooking pot, from raw fish with tomato sauce and onion.",
    "",
    "Aurelia's charter for the Ark begins, surprisingly, with food. Whoever comes through must be fed."
  ],
  "quest.3B412771A4C57233.title": "Something fresh on the shelf",
  "quest.3B412771A4C57233.quest_desc": [
    "Aurelia · A place to return to",
    "",
    "Make two mixed salads from a leafy green, tomato, beetroot and bowl.",
    "",
    "A fresh plate on the charter's list, in Juan's hand. Aurelia signed underneath without changing a word."
  ],
  "quest.77320E2B7BDC2510.title": "A count the next person can read",
  "quest.77320E2B7BDC2510.quest_desc": [
    "Aurelia · A place to return to",
    "",
    "Add one AE2 calculation processor, printed in the Inscriber, to the Habitation Charter.",
    "",
    "Aurelia counts everything; it is how she governs. For once, the count is for the people arriving, not for the council."
  ],
  "quest.7CDE8A7F14D2DA00.title": "Food for the road and the return",
  "quest.7CDE8A7F14D2DA00.quest_desc": [
    "Aurelia · A place to return to",
    "",
    "Set aside two packs of Travel Rations (two vegetable soups and two cooked fish fillets each), apart from the stew and salad.",
    "",
    "The same rations Juan packed for the workshop's long shifts. This time they are for a door that opens both ways."
  ],
  "quest.7D7BB71A417C6A1F.title": "A charter for an inhabited place",
  "quest.7D7BB71A417C6A1F.quest_desc": [
    "Aurelia · A place to return to",
    "",
    "Combine two fish stews, two mixed salads, one calculation processor and two packs of Travel Rations: seven slots make one Habitation Charter, and the four bowls come back to you.",
    "",
    "Aurelia's seal on a promise: whoever crosses will find a place to live. She has not yet said what she wants in return."
  ],
  "quest.64A39E89998AE121.title": "Field note: a room someone can use",
  "quest.64A39E89998AE121.quest_desc": [
    "Optional field notes · self-reported",
    "",
    "Optional, self-reported: walk from your arrival point to a lit bed, a reachable kitchen and a pantry with readable stock, and ask whether a newcomer could manage alone.",
    "",
    "Soon, people who have not walked in the sun for years will come through. Bodhi asks only that they feel welcome."
  ],
  "quest.41D22D9557C9E920.title": "A Place Worth Returning To",
  "quest.41D22D9557C9E920.quest_desc": [
    "Aurelia · A place to return to",
    "",
    "Deliver one Habitation Charter to A Place to Return To in the Atlas.",
    "",
    "The first day's sentence, complete at last. Terra: 'Make room for those who have not arrived yet. We are the ones.'"
  ],
  "quest.49D5419C7B57F699.title": "Field note: a visible pause",
  "quest.49D5419C7B57F699.quest_desc": [
    "Optional field notes · self-reported",
    "",
    "Optional, self-reported: if you enjoy ComputerCraft, build a small panel that shows a buffer's count and whether it is paused; a sign and a manual stop work just as well.",
    "",
    "Terra's workshop had a board like this on every wall. Nobody should have to guess whether a machine is running."
  ],
  "quest.2186E0A1EC9CA518.title": "A door, not a god",
  "quest.2186E0A1EC9CA518.quest_desc": [
    "Terra · The Ark's plan",
    "",
    "When the three projects are recorded, deliver three paper and one copper ingot to World Network in the Atlas. Bring the Star Chart, from the Void Observatory, as well. The six module projects open next, in V · The Activation; there is no Advance here.",
    "",
    "The Ark's plan is complete: six modules around a controller that opens a rift in the light. Once you activate it, the Ark will forge the Light Key. Bodhi's only condition: 'Open it. Never own it.'"
  ],
  "image.282226BC39CBEDE9.title": "&#E8DCB5A network that\\nrecovers",
  "image.190ECD9B1C347E05.title": "&#E8DCB5Juan\\nA reserve that grows\\nback",
  "image.30AFDFA039D87D2A.title": "&#E8DCB5Aurelia\\nA place to return to\\n ",
  "image.6FD005BB32A7B418.title": "V · The Ark",
  "chapter.74FF10FB2B3398AB.title": "V · The Activation",
  "chapter.74FF10FB2B3398AB.chapter_subtitle": [
    "The Ark stands with its six modules and its controller: one deliberate act opens a seam in the light and forges the Light Key."
  ],
  "quest.7DC68DC8093ED0F0.title": "The Ark takes shape",
  "quest.7DC68DC8093ED0F0.quest_desc": [
    "Terra · The Ark's controller",
    "",
    "Build six different Ark modules, place them around the controller and commission them one batch at a time; activating the Ark forges the Light Key and opens act VI.",
    "",
    "Terra spreads the plan across the Atlas: six chambers, one for each discipline of Heliodor. 'The fusion wanted one machine to hold everything. This time, six hands hold one door.'"
  ],
  "quest.6ADB6852EF50938D.title": "A controller, not a throne",
  "quest.6ADB6852EF50938D.quest_desc": [
    "Terra · The Ark's controller",
    "",
    "Craft the Ark Controller shapelessly from one lodestone, one signal core and one diamond. It marks where the Ark stands and the modules need it: place it first and build around it with the guide the Atlas projects.",
    "",
    "Aurelia wanted a throne at the centre of the fusion machine. Terra built a controller instead: anyone can read it, and it obeys only a team that finished its work."
  ],
  "quest.6FAA2E089CEFD78E.title": "Field note: the Ark on its feet",
  "quest.6FAA2E089CEFD78E.quest_desc": [
    "The Ark · The activation",
    "",
    "Optional, self-reported: build the Ark round its controller. In the Atlas, select The Ark and choose Show guide: a ghost marks every block. Each module works once it is in its place, the Ark is whole and the controller stands.",
    "",
    "An astrolabe of stone and copper. Terra drew it so anyone could read the sky from it, even a child."
  ],
  "quest.5B5E7641B77420D5.title": "Logistics: trade from afar",
  "quest.5B5E7641B77420D5.quest_desc": [
    "The last two modules",
    "",
    "Deliver one routing matrix, sixteen emeralds and eight ender pearls to Logistics Module in the Atlas. In its place in the Ark your team buys from the Atlas in the Solsticio shops it knows, and villagers treat you as a Hero of the Village.",
    "",
    "Aurelia kept a ledger of every debt of the fusion. Its last line reads: 'Trade honestly with those who stayed.'"
  ],
  "quest.50643B60ED2D63DF.title": "Engineering: charge without wires",
  "quest.50643B60ED2D63DF.quest_desc": [
    "The last two modules",
    "",
    "Deliver one Ark Connection Bus, eight blocks of redstone and eight blocks of copper to Engineering Module in the Atlas. In its place in the Ark every item with energy your team carries charges itself, in any dimension.",
    "",
    "Terra's first rule for the fusion machine: 'Power goes where the people are, not where the cables end.'"
  ],
  "quest.0755047847D475BE.title": "The old doorway",
  "quest.0755047847D475BE.quest_desc": [
    "The End · A witnessed journey",
    "",
    "Craft Eyes of Ender from ender pearls and blaze powder. A thrown eye leads toward a stronghold, and its portal frame needs eyes to open; bring enough for both. Carrying eyes only prepares the trip: your campaign still has to enter the End.",
    "",
    "The Atlas remembers this doorway from Heliodor's oldest charts. They never used it. They were too busy looking up."
  ],
  "quest.29624D0B73CD7B51.title": "Field note: a way home",
  "quest.29624D0B73CD7B51.quest_desc": [
    "The End · A witnessed journey",
    "",
    "Optional, self-reported: pack food, protection and blocks before the stronghold portal and agree on a return route. In a new End, defeating the dragon opens the exit home; on a shared world it may already be open, and your team needs no second kill.",
    "",
    "Bodhi asks one thing of every journey: that it ends where it began, with everyone."
  ],
  "quest.0ED905C35BF0C497.title": "A horizon actually crossed",
  "quest.0ED905C35BF0C497.quest_desc": [
    "The End · A witnessed journey",
    "",
    "Enter the End with your current team. The server witnesses real entry, login or respawn there; an earlier visit counts, even before act V. Joining a team does not bring your personal travels with you, and clicking this task does nothing.",
    "",
    "Terra needs the End's silence measured for the exploration module: the one place the light of the Aether never reached."
  ],
  "quest.70A235F354AA1ED4.title": "The Ark opens the light",
  "quest.70A235F354AA1ED4.quest_desc": [
    "The Ark · The activation",
    "",
    "With the Ark standing, its six modules and controller in place, World Network complete and the End journey witnessed, crouch and interact with the controller with an empty main hand. It consumes nothing and forges your team's Light Key. Act VI begins.",
    "",
    "The light parts along a seam. Bodhi, very quietly: 'Open it. Never own it.' Behind it, Solsticio."
  ],
  "quest.58F2D36080402035.title": "Afterward: two routes",
  "quest.58F2D36080402035.quest_desc": [
    "After the activation · self-reported",
    "",
    "Optional, self-reported: make two different ways to move one useful supply between your settlements, then pause one and see whether the other is understandable and usable. Note what failed and what was easy to repair.",
    "",
    "Terra's favourite test, older than the fusion: a system is only as good as its second path."
  ],
  "quest.3554A2E575F882C0.title": "Afterward: a shared reserve",
  "quest.3554A2E575F882C0.quest_desc": [
    "After the activation · self-reported",
    "",
    "Optional, self-reported: pick one renewable food or material reserve, let a visitor take a known amount and time how long your usual process takes to replace it. Note what would make the reserve fair to share.",
    "",
    "Juan's question, the one he asks Solsticio every morning: if someone new arrives today, will there be enough tomorrow?"
  ],
  "image.74D63C02CC64588E.title": "&#E8DCB5Terra\\nThe Ark's controller\\n ",
  "image.373F236C52896BC6.title": "&#E8DCB5The End\\nA witnessed journey",
  "image.4D2C12DBA367955C.title": "&#E8DCB5After the activation\\nself-reported\\n ",
  "image.67E978C9D0FD2690.title": "V · The Activation",
  "chapter.74950145DD0B7777.title": "VI · Solsticio",
  "chapter.74950145DD0B7777.chapter_subtitle": [
    "The capital of Heliodor, frozen inside the Entrelumen. Cross with the Light Key: the voices are waiting in person."
  ],
  "quest.0C1B162D867478B1.title": "Inside the light",
  "quest.0C1B162D867478B1.quest_desc": [
    "The Light Key · The crossing",
    "",
    "Hold use with your Light Key until the ring closes. It carries you into Solsticio and breaks as you cross; what is left takes you home and back.",
    "",
    "Noon over copper and glass, and nobody has aged a day. Terra is already waving."
  ],
  "quest.4B9FF6036B58B45C.title": "The City That Never Dawns",
  "quest.4B9FF6036B58B45C.quest_desc": [
    "Aurelia · The town hall",
    "",
    "Talk to Aurelia in the town hall, beside the portal.",
    "",
    "'Three relics and the key that brought you. Juan, Terra and Bodhi each hold one. The Heart of Heliodor I would keep myself, of course.'"
  ],
  "quest.2B8961936F4D5A47.title": "Seeds of the World",
  "quest.2B8961936F4D5A47.quest_desc": [
    "Juan · The gardens",
    "",
    "Bring Juan seeds of eight different species from outside: wheat, beetroot, melon, carrot, potato, berries, cocoa, Farmer's Delight crops...",
    "",
    "'Same seeds since the light fell. The beds are tired. Variety, not sacks.'"
  ],
  "quest.4B4467623D387F88.title": "A Harvest for Everyone",
  "quest.4B4467623D387F88.quest_desc": [
    "Juan · The gardens",
    "",
    "Bring Juan four different Farmer's Delight meals, sixteen of each; Central Kitchen or Slice and Dice can cook them. He gives you the Luminous Seed.",
    "",
    "'A city eats every day. Feed it, and the seed that carries the light is yours.'"
  ],
  "quest.0FB869472B3FEFE1.title": "Power from Outside",
  "quest.0FB869472B3FEFE1.quest_desc": [
    "Terra · The workshop",
    "",
    "Bring Terra four Generator Coils, two Advanced Solar Heating Plates and a charged battery from any energy mod (100,000 FE or more). She gives you the Terraprism diagram.",
    "",
    "'Frozen light runs machines badly. I need power from outside. Charged means full.'"
  ],
  "quest.1F02073F3CFFC2AF.title": "Channelling the Light",
  "quest.1F02073F3CFFC2AF.quest_desc": [
    "Terra · The workshop",
    "",
    "Bring Terra one Luminosity of each discipline, all six; the natives of the trading hall sell them once they have seen their biome. She gives you the Terraprism.",
    "",
    "'It takes the light and gives it back as power people can use. That is all I ever wanted it to do.'"
  ],
  "quest.67AAA396175290D7.title": "Good Works",
  "quest.67AAA396175290D7.quest_desc": [
    "Bodhi · The chapel",
    "",
    "Do the errands of the four innkeepers, two each. Every errand raises your relation with Bodhi; at five, he listens.",
    "",
    "'I do not bless on request. Help the people here; I will hear about it.'"
  ],
  "quest.301807F294656252.title": "The Blessing",
  "quest.301807F294656252.quest_desc": [
    "Bodhi · The chapel",
    "",
    "Talk to Bodhi: your Atlas gives back the Heart of Heliodor. Hand it to him and it becomes the Blessed Heart of Heliodor. If the Sun Spirit still has it, beat it first.",
    "",
    "'It was never a machine's heart. With love, then.'"
  ],
  "quest.3D6E10D1A9FBFA20.title": "The Table of Two Lights",
  "quest.3D6E10D1A9FBFA20.quest_desc": [
    "Aurelia · The town hall",
    "",
    "With the three relics, talk to Aurelia in the town hall and to Bodhi in the chapel, in either order.",
    "",
    "She wants the crystal to rule the light; he fears a second fusion. The only way out is that nobody keeps it."
  ],
  "quest.59DCA82BB3F25E0A.title": "The Portal",
  "quest.59DCA82BB3F25E0A.quest_desc": [
    "The portal · The Entrelumen",
    "",
    "Right-click the town hall portal with each of your three relics, then with your own Broken Light Key in your pack. The first team to open it frees the Entrelumen for everyone, and every shop gets cheaper.",
    "",
    "Still a shelter. No longer a prison."
  ],
  "quest.2F34597F922F9618.title": "Elections in Solsticio",
  "quest.2F34597F922F9618.quest_desc": [
    "Aurelia · The town hall",
    "",
    "Three days after the portal first opens, the square votes. Then talk to Aurelia.",
    "",
    "'Elected. It sounds different from appointed.' Nobody asks too loudly about the new windows."
  ],
  "image.38A380ECBB629012.title": "VI · Solsticio",
  "chapter.551D4E474ABCF322.title": "An Inventory That Remembers",
  "quest.3D6A85207D225A5A.title": "Self-check: Two columns in the margin",
  "quest.3D6A85207D225A5A.quest_desc": [
    "Mara's margin",
    "",
    "After the first light answered, Mara drew TAKE and LEAVE beside the map. Choose one supply to carry through a hurried return and one material to leave at the workshop. Decide which column each belongs in, then mark this note.",
    "",
    "These notes are optional. A square fills when you carry its item and takes nothing from you; a circle is yours to mark after you try its exercise. Neither holds up the journey."
  ],
  "quest.73A9E5C7AAD95425.title": "A bag for the road",
  "quest.73A9E5C7AAD95425.quest_desc": [
    "What travels with you",
    "",
    "Make a basic Sophisticated Backpack with leather, string and a wooden chest; check the recipe for their placement. Put an ordinary block inside, close the bag, then find and remove it again. Look for the backpack action under Controls if you want quick access. This basic bag is enough for the exercises ahead."
  ],
  "quest.0BD095E6B6E17434.title": "A place that stays",
  "quest.0BD095E6B6E17434.quest_desc": [
    "A bench with a memory",
    "",
    "Combine an ordinary chest and a lever to make a Sophisticated Storage chest. Set it beside the bench you use and give it one job: incoming stone, repair supplies or food for the next journey. Put a matching stack inside and leave room for your return. The bag travels with you; this chest tells anyone coming home where to look."
  ],
  "quest.06DF53C2BFE4AFD2.title": "Self-check: What must stay aboard",
  "quest.06DF53C2BFE4AFD2.quest_desc": [
    "What travels with you",
    "",
    "Pack food for a short trip and a spare tool in places you can remember. Keep the working tool within reach; the spare is for a broken handle. Leave a food reserve at home so an empty return can still lead to another departure.",
    "",
    "Before you leave, open the bag and the home chest and point to each reserve. Mark this note when you can find both without searching every slot."
  ],
  "quest.5D95843A3184F140.title": "Self-check: An empty slot with a name",
  "quest.5D95843A3184F140.quest_desc": [
    "A bench with a memory",
    "",
    "In the chest's settings, set Memory on one slot holding a common workshop material. Remove its last stack, then try putting the same material and a different one back. Notice where each goes. If the result differs from your plan, revisit the slot and its setting before using scarce stock. The empty space can keep a place for tomorrow's stone."
  ],
  "quest.6C84395CBBF885D1.title": "The bag learns to gather",
  "quest.6C84395CBBF885D1.quest_desc": [
    "What travels with you",
    "",
    "The basic Pickup Upgrade uses an Upgrade Base, a sticky piston, string and redstone; check the recipe viewer for their placement. Put it in the backpack's upgrade slot and open its settings. Start with one plentiful block in the filter. Leave rare tools out of the first ground test; the next note follows two ordinary drops."
  ],
  "quest.7C2785BCD9168E16.title": "A second stack within reach",
  "quest.7C2785BCD9168E16.quest_desc": [
    "What travels with you",
    "",
    "The Refill Upgrade can supply a selected inventory stack from the backpack. Its recipe uses an Upgrade Base, an ender pearl, a chest, iron and redstone; check the recipe viewer before crafting it. Keep spare torches in the bag for the first trial: each torch you use leaves a gap you can see. Keep another reserve at home before relying on the bag in a cave."
  ],
  "quest.075CA7AC583930A5.title": "A rule at the workshop door",
  "quest.075CA7AC583930A5.quest_desc": [
    "A bench with a memory",
    "",
    "Make a Sophisticated Storage Filter Upgrade for the workshop chest. It governs items moved into or out of storage by a hopper or other transport; the backpack's Pickup Upgrade has a different job. Choose one plentiful block to allow and another cheap block to reject, then set the rule in the upgrade's controls. Test both before sending scarce materials through."
  ],
  "quest.4063D2008AF59266.title": "A shared doorstep",
  "quest.4063D2008AF59266.quest_desc": [
    "A bench with a memory",
    "",
    "A Storage Controller gives connected Sophisticated Storage blocks one place for deposits and external item transfer. Its recipe starts with a wooden storage block and comparators; check the recipe viewer for the arrangement. Place it near two stores you can inspect easily, with a different common material in each. Keep the individual stores useful so you can trace a deposit to its shelf."
  ],
  "quest.77EC138087997CE7.title": "Self-check: Two drops, one decision",
  "quest.77EC138087997CE7.quest_desc": [
    "What travels with you",
    "",
    "Install Pickup and set its filter for one plentiful block. In a safe place, drop that block and a different expendable item, one at a time. Look in the backpack, your inventory and the ground to find both. If the route surprises you, adjust the filter and repeat with cheap materials. Mark this note when you can account for both drops."
  ],
  "quest.2B06BADADE64C6EC.title": "Self-check: The last torch is visible",
  "quest.2B06BADADE64C6EC.quest_desc": [
    "What travels with you",
    "",
    "The basic backpack has one upgrade slot. Remove Pickup or the previous upgrade and install Refill. Put spare torches in the bag and select torches in Refill's settings. Use one from your inventory, then compare the carried stack with the bag's reserve. Remove the spare torches and repeat to see what happens when the reserve runs out. Keep food and the spare tool in their own places, ready for the trip home."
  ],
  "quest.76C13553573D6B65.title": "Self-check: The chest accepts one kind",
  "quest.76C13553573D6B65.quest_desc": [
    "A bench with a memory",
    "",
    "Fit the Filter Upgrade to the workshop chest and feed it through a hopper. Try one permitted block, then one rejected block, separately. Check the hopper and chest after each attempt; a rejected item may wait upstream. Manual insertion and piped insertion can follow different rules. Mark this note once you know where both blocks ended, and clear the hopper before a real batch."
  ],
  "quest.0AA71C8CE15A3C4D.title": "Self-check: One entrance, two shelves",
  "quest.0AA71C8CE15A3C4D.quest_desc": [
    "A bench with a memory",
    "",
    "Place the controller beside two connected Sophisticated Storage blocks. Put a different ordinary material in each store, then make a small deposit through the controller. Find the deposited items in the physical stores and take them back out. If nothing moves, inspect the connections before adding more shelves. Mark this note after you can follow the route in both directions."
  ],
  "quest.2D86B44DFFE54B85.title": "The return has a gesture",
  "quest.2D86B44DFFE54B85.quest_desc": [
    "The return route",
    "",
    "The Backpack Deposit Upgrade moves items from the bag into an inventory you sneak-right-click. Its recipe uses an Upgrade Base, a piston, a wooden chest, iron and redstone; check the recipe viewer for the layout. Put ordinary stone in the workshop chest and in your bag before trying Match Inventory Contents. Keep food and a spare tool in the bag so you can see what stays with you."
  ],
  "quest.6A3E9ACF03298C69.title": "Self-check: The bag comes home lighter",
  "quest.6A3E9ACF03298C69.quest_desc": [
    "The return route",
    "",
    "Swap the previous upgrade for Deposit in the basic backpack's single upgrade slot. Put a small stack of stone in the bag beside the food and spare tool you chose to keep. Stock the workshop chest with stone, set Deposit to Match Inventory Contents, and sneak-right-click that chest with the bag. Count stone in both places, then check the food and tool. If the result surprises you, retrieve the items and repeat with cheap stock. Mark this note after the travel reserve stays aboard."
  ],
  "quest.56BE1D70BFD96C1B.title": "Self-check: A shelf after the network",
  "quest.56BE1D70BFD96C1B.quest_desc": [
    "One shelf stays local",
    "",
    "Sera's later sketches show a digital network; Mara keeps a physical shelf beside the bench. When you have AE2, close its terminal and take one food stack and one repair supply from that local shelf. Decide which reserve should remain within reach if the network is unavailable. Mark this note after you can retrieve both without the terminal, then restock the shelf for the next return."
  ],
  "image.6CFB251A3F6DA4D4.title": "&#E8DCB5What travels with you",
  "image.0A016725085D1DEB.title": "&#E8DCB5A bench with a memory",
  "image.228EA175BAB72CD1.title": "&#E8DCB5The return route",
  "chapter_group.192C7E7D9BC8BCFF.title": "Heliodor's Legacy",
  "chapter_group.7B00A650A207F91E.title": "Quality of Life",
  "chapter_group.56152B099337B914.title": "Technology",
  "chapter_group.4D74159E6A679408.title": "Magic",
  "chapter_group.4D7F6E113F6DB815.title": "Exploration",
  "reward_table.0000000014466D3A.title": "Pick one · Salvage",
  "reward_table.000000001998C87C.title": "Pick one · Workshop",
  "reward_table.0000000061FBC412.title": "Pick one · Courier",
  "reward_table.000000000323851D.title": "Pick one · Expedition",
  "reward_table.000000003EF33D8B.title": "Pick one · Ark",
  "reward_table.0000000067F55CD0.title": "Pick one · Solstice",
  "reward_table.0000000019FA24E6.title": "Salvage Crate",
  "reward_table.000000006551780F.title": "Workshop Crate",
  "reward_table.000000005B3962F9.title": "Courier Crate",
  "reward_table.0000000070F8C581.title": "Expedition Crate",
  "reward_table.000000004D29D48E.title": "Ark Crate",
  "reward_table.000000007EF5DAAD.title": "Solstice Crate",
  "reward_table.00000000624A0EA0.title": "Odds and ends · act I",
  "reward_table.000000004DE0911A.title": "Odds and ends · act II",
  "reward_table.0000000047901A17.title": "Odds and ends · act III",
  "reward_table.00000000467286CE.title": "Odds and ends · act IV",
  "reward_table.0000000012D36307.title": "Odds and ends · act V",
  "reward_table.000000005C4C41E9.title": "Odds and ends · act VI",
  "chapter.0216243AA5083CE1.title": "Waking Among Ruins",
  "chapter.0216243AA5083CE1.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Empty pockets, a ruined sun patio and the light that guards Heliodor's places."
  ],
  "quest.7B2FDFC0D74F1790.title": "You Wake Among Ruins",
  "quest.7B2FDFC0D74F1790.quest_desc": [
    "Every world starts the same: you appear beside a ruined sun patio with empty pockets. The ruin, its compass and the Atlas are your only guides.",
    "",
    "No tutorial, no kit, no welcome committee. Heliodor has been busy being frozen."
  ],
  "quest.51F1081FE91AE567.title": "Empty Pockets, on Purpose",
  "quest.51F1081FE91AE567.quest_desc": [
    "The pack turns off every join gift: Ars Nouveau's notebook, the Integrated Dynamics manual, Silent Gear's blueprints, the Actually Additions booklet and more. Every one of those books is still craftable.",
    "",
    "Nothing is lost, only not gifted. Not even the plush toy."
  ],
  "quest.5DF068ECC8A3C79B.title": "Quirk: the Aether Says Hi",
  "quest.5DF068ECC8A3C79B.quest_desc": [
    "One gift survives: the first time you enter the Aether, it hands you its Book of Lore and golden parachutes. It is not a login gift, it is a safety net.",
    "",
    "Floating islands, long drops. Take the hint."
  ],
  "quest.54D8683481D00162.title": "The Start Ruin",
  "quest.54D8683481D00162.quest_desc": [
    "A new world places it once, on the flattest ground within 64 blocks of spawn: a tuff and calcite patio with an oxidized copper sun, eight quartz columns (four broken) and the &eHeliodor Pedestal&r in the middle.",
    "",
    "World spawn moves beside it, and your first login faces it."
  ],
  "quest.3A3D2F69F7A51597.title": "Take the Compass",
  "quest.3A3D2F69F7A51597.quest_desc": [
    "Use the pedestal: it gives each player one &eHeliodor Compass&r per world, ever. Its first target is the ruin itself, until you wake the Atlas with a book and a copper ingot.",
    "",
    "Everything else about it: The Heliodor Compass chapter."
  ],
  "quest.04910797C8A95EC6.title": "First Steps That Work",
  "quest.04910797C8A95EC6.quest_desc": [
    "Tree, wooden tools, crafting table, stone, coal. Then go after &ecopper&r: the Atlas and its first projects want copper ingots, paper and glass.",
    "",
    "The compass will send you to a village for bread and paper, then to trial chambers, full of copper and tuff like the ruin."
  ],
  "quest.393FB3DA62E83A3D.title": "The Light Keeps These Places",
  "quest.393FB3DA62E83A3D.quest_desc": [
    "Inside a protected ruin nobody can break or place blocks, and neither can explosions, pistons, flowing fluids, spreading fire, griefing mobs or trampling. Frames, paintings and armor stands are safe too.",
    "",
    "The server checks at the moment it happens: creative, spectator and noclip get the same polite no."
  ],
  "quest.73BFA7978DF2985A.title": "Free, Sealed and Locked",
  "quest.73BFA7978DF2985A.quest_desc": [
    "Right-clicks inside a protected place fall in three groups. &eFree&r: doors, buttons, levers, beds, simple workstations, ender chests and the pedestal. &eSealed&r: containers, lecterns and altars, which open when your team reaches that place's act. &eLocked&r: anything else that would change a block, and anvils.",
    "",
    "A frame's item can be taken once your team is unlocked; the frame stays."
  ],
  "quest.76BB64F3BA0C95E3.title": "Why Ruins Are Protected",
  "quest.76BB64F3BA0C95E3.quest_desc": [
    "Ruins are the story's levels: their lore and key pieces open when your team gets there, whatever tricks anyone tries.",
    "",
    "It also stops a friend from blowing up the exact spot the compass is pointing at. Do not ask how we know."
  ],
  "quest.0430D747262F84EB.title": "Quirk: Tools Stop at the Edge",
  "quest.0430D747262F84EB.quest_desc": [
    "Ultimine, gadgets, construction sticks, Carry On and the land-shaping altars all act as a player, so they stop at a ruin's edge; Carry On's break check before lifting is refused too.",
    "",
    "Build around a ruin, not into it."
  ],
  "quest.3C0CF3ADDFD6F214.title": "The Same Light Covers Solsticio",
  "quest.3C0CF3ADDFD6F214.quest_desc": [
    "The city at the end of the story uses the same protection, gated by act VI. The exception is the player plots: 16 by 16, one per team, where only your team builds.",
    "",
    "How to claim one: the Solsticio chapter."
  ],
  "quest.2D3295A6543F9E15.title": "Tip: Your Spawn Is the Ruin",
  "quest.2D3295A6543F9E15.quest_desc": [
    "Until you sleep in a bed, you respawn at the start ruin. Set a bed or a Comforts sleeping spot near your first base early.",
    "",
    "Tombstone keeps your items in a grave where you fall, so the walk back only costs you dignity."
  ],
  "quest.3925C4CC5C5C7AE4.title": "For Operators: Older Worlds",
  "quest.3925C4CC5C5C7AE4.quest_desc": [
    "Only brand-new worlds get the start ruin. In an older one, an operator places it with &e/entrelumen admin ruin&r (running it twice does nothing) and toggles a personal protection bypass for repairs with &e/entrelumen admin protection bypass&r."
  ],
  "quest.5BBA78C05C867FBA.title": "Quirk: Blind Spots",
  "quest.5BBA78C05C867FBA.quest_desc": [
    "A few things slip past: blocks changed by mods that skip the usual game events, projectiles breaking fragile blocks such as pots, and plot machines placing fluids or blocks right against a protected one (placed that way, they cannot spread further).",
    "",
    "Found a hole? Report it. Heliodor has enough holes already."
  ],
  "quest.0616E7C527841913.title": "Ready to Leave the Patio",
  "quest.0616E7C527841913.quest_desc": [
    "Empty pockets, a compass that knows the way and ruins that will not let you dig them up. Craft the Atlas and let it start talking.",
    "",
    "Good luck, traveller. Mind the columns: four are already broken."
  ],
  "chapter.7E9AE182E0AEBD76.title": "The Living Atlas",
  "chapter.7E9AE182E0AEBD76.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Projects, deliveries, act components and the Ark: how the story moves."
  ],
  "quest.23BA57C16A45AEBB.title": "A Book That Answers Back",
  "quest.23BA57C16A45AEBB.quest_desc": [
    "The &6Living Atlas&r moves the story. Each act is a set of projects, each project a delivery; finish them all and the next act opens. Along the way it hands out rewards and tells, in broken fragments, what happened to Heliodor.",
    "",
    "Someone is talking through it. The interference is not your fault."
  ],
  "quest.2B3B9A46DA117973.title": "Get the Atlas",
  "quest.2B3B9A46DA117973.quest_desc": [
    "Craft it from a &ebook&r and a &ecopper ingot&r; its first project, The Atlas Awakens, asks for exactly that. Open it with right-click, with &e/entrelumen&r, or by using a Survey Station with an empty hand.",
    "",
    "Waking it is also the compass's first target."
  ],
  "quest.5F6D93279A928C87.title": "Reading the Atlas",
  "quest.5F6D93279A928C87.quest_desc": [
    "Left page: the act's projects and their state. Right page: the selected project, its materials (carried and missing) and the projects it needs first. &eDeliver&r sends the materials, &eRefresh&r asks the server again and &eAdvance&r appears when the act is done.",
    "",
    "The list opens with the compass entry and its fragments."
  ],
  "quest.21132BDE339A66BD.title": "Delivery Rules",
  "quest.21132BDE339A66BD.quest_desc": [
    "Deliveries take from your &emain inventory and offhand&r only: backpacks, shulker boxes and the ender chest do not count. Only projects of your &ecurrent act&r, after their prerequisites.",
    "",
    "A delivered project cannot be delivered again, so reconnecting never duplicates a reward. Nice try."
  ],
  "quest.622A0BC02FB63453.title": "Tip: the Atlas From Chat",
  "quest.622A0BC02FB63453.quest_desc": [
    "&e/entrelumen status&r lists your act's pending projects, their prerequisites and, for each material, how many you carry and lack. &e/entrelumen deliver <project>&r delivers by name with the button's rules, and the chat suggests names as you type."
  ],
  "quest.1DBCB83716EBFCBF.title": "Act I: A Light Among Ruins",
  "quest.1DBCB83716EBFCBF.quest_desc": [
    "Five projects, ordinary materials:\n- The Atlas Awakens: a book, a copper ingot;\n- A Table for Travellers: 3 bread, 4 bowls;\n- Assemble the Lens: 4 copper ingots, 4 glass (&eRaw Lens&r);\n- Field Survey: 3 paper, a compass (&eSurvey Notes&r);\n- First Signal: lens, notes, 4 copper ingots (&eSignal Core&r).",
    "",
    "Then press Advance."
  ],
  "quest.161CC52C300C99FD.title": "Act Components",
  "quest.161CC52C300C99FD.quest_desc": [
    "From act II, projects ask for &6act components&r: prototypes crafted in an ordinary grid from two or three mods plus an earlier component. The recipes are public and never check your act.",
    "",
    "In EMI, &eR&r on a component shows its recipe and &eU&r everything it unlocks."
  ],
  "quest.097843E8ED7FB61E.title": "Act II: The Lost Crafts",
  "quest.097843E8ED7FB61E.quest_desc": [
    "Four components, then the closing project:\n- &eCalibration Frame&r: Create and Immersive Engineering, plus the raw lens;\n- &eEnergy Coupler&r: Actually Additions and Create;\n- &eLiving Matrix&r: Ars Nouveau, plus a frame;\n- &eTravel Rations&r: see the Kitchen chapter.",
    "",
    "Workshop Archive closes the act and gives &eTerra's Arm&r."
  ],
  "quest.77007F86F56D8B6C.title": "Act III: Routes of Exchange",
  "quest.77007F86F56D8B6C.quest_desc": [
    "Five components; three pay an altar:\n- &eRouting Matrix&r (AE2, PneumaticCraft, Actually Additions): &eAltar of Peace&r;\n- &ePropagation Core&r (Mystical Agriculture, bee wax): &eAltar of Growth&r;\n- &ePower Regulator&r (Mekanism, Immersive Engineering);\n- &eInventory Sensor&r (Integrated Dynamics, LaserIO);\n- &eHandling Core&r (Modular Routers, Create): &eAltar of Levelling&r.",
    "",
    "Exchange Route closes the act."
  ],
  "quest.58244B38F375C1C7.title": "Act IV: Voices of the Atlas",
  "quest.58244B38F375C1C7.quest_desc": [
    "The expedition act: the Atlas records journeys by itself when your team arrives, and asks for four components:\n- &eSpectral Lens&r (Occultism, Malum);\n- &eHorizon Chart&r (Aether, Twilight; its project needs both reached): &eAltar of Repose&r;\n- &eEcosystem Capsule&r (Bumblezone; its project needs it reached): &eAltar of Renewal&r;\n- &eContainment Seal&r (EvilCraft, Malum): &eAltar of Time&r."
  ],
  "quest.37DC25FD6EE9DEA9.title": "The Heart of Heliodor",
  "quest.37DC25FD6EE9DEA9.quest_desc": [
    "Act IV ends at the &6Sun Spirit&r, boss of the Aether's gold dungeon. It drops the &eHeart of Heliodor&r, once per campaign. Deliver it in A Clear Voice; only then can Voices of the Atlas close the act.",
    "",
    "On the ground it cannot burn, despawn or fall into the void. It has been lost once already."
  ],
  "quest.1866D1F9DD733322.title": "Act V: The Ark",
  "quest.1866D1F9DD733322.quest_desc": [
    "Knowing the truth, you build the Ark. Three components: &eArk Connection Bus&r (Mekanism, PneumaticCraft, handling cores, a sensor), &eRenewal Engine&r (Nature's Aura, Mystical Agriculture, capsules, cores) and &eHabitation Charter&r (fish stew, mixed salad, AE2, rations).",
    "",
    "World Network closes the act. On the way, the last two modules: &eLogistics&r and &eEngineering&r."
  ],
  "quest.72C3A1232F9FF6FF.title": "Build the Ark",
  "quest.72C3A1232F9FF6FF.quest_desc": [
    "An astrolabe of stone, tuff, calcite, copper and amethyst round the &eArk Controller&r. The rim's polished amethyst comes from amethyst blocks through Rechiseled's &eChisel&r (iron ingot and stick). In the Atlas, The Ark's &eShow guide&r projects a ghost of every block, on your controller or where you look.",
    "",
    "Each act gives one module: I Habitation, II Exploration, III Nature, IV Arcane, V Logistics and Engineering. A module works in its place, with the Ark whole and the controller on. One Ark per team."
  ],
  "quest.3DD568980F26C458.title": "The Activation",
  "quest.3DD568980F26C458.quest_desc": [
    "The Ark whole with its six modules and controller, World Network done and the End reached: the Atlas and the Ark's screen tick the list. Then crouch on the controller with an empty hand. The Ark forges the &6Light Key&r and the campaign enters &eact VI, Solsticio&r.",
    "",
    "The door has been waiting a long time. Knock politely."
  ],
  "quest.62CBF13A5CB4C3E5.title": "What the Ark Gives",
  "quest.62CBF13A5CB4C3E5.quest_desc": [
    "A beacon for the whole team, anywhere. &eHabitation&r: /sethome and /home. &eExploration&r: free waystones and /rtp. &eNature&r: Regeneration and half hunger, and a compass marks your garden. &eArcane&r: +50% mana and regeneration. &eLogistics&r: Solsticio's shops from the Atlas, Hero of the Village. &eEngineering&r: energy items charge themselves.",
    "",
    "A beacon on each column adds a level to the potions and the mana."
  ],
  "quest.306B717DBAA85638.title": "The Survey Station",
  "quest.306B717DBAA85638.quest_desc": [
    "Copper, glass, smooth stone and a signal core make a movable bookmark. With an empty hand it opens the Atlas; with a vanilla compass it points that compass at itself, like a lodestone, and the link survives moving the station.",
    "",
    "The Ark's Nature module uses such a compass to mark your team's garden."
  ],
  "quest.4E722FFB64F4F76D.title": "Components Unlock the World",
  "quest.4E722FFB64F4F76D.quest_desc": [
    "A component closes a few milestones, never a pile of basics: the metallurgic infuser and the mining portal (Calibration Frame), the AE2 and Refined Storage controllers (Routing Matrix), Mekanism's jetpack and Psi's CAD Assembler (Power Regulator), the Digital Miner and the Lumen Shelf (Spectral Lens). The other steps of an act take its material: an alloy of Mekanism, ironwood or zanite.",
    "",
    "&eU&r on a component in EMI shows everything it opens."
  ],
  "quest.21BEA1DA85BCD908.title": "Quirk: Psi Waits for Act III",
  "quest.21BEA1DA85BCD908.quest_desc": [
    "Psi's CAD Assembler carries a Power Regulator; its psigem cores keep their native recipes. No assembler, no CAD, no spells: plan Psi alongside your act III logistics.",
    "",
    "When in doubt, EMI shows your version's recipe."
  ],
  "quest.621B66430D137B31.title": "Tip: Automate the Components",
  "quest.621B66430D137B31.quest_desc": [
    "Components are ordinary shaped recipes, each a small drawing, so any storage network can autocraft them, and later ones eat earlier ones. Set up a pattern for each early in act III.",
    "",
    "Each module takes one of them: a propagation core, a spectral lens, a routing matrix, an Ark bus."
  ],
  "quest.4B04E34A144A490D.title": "Rewards Come From the Atlas",
  "quest.4B04E34A144A490D.quest_desc": [
    "Story rewards come from the Atlas when you deliver, never from the quest book: the Atlas, lens, notes, signal core, Terra's Arm and the six altars. Each comes once per campaign to whoever delivered, or drops at their feet if the inventory is full, and a chat line names it.",
    "",
    "The quest book only keeps score."
  ],
  "quest.2C31D583B80F31E8.title": "Why the Atlas Stutters",
  "quest.2C31D583B80F31E8.quest_desc": [
    "Until the Heart of Heliodor reaches it, the Atlas speaks in fragments: crossed-out words, gaps and short glitches, always with readable parts. From act V the text comes through clear.",
    "",
    "Do not skip them. The lore is a puzzle, and you are holding the pieces."
  ],
  "quest.45AF0BF75021DA63.title": "The Story in Your Hands",
  "quest.45AF0BF75021DA63.quest_desc": [
    "Projects, deliveries, components and the Ark: the rest is walking the road.",
    "",
    "Keep the Heliodor Compass close. It already knows where the Atlas wants you next."
  ],
  "chapter.34DC677E5D339B3F.title": "The Heliodor Compass",
  "chapter.34DC677E5D339B3F.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Where it points, what its colors mean and why it sometimes rests."
  ],
  "quest.40194B53EA674D94.title": "Never Lost",
  "quest.40194B53EA674D94.quest_desc": [
    "The Heliodor Compass always points to the next place the story needs: a structure, a dungeon, a guardian or another world. Meet the condition and it turns to the next one on its own.",
    "",
    "It never sends you thousands of blocks away and never spins for show."
  ],
  "quest.70E93F659F6828C9.title": "Take It From the Pedestal",
  "quest.70E93F659F6828C9.quest_desc": [
    "Use the &eHeliodor Pedestal&r in the start ruin, with anything in hand, to get your compass: &eone&r per player, per world, ever. A second try only reminds you. No recipe makes another.",
    "",
    "If you die, Tombstone keeps it in your grave. Otherwise, treat it like your house keys."
  ],
  "quest.6F6A288871FD98BD.title": "Carry It to Attune It",
  "quest.6F6A288871FD98BD.quest_desc": [
    "A fresh compass is not attuned yet: carry it a moment. While carried it refreshes about once a second, so it follows you as you walk.",
    "",
    "Hover it for its state; the Atlas's first entry shows the target, why it matters and the fragments you recovered."
  ],
  "quest.5B6FBD4B88937613.title": "Needle Colors",
  "quest.5B6FBD4B88937613.quest_desc": [
    "The needle's color tells you which world the target is in: &3turquoise&r Overworld, &4red&r Nether, &5violet&r End, &6gold&r Aether, &2green&r Twilight Forest, &bsky blue&r another world (Bumblezone, Solsticio) and &7grey&r no trace, locked or nothing pending.",
    "",
    "Grey is not broken. Grey is waiting."
  ],
  "quest.704E2DF71D58FC0A.title": "What the Needle Is Saying",
  "quest.704E2DF71D58FC0A.quest_desc": [
    "The tooltip shows one of five states: &ePointing&r (follow it), &eAnother dimension&r (travel there first), &eSearching&r (a short spin while the server looks), &eNo trace nearby&r (advance the Atlas or try another region) and &eLocked&r (the next act opens it).",
    "",
    "When there is nothing left for now, it says that too."
  ],
  "quest.76B34644E6DE0B02.title": "Never Thousands of Blocks",
  "quest.76B34644E6DE0B02.quest_desc": [
    "It searches at most &e1,500 blocks&r around you. Anything farther reads as no trace nearby instead of dragging you across the map; walk 512 blocks from a failed search and it looks again.",
    "",
    "The story never asks for epic treks, jetpacks or chunk-loading."
  ],
  "quest.22D3EA2BD8DBF425.title": "The Compass Follows the Team",
  "quest.22D3EA2BD8DBF425.quest_desc": [
    "It follows your team's campaign: everyone sees the same target, new destinations are announced to all, and a condition met by any online member counts for everyone. A new party inherits its founder's progress.",
    "",
    "Reached stays reached: losing an item never rewinds it."
  ],
  "quest.44DBD22DB832F5A1.title": "Quirk: Found Places Are Shared",
  "quest.44DBD22DB832F5A1.quest_desc": [
    "Every place a search finds is remembered for the whole world. If another team already found a fortress near you, your compass points there without searching.",
    "",
    "Searches run a little each tick and never wait for chunks, so they never freeze the server."
  ],
  "quest.60F361B6A2A611B1.title": "The Route: Acts I and II",
  "quest.60F361B6A2A611B1.quest_desc": [
    "Early targets, each until its condition:\n- &eThe Ruin Where You Woke&r, until the Atlas awakens;\n- &eThose Who Stayed&r, a village, until Field Survey;\n- &eThe Proving Halls&r, the trial chambers, until First Signal;\n- &eBuried Streets&r, trail ruins, until Workshop Archive closes act II."
  ],
  "quest.265E3B24DA46A5F4.title": "The Route: Acts III and IV",
  "quest.265E3B24DA46A5F4.quest_desc": [
    "Then the other worlds.\n- Act III: a &eNether fortress&r (until someone carries a blaze rod), the &eTwilight Forest&r and the &eNaga's Courtyard&r.\n- Act IV: the &eAether&r, the Slider's &eBronze Dungeon&r, the &eLich's Tower&r, the &eBumblezone&r, the &eSilver Dungeon&r and the &eGolden Dungeon&r, where the Sun Spirit keeps the Heart of Heliodor.",
    "",
    "Guardian targets advance when the boss falls."
  ],
  "quest.2F469EE97767853E.title": "The Route: Acts V and VI",
  "quest.2F469EE97767853E.quest_desc": [
    "The last stretch.\n- Act V: the &eDrowned Monument&r (until someone carries a wet sponge), the &eStronghold&r (until your team reaches the End) and &eThe End&r itself (until the dragon falls).\n- Act VI: &eSolsticio&r, until your team crosses into the city.",
    "",
    "Keep what the Wither, the dragon and the Elder Guardian drop: later recipes want it."
  ],
  "quest.251DFE202BDBF604.title": "Tip: Early Work Counts",
  "quest.251DFE202BDBF604.quest_desc": [
    "If your team already met a later condition, say it reached the Twilight Forest early, the compass skips that target the moment its act opens.",
    "",
    "Nothing done early is wasted. Curiosity is never punished here."
  ],
  "quest.301485EAA30C69E6.title": "Other Compasses",
  "quest.301485EAA30C69E6.quest_desc": [
    "Off the story path, &eNature's Compass&r finds biomes and &eExplorer's Compass&r finds structures; Solsticio's cartographer sells both, plus survey maps.",
    "",
    "The Heliodor Compass only follows the story. Do not ask it for a jungle."
  ],
  "quest.6BBD7EE9A8E018A1.title": "Fragments of Lore",
  "quest.6BBD7EE9A8E018A1.quest_desc": [
    "Many targets add a lore fragment to the Atlas's compass entry, newest first. The early ones keep the mystery; the whole truth arrives with the Heart of Heliodor.",
    "",
    "Read them in order and the static starts to make sense."
  ],
  "quest.7C5FFA4CF9C12078.title": "Follow the Light",
  "quest.7C5FFA4CF9C12078.quest_desc": [
    "When in doubt, hover the compass for its state, or open the Atlas for the target and why it matters.",
    "",
    "Heliodor's light has waited a long time. It can wait for you to read a tooltip."
  ],
  "chapter.073625DCC50D40F5.title": "World Tiers: the Story Decides",
  "chapter.073625DCC50D40F5.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Apotheosis difficulty tiers, raised by the story and never by you."
  ],
  "quest.0F7D705A8BA5E65A.title": "A World That Grows With You",
  "quest.0F7D705A8BA5E65A.quest_desc": [
    "Apotheosis has five &eWorld Tiers&r: Haven, Frontier, Ascent, Summit and Pinnacle. Each makes monsters tougher and loot better. Here the &estory&r raises them: when your team's campaign reaches a new stage, the world climbs one tier by itself.",
    "",
    "No guessing whether you are ready. The story decides; you survive it."
  ],
  "quest.5BC7B113AE36BF58.title": "The Ladder",
  "quest.5BC7B113AE36BF58.quest_desc": [
    "- &eHaven&r: from the start, through acts I and II;\n- &eFrontier&r: once act II is complete;\n- &eAscent&r: once act III is complete, as the expeditions begin;\n- &eSummit&r: once act IV is complete and the Ark begins;\n- &ePinnacle&r: when your team activates the Ark and opens act VI.",
    "",
    "Chat announces each step: \"The story sets your World Tier to...\"."
  ],
  "quest.729DB33C65E3D107.title": "It Only Goes Up",
  "quest.729DB33C65E3D107.quest_desc": [
    "Your tier is the &ehighest you ever reached&r. Dying, leaving a team or joining one that is behind never lowers it; joining one that is ahead raises you at once.",
    "",
    "It is stored on you, so it follows you across dimensions and restarts. Like prices: it only goes up."
  ],
  "quest.3E2EAA408A21FC08.title": "Pack Change: Hands Off the Dial",
  "quest.3E2EAA408A21FC08.quest_desc": [
    "&eCtrl+T&r still opens Apotheosis's World Tier screen, where you can read every tier's details, but the activate button stays disabled. If anything moves your tier outside the story, the pack puts it back within a second.",
    "",
    "You may look. You may not touch."
  ],
  "quest.2C2A73CEB13367AD.title": "Read the Details",
  "quest.2C2A73CEB13367AD.quest_desc": [
    "On the World Tier screen, the details button lists what each tier changes: buffs and debuffs for players and monsters, and the odds of each loot rarity and gem purity.",
    "",
    "Apotheosis's guidebook, the Chronicle of Shadows, explains rarities, affixes and gems."
  ],
  "quest.3EA0CA6AD9E05199.title": "Invaders From Frontier On",
  "quest.3EA0CA6AD9E05199.quest_desc": [
    "From &eFrontier&r, Apotheosis &einvaders&r can appear: tough mini-bosses in affixed gear. Haven has none, and no epic or mythic loot. The pack spaces them 10 minutes apart instead of three.",
    "",
    "They like the Twilight Forest. Dress for the occasion."
  ],
  "quest.15289447AA613BCF.title": "Loot Rarity by Tier",
  "quest.15289447AA613BCF.quest_desc": [
    "Better rarities only drop at higher tiers: in this pack &euncommon&r materials come from Haven on, &erare&r ones higher up, &eepic&r from Ascent and &emythic&r from Summit.",
    "",
    "Salvage affixed loot at a &eSalvaging Table&r for the rarity materials that reforging and gems use. That sword with the silly name is an ingredient."
  ],
  "quest.69C926655A9EDEF3.title": "Spawner Augments Follow Tiers",
  "quest.69C926655A9EDEF3.quest_desc": [
    "Apotheosis's spawner runes are replaced by ENTRELUMEN &espawner augments&r: copper medallions that tweak a spawner where it stands. Each takes an act component, from act III to act V, in place of Apotheosis's materials.",
    "",
    "Silk Touch does not pick up spawners in this pack."
  ],
  "quest.057E195FC015C164.title": "The Godforged Pearl",
  "quest.057E195FC015C164.quest_desc": [
    "The &eLuminous Ingot&r needs Apotheosis's &eGodforged Pearl&r, which only comes from salvaging mythic loot. Mythic loot starts at Summit, so the pearl arrives with the Ark act, right before Solsticio.",
    "",
    "Mythic drops go to the Salvaging Table, not to the trophy shelf."
  ],
  "quest.116957591A1DC800.title": "Enchanting Climbs in Steps",
  "quest.116957591A1DC800.quest_desc": [
    "The pack spaces Apothic Enchanting's shelves by act, and your World Tier's Eterna ceiling keeps pace: 45 in acts I and II, 75 in act III, 90 in act IV and 100 from act V. Four ENTRELUMEN shelves join the ladder: Cartographer's, Patina, Lumen and Horizon.",
    "",
    "From act V, the Atlas Library writes any eligible enchantment up to level 40."
  ],
  "quest.1EA195F042214D5C.title": "The Atlas Library",
  "quest.1EA195F042214D5C.quest_desc": [
    "An upgrade on Apothic's Ender Library: deposit enchanted books into a shared pool of &elumen&r, then write any eligible enchantment onto a book, even ones you never deposited. Its level cap follows the Eterna around it; 100 Eterna reaches level 40.",
    "",
    "A deposit is worth less than writing costs, curses are refused and breaking it keeps the pool. No infinite loops, sorry."
  ],
  "quest.18276CF7A859D7F0.title": "Tip: Gear Up Before Advancing",
  "quest.18276CF7A859D7F0.quest_desc": [
    "The world hardens the moment an act closes, so upgrade before pressing Advance on acts II and III: better armor, a few gems, food for the satiety buffs.",
    "",
    "There is no timer. The current tier will wait as long as you like."
  ],
  "quest.1988E6C9176E95D5.title": "Quirk: Items That Need a Tier",
  "quest.1988E6C9176E95D5.quest_desc": [
    "Some Apotheosis items say \"Requires World Tier\" and stay inert until your tier gets there. The story raises it, so just keep advancing the Atlas.",
    "",
    "No button to press. Well, there is one, but it is disabled."
  ],
  "quest.7D0FE71142574884.title": "For Operators",
  "quest.7D0FE71142574884.quest_desc": [
    "&e/entrelumen admin set <act>&r moves the story, and the tier with it. The tier still never drops: lowering it means clearing the player's stored story tier offline, deliberately not a command. Apotheosis's own tier command is undone at the next sync."
  ],
  "quest.373527F04C56E65F.title": "Difficulty With a Reason",
  "quest.373527F04C56E65F.quest_desc": [
    "Five tiers, raised by the story and never lowered, each with tougher monsters and better loot. Play the acts at your own pace.",
    "",
    "The world keeps time with you, not with the clock."
  ],
  "chapter.197D584486CC04B0.title": "Terra's Arm",
  "chapter.197D584486CC04B0.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Heliodor's inventor built herself a longer reach. Three more blocks, and a lot of scaffolding you will not need."
  ],
  "quest.204B7548FB3ED6C6.title": "An Arm Built to Reach",
  "quest.204B7548FB3ED6C6.quest_desc": [
    "Terra, Heliodor's inventor, built herself a cyborg arm to reach where the machine would not let her. It closes act II and does one thing: it lets you reach blocks from farther away.",
    "",
    "Small on paper. Huge the first time you roof a house without scaffolding."
  ],
  "quest.26B8D05294234A42.title": "Earn It in Act II",
  "quest.26B8D05294234A42.quest_desc": [
    "Finish act II's four prototype projects (Calibration Frame, Energy Coupler, Living Matrix and Travel Rations), then deliver &eWorkshop Archive&r: three paper and a copper ingot. The Atlas hands &eTerra's Arm&r to whoever delivers.",
    "",
    "No recipe. The sunken workshop ruin also keeps one in a chest."
  ],
  "quest.75CB722DD2FD6FE4.title": "Wear It on a Hand",
  "quest.75CB722DD2FD6FE4.quest_desc": [
    "It is a curio: press &eG&r (or use the Curios button in your inventory) and put the arm in a &ehands&r slot, which the pack guarantees every player.",
    "",
    "In a pocket it does nothing. Arms work better attached."
  ],
  "quest.2AB0505CB19719FA.title": "Three More Blocks",
  "quest.2AB0505CB19719FA.quest_desc": [
    "Worn, it adds &e+3 block reach&r: break, place and use blocks from 7.5 blocks away instead of 4.5. The tooltip shows the bonus in blue, like vanilla attribute lines.",
    "",
    "It is checked twice a second, so it switches on a moment after you put it on."
  ],
  "quest.0779CD7A84AB475B.title": "Blocks, Not Swords",
  "quest.0779CD7A84AB475B.quest_desc": [
    "Only &eblock&r reach grows. Attacking and interacting with creatures keep the normal range, so it gives no edge in combat.",
    "",
    "Terra built a tool, not a weapon."
  ],
  "quest.5385DF51A7FAC937.title": "Quirk: Two Arms, Same Reach",
  "quest.5385DF51A7FAC937.quest_desc": [
    "Players have two hands slots, but a second arm adds nothing: the bonus is one modifier, on or off, and taking off one of two keeps it. Other sources of block reach do stack with its flat +3."
  ],
  "quest.129FF0157ED39EF3.title": "Tip: Building Tall",
  "quest.129FF0157ED39EF3.quest_desc": [
    "Place the top rows of a wall, a roof ridge or a ceiling light without scaffolding, and reach across gaps. With a Construction Stick, extend faces you could not reach before.",
    "",
    "Scaffolding makers hate this one trick."
  ],
  "quest.51CF708529CE925C.title": "Tip: Machine Rooms",
  "quest.51CF708529CE925C.quest_desc": [
    "Reach the machine behind another, the lever past a pipe run or the chest at the back of a shelf without walking around. Dense rooms of LaserIO nodes and Create contraptions get much friendlier."
  ],
  "quest.25B9C7768CA15451.title": "Tip: Fields and Trees",
  "quest.25B9C7768CA15451.quest_desc": [
    "Harvest a wider strip of field from the path, reach the top logs and fruit of tall trees, and plant without stepping on farmland. With Ultimine, start a vein you would otherwise have to climb to."
  ],
  "quest.23E4CF25D0448A74.title": "Quirk: Carry On Reaches Too",
  "quest.23E4CF25D0448A74.quest_desc": [
    "The pack scales Carry On's pick-up distance with your reach, so the arm also lets you lift chests, furnaces and animals from farther away."
  ],
  "quest.3589E9C66EE3ADC7.title": "Reach Opens No Doors",
  "quest.3589E9C66EE3ADC7.quest_desc": [
    "More reach bypasses nothing: Heliodor's ruins, Solsticio outside your plot and other teams' claims refuse breaking and placing from any distance, and the server checks.",
    "",
    "The long arm of the law is still longer."
  ],
  "quest.79F61128A0C573B6.title": "One Arm per Campaign",
  "quest.79F61128A0C573B6.quest_desc": [
    "Atlas rewards come once per campaign, to whoever delivers, so the Atlas gives a team one arm: hand it to your main builder or pass it around. Replaying or reconnecting never makes a second.",
    "",
    "It survives fire and lava, and Tombstone keeps it in your grave if you die."
  ],
  "quest.2021A7FC13489E8C.title": "Terra's Story",
  "quest.2021A7FC13489E8C.quest_desc": [
    "Terra wanted technology to make life in Heliodor better, and she built the Atlas from inside the light. At the close of act II the Atlas returns her arm to you and, for the first time, half-speaks her name.",
    "",
    "Her later gifts, the Terraprism among them, come in the story's final act."
  ],
  "quest.77D6E1B05A0CB693.title": "Quirk: a Curio by Data",
  "quest.77D6E1B05A0CB693.quest_desc": [
    "Held in your hand, in armor slots or in a backpack, the arm is a trophy with a line of lore. It only works from the Curios hands slot, which the pack adds by data even if other mods stop adding it."
  ],
  "quest.35F251C084EFAC2E.title": "Three Blocks Closer",
  "quest.35F251C084EFAC2E.quest_desc": [
    "Put it on, look up at the unfinished roof, and finish it from the ground.",
    "",
    "Terra would be glad to see it working again."
  ],
  "chapter.19D7B33A90883E23.title": "The Six Altars of Heliodor",
  "chapter.19D7B33A90883E23.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Earned in the Atlas, fed with fuel and left to work. And copied, if you love them."
  ],
  "quest.3CC1A133C8AFFEA6.title": "Machines That Remember the Land",
  "quest.3CC1A133C8AFFEA6.quest_desc": [
    "Six blocks you place, feed and leave working: they grow gardens, shape the land, keep monsters away, speed up crops, slow enemies and mend gear. None is crafted from scratch: the Atlas grants one of each in acts III and IV, and an original can be copied.",
    "",
    "Heliodor's groundskeepers, still clocking in."
  ],
  "quest.4905B81B132E440D.title": "How Every Altar Works",
  "quest.4905B81B132E440D.quest_desc": [
    "&eFuel in your main hand&r feeds it; hoppers and pipes can too, but nothing comes out. An &eempty hand&r shows its status and outlines its area. &eCrouching with an empty hand&r pauses or resumes it (Levelling and Repose use it differently).",
    "",
    "Fuel burns only while it works and its area is loaded. Broken, it drops with its fuel and contents."
  ],
  "quest.1B998C29999C119B.title": "Where Each Altar Comes From",
  "quest.1B998C29999C119B.quest_desc": [
    "One per Atlas project, once per campaign, to whoever delivers:\n- act III: &ePeace&r (Routing Matrix), &eGrowth&r (Propagation Core) and &eLevelling&r (Handling Core);\n- act IV: &eRenewal&r (Ecosystem Capsule), &eRepose&r (Horizon Chart) and &eTime&r (Containment Seal)."
  ],
  "quest.1E38047DAE4742C0.title": "Copies, Like Smithing Templates",
  "quest.1E38047DAE4742C0.quest_desc": [
    "Altar in the center, its act's component in the four side slots, diamonds in the corners: two altars come out. Peace takes a Routing Matrix; Growth and Renewal a Propagation Core; Levelling a Handling Core; Repose a Horizon Chart; Time a Containment Seal.",
    "",
    "Like a smithing template: the original survives, the copy costs the act."
  ],
  "quest.25E87DD1392D07A3.title": "Altar of Peace",
  "quest.25E87DD1392D07A3.quest_desc": [
    "Burns &ecandles&r, 10 minutes each. While lit, no hostile mob spawns naturally in the &e129-block cube&r around it: 64 blocks each way, up and down included, so a deep mine below still bites. It replaces Torchmaster's Mega Torch.",
    "",
    "About six candles an hour keep a base safe; bees make the wax renewable."
  ],
  "quest.3D589D8B4BEB4346.title": "What Peace Does Not Stop",
  "quest.3D589D8B4BEB4346.quest_desc": [
    "Only &enatural&r monster spawns are refused. Spawners, trial spawners, eggs, summons, conversions, raids, patrols, zombie sieges and every boss still happen, and a modded hostile filed outside the monster category may slip through.",
    "",
    "Peace, not a force field."
  ],
  "quest.63161B4946C2017A.title": "Altar of Growth",
  "quest.63161B4946C2017A.quest_desc": [
    "Burns &ebone blocks&r, 3 minutes each. Crops and saplings in the &e33 by 33&r field around it, from four blocks below to four above, grow about &e20 times&r faster, and ripe harvests drop &edouble&r.",
    "",
    "Seeds never double and unripe crops get nothing. Melons, pumpkins, cane, cactus and bamboo only grow faster, and Mystical Agriculture essence is not multiplied."
  ],
  "quest.7B978688277626D4.title": "Altar of Time",
  "quest.7B978688277626D4.quest_desc": [
    "Burns &eamethyst shards&r, 2 minutes each. Hostile mobs in the &e33-block cube&r move and strike at a third of their strength, and their projectiles fly at a third of the speed. Monsters a player kills inside drop &etriple&r loot and experience.",
    "",
    "Bosses are never slowed or multiplied. They have a schedule to keep."
  ],
  "quest.6878AADB79EAAC41.title": "Quirk: Only Real Kills Triple",
  "quest.6878AADB79EAAC41.quest_desc": [
    "Triple loot needs a real player's kill: fake-player grinders, pets and traps get the slow motion, not the bonus. Nether stars, dragon eggs, mob heads and trial keys never multiply, and gear a mob wore drops once.",
    "",
    "Slowed mobs hit a third as hard, not a third as often: their cadence comes from behavior, not stats."
  ],
  "quest.3112575E98734D79.title": "Altar of Repose",
  "quest.3112575E98734D79.quest_desc": [
    "A four-slot coffer that slowly mends what it holds, like Mending without orbs. It burns &eBottles o' Enchanting&r, one a minute, only while something inside is damaged; every 5 seconds each item regains a point, so a bottle is 12 points for one item or 48 for four.",
    "",
    "Pipes insert only damaged items and pull only whole ones, so a pipe through it is a repair line. Crouch with an empty hand to see progress."
  ],
  "quest.2D38C4F6A4B505C4.title": "Quirk: Slow on Purpose",
  "quest.2D38C4F6A4B505C4.quest_desc": [
    "From zero, an iron chestplate takes about 20 minutes, an elytra about 36 and a diamond pickaxe over two hours. Mending with the same bottle is faster but needs you there. Energy or custom-bar durability is not mended, and unbreakable items are refused.",
    "",
    "Cheap, patient and unattended, like a good grandmother."
  ],
  "quest.57AABE5F2FCD4F97.title": "Altar of Renewal",
  "quest.57AABE5F2FCD4F97.quest_desc": [
    "Grows its biome in the &e49 by 49&r square around it: the biome's trees, giant cacti in the desert, giant spruces in old taigas, mangroves, huge fungi in the Nether, chorus in the End, and flowers. Near your team's Ark garden it grows 65 by 65.",
    "",
    "It only eats &ebone meal&r or other fertilizers: each one pays 10 seconds of work and four plants, and a whole tree takes up to four. Keep the square loaded."
  ],
  "quest.0F468D5DF1795B72.title": "Every Dye, Always",
  "quest.0F468D5DF1795B72.quest_desc": [
    "Around the altar grows a symmetric dye garden: lily of the valley, poppy, dandelion, cornflower, conebloom, swamp rose and ink mushrooms, plus four huge ink mushrooms whose caps drop ink mushrooms. Its harvest crafts all 16 dyes.",
    "",
    "On sand, stone, netherrack or end stone each bed lays its own block of grass, or podzol for mushrooms. Ores, ice, water, builds and claims keep their bed empty; wither roses and berry bushes never grow."
  ],
  "quest.531B7B268260E855.title": "Altar of Levelling",
  "quest.531B7B268260E855.quest_desc": [
    "Free terrain work with the land's own plain blocks: it asks for no materials and keeps none. Burns &ecoal, charcoal or redstone&r, a minute each.\n- Empty hand: 10-second preview; use again to start; while working, pause or resume.\n- Crouch during the preview: next setting, flat 9, 17, 25 or 33 wide with a 4-block slope, then repair 49 by 49.\n- Crouch otherwise: its status."
  ],
  "quest.5014C34B7A0D89C2.title": "Only Real Terrain",
  "quest.5014C34B7A0D89C2.quest_desc": [
    "Flatten copies the top, subsurface and deep blocks around it: what it cuts vanishes and what it fills is free. Repair rebuilds pits and bare dirt as the world generator made them, with ores turned into plain rock.",
    "",
    "It never removes or creates ores, trees, ice or builds: a column holding one, a container, a crop or a fluid is left whole. Fell the trees first.",
    "",
    "Under a roof (the Nether, caves) it works the floor, never the roof or what hangs from it."
  ],
  "quest.726D5571973055F5.title": "Quirk: Everything Is Symmetric",
  "quest.726D5571973055F5.quest_desc": [
    "Every area is a square centered on the altar, worked in rings from the center out. The Levelling slope is the same on every side, and Renewal's dye garden is a pattern of coloured rings. Put the altar at the exact center of what you want to affect.",
    "",
    "Heliodor built with symmetry. Its altars never learned any other way."
  ],
  "quest.77C6298820A4A20A.title": "Altars Act as Their Owner",
  "quest.77C6298820A4A20A.quest_desc": [
    "The owner is whoever placed the altar, or the first player who fed it. Altars that change blocks act on the owner's behalf, so claims, protected ruins and Solsticio refuse them exactly as they would refuse the owner.",
    "",
    "In a team, place them where your claims allow the work."
  ],
  "quest.6CE054C946B800A9.title": "Tip: Stack the Effects",
  "quest.6CE054C946B800A9.quest_desc": [
    "Peace over the base, Growth in the middle of the fields, Time in the mob room where you fight, Repose next to the bed where you drop damaged gear.",
    "",
    "If you copy one, copy Growth first."
  ],
  "quest.2DE34E6E418790EF.title": "Six Gifts From the Past",
  "quest.2DE34E6E418790EF.quest_desc": [
    "Peace for the base, Growth for the fields, Renewal for the gardens, Levelling for the land, Time for the fights and Repose for the gear.",
    "",
    "Heliodor could not save itself, but it left very good tools."
  ],
  "chapter.0882BD4FA4DB1326.title": "Luminosities and Luminous Gear",
  "chapter.0882BD4FA4DB1326.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Six Luminosities, one ingot, the best gear in the pack and creative items made of light."
  ],
  "quest.71E023F277E7AA8B.title": "Light, Held in Your Hand",
  "quest.71E023F277E7AA8B.quest_desc": [
    "Heliodor's light, held in six shapes, is the pack's final material. Only Solsticio's natives trade the six &6Luminosities&r, and from them come the &eLuminous Ingot&r, by far the strongest gear in the pack and the recipes for creative items.",
    "",
    "The top of the ladder, and it glows."
  ],
  "quest.3564F46BB7183E54.title": "The Six Luminosities",
  "quest.3564F46BB7183E54.quest_desc": [
    "One per discipline: &6Engineering&r copper-orange, &5Arcane&r violet, &aNature&r green, &bExploration&r sky blue, &3Logistics&r turquoise and &eHabitation&r warm gold.",
    "",
    "No recipe makes them, and the pack removes any that would. Only Solsticio's awake natives sell them."
  ],
  "quest.457C56A252E9B15D.title": "The Luminous Ingot",
  "quest.457C56A252E9B15D.quest_desc": [
    "Six Luminosities, one of each, fill the outer columns of the grid. The middle column fuses magic, the divine and the machine: a Nature's Aura &esky ingot&r, an Apotheosis &egodforged pearl&r and a Mekanism &eatomic alloy&r. One recipe, one ingot.",
    "",
    "Fireproof, faintly glowing, and it repairs any luminous piece at an anvil."
  ],
  "quest.19A3618A96EB4B87.title": "Gathering the Middle Column",
  "quest.19A3618A96EB4B87.quest_desc": [
    "The &esky ingot&r is Nature's Aura magic, from its altar and aura. The &egodforged pearl&r only comes from salvaging mythic Apotheosis loot, which drops from World Tier Summit on. The &eatomic alloy&r is Mekanism's top alloy.",
    "",
    "All three are Ark materials too, so your act V setup keeps paying off."
  ],
  "quest.7251812C8E588515.title": "Netherite, Then Luminous",
  "quest.7251812C8E588515.quest_desc": [
    "The nine luminous pieces (four armor, five tools and weapons) come from the smithing table, like netherite from diamond: a &enether star&r as the template, the matching &enetherite&r piece and a &eLuminous Ingot&r. Enchantments, affixes, gems, name and wear carry over.",
    "",
    "A full kit: 9 ingots, 9 stars, 9 netherite pieces."
  ],
  "quest.143B871581ED4583.title": "By Far the Strongest",
  "quest.143B871581ED4583.quest_desc": [
    "Armor &e60&r for the set (12, 22, 16, 10), toughness &e15&r and knockback resistance 0.25 per piece (immune with all four), enchantability &e60&r. Tools mine at speed &e60&r, harvest everything and last 32,768 uses; the sword hits for &e30&r at 1.6 per second, the axe &e32&r at 1.0.",
    "",
    "AttributeFix lifts vanilla's armor cap, so none of it is wasted."
  ],
  "quest.225BFC5F2FF7C7F4.title": "It Never Breaks",
  "quest.225BFC5F2FF7C7F4.quest_desc": [
    "At its last durability point a piece goes &edim&r: armor stops protecting, tools mine at hand speed and weapons lose their bonus, like an elytra that stops gliding. Repair it and it lights up again.",
    "",
    "Fireproof, and both Mending and the Luminous Ingot at an anvil work."
  ],
  "quest.1B716F47603A296D.title": "Repaired by Light",
  "quest.1B716F47603A296D.quest_desc": [
    "Once a second, the light at your eyes repairs every luminous piece you carry, wear or hold: brightness minus 11 points each, nothing below light 12, about 4 a second in full sun. The night sky does not count.",
    "",
    "A drained chestplate is whole in under 17 minutes of sun. Solar-powered, like Heliodor."
  ],
  "quest.4B504EF68D518396.title": "The Full Set: Flight",
  "quest.4B504EF68D518396.quest_desc": [
    "All four armor pieces, lit: &ecreative-style flight&r without energy, steady night vision and no fall damage. Take one off and only the set's flight goes; other flight sources keep working. If you were airborne, you get 8 seconds of slow falling.",
    "",
    "Losing the set never kills you. Gravity asks nicely first."
  ],
  "quest.1C42854FA3D4A9F7.title": "The Luminous Sword",
  "quest.1C42854FA3D4A9F7.quest_desc": [
    "Every hit marks the target with Glowing for 5 seconds and deals &e25% more&r damage to undead. Handy in the Twilight Forest and against the Wither's escort.",
    "",
    "The undead never liked the light."
  ],
  "quest.6EEF0D18FEFDC6B1.title": "Gear That Lights the Way",
  "quest.6EEF0D18FEFDC6B1.quest_desc": [
    "With LambDynamicLights, lit luminous armor and tools shine at full brightness around you, and the ingot and Luminosities glow a little in hand. Dim pieces give no light.",
    "",
    "Caves hate you now."
  ],
  "quest.360B04E85E0041D8.title": "Luminous in Silent Gear",
  "quest.360B04E85E0041D8.quest_desc": [
    "The ingot is also a &eSilent Gear&r material, the best of all 138, with its own trait, &eRadiant&r: radiant pieces count toward the luminous set bonus, give dynamic light and are repaired by light. The main part adds Holy V, Lustrous V, Refractive and Kitty Vision, and is fireproof.",
    "",
    "Salvaging it never returns Luminosities."
  ],
  "quest.5961E56C53335CFC.title": "Quirk: Two Rivals Remain",
  "quest.5961E56C53335CFC.quest_desc": [
    "Two powered systems still do something luminous does not: a charged MekaSuit can absorb up to all damage, and Draconic's chaotic shield grows with damage modules.",
    "",
    "They are the ceiling for players who build the infrastructure; luminous is cheaper and needs no power."
  ],
  "quest.6DF9E392A1E87CB0.title": "Creative Items From Light",
  "quest.6DF9E392A1E87CB0.quest_desc": [
    "Twelve creative items get a recipe here, never a sale: among them Mekanism's energy cube (it comes out full), Create's creative motor, Ars Nouveau's source jar and Draconic's capacitor. Each grid is symmetric: Luminosities of two disciplines in the corners, two boss drops on the axis, the mod's expensive material and its best non-creative version in the middle.",
    "",
    "48 Luminosities for all twelve."
  ],
  "quest.750242C1312F40F8.title": "The Boss Drops Matter",
  "quest.750242C1312F40F8.quest_desc": [
    "Creative recipes use a &enether star&r (Wither), a &edragon heart&r (Draconic Evolution's Ender Dragon drop) and a &ewet sponge&r (Elder Guardian), and every luminous piece takes a star as its template.",
    "",
    "Act VI wants more than one of each: farm the Wither and pay the dragon a few more visits."
  ],
  "quest.3FEFFE5C3CDE9AF1.title": "Pack Change: No Duplicators",
  "quest.3FEFFE5C3CDE9AF1.quest_desc": [
    "Creative items that copy items get no recipe: the creative crate, storage cell and bin, Functional Storage's creative vending upgrade, the creative router module and Sophisticated's infinity upgrades. They would clone Luminosities, stars and pearls.",
    "",
    "No recipe turns luminous or creative items back into their inputs either."
  ],
  "quest.592061ECDBD42A57.title": "Tip: Count Your Light",
  "quest.592061ECDBD42A57.quest_desc": [
    "A full luminous set takes 54 Luminosities (nine ingots), and all twelve creative items 48 more. Each awake native sells up to four per restock, once a game day.",
    "",
    "Wake all six early in act VI and visit often; after the liberation, prices drop further."
  ],
  "quest.45F621229EAF6C22.title": "The Brightest Things You Own",
  "quest.45F621229EAF6C22.quest_desc": [
    "Gear that never breaks and flies, and creative items forged from light: the top of ENTRELUMEN's ladder.",
    "",
    "What you do with it is yours. The city and the world stay open, and now you glow in the dark."
  ],
  "chapter.670A7FABD9529818.title": "Solsticio: the City in the Light",
  "chapter.670A7FABD9529818.chapter_subtitle": [
    "The Light Key, your plot, sixteen shops, half-price villagers and the natives who sell Luminosities."
  ],
  "quest.23154202E971D33D.title": "The Capital of Heliodor",
  "quest.23154202E971D33D.quest_desc": [
    "Heliodor's capital, frozen inside the Entrelumen: an island city of gardens, copper and glass under an eternal noon. You reach it in act VI, after activating the Ark.",
    "",
    "Everyone inside has been waiting a very long time. Try not to be late."
  ],
  "quest.5B07250B9653E98A.title": "The Light Key",
  "quest.5B07250B9653E98A.quest_desc": [
    "Activating the Ark forges the &eLight Key&r for whoever activates it; teammates craft their own from an amethyst shard, two gold ingots, a Spectral Lens and a Horizon Chart. A key works only for teams whose Ark is active.",
    "",
    "Hold use for two seconds while a ring of light closes around you. Let go early and nothing is spent."
  ],
  "quest.384435517F0C36BE.title": "Broken, and Better for It",
  "quest.384435517F0C36BE.quest_desc": [
    "The key opens the way once and breaks as you cross. The &eBroken Light Key&r is bound to you: use it the same way to go home and back, as often as you like. Only its owner can use it.",
    "",
    "Home is where you last left the Overworld, or your bed, or world spawn, always checked for a safe spot. Mounts stay behind."
  ],
  "quest.23E16658D1A73696.title": "No Night, No Monsters",
  "quest.23E16658D1A73696.quest_desc": [
    "Eternal noon: no weather, no night, no hostile spawns, and interiors are never pitch black. Fall off the edge or walk past the border and the barrier of light brings you back to the arrival point, so the void never kills you.",
    "",
    "The first visit places the whole city. If the key says try again, give it a moment."
  ],
  "quest.0EEC4C8640CDE7BA.title": "Your Team's Plot",
  "quest.0EEC4C8640CDE7BA.quest_desc": [
    "The first member of a team to stand in the city claims a 16 by 16 plot for the team's campaign: one per team, kept while the campaign exists. Inside it your team builds freely; the rest of the city is protected.",
    "",
    "When every plot is taken, newcomers can still visit, and an operator can free one."
  ],
  "quest.2A148EEE6F6F68CD.title": "The Town Hall Portal",
  "quest.2A148EEE6F6F68CD.quest_desc": [
    "The Ayuntamiento holds a dormant portal with four sockets. Set act VI's &ethree relics&r in it (Juan's Luminous Seed, Terra's Terraprism and Bodhi's Blessed Heart of Heliodor), then show it your broken key: it opens for everyone.",
    "",
    "Walking in sends anyone home. The key is only shown, never kept."
  ],
  "quest.727A4BC4EDD7F47B.title": "A Waystone for Everyone",
  "quest.727A4BC4EDD7F47B.quest_desc": [
    "When the portal opens, a global Solsticio waystone appears in the Town Hall, so every waystone in the world can reach the city. Without Waystones, a twin portal appears near world spawn instead.",
    "",
    "Arriving on the portal never bounces you back: it rests for a few seconds and while you stand in it."
  ],
  "quest.3805C8D7CD312447.title": "How the Market Works",
  "quest.3805C8D7CD312447.quest_desc": [
    "The sixteen shops sell and never buy, so no loop turns items back into emeralds. Prices are in &eemeralds&r up to 64 and &eemerald blocks&r above; some offers want a second item, like a book.",
    "",
    "Shops restock once a game day when someone opens them, popular offers get dearer for a while, and reputation and Hero of the Village still count."
  ],
  "quest.4AC078B71F8995FF.title": "The Sixteen Shops",
  "quest.4AC078B71F8995FF.quest_desc": [
    "The highlights: &eLucerna&r sells enchanted books at vanilla maximum (&eMending&r for 40 emeralds and a book); &eCenit&r, rarities like elytra, totems and shulker shells; &eBrasa&r, circuits, alloys and machine parts from many tech mods; &eFulgor&r, the netherite upgrade and every armor trim.",
    "",
    "Plus twelve more, from seeds to curiosities."
  ],
  "quest.39908CEF070C2E51.title": "Offers That Wait for Your Act",
  "quest.39908CEF070C2E51.quest_desc": [
    "Some offers carry an act: elytra wait for VI, totems and shulker shells for V, heart of the sea, trident and netherite scrap for IV, echo shards for III, plus a few books and parts. Until then they show out of stock, with a hint on the action bar.",
    "",
    "It matters when a team arrives early through another team's portal or waystone."
  ],
  "quest.79D8A04CF5081F62.title": "Pack Change: Never for Sale",
  "quest.79D8A04CF5081F62.quest_desc": [
    "No emeralds, nether stars, dragon eggs, sponges, beacons, wither skulls, spawners, spawn eggs, Luminous Ingots or their rare ingredients, Light Keys or portal relics. Luminosities come only from their own native.",
    "",
    "Some things you still earn in the world. Bosses need a reason to exist."
  ],
  "quest.56F6DFDD05003993.title": "Move Villagers In",
  "quest.56F6DFDD05003993.quest_desc": [
    "Bring any Overworld villager into the &etrading hall&r and it &esettles&r: same profession and trades, but &ehalf price&r forever, wherever it trades later, and it restocks on its own daily.",
    "",
    "Carry them with Easy Villagers (&eAlt+O&r), a minecart or Carry On. A librarian with good books is the classic move."
  ],
  "quest.11E8992E59258C44.title": "The Six Natives",
  "quest.11E8992E59258C44.quest_desc": [
    "Six natives wait around the trading hall, their &eLuminosity&r out of stock until they have stood in their Overworld biome:\n- &eIgnea&r, engineering: Badlands;\n- &eArcadio&r, arcane: Swamp or Mangrove Swamp;\n- &eSilvano&r, nature: Jungle;\n- &eBrisa&r, exploration: Jagged, Frozen or Stony Peaks;\n- &eMarea&r, logistics: Warm, Lukewarm or Deep Lukewarm Ocean;\n- &eSolana&r, habitation: Sunflower Plains.",
    "",
    "Right-click a sleeping native to hear its wish."
  ],
  "quest.1EB57C6214238492.title": "Wake a Native",
  "quest.1EB57C6214238492.quest_desc": [
    "Carry it to its biome (Easy Villagers, a minecart or Carry On) and set it down: it wakes and stays awake for good, even back in Solsticio. Awake, it sells its Luminosity for &e8 emerald blocks&r plus a catalyst from its discipline, up to 4 per restock, and its other offers at half price.",
    "",
    "None of the six biomes is rare, and Nature's Compass finds them."
  ],
  "quest.18DB6AE80E859DE8.title": "Prices After the Liberation",
  "quest.18DB6AE80E859DE8.quest_desc": [
    "When the Entrelumen is freed, every price in the city drops: shopkeepers sell at &e60%&r, stacking with native and settled-villager discounts, so an awake native's Luminosity costs 5 emerald blocks. Prices round, never go below one item and always drop by at least one.",
    "",
    "Freedom has perks. Aurelia would like you to notice."
  ],
  "quest.25906E351DD1BD36.title": "Quirk: Shopkeepers Stay Put",
  "quest.25906E351DD1BD36.quest_desc": [
    "Shopkeepers and innkeepers refuse carrying mods, cannot be hurt and never level up; if one vanishes, a new one takes the post. Natives and ordinary residents can be carried off, and only their death brings a replacement.",
    "",
    "Residents chat, and some of their lines are rumors worth hearing."
  ],
  "quest.63AD5F7059C1A754.title": "Tip: Plan Your Emeralds",
  "quest.63AD5F7059C1A754.quest_desc": [
    "Six Luminosities per ingot, nine ingots per set, eight Luminosities per creative item: it adds up. Start an emerald income before act VI with Easy Villagers traders, farms of what villagers buy or your own trading hall.",
    "",
    "Heliodor runs on light. Its shops run on emeralds."
  ],
  "quest.62F97D06472111F4.title": "Tip: Motes and Frame Rate",
  "quest.62F97D06472111F4.quest_desc": [
    "The drifting motes of light are client-side and follow your particle setting: halved on Decreased, gone on Minimal. For finer control, the ENTRELUMEN client config has &esolsticio.ambientMotes&r (on or off) and &esolsticio.moteDensity&r (0 to 8, default 2).",
    "",
    "The city is big: if frames drop, lower particles or render distance."
  ],
  "quest.3DAE84462B7F4FCF.title": "A Home Inside the Light",
  "quest.3DAE84462B7F4FCF.quest_desc": [
    "Cross and return, build on your plot, trade, move villagers in and wake the six natives. The city stays open for as long as you play.",
    "",
    "Stay for the noon. It never ends."
  ],
  "chapter.08B147AC6886788B.title": "The Pack's Controls",
  "chapter.08B147AC6886788B.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Every key the preset moved, grouped by what you are doing."
  ],
  "quest.6D8C6475ADC2E030.title": "A Keyboard for 300 Mods",
  "quest.6D8C6475ADC2E030.quest_desc": [
    "V, B, R, G, H, C, Z and the arrows were each claimed by five or six mods. The pack's key preset moves the clashing ones to free keys or to Alt, Ctrl and Shift combinations, and only fills keys you never set yourself: change one and your choice stays.",
    "",
    "Three hundred mods, one keyboard. Somebody had to negotiate."
  ],
  "quest.587CCA4077F3D371.title": "Find Any Key",
  "quest.587CCA4077F3D371.quest_desc": [
    "&eControlling&r (Options, Controls, Key Binds) adds a search box and a conflict filter; red keys are used twice, which is fine when they act in different places.",
    "",
    "Unbound on purpose: Accessories' own screen (the Aether's stays on &eI&r), Crafting on a Stick's second Curios key, Ars Nouveau's next and previous spell slot (use the F6 radial), Twilight's goggle zoom (Just Zoom covers it) and the Key Bundles radial."
  ],
  "quest.3010187592F12FD0.title": "Everyday Keys",
  "quest.3010187592F12FD0.quest_desc": [
    "- &eF8&r quest book (it used to sit on the grave key).\n- &eG&r Curios: Terra's Arm and the Ultimine curio go there.\n- &eV&r (hold) FTB Ultimine.\n- &eB&r the backpack you wear or carry.\n- &eR&r Tool Belt radial, &eShift+R&r its slot inventory.\n- &eJ&r full map, &eM&r new waypoint, &eK&r claim manager.\n- &eZ&r zoom (Just Zoom)."
  ],
  "quest.1FFF4DEA44FFBB8C.title": "Map and Waypoints",
  "quest.1FFF4DEA44FFBB8C.quest_desc": [
    "&eJourneyMap&r is the pack's map: &eJ&r opens it full-screen, &eM&r makes a waypoint where you stand and, inside the map, &eB&r one at the cursor.",
    "",
    "FTB Chunks' map key is unbound and its minimap off: it only handles teams and claims, with its claim manager on &eK&r."
  ],
  "quest.2B804294ADD68A3D.title": "R and Shift+R: the Tool Belt",
  "quest.2B804294ADD68A3D.quest_desc": [
    "With a Tool Belt in its slot, hold &eR&r for a radial menu that swaps your held item with one on the belt; &eShift+R&r opens the belt's slots.",
    "",
    "R is also the recipe key inside screens, but the belt only opens with no screen open, so they never clash. Aircraft dismount moved to &eF12&r for the same reason."
  ],
  "quest.5560B3BDAFB2503C.title": "V: Ultimine",
  "quest.5560B3BDAFB2503C.quest_desc": [
    "Hold &eV&r while breaking a block to break the whole connected vein, up to the reach of the vein resonator worn in a Curios charm slot (8, 16, 32 or 64 blocks by tier; without one there is no Ultimine), at extra hunger per block. With V held, Shift and the mouse wheel (or up and down arrows) switch shape: shapeless, tunnels or 3x3.",
    "",
    "Modern Industrialization's 3x3 tool toggle moved to &eAlt+V&r."
  ],
  "quest.6EFB8442677ABC33.title": "Mekanism Armor: Alt + Arrows",
  "quest.6EFB8442677ABC33.quest_desc": [
    "Mekanism's armor mode keys left V, G, J and B for the arrows with &eAlt&r: &eAlt+Up&r helmet, &eAlt+Left&r chestplate, &eAlt+Down&r leggings, &eAlt+Right&r boots.",
    "",
    "The MekaSuit HUD toggles with Ctrl and the module tweaker with Alt, each plus the key where US keyboards have the backslash."
  ],
  "quest.606412CA5CDED070.title": "Flight and Travel Keys",
  "quest.606412CA5CDED070.quest_desc": [
    "- &eF4&r Iron Jetpacks engine, &eAlt+H&r its hover.\n- &eShift+F4&r Modern Industrialization flight.\n- &eCtrl+F4&r Ad Astra suit flight, &eAlt+R&r Ad Astra radio.\n- &eAlt+E&r Ender IO Staff of Travelling.\n- &eF12&r get off an Immersive Aircraft plane, &eCtrl+F12&r its boost.",
    "",
    "Every way of flying got its own key. Crashing is still shared."
  ],
  "quest.48B114C209222330.title": "Magic Keys",
  "quest.48B114C209222330.quest_desc": [
    "- &eF6&r Ars Nouveau spell radial, &e0&r its crown potion radial.\n- Iron's Spells wheel on the key left of 1 (grave accent on US keyboards), &eAlt+Q&r cast from the spellbook.\n- &eAlt+F&r Psi's main key (C stays for the vanilla hotbar save and the Ars book).\n- Mahou Tsukai: &eAlt+M&r magic circle, &eShift+Y&r mystic code, &eCtrl+H&r selective displacement, &eAlt+.&r settings, &ePage Up/Down&r its guns."
  ],
  "quest.16A91FEE3BA9C17E.title": "Exploration and Armor Abilities",
  "quest.16A91FEE3BA9C17E.quest_desc": [
    "- Aether: &eHome&r invisibility cloak; Deep Aether &eShift+Home&r skyjade transparency, &eAlt+G&r stratus dash, &eShift+H&r slider eye.\n- Twilight: the US semicolon key swaps the hotbar, and Shift plus it handles item display maps.\n- Eternal Starlight: &eH&r switches crest.\n- Deeper and Darker: &eAlt+B&r boost, &eAlt+N&r transmit.\n- Cataclysm armor: &eAlt+J&r, &eAlt+K&r helmet, &eAlt+L&r chestplate, &eAlt+I&r boots."
  ],
  "quest.181BA0D5FFEF2462.title": "Utility Keys",
  "quest.181BA0D5FFEF2462.quest_desc": [
    "- &eAlt+O&r pick up a villager (Easy Villagers).\n- &eShift+M&r Simple Magnets, &eCtrl+M&r Ender IO magnet.\n- US apostrophe key: Supplementaries quiver.\n- &eO&r Occultism ender satchel, &eShift+O&r its storage remote, &eInsert&r its satchel.\n- &eF10&r clear notifications.\n- &eEnd&r Building Gadgets range, &eShift+End&r settings, &eCtrl+End&r anchor.\n- &eAlt+T&r, &eShift+T&r Just Dire Things.\n- &eAlt+P&r, &eAlt+Y&r Draconic; &eAlt+U&r Hostile Neural Networks; &eAlt+Z&r Oritech implants (hold)."
  ],
  "quest.5085B25979D0B540.title": "Ctrl+T, Ctrl+O and Shift+T",
  "quest.5085B25979D0B540.quest_desc": [
    "Three Apotheosis keys keep their native combinations: &eCtrl+T&r opens the World Tier screen (readable, but the story sets the tier), &eCtrl+O&r toggles radial mining on gear that has it, and &eShift+T&r in an inventory links the hovered item in chat for your team to admire."
  ],
  "quest.2AD44E12B13F4108.title": "LittleTiles Keys",
  "quest.2AD44E12B13F4108.quest_desc": [
    "LittleTiles, the small-block builder, has its own set: &eN&r mirror, &eU&r mark, &eCtrl+I&r configure the held tool (&eShift+I&r secondary settings), &eCtrl+Home&r building mode, &eCtrl+Z&r undo, &eCtrl+Y&r redo.",
    "",
    "How to use them: the Building Tools chapter."
  ],
  "quest.7120653E6832BDAE.title": "Tip: Keys Named by Position",
  "quest.7120653E6832BDAE.quest_desc": [
    "A few preset keys are named after US symbols, the semicolon and the apostrophe, and on a Spanish or Latin American keyboard those physical keys print something else.",
    "",
    "Do not hunt for the symbol: read the label in Controls, which shows what your layout prints, or rebind it."
  ],
  "quest.4625B97E61B1C74D.title": "Tip: Key Bundles",
  "quest.4625B97E61B1C74D.quest_desc": [
    "&eKeyBind Bundles&r gathers rarely used actions into a radial menu behind one key. It ships unbound: bind &eOpen Bundle radial menu&r in Controls and build bundles from its screen.",
    "",
    "Good candidates: armor abilities, magic toggles, every Mahou Tsukai key."
  ],
  "quest.0C7671DD3A4A0940.title": "Quirk: Alt, Ctrl and Shift Win",
  "quest.0C7671DD3A4A0940.quest_desc": [
    "When a modified combination and a plain key share a letter, the combination whose modifier you hold wins: &eAlt+Q&r casts a spell without dropping your item, and &eCtrl+O&r toggles radial mining instead of opening the ender satchel.",
    "",
    "If a combination ever fires both actions, report it."
  ],
  "quest.38BCA7D778496F93.title": "Pack Change: Client Defaults",
  "quest.38BCA7D778496F93.quest_desc": [
    "A new profile also gets the pack's performance settings (see Performance, Sound and Screen), auto-jump off and the pack's resource pack enabled.",
    "",
    "They are only defaults: if your launcher already made an options file, existing values stay and only missing ones are added."
  ],
  "quest.487DF43C29D28D87.title": "Your Keyboard, Your Rules",
  "quest.487DF43C29D28D87.quest_desc": [
    "Everything here is a suggestion: keep what feels natural, rebind the rest with Controlling and put rare actions in a bundle.",
    "",
    "When a new tool shows up, check back here: its key is probably already waiting."
  ],
  "chapter.64B80719A7DF9516.title": "Recipes and Information",
  "chapter.64B80719A7DF9516.chapter_subtitle": [
    "EMI, Jade and the tooltips: how to find out what anything does without leaving the game."
  ],
  "quest.3CF1DB3935AAE039.title": "Where Answers Live",
  "quest.3CF1DB3935AAE039.quest_desc": [
    "Three hundred mods, and nobody remembers every recipe. You do not need a wiki: the game tells you how to make an item, what it is for, what a block holds and what an enchantment or effect does.",
    "",
    "R, U and a little curiosity replace most forum threads."
  ],
  "quest.55262A03C2144680.title": "EMI: the Item List",
  "quest.55262A03C2144680.quest_desc": [
    "The item column on the right of your inventory is &eEMI&r, the recipe viewer; its search bar sits at the bottom. Names follow your game language, and untranslated mods show English. &eCtrl+F&r jumps to the search, &eCtrl+O&r hides the whole overlay, and the mouse wheel turns pages."
  ],
  "quest.61CA4F1B5C30E59D.title": "R: How Do I Make This?",
  "quest.61CA4F1B5C30E59D.quest_desc": [
    "Hover any item, in EMI or any inventory, and press &eR&r (or left-click it in the list): every recipe that makes it appears, one tab per machine or crafting type. Hover a tab's icon to see which blocks run it, and &eBackspace&r goes back.",
    "",
    "The most-pressed key in the pack, by a mile."
  ],
  "quest.31B358B0E659662B.title": "U: What Is This For?",
  "quest.31B358B0E659662B.quest_desc": [
    "&eU&r over an item (or right-click in the list) shows every recipe that uses it: the fastest way to decide whether that strange drop is worth keeping.",
    "",
    "Try U on a machine to see everything it can process."
  ],
  "quest.0E7FE69D2A058E7E.title": "Search Like a Pro",
  "quest.0E7FE69D2A058E7E.quest_desc": [
    "EMI search understands prefixes: &e@create&r filters by mod, &e#c:ingots&r by tag, &e$fortune&r searches tooltips, a leading &e-&r excludes (&edirt -@minecraft&r), &e|&r means or (&etin|lead&r), slashes make a regular expression and quotes keep spaces together.",
    "",
    "Try one and you will never scroll again."
  ],
  "quest.566F682243FD07BC.title": "A: Favorites",
  "quest.566F682243FD07BC.quest_desc": [
    "&eA&r over an item pins it to the favorites bar on the left; A on a recipe pins that exact recipe, and A again removes it. Favorites survive between sessions.",
    "",
    "Keep there what you craft often: rations, torches, the next act component."
  ],
  "quest.53291CF6E456E08B.title": "The + Button Fills the Grid",
  "quest.53291CF6E456E08B.quest_desc": [
    "The small &e+&r beside a recipe moves its ingredients from your inventory into the open grid or machine, and &eShift+click&r fills as many batches as you can afford.",
    "",
    "Open the crafting table first, then look up the recipe. The other way round, nothing happens."
  ],
  "quest.3EC6B1E3A960D9DD.title": "The Recipe Tree",
  "quest.3EC6B1E3A960D9DD.quest_desc": [
    "On a recipe, &eView Recipe Tree&r draws the whole chain down to raw materials with the total cost. Click a node to pick its recipe (Shift lets EMI choose from your inventory), right-click to fold a branch, and crafting mode adds &bsynthetic favorites&r: the steps you still have to make.",
    "",
    "Made for act components."
  ],
  "quest.406D38FB9E0D4DF3.title": "Default Recipes",
  "quest.406D38FB9E0D4DF3.quest_desc": [
    "When an item has several recipes, &eCtrl+click&r the output of the one you prefer to make it the default for the tree and synthetic favorites.",
    "",
    "Handy when the same plate comes from Create, Immersive Engineering and Mekanism and you only built one of them."
  ],
  "quest.6CE1567F3B363FF1.title": "Why JEI Is Installed Too",
  "quest.6CE1567F3B363FF1.quest_desc": [
    "EMI is the viewer you see, but JEI stays so that add-ons written for it still reach you: EMI reads JEI plugins and shows their pages inside its own interface, from Mekanism multiblocks to villager professions.",
    "",
    "A page that looks slightly different probably comes from a JEI plugin."
  ],
  "quest.4B4E944BB1EAB381.title": "Pages You Did Not Know About",
  "quest.4B4E944BB1EAB381.quest_desc": [
    "&eJust Enough Professions&r (which workstation gives which job), &eJust Enough Breeding&r (what each animal eats), &eJust Enough Archaeology&r (what each suspicious block drops), &eJust Enough Mekanism Multiblocks&r (sizes and parts) and &eSmithing Template Viewer&r (what each template makes).",
    "",
    "U over a lectern, a cow or a brush finds them fast."
  ],
  "quest.66D47A11A965B2B7.title": "Jade: What Am I Looking At?",
  "quest.66D47A11A965B2B7.quest_desc": [
    "The small panel at the top of the screen is &eJade&r: the name of the block or creature you look at, its mod and useful state such as a machine's energy, a crop's growth or a furnace's progress; Jade Addons covers more mods.",
    "",
    "The mod name alone solves half the questions in a big pack."
  ],
  "quest.674B69F2C86D4CA3.title": "Jade's Keypad Keys",
  "quest.674B69F2C86D4CA3.quest_desc": [
    "&eNumpad 0&r opens Jade's settings (hide lines you do not care about), &eNumpad 1&r hides the panel, &eNumpad 2&r toggles fluids, and &eNumpad 3&r and &eNumpad 4&r show recipes and uses of what you are looking at.",
    "",
    "No keypad? Rebind them in Controls. Laptops, we see you."
  ],
  "quest.0F7DBD2F6C93F685.title": "Tooltips That Explain",
  "quest.0F7DBD2F6C93F685.quest_desc": [
    "&eEnchantment Descriptions&r explains every enchantment; &eAppleSkin&r shows a food's hunger and saturation and previews them on the bar; &eEquipment Compare&r sets armor or weapons beside yours while you hold &eLeft Shift&r; and &eF3+H&r, extended by Better Advanced Tooltips, adds IDs, durability and technical data."
  ],
  "quest.712D684D42FF0AF7.title": "Peek Inside Containers",
  "quest.712D684D42FF0AF7.quest_desc": [
    "&eShulker Box Tooltip&r shows a shulker box's contents without placing it: &eLeft Shift&r for a compact view, &eAlt+Shift&r for the full grid, &eLeft Ctrl&r to lock the preview.",
    "",
    "Sophisticated Backpacks list their contents when you hold Shift over them."
  ],
  "quest.64CCA8C454B93ADC.title": "What Does This Effect Do?",
  "quest.64CCA8C454B93ADC.quest_desc": [
    "Search an effect's name in EMI: &eJust Enough Effect Descriptions&r adds a page per effect with an explanation and the items that cause it.",
    "",
    "Handy for the satiety system's random buffs and the potions from Solsticio's apothecary."
  ],
  "quest.2136A30BA938D958.title": "Two Recipes, One Grid",
  "quest.2136A30BA938D958.quest_desc": [
    "When two recipes share a pattern, &ePolymorph&r adds a small button beside the output slot so you can pick the result.",
    "",
    "If the table hands you the \"wrong\" item, look for that button before blaming the recipe."
  ],
  "quest.3DE198C3AFAF7F1C.title": "Guide Books Are Crafted",
  "quest.3DE198C3AFAF7F1C.quest_desc": [
    "Nobody hands you a book on login, but every manual is still craftable: Ars Nouveau's Tattered Tome, the Integrated Dynamics manual, the Actually Additions booklet, Modern Industrialization's guidebook, Silent Gear's material book, the PneumaticCraft and Psi manuals and more.",
    "",
    "EMI has each recipe, and the Akashic Tome keeps them all in one."
  ],
  "quest.4178311F064476BB.title": "Tip: Which Mod Is This?",
  "quest.4178311F064476BB.quest_desc": [
    "Item tooltips in EMI end with the mod's name in blue italics, and Jade shows it for blocks in the world.",
    "",
    "When a wiki and the game disagree, trust the game: the pack changes some recipes, and EMI always shows the version you really have."
  ],
  "quest.7C55DEA7E7A3F179.title": "Pack Change: One Slot for the Act",
  "quest.7C55DEA7E7A3F179.quest_desc": [
    "Milestones swap one slot on their drawing's axis for an &6act component&r (Calibration Frame, Routing Matrix, Spectral Lens...): the AE2 and Refined Storage controllers, the Digital Miner or the Botany Pots upgrades. Other steps take an act material: a Mekanism alloy, ironwood or zanite.",
    "",
    "Unfamiliar ENTRELUMEN item in a grid? Press &eR&r on it; the Atlas chapter has the rest."
  ],
  "quest.73F28D876C6411ED.title": "Pack Change: One Route per Recipe",
  "quest.73F28D876C6411ED.quest_desc": [
    "Where mods copy each other's recipes, the pack switches off the copies so each recipe shows once in EMI; the kitchen machines are the classic case (see The Kitchen).",
    "",
    "Apotheosis's own item comparison is off too: Equipment Compare already does it on Shift."
  ],
  "quest.43CB273891F7D134.title": "Pack Change: No Recipe on Purpose",
  "quest.43CB273891F7D134.quest_desc": [
    "The six &6Luminosities&r (only Solsticio's natives trade them), item duplicators such as the creative crate, storage cell, bin and infinity upgrades, and Torchmaster's Mega Torch (the Altar of Peace replaces it) have no recipe at all.",
    "",
    "When U shows uses but R shows nothing, read the tooltip: it usually says where the item comes from."
  ],
  "quest.180B2B2465B8EE5E.title": "F7 and F9: Light and Chunk Lines",
  "quest.180B2B2465B8EE5E.quest_desc": [
    "&eMore Overlays&r adds two world toggles: &eF7&r marks blocks where hostile mobs can spawn because the light is too low, and &eF9&r draws chunk borders, handy before claiming land or building a chunk-sized farm.",
    "",
    "Light a cave with F7 on until no marks remain."
  ],
  "quest.4221014B1F59149C.title": "You Can Look Anything Up",
  "quest.4221014B1F59149C.quest_desc": [
    "R for recipes, U for uses, A for favorites, the tree for long chains, Jade for the world and tooltips for everything else.",
    "",
    "The wiki can rest now."
  ],
  "chapter.31A61F4C1354DBD2.title": "Inventory Without Pain",
  "chapter.31A61F4C1354DBD2.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Mouse gestures, sorting, trash, portable stations, magnets and the Tool Belt."
  ],
  "quest.40752BE0BC2CF1E7.title": "Less Clicking, More Playing",
  "quest.40752BE0BC2CF1E7.quest_desc": [
    "Big pack, big inventory. A handful of small mods remove clicks: drag gestures, one-key sorting, a trash slot, crafting tables on a stick, magnets and a tool belt. None of them touches progression.",
    "",
    "Moving items should never feel like a second job."
  ],
  "quest.43411C7BA4F791B5.title": "Mouse Tweaks",
  "quest.43411C7BA4F791B5.quest_desc": [
    "In any inventory: hold &eright click&r and drag over empty slots to drop one item in each; hold &eleft click&r with a stack and drag to gather the same kind; &eShift&r plus left-drag with an empty hand sends every slot you touch across; the &emouse wheel&r over an item moves it one at a time."
  ],
  "quest.2ED5039CAADCDB2D.title": "Sorting With Inventory Tweaks",
  "quest.2ED5039CAADCDB2D.quest_desc": [
    "&eInventory Tweaks Refoxed&r is the pack's only sorter: the &ebackslash&r key sorts your inventory and the &egrave-accent&r key the open chest (check Controls for your layout's labels).",
    "",
    "It also refills a hotbar slot from your inventory when a tool breaks or a stack runs out."
  ],
  "quest.728C08F385A0AAAB.title": "Vanilla Tricks Worth Knowing",
  "quest.728C08F385A0AAAB.quest_desc": [
    "&eDouble-click&r gathers every item of a kind onto the cursor; &eShift+double-click&r moves all those stacks across. &e1-9&r swap the hovered slot with the hotbar, &eF&r with the offhand. &eQ&r over a slot drops one, &eCtrl+Q&r the whole stack.",
    "",
    "Minecraft had these all along. Nobody told you."
  ],
  "quest.29FA4CC3289502F3.title": "Crafting Tweaks",
  "quest.29FA4CC3289502F3.quest_desc": [
    "Small buttons beside the crafting grid &erotate&r it, &ebalance&r and &espread&r ingredients, and &eclear&r it back to your inventory (force clear drops items if you are full). They show up on many modded stations too.",
    "",
    "With EMI's + button, shaped recipes become painless."
  ],
  "quest.099E800BF0796631.title": "Fuel Goes Where It Should",
  "quest.099E800BF0796631.quest_desc": [
    "&eFuel Goes Here&r sends Shift-clicked coal, charcoal or any fuel to a furnace's fuel slot first, not the input.",
    "",
    "Fast Workbench and Fast Furnace cache recipe lookups, so crafting and smelting stay quick with this many recipes."
  ],
  "quest.768C2BFC98D0D302.title": "Getting Rid of Things",
  "quest.768C2BFC98D0D302.quest_desc": [
    "&eTrashSlot&r adds a trash slot to your inventory; it keeps the last item until you trash another, so a misclick can be undone. &eTrash Cans&r are blocks that void whatever pipes send them (items, fluids, energy or everything), with a 9-entry filter on the item and fluid ones.",
    "",
    "Farm overflow goes to a can, not to the floor."
  ],
  "quest.12F24BEA959401E4.title": "Quirk: TrashSlot on Servers",
  "quest.12F24BEA959401E4.quest_desc": [
    "TrashSlot works in single player, but on a dedicated server only if the server has it too; otherwise it says so in chat and turns itself off.",
    "",
    "A Trash Can block does the same job for everyone."
  ],
  "quest.5117E4B67334A4B3.title": "Stations on a Stick",
  "quest.5117E4B67334A4B3.quest_desc": [
    "&eCrafting On A Stick&r turns the crafting table, stonecutter, loom, cartography table, smithing table, grindstone and anvil into hotbar items you right-click to open anywhere.",
    "",
    "Perfect for early expeditions, when every slot counts."
  ],
  "quest.3B11AF8418138B60.title": "The Tool Belt",
  "quest.3B11AF8418138B60.quest_desc": [
    "A &eTool Belt&r (leather, string and an iron ingot) goes in its own slot, and its tools leave your hotbar free: hold &eR&r for the radial menu, &eShift+R&r for the belt's slots.",
    "",
    "It starts small; combine it with a &eBelt Pouch&r in an anvil for more room."
  ],
  "quest.5131D32867AE6A92.title": "One Book for All Books",
  "quest.5131D32867AE6A92.quest_desc": [
    "The &eAkashic Tome&r (a book and a bookshelf) stores every guide book in one item: craft it with a book to add it, then &eShift+right-click&r to pick which one it becomes.",
    "",
    "Ars Nouveau, Integrated Dynamics, PneumaticCraft, Psi and friends, all in one pocket."
  ],
  "quest.580411F1188ABEEA.title": "Magnets",
  "quest.580411F1188ABEEA.quest_desc": [
    "&eSimple Magnets&r pull items and experience to you while switched on (&eShift+M&r). The basic one has a fixed range; the advanced one adjusts range and filters, so it can ignore cobblestone.",
    "",
    "Near farms your magnet must not loot, place a &eDemagnetization Coil&r."
  ],
  "quest.7A572E4824CB3002.title": "Item Collectors",
  "quest.7A572E4824CB3002.quest_desc": [
    "An &eItem Collector&r (an ender pearl on obsidian) picks up dropped items around it and holds them for a hopper or pipe; the advanced one has a configurable range and a filter.",
    "",
    "Put one under a tree farm or in a mob room. Fewer loose items, less lag."
  ],
  "quest.0295F66723444CF2.title": "Tip: Experience in Clumps",
  "quest.0295F66723444CF2.quest_desc": [
    "&eClumps&r merges nearby experience orbs into one, so a mob farm or a big smelting session no longer carpets the floor with orbs, and picking them up is instant.",
    "",
    "Less disco, more XP."
  ],
  "quest.4E08471DA70A04CF.title": "A Real Backpack",
  "quest.4E08471DA70A04CF.quest_desc": [
    "Sophisticated Backpacks carry dozens of slots, open with &eB&r and take upgrades that pick up, sort, restock and feed you. Start with a basic one.",
    "",
    "Tiers and upgrades: the Storage chapter."
  ],
  "quest.1398AE437E30A689.title": "Pack Change: Nothing to Start",
  "quest.1398AE437E30A689.quest_desc": [
    "No mod puts items in your inventory when you join: books, kits and plushies are all switched off, and everything here is crafted from ordinary materials.",
    "",
    "Why: the start chapter, Waking Among Ruins."
  ],
  "chapter.4208B1046BA4147D.title": "Building Tools",
  "chapter.4208B1046BA4147D.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Framed blocks, tiny tiles, construction sticks, gadgets and measuring tape: detail and scale."
  ],
  "quest.552EB40238B52126.title": "Tools for Builders",
  "quest.552EB40238B52126.quest_desc": [
    "Two kinds of tools: some for &edetail&r (shapes smaller than a block, blocks that wear any texture) and some for &escale&r (placing, swapping and copying hundreds of blocks at once). Only the heavy machines at the end wait for the story.",
    "",
    "Scaffolding optional. Taste not included."
  ],
  "quest.39516BD2BFA84B5C.title": "Construction Sticks",
  "quest.39516BD2BFA84B5C.quest_desc": [
    "Right-click a face with a &eConstruction Stick&r and it lays a whole new layer of that block from your inventory. Wooden, copper, iron, diamond and netherite tiers place more at once, and there is an undo.",
    "",
    "Templates add upgrades such as placing in mid-air, replacing, destroying or running on energy; EMI shows how."
  ],
  "quest.7486910B168693D2.title": "Measure Before You Build",
  "quest.7486910B168693D2.quest_desc": [
    "The &eTape Measure&r (gray wool, yellow wool and an iron ingot) shows the size between two positions you mark. Measure the plot, the farm or the machine room before placing a block.",
    "",
    "LittleTiles has its own Little Measure Tape for tiny work. Measure twice, place once."
  ],
  "quest.3289836EB14EC8B3.title": "FramedBlocks: Any Texture",
  "quest.3289836EB14EC8B3.quest_desc": [
    "&eFramedBlocks&r makes shapes (slabs, stairs, panels, slopes, corners, doors, fences and many more) from an empty frame; right-click a placed one with any block to wear its texture: a copper sloped roof, a stone door.",
    "",
    "Craft each shape normally or pick it at the &eFraming Saw&r, which lists them all."
  ],
  "quest.66D34FD3FF9FAF0A.title": "Framed Tools and Tricks",
  "quest.66D34FD3FF9FAF0A.quest_desc": [
    "The &eFramed Wrench&r rotates and configures framed blocks and the &eFramed Hammer&r toggles styles and recovers the camo; &eglowstone dust&r makes one glow and a &eFramed Reinforcement&r makes it blast-proof.",
    "",
    "The &eFramed Blueprint&r copies a framed block with its camo and places copies from your materials."
  ],
  "quest.2ABFC8B03407EFD0.title": "LittleTiles: Inside a Block",
  "quest.2ABFC8B03407EFD0.quest_desc": [
    "Build with pieces much smaller than a block: the &eLittle Chisel&r places shapes of a block, the &eHammer&r carves them out, the &eGlove&r selects and moves pieces, the &ePaint Brush&r colors them, the &eBag&r holds materials and colors, and the &eBlueprint&r copies small builds.",
    "",
    "&eCtrl+I&r sets grid size and shape; the full key list is in the Controls chapter."
  ],
  "quest.76FD0835952BE5CB.title": "Quirk: Tiny Tiles Cost Frames",
  "quest.76FD0835952BE5CB.quest_desc": [
    "Each LittleTiles block can hold a lot of geometry, paid by your graphics card rather than the server. A few detailed rooms are fine; a whole city of micro-detail will drop your frame rate.",
    "",
    "LittleTiles for statues, furniture and signs; FramedBlocks or Copycats for big surfaces."
  ],
  "quest.4C2F9A63176C8DFE.title": "LittleTiles Doors",
  "quest.4C2F9A63176C8DFE.quest_desc": [
    "The Little Blueprint saves a selection as a structure, and some structures move: doors slide or rotate by the distance and angle you choose, and can open with a right-click.",
    "",
    "A secret bookshelf door made of tiny pieces is a rite of passage."
  ],
  "quest.27D44B4CD8346A17.title": "Building Gadgets 2",
  "quest.27D44B4CD8346A17.quest_desc": [
    "Five powered gadgets: &eBuilding&r places shapes (walls, floors, surfaces), &eExchanging&r swaps an area's blocks, &eCopy-Paste&r and &eCut-Paste&r copy or move whole structures, and &eDestruction&r clears a box. Each has undo in its radial menu.",
    "",
    "Charge them in any FE charger, like a Mekanism energy cube's charge slot."
  ],
  "quest.1815847FD7276ACD.title": "Gadget Keys and Templates",
  "quest.1815847FD7276ACD.quest_desc": [
    "With a gadget in hand, &eShift+End&r opens its settings, &eEnd&r changes the range and &eCtrl+End&r (Anchor) locks the preview so you can walk around it.",
    "",
    "The &eTemplate Manager&r stores Copy-Paste templates for reuse."
  ],
  "quest.5E8ECEB07E12638F.title": "Quirk: Protected Areas",
  "quest.5E8ECEB07E12638F.quest_desc": [
    "Other teams' claims, Heliodor ruins and Solsticio outside your plot refuse breaking and placing, so do not plan big gadget jobs there. On your own land, gadgets, sticks and altars act as you and follow your team's claim settings."
  ],
  "quest.48FE30F982594D40.title": "Flatten Land the Pack's Way",
  "quest.48FE30F982594D40.quest_desc": [
    "For big flat areas, the &eAltar of Levelling&r (act III) levels a square with a smooth symmetric slope, or repairs dug land, using the land's own blocks for free.",
    "",
    "Sizes, fuel and gestures: The Six Altars of Heliodor."
  ],
  "quest.50C34B4F07576EBA.title": "Pack Change: Heavy Builders",
  "quest.50C34B4F07576EBA.quest_desc": [
    "The &eRFTools Builder&r needs a Handling Core and the &eMining Gadgets&r a reinforced alloy, both act III, because they move or mine huge volumes.",
    "",
    "Everything else here is free from day one."
  ],
  "quest.6480EAD988459A99.title": "Tip: a Builder's Workflow",
  "quest.6480EAD988459A99.quest_desc": [
    "Measure with the tape, flatten with the Altar of Levelling or a Destruction Gadget, raise walls with a Construction Stick, swap materials with the Exchanging Gadget, then add detail with FramedBlocks, Macaw's and LittleTiles.",
    "",
    "Then Copy-Paste your best house and call it a street."
  ],
  "quest.3E2BA0EA29D6168D.title": "Detail and Scale",
  "quest.3E2BA0EA29D6168D.quest_desc": [
    "Pieces smaller than a block, any texture on any shape, thousands of blocks placed without breaking a sweat.",
    "",
    "Every good house needs a garden. The farming chapters are next door."
  ],
  "chapter.4259956EC2B18EFD.title": "Building: Blocks and Variants",
  "chapter.4259956EC2B18EFD.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Chipped, Rechiseled, Macaw's, Create Deco and functional glass: where every variant comes from and how to find it."
  ],
  "quest.3FD036B18FD541E2.title": "Thousands of Blocks, One Idea",
  "quest.3FD036B18FD541E2.quest_desc": [
    "Thousands of decorative blocks, but only a few sources: a workbench, a chisel, the stonecutter or the crafting table. Learn the sources, not the blocks.",
    "",
    "The story never asks for any of them. Build however you like; the cube house is also valid. Technically."
  ],
  "quest.4499259E5C4284D8.title": "Find Every Variant",
  "quest.4499259E5C4284D8.quest_desc": [
    "Hover a block and press &eU&r in EMI: every recipe that uses it appears, including each Chipped, chisel and stonecutter variant. Search &e@chipped&r, &e@mcw&r or &e@createdeco&r to browse a whole mod.",
    "",
    "This one trick replaces most building wikis."
  ],
  "quest.3FD169F826E0CEC2.title": "Chipped Workbenches",
  "quest.3FD169F826E0CEC2.quest_desc": [
    "Hundreds of vanilla variants, one to one, in seven benches: &eMason Table&r (stone, bricks, concrete, terracotta), &eCarpenters Table&r (wood), &eGlassblower&r (glass), &eLoom Table&r (wool, carpets), &eBotanist Workbench&r (dirt, sand, leaves, ice, pumpkins), &eAlchemy Bench&r (mineral blocks, amethyst, waxed copper) and &eTinkering Table&r (lamps, bars, redstone).",
    "",
    "Nothing is lost."
  ],
  "quest.16FFDBCA7DA034F1.title": "The Rechiseled Chisel",
  "quest.16FFDBCA7DA034F1.quest_desc": [
    "Right-click with the &eChisel&r, put blocks in, pick a variant (many with connected textures) and take them out; previews show 1x1, 3x1 or 3x3.",
    "",
    "Here it also reaches Chipped's variants through Rechiseled: Chipped, so one tool covers both families."
  ],
  "quest.2E768D0705A83924.title": "Chiseling by the Stack",
  "quest.2E768D0705A83924.quest_desc": [
    "Once you have a Create workshop, the &eMechanical Chisel&r (Rechiseled: Create) converts blocks by itself: give it rotation, set the output filter and feed it by belt or funnel.",
    "",
    "For when a build needs a few thousand of the same chiseled brick. It happens."
  ],
  "quest.2E270670E1203AAD.title": "Macaw's: Nine Families",
  "quest.2E270670E1203AAD.quest_desc": [
    "Roofs, Windows, Doors, Trapdoors, Fences and Walls, Bridges, Stairs and Balconies, Paths and Pavings, and Lights and Lamps. Wooden pieces are crafted; most stone roofs, stairs, fences and bridges and nearly all paths come from the &estonecutter&r.",
    "",
    "Drop stone in a stonecutter and scroll: dozens of Macaw's options appear."
  ],
  "quest.1901870848FC4CA2.title": "Macaw's Moving Parts",
  "quest.1901870848FC4CA2.quest_desc": [
    "Windows open and some resize to fill bigger openings, shutters and blinds open with a click, gates stack two high, trapdoors and barn doors open like vanilla ones, and many lights switch on and off.",
    "",
    "Right-click things before deciding they are only decoration."
  ],
  "quest.5612D039A8FE9624.title": "Create Deco: Industrial Style",
  "quest.5612D039A8FE9624.quest_desc": [
    "Colored bricks, sheet metal, catwalks with railings and stairs, bars, mesh fences, supports, industrial doors and windows, hull blocks, placards, shipping containers and lamps in several metals.",
    "",
    "Almost all of it comes from the stonecutter, from bricks, andesite alloy, iron, copper, brass or zinc."
  ],
  "quest.29A2A50413524CD2.title": "Glass That Does Things",
  "quest.29A2A50413524CD2.quest_desc": [
    "&eGlassential&r glass: redstone (full signal), light (full glow), ghostly (anything walks through), ethereal (players pass, mobs do not; reverse does the opposite; dark versions block light), one-way (a secret window), smart (frosts with redstone) and protected (blast-proof), plus glass doors and trapdoors.",
    "",
    "Secret doors and mob-proof windows, sorted."
  ],
  "quest.0D2382C1E7856E7F.title": "Light as a Material",
  "quest.0D2382C1E7856E7F.quest_desc": [
    "Macaw's Lights and Lamps (garden, wall and ceiling lights, chandeliers, fans), &eSimply Light&r edge strips and flush blocks that switch with redstone, Supplementaries sconces and candle holders, Create Deco lamps and Glassential light glass.",
    "",
    "Hide light in floors and ceilings instead of dotting torches everywhere."
  ],
  "quest.75651965718D0718.title": "Copycat Blocks",
  "quest.75651965718D0718.quest_desc": [
    "&eCopycats+&r adds Create copycat shapes (slabs, stairs, beams, panels and more) that take the look of any block you right-click them with. With FramedBlocks, curves and thin details in any material become easy.",
    "",
    "FramedBlocks and LittleTiles: the Building Tools chapter."
  ],
  "quest.2B856A81E120ECF9.title": "Hard-Light Bridges",
  "quest.2B856A81E120ECF9.quest_desc": [
    "&eLaser Bridges and Doors&r source blocks project a solid bridge or fence of light while powered by redstone; cut the signal and it vanishes.",
    "",
    "Drawbridges, hangar doors and lever-operated gates, with a sci-fi hum included."
  ],
  "quest.2DD56B446E130054.title": "Tip: Three Materials and Depth",
  "quest.2DD56B446E130054.quest_desc": [
    "Pick two or three main materials plus one accent and repeat them; Heliodor's own palette is tuff, calcite, quartz and waxed oxidized copper. Then add depth: windows one block back, walls framed with logs or pillars, trims, roof overhangs.",
    "",
    "A row of stairs or slabs at the base of a flat wall changes everything."
  ],
  "quest.1BD763C4EC00F8A4.title": "Tip: Roofs and Paths",
  "quest.1BD763C4EC00F8A4.quest_desc": [
    "Roofs make the silhouette: Macaw's Roofs has steep, low, attic and rounded roofs in wood, stone and terracotta, so mix two slopes on one house. Paths make the village: patterned Macaw's pavings sit well beside shovel paths.",
    "",
    "For slopes that meet the terrain smoothly, the Altar of Levelling."
  ],
  "quest.195C0B8F12D7F1C5.title": "Look at Solsticio",
  "quest.195C0B8F12D7F1C5.quest_desc": [
    "Solsticio, the city at the end of the story, is built from the same kinds of blocks you have, around a copper, glass and calcite palette. When you get there, look closely and steal ideas.",
    "",
    "Your plot there is 16 by 16, and it is yours to fill."
  ],
  "quest.3F67FB5103402B8C.title": "Pack Change: Building Is Free",
  "quest.3F67FB5103402B8C.quest_desc": [
    "No decorative block, workbench or chisel carries an act component, and no quest or Atlas project asks for a specific decorative block. Everything here is available from day one with ordinary materials.",
    "",
    "Build the house you want before the story asks anything of you."
  ],
  "quest.4A560963002F55E4.title": "A Palette in Your Hands",
  "quest.4A560963002F55E4.quest_desc": [
    "U in EMI for variants, seven Chipped benches, one chisel, the stonecutter for Macaw's and Create Deco, glass that does things and light as a material.",
    "",
    "Heliodor was all copper, glass and gardens. No pressure."
  ],
  "chapter.640F39A02855835E.title": "Furniture and Functional Decor",
  "chapter.640F39A02855835E.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Handcrafted, Another Furniture, Refurbished Furniture, kitchens, Supplementaries and Amendments: rooms that work."
  ],
  "quest.62707CA5C04CB701.title": "A House, Not a Box",
  "quest.62707CA5C04CB701.quest_desc": [
    "Three furniture sets with different jobs, two kitchen systems, and Supplementaries and Amendments, with hundreds of small blocks that actually do something.",
    "",
    "Walls make a shelter; furniture makes a home."
  ],
  "quest.01D40C5A681156DE.title": "Handcrafted: the Living Room",
  "quest.01D40C5A681156DE.quest_desc": [
    "The classic set: chairs, benches, couches, tables, desks, nightstands, cupboards, shelves, counters and fancy beds in every wood, and you can sit on the seats.",
    "",
    "Dress them with &ecushions&r and &esheets&r in sixteen colors, then finish with trims, crockery, jars and mounted trophies."
  ],
  "quest.41732879A0DB8E73.title": "Another Furniture: Cozy Details",
  "quest.41732879A0DB8E73.quest_desc": [
    "It fills the gaps: seats and tables, &eshelves&r that display, &edrawers&r that store, &ecurtains&r and &eshutters&r that open, flower boxes, lattices, awnings, lamps joined by a &elamp connector&r and a &eservice bell&r for the counter.",
    "",
    "Its &eHammer&r restyles some placed pieces."
  ],
  "quest.39FE892EFCB015B7.title": "Refurbished Furniture: Appliances",
  "quest.39FE892EFCB015B7.quest_desc": [
    "Furniture that works: fridges and freezers that store and freeze, stoves and ovens that cook, microwaves, toasters, grills, sinks, cutting boards and frying pans. Most pieces come from its own &eWorkbench&r, which needs electricity.",
    "",
    "Its kitchen recipes get their own EMI tabs."
  ],
  "quest.17776D09FC64AB58.title": "Electricity for Your Home",
  "quest.17776D09FC64AB58.quest_desc": [
    "Refurbished Furniture runs its own small grid: fuel an &eElectricity Generator&r and link it with the &eWrench&r (one node, then the other) to the workbench, lights, TV or computer.",
    "",
    "A screen that says it lacks power needs a link to a running generator. Check the cable before the fuse."
  ],
  "quest.5EA0DD3021C6C45E.title": "Mail Between Players",
  "quest.5EA0DD3021C6C45E.quest_desc": [
    "The &ePost Box&r sends packages to any &eMailbox&r: pick one from the list (search players with @), load the package slots, add a message and send.",
    "",
    "The friendliest way to share items without meeting up. The computer has a paddle-ball game, for the slow days."
  ],
  "quest.05F5E01F06961171.title": "A Kitchen That Cooks for You",
  "quest.05F5E01F06961171.quest_desc": [
    "&eCooking for Blockheads&r turns connected kitchen blocks into one kitchen, and its &eCooking Table&r lists and crafts every food the kitchen can make. The fridge, counters, spice rack and fruit basket store ingredients; the sink gives water, the oven bakes, the tool rack lends tools; milk jars and the ice unit supply milk, snow and ice."
  ],
  "quest.4602CFEDAF691E57.title": "Pantry Storage",
  "quest.4602CFEDAF691E57.quest_desc": [
    "&eStorage Delight&r adds kitchen furniture that stores: cabinets with stone countertops or glass doors, drawers and bookshelves with doors, in every wood.",
    "",
    "With a Cooking for Blockheads kitchen, you get a pantry that looks the part."
  ],
  "quest.7A6CE5FCA1EB96A0.title": "Supplementaries: Keep and Show",
  "quest.7A6CE5FCA1EB96A0.quest_desc": [
    "The &eJar&r holds and shows bowls, bottles, buckets, cookies and small mobs; the &eSack&r is a portable, heavy bag; the &eSafe&r locks to its owner or a key; the &eItem Shelf&r, &ePedestal&r and &eHat Stand&r show off items and armor; the &eNotice Board&r pins a book or map for everyone."
  ],
  "quest.2A79E25091CC60D7.title": "Supplementaries: Decoration",
  "quest.2A79E25091CC60D7.quest_desc": [
    "Flags with banner patterns, awnings and buntings on ropes, &etimber frames&r that take any full block for half-timbered walls, flower boxes, planters and doormats, sconces and stackable candle holders, &eblackboards&r you can draw on, globes and &eway signs&r that point to places.",
    "",
    "Character, one block at a time."
  ],
  "quest.460D72D9BCBC9693.title": "Supplementaries: Gadgets",
  "quest.460D72D9BCBC9693.quest_desc": [
    "The &eHourglass&r is a redstone timer filled with any sand or powder, the &eWind Vane&r reacts to weather, the &eTurn Table&r spins the block on top, the &eFaucet&r pours from jars, cauldrons and tanks, &eRope&r and &ePulley&r climb and haul, a &eLock Block&r opens only for its &eKey&r, and the Clock, Crank and Bellows feed your machinery."
  ],
  "quest.2C5C641F7EA38538.title": "Supplementaries: Carry Tools",
  "quest.2C5C641F7EA38538.quest_desc": [
    "The &eQuiver&r holds arrows and picks which to shoot (open it with the US apostrophe key), the &eSlingshot&r throws blocks and items, the &eCannon&r shoots almost anything, the &eCage&r catches small or tamed animals, &ePresents&r wrap items for a player, and the &eLunch Basket&r carries food.",
    "",
    "Yes, the cannon. Almost anything."
  ],
  "quest.3D63FBB8415A0FF7.title": "Amendments: Vanilla, Improved",
  "quest.3D63FBB8415A0FF7.quest_desc": [
    "Lanterns hang on walls and flower pots from ceilings; banners hang from ceilings and carpets lie on stairs and slabs; tools hang on tripwire hooks; skulls stack and take candles; cauldrons hold potions and mix dyes; cakes can be eaten from any side, and two stack into a double cake.",
    "",
    "Vanilla, minus the old annoyances."
  ],
  "quest.132C807FE691F1ED.title": "Quirk: Cake Bites Count",
  "quest.132C807FE691F1ED.quest_desc": [
    "A bite of an Amendments directional cake still counts for ENTRELUMEN's satiety overflow: food eaten from a block, like cake or a Farmer's Delight pie, is measured like food from your hand.",
    "",
    "How surplus food turns into buffs: the Satiety chapter."
  ],
  "quest.32DC6502B2C871AA.title": "Tip: Where You Can Sit",
  "quest.32DC6502B2C871AA.quest_desc": [
    "Handcrafted and Another Furniture chairs, benches, stools and couches seat you with an empty-hand right-click; sneak to stand up.",
    "",
    "Purely cosmetic, and exactly what co-op evenings and screenshots needed."
  ],
  "quest.655997FD290E2F74.title": "Quirk: Heavy Furniture Stays",
  "quest.655997FD290E2F74.quest_desc": [
    "Carry On refuses Cooking for Blockheads kitchen blocks, Farmer's Delight blocks and Sophisticated and Functional storage on purpose. Break and replace them, or use Packing Tape on Sophisticated chests.",
    "",
    "Plain chests, barrels and furnaces still travel."
  ],
  "quest.2BE277607ACAB07B.title": "Pack Change: One Role per Set",
  "quest.2BE277607ACAB07B.quest_desc": [
    "Each furniture set has a job: Handcrafted for classics, Refurbished Furniture for working appliances, Another Furniture for cozy details and Storage Delight for kitchen storage. Macaw's Furniture stayed out as a third palette with nothing new to do.",
    "",
    "Macaw's windows, doors, roofs and lights are in: the Blocks and Variants chapter."
  ],
  "quest.1F47E9121F669203.title": "Home, Furnished",
  "quest.1F47E9121F669203.quest_desc": [
    "A living room to sit in, a kitchen that cooks, appliances with power, jars and shelves full of things, and vanilla blocks that finally hang where you want.",
    "",
    "Now invite someone over. The Post Box is right there."
  ],
  "chapter.07F1D898223AE695.title": "Helpers in the World",
  "chapter.07F1D898223AE695.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Ultimine, Carry On, pocket villagers, elevators, lights, beds for the road and small fixes."
  ],
  "quest.325DD88D37F6C953.title": "Work Smarter Outside",
  "quest.325DD88D37F6C953.quest_desc": [
    "Inventory helpers save clicks; these save hours. Mining veins, moving chests, pocketing villagers, climbing, lighting and sleeping far from home, each with a limit the pack sets.",
    "",
    "Know the limit and nothing surprises you. Mostly."
  ],
  "quest.6F7BA1BEB737FF7F.title": "Ultimine: One Swing, One Vein",
  "quest.6F7BA1BEB737FF7F.quest_desc": [
    "Hold &eV&r and break a block: every connected block of the same kind goes with it, up to the reach of your vein resonator (&e8&r, &e16&r, &e32&r or &e64&r blocks by tier); it goes in a Curios charm slot, and without one Ultimine is off. Each extra block costs hunger and tool durability, so eat and bring a good pick; the HUD warns when you are too hungry.",
    "",
    "It respects claims and ruins."
  ],
  "quest.34D3B9788044C1CF.title": "Ultimine Shapes",
  "quest.34D3B9788044C1CF.quest_desc": [
    "With V held, &eShift&r and the wheel (or up and down) cycle shapes: &eShapeless&r follows the vein (ores, trees), &eSmall&r and &eLarge tunnel (3x3)&r dig corridors, &eSmall square (3x3)&r clears flat ground, and &eMining&r and &eEscape tunnel&r do branch mining and a staircase up.",
    "",
    "The outline shows what breaks before you swing."
  ],
  "quest.4721D87B06E32449.title": "Ultimine With Right Click",
  "quest.4721D87B06E32449.quest_desc": [
    "With V held, right-click actions multiply too: an &eaxe&r strips logs or scrapes and unwaxes copper, a &eshovel&r makes paths, a &ehoe&r tills a whole field, and on crops it harvests every ripe one in reach.",
    "",
    "Even without V, right-clicking a ripe crop harvests it."
  ],
  "quest.07E6520EC32BD592.title": "Carry On: Pick Up a Chest",
  "quest.07E6520EC32BD592.quest_desc": [
    "With an &eempty hand&r, &esneak and right-click&r a chest, furnace or barrel to lift it with everything inside, and right-click again to set it down; passive animals and villagers ride along too.",
    "",
    "You move slower, heavier blocks slow you more, and you cannot attack. Only blocks with an inventory lift."
  ],
  "quest.4A3DBA14B5939CD9.title": "What Carry On Refuses",
  "quest.4A3DBA14B5939CD9.quest_desc": [
    "A long blacklist keeps things from breaking: every ENTRELUMEN block, spawners, vaults and Lootr chests; whole mods with multiblocks or networks (Create, AE2, Refined Storage, MI, Oritech, IE, Industrial Foregoing, Powah, Functional and Sophisticated Storage, Ender Storage, Farmer's Delight, FramedBlocks, LittleTiles, Waystones); Mekanism casings and ports; Ender IO conduits; hostiles, bosses, frames and armor stands."
  ],
  "quest.706F751CEDE5DD09.title": "Quirk: Stacks, Players, Reach",
  "quest.706F751CEDE5DD09.quest_desc": [
    "Carried animals stack on top of each other, up to 10. Players can be picked up too, so behave in co-op. Pick-up distance follows your reach, so Terra's Arm stretches it as well.",
    "",
    "A tower of ten sheep is technically allowed."
  ],
  "quest.090C768610DD6B3B.title": "Villagers in Your Pocket",
  "quest.090C768610DD6B3B.quest_desc": [
    "&eEasy Villagers&r turns villagers into items: look at one and press &eAlt+O&r, then place it anywhere or inside one of its blocks: &eTrader&r (compact trading), &eFarmer&r (it grows crops), &eBreeder&r, &eIncubator&r and &eConverter&r (more villagers, grown babies, cured zombies).",
    "",
    "In a trading screen, &eC&r cycles its trades."
  ],
  "quest.5D3FA46224B03D71.title": "Pack Change: Two Blocks Wait",
  "quest.5D3FA46224B03D71.quest_desc": [
    "The &eIron Farm&r needs a Living Matrix (act II) and the &eAuto Trader&r a Handling Core (act III), each on the top of its drawing; the other Easy Villagers blocks keep their native recipes.",
    "",
    "Worth knowing later: villagers settled in Solsticio's trading hall trade cheaper forever."
  ],
  "quest.400261324AFA96E7.title": "Elevators",
  "quest.400261324AFA96E7.quest_desc": [
    "Two &eElevator&r blocks in the same column, with room to stand on each: &ejump&r to go up, &esneak&r to go down, instantly. They come in all sixteen dye colors.",
    "",
    "If one refuses to teleport, try two of the same color: the server may require it."
  ],
  "quest.078A1C5D7D7FE457.title": "Light Without Torch Spam",
  "quest.078A1C5D7D7FE457.quest_desc": [
    "The &eFeral Flare Lantern&r places invisible lights in dark areas around it, great for caves; the &eFrozen Pearl&r clears them; the &eDread Lamp&r stops bats, squid and other passive spawns nearby.",
    "",
    "The Mega Torch is gone here: the Altar of Peace does its job."
  ],
  "quest.3AE12491BA59667D.title": "Beds for the Road",
  "quest.3AE12491BA59667D.quest_desc": [
    "&eComforts&r adds the &eSleeping Bag&r, for nights far from home (it can wear out), and the &eHammock&r, hung between two &eRope and Nail&r blocks, for sleeping through the day.",
    "",
    "The server decides how many players must sleep to skip time. Somebody will always be mining."
  ],
  "quest.7FF3C0D9AEEBFA79.title": "Small Fixes You Will Notice",
  "quest.7FF3C0D9AEEBFA79.quest_desc": [
    "&eClean Swing&r hits mobs through tall grass, &eHey Berry Shut Up&r lets leggings and boots shrug off berry bushes and cactus, &eAccelerated Decay&r drops leaves fast after you fell a tree, boats hop ashore or survive lava (Jump Boat, Fireproof Boats), and &eJust Zoom&r zooms on &eZ&r."
  ],
  "quest.0BFCB9842C3F988B.title": "Tip: Test Your Damage",
  "quest.0BFCB9842C3F988B.quest_desc": [
    "A &eTarget Dummy&r shows the damage of every hit and your damage per second. Compare weapons, enchantments and Apotheosis gems before a boss, not during."
  ],
  "quest.6D0284FD17470EC0.title": "Tip: Safe Zones Come Later",
  "quest.6D0284FD17470EC0.quest_desc": [
    "A whole base free of natural hostile spawns is the &eAltar of Peace&r, an act III reward (see The Six Altars of Heliodor).",
    "",
    "Until then, light is your friend: &eF7&r shows where mobs can spawn."
  ],
  "quest.147332C8C4BF6261.title": "A Lighter World",
  "quest.147332C8C4BF6261.quest_desc": [
    "Veins in one swing, chests on your back, villagers in your pocket, elevators, lit caves and a bed anywhere.",
    "",
    "The world is just as big. It just weighs less now."
  ],
  "chapter.0F589FD1738516F7.title": "Moving Items, Fluids and Energy",
  "chapter.0F589FD1738516F7.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Pipes, filters, laser nodes, routers and cables: which one to use and how energy crosses between mods."
  ],
  "quest.6611059F058DEAC6.title": "Stop Carrying, Start Piping",
  "quest.6611059F058DEAC6.quest_desc": [
    "Sooner or later everything should flow on its own: ore to the crusher, ingots to chests, fuel to generators, power to machines. The pack's transport systems overlap on purpose, from the simplest to the most flexible.",
    "",
    "Pick the one whose style you like. Nobody is grading the spaghetti."
  ],
  "quest.4D925148310D452A.title": "Early: Hoppers and Create",
  "quest.4D925148310D452A.quest_desc": [
    "Before pipes, you already have vanilla hoppers and droppers, and Create's belts, chutes, funnels and mechanical arm, which move items with rotation and look great doing it.",
    "",
    "Create's logistics has its own chapter."
  ],
  "quest.5B9D62223F724826.title": "Fluids",
  "quest.5B9D62223F724826.quest_desc": [
    "Fluid pipes work like item pipes: Pipez fluid pipes, Mekanism mechanical pipes, Create fluid pipes driven by a mechanical pump, and Ender Storage tanks for long distances.",
    "",
    "A Fluid Trash Can at the end of a line voids the overflow."
  ],
  "quest.449E5E1DB3B1C498.title": "Rotation and Electricity",
  "quest.449E5E1DB3B1C498.quest_desc": [
    "&eCreate: Crafts and Additions&r has the &eAlternator&r (rotation to FE) and &eElectric Motor&r (FE to rotation), with wires. &eCreate: New Age&r, Heliodor's own technology, spins a &eGenerator Coil&r between magnets, collects it with carbon brushes and turns it back into rotation with motors.",
    "",
    "Its carbon brushes take an Energy Coupler (act II), and its better motors act materials."
  ],
  "quest.739B53602D9058E2.title": "Mekanism Transmitters",
  "quest.739B53602D9058E2.quest_desc": [
    "&eLogistical transporters&r for items, &emechanical pipes&r for fluids, &epressurized tubes&r for chemicals and &euniversal cables&r for energy, four tiers each; transporters can be color-coded and sorted with a &eLogistical Sorter&r.",
    "",
    "Machines pick what each face does in their &eside configuration&r tab, and &eMekanism Covers&r hide transmitters behind any block's look."
  ],
  "quest.1FB4FD3C079FE46A.title": "XNet: One Controller (Act III)",
  "quest.1FB4FD3C079FE46A.quest_desc": [
    "Connectors touch the machines, thin cables join them to a &eController&r, and its menu defines up to eight channels (item, fluid, energy or logic) with rules per connector: a whole logistics network, hidden.",
    "",
    "The controller takes a reinforced alloy, so it arrives in act III; routers need a controller anyway. Its manual is craftable."
  ],
  "quest.1CED0A985AB18B7C.title": "Integrated Tunnels",
  "quest.1CED0A985AB18B7C.quest_desc": [
    "For programmers: items, fluids and energy through Integrated Dynamics networks, with importers and exporters driven by variable cards and logic. The most flexible system here, and the slowest to learn.",
    "",
    "Its guide is the Integrated Dynamics manual, craftable from day one."
  ],
  "quest.1E0C97FDD675306D.title": "Which One Should I Use?",
  "quest.1E0C97FDD675306D.quest_desc": [
    "A few machines: &ePipez&r, extracting only where needed. A dense room: &eLaserIO&r. A big, tidy base: &eXNet&r from act III, or a storage network. Placing, breaking and odd jobs: &eModular Routers&r. A factory worth watching: &eCreate&r.",
    "",
    "Mixing is fine: most bases end up with three of them."
  ],
  "quest.2E5A18FC60DED15A.title": "Tip: Filter With Tags",
  "quest.2E5A18FC60DED15A.quest_desc": [
    "&e#c:ores&r catches every ore from every mod and &e#c:ingots&r every ingot: Pipez filters take a #tag, and LaserIO has a Tag Filter.",
    "",
    "F3+H shows an item's tags in its tooltip, and EMI searches them with #."
  ],
  "quest.2FA69EC10654DE68.title": "Quirk: a Full Chest Stops All",
  "quest.2FA69EC10654DE68.quest_desc": [
    "When the destination fills, the line backs up and the machine upstream stops. Plan for overflow: a Void upgrade in a drawer, a Trash Can at the end of the line, or a second destination further down.",
    "",
    "Every factory learns this once."
  ],
  "quest.6E189022971819C4.title": "Things Flow on Their Own",
  "quest.6E189022971819C4.quest_desc": [
    "Items, fluids and energy now move without you. The last step is a storage network that knows where everything is and crafts on request.",
    "",
    "The spaghetti is optional. The satisfaction is not."
  ],
  "chapter.3BF93B1AC8D3E2BD.title": "Performance, Sound and Screen",
  "chapter.3BF93B1AC8D3E2BD.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Settings that keep a 300-mod pack smooth, quiet when you want it and readable."
  ],
  "quest.31CFA01185FA98C4.title": "A Heavy Pack on a Normal PC",
  "quest.31CFA01185FA98C4.quest_desc": [
    "ENTRELUMEN is meant to run on ordinary PCs: it ships with rendering and memory optimizations and a cautious first profile, and leaves you room to tune.",
    "",
    "Three hundred mods, one potato-friendly start."
  ],
  "quest.572656FC02703CC9.title": "What Is Already Optimized",
  "quest.572656FC02703CC9.quest_desc": [
    "Already in: &eSodium&r (a faster renderer with its own video pages), &eImmediatelyFast&r (text, items and HUD), &eModernFix&r and &eFerriteCore&r (loading and memory), &eAllTheLeaks&r (leak fixes for long sessions) and &eAI Improvements&r (lighter mob thinking on the server).",
    "",
    "Another optimizer on top usually brings conflicts, not frames."
  ],
  "quest.375C479FC614F2AE.title": "The First Profile",
  "quest.375C479FC614F2AE.quest_desc": [
    "A new profile starts at render distance &e10&r, simulation &e6&r, a &e120 FPS&r cap without VSync, fast graphics, no clouds, fewer particles, no entity shadows, entity distance 75%, darkness and screen effects at half, GUI scale 3.",
    "",
    "A safe start, not a rule: raise render distance first, since simulation distance costs the server far more."
  ],
  "quest.5D3F2F532595406E.title": "Sodium's Video Settings",
  "quest.5D3F2F532595406E.quest_desc": [
    "Options, Video Settings opens Sodium's pages (General, Quality, Performance, Advanced) plus pages other mods add. Hover any option to read what it does and what it costs.",
    "",
    "On a weak PC: lower render distance, keep particles decreased and leave the performance options alone."
  ],
  "quest.5F9D459224CCEDBF.title": "Dynamic Lights",
  "quest.5F9D459224CCEDBF.quest_desc": [
    "&eLambDynamicLights&r makes held torches, lanterns and glowing items light your surroundings, and lights up burning or glowing entities. Its page sits in Sodium's video settings, where you can lower it or turn it off.",
    "",
    "Solsticio's luminous gear shines with it too. Obviously."
  ],
  "quest.39B57F7649021B1E.title": "Silence the Factory",
  "quest.39B57F7649021B1E.quest_desc": [
    "&eExtreme Sound Muffler&r adds a &eMuffler&r button to your inventory that lists nearby sounds: lower or mute any, for the whole world or only inside an &eanchor&r area around your machines. Right-drag the button if it covers something.",
    "",
    "Leave combat sounds on. They are the ones that keep you alive."
  ],
  "quest.689260C1B854A07B.title": "Fewer Pop-ups",
  "quest.689260C1B854A07B.quest_desc": [
    "&eToast Control&r handles the top-right notifications: recipe unlocks, advancements and tutorial hints. &eF10&r clears the ones on screen, and its settings block whole kinds.",
    "",
    "You miss nothing important: quests and the Atlas speak in their own screens and in chat."
  ],
  "quest.3E474B9B801F50F6.title": "A HUD That Scales",
  "quest.3E474B9B801F50F6.quest_desc": [
    "Health and armor grow far past vanilla here: Spice of Life adds hearts for food variety and late armor passes 20. &eColorful Hearts&r stacks extra hearts in colored rows and &eOverloaded Armor Bar&r does the same for armor, so the HUD never swallows the screen.",
    "",
    "&eNot Enough Animations&r adds eating and map animations; purely cosmetic."
  ],
  "quest.187F30877B47077A.title": "Protect Your Save",
  "quest.187F30877B47077A.quest_desc": [
    "&eCherished Worlds&r lets you mark a world as a favorite: it stays at the top of the list and resists accidental deletion. &eSimple Backups&r makes automatic ZIP copies and announces them in chat.",
    "",
    "Restore a backup only with the game or server closed. Future you will thank you."
  ],
  "quest.29E494460AEDC6F2.title": "Solsticio's Motes of Light",
  "quest.29E494460AEDC6F2.quest_desc": [
    "The drifting motes in Solsticio are client-side and follow your particle setting: halved on Decreased, gone on Minimal.",
    "",
    "Finer controls live in the ENTRELUMEN client config; the Solsticio chapter has them."
  ],
  "quest.00C6A92105A1B302.title": "Tip: Find the Lag",
  "quest.00C6A92105A1B302.quest_desc": [
    "When the game or server stutters, &espark&r says why: an operator runs &e/spark profiler&r, reproduces the lag and stops it to see which mod or machine eats the time; &e/spark tps&r shows server ticks per second.",
    "",
    "Check the obvious first: item piles, giant farms in loaded chunks, too many force-loaded chunks."
  ],
  "quest.53171C9A7C748B49.title": "Tip: The Floor Is Not Storage",
  "quest.53171C9A7C748B49.quest_desc": [
    "Every dropped item is an entity the server must tick, and farms that spill their output are the classic cause of lag. Collect with hoppers, Item Collectors or machine outputs, void overflow with a Trash Can, and let Clumps merge experience orbs."
  ],
  "quest.44DC2092AA284411.title": "Pack Menus and Loading Screen",
  "quest.44DC2092AA284411.quest_desc": [
    "FancyMenu and Drippy Loading Screen dress up the title and loading screens without touching your settings.",
    "",
    "At a very high GUI scale a button may fall off screen: drop the scale to 3 or 2."
  ],
  "quest.4CEFDFA59AAE55AB.title": "Quirk: GUI Scale and Big Screens",
  "quest.4CEFDFA59AAE55AB.quest_desc": [
    "Many modded screens are wider than vanilla ones (the Atlas is 300 by 210 GUI units), so at a high GUI scale in a small window they may not fit.",
    "",
    "If a screen looks cut off, lower the GUI scale in Options, Video Settings."
  ],
  "quest.02071930B3199174.title": "Smooth and Quiet",
  "quest.02071930B3199174.quest_desc": [
    "Play the way your PC likes: the story never needs a jetpack, a huge render distance or chunk-loading.",
    "",
    "A quiet factory is a happy factory. Or at least a muffled one."
  ],
  "chapter.2AEF3B16A131D400.title": "Teams and Claims",
  "chapter.2AEF3B16A131D400.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Play together with FTB Teams, protect your land with FTB Chunks, and know what the team shares."
  ],
  "quest.3C597B86B27930E7.title": "Solo First, Better Together",
  "quest.3C597B86B27930E7.quest_desc": [
    "Everything can be done alone. With friends, the campaign, the compass and the World Tier become shared, so you can split branches: one cooks, one builds machines, one explores.",
    "",
    "Someone always ends up doing the paperwork. Usually the one with the Atlas."
  ],
  "quest.58EAC9E8C5071663.title": "Create a Party",
  "quest.58EAC9E8C5071663.quest_desc": [
    "The &eMy Team&r button on the side of your inventory creates and names a party and invites online players, who accept from their own My Team screen or the chat message.",
    "",
    "Without a party you are still a team: a team of one."
  ],
  "quest.27E62163ED06BC7B.title": "What the Team Shares",
  "quest.27E62163ED06BC7B.quest_desc": [
    "Atlas projects, acts and milestones are shared and any member can deliver; the compass points everyone to the same objective; the World Tier follows the team's progress; and in Solsticio the team claims one plot.",
    "",
    "Items are not shared: each keeps their own inventory, and a reward goes to whoever delivered."
  ],
  "quest.68A95699EF8E40F9.title": "Joining and Leaving",
  "quest.68A95699EF8E40F9.quest_desc": [
    "Creating a party copies the founder's campaign once. Joining someone else's does not merge histories: you play theirs while your personal campaign waits, and leaving brings you back to it. When the last owner leaves, the party's campaign is archived; an operator can restore it with &e/entrelumen admin recover&r.",
    "",
    "Your World Tier never drops on the way out."
  ],
  "quest.28A8E9C9DECB15C7.title": "Allies",
  "quest.28A8E9C9DECB15C7.quest_desc": [
    "My Team can mark other teams as &eallies&r, who may interact with your claimed land as your settings allow, without joining your campaign.",
    "",
    "Alliances for the neighbors, parties for the people playing your story."
  ],
  "quest.7455FFA73D0FEC2E.title": "Claim Your Land",
  "quest.7455FFA73D0FEC2E.quest_desc": [
    "&eK&r opens the claim manager: &eleft-drag&r claims, &eright-drag&r unclaims, &eTab&r hides the grid and &eAlt&r shows when each claim was made. Claimed chunks keep other teams from breaking, placing or opening containers unless you allow it.",
    "",
    "Up to 500 chunks per player by default. Nobody needs 500. Somebody will try."
  ],
  "quest.0B2F97229BEF1DE1.title": "Keep Machines Running",
  "quest.0B2F97229BEF1DE1.quest_desc": [
    "In the claim manager, &eShift+left-drag&r force-loads claimed chunks so machines keep working while you are away, and &eShift+right-drag&r stops it; the mouse wheel sets when it expires. Default limit: 25 per player.",
    "",
    "Whether they stay loaded with nobody online is a server setting. Force-load only what needs it: every chunk costs server time."
  ],
  "quest.038A595B1B7200A4.title": "Team Protection Settings",
  "quest.038A595B1B7200A4.quest_desc": [
    "My Team also sets whether explosions and mobs can damage your land, who sees your claims on the map, and which fake players (machines that act as players, like Create deployers or block breakers) count as friends.",
    "",
    "If a machine suddenly refuses to work, check the fake player setting first."
  ],
  "quest.21F833844C0F26B6.title": "Quirk: Two Maps, One Visible",
  "quest.21F833844C0F26B6.quest_desc": [
    "FTB Chunks' minimap is off and its map key unbound, so JourneyMap is the map you see; FTB Chunks only handles teams and claims (&eK&r or the inventory side button).",
    "",
    "Prefer the FTB minimap? Your personal config file can turn it back on."
  ],
  "quest.79A1D0DB3C8F0B51.title": "Claims Stop Altars Too",
  "quest.79A1D0DB3C8F0B51.quest_desc": [
    "Land-shaping altars act as their owner, so another team's Altar of Renewal or Levelling skips your claimed chunks and charges nothing for them. The same goes for Ultimine and other tools wielded by outsiders.",
    "",
    "Good fences make good neighbors, even magical ones."
  ],
  "quest.27B135D314100B6A.title": "Tip: Split the Branches",
  "quest.27B135D314100B6A.quest_desc": [
    "Each act asks for several Atlas projects at once, each from a different discipline, so a team of three can take one each: engineering, nature and logistics in act III, for example.",
    "",
    "A delivery counts for the whole team the moment anyone makes it, so no need to pass items around first."
  ],
  "quest.47FFD44331256607.title": "Co-op Comforts",
  "quest.47FFD44331256607.quest_desc": [
    "&eChat Heads&r puts each player's face beside their messages, &eBetter Ping Display&r turns the Tab list bars into milliseconds, and &eNo Chat Reports&r strips signed-report data from server chat.",
    "",
    "None changes the game; they just make a shared server easier to read."
  ],
  "quest.20AD0D6306A80B83.title": "Quirk: Loot Is Per Player",
  "quest.20AD0D6306A80B83.quest_desc": [
    "&eLootr&r gives every player their own loot from dungeon and structure chests, so opening first steals nothing and exploring a ruin together is fine.",
    "",
    "A Lootr chest you already opened looks different from a fresh one."
  ],
  "quest.469B35F5128965CF.title": "Gifts Help, Progress Stays",
  "quest.469B35F5128965CF.quest_desc": [
    "Hand another team anything, even a finished prototype, and they can deliver it to their own Atlas. Progress cannot be gifted: arrivals, boss milestones and completed projects stay with the campaign that earned them.",
    "",
    "The Heart of Heliodor only counts for the team whose member took it from the Sun Spirit."
  ],
  "quest.1923090E6BED7E18.title": "Tip: a Team Frequency",
  "quest.1923090E6BED7E18.quest_desc": [
    "From act III, &eEnder Storage&r shares contents between every chest, tank and pouch with the same three colors, across dimensions. Pick a team code, keep a supply chest at home and give each explorer a pouch.",
    "",
    "How it works: the Storage chapter."
  ],
  "quest.17B1C1BCA708F7EB.title": "A Team With a Home",
  "quest.17B1C1BCA708F7EB.quest_desc": [
    "Party created, land claimed, machines loaded, allies set. From here, the story moves at the speed of the whole team.",
    "",
    "Which means at the speed of whoever is still sorting their inventory."
  ],
  "chapter.212218BAD3D67D30.title": "Resource Farming: Fishing",
  "chapter.212218BAD3D67D30.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Aquaculture: rods, hooks, fillets and treasure from the water."
  ],
  "quest.0B5BD3D3F3ED95E0.title": "Fish That Pay",
  "quest.0B5BD3D3F3ED95E0.quest_desc": [
    "Aquaculture fishes up metal, treasure and fillets: dozens of fish by biome, better rods, hooks and bait. Slow to start, endless once running, and the travel food the Atlas asks for in act II comes from here.",
    "",
    "Productive Bees has two chapters of its own; Mystical Agriculture too."
  ],
  "quest.25D22601D4E688AC.title": "Aquaculture: Better Fishing",
  "quest.25D22601D4E688AC.quest_desc": [
    "Dozens of biome fish, better rods (iron, gold, diamond, neptunium), hooks, bait like worms, lines and bobbers, a &eTackle Box&r for gear and a &eFillet Knife&r for fillets.",
    "",
    "It also fishes up treasure: &eNeptune's Bounty&r chests hold neptunium, a metal for underwater gear."
  ],
  "quest.203022B5C269A142.title": "The Tackle Box",
  "quest.203022B5C269A142.quest_desc": [
    "Five iron, an iron block, a chest and two green dyes make a &eTackle Box&r: it stores the fishing gear, and a rod set in it takes a hook, a line, a bobber and bait."
  ],
  "quest.3F5323236DF4A223.title": "Hooks",
  "quest.3F5323236DF4A223.quest_desc": [
    "Four iron nuggets make an &eIron Hook&r, which saves durability one cast in five, and two iron hooks make a &eDouble Hook&r that can land two catches at once. Gold and glowstone hooks add luck; redstone ones give you longer to reel in."
  ],
  "quest.1412E509E7C564FE.title": "The Fillet Knife",
  "quest.1412E509E7C564FE.quest_desc": [
    "Two iron ingots and a stick make an &eIron Fillet Knife&r. A fish and the knife on a crafting grid become raw fillets, and the neptunium knife cuts more of them."
  ],
  "quest.3DFCD4210E1E9F9A.title": "Fillets for the Story",
  "quest.3DFCD4210E1E9F9A.quest_desc": [
    "Two vegetable soups and two cooked Aquaculture fillets make the first &eTravel Rations&r, the travel food the Atlas asks for in act II.",
    "",
    "A &eWorm Farm&r keeps the bait coming."
  ],
  "quest.3D392448BE3407E3.title": "Neptunium Gear",
  "quest.3D392448BE3407E3.quest_desc": [
    "Built for underwater: the rod gets faster bites, the helmet clearer vision, the chestplate breath, the leggings weightlessness and the boots speed; the pickaxe and shovel lose no speed underwater, and the hoe keeps farmland moist.",
    "",
    "Ocean monuments will not know what hit them."
  ],
  "quest.3D28CDAE58037BFE.title": "Endless Supplies",
  "quest.3D28CDAE58037BFE.quest_desc": [
    "A fishing line that pays in treasure, fillets for the road and neptunium for the deep.",
    "",
    "Somewhere, a fish is swimming toward your hook right now."
  ],
  "chapter.5F5C5CDA9C2B7B1E.title": "Storage Networks: AE2 or Refined Storage",
  "chapter.5F5C5CDA9C2B7B1E.chapter_subtitle": [
    "One terminal for everything you own: how the two networks differ, where the pack gates them, and how to start."
  ],
  "quest.20934DE77061EA1E.title": "A Terminal That Knows Everything",
  "quest.20934DE77061EA1E.quest_desc": [
    "A storage network turns items into data: insert once, then search, count, pull and autocraft from one terminal. The pack offers &eApplied Energistics 2&r and &eRefined Storage&r side by side, both complete; pick one per base.",
    "",
    "The tech guides go deeper into autocrafting."
  ],
  "quest.40255AEA7E3FBC84.title": "AE2 or RS?",
  "quest.40255AEA7E3FBC84.quest_desc": [
    "&eAE2&r is deeper and more rewarding: cables carry limited &echannels&r (8 per normal cable, 32 per dense), so layout matters, and the pack has lots of add-ons for it. &eRefined Storage&r is simpler: no channels, just connect and power, faster to set up.",
    "",
    "Both store items, fluids and, with Mekanism add-ons, chemicals, and both craft on request."
  ],
  "quest.4D7E5DE146382857.title": "Pack Change: When Each Opens",
  "quest.4D7E5DE146382857.quest_desc": [
    "Both networks enter in act III: the Refined Storage &eController&r takes a &eRouting Matrix&r and its &eAutocrafter&r a &eHandling Core&r, while AE2 needs its inscriber's &eLogic Processors&r, the same ones the Routing Matrix is made from.",
    "",
    "The AE2 controller carries a Routing Matrix too, but a small AE2 network without a controller can start a little earlier."
  ],
  "quest.0D69E2FB61D264F7.title": "AE2 Step 1: a Meteorite",
  "quest.0D69E2FB61D264F7.quest_desc": [
    "AE2 starts in a crater: meteorites hold a &eMysterious Cube&r with the four &einscriber presses&r (calculation, engineering, logic, silicon) and sky stone. Presses plus an &eInscriber&r print processors.",
    "",
    "Certus quartz grows from budding certus; charge it in a &eCharger&r and drop it with redstone and nether quartz in water for fluix."
  ],
  "quest.793454F581FA5AB2.title": "AE2 Step 2: a First Network",
  "quest.793454F581FA5AB2.quest_desc": [
    "An &eME Drive&r with a &e1k storage cell&r, a &eterminal&r and power from an energy acceptor or a controller. Without a controller the network handles up to 8 channel devices; with a &eController&r and cables it grows far beyond.",
    "",
    "Your first terminal is the moment the chests start feeling old."
  ],
  "quest.26E80B5A5FA63E3D.title": "Tip: AE2 Has Its Own Guide",
  "quest.26E80B5A5FA63E3D.quest_desc": [
    "AE2 ships an in-game guide with pictures and 3D scenes of every block: craft the &eGuide&r, or bind &eOpen Guide for Items&r in Controls to jump from any AE2 item to its page.",
    "",
    "Read it once; it saves ten forum threads."
  ],
  "quest.5BE6F260A3E327EA.title": "AE2 Add-ons in the Pack",
  "quest.5BE6F260A3E327EA.quest_desc": [
    "&eMEGA Cells&r (much bigger cells), &eExtendedAE&r and &eAdvancedAE&r (better providers, interfaces and crafting), &eApplied Mekanistics&r (chemicals), &eAE2WTLib&r (a wireless universal terminal), &eME Requester&r (keeps chosen items in stock), &eAE2 Network Analyzer&r (see channels and cables) and &eArsEng&r (Ars Nouveau source on the network)."
  ],
  "quest.48E6E7A9BC97530B.title": "RS: a First Network",
  "quest.48E6E7A9BC97530B.quest_desc": [
    "A powered &eController&r, a &eDisk Drive&r with a storage disk and a &eGrid&r or &eCrafting Grid&r, joined by cables or touching. No channels: add as many devices as you like.",
    "",
    "The controller takes a Routing Matrix here, so RS starts in act III."
  ],
  "quest.7F33B19BDC69D950.title": "RS: Growing the Network",
  "quest.7F33B19BDC69D950.quest_desc": [
    "&eImporter&r and &eExporter&r move items in and out of machines, &eConstructor&r and &eDestructor&r place and break blocks, the &eDetector&r emits redstone by amount, a &eWireless Transmitter&r serves a wireless grid, &eNetwork Transmitter&r and &eReceiver&r link distant parts, and the &eAutocrafter&r runs &ePattern Grid&r patterns.",
    "",
    "RS Mekanism Integration adds chemicals."
  ],
  "quest.7E760A5EA79B9C7C.title": "Keep Your Drawers",
  "quest.7E760A5EA79B9C7C.quest_desc": [
    "No need to empty your chests: AE2's &eStorage Bus&r and RS's &eExternal Storage&r read any inventory they face, drawers and storage controllers included, and the terminal shows those items too.",
    "",
    "The drawer wall joins the network without moving a single cobblestone."
  ],
  "quest.3C697DA1AB61BAA2.title": "Autocrafting in One Paragraph",
  "quest.3C697DA1AB61BAA2.quest_desc": [
    "Encode a recipe into a &epattern&r, give the network somewhere to run it (an AE2 pattern provider with a molecular assembler or a machine, or an RS autocrafter) plus a crafting CPU in AE2, then ask the terminal for 64 of anything: it crafts the intermediate steps too.",
    "",
    "Act components are ordinary shaped recipes, so they autocraft like anything else."
  ],
  "quest.2A2C0CF0B5664397.title": "Quirk: Both Can Coexist",
  "quest.2A2C0CF0B5664397.quest_desc": [
    "AE2 in one base and Refined Storage in another is fine, but they do not share storage directly: bridge them through an inventory both can read, like a drawer or chest.",
    "",
    "For one team, one network is almost always easier."
  ],
  "quest.574E671F47BF610A.title": "Tip: Channels Without Tears",
  "quest.574E671F47BF610A.quest_desc": [
    "Each AE2 device uses one channel; normal cables carry 8, dense ones 32, and each controller face feeds 32. Run dense cable as the backbone and branch with normal cable.",
    "",
    "A powered device that stops working probably ran out of channels. The Network Analyzer shows where."
  ],
  "quest.1AE56B10894D452F.title": "The Network Feeds the Story",
  "quest.1AE56B10894D452F.quest_desc": [
    "Several act components are made from network parts: the Routing Matrix from logic processors and a circuit board, the Habitation Charter from a calculation processor, the Inventory Sensor from LaserIO logic chips.",
    "",
    "A network that autocrafts processors makes acts III and V much lighter."
  ],
  "quest.1EE0CB511BEDE3D0.title": "Everything in One Place",
  "quest.1EE0CB511BEDE3D0.quest_desc": [
    "With a network, the whole base is one searchable inventory, and logistics becomes feeding machines instead of finding items.",
    "",
    "You will never again lose a stack of iron in chest number forty."
  ],
  "chapter.7BF8A0F5CDAED7CF.title": "Create · Kinetics",
  "chapter.7BF8A0F5CDAED7CF.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Rotation does the work: from a water wheel to a wall of crafters."
  ],
  "quest.36D2DD9AC13B9B6B.title": "Andesite Alloy",
  "quest.36D2DD9AC13B9B6B.quest_subtitle": "Create's duct tape.",
  "quest.36D2DD9AC13B9B6B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Checkerboard \"},{\"text\":\"andesite\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:andesite\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and \"},{\"text\":\"iron nuggets\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:iron_nugget\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in a 2×2 grid for one alloy. Shafts, casings, belts and half the early machines start here.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Later a \"},{\"text\":\"Mechanical Mixer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:mechanical_mixer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" makes it from one of each: half price.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2BAB95C4EE0C4C28.title": "Ponder it",
  "quest.2BAB95C4EE0C4C28.quest_subtitle": "The manual that moves.",
  "quest.2BAB95C4EE0C4C28.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Hover any Create block and hold \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.ponder.ponder\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\": an animated scene shows how it works, step by step. The addons have scenes too.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0DFA49B47F44AFC1.title": "Shafts and cogs",
  "quest.0DFA49B47F44AFC1.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two alloys stacked make eight \"},{\"text\":\"Shafts\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:shaft\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; a shaft and a plank make a \"},{\"text\":\"Cogwheel\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:cogwheel\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Shafts carry rotation straight, cogs pass it to their neighbours, each turning the other way.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Machine running backwards? Add or remove one cog.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.292FAA46D06198DB.title": "Shifting gears",
  "quest.292FAA46D06198DB.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Mesh a \"},{\"text\":\"Large Cogwheel\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:large_cogwheel\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" diagonally with a small one: big to small doubles the speed, small to big halves it.\"}]",
    "",
    "Faster machines eat more stress, so speed up only what needs it."
  ],
  "quest.06677D656B930724.title": "Elbow grease",
  "quest.06677D656B930724.quest_subtitle": "The first engine is you.",
  "quest.06677D656B930724.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three planks and an alloy make a \"},{\"text\":\"Hand Crank\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:hand_crank\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Hold right-click on it and the machine on the other end turns, for as long as your arm lasts.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7B2185253A34244F.title": "Let the river work",
  "quest.7B2185253A34244F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight planks around a \"},{\"text\":\"Shaft\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:shaft\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It spins in flowing water: a river, a waterfall, a short stream. More water on more sides adds nothing; more wheels do.\"}]",
    "",
    "Any plank reskins it. Free, steady, silent power."
  ],
  "quest.2EAA71F49CB4FDAC.title": "Bigger, slower, stronger",
  "quest.2EAA71F49CB4FDAC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Planks around a \"},{\"text\":\"Water Wheel\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:water_wheel\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make the large one: half the speed, much more stress capacity. A large-to-small cog step wins the speed back.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3FBE996BD4292871.title": "Where the water isn't",
  "quest.3FBE996BD4292871.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Windmill Bearing\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:windmill_bearing\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" spins a glued structure with at least 8 sail blocks; sails stick without glue. Right-click it to start or stop. More sails, more speed.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6B9320A212975341.title": "Hot wheels",
  "quest.6B9320A212975341.quest_subtitle": "This shouldn't have worked.",
  "quest.6B9320A212975341.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Lava turns a \"},{\"text\":\"Water Wheel\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:water_wheel\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" too. Nobody in Heliodor wrote that down, and there was a reason.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.55DD3FA18A257CC5.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.32437B2EDDAA6C80.title": "Dress the wood",
  "quest.32437B2EDDAA6C80.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Right-click stripped logs or wood with \"},{\"text\":\"Andesite Alloy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:andesite_alloy\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Press, mixer, fan, millstone, drill, saw, bearing and gearbox all wear it.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Deployer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:deployer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" applies it for you later.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.192801180FAC4131.title": "Round the corner",
  "quest.192801180FAC4131.quest_subtitle": "Cleaner than cog spaghetti.",
  "quest.192801180FAC4131.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four cogs around an \"},{\"text\":\"Andesite Casing\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:andesite_casing\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": one block that turns rotation round corners. Side outputs mirror each other; the straight-through side runs reversed.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.52292575E3352219.title": "Flat out",
  "quest.52292575E3352219.quest_subtitle": "Ingots in, pancakes out.",
  "quest.52292575E3352219.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Mechanical Press\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:mechanical_press\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" flattens what sits below it: an item on the ground, on a \"},{\"text\":\"Depot\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:depot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" or riding a belt. Ingots come out as sheets.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Over a \"},{\"text\":\"Basin\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:basin\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" it compacts instead: 2×2 and 3×3 recipes, no hands.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2324180555060EA4.title": "Belts",
  "quest.2324180555060EA4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Six dried kelp make a \"},{\"text\":\"Mechanical Belt\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:belt_connector\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Click two shafts to link them, 2 to 20 blocks apart, even on a slope. Belts carry items and mobs, and machines above work on what rides past.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3D9C0C0B645B0ABC.title": "In and out",
  "quest.3D9C0C0B645B0ABC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Placed normally, an \"},{\"text\":\"Andesite Funnel\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:andesite_funnel\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" pulls from an inventory; placed while sneaking, it pushes into it. A \"},{\"text\":\"Depot\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:depot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" is a one-slot belt for machines and arms.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Funnels can't join two chests directly: put a chute or a belt between them.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7FEAA44F45D5393B.title": "Down the chute",
  "quest.7FEAA44F45D5393B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Chutes\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:chute\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" drop items straight down between inventories. An \"},{\"text\":\"Encased Fan\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:encased_fan\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" at one end sends them up instead.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.58F59827A9B35689.title": "The big box",
  "quest.58F59827A9B35689.quest_subtitle": "No peeking.",
  "quest.58F59827A9B35689.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Item Vaults\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:item_vault\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" merge up to 3 wide and hold a lot, but no hand opens them: funnels, chutes and arms do. The perfect buffer between machines.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.197D3E006CBF3A20.title": "Read the strain",
  "quest.197D3E006CBF3A20.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Engineer's Goggles\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:goggles\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" show every machine's stress; a \"},{\"text\":\"Wrench\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:wrench\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" turns parts and, sneaking, picks them up whole. The goggles need a golden sheet: the press makes it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.774F011ABDD83F74.title": "Stress is the budget",
  "quest.774F011ABDD83F74.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Sources add \"},{\"text\":\"stress capacity\",\"color\":\"#D8C8FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_text\",\"contents\":\"Counted in su (stress units). Engineer's Goggles show it.\"}},{\"text\":\"; machines spend it, more the faster they spin. \"},{\"text\":\"Overspend\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\" and the whole network stops. The fix: more sources, slower machines, or two networks.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5D15941A9CF83546.title": "Wireless, the old way",
  "quest.5D15941A9CF83546.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two items in its slots set a \"},{\"text\":\"Redstone Link\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:redstone_link\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"'s frequency; links with the same pair talk across \"},{\"text\":\"256 blocks\",\"color\":\"#E5A16A\"},{\"text\":\". Sneak-click swaps sender and receiver.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A link driving a \"},{\"text\":\"Clutch\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:clutch\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" is the tidiest remote off switch.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.14D03D7EA54ADFD0.title": "Stir it up",
  "quest.14D03D7EA54ADFD0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Mechanical Mixer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:mechanical_mixer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" over a \"},{\"text\":\"Basin\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:basin\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" runs shapeless recipes and Create mixing: alloys, dough, liquids. Results leave by the basin's outlet into an inventory below or beside.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Two recipes match? A filter on the mixer picks one.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1DC4E2140C4FC88C.title": "Hot air",
  "quest.1DC4E2140C4FC88C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An \"},{\"text\":\"Encased Fan\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:encased_fan\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" pushes or pulls air by its spin, dragging items and mobs along. A catalyst block in the stream processes whatever flies through.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.77B5FE48A4FA129E.title": "Catalysts",
  "quest.77B5FE48A4FA129E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Lava or a lit \"},{\"translate\":\"block.create.blaze_burner\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\"},{\"text\":\" in the stream smelts, fire smokes, water washes, soul fire haunts. Food in lava burns: smoke it instead. Fan speed changes the reach, not the time.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.49913C7985EE46B8.title": "Grind, slowly",
  "quest.49913C7985EE46B8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Millstone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:millstone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" fed from the top grinds gravel into flint, wheat into flour, flowers into dye. Slow and cheap; crushing wheels do it better later.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.175083F5E8E666B3.title": "Fire in a cage",
  "quest.175083F5E8E666B3.quest_subtitle": "Blaze, meet your new job.",
  "quest.175083F5E8E666B3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Iron sheets and netherrack make an empty \"},{\"text\":\"Blaze Burner\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:blaze_burner\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; right-click a Blaze or its spawner to fill it. Fed fuel, it heats the basin above; fed a \"},{\"text\":\"Blaze Cake\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:blaze_cake\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", it superheats.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.28659381D2A10DC1.title": "Pipes and pumps",
  "quest.28659381D2A10DC1.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Copper on stripped wood gives \"},{\"text\":\"Copper Casing\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:copper_casing\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". A cog on a \"},{\"text\":\"Fluid Pipe\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:fluid_pipe\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" makes a \"},{\"text\":\"Mechanical Pump\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:mechanical_pump\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": its arrow, not the rotation, sets which way the fluid goes.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3DBB3FB6F656AA03.title": "Tanks",
  "quest.3DBB3FB6F656AA03.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Fluid Tanks\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:fluid_tank\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" merge up to 3×3 wide and over 30 tall; a comparator reads the level. Hands can't pour into them: use a basin, a spout or an item drain.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Hose Pulley\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:hose_pulley\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in a big enough lake pumps forever.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.76BB178286CE5FED.title": "Full steam",
  "quest.76BB178286CE5FED.quest_subtitle": "The whistle is optional. Mostly.",
  "quest.76BB178286CE5FED.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Steam Engines\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:steam_engine\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on a tank, burners below and water piped in: a boiler. Each boiler level runs one more engine at full power; the goggles say what's missing.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.504F53D3F800ED8B.title": "Pipe dream",
  "quest.504F53D3F800ED8B.quest_subtitle": "The neighbours have opinions.",
  "quest.504F53D3F800ED8B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Twelve \"},{\"text\":\"Steam Whistles\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:steam_whistle\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", twelve pitches, one tank. Heliodor's copper had a sound; now yours does too.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.137B52306D96A3F3.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.26297EDEF72560DF.title": "Down to brass tacks",
  "quest.26297EDEF72560DF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"One copper and one \"},{\"text\":\"Zinc Ingot\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:zinc_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in a heated basin give two \"},{\"text\":\"Brass Ingots\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:brass_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Zinc ore spawns in the Overworld.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Brass opens the second age: smart logistics, deployers, arms, crafters and the \"},{\"text\":\"addons\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"2FD24C6ADC23649E\"}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.40B30AC5E7D15961.title": "Pink and polished",
  "quest.40B30AC5E7D15961.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"One quartz and eight redstone make \"},{\"text\":\"Rose Quartz\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:rose_quartz\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Polish it with \"},{\"text\":\"Sand Paper\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:sand_paper\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in your hand and the quartz in the other, or leave it to a deployer.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.411293F478ED352C.title": "The brass jacket",
  "quest.411293F478ED352C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Brass Ingot\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:brass_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on stripped wood: the body of every smart machine. Crafters, arms, tunnels and the speed controller all wear it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.21FEAE578271FEFD.title": "Picky funnels",
  "quest.21FEAE578271FEFD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Brass Funnel\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:brass_funnel\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" moves whole stacks, exact amounts and only what its filter lets through. A \"},{\"text\":\"Brass Tunnel\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:brass_tunnel\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on a belt filters each side: blocks what comes in, sorts what goes out.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2D7CF472187B0DCC.title": "Tunnel modes",
  "quest.2D7CF472187B0DCC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Tunnels on side-by-side belts join up. Split spreads a stack evenly, Round Robin cycles whole stacks, Prefer Nearest favours the closest exit, Synchronize waits for every belt.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.25D97F2683BD89CD.title": "Filters with taste",
  "quest.25D97F2683BD89CD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"List Filter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:filter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" matches a set of items; an \"},{\"text\":\"Attribute Filter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:attribute_filter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" matches a property, like 'can be smelted' or a tag. Either fits any Create filter slot.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3D18D702CE0F07CE.title": "Stop when full",
  "quest.3D18D702CE0F07CE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Threshold Switch\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:stockpile_switch\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" turns on above one fill level and off below another. Wire it to a clutch and the machine rests when the chest is full.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3469F859B3B7AB74.title": "Brains in a bulb",
  "quest.3469F859B3B7AB74.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Polished Rose Quartz\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:polished_rose_quartz\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on an \"},{\"text\":\"Iron Sheet\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:iron_sheet\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Every smart block carries one: funnels, tunnels, deployers, crafters, observers. Make a handful; they go fast.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6DCD494665B52E7A.title": "Signs of life",
  "quest.6DCD494665B52E7A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Display Link\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:display_link\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" reads a source (stock, boiler, stress, train arrivals) and writes it on a \"},{\"text\":\"Display Board\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:display_board\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a sign or nixie tubes. Click the display first, then place the link on the source.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7DA2CEAEEF72E8D0.title": "Launch, precisely",
  "quest.7DA2CEAEEF72E8D0.quest_subtitle": "Yeeting, but polite.",
  "quest.7DA2CEAEEF72E8D0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Sneak-click to aim a \"},{\"text\":\"Weighted Ejector\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:weighted_ejector\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", then place it. Anything set on it flies to the target: items, mobs, you. Aimed at an inventory, it waits for room.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.66A1273DEB5E3931.title": "A second pair of hands",
  "quest.66A1273DEB5E3931.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Deployer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:deployer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" is a mechanical you: it places, uses, harvests and hits two blocks ahead. With an item in hand, it works on whatever sits below on a depot or belt.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.45749A42F9EAE9F2.title": "Assembly, in order",
  "quest.45749A42F9EAE9F2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Some parts are built in steps: the base becomes an unfinished item that passes a list of machines a set number of times. A belt looping back to its start runs it hands-free.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3BA376D13AB65787.title": "One swing only",
  "quest.3BA376D13AB65787.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"With a filter, a deployer only acts while holding the matching item. Redstone stops it after the current swing, so a short pulse gives exactly one use.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.748EE5CD50175AA3.title": "Pound it",
  "quest.748EE5CD50175AA3.quest_subtitle": "Solidarity among machines.",
  "quest.748EE5CD50175AA3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two \"},{\"text\":\"Deployers\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:deployer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" face to face, both punching. Somewhere a union is forming.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.4595F147678799D6.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.2EC497FEE0F48D91.title": "Precision work",
  "quest.2EC497FEE0F48D91.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Golden Sheet\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:golden_sheet\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" from the \"},{\"text\":\"press\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"52292575E3352219\"}},{\"text\":\", then five loops of deployers adding a cogwheel, a large cogwheel and an iron nugget. About four runs in five end as a \"},{\"text\":\"Precision Mechanism\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:precision_mechanism\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; the rest is scrap.\"}]",
    "",
    "Arms, speed controllers and train controls need it. So do two act components."
  ],
  "quest.1900C15D452488A4.title": "Cruise control",
  "quest.1900C15D452488A4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Brass casing and a precision mechanism: a \"},{\"text\":\"Rotation Speed Controller\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:rotation_speed_controller\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" drives a large cog on top at the exact speed on its panel. Run a line at what the recipe needs, not a notch more.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.10FBE1404F8230D8.title": "Pick and place",
  "quest.10FBE1404F8230D8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Before placing a \"},{\"text\":\"Mechanical Arm\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:mechanical_arm\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", click its targets with it in hand: blue takes, click again for yellow, which gives. Then it shuttles items between any number of them.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.55DA919A83044D72.title": "Arm etiquette",
  "quest.55DA919A83044D72.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"With several outputs: Round Robin cycles, Forced Round Robin waits for each, Prefer First fills the first. Feeding blaze burners is the classic first job.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.109581D1AA0DA93E.title": "Kitchen shift",
  "quest.109581D1AA0DA93E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"With Central Kitchen, Create runs Farmer's Delight pots, stoves and feasts. The \"},{\"text\":\"Slicer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sliceanddice:slicer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" does the knife work. Dinner, automated.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.03BDE2ED061B5940.title": "DJ Arm",
  "quest.03BDE2ED061B5940.quest_subtitle": "Requests not accepted.",
  "quest.03BDE2ED061B5940.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Mechanical Arm\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:mechanical_arm\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" working a jukebox. It has one song and it loves it.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.445533AD3AEB408F.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.5E11DCB2FA716F05.title": "Crafting, industrialised",
  "quest.5E11DCB2FA716F05.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A tube, a brass casing and a crafting table make three \"},{\"text\":\"Mechanical Crafters\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:mechanical_crafter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". In a grid they craft any recipe, 5×5 ones included. Wrench their arrows so every path ends at one exit.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7E52D88B6EC82066.title": "Fill 'er up",
  "quest.7E52D88B6EC82066.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A pipe-fed \"},{\"text\":\"Spout\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:spout\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" fills what sits below: buckets, bottles, potions, honey. An \"},{\"text\":\"Item Drain\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:item_drain\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" does the opposite.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Spout lava onto \"},{\"text\":\"Powdered Obsidian\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:powdered_obsidian\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and press it twice: \"},{\"text\":\"Sturdy Sheets\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:sturdy_sheet\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", where \"},{\"text\":\"trains\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"06C76EF421D48687\"}},{\"text\":\" begin.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.44862012259D890D.title": "Cake for the blaze",
  "quest.44862012259D890D.quest_subtitle": "The cake is not a lie.",
  "quest.44862012259D890D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Compact egg, sugar and \"},{\"text\":\"Cinder Flour\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:cinder_flour\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" into a base; a spout fills it with 250 mB of lava. A burner fed a \"},{\"text\":\"Blaze Cake\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:blaze_cake\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" superheats, and some recipes demand it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1CAAE66B26E73138.title": "Alloy run",
  "quest.1CAAE66B26E73138.quest_subtitle": "Same time tomorrow?",
  "quest.1CAAE66B26E73138.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Thirty-two \"},{\"text\":\"Andesite Alloy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:andesite_alloy\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for the common store, once a day. A mixer on a belt makes this a coffee break.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.188EC2F2CE68070A.title": "The big grind",
  "quest.188EC2F2CE68070A.quest_subtitle": "It takes twenty-five crafters.",
  "quest.188EC2F2CE68070A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A 5×5 mechanical recipe of \"},{\"text\":\"Andesite Alloy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:andesite_alloy\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", planks and stone makes a pair of \"},{\"text\":\"Crushing Wheels\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:crushing_wheel\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Side by side, spinning into each other, they chew whatever falls on top.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "{image:entrelumen:textures/gui/quests/diagram_crushing.png width:96 height:48 align:center}",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Raw ore comes out crushed, with bonus nuggets and a chance of XP. Netherrack becomes \"},{\"text\":\"Cinder Flour\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:cinder_flour\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Faster wheels, faster grind.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.41BF50CEC2C30E7E.title": "Ore arithmetic",
  "quest.41BF50CEC2C30E7E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"One raw iron, one crushed iron, plus 75% of an XP nugget. Smelt it for an ingot, or wash it with a fan for nine nuggets and a chance of redstone. Silk-touched ore crushes into more.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3D3DA4463A800E10.title": "Crushing it",
  "quest.3D3DA4463A800E10.quest_subtitle": "Somewhere, a mountain flinched.",
  "quest.3D3DA4463A800E10.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Crushing Wheels\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:crushing_wheel\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" at maximum speed. The stress bill is someone else's problem, right?\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.39F4127F304A766F.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.746839F1A3A4F3E8.title": "A note in the margin",
  "quest.746839F1A3A4F3E8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two wheels, one purpose: whatever falls between them comes out useful. We built a whole city on that idea. —T.\",\"italic\":true}]"
  ],
  "quest.2BCA4E743126A82D.title": "Creative parts",
  "quest.2BCA4E743126A82D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Creative Motor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:creative_motor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", tank and blaze cake cost two Luminosities each, from Solsticio in act VI. The Creative Crate can't be crafted. Real power runs on water, wind and steam.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.580233BFC09F3DB6.title": "Air on tap",
  "quest.580233BFC09F3DB6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Copper, a copper block, alloy and a shaft make a \"},{\"text\":\"Copper Backtank\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:copper_backtank\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Set it on a spinning shaft and it fills with air, faster the faster it spins; worn on your back, it feeds that air to Create's equipment.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"It holds 900 air by default, and each level of the Capacity enchantment adds 300.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7B6FA9536DD302E1.title": "Deep breath",
  "quest.7B6FA9536DD302E1.quest_subtitle": "Glub.",
  "quest.7B6FA9536DD302E1.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Copper around a glass block makes a \"},{\"text\":\"Copper Diving Helmet\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:copper_diving_helmet\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": with the backtank on, you breathe underwater while the air lasts. \"},{\"text\":\"Copper Diving Boots\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:copper_diving_boots\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" sink you fast and let you walk and jump on the seabed.\"}]",
    "",
    "With those boots on, belts don't carry you off either."
  ],
  "quest.7C90B6B91D100029.title": "Swim with the striders",
  "quest.7C90B6B91D100029.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"At a smithing table, netherite upgrades turn the copper set into a \"},{\"text\":\"Netherite Diving Helmet\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:netherite_diving_helmet\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", \"},{\"text\":\"Netherite Backtank\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:netherite_backtank\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and \"},{\"text\":\"Netherite Diving Boots\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:netherite_diving_boots\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". With netherite leggings as well, fire and lava can't touch you while the air lasts.\"}]",
    "",
    "The helmet also lets you see inside lava."
  ],
  "quest.05AA974586D4598C.title": "Drink the lake",
  "quest.05AA974586D4598C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A copper casing, a dried kelp block and a copper sheet make a \"},{\"text\":\"Hose Pulley\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:hose_pulley\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Turned one way it lowers its hose, the other way it reels it in; pipes on its far side feed it to fill a pool, or pull from it to drain one.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"In a big enough ocean or lava lake it never runs dry and never changes the source. How fast it moves fluid depends only on the pipes.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.586B4F391CD54421.title": "A longer arm",
  "quest.586B4F391CD54421.quest_subtitle": "Boioioing.",
  "quest.586B4F391CD54421.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Mechanical crafters build it from a \"},{\"text\":\"Brass Hand\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:brass_hand\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a precision mechanism, brass and sticks. In the off-hand, the \"},{\"text\":\"Extendo Grip\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:extendo_grip\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" gives your main hand 3 more blocks of reach.\"}]",
    "",
    "With a backtank on, it spends air instead of durability."
  ],
  "quest.16C5898A367F6101.title": "Both hands",
  "quest.16C5898A367F6101.quest_subtitle": "The top shelf is no longer safe.",
  "quest.16C5898A367F6101.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An \"},{\"text\":\"Extendo Grip\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:extendo_grip\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in each hand: 5 extra blocks of reach. Cookie jars everywhere, beware.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.4CE0F61439CFB2E7.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.1B9743748D07B4F4.title": "Hot potato",
  "quest.1B9743748D07B4F4.quest_subtitle": "Fwoomp.",
  "quest.1B9743748D07B4F4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Potato Cannon\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:potato_cannon\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" fires food from your inventory, each kind its own way: potatoes knock back hard, carrots and potatoes plant themselves where they land, and a golden apple cures a zombie villager.\"}]",
    "",
    "With a backtank on, it spends air instead of durability."
  ],
  "quest.0A05E93762155161.title": "Food fight",
  "quest.0A05E93762155161.quest_subtitle": "Nobody wins. Everyone's hungry.",
  "quest.0A05E93762155161.quest_desc": [
    "Two different vegetables, fired into each other in midair. It was never about the aim."
  ],
  "reward.6B05F217F9BF73FB.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.40ADDA07025F7B71.title": "Mirror, mirror",
  "quest.40ADDA07025F7B71.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Build one side and get the other free. Anywhere in your hotbar, a \"},{\"text\":\"Wand Of Symmetry\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:wand_of_symmetry\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" mirrors every block you place; use it on a surface to set or move the mirror, and sneak while using it to pick the kind of mirror.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.05E72338D4DA667D.title": "Any toolbox",
  "quest.7F3A78A2696CD6DA.title": "A place for every tool",
  "quest.7F3A78A2696CD6DA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A cogwheel, two golden sheets, a chest and leather make a \"},{\"text\":\"Toolbox\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:brown_toolbox\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", and dye recolors it. It holds 8 kinds of items, up to 4 stacks of each, and keeps them when you pick it up.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Within 10 blocks, hold \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"create.keyinfo.toolbelt\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" to take a tool straight out of it; the same menu puts it back.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5AD77CC119527E20.title": "Copy, paste",
  "quest.5AD77CC119527E20.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Alloy, paper and planks make a \"},{\"text\":\"Clipboard\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:clipboard\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for notes and checklists; sneak-click to hang it on a wall. Right-click a block with it to copy its settings, like a filter, and left-click another block to paste them.\"}]",
    "",
    "A schematicannon prints a schematic's list of materials onto it."
  ],
  "quest.61D286FCE52F9734.title": "Save a building",
  "quest.61D286FCE52F9734.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Paper and light blue dye make an \"},{\"text\":\"Empty Schematic\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:empty_schematic\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; add a feather for a \"},{\"text\":\"Schematic And Quill\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:schematic_and_quill\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Right-click two corners, stretch the faces with \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"create.keyinfo.ctrl_modifier\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" and the scroll wheel, then right-click again to save it to a file.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.70E9C61DD9F565CC.title": "From file to paper",
  "quest.70E9C61DD9F565CC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Wooden slabs on smooth stone make a \"},{\"text\":\"Schematic Table\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:schematic_table\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Put an empty schematic in and pick a file from your schematics folder: out comes a \"},{\"text\":\"Schematic\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:schematic\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a hologram to move, turn and mirror before you set it in place.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2F29287CA2D3B1E5.title": "Print it",
  "quest.2F29287CA2D3B1E5.quest_subtitle": "Aim at the plan, not the neighbours.",
  "quest.2F29287CA2D3B1E5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Schematicannon\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:schematicannon\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" builds a positioned schematic block by block from the chests next to it. Gunpowder is its fuel: one piece fires 400 blocks by default.\"}]",
    "",
    "Its settings choose what it may replace, and a clipboard or a book in its printer slot gets the list of missing materials."
  ],
  "quest.7546418F3079CEC6.title": "Recipes on the wall",
  "quest.7546418F3079CEC6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A painting and a crafting table make a \"},{\"text\":\"Crafting Blueprint\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:crafting_blueprint\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Hang it up and set a recipe in each slot; right-click a slot to craft it from what you carry, sneaking for a whole stack.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4A0BFFF481476506.title": "Tea break",
  "quest.4A0BFFF481476506.quest_subtitle": "Motivating. Also filling.",
  "quest.4A0BFFF481476506.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Leaves, water and milk in a heated mixer brew tea, and a spout pours 250 mB into a glass bottle. \"},{\"text\":\"Builder's Tea\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:builders_tea\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" gives three minutes of Haste and goes down even on a full stomach.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.06545029F3897532.title": "Sweet tooth",
  "quest.06545029F3897532.quest_subtitle": "A balanced diet, technically.",
  "quest.06545029F3897532.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Sugar, cocoa and milk in a heated mixer melt into chocolate. Then, from one spout: chocolate on sweet berries, honey on an apple, milk on bread. \"},{\"text\":\"Chocolate Glazed Berries\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:chocolate_glazed_berries\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a \"},{\"text\":\"Honeyed Apple\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:honeyed_apple\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a \"},{\"text\":\"Sweet Roll\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:sweet_roll\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A press over a basin compacts chocolate into a \"},{\"text\":\"Bar of Chocolate\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:bar_of_chocolate\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4910DBA213EDF501.title": "Is it time?",
  "quest.4910DBA213EDF501.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Planks, an andesite casing and a clock make a \"},{\"text\":\"Cuckoo Clock\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:cuckoo_clock\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Give it rotation and it shows the time, and its bird sings twice a day: at noon, and at dusk once you can sleep.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Gunpowder around one makes a clock that looks the same and ends its song with a bang.\",\"color\":\"#FF8C7A\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.50DFA9AA910E93C3.title": "Ring for trouble",
  "quest.50DFA9AA910E93C3.quest_subtitle": "It hears the dark.",
  "quest.50DFA9AA910E93C3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A block of brass on a brass sheet makes a \"},{\"text\":\"Peculiar Bell\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:peculiar_bell\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Set it over soul fire, or haunt it with a fan, and it wakes up as a \"},{\"text\":\"Haunted Bell\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:haunted_bell\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": held or rung, it shows the dark spots where monsters can spawn.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.7968684ACFC2A3DE.title": "Zinc from the ground",
  "quest.51319C53C1B7B9D7.title": "Where the zinc is",
  "quest.51319C53C1B7B9D7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Zinc veins of up to a dozen blocks run through the Overworld from the deepslate up to height 70. Smelt the \"},{\"text\":\"Raw Zinc\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:raw_zinc\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", or crush it first: a crushed zinc and a chance of XP each, and washed with a fan, nine nuggets and sometimes gunpowder.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.1BF037F5B63180E7.title": "Sixteen of Create's stones",
  "quest.75FCF0FB22AFD634.title": "Stone with a streak",
  "quest.75FCF0FB22AFD634.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Striped layers underground hide Create's stones: \"},{\"text\":\"Asurine\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:asurine\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", \"},{\"text\":\"Crimsite\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:crimsite\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", \"},{\"text\":\"Ochrum\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:ochrum\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", \"},{\"text\":\"Veridium\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:veridium\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and \"},{\"text\":\"Limestone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:limestone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Crushed, the colored ones give bits of zinc, iron, gold or copper.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Nether's layers bring \"},{\"text\":\"Scoria\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:scoria\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and \"},{\"text\":\"Scorchia\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:scorchia\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Each stone comes cut, polished, as bricks or as a pillar at the stonecutter.\"}]"
  ],
  "image.333B0EF01F70DBD7.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Belts and funnels\",\"color\":\"#E5A16A\"}]",
  "image.26C61E15ED438248.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Pipes and steam\",\"color\":\"#E5A16A\"}]",
  "image.775CB44E2374A97A.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Smart logistics\",\"color\":\"#E5A16A\"}]",
  "image.1D924884A06E32F4.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Diving gear\",\"color\":\"#E5A16A\"}]",
  "image.1D04815C6D24EAA9.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Treats\",\"color\":\"#E5A16A\"}]",
  "image.3F089C5EEF3B0E04.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Tools of the trade\",\"color\":\"#E5A16A\"}]",
  "image.1156AFC07E896ECD.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Schematics\",\"color\":\"#E5A16A\"}]",
  "image.71D536B654B4F464.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Zinc and stone\",\"color\":\"#E5A16A\"}]",
  "image.2A653D76CA25CD0C.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Create · Kinetics\",\"color\":\"#E5A16A\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.1FE0475DAAB53FD5.title": "Back to the Sun of Heliodor",
  "chapter.5A7AEEAF7E51A9E7.title": "Create · Contraptions",
  "chapter.5A7AEEAF7E51A9E7.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Glue it, move it, put it to work: machines that go where the work is."
  ],
  "quest.576CE9D64BAE34C7.title": "Things that move",
  "quest.576CE9D64BAE34C7.quest_subtitle": "Every contraption starts with a turn.",
  "quest.576CE9D64BAE34C7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Mechanical Bearing\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:mechanical_bearing\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" grabs the block in front of it and everything stuck to that block. Spin the bearing and the lot turns as one; stop it and it settles back into blocks.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Built something in front of a bearing that is already spinning? Right-click the bearing with an empty hand to take it aboard.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.01CEFE6A056B4953.title": "Stick together",
  "quest.01CEFE6A056B4953.quest_subtitle": "Not for mending vases.",
  "quest.01CEFE6A056B4953.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two slimeballs, an iron sheet and an iron nugget make \"},{\"text\":\"Super Glue\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:super_glue\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Click two corners to glue a box: the blocks inside hold on to each other and move as one. Punch a box with the glue in hand to take it off.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0BAB084884161BB3.title": "In a straight line",
  "quest.0BAB084884161BB3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Mechanical Piston\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:mechanical_piston\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" slides the structure in front of it as far as the \"},{\"text\":\"Piston Extension Poles\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:piston_extension_pole\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" behind it allow. Rotation sets the speed and which way it goes.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"No poles, no movement. The default limit is 64 poles.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.76212786ECF9AAA2.title": "Drill and saw",
  "quest.76212786ECF9AAA2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Standing still, a \"},{\"text\":\"Mechanical Drill\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:mechanical_drill\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" breaks the block in front and a \"},{\"text\":\"Mechanical Saw\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:mechanical_saw\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" fells a whole tree from its bottom log. On a moving contraption, both work every block they pass.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A saw facing up cuts one alloy into six shafts. Crafting gives four.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.573C0C430FF452E0.title": "Put it to work",
  "quest.573C0C430FF452E0.quest_desc": [
    "Build a structure with drills, saws or harvesters aboard and set it moving. What they break goes into the chests, barrels or vaults glued to it; with nowhere to go, it drops.",
    "",
    "A piston full of drills bores a tunnel; a bearing full of saws clears a grove."
  ],
  "quest.207B6029DE60C862.title": "Unload on the fly",
  "quest.207B6029DE60C862.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An andesite casing and a chute make a \"},{\"text\":\"Portable Storage Interface\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:portable_storage_interface\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". One rides on the structure, another stands still one or two blocks away; when they meet, the still one acts as every inventory aboard, for funnels and chutes to fill or empty.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "The structure waits while items move and sets off once they stop. Redstone on the still interface keeps it from connecting."
  ],
  "quest.0DDEA08A35DA640B.title": "On rails",
  "quest.0DDEA08A35DA640B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Cart Assembler\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:cart_assembler\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" sits on a rail. Powered, it mounts the structure attached to it on the next minecart that passes; unpowered, it turns passing cart structures back into blocks.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A wrench on the minecart picks up the whole thing as one item, to set down on other rails.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.438DF3D8ABD46C10.title": "A cart that paves its way",
  "quest.438DF3D8ABD46C10.quest_subtitle": "It lays the track it runs on.",
  "quest.438DF3D8ABD46C10.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Build a minecart structure with a \"},{\"text\":\"Deployer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:deployer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" aimed at the ground ahead and rails in a chest aboard. As it rolls, the deployer lays the next rail and the cart keeps going.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "A furnace minecart feeds itself from the chests aboard, and couplings add room. The same idea paves roads with a roller, or builds a whole schematic from a deployer's filter."
  ],
  "quest.3AD62FB30D7F2FFC.title": "Telling time",
  "quest.3AD62FB30D7F2FFC.quest_subtitle": "The hands are yours to build.",
  "quest.3AD62FB30D7F2FFC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A slab, a brass casing and an electron tube make a \"},{\"text\":\"Clockwork Bearing\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:clockwork_bearing\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": it turns its structure with the time of day, an hour hand. Build a second structure in front of it, not glued to the first, and that one becomes the minute hand.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Right-click to start or stop it. Its panel swaps which hand goes first, or makes a 24-hour dial."
  ],
  "quest.75F7746CA473FDC0.title": "Stay or settle",
  "quest.75F7746CA473FDC0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A stopped bearing sets its blocks down at the nearest right angle; pistons and pulleys, wherever they stop. Each one's panel can keep the structure assembled at rest instead, or set it down only back at the start.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.58A9E1C9958DE307.title": "Keep it level",
  "quest.58A9E1C9958DE307.quest_subtitle": "Ferris wheel rules.",
  "quest.58A9E1C9958DE307.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A bearing that rides on another moving structure keeps itself upright, and so does whatever hangs from it. Cabins on a big wheel stay level all the way round.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.55805B91CE320A6F.title": "Sail cloth",
  "quest.55805B91CE320A6F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Any structure with at least 8 sail blocks on a \"},{\"text\":\"Windmill Bearing\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:windmill_bearing\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" is a windmill. \"},{\"text\":\"Windmill Sails\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:white_sail\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and their frames attach without glue; wool counts as sail too, glued like any block. Every 8 sails add 1 RPM, up to 16.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Dye paints a sail and shears turn it back into a \"},{\"text\":\"Windmill Sail Frame\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:sail_frame\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Frames let a fan's air through.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.471C1E864A869416.title": "Gale force",
  "quest.471C1E864A869416.quest_subtitle": "Hold on to your hat.",
  "quest.471C1E864A869416.quest_desc": [
    "A windmill at full strength: 128 sails, 16 RPM. Somewhere, a kite is green with envy."
  ],
  "reward.261432547F7E92BB.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.7A14A705869A2D7D.title": "How big can it get",
  "quest.7A14A705869A2D7D.quest_desc": [
    "Create's defaults, which this pack keeps: up to 2048 blocks per structure, chassis reach 16, 64 piston poles, 384 blocks of rope and 12 blocks of roller fill. Bigger than that, build two."
  ],
  "quest.0001FA03256BDB03.title": "Sticky sides",
  "quest.0001FA03256BDB03.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Logs and alloy make three \"},{\"text\":\"Linear Chassis\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:linear_chassis\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Right-click an open face with a slimeball and that face picks up the line of blocks in front of it, up to 16 long; the wrench sets the exact reach.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Chassis of the same kind on the same axis link up and travel together. A \"},{\"text\":\"Secondary Linear Chassis\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:secondary_linear_chassis\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" won't join the plain ones: two groups side by side.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0DEACFC34FFB0AB6.title": "Grab and let go",
  "quest.0DEACFC34FFB0AB6.quest_subtitle": "A claw machine you actually win.",
  "quest.0DEACFC34FFB0AB6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Sticker\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:sticker\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" flips with each redstone signal: on, it holds the block in front and takes it along when the structure moves; flipped again, it lets go. Cranes and block movers start here.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4092A16E02C683AD.title": "In the round",
  "quest.4092A16E02C683AD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Radial Chassis\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:radial_chassis\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" with a slimed side grabs every block it can reach on that layer, within a radius set with the wrench. Stack a column of them on one bearing and a whole wheel turns.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.50B48C71EAEBF893.title": "When glue isn't needed",
  "quest.50B48C71EAEBF893.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Blocks that hang on others, like torches or ladders, come along without glue. Overlapping glue boxes move together, and so do blocks sharing one box.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0F73152348B2F958.title": "Bring it back",
  "quest.0F73152348B2F958.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A slimeball on a piston makes a \"},{\"text\":\"Sticky Mechanical Piston\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:sticky_mechanical_piston\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". The plain one only pushes; the sticky one also pulls its structure back when the rotation reverses. Doors, bridges and lifts that come home.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.69E8A1D1A706CF85.title": "Straight down",
  "quest.69E8A1D1A706CF85.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Rope Pulley\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:rope_pulley\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" lowers the structure beneath it on a rope and hauls it back up; rotation sets the speed and the way. Up to 384 blocks of rope by default.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Other pulleys on the same layer hook onto the load, only for looks. A pulley carried by another structure drags its load along, but it can only be moved while it's stopped."
  ],
  "quest.28EEE016DEAF098C.title": "Going up",
  "quest.28EEE016DEAF098C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An \"},{\"text\":\"Elevator Pulley\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:elevator_pulley\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" moves a cabin between floors. Glue a \"},{\"text\":\"Redstone Contact\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:redstone_contact\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" to the cabin facing a fixed one, give the pulley rotation and right-click it to assemble.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Every fixed contact in that column becomes an \"},{\"text\":\"Elevator Contact\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:elevator_contact\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": a floor. A redstone pulse there calls the cabin; right-click the pulley again to turn the cabin back into blocks.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.55A135C42438CD85.title": "All the way down",
  "quest.55A135C42438CD85.quest_subtitle": "Is it still going?",
  "quest.55A135C42438CD85.quest_desc": [
    "Over 200 blocks of rope, and the bottom is still out of sight. Tie a note to the end for whoever finds it."
  ],
  "reward.15613D29B64A2A3B.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.1F36AA47D9A7ADB7.title": "Ding, third floor",
  "quest.1F36AA47D9A7ADB7.quest_subtitle": "Mind the doors.",
  "quest.1F36AA47D9A7ADB7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Name each floor in its contact. \"},{\"text\":\"Contraption Controls\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:contraption_controls\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in the cabin pick a floor from inside, sliding doors on board open on arrival and a \"},{\"text\":\"Desk Bell\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:desk_bell\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" rings when it gets there.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Each contact gives a signal while the cabin is at its floor, and a display link on one shows the current floor."
  ],
  "quest.21B27FABDE1FB23F.title": "Along the rack",
  "quest.21B27FABDE1FB23F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two alloys and a redstone make eight \"},{\"text\":\"Gantry Shafts\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:gantry_shaft\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; a \"},{\"text\":\"Gantry Carriage\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:gantry_carriage\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" mounts on them and carries its structure along. Spin the shaft and the carriage slides; the shaft's facing and the spin decide which way.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Power a shaft with redstone and its carriages stop, while the spin passes on to the shaft sticking out of each carriage."
  ],
  "quest.094AAFE60FF3FF14.title": "Gantries on gantries",
  "quest.094AAFE60FF3FF14.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A gantry shaft sticks to a carriage without glue, and a carriage rides its shaft even while that shaft is being moved. Stack them and one machine covers two or three axes: a crane, a quarry, a 3D printer.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2F49B4B21B3181B3.title": "Harvest on the move",
  "quest.2F49B4B21B3181B3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"On a moving structure, a \"},{\"text\":\"Mechanical Harvester\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:mechanical_harvester\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" reaps every ripe crop it passes and plants it again. Unripe crops are left alone.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2998B1ADE612ACCA.title": "Plough through",
  "quest.2998B1ADE612ACCA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A moving \"},{\"text\":\"Mechanical Plough\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:mechanical_plough\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" breaks whatever has no solid hitbox, like grass, flowers or torches, and tills dirt into farmland. Mobs in its way get launched, unhurt.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.43881B22666000B8.title": "Heavy delivery",
  "quest.43881B22666000B8.quest_subtitle": "Return to sender.",
  "quest.43881B22666000B8.quest_desc": [
    "A plough launches anvils too. Please aim away from the workshop."
  ],
  "reward.3827429B4948B776.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.36EA364D9557CAC2.title": "Farms that walk",
  "quest.36EA364D9557CAC2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Harvesters on a sticky piston that sweeps a field back and forth make a crop farm. For wood, saws on the move and \"},{\"text\":\"Tree Fertilizer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:tree_fertilizer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", which grows a tree even where there's no room for one.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2FC39C5CD9FD451E.title": "Paving the way",
  "quest.2FC39C5CD9FD451E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An electron tube, an andesite casing and a \"},{\"text\":\"Crushing Wheel\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:crushing_wheel\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make a \"},{\"text\":\"Mechanical Roller\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:mechanical_roller\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". With no material set it clears like a drill; give it a paving block, stocked in a chest aboard, and it replaces the layer below as it goes.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Its fill modes lay columns or slopes down to the ground, up to 12 deep, without breaking anything. Blocks a roller breaks may drop nothing."
  ],
  "quest.353FA4651917FE89.title": "Hands on the move",
  "quest.353FA4651917FE89.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A deployer on a moving structure acts at every block it passes, with items from any inventory aboard; its filter picks which. Put a positioned schematic in that filter and it builds the schematic as it goes.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5799D2801D01D95F.title": "Off switch",
  "quest.5799D2801D01D95F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Actors on a moving structure are always on. A button, an andesite casing and an electron tube make \"},{\"text\":\"Contraption Controls\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:contraption_controls\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", which toggle them on the fly from anywhere aboard. Set the filter before assembling to target one kind; powered as it assembles, that kind starts off.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.29F99EA50E783C52.title": "Any seat",
  "quest.65B5F49A8836E99B.title": "Take a seat",
  "quest.65B5F49A8836E99B.quest_subtitle": "Please keep your arms inside.",
  "quest.65B5F49A8836E99B.quest_desc": [
    "Wool and a wooden slab make a seat, and dye recolors it. Sit on one aboard a moving structure and you ride along; a mob that steps on one sits down and travels too, hostile ones included."
  ],
  "quest.7C4834A1821EC308.title": "Tanks on the go",
  "quest.7C4834A1821EC308.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Pipes can't reach tanks on a moving structure. A copper casing and a chute make a \"},{\"text\":\"Portable Fluid Interface\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:portable_fluid_interface\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": pair two, one or two blocks apart, and the still one stands in for every tank aboard.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.65D996B03A1616D6.title": "Remote control",
  "quest.65D996B03A1616D6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Redstone Link\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:redstone_link\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" ringed by six wooden buttons makes a \"},{\"text\":\"Linked Controller\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:linked_controller\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Right-click a receiving link with it, then press one of its six controls: that key now sends the link's frequency.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Right-click to take it in hand and your movement keys work its buttons instead of you. On a lectern it stays put and handy; sneak-click the lectern to take it back."
  ],
  "quest.6716BFBE3A5D99A5.title": "Couple them up",
  "quest.6716BFBE3A5D99A5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two alloys and an iron sheet make a \"},{\"text\":\"Minecart Coupling\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:minecart_coupling\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Link two carts and they move as a group: two couplings per cart at most, and no loops. Two cart assemblers sharing one structure build a two-cart carriage by themselves.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.0AC36AFE0D1E0DB2.title": "Any cart contraption",
  "quest.34848088A476953B.title": "Take it with you",
  "quest.34848088A476953B.quest_desc": [
    "Right-click a cart structure with a wrench and it leaves the rails as one item, blocks and all. Set it on any rail and it's ready to roll. It won't fit in a shulker box."
  ],
  "quest.4B33D50EB9E7D80C.title": "Pocket freight",
  "quest.4B33D50EB9E7D80C.quest_subtitle": "Lift with your legs.",
  "quest.4B33D50EB9E7D80C.quest_desc": [
    "Two hundred blocks of cart structure, in one hand. Your back will file a complaint in the morning."
  ],
  "reward.24C95D07138C72CF.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.37C23B93C9A55DE4.title": "Speed by signal",
  "quest.37C23B93C9A55DE4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Gold, a stick and an electron tube make six \"},{\"text\":\"Controller Rails\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:controller_rail\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": one-way powered rails that push as hard as the signal is strong. On one, a cart assembler holds the cart until the rail gets power.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.00BE273C9D78F2F0.title": "Which cart, which rail",
  "quest.00BE273C9D78F2F0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"On a plain rail the assembler leaves the cart's speed alone. Chest and furnace minecarts work as the base too, and a furnace one refuels itself from the inventories aboard. The assembler's panel locks the structure's facing, or turns it to follow the track.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3213AB1221B63BCA.title": "Drill order",
  "quest.3213AB1221B63BCA.quest_subtitle": "The mines never have enough.",
  "quest.3213AB1221B63BCA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four \"},{\"text\":\"Mechanical Drills\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:mechanical_drill\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for the common store, once a day. Tunnel crews always want spares.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.50D13918BA1C6BA7.title": "A note under the seat",
  "quest.50D13918BA1C6BA7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A cart that lays its own track needs nobody to build it a road. I meant it for the farm villages the rails never reached. —T.\",\"italic\":true}]"
  ],
  "image.268C9DA32366AE30.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Bearings\",\"color\":\"#E5A16A\"}]",
  "image.1E88BD9EFDD7DE4D.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Wind\",\"color\":\"#E5A16A\"}]",
  "image.3FEE3E641B80B6E0.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Glue and chassis\",\"color\":\"#E5A16A\"}]",
  "image.506DB80141CC904B.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Pistons and pulleys\",\"color\":\"#E5A16A\"}]",
  "image.0E4909ADA9F4A1D9.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Gantries\",\"color\":\"#E5A16A\"}]",
  "image.64B468A2650BB2A7.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Actors\",\"color\":\"#E5A16A\"}]",
  "image.2068E1E10BA96AD0.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"On board\",\"color\":\"#E5A16A\"}]",
  "image.4CEF45B8E8F16612.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Create · Contraptions\",\"color\":\"#E5A16A\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.4DC7C375E076A7C0.title": "Back to Create · Kinetics",
  "image.60E5C419E5F04BA4.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Minecart contraptions\",\"color\":\"#E5A16A\"}]",
  "chapter.2F36751BF3F95B59.title": "Create · Logic and Measurement",
  "chapter.2F36751BF3F95B59.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Signals you can dial, time, sense and read: the redstone side of Create."
  ],
  "quest.1851633B4F209673.title": "Fifteen notches",
  "quest.1851633B4F209673.quest_subtitle": "On, off and thirteen opinions in between.",
  "quest.1851633B4F209673.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A stick on \"},{\"text\":\"Andesite Casing\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:andesite_casing\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" makes an \"},{\"text\":\"Analog Lever\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:analog_lever\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Right-click raises its signal one step, sneak-right-click lowers it, anywhere from 0 to 15: a small, exact source for anything that reads strength.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Wire it to a \"},{\"text\":\"Controller Rail\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:controller_rail\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and minecarts run at the speed the lever says.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2DA7E1E9651BF4E8.title": "Needle and dial",
  "quest.2DA7E1E9651BF4E8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A compass on Andesite Casing makes a \"},{\"text\":\"Speedometer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:speedometer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", which shows the speed of whatever it is attached to. Wear goggles for the exact RPM; a comparator beside it turns that speed into a redstone signal.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1EA34274E57B45C7.title": "How close to the edge",
  "quest.1EA34274E57B45C7.quest_subtitle": "Numbers beat hunches.",
  "quest.1EA34274E57B45C7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Stressometer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:stressometer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" has no recipe of its own: a Speedometer alone in the crafting grid turns into one, and back. It shows how much of the network's stress capacity is in use; look at it with goggles on for the exact figure.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.64C8E0BCACFBE515.title": "Keeping time",
  "quest.64C8E0BCACFBE515.quest_subtitle": "Tick, tock, pulse.",
  "quest.64C8E0BCACFBE515.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Amethyst, a brass sheet and a redstone torch on stone make a \"},{\"text\":\"Pulse Timer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:pulse_timer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": a clock that sends a short pulse at every interval you set, from two ticks to an hour. A signal on its input side pauses and resets it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0A6A4F2F26F37ACB.title": "Eyes on the line",
  "quest.0A6A4F2F26F37ACB.quest_subtitle": "It notices. It always notices.",
  "quest.0A6A4F2F26F37ACB.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An electron tube, brass casing and an observer make a \"},{\"text\":\"Smart Observer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:content_observer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It sees items and fluids in containers, on belts, in chutes and pipes, pulses when a funnel moves something, and its filter picks what counts.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5099FD5BADFB7520.title": "Put it on the wall",
  "quest.5099FD5BADFB7520.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Click a display, then place a \"},{\"text\":\"Display Link\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:display_link\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on the block to read. Its screen picks what to send: a stressometer gives stress in su or as a bar, a speedometer its RPM, a vault its fill level.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.44DFBA5862256DEC.title": "Flip the letters",
  "quest.44DFBA5862256DEC.quest_subtitle": "Clack-clack-clack.",
  "quest.44DFBA5862256DEC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An electron tube between two andesite alloys makes two \"},{\"text\":\"Display Boards\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:display_board\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; side by side they grow into one big board, which needs rotation to flip. A written clipboard sets fixed text, a display link live text, and dye colours a line.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.256353C7F43F2E01.title": "Motion by script",
  "quest.256353C7F43F2E01.quest_subtitle": "Turn 90°. Wait. Turn back. Repeat.",
  "quest.256353C7F43F2E01.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Brass casing, a cogwheel and an electron tube make a \"},{\"text\":\"Sequenced Gearshift\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:sequenced_gearshift\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". A redstone signal runs its list: turn by an angle, move a piston, pulley or gantry a set distance, wait, or await the next pulse. A comparator reads its progress.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Create: Connected adds three steps: Loop, Sustain (turn until a new pulse) and Time (turn for a set time).\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.285F341D83DF1895.title": "Exact RPM",
  "quest.285F341D83DF1895.quest_subtitle": "The dial that settles arguments.",
  "quest.285F341D83DF1895.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Put a large cogwheel on a \"},{\"text\":\"Rotation Speed Controller\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:rotation_speed_controller\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and feed it rotation: the cog turns at the speed on its panel, anywhere from −256 to 256 RPM. Machines downstream still pay stress at the new speed.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.682E109880DA80FC.title": "The control room",
  "quest.682E109880DA80FC.quest_subtitle": "Take a seat. The factory reports to you.",
  "quest.682E109880DA80FC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Sequenced Pulse Generator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create_connected:sequenced_pulse_generator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" plays redstone from a program, and a \"},{\"text\":\"Dashboard\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create_connected:dashboard\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" sends its four lines of live data to the HUD of whoever sits in front of it.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The generator takes two electron tubes, a brass sheet, a redstone torch, stone and a \"},{\"text\":\"Control Chip\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create_connected:control_chip\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". The dashboard is a display board on brass casing: feed it with display links; a wrench stops it reaching your HUD.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0C66974A6A223991.title": "Any lever, wireless",
  "quest.0C66974A6A223991.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Craft a Redstone Link alone and it becomes a \"},{\"text\":\"Linked Transmitter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create_connected:linked_transmitter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", and back. Right-click a lever, button or analog lever with it: that switch now sends on the link's frequency. A wrench takes it off again.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Honeycomb waxes its frequency slots against stray clicks; an axe scrapes the wax off.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6D6EF127F904332F.title": "Any frequency",
  "quest.6D6EF127F904332F.quest_subtitle": "The joker of the deck.",
  "quest.6D6EF127F904332F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A transmitter and a crafter slot cover make a \"},{\"text\":\"Redstone Link Wildcard\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create_connected:redstone_link_wildcard\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". In a link's frequency slot it matches any item, so one receiver hears a whole family of transmitters that share the other slot.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.78266496A16097A4.title": "Frequencies go places",
  "quest.78266496A16097A4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Links reach past plain redstone: a train schedule can wait until a frequency is on or off, and a factory gauge can switch a link once its stock is met, or be paused by one.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.543B95A106E14636.title": "Either latch",
  "quest.1F60110305C9F18B.title": "One bit of memory",
  "quest.1F60110305C9F18B.quest_subtitle": "It remembers so you don't have to.",
  "quest.1F60110305C9F18B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Powered Latch\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:powered_latch\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" is a lever redstone can move: a signal at its back turns it on, one at its side turns it off. A \"},{\"text\":\"Powered Toggle Latch\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:powered_toggle_latch\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" flips on every pulse at its back. Both still work by hand.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2D91CA4F31DF04B6.title": "Pick one",
  "quest.2D91CA4F31DF04B6.quest_subtitle": "Radio buttons, in quartz.",
  "quest.2D91CA4F31DF04B6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Polished rose quartz, redstone and zinc make a \"},{\"text\":\"Rose Quartz Lamp\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:rose_quartz_lamp\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". A signal lights it and it stays lit; in a group, lighting one turns the rest off. A comparator reads how far the lit lamp is, and a wrench flips one by hand.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3AF7FF9B0E067069.title": "Wait for it",
  "quest.3AF7FF9B0E067069.quest_subtitle": "Delayed gratification, in ticks.",
  "quest.3AF7FF9B0E067069.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Pulse Repeater\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:pulse_repeater\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" answers an incoming signal with one short pulse, after the delay set on its panel: two ticks to an hour. Chain a few and a single button press becomes a timed sequence.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.18B2A323841645ED.title": "Make it last",
  "quest.18B2A323841645ED.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Pulse Extender\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:pulse_extender\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" stretches a signal: it switches on shortly after the input does and, once the input drops, stays on for the time on its panel, up to an hour. One button press, a minute of light.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6D891FB5E1983637.title": "The negative pulse",
  "quest.6D891FB5E1983637.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Redstone halts funnels, smart chutes, ejectors, deployers and arms. Deployers and arms finish their swing first, so a brief break in the signal buys exactly one cycle. Right-click a pulse timer's base to invert it and it keeps their beat.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.7E5055C249D0BAAF.title": "Look at a working threshold switch",
  "quest.2C8F569700EE6F11.title": "Two thresholds",
  "quest.2C8F569700EE6F11.quest_subtitle": "Hysteresis, but friendly.",
  "quest.2C8F569700EE6F11.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Threshold Switch\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:stockpile_switch\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" has two levels on purpose: on at or above the upper one, off at or below the lower one, so nothing flickers at the edge. A filter counts only some items; it reads tanks too, and even how far a rope pulley hangs.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0D2C01E4491E8B7D.title": "Face to face",
  "quest.0D2C01E4491E8B7D.quest_subtitle": "They only light up together.",
  "quest.0D2C01E4491E8B7D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Cobblestone, redstone and an iron sheet make two \"},{\"text\":\"Redstone Contacts\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:redstone_contact\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Facing each other they give a signal, even when one rides a moving contraption: the tidy way to tell a piston, bearing or gantry where to stop.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"An elevator pulley needs one glued to its cabin; the ones along its shaft become floors.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3EFDF858E68AB90E.title": "Computers at the controls",
  "quest.3EFDF858E68AB90E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"With CC: Tweaked, a computer attached to a display link writes what the program sends, a speed controller takes its target speed, a sequenced gearshift turns on command, and gauges report their readings. The block's own screen says who's in charge.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.343E8AC2BA7EA52D.title": "Chip off the old sheet",
  "quest.343E8AC2BA7EA52D.quest_subtitle": "Some assembly required. Three times.",
  "quest.343E8AC2BA7EA52D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Control Chip\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create_connected:control_chip\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" starts as a golden sheet: a deployer adds an electron tube, another adds redstone, a press seals it, three loops over. About four runs in five end as a chip; the rest comes back as parts.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5E24A92E400AEB9F.title": "Program the pulses",
  "quest.5E24A92E400AEB9F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A signal at its back starts the list; one at a side stops and resets it. Steps: output a strength for a while or until the input reaches a state, loop forever, X times or while a state holds, reshape the input with a formula, end.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3ED93A5C7DFF847B.title": "Infinite loop",
  "quest.3ED93A5C7DFF847B.quest_subtitle": "It's not a bug, it's a feature.",
  "quest.3ED93A5C7DFF847B.quest_desc": [
    "You overloaded a Sequenced Pulse Generator with a program that never lets go. Somewhere, a programmer sighs."
  ],
  "reward.4114923A320C98C1.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.73E592ECC81D8921.title": "Gauges speak redstone",
  "quest.73E592ECC81D8921.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A comparator reads more than chests: speedometers and stressometers give a signal that grows with their reading, sequenced gearshifts and pulse generators give their progress, and a red train signal lights one up.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6DDBA8BB7D784C98.title": "Redline",
  "quest.6DDBA8BB7D784C98.quest_subtitle": "One more cog and everything stops.",
  "quest.6DDBA8BB7D784C98.quest_desc": [
    "You read a stressometer at exactly 100%. Every su spoken for, none to spare: engineering, or nerve."
  ],
  "reward.099A18F2608BE4B6.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.2E0E367F4F022C3D.title": "Numbers that glow",
  "quest.2E0E367F4F022C3D.quest_subtitle": "Retro-futurism, fifteen at a time.",
  "quest.2E0E367F4F022C3D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two electron tubes make four \"},{\"text\":\"Nixie Tubes\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:nixie_tube\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Powered, a tube shows the signal strength as a number; a written clipboard gives it your own text, dye changes its glow, and a display link can write along a row of them.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1BBF8D8B20BF3EDD.title": "What a link can read",
  "quest.1BBF8D8B20BF3EDD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Beyond gauges: the time, a stopwatch, item throughput, fill levels, boiler status, train arrivals, player deaths, the top enchanting cost and package addresses. A link reaches 64 blocks, and while powered it stops updating.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6AD91CB04D211603.title": "Tube order",
  "quest.6AD91CB04D211603.quest_subtitle": "Every smart block wants one.",
  "quest.6AD91CB04D211603.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Sixteen \"},{\"text\":\"Electron Tubes\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:electron_tube\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for the depot, once a day. Polished rose quartz over an iron sheet; mechanical crafters make it routine.\"}]"
  ],
  "image.51E0742F0A4FE5DA.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Wireless\",\"color\":\"#E5A16A\"}]",
  "image.30690C53E51B6465.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Memory\",\"color\":\"#E5A16A\"}]",
  "image.7E8BE60BAB05BEE3.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Timing\",\"color\":\"#E5A16A\"}]",
  "image.3BB5915D8413D6E5.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Sensors\",\"color\":\"#E5A16A\"}]",
  "image.2D57CDAAE03931DB.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Displays\",\"color\":\"#E5A16A\"}]",
  "image.47D1C28B7795AA4F.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Create: Connected\",\"color\":\"#E5A16A\"}]",
  "image.60CA7979AE824432.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Create\",\"color\":\"#FFE3C4\"}]",
  "image.2F400EC2FE3E5B40.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Logic and Measurement\",\"color\":\"#FFF4DA\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.171E78ACB8C6916B.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"sense · time · measure · show\",\"color\":\"#E5A16A\",\"font\":\"minecraft:uniform\"}]",
  "image.350D3129C595683C.title": "Back to Create · Kinetics",
  "image.7F13DFC3264F15FE.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"U1\",\"color\":\"#DCE8DC\"}]",
  "image.320C0A90346B0D39.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"LOGIC\",\"color\":\"#DCE8DC\"}]",
  "image.272C6DAFBE22EEB1.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"MEASUREMENT\",\"color\":\"#DCE8DC\"}]",
  "image.566E664930943BD1.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"15\",\"color\":\"#FF8C2A\"}]",
  "image.77A9D6295DCC0565.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"STRESS 72%  ·  128 RPM\",\"color\":\"#FFB347\"}]",
  "chapter.06C76EF421D48687.title": "Create · Rails and Power",
  "chapter.06C76EF421D48687.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Trains on your own line, parcels on chains, and Heliodor's sun turned into current."
  ],
  "quest.1054891D3522FCFA.title": "Sturdy Sheet",
  "quest.1054891D3522FCFA.quest_subtitle": "Rails start with rocks.",
  "quest.1054891D3522FCFA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Crush obsidian into \"},{\"text\":\"Powdered Obsidian\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:powdered_obsidian\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", then a short sequence: a \"},{\"text\":\"spout\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"7E52D88B6EC82066\"}},{\"text\":\" adds 500 mB of lava, a press stamps it twice. One of each over a looping belt keeps the \"},{\"text\":\"Sturdy Sheets\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:sturdy_sheet\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" coming.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3EDBCACC92228200.title": "Train Casing",
  "quest.3EDBCACC92228200.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Sturdy Sheet\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:sturdy_sheet\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on \"},{\"text\":\"Brass Casing\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:brass_casing\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Every railway block wears it, and used on a track it places a bogey while you build a train.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.696B32ED0CC51858.title": "No Steam 'n' Rails",
  "quest.696B32ED0CC51858.quest_desc": [
    "Steam 'n' Rails stops at Minecraft 1.20.1, so it isn't here: standard Create tracks, stations, signals and bogeys only. To move people between buildings, try Create Hypertube."
  ],
  "quest.42C367280974A1FA.title": "Lay the line",
  "quest.42C367280974A1FA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A slab gets two iron or zinc nuggets, then a press: \"},{\"text\":\"Train Track\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:track\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" by sequenced assembly. To lay it, click a placed piece, then a second spot; bends and slopes fill themselves.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.497E4DA8ED2F1F47.title": "Track manners",
  "quest.497E4DA8ED2F1F47.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Hold sprint while laying for the widest possible bend. Blocks in your off-hand pave under new track. Track laid into a Nether portal builds its twin on the other side.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0E63E76DEBBC6A9C.title": "Dimensional commuter",
  "quest.0E63E76DEBBC6A9C.quest_subtitle": "Mind the gap. The very big gap.",
  "quest.0E63E76DEBBC6A9C.quest_desc": [
    "Ride a train through a Nether portal. Eight blocks of Nether rail cover sixty-four of Overworld: the fastest line you'll ever build."
  ],
  "quest.212CC36CDB8FECE1.title": "Stations",
  "quest.212CC36CDB8FECE1.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Train Casing and a compass make two \"},{\"text\":\"Train Stations\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:track_station\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": select a track, place one beside it. In assembly mode, scheduled trains keep away while you build.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0CEABA006D2B2118.title": "All aboard",
  "quest.0CEABA006D2B2118.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"In assembly mode: casing on the track for bogeys, glue your blocks, \"},{\"text\":\"Train Controls\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:controls\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on board, confirm at the station. Drive with the movement keys; a second set of controls lets it run both ways.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2E7F74B4329FF2BD.title": "Train quirks",
  "quest.2E7F74B4329FF2BD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Trains turn back into blocks only at a station. Fuel in chests on board speeds them up; fuel in vaults never burns. Out of loaded chunks they still obey signals, but drills stop.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.377785343C1E2D9A.title": "Road kill",
  "quest.377785343C1E2D9A.quest_subtitle": "The zombie didn't have a ticket.",
  "quest.377785343C1E2D9A.quest_desc": [
    "A hostile mob met your train, head on. The train won."
  ],
  "reward.6AA96DAB9F7ADCEA.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.071C64C7436E52EA.title": "Timetable",
  "quest.071C64C7436E52EA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Obsidian sheet and paper make four \"},{\"text\":\"Train Schedules\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:schedule\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": stops, waits and conditions. Hand one to a conductor seated at the controls, any mob or a Blaze Burner will do.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.78BDDCA133A5B020.title": "Traffic control",
  "quest.78BDDCA133A5B020.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Casing and an electron tube make four \"},{\"text\":\"Train Signals\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:track_signal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Signals cut the track into sections, one train each: no collisions.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Brass mode, set with a wrench, also holds a train that couldn't clear the next section. Use it at busy junctions.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7B46DD682DD694C6.title": "Expert driver",
  "quest.7B46DD682DD694C6.quest_subtitle": "It was more of an orange.",
  "quest.7B46DD682DD694C6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"You ran a red \"},{\"text\":\"Train Signal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:track_signal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". The signal remembers. The signal always remembers.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.1E6ECEDC1198C856.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.4BD65852229A6C01.title": "Train Observer",
  "quest.4BD65852229A6C01.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Select a track, place a \"},{\"text\":\"Train Observer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:track_observer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" nearby: it gives a redstone pulse when a train passes, optionally only for certain cargo. Doors, counters, loading triggers.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.3F1C95A646D0C53B.title": "Look at a postbox beside a station",
  "quest.1A3D29FDC0AED65F.title": "Mail by rail",
  "quest.1A3D29FDC0AED65F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Postbox\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:white_postbox\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" near a station gets an address. Trains that stop there collect parcels for elsewhere and drop off the ones for here, even in unloaded chunks.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2F45D98085540ED4.title": "Drive-by exchange",
  "quest.2F45D98085540ED4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Portable Storage Interface\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:portable_storage_interface\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on the train and another on the ground, one or two blocks apart, connect as it passes. The train leaves once the items stop moving.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1FCA21CEB61C346B.title": "Freight contract",
  "quest.1FCA21CEB61C346B.quest_subtitle": "The depot always needs more.",
  "quest.1FCA21CEB61C346B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Sixteen \"},{\"text\":\"Sturdy Sheets\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:sturdy_sheet\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for the depot, once a day. A spout, a press and a looping belt make it a formality.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.6D7BC9885BFC3FB6.title": "Watch your train pull in",
  "quest.524CEFA7BBD1F988.title": "The outpost line",
  "quest.524CEFA7BBD1F988.quest_subtitle": "Next stop: everywhere.",
  "quest.524CEFA7BBD1F988.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A scheduled train between home and an outpost, a \"},{\"text\":\"Display Board\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:display_board\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" forecasting its arrival, and a factory board keeping key items stocked by itself.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "{image:entrelumen:textures/gui/quests/diagram_train.png width:96 height:48 align:center}",
    "",
    "Packages move goods far without chunk loading. Storage networks can take over at home later; the line keeps running."
  ],
  "quest.517A7FAE8B813A33.title": "Cardboard",
  "quest.517A7FAE8B813A33.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Pulpable stuff and water mix into \"},{\"text\":\"Pulp\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:pulp\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": bamboo, sugar cane, saplings. A press makes \"},{\"text\":\"Cardboard\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:cardboard\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". The whole package network is made of it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1E0F58C5183DBF70.title": "Post production",
  "quest.1E0F58C5183DBF70.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Packager\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:packager\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on an inventory boxes its items on a redstone pulse. Feed it a package and it unboxes, only if everything fits. Contents stay together on belts, chains and trains.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.478FB83FAE0F57D1.title": "Addresses",
  "quest.478FB83FAE0F57D1.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A sign on a packager stamps its text as the address. A \"},{\"text\":\"Package Filter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:package_filter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" routes by address through funnels, tunnels and chutes. A clipboard learns frogport addresses.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.184A2AFCE40F73A6.title": "Nothing but net",
  "quest.184A2AFCE40F73A6.quest_subtitle": "Three points.",
  "quest.184A2AFCE40F73A6.quest_desc": [
    "You threw a package into a chute from a distance. The mail has never been so athletic."
  ],
  "reward.174E3A94E98068CD.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.49BFAD9BA3EA1AC8.title": "Chain Conveyor",
  "quest.49BFAD9BA3EA1AC8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A large cogwheel ringed by andesite casings makes two \"},{\"text\":\"Chain Conveyors\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:chain_conveyor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; link them with chains. They carry rotation and packages, and you can ride one holding a wrench.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3C2865BB6A36E878.title": "Hungry frogs",
  "quest.3C2865BB6A36E878.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Click a chain with a \"},{\"text\":\"Package Frogport\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:package_frogport\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", place it nearby and name an address. Parcels for that address get snapped off the chain; the rest keep riding.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.49C070B70EA98451.title": "Stock Link",
  "quest.49C070B70EA98451.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A transmitter on an item vault: a \"},{\"text\":\"Stock Link\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:stock_link\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Linked packagers show their inventory to the whole network, at any range; the parcels still need a real route.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Full redstone power silences a link; a weaker signal lowers its priority, so other links serve first.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.41C4000F78AD0C5B.title": "Order up",
  "quest.41C4000F78AD0C5B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Bind a \"},{\"text\":\"Stock Ticker\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:stock_ticker\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" to a link and seat a mob or a blaze burner in front: your stock keeper. Talk to it to browse the network and send anything to any address.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.42885664A4CDB7C2.title": "One button, one delivery",
  "quest.42885664A4CDB7C2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Redstone Requester\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:redstone_requester\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" orders a fixed list on every pulse. Wire it to a button by the door: building materials on demand.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2D4095C7B60D3B42.title": "Open for business",
  "quest.2D4095C7B60D3B42.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Hold a \"},{\"text\":\"Table Cloth\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:white_table_cloth\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and talk to your stock keeper to set up a trade, then place and price it. Buyers pay at the counter; goods come out boxed.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.481386E35D624FCF.title": "High logistics",
  "quest.481386E35D624FCF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A stock link and a precision mechanism make two \"},{\"text\":\"Factory Gauges\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:factory_gauge\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". On a packager, a gauge keeps one item stocked by ordering it; chained gauges form a factory board.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.377C162FFC963F8A.title": "Re-Packager",
  "quest.377C162FFC963F8A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Big orders arrive split and can mix with other parcels. A powered \"},{\"text\":\"Re-Packager\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:repackager\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" waits for every fragment and ships them as one package, in order.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.36A7B2FC383BC500.title": "Sorting by label",
  "quest.36A7B2FC383BC500.quest_subtitle": "The mailroom's secret weapon.",
  "quest.36A7B2FC383BC500.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Zinc nuggets and wool make a \"},{\"text\":\"Package Filter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:package_filter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Give it an address and, in any filter slot, it matches the packages bound there: funnels, tunnels, smart chutes. Addresses take * as a wildcard.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A mechanical saw unpacks packages straight onto a belt.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1C3D7139EC910489.title": "Ship to",
  "quest.1C3D7139EC910489.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Every stock ticker order carries the address you type, so filters, frogports and postboxes steer it home. Lines starting with # on a clipboard you hold or keep nearby autocomplete addresses, like #storage or #factory.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3782292549C451DA.title": "Restock, step by step",
  "quest.3782292549C451DA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Tune the gauge to a stock link before placing it on a packager. Click it with the item to watch, type the address the refill should come to, then hold right-click to set the target. Short of it, the network ships more.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4E43A85265018E0D.title": "A factory on the wall",
  "quest.4E43A85265018E0D.quest_subtitle": "Arrows are the new conveyor belts.",
  "quest.4E43A85265018E0D.quest_desc": [
    "A factory gauge off a packager watches the whole network. Connect ingredient gauges to it, set the batch and the address where it gets made, and it keeps its item stocked by sending ingredients there. Green arrows: target met.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "The outputs have to come back to a linked inventory. Each gauge on the board keeps its own item, so one wall of gauges can run a whole production chain."
  ],
  "quest.37C01E1A137128F5.title": "Crafting by mail",
  "quest.37C01E1A137128F5.quest_subtitle": "Unwrap, craft, ship back.",
  "quest.37C01E1A137128F5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"For a crafting-table recipe the gauge can send the ingredients already arranged: unwrapped into a 3×3 of connected mechanical crafters, they craft at once. A \"},{\"text\":\"Re-Packager\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:repackager\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a packager crafted alone, keeps each order whole.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.185008C88C35EB0B.title": "At the counter",
  "quest.185008C88C35EB0B.quest_subtitle": "Items only. No haggling.",
  "quest.185008C88C35EB0B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"With an empty hand, click a priced table cloth: you get a \"},{\"text\":\"Shopping List\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:shopping_list\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Add to it, then hand it to the keeper to pay; the goods leave boxed. Payments pile up inside the stock ticker block.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Lock the keeper's network and other players can only buy through lists.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1BFAB003A278D495.title": "Rolling Mill",
  "quest.1BFAB003A278D495.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Rolling Mill\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"createaddition:rolling_mill\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" rolls long parts: an ingot into two rods, a plate into two wires, bamboo or paper into straw. Drop items on top; a belt and two funnels automate it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6AAB9425E04AADB7.title": "A straw for the blaze",
  "quest.6AAB9425E04AADB7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Use \"},{\"text\":\"Straw\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"createaddition:straw\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on a blaze burner and it drinks liquid fuel by bucket or pipe. Lava keeps it lit 20000 ticks a bucket; biofuel superheats it. Goodbye, coal by hand.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.70608772E702AD35.title": "Fuel from the field",
  "quest.70608772E702AD35.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Compacted seeds give seed oil; crops, leaves or flowers mixed hot with plant oil give biomass; sugar, cinder flour and biomass mix into \"},{\"text\":\"Biofuel\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"createaddition:bioethanol_bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". A wheat farm is a gas station.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.160207A457B0B0F2.title": "Wires and connectors",
  "quest.160207A457B0B0F2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Small Connectors\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"createaddition:connector\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" link FE blocks with \"},{\"text\":\"Copper Spool\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"createaddition:copper_spool\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" wire; large ones take gold or electrum. A wrench cycles push, pull and none: generators push, machines pull.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.40D2195EF4AA050D.title": "Rotation to current",
  "quest.40D2195EF4AA050D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An \"},{\"text\":\"Alternator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"createaddition:alternator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" turns rotation into FE, the energy most tech mods run on, from 32 RPM up, more the faster it spins. A water wheel can now run a Mekanism machine.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2942848DCFF562A8.title": "And back again",
  "quest.2942848DCFF562A8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An \"},{\"text\":\"Electric Motor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"createaddition:electric_motor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" turns FE into rotation; scroll its back panel to set the RPM, and more RPM costs more energy. Silent, compact rotation wherever the wires reach.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.007932E8F2D12779.title": "Accumulator",
  "quest.007932E8F2D12779.quest_desc": [
    "A stackable multiblock battery: set one connector as input and one as output. A portable energy interface pair charges one riding a train."
  ],
  "quest.5572EB452CE49149.title": "Tesla Coil",
  "quest.5572EB452CE49149.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Tesla Coil\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"createaddition:tesla_coil\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" charges FE items below it and runs charging recipes, like electrum. Powered by redstone, it also shocks what stands nearby, you included.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4359AD5F556388A3.title": "A switch for current",
  "quest.4359AD5F556388A3.quest_subtitle": "Redstone says when.",
  "quest.4359AD5F556388A3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two small connectors, an electron tube and redstone on stone make a \"},{\"text\":\"Redstone Relay\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"createaddition:redstone_relay\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Power only passes from its input connector to its output while it gets a redstone signal: a breaker a lever can throw.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2376057ED163A454.title": "Motor on a script",
  "quest.2376057ED163A454.quest_subtitle": "rotate(90), then a coffee.",
  "quest.2376057ED163A454.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A computer beside an \"},{\"text\":\"Electric Motor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"createaddition:electric_motor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" drives it through peripheral.wrap: setSpeed and stop, plus rotate and translate, which give the seconds a turn of N degrees or a move of N blocks takes. Sleep that long, then stop.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Accumulators, portable interfaces and relays answer too; /cca_api opens the full list, and \"},{\"text\":\"Create and computers\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"77AB5A14AB23ED5D\"}},{\"text\":\" covers boards, gauges and pulleys.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2678AC13AF640F1E.title": "Charge on the move",
  "quest.2678AC13AF640F1E.quest_subtitle": "A pit stop without stopping.",
  "quest.2678AC13AF640F1E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Brass casing, a chute and a copper spool make a \"},{\"text\":\"Portable Energy Interface\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"createaddition:portable_energy_interface\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". One on a contraption and one on the ground, one or two blocks apart, couple as they pass; the ground one speaks for every accumulator aboard.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Energy follows each connector's push or pull setting; once it stops flowing for a while, the contraption moves on. Redstone on the ground interface keeps it from coupling."
  ],
  "quest.55D2351D5C48CA80.title": "Magnetite and thorium",
  "quest.55D2351D5C48CA80.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Magnetite\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create_new_age:magnetite_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and \"},{\"text\":\"Thorium Ore\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create_new_age:thorium_ore\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" spawn in the Overworld. Magnetite makes magnets and motors; crushed thorium sometimes gives radioactive thorium for reactors.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Thorium has no common ore tag here, on purpose: dimensional miners skip it. Dig for it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2D13EC7992A1F5E6.title": "Sunlight as heat",
  "quest.2D13EC7992A1F5E6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"New Age has no photovoltaic panels: solar plates make heat, a boiler or a Stirling engine makes rotation, magnets and coils make current. Light, heat, motion, current: Heliodor's loop.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.41BC5584D4C11B0F.title": "Generator Coil",
  "quest.41BC5584D4C11B0F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A spinning \"},{\"text\":\"Generator Coil\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create_new_age:generator_coil\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" ringed by magnets makes current; \"},{\"text\":\"Carbon Brushes\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create_new_age:carbon_brushes\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" collect it. Stronger magnets turn more stress into power.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Pack change: the brushes take an \"},{\"text\":\"Energy Coupler\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:energy_coupler\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (act II) in place of an andesite alloy; the coils don't.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0CC87E8CE3690B51.title": "Magnet ladder",
  "quest.0CC87E8CE3690B51.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Magnetic force per block: magnetite 1, redstone 2, layered 4, fluxuated magnetite 8, netherite 24. The goggles show a coil's force and efficiency. Better magnets first: efficiency is free power.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1AF466ECB9C6F7F2.title": "Copper Wire",
  "quest.1AF466ECB9C6F7F2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A saw cuts a copper sheet into four \"},{\"text\":\"Copper Wires\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create_new_age:copper_wire\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for \"},{\"text\":\"Electrical Connectors\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create_new_age:electrical_connector\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". A connector on pull draws power from other mods' blocks.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.25041E85AE09DAA7.title": "Energise it",
  "quest.25041E85AE09DAA7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"With current and rotation, a \"},{\"text\":\"Basic Energiser\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create_new_age:basic_energiser\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" charges items below it on a depot or belt: iron becomes \"},{\"text\":\"Overcharged Iron\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create_new_age:overcharged_iron\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for 1000 energy, gold 2000, diamond 10000.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3B52B315368D80BC.title": "Expensive miracles",
  "quest.3B52B315368D80BC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"An energiser can make an Enchanted Golden Apple by sequenced assembly, at two million energy per step, and bottles o' enchanting at 50000 each. Renewable, not cheap.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.30DCDED6F3E8103A.title": "Basic Motor",
  "quest.30DCDED6F3E8103A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Current back into rotation: a wrench sets a \"},{\"text\":\"Basic Motor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create_new_age:basic_motor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"'s speed. Extensions behind it raise its capacity and its energy use. The advanced motor takes a \"},{\"text\":\"Reinforced Alloy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:alloy_reinforced\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (act III).\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4FD6592D778686FD.title": "Solar heating",
  "quest.4FD6592D778686FD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"In daylight, a \"},{\"text\":\"Basic Solar Heating Plate\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create_new_age:basic_solar_heating_plate\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" makes heat; heat pipes carry it. Too much heat in one block melts it to lava: always give heat somewhere to go.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The basic plate takes an \"},{\"text\":\"Infused Alloy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:alloy_infused\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (act II) in place of one glass.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4C05F500C1209A2A.title": "A boiler that eats sunlight",
  "quest.4C05F500C1209A2A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Heater\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create_new_age:heater\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" under a Create boiler burns heat instead of fuel: more heat in, more steam out. Plates, pipes and a heater make a sun-powered steam engine.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.022A04310ADE0F93.title": "Thorium reactor",
  "quest.022A04310ADE0F93.quest_subtitle": "Glow responsibly.",
  "quest.022A04310ADE0F93.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Reactor Rods\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create_new_age:reactor_rod\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a fuel acceptor and heat vents. \"},{\"text\":\"Radiation kills\",\"color\":\"#FF8C7A\"},{\"text\":\": wear leather armour or seal it in reactor casing. If nothing takes its heat, it melts down. Rods take an \"},{\"text\":\"Ironwood Ingot\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:ironwood_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (act IV).\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.37752415929A2864.title": "Street lights",
  "quest.37752415929A2864.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Street Lights\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create_new_age:street_light\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" run on current; lamp posts hold them up. A lit road home, a small nod to the city that kept its light.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.00B8D71B50937179.title": "Heliodor's loop, closed",
  "quest.00B8D71B50937179.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Sun heats a boiler, the boiler spins coils, coils feed energisers, energised parts build the \"},{\"text\":\"Reinforced Motor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create_new_age:reinforced_motor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It takes an \"},{\"text\":\"Ironwood Ingot\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:ironwood_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (act IV).\"}]"
  ],
  "image.2127BC4E8B22BCE0.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Crafts & Additions: rotation to FE and back\",\"color\":\"#E5A16A\"}]",
  "image.4032F7C374F7D126.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Create · Rails and Power\",\"color\":\"#E5A16A\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.50DB3FDC0CC7AD97.title": "Back to Create · Kinetics",
  "image.73B828EAE340FEA3.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Package network\",\"color\":\"#E5A16A\"}]",
  "image.068567F75027201D.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"New Age: sunlight, magnets, current\",\"color\":\"#E5A16A\"}]",
  "chapter.2FD24C6ADC23649E.title": "Create · Addons",
  "chapter.2FD24C6ADC23649E.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Nine addons on one pegboard: liquid experience, smarter gearboxes, new fans, copycat blocks, tubes you ride, a kitchen, a chisel, storage on the move and stronger magnets."
  ],
  "quest.50EABAD3AA74115B.title": "Experience, bottled",
  "quest.50EABAD3AA74115B.quest_subtitle": "Levels you can pour.",
  "quest.50EABAD3AA74115B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Click an \"},{\"text\":\"Experience Hatch\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create_enchantment_industry:experience_hatch\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" to deposit your levels; sneak-click to take them back. Inside, they are Liquid Experience: pipes, spouts and drains move it like water.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3B9A67575AD7DF9C.title": "A shower experience",
  "quest.3B9A67575AD7DF9C.quest_subtitle": "Refreshing. Educational.",
  "quest.3B9A67575AD7DF9C.quest_desc": [
    "You broke a pipe full of Liquid Experience and stood under it. Worth every level you soaked up."
  ],
  "reward.448C6B96F1F21F37.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.0E1E17A383C2E5C1.title": "Every experience counts",
  "quest.0E1E17A383C2E5C1.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The pack teaches Enchantment Industry the experience fluids of Ender IO, Industrial Foregoing, Just Dire Things, PneumaticCraft, Reliquary and Sophisticated. The \"},{\"text\":\"Creative Bookshelf\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create_enchantment_industry:creative_bookshelf\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" takes four Luminosities (act VI).\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.638D14DBD895685C.title": "Grind the drops",
  "quest.638D14DBD895685C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight andesite alloys around a shaft: a \"},{\"text\":\"Mechanical Grindstone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create_enchantment_industry:mechanical_grindstone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Over an item drain it grinds \"},{\"text\":\"Nuggets of Experience\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:experience_nugget\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" into liquid. Mob farms feed it directly.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4A7B59096069FFBB.title": "Nugget tax",
  "quest.4A7B59096069FFBB.quest_subtitle": "Paid in wisdom.",
  "quest.4A7B59096069FFBB.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Thirty-two \"},{\"text\":\"Nuggets of Experience\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:experience_nugget\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for the common store, once a day. Crushing wheels and deployers that kill mobs drop them now.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7B70C2EA603E91CF.title": "Blaze Enchanter",
  "quest.7B70C2EA603E91CF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Smith an enchanting table onto a blaze burner with the Blaze Upgrade template: a \"},{\"text\":\"Blaze Enchanter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create_enchantment_industry:blaze_enchanter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Feed it liquid experience, set the level, and it enchants whatever arms or belts bring.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.11F14228ED3BBB5E.title": "Brass library",
  "quest.11F14228ED3BBB5E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"With Apotheosis around, a \"},{\"text\":\"Brass Bookshelf\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create_enchantment_industry:brass_bookshelf\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" gives adjustable enchanting stats while it turns. A fan through infused dragon's breath salvages gear in bulk: stay out of the stream.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5C6B37C1585CA8CE.title": "Infusion on tap",
  "quest.5C6B37C1585CA8CE.quest_subtitle": "The enchanting table's other job, minus the clicking.",
  "quest.5C6B37C1585CA8CE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A brass sheet, a spout and three nixie tubes make an \"},{\"text\":\"Infuser\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create_enchantment_industry:infuser\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Over a basin it runs Apothic Enchanting's infusion recipes: the bookshelves around it give the stats, and it pays in liquid experience instead of levels.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"It ignores a recipe's stat maximums, so Infused Dragon's Breath no longer needs quanta kept under 30. Flimsy Ender Leads come out as \"},{\"text\":\"Ender Leads\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apothic_enchanting:ender_lead\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", the thread of the woven bag.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3CEA2B609A309611.title": "Mobs to go",
  "quest.3CEA2B609A309611.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Six Ender Leads around a rose quartz lamp, a precision mechanism and a brass casing make an \"},{\"text\":\"Ender Woven Bag\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create_enchantment_industry:ender_woven_bag\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It pulls nearby mobs in and keeps them; its light comes on when it is full, and a redstone signal lets them out.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "It works on a contraption too, and there it lets its mobs out when it faces a redstone block: a delivery van for your mob farm."
  ],
  "quest.1B6F6F3AE0F6A3A6.title": "An anvil that never gets tired",
  "quest.1B6F6F3AE0F6A3A6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Blaze Forger\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create_enchantment_industry:blaze_forger\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" merges enchantments with no repair cost, applies templates and pulls an enchantment onto a blank template. Move a great enchantment from an old tool to a new one.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0CB361E7D10525AD.title": "Copy that",
  "quest.0CB361E7D10525AD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Printer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create_enchantment_industry:printer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" copies books, enchanted books, names, schedules and package addresses, paid in liquid experience. Every copy costs, so the recipe stays native.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0FDBAEE270D46484.title": "Seething",
  "quest.0FDBAEE270D46484.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Feed an enchanter or forger a \"},{\"text\":\"Cake o' Enchanting\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create_enchantment_industry:experience_cake\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and it seethes: higher caps, treasure enchantments, conflicting ones merged. It calls lightning, so keep a rod nearby.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.75546C046FB78F53.title": "Past the cap",
  "quest.75546C046FB78F53.quest_subtitle": "Level limits were more of a suggestion.",
  "quest.75546C046FB78F53.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Strike \"},{\"text\":\"Blocks of Super Experience\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create_enchantment_industry:super_experience_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" with lightning, craft a \"},{\"text\":\"Super Enchanting Template\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create_enchantment_industry:super_enchanting_template\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and run a \"},{\"text\":\"seething\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"0FDBAEE270D46484\"}},{\"text\":\" enchanter by a lightning rod until an enchantment goes past its vanilla cap.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3A4EFB035F8DC1B8.title": "The missing parts",
  "quest.3A4EFB035F8DC1B8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Create: Connected adds what the base lacks: a \"},{\"text\":\"6-way Gearbox\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create_connected:six_way_gearbox\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a brass gearbox with wrench-set sides, freewheel and overstress clutches, a brake, a crank wheel and a cross connector.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5596725A549B09EA.title": "Kinetic Battery",
  "quest.5596725A549B09EA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Kinetic Battery\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create_connected:kinetic_battery\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" stores stress. Unpowered, it charges from rotation; with redstone it gives it back at a fixed speed. A windmill by day, a battery by night.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.460FC472B3C569F0.title": "Snap",
  "quest.460FC472B3C569F0.quest_subtitle": "Better the pin than the factory.",
  "quest.460FC472B3C569F0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Shear Pin\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create_connected:shear_pin\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" breaks when its branch is overstressed, and only that branch stops. The \"},{\"text\":\"Overstress Clutch\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create_connected:overstress_clutch\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" does the same, and resets.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2FA77368629A7144.title": "Overpowered",
  "quest.2FA77368629A7144.quest_subtitle": "The brake did its best.",
  "quest.2FA77368629A7144.quest_desc": [
    "A network kept running at speed with a powered brake on it. The brake would like a word."
  ],
  "reward.7B65EF304FCE0DF1.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.0DEFF29404B28832.title": "Catalysts in a cage",
  "quest.0DEFF29404B28832.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Brass and iron bars make an \"},{\"text\":\"Empty Fan Catalyst\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create_connected:empty_fan_catalyst\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Fill it and a fan blows through it as if through the real thing, with no spills: lava, water, soul sand or netherrack, and the new fan types of the Dragons Plus panel.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Brass Chute\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create_connected:brass_chute\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" moves 64 items at a time.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.39CEA4922F07C72B.title": "One copycat family",
  "quest.39CEA4922F07C72B.quest_desc": [
    "Connected's own copycat blocks are off in its config: Copycats+ covers those shapes. If the recipe viewer shows two versions of a shape, the Copycats+ one is the real one."
  ],
  "quest.6882BE836ECECFFE.title": "Ports and bridges",
  "quest.6882BE836ECECFFE.quest_subtitle": "Reach in from anywhere.",
  "quest.6882BE836ECECFFE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A brass casing, a chute and an electron tube make two \"},{\"text\":\"Inventory Access Ports\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create_connected:inventory_access_port\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Stuck to a chest, a port lets the funnels and arms on it reach the chest as if they touched it. Two ports make an \"},{\"text\":\"Inventory Bridge\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create_connected:inventory_bridge\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", which reaches two inventories at once.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The bridge's filter slots pick the side each item goes to, and items matching neither are refused. Neither ports nor bridges chain, and a redstone signal turns them off.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.13F1D7A4E1BC3F4F.title": "Stand it up",
  "quest.13F1D7A4E1BC3F4F.quest_subtitle": "Same vault, better posture.",
  "quest.13F1D7A4E1BC3F4F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The vault's recipe turned on its side (iron sheet, barrel, iron sheet in a row) makes an \"},{\"text\":\"Item Silo\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create_connected:item_silo\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": a vault that grows upward instead of sideways, and rides contraptions like one. A vault and a silo swap for each other in the crafting grid.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.77BCFA0009CEC5FD.title": "Dragons Plus",
  "quest.77BCFA0009CEC5FD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The base that Enchantment Industry and Central Kitchen build on. A \"},{\"text\":\"Fluid Hatch\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create_dragons_plus:fluid_hatch\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" fills or drains a tank with buckets and bottles by hand.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.238A1E08F4CC4D13.title": "Clouds that enchant",
  "quest.238A1E08F4CC4D13.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A fan blowing through a \"},{\"text\":\"Golden Aercloud\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:golden_aercloud\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" from the Aether runs its altar recipes in bulk: it enchants, repairs gear and even hatches Moa eggs.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.33EF4F3EC2316620.title": "Deep freeze",
  "quest.33EF4F3EC2316620.quest_subtitle": "Even a blaze needs to chill.",
  "quest.33EF4F3EC2316620.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A fan blowing through powder snow freezes what it carries: ice packs down, then turns into \"},{\"text\":\"Blue Ice\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:blue_ice\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", magma cream becomes slime and a blaze rod cools into a \"},{\"text\":\"Breeze Rod\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:breeze_rod\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Mobs in the stream freeze and stop burning.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A powder snow bucket on an \"},{\"text\":\"Empty Fan Catalyst\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"0DEFF29404B28832\"}},{\"text\":\" makes a freezing catalyst that never spills.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.7352D1BDD8E71936.title": "Look at a sanding catalyst",
  "quest.66894DA5D56965D3.title": "Polish in bulk",
  "quest.66894DA5D56965D3.quest_subtitle": "Sandpaper, but it's weather.",
  "quest.66894DA5D56965D3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Dragons Plus sands with quicksand, and no mod here has any. Apply sand to an \"},{\"text\":\"Empty Fan Catalyst\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"0DEFF29404B28832\"}},{\"text\":\" instead: a fan through it runs Create's sandpaper recipes in bulk, so rose quartz comes out as \"},{\"text\":\"Polished Rose Quartz\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:polished_rose_quartz\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" by the beltful.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.76B29CA7B90BFBD8.title": "Any liquid dye bucket",
  "quest.32F1B321C9CE81EA.title": "Paint job",
  "quest.32F1B321C9CE81EA.quest_subtitle": "Sixteen colours, no brushes.",
  "quest.32F1B321C9CE81EA.quest_desc": [
    "A mixer turns a dye and 250 mB of water into 250 mB of liquid dye. A fan blowing through it dyes items in bulk (the recipe viewer lists which), recolours sheep and other mobs, and dyes the armour they wear.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A dye bucket on an \"},{\"text\":\"Empty Fan Catalyst\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"0DEFF29404B28832\"}},{\"text\":\" makes a dyeing catalyst of that colour, with no puddle to step in.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3C049F5B915AE57E.title": "Dragon's breath, piped",
  "quest.3C049F5B915AE57E.quest_subtitle": "Handle with a fan.",
  "quest.3C049F5B915AE57E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An item drain turns each bottle of dragon's breath into 250 mB of fluid and a spout bottles it back; four fill a \"},{\"text\":\"Dragon's Breath Bucket\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create_dragons_plus:dragon_breath_bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It fills cauldrons too, and where flowing breath meets lava it hardens into end stone.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A fan through the breath, or through a dragon head, runs Bulk Ending: cobblestone becomes end stone, stone bricks become end stone bricks, apples become \"},{\"text\":\"Chorus Fruit\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:chorus_fruit\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and leather becomes phantom membrane. Mobs in the stream take instant damage; the undead enjoy it.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"An \"},{\"text\":\"Infuser\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"5C6B37C1585CA8CE\"}},{\"text\":\" over a basin of breath turns 250 mB into 750 mB of Infused Dragon's Breath, the fluid behind the \"},{\"text\":\"salvaging fan\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"11F14228ED3BBB5E\"}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.16D128C530556B90.title": "Copycats",
  "quest.16D128C530556B90.quest_subtitle": "Any block, any shape.",
  "quest.16D128C530556B90.quest_desc": [
    "Click a copycat block with a material and it takes that look; a wrench removes it. Slopes, steps, beams, doors, ladders, a ghost block. Most are cut from zinc in a stonecutter."
  ],
  "quest.1089FF521C5397C8.title": "Sheet metal and friends",
  "quest.1089FF521C5397C8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Create Deco adds \"},{\"text\":\"sheet metal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"createdeco:andesite_sheet_metal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", coloured bricks, lamps, decals, bars, doors and windows in Create's style. Rechiseled Create chisels the base blocks.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.660ACF6373137B51.title": "Bells and whistles",
  "quest.660ACF6373137B51.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Headlights\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"bellsandwhistles:headlight\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", cowcatchers, platforms, metro casing and grab bars: dressing for trains and stations. Glue it on like any block.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.387AED26C270661F.title": "Hypertube",
  "quest.387AED26C270661F.quest_subtitle": "Commuting, but in a tube.",
  "quest.387AED26C270661F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Glass tubes that carry players and mobs. A \"},{\"text\":\"Hypertube Entrance\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create_hypertube:hypertube_entrance\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" needs 16 RPM or more; the faster it turns, the faster you fly.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.709B5FD65DF2AC6B.title": "Faster, or slower",
  "quest.709B5FD65DF2AC6B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Accelerators\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create_hypertube:hypertube_accelerator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" speed a rider up or brake them; junctions split the line and you steer with the movement keys. Link tubes by clicking a placed one with the next.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.28984D492046759D.title": "Slicer",
  "quest.28984D492046759D.quest_subtitle": "Knife skills, outsourced.",
  "quest.28984D492046759D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A cogwheel, an andesite casing and a turntable: the \"},{\"text\":\"Slicer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sliceanddice:slicer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Right-click it with a knife and it cuts what passes beneath, on a depot, a belt or in a basin: Farmer's Delight cutting board recipes, no hands.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7513397D32714F6A.title": "Sprinkles on top",
  "quest.7513397D32714F6A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Copper plates, a fluid pipe and iron bars: a \"},{\"text\":\"Sprinkler\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sliceanddice:sprinkler\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Put it under a pipe and it sprays the fluid over the area; water, liquid fertilizer and other fluids each do something different to crops and creatures.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6070A59336C59BC8.title": "A kitchen on autopilot",
  "quest.6070A59336C59BC8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Cutting boards automate too: a Mechanical Arm puts raw ingredients on a \"},{\"text\":\"Cutting Board\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"farmersdelight:cutting_board\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a deployer holding a knife in Use mode cuts them. Arms also take servings off feasts and slices off pies, and leave the last one in place.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.08668E9211F80A6E.title": "Sixteen bowls from the pot",
  "quest.103D9F34E56F2F0E.title": "Pot on the line",
  "quest.103D9F34E56F2F0E.quest_subtitle": "Nobody stirs by hand anymore.",
  "quest.103D9F34E56F2F0E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Central Kitchen hooks the \"},{\"text\":\"Cooking Pot\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"farmersdelight:cooking_pot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" up to Create: a packager unpacks the ingredients into it (factory gauges help order them), a mechanical arm adds the bowls, and an arm or a funnel takes the meal out. A blaze burner underneath counts as heat.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7EA423253377FE28.title": "Mechanical Chisel",
  "quest.7EA423253377FE28.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An andesite casing and a chisel: the \"},{\"text\":\"Mechanical Chisel\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rechiseledcreate:mechanical_chisel\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Rechiseled: Create adds cut and polished variants of Create's stones and new window styles to chisel into.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.25CB45905C2979C7.title": "Storage on rails",
  "quest.25CB45905C2979C7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Craft a Sophisticated chest, barrel or shulker box with a minecart and it becomes a \"},{\"text\":\"storage minecart\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedstorageinmotion:storage_minecart\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", upgradable by tier like the block. Boats and rafts work the same way.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.170FE2044196CF14.title": "Upgrades that ride along",
  "quest.170FE2044196CF14.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Two small integrations make Sophisticated backpacks and storage fully featured on Create contraptions: their upgrades keep working while the contraption moves.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.391CBF85EECF8E46.title": "Eight magnets for one coil",
  "quest.66037C7B60577D4C.title": "A ring of magnets",
  "quest.66037C7B60577D4C.quest_subtitle": "Opposites attract; netherite, most of all.",
  "quest.66037C7B60577D4C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight magnets ring a \"},{\"text\":\"Generator Coil\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create_new_age:generator_coil\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and their force adds up; each block's tooltip shows its own. Magnetite gives 1, a \"},{\"text\":\"Redstone Magnet\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create_new_age:redstone_magnet\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" 2, a \"},{\"text\":\"Layered Magnet\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create_new_age:layered_magnet\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" 4, \"},{\"text\":\"Fluxuated Magnetite\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create_new_age:fluxuated_magnetite\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" 8 and a \"},{\"text\":\"Netherite Magnet\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create_new_age:netherite_magnet\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" 24.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "More force turns a bigger share of the coil's stress into current, but the coil also draws more stress: size the rotation for it.",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A redstone magnet is a redstone block in iron nuggets; a layered one, overcharged iron and gold; fluxuated magnetite, magnetite with overcharged gold and diamond; a netherite magnet, scrap and five overcharged diamonds.\"}]"
  ],
  "image.17A266723707C0C8.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Create · Addons\",\"color\":\"#E5A16A\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.4DDE711656B995C6.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Enchantment Industry\",\"color\":\"#E5A16A\"}]",
  "image.583088DA9793DA58.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Connected\",\"color\":\"#E5A16A\"}]",
  "image.2E3A2181AAFC88B8.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Dragons Plus\",\"color\":\"#E5A16A\"}]",
  "image.7F8B933F6176C0F8.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Copycats and Deco\",\"color\":\"#E5A16A\"}]",
  "image.04CF75E5E708276B.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Hypertube\",\"color\":\"#E5A16A\"}]",
  "image.3B7E2213A4E4625F.title": "Back to Create · Kinetics",
  "image.3B3567550545369B.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Farmer's Delight\",\"color\":\"#E5A16A\"}]",
  "image.5F17ADFEDC4E7EBA.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Rechiseled\",\"color\":\"#E5A16A\"}]",
  "image.7C26A0016646BEF9.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Storage in motion\",\"color\":\"#E5A16A\"}]",
  "image.61A7C3B671BBDADD.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"New Age\",\"color\":\"#E5A16A\"}]",
  "chapter.04F18C84B664FCFB.title": "Energy in ENTRELUMEN",
  "chapter.04F18C84B664FCFB.chapter_subtitle": [
    "One currency, many names: first generators, units, bridges to rotation and pressure, storage, cables and act gates."
  ],
  "quest.65BC69F4A047247E.title": "FE: one currency",
  "quest.65BC69F4A047247E.quest_desc": [
    "Almost every tech mod runs on Forge Energy (FE), sometimes under another name: RF in Oritech and Industrial Foregoing, OP in Draconic, µI in Ender IO. Any of them powers the others with a plain cable.",
    "",
    "The odd ones out: Mekanism (Joules inside), AE2 (AE), Modern Industrialization (EU), Create (rotation) and PneumaticCraft (pressure)."
  ],
  "quest.06BFA19A5271724A.title": "Free first power",
  "quest.06BFA19A5271724A.quest_desc": [
    "Early generators need no campaign component, on purpose: the Actually Additions and RFTools Coal Generators, the Powah Furnator, the Just Dire Things coal generator, and an Immersive Engineering water wheel or windmill on a Kinetic Dynamo. Throw coal in and your first machines hum."
  ],
  "quest.3ECC537E1727CCDF.title": "Units that convert",
  "quest.3ECC537E1727CCDF.quest_desc": [
    "Mekanism counts Joules inside (1 FE = 2.5 J) but shows FE by default. AE2 turns FE into AE one way: 2 FE per AE, via an Energy Acceptor or the controller. MI's EU is worth 10 FE here and converts one way only, so keep MI power inside MI."
  ],
  "quest.01B1492E9A898747.title": "Rotation to FE and back",
  "quest.01B1492E9A898747.quest_desc": [
    "The Crafts and Additions Alternator makes FE from 32 RPM or more; its Electric Motor spins at the speed you set, paid in FE. Create: New Age makes power with Generator Coils ringed by magnets. Pack note: New Age's carbon brushes take an Energy Coupler (Act II)."
  ],
  "quest.521A75B666C9FA3D.title": "Pressure and FE",
  "quest.521A75B666C9FA3D.quest_desc": [
    "PneumaticCraft's Flux Compressor turns FE into air pressure; the Pneumatic Dynamo turns pressure back into FE. Both run hot: give them cooling or they slow down."
  ],
  "quest.36FC798DD6C0C68E.title": "Mid-game generators",
  "quest.36FC798DD6C0C68E.quest_desc": [
    "Pick one that eats something you already farm: Mekanism's Heat, Solar, Wind, Bio or Gas-Burning generators, Powah's Magmator, IF's Biofuel Generator (160 RF/t), Oritech's basic generator (32 RF/t), Ender IO's Stirling, IE's diesel generator."
  ],
  "quest.1D7A85CD9B7D2262.title": "Big power",
  "quest.1D7A85CD9B7D2262.quest_desc": [
    "Late-game plants, each with its own chapter: Oritech's Steam Engine (up to 50,000 RF/t), Mekanism fission with a turbine and later fusion, the Powah Reactor, MI's large boilers and turbines, and the Draconic Reactor for the brave."
  ],
  "quest.572C910CE861DAF6.title": "Storing energy",
  "quest.572C910CE861DAF6.quest_desc": [
    "A buffer between generators and machines smooths every spike: Mekanism Energy Cubes and the Induction Matrix, Powah Energy Cells, RFTools Powercells, Flux Storage, and Draconic's Energy Core at the top. AE2 keeps its own Energy Cells."
  ],
  "quest.12AE0449F841ECD7.title": "Moving energy",
  "quest.12AE0449F841ECD7.quest_desc": [
    "Cables: Mekanism Universal Cables, Pipez Energy Pipes, Powah cables, Ender IO conduits, IE wires. No cables: Flux Networks (even across dimensions), LaserIO energy cards (up to 1,000,000 FE/t), XNet channels, the JDT Energy Transmitter."
  ],
  "quest.4C9F577BAA9D57ED.title": "Energy Meter",
  "quest.4C9F577BAA9D57ED.quest_desc": [
    "Drop it into a cable line to read the flow, instant or smoothed. It can also cap the flow, and computers can read it. The fastest bottleneck hunter in the pack."
  ],
  "quest.2C79BDE68081E6D8.title": "Charging your gear",
  "quest.2C79BDE68081E6D8.quest_desc": [
    "Stand on a Mekanism Chargepad to charge any mod's FE items. The Powah Player Transmitter charges your whole inventory wirelessly through a Binding Card (the dimensional card works anywhere), and a Flux Controller charges its network members."
  ],
  "quest.65B736FBC35BD88E.title": "Energy and the acts",
  "quest.65B736FBC35BD88E.quest_desc": [
    "The Power Regulator (Act III: two Mekanism basic circuits, two steel plates and an Energy Coupler) gates Mekanism's jetpack, Psi's CAD Assembler and the aircraft engine; Flux plugs, dimensional cells, jetpack straps and mining gadgets take a reinforced alloy instead. Generators are never gated."
  ],
  "quest.1D421CED31F05B4F.title": "Quirks worth knowing",
  "quest.1D421CED31F05B4F.quest_desc": [
    "An AE2 network only spends what it has stored per tick: add an Energy Cell before big imports. Oritech power is push-only, so generators must push into pipes. IE wires carry one voltage each; put transformers between LV, MV and HV."
  ],
  "quest.2FB875EDE69CD455.title": "Creative power",
  "quest.2FB875EDE69CD455.quest_desc": [
    "Infinite energy waits at the very end: Mekanism's Creative Energy Cube, Powah's Creative Cell, Create's Creative Motor, AE2's Creative Energy Cell and Draconic's Creative Capacitor each cost two Luminosities (Act VI)."
  ],
  "quest.0E7550D2B4347BBB.title": "Mastery: a power plant",
  "quest.0E7550D2B4347BBB.quest_desc": [
    "One big plant, one big buffer, one wireless link to every corner of the base and to outposts in other dimensions. An Energy Meter on the main line, always in the green."
  ],
  "chapter.7E2F499D96852FED.title": "Ore processing",
  "chapter.7E2F499D96852FED.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Fortune or Silk Touch, and which machine turns one ore into the most ingots, with real numbers for iron."
  ],
  "quest.14B80E1A7F7061F7.title": "Ore, raw or block?",
  "quest.14B80E1A7F7061F7.quest_desc": [
    "Fortune gives raw ore (Fortune III: 2.2 raw iron or gold per ore on average). Silk Touch gives the ore block. Every machine pays differently for each, so pick your pickaxe by the machine you will feed. All numbers here are for iron."
  ],
  "quest.7AD07B9921AA3CD8.title": "Create: crush and wash",
  "quest.7AD07B9921AA3CD8.quest_desc": [
    "Crushing Wheels turn raw iron into 1 Crushed Raw Iron (plus a 75% chance of an XP nugget). Smelt it for 1 ingot, or wash it with a fan for 9 nuggets and a 75% chance of redstone. Silk-touched blocks crush a bit better: 1.75 per stone ore, 2.25 per deepslate ore."
  ],
  "quest.23019D0A97A8F00C.title": "Immersive Engineering",
  "quest.23019D0A97A8F00C.quest_desc": [
    "The Crusher makes 2 dusts per ore block but only 1.33 per raw ore. The Arc Furnace smelts an ore block into 2 ingots plus slag, and a raw ore into 1.5 ingots on average: with Fortune that is 3.3 ingots per ore, no dust step."
  ],
  "quest.2A4733EA6E7036DA.title": "Modern Industrialization: Silk Touch wins",
  "quest.2A4733EA6E7036DA.quest_desc": [
    "The Macerator turns an ore block into 3 raw ores, and each raw into 1.5 dust on average. Silk Touch: 4.5 dust per ore. Fortune: 3.3. The steam Forge Hammer gives 2 raw per ore, 3 with a Hammer tool in its slot."
  ],
  "quest.0BDE2EBD8D54FEFD.title": "Ender IO SAG Mill",
  "quest.0BDE2EBD8D54FEFD.quest_desc": [
    "A raw ore gives 1.8 powder on average (Fortune: about 4 per ore), while an ore block only gives 1.33 raw. Grinding Balls in the mill add bonus output and speed. Keep Fortune for this one."
  ],
  "quest.2B97086271E1EA71.title": "Actually Additions Crusher",
  "quest.2B97086271E1EA71.quest_desc": [
    "An early electric option: an iron ore block becomes 2 raw iron with a 20% chance of raw gold. Fine before Fortune III, then outgrown."
  ],
  "quest.2FC8BA3D26A234E5.title": "Mekanism: 2 to 5 per ore",
  "quest.2FC8BA3D26A234E5.quest_desc": [
    "Per ore block Mekanism gives 2, 3, 4 or 5 ingots by tier; per raw ore about 1.33, 2, 2.67 or 3.33. With Fortune III that is roughly 2.9, 4.4, 5.9 or 7.3 per ore: raw wins at every tier. The details live in the Mekanism ore chapter."
  ],
  "quest.61418A5DA4757B2D.title": "Oritech: the gem route",
  "quest.61418A5DA4757B2D.quest_desc": [
    "The Fragment Forge turns a raw ore into 1.33 clumps. The Centrifuge makes 1 gem per clump dry, 2 with water, 3 with sulfuric acid, and the Foundry turns 2 gems into 3 ingots. Top of the line: about 6 ingots per raw iron, the richest route in the pack."
  ],
  "quest.3BE1CBEF0802DB1C.title": "Cheat sheet",
  "quest.3BE1CBEF0802DB1C.quest_desc": [
    "Ingots per iron ore, Fortune III raw vs Silk Touch block: furnace 2.2 vs 1; Create 2.2 vs 1.75-2.25; IE Arc Furnace 3.3 vs 2; MI Macerator 3.3 vs 4.5; Ender IO about 4 vs 2.4; Mekanism x5 7.3 vs 5; Oritech with acid about 13 vs 12."
  ],
  "quest.714000127752F16B.title": "Byproducts",
  "quest.714000127752F16B.quest_desc": [
    "Processing pays extras: Create washing gives redstone from iron, quartz from gold, clay from copper; the IE Crusher sometimes drops nickel dust from iron; Oritech iron yields nickel, and nickel fragmenting is an early platinum source; the AA Crusher gives raw gold from iron."
  ],
  "quest.23F039D6DBAAD79F.title": "One ingot per metal",
  "quest.23F039D6DBAAD79F.quest_desc": [
    "Almost Unified makes every machine output the same ingot, dust or plate for each metal, preferring vanilla, then Create, IE, Mekanism, Oritech, Ender IO, Ad Astra and MI. JEI hides the duplicates. Loot is not unified, but all copies share tags, so they still work in recipes."
  ],
  "quest.4E3B021E19511C86.title": "Uraninite: energize the ore",
  "quest.4E3B021E19511C86.quest_desc": [
    "Powah’s Energizing Orb turns a silk-touched uraninite ore into 5 uraninite (dense 10, poor 3). Mined normally, the ore drops 2 raw, about 4.4 with Fortune III, one uraninite each. Energizing wins, by a nose."
  ],
  "quest.3B78D5C6732777EF.title": "Mining dimensions",
  "quest.3B78D5C6732777EF.quest_desc": [
    "JAMD portals open throwaway mining worlds so your home stays intact. Pack gates: the Overworld mine needs a Calibration Frame (Act II), the Nether mine a Containment Seal (Act IV), the End mine a Horizon Chart (Act IV)."
  ],
  "quest.41E9F3FDC372449C.title": "Quarries and their gates",
  "quest.41E9F3FDC372449C.quest_desc": [
    "Automated mining comes later: Mekanism's Digital Miner needs a Spectral Lens (Act IV); MI's Electric Quarry, IF's Ore Laser Drill, Oritech's Bedrock Extractor, the RFTools quarry card and Occultism's mineshaft need ironwood (Act IV); the Mining Gadgets a reinforced alloy (Act III)."
  ],
  "quest.1756B7A4FD944A67.title": "Mastery: never smelt raw ore again",
  "quest.1756B7A4FD944A67.quest_desc": [
    "Pick your top route, automate it end to end and feed it with Fortune-mined raw ore (or silk-touched blocks for MI). A chest of raw iron should come out as a small mountain of ingots."
  ],
  "chapter.1EC8C85A19A48FCD.title": "Automation basics",
  "chapter.1EC8C85A19A48FCD.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Hoppers, pipes, machine sides, filters, redstone, buffers and crafting: the habits every factory needs."
  ],
  "quest.19AA52C75FC8F28F.title": "The automation loop",
  "quest.19AA52C75FC8F28F.quest_desc": [
    "Every factory is the same loop: input, machine, output, storage. Build one line, watch it run for a minute, then copy it. If something stops, follow the items: they always pile up right before the problem."
  ],
  "quest.7DABF9C654292148.title": "Hoppers",
  "quest.7DABF9C654292148.quest_desc": [
    "A hopper moves one item every 8 ticks (2.5 per second) into whatever it points at. Chest, hopper, furnace, hopper, chest: your first automatic smelter. A comparator next to a container reads how full it is."
  ],
  "quest.23768FBE28F5B3EA.title": "Pipes that pull",
  "quest.23768FBE28F5B3EA.quest_desc": [
    "Pipez pipes connect to anything, but only pull where you say: click the end touching the source with the Pipe Wrench to make it extract; sneak-click cuts a connection. The extract menu sets distribution, redstone mode and filters."
  ],
  "quest.7B4B6BFE3D5FA17A.title": "Fluids",
  "quest.7B4B6BFE3D5FA17A.quest_desc": [
    "Pipez Fluid Pipes and Mekanism Mechanical Pipes move fluids like items, wrench and all. Create pipes need a Mechanical Pump; its arrow shows the flow. The Ranged Pumps Pump drains a whole lake with FE, scanning outwards block by block."
  ],
  "quest.05B443D66D43BA72.title": "Machine sides",
  "quest.05B443D66D43BA72.quest_desc": [
    "Most tech machines choose what goes in and out by side. In Mekanism, open the side tab or right-click with the Configurator, and turn on auto-eject so output pushes itself into the next pipe. Other mods have the same idea in their I/O tabs."
  ],
  "quest.718B726433BB5A90.title": "Belts, funnels and arms",
  "quest.718B726433BB5A90.quest_desc": [
    "In Create, belts carry items, funnels put them on and take them off, and depots hold one stack for a machine to work on. The brass Mechanical Arm picks from and drops into many targets around it, no belts needed."
  ],
  "quest.20067837AD551995.title": "Filters everywhere",
  "quest.20067837AD551995.quest_desc": [
    "Almost every mover takes a filter: Create funnels and arms, Pipez extract menus (item IDs or #tags), LaserIO filter cards, Modular Routers module slots, the Mekanism Logistical Sorter. Filter at the source and the rest of the line stays clean."
  ],
  "quest.53E12EA132885122.title": "Redstone control",
  "quest.53E12EA132885122.quest_desc": [
    "Run machines only when needed: most have a redstone mode (ignored, on or off when powered). A comparator on a chest turns fill level into a signal, Functional Storage drawers do the same with a Redstone Upgrade, and Utilitarian's Redstone Clock pulses at a rate you set by right-clicking it."
  ],
  "quest.7F0C46AC3082F194.title": "Buffers and overflow",
  "quest.7F0C46AC3082F194.quest_desc": [
    "Put a chest or drawer between machines so a slow step never stalls the fast one. Then decide what happens when storage fills: a Void Upgrade on a drawer or a Trash Can at the end of the line deletes the excess instead of jamming everything."
  ],
  "quest.5268F4017AEE3BBA.title": "Automatic crafting",
  "quest.5268F4017AEE3BBA.quest_desc": [
    "Pick by what you already run: Create Mechanical Crafters for big shaped recipes, the RFTools Crafter (up to 8 recipes in one block), MI's Assembler, or AE2 and Refined Storage patterns once you have a network."
  ],
  "quest.63F545CBDE937710.title": "Farms that feed the line",
  "quest.63F545CBDE937710.quest_desc": [
    "A farm is automation with a field attached: Industrial Foregoing's Plant Sower and Plant Gatherer, Create harvesters on a moving contraption, Mekanism or Powah generators fed by what grows. Always collect the drops: items on the ground are lag."
  ],
  "quest.3944A93667D89759.title": "When lines become a network",
  "quest.3944A93667D89759.quest_desc": [
    "With many lines, a storage network pays off: AE2 or Refined Storage import and export buses feed machines straight from storage, and autocrafting orders the rest. LaserIO and XNet do the same between machines without a central storage."
  ],
  "quest.1E354FE92CDDB0C1.title": "Keep the server happy",
  "quest.1E354FE92CDDB0C1.quest_desc": [
    "Fewer entities, fewer ticks: collect drops, prefer bigger stacks per operation over faster ticking (Modular Routers says it outright), and let idle machines sleep on redstone. Utilitarian's TPS Meter outputs redstone by the dimension's TPS, so a line can pause itself when the server struggles."
  ],
  "quest.65263D529EBC60BC.title": "Machines sleep when nobody is near",
  "quest.65263D529EBC60BC.quest_desc": [
    "Blocks only work in loaded chunks. Claim your base and force-load the machine chunks with FTB Chunks (see the teams chapter), and keep the count small: every loaded chunk costs the server."
  ],
  "quest.4B1C0C1C336CA7BB.title": "Mastery: a line that runs while you sleep",
  "quest.4B1C0C1C336CA7BB.quest_desc": [
    "Raw materials in, finished goods out, overflow handled, no hands. Leave it for a night in-game and come back to full chests and an empty trash log."
  ],
  "chapter.7D58BA957E127EAE.title": "Silent Gear",
  "chapter.7D58BA957E127EAE.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Tools, weapons and armour built from parts: blueprints, materials and traits, repair kits, alloys and the luminous material."
  ],
  "quest.3E8C6596D76CCEA3.title": "Gear built from parts",
  "quest.3E8C6596D76CCEA3.quest_desc": [
    "A head or blade from main materials, a rod and optional extras: every material adds its own stats and traits, and mixing changes the result. Broken gear does not vanish, it waits for repair. Nobody spawns with blueprints or the material book here; both are cheap to craft."
  ],
  "quest.7436213DB8D718D5.title": "Stone Anvil and crude knife",
  "quest.7436213DB8D718D5.quest_desc": [
    "Start in the Stone Age: cobblestone and dirt make the Stone Anvil and the Crude Tool Parts, which become a Crude Knife. Put a log on the anvil and use the knife on it to get six Template Boards.",
    "",
    "Any knife or dagger works on the anvil, including the Silent Gear ones later."
  ],
  "quest.3574048549EEC217.title": "Templates",
  "quest.3574048549EEC217.quest_desc": [
    "Template Boards around a stick shape a Template for each gear type (pickaxe, sword, helmet...). A template is used up in one craft. Its tooltip tells how many main materials the part needs."
  ],
  "quest.5B513654FB93EAAA.title": "Your first Silent Gear tool",
  "quest.5B513654FB93EAAA.quest_desc": [
    "Craft a template with the main materials to get a head, then the head with a rod to get the tool. A quick recipe does both in one step: template, materials and rod together.",
    "",
    "Stone, flint, iron, copper, gems, bone and many modded metals are valid materials: check a material tooltip for its stats."
  ],
  "quest.6964FE44D886F549.title": "Blueprints",
  "quest.6964FE44D886F549.quest_desc": [
    "Four paper and a blue dye make Blueprint Paper; shape it like a template to get a Blueprint, which is never used up. A Blueprint Book holds many blueprints and works as the selected one; cycle it with the keys its tooltip shows.",
    "",
    "Move from templates to blueprints once you craft the same part often."
  ],
  "quest.7BF828D333F31D0E.title": "Parts beyond the head",
  "quest.7BF828D333F31D0E.quest_desc": [
    "Rods, Bindings, Grips, Tips and Coatings add stats or traits. Netherite only works as a coating: on diamond it behaves almost like vanilla netherite. The Gear Mod Kit removes or repaints parts. Hold Ctrl over a part to see its numbers."
  ],
  "quest.2A6685D98DA1FA5D.title": "The gear roster",
  "quest.2A6685D98DA1FA5D.quest_desc": [
    "Hammer (3x3 stone, ores only when aimed at one), Excavator (3x3 soil), Saw (whole trees), Sickle (clears plants, replants crops), Mattock (tills, digs, chops), Paxel (three in one); katana, machete, dagger, knife, spear, mace, bows, crossbows, slingshot. The Prospector Hammer scans ahead for ores."
  ],
  "quest.67B078299DE88913.title": "Armour",
  "quest.67B078299DE88913.quest_desc": [
    "Helmet, chestplate, leggings and boots come from their own blueprints or templates, built from plates of any armour-capable material. Linings made of fabrics add traits. Armour follows the same rules: it breaks into a repairable state and mixes materials."
  ],
  "quest.767797906C0DD96F.title": "Broken gear and repair kits",
  "quest.767797906C0DD96F.quest_desc": [
    "When durability runs out the item becomes broken, not destroyed. Fill a repair kit by crafting it with materials, then craft the kit with the gear to repair it; a stick empties the kit. Better kits (very crude, crude, sturdy, crimson, azure) hold more and waste less.",
    "",
    "A Red Card upgrade makes an item break for good, like vanilla, if you prefer that."
  ],
  "quest.6BDC2490EB1BE98C.title": "Upgrades",
  "quest.6BDC2490EB1BE98C.quest_desc": [
    "Upgrade Base (paper, planks and stone) and its advanced version start the upgrades: Spoon lets a pickaxe dig like a shovel, Wide Plate adds 1 to the radius of hammers and excavators, Road Maker makes paths with an excavator, and Red Card allows permanent breaking. Craft the upgrade together with the gear."
  ],
  "quest.3DD29656FE7C8536.title": "Fibres and drops",
  "quest.3DD29656FE7C8536.quest_desc": [
    "Wild flax and fluffy plants grow in the world; their fibres make strings and fabrics for bowstrings, cords and linings. Animals sometimes drop sinew and spiders rarely drop fine silk, both better cord materials. Leather scraps drop too."
  ],
  "quest.30DF358C5B7F5045.title": "Silent Gear ores",
  "quest.30DF358C5B7F5045.quest_desc": [
    "Three ores of its own: Bort, a hard gem deep in the Overworld (Y -60 to 10); Crimson Iron all through the Nether; and Azure Silver in the End (Y 16 to 92). They feed the alloys that come next."
  ],
  "quest.43D69EA32C741FCF.title": "Alloys",
  "quest.43D69EA32C741FCF.quest_desc": [
    "Blaze Gold (gold and blaze powder), Crimson Steel (crimson iron, blaze rods and magma cream) and Azure Electrum (azure silver, gold and an ender pearl) can be crafted at a crafting table. Crimson steel is strong all around and fire-resistant; azure electrum is fast but fragile."
  ],
  "quest.6C794340168FB182.title": "Alloy Forge and Tyrian Steel",
  "quest.6C794340168FB182.quest_desc": [
    "The Alloy Forge (blackstone, crimson steel and an iron block) makes the same alloys more efficiently than the crafting table, and it is the only way to make Tyrian Steel: crimson steel, azure electrum, crushed shulker shell and netherite scrap. Tyrian steel is the strongest basic material in Silent Gear."
  ],
  "quest.37B2F02FEFEAD4DB.title": "Compound materials",
  "quest.37B2F02FEFEAD4DB.quest_desc": [
    "Machines that fuse materials into new ones: the Crude Mixer takes anything but marks the result Crude (weaker); the Recrystallizer makes hybrid gems; the Refabricator blends fabrics; the Super Mixer takes any material with no penalty. The result keeps a mix of its inputs' properties."
  ],
  "quest.556CC166B490647F.title": "Material Grader",
  "quest.556CC166B490647F.quest_desc": [
    "Grades a material with a catalyst, raising its stats: grades go from E up to SSS and MAX. Catalyst tiers are Glowing Dust (tier 1), Blazing Dust (tier 2) and Glittery Dust (tier 3); higher tiers reach higher grades. Grade the stack before you use it as a main material."
  ],
  "quest.5A3D56A181853420.title": "Starlight Charger",
  "quest.5A3D56A181853420.quest_desc": [
    "Builds charge under the night sky and applies Starcharged to materials, which raises their stats a lot. It takes a catalyst (blaze gold dust first, then azure silver dust) and its surrounding structure level can take up to 30 seconds to update."
  ],
  "quest.054210025010EBCC.title": "Salvager",
  "quest.054210025010EBCC.quest_desc": [
    "Breaks gear you no longer need back into parts and some of its materials. The luminous material has salvage disabled on purpose, so it never returns Luminosities."
  ],
  "quest.0E364ED62BB2A9DA.title": "Jewellery",
  "quest.0E364ED62BB2A9DA.quest_desc": [
    "Jeweler Tools make rings, bracelets and necklaces, optionally with a gem setting. They sit in accessory slots and carry the traits of their materials, so a ring can add a trait your armour lacks."
  ],
  "quest.3946F41738A526C5.title": "Mastery: the luminous material",
  "quest.3946F41738A526C5.quest_desc": [
    "The Luminous Ingot (Act VI) is a main material with absurd stats: Radiant, Holy V, Lustrous V, Refractive, Kitty Vision, fireproof. Light repairs radiant pieces, they glow, and four worn (luminous armour counts) give flight, night vision and no fall damage. Luminous tips and coatings exist too."
  ],
  "chapter.58E7DAF254E21B83.title": "Storage and Backpacks",
  "chapter.58E7DAF254E21B83.chapter_subtitle": [
    "What travels with you, what stays home and what goes in the bin."
  ],
  "quest.5B974C49A559E883.title": "Carry more",
  "quest.5B974C49A559E883.quest_subtitle": "Pockets were never enough.",
  "quest.5B974C49A559E883.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four leather, four string and a wooden chest make a \"},{\"text\":\"Backpack\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedbackpacks:backpack\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": 27 slots and one upgrade slot. Wear it or keep it in your inventory; \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.sophisticatedbackpacks.open_backpack\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" opens it anywhere.\"}]",
    "",
    "Sneak-right-click a block to set it down, and sneak-right-click it with an empty hand to pick it up."
  ],
  "quest.34135DB9A14BC9BD.title": "The back slot",
  "quest.34135DB9A14BC9BD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A backpack fits the back slot, so the chestplate stays on. Worn and visible, another player can open it by right-clicking your back; the backpack's settings tab turns that off.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6E332DA664D660DC.title": "A place for everything",
  "quest.6E332DA664D660DC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The sort button orders by name, mod, count or tags. In the settings tab, Memory keeps a slot for its item even when empty, No Sort shields slots from sorting and Item Display shows one item on the outside.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.666D61844B0BC97D.title": "Switch it off",
  "quest.666D61844B0BC97D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.sophisticatedbackpacks.toggle_upgrade_1\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" and \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.sophisticatedbackpacks.toggle_upgrade_2\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" switch the upgrades in the first two slots on and off without opening the backpack. A magnet you can mute is a magnet you keep.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0E7256B27FCD77F4.title": "Loot with legs",
  "quest.0E7256B27FCD77F4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"About one in a hundred zombies, skeletons, piglins or drowned spawns with a backpack full of loot, and better armor to match. Kill it and half the time the backpack drops; each level of Looting adds 15%.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.73BA0DCCF7B349DD.title": "Room for tricks",
  "quest.73BA0DCCF7B349DD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four string, four iron ingots and a leather make an \"},{\"text\":\"Upgrade Base\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedbackpacks:upgrade_base\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", the blank every backpack upgrade starts from. Upgrades sit in the column beside the slots; a basic backpack has room for one.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1C61CB75574EDC3D.title": "Into the void",
  "quest.1C61CB75574EDC3D.quest_subtitle": "Gravel, begone.",
  "quest.1C61CB75574EDC3D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An ender pearl, three obsidian and two redstone on a base make a \"},{\"text\":\"Void Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedbackpacks:void_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It deletes what its filter names: always, or only what overflows a full slot or the whole backpack.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4B51D4F7EE8FA710.title": "Door policy",
  "quest.4B51D4F7EE8FA710.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four redstone and four string on a base: a \"},{\"text\":\"Filter Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedbackpacks:filter_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". A backpack set down as a block is a chest that hoppers and pipes can reach; the filter decides what they may put in or take out.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.298F56701060EA3B.title": "Nothing left on the floor",
  "quest.298F56701060EA3B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A sticky piston, two string and three redstone on a base: a \"},{\"text\":\"Pickup Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedbackpacks:pickup_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". What you walk over goes straight into the backpack instead of your hotbar, and its filter says what is welcome.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.689D3B50F22D0F95.title": "Magnetic personality",
  "quest.689D3B50F22D0F95.quest_subtitle": "Now the loot comes to you.",
  "quest.689D3B50F22D0F95.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two ender pearls, three iron, a redstone and a lapis around a \"},{\"text\":\"Pickup Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedbackpacks:pickup_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make the \"},{\"text\":\"Magnet Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedbackpacks:magnet_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": it pulls items from 3 blocks away, 5 when advanced. Set down, the backpack pulls around itself.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"With a \"},{\"text\":\"Tank Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedbackpacks:tank_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in the backpack, the magnet also collects experience.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.736353EECCF1E398.title": "Advanced versions",
  "quest.736353EECCF1E398.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Most upgrades have an advanced version: one diamond, two gold and three redstone around the basic one. It brings 16 filter slots instead of 9, and filters that match by mod or by tag.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6E943037AEF674D2.title": "Crunch time",
  "quest.6E943037AEF674D2.quest_subtitle": "Nine nuggets walk into a backpack...",
  "quest.6E943037AEF674D2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two iron, four pistons and two redstone on a base: a \"},{\"text\":\"Compacting Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedbackpacks:compacting_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It packs items that have 2×2 recipes, like clay balls into clay. The \"},{\"text\":\"Advanced Compacting Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedbackpacks:advanced_compacting_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" adds 3×3: nuggets to ingots, ingots to blocks.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5044BB1E74772210.title": "A chest that grows",
  "quest.5044BB1E74772210.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight planks around a lever, or a plain chest with a lever, make a \"},{\"text\":\"Sophisticated chest\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedstorage:chest\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": 27 slots, an upgrade slot and its own versions of most backpack upgrades. Two matching chests side by side join into a double chest.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5B18FDC304BD1F69.title": "Barrels in a row",
  "quest.5B18FDC304BD1F69.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Planks, slabs and a lever make a \"},{\"text\":\"Sophisticated barrel\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedstorage:barrel\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", and so do a plain barrel and a lever. Same slots, tiers and upgrades as the chest, in a full block that builds walls.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0CCBDEAD564B0BAC.title": "Moving day",
  "quest.0CCBDEAD564B0BAC.quest_subtitle": "Nobody likes moving. Tape helps.",
  "quest.0CCBDEAD564B0BAC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A slime ball and paper make \"},{\"text\":\"Packing Tape\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedstorage:packing_tape\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Tape a chest or barrel, break it, and it drops as one item with everything inside. Four tapes make \"},{\"text\":\"Super Packing Tape\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedstorage:super_packing_tape\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", with more uses.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Breaking a chest that would spill more than 200 items is refused unless you sneak: that is the tape's cue. Carry On can't lift these blocks in this pack.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6FD5FB0A38761410.title": "Shell on the outside",
  "quest.6FD5FB0A38761410.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two shulker shells, a chest and a lever make a Sophisticated \"},{\"text\":\"Shulker Box\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedstorage:shulker_box\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; two shells on a tiered chest keep the tier. Broken, it keeps what's inside, with up to 132 slots at netherite.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.644FA66A32840A03.title": "One item, lots of it",
  "quest.644FA66A32840A03.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Planks, a slab and a lever make a \"},{\"text\":\"Limited Barrel I\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedstorage:limited_barrel_1\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": one slot for 32 stacks, with the item and the count on its face. Types II, III and IV split that into two to four slots. Click the front to put in and take out.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.073F17E1495FD033.title": "Nuggets, ingots, blocks",
  "quest.073F17E1495FD033.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two iron, two pistons and two redstone on a Sophisticated Storage base make a \"},{\"text\":\"Compression Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedstorage:compression_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It chains neighbouring slots: nuggets, ingots and blocks in order convert up and down on their own. A limited barrel III fits it like a glove.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6C132B0F92E78D11.title": "Keep the old chests",
  "quest.6C132B0F92E78D11.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four sticks and a lever make a \"},{\"text\":\"Basic Tier Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedstorage:basic_tier_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Right-click a plain chest, barrel or shulker box with it and it turns into the Sophisticated version on the spot, contents and all.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4899F04D7F3F1898.title": "Don't craft it twice",
  "quest.4899F04D7F3F1898.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Backpack and chest upgrades are separate items that convert: a backpack upgrade with five planks becomes the chest version, and a chest upgrade with four string and a leather becomes the backpack one.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.76BEC68B0BE8084E.title": "Copper step",
  "quest.76BEC68B0BE8084E.quest_subtitle": "Cheaper than it looks.",
  "quest.76BEC68B0BE8084E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight copper around a backpack make a \"},{\"text\":\"Copper Backpack\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedbackpacks:copper_backpack\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; eight around a lever make a \"},{\"text\":\"Basic to Copper Tier Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedstorage:basic_to_copper_tier_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for any placed chest or barrel. Both go to 45 slots, keeping contents and upgrades.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Copper first saves iron: the next step asks for four.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.393CF1C2E82B4CEB.title": "Iron step",
  "quest.393CF1C2E82B4CEB.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four iron finish the step from copper: an \"},{\"text\":\"Iron Backpack\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedbackpacks:iron_backpack\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a \"},{\"text\":\"Copper to Iron Tier Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedstorage:copper_to_iron_tier_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". 54 slots and a second upgrade slot on both.\"}]",
    "",
    "Skipped copper? Eight iron around the basic backpack also jump straight here."
  ],
  "quest.664677B8E02FDB8C.title": "Gold step",
  "quest.664677B8E02FDB8C.quest_subtitle": "Shiny, and a bit heavy.",
  "quest.664677B8E02FDB8C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight gold ingots each: a \"},{\"text\":\"Gold Backpack\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedbackpacks:gold_backpack\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and an \"},{\"text\":\"Iron to Gold Tier Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedstorage:iron_to_gold_tier_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". 81 slots and three upgrade slots: a magnet, a feeder and a tool swapper at once.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.13E81BA9F60E00F5.title": "Diamond step",
  "quest.13E81BA9F60E00F5.quest_subtitle": "Now we're talking.",
  "quest.13E81BA9F60E00F5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight diamonds each: a \"},{\"text\":\"Diamond Backpack\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedbackpacks:diamond_backpack\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a \"},{\"text\":\"Gold to Diamond Tier Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedstorage:gold_to_diamond_tier_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". 108 slots on both; five upgrade slots on the backpack, four on the chest.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5FF3A3B257FA29AC.title": "Netherite, top to bottom",
  "quest.5FF3A3B257FA29AC.quest_subtitle": "Fireproof luggage.",
  "quest.5FF3A3B257FA29AC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A diamond backpack, a netherite ingot and a smithing template at a smithing table make the \"},{\"text\":\"Netherite Backpack\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedbackpacks:netherite_backpack\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": 120 slots, seven upgrade slots, and lava can't burn it. A lever and an ingot make the \"},{\"text\":\"Diamond to Netherite Tier Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedstorage:diamond_to_netherite_tier_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": 132 slots.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Lava can't touch it, but the void still can: that's the job of the \"},{\"text\":\"Everlasting Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedbackpacks:everlasting_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6C55F3222E7BCBC8.title": "Mara's margin",
  "quest.6C55F3222E7BCBC8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Heliodor packed for journeys, never for returns. Every bag in the ruins is still full. Carry what one day asks for, and leave the rest where someone can find it. —M.\",\"italic\":true}]"
  ],
  "quest.6646D3E1F66DEA4B.title": "The right tool, always",
  "quest.6646D3E1F66DEA4B.quest_subtitle": "Your pickaxe finds itself.",
  "quest.6646D3E1F66DEA4B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A wooden sword, pickaxe, axe and shovel, two iron and two redstone on a base: a \"},{\"text\":\"Tool Swapper Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedbackpacks:tool_swapper_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Left-click a block or a mob and the right tool from the backpack jumps into your hand.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.74BC5EF7BFD7954D.title": "Wrench on demand",
  "quest.74BC5EF7BFD7954D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Advanced Tool Swapper Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedbackpacks:advanced_tool_swapper_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" adds filters and a key of its own, unbound until you set it in Controls: look at a machine, press \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.sophisticatedbackpacks.tool_swap\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" and the wrench that fits it is in your hand. One wrench per mod, zero digging.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5D9D8387912C5D40.title": "Lunch is packed",
  "quest.5D9D8387912C5D40.quest_subtitle": "Mom packed it.",
  "quest.5D9D8387912C5D40.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A golden carrot, a golden apple, a glistering melon slice and an ender pearl on a base: a \"},{\"text\":\"Feeding Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedbackpacks:feeding_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". You eat from the backpack when hungry, and its tab sets how hungry so no food goes to waste.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7AB955768B696852.title": "Self-service potions",
  "quest.7AB955768B696852.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A ghast tear, a glass bottle, a fermented spider eye, two blaze rods, two iron and an ender pearl make an \"},{\"text\":\"Alchemy Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedbackpacks:alchemy_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It drinks potions, eats effect food or milk from the backpack when you say: on fire, underwater, falling, hurt.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Fire Resistance set to 'On Fire' is a lava swim you walk out of.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3F8E6EEF8C9BAAA7.title": "Never the last torch",
  "quest.3F8E6EEF8C9BAAA7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An ender pearl, two iron, two redstone and a chest on a base: a \"},{\"text\":\"Refill Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedbackpacks:refill_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It keeps the stacks you pick topped up in your inventory from the backpack. The \"},{\"text\":\"Advanced Refill Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedbackpacks:advanced_refill_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" picks the slot, and middle-click pulls blocks out of the backpack.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2C9867271C931906.title": "The trip home, one click",
  "quest.2C9867271C931906.quest_subtitle": "Unpacking is for other people.",
  "quest.2C9867271C931906.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A piston or a sticky piston with iron, redstone and a chest: \"},{\"text\":\"Deposit Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedbackpacks:deposit_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and \"},{\"text\":\"Restock Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedbackpacks:restock_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Sneak-right-click a chest with the backpack in hand, or look at it and press \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.sophisticatedbackpacks.inventory_interaction\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\": one unloads, the other fills the backpack.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.71A1D342D8870E09.title": "Pocket pets",
  "quest.71A1D342D8870E09.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An ender pearl, two iron and two leads on a base: a \"},{\"text\":\"Mob Catcher Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedbackpacks:mob_catcher_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Sneak-right-click a passive mob to stow it in the backpack, where it takes slots by size. The advanced one, made with a wither skeleton skull, takes hostile mobs too.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2789AFDD6A9EC444.title": "A table in a tab",
  "quest.2789AFDD6A9EC444.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A crafting table, two iron and a chest on a base give the \"},{\"text\":\"Crafting Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedbackpacks:crafting_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; a stonecutter, two iron and a redstone give the \"},{\"text\":\"Stonecutter Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedbackpacks:stonecutter_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Each opens as a tab and works straight from the backpack.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.28E3058FA7EF46FD.title": "Workshop radio",
  "quest.28E3058FA7EF46FD.quest_subtitle": "Aux cable not included.",
  "quest.28E3058FA7EF46FD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A jukebox, two iron and a redstone on a base: the \"},{\"text\":\"Jukebox Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedbackpacks:jukebox_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" plays a disc wherever you go. The \"},{\"text\":\"Advanced Jukebox Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedbackpacks:advanced_jukebox_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" holds 12 discs and plays them in order, shuffled or on repeat.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5ADC597B6647DF0E.title": "Forge on the go",
  "quest.5ADC597B6647DF0E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two anvils, a diamond, two iron and a chest make the \"},{\"text\":\"Anvil Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedbackpacks:anvil_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; a smithing table, two iron and a chest make the \"},{\"text\":\"Smithing Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedbackpacks:smithing_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Repairs, names and netherite work, far from home.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.57C73008F5D924B2.title": "Chisel in the pocket",
  "quest.57C73008F5D924B2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Every Chipped workbench, with two iron and a redstone on a base, becomes an upgrade: the \"},{\"text\":\"Chipped: Mason Table Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedbackpacks:chipped/mason_table_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" turns stone into its variants from a tab. Seven tables, seven upgrades.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.47B1F8F28F1C8F86.title": "Pocket furnace",
  "quest.47B1F8F28F1C8F86.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A furnace, two iron and four redstone on a base: a \"},{\"text\":\"Smelting Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedbackpacks:smelting_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a furnace in a tab. Four logs around it make the \"},{\"text\":\"Smoking Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedbackpacks:smoking_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; five iron and three smooth stone, the \"},{\"text\":\"Blasting Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedbackpacks:blasting_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.25032CE2BB19689F.title": "It cooks while you walk",
  "quest.25032CE2BB19689F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two diamonds, three hoppers, a redstone and two gold around a smelting upgrade: an \"},{\"text\":\"Auto-smelting Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedbackpacks:auto_smelting_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It takes ore and fuel from the backpack by its filters and puts the ingots back in.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4C743BC0B3EFF3A8.title": "One door for every chest",
  "quest.4C743BC0B3EFF3A8.quest_subtitle": "Sorting, solved. Mostly.",
  "quest.4C743BC0B3EFF3A8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Stone, two comparators, two planks and a wooden chest or barrel make a \"},{\"text\":\"Storage Controller\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedstorage:controller\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Every Sophisticated storage touching it, or touching one that does, up to 15 blocks away, becomes one inventory for you and for pipes.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Right-click it with a stack and the stack goes where that item already lives. Click twice fast and everything you carry that has a home goes in.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.12D8EBA833E0B586.title": "Far-flung shelves",
  "quest.12D8EBA833E0B586.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Storage Link\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedstorage:storage_link\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" adds a separate cluster of storage to the controller; bind it with the \"},{\"text\":\"Storage Tool\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedstorage:storage_tool\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". The tool also locks storage and hides the counts, tiers and upgrades shown on its face.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A controller and an ender pearl make three links at once.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6F931B1EDAEE841B.title": "A port for pipes",
  "quest.6F931B1EDAEE841B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Stone, planks, a repeater, gold and a wooden storage make \"},{\"text\":\"Storage I/O\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedstorage:storage_io\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": set in the multiblock, it gives pipes one face to push into and pull from. Crafted alone it turns into Input and Output, which only take or only give.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.24B436B63D38F3BC.title": "Hopper built in",
  "quest.24B436B63D38F3BC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A hopper, two iron and three redstone on a Sophisticated Storage base: a \"},{\"text\":\"Hopper Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedstorage:hopper_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". The storage pulls from the block above and pushes into the one below. The advanced one is faster and works through any side.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.02E23FB0BE8B714A.title": "The chest that collects",
  "quest.02E23FB0BE8B714A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A chest with a magnet upgrade pulls items from 3 blocks around it, 5 advanced. Next to the kill floor of a mob farm, nothing is left on the ground.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7C70F44455221695.title": "The same chest everywhere",
  "quest.7C70F44455221695.quest_subtitle": "Teleportation, for socks.",
  "quest.7C70F44455221695.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Blaze rods, wool, obsidian, a wooden chest and a \"},{\"text\":\"Reinforced Alloy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:alloy_reinforced\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make an \"},{\"text\":\"Ender Storage chest\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"enderstorage:ender_chest\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": 27 slots shared with every chest of the same three colors, in any dimension. In this pack the alloy takes the ender pearl's place (act III).\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Dye the three buttons on the lid to set the colors. A diamond on the latch makes it yours alone.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.57312756653E2471.title": "Shared tank",
  "quest.57312756653E2471.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The same frame around a cauldron makes an \"},{\"text\":\"Ender Storage tank\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"enderstorage:ender_tank\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": 16 buckets of fluid shared with every tank of its colors. With a redstone signal it pushes fluid into the blocks around it; a click on the valve inverts that.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7C430F071F537F08.title": "A chest in your pocket",
  "quest.7C430F071F537F08.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Blaze powder, leather, wool, an ender pearl and a reinforced alloy make an \"},{\"text\":\"Ender Storage pouch\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"enderstorage:ender_pouch\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Sneak-right-click an Ender Storage chest to copy its colors; from then on the pouch opens that chest wherever you are.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3CD9F01DEB4EFCC2.title": "Pick a team code",
  "quest.3CD9F01DEB4EFCC2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Three colors out of sixteen give 4,096 frequencies. Agree on one with the team: a supply chest at home, a pouch for each explorer and a tank at the far base for lava.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2165179220C8395C.title": "More per slot",
  "quest.2165179220C8395C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight copper blocks around a base make a \"},{\"text\":\"Stack Upgrade Starter Tier\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedbackpacks:stack_upgrade_starter_tier\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": each slot holds one and a half stacks. Iron, gold, diamond and netherite blocks climb to ×2, ×4, ×8 and ×16. Up to three per backpack.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.041A907A91FB513B.title": "Chests stack for cheap",
  "quest.041A907A91FB513B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Chests have their own ladder, and it starts with eight logs around a Sophisticated Storage base: \"},{\"text\":\"Stack Upgrade Tier 1\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedstorage:stack_upgrade_tier_1\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", ×2. Copper, iron, gold, diamond and netherite go up to ×32. Two per chest, barrel or shulker box.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.249A414C200406B9.title": "A backpack in a backpack",
  "quest.249A414C200406B9.quest_subtitle": "We need to go deeper.",
  "quest.249A414C200406B9.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four eyes of ender, a nether star and three diamonds on a base: an \"},{\"text\":\"Inception Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedbackpacks:inception_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Backpacks fit inside the backpack, and their upgrades keep working from in there.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.67F8DF112006E85F.title": "Built to outlast you",
  "quest.67F8DF112006E85F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four end crystals and four nether stars on a base: an \"},{\"text\":\"Everlasting Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedbackpacks:everlasting_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". The backpack can't be destroyed, never despawns and doesn't fall out of the world. Die in the void and it waits for you.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.247E02B8BEE99820.title": "Omega",
  "quest.247E02B8BEE99820.quest_subtitle": "Somebody had to.",
  "quest.247E02B8BEE99820.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Nine times the \"},{\"text\":\"Stack Upgrade Tier 4\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedbackpacks:stack_upgrade_tier_4\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", each built on eight netherite blocks, make the \"},{\"text\":\"Stack Upgrade Omega Tier\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedbackpacks:stack_upgrade_omega_tier\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": every slot times 33,554,431. Seventy-two netherite blocks for a very tidy backpack.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.0F1E6A3C690F6503.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.14EF23378364326D.title": "Less is less",
  "quest.14EF23378364326D.quest_subtitle": "Two cobblestones per slot. On purpose.",
  "quest.14EF23378364326D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Flint and sticks on a base make a \"},{\"text\":\"Stack Downgrade Tier 3\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedbackpacks:stack_downgrade_tier_3\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": every slot now holds a stack divided by 32. Somewhere, a sorting machine needed exactly that.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.5C32C38EBB212869.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.0C9552E3AC39EE25.title": "No infinity here",
  "quest.0C9552E3AC39EE25.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The infinity upgrades of both Sophisticated mods and the \"},{\"text\":\"Creative Vending Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"functionalstorage:creative_vending_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" have no recipe in this pack, on purpose: they copy any item, and that would break Solsticio's trade and the Luminosities.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.68556759C44943D7.title": "Water to go",
  "quest.68556759C44943D7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight glass around a base: a \"},{\"text\":\"Tank Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedbackpacks:tank_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It trades some slots for a fluid tank of 4 buckets per row of the backpack, and stack upgrades grow it too. Fill and empty it with buckets in its slots.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.702BAF75086AEB1C.title": "Charged up",
  "quest.702BAF75086AEB1C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four gold and four redstone blocks on a base: a \"},{\"text\":\"Battery Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedbackpacks:battery_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", 10,000 FE per row of the backpack. Charge it through its slots or, with the backpack set down, from a cable.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3E95CF62E84785AA.title": "Pump it",
  "quest.3E95CF62E84785AA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four glass, two buckets, a piston and a sticky piston on a base: the \"},{\"text\":\"Pump Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedbackpacks:pump_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" moves fluid between the tank and the blocks around a backpack set down. The advanced one also drinks from the world and from buckets in your hand.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.59E5ED4EFBBD116C.title": "Bank your levels",
  "quest.59E5ED4EFBBD116C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two bottles o' enchanting, two eyes of ender and four redstone around an advanced pump: an \"},{\"text\":\"Experience Pump Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedbackpacks:xp_pump_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It stores your levels in the tank, hands them back or keeps you at a set level, and feeds Mending tools.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4EF5D55CA3A51F5A.title": "Interior design",
  "quest.4EF5D55CA3A51F5A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Logs, planks and a Sophisticated Storage base make a \"},{\"text\":\"Decoration Table\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedstorage:decoration_table\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": new materials, colors and accents for Sophisticated storage. A \"},{\"text\":\"Paintbrush\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedstorage:paintbrush\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" set at the table applies that look to storage already in place.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.730D9F45B252B76A.title": "Storage that looks like furniture",
  "quest.730D9F45B252B76A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Storage Delight turns slabs and trapdoors into kitchen furniture that holds 27 slots: an \"},{\"text\":\"Oak Drawer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"storagedelight:oak_drawer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", an \"},{\"text\":\"Oak Cabinet with Polished Andesite Countertop\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"storagedelight:oak_cabinet_with_polished_andesite_countertop\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", glass cabinets and bookshelves with doors, in every wood.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"They burn like planks, so a wrong craft still heats the furnace.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7B041D0F6A415B3F.title": "Take out the trash",
  "quest.7B041D0F6A415B3F.quest_subtitle": "Don't forget to recycle. It won't.",
  "quest.7B041D0F6A415B3F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three stone, five cobblestone and a chest: an \"},{\"text\":\"Item Trash Can\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"trashcans:item_trash_can\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It deletes whatever pipes or hands put in, with a nine-item filter that allows or blocks. Its screen can hand back the last few items, for misclicks.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.62B0FE2281172662.title": "Down the drain",
  "quest.62B0FE2281172662.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A bucket in place of the chest: a \"},{\"text\":\"Fluid Trash Can\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"trashcans:liquid_trash_can\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It voids liquids and gases, with a nine-fluid filter. It refuses Mekanism's radioactive waste: that gets dealt with, not hidden.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.18D6A20476704DC7.title": "Burn off the surplus",
  "quest.18D6A20476704DC7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Redstone in place of the chest: an \"},{\"text\":\"Energy Trash Can\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"trashcans:energy_trash_can\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It swallows energy, all of it or up to a limit you set in FE per tick, which makes it a handy dummy load for testing generators.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4637164EC0DE5FA4.title": "One bin for everything",
  "quest.4637164EC0DE5FA4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The three cans together in the crafting grid make an \"},{\"text\":\"Ultimate Trash Can\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"trashcans:ultimate_trash_can\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": items, fluids and energy, each with its own filter or limit.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.00E5D95C0155A1B1.title": "A lot of one thing",
  "quest.00E5D95C0155A1B1.quest_subtitle": "Marie Kondo approves.",
  "quest.00E5D95C0155A1B1.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight planks around a chest: an \"},{\"text\":\"Oak Drawer (1x1)\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"functionalstorage:oak_1\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" holds 32 stacks of one item, shown on its face. Right-click to put in, double right-click to put in every matching stack you carry; left-click takes one, sneak-left-click a stack.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Sneak-right-click opens its upgrade slots.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2FBFCD89DA3CCDF8.title": "Split drawers",
  "quest.2FBFCD89DA3CCDF8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two chests make a pair of the \"},{\"text\":\"Oak Drawer (1x2)\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"functionalstorage:oak_2\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", 16 stacks per compartment; four chests make four of the \"},{\"text\":\"Oak Drawer (2x2)\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"functionalstorage:oak_4\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", 8 stacks each. Same space, more kinds of item.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.549845D2797BA5B0.title": "Liquid assets",
  "quest.549845D2797BA5B0.quest_subtitle": "Buckets not included. Well, one is.",
  "quest.549845D2797BA5B0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight planks around an empty bucket: a \"},{\"text\":\"Fluid Drawer (1x1)\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"functionalstorage:fluid_1\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It keeps one fluid the way a drawer keeps an item; fill and drain it with buckets or pipes.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.32B8755F62256BB1.title": "Nine in, one out",
  "quest.32B8755F62256BB1.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Stone, two pistons, a drawer and an iron ingot make a \"},{\"text\":\"Compacting Drawer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"functionalstorage:compacting_drawer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": one material in three forms that convert by themselves. Put in iron ingots and it also offers nuggets and blocks. The \"},{\"text\":\"Simple Compacting Drawer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"functionalstorage:simple_compacting_drawer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" handles two forms.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6497C389DD3537F4.title": "Not just metals",
  "quest.6497C389DD3537F4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Compacting drawers also know melon slices and melons, ice to packed ice to blue ice, quartz, amethyst shards and glowstone dust. The end of a melon farm deserves one.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3F2AB889FCBD78E5.title": "Hidden in plain sight",
  "quest.3F2AB889FCBD78E5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Iron nuggets around a chest make a \"},{\"text\":\"Framed Drawer (1x1)\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"functionalstorage:framed_1\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". In the crafting grid, give it one block for the outside, one for the inside and one for the divider, and it wears their textures.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.11771CC46C1158B2.title": "The armory",
  "quest.11771CC46C1158B2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Stone, three drawers, a comparator and a netherite ingot make an \"},{\"text\":\"Armory Cabinet\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"functionalstorage:armory_cabinet\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": 4,096 slots for what doesn't stack, like tools, armor and enchanted books, one item per slot.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.33DD3545E3DC75C6.title": "The drawer wall",
  "quest.33DD3545E3DC75C6.quest_subtitle": "It knows where everything is.",
  "quest.33DD3545E3DC75C6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Stone, two quartz blocks, two drawers and a comparator make a \"},{\"text\":\"Storage Controller\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"functionalstorage:storage_controller\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Drawers linked to it within 8 blocks become one inventory: right-click it with anything to file it in the right drawer, and pipe into it.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Storage upgrades in the controller's own slots widen its reach.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0AA9FE2BC08B2311.title": "Link them up",
  "quest.0AA9FE2BC08B2311.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Five paper, two gold, a drawer and a diamond make a \"},{\"text\":\"Linking Tool\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"functionalstorage:linking_tool\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Right-click the controller, then the drawers to link; sneak-right-click the air for multiple mode, which links everything between two corners. Holding it shows what's linked.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5BC2EE2B5C484C5F.title": "Another door",
  "quest.5BC2EE2B5C484C5F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The controller's recipe with a repeater in the middle makes a \"},{\"text\":\"Controller Access Point\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"functionalstorage:controller_extension\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": another face of the same wall, somewhere else, for hands or pipes.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7396A619FAECDE1A.title": "A drawer with a twin",
  "quest.7396A619FAECDE1A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Planks, two drawers and an ender chest make an \"},{\"text\":\"Ender Drawer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"functionalstorage:ender_drawer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": every ender drawer on the same frequency shares one slot. Left-click one with the linking tool to copy its frequency, right-click another to paste it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.72E3F9606C4E812E.title": "Label it",
  "quest.72E3F9606C4E812E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Paper, gold, a drawer and an emerald make a \"},{\"text\":\"Configuration Tool\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"functionalstorage:configuration_tool\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Lock a drawer to its item so the place stays when it empties, or hide counts, icons and upgrades; sneak-right-click the air to change what it toggles.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.799B566A885ECFC8.title": "Sort once, then automate",
  "quest.799B566A885ECFC8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Drawers for the few items you have thousands of, chests for everything else, a backpack with Deposit for the trip home and a void upgrade on the cobblestone drawer. Future you finds everything on the first try.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0B98E9CC224A0976.title": "Bigger drawers",
  "quest.0B98E9CC224A0976.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Copper ingots and blocks, two chests and a drawer make a \"},{\"text\":\"Copper Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"functionalstorage:copper_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": ×8 capacity in a drawer's storage slots. Built one on the other, the \"},{\"text\":\"Gold Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"functionalstorage:gold_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" gives ×16 and the \"},{\"text\":\"Diamond Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"functionalstorage:diamond_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" ×24.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5B2BCD66CABD0839.title": "Top drawer",
  "quest.5B2BCD66CABD0839.quest_subtitle": "Literally.",
  "quest.5B2BCD66CABD0839.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"First a \"},{\"text\":\"Diamond Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"functionalstorage:diamond_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; then, with a netherite ingot and a smithing template at a smithing table, the \"},{\"text\":\"Netherite Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"functionalstorage:netherite_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", ×32. An oak drawer with it holds 1,024 stacks of one item.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.52487C7FD4D9671E.title": "No pipes needed",
  "quest.52487C7FD4D9671E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Stone, a hopper, redstone and a drawer make a \"},{\"text\":\"Puller Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"functionalstorage:puller_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; crafted alone it turns into a \"},{\"text\":\"Pusher Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"functionalstorage:pusher_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and back. Every 4 ticks they move 4 items or 500 mB through the side you pick in the drawer's screen.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.645F5B27D508A238.title": "Never full",
  "quest.645F5B27D508A238.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight obsidian around a drawer: a \"},{\"text\":\"Void Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"functionalstorage:void_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". When the drawer is full, the excess vanishes instead of backing up the machine that feeds it. A cobblestone generator's best friend.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7F095E769E5FE2FD.title": "Floor sweeper",
  "quest.7F095E769E5FE2FD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two hoppers, two redstone, stone and a drawer make a \"},{\"text\":\"Collector Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"functionalstorage:collector_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": the drawer picks up the items lying on the side you choose, and a fluid drawer picks up fluid blocks.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.34B97CF9A4063608.title": "How full is it?",
  "quest.34B97CF9A4063608.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Redstone, two comparators, two redstone blocks and a drawer make a \"},{\"text\":\"Redstone Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"functionalstorage:redstone_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": the drawer gives off a signal by how full the slot you choose is. Wire it to stop a farm before the shelf overflows.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.161FE65B90F335F3.title": "Drawers that make things",
  "quest.161FE65B90F335F3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Stone, two water buckets and a bucket make a \"},{\"text\":\"Water Generator Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"functionalstorage:water_generator_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": a fluid drawer with it never runs out of water. A \"},{\"text\":\"Dripping Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"functionalstorage:dripping_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" drips a little lava.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four dripping upgrades and a water generator make the \"},{\"text\":\"Obsidian Generator Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"functionalstorage:obsidian_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": one obsidian every 15 seconds, in an item drawer.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4E9F2C9D2528EBC8.title": "Tools on the hip",
  "quest.4E9F2C9D2528EBC8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Five leather, two string and an iron ingot make a \"},{\"text\":\"Tool Belt\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"toolbelt:belt\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" with two pockets. Wear it in the belt slot, which \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.toolbelt.slot\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" opens, and hold \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.toolbelt.open\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" for a wheel that swaps your hand with a belt tool.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5BC7A61EE2344022.title": "One more pocket",
  "quest.5BC7A61EE2344022.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four string, three leather and a gold ingot make a \"},{\"text\":\"Belt Pouch\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"toolbelt:pouch\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". A belt and a pouch in an anvil add one pocket, up to nine. Each step costs more levels, from 3 to 30.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.386A4771C4C3A58C.title": "A Tool Belt with nine pockets",
  "quest.7E6689470068C322.title": "Nine pockets",
  "quest.7E6689470068C322.quest_subtitle": "Ninety-three levels well spent.",
  "quest.7E6689470068C322.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Tool Belt\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"toolbelt:belt\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" with all nine pockets. The anvil's bill came to 93 levels, and not one was wasted.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.45CB5DFCDA3F36AF.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.5244F747EC00E74D.title": "Barrels for the common store",
  "quest.5244F747EC00E74D.quest_subtitle": "There's always room for more room.",
  "quest.5244F747EC00E74D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight \"},{\"text\":\"Sophisticated barrels\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sophisticatedstorage:barrel\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for the common store, once a day. With a tree farm, it's a short errand.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.784E50C18918D17E.title": "When a network pays off",
  "quest.784E50C18918D17E.quest_desc": [
    "Drawers and chests stop scaling when finding things takes longer than using them. Then comes a network: one terminal that searches everything, crafts on request and feeds machines. Applied Energistics 2 and Refined Storage have their own chapters."
  ],
  "image.6D6EDA1392D2AC52.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"On the road\",\"color\":\"#E8C48A\"}]",
  "image.6898F83E335B471A.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Workbench on your back\",\"color\":\"#E8C48A\"}]",
  "image.54BD546EFF120291.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Chests at work\",\"color\":\"#E8C48A\"}]",
  "image.0FAE105856933806.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Across dimensions\",\"color\":\"#E8C48A\"}]",
  "image.7AD93AF9DA46E79F.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Bigger inside\",\"color\":\"#E8C48A\"}]",
  "image.4AD695D8E77FE493.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Tanks and batteries\",\"color\":\"#E8C48A\"}]",
  "image.0FAE4FD69A78B091.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Good looks\",\"color\":\"#E8C48A\"}]",
  "image.0A264A0D51DB8B65.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Overflow\",\"color\":\"#E8C48A\"}]",
  "image.61D747E42E228DD0.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Drawers\",\"color\":\"#E8C48A\"}]",
  "image.04E9740130FDA170.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"One wall, one face\",\"color\":\"#E8C48A\"}]",
  "image.5AE49BA6D2F27015.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Drawer upgrades\",\"color\":\"#E8C48A\"}]",
  "image.3A4FADA58DFEF569.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"On the hip\",\"color\":\"#E8C48A\"}]",
  "image.14519ACAEB308140.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Storage and Backpacks\",\"color\":\"#E8C48A\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.0F9F507E1AD133C2.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"what travels what stays\",\"color\":\"#E8C48A\",\"font\":\"minecraft:alt\"}]",
  "image.62F1D2C11BB527D7.title": "Back to the Sun of Heliodor",
  "image.7EA9EA5A393DF578.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Hands-free\",\"color\":\"#E8C48A\"}]",
  "image.5C30BF45F0280271.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Chests and barrels\",\"color\":\"#E8C48A\"}]",
  "image.767C46DFB07DB21B.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"One ladder\",\"color\":\"#E8C48A\"}]",
  "chapter.2F4D57204C0D4367.title": "Actually Additions",
  "chapter.2F4D57204C0D4367.chapter_subtitle": [
    "The Atomic Reconstructor's beam, six crystals and the Empowerer; laser relays, phantomfaces, farms, drills and coffee."
  ],
  "quest.0329621E779C4D03.title": "Black Quartz",
  "quest.0329621E779C4D03.quest_subtitle": "Nether quartz, dressed for a funeral.",
  "quest.0329621E779C4D03.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Black Quartz Ore\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:black_quartz_ore\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" hides in stone and deepslate between Y -25 and 45, eight veins to a chunk. Smelt or blast it; Fortune adds more.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Almost every Actually Additions recipe starts here: casings, coils, lenses, lamps. A \"},{\"text\":\"Crusher\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"2B97086271E1EA71\"}},{\"text\":\" gets two out of each ore.\"}]",
    "",
    "Old chests in dungeons, mineshafts, stronghold libraries, fortresses, end cities and a few more sometimes hold black quartz, crystals or a drill core."
  ],
  "quest.44119EC6EE0DCD9A.title": "Iron Casing",
  "quest.44119EC6EE0DCD9A.quest_desc": [
    "Four iron ingots at the corners, four sticks on the sides, a black quartz in the middle: the frame of most machines here. Make four; the coal generator takes two and the reconstructor one."
  ],
  "quest.0A875C7364794AE3.title": "Coal Generator",
  "quest.0A875C7364794AE3.quest_subtitle": "Whatever a furnace eats, it eats.",
  "quest.0A875C7364794AE3.quest_desc": [
    "Six cobblestone, two iron casings and a coal. It burns furnace fuel for 20 CF/t, stores 60,000 CF and only lights new fuel when it isn't full; a redstone signal stops it.",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"CF (Crystal Flux) is ordinary Forge Energy: cables and machines from other mods take it as it is.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1B0EC5EE12C42EFA.title": "Atomic Reconstructor",
  "quest.1B0EC5EE12C42EFA.quest_subtitle": "Point, shoot, transmute.",
  "quest.1B0EC5EE12C42EFA.quest_desc": [
    "Four iron, four redstone and a casing. Every five seconds it fires up to 10 blocks for 1,000 CF plus the recipe: the first block it hits changes, with the 3×3 around it facing the beam, and so do items dropped along the way.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A redstone signal switches it off; right-click it with a \"},{\"text\":\"Redstone Torch\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:redstone_torch\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and it fires only on pulses instead. It holds 300,000 CF, so one coal generator keeps it busy.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.451A755C39750036.title": "Four everyday crystals",
  "quest.451A755C39750036.quest_subtitle": "Redstone, lapis, iron and coal, now shiny.",
  "quest.451A755C39750036.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Drop the material in the beam: redstone turns into \"},{\"text\":\"Restonia\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:restonia_crystal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", lapis into \"},{\"text\":\"Palis\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:palis_crystal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", iron ingots into \"},{\"text\":\"Enori\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:enori_crystal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", coal or charcoal into \"},{\"text\":\"Void\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:void_crystal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". On top of the shot: 40, 40, 80 and 60 CF each.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Storage blocks convert too, nine crystals at once: a block of redstone becomes a \"},{\"text\":\"Restonia Crystal Block\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:restonia_crystal_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for 400 CF.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6A633E45285E72C9.title": "The precious two",
  "quest.6A633E45285E72C9.quest_subtitle": "Same beam, pricier lunch.",
  "quest.6A633E45285E72C9.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Diamonds turn into \"},{\"text\":\"Diamatine\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:diamatine_crystal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for 60 CF and emeralds into \"},{\"text\":\"Emeradic\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:emeradic_crystal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for 100. Diamatine goes into area augments, the Range Booster and the Handheld Filler; Emeradic, into the silk touch augment and little else.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1704D4962502E95E.title": "Basic and Advanced Coils",
  "quest.1704D4962502E95E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four Restonia around a black quartz make a \"},{\"text\":\"Basic Coil\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:basic_coil\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; eight gold nuggets around one of those make an \"},{\"text\":\"Advanced Coil\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:advanced_coil\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Nearly every machine from here on asks for one or the other.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5DDFAEAB5D453C56.title": "Four Display Stands",
  "quest.5DDFAEAB5D453C56.quest_subtitle": "Pedestals first, altar second.",
  "quest.5DDFAEAB5D453C56.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The beam turns a quartz block into \"},{\"text\":\"Ethetic Quartz\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:ethetic_white_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a chiseled one into \"},{\"text\":\"Ethetic Green Quartz\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:ethetic_green_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", 10 CF each. Three of each under an advanced coil make a \"},{\"text\":\"Display Stand\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:display_stand\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; the Empowerer wants four.\"}]",
    "",
    "On its own, a stand shows off whatever you right-click onto it."
  ],
  "quest.521902565B5E1FF5.title": "Single and Double Batteries",
  "quest.521902565B5E1FF5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Restonia over an advanced coil and five Enori makes a \"},{\"text\":\"Single Battery\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:single_battery\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (200,000 CF); a single battery in the Restonia's place makes a \"},{\"text\":\"Double Battery\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:double_battery\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (350,000), charge kept. The Empowerer is built on a double.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Hold one, \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.sneak\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" and right-click: in discharge mode it charges the other items in your inventory.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1E645F439719399C.title": "Empowerer",
  "quest.1E645F439719399C.quest_subtitle": "An altar with four assistants.",
  "quest.1E645F439719399C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Restonia, a double battery, two iron casings and a display stand. Place it, then a \"},{\"text\":\"Display Stand\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:display_stand\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" three blocks away in each of the four directions: the crystal goes on the Empowerer, one modifier on each stand.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Each stand holds 80,000 CF, takes 1,000 CF/t and pays its share while it works: 5,000 over two and a half seconds for a crystal. No power in the stands, no deal."
  ],
  "quest.16AB01C7FF8B59A8.title": "First empowered crystal",
  "quest.16AB01C7FF8B59A8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Restonia on the Empowerer; red dye, a nether brick, redstone and a brick on the four stands; power in. Two and a half seconds later: \"},{\"text\":\"Empowered Restonia\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:empowered_restonia_crystal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.59822045237A8D4D.title": "Empower whole blocks",
  "quest.59822045237A8D4D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A crystal block takes the same four modifiers as a single crystal: nine crystals for four modifiers and 200,000 CF, against 36 modifiers and 180,000 CF one by one. Each stand pays 50,000 of it and holds 80,000, so it fits.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.51416817D54FBE2D.title": "Six crystals, empowered",
  "quest.51416817D54FBE2D.quest_subtitle": "The emerald one is just for show.",
  "quest.51416817D54FBE2D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Empower all six; each takes its own four modifiers. \"},{\"text\":\"Palis\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:empowered_palis_crystal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": cyan dye and three prismarine shards. \"},{\"text\":\"Diamatine\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:empowered_diamatine_crystal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": light blue dye, two clay balls and a clay block. \"},{\"text\":\"Void\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:empowered_void_crystal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": black dye, coal, flint and stone.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Emeradic\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:empowered_emeradic_crystal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": lime dye, short grass, a sapling and a slimeball. \"},{\"text\":\"Enori\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:empowered_enori_crystal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": gray dye, a snowball, a stone button and cobblestone.\"}]",
    "",
    "Item laser relays can load the stands for you. No recipe asks for Empowered Emeradic: that one is for the shelf."
  ],
  "quest.73AC1DB6491C9600.title": "A crate of crystals",
  "quest.73AC1DB6491C9600.quest_subtitle": "Red and blue, by the dozen.",
  "quest.73AC1DB6491C9600.quest_desc": [
    "Thirty-two Restonia and thirty-two Palis for the common store, once a day. A 3×3 wall of redstone blocks where the beam stops, then one of lapis blocks, covers an order in two shots."
  ],
  "task.4E3B5F862EA00590.title": "Open the Actually Additions Manual",
  "quest.54BCE8D235829045.title": "A manual under construction",
  "quest.54BCE8D235829045.quest_subtitle": "Five entries and a lot of goodwill.",
  "quest.54BCE8D235829045.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Paper and \"},{\"text\":\"Canola Seeds\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:canola_seeds\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make the \"},{\"text\":\"Actually Additions Manual\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:booklet\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; right-click opens it. This version has five entries, crystals and the Engineers' house among them, so EMI carries the rest.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Canola grows wild in hot or sparse biomes and in some village fields; the \"},{\"text\":\"Market\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"50A6912B6169501B\"}},{\"text\":\" sells its seeds.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Villages can build the Engineers' house: its chests hold casings, black quartz and crystals, now and then a drill core, and its garden grows canola, coffee, flax and rice.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.356CFF06141D0852.title": "What the pack adds",
  "quest.356CFF06141D0852.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Actually Additions keeps its own recipes here. Two of its crystals feed the Atlas: two Restonia go into the \"},{\"text\":\"Energy Coupler\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:energy_coupler\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for \"},{\"text\":\"A Crystal Connection\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"5281CA2BAADED9DF\"}},{\"text\":\" (act II), two Palis into the \"},{\"text\":\"Routing Matrix\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:routing_matrix\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for \"},{\"text\":\"A Shared Language\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"17BBD680007901AB\"}},{\"text\":\" (act III).\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4AFC77B063DB1B2F.title": "Lamps and a controller",
  "quest.4AFC77B063DB1B2F.quest_subtitle": "One switch, a whole ceiling.",
  "quest.4AFC77B063DB1B2F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four glowstone, two Palis, two dyes and a black quartz make six lamps; dye one in place to recolour it, right-click to switch it. A \"},{\"text\":\"Lamp Controller\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:lamp_controller\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" facing a lamp switches it, and every lamp touching it, with one redstone signal.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Black quartz also comes as blocks, pillars, chiseled, smooth and bricks, each with stairs, slabs and walls. Paper with a drill core, a leaf blower, a phantom connector or the Manual gives a banner pattern."
  ],
  "quest.00BB4463AE6EC36A.title": "Batting practice",
  "quest.00BB4463AE6EC36A.quest_subtitle": "Sorry, little guy.",
  "quest.00BB4463AE6EC36A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Bat's Wing\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:bats_wing\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": bats killed by a player drop them, and old chests hide a few. Its one recipe is the Wings of the Bats, still marked unfinished in this version, with an Ender Star in the middle.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.1121685799177631.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.0A8C6CDCDF2E1458.title": "Two bosses in one star",
  "quest.0A8C6CDCDF2E1458.quest_subtitle": "Leftovers from the Wither and the Dragon.",
  "quest.0A8C6CDCDF2E1458.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Nether Star, Dragon's Breath, a black quartz and a prismarine shard: an \"},{\"text\":\"Ender Star\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:ender_star\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It goes into the Wings of the Bats, which this version still marks as unfinished, so for now it mostly sparkles.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.6926B2C4EDFFDAF6.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.271551CB4A93BB2E.title": "A blank lens",
  "quest.271551CB4A93BB2E.quest_subtitle": "Glass, with ambitions.",
  "quest.271551CB4A93BB2E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight glass around a black quartz make a \"},{\"text\":\"Lens\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:lens\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", the blank every other lens starts from. Right-click the reconstructor with a finished lens to fit it; an empty hand takes it back. A fitted lens replaces the plain conversion.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7D8B4263D0CEB0EB.title": "One lens, three lenses",
  "quest.7D8B4263D0CEB0EB.quest_subtitle": "Colour, boom, doom.",
  "quest.7D8B4263D0CEB0EB.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Drop a lens in the beam: each hit turns it into the next, 5,000 CF a step. \"},{\"text\":\"Color\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:lens_of_color\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" recolours wool, glass, terracotta and lamps; \"},{\"text\":\"Detonation\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:lens_of_detonation\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" sets off a big blast that breaks no blocks; \"},{\"text\":\"Certain Death\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:lens_of_certain_death\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" deals 20 damage through armour.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Certain Death kills an unprotected player in one shot.\",\"color\":\"#FF8C7A\"},{\"text\":\" Detonation pays 250,000 CF a blast and reaches 30 blocks; Certain Death, 350 CF per victim and 15 blocks. One more hit turns it back into a blank lens.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A diamond sword and a Sharpness V book turn Certain Death into the unfinished \"},{\"text\":\"Lens of the Killer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:lens_of_the_killer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", which also drops loot and experience, for 2,500 CF a victim.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.176D11288A522F84.title": "Lens of the Miner",
  "quest.176D11288A522F84.quest_subtitle": "Stone in, ore out, CF gone.",
  "quest.176D11288A522F84.quest_desc": [
    "A lens ringed by a diamond, gold, iron, coal, black quartz, quartz, lapis and an emerald. Fitted, each shot turns the stone, granite, diorite or andesite it hits into a random ore for 60,000 CF: coal and copper often, diamonds and emeralds rarely.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Deepslate and tuff give deepslate ores. Netherrack gives nether quartz, nether gold and, very rarely, \"},{\"text\":\"Ancient Debris\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:ancient_debris\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". The stone list also has black quartz and ores from Mekanism, Powah, Immersive Engineering and Modern Industrialization.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2C7F9AFA32E04AE3.title": "Lens of Disenchanting",
  "quest.2C7F9AFA32E04AE3.quest_subtitle": "Give it back, politely.",
  "quest.2C7F9AFA32E04AE3.quest_desc": [
    "A lens, an enchanting table and seven Empowered Diamatine. Drop one enchanted item and one book, plain or enchanted, into the same block in the beam: the item's top enchantment moves onto the book, for 250,000 CF. It reaches 5 blocks."
  ],
  "quest.43689517C893C3AD.title": "Hands-free crystals",
  "quest.43689517C893C3AD.quest_subtitle": "Drop, zap, collect, repeat.",
  "quest.43689517C893C3AD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Aim an \"},{\"text\":\"Automatic Precision Dropper\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:dropper\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" into the beam's path: it drops one item every quarter second, straight ahead, no redstone needed. A \"},{\"text\":\"Ranged Collector\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:ranged_collector\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" within 6 blocks, set to take only crystals, gathers the results.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0083A93C97189499.title": "Whole stacks, whole walls",
  "quest.0083A93C97189499.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A dropped stack converts in a single shot, as many items as the stored CF pays for. Where the beam stops, the 3×3 facing it converts too: a wall of nine redstone blocks becomes nine Restonia blocks at once.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.21BF555D1E2AFCF1.title": "Not only crystals",
  "quest.21BF555D1E2AFCF1.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The bare beam also turns rotten flesh into leather and sand into soul sand (20,000 CF each), nether quartz into prismarine shards (30,000) and a red mushroom into nether wart (150,000).\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.13CFB7AFD9D8245C.title": "Coffee beans",
  "quest.13CFB7AFD9D8245C.quest_subtitle": "Grown in the heat.",
  "quest.13CFB7AFD9D8245C.quest_desc": [
    "Coffee grows wild in hot biomes and in some village fields, and the beans are also its seeds. The Coffee Maker turns each bean into two portions and a cup takes 35, so eighteen beans make the first cup."
  ],
  "quest.72A03400402FAEE6.title": "Coffee Maker",
  "quest.72A03400402FAEE6.quest_subtitle": "Brewed on CF.",
  "quest.72A03400402FAEE6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Coffee beans, an iron casing, two basic coils and a Void crystal. It takes beans, water and an \"},{\"text\":\"Empty Cup\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:empty_cup\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (six stone around a bean); each cup costs 500 mB of water and 150 CF/t for 25 seconds.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.277920AB9FEE6CFC.title": "A cup of coffee",
  "quest.277920AB9FEE6CFC.quest_subtitle": "Three sips, then the cup comes back.",
  "quest.277920AB9FEE6CFC.quest_desc": [
    "Items in the eight ingredient slots add effects: sugar gives Speed, blaze powder Strength, magma cream Fire Resistance, a golden carrot Night Vision. The same item twice raises the level. Each cup is three sips worth 8 hunger points each, and the cup comes back."
  ],
  "quest.39029CCCCD6FBA79.title": "The full menu",
  "quest.39029CCCCD6FBA79.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Also: a pufferfish gives Water Breathing, a ghast tear Regeneration, a fermented spider eye Invisibility. Sugar and blaze powder stack four times, ghast tears three, the rest twice. Each effect lasts 5 to 30 seconds a sip: coffee is a sprint, not a potion.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.52F988DC169DB793.title": "Energy Laser Relays",
  "quest.52F988DC169DB793.quest_subtitle": "Cables are so last century.",
  "quest.52F988DC169DB793.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Obsidian, redstone blocks, Restonia and an advanced coil make four \"},{\"text\":\"Energy Laser Relays\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:laser_relay\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Right-click one with the \"},{\"text\":\"Laser Wrench\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:laser_wrench\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", then another up to 15 blocks away: every relay in the network moves CF between the blocks beside it.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Linking two linked relays again unlinks them. The loss is taken once per transfer, not per hop, so a long chain costs the same as a short one. Four stands around an Empowerer, one relay each, is the classic."
  ],
  "quest.236E9217D8E7805C.title": "Advanced and Extreme relays",
  "quest.236E9217D8E7805C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An energy relay with two Enori and two Restonia becomes \"},{\"text\":\"Advanced\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:laser_relay_advanced\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", 10,000 CF/t; that one with two Empowered Diamatine and two Restonia becomes \"},{\"text\":\"Extreme\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:laser_relay_extreme\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", 100,000 CF/t. A basic relay carries 1,000.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4D4E416AAC996B4C.title": "Bigger relays leak more",
  "quest.4D4E416AAC996B4C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Loss per transfer is 5% on basic relays, 8% on advanced and 10% on extreme; between two tiers the lower cap and the higher loss win. Right-click a relay with a \"},{\"text\":\"Compass\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:compass\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" to make it only feed, or only drain, the block beside it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7AE90843B7666FD0.title": "Fluid Laser Relays",
  "quest.7AE90843B7666FD0.quest_subtitle": "Same beam, wetter.",
  "quest.7AE90843B7666FD0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Beam an energy relay and it becomes a \"},{\"text\":\"Fluid Laser Relay\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:laser_relay_fluids\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (2,000 CF); beam that one for an item relay, and that one again for an energy relay. Fluid relays move up to 10,000 mB/t between tanks; set to drain only, they pull by themselves.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.14FA2F8C469F7112.title": "Item relays and the interface",
  "quest.14FA2F8C469F7112.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An \"},{\"text\":\"Item Laser Relay\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:laser_relay_item\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" beside each chest joins their slots; an \"},{\"text\":\"Item Interface\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:item_interface\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" next to any relay of the network acts as one big chest holding all of them. Pipe into it, pull out of it.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Hopping Item Interface\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:hopping_item_interface\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", crafted from a plain one, pushes and pulls like a hopper on its own.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A compass sets an item relay's priority: right-click raises it, \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.sneak\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" and right-click lowers it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.737922A7C214A880.title": "Advanced Item Laser Relay",
  "quest.737922A7C214A880.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An item relay, an advanced coil and a black quartz. Its window keeps an allow or block list for what goes into its container and another for what comes out; an \"},{\"text\":\"Item Filter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:filter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (iron bars around a black quartz) widens one list slot.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.30630C6BDF12D03A.title": "Engineer's Goggles",
  "quest.30630C6BDF12D03A.quest_subtitle": "See the beams nobody else sees.",
  "quest.30630C6BDF12D03A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Restonia over glass between two iron bars. Worn, they show relay modifiers and the beams the Invisibility modifier hides; the \"},{\"text\":\"Infrared\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:engineers_goggles_advanced\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" version, with Empowered Restonia, also outlines nearby creatures through walls.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.339806A25E363ED1.title": "Longer and invisible links",
  "quest.339806A25E363ED1.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Range modifier\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:laser_upgrade_range\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on each end stretches a link from 15 to 35 blocks; \"},{\"text\":\"Invisibility modifiers\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:laser_upgrade_invisibility\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on both ends hide the beam. Right-click a relay to fit one, \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.sneak\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" and right-click to take it off.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4458CD1CE2D02A2F.title": "Ender Casing and Connector",
  "quest.4458CD1CE2D02A2F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four ender pearls, four Empowered Diamatine and a black quartz block make the \"},{\"text\":\"Ender Casing\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:ender_casing\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" every phantom block is built on. Two eyes of ender, two pearls and a stick make the \"},{\"text\":\"Phantom Connector\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:phantom_connector\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.59C0B0D723A37D0A.title": "Phantom Itemface",
  "quest.59C0B0D723A37D0A.quest_subtitle": "It isn't there. It's there.",
  "quest.59C0B0D723A37D0A.quest_desc": [
    "A chest, two phantom membranes, an Ender Casing and an advanced coil. Right-click a container with the connector, then the face: from up to 16 blocks away, the face now is that inventory. Pipe into a machine with no free sides.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "It mirrors one block; it isn't a wireless pipe. Laser relays can't be reached through it."
  ],
  "quest.762848100B32F5F6.title": "Liquid, energy, redstone",
  "quest.762848100B32F5F6.quest_subtitle": "Three more faces.",
  "quest.762848100B32F5F6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two buckets beside an itemface make a \"},{\"text\":\"Phantom Liquiface\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:phantom_liquiface\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; four Empowered Restonia around one, a \"},{\"text\":\"Phantom Energyface\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:phantom_energyface\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; add four redstone for a \"},{\"text\":\"Phantom Redstoneface\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:phantom_redstoneface\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", which repeats its block's signal one way only.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.15210413AF5A5B71.title": "Range Booster",
  "quest.15210413AF5A5B71.quest_subtitle": "Stack them. Up to three.",
  "quest.15210413AF5A5B71.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four Restonia, four Diamatine and an Ender Casing. Each \"},{\"text\":\"Range Booster\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:phantom_booster\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" stacked straight on top of a phantom block doubles its reach, up to three: a face goes from 16 to 128 blocks.\"}]",
    "",
    "The Vertical Digger and the Player Interface read boosters the same way."
  ],
  "quest.083C6ED31A1FFA4B.title": "Phantom Breaker and Placer",
  "quest.083C6ED31A1FFA4B.quest_desc": [
    "An Auto-Breaker or Auto-Placer crafted with an itemface. Bind them with the connector to a spot up to 3 blocks away (boosters double it) and they break or place there instead of in front; for an empty spot, place a block, bind it, break it."
  ],
  "quest.389BD9D0DC2C95F8.title": "Player Interface",
  "quest.389BD9D0DC2C95F8.quest_subtitle": "Your inventory, as a block.",
  "quest.389BD9D0DC2C95F8.quest_desc": [
    "Five Ender Casings, a wither skeleton skull, two Empowered Diamatine and an advanced coil. It binds to whoever places it: items piped in land in that player's inventory, and CF fed in charges their items, within 32 blocks.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Player Probe\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:player_probe\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" right-clicked on another player, then on the interface, hands it to them; they get a warning and can break the link by sneaking.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.69AA923D35150556.title": "Canola oil",
  "quest.69AA923D35150556.quest_subtitle": "Salad dressing, but it runs machines.",
  "quest.69AA923D35150556.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Canola Press\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:canola_press\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" squeezes 80 mB of oil from each \"},{\"text\":\"Canola\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:canola\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for 35 CF/t; an \"},{\"text\":\"Oil Generator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:oil_generator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" burns it at 40 CF/t, 50 mB every five seconds.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Four oils, one generator: canola 40 CF/t, refined 80, crystallized 100, empowered 120. The better the oil, the longer each 50 mB lasts."
  ],
  "quest.55F0CBD17B8F593E.title": "Refined canola oil",
  "quest.55F0CBD17B8F593E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Fermenting Barrel\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:fermenting_barrel\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (logs, a canola, an Enori and a wood casing) turns 80 mB of canola oil into 80 mB of refined oil in five seconds, with no power. The Oil Generator gets 80 CF/t out of it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.617DBDDA4B399332.title": "Crystallized oil",
  "quest.617DBDDA4B399332.quest_subtitle": "Seeds in, power up.",
  "quest.617DBDDA4B399332.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The beam turns \"},{\"text\":\"Canola Seeds\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:canola_seeds\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" into \"},{\"text\":\"Crystallized Canola Seeds\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:crystallized_canola_seed\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for 2,000 CF. Toss one into a source block of refined oil in the world and the whole block turns into crystallized oil: 100 CF/t.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.703106A349BB3AEC.title": "Empowered oil",
  "quest.703106A349BB3AEC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"On the Empowerer, a crystallized seed with four canola seeds on the stands becomes an \"},{\"text\":\"Empowered Canola Seed\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:empowered_canola_seed\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", 1,000 CF per stand. Dropped into a source of crystallized oil, it makes empowered oil: 120 CF/t.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.125C1EA47BE1591B.title": "Heat Collector",
  "quest.125C1EA47BE1591B.quest_subtitle": "Lava, the patient kind.",
  "quest.125C1EA47BE1591B.quest_desc": [
    "Iron bars, a repeater, two advanced coils, an Enori and a casing. With four or more lava blocks touching it on any side but the top, it makes 40 CF/t with no fuel. Now and then it swallows one of them, so keep the pool topped up."
  ],
  "quest.07D8640C01E4D11B.title": "Lava Factory",
  "quest.07D8640C01E4D11B.quest_subtitle": "Lava, bought with CF.",
  "quest.07D8640C01E4D11B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The controller (three advanced coils, a casing, two Empowered Enori blocks and three lava buckets) makes a lava source in the block above it for 150,000 CF, once four \"},{\"text\":\"Lava Factory Casings\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:lava_factory_casing\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" surround that spot.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6B284FCC993DA54B.title": "Leaf-Eating Generator",
  "quest.6B284FCC993DA54B.quest_subtitle": "Munch, munch, 300 CF.",
  "quest.6B284FCC993DA54B.quest_desc": [
    "Four Enori, a casing, two Empowered Restonia blocks, an advanced coil and leaves. It eats a leaf block every quarter second in the 7×7×7 around it, 300 CF each: up to 60 CF/t out of a forest."
  ],
  "quest.5E33AEF7C4464417.title": "Bio Reactor",
  "quest.5E33AEF7C4464417.quest_subtitle": "Variety is the spice of power.",
  "quest.5E33AEF7C4464417.quest_desc": [
    "Six Empowered Enori, two iron casings and a sapling. It burns seeds, crops and food from its eight slots, and the more different kinds it holds at once, the more CF it makes."
  ],
  "quest.28E5525DD1530141.title": "Coal in bite sizes",
  "quest.28E5525DD1530141.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A coal splits into eight \"},{\"text\":\"Tiny Coal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:tiny_coal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (charcoal into Tiny Charcoal), each burning just long enough to smelt one item. A tiny coal on a stick makes two \"},{\"text\":\"Tiny Torches\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:tiny_torch\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2F0A53A8F1D988B3.title": "Farmer",
  "quest.2F0A53A8F1D988B3.quest_subtitle": "Tills, plants, harvests, repeats.",
  "quest.2F0A53A8F1D988B3.quest_desc": [
    "Four Enori crystal blocks, four seeds and an iron casing. It farms a 9×9 in front of it: tills, plants from its left slots and harvests into its right ones, 350 CF to plant and 250 to harvest a crop. Cactus and cane want sand, nether wart soul sand.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Melons and pumpkins get a checkerboard of empty spaces to grow into."
  ],
  "quest.3D0F5CD17730685D.title": "Shrink the field",
  "quest.3D0F5CD17730685D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Right-click the Farmer with a \"},{\"text\":\"Compass\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:compass\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" to cycle its area: 1×1, 3×3, 5×5, 7×7, 9×9. Handy for a single row or a small bed.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.41A47CA16AEAAB6D.title": "Greenhouse Glass",
  "quest.41A47CA16AEAAB6D.quest_subtitle": "Sunlight, concentrated.",
  "quest.41A47CA16AEAAB6D.quest_desc": [
    "Four glass, four saplings and an Empowered Palis make two. In daylight, with open sky above it, each one now and then bonemeals the first growing plant below."
  ],
  "quest.7F50C8FB252ED9C6.title": "Automatic Feeder",
  "quest.7F50C8FB252ED9C6.quest_subtitle": "Room service for cows.",
  "quest.7F50C8FB252ED9C6.quest_desc": [
    "Planks, two golden carrots, two basic coils and a wood casing. Set in a pen with wheat, seeds or carrots inside, it feeds the animals every five seconds and stops by itself once 30 are around."
  ],
  "quest.46684B1D0B9DBF53.title": "Worms",
  "quest.46684B1D0B9DBF53.quest_subtitle": "Early birds, look away.",
  "quest.46684B1D0B9DBF53.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Tilling a grass block with a hoe turns up a \"},{\"text\":\"Worm\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:worm\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" one time in twenty. Set on dirt or grass, it tills and waters the 3×3 around it and makes what grows there grow faster.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Right-click water with a bowl for a \"},{\"text\":\"Bowl of Water\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:water_bowl\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": it places water like a bucket, but move carelessly and it spills; sneaking keeps it steady.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2EDEBCAFB2808A31.title": "Flax and rice",
  "quest.2EDEBCAFB2808A31.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Ripe \"},{\"text\":\"Flax\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:flax_seeds\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" gives two to six string: a renewable bowstring patch. Wild rice grows beside water; this pack unifies its rice into Farmer's Delight's.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Garden Cloche\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"29ABDA7768135140\"}},{\"text\":\" grows canola, coffee, flax and rice as well.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1A238FF74011D248.title": "Auto-Breaker and Auto-Placer",
  "quest.1A238FF74011D248.quest_subtitle": "One takes, one gives.",
  "quest.1A238FF74011D248.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Seven cobblestone and a basic coil, plus a Void crystal for the \"},{\"text\":\"Auto-Breaker\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:breaker\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" or a Palis for the \"},{\"text\":\"Auto-Placer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:placer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". No power: every 15 ticks one breaks the block in front, the other places one from its nine slots.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A redstone signal pauses them; a redstone torch switches them to pulse mode. Three breakers and a Void make a \"},{\"text\":\"Long-Range Breaker\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:long_range_breaker\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", which clears up to 8 blocks ahead at 5 CF a block.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.33A7667DD917B412.title": "Fluid Collector and Placer",
  "quest.33A7667DD917B412.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A breaker between two buckets makes the \"},{\"text\":\"Fluid Collector\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:fluid_collector\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", which drinks the source block in front of it, a bucket at a time; a placer between two buckets makes the \"},{\"text\":\"Fluid Placer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:fluid_placer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", which spends 1,000 mB to set one down.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.25E50789A57729E7.title": "Energizer",
  "quest.25E50789A57729E7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four Restonia, two advanced coils and an iron casing. A drill, ring or battery put in it charges at up to 1,000 CF/t; the \"},{\"text\":\"Enervator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:enervator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", with two Restonia instead of four, drains them back out.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.63A3335C52F9C291.title": "Drill",
  "quest.63A3335C52F9C291.quest_subtitle": "Pickaxe and shovel, on a battery.",
  "quest.63A3335C52F9C291.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Drill Core\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:drill_core\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (four Enori, four basic coils and a Restonia) under three diamonds, between two advanced coils, over three Enori. It never breaks and digs like a netherite pickaxe and shovel, for 100 CF a block out of 250,000.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Hold it, \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.sneak\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" and right-click to open its augment slots. Any dye beside it in the grid recolours it, charge and augments kept.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2BBF987BE9CC486B.title": "Speed augments I to III",
  "quest.2BBF987BE9CC486B.quest_subtitle": "Sugar rush.",
  "quest.2BBF987BE9CC486B.quest_desc": [
    "Sugar around Enori and a Restonia, then around Enori and a cake, then around Empowered Enori and Empowered Diamatine. Each needs the ones below installed; together they lift mining speed from 8 to 45 and the cost per block from 100 to 400 CF."
  ],
  "quest.680E815295C05D91.title": "Area augments",
  "quest.680E815295C05D91.quest_subtitle": "Why mine one block when you can mine 25?",
  "quest.680E815295C05D91.quest_desc": [
    "Diamatine and Enori around a basic coil dig 3×3; Diamatine and Empowered Enori around an advanced coil, 5×5, with the 3×3 still installed. Every block of the hole costs CF, and area slows the swing: half speed at 3×3, about a sixth at 5×5."
  ],
  "quest.0F0FCF873A7D2F3B.title": "Fortune augments",
  "quest.0F0FCF873A7D2F3B.quest_subtitle": "The second one says III. It means it.",
  "quest.0F0FCF873A7D2F3B.quest_desc": [
    "Glowstone and redstone around an Empowered Diamatine block give Fortune I. Glowstone and Empowered Restonia around an Ender Casing, installed with the first, give Fortune III, as the name promises. Each adds to the CF a block costs."
  ],
  "quest.7C844BF362F5C8D6.title": "Silk touch and placing",
  "quest.7C844BF362F5C8D6.quest_desc": [
    "Emeradic and Diamatine around an advanced coil give silk touch, which beats Fortune. Right-click the placing augment (cobblestone, paper, Enori, a basic coil) in a hotbar slot to bind it; the drill then places that slot's block on right-click.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"With an area augment in, sneak to mine a single block.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.39A7562BE7ABC1C2.title": "Vertical Digger",
  "quest.39A7562BE7ABC1C2.quest_subtitle": "Digs straight down, politely.",
  "quest.39A7562BE7ABC1C2.quest_desc": [
    "Four iron casings, three redstone blocks, an Empowered Void and a whole drill. It mines down a 5×5 column into a nine-slot buffer, 650 CF a block; in ores-only mode it skips the rest, at 1,950 CF per ore.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Up to three Range Boosters on top double its radius each: 5×5, 9×9, 17×17, 33×33."
  ],
  "quest.7B71F85B50C2D72D.title": "Double Crusher, Powered Furnace",
  "quest.7B71F85B50C2D72D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two Crushers, an iron casing, two advanced coils and cobblestone make a \"},{\"text\":\"Double Crusher\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:crusher_double\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": two lanes at 40 CF/t, each ore into two raw pieces in five seconds. The \"},{\"text\":\"Powered Furnace\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:powered_furnace\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" smelts two stacks side by side at 25 CF/t.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The single Crusher is in the \"},{\"text\":\"ore processing guide\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"2B97086271E1EA71\"}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0CCA0F0E65869349.title": "Triple to Quintuple batteries",
  "quest.0CCA0F0E65869349.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Each battery sits on top of the next one's recipe, charge kept: the triple and quadruple take Empowered Enori, the quintuple Empowered Diamatine. They hold 600,000, 1,000,000 and 2,000,000 CF. A \"},{\"text\":\"Battery Box\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:battery_box\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" turns one into a placed storage block.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.40A913BCC86919E0.title": "Rings and a staff",
  "quest.40A913BCC86919E0.quest_subtitle": "Charge them first.",
  "quest.40A913BCC86919E0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"All three run on CF from the Energizer. The \"},{\"text\":\"Ring of Magnetizing\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:ring_of_magnetizing\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in your inventory pulls items from 5 blocks, 50 CF each; \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.sneak\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" and right-click toggles it. The \"},{\"text\":\"Ring of Growth\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:ring_of_growth\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", in your main hand, speeds up plants around you.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Teleport Staff\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:teleport_staff\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" jumps you up to 100 blocks where you look, costing more the farther you go, then rests for two and a half seconds.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5359B925628A19B9.title": "Handheld Filler",
  "quest.5359B925628A19B9.quest_subtitle": "A builder's shortcut.",
  "quest.5359B925628A19B9.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two Empowered Enori, a Palis, two Diamatine, an advanced coil and a triple battery. \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.sneak\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" and right-click a block to choose it; then hold right-click from one corner to the other and it fills that plane or box from your inventory, for CF.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0DAF18BFF9502E9D.title": "Experience Solidifier",
  "quest.0DAF18BFF9502E9D.quest_subtitle": "Levels that fit in a chest.",
  "quest.0DAF18BFF9502E9D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Six bottles o' enchanting, two Empowered Diamatine blocks and an advanced coil. Its buttons turn your levels into \"},{\"text\":\"Solidified Experience\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:solidified_experience\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", 8 points each; right-click one to take it back, sneaking for the whole stack.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.62B9120AFADC9F6A.title": "Shock Absorber",
  "quest.62B9120AFADC9F6A.quest_subtitle": "Creepers hate this one trick.",
  "quest.62B9120AFADC9F6A.quest_desc": [
    "Four obsidian, four Empowered Void and an advanced coil. Powered, it keeps explosions from breaking blocks or hitting anything within 5 blocks of it, paying 300 CF for each thing it spares."
  ],
  "quest.3E59CE30AE2CC842.title": "All-in-one tools",
  "quest.3E59CE30AE2CC842.quest_subtitle": "Five tools, one slot.",
  "quest.3E59CE30AE2CC842.quest_desc": [
    "The five tools of one material, shapeless, make an AIOT: pickaxe, axe, shovel, sword and hoe in one, from wood to netherite. Right-click strips logs or tills dirt; crouching, it makes paths."
  ],
  "quest.367A492EF422B3F9.title": "Firework Box",
  "quest.367A492EF422B3F9.quest_subtitle": "Every night is New Year's.",
  "quest.367A492EF422B3F9.quest_desc": [
    "An iron casing, a firework rocket, gunpowder, sticks and three Enori. With CF it launches random fireworks around itself, 500 CF a rocket; its window sets colours, shapes and how often."
  ],
  "quest.601ABC2C2406FAD7.title": "A crafting table on a stick",
  "quest.601ABC2C2406FAD7.quest_subtitle": "Portable, and a little silly.",
  "quest.601ABC2C2406FAD7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A crafting table and any sign. Right-click it for a 3×3 grid anywhere; give «Open the Crafting Stick» a key in Controls and \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.actualladditions.crafting_stick_open.desc\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" opens it straight from your inventory.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0CFD2366D954E4A4.title": "Traveler's Sack",
  "quest.0CFD2366D954E4A4.quest_subtitle": "Pockets with opinions.",
  "quest.0CFD2366D954E4A4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"String, leather, a chest and a Void Crystal block. Carried with auto-insert on, it catches what you pick up, filtered from its window. The \"},{\"text\":\"Void Sack\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:void_sack\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (a sack, an ender pearl, obsidian and another Void block) catches the same way and deletes it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.560F1A511C9049FF.title": "Leaf Blower",
  "quest.560F1A511C9049FF.quest_subtitle": "Autumn, automated.",
  "quest.560F1A511C9049FF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Flint, a piston, two Enori and an advanced coil. Hold right-click to blow away the grass and flowers around you; the \"},{\"text\":\"Advanced\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"actuallyadditions:advanced_leaf_blower\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" one, made with Diamatine, works faster and clears leaves too.\"}]"
  ],
  "image.47D1D422C673B4B6.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The beam and its lenses\",\"color\":\"#8CB8FF\"}]",
  "image.6DE6DDD4F00A1D74.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Coffee\",\"color\":\"#8CB8FF\"}]",
  "image.142B0590D43CF28E.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Laser relays\",\"color\":\"#8CB8FF\"}]",
  "image.493F6E1B05D1B802.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Phantomfaces\",\"color\":\"#8CB8FF\"}]",
  "image.2F0A1A5D6E38E0B4.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Power\",\"color\":\"#8CB8FF\"}]",
  "image.6752EEA516EC45CE.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Farmers and breakers\",\"color\":\"#8CB8FF\"}]",
  "image.46D4C9897157903D.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Drills and upgrades\",\"color\":\"#8CB8FF\"}]",
  "image.32DA17B1B8CC3E1F.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Gadgets\",\"color\":\"#8CB8FF\"}]",
  "image.46BBE5E5436F5C10.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Actually Additions\",\"color\":\"#EAF2FF\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.4CF0F0949366D6A1.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"beam · crystal · empower\",\"color\":\"#8CB8FF\",\"font\":\"minecraft:uniform\"}]",
  "image.2B55D7F72FD032F6.title": "Back to the Sun of Heliodor",
  "chapter.2ABB1BEF574D3E85.title": "Ender IO",
  "chapter.2ABB1BEF574D3E85.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Alloys and binder, conduits nine to a block, the SAG mill, capacitors, soul binding, travel anchors and dark steel."
  ],
  "quest.7DA214A4F9BC59FA.title": "Grains of Infinity",
  "quest.7DA214A4F9BC59FA.quest_subtitle": "Bedrock burns, if you're patient.",
  "quest.7DA214A4F9BC59FA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Light a fire on \"},{\"text\":\"Bedrock\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:bedrock\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in the Overworld and let it go out on its own: if it burned 13 seconds, 80% of the time it drops one to three \"},{\"text\":\"Grains of Infinity\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"enderio:grains_of_infinity\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", and 30% of the time a \"},{\"text\":\"Suspicious Seed\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"enderio:suspicious_seed\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Deepslate\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:deepslate\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" works too: one grain 40% of the time, and the block turns to cobblestone. Light the fire in a pit, away from anything that burns.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7E0D175CBBC7CDD3.title": "Void Chassis",
  "quest.7E0D175CBBC7CDD3.quest_subtitle": "Every machine starts hollow.",
  "quest.7E0D175CBBC7CDD3.quest_desc": [
    "Four iron ingots and four Grains of Infinity. The alloy smelter, the SAG mill, the Stirling generator and most basic Ender IO machines are built around one."
  ],
  "quest.1BD93E18D312F8BF.title": "Infinity Bimetal Gear",
  "quest.1BD93E18D312F8BF.quest_subtitle": "One gear to rule the iron ones.",
  "quest.1BD93E18D312F8BF.quest_desc": [
    "Four iron ingots, four iron nuggets and a grain in the middle. Each of the first machines takes two.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The pack unifies iron gears into this one: Industrial Foregoing's recipe, four iron ingots around an empty middle, hands it out too.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0E115DD749F11524.title": "Basic Capacitor",
  "quest.0E115DD749F11524.quest_subtitle": "No capacitor, no work.",
  "quest.0E115DD749F11524.quest_desc": [
    "Two grains, a copper ingot and four gold nuggets. Machines with a capacitor slot don't run without one, and its level sets how fast they work and how much they buffer."
  ],
  "quest.6676A6EF8CFE49DE.title": "Stirling Generator",
  "quest.6676A6EF8CFE49DE.quest_subtitle": "Coal in, micro infinity out.",
  "quest.6676A6EF8CFE49DE.quest_desc": [
    "Furnace fuel in, 40 µI per tick out; µI is plain FE. With a basic capacitor a piece of coal lasts 30 seconds, 24,000 µI, and it only lights new fuel while its buffer has room.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A double-layer capacitor doubles the output and stretches each fuel 20%; an octadic triples it and stretches it 40%.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.64098CFB83DA95CD.title": "Alloy Smelter",
  "quest.64098CFB83DA95CD.quest_subtitle": "Three slots, one ingot.",
  "quest.64098CFB83DA95CD.quest_desc": [
    "Three furnaces, two gears, iron and obsidian around a void chassis. Up to three ingredients melt into an alloy, and it runs furnace recipes too: its mode switches between alloys, smelting or both.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"At 20 µI per tick a basic smelter makes two conductive alloy ingots in 8 seconds; with a double-layer capacitor, in 2.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.33ED3C018BECFAAB.title": "Conductive Alloy",
  "quest.33ED3C018BECFAAB.quest_subtitle": "Iron and copper, finally together.",
  "quest.33ED3C018BECFAAB.quest_desc": [
    "An iron ingot and a copper ingot make two. It goes into every energy, item and fluid conduit, the painting machine, the chargers and the advanced capacitor banks."
  ],
  "quest.309EAE8E4ACFFE7B.title": "Energetic Alloy",
  "quest.309EAE8E4ACFFE7B.quest_subtitle": "Gold with a spark in it.",
  "quest.309EAE8E4ACFFE7B.quest_desc": [
    "Conductive alloy, a gold ingot and redstone make two. The double-layer capacitor, the energized gear of the soul machines and the second tier of conduits are built on it."
  ],
  "quest.7413DB129100FEFE.title": "Double-Layer Capacitor",
  "quest.7413DB129100FEFE.quest_subtitle": "Twice the level, four times the pace.",
  "quest.7413DB129100FEFE.quest_desc": [
    "Two basic capacitors, two energetic alloy ingots and coal dust. A machine's draw and buffer grow with the square of its capacitor's level while each job costs the same energy: at level 2 it works four times as fast.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Coal dust comes from the SAG mill: one piece of coal gives one, and a second 10% of the time.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0232182B4E70EC0E.title": "Vibrant Alloy",
  "quest.0232182B4E70EC0E.quest_subtitle": "It hums if you listen closely.",
  "quest.0232182B4E70EC0E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Energetic alloy, an ender pearl and glowstone dust make two. Its nuggets around an emerald give the \"},{\"text\":\"Vibrant Crystal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"enderio:vibrant_crystal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; the top conduits and the octadic capacitor need the ingot.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.76EAC1BDC93AA5BB.title": "Octadic Capacitor",
  "quest.76EAC1BDC93AA5BB.quest_subtitle": "Eight layers, nine times the work.",
  "quest.76EAC1BDC93AA5BB.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two double-layer capacitors, glowstone, a vibrant alloy ingot and, in this pack, an \"},{\"text\":\"Atomic Alloy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:alloy_atomic\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (act V, where the second vibrant ingot was). Level 3: a machine runs nine times as fast as on a basic one, with nine times the buffer.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "{image:enderio:textures/item/octadic_capacitor.png width:48 height:48 align:center}",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Octadics also build the \"},{\"text\":\"Vibrant Capacitor Bank\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"enderio:vibrant_capacitor_bank\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", 4,000,000 µI, and the \"},{\"text\":\"Vibrant Photovoltaic Module\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"enderio:vibrant_photovoltaic_module\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", 64 µI per tick at noon.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.70FFC2D8E5E40B15.title": "Place a Capacitor Bank",
  "quest.34C474CC7A477F8B.title": "Capacitor Bank",
  "quest.34C474CC7A477F8B.quest_subtitle": "Stack them: they share.",
  "quest.34C474CC7A477F8B.quest_desc": [
    "Four basic capacitors, four iron ingots and a block of redstone: 500,000 µI. Banks of the same tier set side by side share one pool, and each face can show a gauge or push power out."
  ],
  "quest.78145E2B45A44B6F.title": "Advanced Capacitor Bank",
  "quest.78145E2B45A44B6F.quest_subtitle": "Four times the room.",
  "quest.78145E2B45A44B6F.quest_desc": [
    "Four double-layer capacitors, four conductive alloy and a block of redstone: 2,000,000 µI. Two basic banks, a double-layer capacitor and six energetic alloy make one too."
  ],
  "quest.78DA0040032ADA50.title": "Liquid Sunshine",
  "quest.78DA0040032ADA50.quest_subtitle": "Noon, bottled. Well, bucketed.",
  "quest.78DA0040032ADA50.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"In the \"},{\"text\":\"VAT\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"121C58CC59F088F1\"}},{\"text\":\", water with glowstone and a sunflower ferments into Liquid Sunshine. A source block of it touching a photovoltaic module runs that module at full output: any hour, any weather, underground, even in the Nether.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "A module bound with a phantom's soul wants Liquid Darkness instead: Liquid Sunshine fermented with amethyst and obsidian dust. Each module checks its own six sides."
  ],
  "quest.019C6B4F05FF7D12.title": "Photovoltaic Module",
  "quest.019C6B4F05FF7D12.quest_subtitle": "Free power, weather permitting.",
  "quest.019C6B4F05FF7D12.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Silicon\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"6FFD74DD4F169CB5\"}},{\"text\":\", lapis dust and coal dust make the composite; two composites in the smelter give a \"},{\"text\":\"Photovoltaic Plate\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"enderio:photovoltaic_plate\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; three plates, gold, glass, redstone and two basic capacitors make the module: 4 µI per tick at noon under open sky.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Rain and thunder cut it, and modules side by side join into one panel with one output. The \"},{\"text\":\"Pulsating\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"enderio:pulsating_photovoltaic_module\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" module makes 16 µI per tick.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.25C8FD789B52567E.title": "Wired Charger",
  "quest.25C8FD789B52567E.quest_subtitle": "Juice for your gear.",
  "quest.25C8FD789B52567E.quest_desc": [
    "Eight conductive alloy around a void chassis. Any item that stores FE charges in its slot, the staff of travelling and the electromagnet included."
  ],
  "quest.175EF0469BEB8905.title": "SAG Mill",
  "quest.175EF0469BEB8905.quest_subtitle": "Semi-autogenous, fully grinding.",
  "quest.175EF0469BEB8905.quest_desc": [
    "Flint, a piston, two gears, iron and obsidian around a void chassis. Raw iron gives one dust and a second 80% of the time; iron, copper and gold ores give their raw ore and a third more on average; flowers, cobblestone and bones become dyes, gravel and bone meal."
  ],
  "quest.4C653C2D2CF9FA86.title": "Grinding Balls",
  "quest.4C653C2D2CF9FA86.quest_subtitle": "Ball bearings for a better grind.",
  "quest.4C653C2D2CF9FA86.quest_desc": [
    "Five ingots in a plus make 24 balls. One in the mill's ball slot multiplies the main output, raises every bonus chance and changes the power draw, until it has worn through its share of energy.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Recipes that turn ingots into dust ignore the ball and don't wear it."
  ],
  "quest.5E22EBC1D45D8F54.title": "Dust math",
  "quest.5E22EBC1D45D8F54.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Per raw iron: 1.8 dust bare, 2.4 with flint (it works as a ball), 2.7 with dark steel at 70% power, 3.0 with energetic alloy and 3.5 with vibrant alloy, which draws 13% more.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6FFD74DD4F169CB5.title": "Silicon",
  "quest.6FFD74DD4F169CB5.quest_subtitle": "Sand, but smarter.",
  "quest.6FFD74DD4F169CB5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The SAG mill turns sand into \"},{\"text\":\"Silicon\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"enderio:silicon\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" half the time, a clay block into two 80% of the time, and redstone ore adds one to its redstone. The crafter, the solar composite and most Slice'N'Splice parts need it.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Any silicon works: Applied Energistics, Oritech and Refined Storage silicon share the tag these recipes ask for.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6E4F85226F32DCAD.title": "Grains without fire",
  "quest.6E4F85226F32DCAD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The SAG mill turns \"},{\"text\":\"Cobbled Deepslate\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:cobbled_deepslate\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" into cobblestone with a 12% chance of a grain of infinity, and a ball's bonus raises it: 24% with dark steel. A deepslate quarry becomes a grain farm.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.51D746C0363F1B17.title": "Crafter",
  "quest.51D746C0363F1B17.quest_subtitle": "The crafting table that works nights.",
  "quest.51D746C0363F1B17.quest_desc": [
    "Three silicon, iron, two gears and a crafting table on a void chassis. Show it a recipe in its grid and keep it fed: it crafts on its own, 3,200 µI a craft with a basic capacitor."
  ],
  "quest.2D284D567AB1DD2C.title": "Part of a balanced breakfast",
  "quest.2D284D567AB1DD2C.quest_subtitle": "Snap, crackle, teleport.",
  "quest.2D284D567AB1DD2C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A bowl, milk, wheat and powdered ender pearl make \"},{\"text\":\"\\\"Enderios\\\"\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"enderio:enderios\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Each serving has a 30% chance to teleport you up to 16 blocks away. Eat them near a wall, not a cliff.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.1B49F82FB37AA2F0.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.72370EF5D8B4B9E2.title": "Fused Quartz and Clear Glass",
  "quest.72370EF5D8B4B9E2.quest_subtitle": "Glass you can hide behind.",
  "quest.72370EF5D8B4B9E2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four nether quartz, or a quartz block, melt into \"},{\"text\":\"Fused Quartz\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"enderio:fused_quartz\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": glass that shrugs off explosions. Plain glass through the smelter comes out as \"},{\"text\":\"Clear Glass\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"enderio:clear_glass\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Glowstone makes either one glow and amethyst makes it block light; eight blocks around a dye tint them."
  ],
  "quest.1A93F83E09C77EC2.title": "Painting Machine",
  "quest.1A93F83E09C77EC2.quest_subtitle": "Every block a disguise.",
  "quest.1A93F83E09C77EC2.quest_desc": [
    "Red, green and blue dye, conductive and redstone alloy, two gears and a void chassis. It takes a block to paint and a block to copy, and returns the first wearing the second's look: stairs, slabs, fences, walls, facades, even a travel anchor."
  ],
  "quest.258C299283890FE1.title": "Conduit Facades",
  "quest.258C299283890FE1.quest_subtitle": "Out of sight, still in the circuit.",
  "quest.258C299283890FE1.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight conduit binder around nothing make a \"},{\"text\":\"Conduit Facade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"enderio:conduit_facade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Paint it, then use it on a conduit bundle: the bundle hides behind the block you painted it with.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Obsidian dust around a facade hardens it against explosions; clear glass makes it transparent, so even a glassy paint keeps the conduits out of sight."
  ],
  "quest.5D78D666B40ED14D.title": "Disguised machinery",
  "quest.5D78D666B40ED14D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Paint changes the look, not the job: a painted block of redstone still powers, painted glowstone still lights up, a painted crafting table still crafts and painted sand still falls.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3B1B081436182957.title": "Faux diamonds",
  "quest.3B1B081436182957.quest_subtitle": "Diamonds on the outside.",
  "quest.3B1B081436182957.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"You painted a block to look like a \"},{\"text\":\"Block of Diamond\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:diamond_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Nobody has to know what's underneath.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.14AF16B81693E52C.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.60147EF5F6F9EE48.title": "Netherite, allegedly",
  "quest.60147EF5F6F9EE48.quest_subtitle": "Richer than rich, on paper.",
  "quest.60147EF5F6F9EE48.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"This time the paint came from a \"},{\"text\":\"Block of Netherite\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:netherite_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Same block underneath, twice the swagger.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.040D1F33B176CF08.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.467FB019AFE5FA43.title": "Conduit Binder",
  "quest.467FB019AFE5FA43.quest_subtitle": "The glue of every pipe.",
  "quest.467FB019AFE5FA43.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Five gravel, two sand and two clay balls make eight \"},{\"text\":\"Conduit Binder Composite\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"enderio:conduit_binder_composite\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; each smelts into two \"},{\"text\":\"Conduit Binder\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"enderio:conduit_binder\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Every conduit is six binder around its core.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.06BDBF18B0055322.title": "Energy Conduit",
  "quest.5D34C9D6A9BFD890.title": "Energy Conduit",
  "quest.5D34C9D6A9BFD890.quest_subtitle": "Nine lines, one block.",
  "quest.5D34C9D6A9BFD890.quest_desc": [
    "Three conductive alloy ingots between six binder make eight. It carries 8,000 µI per tick, and one block holds up to nine conduits of different kinds, each connection with its own screen."
  ],
  "quest.5EC07ABB15BBC805.title": "Pulsating Alloy",
  "quest.5EC07ABB15BBC805.quest_subtitle": "An ender pearl with a heartbeat.",
  "quest.5EC07ABB15BBC805.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An iron ingot and an ender pearl make two. The item conduit takes one per eight, and eight of its nuggets around a diamond make the \"},{\"text\":\"Pulsating Crystal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"enderio:pulsating_crystal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" that anchors and vacuums run on.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.125E2AF024654E35.title": "Item Conduit",
  "quest.4CAD7C2A3A85D688.title": "Item Conduit",
  "quest.4CAD7C2A3A85D688.quest_subtitle": "Hoppers, but with ambition.",
  "quest.4CAD7C2A3A85D688.quest_desc": [
    "Two conductive alloy and a pulsating alloy between six binder. Set a connection to extract and it pulls from that inventory, 32 items a second, into every connection set to insert.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Round robin takes turns among the inserts, priority fills the highest first, and self feed lets a machine take back what it gave."
  ],
  "task.06041C3E91B37C5F.title": "Fluid Conduit",
  "quest.3FD5746CCA83F27A.title": "Fluid Conduit",
  "quest.3FD5746CCA83F27A.quest_subtitle": "One fluid at a time, please.",
  "quest.3FD5746CCA83F27A.quest_desc": [
    "Two conductive alloy and a clear glass between six binder. A network locks to the first fluid it carries; to switch fluids, reset it in the connection's screen."
  ],
  "task.06DACD0C2BF4332A.title": "Redstone Conduit",
  "quest.27DD38D5B417A9E9.title": "Redstone Conduit",
  "quest.27DD38D5B417A9E9.quest_subtitle": "Sixteen wires in one.",
  "quest.27DD38D5B417A9E9.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Redstone and a copper ingot make \"},{\"text\":\"Redstone Alloy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"enderio:redstone_alloy_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; three between six binder make eight conduits. Signals ride on sixteen colour channels, so one line carries many signals.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Paper, redstone alloy and iron make the \"},{\"text\":\"Redstone Filter Base\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"enderio:redstone_filter_base\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", the start of every \"},{\"text\":\"logic\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"7F12844DDDB0A550\"}},{\"text\":\" and \"},{\"text\":\"signal\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"417D82DCD738CAB4\"}},{\"text\":\" filter a connection can hold.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.131FA09A79EDDAF0.title": "Any logic filter",
  "quest.7F12844DDDB0A550.title": "Logic Filters",
  "quest.7F12844DDDB0A550.quest_subtitle": "Boolean algebra, one colour at a time.",
  "quest.7F12844DDDB0A550.quest_desc": [
    "A redstone conduit connection has two filter slots: one for what it reads, one for what it outputs. AND, OR and XOR go in the output slot and combine two colour channels you pick; a redstone torch turns them into NAND, NOR and XNOR. NOT inverts, in either slot.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "From the filter base: two redstone torches make AND, two redstone alloy make OR, all four make XOR, and a torch with one alloy makes NOT."
  ],
  "task.382985DAF33C046B.title": "Any timer, sensor, toggle or counter",
  "quest.417D82DCD738CAB4.title": "Timers, Sensors and Counters",
  "quest.417D82DCD738CAB4.quest_subtitle": "A clock, an eye and an abacus.",
  "quest.417D82DCD738CAB4.quest_desc": [
    "In the input slot, a timer filter sends a pulse every so many ticks you type (20 make a second), and a sensor filter reads what a comparator would: a chest's fill level becomes the channel's strength.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "In the output slot, a toggle filter flips with each pulse, and a count filter switches on at the pulse number you set and off at the next.",
    "",
    "A clock, a comparator or a lever next to the filter base and a redstone alloy make the timer, sensor and toggle; four redstone alloy make the counter."
  ],
  "quest.5DD4477B3B2385DE.title": "Conduit Probe and Yeta Wrench",
  "quest.5DD4477B3B2385DE.quest_subtitle": "Copy, paste, switch.",
  "quest.5DD4477B3B2385DE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Conduit Probe\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"enderio:conduit_probe\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" copies a connection's settings and pastes them onto another. The \"},{\"text\":\"Yeta Wrench\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"enderio:yeta_wrench\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", three copper and a grain, cycles a machine face through its push and pull modes.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Crafting a configured machine, bank or filter alone in the grid resets it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1A8066C2C936454C.title": "Channels by colour",
  "quest.1A8066C2C936454C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Each connection has an insert colour and an extract colour, and items only flow between matching ones: two item lines share one bundle without mixing. An extract can also wait for a redstone conduit signal on a colour you pick.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7C1DD4EA390A0EC6.title": "Filters",
  "quest.7C1DD4EA390A0EC6.quest_subtitle": "Bouncers for your pipes.",
  "quest.7C1DD4EA390A0EC6.quest_desc": [
    "Paper around a hopper, or around a bucket. Slot one into a connection and only what it lists gets through; use it while sneaking to set it up as an allow or a deny list.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"advanced and big\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"10D4E2BDD7F0631E\"}},{\"text\":\" filters and the \"},{\"text\":\"limited\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"0DD11BACC0E7C89D\"}},{\"text\":\" one come later, from a Z-Logic Controller, comparators and a skeletal contractor or shulker shells.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.10D4E2BDD7F0631E.title": "Advanced and Big Filters",
  "quest.10D4E2BDD7F0631E.quest_subtitle": "For when 'iron pickaxe' isn't specific enough.",
  "quest.10D4E2BDD7F0631E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Z-Logic Controller in paper and redstone makes the \"},{\"text\":\"Advanced Item Filter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"enderio:advanced_item_filter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": 18 slots that can match components, so an enchanted book isn't just any book, and sort tools by wear, from untouched to nearly broken.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Big Item Filter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"enderio:big_item_filter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" trades both for 36 slots (a skeletal contractor and obsidian dust); two shulker shells around an advanced filter make the \"},{\"text\":\"Big Advanced Item Filter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"enderio:big_advanced_item_filter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", with both.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0DD11BACC0E7C89D.title": "Limited Item Filter",
  "quest.0DD11BACC0E7C89D.quest_subtitle": "Enough is enough. Exactly sixteen is enough.",
  "quest.0DD11BACC0E7C89D.quest_desc": [
    "An advanced filter between two comparators. Each of its 18 slots holds a stack whose size is a cap: on an insert connection it lets that item in only while the target holds fewer. A furnace keeps sixteen coal and the rest waits in the chest."
  ],
  "task.4DF9D12A6CB6D1B3.title": "Energetic Energy Conduit",
  "task.038F37708A8B5BC0.title": "Energetic Item Conduit",
  "task.68180F6F9B6BDDF5.title": "Energetic Fluid Conduit",
  "quest.70D0180A79EF9172.title": "Energetic Conduits",
  "quest.70D0180A79EF9172.quest_subtitle": "Same pipes, more pressure.",
  "quest.70D0180A79EF9172.quest_desc": [
    "Energetic alloy where the conductive went: 48,000 µI per tick, 64 items a second, and fluid conduits five times as fast (they take fused quartz). A conduit of the tier below can stand in for one of the ingots."
  ],
  "task.73F2B36824C2D65D.title": "Vibrant Energy Conduit",
  "task.73628E5C52F6B911.title": "Vibrant Item Conduit",
  "task.26CF773CEB018726.title": "Vibrant Fluid Conduit",
  "quest.4EFCF3329275B3FC.title": "Vibrant Conduits",
  "quest.4EFCF3329275B3FC.quest_subtitle": "Top of the line.",
  "quest.4EFCF3329275B3FC.quest_desc": [
    "Vibrant alloy: 192,000 µI per tick, 128 items a second, and fluid conduits forty times as fast as the first ones."
  ],
  "task.38DC1709DC204873.title": "ME Conduit",
  "quest.3594C116B270FB8C.title": "ME in the bundle",
  "quest.3594C116B270FB8C.quest_subtitle": "Applied Energistics, tucked away.",
  "quest.3594C116B270FB8C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three Applied Energistics \"},{\"text\":\"covered\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:fluix_covered_cable\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" or glass cables between six binder make three ME conduits; dense covered cables make dense ones. Refined Storage cables go in the same way, as Refined Storage conduits.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.133BEB322344FFE4.title": "Chemical Conduit",
  "quest.524499B40B4627BF.title": "Chemicals in the bundle",
  "quest.524499B40B4627BF.quest_subtitle": "Mekanism's gases ride along.",
  "quest.524499B40B4627BF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three Mekanism \"},{\"text\":\"Basic Pressurized Tubes\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:basic_pressurized_tube\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" between six binder make three chemical conduits. Eight of them around an infused alloy become pressurized ones, and eight of those around a reinforced alloy, ender chemical conduits.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Advanced thermodynamic conductors make heat conduits the same way."
  ],
  "quest.773510A63E2A5AC8.title": "Impulse Hopper",
  "quest.773510A63E2A5AC8.quest_subtitle": "It waits for the whole order.",
  "quest.773510A63E2A5AC8.quest_desc": [
    "Conductive and redstone alloy, a hopper and two gears on a void chassis. Its six ghost slots set exact amounts, and once a second it moves those amounts from its input to its output, 10 µI per item."
  ],
  "quest.4419E9DC3558865A.title": "Tanks and the Drain",
  "quest.4419E9DC3558865A.quest_subtitle": "Buckets, industrialised.",
  "quest.4419E9DC3558865A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Iron, iron bars and glass make a \"},{\"text\":\"Fluid Tank\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"enderio:fluid_tank\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" of 16,000 mB; dark steel and fused quartz, one of 32,000 mB. Its slots fill items too: a glass bottle takes 250 mB of XP Juice and comes out as a Bottle o' Enchanting.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Drain\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"enderio:drain\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" sucks the fluid source blocks under it into its tank, at 10 µI per tick.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4C38BF6AE75BD3CD.title": "Industrial Insulation",
  "quest.4C38BF6AE75BD3CD.quest_subtitle": "A sponge that isn't afraid of lava.",
  "quest.4C38BF6AE75BD3CD.quest_desc": [
    "Lapis dust, wool and iron or tin dust in the smelter. Placed, it clears the fluids around it as far as a sponge reaches, lava and modded ones included, and drains waterlogged blocks. It never gets wet: break it and place it again."
  ],
  "quest.60F9F4CA4CAA8196.title": "Dark Steel",
  "quest.60F9F4CA4CAA8196.quest_subtitle": "Iron that went through something.",
  "quest.60F9F4CA4CAA8196.quest_desc": [
    "An iron ingot, coal dust and obsidian make two in the smelter; two pieces of coal can replace the dust. The sword, the glider, the VAT, the enchanter and the staff of travelling are built on it."
  ],
  "quest.0C06EBFD1EF57C04.title": "The Ender",
  "quest.0C06EBFD1EF57C04.quest_subtitle": "Heads will roll. Seven percent of them.",
  "quest.0C06EBFD1EF57C04.quest_desc": [
    "Two dark steel ingots on a stick: a diamond sword's damage, 2,000 durability and enchantability 25. A killing blow with it has a 7% chance to drop the victim's head, and it's the only way to an Enderman Head."
  ],
  "quest.640920E2BC9B8022.title": "Trophy wall",
  "quest.640920E2BC9B8022.quest_subtitle": "Zombies first, endermen later.",
  "quest.640920E2BC9B8022.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Under The Ender, zombies, husks and drowned drop zombie heads, which the Slice'N'Splice needs; skeletons, creepers, wither skeletons and piglins drop theirs. The \"},{\"text\":\"Enderman Head\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"enderio:enderman_head\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" goes into the aversion obelisk and the Ender Resonator.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.055FE15368665A76.title": "Glider",
  "quest.055FE15368665A76.quest_subtitle": "Leather wings, steel nerves.",
  "quest.055FE15368665A76.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three dark steel and three leather make a \"},{\"text\":\"Glider Wing\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"enderio:glider_wing\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; two wings and two dark steel ingots make the \"},{\"text\":\"Glider\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"enderio:glider\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Wear it in the chest slot: after half a second of falling you glide, and sneaking lets go.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.614FDF9DEE894FE3.title": "Dark steel blocks",
  "quest.614FDF9DEE894FE3.quest_subtitle": "Tougher than they look. They look tough.",
  "quest.614FDF9DEE894FE3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three ingots make twelve ladders that climb faster than wooden ones, and dark steel bars, obsidian and grains make \"},{\"text\":\"Reinforced Obsidian\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"enderio:reinforced_obsidian_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": the Wither can't break it.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Dark steel doors and trapdoors open only with redstone, like iron ones, but shrug off explosions."
  ],
  "task.491B4B77A0B66D5F.title": "Any silent pressure plate",
  "quest.01E0AD2C3FF10A52.title": "Silent Pressure Plates",
  "quest.01E0AD2C3FF10A52.quest_subtitle": "Sneaking, now with hardware support.",
  "quest.01E0AD2C3FF10A52.quest_desc": [
    "Wool on top of most pressure plates, Ender IO's own included, silences them. Two dark steel ingots make a plate that only notices players; two soularium, one that only notices monsters. A trap that lets you walk by.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A silent stone or blackstone plate reacts to dropped items too\",\"color\":\"#FF8C7A\"},{\"text\":\", like a wooden one.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.3636211248CDB818.title": "Any resetting lever",
  "quest.0F323C914FA33BE3.title": "Resetting Levers",
  "quest.0F323C914FA33BE3.quest_subtitle": "Flip it and walk away.",
  "quest.0F323C914FA33BE3.quest_desc": [
    "A lever with redstone springs back by itself after 5 seconds; two, three, four or five redstone make it 10, 30, 60 or 300. A redstone torch inverts it: on until you pull it, off for the delay. A door that shuts behind you, no clock needed."
  ],
  "quest.5129ED4E41F37A2B.title": "End Steel",
  "quest.5129ED4E41F37A2B.quest_subtitle": "Dark steel that went further.",
  "quest.5129ED4E41F37A2B.quest_desc": [
    "End stone, dark steel and obsidian make two, at 6,400 µI. Five in a plus make 24 End Steel grinding balls: ×2.4 on every bonus chance and ×1.4 main output, at 70% of the power."
  ],
  "quest.121C58CC59F088F1.title": "The VAT",
  "quest.121C58CC59F088F1.quest_subtitle": "Home brewing, industrial scale.",
  "quest.121C58CC59F088F1.quest_desc": [
    "Dark steel, conductive and redstone alloy, a barrel and two gears on a void chassis; it needs no power. It ferments a fluid with a reagent on each side: water with meat and crops makes Nutrient Distillation, with seeds and crops Hootch, and Hootch with gunpowder and redstone becomes Rocket Fuel.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Liquid Sunshine clears the sky in a \"},{\"text\":\"weather obelisk\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"2C00D6FBBDF5EDB7\"}},{\"text\":\" and Cloud Seed brings rain; Nutrient Distillation and Rocket Fuel feed the \"},{\"text\":\"soul engine\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"730DF7082497C5E9\"}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7659E93C20581BC2.title": "Fire Water",
  "quest.7659E93C20581BC2.quest_subtitle": "Pour it on bedrock, not on your house.",
  "quest.7659E93C20581BC2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Hootch with blaze powder and redstone ferments into Fire Water. Poured on bedrock in the Overworld, now and then it does what a bedrock fire does, no flint and steel needed: one to three \"},{\"text\":\"Grains of Infinity\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"enderio:grains_of_infinity\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", sometimes a suspicious seed.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"It sets fire to anything flammable around it, like lava.\",\"color\":\"#FF8C7A\"},{\"text\":\" On deepslate it drops a grain 40% of the time and turns the block into cobblestone.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3369900C1032C87F.title": "Enchanter",
  "quest.3369900C1032C87F.quest_subtitle": "Pick your enchantment, pay in lapis.",
  "quest.3369900C1032C87F.quest_desc": [
    "Dark steel, two diamonds, a book and a lectern. A book, lapis and an ingredient give the enchanted book it stands for: a slimeball for Silk Touch, an emerald for Fortune, a Vial of the Void for Mending. More ingredient, higher level.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Each level costs three lapis and some experience levels: twelve redstone per level of Efficiency, one skeleton skull per level of Looting."
  ],
  "quest.3F95DB3D7CFA5EE1.title": "Soularium",
  "quest.3F95DB3D7CFA5EE1.quest_subtitle": "Gold that remembers something.",
  "quest.3F95DB3D7CFA5EE1.quest_desc": [
    "Soul sand or soul soil with a gold ingot, one per run. Every soul machine is framed in it: the vial, the soul chain, the ensouled chassis and the obelisks."
  ],
  "quest.576BD65CB87BF19A.title": "Soul Vial",
  "quest.576BD65CB87BF19A.quest_subtitle": "Bosses don't like bottles.",
  "quest.576BD65CB87BF19A.quest_desc": [
    "A soularium ingot over three fused quartz. Use it on a mob to bottle its soul and on a block to let it out; bosses and the Warden refuse. Filled vials are what the soul binder works with."
  ],
  "quest.36D3D56CD6539A3D.title": "Ensouled Chassis",
  "quest.36D3D56CD6539A3D.quest_subtitle": "A machine frame with a pulse.",
  "quest.36D3D56CD6539A3D.quest_desc": [
    "Four soul chains, four soularium and a nether quartz; a soularium ingot, two nuggets and two quartz dust make two chains. The Slice'N'Splice, the soul binder, the soul engine, the obelisks and the powered spawner are built on it."
  ],
  "quest.10AD70D063F194D4.title": "Slice'N'Splice",
  "quest.10AD70D063F194D4.quest_subtitle": "Six slots of mad science.",
  "quest.10AD70D063F194D4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Soularium, iron bars, two energized gears and any mob head from \"},{\"text\":\"The Ender\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"0C06EBFD1EF57C04\"}},{\"text\":\" on an ensouled chassis. Six ingredients in, one part out, 20,000 µI each: zombie heads give the \"},{\"text\":\"Z-Logic Controller\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"enderio:z_logic_controller\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and the \"},{\"text\":\"Zombie Electrode\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"enderio:zombie_electrode\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An Enderman Head gives the \"},{\"text\":\"Ender Resonator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"enderio:ender_resonator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" of the wireless charger; a skeleton skull and rotten flesh, the skeletal contractor of the big filter. Energized gears are energetic alloy around an iron gear.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2623C38525221AD5.title": "Z-Logic Controller",
  "quest.2623C38525221AD5.quest_subtitle": "Brains, repurposed.",
  "quest.2623C38525221AD5.quest_desc": [
    "A zombie head, two soularium, two silicon and redstone in the Slice'N'Splice. The soul binder and the advanced item filter need one; in this pack the powered spawner takes an Ecosystem Capsule instead."
  ],
  "quest.5A78DF7A13BA1B0E.title": "Soul Binder",
  "quest.5A78DF7A13BA1B0E.quest_subtitle": "Put a little soul into it.",
  "quest.5A78DF7A13BA1B0E.quest_desc": [
    "Soularium, two energized gears, a soul vial and a Z-Logic Controller on an ensouled chassis. It pours a vial's soul into an item, and each binding also costs experience levels: that's how you get crystals, tokens, bound modules and spawners with a new mob."
  ],
  "quest.730DF7082497C5E9.title": "Soul Engine",
  "quest.730DF7082497C5E9.quest_subtitle": "Runs on spirit. And lava.",
  "quest.730DF7082497C5E9.quest_desc": [
    "Soularium, fused quartz, two buckets and a zombie electrode on an ensouled chassis. Bind a soul to it and it burns that mob's fuel: a blaze's burns lava at 800 µI per mB, a zombie's or husk's Nutrient Distillation at 1,000, a creeper's Rocket Fuel at 800."
  ],
  "quest.0BCADE43AF94113C.title": "Powered Spawner",
  "quest.0BCADE43AF94113C.quest_subtitle": "A spawner that takes requests.",
  "quest.0BCADE43AF94113C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Breaking a monster spawner drops a \"},{\"text\":\"Broken Spawner\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"enderio:broken_spawner\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" that keeps its mob. With soularium, an ensouled chassis, two vibrant crystals and, in this pack, an \"},{\"text\":\"Ecosystem Capsule\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:ecosystem_capsule\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (act IV, where the Z-Logic Controller was), it becomes the \"},{\"text\":\"Powered Spawner\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"enderio:powered_spawner\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"It spawns four at a time and waits while two of its mob are near. The soul binder changes its mob, and a \"},{\"text\":\"Mind Killer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"enderio:mind_killer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on top leaves its spawns standing still, without a thought in their heads.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4BB79B63B2F0F186.title": "Bound crystals",
  "quest.4BB79B63B2F0F186.quest_subtitle": "Minerals with a mind of their own.",
  "quest.4BB79B63B2F0F186.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"In the soul binder, an enderman's soul turns a vibrant crystal into an \"},{\"text\":\"Ender Crystal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"enderio:ender_crystal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", and a villager's turns an emerald into an \"},{\"text\":\"Enticing Crystal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"enderio:enticing_crystal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "The ender crystal goes into the staff of travelling, the inhibitor obelisk and the weather crystal; the enticing crystal into the attractor obelisk."
  ],
  "quest.02E5F91D7575EC21.title": "Obelisks",
  "quest.02E5F91D7575EC21.quest_subtitle": "Crowd control, soul by soul.",
  "quest.02E5F91D7575EC21.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A soul filter, paper around a soul vial, tells an obelisk which mobs it acts on: up to nine souls, as an allow or a deny list. The \"},{\"text\":\"Aversion Obelisk\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"enderio:aversion_obelisk\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", an enderman head over energetic alloy and soularium, stops them spawning up to 16 blocks away.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "It only stops natural spawns, so spawners keep working. It needs a capacitor and power, like the attractor, relocator and inhibitor: a double-layer capacitor doubles their reach, an octadic triples it, and a smaller range in the screen draws less power. The screen can also show the range."
  ],
  "quest.10EAA924300B41A4.title": "Attractor Obelisk",
  "quest.10EAA924300B41A4.quest_subtitle": "Come closer. I don't bite. The grinder does.",
  "quest.10EAA924300B41A4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An \"},{\"text\":\"Enticing Crystal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"enderio:enticing_crystal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on top, energetic alloy, soularium and an energized gear around an ensouled chassis. The mobs its soul filter lists walk to it from up to 8 blocks away; slimes and phantoms chase it, ghasts get dragged in, bosses stay put.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7374C26E9ECA287A.title": "Relocator Obelisk",
  "quest.7374C26E9ECA287A.quest_subtitle": "Spawn wherever you like, as long as it's here.",
  "quest.7374C26E9ECA287A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Prismarine on top of an \"},{\"text\":\"Aversion Obelisk\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"enderio:aversion_obelisk\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It doesn't cancel spawns, it moves them: a listed mob that spawns naturally up to 16 blocks away appears within 5 blocks of the obelisk instead. Build the killing floor around it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.40D1D0464F984914.title": "Inhibitor Obelisk",
  "quest.40D1D0464F984914.quest_subtitle": "Stay put. Yes, you too, enderman.",
  "quest.40D1D0464F984914.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An \"},{\"text\":\"Ender Crystal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"enderio:ender_crystal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on top and an infinity bimetal gear in the middle; it needs no filter. Any teleport that starts or ends up to 16 blocks away fails: endermen, shulkers, ender pearls, chorus fruit.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Your own staff of travelling and anchors fail too\",\"color\":\"#FF8C7A\"},{\"text\":\", so keep it away from your travel network. Only commands get through.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7FA0FE7B6CF3E4F6.title": "Glass with a guest list",
  "quest.7FA0FE7B6CF3E4F6.quest_subtitle": "Monsters only. Dress code enforced.",
  "quest.7FA0FE7B6CF3E4F6.quest_desc": [
    "The soul binder puts a creature's, a monster's or a villager's soul into a soularium or dark steel grinding ball: an animal, a monster or a player token. Eight clear glass around a token let only that kind walk through; a redstone torch inverts it."
  ],
  "quest.053B1DD6C44B6BBD.title": "Night shift",
  "quest.053B1DD6C44B6BBD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A photovoltaic module bound with a phantom's soul works at night instead of by day. Set one beside a regular module and the sun never sets on your power.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.145E2008DDBD786D.title": "Wireless Charger",
  "quest.145E2008DDBD786D.quest_subtitle": "Charging at a distance.",
  "quest.145E2008DDBD786D.quest_desc": [
    "Seven conductive alloy, an Ender Resonator and a void chassis. It charges the gear of every player within 16 blocks; a pulsating antenna on top adds 16 more, a vibrant one 32."
  ],
  "quest.6D2602E31E10A196.title": "XP Obelisk",
  "quest.6D2602E31E10A196.quest_subtitle": "A bank for your levels.",
  "quest.6D2602E31E10A196.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two \"},{\"text\":\"Suspicious Seeds\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"enderio:suspicious_seed\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" from the bedrock fire, two soularium and a vibrant alloy make the \"},{\"text\":\"Experience Rod\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"enderio:experience_rod\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; on an ensouled chassis it becomes the \"},{\"text\":\"XP Obelisk\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"enderio:xp_obelisk\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It stores your levels, one, ten or all at a time, as XP Juice.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The same seeds, fused quartz, soularium and grains make the \"},{\"text\":\"Vial of the Void\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"enderio:void_vial\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": it gathers experience orbs for you and pours them into tanks. XP Juice is 20 mB per point, and Create Enchantment Industry takes it too.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2C00D6FBBDF5EDB7.title": "Weather Obelisk",
  "quest.2C00D6FBBDF5EDB7.quest_subtitle": "Rain dance, automated.",
  "quest.2C00D6FBBDF5EDB7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two pulsating and two vibrant crystals around an ender crystal make the \"},{\"text\":\"Weather Crystal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"enderio:weather_crystal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; with energetic alloy and soularium on a void chassis it becomes the obelisk. A bucket of Liquid Sunshine clears the sky, Cloud Seed brings rain, Concentrated Cloud Seed a thunderstorm.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3048B9DA65FC70F9.title": "Scratched on a soul vial",
  "quest.3048B9DA65FC70F9.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The binder never asked whose soul it held. A zombie's hunger turned our gears, a villager's want filled the square. Then Aurelia asked if the light could be bound the same way. —T.\",\"italic\":true}]"
  ],
  "quest.1406691E2833E3E1.title": "Pulsating Crystal",
  "quest.1406691E2833E3E1.quest_subtitle": "A diamond, wrapped in a heartbeat.",
  "quest.1406691E2833E3E1.quest_desc": [
    "Eight pulsating alloy nuggets around a diamond. Travel anchors, the vacuum chest, the XP vacuum and the weather crystal run on it."
  ],
  "quest.1D4A911B1A08FD3B.title": "Travel Anchor",
  "quest.1D4A911B1A08FD3B.quest_subtitle": "Jump here, land there.",
  "quest.1D4A911B1A08FD3B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Iron, conduit binder, a pulsating crystal and, in this pack, a \"},{\"text\":\"Reinforced Alloy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:alloy_reinforced\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (act III, where the top binder was). Stand on one, look at another within 96 blocks and jump: you're on top of it.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "An anchor you aim at has to be more than 5 blocks away, with nothing solid on top. Its screen gives it a name and an icon, and can hide it: a hidden anchor still works as an elevator stop, but you can't aim at it."
  ],
  "quest.1CBC5CD12D589E2C.title": "Coordinate Selector",
  "quest.1CBC5CD12D589E2C.quest_subtitle": "X marks the spot. So do Y and Z.",
  "quest.1CBC5CD12D589E2C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four conductive alloy, an ender pearl and a compass. Aim it at a block up to 64 blocks away, or use it on one, with paper in your inventory: name the spot and it prints a \"},{\"text\":\"Location Printout\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"enderio:location_printout\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" with its coordinates and dimension.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Nothing in this version reads printouts: they're notes. Hand one to a teammate to find your anchors; sneak and use it to look at it again."
  ],
  "quest.4C0960D2B324605B.title": "Anchor elevator",
  "quest.4C0960D2B324605B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Stack anchors in a shaft: jump on one to rise to the next anchor above, sneak to drop to the one below. Painted in the painting machine, an anchor passes for any block.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1C31B9A349119E42.title": "Staff of Travelling",
  "quest.1C31B9A349119E42.quest_subtitle": "Blink and you'll miss it.",
  "quest.1C31B9A349119E42.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two dark steel ingots, an \"},{\"text\":\"Ender Crystal\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"4BB79B63B2F0F186\"}},{\"text\":\" and, in this pack, a \"},{\"text\":\"Reinforced Alloy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:alloy_reinforced\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (act III). Aimed at an anchor up to 192 blocks away it takes you there; aimed at nothing it blinks you up to 24 blocks ahead.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Each jump costs 1,000 µI of the 100,000 it holds: a \"},{\"text\":\"wired charger\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"25C8FD789B52567E\"}},{\"text\":\" tops it up.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.464B32F40AA64FFF.title": "Hands-free travel",
  "quest.464B32F40AA64FFF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The staff and the electromagnet fit the two charm slots. Worn there, \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.enderio.travel_staff\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" fires the staff without holding it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.21A75B7236607A5D.title": "Electromagnet",
  "quest.21A75B7236607A5D.quest_subtitle": "Loot comes to you.",
  "quest.21A75B7236607A5D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four energetic alloy, two conductive and a vibrant crystal. Charged, it pulls up to 20 items at a time within 5 blocks; \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.enderio.toggle_magnet\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" switches it on and off.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.227CE8A025FDAF03.title": "Vacuums",
  "quest.227CE8A025FDAF03.quest_subtitle": "Nature abhors a loose item.",
  "quest.227CE8A025FDAF03.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A chest or a Vial of the Void, iron and a pulsating crystal. The \"},{\"text\":\"Vacuum Chest\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"enderio:vacuum_chest\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" pulls in dropped items and the \"},{\"text\":\"XP Vacuum\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"enderio:xp_vacuum\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" experience orbs, up to 6 blocks away and with no power; a filter picks what they take.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.135564FDD80E7A6E.title": "What the pack changes",
  "quest.135564FDD80E7A6E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four Ender IO recipes wait on the Atlas: the travel anchor and the staff take a \"},{\"text\":\"Reinforced Alloy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:alloy_reinforced\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (III), the powered spawner an \"},{\"text\":\"Ecosystem Capsule\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:ecosystem_capsule\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (IV), the octadic capacitor an \"},{\"text\":\"Atomic Alloy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:alloy_atomic\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (V).\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Three parts Ender IO marks as unfinished stay off: the Farming Station, the Niard and the Ender IO block. The Staff of Levity and the Cold Fire Igniter burn Vapor of Levity, which nothing makes in this version."
  ],
  "quest.06AB35A28BAEDC31.title": "Found in the rubble",
  "quest.06AB35A28BAEDC31.quest_subtitle": "Some capacitors age like wine.",
  "quest.06AB35A28BAEDC31.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Dungeon, mineshaft, temple and stronghold chests hide \"},{\"text\":\"Loot Capacitors\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"enderio:loot_capacitor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Each rolls a base level from 1 to 4, past an octadic's 3, and one random bonus, sometimes two or three: Hot, Efficient, Hungry or Insatiable.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.1993F4C76B5CF7D1.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.56225D9E8536B681.title": "Energetic by the batch",
  "quest.56225D9E8536B681.quest_subtitle": "The smelter's favourite shift.",
  "quest.56225D9E8536B681.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Thirty-two \"},{\"text\":\"Energetic Alloy Ingots\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"enderio:energetic_alloy_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for the common store, once a day. Two smelters in a row, one making conductive alloy for the other, keep up with ease.\"}]"
  ],
  "image.729879EF23EBF09F.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Power\",\"color\":\"#D6E0E4\"}]",
  "image.11D6A9D6BE1B0BF2.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Paint and glass\",\"color\":\"#D6E0E4\"}]",
  "image.7BC359FAFE617584.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Conduits\",\"color\":\"#D6E0E4\"}]",
  "image.7748E93585D6CA22.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Crystals and travel\",\"color\":\"#D6E0E4\"}]",
  "image.262F4BA66D9BAB68.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"SAG mill\",\"color\":\"#D6E0E4\"}]",
  "image.78CAB25F9B37A342.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Dark steel\",\"color\":\"#D6E0E4\"}]",
  "image.1EA83E1FF23CEAED.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Souls\",\"color\":\"#D6E0E4\"}]",
  "image.51291033B7BAC1F4.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Ender IO\",\"color\":\"#EFFFF8\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.2A8451DF0763E978.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"alloy · grind · bind · travel\",\"color\":\"#D6E0E4\",\"font\":\"minecraft:uniform\"}]",
  "image.1C1528B3CF103AFD.title": "Back to the Sun of Heliodor",
  "chapter.1D73780D03CDB8CA.title": "Immersive Engineering · Workshop",
  "chapter.1D73780D03CDB8CA.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Coke, steel and a workbench; then one power line, from copper to high voltage."
  ],
  "quest.2B1BA98A994FB367.title": "Engineer's Hammer",
  "quest.2B1BA98A994FB367.quest_subtitle": "Everything looks like a multiblock now.",
  "quest.2B1BA98A994FB367.quest_desc": [
    "Two iron ingots, a string and two sticks. Hit the right block of a finished structure and it becomes a machine; put the hammer in the grid with an ingot and a plate comes out."
  ],
  "quest.16C6724941C8D5A0.title": "Plates and wire",
  "quest.16C6724941C8D5A0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two sticks and an iron ingot make the \"},{\"text\":\"Wire Cutters\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:wirecutter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", which cut a plate into \"},{\"text\":\"Copper Wire\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:wire_copper\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Copper, iron and gold plates come out as Create's sheets here: the pack unifies them, and every IE recipe takes them.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.62E79350144A921A.title": "Coke bricks",
  "quest.62E79350144A921A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four clay balls, four bricks and a sandstone make three \"},{\"text\":\"Coke Bricks\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:cokebrick\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". The oven takes twenty-seven: nine crafts.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.16BB750E0B5100BC.title": "Form the Coke Oven",
  "quest.6342BA3BE73211E7.title": "Coke Oven",
  "quest.6342BA3BE73211E7.quest_subtitle": "Slow cooking, industrial edition.",
  "quest.6342BA3BE73211E7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A 3×3×3 cube of coke bricks, hammered on the middle of one side. Coal becomes \"},{\"text\":\"Coal Coke\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:coal_coke\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", logs become charcoal, and \"},{\"text\":\"Creosote Oil\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:creosote_bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" pools inside: the oven never pushes it out.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.198DDD6970B0D71E.title": "Black gold, the cheap kind",
  "quest.198DDD6970B0D71E.quest_desc": [
    "Put an empty bucket in the oven's container slot, or pump the oil out: the oven keeps it but never pushes it. Creosote treats wood, burns in a diesel generator and bakes graphite later on."
  ],
  "quest.1045167B3B74EF65.title": "Treated wood",
  "quest.1045167B3B74EF65.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight planks around a bucket of creosote make eight \"},{\"text\":\"Treated Wood Planks\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:treated_wood_horizontal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", and the bucket comes back empty. Posts, crates, barrels, the workbench and the windmill blades are made of it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7F780E719DB499E8.title": "A table that remembers",
  "quest.7F780E719DB499E8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A crafting table under three treated slabs, on four treated sticks. The \"},{\"text\":\"Engineer's Crafting Table\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:craftingtable\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" keeps the ingredients in its grid when you close it, has a drawer for parts, and goes into the workbench.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7FB271D328A5C07B.title": "Engineer's Workbench",
  "quest.7FB271D328A5C07B.quest_subtitle": "Measure twice, craft once.",
  "quest.7FB271D328A5C07B.quest_desc": [
    "Two treated slabs, an iron ingot, the engineer's crafting table and a treated fence. With a blueprint in the left slot it builds what the drawing describes; with a tool in the middle it opens that tool's upgrade slots."
  ],
  "quest.61CECFCE3044B172.title": "Drawing the parts",
  "quest.61CECFCE3044B172.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Copper, lead and iron ingots over three blue dyes and three paper: the components \"},{\"text\":\"Engineer's Blueprint\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:blueprint\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". At the workbench it makes mechanical parts from half the plates, plus electronic parts, vacuum tubes and light bulbs, which have no other recipe.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6C49A30A43C4333B.title": "Blast bricks",
  "quest.6C49A30A43C4333B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four nether bricks, four bricks and a magma block make three \"},{\"text\":\"Blast Bricks\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:blastbrick\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; twenty-seven again. A trip to the Nether is the price of steel.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.112F07CF5A566D95.title": "Form the Crude Blast Furnace",
  "quest.06A796A61550B901.title": "Steel, the slow way",
  "quest.06A796A61550B901.quest_subtitle": "Iron in, patience out.",
  "quest.06A796A61550B901.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Blast bricks in a 3×3×3, hammered on the middle of a side. Iron and coke become \"},{\"text\":\"Steel\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:ingot_steel\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and \"},{\"text\":\"Slag\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:slag\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", one minute per ingot; \"},{\"text\":\"empty the slag\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\" or it stops. It can't be automated: the improved furnace can.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2BE2EAD98ED9C297.title": "Moving parts",
  "quest.2BE2EAD98ED9C297.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four plates around a copper ingot make an \"},{\"text\":\"Iron Mechanical Component\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:component_iron\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; steel plates make the \"},{\"text\":\"Steel Mechanical Component\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:component_steel\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". The components blueprint builds either from two plates.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Iron plates here are Create's iron sheets: a Mechanical Press makes them by the stack.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.793BFE553E1E2058.title": "From turning to current",
  "quest.793BFE553E1E2058.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Redstone, iron, an iron component and a \"},{\"text\":\"Copper Coil Block\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:coil_lv\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (eight LV wire coils around iron) make the \"},{\"text\":\"Kinetic Dynamo\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:dynamo\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It turns IE windmills and water wheels into power; other mods' rotation doesn't count.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.666D53F2AC1B9BF1.title": "Catch the wind",
  "quest.666D53F2AC1B9BF1.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight treated \"},{\"text\":\"Windmill Blades\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:windmill_blade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" around an iron ingot. Place it after the dynamo, facing open air: the more clear space, the faster it turns. Rain speeds it up and a thunderstorm doubles it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.06A06670E2922640.title": "Power in a box",
  "quest.06A06670E2922640.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four redstone and a water bucket make \"},{\"text\":\"Redstone Acid\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:redstone_acid_bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; with copper, lead plates and a basic engineering block it fills an \"},{\"text\":\"LV Accumulator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:capacitor_lv\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": \"},{\"text\":\"100,000 FE\",\"color\":\"#F2C14E\"},{\"text\":\", 256 FE/t each way. The hammer sets each side: blue takes, orange gives.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.6BB67CF5FEF2DD49.title": "String a wire",
  "quest.05A81D1DB02F0938.title": "Low voltage",
  "quest.05A81D1DB02F0938.quest_subtitle": "Birds sold separately.",
  "quest.05A81D1DB02F0938.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Copper wire around a stick makes \"},{\"text\":\"LV Wire Coils\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:wirecoil_copper\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Click a coil on one \"},{\"text\":\"LV Wire Connector\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:connector_lv\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", then on another up to 16 blocks away; a block in the way breaks it. Connectors feed in or out, \"},{\"text\":\"relays\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:connector_lv_relay\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" only join.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0168B4C9C96BFEAC.title": "Mixing metals",
  "quest.0168B4C9C96BFEAC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two sandstone and two bricks make two \"},{\"text\":\"Kiln Bricks\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:alloybrick\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; eight form a 2×2×2 kiln with the hammer. On ordinary fuel it melts gold and silver into \"},{\"text\":\"Electrum\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:ingot_electrum\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and copper and nickel into \"},{\"text\":\"Constantan\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:ingot_constantan\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", two ingots from two.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.75BC7C36CE640594.title": "Medium voltage",
  "quest.75BC7C36CE640594.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Electrum wire makes \"},{\"text\":\"MV Wire Coils\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:wirecoil_electrum\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and electrum ingots make \"},{\"text\":\"MV Wire Connectors\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:connector_mv\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Four times the LV rate: 1,024 FE/t per connector, over the same 16-block spans.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1FFE721A59721D92.title": "A brain for the grid",
  "quest.1FFE721A59721D92.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The components blueprint turns a treated slab, quartz, redstone and \"},{\"text\":\"Electrum Wire\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:wire_electrum\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" into an \"},{\"text\":\"Electronic Component\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:component_electronic\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Transformers, the item batcher, the current transformer and the redstone breaker all need one.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0570C07787BD0498.title": "Stepping up",
  "quest.0570C07787BD0498.quest_subtitle": "Two voltages, one handshake.",
  "quest.0570C07787BD0498.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"LV and MV connectors, an electronic component, an \"},{\"text\":\"Electrum Coil Block\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:coil_mv\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and iron make the \"},{\"text\":\"Transformer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:transformer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". A wire only takes its own voltage; this box joins an LV line to an MV one.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Standard transformers sit on posts. The HV one doesn't.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.20953157B0C5536F.title": "Light metal",
  "quest.20953157B0C5536F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Bauxite sits high, between y 32 and 112, and its raw ore smelts into \"},{\"text\":\"Aluminium Ingots\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:ingot_aluminum\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". HV connectors and relays, and the HV wire itself, need it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3CE2C97FBB40FB47.title": "Steel wire",
  "quest.3CE2C97FBB40FB47.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Cut steel and aluminium plates into wire; two of each around a stick make four \"},{\"text\":\"HV Wire Coils\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:wirecoil_steel\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". A span reaches 32 blocks and carries up to 32,768 FE/t.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"HV can't be insulated.\",\"color\":\"#FF8C7A\"},{\"text\":\" Keep it high and out of reach.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.66E20CE4690CCA57.title": "Insulators",
  "quest.66E20CE4690CCA57.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Aluminium and terracotta make \"},{\"text\":\"HV Wire Connectors\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:connector_hv\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". The \"},{\"text\":\"HV Wire Relay\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:connector_hv_relay\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" needs glass that insulates: \"},{\"text\":\"Insulating Glass\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:insulating_glass\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" from the kiln (glass and iron grit) or \"},{\"text\":\"Slag Glass\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:slag_glass\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" from smelting slag.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.074506465E69FF91.title": "High voltage",
  "quest.074506465E69FF91.quest_subtitle": "Mind the gap. And the wire.",
  "quest.074506465E69FF91.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"MV and HV connectors, an electronic component, a \"},{\"text\":\"High-Voltage Coil Block\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:coil_hv\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and iron make the \"},{\"text\":\"HV Transformer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:transformer_hv\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It steps MV up to HV, or LV straight to HV.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"One HV connector moves 4,096 FE/t, exactly what a \"},{\"text\":\"diesel generator\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"6501E1AE152E3230\"}},{\"text\":\" puts out. The line is ready for \"},{\"text\":\"industry\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"693B56B9AD358543\"}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.56C0E235A8D6BCD8.title": "Read the manual",
  "quest.56C0E235A8D6BCD8.quest_subtitle": "The first advancement literally says RTFM.",
  "quest.56C0E235A8D6BCD8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A book and a lever make the \"},{\"text\":\"Engineer's Manual\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:manual\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": every multiblock in 3D, layer by layer, with its recipes and the real numbers of this pack's config.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.63232AC715A83A6E.title": "The hammer's side job",
  "quest.63232AC715A83A6E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Raw ore and the hammer in the grid make one grit. Gold and silver grit mix into electrum grit, copper and nickel into constantan: smelt it and you have alloys before any kiln.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.1A89B417D00E8D72.title": "Lead: y -32 to 80",
  "task.374CA01752C6C34B.title": "Silver: y -48 to 32",
  "task.3F845230662ED85B.title": "Nickel: y -64 to 24",
  "task.2C7F71ACAE780D4E.title": "Bauxite: y 32 to 112",
  "task.4BE7C9ADCF866D89.title": "Uranium: y -64 to -16",
  "quest.47A1ECFDC78DB908.title": "Five new ores",
  "quest.47A1ECFDC78DB908.quest_desc": [
    "Lead, silver, nickel, bauxite and uranium, each at its own depth: the task titles say where. Bauxite needs a stone pickaxe, the rest iron. Almost Unified ranks IE right after Create, so other mods' lead and uranium come out as IE's."
  ],
  "quest.370620B2987FD43B.title": "Industrial hemp",
  "quest.370620B2987FD43B.quest_subtitle": "Strictly for rope.",
  "quest.370620B2987FD43B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Breaking grass drops \"},{\"text\":\"Industrial Hemp Seeds\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:seed\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" one time in ten, never with shears. Planted, it grows two blocks tall, and the grown plant drops \"},{\"text\":\"Industrial Hemp Fiber\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:hemp_fiber\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4195B6C62C7700B6.title": "Tough fabric",
  "quest.4195B6C62C7700B6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight fibres around a stick make \"},{\"text\":\"Tough Fabric\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:hemp_fabric\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": windmill sails, insulated wire, survey tools, the maintenance kit and balloons. Eight around a honeycomb become \"},{\"text\":\"Ersatz Leather\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:ersatz_leather\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", which conveyors take as leather.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.782D87D166D2FD93.title": "Soft landings",
  "quest.782D87D166D2FD93.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight tough fabric make three \"},{\"text\":\"Jump Cushions\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:cushion\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": land on one and it costs no health, and it won't bounce you like slime. Fabric, aluminium rods and a leather chestplate make a \"},{\"text\":\"Collapsible Glider\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:glider\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", an elytra for engineers: frailer, and mended with fabric.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7A427A01ECF4C8A0.title": "Batches",
  "quest.7A427A01ECF4C8A0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The oven cooks in batches: up to 16 coal or 8 logs at once, five minutes for coal, and 500 mB of creosote per coal. Build a second oven before you start waiting on the first.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.69019B46EA324FC8.title": "Coke run",
  "quest.69019B46EA324FC8.quest_subtitle": "Fresh from the oven.",
  "quest.69019B46EA324FC8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Thirty-two \"},{\"text\":\"Coal Coke\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:coal_coke\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for the common store, once a day. Two ovens fed and emptied by hoppers, and you'll forget it's a chore.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.42CCE14A2EC05A80.title": "Fuel for steel",
  "quest.42CCE14A2EC05A80.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"In the blast furnace a coke burns 1,200 ticks, exactly one steel ingot; charcoal lasts a quarter of that. A block of coke feeds ten ingots.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.43F1084DA3F23C1A.title": "Form the Improved Blast Furnace",
  "quest.0F81B6C555554DD9.title": "Hands-free steel",
  "quest.0F81B6C555554DD9.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A steel plate on a blast brick reinforces it; twenty-seven plus a hopper on top form the \"},{\"text\":\"Improved Blast Furnace\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:advanced_blast_furnace\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Iron and coke go in the hopper, steel leaves by the front and slag by the back, on its own.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.333B532EFD4B639C.title": "Hot air",
  "quest.333B532EFD4B639C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Iron sheetmetal, a fluid pipe and an \"},{\"text\":\"External Heater\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:furnace_heater\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make a \"},{\"text\":\"Blast Furnace Preheater\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:blastfurnace_preheater\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Up to two per improved furnace, one on each side port, 32 FE/t each: they speed up the refining.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.19EF7BC578945909.title": "Nothing wasted",
  "quest.19EF7BC578945909.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Smelt \"},{\"text\":\"Slag\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:slag\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" into \"},{\"text\":\"Slag Glass\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:slag_glass\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", an HV relay insulator; four slag make four slag bricks. Crushed, it becomes a gravel that waterlogged plants grow faster on.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7ECE80B5C64FDB89.title": "Concrete",
  "quest.7ECE80B5C64FDB89.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Sand, gravel, clay and a water bucket make eight \"},{\"text\":\"Concrete\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:concrete\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". A lead plate turns one into \"},{\"text\":\"Leaded Concrete\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:concrete_leaded\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": endermen, ender pearls and chorus fruit can't teleport through it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6FC66E15CFE88934.title": "River power",
  "quest.6FC66E15CFE88934.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four treated \"},{\"text\":\"Waterwheel Segments\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:waterwheel_segment\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" around a steel ingot make the \"},{\"text\":\"Water Wheel\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:watermill\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It spins in flowing water, faster with more water around it, and up to three wheels share one dynamo's shaft.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.622EE9D4CE4B401E.title": "Cloth on the blades",
  "quest.622EE9D4CE4B401E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Six tough fabric make a \"},{\"text\":\"Windmill Sail\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:windmill_sail\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; right-click the windmill to fit one, up to eight. With all eight it turns three times as fast as bare.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.030B03014D4055F2.title": "Hot and cold",
  "quest.030B03014D4055F2.quest_subtitle": "No moving parts, no excuses.",
  "quest.030B03014D4055F2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Steel, constantan plates and a copper coil block make the \"},{\"text\":\"Thermoelectric Generator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:thermoelectric_generator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Something hot on one side, something cold on the opposite one: the bigger the gap, the more power.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Blocks count too: magma is 1,300 K, blue ice 200 K and a block of uranium 2,000 K.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.50B780D40275F29E.title": "A bigger battery",
  "quest.50B780D40275F29E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Electrum, a nickel plate, an iron plate and redstone acid on a basic engineering block make the \"},{\"text\":\"MV Accumulator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:capacitor_mv\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": 1,000,000 FE, 1,024 FE/t each way.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.331AA361ACB8B24F.title": "Know your limits",
  "quest.331AA361ACB8B24F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Per connector: LV 256, MV 1,024, HV 4,096 FE/t. A wire burns out past eight connectors' worth: 2,048, 8,192 and 32,768 FE/t. Loss grows with length, least on HV.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5FDB4A08FB06C113.title": "Switches and meters",
  "quest.5FDB4A08FB06C113.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Breaker Switch\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:breaker_switch\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" cuts an LV or MV line by hand; the \"},{\"text\":\"Redstone Breaker\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:redstone_breaker\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" also handles HV, but only redstone flips it. A \"},{\"text\":\"Current Transformer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:current_transformer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in a line reports the average FE/t through it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5C95176D4AF2CDAF.title": "The frame of small machines",
  "quest.5C95176D4AF2CDAF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four iron ingots and four treated planks make four \"},{\"text\":\"Basic Engineering Blocks\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:basic_engineering\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", the core of single-block machines: accumulators, routers, batchers, the cloche and the logic unit.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6FF1D244B797D182.title": "Crates that travel",
  "quest.6FF1D244B797D182.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight treated planks make a \"},{\"text\":\"Wooden Storage Crate\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:crate\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": 27 slots, a comparator reading and a name you can edit. Hold the hammer on it to seal it, and it keeps its contents when broken. The \"},{\"text\":\"Reinforced Storage Crate\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:reinforced_crate\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" shrugs off explosions.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.1DEB4688502D6A1C.title": "Any IE storage minecart",
  "quest.7F04D1787B1D35A5.title": "Freight on rails",
  "quest.7F04D1787B1D35A5.quest_subtitle": "Choo-choo, with inventory.",
  "quest.7F04D1787B1D35A5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A crate or a barrel over a minecart in the crafting grid puts it on rails. A \"},{\"text\":\"Minecart with Wooden Storage Crate\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:minecart_woodencrate\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" keeps its items when broken, which a chest cart never did, and a barrel cart still fills and empties with buckets.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2A77986568EE89F3.title": "Everything in one box",
  "quest.2A77986568EE89F3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three aluminium plates, red dye and a crate make the \"},{\"text\":\"Engineer's Toolbox\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:toolbox\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": slots for tools, wiring, food and anything else. Sneak-click to set it down as a block, and again to pick it up.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6416A424C49357EB.title": "Barrels",
  "quest.6416A424C49357EB.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Wooden Barrel\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:wooden_barrel\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" holds 12 buckets of anything cool; the \"},{\"text\":\"Metal Barrel\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:metal_barrel\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" also takes hot fluids and gases, and redstone stops its output. The hammer picks which side pushes.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1EEC49E6F49D96A4.title": "Repairs on the road",
  "quest.1EEC49E6F49D96A4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A screwdriver, wire cutters and three tough fabric roll up into a \"},{\"text\":\"Maintenance Kit\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:maintenance_kit\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It does the workbench's tool job anywhere: swap the drill head in the mine, retune the ear defenders on the spot.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.2545037B03BBB219.title": "Buy a shader grabbag",
  "quest.31470A3BB9E83CF8.title": "Paint jobs",
  "quest.31470A3BB9E83CF8.quest_subtitle": "Form follows function. Then it gets a paint job.",
  "quest.31470A3BB9E83CF8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An Outfitter sells \"},{\"text\":\"Shader Grabbags\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:shader_bag_common\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": each holds a random shader at least as rare as the bag, likelier one you don't own. At the workbench a shader restyles the revolver, drill, railgun, shield or backpack; right-click one onto a minecart, banner or balloon.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.54369146F83D7220.title": "Look at a banner wearing a shader",
  "quest.622E64F2F4C6925A.title": "The Outfitter's banner",
  "quest.622E64F2F4C6925A.quest_subtitle": "Now hiring: one villager with taste.",
  "quest.622E64F2F4C6925A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Right-click a placed banner with a \"},{\"text\":\"Shader\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:shader\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and it takes the design. That banner is the Outfitter's job site, so a villager without a trade nearby can claim it. The same click dresses a minecart or a balloon.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.5F486649A635DFBA.title": "Meet an IE villager",
  "quest.5DCC6AFF9F914661.title": "Colleagues in the village",
  "quest.5DCC6AFF9F914661.quest_desc": [
    "Five IE trades take an IE workstation: Structural Engineer, Machinist, Electrician, Gunsmith and Outfitter. They sell parts, wire and blueprints, and even maps to mineral veins. Talk to one.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Job sites: a \"},{\"text\":\"Turntable\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:turntable\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for the Structural Engineer, the \"},{\"text\":\"Engineer's Crafting Table\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:craftingtable\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for the Machinist, the \"},{\"text\":\"Engineer's Circuit Workbench\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:circuit_table\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for the Electrician, the \"},{\"text\":\"Engineer's Workbench\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:workbench\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for the Gunsmith and a banner wearing a shader for the Outfitter. Villages can generate a house for each.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.5811F3A9CA334254.title": "Win a raid",
  "quest.5E8E96C4F7D55EF1.title": "Hero of the engineers",
  "quest.5E8E96C4F7D55EF1.quest_subtitle": "Paid in steel.",
  "quest.5E8E96C4F7D55EF1.quest_desc": [
    "Win a raid and the village's engineers throw gifts like any villager: rods from the Structural Engineer, components from the Machinist, a piece of Faraday armour from the Electrician, special cartridges or an extended magazine from the Gunsmith, a banner or a rare or epic shader grabbag from the Outfitter."
  ],
  "quest.0C07FF6EDA513F23.title": "Things that roll",
  "quest.0C07FF6EDA513F23.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three leather, two iron and redstone make eight \"},{\"text\":\"Conveyor Belts\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:conveyor_basic\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". No power needed: they carry items and mobs and push into inventories. The hammer turns a belt, and sneaking with it tilts it up or down.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.38CE2338F5B226F8.title": "Extracting",
  "task.1AEAA982AB7A6EB9.title": "Dropping",
  "task.652C3BE1B222E3E0.title": "Vertical",
  "task.2F5AB70CF4014B4B.title": "Splitting",
  "quest.0984C08286279208.title": "Belt family",
  "quest.0984C08286279208.quest_desc": [
    "Extracting belts pull from the inventory behind them, dropping belts open a hatch downward, vertical belts lift items straight up and splitting belts alternate left and right. Dye paints the side walls."
  ],
  "quest.77BABC19265883F0.title": "Sorting",
  "quest.77BABC19265883F0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Item Router\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:sorter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" sends each item out the side whose filter matches, else any open side; filters can match a tag. The \"},{\"text\":\"Item Batcher\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:item_batcher\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" holds items until a whole batch is ready, then lets it go.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0803D2E2006743A4.title": "Sheetmetal chutes",
  "quest.0803D2E2006743A4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Six iron sheetmetal make twelve \"},{\"text\":\"Iron Sheetmetal Chutes\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:chute_iron\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Items and creatures inside drop straight into whatever is below, safe from magnets and players. Sneak with the hammer to make a corner.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.46C91BF04182491E.title": "Express delivery",
  "quest.46C91BF04182491E.quest_subtitle": "You are the item now.",
  "quest.46C91BF04182491E.quest_desc": [
    "You bounced all the way down a run of chutes. The chutes didn't enjoy it either."
  ],
  "reward.167FBE3CE91CE51B.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.727F196F0EA8255E.title": "Plumbing",
  "quest.727F196F0EA8255E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Six iron plates make eight \"},{\"text\":\"Fluid Pipes\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:fluid_pipe\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", which split flow evenly between outputs. A \"},{\"text\":\"Fluid Pump\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:fluid_pump\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" pressurizes them, far faster with FE. It also pumps pools dry and leaves cobblestone behind, unless you sneak-hammer its top.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7EE646AA35F4958C.title": "Valves and routers",
  "quest.7EE646AA35F4958C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Fluid Router\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:fluid_sorter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" sends each fluid to its filtered side, a \"},{\"text\":\"Pipe Valve\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:pipe_valve\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" shuts the flow on a redstone signal, and a \"},{\"text\":\"Fluid Outlet\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:fluid_placer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" pours it into the world.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.54D72408B635D191.title": "Form the silo",
  "task.689C6D35DD323AA5.title": "Form the tank",
  "quest.5FFC0B0935C3D644.title": "Bulk storage",
  "quest.5FFC0B0935C3D644.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Sheetmetal and four treated fences form two tall multiblocks: the \"},{\"text\":\"Item Silo\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:silo\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", 41,472 of one item (24 chests), and the \"},{\"text\":\"Fluid Tank\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:tank\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", 512 buckets. Both empty through the bottom centre.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6A3B8706127D108C.title": "Furnaces on the grid",
  "quest.6A3B8706127D108C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An \"},{\"text\":\"External Heater\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:furnace_heater\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" against a vanilla furnace heats it with \"},{\"text\":\"no fuel\",\"color\":\"#9BE08A\"},{\"text\":\": 8 FE/t per furnace, up to 32 FE/t once hot, for faster smelting. Redstone turns the boost off.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.29ABDA7768135140.title": "A greenhouse in a jar",
  "quest.29ABDA7768135140.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Glass, a light bulb, an iron component and a basic engineering block make the \"},{\"text\":\"Garden Cloche\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:cloche\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Soil and a seed in the middle, water and 8 FE/t, and it harvests by itself through the front hatch.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.644CEC7C251D8ABD.title": "Plant food",
  "quest.644CEC7C251D8ABD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"One fertilizer at a time dissolves in the cloche's water: bone meal ×1.3, slag ×1.3, \"},{\"text\":\"Industrial Fertilizer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:fertilizer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" ×1.6. The industrial one is nitrate, slag, sulfur and water.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5A755D7FE3D7DB5D.title": "Out of this world",
  "quest.5A755D7FE3D7DB5D.quest_subtitle": "It came from the End. Now it lives in a jar.",
  "quest.5A755D7FE3D7DB5D.quest_desc": [
    "Chorus fruit growing under glass, in a cloche. Nobody asked the fruit."
  ],
  "reward.3600D33DE1C2CC9C.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.185DBC6D711573E8.title": "Lights on",
  "quest.185DBC6D711573E8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A light bulb, glass, an iron plate and copper wire make a \"},{\"text\":\"Powered Lantern\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:electric_lantern\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": on LV wire it also stops hostile mobs spawning within 32 blocks. A \"},{\"text\":\"Floodlight\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:floodlight\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" throws a 32-block cone, aimed with the hammer.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2BE9D215D68B9AB0.title": "Screwdriver and meter",
  "quest.2BE9D215D68B9AB0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Engineer's Screwdriver\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:screwdriver\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" inverts a machine's redstone control. The \"},{\"text\":\"Engineer's Multimeter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:voltmeter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" reads any energy storage, and sneak-clicking two connectors measures the loss between them.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.540D9CBDBE24FB57.title": "Up on the posts",
  "quest.540D9CBDBE24FB57.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two treated fences on stone bricks make a four-block \"},{\"text\":\"Wooden Post\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:treated_post\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; the hammer on its top adds arms for connectors. \"},{\"text\":\"Wooden Wallmounts\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:treated_wallmount\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" hold connectors on a wall, facing up or down.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4DA2C7B835071026.title": "Insulated LV",
  "quest.4DA2C7B835071026.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Live bare wire hurts\",\"color\":\"#FF8C7A\"},{\"text\":\" whoever touches it. Four LV coils wrapped in five tough fabric make four \"},{\"text\":\"Insulated LV Wire Coils\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:wirecoil_copper_ins\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": safe along paths and inside the base.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.284DB7D565E0DB16.title": "Through the wall",
  "quest.284DB7D565E0DB16.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Put a connector on each side of a one-block wall and hammer one: they fuse into a \"},{\"text\":\"Feedthrough Insulator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:feedthrough\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" around the block. Wires can't cross blocks; this can.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.7286625CCE3813BF.title": "1 km on the wire",
  "quest.333A89813E96B76F.title": "Ride the line",
  "quest.333A89813E96B76F.quest_subtitle": "Zip-lining, but it's work.",
  "quest.333A89813E96B76F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Steel, an iron component and two wooden grips make the \"},{\"text\":\"Engineer's Skyhook\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:skyhook\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Hold right-click near a wire to hook on: downhill is free, uphill takes walking, sneaking lets go. \"},{\"text\":\"A live wire shocks you\",\"color\":\"#FF8C7A\"},{\"text\":\" unless the grip is insulated.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2D5E5C23E88FD31C.title": "Short circuit",
  "quest.2D5E5C23E88FD31C.quest_subtitle": "Birds sit on wires. They don't fly into them.",
  "quest.2D5E5C23E88FD31C.quest_desc": [
    "You glided into a live wire and the wire won. Insulation exists for a reason."
  ],
  "reward.1B3FC844C785FCF6.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.7ADE1D1A20F941FF.title": "A line on the drawing",
  "quest.7ADE1D1A20F941FF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"We strung copper first, because copper forgives. Steel came later, when we stopped asking whether we should. —T.\",\"italic\":true}]"
  ],
  "image.67BC9F8B2252EA80.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Ores and hemp\",\"color\":\"#F2C14E\"}]",
  "image.585458E34805669A.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Coke\",\"color\":\"#F2C14E\"}]",
  "image.7D8FE762734770B0.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Furnaces and slag\",\"color\":\"#F2C14E\"}]",
  "image.2274E3267E103152.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Power sources\",\"color\":\"#F2C14E\"}]",
  "image.310F29B10BD7E738.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"MV and HV\",\"color\":\"#F2C14E\"}]",
  "image.095E69CBF9819CBF.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Drafting table\",\"color\":\"#F2C14E\"}]",
  "image.1C703EADD366D3A1.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Belts and pipes\",\"color\":\"#F2C14E\"}]",
  "image.0CF29A0C7DCFA1D9.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"On the grid\",\"color\":\"#F2C14E\"}]",
  "image.6896E8E9030A9C4F.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Wiring kit\",\"color\":\"#F2C14E\"}]",
  "image.736E424CBBE98458.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"rope · no power yet\",\"color\":\"#C9B48A\"}]",
  "image.0A7260FB95E7EAC2.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"LV · 256 FE/t\",\"color\":\"#D9894A\"}]",
  "image.4053BA1EA46032EC.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"MV · 1,024 FE/t\",\"color\":\"#E8CF5A\"}]",
  "image.13EB9A37E59F896C.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"HV · 4,096 FE/t\",\"color\":\"#BAC6D2\"}]",
  "image.318D056326AB345A.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Immersive Engineering · Workshop\",\"color\":\"#F2C14E\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.2401E735452FAF33.title": "Back to the Sun of Heliodor",
  "image.04262183CB436117.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"IMMERSIVE ENGINEERING\",\"color\":\"#F2C14E\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.46B2B36CDA4E19E4.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Workshop · sheet 1 of 2 · drawn: T.\",\"color\":\"#F2C14E\"}]",
  "chapter.27A03545380FC2EA.title": "Industrial Foregoing",
  "chapter.27A03545380FC2EA.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Machines for every chore: latex to plastic, four frames, farms, mobs, lasers and the Infinity tools."
  ],
  "quest.6E84BC104C71370E.title": "A frame to start",
  "quest.6E84BC104C71370E.quest_subtitle": "Pity is its real name. Honest.",
  "quest.6E84BC104C71370E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four logs at the corners, four iron ingots and a block of redstone in the middle make the \"},{\"text\":\"Pity Machine Frame\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:machine_frame_pity\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". The first IF machines are built around one: the extractor, the latex unit, the Dissolution Chamber.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.39204F03E7858E49.title": "Tapping trees",
  "quest.39204F03E7858E49.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Aim a \"},{\"text\":\"Fluid Extractor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:fluid_extractor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" at a log and it drips latex: 2 mB per operation from a vanilla log, 1 mB from any other, three times as much with power. Now and then the log gets stripped, and a stripped log ends up gone.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Several extractors can drain the same log at once. A tree ringed with them is a latex farm, and power makes each one faster.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2A513DF079BC7D4D.title": "Latex into rubber",
  "quest.2A513DF079BC7D4D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Latex Processing Unit\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:latex_processing_unit\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" turns 750 mB of latex and 500 mB of water into one \"},{\"text\":\"Dry Rubber\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:dryrubber\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", at 20 FE per tick. Pipe both fluids in and let it run.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.727410A74B375E43.title": "Everything is plastic",
  "quest.727410A74B375E43.quest_subtitle": "The currency of the mod.",
  "quest.727410A74B375E43.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Smelt \"},{\"text\":\"Dry Rubber\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:dryrubber\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" into \"},{\"text\":\"Plastic\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:plastic\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Almost every IF machine asks for some, and belts, the straw and the Mob Imprisonment Tool are made of it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4D1BE172ABD25E27.title": "Dissolve and rebuild",
  "quest.4D1BE172ABD25E27.quest_subtitle": "Eight items, one fluid, no pattern.",
  "quest.4D1BE172ABD25E27.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two plastic, a chest, two buckets, two gold ingots, a \"},{\"text\":\"Diamond Gear\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:diamond_gear\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a pity frame make the \"},{\"text\":\"Dissolution Chamber\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:dissolution_chamber\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": up to eight items and one fluid in, in any order, at 90 FE per tick.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Frames, addons, lenses and the Infinity tools all come out of it. With a recipe inside it locks its slots, so pipes can't jam it with the wrong items."
  ],
  "quest.5D0DB71E2671162C.title": "Simple, not easy",
  "quest.5D0DB71E2671162C.quest_subtitle": "Held together with latex.",
  "quest.5D0DB71E2671162C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"In the chamber, a pity frame, two plastic, two nether bricks, two iron ingots, a gold gear and 250 mB of latex make the \"},{\"text\":\"Simple Machine Frame\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:machine_frame_simple\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It opens the laser drill, the hydroponic bed, the fertilizer and the marine fisher.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.45C461F92D8E0EA0.title": "Advanced, and pink",
  "quest.45C461F92D8E0EA0.quest_subtitle": "Nobody asks what's in the slime.",
  "quest.45C461F92D8E0EA0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A simple frame, two plastic, two netherite scrap, two gold ingots, a diamond gear and 500 mB of pink slime make the \"},{\"text\":\"Advanced Machine Frame\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:machine_frame_advanced\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". The Mob Crusher, the laser bases, the enchanting machines and the StoneWork Factory sit on it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1AA1CF8C56E02537.title": "Top of the ladder",
  "quest.1AA1CF8C56E02537.quest_subtitle": "Sealed with a Wither's breath.",
  "quest.1AA1CF8C56E02537.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An advanced frame, two plastic, two netherite ingots, two diamonds, a diamond gear and 135 mB of \"},{\"text\":\"ether gas\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"0863D9EFF6720E00\"}},{\"text\":\" make the \"},{\"text\":\"Supreme Machine Frame\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:machine_frame_supreme\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Only the Wither Builder and three mycelial generators need it, and the Mycelial Reactor starts from one.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.611CC8944281877D.title": "Mining without a pickaxe",
  "quest.611CC8944281877D.quest_subtitle": "Foregoing the pickaxe, industrially.",
  "quest.611CC8944281877D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two plastic, a diamond pickaxe, two iron ores, two diamond gears, an advanced frame and, here, an \"},{\"text\":\"Ironwood Ingot\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:ironwood_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make the \"},{\"text\":\"Ore Laser Base\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:ore_laser_base\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Laser Drills around it charge it, and each full bar is one ore, picked by biome, depth and \"},{\"text\":\"lenses\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"632876665F709C4E\"}},{\"text\":\".\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "{image:industrialforegoing:textures/block/laser_base_top.png width:48 height:48 align:center}",
    "",
    "Act IV: the ironwood takes the place of the redstone dust. Each drill adds to the bar, so more drills mean more ore."
  ],
  "quest.55438056C6AFB0DB.title": "Three gears",
  "quest.55438056C6AFB0DB.quest_subtitle": "Unified, with a surprise.",
  "quest.55438056C6AFB0DB.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four ingots or diamonds around an empty middle make a gear. Iron ones go into sowers, sewers and collectors, gold ones into most machines, the \"},{\"text\":\"Diamond Gear\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:diamond_gear\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" into the chamber and the lasers.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The pack unifies gears: IF's iron one comes out as Ender IO's \"},{\"text\":\"Infinity Bimetal Gear\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"enderio:iron_gear\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", the gold one as Modern Industrialization's \"},{\"text\":\"Gold Gear\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modern_industrialization:gold_gear\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". IF machines take them all the same.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.31FFECC7D1A49201.title": "Pity power",
  "quest.31FFECC7D1A49201.quest_subtitle": "It burns even when nobody asked.",
  "quest.31FFECC7D1A49201.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Cobblestone, iron bars, a gold ingot, a furnace and a pity frame make the \"},{\"text\":\"Pitiful Generator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:pitiful_generator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": 30 FE per tick from anything a furnace burns. It keeps burning with its 100,000 FE buffer full, so feed it slowly.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6844F2CA96FB85E6.title": "Any plastic will do",
  "quest.6844F2CA96FB85E6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"IF recipes ask for the plastics tag, so Oritech's \"},{\"text\":\"Plastic Sheet\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:plastic_sheet\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" works too. Only the Meat Feeder insists on IF's own \"},{\"text\":\"Plastic\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:plastic\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7121709373E2741C.title": "Plastic by the stack",
  "quest.7121709373E2741C.quest_subtitle": "Recycling can wait.",
  "quest.7121709373E2741C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Sixty-four \"},{\"text\":\"Plastic\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:plastic\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for the common store, once a day. A ring of extractors around a few trees keeps the latex unit busy.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.013D285F0A870979.title": "Industrial Foregoing's Manual",
  "quest.741230D6934E57D0.title": "Read the manual",
  "quest.741230D6934E57D0.quest_subtitle": "Dirt included.",
  "quest.741230D6934E57D0.quest_desc": [
    "A book, a redstone dust and a block of dirt make Industrial Foregoing's manual: every machine with its recipe and what it does. The rates it leaves out are in EMI."
  ],
  "quest.71A29C6CA68EFB8B.title": "What the pack changes",
  "quest.71A29C6CA68EFB8B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Five IF recipes wait for later acts: the Fluid Laser Base and the Infinity Drill take \"},{\"text\":\"Reinforced Alloy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:alloy_reinforced\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (III); the Ore Laser Base and the Infinity Nuke an \"},{\"text\":\"Ironwood Ingot\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:ironwood_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (IV); the Mob Duplicator an \"},{\"text\":\"Ecosystem Capsule\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:ecosystem_capsule\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (IV).\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0605447BDA58AC2E.title": "Pipes without pipes",
  "quest.0605447BDA58AC2E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A pity frame, an ender pearl, four redstone, two gold ingots and a piston make two \"},{\"text\":\"Item Transporters\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:item_transporter_type\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; lapis makes the \"},{\"text\":\"Fluid\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:fluid_transporter_type\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" kind, hoppers and a dropper the \"},{\"text\":\"World\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:world_transporter_type\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" kind. The first two move things between inventories one block apart; the World kind picks items up and drops them.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Several kinds fit in one block. Right-click the middle to switch between extract and insert; Speed and Efficiency addons go on the outer ring.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.281A71D50447ACE1.title": "No black holes here",
  "quest.281A71D50447ACE1.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"This version of IF has no Black Hole Units or Tanks. For a lot of one item, Functional Storage drawers do the job: \"},{\"text\":\"with a Netherite Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"5B2BCD66CABD0839\"}},{\"text\":\" one oak drawer holds 1,024 stacks.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3BE2635A2FFC7363.title": "Copy, paste",
  "quest.3BE2635A2FFC7363.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four paper, three plastic and two redstone make the \"},{\"text\":\"Machine Settings Copier\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:machine_settings_copier\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Sneak-right-click a machine you've set up to store its settings, then right-click another to paste them.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2B9039FB10DBFAD5.title": "Don't drink the lava",
  "quest.2B9039FB10DBFAD5.quest_subtitle": "Obsidian-flavoured.",
  "quest.2B9039FB10DBFAD5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four plastic make a \"},{\"text\":\"Straw\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:straw\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" that drinks a whole bucket from the world or a tank. Lava hurts and sets you on fire; drink water within six seconds and it puts you out, and you burp up obsidian.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.4D0E7491EE1571ED.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.7BCF4869E3A03331.title": "Belts",
  "quest.7BCF4869E3A03331.quest_subtitle": "Items, mobs, and fluids on the flat.",
  "quest.7BCF4869E3A03331.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Six plastic, two iron ingots and a redstone make six \"},{\"text\":\"Conveyor Belts\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:conveyor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". They carry items and mobs up and down slopes, and fluids only on the flat. Right-click one with a dye to recolour it.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Right-click a belt with glowstone dust and it runs fast; with plastic, nobody can pick up what it carries.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.79139B0E82106705.title": "In and out of chests",
  "quest.79139B0E82106705.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A belt, six iron ingots, plastic and a dispenser or a hopper make the \"},{\"text\":\"Extraction\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:conveyor_extraction_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and \"},{\"text\":\"Insertion\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:conveyor_insertion_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" upgrades. One pulls from the inventory it touches, the other fills it, both with a filter.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2FBF2B9A2926D2A6.title": "Belt tricks",
  "quest.2FBF2B9A2926D2A6.quest_subtitle": "A theme park for zombies.",
  "quest.2FBF2B9A2926D2A6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"More upgrades from a belt and iron: \"},{\"text\":\"Bouncing\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:conveyor_bouncing_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" launches, \"},{\"text\":\"Dropping\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:conveyor_dropping_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" drops through, \"},{\"text\":\"Blinking\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:conveyor_blinking_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" teleports, \"},{\"text\":\"Splitting\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:conveyor_splitting_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" divides by ratio and \"},{\"text\":\"Detection\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:conveyor_detection_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" gives a redstone signal.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A Mob Imprisonment Tool with a mob inside works as a mob filter on any of them.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7B14B966A928BC45.title": "Tier 1 addons",
  "quest.7B14B966A928BC45.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"In the chamber, redstone, glass panes, two gold gears and 1,000 mB of latex make the first addons: sugar for \"},{\"text\":\"Speed\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:speed_addon_tier_1\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", blaze rods for \"},{\"text\":\"Efficiency\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:efficiency_addon_tier_1\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a furnace and a crafting table for \"},{\"text\":\"Processing\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:processing_addon_tier_1\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Speed adds 1 to the work bar each tick, Efficiency cuts the ticks per job by 10%, Processing runs one extra job per cycle and pays its power. A machine takes one addon of each kind.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5E1C5DE805D66E3F.title": "Tier 2 addons",
  "quest.5E1C5DE805D66E3F.quest_subtitle": "Swap the gold for diamond.",
  "quest.5E1C5DE805D66E3F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The same recipes with two \"},{\"text\":\"Diamond Gears\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:diamond_gear\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" instead of gold ones: +2 speed, 20% fewer ticks, two extra jobs. Take the tier 1 out first; a machine holds one addon of each kind.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7D6DC05D3B134301.title": "Twelve steps of range",
  "quest.7D6DC05D3B134301.quest_subtitle": "From cobblestone to emeralds.",
  "quest.7D6DC05D3B134301.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Each range addon adds a block of reach and takes four of something: cobblestone, lapis, bone meal, iron nuggets, copper, gold nuggets, iron, gold, quartz, diamonds, popped chorus, emeralds. The \"},{\"text\":\"emerald one\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:range_addon_tier_11\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" goes into every Infinity tool but the backpack.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.77015897792B3AC2.title": "Pink metal",
  "quest.77015897792B3AC2.quest_subtitle": "Two metals and a mystery.",
  "quest.77015897792B3AC2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two iron ingots, two gold ingots and 1,000 mB of pink slime make a \"},{\"text\":\"Pink Slime Ingot\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:pink_slime_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; the \"},{\"text\":\"Washing Factory\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"23F45EA54BF826E0\"}},{\"text\":\" takes two. A glass pane and 300 mB make a \"},{\"text\":\"Pink Slime\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:pink_slime\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" ball, which counts as a slimeball.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3476A97FD3FC45EC.title": "A drill that levels up",
  "quest.3476A97FD3FC45EC.quest_subtitle": "Power is its only upgrade.",
  "quest.3476A97FD3FC45EC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two diamond blocks, a diamond shovel, the emerald range addon, three gold gears, \"},{\"text\":\"Reinforced Alloy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:alloy_reinforced\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (act III, where a third diamond block was) and 2,000 mB of pink slime make the \"},{\"text\":\"Infinity Drill\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:infinity_drill\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in the chamber. The more power it holds, the wider it digs.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Common digs a 3×3 face and each tier after it two blocks more, up to 11×11 at Legendary. Sneak-right-click opens its screen, to pick a smaller area or stop charging."
  ],
  "quest.02C93942F0E8B904.title": "Timber, industrially",
  "quest.02C93942F0E8B904.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A diamond block, a diamond pickaxe, two diamond axes, the emerald range addon, three gold gears and 2,000 mB of pink slime make the \"},{\"text\":\"Infinity Saw\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:infinity_saw\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It fells as many blocks at once as its tier allows; keep hitting the same block on big trees.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7F551C310CD4A8A6.title": "Heads will roll",
  "quest.7F551C310CD4A8A6.quest_subtitle": "Literally. That's the enchantment.",
  "quest.7F551C310CD4A8A6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two diamond blocks, a diamond sword, a diamond axe, the emerald range addon, three gold gears and pink slime make the \"},{\"text\":\"Infinity Hammer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:infinity_hammer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": it hits everything in an area, and higher tiers unlock Beheading for skeleton, wither skeleton, zombie, creeper and dragon heads.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.31B2951BF71E60D8.title": "A crater to go",
  "quest.31B2951BF71E60D8.quest_subtitle": "Please don't.",
  "quest.31B2951BF71E60D8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three TNT, a diamond block, two nether stars, the emerald range addon, 2,000 mB of ether gas and, here, an \"},{\"text\":\"Ironwood Ingot\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:ironwood_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (act IV, in a fourth TNT's place) make the \"},{\"text\":\"Infinity Nuke\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:infinity_nuke\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Place it, right-click to arm it, then light it with flint and steel.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The blast grows with its tier and the biofuel inside.\",\"color\":\"#FF8C7A\"},{\"text\":\" Claimed chunks are left standing.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.235F809DCFFB1CA7.title": "Look at a placed Infinity Nuke",
  "quest.5587DF239F9F01E4.title": "Don't touch the red button",
  "quest.5587DF239F9F01E4.quest_subtitle": "Is it armed? Better not check.",
  "quest.5587DF239F9F01E4.quest_desc": [
    "You spent two seconds staring at a placed Infinity Nuke. It only goes off armed and lit, and it spares claimed chunks, but nobody wants one in the living room."
  ],
  "reward.02F59332A4BC4859.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.4B20D01A143C418B.title": "Filling the bar",
  "quest.4B20D01A143C418B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three plastic, two repeaters, a diamond gear, two blocks of redstone and an advanced frame make the \"},{\"text\":\"Infinity Charger\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:infinity_charger\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": it charges anything that holds power, and Infinity tools very fast.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.43CE3178E86B5162.title": "Seven tiers of power",
  "quest.43CE3178E86B5162.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Infinity tools rank up by stored power: Common at 4 million FE, then 16 M, 80 M, 480 M and Legendary at 3,360 M. With biofuel inside they burn that instead, Unbreaking cuts both costs, and everything they break comes straight to you.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1290C16D3201A7C6.title": "A trident with ambitions",
  "quest.1290C16D3201A7C6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two diamond blocks, a trident, a diamond hoe, the emerald range addon, three gold gears and pink slime make the \"},{\"text\":\"Infinity Trident\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:infinity_trident\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Its tiers unlock Loyalty and Riptide up to VII and Channeling, and its hits and lightning land in an area.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.027716F892ACE71C.title": "Plunger delivery",
  "quest.027716F892ACE71C.quest_subtitle": "Moving mobs, from a distance.",
  "quest.027716F892ACE71C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A bow, a Mob Imprisonment Tool, two diamond blocks, the emerald range addon, three gold gears and pink slime make the \"},{\"text\":\"Infinity Launcher\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:infinity_launcher\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It fires a plunger that catches a mob into a tool in your inventory, or lets one out, from afar.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5F30D31A2B1DF946.title": "A backpack with a magnet",
  "quest.5F30D31A2B1DF946.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two chests, two buckets, an ender pearl, a diamond gear and three gold gears make the \"},{\"text\":\"Infinity Backpack\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:infinity_backpack\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Its magnet pulls nearby items; it holds biofuel, Essence from the experience you pick up and liquid meat that feeds you.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.industrialforegoing.backpack.desc\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" opens it once you give that key a binding; it also fits the Curios back slot.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4478747B4E03DE0C.title": "Biofuel",
  "quest.4478747B4E03DE0C.quest_subtitle": "Variety is the spice of fuel.",
  "quest.4478747B4E03DE0C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Water plus seeds, saplings, crops, dyes, mushrooms, sweet berries or skulls become biofuel in the \"},{\"text\":\"Bioreactor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:bioreactor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It eats one of each kind per round, and nine kinds make far more per item than one.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3F405B0FE49051D6.title": "Nine slots, nine kinds",
  "quest.3F405B0FE49051D6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"One kind alone makes 95 mB of biofuel per round; nine different kinds in the nine slots make 3,719 mB, and drink as much water. Each slot keeps to one kind.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0F1FF4F3DFBC1348.title": "Burning purple",
  "quest.0F1FF4F3DFBC1348.quest_subtitle": "It stops when full. Unlike some.",
  "quest.0F1FF4F3DFBC1348.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two plastic, two pistons, a furnace, two gold gears and a pity frame make the \"},{\"text\":\"Biofuel Generator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:biofuel_generator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": 160 FE per tick, 640 FE per mB, into a 1,000,000 FE buffer. It stops burning when the buffer is full.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.02B9CCE34B2AF277.title": "Mycelial, simple frame",
  "quest.02B9CCE34B2AF277.quest_subtitle": "Sixteen appetites, four to start.",
  "quest.02B9CCE34B2AF277.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Each mycelial generator burns one thing: the \"},{\"text\":\"Furnace\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:mycelial_furnace\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" one anything a furnace takes, at 80 FE per tick, the \"},{\"text\":\"Culinary\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:mycelial_culinary\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" one food, the \"},{\"text\":\"Frosty\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:mycelial_frosty\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" one snow and ice, the \"},{\"text\":\"Pink\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:mycelial_pink\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" one pink dye. These four sit on simple frames.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7EA5838AE36FBEDA.title": "Mycelial, advanced frame",
  "quest.7EA5838AE36FBEDA.quest_subtitle": "Nine more mouths to feed.",
  "quest.7EA5838AE36FBEDA.quest_desc": [
    "Nine more on advanced frames: Nether fungi, bones and rotten flesh, enchanted items, ender pearls, TNT, lava, potions, firework rockets and slime. The reactor needs every kind running."
  ],
  "quest.4B98D05D95DAF7BD.title": "Mycelial, supreme frame",
  "quest.4B98D05D95DAF7BD.quest_subtitle": "One of them eats nether stars.",
  "quest.4B98D05D95DAF7BD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The last three want supreme frames and rare food: the \"},{\"text\":\"Halitosis\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:mycelial_halitosis\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" one dragon's breath, the \"},{\"text\":\"Meatallurgic\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:mycelial_meatallurgic\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" one liquid meat with ingots, the \"},{\"text\":\"Netherstar\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:mycelial_netherstar\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" one nether stars.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5CAD2D20DC616CED.title": "Sixteen at once",
  "quest.5CAD2D20DC616CED.quest_subtitle": "Twenty-five million per tick. Yes, million.",
  "quest.5CAD2D20DC616CED.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"In the chamber, a supreme frame, two plastic, two netherite ingots, two diamond gears, a nether star and 500 mB of ether gas make the \"},{\"text\":\"Mycelial Reactor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:mycelial_reactor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". While one of each of the sixteen mycelial generators you placed runs, it makes 25,000,000 FE per tick.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0C88FF716F10EB13.title": "Harvest and fell",
  "quest.0C88FF716F10EB13.quest_subtitle": "Not even the stump survives.",
  "quest.0C88FF716F10EB13.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two plastic, an iron hoe, two iron axes, two gold gears, redstone and a pity frame make the \"},{\"text\":\"Plant Gatherer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:plant_gatherer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It harvests crops and fells whole trees, logs and leaves, and leaves a little sludge each time.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"It breaks crops it could have right-clicked; a trickle of ether gas makes it replant them.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6CA1AD2BA873C2B0.title": "Nine colours, nine plots",
  "quest.6CA1AD2BA873C2B0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Plant Sower\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:plant_sower\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" plants seeds and saplings above it. Its nine slots are colour-coded like the marks on its top, and each slot only sows its own ninth of the area.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.44BBC0478DB10FAE.title": "Bone meal on a schedule",
  "quest.44BBC0478DB10FAE.quest_subtitle": "Allergic to sunflowers.",
  "quest.44BBC0478DB10FAE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"On a simple frame, the \"},{\"text\":\"Plant Fertilizer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:plant_fertilizer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" feeds bone meal or \"},{\"text\":\"Fertilizer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:fertilizer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" to each plant until it can't grow any more. A plant that always takes bone meal, like a sunflower, jams it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.067CDFCE48864834.title": "Soil in a box",
  "quest.067CDFCE48864834.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two plastic, dirt, two iron hoes, \"},{\"text\":\"Fertilizer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:fertilizer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", two gold gears and a simple frame make the \"},{\"text\":\"Hydroponic Bed\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:hydroponic_bed\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". With power and water, or lava for Nether crops, the crop on it grows faster; a little ether also replants it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.19565FB4AAB180DF.title": "A farm on a chip",
  "quest.19565FB4AAB180DF.quest_subtitle": "It learned from the real one.",
  "quest.19565FB4AAB180DF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Put a \"},{\"text\":\"Hydroponic Simulation Processor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:hydroponic_simulation_processor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in a working Hydroponic Bed and it records every harvest. Moved to a \"},{\"text\":\"Simulated Hydroponic Bed\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:simulated_hydroponic_bed\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", it grows that crop's drops with no plant at all.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "The more harvests it has recorded, the better it simulates, and the simulated bed keeps adding to them now and then."
  ],
  "quest.6F4237A8DB791E0C.title": "Mud, refined",
  "quest.6F4237A8DB791E0C.quest_subtitle": "What the gatherer leaves behind.",
  "quest.6F4237A8DB791E0C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Sludge Refiner\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:sludge_refiner\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" turns the gatherer's sludge into dirt, clay, gravel, sand, red sand or soul sand, at 40 FE per tick.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2D3F4D934B3ACB03.title": "Mushroom copier",
  "quest.2D3F4D934B3ACB03.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Spores Recreator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:spores_recreator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" duplicates mushrooms with 100 mB of water per round, and crimson or warped fungi with lava instead, at 40 FE per tick.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.00B938A21172F035.title": "See the area",
  "quest.00B938A21172F035.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Machines that work an area have a button in their screen that draws it in the world. Range addons grow it a block per step; the tooltip says which machines take them.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5589CAA70DF2FAA4.title": "Water from water",
  "quest.5589CAA70DF2FAA4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Touching two or more water sources, the \"},{\"text\":\"Water Condensator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:water_condensator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" fills its tank; more sources and power make it faster. Latex units and hydroponic beds drink a lot.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5265C284C3646F9D.title": "Gone fishing",
  "quest.5265C284C3646F9D.quest_subtitle": "A cat's best friend.",
  "quest.5265C284C3646F9D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Over a pool at least 3×3 and one block deep, the \"},{\"text\":\"Marine Fisher\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:marine_fisher\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" fishes with the vanilla fishing loot, treasure included, at 5,000 FE per catch.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.29AFDBA1ED9999CA.title": "A ranch with no rancher",
  "quest.29AFDBA1ED9999CA.quest_subtitle": "The cows don't miss you.",
  "quest.29AFDBA1ED9999CA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Animal Feeder\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:animal_feeder\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" breeds animals with their food, the \"},{\"text\":\"Animal Rancher\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:animal_rancher\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" shears and milks, and the \"},{\"text\":\"Baby Separator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:animal_baby_separator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" moves the young behind it. The Feeder stops at 35 animals in its area.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3AAA7344BD88DDC6.title": "What animals leave behind",
  "quest.3AAA7344BD88DDC6.quest_subtitle": "You don't want to know.",
  "quest.3AAA7344BD88DDC6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Sewer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:sewer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" collects 50 mB of sewage per animal each round and turns loose experience orbs into Essence. The \"},{\"text\":\"Sewage Composter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:sewage_composter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" makes one \"},{\"text\":\"Fertilizer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:fertilizer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" from 1,000 mB of sewage.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Fertilizer works like bone meal, and the \"},{\"text\":\"Hydroponic Bed\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"067CDFCE48864834\"}},{\"text\":\" is made with it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5C7DAD790FAABD23.title": "A drill that never touches stone",
  "quest.5C7DAD790FAABD23.quest_subtitle": "Mining by proxy.",
  "quest.5C7DAD790FAABD23.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two plastic, two pistons, a diamond gear, two gold gears, redstone and a simple frame make a \"},{\"text\":\"Laser Drill\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:laser_drill\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Set one block away from a laser base, it charges the base with power; a misplaced drill shows a tag above it saying so.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.632876665F709C4E.title": "Tinted odds",
  "quest.632876665F709C4E.quest_subtitle": "Sixteen colours, one lens each.",
  "quest.632876665F709C4E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four glass panes, a dye and 250 mB of latex make a laser lens in the chamber. Each colour favours its ores: \"},{\"text\":\"brown\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:brown_laser_lens\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" iron, \"},{\"text\":\"yellow\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:yellow_laser_lens\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" gold, \"},{\"text\":\"light blue\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:light_blue_laser_lens\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" diamonds, \"},{\"text\":\"red\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:red_laser_lens\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" redstone. EMI lists them all.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5ACB71930E5D3EBB.title": "Six lenses, one depth",
  "quest.5ACB71930E5D3EBB.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The ore base holds six lenses, and each one matching an ore adds 8 to its weight. Mining depth starts at the base's own height and changes in its screen: diamonds and redstone peak between 5 and 16.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3DE6BB618580D394.title": "Fluids from the deep",
  "quest.3DE6BB618580D394.quest_subtitle": "Alloy in, redstone out.",
  "quest.3DE6BB618580D394.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Here the \"},{\"text\":\"Fluid Laser Base\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:fluid_laser_base\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" takes \"},{\"text\":\"Reinforced Alloy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:alloy_reinforced\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (act III) where its redstone was. With a lens it pumps lava in the Nether, oil under oceans and deserts, or ether gas from a Wither right below it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6576F9CFC91A67CC.title": "Hold still",
  "quest.6576F9CFC91A67CC.quest_subtitle": "Even the Wither.",
  "quest.6576F9CFC91A67CC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three soul sand, two ghast tears, a piston, two gold gears and an advanced frame make the \"},{\"text\":\"Stasis Chamber\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:stasis_chamber\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": mobs in its area freeze in place and heal a little every round, and their boss bars stay hidden.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The fluid laser only hurts a Wither above 5 health, so it never kills it. Frozen by the chamber, the Wither stays put under the base and heals back: an ether farm that can't escape.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0863D9EFF6720E00.title": "A Wither's breath",
  "quest.0863D9EFF6720E00.quest_subtitle": "The Wither doesn't enjoy it either.",
  "quest.0863D9EFF6720E00.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"purple lens\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:purple_laser_lens\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in the fluid base and a Wither under it give 10 mB of ether gas per round; each round costs the Wither 5 health. Supreme frames, replanting farms and the Mycelial Reactor run on it.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.6DC0E02DA8906619.title": "Look at a Wither for five seconds",
  "quest.7D0C6612EF943596.title": "Staring contest",
  "quest.7D0C6612EF943596.quest_subtitle": "You blinked first. It can't.",
  "quest.7D0C6612EF943596.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"You held a Wither's gaze for five seconds. With a \"},{\"text\":\"Stasis Chamber\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:stasis_chamber\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" under it, it can't even turn its heads, and a fluid laser base above keeps the ether coming.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.24432EE7BB1095E2.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.57E19EBEDE586B06.title": "Meat and pink slime",
  "quest.57E19EBEDE586B06.quest_subtitle": "No drops, no questions.",
  "quest.57E19EBEDE586B06.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Mob Slaughter Factory\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:mob_slaughter_factory\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" grinds mobs into liquid meat and pink slime, with no drops or experience. Animals give 20 mB of pink slime per point of health; monsters give that much meat instead.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Pink slime goes into the \"},{\"text\":\"Advanced Machine Frame\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"45C461F92D8E0EA0\"}},{\"text\":\"; liquid meat feeds Mechanical Dirt and the Meat Feeder.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7A8D2E737EEFDBF0.title": "Dirt that spawns",
  "quest.7A8D2E737EEFDBF0.quest_subtitle": "Fertilized with meat.",
  "quest.7A8D2E737EEFDBF0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"In the chamber, two dirt, two rotten flesh, a pity frame and 1,000 mB of liquid meat make \"},{\"text\":\"Mechanical Dirt\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:mechanical_dirt\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". In the dark, at light 7 or less, it spawns mobs for 1,000 FE and 20 mB of meat each, and shares both with the blocks it touches.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.72C5245C8ADF8D10.title": "It fights like you do",
  "quest.72C5245C8ADF8D10.quest_subtitle": "Looting sold separately.",
  "quest.72C5245C8ADF8D10.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two plastic, an iron sword, two books, two gold gears, redstone and an advanced frame make the \"},{\"text\":\"Mob Crusher\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:mob_crusher\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": it kills like a player, so mobs drop their loot, and it turns their experience into Essence, 20 mB per point.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"In Looting mode it trades the Essence for a random Looting level, up to III, on every kill. Babies and bosses still invulnerable are left alone.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3C76D7BD925363A6.title": "A mob in your pocket",
  "quest.3C76D7BD925363A6.quest_subtitle": "It's roomy in there. Probably.",
  "quest.3C76D7BD925363A6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four plastic around a ghast tear make the \"},{\"text\":\"Mob Imprisonment Tool\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:mob_imprisonment_tool\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Right-click a mob to store it inside; right-click the ground to let it out.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5E5E2E7977702FF5.title": "Copy, paste, mob",
  "quest.5E5E2E7977702FF5.quest_subtitle": "Nether wart out, ecosystem in.",
  "quest.5E5E2E7977702FF5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Here the \"},{\"text\":\"Mob Duplicator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:mob_duplicator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" takes an \"},{\"text\":\"Ecosystem Capsule\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:ecosystem_capsule\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (act IV) where its nether wart was. Give it a tool with a mob, Essence and 5,000 FE a round: it spawns one to four copies, at 12 mB of Essence per point of health.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"It pauses when more than 32 of that mob stand in its area, and it copies the kind, not the individual. The Atlas also asks for a capsule in \"},{\"text\":\"A small agreement\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"780224C0B0190A32\"}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.54F34F4D22EB3F58.title": "Unenchanting",
  "quest.54F34F4D22EB3F58.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two plastic, nether bricks, two books, two diamonds, a gold gear and an advanced frame make the \"},{\"text\":\"Enchantment Extractor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:enchantment_extractor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". With a book it moves an item's enchantments onto the book; in its other mode it turns them into Essence, no book needed.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.486A9D7E79A68ED7.title": "An anvil that takes Essence",
  "quest.486A9D7E79A68ED7.quest_subtitle": "Sharpness VI? Why not.",
  "quest.486A9D7E79A68ED7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three plastic, three anvils, two gold gears and an advanced frame make the \"},{\"text\":\"Enchantment Applicator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:enchantment_applicator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": an anvil paid in Essence. It ignores maximum levels, so two Sharpness V books make Sharpness VI.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5119EF173B540A28.title": "An enchanting line",
  "quest.5119EF173B540A28.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Enchantment Factory\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:enchantment_factory\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" enchants items like a table at the level you set, 30 unless you change it, paid in Essence, and the \"},{\"text\":\"Enchantment Sorter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:enchantment_sorter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" splits enchanted items from plain ones.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Enchantment Industry drinks IF Essence too: \"},{\"text\":\"Every experience counts\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"0E1E17A383C2E5C1\"}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3EFB9EEFA889AE37.title": "Essence to go",
  "quest.3EFB9EEFA889AE37.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"With no items inside, the Dissolution Chamber turns 250 mB of Essence, or any other experience fluid, into a \"},{\"text\":\"Bottle o' Enchanting\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:experience_bottle\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" every 5 ticks.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.647E43894EA48211.title": "Cobblestone, next generation",
  "quest.647E43894EA48211.quest_subtitle": "Sand in, silicon out.",
  "quest.647E43894EA48211.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"With water and lava in its tanks, the \"},{\"text\":\"Material StoneWork Factory\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:material_stonework_factory\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" makes cobblestone, andesite, diorite, granite, netherrack or obsidian, then smelts, crushes or crafts it. Crushing goes cobblestone, gravel, sand, silicon.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.38ACD536AE50E0E8.title": "Hands on the world",
  "quest.38ACD536AE50E0E8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Block Breaker\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:block_breaker\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and \"},{\"text\":\"Block Placer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:block_placer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" mine blocks and place them from their inventory; the \"},{\"text\":\"Fluid Collector\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:fluid_collector\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and \"},{\"text\":\"Fluid Placer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:fluid_placer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" take and pour source blocks. 1,000 FE per operation each.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.25B824475C529D64.title": "Three furnaces in one",
  "quest.25B824475C529D64.quest_subtitle": "Smelting, with a side of Essence.",
  "quest.25B824475C529D64.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Resourceful Furnace\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:resourceful_furnace\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" smelts three items at once for 40 FE per tick, and keeps the smelting experience as Essence: 20 mB per point.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.71653FA4168970C6.title": "An alchemist on a frame",
  "quest.71653FA4168970C6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Potion Brewer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:potion_brewer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" brews vanilla potions from the ingredients you give it and fills bottles from its water tank. Set the potion you want in its green filter, or nothing comes out.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.23F45EA54BF826E0.title": "Meat that remembers ore",
  "quest.23F45EA54BF826E0.quest_subtitle": "Metallurgy, but make it gross.",
  "quest.23F45EA54BF826E0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two Pink Slime Ingots, a Meat Feeder, two plastic, two diamond gears, a furnace and an advanced frame make the \"},{\"text\":\"Washing Factory\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:washing_factory\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It washes a raw ore in 100 mB of liquid meat into 100 mB of raw ore meat of that metal.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3740F1DE055A4866.title": "Let it ferment",
  "quest.3740F1DE055A4866.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Fermentation Station\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:fermentation_station\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" seals raw ore meat and ferments it: twice the amount after 100 ticks, three times after 900, four times with pink slime after 2,400, five times with ether gas after 6,000.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.17CEF172D96A89CF.title": "Back from meat to metal",
  "quest.17CEF172D96A89CF.quest_subtitle": "Five dusts from one raw ore.",
  "quest.17CEF172D96A89CF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Fluid Sieving Machine\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:fluid_sieving_machine\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" runs 100 mB of fermented ore meat through sand and leaves one dust of that metal. Washed, fermented to five times and sieved, one raw ore ends up as five dusts.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.38C99897062F30FE.title": "Withers to order",
  "quest.38C99897062F30FE.quest_subtitle": "What could possibly go wrong?",
  "quest.38C99897062F30FE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three soul sand, two wither skeleton skulls, a nether star, two plastic and a supreme frame make the \"},{\"text\":\"Wither Builder\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:wither_builder\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". With 3 skulls, 4 soul sand and 20,000 FE it builds a whole Wither in its area.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.500C1D45CD955623.title": "Tag on a sower",
  "quest.500C1D45CD955623.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The farms kept going for a year after the city emptied: sowing, harvesting, bottling what nobody would drink. We automated the chores so well that we forgot who they were for. —J.\",\"italic\":true}]"
  ],
  "image.76C556BEC01A9FB9.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Latex and plastic\",\"color\":\"#93D9F3\"}]",
  "image.73B413DBEA4517C5.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Belts and transporters\",\"color\":\"#93D9F3\"}]",
  "image.2BC7EB34DAA42CD2.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"In the chamber\",\"color\":\"#93D9F3\"}]",
  "image.68D4D34E6F0C3E15.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Infinity tools\",\"color\":\"#93D9F3\"}]",
  "image.52D03AB392226568.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Power\",\"color\":\"#93D9F3\"}]",
  "image.5E6D98F462341FD5.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Fields and pens\",\"color\":\"#93D9F3\"}]",
  "image.25C562DC92DD395C.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Lasers and lenses\",\"color\":\"#93D9F3\"}]",
  "image.0B726B6719CBFF0A.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Mobs and Essence\",\"color\":\"#93D9F3\"}]",
  "image.2B87C0EB323FB97A.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Resources\",\"color\":\"#93D9F3\"}]",
  "image.25F9819D76620FCC.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Industrial Foregoing\",\"color\":\"#F4F9FF\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.128D3E45400B46FC.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"tap · melt · dissolve · drill\",\"color\":\"#93D9F3\",\"font\":\"minecraft:uniform\"}]",
  "image.0772FC6DF28E3436.title": "Back to the Sun of Heliodor",
  "chapter.57D95FCA49DD6FFA.title": "Logistics Networks",
  "chapter.57D95FCA49DD6FFA.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Pipes, lasers and wireless power: everything moves on its own."
  ],
  "quest.05CCF43C232C2870.title": "Item Pipes",
  "quest.05CCF43C232C2870.quest_subtitle": "Plumbing for things that don't get wet.",
  "quest.05CCF43C232C2870.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Six iron ingots, two \"},{\"text\":\"Droppers\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:dropper\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a redstone make sixteen \"},{\"text\":\"Item Pipes\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pipez:item_pipe\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". They hook onto every inventory they touch, but move nothing until an end is set to extract; bare, that end sends 4 items a second.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4D5DE8F1242EB133.title": "Pipe Wrench",
  "quest.4D5DE8F1242EB133.quest_subtitle": "The only tool a plumber needs.",
  "quest.4D5DE8F1242EB133.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two flint and two sticks make the \"},{\"text\":\"Pipe Wrench\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pipez:wrench\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". With \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.sneak\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" held, use it on a pipe's arm at a chest and that end starts extracting; do it again and the arm comes off. Use it on the bare pipe to hook it back.\"}]",
    "",
    "Right-click an extracting end to open its menu: the upgrade slot and how much it moves."
  ],
  "quest.45164382B7C13FAD.title": "Fluid Pipes",
  "quest.45164382B7C13FAD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Swap the droppers for two \"},{\"text\":\"Buckets\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and you get sixteen \"},{\"text\":\"Fluid Pipes\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pipez:fluid_pipe\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". They drain tanks and machines, never lakes, and a bare extracting end moves 50 mB a tick.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"To empty a lake, the \"},{\"text\":\"Pump\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"264F40F4997AB53E\"}},{\"text\":\" feeds straight into them.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6FBC8B5A92839CF1.title": "Energy Pipes",
  "quest.6FBC8B5A92839CF1.quest_subtitle": "Watts in a tube. Well, FE.",
  "quest.6FBC8B5A92839CF1.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two \"},{\"text\":\"Blocks of Redstone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:redstone_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in place of the droppers make sixteen \"},{\"text\":\"Energy Pipes\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pipez:energy_pipe\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Set the generator's end to extract: bare, it pushes 256 FE a tick. Energy takes no filters.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3E142C40C47A6741.title": "Gas Pipes",
  "quest.3E142C40C47A6741.quest_subtitle": "Mekanism's chemicals, by pipe.",
  "quest.3E142C40C47A6741.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two \"},{\"text\":\"Infused Alloys\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:alloy_infused\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in the middle row make sixteen \"},{\"text\":\"Gas Pipes\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pipez:gas_pipe\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a recipe that exists only because Mekanism is here. They carry its chemicals, hydrogen, oxygen and the rest: 200 mB a tick bare.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0B4639123B636864.title": "Universal Pipes",
  "quest.0B4639123B636864.quest_subtitle": "One pipe to carry them all.",
  "quest.0B4639123B636864.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two each of item, energy and fluid pipes, two iron and a \"},{\"text\":\"Block of Redstone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:redstone_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make six \"},{\"text\":\"Universal Pipes\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pipez:universal_pipe\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". One line carries items, fluids, energy and Mekanism's chemicals at once, each at its own rate.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"One upgrade in a universal pipe keeps separate settings per kind: the menu has a tab for items, fluids, energy and gas, and the upgrade's tooltip lists the kinds it's set up for.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2B72673A26EA44B0.title": "Basic Pipe Upgrade",
  "quest.2B72673A26EA44B0.quest_subtitle": "Speed, and a say in the matter.",
  "quest.2B72673A26EA44B0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four iron ingots, four iron nuggets and a redstone make the \"},{\"text\":\"Basic Pipe Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pipez:basic_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". In an extracting end's menu it moves 8 items every 15 ticks and unlocks the redstone mode: ignored, off when powered, on when powered or always off.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"An upgrade serves one extracting end, not the whole line: upgrade only where things go in.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3172DB3AF7591A90.title": "Improved Pipe Upgrade",
  "quest.3172DB3AF7591A90.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The basic one in gold and redstone: 16 items every 10 ticks, 500 mB or 8,192 FE a tick. The \"},{\"text\":\"Improved Pipe Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pipez:improved_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" also picks where things go: nearest first, furthest first, round robin or random.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Item pipes start on nearest first; fluid, energy and gas pipes on round robin.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7875A03ECFC8A19D.title": "Advanced Pipe Upgrade",
  "quest.7875A03ECFC8A19D.quest_subtitle": "Now it gets picky.",
  "quest.7875A03ECFC8A19D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Diamonds and redstone blocks around the improved one: 32 items every 5 ticks, 2,000 mB, 32,768 FE or 8,000 mB of gas a tick. The \"},{\"text\":\"Advanced Pipe Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pipez:advanced_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" unlocks filters: an item ID or a #tag, exact data or not, as allow or deny list.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.34212E794968133A.title": "Ultimate Pipe Upgrade",
  "quest.34212E794968133A.quest_subtitle": "Netherite plumbing. As one does.",
  "quest.34212E794968133A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four \"},{\"text\":\"Netherite Ingots\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:netherite_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and four redstone blocks around the advanced one: a stack of 64 every tick, 10,000 mB, 131,072 FE or 40,000 mB of gas. The \"},{\"text\":\"Infinity Pipe Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pipez:infinity_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" above it has no recipe.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.145C4C8C661D8832.title": "Filter Destination Tool",
  "quest.145C4C8C661D8832.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Five iron, two redstone, a glass pane and a button make the \"},{\"text\":\"Filter Destination Tool\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pipez:filter_destination_tool\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Click a block with it, then add it to a filter: matching items go to that block only. Ore to the crusher and the rest to the chest, on one line.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.017A24D7E626BCAE.title": "One kind per line",
  "quest.017A24D7E626BCAE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A pipe only joins pipes of its own kind. An item line and a fluid line can run side by side, touching, and never mix; a universal pipe only joins other universal ones.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.021B5B090C544FE2.title": "Slot it in",
  "quest.021B5B090C544FE2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Hold an upgrade, keep \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.sneak\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" down and use it on an extracting end: the upgrade goes straight in, no menu needed. The one that was there comes back to you.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2C9BE8AC9F32F520.title": "Copy the settings",
  "quest.2C9BE8AC9F32F520.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A configured upgrade next to an empty one in the crafting grid: the new one copies its filters and modes, and the original stays in the grid. An upgrade alone in the grid comes out wiped.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.748A35F0C0CFD79B.title": "Logic Chips",
  "quest.748A35F0C0CFD79B.quest_subtitle": "Baked, not fried.",
  "quest.748A35F0C0CFD79B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four redstone, two gold nuggets, two \"},{\"text\":\"Clay Balls\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:clay_ball\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a \"},{\"text\":\"Block of Quartz\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:quartz_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make four \"},{\"text\":\"Raw Logic Chips\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"laserio:logic_chip_raw\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; the furnace finishes them. Every LaserIO part starts from a \"},{\"text\":\"Logic Chip\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"laserio:logic_chip\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"In this pack, two of them also go into each \"},{\"text\":\"Inventory Sensor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:inventory_sensor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "task.09B9595F1F9E8370.title": "The LaserIO guide",
  "quest.7C0D33EF6E50BCD7.title": "The LaserIO guide",
  "quest.7C0D33EF6E50BCD7.quest_subtitle": "Reading is a mechanic too.",
  "quest.7C0D33EF6E50BCD7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Logic Chip\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"laserio:logic_chip\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a \"},{\"text\":\"Book\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:book\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", shapeless, make LaserIO's guide: every card, filter and setting, with a picture of each menu.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.002FECF554B908EC.title": "Laser Connector",
  "quest.002FECF554B908EC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Glass, two redstone, a \"},{\"text\":\"Logic Chip\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"laserio:logic_chip\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and three iron make a \"},{\"text\":\"Laser Connector\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"laserio:laser_connector\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": a cheap relay that bridges the gap between nodes, 8 blocks per jump. It is also the heart of every node.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.193756AA70D33B62.title": "Laser Node",
  "quest.193756AA70D33B62.quest_subtitle": "Beams, not pipes.",
  "quest.193756AA70D33B62.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Iron, glass panes and a connector make a \"},{\"text\":\"Laser Node\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"laserio:laser_node\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Put it beside your machines: each of its six sides holds a 3×3 grid of cards for the neighbour it faces. Right-click a side to open it; the buttons on top reach the sides you can't see.\"}]",
    "",
    "One node serves up to six neighbours at once."
  ],
  "quest.51B53009F045057E.title": "Laser Wrench",
  "quest.51B53009F045057E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three iron and a chip make the \"},{\"text\":\"Laser Wrench\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"laserio:laser_wrench\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". With \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.sneak\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" held, right-click one node or connector, then right-click another: a beam joins them, up to 8 blocks apart. Everything hanging from the beams is one network.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.65059B594388E787.title": "Advanced Laser Connector",
  "quest.65059B594388E787.quest_subtitle": "Long distance, no roaming charges.",
  "quest.65059B594388E787.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two ender pearls, a diamond, three gold and a connector make an \"},{\"text\":\"Advanced Laser Connector\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"laserio:laser_connector_advanced\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Two of them pair up at any distance, even across dimensions; the wrench shows the partner's coordinates.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Neither end loads its chunk:\",\"color\":\"#FF8C7A\"},{\"text\":\" keep both loaded yourself, or the nodes on the far side stop.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2B8419E5F3058AE3.title": "Item Cards",
  "quest.2B8419E5F3058AE3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Redstone, lapis, quartz, a chip and gold nuggets make an \"},{\"text\":\"Item Card\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"laserio:card_item\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Right-click it in hand to pick its mode: Insert, the default, receives; Extract pulls from its neighbour; Stock keeps an amount topped up; Sensor only watches.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.6EB1996533456031.title": "An Item Card set to Extract",
  "quest.48CABBDBCA26A940.title": "The first route",
  "quest.48CABBDBCA26A940.quest_subtitle": "From A to B, no pipes attached.",
  "quest.48CABBDBCA26A940.quest_desc": [
    "Set an Item Card to Extract and slot it into the node side facing a chest, and an Insert card into the side facing where things should go. Same channel on both, and items flow: 1 every 20 ticks at first, up to 8 per trip by raising the Extract Amount."
  ],
  "quest.3BECEEB8A907FED2.title": "Fluid Cards",
  "quest.3BECEEB8A907FED2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A bucket in place of the lapis makes a \"},{\"text\":\"Fluid Card\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"laserio:card_fluid\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Tanks and machines trade fluids over the beams: 5,000 mB every 20 ticks bare, and up to 40,000 mB every tick with four Card Overclockers.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.42F00C80E7A39912.title": "Energy Cards",
  "quest.42F00C80E7A39912.quest_subtitle": "A million per tick. Per card.",
  "quest.42F00C80E7A39912.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Block of Redstone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:redstone_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in place of the lapis makes an \"},{\"text\":\"Energy Card\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"laserio:card_energy\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It works every tick with no overclockers, up to 1,000,000 FE a tick.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Its Limit % sets how full to fill a target on Insert or Stock, or how much to leave behind on Extract: keep a battery half full for emergencies.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4E2331417D3C4BEF.title": "Chemical Cards",
  "quest.4E2331417D3C4BEF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Basic Control Circuit\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:basic_control_circuit\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in place of the lapis makes a \"},{\"text\":\"Chemical Card\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"laserio:card_chemical\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", because Mekanism is here. Its chemicals ride the same beams: 15,000 mB every 20 ticks, up to 240,000 mB a tick with overclockers.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4BC75B98C5222905.title": "Redstone over lasers",
  "quest.4BC75B98C5222905.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three redstone on top make a \"},{\"text\":\"Redstone Card\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"laserio:card_redstone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Input reads a lever or dust beside its node; Output emits there, weak or strong. Signals travel on their own redstone channels, and any card can obey one: run only while it's low, or only while it's high.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.6FFA385F77788489.title": "An Item Card set to Sensor",
  "quest.67ED8C68842E47D9.title": "A chest that talks",
  "quest.67ED8C68842E47D9.quest_subtitle": "It says 15. It always says 15.",
  "quest.67ED8C68842E47D9.quest_desc": [
    "An Item Card in Sensor mode moves nothing. Give it a filter and it watches its neighbour, lighting a redstone channel at strength 15 while the filter matches; with several entries, And needs all of them and Or any one.",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A Counting Filter turns it into «at least N», and Exact into «exactly N».\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6AD65369CE259224.title": "Card Overclockers",
  "quest.6AD65369CE259224.quest_subtitle": "Four is the magic number.",
  "quest.6AD65369CE259224.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four gold, two redstone and a chip make a \"},{\"text\":\"Card Overclocker\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"laserio:overclocker_card\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Each one in a card raises its limits: 16 items every 15 ticks, then 32 every 10, 48 every 5 and, with four, 64 every tick. Set the Extract Amount and Tick Speed to match.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.38B28FAD603C8E3A.title": "Node Overclocker",
  "quest.38B28FAD603C8E3A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A node side runs one card per tick: if the first does nothing, the next one tries. Diamonds in place of gold make a \"},{\"text\":\"Node Overclocker\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"laserio:overclocker_node\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; each one lets a side run one more card per tick, up to eight for all nine.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Only Extract and Stock cards need them: Insert cards never wait.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7388BA469C7D8C8C.title": "Basic Filter",
  "quest.7388BA469C7D8C8C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Iron bars, glass panes and a chip make four \"},{\"text\":\"Basic Filters\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"laserio:filter_basic\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Put one in a card and fill its ghost slots: Allow passes only those items, Deny everything but them. Compare NBT tells a worn sword from a new one.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0A991223C6FB52A7.title": "Counting Filter",
  "quest.0A991223C6FB52A7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Basic Filter and an \"},{\"text\":\"Observer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:observer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make a \"},{\"text\":\"Counting Filter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"laserio:filter_count\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", with counts from 1 to 4096. On an Extract card it leaves that many behind; on Insert, it caps what the target receives; on Stock, it is the amount to keep.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.44730D60B861E2EE.title": "An Item Card set to Stock",
  "quest.1A22FC3CCB620016.title": "The quiet factory",
  "quest.1A22FC3CCB620016.quest_subtitle": "Every furnace fed, nobody hauling coal.",
  "quest.1A22FC3CCB620016.quest_desc": [
    "Set an Item Card to Stock, give it a Counting Filter of 16 coal and slot one on every furnace's side: each pulls what it's missing from the network's Insert cards. With Regulate on, extras go back out too.",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Stock cards need a filter set to Allow; without one they do nothing.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6B640C2594311E78.title": "Tag Filter",
  "quest.6B640C2594311E78.quest_subtitle": "All ingots, one entry.",
  "quest.6B640C2594311E78.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Basic Filter and \"},{\"text\":\"Paper\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:paper\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make a \"},{\"text\":\"Tag Filter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"laserio:filter_tag\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Put an item in its top slot, pick one of its tags and press +: everything carrying that tag matches. The list means «any of these».\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.79D777F5BE49833B.title": "Mod Filter",
  "quest.79D777F5BE49833B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Basic Filter and a \"},{\"text\":\"Book\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:book\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make a \"},{\"text\":\"Mod Filter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"laserio:filter_mod\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": an item inside it matches everything from the same mod. Drop the Laser Wrench in and all of LaserIO matches.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1BB1B1C6263B45A8.title": "Data Filter",
  "quest.1BB1B1C6263B45A8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Basic Filter and \"},{\"text\":\"White Wool\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:white_wool\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make a \"},{\"text\":\"Data Filter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"laserio:filter_nbt\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It lists the data labels an item carries, like its enchantments, and matches anything that has them, whatever the values: enchanted gear one way, plain gear the other.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3F94E29FF26E96C2.title": "Card Holder",
  "quest.3F94E29FF26E96C2.quest_subtitle": "A deck for your cards.",
  "quest.3F94E29FF26E96C2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Iron, two chests and a chip make a \"},{\"text\":\"Card Holder\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"laserio:card_holder\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": cards with the same settings stack to 64 inside, filters and overclockers too. Sneak and use it to toggle auto-pickup: it glows, pulls cards from your inventory and shows them whenever you open a node.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A card crafted on its own comes out reset, ready to stack.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7795C8EF5A6B8D63.title": "Card Cloner",
  "quest.7795C8EF5A6B8D63.quest_subtitle": "Copy, paste, repeat.",
  "quest.7795C8EF5A6B8D63.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Paper around a chip, iron in the corners: the \"},{\"text\":\"Card Cloner\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"laserio:card_cloner\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". In a node's screen, pick it up on the cursor, left-click a card to copy it and right-click others to paste. Filters and overclockers come from your Card Holder; if one is missing, nothing is pasted.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.022660B580FAC0BE.title": "Channels by colour",
  "quest.022660B580FAC0BE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Cards only talk to cards on the same channel colour. Extract cobblestone on orange and coal on black from one chest's node; an orange Insert card above a furnace and a black one below it split them up. One network, many routes.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.310F29B32CC27EAD.title": "Sneaky sides",
  "quest.310F29B32CC27EAD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A card's Sneaky setting picks which face of the neighbour it works on. One node beside a furnace can feed ore into its top and fuel into its bottom: two cards, Sneaky Up and Sneaky Down.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6BD1123215004209.title": "Fair shares",
  "quest.6BD1123215004209.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Inserters fill by Priority, highest first, then nearest. An Extract card with Round Robin deals items out in turns instead; Enforced waits while one target is full, so a row of furnaces stays even. Exact only moves full batches.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4424B98D90ACB643.title": "Now you see them",
  "quest.4424B98D90ACB643.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The settings button in any node changes the whole network's beam colour and opacity. Set Alpha to 0 and Wrench Alpha to 80, and the lasers only show while you hold the Laser Wrench.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7681C3B3F5C1B7D3.title": "Flux Dust",
  "quest.7681C3B3F5C1B7D3.quest_subtitle": "Redstone, under pressure.",
  "quest.7681C3B3F5C1B7D3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Put obsidian two blocks above bedrock with an air gap between, drop redstone into the gap and left-click the obsidian: each redstone turns into one \"},{\"text\":\"Flux Dust\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"fluxnetworks:flux_dust\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", up to 512 at a time.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The obsidian drops into the gap\",\"color\":\"#FF8C7A\"},{\"text\":\", and in big batches it may turn to cobblestone instead: with a stack of 64 it does more often than not.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.44CCDE8B259FA12F.title": "Flux Cores",
  "quest.44CCDE8B259FA12F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four Flux Dust, four obsidian and an \"},{\"text\":\"Eye of Ender\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:ender_eye\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make four \"},{\"text\":\"Flux Cores\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"fluxnetworks:flux_core\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Every Flux device is built around them.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4A00514510C87A7B.title": "Flux Block",
  "quest.4A00514510C87A7B.quest_subtitle": "Bedrock, to go.",
  "quest.4A00514510C87A7B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Five Flux Dust and four cores make a \"},{\"text\":\"Flux Block\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"fluxnetworks:flux_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", the base of storage and plugs. It also stands in for bedrock under the obsidian, so the next batch of dust can be made anywhere.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5F37A164B3A0D59F.title": "Flux Plug",
  "quest.5F37A164B3A0D59F.quest_subtitle": "It takes. The network gives.",
  "quest.5F37A164B3A0D59F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"In this pack the \"},{\"text\":\"Flux Plug\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"fluxnetworks:flux_plug\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" trades one of its four cores for a \"},{\"text\":\"Reinforced Alloy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:alloy_reinforced\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": act III. It pulls energy from the blocks it touches into a network. Right-click it to create a network or join one.\"}]",
    "",
    "No plug, no energy in the network: that is the whole gate. Points, storage and the controller keep their own recipes."
  ],
  "quest.27801123FEE6C86A.title": "Flux Point",
  "quest.27801123FEE6C86A.quest_subtitle": "Energy wherever the network reaches.",
  "quest.27801123FEE6C86A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four cores around a \"},{\"text\":\"Block of Redstone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:redstone_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make a \"},{\"text\":\"Flux Point\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"fluxnetworks:flux_point\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It pushes network energy into the blocks it touches, at any distance and in any dimension, up to 800,000 FE a tick by default.\"}]",
    "",
    "Each player can own up to five networks, and the Statistics tab graphs what flows through each one."
  ],
  "quest.0745E3328F6CFACD.title": "Flux Configurator",
  "quest.0745E3328F6CFACD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two obsidian, two Flux Dust and an Eye of Ender make the \"},{\"text\":\"Flux Configurator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"fluxnetworks:flux_configurator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Sneak-use it on a device to copy its settings, then use it on others to paste them: priority, transfer limit or Bypass Limit, Power Surge to jump the queue, and chunk loading.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Its sibling, the Admin Configurator, has no recipe: it is the server operators' tool."
  ],
  "quest.5305E83D3AC47468.title": "Basic Flux Storage",
  "quest.5305E83D3AC47468.quest_subtitle": "A battery with a membership card.",
  "quest.5305E83D3AC47468.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Six Flux Blocks and two glass panes make a \"},{\"text\":\"Basic Flux Storage\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"fluxnetworks:basic_flux_storage\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": 2,000,000 FE inside the network, 20,000 FE a tick in or out. It keeps what the plugs bring and the points don't want, and pays it back when they do.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6514BCC7DE926E05.title": "Herculean Flux Storage",
  "quest.6514BCC7DE926E05.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Six Basic Flux Storages and two panes make a \"},{\"text\":\"Herculean Flux Storage\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"fluxnetworks:herculean_flux_storage\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": 16,000,000 FE and 120,000 FE a tick. The energy the six already held carries over into the new one.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2E6B2F7C80184079.title": "The far end stays on",
  "quest.2E6B2F7C80184079.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A plug or a point can keep its own chunk loaded: switch on Chunk Loading in its settings. A generator room at the other end of the world keeps running while you're at home.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3ED26AD930E4E001.title": "A clean slate",
  "quest.3ED26AD930E4E001.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A device you break keeps its network and settings, so it rejoins wherever you place it. Craft it on its own to wipe them; a storage keeps its energy.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.400CC8C3E82C8338.title": "Members only",
  "quest.400CC8C3E82C8338.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A network is Public, Private or Encrypted with a password, and its Members tab sets who is owner, admin or user; strangers can't touch it. The Connections tab edits many devices at once.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1FEBB12F4C968D10.title": "Gargantuan",
  "quest.1FEBB12F4C968D10.quest_subtitle": "Two hundred and sixteen Flux Blocks, give or take none.",
  "quest.1FEBB12F4C968D10.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Six herculean storages make a \"},{\"text\":\"Gargantuan Flux Storage\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"fluxnetworks:gargantuan_flux_storage\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": 128,000,000 FE and 720,000 FE a tick, the largest battery Flux has. Inside it sit two hundred and sixteen Flux Blocks' worth of work.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.27B0324660ED6CA9.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.3F1F2E0C732124B8.title": "Five hundred and twelve",
  "quest.3F1F2E0C732124B8.quest_subtitle": "The most a single click will take.",
  "quest.3F1F2E0C732124B8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Five hundred and twelve \"},{\"text\":\"Flux Dust\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"fluxnetworks:flux_dust\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": exactly the most one left-click can press. If it went in one batch, that obsidian almost surely came out as cobblestone.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.18A9D4F0E058AC84.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.264F40F4997AB53E.title": "Pump",
  "quest.264F40F4997AB53E.quest_subtitle": "Drink the ocean. Politely.",
  "quest.264F40F4997AB53E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Obsidian, two iron pickaxes, a lava and a water bucket around a \"},{\"text\":\"Block of Diamond\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:diamond_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make the \"},{\"text\":\"Pump\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rangedpumps:pump\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It drains every fluid source up to 64 blocks around and all the way down, one block every 8 ticks, into a 32,000 mB tank.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Each drained block costs 100 FE, so a Flux Point beside it powers it anywhere. It pushes what it holds into every tank or pipe it touches. \"},{\"text\":\"It leaves stone where the fluid was.\",\"color\":\"#FF8C7A\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3B885EC6399E58F0.title": "Ask the pump",
  "quest.3B885EC6399E58F0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Right-click the Pump for its status: the block it's scanning, the range it has reached, its tank and its energy. A redstone signal pauses it, and it says «Done.» when nothing is left. Mekanism's \"},{\"text\":\"Electric Pump\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:electric_pump\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" follows one lake instead of sweeping a square.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.08F172F80A57CAE0.title": "Basic Item Collector",
  "quest.08F172F80A57CAE0.quest_subtitle": "A hopper with ambition.",
  "quest.08F172F80A57CAE0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An ender pearl over four obsidian makes the \"},{\"text\":\"Basic Item Collector\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"itemcollectors:basic_collector\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Stick it to a chest and it grabs items off the ground around it: 7×7×7 at first and up to 11×11×11, each axis set on its own in the menu.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.789EC5609BA1C0AA.title": "Advanced Item Collector",
  "quest.789EC5609BA1C0AA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An \"},{\"text\":\"Eye of Ender\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:ender_eye\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" over a basic collector and three obsidian: the \"},{\"text\":\"Advanced Item Collector\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"itemcollectors:advanced_collector\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" reaches 15×15×15 and filters. Nine slots, whitelist or blacklist, and whether the item data must match too.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.07D887054758DE58.title": "Straight into the chest",
  "quest.07D887054758DE58.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A collector has no inventory of its own: what it picks up goes straight into the block it's stuck to. No chest behind it, nothing collected. The show-area button draws the box it covers.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.014A8F84EBC9F691.title": "Energy Meter",
  "quest.014A8F84EBC9F691.quest_subtitle": "Numbers for your power lines.",
  "quest.014A8F84EBC9F691.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Iron, a \"},{\"text\":\"Redstone Comparator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:comparator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", an \"},{\"text\":\"Observer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:observer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", redstone and glass make an \"},{\"text\":\"Energy Meter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"energymeter:meter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Put it in a power line like a cable: its front screen shows the flow, its menu the total, the status and a graph of the last ten readings.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "The other five sides are inputs, outputs or off, in its I/O grid. Split, the default, shares energy evenly between outputs; Transfer fills them by priority. It measures every 5 ticks, Instant or Smoothed, and Tolerance ends a reading early when the flow stops."
  ],
  "quest.536708F45C27D271.title": "Test bench",
  "quest.536708F45C27D271.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Consume mode deletes every FE that comes in and allows no outputs: put a meter on a generator in this mode and you read its true maximum. \"},{\"text\":\"Don't leave it like that.\",\"color\":\"#FF8C7A\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.39B52DB018FA73DA.title": "A meter as a throttle",
  "quest.39B52DB018FA73DA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Limit caps what passes per tick, all inputs together, and the rest stays with the sender. Put one between a huge battery and a fussy machine. Its text fields even take math, like 20*64.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.336A0FDDE44FA90F.title": "Read it from a computer",
  "quest.336A0FDDE44FA90F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Next to a ComputerCraft computer the meter becomes an «energymeter» peripheral: getEnergyRate() and getTotalEnergy() return its numbers, and it fires an energymeter_changed event whenever they move.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.547643738565E9CE.title": "Not yet",
  "quest.547643738565E9CE.quest_desc": [
    "Four meters around an ender pearl make four External Monitors, which join into bigger screens. In this version their own tooltip reads «Work in progress!»: keep the meters for your lines."
  ],
  "quest.3A13853061DAA755.title": "Chips for the common store",
  "quest.3A13853061DAA755.quest_subtitle": "Fresh from the oven.",
  "quest.3A13853061DAA755.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Thirty-two \"},{\"text\":\"Logic Chips\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"laserio:logic_chip\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for the common store, once a day. That is eight blocks of quartz: a furnace line pays for itself.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1AC267ABDA85EAC5.title": "All nine at once",
  "quest.1AC267ABDA85EAC5.quest_subtitle": "Thirty-two diamonds of pure impatience.",
  "quest.1AC267ABDA85EAC5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight \"},{\"text\":\"Node Overclockers\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"laserio:overclocker_node\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": enough for one node side to run all nine of its cards in the same tick. Thirty-two diamonds so that nothing ever waits its turn.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.1720F5CBE9E22DA5.title": "Secret found",
  "task.5828B96AC70E1B53.title": "Look at an Item Pipe under water",
  "quest.3014F6E8C84B80C2.title": "Plumbing, literally",
  "quest.3014F6E8C84B80C2.quest_subtitle": "The pipe doesn't mind. The fish might.",
  "quest.3014F6E8C84B80C2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"You found an \"},{\"text\":\"Item Pipe\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pipez:item_pipe\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" under water. Pipez pipes waterlog like a slab: they keep working, and the water stays put around them.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.3F476E793EF67F8D.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.7E7602760B6FAD57.title": "Inventory Sensor",
  "quest.7E7602760B6FAD57.quest_subtitle": "It knows when the shelf is full.",
  "quest.7E7602760B6FAD57.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two \"},{\"text\":\"Crystallized Menril Chunks\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"integrateddynamics:crystalized_menril_chunk\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", two \"},{\"text\":\"Logic Chips\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"laserio:logic_chip\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a \"},{\"text\":\"Routing Matrix\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:routing_matrix\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make an \"},{\"text\":\"Inventory Sensor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:inventory_sensor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". The first goes to \"},{\"text\":\"When the Shelf is Full\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"27A67154B0D96862\"}},{\"text\":\"; QIO drive arrays and the Ark's bus want more.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.48039F57E19CAEE5.title": "Charged on the go",
  "quest.48039F57E19CAEE5.quest_subtitle": "The cable finally lost.",
  "quest.48039F57E19CAEE5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Five Flux Blocks, a core and two dust make the \"},{\"text\":\"Flux Controller\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"fluxnetworks:flux_controller\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", one per network. In its Wireless Charging tab the network charges what you carry, hotbar, hands, armour and Curios slots, wherever you stand.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "{image:fluxnetworks:textures/block/flux_controller.png width:48 height:48 align:center}",
    "",
    "Items by pipe and by beam, fluids from the pump, power by flux: the base now runs without you, and follows you around."
  ],
  "quest.22FA7C44E9520C91.title": "Route ledger",
  "quest.22FA7C44E9520C91.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Every route in Heliodor had a meter on it. We knew to the joule what each district drew, and to the day when the light would be ready. Nobody measured what it would cost. —J.\",\"italic\":true}]"
  ],
  "image.3D638D687B2A0514.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Pipez · by kind\",\"color\":\"#FF6B5A\"}]",
  "image.58AA0E4580DC87B8.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Pipez · upgrades\",\"color\":\"#FF6B5A\"}]",
  "image.0E76E2A0D7E9D8C3.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"LaserIO · cards\",\"color\":\"#FF6B5A\"}]",
  "image.2D29DCF22790EBB4.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"LaserIO · card kit\",\"color\":\"#FF6B5A\"}]",
  "image.4DE318F3C6ACD118.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Item Collectors\",\"color\":\"#FF6B5A\"}]",
  "image.64C9FEACC199358E.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"LaserIO · overclock\",\"color\":\"#FF6B5A\"}]",
  "image.3AFC4C70A2868876.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"LaserIO · filters\",\"color\":\"#FF6B5A\"}]",
  "image.5E26E7841A00FC6E.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Flux Networks · storage\",\"color\":\"#FF6B5A\"}]",
  "image.118C33B4E7E15859.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Ranged Pumps · Energy Meter\",\"color\":\"#FF6B5A\"}]",
  "image.1EECB7FFA3E2395E.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Logistics Networks\",\"color\":\"#EAF6FF\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.31025B82BE846A1E.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"pipe · beam · flux\",\"color\":\"#FF8A7A\",\"font\":\"minecraft:uniform\"}]",
  "image.2BA627D58647ED27.title": "Back to the Sun of Heliodor",
  "chapter.42B819B4DF274C89.title": "Mekanism · Basics",
  "chapter.42B819B4DF274C89.chapter_subtitle": [
    "From the infuser to five ingots per ore: alloys, circuits, the ore ladder, chemistry and factories."
  ],
  "quest.19CB5696848FEBD9.title": "Metallurgic Infuser",
  "quest.19CB5696848FEBD9.quest_subtitle": "Mekanism's front door, and every alloy's.",
  "quest.19CB5696848FEBD9.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Iron, redstone and two furnaces around a \"},{\"text\":\"Calibration Frame\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:calibration_frame\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": the pack puts the Frame from \"},{\"text\":\"First Signal\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"762B0B9FB46F552F\"}},{\"text\":\" where Mekanism wanted an osmium ingot. Material on the left, item in the middle; it spends the stored infusion.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"It copies Frames too: a \"},{\"text\":\"Raw Lens\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:raw_lens\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" with 40 redstone (four dust) makes one. Keep the infuser running and you never run short.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.453870346F22C04D.title": "Osmium",
  "quest.453870346F22C04D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Osmium Ore\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:osmium_ore\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" turns up at almost any height. Circuits, casings, tanks and upgrades all eat \"},{\"text\":\"Osmium Ingots\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:ingot_osmium\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", so dig a lot of it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.632A4DCDEDCA47B9.title": "Basic Control Circuit",
  "quest.632A4DCDEDCA47B9.quest_subtitle": "A rock that learned to count.",
  "quest.632A4DCDEDCA47B9.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"One osmium ingot and 20 redstone in the infuser: a \"},{\"text\":\"Basic Control Circuit\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:basic_control_circuit\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". The \"},{\"text\":\"Power Regulator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:power_regulator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" of act III takes two, and almost every Mekanism machine takes one.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.091376A558055EC0.title": "Steel",
  "quest.091376A558055EC0.quest_subtitle": "Carbon, twice. Then heat.",
  "quest.091376A558055EC0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Iron plus 10 carbon makes \"},{\"text\":\"Enriched Iron\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:enriched_iron\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; 10 more makes \"},{\"text\":\"Steel Dust\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:dust_steel\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; smelt it into a \"},{\"text\":\"Steel Ingot\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:ingot_steel\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". One coal is 10 carbon. Almost Unified keeps a single steel for the whole pack.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.49BE73F80D49E351.title": "Steel Casing",
  "quest.49BE73F80D49E351.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four steel, four glass and an osmium ingot: one \"},{\"text\":\"Steel Casing\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:steel_casing\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Nearly every Mekanism machine is built around one, so make a stack while the infuser is warm.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4F591F844FDAF9EA.title": "Enrichment Chamber",
  "quest.4F591F844FDAF9EA.quest_subtitle": "Two for one, forever.",
  "quest.4F591F844FDAF9EA.quest_desc": [
    "An ore block becomes two dusts; three raw ores become four. It also enriches coal, redstone and diamonds for the infuser, turns fluorite ore into six gems and scrubs the green off old copper.",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Point its output at an \"},{\"text\":\"Energized Smelter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:energized_smelter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" with auto-eject and every ore doubles on its own.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7654D937DFCAE528.title": "The other four ores",
  "quest.7654D937DFCAE528.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Mekanism also buries tin, lead, uranium and fluorite. \"},{\"text\":\"Tin\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:ingot_tin\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" goes into bronze and heaters, \"},{\"text\":\"Lead\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:ingot_lead\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" into reactors and radiation gear, \"},{\"text\":\"Fluorite\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:fluorite_gem\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" into the ×5 crystallizer. Uranium waits for the reactor chapter.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Fluorite sits deep. Enriched, one ore gives six gems.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6F8B736B8BD5A211.title": "Bronze by infusion",
  "quest.6F8B736B8BD5A211.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three copper ingots and 10 tin infusion make four \"},{\"text\":\"Bronze Ingots\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:ingot_bronze\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". The flamethrower, the Solar Neutron Activator, armored jetpacks and a whole Mekanism Tools set ask for it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.49145D699B5F7037.title": "Dictionary",
  "quest.49145D699B5F7037.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A book and a basic circuit. Right-click an item, block or fluid and it lists its tags, which is what most pack recipes actually check. A machine refusing an ingot? Ask the \"},{\"text\":\"Dictionary\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:dictionary\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" first.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5452400605B2E16E.title": "Infuser party tricks",
  "quest.5452400605B2E16E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Bio fuel turns dirt into podzol, cobblestone into mossy and clay into slime balls; mushrooms turn dirt into mycelium and netherrack into nylium; gold dust gilds blackstone. Cheap decoration, zero farming.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.54780C8D09E34E22.title": "Smelter and crusher",
  "quest.54780C8D09E34E22.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Energized Smelter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:energized_smelter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" is a furnace that runs on power and takes upgrades. The \"},{\"text\":\"Crusher\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:crusher\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" grinds ingots into dust, obsidian into four dusts and crops into bio fuel. The ore lines need both.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.14E5910A3E3F2429.title": "Precision Sawmill",
  "quest.14E5910A3E3F2429.quest_subtitle": "Measure once, cut six.",
  "quest.14E5910A3E3F2429.quest_desc": [
    "A log becomes six planks instead of four, plus a sawdust one time in four. It also takes apart chests, doors, beds and boats for their wood, and sawdust makes the Cardboard Box."
  ],
  "quest.60B4DC47E9B5A19E.title": "Redstone in a pinch",
  "quest.60B4DC47E9B5A19E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A machine with no generator still runs: redstone dust in its energy slot is 10,000 joules, a block 90,000. Fine for a first test, not for a factory.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.28555724F48F4C98.title": "Woop woop",
  "quest.28555724F48F4C98.quest_subtitle": "Your neighbours have questions.",
  "quest.28555724F48F4C98.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"You built an \"},{\"text\":\"Industrial Alarm\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:industrial_alarm\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": lead, two circuits and a lamp that screams on redstone. Wire it to a reactor, not to the doorbell.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.3D64BD97EF4159F6.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.23DDAEDB68C22955.title": "Twice the iron",
  "quest.23DDAEDB68C22955.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Ore in, \"},{\"text\":\"Iron Grit\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:dust_iron\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" out, smelter behind: two ingots per ore block. A raw iron block gives twelve grit, where a furnace gives nine ingots.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1C262970740A5BD8.title": "Raw or Silk Touch?",
  "quest.1C262970740A5BD8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Per ore block the ladder pays 2, 3, 4 or 5 ingots; per raw ore about 1.3, 2, 2.7 or 3.3. Fortune III averages 2.2 raw per iron or gold ore, so raw wins at every rung. Never combine raw back into ore: it costs eight.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0DEC133F39D372BF.title": "Every ore counts",
  "quest.0DEC133F39D372BF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The ore lines read common tags, so any mod's copper, tin, lead or uranium ore runs the same chain, and Almost Unified hands you the pack's ingot at the end.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3C5B69282B68529E.title": "Enrich before you infuse",
  "quest.3C5B69282B68529E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"One coal gives the infuser 10 carbon; enriched first, \"},{\"text\":\"Enriched Carbon\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:enriched_carbon\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" gives 80. Redstone, diamond, gold, tin and refined obsidian work the same way: eight times less mining for every alloy.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5FFBDA5C1966E63E.title": "Three scraps per debris",
  "quest.5FFBDA5C1966E63E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Crush \"},{\"text\":\"Ancient Debris\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:ancient_debris\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" into three \"},{\"text\":\"Dirty Netherite Scrap\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:dirty_netherite_scrap\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and enrich each into a scrap: three per debris, not one. Four scraps and 40 gold infusion make \"},{\"text\":\"Netherite Dust\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:dust_netherite\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.638F7FA395E0DF69.title": "More than ore",
  "quest.638F7FA395E0DF69.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The chamber also doubles diamond, emerald and coal ores, pulls nine string out of a cobweb, four clay balls out of a clay block and four salt out of a salt block.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4B74368CFAAEB506.title": "Advanced tier",
  "quest.4B74368CFAAEB506.quest_subtitle": "Red: copper learns redstone.",
  "quest.4B74368CFAAEB506.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Copper and 10 redstone make \"},{\"text\":\"Infused Alloy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:alloy_infused\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; a basic circuit between two of them is an \"},{\"text\":\"Advanced Control Circuit\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:advanced_control_circuit\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; both make the \"},{\"text\":\"Advanced Tier Installer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:advanced_tier_installer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Infused alloy is the pack's act II material.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Right-click a placed factory with the installer: it becomes an advanced factory, five jobs at once, with everything inside kept.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.442828417CA8E4B1.title": "Elite tier",
  "quest.442828417CA8E4B1.quest_subtitle": "Cyan: diamonds make everything better.",
  "quest.442828417CA8E4B1.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Infused alloy and 20 diamond infusion make \"},{\"text\":\"Reinforced Alloy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:alloy_reinforced\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; with an advanced circuit it gives the \"},{\"text\":\"Elite Control Circuit\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:elite_control_circuit\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and the \"},{\"text\":\"Elite Tier Installer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:elite_tier_installer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": seven jobs per factory. It is the act III material of the pack.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Enrich diamonds before infusing: one diamond becomes 80 units, four alloys. Crushed, it gives 10.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0D42E7962747E44D.title": "Ultimate tier",
  "quest.0D42E7962747E44D.quest_subtitle": "Purple: the top of the ladder, for now.",
  "quest.0D42E7962747E44D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Reinforced alloy and 40 refined obsidian infusion make \"},{\"text\":\"Atomic Alloy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:alloy_atomic\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; the \"},{\"text\":\"Ultimate Control Circuit\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:ultimate_control_circuit\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and the \"},{\"text\":\"Ultimate Tier Installer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:ultimate_tier_installer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" follow: nine jobs per factory. Atomic alloy is the act V material: the Ark bus and the NASA workbench take it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.68A3BD4A0922BE6C.title": "Creative, at a price",
  "quest.68A3BD4A0922BE6C.quest_desc": [
    "The creative energy cube, fluid tank and chemical tank each cost two Luminosities, two antimatter pellets and an ultimate block of the same kind: act VI. Nothing else in Mekanism is creative here."
  ],
  "quest.03EDC15E24003218.title": "Purification Chamber",
  "quest.03EDC15E24003218.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"With oxygen piped in, an ore block becomes three \"},{\"text\":\"Clumps\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:clump_iron\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a raw ore two. A \"},{\"text\":\"Crusher\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:crusher\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" turns clumps into dirty dust, the Enrichment Chamber cleans it, the smelter finishes.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3E8848EBCF6C0F99.title": "Dirty work",
  "quest.3E8848EBCF6C0F99.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Clumps leave the \"},{\"text\":\"Crusher\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:crusher\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" as \"},{\"text\":\"Dirty Iron Dust\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:dirty_dust_iron\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and go back into the Enrichment Chamber. Auto-eject each machine into the next and the ×3 line runs alone.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1542F3F004374F41.title": "Laying out the line",
  "quest.1542F3F004374F41.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Build backwards from the smelter and auto-eject each machine into the next. Items ride Logistical Transporters, chemicals Pressurized Tubes, water Mechanical Pipes. When one stage backs up, turn it into a factory right there.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.69531B1053799E84.title": "Chemical Injection Chamber",
  "quest.69531B1053799E84.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Hydrogen chloride turns an ore block into four \"},{\"text\":\"Shards\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:shard_iron\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", three raw ores into eight. Shards go into the Purification Chamber as if they were ore and follow the ×3 line from there.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.629779C586663C42.title": "Injected",
  "quest.629779C586663C42.quest_subtitle": "Hold the chloride.",
  "quest.629779C586663C42.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Iron Shards\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:shard_iron\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" by the stack mean the injector never runs dry. It burns hydrogen chloride every tick it works, so keep a full tank beside it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4BF21CA6DB94B673.title": "Dissolve, wash, crystallize",
  "quest.4BF21CA6DB94B673.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"In the \"},{\"text\":\"Chemical Dissolution Chamber\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:chemical_dissolution_chamber\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", sulfuric acid turns an ore block into 1000 mB of dirty slurry; the \"},{\"text\":\"Chemical Washer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:chemical_washer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" cleans it with water and the \"},{\"text\":\"Chemical Crystallizer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:chemical_crystallizer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" makes a crystal every 200 mB: five per ore.\"}]",
    "",
    "Crystals enter the Injection Chamber and ride the rest of the ladder down."
  ],
  "quest.097681B4961E86A7.title": "Five per ore",
  "quest.097681B4961E86A7.quest_subtitle": "Every ore, all five rungs.",
  "quest.097681B4961E86A7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Automate the whole ladder, dissolution to smelter, and bring 32 \"},{\"text\":\"Iron Crystals\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:crystal_iron\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". One ore block, five ingots; one raw iron block, thirty.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"×2\",\"color\":\"#7FD4F0\"},{\"text\":\" dust, \"},{\"text\":\"×3\",\"color\":\"#7FD4F0\"},{\"text\":\" clumps, \"},{\"text\":\"×4\",\"color\":\"#7FD4F0\"},{\"text\":\" shards, \"},{\"text\":\"×5\",\"color\":\"#7FD4F0\"},{\"text\":\" crystals. Each rung is one machine in front of the last, and nothing from a lower rung is wasted.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2F668AA8CC2CD507.title": "Tanks and tubes",
  "quest.2F668AA8CC2CD507.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Redstone and osmium make a \"},{\"text\":\"Basic Chemical Tank\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:basic_chemical_tank\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; steel and glass, eight \"},{\"text\":\"Pressurized Tubes\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:basic_pressurized_tube\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Gases never share a pipe with fluids.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.665DAC3A063D6BCE.title": "Electrolytic Separator",
  "quest.665DAC3A063D6BCE.quest_desc": [
    "Two parts water become two of hydrogen and one of oxygen. Send the oxygen to the Purification Chamber; the hydrogen feeds jetpacks and gas generators, or gets dumped.",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"In a hurry? Flint in a machine's chemical slot counts as 10 oxygen.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7AAD6A41961878DE.title": "Thermal Evaporation Plant",
  "quest.7AAD6A41961878DE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A hollow 4×4 tower, 3 to 18 blocks high, of \"},{\"text\":\"Thermal Evaporation Blocks\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:thermal_evaporation_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" with one \"},{\"text\":\"Controller\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:thermal_evaporation_controller\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and valves. Ten water makes one brine, ten brine one lithium. Taller and hotter runs faster.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7AD47E00FF7F365B.title": "Salt shortcuts",
  "quest.7AD47E00FF7F365B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Salt\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:salt\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in a chemical slot becomes hydrogen chloride on the spot, two units each: enough to test the injector. An oxidizer turns it into brine, and brine crystallizes back into salt.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.22349F7776839BAD.title": "Chemical Infuser",
  "quest.22349F7776839BAD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Brine through the separator gives sodium and chlorine; the \"},{\"text\":\"Chemical Infuser\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:chemical_infuser\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" joins chlorine with hydrogen into hydrogen chloride, one to one. Later it makes sulfur trioxide, sulfuric acid and fusion fuel.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2C7583D99D19BD77.title": "Rotary Condensentrator",
  "quest.2C7583D99D19BD77.quest_subtitle": "It condenses and it concentrates. Pick one.",
  "quest.2C7583D99D19BD77.quest_desc": [
    "Turns a gas into its liquid and back: water into water vapor for sulfuric acid, hydrogen or ethene into buckets you can store anywhere. Toggle the direction in its screen."
  ],
  "quest.3152C87C85D96BA6.title": "Chemical Oxidizer",
  "quest.3152C87C85D96BA6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Solids into gas: \"},{\"text\":\"Sulfur Dust\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:dust_sulfur\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" into 100 sulfur dioxide, yellow cake into uranium oxide, lithium dust into lithium. Its recipe wants a Dynamic Tank block and a personal chest or barrel.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.23C2CF85615E3DD8.title": "Pressurized Reaction Chamber",
  "quest.23C2CF85615E3DD8.quest_subtitle": "Solid, liquid and gas walk into a chamber.",
  "quest.23C2CF85615E3DD8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"One coal, 100 water and 100 oxygen give 100 hydrogen and a \"},{\"text\":\"Sulfur Dust\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:dust_sulfur\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": the sulfur mine you never dig. Bio fuel, water and hydrogen give ethene and substrate, the road to plastic.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.79384642C4B83DC2.title": "Sulfuric acid",
  "quest.79384642C4B83DC2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Oxidize \"},{\"text\":\"Sulfur Dust\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:dust_sulfur\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" into sulfur dioxide, infuse it with oxygen into sulfur trioxide, then with water vapor into sulfuric acid. The Dissolution Chamber drinks it every tick it works.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0B32EB1212C72099.title": "Plastic",
  "quest.0B32EB1212C72099.quest_subtitle": "Future MekaSuit, currently a pellet.",
  "quest.0B32EB1212C72099.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Substrate, 50 ethene and 10 oxygen in the reaction chamber make an HDPE pellet; three pellets enriched make an \"},{\"text\":\"HDPE Sheet\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:hdpe_sheet\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". The MekaSuit, the SPS casing and most MekaSuit modules are made of it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5BC3AE9B229AF367.title": "Spring cleaning",
  "quest.5BC3AE9B229AF367.quest_subtitle": "Not a drop wasted. Well, one.",
  "quest.5BC3AE9B229AF367.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Gauge Dropper\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:gauge_dropper\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on a tank gauge in a machine screen empties it. Wrong gas in the wrong tank? That is the undo button.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.1DCA66A8D4BF2B9B.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.571E4609C7DBE405.title": "Osmium Compressor",
  "quest.571E4609C7DBE405.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"It burns osmium like fuel, 200 units per ingot. Glowstone dust becomes \"},{\"text\":\"Refined Glowstone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:ingot_refined_glowstone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and refined obsidian dust becomes ingots. Built from an advanced circuit and infused alloy.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3F0A3D4BD7CD7DC3.title": "Refined Glowstone",
  "quest.3F0A3D4BD7CD7DC3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two uses, both worth it: the \"},{\"text\":\"Teleporter Frame\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:teleporter_frame\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and the refined glowstone set of Mekanism Tools, bright enough to light your way.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5ADD5F6244D85EAA.title": "Refined Obsidian",
  "quest.5ADD5F6244D85EAA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Crush obsidian into dust and infuse it with 10 diamond: \"},{\"text\":\"Refined Obsidian Dust\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:dust_refined_obsidian\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", the infusion behind atomic alloy. The \"},{\"text\":\"Osmium Compressor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:osmium_compressor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" presses it into \"},{\"text\":\"Refined Obsidian Ingots\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:ingot_refined_obsidian\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for the ×5 machines.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6F5634156B7CBD6D.title": "Sides and colors",
  "quest.6F5634156B7CBD6D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Every machine face has a color: input, output, energy or off. Turn on auto-eject and results leave by themselves. Most \\\"my machine does nothing\\\" is a side set wrong.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.00A44CBA44389978.title": "Configurator",
  "quest.00A44CBA44389978.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two iron, an osmium ingot and a steel ingot. Shift-right-click cycles its modes: configure a face in the world, empty a machine, rotate it, or use it as a wrench. \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.mekanism.mode\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" switches mode too.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6E47A63690BB78E6.title": "Copy, paste",
  "quest.6E47A63690BB78E6.quest_subtitle": "Twenty machines, one click each.",
  "quest.6E47A63690BB78E6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Configuration Card\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:configuration_card\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" copied one machine's sides and pasted them onto another. Set one up right, then stamp it on the rest.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.26855CCD17F36AC7.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.661FA7821F2D1A57.title": "Speed and energy",
  "quest.661FA7821F2D1A57.quest_subtitle": "Go faster. Pay for it.",
  "quest.661FA7821F2D1A57.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Infused alloy and glass around osmium dust make a \"},{\"text\":\"Speed Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:upgrade_speed\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; around gold dust, an \"},{\"text\":\"Energy Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:upgrade_energy\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Up to eight of each per machine. Speed alone drinks power: pair them.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3ABD5123B10FB27B.title": "The rest of the drawer",
  "quest.3ABD5123B10FB27B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Muffling\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:upgrade_muffling\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" quiets a machine; \"},{\"text\":\"Chemical\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:upgrade_chemical\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" makes chemical-hungry machines use less, up to eight. Filter pulls heavy water, Anchor keeps a chunk loaded, Stone Generator refills what a miner digs.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.21FFB243EABD11B6.title": "Upgrades travel",
  "quest.21FFB243EABD11B6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Pull upgrades out in the machine's upgrade tab and move them where the bottleneck is. Upgrading a machine to a factory with an installer keeps them in.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.1C7BED26A40D73D6.title": "Make a factory or use an installer",
  "quest.44FCC2FE085BE2FB.title": "The factory must grow",
  "quest.44FCC2FE085BE2FB.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A machine, basic circuits, iron and redstone make its factory; a \"},{\"text\":\"Basic Tier Installer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:basic_tier_installer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" does it in place. Basic factories run three jobs at once, advanced five, elite seven, ultimate nine, from one power and gas supply.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6EFE26582A231FEF.title": "Factories for the ladder",
  "quest.6EFE26582A231FEF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Enriching, purifying and injecting all have factories: an ultimate \"},{\"text\":\"Purifying Factory\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:basic_purifying_factory\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" takes nine ores on one oxygen supply. A Speed and an Energy upgrade per stage, then raise the tier where the queue grows.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.66246893B6524D29.title": "Formulaic Assemblicator",
  "quest.66246893B6524D29.quest_subtitle": "A crafting table that never blinks.",
  "quest.66246893B6524D29.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Write a recipe onto a \"},{\"text\":\"Crafting Formula\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:crafting_formula\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in the \"},{\"text\":\"Formulaic Assemblicator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:formulaic_assemblicator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and it crafts it from whatever you pipe in. Small automation before AE2 or Refined Storage.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0D9972EE20897060.title": "Paint by machine",
  "quest.0D9972EE20897060.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Pigment Extractor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:pigment_extractor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" pulls pigment out of dyes and flowers, the Pigment Mixer blends two, and the \"},{\"text\":\"Painting Machine\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:painting_machine\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" recolors blocks and items from the pigment tank.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7B469A385C394E88.title": "Osmium for the common store",
  "quest.7B469A385C394E88.quest_subtitle": "Somebody always needs another casing.",
  "quest.7B469A385C394E88.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Thirty-two \"},{\"text\":\"Osmium Ingots\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:ingot_osmium\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for the common store, once a day. An enrichment line makes it painless.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2E9CD35014A85B5B.title": "Absolute tier",
  "quest.2E9CD35014A85B5B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Compress glowstone dust with uranium oxide for radiance, then infuse atomic alloy with it: \"},{\"text\":\"Radiance Alloy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism_extras:alloy_radiance\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It makes the \"},{\"text\":\"Absolute Control Circuit\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism_extras:absolute_control_circuit\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and the \"},{\"text\":\"Absolute Tier Installer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism_extras:absolute_tier_installer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4C3CB7574EACF7B7.title": "Supreme tier",
  "quest.4C3CB7574EACF7B7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A netherite ingot, superheated sodium and lava in the reaction chamber make molten thermonuclear; it turns enriched radiance into thermonuclear, and that into \"},{\"text\":\"Thermonuclear Alloy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism_extras:alloy_thermonuclear\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for the \"},{\"text\":\"Supreme Control Circuit\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism_extras:supreme_control_circuit\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and \"},{\"text\":\"installer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism_extras:supreme_tier_installer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0DE663CD7C4E675B.title": "Cosmic tier",
  "quest.0DE663CD7C4E675B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"One antimatter unit in the Nucleosynthesizer turns enriched thermonuclear into enriched shining; infused into thermonuclear alloy, \"},{\"text\":\"Shining Alloy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism_extras:alloy_shining\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Cosmic circuits and \"},{\"text\":\"installers\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism_extras:cosmic_tier_installer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" follow, and the Naquadah reactor needs both.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.236F32D4B9AEB4F9.title": "Infinite tier",
  "quest.236F32D4B9AEB4F9.quest_subtitle": "Can it run Minecraft yet? Yes.",
  "quest.236F32D4B9AEB4F9.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Osmium Compressor, fed antimatter instead of osmium, turns enriched shining into spectrum; infused into shining alloy it gives \"},{\"text\":\"Spectrum Alloy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism_extras:alloy_spectrum\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". The \"},{\"text\":\"Infinite Tier Installer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism_extras:infinite_tier_installer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" also wants a plutonium and a polonium pellet.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5511D399DC176949.title": "Stack Upgrade",
  "quest.5511D399DC176949.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Thermonuclear alloy around a chest: the \"},{\"text\":\"Stack Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism_extras:upgrade_stack\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" makes a machine run several operations in parallel, on top of Speed.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6F0050EE9FA20B34.title": "Naquadah",
  "quest.6F0050EE9FA20B34.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Mekanism Extras hides \"},{\"text\":\"Naquadah Ore\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism_extras:naquadah_ore\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" near the Overworld's bedrock and, more often, near the void in the End. It climbs the same five rungs, and its ingots fuel the Extras reactor.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2116AE17C6925F49.title": "Planting Station",
  "quest.2116AE17C6925F49.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Planting Station\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekmm:planting_station\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" grows a sapling or crop into its harvest on nutrient solution. In this pack Mystical Agriculture seeds are left out and the replicators are gone, so nothing copies items from thin air.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.10FBA27EFA91E675.title": "Stamper and presser",
  "quest.10FBA27EFA91E675.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"CNC Stamper\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekmm:cnc_stamper\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" uses AE2 presses as molds to print circuits; the \"},{\"text\":\"Presser\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekmm:presser\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" adds redstone and printed silicon to finish the processor. An inscriber that takes Speed upgrades.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6C7BA901E570CBE7.title": "Rods and wires",
  "quest.6C7BA901E570CBE7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"CNC Rolling Mill\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekmm:cnc_rolling_mill\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" bends an ingot into two Immersive Engineering wires; the \"},{\"text\":\"CNC Lathe\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekmm:cnc_lathe\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" turns one into two rods. The lathe is built around a Robit, so plan the atomic alloy.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3E15AFD47884626A.title": "Large machines",
  "quest.3E15AFD47884626A.quest_subtitle": "Each one eats a Robit. Sorry, buddy.",
  "quest.3E15AFD47884626A.quest_desc": [
    "MoreMachine's big chemical infuser, separator and condensentrator do the work of many, and each recipe has a Robit at its heart, steel blocks and ultimate chemical tanks around it."
  ],
  "quest.63823B8696EDD879.title": "More factories",
  "quest.63823B8696EDD879.quest_desc": [
    "MoreMachine gives factories to the machines Mekanism left alone: oxidizing, dissolving, washing, crystallizing, centrifuging, reacting and more, in the same four tiers and the four of Extras."
  ],
  "quest.4336AA8A316A2D87.title": "Bio fuel",
  "quest.4336AA8A316A2D87.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Crusher\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:crusher\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" turns crops, seeds, saplings and food into \"},{\"text\":\"Bio Fuel\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:bio_fuel\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": an apple gives two, bread four, a cake six. It runs the bio generator, becomes ethene in the reaction chamber and feeds the Planting Station.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.59093824C14EB8E1.title": "What to do with hydrogen",
  "quest.59093824C14EB8E1.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The separator makes twice as much hydrogen as oxygen. Burn it in a gas generator, fill jetpacks, or set that output to dump: with the hydrogen tank full, the oxygen stops too.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6B6B9198208253F1.title": "Crusher bonuses",
  "quest.6B6B9198208253F1.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Crushed, a bone gives six bone meal, a blaze rod four blaze powder and a breeze rod six wind charges, all better than by hand. Cobblestone becomes gravel.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6D6440D5A185969C.title": "Combiner",
  "quest.6D6440D5A185969C.quest_desc": [
    "It presses two items into one: flint and cobblestone into gravel, glowstone dust into glow berries, glow ink and glow frames, four obsidian dusts and cobbled deepslate into obsidian. Raw ore and cobble make ore blocks, at eight raw a block."
  ],
  "quest.6BAE50C1E5FB03AC.title": "Energy Tablet",
  "quest.6BAE50C1E5FB03AC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Infused alloy, gold and redstone make an \"},{\"text\":\"Energy Tablet\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:energy_tablet\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a battery that fits in a pocket. Energy cubes, solar and wind generators, induction cells, heaters and the Robit are all built around one.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2160F64C571685B7.title": "Cheaper compressor fuel",
  "quest.2160F64C571685B7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"With Extras, crush an osmium ingot and enrich the dust: \"},{\"text\":\"Enriched Osmium\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism_extras:enriched_osmium\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" is 1600 units of compressor fuel, eight ingots' worth.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1F0B0B49C7994474.title": "Injector side jobs",
  "quest.1F0B0B49C7994474.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Gunpowder with hydrogen chloride becomes sulfur dust. With water vapor instead, the injector revives dead coral, hardens concrete powder and turns terracotta back into clay.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3A6DA1E7B25184C6.title": "Moving day",
  "quest.3A6DA1E7B25184C6.quest_subtitle": "Some assembly required. None allowed.",
  "quest.3A6DA1E7B25184C6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four sawdust make a \"},{\"text\":\"Cardboard Box\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:cardboard_box\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; you boxed up a block with everything inside and unpacked it somewhere else. Chests travel full.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.46161886BA3D605A.title": "Secret found",
  "image.60B7E86452087B87.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"MoreMachine\",\"color\":\"#7FD4F0\"}]",
  "image.17C3663C7E344DAB.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Chemistry\",\"color\":\"#7FD4F0\"}]",
  "image.7112FFF1F0B8F813.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Workshop\",\"color\":\"#7FD4F0\"}]",
  "image.5FD52CCEE86703C8.title": "Back to the Sun of Heliodor",
  "image.1A18AFDE818EDACF.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Mekanism · Basics\",\"color\":\"#7FD4F0\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.5F01512E7032CF02.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» Energy and reactors\",\"color\":\"#7FD4F0\"}]",
  "image.1C2B9183503F7D4E.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» Logistics and gear\",\"color\":\"#7FD4F0\"}]",
  "image.2E8A459C56FF48A9.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"infuse enrich repeat\",\"color\":\"#9FB8C8\",\"font\":\"minecraft:alt\"}]",
  "image.46AB7624C287E317.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Basic\",\"color\":\"#1EA05C\"}]",
  "image.20FAE49775986EE8.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Advanced\",\"color\":\"#CF443F\"}]",
  "image.7F2DFA8D7851CBC3.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Elite\",\"color\":\"#269BA1\"}]",
  "image.15BBB859CAB6FF26.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Ultimate\",\"color\":\"#AB5AAF\"}]",
  "image.4F0B645B097BC66A.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Mekanism Extras\",\"color\":\"#7FD4F0\"}]",
  "chapter.335E1EBA8FB3C477.title": "Modular Routers",
  "chapter.335E1EBA8FB3C477.chapter_subtitle": [
    "One block, nine modules: it sends, pulls, breaks, places and throws whatever you tell it to."
  ],
  "quest.0736402840CEA2F5.title": "Blank Modules",
  "quest.0736402840CEA2F5.quest_subtitle": "Every job starts on paper.",
  "quest.0736402840CEA2F5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three \"},{\"text\":\"Paper\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:paper\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", three gold nuggets and a redstone make six \"},{\"text\":\"Blank Modules\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularrouters:blank_module\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Every module starts as one, and so does the router itself.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"In this pack, two of them also go into each \"},{\"text\":\"Handling Core\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:handling_core\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.058BE65D29FE0DB7.title": "Modular Router",
  "quest.058BE65D29FE0DB7.quest_subtitle": "One slot, nine jobs.",
  "quest.058BE65D29FE0DB7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four iron, four iron bars and a Blank Module make four \"},{\"text\":\"Modular Routers\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularrouters:modular_router\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Alone it's a one-stack chest that pipes and hoppers can fill. With modules, up to nine, it does their jobs left to right, once a second.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.17F3126FB82FF091.title": "The Modular Routers manual",
  "quest.35C219094495CADB.title": "The router manual",
  "quest.35C219094495CADB.quest_subtitle": "Twenty modules, one index.",
  "quest.35C219094495CADB.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Book\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:book\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a Blank Module, shapeless, make the Modular Routers manual: a page for every module, upgrade, augment and filter, with ranges and quirks.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.47055EB557E19626.title": "It's also a chest",
  "quest.47055EB557E19626.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The buffer is an ordinary inventory: pipes and hoppers fill and empty it, and a comparator reads how full it is. With a tank item inside, fluid pipes can pump in and out of the router, no Fluid Module needed.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.639F2B09CF28C648.title": "Tune it in place",
  "quest.639F2B09CF28C648.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"In the router's screen, hover a module and press \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.modularrouters.configure\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\", or middle-click it, to open its settings without taking it out. \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.modularrouters.moduleInfo\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" shows its extra info.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.600E4C311B03D4A3.title": "When it runs",
  "quest.600E4C311B03D4A3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The router's top-right button sets when it runs: always, only without a signal, only with one, never, or once per pulse. Eco Mode slows an idle router to one run every 5 seconds until it has work again.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.00424957C313275B.title": "Front is relative",
  "quest.00424957C313275B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A module's direction counts from the router's front, not the compass. Turn the router and every module turns with it, so one tested setup can be copied facing any way.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.59CE29FBA0E14B10.title": "Who gets through",
  "quest.59CE29FBA0E14B10.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A module's nine filter slots take ghost copies, so nothing is used up. A new module is a blacklist: empty, it lets everything through. Switch it to a whitelist and, empty, it never runs.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "The buttons beside the slots decide whether damage, components like enchantments and shared tags count, and whether one entry is enough or all of them must match."
  ],
  "quest.0A923CBC44ADDA88.title": "Stop right there",
  "quest.0A923CBC44ADDA88.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A module's T button ends the router's run whenever that module did some work. A Void Module on cobblestone with T on, then a Sender: the cobblestone never leaks into your storage.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.290163B23A0B2F75.title": "Clean slate",
  "quest.290163B23A0B2F75.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A module crafted on its own comes out as new: filter and settings wiped, and a breaker keeps its pickaxe. \"},{\"text\":\"Take its augments out first:\",\"color\":\"#FF8C7A\"},{\"text\":\" they don't come back.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.12009C89323A4C1B.title": "Sender Module Mk1",
  "quest.12009C89323A4C1B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Blank Module with a bow and an arrow, or with a piston, makes a \"},{\"text\":\"Sender Module Mk1\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularrouters:sender_module_1\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It pushes the buffer into an inventory straight along its direction, up to 8 blocks away with clear sight; glass and fences don't block it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0DF16B8B6D8DC75E.title": "Sender Module Mk2",
  "quest.0DF16B8B6D8DC75E.quest_subtitle": "Aim, click, deliver.",
  "quest.0DF16B8B6D8DC75E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Sender Mk1 and an ender pearl make a \"},{\"text\":\"Sender Module Mk2\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularrouters:sender_module_2\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; four Mk1s and one pearl make four. Sneak-use it on an inventory to target it: up to 24 blocks away, 48 with augments, no line of sight needed.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0CBD0FC2D59E003A.title": "Puller Module Mk1",
  "quest.0CBD0FC2D59E003A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Blank Module and a \"},{\"text\":\"Sticky Piston\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:sticky_piston\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make a \"},{\"text\":\"Puller Module Mk1\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularrouters:puller_module_1\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": it pulls the first matching item from the inventory next to it into the buffer. A router with a puller and a sender is already a filtered hopper.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5A37E5452F496508.title": "Puller Module Mk2",
  "quest.5A37E5452F496508.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Puller Mk1 and an ender pearl make a \"},{\"text\":\"Puller Module Mk2\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularrouters:puller_module_2\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Sneak-use it on an inventory to target it: it pulls from up to 12 blocks away, 24 with augments, through walls.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.15372149A2940BF5.title": "Sender Module Mk3",
  "quest.15372149A2940BF5.quest_subtitle": "Any inventory, any dimension.",
  "quest.15372149A2940BF5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Sender Mk2, \"},{\"text\":\"End Stone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:end_stone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and an \"},{\"text\":\"Ender Chest\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:ender_chest\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make a \"},{\"text\":\"Sender Module Mk3\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularrouters:sender_module_3\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": it delivers to its target at any distance, in any dimension. \"},{\"text\":\"The target's chunk must be loaded;\",\"color\":\"#FF8C7A\"},{\"text\":\" the router won't load it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6881A47FBF06BE77.title": "Distributor Module",
  "quest.6881A47FBF06BE77.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three Sender Mk2s around a Blank Module make a \"},{\"text\":\"Distributor Module\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularrouters:distributor_module\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Sneak-use it on up to eight inventories to add them, again to drop one: it deals the buffer out round robin, at random, nearest first or furthest first.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1C002A613C85D948.title": "Void Module",
  "quest.1C002A613C85D948.quest_subtitle": "A trash can with a filter.",
  "quest.1C002A613C85D948.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Blank Module and a \"},{\"text\":\"Lava Bucket\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:lava_bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make a \"},{\"text\":\"Void Module\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularrouters:void_module\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": it destroys whatever sits in the buffer, for good. \"},{\"text\":\"Give it a whitelist before you plug it in.\",\"color\":\"#FF8C7A\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5FAA9B8ADDEBCC18.title": "Detector Module",
  "quest.5FAA9B8ADDEBCC18.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Blank Module and a \"},{\"text\":\"Redstone Comparator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:comparator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make a \"},{\"text\":\"Detector Module\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularrouters:detector_module\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It moves nothing: when the buffer matches its filter, the router emits redstone in the module's direction, level 15 by default, weak or strong.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.062014D5E8DC4A34.title": "Breaker Module",
  "quest.062014D5E8DC4A34.quest_subtitle": "It mines like the pickaxe you gave it.",
  "quest.062014D5E8DC4A34.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Blank Module and any pickaxe make a \"},{\"text\":\"Breaker Module\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularrouters:breaker_module\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" that keeps the pickaxe's tier and enchantments: Silk Touch and Fortune work. It breaks the block in its direction and pulls the drops into the buffer.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"It filters on the drops: to break stone, filter cobblestone, unless it has Silk Touch. Its settings can switch it to match the block itself.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.047A8907AA7D2A00.title": "Placer Module",
  "quest.047A8907AA7D2A00.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Blank Module, a \"},{\"text\":\"Dispenser\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:dispenser\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and \"},{\"text\":\"Dirt\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:dirt\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make a \"},{\"text\":\"Placer Module\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularrouters:placer_module\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": it places the buffer item as a block in its direction, by the usual rules. It plants seeds on farmland too.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2A1381800A39DDE5.title": "Dropper Module",
  "quest.2A1381800A39DDE5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Blank Module and a \"},{\"text\":\"Dropper\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:dropper\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make a \"},{\"text\":\"Dropper Module\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularrouters:dropper_module\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": it drops buffer items in its direction with no velocity at all, none of a vanilla dropper's random spit.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.64C39BFA006BAC0E.title": "Flinger Module",
  "quest.64C39BFA006BAC0E.quest_subtitle": "Yeet, but configurable.",
  "quest.64C39BFA006BAC0E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Dropper Module and \"},{\"text\":\"Gunpowder\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:gunpowder\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make a \"},{\"text\":\"Flinger Module\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularrouters:flinger_module\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": it throws items with the speed, pitch and yaw you set. Speed 1.0 on the level throws an item about 7 blocks.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3DB8A14253AD451C.title": "Vacuum Module",
  "quest.3DB8A14253AD451C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Blank Module, a \"},{\"text\":\"Hopper\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:hopper\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and an \"},{\"text\":\"Eye of Ender\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:ender_eye\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make a \"},{\"text\":\"Vacuum Module\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularrouters:vacuum_module\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": it sucks dropped items into the buffer from a 13×13×13 cube, up to 25 wide with Range Up. Give it a direction and the cube shifts that way.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2F370A8E9F45CC02.title": "Activator Module",
  "quest.2F370A8E9F45CC02.quest_subtitle": "A fake player with a real job.",
  "quest.2F370A8E9F45CC02.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two dispensers, a lever, redstone and quartz around a Blank Module make an \"},{\"text\":\"Activator Module\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularrouters:activator_module\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": a fake player using the buffer item. It right-clicks blocks, right-clicks animals for milk and wool, or attacks.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Attacking costs 150 FE per hit by default, so it wants an Energy Upgrade. It reaches about 4 blocks and can look above, below or level."
  ],
  "quest.10A239B4537B4512.title": "Extruder Module Mk1",
  "quest.10A239B4537B4512.quest_subtitle": "Drawbridges, on demand.",
  "quest.10A239B4537B4512.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Blank Module, a Placer Module and a Breaker Module make an \"},{\"text\":\"Extruder Module Mk1\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularrouters:extruder_module_1\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", with the breaker's pickaxe. With redstone it pushes a row of buffer blocks out in its direction; without, it pulls them back: bridges and hidden doors, 16 blocks long, 32 with augments.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The manual still says 12;\",\"color\":\"#FF8C7A\"},{\"text\":\" in this version the base range is 16. Break the router while the blocks are out and they stay out.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.63DFBAEFF20FF40D.title": "Extruder Module Mk2",
  "quest.63DFBAEFF20FF40D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Blank Module and a wooden chest make an \"},{\"text\":\"Extruder Module Mk2\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularrouters:extruder_module_2\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It builds from a 9-slot template of ghost blocks instead of the buffer: what it puts out are fakes that drop nothing, 32 long by default, 64 with augments.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.18145D5B11B6BD18.title": "Mimic Augment",
  "quest.18145D5B11B6BD18.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An Augment Core, obsidian, redstone and glowstone make a \"},{\"text\":\"Mimic Augment\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularrouters:mimic_augment\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", for the Extruder Mk2 only: its fakes take the real block's light, redstone, hardness and blast resistance. Fake obsidian stops creepers for real.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4010D7C602744018.title": "Pushing Augment",
  "quest.4010D7C602744018.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two pistons around an Augment Core make a \"},{\"text\":\"Pushing Augment\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularrouters:pushing_augment\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for either extruder. Every one you stack shoves whoever stands in the way harder when the blocks come out.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1DF940B5A333083D.title": "Fluid Module Mk1",
  "quest.1DF940B5A333083D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Cauldron\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:cauldron\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and two glass over a Blank Module make a \"},{\"text\":\"Fluid Module Mk1\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularrouters:fluid_module\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". With a bucket or tank item in the buffer, it fills it from the block in front or pours it out, into a tank or the world, 50 mB a tick: a bucket a second.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2F8F69E80A1891A6.title": "Fluid Module Mk2",
  "quest.2F8F69E80A1891A6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Fluid Mk1 and a \"},{\"text\":\"Prismarine Shard\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:prismarine_shard\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make a \"},{\"text\":\"Fluid Module Mk2\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularrouters:fluid_module_2\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": sneak-use it on any block up to 12 away, 24 with augments, to target it. Break that block and it pours into the world right there.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7E575940DB3FE88A.title": "Fluid Transfer Upgrade",
  "quest.7E575940DB3FE88A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A bucket and two glass over a Blank Upgrade make three \"},{\"text\":\"Fluid Transfer Upgrades\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularrouters:fluid_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Each adds 10 mB a tick to the router's fluid rate, from 50 up to 400: thirty-five of them. Speed Upgrades only make transfers more frequent, not bigger.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6D81B84C59869072.title": "Energy Output Module",
  "quest.6D81B84C59869072.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Blank Module with a block of redstone, two gold and quartz makes an \"},{\"text\":\"Energy Output Module\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularrouters:energy_output_module\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": it pushes FE from the router's energy buffer, or from a charged item in its item buffer, into the block in its direction.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.295DD2E5745455FA.title": "Energy Distributor Module",
  "quest.295DD2E5745455FA.quest_subtitle": "Wireless power, router style.",
  "quest.295DD2E5745455FA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An Energy Output Module and a Distributor Module make an \"},{\"text\":\"Energy Distributor Module\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularrouters:energy_distributor_module\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": sneak-use it on up to eight energy blocks nearby and the router feeds them all, no cables.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1DBBC4B6A66A6B13.title": "Blank Upgrades",
  "quest.1DBBC4B6A66A6B13.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Paper, lapis and gold nuggets make four \"},{\"text\":\"Blank Upgrades\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularrouters:blank_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", the base of every router upgrade. A router has five upgrade slots, and each one holds several of a kind, up to that upgrade's limit.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.54C9A1DC5FD165C8.title": "Stack Upgrade",
  "quest.54C9A1DC5FD165C8.quest_subtitle": "Kinder to your server than speed.",
  "quest.54C9A1DC5FD165C8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Blank Upgrade, stone bricks and bricks make a \"},{\"text\":\"Stack Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularrouters:stack_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". A module moves one item per run; each Stack Upgrade doubles that, up to a full stack with six. Prefer them to Speed Upgrades: the same throughput in fewer runs.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0018BDEEF2C2E4E5.title": "Speed Upgrade",
  "quest.0018BDEEF2C2E4E5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Gold, redstone, gunpowder and a blaze rod around a Blank Upgrade make three \"},{\"text\":\"Speed Upgrades\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularrouters:speed_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Each cuts 2 ticks off the router's 20-tick cycle; nine bring it to 10 runs a second, as fast as it goes.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0A3052BF756CB330.title": "Energy Upgrade",
  "quest.0A3052BF756CB330.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Quartz, a block of redstone and gold around a Blank Upgrade make an \"},{\"text\":\"Energy Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularrouters:energy_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": 50,000 FE of buffer and 1,000 FE per run, each, up to 64 of them. It charges or drains powered items in the buffer and feeds the energy modules.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Those rates are per router run, not per tick: with no Speed Upgrades, a run comes every 20 ticks.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7988B7B4D2D667BD.title": "Security Upgrade",
  "quest.7988B7B4D2D667BD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Quartz, gold nuggets and redstone around a Blank Upgrade make a \"},{\"text\":\"Security Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularrouters:security_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": only you and up to six players you right-click with it can open the router. Placers, breakers and activators then act as you, which land claims prefer.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "An attacking Activator spares the players on the list. The Security Override Card, creative only, opens any router."
  ],
  "quest.7B503AA0EF338341.title": "Camouflage Upgrade",
  "quest.7B503AA0EF338341.quest_subtitle": "Nothing to see here. Literally.",
  "quest.7B503AA0EF338341.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Blank Upgrade with red, green and blue dye makes a \"},{\"text\":\"Camouflage Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularrouters:camouflage_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Sneak-use it on a block to copy its look, and the router wears it. Holding a router shows the camouflaged ones nearby.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1C1CD517D17895B0.title": "Muffler Upgrade",
  "quest.1C1CD517D17895B0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Wool around a Blank Upgrade makes four \"},{\"text\":\"Muffler Upgrades\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularrouters:muffler_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". One silences the router, two also hide its beams and flying items, and three stop its front from pulsing.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.440F3E247F87DB19.title": "Sync Upgrade",
  "quest.440F3E247F87DB19.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Redstone, stone and a redstone torch with a Blank Upgrade make sixteen \"},{\"text\":\"Sync Upgrades\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularrouters:sync_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Routers with the same tuning, 0 to 19, and the same number of Speed Upgrades always run on the same tick: a wide drawbridge moves as one.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4DD482359E9A52C5.title": "Blast Upgrade",
  "quest.4DD482359E9A52C5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Iron bars and obsidian around a Blank Upgrade make a \"},{\"text\":\"Blast Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularrouters:blast_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": the router shrugs off explosions and bosses can't destroy it. Your Wither farm's router will thank you.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1EADF9B87E560C87.title": "Augment Cores",
  "quest.1EADF9B87E560C87.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Blank Module and a Blank Upgrade make four \"},{\"text\":\"Augment Cores\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularrouters:augment_core\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Augments are upgrades for a single module: each module has four augment slots, and not every augment fits every module.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.48633B7996879137.title": "Regulator Augment",
  "quest.48633B7996879137.quest_subtitle": "Enough is a number.",
  "quest.48633B7996879137.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An Augment Core, two comparators and quartz make a \"},{\"text\":\"Regulator Augment\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularrouters:regulator_augment\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It gives the module a count: a sender stops once the target holds that many, a puller leaves that many behind, a breaker stops when the buffer has that many.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Fluid modules take it in mB or as a percentage of the tank."
  ],
  "quest.53F40BAFEBE07057.title": "Range Augments",
  "quest.53F40BAFEBE07057.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Quartz, a stick and an Augment Core make four \"},{\"text\":\"Range Up Augments\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularrouters:range_up_augment\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", each +1 block for a ranged module up to its limit; a \"},{\"text\":\"Range Down Augment\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularrouters:range_down_augment\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" takes one off. Craft either one alone to flip it into the other.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.267A0F561CDA0EE3.title": "Redstone Augment",
  "quest.267A0F561CDA0EE3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Redstone and two redstone torches around an Augment Core make a \"},{\"text\":\"Redstone Augment\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularrouters:redstone_augment\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": that module follows its own redstone rule, apart from the router's. One router can run its sender only while powered and its vacuum always.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.47A06CF4E6214F0B.title": "Stack Augment",
  "quest.47A06CF4E6214F0B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Stack Upgrade and an Augment Core make a \"},{\"text\":\"Stack Augment\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularrouters:stack_augment\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": each doubles the items that one module handles, and it overrides the router's Stack Upgrades for that module, up or down.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.79D22D75BC4F1458.title": "Pickup Delay Augment",
  "quest.79D22D75BC4F1458.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A slimeball and an Augment Core make a \"},{\"text\":\"Pickup Delay Augment\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularrouters:pickup_delay_augment\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for droppers and flingers: each one, up to twenty, keeps what they throw out of reach for half a second more.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.53A4F34EC5996A82.title": "Fast Pickup Augment",
  "quest.53A4F34EC5996A82.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A fishing rod and an Augment Core make a \"},{\"text\":\"Fast Pickup Augment\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularrouters:fast_pickup_augment\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for the vacuum: it skips the pickup delay, 40 ticks on a player's drops and 10 on the rest, and grabs items the moment they land.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.081DD6650554363D.title": "XP Vacuum Augment",
  "quest.081DD6650554363D.quest_subtitle": "Bottled experience, 7 at a time.",
  "quest.081DD6650554363D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Soul sand and an Augment Core make an \"},{\"text\":\"XP Vacuum Augment\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularrouters:xp_vacuum_augment\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": the vacuum takes experience orbs instead of items and bottles them as \"},{\"text\":\"Bottles o' Enchanting\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:experience_bottle\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", 7 XP each. With a tank in the buffer or beside the router, it can fill it with liquid XP instead.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1ED00A2E70DA5FCA.title": "Filter Round Robin Augment",
  "quest.1ED00A2E70DA5FCA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A clock and an Augment Core make a \"},{\"text\":\"Filter Round Robin Augment\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularrouters:filter_round_robin_augment\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": instead of matching any filter entry, the module takes one entry per run, in order. Things that must go in a set sequence stop being a puzzle.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2BCD75739D1FCDA6.title": "Bulk Item Filter",
  "quest.2BCD75739D1FCDA6.quest_subtitle": "It remembers what belongs where.",
  "quest.2BCD75739D1FCDA6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Iron, glass, a diamond and two Blank Modules make a \"},{\"text\":\"Bulk Item Filter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularrouters:bulk_item_filter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": up to 54 items in one filter slot. Sneak-use it on a chest to copy what's inside; on a Sender Mk2 aimed at that chest, it keeps sorting there even after the chest is emptied.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.331CE58858E405F5.title": "Tag Filter",
  "quest.331CE58858E405F5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Bulk Item Filter, paper and black dye make a \"},{\"text\":\"Tag Filter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularrouters:tag_filter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": it matches items by the tags they belong to, like every ingot at once.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7FDFC242DDD5A265.title": "Mod Filter",
  "quest.7FDFC242DDD5A265.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Bulk Item Filter, a repeater and a redstone torch make a \"},{\"text\":\"Mod Filter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularrouters:mod_filter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": drop any item in its slot, press + and everything from that mod matches, up to six mods per filter.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1468FFEF3E8A23EC.title": "Regex Filter",
  "quest.1468FFEF3E8A23EC.quest_subtitle": "For people who enjoy backslashes.",
  "quest.1468FFEF3E8A23EC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Bulk Item Filter and a comparator make a \"},{\"text\":\"Regex Filter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularrouters:regex_filter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": up to six regular expressions, matched against the registry name after the colon, case-insensitive. _ore$ catches every ore and skips drill_core.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.13BA92EF743C36BE.title": "Inspection Filter",
  "quest.13BA92EF743C36BE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Bulk Item Filter, two spider eyes and paper make an \"},{\"text\":\"Inspection Filter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularrouters:inspection_filter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It checks a number on the item: durability, energy or fluid as a percentage, top enchantment level, or food value. Pull worn tools out for repair, or charged batteries off the line.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.70CD44EBFAC144C4.title": "Chemical Transfer Upgrade",
  "quest.70CD44EBFAC144C4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Osmium and glass around a Blank Upgrade make a \"},{\"text\":\"Chemical Transfer Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanisticrouters:chemical_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", from Mekanistic Routers: each adds 200 mB a tick to the router's chemical rate, which starts at 1,000. The chemical modules are in \"},{\"text\":\"Mekanistic Routers\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"69FAA53443B0B9B7\"}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.59B9705F321CB1CE.title": "Chemical Refill Module",
  "quest.59B9705F321CB1CE.quest_subtitle": "Never land on an empty jetpack again.",
  "quest.59B9705F321CB1CE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A diamond helmet over a \"},{\"text\":\"Chemical Module Mk2\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanisticrouters:chemical_module_mk2\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" over a wither skeleton skull make a \"},{\"text\":\"Chemical Refill Module\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanisticrouters:chemical_refill_module\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": from the router, it refills jetpacks and other chemical items in a player's inventory, wirelessly.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.253A1B7E8ED6EC04.title": "Handling Core",
  "quest.253A1B7E8ED6EC04.quest_subtitle": "Small hands for large workshops.",
  "quest.253A1B7E8ED6EC04.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Precision Mechanism\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:precision_mechanism\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", two Blank Modules and a \"},{\"text\":\"Power Regulator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:power_regulator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make a \"},{\"text\":\"Handling Core\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:handling_core\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". The first goes to \"},{\"text\":\"Small Hands, Large Workshops\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"6C696AA48D00D512\"}},{\"text\":\"; Refined Storage's autocrafter, the auto trader and the Ark's bus want more.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3811C10E5B930174.title": "Creative only",
  "quest.3811C10E5B930174.quest_desc": [
    "Two router items have no recipe: the Creative Module, which conjures the items in its filter into the buffer in turn, and the Security Override Card, which opens any secured router while held."
  ],
  "task.11CC52A390629D05.title": "Look at a block an Extruder Mk2 built",
  "quest.1B140231A4A7908D.title": "Nothing there",
  "quest.1B140231A4A7908D.quest_subtitle": "Knock knock. Who's there? Nobody.",
  "quest.1B140231A4A7908D.quest_desc": [
    "You're looking at a template frame, the fake block an Extruder Mk2 builds. It drops nothing when broken, and without a Mimic Augment it is only a picture of the real thing."
  ],
  "reward.3E5D1EE017B8FCEA.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.484452C15D2487BC.title": "Be kind to your server",
  "quest.484452C15D2487BC.quest_subtitle": "Ten runs a second. The server noticed.",
  "quest.484452C15D2487BC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Nine \"},{\"text\":\"Speed Upgrades\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularrouters:speed_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": a router at its hard limit, one run every 2 ticks. Its own manual pleads for Stack Upgrades instead, and it has a point.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.6D854AA4F49E7F6C.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.14AB0C29C147264E.title": "Modules for the common store",
  "quest.14AB0C29C147264E.quest_subtitle": "Paperwork, literally.",
  "quest.14AB0C29C147264E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Thirty-two \"},{\"text\":\"Blank Modules\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularrouters:blank_module\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for the common store, once a day: six batches of paper, gold and redstone.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2F65F08A98EB7F04.title": "Player Module",
  "quest.2F65F08A98EB7F04.quest_subtitle": "Your inventory, on the network.",
  "quest.2F65F08A98EB7F04.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A diamond helmet and chestplate, a wither skeleton skull, a Sender Mk3 and a Puller Mk2 make the \"},{\"text\":\"Player Module\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularrouters:player_module\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It moves items between the router and its owner's inventory, armour, offhand or ender chest, wherever they are, in any dimension.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "{image:modularrouters:textures/item/module/player_module.png width:48 height:48 align:center}",
    "",
    "Mine far from home and let the ores leave your pockets for the base on their own, or swap armour sets with a lever. It belongs to whoever crafted it: sneak-use it to claim one, and add a Security Upgrade on a server."
  ],
  "quest.4538DEA7854D8F7A.title": "Instruction card",
  "quest.4538DEA7854D8F7A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"In Heliodor we wrote every job down before we handed it to a machine. The machines followed the cards perfectly. The cards were the problem. —T.\",\"italic\":true}]"
  ],
  "image.01466224240CBD19.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Filters\",\"color\":\"#F2C04E\"}]",
  "image.2E7B7C86FD290C68.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Augments\",\"color\":\"#F2C04E\"}]",
  "image.47E931CADEEEEDBE.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Fluids and chemicals\",\"color\":\"#F2C04E\"}]",
  "image.630A819299168D40.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"More upgrades\",\"color\":\"#F2C04E\"}]",
  "image.5716943F3082399D.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Router power\",\"color\":\"#F2C04E\"}]",
  "image.0B9D4B517E75D6A8.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Modular Routers\",\"color\":\"#FFF4DA\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.6BAF9F9A213FB194.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"send · pull · break · place\",\"color\":\"#F2C04E\",\"font\":\"minecraft:uniform\"}]",
  "image.249FBD053552F64F.title": "Back to the Sun of Heliodor",
  "image.76CC4B6474FCB2F4.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Modular Router\",\"color\":\"#3B3733\"}]",
  "image.027C2ECFEBB380AB.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Buffer\",\"color\":\"#3B3733\"}]",
  "image.74F545394BDE06E0.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Upgrades\",\"color\":\"#3B3733\"}]",
  "image.23D9C12E444F0697.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Modules\",\"color\":\"#3B3733\"}]",
  "image.6577A145F846327D.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Module: filter and augments\",\"color\":\"#3B3733\"}]",
  "chapter.75EF5037C77E6FF2.title": "PneumaticCraft · Pressure",
  "chapter.75EF5037C77E6FF2.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Compressed air as power: tubes and compressors, the Pressure Chamber, heat, oil and plastic, and the PCB line up to twenty bar."
  ],
  "quest.3150D58D03E04401.title": "Compressed Iron",
  "quest.3150D58D03E04401.quest_subtitle": "Step back. No, further.",
  "quest.3150D58D03E04401.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"PneumaticCraft adds no ores: its metal is iron that went through an explosion. Drop iron ingots and set off TNT next to them; they come back as \"},{\"text\":\"Compressed Iron Ingots\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:ingot_iron_compressed\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", about a fifth fewer.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Blocks of iron blow up into Blocks of Compressed Iron the same way. Once the Pressure Chamber runs, it compresses iron at 2 bar with nothing lost.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.074A05CBCE944BF5.title": "Pressure Tubes",
  "quest.074A05CBCE944BF5.quest_desc": [
    "Two compressed iron and a glass block make eight. They carry air between compressors and machines, up to 5 bar, and any open end leaks with a hiss."
  ],
  "quest.48778579BF06AFAE.title": "Reinforced Stone",
  "quest.48778579BF06AFAE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight stone around one compressed iron make eight \"},{\"text\":\"Reinforced Stone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:reinforced_stone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; four of those make four \"},{\"text\":\"Reinforced Bricks\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:reinforced_bricks\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Compressors, chamber walls and half the machines of the mod are built from them.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.406D06BE3F1FCDC1.title": "Air Compressor",
  "quest.406D06BE3F1FCDC1.quest_subtitle": "Coal in, air out.",
  "quest.406D06BE3F1FCDC1.quest_desc": [
    "Six reinforced bricks, a furnace and a pressure tube. It burns anything a furnace takes and makes 10 mL of air per tick; lava and other liquid fuels go to the Liquid Compressor instead.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Each Speed Upgrade makes a compressor 1.5 times faster and 1.65 times hungrier: quicker, never cheaper.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.47774B423F345834.title": "Charging Station",
  "quest.47774B423F345834.quest_desc": [
    "A pressure tube, three bricks and three reinforced slabs. Tools, armor and drones fill up to the station's own pressure, 10 bar at most, and the arrow above the slot opens their upgrade screen.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A Dispenser Upgrade turns it into a charge pad: it fills items lying on top, players standing on it and drones hovering over it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.40A8D9DB32CEC57F.title": "Walls, a valve, two interfaces",
  "quest.40A8D9DB32CEC57F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight reinforced bricks in a ring make sixteen \"},{\"text\":\"Pressure Chamber Walls\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:pressure_chamber_wall\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". A wall and a tube make a \"},{\"text\":\"Valve\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:pressure_chamber_valve\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; two walls and a hopper, two \"},{\"text\":\"Interfaces\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:pressure_chamber_interface\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Chamber glass can stand in for any wall.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.1AD5B1F89248ED68.title": "Assemble a Pressure Chamber",
  "quest.34253C1A53D95911.title": "Pressure Chamber",
  "quest.34253C1A53D95911.quest_subtitle": "Squeeze, don't smelt.",
  "quest.34253C1A53D95911.quest_desc": [
    "A hollow box, 3×3×3 to 5×5×5: walls or glass on edges and corners, at least one valve fed with air, one interface with its I outward and one with its O outward. It runs recipes up to 5 bar and stores so much air it doubles as a battery."
  ],
  "quest.721672145B1351AF.title": "Seismic Sensor",
  "quest.721672145B1351AF.quest_subtitle": "Listening for black gold.",
  "quest.721672145B1351AF.quest_desc": [
    "Oil lakes are the only thing the mod adds to the world, and most sit deep underground. Right-click the ground with the sensor: it tells you whether oil lies straight below, how far down and roughly how many buckets."
  ],
  "task.709858A5BFA6351B.title": "Fill a bucket with crude oil",
  "quest.4377F5F9BF65B36C.title": "Gas Lift",
  "quest.4377F5F9BF65B36C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Place it where the sensor found oil and load it with \"},{\"text\":\"Drill Pipes\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:drill_pipe\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; three tubes make three. With air it pushes them down, breaks whatever is in the way and pumps the first fluid it meets. Deeper oil needs more pressure, up to 4.9 bar.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "{image:pneumaticcraft:textures/patchouli/oil_pumping.png width:96 height:96 align:center}",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A Gas Lift and a Small Tank keep their fluid when broken: carry the oil home in them.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5FA15976B9F5A7BA.title": "Refinery",
  "quest.5FA15976B9F5A7BA.quest_subtitle": "Crude in, four fuels out.",
  "quest.5FA15976B9F5A7BA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Refinery Controller\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:refinery\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" with two to four \"},{\"text\":\"Refinery Outputs\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:refinery_output\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" stacked on or beside it; each output costs a diamond. It refines from 100 °C, faster the hotter it runs, and the lightest fuel always ends up in the top output.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3044AE58B94956B0.title": "Thermopneumatic Processing Plant",
  "quest.3044AE58B94956B0.quest_subtitle": "Everyone calls it the TPP.",
  "quest.3044AE58B94956B0.quest_desc": [
    "A pressure tube and two small tanks between reinforced slabs. It mixes a fluid and an item with heat, pressure or both: LPG and coal become plastic, diesel and redstone become lubricant, heavy fuels crack into lighter ones."
  ],
  "quest.37D34AE0D251FE6E.title": "Plastic",
  "quest.37D34AE0D251FE6E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"100 mB of LPG and one coal at 100 °C make a bucket of molten plastic; charcoal and biodiesel work too. Pour it into the world and it sets into a \"},{\"text\":\"Plastic Sheet\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:plastic\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in about half a second.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A Liquid Hopper with a Dispenser Upgrade does the pouring, and an Omnidirectional Hopper picks up the sheets.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4B1FD4C2C0FF7ED9.title": "Amadron Tablet",
  "quest.4B1FD4C2C0FF7ED9.quest_subtitle": "Drone delivery is free. The rest isn't.",
  "quest.4B1FD4C2C0FF7ED9.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Seven plastic, a \"},{\"text\":\"GPS Tool\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:gps_tool\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and an air canister. Right-click a chest or tank to bind it: Amadron takes payment from there and a drone drops the order in the same spot. It sells what no bench makes, like the PCB Blueprint and the Assembly Programs.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.051F01FCC5CA2C8A.title": "PCB Blueprint",
  "quest.051F01FCC5CA2C8A.quest_desc": [
    "Eight emeralds on Amadron, or a trade with a Pressure Mechanic: the villager who keeps his own house in some villages and works at a Charging Station. Each UV Light Box eats one blueprint."
  ],
  "quest.0A71335508C3D6D5.title": "UV Light Box",
  "quest.0A71335508C3D6D5.quest_subtitle": "Ten minutes of tanning.",
  "quest.0A71335508C3D6D5.quest_desc": [
    "Three redstone lamps over the blueprint, a tube and compressed iron. An Empty PCB left inside gets better odds in the acid the longer it stays, up to ten minutes; fully exposed, it never fails.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Speed Upgrades shorten the ten minutes, and a redstone signal can set the target exposure: 25% plus 5% per signal level.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2B5DB291FDF7CF71.title": "Empty PCB",
  "quest.2B5DB291FDF7CF71.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two redstone torches, three gold or copper nuggets and a plastic sheet at 1.5 bar in the chamber give three \"},{\"text\":\"Empty PCBs\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:empty_pcb\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Expose them in the UV box before they touch any acid.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.11F56BAF7AA9DC33.title": "Etching Acid and Tank",
  "quest.11F56BAF7AA9DC33.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Molten plastic, two rotten flesh, two spider eyes and two gunpowder at 1 bar make a bucket of \"},{\"text\":\"Etching Acid\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:etching_acid_bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". The \"},{\"text\":\"Etching Tank\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:etching_tank\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" develops up to 25 exposed boards at once: 150 seconds cold, down to 30 hot.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6804AEDD26BCDA14.title": "Capacitors and Transistors",
  "quest.6804AEDD26BCDA14.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Both come from the chamber at 1 bar with a plastic sheet and gold or copper nuggets: two nuggets and a slimeball make a \"},{\"text\":\"Capacitor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:capacitor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", three nuggets and redstone a \"},{\"text\":\"Transistor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:transistor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Every board takes two of each.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.31AD4839D991F0C3.title": "Printed Circuit Board",
  "quest.31AD4839D991F0C3.quest_subtitle": "Where the mod gets clever.",
  "quest.31AD4839D991F0C3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An \"},{\"text\":\"Unassembled PCB\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:unassembled_pcb\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" from the tank, two capacitors and two transistors make a \"},{\"text\":\"Finished PCB\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:printed_circuit_board\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Drones, the programmer, pneumatic armor and the assembly line all start here.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3ADE220C3D504D30.title": "Assembly Line",
  "quest.3ADE220C3D504D30.quest_subtitle": "Six machines, one program.",
  "quest.3ADE220C3D504D30.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Platform\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:assembly_platform\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in the middle, the \"},{\"text\":\"Drill\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:assembly_drill\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and \"},{\"text\":\"Laser\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:assembly_laser\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" touching it, an import and an export IO Unit, which reach diagonally, and the \"},{\"text\":\"Controller\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:assembly_controller\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" beside them, all on one level. Only the Controller needs air.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.51849B762880FA95.title": "Assembly Programs",
  "quest.51849B762880FA95.quest_desc": [
    "Eight emeralds each on Amadron. With Laser in the Controller, Empty PCBs become Unassembled ones directly: no UV box, no acid. Drill turns a Block of Compressed Iron into twenty chamber valves.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A Laser and a Drill program crafted together become Drill & Laser, which runs two-step recipes such as Advanced Pressure Tubes in one go.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7F4E94EA0CDB0D0C.title": "Advanced Pressure Tubes",
  "quest.7F4E94EA0CDB0D0C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The drill turns a Block of Compressed Iron into twenty valves, the laser turns twenty valves into eight \"},{\"text\":\"Advanced Pressure Tubes\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:advanced_pressure_tube\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". They hold 20 bar and four times the air of a basic tube: tier two starts here.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7D3828A28FF6D5C5.title": "Twenty Bar",
  "quest.7D3828A28FF6D5C5.quest_subtitle": "Needle in the red, on purpose.",
  "quest.7D3828A28FF6D5C5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A valve and a Reinforced Air Canister Array, lasered, make the \"},{\"text\":\"Reinforced Pressure Chamber Valve\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:reinforced_pressure_chamber_valve\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": the same chamber then holds 20 bar and four times the air, no other block changed. Add sixteen PCBs from a line that runs by itself.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.60CEC3F961A89DE3.title": "Iron for the common store",
  "quest.60CEC3F961A89DE3.quest_subtitle": "Blow some up for the neighbours.",
  "quest.60CEC3F961A89DE3.quest_desc": [
    "Thirty-two Compressed Iron Ingots, pressed or blown up. Every tube, wall and wrench on the server starts with them."
  ],
  "quest.053308E13DBBF678.title": "Air, not pressure",
  "quest.053308E13DBBF678.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Pressure is air divided by volume, minus one: 20,000 mL in a 5,000 mL machine reads 3 bar. Machines need a minimum pressure to run, but what they spend is air, and air always flows toward lower pressure.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Tier-one tubes and machines take 5 bar, tier one and a half 10, tier two 20. Past that begins the red zone of the gauge, and somewhere in it the explosion."
  ],
  "quest.3978C0CF3796A832.title": "Compress blocks, not ingots",
  "quest.3978C0CF3796A832.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"An interface spends 1,000 mL of air on every item it moves, so a stack costs 64,000 mL, 4 bar of a 3×3×3 chamber. Feed it Blocks of Iron and the same iron moves for a ninth of the air.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.59EA5DB0BB6BD00B.title": "Pressure makes diamonds",
  "quest.59EA5DB0BB6BD00B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Eight blocks of coal at 4 bar make a diamond. The chamber also turns four snow blocks into ice at 1.5 bar, four ice into packed ice at 2 and four packed ice into blue ice at 2.5: cold sources for the heat work to come.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5326DE3052C2CB47.title": "Heat takes the short way",
  "quest.5326DE3052C2CB47.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Heat flows from hot to cold, faster across a big gap and through conductors such as Blocks of Compressed Iron. Every face open to air leaks it: cover a heated machine with any non-conducting block, even slabs or trapdoors.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3E6344FA58ECF3D8.title": "Two, three or four outputs",
  "quest.3E6344FA58ECF3D8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"From 10 mB of oil, two outputs give 2 LPG and 4 diesel; three give 2 LPG, 3 kerosene and 2 diesel; four add 3 gasoline on top. More outputs, more fuel per bucket, and adding one later rearranges the stack by itself.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.738124A8BAD04AC0.title": "Amadron buys fuel",
  "quest.738124A8BAD04AC0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Amadron pays an emerald for 1,000 mB of LPG, 2,000 of gasoline, 3,000 of kerosene or 4,000 of diesel, and sells crude oil at one emerald a bucket. A spare refinery pays for every blueprint and program.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.088ACAD691D08F43.title": "Failed boards come back",
  "quest.088ACAD691D08F43.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A board taken out of the UV box before full exposure may fail in the acid. Failed PCBs are not waste: a blast furnace turns each one back into an Empty PCB for another try.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.096DC7A2B6B67B2F.title": "PCBs for the Atlas",
  "quest.096DC7A2B6B67B2F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"One PCB goes into the \"},{\"text\":\"routing matrix\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"17BBD680007901AB\"}},{\"text\":\" of act III and two into each \"},{\"text\":\"Ark Connection Bus\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"765DEE642FC97F72\"}},{\"text\":\" of act V. No PneumaticCraft recipe asks for a pack component, so a steady line pays off early.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4E115C131D552D52.title": "Pickaxe diplomacy",
  "quest.4E115C131D552D52.quest_subtitle": "The wrench was right there.",
  "quest.4E115C131D552D52.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"You broke a PneumaticCraft machine by force. Next time, sneak and right-click it with a charged \"},{\"text\":\"Pneumatic Wrench\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:pneumatic_wrench\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": it comes off whole, with its air and upgrades inside.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.754686460B3C53AC.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.6BBB0DED2A3A92C2.title": "Fish supper",
  "quest.6BBB0DED2A3A92C2.quest_subtitle": "Wrapped in yesterday's paper.",
  "quest.6BBB0DED2A3A92C2.quest_desc": [
    "Potatoes fried in vegetable oil at 150 °C in the processing plant make chips; add cooked cod and a sheet of paper. The best by-product of an oil industry, arguably."
  ],
  "reward.2CF0E8264D3CCDB1.title": "Secret found",
  "task.5871EDC94E74B9BD.title": "The PneumaticCraft manual",
  "quest.51D2947340B730B4.title": "The manual",
  "quest.51D2947340B730B4.quest_subtitle": "Read it under pressure.",
  "quest.51D2947340B730B4.quest_desc": [
    "A book and one Compressed Iron Ingot. Its pages open as you earn the mod's advancements, so it grows with you, and every machine has a page with its numbers."
  ],
  "quest.25C690D3A3687FE0.title": "Omnidirectional Hopper",
  "quest.25C690D3A3687FE0.quest_desc": [
    "Five compressed iron and a chest. Its input faces you when placed and its output the block you clicked; a wrench turns either end. It needs no air, takes Speed Upgrades, and with a Dispenser Upgrade it drops items into the world."
  ],
  "quest.4EF4B21550AC08D1.title": "Liquid Hopper",
  "quest.4EF4B21550AC08D1.quest_desc": [
    "A small tank on a hopper. It moves fluids in any direction and fills or drains buckets lying in front of it; with a Dispenser Upgrade it also pumps whole fluid blocks and turns XP orbs into Memory Essence."
  ],
  "quest.2D248A72E865B0BE.title": "Pressure Gauge Module",
  "quest.2D248A72E865B0BE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Pressure Gauge\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:pressure_gauge\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", compressed iron ringed with copper, over a tube and two redstone. Fixed on a tube, it shows the pressure and emits twice that as redstone: 3.5 bar gives a signal of 7.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1EE5CB4B39A2B5F0.title": "Safety Module",
  "quest.1EE5CB4B39A2B5F0.quest_subtitle": "Better a hiss than a bang.",
  "quest.1EE5CB4B39A2B5F0.quest_desc": [
    "A gauge, a tube and two levers. It vents anything above 4.9 bar on basic tubes, or 19.9 on advanced ones, so nothing explodes. The air it dumps is lost: let a gauge module switch the compressors off first."
  ],
  "quest.6DDB996A03821727.title": "Regulator Module",
  "quest.6DDB996A03821727.quest_desc": [
    "A tube between two safety modules, fitted inline on a tube's open end. It lets no more than 4.9 bar through to its narrow side, so a tier-two line can feed tier-one machines; under a full redstone signal it becomes a one-way valve."
  ],
  "quest.699CF2DD4F51E8C6.title": "Air Grate Module",
  "quest.699CF2DD4F51E8C6.quest_desc": [
    "A tube in iron bars. With pressure it pushes entities away, 4 blocks per bar; under vacuum it pulls them in, 16 blocks per bar below zero, and drops items into the inventory behind it. From 0.75 bar it also cools heat sinks in front."
  ],
  "quest.4ECDA7D45DD0BB49.title": "Manual Compressor",
  "quest.4ECDA7D45DD0BB49.quest_subtitle": "Leg day, but for arms.",
  "quest.4ECDA7D45DD0BB49.quest_desc": [
    "Hold right-click on it to pump air, paid in hunger; the higher the pressure, the slower each stroke, until nothing more goes in. Enough to try a machine before the coal arrives."
  ],
  "quest.1E016F08FE4534B0.title": "Reinforced Chest",
  "quest.1E016F08FE4534B0.quest_subtitle": "Creeper-rated.",
  "quest.1E016F08FE4534B0.quest_desc": [
    "A chest wrapped in compressed iron, reinforced brick walls, obsidian and a gold nugget. Thirty-six slots, obsidian-grade blast resistance, and it keeps its contents when broken: a backpack you can't wear."
  ],
  "task.169EFE7290B4C0C4.title": "Charge a Pneumatic Wrench to 3 bar",
  "quest.6E014E99794C727D.title": "Pneumatic Wrench",
  "quest.6E014E99794C727D.quest_desc": [
    "Compressed iron, an air canister, a lever and orange dye, charged in the station. It shuts and opens tube sides, turns blocks, and a sneaking right-click picks a machine up with its air and upgrades inside."
  ],
  "quest.3E7CA8E1D46D0EB4.title": "Turbine Rotors",
  "quest.3E7CA8E1D46D0EB4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A gold ingot and two redstone at 1 bar make a \"},{\"text\":\"Turbine Blade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:turbine_blade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; three blades around compressed iron make a \"},{\"text\":\"Turbine Rotor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:turbine_rotor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Vacuum pumps, fluid mixers, the programmer and every drone spin on them.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.75346175EA271AE5.title": "Vacuum Pump",
  "quest.75346175EA271AE5.quest_subtitle": "Negative about everything.",
  "quest.75346175EA271AE5.quest_desc": [
    "Two turbine rotors, two gauges, two tubes and reinforced slabs. Air into the + side pulls the − side down to −1 bar. A chamber under vacuum moves one random enchantment from an item that has several onto a plain book."
  ],
  "quest.673F414D370B954F.title": "Vortex Tube",
  "quest.673F414D370B954F.quest_desc": [
    "Air goes in, one end heats and the other cools; the hot end faces you when you place it. Set it against the refinery and put a heat sink on the cold end: the two ends are linked, so the one you don't use needs venting."
  ],
  "quest.339060EEC077FE20.title": "Lagging and Heat Pipes",
  "quest.339060EEC077FE20.quest_subtitle": "A sweater for the refinery.",
  "quest.339060EEC077FE20.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Wool and glass make six \"},{\"text\":\"Thermal Lagging\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:thermal_lagging\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": it insulates, and clicks go through it to the machine behind. Lagging around Blocks of Compressed Iron or copper makes six \"},{\"text\":\"Heat Pipes\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:heat_pipe\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", which carry heat without losing it to air.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.25A96BD9C6127454.title": "Heat Sink",
  "quest.25A96BD9C6127454.quest_desc": [
    "Iron bars over compressed iron and copper. It sheds the heat or cold of the block it touches into the air, and burns you above 60 °C or below −60 °C. Heat Pipes give it more faces; an Air Grate Module in front cools it harder."
  ],
  "quest.1082DE08943B6012.title": "Heat Frame",
  "quest.1082DE08943B6012.quest_desc": [
    "Eight compressed iron around a furnace, stuck on any inventory. Hot, it smelts what's inside, up to one item a second; cold, it freezes water into ice, lava into obsidian and molten plastic into sheets, with a chance of a bonus sheet."
  ],
  "quest.49771D5A9A6CB349.title": "Thermal Compressor",
  "quest.49771D5A9A6CB349.quest_desc": [
    "An air compressor between compressed iron, tubes and two heavy pressure plates. It makes air from the temperature gap between opposite sides, north-south and east-west apart: lava against packed ice, or the spare end of a Vortex Tube."
  ],
  "quest.1D21178E43A3A35C.title": "Furnaces without fuel",
  "quest.1D21178E43A3A35C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A furnace, blast furnace or smoker next to a dynamic heat source, such as a Vortex Tube or an Advanced Air Compressor, runs on heat alone from 100 °C, faster the hotter it gets.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5E5AAA4730BAAB7B.title": "Four fuels",
  "quest.5E5AAA4730BAAB7B.quest_desc": [
    "A four-output refinery yields all four at once. Otherwise crack them in the processing plant: 100 mB of diesel becomes 80 of kerosene, kerosene becomes gasoline and gasoline becomes LPG, each step at 300 °C and 2 bar."
  ],
  "quest.75209C11B9C910B8.title": "Kerosene Lamp",
  "quest.75209C11B9C910B8.quest_desc": [
    "A small tank, glass panes and compressed iron. It lights everything within 10 blocks, up to 30 if you raise it in its screen, but fuel use grows with the square of the range. A bucket of kerosene lasts about forty real minutes at 10."
  ],
  "quest.466404FA3EB2A816.title": "Liquid Compressor",
  "quest.466404FA3EB2A816.quest_desc": [
    "An air compressor with a small tank, two tubes and leather. It burns liquid fuels, hot fluids such as lava included; its fuel tab lists them all. LPG is the best, 1,800,000 mL of air per bucket, then gasoline at 1,500,000."
  ],
  "quest.0C76C7E984EAAAF9.title": "Lubricant and Speed Upgrades",
  "quest.0C76C7E984EAAAF9.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A bucket of diesel and one redstone at 100 °C in the plant make a bucket of \"},{\"text\":\"Lubricant\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:lubricant_bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Ring it with four sugar and four lapis for a \"},{\"text\":\"Speed Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:speed_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; four Glycerol instead of the sugar make two.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4AB997B4BA6CA43A.title": "Upgrade Matrix",
  "quest.4AB997B4BA6CA43A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"One lapis lazuli and a bucket of water at 2 bar in the plant make four \"},{\"text\":\"Upgrade Matrices\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:upgrade_matrix\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Every upgrade recipe takes them in place of lapis, so each lapis now covers four slots.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6A544912C5A076BD.title": "Reinforced Pressure Tubes",
  "quest.6A544912C5A076BD.quest_desc": [
    "A pressure tube dipped in 50 mB of molten plastic at 1.5 bar in the processing plant. Reinforced tubes take 10 bar with the same 1,000 mL of air: the half tier between basic and advanced."
  ],
  "quest.197F67066B08564D.title": "Yeast Culture",
  "quest.197F67066B08564D.quest_subtitle": "It's alive. It likes it warm.",
  "quest.197F67066B08564D.quest_desc": [
    "Mushrooms and water in the processing plant, held between 30 and 60 °C: warm biomes do it alone, and it gets warmer the deeper you go. With one bucket made, pour it in a pool, drop sugar in and pour water beside it: the culture spreads into the water."
  ],
  "quest.6FECF8D27B98B37F.title": "Sourdough",
  "quest.6FECF8D27B98B37F.quest_subtitle": "It rises to the occasion.",
  "quest.6FECF8D27B98B37F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Wheat at 1.5 bar in the chamber becomes three \"},{\"text\":\"Wheat Flour\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:wheat_flour\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; eight flour around a bucket of yeast culture make eight \"},{\"text\":\"Sourdough\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:sourdough\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Baked, it beats the plain loaf.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4B1BE5F103A97811.title": "Ethanol",
  "quest.4B1BE5F103A97811.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Yeast culture and sugar in the plant, again between 30 and 60 °C, give \"},{\"text\":\"Ethanol\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:ethanol_bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": 50 mB per sugar or apple, less from potatoes, melon or berries. It burns in the Liquid Compressor too, weakly.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.698932AB8D2FBF85.title": "Biodiesel",
  "quest.698932AB8D2FBF85.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Seeds squeezed at 2 bar in the plant give 50 mB of \"},{\"text\":\"Vegetable Oil\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:vegetable_oil_bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" each. A \"},{\"text\":\"Fluid Mixer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:fluid_mixer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" at 2 bar turns equal parts oil and ethanol into \"},{\"text\":\"Biodiesel\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:biodiesel_bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and Glycerol: diesel's twin for fuel, plastic and lubricant.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.54E679499F54C684.title": "Module Expansion Card",
  "quest.54E679499F54C684.quest_desc": [
    "A PCB, four plastic and four redstone make four cards. Right-click one onto a tube module: gauges get thresholds, safety and regulator modules a precise setting, air grates an entity filter and charging modules ten times the speed."
  ],
  "quest.65345EFB4CA13BBE.title": "Smart Chest",
  "quest.65345EFB4CA13BBE.quest_subtitle": "Seventy-two slots, with opinions.",
  "quest.65345EFB4CA13BBE.quest_desc": [
    "Two reinforced chests, a PCB, an omnidirectional hopper and two diamonds. Each face can push or pull items, any slot can be kept for a single item, and a Magnet Upgrade pulls in what lies nearby."
  ],
  "quest.7C3BB7D02F471ABC.title": "Aphorism Tiles",
  "quest.7C3BB7D02F471ABC.quest_desc": [
    "The laser cuts a quartz block into four. A tile shows as much text as you type, scaled to fit, plus items from its Insert Item button; made invisible, it labels a chest and lets clicks through."
  ],
  "quest.50D6F9ACF9E4CF69.title": "Advanced Compressors",
  "quest.50D6F9ACF9E4CF69.quest_desc": [
    "Each wraps its basic compressor in compressed iron and advanced tubes. They reach 20 bar and make a base 50 mL per tick, five times the Air Compressor, but heat up as they work and slow down until they stop: give them heat sinks."
  ],
  "quest.0D9563D12CA17408.title": "Electrostatic Compressor",
  "quest.0D9563D12CA17408.quest_subtitle": "Waiting for a storm.",
  "quest.0D9563D12CA17408.quest_desc": [
    "An advanced air compressor caged in iron bars, plastic and a rotor. When lightning strikes it, rare under clear skies and common in thunderstorms, it takes 200,000 mL of air at once. A grid of iron bars or lightning rods up to 5 blocks around raises the odds.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Each iron bar straight below it bleeds off 10,000 mL once it reaches danger pressure, so a strike never blows it up.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7EEAD423F8D05024.title": "Flux Compressor",
  "quest.7EEAD423F8D05024.quest_desc": [
    "It turns Forge Energy into air: a base 40 FE per tick, more with Speed Upgrades, drawn from a 100,000 FE buffer that fills at twice that rate. It needs cooling, like every tier-two compressor."
  ],
  "quest.39187F5A437A8570.title": "Solar Compressor",
  "quest.39187F5A437A8570.quest_subtitle": "Sunbathing, professionally.",
  "quest.39187F5A437A8570.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An upgrade matrix and an amethyst shard at 2.5 bar make a Solar Wafer; the assembly drill finishes it into a \"},{\"text\":\"Solar Cell\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:solar_cell\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". The compressor needs open sky, works best at 350 °C and breaks past 425 °C until you mend it with a cell.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.50D2F8589687A786.title": "Pneumatic Dynamo",
  "quest.50D2F8589687A786.quest_desc": [
    "Air back into Forge Energy: 40 FE per tick by default, more with Speed Upgrades, at the cost of heat, so keep it cool or its output falls. Handy where tubes reach and cables don't."
  ],
  "image.3C55017C208B3F5D.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Tube modules\",\"color\":\"#E3A93F\"}]",
  "image.756C4B7F1BF9DE3E.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Hoppers\",\"color\":\"#E3A93F\"}]",
  "image.65F1A3627A2D108C.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Rotors and vacuum\",\"color\":\"#E3A93F\"}]",
  "image.00B969D27CF8C61C.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Heat\",\"color\":\"#E3A93F\"}]",
  "image.1B6E202E045A417C.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Fuels and upgrades\",\"color\":\"#E3A93F\"}]",
  "image.427B603D925F7891.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Renewables\",\"color\":\"#E3A93F\"}]",
  "image.03D165BE462B7B21.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Twenty bar\",\"color\":\"#E3A93F\"}]",
  "image.37963DA3000C0500.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"On the board\",\"color\":\"#E3A93F\"}]",
  "image.15A6759C1E21EA49.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"PneumaticCraft\\nPressure\",\"color\":\"#FFF3D6\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.2ED2893759B78B53.title": "Back to the Sun of Heliodor",
  "image.2020AE0D1A551592.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» Drones and armor\",\"color\":\"#E3A93F\"}]",
  "image.5B4E0A895DA6AB40.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"compress · heat · refine · etch\",\"color\":\"#B9A27A\",\"font\":\"minecraft:alt\"}]",
  "image.21A6CACD6761D879.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"-1\",\"color\":\"#E6E1D3\"}]",
  "image.4CBE54644B369C53.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"0\",\"color\":\"#E6E1D3\"}]",
  "image.7EB41511F99F0B4C.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"5\",\"color\":\"#E6E1D3\"}]",
  "image.161D6C087FD80C61.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"10\",\"color\":\"#E6E1D3\"}]",
  "image.1E9098720106D17E.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"15\",\"color\":\"#E6E1D3\"}]",
  "image.426E09765FB2DE80.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"20\",\"color\":\"#E6E1D3\"}]",
  "image.72776BF51839C0F8.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"bar\",\"color\":\"#E6E1D3\"}]",
  "image.7D51E9F9656C0613.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"tier 1 · 1.5 · 2\",\"color\":\"#B9A27A\"}]",
  "chapter.1C99C6436BCDCC3D.title": "Powah!",
  "chapter.1C99C6436BCDCC3D.chapter_subtitle": [
    "The Energizing Orb, seven tiers from Starter to Nitro, a self-building reactor and a wireless grid."
  ],
  "quest.1F371F6CAEB5D31A.title": "Dielectric Paste",
  "quest.1F371F6CAEB5D31A.quest_subtitle": "Every Powah block starts as black goo.",
  "quest.1F371F6CAEB5D31A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three coal or charcoal, two \"},{\"text\":\"Clay Balls\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:clay_ball\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a \"},{\"text\":\"Lava Bucket\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:lava_bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make 24 \"},{\"text\":\"Dielectric Paste\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:dielectric_paste\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", shapeless; two coal, a clay ball and a \"},{\"text\":\"Blaze Powder\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:blaze_powder\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make 16.\"}]",
    "",
    "Rods, casings, capacitors and almost every Powah machine are built on it. The bucket comes back empty."
  ],
  "quest.37110416738B3D43.title": "Rods and casing",
  "quest.37110416738B3D43.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Six paste around three \"},{\"text\":\"Iron Bars\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:iron_bars\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make eight \"},{\"text\":\"Dielectric Rods\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:dielectric_rod\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", upright or \"},{\"text\":\"horizontal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:dielectric_rod_horizontal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", and either turns into the other in the grid. Four iron and two of each make a \"},{\"text\":\"Dielectric Casing\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:dielectric_casing\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", the frame inside every machine.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.07F0640B56165C7F.title": "Three-mode wrench",
  "quest.07F0640B56165C7F.quest_subtitle": "Righty-tighty, lefty-linky.",
  "quest.07F0640B56165C7F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two iron and three paste make the \"},{\"text\":\"Wrench\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:wrench\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Hold \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.sneak\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" and right-click the air to switch modes: Config sets each side of a cable to in, out, both or off; Link pairs a rod with an orb; Rotate turns Powah blocks.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2FCC93B4D6121196.title": "Read the manual",
  "quest.2FCC93B4D6121196.quest_subtitle": "Nobody does. You should.",
  "quest.2FCC93B4D6121196.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Paste on a \"},{\"text\":\"Book\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:book\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" makes the \"},{\"text\":\"Powah manual\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:book\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Its pages list capacity, output and transfer for every tier of every machine, filled in from the game's own config.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.129F1FE153F2D864.title": "Starter tier",
  "quest.129F1FE153F2D864.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four iron, two paste and a \"},{\"text\":\"Block of Redstone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:redstone_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make four \"},{\"text\":\"Basic Capacitors\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:capacitor_basic\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; one splits into two \"},{\"text\":\"Tiny Capacitors\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:capacitor_basic_tiny\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Most Starter generators are two tiny ones and a casing, wrapped in paste around their own part: a furnace, a bucket, thermo plates or photoelectric panes.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"At Starter: \"},{\"text\":\"Furnator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:furnator_starter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and \"},{\"text\":\"Magmator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:magmator_starter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" 20 FE/t, \"},{\"text\":\"Thermo Generator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:thermo_generator_starter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and \"},{\"text\":\"Solar Panel\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:solar_panel_starter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" 20, \"},{\"text\":\"Reactor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:reactor_starter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" up to 250. \"},{\"text\":\"Energy Cells\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:energy_cell_starter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" hold 1,000,000 FE; the \"},{\"text\":\"Energizing Rod\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:energizing_rod_starter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" pours 100 FE/t.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.10F4C13DAD0CEEEF.title": "Basic tier",
  "quest.10F4C13DAD0CEEEF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Furnators, Magmators and Thermo Generators climb alike: the one a tier down, two capacitors of the new tier, a casing and the tier's material, plus two plates for a Thermo. Basic takes two \"},{\"text\":\"Basic Capacitors\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:capacitor_basic\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and iron. Two basics also make a \"},{\"text\":\"Large\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:capacitor_basic_large\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" one, the core of every capacitor above.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The others go their own way: \"},{\"text\":\"Solar Panels\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:solar_panel_basic\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" merge three of the tier below, \"},{\"text\":\"Reactor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:reactor_basic\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" blocks go four at a time with four large capacitors, \"},{\"text\":\"Energy Cells\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:energy_cell_basic\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" can merge two.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"At Basic: \"},{\"text\":\"Furnator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:furnator_basic\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and \"},{\"text\":\"Magmator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:magmator_basic\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" 80 FE/t, \"},{\"text\":\"Thermo Generator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:thermo_generator_basic\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and Solar Panel 60, Reactor up to 1,000; cells hold 4,000,000 FE.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0B8FAFE3ED58698A.title": "Energized Steel",
  "quest.0B8FAFE3ED58698A.quest_subtitle": "Iron and gold, but make it electric.",
  "quest.0B8FAFE3ED58698A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Put an \"},{\"text\":\"Iron Ingot\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:iron_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a \"},{\"text\":\"Gold Ingot\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:gold_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in the orb: 10,000 FE later they are two \"},{\"text\":\"Energized Steel\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:steel_energized\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It is the Hardened tier's material and the orb's first everyday job.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3BE186E4B0C3A349.title": "Hardened tier",
  "quest.3BE186E4B0C3A349.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four \"},{\"text\":\"Energized Steel\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:steel_energized\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", four paste and a large capacitor make two \"},{\"text\":\"Hardened Capacitors\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:capacitor_hardened\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Hardened blocks take steel as their material: five for a Furnator or a Magmator, one for a Thermo Generator, three for a Solar Panel.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"At Hardened: \"},{\"text\":\"Furnator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:furnator_hardened\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and \"},{\"text\":\"Magmator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:magmator_hardened\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" 200 FE/t, \"},{\"text\":\"Thermo Generator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:thermo_generator_hardened\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and \"},{\"text\":\"Solar Panel\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:solar_panel_hardened\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" 100, \"},{\"text\":\"Reactor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:reactor_hardened\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" up to 2,500; the \"},{\"text\":\"rod\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:energizing_rod_hardened\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" pours 1,000 FE/t.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.238EF8CD0FFD0F3B.title": "Blazing tier",
  "quest.238EF8CD0FFD0F3B.quest_subtitle": "Hot stuff.",
  "quest.238EF8CD0FFD0F3B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Blaze Rod\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:blaze_rod\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" takes 120,000 FE in the orb to become a \"},{\"text\":\"Blazing Crystal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:crystal_blazing\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; four \"},{\"text\":\"Blaze Powder\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:blaze_powder\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" cost the same. Four crystals, four paste and a large capacitor make two \"},{\"text\":\"Blazing Capacitors\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:capacitor_blazing\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Energize the rods, not the powder: one rod grinds into two powder, half a crystal.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"At Blazing: \"},{\"text\":\"Furnator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:furnator_blazing\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and \"},{\"text\":\"Magmator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:magmator_blazing\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" 800 FE/t, \"},{\"text\":\"Thermo Generator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:thermo_generator_blazing\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and \"},{\"text\":\"Solar Panel\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:solar_panel_blazing\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" 200, \"},{\"text\":\"Reactor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:reactor_blazing\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" up to 10,000; the \"},{\"text\":\"rod\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:energizing_rod_blazing\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" pours 4,000 FE/t.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0CF0FB72E18ED249.title": "Tier gates in this pack",
  "quest.0CF0FB72E18ED249.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three capacitors take an act material in place of one of their four crystals: Niotic an \"},{\"text\":\"Ironwood Ingot\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:ironwood_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (act IV), Spirited an \"},{\"text\":\"Ingot of the Skies\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:sky_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and Nitro an \"},{\"text\":\"Atomic Alloy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:alloy_atomic\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (act V). Starter to Blazing are native.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2D61C38C13C97286.title": "Niotic tier",
  "quest.2D61C38C13C97286.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Diamond\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:diamond\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" takes 300,000 FE to become a \"},{\"text\":\"Niotic Crystal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:crystal_niotic\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Three crystals, an \"},{\"text\":\"Ironwood Ingot\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:ironwood_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", four paste and a large capacitor make one \"},{\"text\":\"Niotic Capacitor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:capacitor_niotic\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"At Niotic: \"},{\"text\":\"Furnator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:furnator_niotic\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and \"},{\"text\":\"Magmator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:magmator_niotic\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" 2,000 FE/t, \"},{\"text\":\"Thermo Generator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:thermo_generator_niotic\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and \"},{\"text\":\"Solar Panel\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:solar_panel_niotic\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" 400, \"},{\"text\":\"Reactor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:reactor_niotic\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" up to 25,000; the \"},{\"text\":\"rod\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:energizing_rod_niotic\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" pours 10,000 FE/t.\"}]",
    "",
    "A Niotic reactor is nine crafts of four capacitors: 36 ironwood."
  ],
  "quest.367B407202BB9240.title": "Spirited tier",
  "quest.367B407202BB9240.quest_subtitle": "Emeralds, finally good for something.",
  "quest.367B407202BB9240.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An \"},{\"text\":\"Emerald\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:emerald\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" takes 1,000,000 FE to become a \"},{\"text\":\"Spirited Crystal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:crystal_spirited\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Three crystals, an \"},{\"text\":\"Ingot of the Skies\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:sky_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", four paste and a large capacitor make one \"},{\"text\":\"Spirited Capacitor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:capacitor_spirited\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"At Spirited: \"},{\"text\":\"Furnator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:furnator_spirited\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" 8,000 FE/t, \"},{\"text\":\"Magmator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:magmator_spirited\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" 8,000 on paper but 5,000 on lava, \"},{\"text\":\"Thermo Generator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:thermo_generator_spirited\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and \"},{\"text\":\"Solar Panel\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:solar_panel_spirited\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" 800, \"},{\"text\":\"Reactor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:reactor_spirited\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" up to 100,000; the \"},{\"text\":\"rod\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:energizing_rod_spirited\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" pours 40,000 FE/t.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.19C1BD8B46C7ED1D.title": "Nitro",
  "quest.19C1BD8B46C7ED1D.quest_subtitle": "Twenty million FE and a star.",
  "quest.19C1BD8B46C7ED1D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Nether Star\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:nether_star\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", two \"},{\"text\":\"Blocks of Redstone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:redstone_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a \"},{\"text\":\"Block of Blazing Crystal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:blazing_crystal_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" take 20,000,000 FE to become sixteen \"},{\"text\":\"Nitro Crystals\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:crystal_nitro\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Three of them and an \"},{\"text\":\"Atomic Alloy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:alloy_atomic\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make a \"},{\"text\":\"Nitro Capacitor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:capacitor_nitro\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"At Nitro: \"},{\"text\":\"Furnator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:furnator_nitro\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" 40,000 FE/t on coal blocks (one coal lasts two ticks), \"},{\"text\":\"Magmator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:magmator_nitro\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" 10,000 on lava, \"},{\"text\":\"Thermo Generator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:thermo_generator_nitro\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and \"},{\"text\":\"Solar Panel\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:solar_panel_nitro\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" 2,000, \"},{\"text\":\"Reactor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:reactor_nitro\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" up to 500,000; the \"},{\"text\":\"rod\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:energizing_rod_nitro\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" pours 200,000 FE/t.\"}]",
    "",
    "{image:powah:textures/item/capacitor_nitro.png width:32 height:32 align:center}"
  ],
  "quest.13F36FB6A1E76C79.title": "Energizing Orb",
  "quest.13F36FB6A1E76C79.quest_subtitle": "Charge it, and it becomes something else.",
  "quest.13F36FB6A1E76C79.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Five glass, a casing and three horizontal rods make the \"},{\"text\":\"Energizing Orb\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:energizing_orb\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It holds up to six ingredients and needs no power itself: \"},{\"text\":\"Energizing Rods\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:energizing_rod_starter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in the 9×9×9 cube around it pour FE in until the recipe is paid.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A rod is a \"},{\"text\":\"Nether Quartz\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:quartz\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", two tiny capacitors, a casing and a dielectric rod. It drinks only from the block it is mounted on, so mount it on a cable, a cell or a generator.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.369EE899CDF799C4.title": "Rods find their orb",
  "quest.369EE899CDF799C4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A rod links itself to an orb within four blocks when either one is placed. With two orbs close together, set the wrench to Link and click the orb, then the rod.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.50705D23CF139DAB.title": "Hands-free orb",
  "quest.50705D23CF139DAB.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Pipes and hoppers can fill the orb, one item per input slot, but only while the output slot is empty; pull the results out of it. A comparator reads how many slots hold something.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2FB0C5B2B7D35910.title": "More rods",
  "quest.2FB0C5B2B7D35910.quest_subtitle": "Many hands make light work.",
  "quest.2FB0C5B2B7D35910.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Rods add up: four \"},{\"text\":\"Starter Rods\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:energizing_rod_starter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" pour 400 FE/t, four times one. Each tier's rod is faster, from 100 FE/t at Starter to 200,000 at Nitro. A batch of Nitro Crystals costs 20,000,000 FE: almost three hours on one Starter rod.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.37CFA4BF8EA40332.title": "Charged Snowball",
  "quest.37CFA4BF8EA40332.quest_subtitle": "Snow chance of a quiet night.",
  "quest.37CFA4BF8EA40332.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Snowball\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:snowball\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" soaks up 500,000 FE and comes out as a \"},{\"text\":\"Charged Snowball\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:charged_snowball\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Throw it: lightning strikes where it lands, charging creepers and turning pigs and villagers into something worse.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.39FA5D7BD99D1B10.title": "Witch craft",
  "quest.39FA5D7BD99D1B10.quest_subtitle": "The villager is not taking questions.",
  "quest.39FA5D7BD99D1B10.quest_desc": [
    "Your charged snowball's lightning struck a villager, and on any difficulty but Peaceful that makes a witch. Minecraft counts it as Very Very Frightening, the trident's advancement: the bolt carries your name."
  ],
  "reward.2DD0F0B035D18AC8.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.051906D533BE18A8.title": "Not just Powah",
  "quest.051906D533BE18A8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Other mods write recipes for the orb too. Oritech's \"},{\"text\":\"Fluxite\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:fluxite\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" comes from an \"},{\"text\":\"Amethyst Shard\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:amethyst_shard\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for 12,000 FE, and fluxite with a nickel ingot becomes an \"},{\"text\":\"Energite Ingot\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:energite_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for 20,000.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.03588046E50281CD.title": "The fastest rod",
  "quest.03588046E50281CD.quest_subtitle": "Twenty million FE in a hundred ticks.",
  "quest.03588046E50281CD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Six upgrades from a Starter rod, the \"},{\"text\":\"Nitro Energizing Rod\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:energizing_rod_nitro\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" pours 200,000 FE/t: a whole batch of Nitro Crystals in 100 ticks. Each step takes a block of quartz, two capacitors of its tier, a casing and the rod before it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.11C240121981F86F.title": "Which generator?",
  "quest.11C240121981F86F.quest_desc": [
    "Furnator: anything a furnace burns. Magmator: lava. Thermo Generator: a heat source below and water, nothing burned. Solar Panel: free by day under open sky. Reactor: uraninite, and the biggest numbers of all. They mix freely on one grid."
  ],
  "quest.3C5CE7153B94BB30.title": "Furnator",
  "quest.3C5CE7153B94BB30.quest_subtitle": "A furnace that forgot how to cook.",
  "quest.3C5CE7153B94BB30.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Five paste, two tiny capacitors, a casing and a \"},{\"text\":\"Furnace\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:furnace\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make the \"},{\"text\":\"Starter Furnator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:furnator_starter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It burns anything a furnace does at 30 FE per burn tick: a coal is 48,000 FE in every tier, and higher tiers only burn it faster.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.476F2319E65D8D73.title": "Lava goes further in a Furnator",
  "quest.476F2319E65D8D73.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A lava bucket in a Furnator gives 600,000 FE and the empty bucket back; the same lava in a Magmator gives 100,000. The Magmator wins on pipes and pumps, not on energy.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.04AF1F9556CFEA5B.title": "Magmator",
  "quest.04AF1F9556CFEA5B.quest_subtitle": "Drinks lava, burps FE.",
  "quest.04AF1F9556CFEA5B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Furnator recipe with a \"},{\"text\":\"Bucket\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in place of the furnace makes the \"},{\"text\":\"Starter Magmator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:magmator_starter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Right-click it with lava or pipe some in: four buckets of tank, 10,000 FE per 100 mB. Broken, it keeps its lava and its charge.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"It drains at most 100 mB per tick, so on lava a Magmator tops out at 10,000 FE/t whatever its tier says.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5FCC81AD493C0E00.title": "Thermo Generator",
  "quest.5FCC81AD493C0E00.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four blaze powder, four redstone and a tiny capacitor make a \"},{\"text\":\"Thermo Plate\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:thermoelectric_plate\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; three, with three paste, two tiny capacitors and a casing, make the \"},{\"text\":\"Starter Thermo Generator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:thermo_generator_starter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Set it on lava or a \"},{\"text\":\"Magma Block\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:magma_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", fill it with water and it runs on heat alone.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Output follows the heat under it: a lava source counts 1,000, a magma block 800. The water drains 1 mB every two seconds, so a bucket lasts over half an hour."
  ],
  "quest.49FA3B4E66F57263.title": "Hotter than lava",
  "quest.49FA3B4E66F57263.quest_subtitle": "2,800 degrees of pure showing off.",
  "quest.49FA3B4E66F57263.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Nine Blazing Crystals make a \"},{\"text\":\"Block of Blazing Crystal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:blazing_crystal_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", and a Thermo Generator on top counts it as 2,800 heat: 2.8 times lava. It is also what a batch of Nitro Crystals eats.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.25460E08E4BE47CE.title": "Solar Panel",
  "quest.25460E08E4BE47CE.quest_subtitle": "Free power, weather permitting.",
  "quest.25460E08E4BE47CE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four paste and four \"},{\"text\":\"Lapis Lazuli\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:lapis_lazuli\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" around a \"},{\"text\":\"Glass Pane\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:glass_pane\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make a \"},{\"text\":\"Photoelectric Pane\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:photoelectric_pane\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; three, with three paste, two tiny capacitors and a casing, make the \"},{\"text\":\"Starter Solar Panel\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:solar_panel_starter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It works by day with open sky above, never in the Nether or the End.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5ABE8859841EB06A.title": "Solar through the roof",
  "quest.5ABE8859841EB06A.quest_subtitle": "A window for your panel. Sort of.",
  "quest.5ABE8859841EB06A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Right-click a plain Enderman or an Endermite with a \"},{\"text\":\"Photoelectric Pane\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:photoelectric_pane\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": the mob is gone and you hold a \"},{\"text\":\"Lens of Ender\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:lens_of_ender\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Used on a Solar Panel, it lets the panel see through blocks, and it drops back if you break the panel.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Enderman Overhaul's biome endermen don't count: it has to be the plain one.\",\"color\":\"#FF8C7A\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6579E585156B0CEE.title": "Solar merges three for one",
  "quest.6579E585156B0CEE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Every solar upgrade eats three panels of the tier below. Basic makes exactly what three Starters did (60 FE/t); past Basic the new panel makes less than the three it ate. Upgrade solar for space, not for power.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6F04A087B6A5D44E.title": "Uraninite",
  "quest.6F04A087B6A5D44E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Uraninite ore hides below Y 64 (poor), Y 20 and Y 0 (dense) and needs an iron pickaxe. It drops 1, 2 or 4 \"},{\"text\":\"Raw Uraninite\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:uraninite_raw\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": a furnace makes one \"},{\"text\":\"Uraninite\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:uraninite\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" of each, the orb makes two for 2,000 FE.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Any mod's uranium ingot also energizes into one uraninite, for 30,000 FE."
  ],
  "quest.5FE85F3814ED74AA.title": "Fortune beats Silk Touch",
  "quest.5FE85F3814ED74AA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Silk-touched ore energizes into 3, 5 or 10 uraninite. Fortune III averages 2.2 times the raw drop, and each raw makes two in the orb: about 4.4, 8.8 and 17.6. Mine with Fortune, then energize.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.1D21F141EED4A9B5.title": "Look at Dense Deepslate Uraninite Ore",
  "quest.1BE5A94192E020A0.title": "Rich vein",
  "quest.1BE5A94192E020A0.quest_subtitle": "Glowing? No. Promising? Very.",
  "quest.1BE5A94192E020A0.quest_desc": [
    "You spotted dense uraninite. It only forms below Y 0, in small veins; mined, it drops four raw uraninite before Fortune, and silk-touched and energized it gives ten."
  ],
  "reward.3497C0D8656AB275.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.15318E1EC838402F.title": "Dry Ice",
  "quest.15318E1EC838402F.quest_subtitle": "Cooler than cool.",
  "quest.15318E1EC838402F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two \"},{\"text\":\"Blue Ice\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:blue_ice\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" become one \"},{\"text\":\"Dry Ice\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:dry_ice\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for 10,000 FE, or mine it in veins under icy biomes, below Y 64. It is the coldest solid coolant: one block keeps a working reactor cold for about 24 minutes.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.14D998DFD0F054B0.title": "Look at your reactor, built",
  "quest.5A9CC0F268D579EC.title": "Powah Reactor",
  "quest.5A9CC0F268D579EC.quest_subtitle": "Some assembly required. By itself.",
  "quest.5A9CC0F268D579EC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four \"},{\"text\":\"Uraninite\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:uraninite\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", four tiny capacitors and a casing make four \"},{\"text\":\"Starter Reactor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:reactor_starter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" blocks. With 36 in your inventory, place one where a 3×3 space four blocks tall is free, with nobody inside: the reactor builds itself.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "It burns uraninite, holds a bucket of water and takes carbon, redstone and a solid coolant in its slots. Auto mode stops it when its buffer is full and restarts it at 70%. Break any block and the whole reactor falls back into 36 blocks."
  ],
  "quest.030FC7BDDF4253CE.title": "A cold reactor pays",
  "quest.030FC7BDDF4253CE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Heat eats output and fuel. With water in its tank, a solid coolant divides the temperature: dry ice by 33. A cold reactor burns about a thirtieth of the uraninite, and with boosts it runs near its full rating. The water is never used up.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.79730F38F37F94C5.title": "Boost only when cold",
  "quest.79730F38F37F94C5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Coal or another furnace fuel in the carbon slot adds 20% output and 180 heat; redstone adds 40% and 120 heat. On a hot reactor that heat costs more than the boost gives: coolant first, boosts after.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0C17E3CDD19DDAE5.title": "Where the power comes out",
  "quest.0C17E3CDD19DDAE5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Pipes can feed fuel, coolant and water through any block of the reactor, but power only leaves through the middle block of each side's bottom row, the top center and the floor under the core.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.13A2D2674EA6FFD8.title": "Rebuild at Basic",
  "quest.13A2D2674EA6FFD8.quest_subtitle": "Nine crafts, one very big upgrade.",
  "quest.13A2D2674EA6FFD8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Break your reactor to get its 36 blocks back. Four of them, four \"},{\"text\":\"Large Basic Capacitors\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:capacitor_basic_large\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a uraninite make four \"},{\"text\":\"Basic Reactor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:reactor_basic\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" blocks: nine crafts for a reactor rated 1,000 FE/t, four times the Starter.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.08AFF80CF831A282.title": "Half a million per tick",
  "quest.08AFF80CF831A282.quest_subtitle": "Bring coolant. Bring a lot.",
  "quest.08AFF80CF831A282.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Climb the reactor through every tier, four blocks at a time, and the \"},{\"text\":\"Nitro Reactor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:reactor_nitro\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" is rated 500,000 FE/t. On the way it eats 36 capacitors a tier: 36 ironwood, 36 sky ingots and 36 atomic alloys.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1F1CD222C834645E.title": "Energy Cables",
  "quest.1F1CD222C834645E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Six horizontal dielectric rods, two iron nuggets and a tiny capacitor make twelve \"},{\"text\":\"Starter Energy Cables\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:energy_cable_starter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": 500 FE/t. They connect to any mod's FE block, and the wrench in Config mode sets each side to in, out, both or off.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Each tier's cable carries more, up to 1,000,000 FE/t at Nitro: six rods, two of the tier's material and one capacitor make twelve."
  ],
  "quest.16ACDFEC566167E4.title": "Energy Cell",
  "quest.16ACDFEC566167E4.quest_subtitle": "A battery you can stand on.",
  "quest.16ACDFEC566167E4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four iron, two tiny capacitors and a casing make a \"},{\"text\":\"Starter Energy Cell\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:energy_cell_starter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": 1,000,000 FE, 1,000 FE/t in and out. Put it between generators and machines to smooth the peaks; its two slots charge tools.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1EC6E4B809E11FA6.title": "Cells keep their charge",
  "quest.1EC6E4B809E11FA6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A broken cell keeps its energy, so moving one costs nothing. From Hardened up, each upgrade merges two cells of the tier below: 1 million FE at Starter, 2 billion at Nitro.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4E9DEEF6B7228661.title": "Battery",
  "quest.4E9DEEF6B7228661.quest_subtitle": "Charge on the go.",
  "quest.4E9DEEF6B7228661.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four Basic Capacitors, four paste and a \"},{\"text\":\"Block of Redstone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:redstone_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make a \"},{\"text\":\"Starter Battery\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:battery_starter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": 1,000,000 FE in your pocket. Hold \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.sneak\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" and right-click to switch charging on, and it tops up your other items.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.202763CA4CCA4E60.title": "Energy Hopper",
  "quest.202763CA4CCA4E60.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Five paste, two tiny capacitors, a casing and a \"},{\"text\":\"Hopper\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:hopper\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make the \"},{\"text\":\"Starter Energy Hopper\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:energy_hopper_starter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Point it at a chest and it charges every tool inside: a charging station for the whole team.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2C609AF96798E72A.title": "Energy Discharger",
  "quest.2C609AF96798E72A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Six paste, two tiny capacitors and a casing make the \"},{\"text\":\"Starter Energy Discharger\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:energy_discharger_starter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Its seven slots drain charged items back into the grid: batteries from another base, tools you no longer use.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.67B57EF11DC9C268.title": "A pearl with a face",
  "quest.67B57EF11DC9C268.quest_subtitle": "The zombie volunteered. More or less.",
  "quest.67B57EF11DC9C268.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four paste and four iron bars around an \"},{\"text\":\"Ender Pearl\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:ender_pearl\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make an \"},{\"text\":\"Aerial Pearl\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:aerial_pearl\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Right-click a Zombie, a Husk or a Zombie Villager with it: the zombie is gone and you hold a \"},{\"text\":\"Player Aerial Pearl\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:player_aerial_pearl\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4E6361BFFEB4C669.title": "Player Transmitter",
  "quest.4E6361BFFEB4C669.quest_subtitle": "Charging cables are so last tier.",
  "quest.4E6361BFFEB4C669.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The pearl, two tiny capacitors, a casing and a dielectric rod make the \"},{\"text\":\"Starter Player Transmitter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:player_transmitter_starter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Right-click with a \"},{\"text\":\"Binding Card\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:binding_card\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" to bind it to you, then slot it in: it charges your inventory, armor and off-hand anywhere in its dimension.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Blank Card\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:blank_card\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" is two dielectric rods; with two redstone and a rotten flesh it becomes a Binding Card. The Starter transmitter charges 500 FE/t per item, the Nitro one 1,000,000, and Curios slots count too.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.480D0D25E99C8830.title": "Across dimensions",
  "quest.480D0D25E99C8830.quest_subtitle": "Enderman-approved. Posthumously.",
  "quest.480D0D25E99C8830.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"No recipe makes the \"},{\"text\":\"Dimensional Binding Card\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:binding_card_dim\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": right-click a plain Enderman or an Endermite with a Binding Card, bound or not. The mob vanishes, the card keeps its owner, and the transmitter reaches you in any dimension.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Enderman Overhaul's biome endermen don't count: it has to be the plain one.\",\"color\":\"#FF8C7A\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.578F34D069A2AD44.title": "Ender Core",
  "quest.578F34D069A2AD44.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An \"},{\"text\":\"Eye of Ender\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:ender_eye\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a casing and a tiny capacitor take 50,000 FE in the orb to become an \"},{\"text\":\"Ender Core\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:ender_core\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", the heart of every Ender Cell and Ender Gate.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5BE24994F4FBEE4D.title": "Ender Cell",
  "quest.5BE24994F4FBEE4D.quest_subtitle": "Your energy, on speed dial.",
  "quest.5BE24994F4FBEE4D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four obsidian, four iron nuggets and a core make a \"},{\"text\":\"Starter Ender Cell\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:ender_cell_starter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It stores into a channel of its owner's network: every cell on the same channel, in any dimension, shares one pool. Higher tiers open more channels, up to twelve.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Channels by tier: 1, 2, 3, 5, 7, 9 and 12. Transfer goes from 1,000 FE/t at Starter to 2,000,000 at Nitro."
  ],
  "quest.4788B27FF9395F24.title": "An empty channel holds nothing",
  "quest.4788B27FF9395F24.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A new channel has no capacity at all. Shift-click an Energy Cell or a Battery into the Ender Cell's screen: its capacity and its charge join the channel for good, and the item is used up.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7ADD644FC1D2480D.title": "Ender Gate",
  "quest.7ADD644FC1D2480D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four obsidian, four Starter cables and a core make four \"},{\"text\":\"Starter Ender Gates\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:ender_gate_starter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". A gate moves energy between the block it faces and a channel at cable speed, but it cannot add capacity: that is the cell's job.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.13DB6D5ADC0BCBF5.title": "One network per player",
  "quest.13DB6D5ADC0BCBF5.quest_desc": [
    "The network belongs to whoever placed the cell. Teammates each get twelve channels of their own; to share one pool, let one player place every cell."
  ],
  "quest.453C8E2B6048152C.title": "Bottomless",
  "quest.453C8E2B6048152C.quest_subtitle": "The last cell you will ever need.",
  "quest.453C8E2B6048152C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two \"},{\"text\":\"Engineering\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:luminosity_engineering\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and two \"},{\"text\":\"Habitation Luminosities\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:luminosity_habitation\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", two \"},{\"text\":\"Dragon Hearts\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"draconicevolution:dragon_heart\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", two \"},{\"text\":\"Blocks of Nitro Crystal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:nitro_crystal_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a Nitro cell made a \"},{\"text\":\"Creative Energy Cell\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:energy_cell_creative\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It never runs dry.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.420C8A1788FF12DA.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.5EC5E5C247F2E86B.title": "Steel for the common store",
  "quest.5EC5E5C247F2E86B.quest_subtitle": "Charged, stacked, delivered.",
  "quest.5EC5E5C247F2E86B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Thirty-two \"},{\"text\":\"Energized Steel\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"powah:steel_energized\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for the common store, once a day. Sixteen iron and sixteen gold through the orb: 160,000 FE, a short break for four Starter rods.\"}]"
  ],
  "image.3B692AE6B6ACCDCD.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Generators\",\"color\":\"#46E0C8\"}]",
  "image.17631C116C69B3EC.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Reactor\",\"color\":\"#46E0C8\"}]",
  "image.07EB07FE1ABA4CA3.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Cells and cables\",\"color\":\"#46E0C8\"}]",
  "image.3220A2F395196E55.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Wireless charging\",\"color\":\"#46E0C8\"}]",
  "image.2B3607317A39C68D.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Ender network\",\"color\":\"#46E0C8\"}]",
  "image.0A1F3A825FF749E8.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Powah!\",\"color\":\"#E9FFFB\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.5F3E35F38B152AE3.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"charge it and it changes\",\"color\":\"#7FE9D8\",\"font\":\"minecraft:alt\"}]",
  "image.43F1C98451EDD071.title": "Back to the Sun of Heliodor",
  "image.6D8B3DE584A7F0DD.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Starter\",\"color\":\"#A7A7A7\"}]",
  "image.765A38A533A62F45.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Basic\",\"color\":\"#A3AB9F\"}]",
  "image.583D33F518828337.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Hardened\",\"color\":\"#BBA993\"}]",
  "image.346477BC2327F9F1.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Blazing\",\"color\":\"#E4B040\"}]",
  "image.4D34D9656FE75476.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Niotic\",\"color\":\"#13EED2\"}]",
  "image.1494C53C57830ED9.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Spirited\",\"color\":\"#AFE241\"}]",
  "image.547C7804EA5AA9FF.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Nitro\",\"color\":\"#D7746C\"}]",
  "chapter.369BBB754F0B5AB0.title": "AE2 · Automation",
  "chapter.369BBB754F0B5AB0.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Patterns, providers, assemblers and CPUs, then the classic setups: pipes made of network, autostock, certus farms, press lines and crafts that copy themselves."
  ],
  "quest.1B1E6D801ECE853D.title": "Write it down",
  "quest.1B1E6D801ECE853D.quest_subtitle": "Recipes, but on paper.",
  "quest.1B1E6D801ECE853D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Crafting Terminal and an Engineering Processor make the \"},{\"text\":\"ME Pattern Encoding Terminal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:pattern_encoding_terminal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It turns \"},{\"text\":\"Blank Patterns\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:blank_pattern\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" into recipes the network can follow: crafting, smithing, stonecutting or processing.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.00455A2B03F16107.title": "Hands of the network",
  "quest.00455A2B03F16107.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An \"},{\"text\":\"ME Pattern Provider\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:pattern_provider\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" holds nine patterns and pushes each recipe's ingredients into the block beside it, a whole batch at once. Results can come back in through it, no import bus needed.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Blocking mode waits for the machine to empty before the next batch. A wrench makes it push to one face only.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.07B9805451689768.title": "An assembly line of one",
  "quest.07B9805451689768.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Molecular Assembler\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:molecular_assembler\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" beside a provider crafts any crafting, smithing or stonecutting pattern the provider sends, then pushes the result back. One provider feeds an assembler on every free face.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.138B171B22C0BA4F.title": "A brain per job",
  "quest.138B171B22C0BA4F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Crafting CPUs are solid boxes of \"},{\"text\":\"Crafting Storage\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:1k_crafting_storage\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", \"},{\"text\":\"Co-Processing Units\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:crafting_accelerator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", monitors and filler units. Storage holds a job's ingredients along the way. One CPU runs one job at a time, so build a second for two.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1809FBBFB9306A3C.title": "Any machine will do",
  "quest.1809FBBFB9306A3C.quest_desc": [
    "A processing pattern says: push these ingredients out and this result will come back, sooner or later. A provider on a furnace, a charger or a whole factory turns it into an autocraft. The result must enter the network; a chest a storage bus watches doesn't count."
  ],
  "quest.76C671D5C71577CE.title": "Keep it topped up",
  "quest.76C671D5C71577CE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An export bus with a \"},{\"text\":\"Crafting Card\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:crafting_card\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a redstone card, driven by a \"},{\"text\":\"Level Emitter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:level_emitter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", orders a craft whenever an item drops below your number. An interface with a crafting card does the same for a little of many things.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.72D6F95CFE0EF98A.title": "All patterns, one screen",
  "quest.72D6F95CFE0EF98A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"ME Pattern Access Terminal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:pattern_access_terminal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" reaches every provider on the network, so a buried wall of providers stays editable. Rows group by the block each provider faces, or by the name you gave it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4244C76541202F57.title": "Ask for it",
  "quest.4244C76541202F57.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"In a terminal, your Pick Block key on an item you can craft opens the order screen. Type a sum like 3*64, or =32 to craft just what brings the stock up to 32.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0A6B4C1993AB1855.title": "Smith and stonecutter",
  "quest.0A6B4C1993AB1855.quest_desc": [
    "The encoding terminal also has smithing and stonecutting tabs. Those patterns run in molecular assemblers exactly like crafting ones, so upgrades and stairs join the same queue."
  ],
  "quest.2B4DA79644B9D3BA.title": "One wood for everything",
  "quest.2B4DA79644B9D3BA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Pick one plank type and use it in every pattern. Substitutions sometimes work, but one wood avoids jams, and spreading patterns across providers lets recipes run side by side.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.52DF8AD0C5D66DE3.title": "Pour, don't bucket",
  "quest.52DF8AD0C5D66DE3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"With fluid substitution on in the encoding terminal, a crafting pattern uses stored fluid where the recipe asks for a bucket. In processing mode, right-click a slot with a bucket or tank to put in the fluid, not the container.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.763DE2302EE8A82C.title": "What it can't do",
  "quest.763DE2302EE8A82C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Autocrafting won't follow a recipe whose output feeds its own input, like duplicating a smithing template. A level emitter set to emit redstone to craft stands in: the network switches a machine on and waits for the item.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.14E3B17DFA82645B.title": "Three shapes of provider",
  "quest.14E3B17DFA82645B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A wrench makes a provider push to one face and not connect there; the flat one sits on a cable, several per block, and swaps back in a crafting grid. Lock crafting waits on redstone or on the last result; higher-priority patterns go first.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0EFA354C7281EA05.title": "One face, many machines",
  "quest.0EFA354C7281EA05.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Put a flat \"},{\"text\":\"ME Interface\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:cable_interface\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on a provider's face and run storage buses from its cable to several machines. The provider pushes straight through an untouched interface into those machines, one channel for all, and blocking mode watches their slots.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4747AD8A1C57C19F.title": "Charge on order",
  "quest.4747AD8A1C57C19F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A provider with a processing pattern pushes certus into a charger and powers it, since providers act like cable. An import bus and a storage bus on a \"},{\"text\":\"tiny subnet\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"744A5BF677ACDD7B\"}},{\"text\":\" pull the charged crystal back into the provider. Charged certus becomes one click.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.71265F1AF9C313ED.title": "A furnace on one channel",
  "quest.71265F1AF9C313ED.quest_subtitle": "Three jobs, one channel.",
  "quest.71265F1AF9C313ED.quest_desc": [
    "A wrenched provider pushes into an interface; behind it, two storage buses face the furnace: one filtered to coal on its side, one with an inverter card blacklisting coal on its top. A hopper underneath hands the results back to the provider."
  ],
  "quest.47C9318B67DD9160.title": "Bucket duty",
  "quest.47C9318B67DD9160.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A dispenser can fill or empty buckets for the network: the provider sends a bucket through an interface and storage bus, a comparator fires the dispenser and locks the provider, and an import bus returns the result. Often \"},{\"text\":\"fluid substitution\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"52DF8AD0C5D66DE3\"}},{\"text\":\" saves the trouble.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.251ED30DEC762DF0.title": "Into the water, automatically",
  "quest.251ED30DEC762DF0.quest_desc": [
    "An interface on the provider feeds a formation plane that drops items into water. An annihilation plane on another subnet can pick up only what a storage bus on the provider accepts, filtered to the results: fluix, or budding certus made from a quartz block."
  ],
  "quest.11850AB76CFBF829.title": "A press line",
  "quest.11850AB76CFBF829.quest_desc": [
    "Five inscribers: silicon, logic, calculation and engineering presses, and a fifth with none for the assembly, each with four acceleration cards. One processing pattern goes from raw materials to the finished processor, press left out; pipe subnets move the prints."
  ],
  "quest.4E7446E938F0E5C6.title": "Sides and buffers",
  "quest.4E7446E938F0E5C6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"An inscriber can be sided, top, bottom and middle slots by face, or take anything from anywhere. It can push results out on its own, and a small input buffer spreads material across a row of inscribers instead of filling the first.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.578DA8C68BB02757.title": "Checkerboard",
  "quest.578DA8C68BB02757.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Alternate pattern providers and molecular assemblers like a checkerboard, in groups of eight per cable, so each provider has several assemblers to fill. One energy cell handles the spikes; giant controller rings are only for the photo.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1CF304655DF2AE5D.title": "Copies of copies",
  "quest.1CF304655DF2AE5D.quest_subtitle": "Autocrafting can't read this recipe. Redstone can.",
  "quest.1CF304655DF2AE5D.quest_desc": [
    "A level emitter with a crafting card, set to emit redstone to craft, offers what autocrafting can't plan, like a template that copies itself. Its signal starts an import bus feeding an assembler that holds the pattern and one template; storage bus priorities send one copy back in."
  ],
  "quest.014961A14E511EE1.title": "Photocopier",
  "quest.014961A14E511EE1.quest_subtitle": "Nobody asked for eight.",
  "quest.014961A14E511EE1.quest_desc": [
    "Eight netherite upgrade templates. Either the loop works, or you raided a lot of bastions."
  ],
  "reward.74764C5761B95E78.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.7842C3280751AB4B.title": "More hands in the brain",
  "quest.7842C3280751AB4B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Each \"},{\"text\":\"Co-Processing Unit\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:crafting_accelerator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" lets a CPU hand out batches faster and run one more step in parallel, so a provider ringed with assemblers keeps them all busy. A \"},{\"text\":\"Crafting Monitor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:crafting_monitor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" shows the job.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.466544EB73FE8D1A.title": "Big brain, small brains",
  "quest.466544EB73FE8D1A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Build one or two big CPUs for long jobs and a few small ones for the rest. Each CPU can take orders from players, from automation or both, so a busy export bus never blocks your own request.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4DBFF0B5E4244D7A.title": "Bigger jobs",
  "quest.4DBFF0B5E4244D7A.quest_desc": [
    "A crafting unit plus a storage component makes crafting storage of that size. More storage holds jobs with more ingredients and steps; a second CPU lets two orders run at once."
  ],
  "quest.744A5BF677ACDD7B.title": "Pipes made of network",
  "quest.744A5BF677ACDD7B.quest_desc": [
    "On a subnet whose only storage is a storage bus, an import bus becomes a pipe: what it pulls lands in the bus's inventory. A filtered export bus pulls the other way. Fluids work alike; import straight to export does nothing, with no storage in between."
  ],
  "quest.7D75834F527E28A2.title": "Pipes that place and break",
  "quest.7D75834F527E28A2.quest_desc": [
    "An interface on a subnet whose only storage is a formation plane places or drops whatever you push in. An annihilation plane on a subnet whose only storage is a filtered storage bus breaks only what that bus accepts. Every plane farm is built from these two."
  ],
  "quest.74E322D8EEB3C491.title": "Ores, twice broken",
  "quest.74E322D8EEB3C491.quest_subtitle": "Fortune favours the plane.",
  "quest.74E322D8EEB3C491.quest_desc": [
    "An import bus with acceleration cards feeds silk-touched ore blocks to formation planes on one subnet; Fortune annihilation planes on another break them straight into a storage bus. Import buses spin up, so the array starts slow."
  ],
  "quest.00C127BFB9D02E5D.title": "Cobble on a leash",
  "quest.00C127BFB9D02E5D.quest_desc": [
    "Annihilation planes on a cobble generator store into an interface on the main network. A level emitter set below your limit drives a toggle bus on the subnet side of the quartz fiber: full stock cuts the planes' power, and only the subnet reboots."
  ],
  "quest.0943FBB7AA060C12.title": "Replace the budding block",
  "quest.0943FBB7AA060C12.quest_desc": [
    "A semi-auto farm is three subnets: a plane that harvests clusters, a Silk Touch plane that breaks the spent budding block once it's plain quartz, and an import bus with a formation plane that sets a fresh flawed one. You keep the input barrel stocked."
  ],
  "quest.1838603AE8DB6CC2.title": "Amethyst needs silk",
  "quest.1838603AE8DB6CC2.quest_desc": [
    "Unripe amethyst buds drop nothing, so a plain annihilation plane breaks them. With Silk Touch they drop themselves and can be filtered out; a formation plane sets the ripe clusters again, and a second plane breaks those into shards."
  ],
  "quest.758E076C087191A4.title": "The farm that feeds itself",
  "quest.758E076C087191A4.quest_subtitle": "Certus in, more certus out.",
  "quest.758E076C087191A4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Swap the input barrel for an interface that keeps one flawed budding block, with a crafting card. The spent blocks go back through it to \"},{\"text\":\"water automation\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"251ED30DEC762DF0\"}},{\"text\":\", which rebuilds budding blocks from charged certus. Nothing left to refill.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5C7574B554959492.title": "One item, a big number",
  "quest.5C7574B554959492.quest_desc": [
    "Filter an export bus to the item, give it a crafting card and a redstone card, set it active with signal and told not to use stocked items. A level emitter below your amount drives it, and an interface behind it sends each craft home."
  ],
  "task.56107C96C24089CF.title": "Four interfaces, block or flat",
  "quest.31B3EBAC5A3A6049.title": "A little of many things",
  "quest.31B3EBAC5A3A6049.quest_desc": [
    "Interfaces with crafting cards keep a set amount of each item inside and order more when short. Storage buses on them, set to extract only, let the network use that stock. Four of each fill the eight channels of one cable."
  ],
  "quest.7D2E1BA757617390.title": "Craft on the move",
  "quest.7D2E1BA757617390.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A crafting table and a calculation processor turn a wireless terminal into a \"},{\"text\":\"Wireless Crafting Terminal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:wireless_crafting_terminal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". AE2WTLib adds restocking: the stack in your hand refills from the network as you use it, and \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.ae2.ae2wtlib_restock\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" toggles it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1500666091F8CEB4.title": "Two crafting modes",
  "quest.1500666091F8CEB4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"With a crafting card, a level emitter can emit while its item is being crafted, to wake a hungry machine only then, or emit to craft: a pattern with no ingredients that runs an infinite farm until the item arrives. Keep no real pattern for it.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.69B44B4E78956332.title": "Four 4k or 16k item cells",
  "quest.57FE3FAF8DF1578B.title": "Three kinds of storage",
  "quest.57FE3FAF8DF1578B.quest_desc": [
    "General: a few drives of 4k or 16k cells at priority 0. Bulk: big cells partitioned to cobble or iron, with equal distribution, in higher-priority drives. Local: a farm's own subnet. Items drift to their place as they come and go; an IO port shuffles the rest."
  ],
  "quest.0D289F0A1283706E.title": "A farm's own storage",
  "quest.0D289F0A1283706E.quest_desc": [
    "Give a farm a subnet with its own drive of partitioned cells and an interface. A storage bus on that interface from the main network, at high priority, reads the drive through one channel, and nothing spills into your main cells."
  ],
  "quest.7C53A1CA301454B8.title": "Empty a cell into a chest",
  "quest.7C53A1CA301454B8.quest_desc": [
    "An IO port with three acceleration cards and a storage bus on a subnet: sending to the network, it dumps a cell into the chest, drawers or backpack the bus faces; flipped, it fills the cell from them. An energy cell covers the power spikes."
  ],
  "quest.36A1DD7F3539AEA8.title": "The base builds itself",
  "quest.36A1DD7F3539AEA8.quest_subtitle": "You just point.",
  "quest.36A1DD7F3539AEA8.quest_desc": [
    "Eight pattern providers and sixteen co-processors on one network: enough hands and brains that every order finishes while you do something else.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "{image:ae2:textures/block/pattern_provider.png width:48 height:48 align:center}",
    "",
    "Keep providers in groups of eight per cable, spread patterns so recipes run side by side, and let crafting cards top up the basics. From here the network works, and you choose what it works on."
  ],
  "quest.19D0DEF2F939DB6A.title": "Every light on",
  "quest.19D0DEF2F939DB6A.quest_subtitle": "The smart cables have never been this bright.",
  "quest.19D0DEF2F939DB6A.quest_desc": [
    "You ran 2048 channels on one network. At this size the network is the base, and the base is one machine."
  ],
  "reward.6828076062258DEF.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.606BCC0D4F37EDF5.title": "Kept in stock",
  "quest.606BCC0D4F37EDF5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The requesters kept the pantry full long after the cooks stopped coming. Machines remember what people forget. —T.\",\"italic\":true}]"
  ],
  "quest.72088CBB6598A2BA.title": "Chip order",
  "quest.72088CBB6598A2BA.quest_subtitle": "Sixteen of each, please.",
  "quest.72088CBB6598A2BA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Sixteen \"},{\"text\":\"Calculation Processors\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:calculation_processor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and sixteen \"},{\"text\":\"Engineering Processors\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:engineering_processor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for the common store, once a day. With a processing pattern per chip, this is one click.\"}]"
  ],
  "image.6156FC19D21F7405.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Pattern craft\",\"color\":\"#E2A3E3\"}]",
  "image.2952B7F3AF6B6D03.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Provider setups\",\"color\":\"#E2A3E3\"}]",
  "image.209FDB8945F8A7BE.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Assemblers at scale\",\"color\":\"#E2A3E3\"}]",
  "image.37D6B8876E354000.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Crafting CPUs\",\"color\":\"#E2A3E3\"}]",
  "image.0BA8F35C8FA288BF.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Pipes and planes\",\"color\":\"#E2A3E3\"}]",
  "image.6D33168F87432F03.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Stock and storage\",\"color\":\"#E2A3E3\"}]",
  "image.570042D98880376A.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"AE2 · Automation\",\"color\":\"#E2A3E3\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.6B39453F70354E2F.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"six faces, one provider\",\"color\":\"#7DA9D2\",\"font\":\"minecraft:uniform\"}]",
  "image.509AC6DD59D34CB6.title": "Back to AE2 · Network",
  "image.0585BA9EBFD8536E.title": "On to AE2 · Addons",
  "chapter.1E24729503A1C81A.title": "Applied Energistics 2 · Network",
  "chapter.1E24729503A1C81A.chapter_subtitle": [
    "From a crater to a network that thinks in channels: certus, processors, cells, the controller and the quantum bridge."
  ],
  "task.7DB42B1FB53B2C4D.title": "Stand in a meteorite crater",
  "quest.1E4E23988E9781B3.title": "Fallen sky",
  "quest.1E4E23988E9781B3.quest_subtitle": "Special delivery from nowhere.",
  "quest.1E4E23988E9781B3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Meteorites leave big craters of \"},{\"text\":\"Sky Stone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:sky_stone_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Dig to the centre: \"},{\"text\":\"Certus Quartz Clusters\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:quartz_cluster\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and budding certus line the way, and a \"},{\"text\":\"Mysterious Cube\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:mysterious_cube\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" waits at the core.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"No crater in sight? The \"},{\"text\":\"Charger\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"2452FCA6FC4CFE2D\"}},{\"text\":\" makes a compass that points at the nearest cube.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0D426B64A4DECFB2.title": "Certus by the handful",
  "quest.0D426B64A4DECFB2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A grown \"},{\"text\":\"Certus Quartz Cluster\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:quartz_cluster\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" drops four \"},{\"text\":\"Certus Quartz Crystals\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:certus_quartz_crystal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", more with Fortune; a bud still growing drops a single dust. Take every cluster on the way down.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2452FCA6FC4CFE2D.title": "Crank it up",
  "quest.2452FCA6FC4CFE2D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Iron and copper make a \"},{\"text\":\"Charger\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:charger\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". With no power yet, put a \"},{\"text\":\"Wooden Crank\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:crank\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on its top or bottom and turn it. It charges \"},{\"text\":\"Certus Quartz Crystals\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:certus_quartz_crystal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and turns a compass into a \"},{\"text\":\"Meteorite Compass\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:meteorite_compass\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.553205EE6C9D1141.title": "Into the water",
  "quest.553205EE6C9D1141.quest_subtitle": "Alchemy, AE2 style.",
  "quest.553205EE6C9D1141.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Drop a \"},{\"text\":\"Charged Certus Quartz Crystal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:charged_certus_quartz_crystal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a redstone dust and a nether quartz into water: two \"},{\"text\":\"Fluix Crystals\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:fluix_crystal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Cables, energy cells and half the network run on fluix.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.25592EB7781F3A38.title": "The four presses",
  "quest.25592EB7781F3A38.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Break the \"},{\"text\":\"Mysterious Cube\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:mysterious_cube\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" without Silk Touch: out come the Silicon, Logic, Calculation and Engineering presses. Printing \"},{\"text\":\"never uses them up\",\"color\":\"#9BE08A\"},{\"text\":\", so one set lasts a lifetime.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.678B55C9B3908621.title": "Print shop",
  "quest.678B55C9B3908621.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Iron, copper and a piston make the \"},{\"text\":\"Inscriber\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:inscriber\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". A press goes in the top slot and the material in the middle; with no press, a crystal is ground into dust.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"It's sided: items fed from the top or bottom land in those slots, from the sides in the middle. A wrench turns it to face your pipes.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7E9BCB0C47A31EDC.title": "Silicon, then print",
  "quest.7E9BCB0C47A31EDC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Grind certus into \"},{\"text\":\"Certus Quartz Dust\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:certus_quartz_dust\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and smelt it: \"},{\"text\":\"Silicon\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:silicon\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". With the Silicon Press on top, the inscriber prints it into \"},{\"text\":\"Printed Silicon\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:printed_silicon\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", the base of every processor.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4F1E7EE66CB33834.title": "Three kinds of brain",
  "quest.4F1E7EE66CB33834.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Print gold with the Logic press, a certus crystal with Calculation, a diamond with Engineering. Press each print with redstone and \"},{\"text\":\"Printed Silicon\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:printed_silicon\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": \"},{\"text\":\"Logic\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:logic_processor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", \"},{\"text\":\"Calculation\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:calculation_processor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and \"},{\"text\":\"Engineering Processors\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:engineering_processor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.41D20416314D72EE.title": "Items become data",
  "quest.41D20416314D72EE.quest_subtitle": "ME: Matter Energy.",
  "quest.41D20416314D72EE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An \"},{\"text\":\"ME Drive\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:drive\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" holds ten storage cells, an \"},{\"text\":\"ME Terminal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:terminal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" searches them all at once and an \"},{\"text\":\"Energy Acceptor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:energy_acceptor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" turns 2 FE into 1 \"},{\"text\":\"AE\",\"color\":\"#D8C8FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_text\",\"contents\":\"AE2's own energy. It never converts back.\"}},{\"text\":\". Join them with cable and the wall of chests is history.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Terminals are cable parts: put the cable down first, then the terminal on it, facing you.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1A01B2BACCF19D90.title": "Craft from storage",
  "quest.1A01B2BACCF19D90.quest_subtitle": "A bigger table. Much bigger.",
  "quest.1A01B2BACCF19D90.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A terminal, a crafting table and a \"},{\"text\":\"Calculation Processor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:calculation_processor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": the \"},{\"text\":\"ME Crafting Terminal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:crafting_terminal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Its grid refills itself from the network, so shift-click the result with care.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5A24342389F499DB.title": "Storage cells",
  "quest.5A24342389F499DB.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The component sets the size: a \"},{\"text\":\"1k Component\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:cell_component_1k\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" takes a Logic Processor, and each tier after it takes three of the one before and a Calculation Processor. In an \"},{\"text\":\"ME Item Cell Housing\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:item_cell_housing\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" it becomes a cell; 4k is the sweet spot to start.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7D1165B36B6C5780.title": "Smooth sky",
  "quest.7D1165B36B6C5780.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Crater \"},{\"text\":\"Sky Stone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:sky_stone_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" smelts into \"},{\"text\":\"Sky Stone Block\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:smooth_sky_stone_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; the controller takes four. Ground in the inscriber, sky stone becomes the dust that 256k cells need.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2325AF6584F70E3F.title": "The controller's core",
  "quest.2325AF6584F70E3F.quest_subtitle": "Made in Heliodor.",
  "quest.2325AF6584F70E3F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Here the controller's heart is a \"},{\"text\":\"Routing Matrix\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:routing_matrix\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": two \"},{\"text\":\"Logic Processors\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:logic_processor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a PneumaticCraft circuit board, two Palis crystals and a calibration frame. The first one belongs to \"},{\"text\":\"A Shared Language\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"17BBD680007901AB\"}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.00CC66AACA668D42.title": "Switchboard",
  "quest.00CC66AACA668D42.quest_subtitle": "Now it thinks in channels.",
  "quest.00CC66AACA668D42.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four \"},{\"text\":\"Sky Stone Blocks\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:smooth_sky_stone_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", four \"},{\"text\":\"Fluix Crystals\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:fluix_crystal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and the matrix make an \"},{\"text\":\"ME Controller\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:controller\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Without one, a network runs eight channel-using devices at most; with it, every face gives out \"},{\"text\":\"32 channels\",\"color\":\"#E2A3E3\"},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0274EB35E79D9821.title": "Trunk line",
  "quest.0274EB35E79D9821.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four \"},{\"text\":\"Covered Cables\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:fluix_covered_cable\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make one dense cable; redstone and glowstone make it smart: \"},{\"text\":\"ME Dense Smart Cable\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:fluix_smart_dense_cable\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It carries 32 channels, but buses and terminals won't mount on it: step down to normal cable first.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.561A39CD67283B8C.title": "Point to point",
  "quest.561A39CD67283B8C.quest_subtitle": "A portal for channels.",
  "quest.561A39CD67283B8C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Link two \"},{\"text\":\"ME P2P Tunnels\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:me_p2p_tunnel\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" with a Memory Card: sneak-click the input, click the output. Each end takes one channel and the pair carries up to 32 through one thin cable; on a subnet of their own, the main network doesn't even pay those two.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.506E30514D0C27C8.title": "Crush it down",
  "quest.506E30514D0C27C8.quest_subtitle": "Everything, but smaller.",
  "quest.506E30514D0C27C8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Matter Condenser\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:condenser\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" deletes whatever enters, or with a storage component inside packs it: 256 items into a \"},{\"text\":\"Matter Ball\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:matter_ball\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", 256,000 into a \"},{\"text\":\"Singularity\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:singularity\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Cobblestone works fine.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.654DF546A8DF23AC.title": "Spooky pair",
  "quest.654DF546A8DF23AC.quest_subtitle": "Action at a distance, sold in pairs.",
  "quest.654DF546A8DF23AC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Blow up a \"},{\"text\":\"Singularity\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:singularity\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" next to \"},{\"text\":\"Ender Dust\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:ender_dust\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" or an ender pearl: two \"},{\"text\":\"Quantum Entangled Singularities\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:quantum_entangled_singularity\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", linked for good. A \"},{\"text\":\"Tiny TNT\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:tiny_tnt\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" or even a creeper does the job.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Pairs look identical: name them in an anvil.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.03DD4E526E89D121.title": "Across any distance",
  "quest.03DD4E526E89D121.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight \"},{\"text\":\"ME Quantum Rings\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:quantum_ring\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" around an \"},{\"text\":\"ME Quantum Link Chamber\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:quantum_link\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", one singularity of the pair in each bridge: a wireless dense cable of 32 channels, across any distance and between dimensions. Both ends must stay chunkloaded.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Only the four rings beside the chamber take cables.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.25950187AE46C6D2.title": "Use 128 channels on one network",
  "quest.42DAD943EBAF99A3.title": "A real network",
  "quest.42DAD943EBAF99A3.quest_subtitle": "Tree-shaped, loop-free, lit up.",
  "quest.42DAD943EBAF99A3.quest_desc": [
    "One hundred and twenty-eight channel-using devices on a single network. Grow it like a tree: dense cable out of the controller, normal cable off the dense, devices in groups of eight or fewer.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "{image:ae2:textures/block/controller_powered.png width:48 height:48 align:center}",
    "",
    "Smart cables light every channel along its path; a device left dark has none. Loops and ambiguous routes are what break big networks, so give every channel exactly one way home."
  ],
  "quest.781A245B828BE5F8.title": "Wrench and knife",
  "quest.781A245B828BE5F8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Certus Quartz Wrench\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:certus_quartz_wrench\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" rotates AE2 machines and, sneaking, takes them apart or pulls one part off a cable. The \"},{\"text\":\"Certus Quartz Cutting Knife\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:certus_quartz_cutting_knife\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" carves cable anchors and name presses out of metal.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.266156A67AA30F44.title": "Look at a Flawless Budding Certus",
  "quest.2BF325869777C6A1.title": "Look, don't mine",
  "quest.2BF325869777C6A1.quest_subtitle": "The goose with the golden eggs.",
  "quest.2BF325869777C6A1.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Flawless Budding Certus Quartz\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:flawless_budding_quartz\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" grows certus forever and never wears out. A pickaxe knocks it down a tier \"},{\"text\":\"even with Silk Touch\",\"color\":\"#FF8C7A\"},{\"text\":\", and only a lucky \"},{\"text\":\"Crystal Fixer\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"31EE3A93EA52F51E\"}},{\"text\":\" undoes that. Build the farm around it, right where it is.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3CCEDB12D4CFF6FC.title": "A villager for certus",
  "quest.3CCEDB12D4CFF6FC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A villager can take a \"},{\"text\":\"Charger\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:charger\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" as its workstation and become a Fluix Researcher: certus, fluix, sky stone and, at Expert level, any processor press for ten emeralds. Lost presses aren't lost.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.62D0DD312E062AAB.title": "Budding by hand",
  "quest.62D0DD312E062AAB.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Certus Quartz Block\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:quartz_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a charged crystal thrown in water make a \"},{\"translate\":\"block.ae2.damaged_budding_quartz\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\"},{\"text\":\"; the same trick lifts it to chipped, then flawed. These wear out as they grow, and no water trick makes a flawless one.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.750B81F61BFEFF77.title": "Grow faster",
  "quest.750B81F61BFEFF77.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Growth Accelerator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:growth_accelerator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" beside a budding block adds random ticks: in theory about ninety times the growth, and they stack. Power it through its top or bottom, by cable or with a crank.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4BFC33B61517567A.title": "Lucky tools",
  "quest.4BFC33B61517567A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Paper and a fluix crystal make a \"},{\"text\":\"Fluix Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:fluix_upgrade_smithing_template\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; with a Fluix Block, a smithing table turns quartz tools into fluix. Three times iron's durability, and every one works as if it had Fortune or Looting I.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0A68196F99C6CA85.title": "Harvest on its own",
  "quest.0A68196F99C6CA85.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Put an \"},{\"text\":\"ME Annihilation Plane\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:annihilation_plane\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on a subnet whose only storage is a Storage Bus filtered to certus crystals. It breaks only grown clusters: a bud still growing would drop dust, and the subnet has nowhere to keep it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4F0420DF05040B01.title": "A spare press",
  "quest.4F0420DF05040B01.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A press on top and an iron block in the middle of the \"},{\"text\":\"Inscriber\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:inscriber\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": out comes a copy. Make spares before an addon recipe eats one, and a second production line needs its own set.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6A3D854777CEC40E.title": "Labels, printed",
  "quest.6A3D854777CEC40E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Right-click a cutting knife, put in an ingot and type a name: an \"},{\"text\":\"Inscriber Name Press\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:name_press\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". In the inscriber it names items like an anvil, which tells pattern providers apart at a glance.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7B5BC57E27EAC057.title": "Glass with a spine",
  "quest.7B5BC57E27EAC057.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Five quartz dusts and four glass make four \"},{\"text\":\"Quartz Glass\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:quartz_glass\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Energy acceptors, cells, patterns and panels all ask for it, so grind a stack of certus early.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.366FDC5BA5970A75.title": "Presses on autopilot",
  "quest.366FDC5BA5970A75.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"With the presses already inside a row of inscribers, one processing pattern can go straight from gold, silicon and redstone to a finished processor. Leave the press out of the pattern: it never moves.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4534F4AB8BC41656.title": "Glass, covered, smart",
  "quest.4534F4AB8BC41656.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Quartz Fiber\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:quartz_fiber\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and two fluix make four \"},{\"text\":\"ME Glass Cables\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:fluix_glass_cable\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; wool covers them. Redstone and glowstone make \"},{\"text\":\"ME Smart Cable\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:fluix_smart_cable\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", which lights up every channel it carries.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.30F0572B87CBE80E.title": "Eight and thirty-two",
  "quest.30F0572B87CBE80E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Normal cable and most full blocks carry \"},{\"text\":\"8\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\" channels; dense cable carries \"},{\"text\":\"32\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\". Channels take the shortest path to the controller, and a network without one is capped at 8 devices in all. Cable colour only keeps neighbours apart.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6A516FC607869EC3.title": "Buffer the surges",
  "quest.6A516FC607869EC3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Dump a full inventory into a small network and it browns out: in one tick it can't spend more AE than it holds. An \"},{\"text\":\"Energy Cell\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:energy_cell\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" stores 200k AE and ends that for most bases.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6EA8BE74D14DF3F0.title": "Deep reserves",
  "quest.6EA8BE74D14DF3F0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight Energy Cells around a Calculation Processor: a \"},{\"text\":\"Dense Energy Cell\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:dense_energy_cell\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", 1.6M AE. Every wireless terminal carries one, and spatial storage can drain several in a single tick.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.295BD482DA159A89.title": "Low battery",
  "quest.295BD482DA159A89.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A redstone torch, a charged certus crystal and a calculation processor make an \"},{\"text\":\"ME Energy Level Emitter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:energy_level_emitter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It reads the energy stored in the network, not items: start a generator when the cells run low and stop it when they're full.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.28206E7B1C55EE71.title": "Burn it",
  "quest.28206E7B1C55EE71.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Vibration Chamber\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:vibration_chamber\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" burns furnace fuel into 40 AE/t. It slows down when the network is full but never quite stops; acceleration and energy cards push it harder.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.052B0394B6FD133F.title": "Free hum",
  "quest.052B0394B6FD133F.quest_subtitle": "Crystals that won't stop singing.",
  "quest.052B0394B6FD133F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Crystal Resonance Generator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:crystal_resonance_generator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" makes 20 AE/t from nothing, forever. Its vibrations clash: only one works per network, and they even travel through quartz fiber.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3A3EA4FC7C2D730A.title": "A network in a box",
  "quest.3A3EA4FC7C2D730A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An \"},{\"text\":\"ME Chest\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:chest\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" is a drive, a terminal and an acceptor for a single cell. Its screen sees only that cell, which makes it handy for checking one cell or filling it by hand.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6C6B2132C25EF1C1.title": "Partition",
  "quest.6C6B2132C25EF1C1.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Cell Workbench\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:cell_workbench\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" filters a cell to chosen items and fits its cards: inverter, fuzzy, equal distribution, overflow destruction. It also sets up \"},{\"text\":\"View Cells\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:view_cell\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", which make a terminal show only what they list.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7DB4E2ABA3A97772.title": "Bigger, not wider",
  "quest.7DB4E2ABA3A97772.quest_desc": [
    "16k, 64k and 256k components each hold four times the last and cost three of it. Types stay at 63, so big cells suit bulk; the 256k needs sky stone dust. A cell crafted with a bigger component upgrades in place, contents and all."
  ],
  "quest.0CCB1D1149EDA3AF.title": "Pocket network",
  "quest.0CCB1D1149EDA3AF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A chest, a 1k component, an energy cell and a housing: a \"},{\"text\":\"1k Portable Item Cell\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:portable_item_cell_1k\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a tiny ME chest you carry. Half the bytes of a normal cell; recharge it in a Charger.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.ae2.portable_item_cell\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" opens it from anywhere in your inventory.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0619ED8CAF98334B.title": "Cell shuffle",
  "quest.0619ED8CAF98334B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An \"},{\"text\":\"ME IO Port\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:io_port\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" empties a cell into the network or fills it from the network, fast, then moves it to the output slots. Acceleration cards speed it up; a redstone card decides when it runs.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5C492F73DAFDF9BB.title": "Who fills first",
  "quest.5C492F73DAFDF9BB.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Items enter the highest-priority storage first and leave from the lowest. A partitioned cell counts as already holding its items, so at equal priority it catches them before a general one does.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3A0E08425838B993.title": "Liquid assets",
  "quest.3A0E08425838B993.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Fluid cells use their own copper housing and the same components, like the \"},{\"text\":\"4k ME Fluid Storage Cell\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:fluid_storage_cell_4k\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Each holds only five fluids, eight buckets to the byte, and the terminal fills and empties buckets for you.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.08DC49D03272CE88.title": "Bytes and types",
  "quest.08DC49D03272CE88.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A cell holds 63 types and counts items in bits: eight to the byte, however they stack. Each type costs bytes up front, so one type fills a cell twice as far as 63. Keep mob loot out: every enchant and scratch is a new type.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.20839BBDFD7238C6.title": "Controller shapes",
  "quest.20839BBDFD7238C6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Controller blocks join into one controller up to 7×7×7, and a network holds only one. Each block may touch others along a single axis; break a rule and the blocks turn red. More blocks, more faces, 32 channels each.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.15E05A2C62807849.title": "Diagnose",
  "quest.15E05A2C62807849.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Right-click any part of a network with a \"},{\"text\":\"Network Tool\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:network_tool\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": channels in use, energy stored and flowing, every device on it. It also keeps nine upgrade cards at hand for any AE2 screen.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5C0794823234A9A0.title": "Copy, paste",
  "quest.5C0794823234A9A0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Sneak-click a device with a \"},{\"text\":\"Memory Card\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:memory_card\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" to copy its settings, then click others to paste them, upgrade cards included. P2P tunnels are linked the same way.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7D2AC8CDC5583A36.title": "Tidy cables",
  "quest.7D2AC8CDC5583A36.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The cutting knife turns metal into \"},{\"text\":\"Cable Anchors\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:cable_anchor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", which block connections on their side and double as ladders. Four around a block make a \"},{\"text\":\"Cable Facade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:facade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" of it; holding a Network Tool hides facades.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.28DD1C4B9E6AE285.title": "Flat parts",
  "quest.28DD1C4B9E6AE285.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Interfaces and pattern providers turn flat in a crafting grid and back. Flat ones sit on a cable, several per block, and don't connect networks through their face: the easy border for a subnet. Sneak-use a wrench to pull off a single part.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2B3B676137DDEE49.title": "In and out",
  "quest.2B3B676137DDEE49.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An \"},{\"text\":\"ME Import Bus\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:import_bus\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" pulls from the inventory it faces into the network; an \"},{\"text\":\"ME Export Bus\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:export_bus\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" pushes out only what its filter names. One on top of a furnace and one below is the classic first job.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.68FFB486CB3B69CD.title": "Keep some handy",
  "quest.68FFB486CB3B69CD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An \"},{\"text\":\"ME Interface\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:interface\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" is a chest and multi-tank that keeps itself stocked from the network with whatever you set, up to nine stacks a tick, and sends everything else back.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2A166286E859AD3A.title": "Keep the chest monster",
  "quest.2A166286E859AD3A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An \"},{\"text\":\"ME Storage Bus\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:storage_bus\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" turns the inventory it touches into network storage. Drawers and barrels work well; huge unoptimised chests hurt performance.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6AEA3FE6522F0D9D.title": "Count and signal",
  "quest.6AEA3FE6522F0D9D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An \"},{\"text\":\"ME Level Emitter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:level_emitter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" gives redstone when an item in storage goes above or below the amount you set. It needs no channel: turn a farm off when the stock is full.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.205E9D78FDDFAAD4.title": "Cards up the sleeve",
  "quest.205E9D78FDDFAAD4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Capacity Cards\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:capacity_card\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" add filter slots; \"},{\"text\":\"Acceleration Cards\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:speed_card\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" move more per operation, from 1 item to 8, 32, 64 and 96. Redstone cards add control, fuzzy ones ignore damage and data, inverters flip a filter.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.557D536A014843BA.title": "Cards for cells",
  "quest.557D536A014843BA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two cards go on cells, in the cell workbench. An \"},{\"text\":\"Equal Distribution Card\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:equal_distribution_card\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" splits a partitioned cell evenly between its items; an \"},{\"text\":\"Overflow Destruction Card\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:void_card\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" deletes what arrives once the cell, or that item's share, is full.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0E90C390A27A9DAA.title": "Place and break",
  "quest.0E90C390A27A9DAA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"ME Formation Plane\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:formation_plane\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" places blocks or drops items whenever the network stores into it. Its twin, the annihilation plane, breaks what's in front and picks up what touches it, but only what its network can store.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3F94A663B87E9DD0.title": "Networkception",
  "quest.3F94A663B87E9DD0.quest_subtitle": "A network looking into a network.",
  "quest.3F94A663B87E9DD0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"You put a \"},{\"text\":\"Storage Bus\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:storage_bus\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on an \"},{\"text\":\"Interface\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:interface\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". An unconfigured interface shows its whole network to the bus: one network reading another through a single channel.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.5DB0CCB1E713BBCF.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.48679B5725498433.title": "Screens on the wall",
  "quest.48679B5725498433.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An \"},{\"text\":\"ME Storage Monitor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:storage_monitor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" shows one item and its count, no channel needed. The \"},{\"text\":\"ME Conversion Monitor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:conversion_monitor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" also takes and gives it: a click pulls a stack, or asks for a craft when there's none.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5EA9CC6DAA389B42.title": "Plane tricks",
  "quest.5EA9CC6DAA389B42.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Annihilation planes take pickaxe enchantments: Fortune multiplies ore drops, Silk Touch keeps blocks whole. Face one up at the very top of the world and it gathers sky stone dust from nothing.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7A072CDE16F967DE.title": "Tunnels for everything",
  "quest.7A072CDE16F967DE.quest_desc": [
    "Right-click a placed P2P tunnel to retune it: a chest or hopper for items, a bucket for fluids, redstone for signals, a charged item for energy, which pays a 2.5% toll. ME tunnels can't run through other ME tunnels."
  ],
  "quest.2448DB828D1B6AA2.title": "Switches and fibres",
  "quest.2448DB828D1B6AA2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Quartz Fiber\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:quartz_fiber\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" shares power between two networks without joining them. An \"},{\"text\":\"ME Toggle Bus\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:toggle_bus\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" connects or cuts a stretch of cable by redstone; each flip may reboot the network.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.35989E0DF590D59B.title": "Networks inside networks",
  "quest.35989E0DF590D59B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A subnet is just a separate network. An import bus and a storage bus on their own little network make an item pipe the main network can't raid. Quartz fiber powers it without joining the two.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.192520C87BEEA2AC.title": "Cut the cord",
  "quest.192520C87BEEA2AC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An \"},{\"text\":\"ME Wireless Access Point\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:wireless_access_point\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" takes one channel and reaches 16 blocks. \"},{\"text\":\"Wireless Boosters\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:wireless_booster\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" stretch it: sixteen of them reach 80 blocks, at a steeper power cost.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4834765FCCB69F7C.title": "Storage in your pocket",
  "quest.4834765FCCB69F7C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A receiver, a terminal and a dense energy cell: a \"},{\"text\":\"Wireless Terminal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:wireless_terminal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Put it in the access point's top-right slot to link it; \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.ae2.wireless_terminal\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" opens it from your inventory while in range.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Its bigger siblings wait in \"},{\"text\":\"AE2 · Automation\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"369BBB754F0B5AB0\"}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0EE122952979DDEA.title": "AE2 armoury",
  "quest.0EE122952979DDEA.quest_subtitle": "Recoil not included.",
  "quest.0EE122952979DDEA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Matter Cannon\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:matter_cannon\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" fires small items for 1600 AE a shot: a gold nugget hits for 10, a matter ball for 2. The \"},{\"text\":\"Charged Staff\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:charged_staff\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" hits for 6 on 300 AE. Both recharge in a Charger.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6243BBEF57E88098.title": "Hot and cold",
  "quest.6243BBEF57E88098.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Right-click with an \"},{\"text\":\"Entropy Manipulator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:entropy_manipulator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" to heat, sneak-click to cool: water freezes or boils away, lava turns to obsidian, logs to charcoal and cobble to stone, in place. Anything else, it lights like flint and steel.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.14BA0FD3A0D11791.title": "Paint job",
  "quest.14BA0FD3A0D11791.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Color Applicator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:color_applicator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" paints cables, wool, glass and concrete in place, with dyes or paintballs: eight matter balls around a dye. A snowball cleans a cable back to fluix.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.72CD6E51F5D7FF61.title": "Replica",
  "quest.72CD6E51F5D7FF61.quest_subtitle": "The mystery is gone. The cube remains.",
  "quest.72CD6E51F5D7FF61.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"You spent a controller and a full set of presses on four \"},{\"text\":\"Not So Mysterious Cubes\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:not_so_mysterious_cube\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". They look exactly like the real one. That was the point, apparently.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.6D60642AE728EA53.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.4FC22C336625A9ED.title": "Cut and paste the world",
  "quest.4FC22C336625A9ED.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Spatial pylons outline a box; a \"},{\"text\":\"Spatial IO Port\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:spatial_io_port\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" swaps what's inside with a pocket dimension on a redstone pulse. It moves what no pickaxe can, like a flawless budding block. \"},{\"text\":\"Anyone inside travels too.\",\"color\":\"#FF8C7A\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.583D0D85AD2ED560.title": "Pocket rooms",
  "quest.583D0D85AD2ED560.quest_desc": [
    "Spatial cells hold 2³, 16³ or 128³ of space, and each size's component takes four of the one before. Once used, a cell keeps that size for good: make a new cell for a new shape."
  ],
  "quest.53D836F6AAEBB9D0.title": "Keep it loaded",
  "quest.53D836F6AAEBB9D0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Spatial Anchor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:spatial_anchor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" forceloads every chunk its network touches, and the load crosses quantum bridges within a dimension. It draws 80 AE/t plus more for each chunk it holds.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.08216441231006A2.title": "Inside the box",
  "quest.08216441231006A2.quest_subtitle": "Please keep your arms inside the cell.",
  "quest.08216441231006A2.quest_desc": [
    "You got stored in a spatial cell. It's dark in there, featureless, and the only way out is the way you came in. Hope someone keeps the cell."
  ],
  "reward.304FD3098CE72A16.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.4B78FA1CA4E7379E.title": "The manual is in the item",
  "quest.4B78FA1CA4E7379E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Hover any AE2 item and hold \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.guideme.guide\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\": its guide page opens, with 3D scenes you can turn. The pack's AE2 addons have pages there too.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3424E99A540DE013.title": "Certus harvest",
  "quest.3424E99A540DE013.quest_subtitle": "The farm does the lifting.",
  "quest.3424E99A540DE013.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Sixty-four \"},{\"text\":\"Certus Quartz Crystals\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:certus_quartz_crystal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for the common store, once a day. A flawless bud with accelerators and a plane pays this while you sleep.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.59CE9179920C376A.title": "Creative AE2",
  "quest.59CE9179920C376A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Creative Energy Cell\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:creative_energy_cell\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" costs two Logistics and two Engineering Luminosities, two dragon hearts, two singularities and a MEGA superdense cell, from Solsticio in act VI. The creative storage cell can't be crafted.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.31EEBC30436CF305.title": "Scribbled on a press",
  "quest.31EEBC30436CF305.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The sky kept dropping the same four presses. I stopped asking who made them and started printing. —T.\",\"italic\":true}]"
  ],
  "image.1259721E33EF044F.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Certus and fluix\",\"color\":\"#E2A3E3\"}]",
  "image.34D816A20B0EDDC5.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Circuits\",\"color\":\"#E2A3E3\"}]",
  "image.119E9875CE9FEBD3.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Power and cable\",\"color\":\"#E2A3E3\"}]",
  "image.2F5A80F260575588.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Storage\",\"color\":\"#E2A3E3\"}]",
  "image.7A59EA97CB3C9F57.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Controller and tools\",\"color\":\"#E2A3E3\"}]",
  "image.3F64E1E14529E721.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Buses and interfaces\",\"color\":\"#E2A3E3\"}]",
  "image.3C4997ABDA3AFD9F.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Tunnels, subnets, wireless\",\"color\":\"#E2A3E3\"}]",
  "image.174964B976C97517.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Matter and odd tools\",\"color\":\"#E2A3E3\"}]",
  "image.2C2A02FF2D875EA7.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Spatial IO\",\"color\":\"#E2A3E3\"}]",
  "image.76B7E7EB785A42B1.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Applied Energistics 2 · Network\",\"color\":\"#E2A3E3\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.20CAE981C267E1C2.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"matter · energy\",\"color\":\"#7DA9D2\",\"font\":\"minecraft:uniform\"}]",
  "image.5305435064DDB41F.title": "Back to the Sun of Heliodor",
  "image.5947353A33AB5F94.title": "On to AE2 · Automation",
  "chapter.774FEAB2CEAA7221.title": "CC: Tweaked",
  "chapter.774FEAB2CEAA7221.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Computers, turtles and monitors programmed in Lua: optional, but they can read and drive half of the pack."
  ],
  "quest.53ADB2066E8E7D23.title": "Computers, optional and powerful",
  "quest.53ADB2066E8E7D23.quest_desc": [
    "Lua computers, robotic turtles, monitors, modems and printers. Fully optional: no quest needs code, and the Act V network milestone accepts a computer panel as one route among others. Never programmed? The built-in programs (help, edit, go, excavate) already do a lot."
  ],
  "quest.37FECE288D04614F.title": "Your first Computer",
  "quest.37FECE288D04614F.quest_desc": [
    "Stone, redstone and a glass pane. Right-click to open the terminal: \"help\" lists topics, \"programs\" lists commands, \"edit name\" opens the editor and \"lua\" gives you a live prompt to try code.",
    "",
    "Hold Ctrl+T for a second to stop a stuck program, Ctrl+R to reboot and Ctrl+S to shut down. A file called startup runs by itself when the computer boots."
  ],
  "quest.799E84461222BBB3.title": "IDs and labels",
  "quest.799E84461222BBB3.quest_desc": [
    "Every computer has a numeric ID (\"id\") and keeps it when broken, so its files travel with it. \"label set Name\" names it; a Name Tag or an anvil also works. Labelled turtles keep their fuel when picked up.",
    "",
    "Crafting a computer into a turtle or an advanced model keeps its ID and data."
  ],
  "quest.6D824B2F8096F006.title": "Advanced Computer",
  "quest.6D824B2F8096F006.quest_desc": [
    "Gold instead of stone. The advanced models show colour and accept mouse clicks, which makes menus and buttons possible. You can upgrade a normal computer in place by surrounding it with gold: it keeps its ID and files.",
    "",
    "The same gold upgrade exists for pocket computers."
  ],
  "quest.5935F07739DC4924.title": "Disk Drive and floppies",
  "quest.5935F07739DC4924.quest_desc": [
    "A Disk Drive beside a computer mounts a floppy as the folder \"disk\". Floppies carry programs between computers, and a startup file on a disk runs at boot. Craft floppies from paper, redstone and a dye.",
    "",
    "Space: 1 MB per computer or turtle and 125 KB per floppy by default. Music discs in a drive can be played too."
  ],
  "quest.750F233DF2536F5C.title": "Redstone from a computer",
  "quest.750F233DF2536F5C.quest_desc": [
    "Computers read and emit redstone on all six sides with no extra block: \"redstone probe\" lists inputs, \"redstone set left true\" turns a side on and \"redstone pulse\" sends pulses. In Lua, the rs API does the same with analog levels.",
    "",
    "The Redstone Relay is a separate block with six sides of its own that a computer controls through a wired modem, for when you need many signals far away."
  ],
  "quest.72792D7D894661AF.title": "Monitors",
  "quest.72792D7D894661AF.quest_desc": [
    "Monitors placed together join into one big screen, up to 8 wide and 6 tall by default. \"monitor right edit notes\" runs any program on the monitor at that side; in Lua, wrap the monitor and use term.redirect or write to it directly.",
    "",
    "Monitors can also be reached through a wired modem, so the screen does not have to touch the computer."
  ],
  "quest.0EDD0B86A59684EF.title": "Advanced Monitors",
  "quest.0EDD0B86A59684EF.quest_desc": [
    "Gold monitors, four per craft. They show colour and fire a monitor_touch event with the X and Y of every right-click, so a wall of them becomes a touch panel with buttons.",
    "",
    "Keep text short: the bigger the screen, the more data the server sends when it changes."
  ],
  "quest.542F669BB6979A73.title": "Wired Modems and cables",
  "quest.542F669BB6979A73.quest_desc": [
    "Networking Cable (six per craft) links Wired Modems. Put a modem on a machine or chest and right-click it: the chat confirms the peripheral name, and every computer on the cable can wrap it by that name.",
    "",
    "Any inventory becomes a peripheral: list its items and push or pull stacks between chests. On NeoForge, tanks and energy storage are readable too."
  ],
  "quest.227AE57B09C73B93.title": "Wireless Modems and rednet",
  "quest.227AE57B09C73B93.quest_desc": [
    "Stone around an ender pearl. A Wireless Modem reaches 64 blocks near the ground, growing above Y 96 up to 384 at the build limit. The rednet API sends to an ID or broadcasts, and \"rednet.host\" plus \"rednet.lookup\" let programs find each other by name.",
    "",
    "Open the modem first: rednet.open with its side."
  ],
  "quest.646AABCD481A864F.title": "Ender Modem",
  "quest.646AABCD481A864F.quest_desc": [
    "Gold around an eye of ender. It works like a wireless modem with no distance limit, and messages cross dimensions, so a base in the Overworld can talk to a mine elsewhere.",
    "",
    "It also fits turtles and pocket computers as an upgrade."
  ],
  "quest.68AA1FD1CEA5B6F0.title": "GPS cluster",
  "quest.68AA1FD1CEA5B6F0.quest_desc": [
    "Four computers with ender modems at the corners of a small cube, three on one level and one above, each running «gps host x y z» with its exact coordinates in startup. Anything in range then finds itself with «gps locate». One wrong coordinate breaks everyone's answer."
  ],
  "quest.73AB617F80FCFB33.title": "Turtles",
  "quest.73AB617F80FCFB33.quest_desc": [
    "A computer, iron and a chest make a Turtle: a computer that moves, digs and places blocks. Turtles need fuel: put coal or a lava bucket in its inventory and run \"refuel\". The tank holds 20,000 fuel on a normal turtle and 100,000 on an advanced one, and each move spends some.",
    "",
    "\"go forward 3 up\" and \"turn left\" drive it without code."
  ],
  "quest.610BEE60A4D95BA8.title": "Mining Turtle",
  "quest.610BEE60A4D95BA8.quest_desc": [
    "Craft a turtle beside a diamond pickaxe (or use \"equip\" from its inventory) to get a Mining Turtle. \"tunnel 20\" digs a 3x2 tunnel, and \"excavate 5\" mines a 5x5 shaft down to bedrock and brings the loot back up.",
    "",
    "Other diamond tools give other turtles: axe (Felling), shovel (Digging), hoe (Farming) and sword (Melee). Only diamond tools work by default."
  ],
  "quest.38ADE6A69AF1BC9D.title": "Crafty Turtle",
  "quest.38ADE6A69AF1BC9D.quest_desc": [
    "A crafting table as upgrade makes a Crafty Turtle. Lay out a recipe in its inventory and run \"craft all\" or call turtle.craft in Lua. A turtle has two upgrade sides, so a mining and crafty turtle is possible."
  ],
  "quest.0C1C4EA1AE54B0F0.title": "Pocket Computer",
  "quest.0C1C4EA1AE54B0F0.quest_desc": [
    "A computer you carry: stone, a golden apple and a glass pane. Use it to talk to your base over rednet or to run \"gps locate\" on the move. It takes one upgrade: wireless or ender modem, or a speaker; \"equip\" puts on the first valid item from your inventory."
  ],
  "quest.5535489EE629D423.title": "Printer",
  "quest.5535489EE629D423.quest_desc": [
    "The Printer takes paper and dye as ink and prints pages from code. Join two or more printed pages with string into Printed Pages, or add leather for a Printed Book. Handy for logbooks and base maps."
  ],
  "quest.0587FAAACBDF8D55.title": "Speaker",
  "quest.0587FAAACBDF8D55.quest_desc": [
    "Stone, a note block and redstone. A speaker plays note block instruments, any game sound by name, or audio: \"speaker play file.dfpwm\" handles DFPWM and mono 8-bit WAV at 48 kHz. Up to 8 notes per tick by default.",
    "",
    "Turtles and pocket computers accept it as an upgrade."
  ],
  "quest.160BD6F65223664A.title": "Internet programs",
  "quest.160BD6F65223664A.quest_desc": [
    "The HTTP API is on: \"wget\" and \"pastebin get\" download programs and \"pastebin run\" runs one directly. Requests to private and local network addresses are blocked by default.",
    "",
    "Read any downloaded code before running it: a program has full control of the computer and whatever it is wired to."
  ],
  "quest.77AB5A14AB23ED5D.title": "Create and computers",
  "quest.77AB5A14AB23ED5D.quest_desc": [
    "Speedometer, Stressometer, Sequenced Gearshift, speed controller, train Station, Signal and Track Observer, Stock Ticker and Packager are peripherals; a Display Link can print «From Computer» on boards. Crafts and Additions' Digital Adapter reaches pulleys, pistons and bearings."
  ],
  "quest.4D9218F6064FD671.title": "Other mods on the wire",
  "quest.4D9218F6064FD671.quest_desc": [
    "Mekanism machines and multiblock ports, Immersive Engineering, PneumaticCraft, the Energy Meter, New Age and Crafts and Additions parts, and Draconic Evolution all answer computers; Ender IO redstone conduits show up as bundled redstone. «peripheral.getMethods» lists what each offers."
  ],
  "quest.7CC68FC53723A2DB.title": "Tips and limits",
  "quest.7CC68FC53723A2DB.quest_desc": [
    "Command Computers are creative-only: they need an operator in creative, and survival players cannot break them. By default all computers share a single server thread, so an endless loop without a sleep or os.pullEvent slows everyone; use events and timers instead of busy loops.",
    "",
    "The in-game \"help\" is short but accurate for this version."
  ],
  "quest.06E2AB6EF48F3F74.title": "Mastery: the base panel",
  "quest.06E2AB6EF48F3F74.quest_desc": [
    "Tie it together: an advanced computer on a wired network reads your energy storage and main chests, shows the numbers on an advanced monitor wall with touch buttons, and hears remote turtles or outposts over an ender modem.",
    "",
    "The same panel is a valid, optional way to watch the Act V network, never a requirement."
  ],
  "chapter.6A7DBBFF70117355.title": "Gadgets: lasers, jetpacks, rooms, simulations",
  "chapter.6A7DBBFF70117355.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Mining Gadgets, Iron Jetpacks, Compact Machines and Hostile Neural Networks: four powerful tools and the pack rules around them."
  ],
  "quest.3B5FFFE461585A6E.title": "Four big gadgets",
  "quest.3B5FFFE461585A6E.quest_desc": [
    "A mining laser, FE jetpacks, pocket rooms inside a single block and simulated mob farms. All four open around Act III, each behind one campaign component, and their top tiers ask for later acts."
  ],
  "quest.6E90715BDE070851.title": "Mining Gadget",
  "quest.6E90715BDE070851.quest_desc": [
    "A mining laser that runs on FE: hold use to carve blocks away, many at once with size upgrades. Three models exist, MK1 to MK3. Sneak and use it to open its settings (range, filters, which blocks to void).",
    "",
    "ENTRELUMEN change: all three models need a reinforced alloy (Act III)."
  ],
  "quest.41F61EBCEC886584.title": "Modification Table and upgrades",
  "quest.41F61EBCEC886584.quest_desc": [
    "Upgrades start from a Blank Upgrade Module and go in through the Modification Table: size up to 7x7, range (+5 per tier), efficiency, fortune, silk touch, magnet, void junk, freezing for lava and water, a light placer, batteries. Each one raises the FE cost per block."
  ],
  "quest.144026C64EC13947.title": "Iron Jetpacks",
  "quest.144026C64EC13947.quest_desc": [
    "FE jetpacks in a ladder of materials, wood up to emerald. Each tier is built from that material's cell, thrusters and capacitor on top of the previous chain, flying faster with a bigger battery. Pack change: the Leather Strap needs a reinforced alloy (III), so every chain starts there. And every jetpack burns 2.5 times its native energy per tick."
  ],
  "quest.656441966D4972F1.title": "Flying a jetpack",
  "quest.656441966D4972F1.quest_desc": [
    "Wear it on your chest or in the back accessory slot and charge it like any FE item. In this pack F4 toggles the engine and Alt+H toggles hover, which holds your height and lets you drift down slowly. Ascend, descend, throttle and HUD have their own keys under Controls; sprinting goes faster but burns more."
  ],
  "quest.1D92B4FDC73E4492.title": "Coils and top tiers",
  "quest.1D92B4FDC73E4492.quest_desc": [
    "Coils go into the thrusters: basic (iron), advanced (gold), elite (diamond) and ultimate (emerald).",
    "",
    "ENTRELUMEN change: the Elite Coil needs a zanite gemstone from the Aether (Act IV) and the Ultimate Coil atomic alloy from Mekanism (Act V), which gates the diamond, platinum and emerald jetpacks."
  ],
  "quest.5BA77EC956046C58.title": "Compact Machine parts",
  "quest.5BA77EC956046C58.quest_desc": [
    "A Compact Machine is a block with a whole room inside. Its parts: Compact Machine Walls (eight from polished deepslate), an Atom Shrinking Module (sticky piston) and an Atom Enlarging Module (piston), both around an eye of ender. The walls are also a building block you can break and reuse."
  ],
  "quest.0A2BE52F61AC0594.title": "Room sizes",
  "quest.0A2BE52F61AC0594.quest_desc": [
    "Walls, both modules and a core make the machine; the core sets the room: copper 3, iron 5, gold 7, diamond 9, obsidian 11, netherite 13, nether star 45, diamond hoe a 21x21 farm with grass. No machine recipes in JEI? An operator must enable the built-in templates (ops get a clickable warning), then restart."
  ],
  "quest.378FA233E5C9F039.title": "Personal Shrinking Device",
  "quest.378FA233E5C9F039.quest_desc": [
    "Use the PSD on a machine to shrink into its room; it has its own accessory slot. Inside there is no weather, beds do not work and the walls cannot be broken. A key under Controls quick-exits the room. Machines can hold machines, room inside room.",
    "",
    "ENTRELUMEN change: the PSD needs a reinforced alloy (Act III)."
  ],
  "quest.078A57D9C7E6D9AD.title": "Working inside a room",
  "quest.078A57D9C7E6D9AD.quest_desc": [
    "Rooms live in their own dimension and load with the machine chunk outside. Plan how power and items get in: cross-dimension tools work well, such as Flux Networks, LaserIO Advanced Connectors or ender chests. Jade shows a machine's owner and bound room."
  ],
  "quest.1C8F40E049E50CFC.title": "Data Models",
  "quest.1C8F40E049E50CFC.quest_desc": [
    "Craft a Model Framework and right-click a mob with it: it attunes into a Data Model of that mob. One model per mob type; the model is what every other Hostile Neural Networks machine works with."
  ],
  "quest.3298A34ED1DAFBCA.title": "Deep Learner",
  "quest.3298A34ED1DAFBCA.quest_desc": [
    "Put models in the Deep Learner, worn as an accessory, and kill that mob yourself: each kill adds data, and the model climbs from Faulty to Basic, Advanced, Superior and Self Aware. A HUD shows the kills left for the next tier. In this pack Alt+U opens the Deep Learner."
  ],
  "quest.744919A3D068C9B6.title": "Simulation Chamber",
  "quest.744919A3D068C9B6.quest_desc": [
    "The Sim Chamber runs a model on FE and Prediction Matrices: each simulation gives a Generalized Prediction of the mob's world and, depending on the model's accuracy, a mob Prediction. It can run in Inference mode (outputs, no data) or Training mode (data, no outputs).",
    "",
    "ENTRELUMEN change: an Ecosystem Capsule (Act IV) is the chamber's core, in place of the obsidian."
  ],
  "quest.2DAC1FCED44B001F.title": "Loot Fabricator",
  "quest.2DAC1FCED44B001F.quest_desc": [
    "Turns Predictions into real drops, using FE. Pick which drop each prediction becomes, in fixed or queue mode; a Fabrication Directive copies those choices to other fabricators (right-click to copy, sneak-right-click to apply)."
  ],
  "quest.4E89E77C43C2662A.title": "Data Center",
  "quest.4E89E77C43C2662A.quest_desc": [
    "The top of the line runs up to 25 Self Aware models at once, one drop each per cycle. It sits in a 7x7x7 hollow shell: obsidian floor, black stained glass walls and ceiling, the controller facing out from the bottom wall. IO Ports replace shell blocks and cycle between Energy, Models, Inputs and Outputs with a right-click."
  ],
  "quest.43242F93257E8715.title": "Mastery: the compact workshop",
  "quest.43242F93257E8715.quest_desc": [
    "Fly in with an emerald jetpack, clear a site with a 7x7 Mining Gadget, and hide a simulation farm inside a Compact Machine, powered from outside through a cross-dimension link. That is a whole production line in one block."
  ],
  "chapter.2E9A7D72E0835EEA.title": "Immersive Aircraft",
  "chapter.2E9A7D72E0835EEA.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Airships, biplanes, a gyrodyne and more: parts, fuel, controls, repairs, upgrades and weapons."
  ],
  "quest.427571CE3B56C67C.title": "Seven flying machines",
  "quest.427571CE3B56C67C.quest_desc": [
    "All crafted from a handful of parts on a crafting table. They fly in any dimension by default, carry cargo, take upgrades and mount weapons. Pack pacing: the Engine needs a Power Regulator and the Gyrodyne a reinforced alloy (Act III), which covers every aircraft. A gifted aircraft flies normally."
  ],
  "quest.64316D614B1F2430.title": "Controls and keys",
  "quest.64316D614B1F2430.quest_desc": [
    "W and S push and pull the controls, A and D turn, Space climbs and Left Shift descends; B fires a rocket boost on aircraft with a booster slot. In this pack Dismount is F12 (R is taken): press it twice in the air to jump out.",
    "",
    "The camera switches to third person in an aircraft by default."
  ],
  "quest.3C52109D4DAAB402.title": "Hulls",
  "quest.3C52109D4DAAB402.quest_desc": [
    "Logs and iron ingots make the Hull, the frame of every aircraft. Most designs take two or more, and so does the Hull Reinforcement upgrade."
  ],
  "quest.72B3D7A1DFB7E1AB.title": "Sails and propellers",
  "quest.72B3D7A1DFB7E1AB.quest_desc": [
    "Sails are white carpet and string; propellers are iron bent into shape. The airship wants six sails, the biplane one propeller, the quadrocopter four."
  ],
  "quest.0C9B6B3192A484AE.title": "Boiler",
  "quest.0C9B6B3192A484AE.quest_desc": [
    "Copper around a furnace makes the Boiler, heart of the Engine. The fuel slot of each aircraft is its boiler: it burns normal furnace fuels, and blaze powder counts as a strong fuel."
  ],
  "quest.19E92EE086F5C840.title": "Engine",
  "quest.19E92EE086F5C840.quest_desc": [
    "Boiler, pistons, a blast furnace and cobblestone make the Engine for the airship, biplane and quadrocopter.",
    "",
    "ENTRELUMEN change: the cobblestone on top is replaced by a Power Regulator (Act III). Everything else in the recipe is native."
  ],
  "quest.4A7E00C064077EA8.title": "Gyrodyne",
  "quest.4A7E00C064077EA8.quest_desc": [
    "A muscle-powered copter with no engine: two sails, two hulls and a propeller. Keep pushing forward on the ground until the rotor reaches minimum speed, then lift off. It burns your hunger, not fuel, so eat before a trip.",
    "",
    "ENTRELUMEN change: a reinforced alloy (Act III) takes the lower sail's place."
  ],
  "quest.41571E5944B41C5F.title": "Airship",
  "quest.41571E5944B41C5F.quest_desc": [
    "Six sails, two hulls and an engine. Slow and forgiving: it climbs and descends straight up and down and holds position, with a weapon slot, three upgrade slots and a 16-slot hold. The best first aircraft."
  ],
  "quest.20D18291E169CAA8.title": "Biplane",
  "quest.20D18291E169CAA8.quest_desc": [
    "Three hulls, an engine and a propeller. Fast and reliable, but it needs a runway: speed up on flat ground before pulling up, and land the same way. It has a booster slot for rockets."
  ],
  "quest.3645241838AF3C28.title": "Quadrocopter",
  "quest.3645241838AF3C28.quest_desc": [
    "An engine, four propellers and bamboo. Slow and precise, it hovers and barely feels the wind: great for building high up, not for travel. It sips fuel."
  ],
  "quest.0527BDAA90FDB0EC.title": "Cargo Airship",
  "quest.0527BDAA90FDB0EC.quest_desc": [
    "An airship plus chests and a hull: extra boxed storage on both sides for moving a whole base, at the cost of more fuel and even less speed."
  ],
  "quest.3E5E43E5ED1910A7.title": "Bamboo Hopper",
  "quest.3E5E43E5ED1910A7.quest_desc": [
    "Built from two biplanes, five bamboo blocks, a hull and another engine. Three seats and pontoons let it land safely on water, with two weapon slots and a booster slot."
  ],
  "quest.70D6B624DE07D0C7.title": "Fuel and wind",
  "quest.70D6B624DE07D0C7.quest_desc": [
    "Put fuel in the boiler slot before takeoff; the hotbar gauge shows the engine. Aircraft warn when fuel runs low. Wind pushes you around, three times harder in rain or thunder; the Gyroscope upgrades cancel it.",
    "",
    "Upgrades change fuel use: the Eco Engine saves a lot, the Nether Engine and Steel Boiler burn more for more power."
  ],
  "quest.767DAAD2F5180B35.title": "Damage, repair and crashes",
  "quest.767DAAD2F5180B35.quest_desc": [
    "Right-click a damaged aircraft to repair it a little each click, at the cost of some hunger. Crashes make a small explosion that breaks no blocks and starts no fires, and by default a crash cannot kill you.",
    "",
    "Breaking an aircraft returns it as an item: its upgrades stay inside, its cargo drops on the ground."
  ],
  "quest.0827E6F45D206DF5.title": "Engine upgrades",
  "quest.0827E6F45D206DF5.quest_desc": [
    "Upgrade slots accept parts that change stats: Sturdy Pipes (+10% power), Industrial Gears (-20% fuel), Steel Boiler (+25% power, +50% fuel), Eco Engine (-20% power, -75% fuel), Nether Engine (+40% power, +30% fuel) and the Enhanced Propeller (much less air friction).",
    "",
    "The tooltip of each upgrade lists its numbers."
  ],
  "quest.3591550FEC33CF17.title": "Gyroscopes and handling",
  "quest.3591550FEC33CF17.quest_desc": [
    "The Gyroscope removes wind and adds stability; the Advanced Gyroscope adds a mechanical dashboard and the Electronic Gyroscope a HUD. Hull Reinforcement doubles durability and the Improved Landing Gear gives 50% faster takeoff."
  ],
  "quest.5EB8D9EFE4993166.title": "Weapons",
  "quest.5EB8D9EFE4993166.quest_desc": [
    "Weapon slots take the Rotary Cannon (fires gunpowder), the Heavy Crossbow (arrows), the Bomb Bay (drops TNT that hurts but breaks no blocks) or the Telescope. Fire with the use key; by default weapons never destroy terrain."
  ],
  "quest.0337268EBFD86CD7.title": "Mastery: Warship",
  "quest.0337268EBFD86CD7.quest_desc": [
    "The Warship is built from a Cargo Airship plus sails, hulls, two engines and industrial gears: a slow flying fortress with three times the durability, several weapon and upgrade slots and a booster. Fit it with a gyroscope, reinforcement and your weapons of choice."
  ],
  "chapter.693B56B9AD358543.title": "Immersive Engineering · Industry",
  "chapter.693B56B9AD358543.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Presses, crushers and a refinery feeding a diesel plant; at the end, an arc furnace that eats electrodes."
  ],
  "task.1481FDEF0BB7041C.title": "Heavy engineering",
  "task.4C2AA15534B0582D.title": "Light engineering",
  "task.4038BA267666AC76.title": "Steel scaffolding",
  "quest.562BC248458CD11F.title": "Machine parts",
  "quest.562BC248458CD11F.quest_subtitle": "Big machines are built, not crafted.",
  "quest.562BC248458CD11F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Light Engineering Blocks\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:light_engineering\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (iron sheetmetal, iron components, copper), \"},{\"text\":\"Heavy Engineering Blocks\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:heavy_engineering\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (steel sheetmetal, steel components, electrum) and \"},{\"text\":\"Steel Scaffolding\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:steel_scaffolding_standard\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make most of IE's big machines.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.65066EE52D0816F2.title": "Shapes for metal",
  "quest.65066EE52D0816F2.quest_desc": [
    "An iron plate over three blue dyes and three paper draws the molds blueprint. At the workbench, three steel plates and a nick of the wire cutters make each mold: plate, rod, wire, gear, casing, packing."
  ],
  "task.09405F7BEC0391A9.title": "Form the Metal Press",
  "quest.7DDF67C0A0C4774B.title": "The press",
  "quest.7DDF67C0A0C4774B.quest_subtitle": "Under new management: you.",
  "quest.7DDF67C0A0C4774B.quest_desc": [
    "A piston on a heavy engineering block, two steel scaffolds, two conveyors and a redstone engineering block: seven blocks, hammered on the piston. Right-click it with a mold; power goes in the plug on top and items ride the belts through."
  ],
  "task.2C5A9F7624460029.title": "Form the Crusher",
  "quest.42E48835149F9A3C.title": "The crusher",
  "quest.42E48835149F9A3C.quest_subtitle": "Hands off. Seriously.",
  "quest.42E48835149F9A3C.quest_desc": [
    "Ten light engineering blocks, ten steel scaffolds, eight steel fences, nine hoppers and a redstone block, hammered on the centre fence of the long side. It grinds ores into grit and stone into gravel, faster with more power."
  ],
  "task.3F2E621B47D2E38A.title": "Form the Squeezer",
  "quest.00409D9993FFA0B6.title": "Seed oil",
  "quest.00409D9993FFA0B6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four wooden barrels, a piston, steel scaffolding and fences, light engineering and pipes form the \"},{\"text\":\"Industrial Squeezer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:squeezer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", hammered on the centre barrel. Each hemp seed gives 120 mB of \"},{\"text\":\"Plant Oil\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:plantoil_bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", wheat seeds 80.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.387926D1C7E329E5.title": "Graphite",
  "quest.387926D1C7E329E5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The crusher grinds coke into \"},{\"text\":\"Coke Dust\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:dust_coke\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", and the squeezer presses eight of it into one \"},{\"text\":\"HOP Graphite Dust\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:dust_hop_graphite\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". That's thirty-two coke per electrode: start a coke line now.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.5EA285A017AEF669.title": "Look at your Bottling Machine",
  "quest.4DBD3BFE9EDFFFB7.title": "Bottling",
  "quest.4DBD3BFE9EDFFFB7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three conveyors, two fluid pumps, iron sheetmetal, light engineering, scaffolding and a redstone block: hammer the centre conveyor to form the \"},{\"text\":\"Bottling Machine\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:bottling_machine\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Fluid goes in its tank, items ride the belt and leave filled.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3D738FF3AE2B8D0E.title": "Electrodes",
  "quest.3D738FF3AE2B8D0E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A rod mold, four HOP graphite dust and a bucket of creosote bottle into one \"},{\"text\":\"Graphite Electrode\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:graphite_electrode\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", packed, soaked and baked in the machine. The arc furnace wants three at once.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.37B3A5F2DA0EE76F.title": "Form the Fermenter",
  "quest.48C6734741715F55.title": "Fermentation",
  "quest.48C6734741715F55.quest_subtitle": "Not for drinking. Probably.",
  "quest.48C6734741715F55.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four cauldrons, iron sheetmetal, scaffolding, light engineering and pipes form the \"},{\"text\":\"Industrial Fermenter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:fermenter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", hammered on the centre cauldron. Sugar cane, potatoes and apples give 80 mB of \"},{\"text\":\"Ethanol\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:ethanol_bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; a honey bottle, 250.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.653124BA8A3C38E9.title": "Form the Refinery",
  "quest.485936812C7CF65C.title": "Refined",
  "quest.485936812C7CF65C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Refinery\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:refinery\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" mixes 8 mB of plant oil with 8 of ethanol into 16 of \"},{\"text\":\"Biodiesel\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:biodiesel_bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", with nitrate dust in its catalyst slot. The catalyst isn't used up, and it \"},{\"text\":\"only goes in by hand\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "task.7A6E9F348C98352E.title": "Form the Diesel Generator",
  "quest.6501E1AE152E3230.title": "Diesel power",
  "quest.6501E1AE152E3230.quest_subtitle": "Loud, thirsty, worth it.",
  "quest.6501E1AE152E3230.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Thirteen heavy engineering blocks, nine radiators, four generator blocks, pipes and scaffolding, hammered on the centre generator. Fuel goes in at the bottom corners; \"},{\"text\":\"4,096 FE/t\",\"color\":\"#F2C14E\"},{\"text\":\" come out of up to three plugs on top.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.356B7280B0D08BA2.title": "Form the Arc Furnace",
  "quest.6E0D8F11804BF736.title": "Lightning in a vat",
  "quest.6E0D8F11804BF736.quest_subtitle": "Three electrodes, one very hot soup.",
  "quest.6E0D8F11804BF736.quest_desc": [
    "Seventy-seven blocks: reinforced blast bricks, steel blocks and sheetmetal, light and heavy engineering, scaffolding and a cauldron. Hammer the cauldron, load three electrodes, feed it plenty of power, and it melts twelve inputs at once.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "{image:immersiveengineering:textures/item/graphite_electrode.png width:32 height:32 align:center}",
    "",
    "Raw ore comes out as an ingot plus a coin-flip for a second. Iron with coke dust turns to steel in 20 seconds, ancient debris gives two netherite scrap, and worn tools and armour melt back into metal."
  ],
  "task.4945A427BDF8D6ED.title": "Look at your Sawmill",
  "quest.43E369905E2BEDE8.title": "The sawmill",
  "quest.43E369905E2BEDE8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Steel ingots and plates make a \"},{\"text\":\"Sawblade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:sawblade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; slot it into the back of the \"},{\"text\":\"Sawmill\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:sawmill\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". A log comes out as six planks instead of four, stripped first, with \"},{\"text\":\"Sawdust\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:dust_wood\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" from both steps.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.1B23C76315A9FD01.title": "Look at your Assembler",
  "task.700855EEFB54B6A4.title": "Look at your Automated Workbench",
  "quest.0440A088E121A363.title": "Crafting on autopilot",
  "quest.0440A088E121A363.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Assembler\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:assembler\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" crafts up to three recipes in a row, using fluid in its tanks in place of buckets. The \"},{\"text\":\"Automated Engineer's Workbench\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:auto_workbench\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" builds whatever the blueprint on its drawing table describes.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.782CC5CC345F5D8D.title": "The full set",
  "quest.782CC5CC345F5D8D.quest_desc": [
    "Rod and wire molds for parts, the casing mold for ammunition, and packing molds that squeeze 4 or 9 items into their block or take them apart again."
  ],
  "quest.1D06185B52FB567C.title": "Double yield",
  "quest.1D06185B52FB567C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"One ingot, two wires: the press doubles what the cutters give. A copper ingot makes two casings, and five blaze powder press back into a blaze rod.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2725113511A576AF.title": "Plate order",
  "quest.2725113511A576AF.quest_subtitle": "Thirty-two, flat, by tomorrow.",
  "quest.2725113511A576AF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Thirty-two \"},{\"text\":\"Steel Plates\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:plate_steel\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for the common store, once a day. A press fed by an improved blast furnace does it in its sleep.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3D1E732607196861.title": "What the drums give",
  "quest.3D1E732607196861.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Raw ore gives one grit and a one-in-three chance of a second; an ore block gives two. Blaze rods give four powder, sandstone two sand, each with a chance of sulfur or nitrate. Anything alive that falls in comes out as drops.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.172892216EF58D9A.title": "Nitrate and sulfur",
  "quest.172892216EF58D9A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Crushed sandstone yields \"},{\"text\":\"Nitrate Dust\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:dust_saltpeter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; blaze rods and nether quartz ore yield \"},{\"text\":\"Sulfur Dust\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:dust_sulfur\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Four nitrate, a sulfur and a charcoal make six gunpowder, and nitrate is the refinery's catalyst for biodiesel.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5CE2B7571BAB2E86.title": "The revolver",
  "quest.5CE2B7571BAB2E86.quest_subtitle": "Six chambers, zero patience.",
  "quest.5CE2B7571BAB2E86.quest_desc": [
    "A barrel, a drum and a hammer, all steel, plus a steel component and a wooden grip. Sneak and right-click it to load cartridges. Shots are loud and draw every monster around."
  ],
  "quest.5951B8F9104EA76D.title": "Ammunition",
  "quest.5951B8F9104EA76D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An empty casing between two gunpowder, over blue dye and paper, draws the Common Projectiles blueprint. At the workbench, four casings, gunpowder and a lead nugget make four \"},{\"text\":\"Casull Cartridges\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:bullet_casull\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; armour-piercing, buckshot and silver come from the same sheet.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3C25F55EE244428C.title": "Special rounds",
  "quest.3C25F55EE244428C.quest_desc": [
    "The Specialized Projectiles blueprint can't be drawn: buy it from a Gunsmith or find it in the chest of a village engineer's house. It makes explosive, dragon's breath, phial, flare, homing and wolfpack rounds."
  ],
  "task.090E6C67BFE7C811.title": "Max out the revolver",
  "quest.57B46BCE27C06DC1.title": "Fully loaded",
  "quest.57B46BCE27C06DC1.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four upgrades fit at the workbench: an \"},{\"text\":\"Extended Magazine\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:toolupgrade_revolver_magazine\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for six more shots, a \"},{\"text\":\"Bayonet\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:toolupgrade_revolver_bayonet\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" that hits like an iron sword, the \"},{\"text\":\"Precision Scope\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:toolupgrade_railgun_scope\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and \"},{\"text\":\"Amplifier Electron Tubes\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:toolupgrade_revolver_electro\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" that stun.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"With the scope fitted, the Zoom with the Railgun control zooms in and the scroll wheel changes magnification.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.6E8A0CC77A1B4F9A.title": "Win with IE weaponry",
  "quest.7D6F6723556B5F30.title": "Raider trouble",
  "quest.7D6F6723556B5F30.quest_desc": [
    "Kill any raider with a revolver, a railgun or a chemical thrower. From then on, raids near you bring IE's own illagers: Fusiliers, Commandos and shield-bearing Bulwarks."
  ],
  "task.296471BA3A54575F.title": "Fusilier",
  "task.3C6E074F3FD59ECD.title": "Commando",
  "task.55A7879F708E073E.title": "Bulwark",
  "quest.3F21F895C99EAD02.title": "The engineers' raid",
  "quest.3F21F895C99EAD02.quest_subtitle": "They brought guns this time.",
  "quest.3F21F895C99EAD02.quest_desc": [
    "In your raids, pillagers may arrive as Fusiliers, and vindicators, evokers or ravagers as Commandos and Bulwarks. Beat one of each. Commandos drop revolver parts; Bulwarks, a masterwork shader bag."
  ],
  "task.4E45AD00A84E6B1C.title": "Look at your Resonanz Observer",
  "quest.380FEF14E73C35D3.title": "Resonanz",
  "quest.380FEF14E73C35D3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An echo shard, lead sheetmetal and advanced components make four \"},{\"text\":\"Resonanz Engineering Blocks\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:resonanz_engineering\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", tuned to a \"},{\"text\":\"resonanz\",\"color\":\"#B98CFF\",\"font\":\"minecraft:alt\"},{\"text\":\" few can hear. Two of them, a calibrated sculk sensor, concrete, steel and windows form the \"},{\"text\":\"Resonanz Observer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:chunk_loader\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": it keeps machines within 32 blocks running while you're away, on one paper a minute.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.2698D78115A111C6.title": "Enter trial chambers",
  "quest.3099BF36415B914B.title": "A faded blueprint",
  "quest.3099BF36415B914B.quest_subtitle": "Good boy. Needs oiling.",
  "quest.3099BF36415B914B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Trial chamber vaults sometimes hold a worn blueprint for an \"},{\"text\":\"Automaton Wolf\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:robot_wolf\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": a thermoelectric heart, a steel body, loyal like a tamed wolf. Mend it with the hammer and a metal plate in your other hand.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2071EFCBCCBB474B.title": "Plastic",
  "quest.2071EFCBCCBB474B.quest_subtitle": "Old-school plastic.",
  "quest.2071EFCBCCBB474B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Ethanol over a \"},{\"text\":\"Silver Plate\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:plate_silver\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" catalyst becomes acetaldehyde; 12 mB of it with 8 of creosote make 8 of \"},{\"text\":\"Phenolic Resin\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:phenolic_resin_bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". A bottling machine with a plate mold sets 250 mB into a \"},{\"text\":\"Duroplast Sheet\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:plate_duroplast\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.695821508B3DA564.title": "Vacuum tubes",
  "quest.695821508B3DA564.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The components blueprint turns glass, a nickel plate, copper wire and redstone into three \"},{\"text\":\"Vacuum Tubes\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:electron_tube\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Two tubes, a duroplast sheet and aluminium wire make an \"},{\"text\":\"Advanced Electronic Component\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:component_electronic_adv\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": railguns, turrets and Tesla coils need it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.46D15DE718E10F0C.title": "Skyhook, upgraded",
  "quest.46D15DE718E10F0C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"High Torque Motor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:toolupgrade_skyhook_slope\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" climbs slopes, the duroplast \"},{\"text\":\"Insulated Grip\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:toolupgrade_skyhook_insulation\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" stops wire shocks, and netherite \"},{\"text\":\"Heavy Impact Hooks\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:toolupgrade_skyhook_mace\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" hit hard on the way down and spare you the landing.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.39D20DD3B06FED6F.title": "The big battery",
  "quest.39D20DD3B06FED6F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Aluminium, a \"},{\"text\":\"HOP Graphite Plate\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:plate_hop_graphite\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" from the bottling machine and redstone acid on a basic engineering block: the \"},{\"text\":\"HV Accumulator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:capacitor_hv\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" holds 4,000,000 FE at 4,096 FE/t.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.2227F72B1703B973.title": "Look at your Lightning Rod",
  "quest.078D6FF6DB4FA984.title": "Catching lightning",
  "quest.078D6FF6DB4FA984.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight copper coil blocks, three HV coils, four HV accumulators, light engineering, scaffolding and fences form the \"},{\"text\":\"Lightning Rod\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:lightning_rod\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Stack steel fences on its top port to draw strikes in storms; each strike stores 16,000,000 FE.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1062CC04AB8C6D5C.title": "The railgun",
  "quest.1062CC04AB8C6D5C.quest_subtitle": "Physics, aimed.",
  "quest.1062CC04AB8C6D5C.quest_desc": [
    "An HV accumulator, an advanced electronic component, two electrum coil blocks, steel and a grip. Hold use until the charge reads 99, then let go. It drinks power: wear an accumulator backpack."
  ],
  "quest.5811BB927D8691B5.title": "Anything rod-shaped",
  "quest.5811BB927D8691B5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Iron, steel or aluminium rods, graphite electrodes, blaze rods that set fire, end and breeze rods, ender pearls for range, sawblades that pierce, even tridents. Sneak and scroll to switch.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.559C604B72FCCA50.title": "Saw through",
  "quest.559C604B72FCCA50.quest_subtitle": "We don't go to that town anymore.",
  "quest.559C604B72FCCA50.quest_desc": [
    "A sawblade from the railgun went through several creatures in one shot. Physics is a tool like any other."
  ],
  "reward.4EF3504E449A7823.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.70D76C7EAD6257AD.title": "Power on your back",
  "quest.70D76C7EAD6257AD.quest_subtitle": "Don't cross the streams.",
  "quest.70D76C7EAD6257AD.quest_desc": [
    "Leather, steel and treated rods, LV connectors and insulated coils make the frame; the workbench puts an accumulator inside. Worn, it charges the tools in your hands and your armour. Its top mount takes one: an antenna or a Tesla coil."
  ],
  "quest.55B3037BF1FF1879.title": "Charging antenna",
  "quest.55B3037BF1FF1879.quest_desc": [
    "Aluminium wire and rod on an LV connector. Walk under a bare power line and the antenna reaches up to it, trickle-charging the pack while you stay close."
  ],
  "quest.4CE4B3BFCDB1720F.title": "Shock armour",
  "quest.4CE4B3BFCDB1720F.quest_desc": [
    "Aluminium plates, electrum coils, a treated fence and an advanced component. When something hits you, the miniature coil shocks it back: thorns, the electric kind."
  ],
  "quest.3AED671BFBCD69BA.title": "Top up",
  "quest.3AED671BFBCD69BA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Treated wood, glass, iron, vacuum tubes and a copper coil block make the \"},{\"text\":\"Charging Station\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:charging_station\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Drop in anything that holds FE; the tubes on its front show the charge, and a comparator reads it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.441C6D618499857B.title": "Home defence",
  "quest.441C6D618499857B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Tesla Coil\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:tesla_coil\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" shocks and stuns anything within about six blocks, for 256 FE/t idle and 512 per zap, and only runs on a redstone signal. A suit of aluminium \"},{\"text\":\"Faraday armour\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:armor_faraday_chestplate\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" shrugs off low-power coils and bare wires.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.582F651D8AB760FC.title": "Mind the electrodes",
  "quest.582F651D8AB760FC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Electrodes wear one point per tick of work: \"},{\"text\":\"96,000 ticks\",\"color\":\"#F2C14E\"},{\"text\":\", about four in-game days nonstop. A comparator on the electrodes reads the most worn one, and replacing them is always by hand.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.195DEC4C7A55C77A.title": "Scribbled on the drawing",
  "quest.195DEC4C7A55C77A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Every machine on this sheet eats something: coal, seeds, electrodes. The one they asked me for would have eaten the light itself. —T.\",\"italic\":true}]"
  ],
  "quest.463BE2CA18938AF2.title": "Fuel on the go",
  "quest.463BE2CA18938AF2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four iron plates around four buckets make a \"},{\"text\":\"Jerrycan\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:jerrycan\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": 10 buckets, refilled at barrels and tanks, poured into machines. Craft it together with the drill and the drill fills up.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.1F1A36314111F334.title": "Form the Mixer",
  "quest.50DF0712E9C6C2C9.title": "The mixer",
  "quest.50DF0712E9C6C2C9.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"It dissolves solids in fluids: two sand, gravel and clay in half a bucket of water make liquid \"},{\"text\":\"Concrete\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:concrete_bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", one redstone makes 250 mB of redstone acid, and brewing ingredients make potions by the bucket.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.52DF8B27D6BD089C.title": "High-cetane",
  "quest.52DF8B27D6BD089C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The refinery blends 95 mB of biodiesel with 5 of Strength potion from the mixer into 100 of \"},{\"text\":\"High-Cetane Biodiesel\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:high_power_biodiesel_bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", which runs the generator 10% longer per bucket.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.486DE6FB2C82B679.title": "Cement shoes",
  "quest.486DE6FB2C82B679.quest_subtitle": "The mob sends its regards.",
  "quest.486DE6FB2C82B679.quest_desc": [
    "You stood in wet concrete until it set. The good news: you're very stable now."
  ],
  "reward.18149815B0E1EF1B.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.6AD41D4C61AA8407.title": "Feeding the engine",
  "quest.6AD41D4C61AA8407.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"At full load it drinks 4 mB a tick: a bucket of biodiesel lasts 12.5 seconds, about a million FE. Creosote burns too, one second a bucket. Plan the farms before the engine.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4D458F0ED49A8098.title": "Spray it",
  "quest.4D458F0ED49A8098.quest_subtitle": "Now with a pilot light.",
  "quest.4D458F0ED49A8098.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A pressurized air tank, a heavy engineering block, a pipe, a bucket and two grips make the \"},{\"text\":\"Chemical Thrower\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:chemthrower\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It sprays whatever fluid it holds, and sneak-right-click lights a pilot flame for the flammable ones. Herbicide strips plants; liquid concrete sets into walls.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.25698021BBCCD892.title": "The mining drill",
  "quest.25698021BBCCD892.quest_subtitle": "Diesel-powered tunnel vision.",
  "quest.25698021BBCCD892.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A heavy engineering block, an iron component and two grips make the \"},{\"text\":\"Mining Drill\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:drill\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Fit a \"},{\"text\":\"Steel Drill Head\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:drillhead_steel\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" at the workbench and fill it with biodiesel: it digs an area, or one block while sneaking.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.6C88B5AFAD518936.title": "Max out the drill",
  "quest.6D8FF2DBBCAE7B7A.title": "Drill, maxed",
  "quest.6D8FF2DBBCAE7B7A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Up to three \"},{\"text\":\"Additional Augers\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:toolupgrade_drill_damage\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for speed and damage, a lubrication system, a \"},{\"text\":\"Pressurized Air Tank\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:toolupgrade_drill_waterproof\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" to dig underwater, a large fuel tank and a \"},{\"text\":\"Rock Softening Acid\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:toolupgrade_drill_fortune\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" that works like Fortune. Fill every slot.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.329172156ECD78B9.title": "Giga drill",
  "quest.329172156ECD78B9.quest_subtitle": "It was meant for rocks.",
  "quest.329172156ECD78B9.quest_desc": [
    "You finished off a creature with the mining drill. Technically, it dug."
  ],
  "reward.4B66BC34F32A09F4.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.26B6B5418935FC75.title": "Clear-cutting",
  "quest.26B6B5418935FC75.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Steel rods, a heavy engineering block and two grips make the \"},{\"text\":\"Buzzsaw\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:buzzsaw\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; with a sawblade and biodiesel it fells whole trees. Swap in a \"},{\"text\":\"Rockcutter Blade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:rockcutter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" to cut stone out whole, like Silk Touch.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.38A0FCCAF463848A.title": "Coloured signals",
  "quest.38A0FCCAF463848A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Aluminium wire and redstone make \"},{\"text\":\"Redstone Wire Coils\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:wirecoil_redstone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": signals travel far without fading. Each \"},{\"text\":\"Redstone Wire Connector\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:connector_redstone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" sends or receives on one of 16 colours, set with the screwdriver.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1B4427D5BA855D22.title": "Logic on a board",
  "quest.1B4427D5BA855D22.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Engineer's Circuit Workbench\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:circuit_table\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" solders vacuum tubes onto backplanes as \"},{\"text\":\"Logic Circuits\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:logic_circuit\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; the \"},{\"text\":\"Logic Unit\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:logic_unit\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" runs up to ten of them with eight registers, through a redstone interface connector.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1FA286CF79856C67.title": "Ask the machine",
  "quest.1FA286CF79856C67.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"On a multiblock's redstone panel, the \"},{\"text\":\"Machine Interface\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:machine_interface\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" turns conditions into coloured signals: machine active, input empty, tank 75% full. It can send a signal back to switch the machine, too.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2ADA08C03E175F63.title": "Prospecting",
  "quest.2ADA08C03E175F63.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A writable book, a glass bottle, three tough fabric and an engineer's hammer, which the kit keeps, make \"},{\"text\":\"Mineral Survey Tools\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:survey_tools\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Used on natural stone or dirt, they point toward nearby mineral veins; more samples, better aim.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.34359A8FE21A59AD.title": "Core samples",
  "quest.34359A8FE21A59AD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Steel scaffolding and fences on light engineering make the \"},{\"text\":\"Core Sample Drill\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:sample_drill\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Start it by hand, feed it 40 FE/t and pull out a \"},{\"text\":\"Core Sample\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:coresample\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": the vein's ores, its saturation and its expected yield.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.53428CBCBCEF2B86.title": "Buy a mineral map",
  "quest.0A6BD6E87C7C7C0A.title": "X marks the vein",
  "quest.0A6BD6E87C7C7C0A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An experienced Structural Engineer sells a \"},{\"text\":\"Mineral Deposit Map\",\"color\":\"#D8C8FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_text\",\"contents\":\"A filled map, marked where a mineral vein lies.\"}},{\"text\":\": the shortcut to a vein, no surveying needed.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.48681408852115BD.title": "Form the Excavator",
  "quest.08C2E03CEB20E7E6.title": "The excavator",
  "quest.08C2E03CEB20E7E6.quest_subtitle": "Dig once, keep digging.",
  "quest.08C2E03CEB20E7E6.quest_desc": [
    "A steel bucket wheel on a sheetmetal engine: hammer the engine's rear heavy engineering block and both form. Over a vein it brings up ores no pickaxe will find, for 4,096 FE/t."
  ],
  "quest.2EB4987343115C79.title": "Reading a vein",
  "quest.2EB4987343115C79.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A vein yields at most 38,400 ores and may start up to 20% spent. Dig near its centre: far from it, more of each bucket is plain rock. The Nether has veins too, ancient debris among them.\"}]"
  ],
  "image.39282305070A9550.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Press and crusher\",\"color\":\"#F2C14E\"}]",
  "image.61D1A56B1BAAA502.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Sidearms\",\"color\":\"#F2C14E\"}]",
  "image.1A028E9B0B227533.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Weird science\",\"color\":\"#F2C14E\"}]",
  "image.46785EFB408075F0.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Plastic and batteries\",\"color\":\"#F2C14E\"}]",
  "image.191CC872E5F5CAEA.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"High-voltage gear\",\"color\":\"#F2C14E\"}]",
  "image.11B0E03593ED81E3.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Fuel\",\"color\":\"#F2C14E\"}]",
  "image.0F9DACB28C084446.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Diesel tools\",\"color\":\"#F2C14E\"}]",
  "image.6555243429C7CE65.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Control\",\"color\":\"#F2C14E\"}]",
  "image.08F9F4C73A289177.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"engine\",\"color\":\"#BAC6D2\"}]",
  "image.027B7237F64A984F.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Immersive Engineering · Industry\",\"color\":\"#F2C14E\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.492D3A86C25A816B.title": "Back to the Workshop",
  "image.587D2AFCF7347EE0.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"IMMERSIVE ENGINEERING\",\"color\":\"#F2C14E\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.3FBC2D5B3229E8C3.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Industry · sheet 2 of 2 · drawn: T.\",\"color\":\"#F2C14E\"}]",
  "chapter.47025B66BFCD747F.title": "Integrated Dynamics and Tunnels",
  "chapter.47025B66BFCD747F.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Menril, cables and variable cards; readers, operators and writers; Tunnels to move items, fluids and energy by rule."
  ],
  "quest.50FB10FD2141D419.title": "Menril Logs",
  "quest.50FB10FD2141D419.quest_subtitle": "Wood with a head for numbers.",
  "quest.50FB10FD2141D419.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Look for tall blue trees with glowing leaves: rare in the wild, about one chunk in a hundred, thick in the Meneglin forest. One wild log in eleven is Enriched: chopped without Silk Touch, it also drops one or two \"},{\"text\":\"Crystallized Menril Chunks\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"integrateddynamics:crystalized_menril_chunk\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5EBF371ED9BA295D.title": "Squeeze and dry",
  "quest.5EBF371ED9BA295D.quest_subtitle": "Jumping counts as work here.",
  "quest.5EBF371ED9BA295D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Put a \"},{\"text\":\"Menril Log\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"integrateddynamics:menril_log\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on the \"},{\"text\":\"Squeezer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"integrateddynamics:squeezer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and jump on it until it's flat. The resin runs into a \"},{\"text\":\"Drying Basin\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"integrateddynamics:drying_basin\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on one of its two sides; a redstone pulse lifts the press for the next log.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Any mob that falls on it presses too.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3B0829A194600C5D.title": "Crystallized Menril",
  "quest.3B0829A194600C5D.quest_subtitle": "Every network starts as sap.",
  "quest.3B0829A194600C5D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A log gives 1000 mB of resin, and the basin dries it into a \"},{\"text\":\"Block of Crystallized Menril\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"integrateddynamics:crystalized_menril_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in seven and a half seconds. A crafting grid breaks the block into nine chunks: cables, cards and every part are made of them.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Keep lava away: hot fluids set the basin on fire.\",\"color\":\"#FF8C7A\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Spare blocks go to the stonecutter as bricks, slabs and stairs; menril logs smelt into charcoal.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.50DB3E215BD52AB5.title": "Logic Cable",
  "quest.50DB3E215BD52AB5.quest_subtitle": "Ten in a row and it's a network.",
  "quest.50DB3E215BD52AB5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Six chunks, two sticks and a redstone dust make three \"},{\"text\":\"Logic Cables\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"integrateddynamics:cable\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Everything joined by cable is one network, and parts go on any of a cable's six faces.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.21E4444D757181F1.title": "Variable Cards",
  "quest.21E4444D757181F1.quest_subtitle": "Twenty-four per sheet of paper.",
  "quest.21E4444D757181F1.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight chunks around a paper make 24 \"},{\"text\":\"Variable Cards\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"integrateddynamics:variable\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". A card doesn't carry a value, only where to find it: a reader, a constant, an operator.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Crafted alone, a card is wiped clean; crafted with a blank one, it's copied.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.42729099F3D782C7.title": "Variable Transformers",
  "quest.42729099F3D782C7.quest_subtitle": "Sticky goes in, plain goes out.",
  "quest.42729099F3D782C7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two cards, two chunks and a \"},{\"text\":\"Sticky Piston\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:sticky_piston\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make four \"},{\"text\":\"Input Transformers\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"integrateddynamics:variable_transformer_input\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; a plain \"},{\"text\":\"Piston\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:piston\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" makes four \"},{\"text\":\"Output Transformers\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"integrateddynamics:variable_transformer_output\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Readers are built on the first kind, writers and panels on the second.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.50B0C40DB79A352B.title": "Bind the Redstone aspect to a card",
  "quest.1F508FE56FB71B63.title": "Redstone Reader",
  "quest.1F508FE56FB71B63.quest_subtitle": "The network's first sense.",
  "quest.1F508FE56FB71B63.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Put the reader on a cable facing a \"},{\"text\":\"Redstone Torch\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:redstone_torch\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", open it and drop a blank card into its \"},{\"text\":\"Redstone\",\"color\":\"#66D9EF\"},{\"text\":\" aspect. From then on that card carries the torch's signal anywhere on the network: every reader works like this, one aspect per thing it can read.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.4ED59F722EEF5416.title": "Show the Redstone card",
  "quest.792F317751A49E5C.title": "Display Panel",
  "quest.792F317751A49E5C.quest_subtitle": "Show your work.",
  "quest.792F317751A49E5C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two \"},{\"text\":\"Static Light Panels\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"integrateddynamics:part_static_light_panel\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", two menril berries and an Output Transformer. Give it the Redstone card and it shows the value live; the wrench turns it to face you.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A program acting up? Put its cards on panels one by one until one shows the wrong value.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.208A495D4205F1BE.title": "Pass a full signal from reader to writer",
  "quest.4FF178E723970DA5.title": "Redstone Writer",
  "quest.4FF178E723970DA5.quest_subtitle": "A wire you never have to lay.",
  "quest.4FF178E723970DA5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The reader's recipe with an Output Transformer. Give the reader's card to the writer's \"},{\"text\":\"Redstone\",\"color\":\"#66D9EF\"},{\"text\":\" aspect and it emits that exact level, as far away as the network reaches.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Redstone Pulse\",\"color\":\"#66D9EF\"},{\"text\":\" aspect fires one pulse each time the value changes.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5D3AA7B4C9C56A9A.title": "Logic Programmer",
  "quest.5D3AA7B4C9C56A9A.quest_subtitle": "Every operator in one box.",
  "quest.5D3AA7B4C9C56A9A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Block of Crystallized Menril\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"integrateddynamics:crystalized_menril_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a \"},{\"text\":\"Crafting Table\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:crafting_table\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Pick a value type or an operator on the left, fill its inputs with cards and write the result to a blank card: that's how every program here is built.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Crafted alone it becomes the \"},{\"text\":\"Portable Logic Programmer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"integrateddynamics:portable_logic_programmer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", and back.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.4AFF0C13E3B6CF5A.title": "Write an Integer constant",
  "quest.6B0B0F7665336FC3.title": "A constant",
  "quest.6B0B0F7665336FC3.quest_subtitle": "Numbers that stay put.",
  "quest.6B0B0F7665336FC3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Type \"},{\"text\":\"Integer\",\"color\":\"#66D9EF\"},{\"text\":\" in the search box, enter a number and write it to a blank card. That's a static card: its value never changes until you put it back in the programmer and rewrite it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0B51F559EA8EC9E2.title": "Variable Store",
  "quest.0B51F559EA8EC9E2.quest_subtitle": "Lazy by design.",
  "quest.0B51F559EA8EC9E2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The network works a card out only when something asks for its value, so every card another card refers to must be within reach. Keep them in a \"},{\"text\":\"Variable Store\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"integrateddynamics:variablestore\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on the same network; use as many stores as you like.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.317E4FD97748B27B.title": "Show a sum on a panel",
  "quest.50F9B3052DA1FAC0.title": "Addition",
  "quest.50F9B3052DA1FAC0.quest_subtitle": "Two plus two, the long way round.",
  "quest.50F9B3052DA1FAC0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Make two Integer cards, pick \"},{\"text\":\"Addition\",\"color\":\"#66D9EF\"},{\"text\":\", drop them into its inputs and a blank card into the output. Keep the two inputs in the store and put the result on a Display Panel.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.0AC3F0F4ED5E9DF2.title": "Add by applying twice",
  "task.750C8E0231641E3B.title": "Filter the list down to 10",
  "quest.281FE73BA5B9CBA6.title": "Operators are values",
  "quest.281FE73BA5B9CBA6.quest_subtitle": "Currying, no curry involved.",
  "quest.281FE73BA5B9CBA6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Write \"},{\"text\":\"Addition\",\"color\":\"#66D9EF\"},{\"text\":\" itself to a card and \"},{\"text\":\"Apply\",\"color\":\"#66D9EF\"},{\"text\":\" an Integer to it: you get an operator that adds that number to whatever comes next. Then \"},{\"text\":\"Filter\",\"color\":\"#66D9EF\"},{\"text\":\" a list of 1, 10 and 100 with \"},{\"text\":\"Equals\",\"color\":\"#66D9EF\"},{\"text\":\" applied to 10.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.00F8B0A1AF2F1CB3.title": "Write a proxied card",
  "quest.526072E0FEE47C21.title": "Proxy",
  "quest.526072E0FEE47C21.quest_subtitle": "Change one card, change the whole program.",
  "quest.526072E0FEE47C21.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Put a card in the \"},{\"text\":\"Proxy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"integrateddynamics:proxy\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and it writes new cards that follow whatever sits in its slot. Build programs on the proxied card and swap the one inside to change a value everywhere, without rewriting a thing; that inner card has to stay put.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.606AF8D639EF0FED.title": "Item Interface",
  "quest.606AF8D639EF0FED.quest_subtitle": "Every chest becomes shared storage.",
  "quest.606AF8D639EF0FED.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Five chunks and a chest make four \"},{\"text\":\"Item Interfaces\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"integratedtunnels:part_interface_item\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". On a cable, an interface opens the inventory it faces to the whole network: importers put things there and exporters take them from there.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"With several interfaces, their priority in the part settings decides which fills first.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7F1E6CAD83572C63.title": "Importers and Exporters",
  "quest.7F1E6CAD83572C63.quest_subtitle": "Blue pulls, orange pushes.",
  "quest.7F1E6CAD83572C63.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An interface and an Input Transformer make an \"},{\"text\":\"Item Importer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"integratedtunnels:part_importer_item\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", which pulls from what it faces into the interfaces; with an Output Transformer, an \"},{\"text\":\"Item Exporter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"integratedtunnels:part_exporter_item\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", which pushes back out. A card in their aspects decides what moves.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.0DD388C72A270D94.title": "Import everything",
  "task.55B1E0687C7A3743.title": "Import a list",
  "task.59C0FC06AF23C8D6.title": "Export what can be enchanted",
  "quest.7B4C878F7B069A8F.title": "Rules of the tunnel",
  "quest.7B4C878F7B069A8F.quest_subtitle": "Everything, a list, or a question.",
  "quest.7B4C878F7B069A8F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Boolean card set to true in \"},{\"text\":\"Import All Items\",\"color\":\"#66D9EF\"},{\"text\":\" takes everything; a list from an Inventory Reader in \"},{\"text\":\"Import Items\",\"color\":\"#66D9EF\"},{\"text\":\" takes exactly that; \"},{\"text\":\"Enchantable\",\"color\":\"#66D9EF\"},{\"text\":\" in \"},{\"text\":\"Export Items Predicate\",\"color\":\"#66D9EF\"},{\"text\":\" sends out only what can be enchanted.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"An aspect's properties hold the rest: rate, slot, exact amount, Blacklist and Round-Robin.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.5F65FA51A6AAC2D7.title": "A door that knows your name",
  "task.73DC6E935571C54C.title": "Stop at ten",
  "quest.14EEA85DB5C4A668.title": "A network that decides",
  "quest.14EEA85DB5C4A668.quest_subtitle": "Not a speck of redstone dust.",
  "quest.14EEA85DB5C4A668.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two decisions, no hands. A door that opens only for your name: an Entity Reader, \"},{\"text\":\"To String\",\"color\":\"#66D9EF\"},{\"text\":\", \"},{\"text\":\"Equals\",\"color\":\"#66D9EF\"},{\"text\":\" with the name first, and a Redstone Writer on the door. And an exporter that stops once the chest holds ten: \"},{\"text\":\"Less Than\",\"color\":\"#66D9EF\"},{\"text\":\" on an Inventory Reader's count.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Atlas asks for the same trick in \"},{\"text\":\"Stop before overflow\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"758AAF75374D9805\"}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "task.650AA067A0C9F9C7.title": "Walk into a Meneglin",
  "quest.0A6ADB1D1AAB5785.title": "Meneglin",
  "quest.0A6ADB1D1AAB5785.quest_subtitle": "A forest that went blue on purpose.",
  "quest.0A6ADB1D1AAB5785.quest_desc": [
    "The resin the trees give off turns this forest blue: one or two menril trees per chunk over blue orchids and white flowers. It takes the place of some forests in the Overworld."
  ],
  "quest.06E82664F98B587E.title": "A grove at home",
  "quest.06E82664F98B587E.quest_subtitle": "Snack, lamp and circuit board.",
  "quest.06E82664F98B587E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Menril leaves drop a sapling one time in forty and berries about one in seven, Fortune helping both. Plant the saplings near the base; the berries go into every panel, and a berry on a stick makes four \"},{\"text\":\"Menril Torches\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"integrateddynamics:menril_torch\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Menril without an axe: a sapling in a Botany Pot yields one to four logs a harvest, three \"},{\"text\":\"Menril Essence\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:menril_essence\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make sixteen logs, and the Menril Bee's combs spin into resin and chunks (\"},{\"text\":\"Productive Bees\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"3256FA24100D6B05\"}},{\"text\":\").\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0A65CC3994122798.title": "The Squeezer crushes too",
  "quest.0A65CC3994122798.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Jump on an ore block: iron ore gives two raw iron and, three times in four, a third. Wool gives string, bones white dye, flowers their dye and ice 1000 mB of water.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.405EB0F2C544D3D5.title": "The book pays",
  "quest.405EB0F2C544D3D5.quest_subtitle": "Homework with a bonus.",
  "quest.405EB0F2C544D3D5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A book and two chunks make \"},{\"text\":\"On the Dynamics of Integration\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"integrateddynamics:on_the_dynamics_of_integration\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": tutorials, a manual of every part, and a reward for each tutorial you finish. The first one alone pays 64 menril logs and 10 blocks of crystallized menril.\"}]",
    "",
    "In this pack it isn't handed out on arrival: craft it."
  ],
  "quest.703F9772D06E2D30.title": "Inventory Sensor",
  "quest.703F9772D06E2D30.quest_subtitle": "Menril goes to the Atlas.",
  "quest.703F9772D06E2D30.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two crystallized menril chunks, two LaserIO \"},{\"text\":\"Logic Chips\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"laserio:logic_chip\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a \"},{\"text\":\"Routing Matrix\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:routing_matrix\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make the \"},{\"text\":\"Inventory Sensor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:inventory_sensor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" that \"},{\"text\":\"When the Shelf is Full\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"27A67154B0D96862\"}},{\"text\":\" asks for in act III, and the Ark's bus again in act V.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4DF9DF457E6F3578.title": "Chunks for the road",
  "quest.4DF9DF457E6F3578.quest_subtitle": "The network's small change.",
  "quest.4DF9DF457E6F3578.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Sixty-four \"},{\"text\":\"Crystallized Menril Chunks\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"integrateddynamics:crystalized_menril_chunk\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for the common store, once a day. A Mechanical Squeezer pays it without a single jump.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.355F05E7E779D518.title": "Batteries and a generator",
  "quest.355F05E7E779D518.quest_subtitle": "Cables run free; machines don't.",
  "quest.355F05E7E779D518.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Networks here run without power; batteries are for the mechanical machines and for moving FE through Tunnels. An \"},{\"text\":\"Energy Battery\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"integrateddynamics:energy_battery\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" holds a million FE, and batteries crafted together add up. A battery and a furnace make a \"},{\"text\":\"Generator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"integrateddynamics:coal_generator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": 20 FE per tick.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Sneak-right-click with a battery in hand to toggle auto-supply: it charges whatever you're holding.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3CC2D73E620A4BF9.title": "No more jumping",
  "quest.3CC2D73E620A4BF9.quest_subtitle": "Your knees will thank you.",
  "quest.3CC2D73E620A4BF9.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Both run on 80 FE per tick. The \"},{\"text\":\"Mechanical Squeezer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"integrateddynamics:mechanical_squeezer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" turns a log into 1000 mB of resin plus two to four chunks in under a second, and an iron ore into three to five raw iron; the \"},{\"text\":\"Mechanical Drying Basin\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"integrateddynamics:mechanical_drying_basin\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" dries ten times faster.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.135F1ACE22AEDB23.title": "Wrench",
  "quest.135F1ACE22AEDB23.quest_subtitle": "Parts come off clean.",
  "quest.135F1ACE22AEDB23.quest_desc": [
    "Sneak and right-click a cable or part to pick it up; a plain right-click cuts the cable's link to its neighbor, and on a Display Panel it turns the screen. Sneak and right-click the air to switch modes."
  ],
  "quest.52C23D0EFE05DC3C.title": "Facades and offsets",
  "quest.52C23D0EFE05DC3C.quest_subtitle": "Hide the cable, stretch the reach.",
  "quest.52C23D0EFE05DC3C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A chunk and four slimeballs make 32 \"},{\"text\":\"Facades\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"integrateddynamics:facade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; crafted with any block, a facade wears its look and hides a cable. Right-click a part with an \"},{\"text\":\"Offset Enhancement\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"integrateddynamics:enhancement_offset\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and it reaches 4 blocks further, up to 32; aim it in its Offset screen or with the wrench's offset mode.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6941BE0EFBB3E988.title": "Mono-Directional Connector",
  "quest.6941BE0EFBB3E988.quest_subtitle": "A cable made of line of sight.",
  "quest.6941BE0EFBB3E988.quest_desc": [
    "Two of them in a straight line, up to 512 blocks apart, join their networks with no cable in between. They light up once the link holds."
  ],
  "quest.47BE4CD0448F189F.title": "Part settings",
  "quest.47BE4CD0448F189F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The button at the top left of a part's screen opens its settings: \"},{\"text\":\"Ticks/Operation\",\"color\":\"#66D9EF\"},{\"text\":\" to run it less often, \"},{\"text\":\"Priority\",\"color\":\"#66D9EF\"},{\"text\":\" to order parts within a tick, and \"},{\"text\":\"Target Side\",\"color\":\"#66D9EF\"},{\"text\":\" to pick which face of the block it works on.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1870FB7DC1253B21.title": "Network diagnostics",
  "quest.1870FB7DC1253B21.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Lag from a network? A server operator can run /integrateddynamics networkdiagnostics: it opens a web page with each network's tick time, a highlight in the world and a button to teleport there.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.62212761D66CEE3C.title": "What's inside",
  "quest.62212761D66CEE3C.quest_subtitle": "Count before you move.",
  "quest.62212761D66CEE3C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Inventory Reader\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"integrateddynamics:part_inventory_reader\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" counts items, slots and fill ratio; the \"},{\"text\":\"Fluid Reader\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"integrateddynamics:part_fluid_reader\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" measures tanks; the \"},{\"text\":\"Machine Reader\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"integrateddynamics:part_machine_reader\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" knows whether a machine is working, its stored FE and the recipes it runs.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.37B0C25B6729D929.title": "What's out there",
  "quest.37B0C25B6729D929.quest_subtitle": "Four more eyes.",
  "quest.37B0C25B6729D929.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Block Reader\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"integrateddynamics:part_block_reader\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" names the block in front of it, the \"},{\"text\":\"Entity Reader\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"integrateddynamics:part_entity_reader\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" sees who stands there, the \"},{\"text\":\"World Reader\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"integrateddynamics:part_world_reader\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" knows day from night, and the \"},{\"text\":\"Extra-Dimensional Reader\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"integrateddynamics:part_extradimensional_reader\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" reads the server: players, TPS, even a random number.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1F17AD2148ECAFB1.title": "Dynamic Light Panel",
  "quest.1F17AD2148ECAFB1.quest_subtitle": "Mood lighting, by the numbers.",
  "quest.1F17AD2148ECAFB1.quest_desc": [
    "Four redstone dust around a Static Light Panel. A Boolean card switches it on and off; an Integer card sets its brightness: a lamp that tells you how full the tank is."
  ],
  "quest.3DCEC9F743591CD9.title": "Sound and sparks",
  "quest.3DCEC9F743591CD9.quest_subtitle": "Your base, now with a voice.",
  "quest.3DCEC9F743591CD9.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Audio Writer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"integrateddynamics:part_audio_writer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" plays any note of any instrument, any sound by name, and reads text aloud; the \"},{\"text\":\"Audio Reader\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"integrateddynamics:part_audio_reader\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" hears note blocks nearby. The \"},{\"text\":\"Effect Writer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"integrateddynamics:part_effect_writer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" throws particles on cue.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.202501665D81F47B.title": "Writers with nothing to say",
  "quest.202501665D81F47B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Entity Writer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"integrateddynamics:part_entity_writer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and \"},{\"text\":\"Machine Writer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"integrateddynamics:part_machine_writer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" have no aspects in this pack, and the \"},{\"text\":\"Inventory Writer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"integrateddynamics:part_inventory_writer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" only gets some on a Refined Storage network. The tooltip warns you before you spend the materials.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1F1E836B88767D8B.title": "Autocrafting on command",
  "quest.1F1E836B88767D8B.quest_subtitle": "Refined Storage takes orders.",
  "quest.1F1E836B88767D8B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Aimed at a block of a \"},{\"text\":\"Refined Storage\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"09DFA10FF144C082\"}},{\"text\":\" network, an Inventory Writer's \"},{\"text\":\"RS craft item\",\"color\":\"#66D9EF\"},{\"text\":\" aspect starts a crafting job for an Item card; its properties set how many and whether to skip what's already stored. An Inventory Reader there lists every stored and craftable item.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.6B08B562E0F89962.title": "Play a wet sponge's step",
  "quest.1097BFC3E34EEB17.title": "Wet footsteps",
  "quest.1097BFC3E34EEB17.quest_subtitle": "Squish.",
  "quest.1097BFC3E34EEB17.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An Audio Writer fed the \"},{\"text\":\"Block Step Sound\",\"color\":\"#66D9EF\"},{\"text\":\" of a Wet Sponge: the network just learned to squelch.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.2F80DF81C8F57A77.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.6F914BAD51E8EE43.title": "Value types",
  "quest.6F914BAD51E8EE43.quest_desc": [
    "Every card has a type: Boolean, Integer, Long, Double, String, List, Operator, NBT, Block, Item, Entity, Fluid, Ingredients or Recipe. Integers stop just past two billion, Longs go much further, and a list holds a single type."
  ],
  "quest.073EB6EEF8A1B0CC.title": "Labeller",
  "quest.073EB6EEF8A1B0CC.quest_subtitle": "Card 47 is a terrible name.",
  "quest.073EB6EEF8A1B0CC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Errors point at cards by ID number; a \"},{\"text\":\"Labeller\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"integrateddynamics:labeller\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" gives them names you'll recognize. Carry it and the Logic Programmer's E button, or \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.integrateddynamics.logic_programmer_open_rename\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\", names each card as it's written.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7F4419664F1CA29A.title": "Programmer shortcuts",
  "quest.7F4419664F1CA29A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"In the Logic Programmer, \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.integrateddynamics.logic_programmer_focus_search\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" jumps to the search box, and a card in a bottom-left slot filters the operators to those taking or giving that type.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.292BBEC0B9BFE58E.title": "If, and, or",
  "quest.292BBEC0B9BFE58E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"And\",\"color\":\"#66D9EF\"},{\"text\":\", \"},{\"text\":\"Or\",\"color\":\"#66D9EF\"},{\"text\":\" and \"},{\"text\":\"Not\",\"color\":\"#66D9EF\"},{\"text\":\" combine Boolean cards, and \"},{\"text\":\"Choice\",\"color\":\"#66D9EF\"},{\"text\":\" is the if: a Boolean first, then the value to use when true and the one when false, both of the same type.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.00B0D67187BD7CBD.title": "Materialize a card",
  "quest.61DAEF084346B4B7.title": "Materializer",
  "quest.61DAEF084346B4B7.quest_subtitle": "Freeze the moment.",
  "quest.61DAEF084346B4B7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A dynamic card on top and a blank one in the slot: the \"},{\"text\":\"Materializer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"integrateddynamics:materializer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" writes the value of that very moment as a static card. Good for logging a reading, or keeping a result once its source is gone.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.007E2BCB837EF531.title": "Delayer",
  "quest.007E2BCB837EF531.quest_subtitle": "The network grows a memory.",
  "quest.007E2BCB837EF531.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Give the \"},{\"text\":\"Delayer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"integrateddynamics:delay\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" a card and the cards it writes read that value's history as a list, newest last, up to 1024 entries. Averages, differences and trends are one operator away.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.23A7A414F86B3C23.title": "Show the list 1, 10, 100",
  "task.39DE3B4BAA036320.title": "Name an item's mod",
  "task.5499EDB3903532E4.title": "What is it looking at?",
  "quest.769D10DB3610D9AA.title": "Lists, items, eyes",
  "quest.769D10DB3610D9AA.quest_subtitle": "What is it, and whose?",
  "quest.769D10DB3610D9AA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"On a Display Panel: a static List of 1, 10 and 100; the mod behind an Item card, through \"},{\"text\":\"Mod\",\"color\":\"#66D9EF\"},{\"text\":\"; and, from an Entity Reader, the block its target is looking at, through \"},{\"text\":\"Target Block\",\"color\":\"#66D9EF\"},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "task.1334C88F37DDD948.title": "Read the crafting recipes",
  "task.4F5D0D96AD687954.title": "Build a recipe",
  "task.1D34DCF7C5079547.title": "Look up the chest",
  "quest.14CB2BEA95F441FA.title": "Recipes as values",
  "quest.14CB2BEA95F441FA.quest_subtitle": "The crafting table, read aloud.",
  "quest.14CB2BEA95F441FA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Machine Reader on a Crafting Table reads its \"},{\"text\":\"Recipes\",\"color\":\"#66D9EF\"},{\"text\":\"; the Logic Programmer builds a Recipe by hand; and \"},{\"text\":\"Apply\",\"color\":\"#66D9EF\"},{\"text\":\" on the reader's \"},{\"text\":\"Recipe By Output\",\"color\":\"#66D9EF\"},{\"text\":\", with Ingredients holding one Chest, shows how a chest is made.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.34CBE36AEFF877E0.title": "Read the lectern",
  "task.72A6553B8F7AD0B2.title": "Open the Book compound",
  "task.7B429106204D2E5B.title": "Find the book's id",
  "quest.110BF9FFB4CD1F26.title": "NBT, the fallback",
  "quest.110BF9FFB4CD1F26.quest_subtitle": "For when no aspect covers it.",
  "quest.110BF9FFB4CD1F26.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Block Reader on a lectern holding a book reads its \"},{\"text\":\"Tile Entity NBT\",\"color\":\"#66D9EF\"},{\"text\":\". Take the Book compound from it, then the book's id with the NBT Path \"},{\"text\":\".Book.id\",\"color\":\"#66D9EF\"},{\"text\":\": a path reaches deep fields in one step.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.2C7488506C6EA61F.title": "A Creeper's health",
  "task.5C2FF6AE5274F7BD.title": "Stone against obsidian",
  "quest.4F02807EA82A8C59.title": "Challenges",
  "quest.4F02807EA82A8C59.quest_subtitle": "Spoiler: the pickaxe can't.",
  "quest.4F02807EA82A8C59.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The book's challenges come without hints. Show a Creeper's health on a Display Panel, and ask \"},{\"text\":\"Can Harvest\",\"color\":\"#66D9EF\"},{\"text\":\" whether a Stone Pickaxe can mine Obsidian.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.0A9D57468E2DFA28.title": "Show an infinite list",
  "quest.55949233ABB05C89.title": "Lists all the way down",
  "quest.55949233ABB05C89.quest_subtitle": "It never ends. Literally.",
  "quest.55949233ABB05C89.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Lazy List Builder\",\"color\":\"#66D9EF\"},{\"text\":\" takes a start value and an operator that turns each element into the next: a list with no end, on a Display Panel.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.2F7869BBE49B5105.title": "Secret found",
  "task.5E1BF3813B4CA159.title": "Open by day only",
  "task.2D87ADE49661DF85.title": "One mod only",
  "quest.257495E598A9C4A2.title": "Filtering Interface",
  "quest.257495E598A9C4A2.quest_subtitle": "Storage with opening hours.",
  "quest.257495E598A9C4A2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two interfaces and a hopper make a \"},{\"text\":\"Filtering Item Interface\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"integratedtunnels:part_interface_filter_item\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", which decides what the network may see. Bind \"},{\"text\":\"Is Day\",\"color\":\"#66D9EF\"},{\"text\":\" and the chest vanishes at night; \"},{\"text\":\"Pipe\",\"color\":\"#66D9EF\"},{\"text\":\" \"},{\"text\":\"Mod\",\"color\":\"#66D9EF\"},{\"text\":\" into \"},{\"text\":\"Equals\",\"color\":\"#66D9EF\"},{\"text\":\" applied to IntegratedDynamics and only that mod's items pass.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6AF012B4D6C7F2F3.title": "Fluid tunnels",
  "quest.6AF012B4D6C7F2F3.quest_subtitle": "Same logic, wetter.",
  "quest.6AF012B4D6C7F2F3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Five chunks and a bucket make four \"},{\"text\":\"Fluid Interfaces\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"integratedtunnels:part_interface_fluid\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", and the fluid importer and exporter come from them like the item ones. Their aspects take Fluid cards, amounts in mB per tick, lists and predicates.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0DE53C876E314F3A.title": "Network Reader",
  "quest.0DE53C876E314F3A.quest_subtitle": "The network counts itself.",
  "quest.0DE53C876E314F3A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Aimed at any cable of a Tunnels network, the \"},{\"text\":\"Network Reader\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"integrateddynamics:part_network_reader\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" reads it whole: \"},{\"text\":\"Network Item Count\",\"color\":\"#66D9EF\"},{\"text\":\", every stack as a list, and \"},{\"text\":\"Network Count Of Item\",\"color\":\"#66D9EF\"},{\"text\":\", an operator that counts one item across every interface.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.061A000C3BD518DE.title": "Energy tunnels",
  "quest.061A000C3BD518DE.quest_subtitle": "Power rides the logic cable.",
  "quest.061A000C3BD518DE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Five chunks and an Energy Battery make four \"},{\"text\":\"Energy Interfaces\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"integratedtunnels:part_interface_energy\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Put an importer on a generator, interfaces on batteries and exporters on machines: FE rides the same cables as your logic.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.54FC4362CD0A37B1.title": "Channels",
  "quest.54FC4362CD0A37B1.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Two tunnels on one network? Give their interfaces different \"},{\"text\":\"Interface Channel\",\"color\":\"#66D9EF\"},{\"text\":\" numbers in the part settings and set the matching \"},{\"text\":\"Channel\",\"color\":\"#66D9EF\"},{\"text\":\" property on each importer or exporter; channel -1 reaches them all.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4F1A09D988FF7591.title": "Crystallized Chorus",
  "quest.4F1A09D988FF7591.quest_subtitle": "The End, squeezed.",
  "quest.4F1A09D988FF7591.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Each \"},{\"text\":\"Popped Chorus Fruit\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:popped_chorus_fruit\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" squeezes into 125 mB of Liquid Chorus, and 1000 mB dry into a block of nine \"},{\"text\":\"Crystallized Chorus Chunks\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"integrateddynamics:crystalized_chorus_chunk\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". No End yet? Two menril berries and two ender pearls make a \"},{\"text\":\"Proto Chorus\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"integrateddynamics:proto_chorus\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" that squeezes the same.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4DBC8C1E45EF8C3A.title": "Logic Director",
  "quest.4DBC8C1E45EF8C3A.quest_subtitle": "Menril thinks, chorus points.",
  "quest.4DBC8C1E45EF8C3A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four chorus chunks, two menril chunks and a diamond make four \"},{\"text\":\"Logic Directors\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"integrateddynamics:logic_director\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Every world part of Tunnels takes one, and the Omni-Directional Connector two.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.287131684A32618B.title": "Items into the world",
  "quest.287131684A32618B.quest_subtitle": "Hoppers only dream of this.",
  "quest.287131684A32618B.quest_desc": [
    "An item importer or exporter plus a Logic Director becomes a world part: it picks up dropped items and throws them back out, with speed, angle and pickup delay as properties. It also reaches entities with an inventory, like a donkey or a dropped shulker box."
  ],
  "quest.6340C4AFAAE246B7.title": "Break and place",
  "quest.6340C4AFAAE246B7.quest_subtitle": "A quarry one block wide.",
  "quest.6340C4AFAAE246B7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Add a \"},{\"text\":\"Diamond Pickaxe\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:diamond_pickaxe\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" to each: the \"},{\"text\":\"World Block Importer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"integratedtunnels:part_importer_world_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" breaks the block it faces, with Silk Touch as a property, and the \"},{\"text\":\"World Block Exporter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"integratedtunnels:part_exporter_world_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" places blocks from the network.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.48C0C9DB04B11312.title": "Swing a Diamond Sword",
  "quest.46EA12AA83949FEF.title": "Player Simulator",
  "quest.46EA12AA83949FEF.quest_subtitle": "Clicking, outsourced.",
  "quest.46EA12AA83949FEF.quest_desc": [
    "All four world parts around an emerald. It clicks with any item from the network: either hand, sneaking or not, once or held down. Give it a Diamond Sword card and it fights on its own."
  ],
  "task.6B4FA84DD7301EFA.title": "Break only stone",
  "task.4626F1B650A95435.title": "Place logs by tag",
  "quest.09C8DA0F31E0FA99.title": "Only stone, only logs",
  "quest.09C8DA0F31E0FA99.quest_subtitle": "Picky on purpose.",
  "quest.09C8DA0F31E0FA99.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Block card of Stone in the importer's \"},{\"text\":\"Pick Up Block\",\"color\":\"#66D9EF\"},{\"text\":\" breaks nothing else. For the exporter, \"},{\"text\":\"Item Tag Values\",\"color\":\"#66D9EF\"},{\"text\":\" on the logs tag gives a list for \"},{\"text\":\"Place Item Blocks\",\"color\":\"#66D9EF\"},{\"text\":\": any log, and nothing but logs.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5D41544DEAC48D30.title": "Pour, pump and charge",
  "quest.5D41544DEAC48D30.quest_subtitle": "A bucket with ideas of its own.",
  "quest.5D41544DEAC48D30.quest_desc": [
    "With a Logic Director, the fluid and energy importers and exporters work on the world: the fluid ones pick up and place source blocks, and all four fill or drain entities that carry a tank or a battery."
  ],
  "task.75A9DD6F301A416C.title": "Drop everything",
  "quest.647B4537F23D8D45.title": "Everything on the floor",
  "quest.647B4537F23D8D45.quest_subtitle": "You did mean to, right?",
  "quest.647B4537F23D8D45.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Boolean true in \"},{\"text\":\"Place All Item Entities\",\"color\":\"#66D9EF\"},{\"text\":\" and the network empties itself onto the ground, stack by stack.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.6BD9111BE8182F77.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.7ADCDCDE756D6AA4.title": "Omni-Directional Connector",
  "quest.7ADCDCDE756D6AA4.quest_subtitle": "One network, many dimensions.",
  "quest.7ADCDCDE756D6AA4.quest_desc": [
    "Two Logic Directors, two Mono-Directional Connectors and a cable. Connectors of one group join their networks wherever they are, other dimensions included; a new craft starts a new group, and crafting with a connector you already have adds to its group."
  ],
  "image.56F248737F6C80C8.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Menril grove\",\"color\":\"#66D9EF\"}]",
  "image.780BF968A2CB7697.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Power\",\"color\":\"#66D9EF\"}]",
  "image.40EC2169C46CAA56.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Cable work\",\"color\":\"#66D9EF\"}]",
  "image.1453ADD136B701F3.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Readers\",\"color\":\"#66D9EF\"}]",
  "image.7ADF477EA16FDDE7.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Writers\",\"color\":\"#66D9EF\"}]",
  "image.39D56F2FC98DB8C8.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"At the programmer\",\"color\":\"#66D9EF\"}]",
  "image.6CC3D695962FBEA0.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Memory\",\"color\":\"#66D9EF\"}]",
  "image.50EAD24021512788.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The book's tutorials\",\"color\":\"#66D9EF\"}]",
  "image.1B53FABF85B10748.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Tunnels\",\"color\":\"#66D9EF\"}]",
  "image.2B85D662C6B9D548.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Into the world\",\"color\":\"#66D9EF\"}]",
  "image.57E0DDFACC4BE794.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Integrated Dynamics\\nand Tunnels\",\"color\":\"#EAFBFF\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.3A9CBBFFF125688A.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"read · decide · move\",\"color\":\"#9DDEEC\",\"font\":\"minecraft:uniform\"}]",
  "image.6D592375A9494096.title": "Back to the Sun of Heliodor",
  "chapter.15BF37D12C480327.title": "Just Dire Things · Goo and Gear",
  "chapter.15BF37D12C480327.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Four goos that eat blocks and leave better ones: Ferricore, Blazegold, Celestigem and Eclipse Alloy, with the tools, armor and upgrades each one opens."
  ],
  "task.29B5707A7AA2704F.title": "Wake it up",
  "quest.33971CF3851DF109.title": "Primogel Goo",
  "quest.33971CF3851DF109.quest_subtitle": "It's alive. Mostly.",
  "quest.33971CF3851DF109.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four \"},{\"text\":\"Clay Balls\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:clay_ball\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", two \"},{\"text\":\"Sugar\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:sugar\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", two \"},{\"text\":\"Rotten Flesh\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:rotten_flesh\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and one \"},{\"text\":\"Dirt\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:dirt\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make \"},{\"text\":\"Primogel Goo\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"justdirethings:gooblock_tier1\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It sits dormant when placed: right-click it with sugar or rotten flesh and it wakes, ready to eat the blocks around it.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.4EED14B0AB003AA6.title": "Just Dire's Guide",
  "quest.2E126AE3714D3399.title": "The dire manual",
  "quest.2E126AE3714D3399.quest_subtitle": "Dire reading, in the good sense.",
  "quest.2E126AE3714D3399.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Book\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:book\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a Primogel Goo, shapeless, make Just Dire's Guide: every goo, machine, tool and upgrade with its recipe. The recipe viewer adds Goo Spreading and Fluid Drop tabs for the changes that happen in the world.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.707DFC8016CB1DCF.title": "One goo, six faces",
  "quest.707DFC8016CB1DCF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A goo works on all six faces at once, so surround it with blocks to convert. Blazebloom runs twice as fast as Primogel, VoidShimmer five times and Shadowpulse ten times, and every goo also does the recipes of the tiers below it.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Each finished block has a 10% chance of putting the goo back to sleep. A sleeping goo finishes what it started but begins nothing new."
  ],
  "task.74F08EA92A727218.title": "Ferricore Honeycomb",
  "quest.3CE879C5E7229F13.title": "Goo-fed bees",
  "quest.3CE879C5E7229F13.quest_subtitle": "The iron bee had it coming.",
  "quest.3CE879C5E7229F13.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"With \"},{\"text\":\"Productive Bees\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"1C397532F8FEF781\"}},{\"text\":\", an Iron Bee fed a Primogel Goo turns into a Ferricore Bee, whose combs spin into \"},{\"text\":\"Raw Ferricore\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"justdirethings:raw_ferricore\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" 80% of the time. Gold Bees take Blazebloom, Diamond Bees VoidShimmer and Ancient Bees Shadowpulse.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "The odds drop with the tier: 60% for Raw Blazegold, 40% for Celestigem and 20% for Raw Eclipse Alloy."
  ],
  "quest.029C6C63C1D5064D.title": "Ferricore",
  "quest.029C6C63C1D5064D.quest_subtitle": "Iron that went to the gym.",
  "quest.029C6C63C1D5064D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An awake Primogel Goo turns a touching \"},{\"text\":\"Block of Iron\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:iron_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" into \"},{\"text\":\"Raw Ferricore Ore\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"justdirethings:raw_ferricore_ore\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in two minutes. Mine it without Silk Touch for three or four \"},{\"text\":\"Raw Ferricore\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"justdirethings:raw_ferricore\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and smelt them into \"},{\"text\":\"Ferricore Ingots\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"justdirethings:ferricore_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5346D080DD8EC0E9.title": "Ferricore for the common store",
  "quest.5346D080DD8EC0E9.quest_subtitle": "About nine blocks of iron, digested.",
  "quest.5346D080DD8EC0E9.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Thirty-two \"},{\"text\":\"Ferricore Ingots\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"justdirethings:ferricore_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", once a day. Blank Upgrades, the first machines and every template start here, so the store never has enough.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5AC1205779494828.title": "Ferricore tools",
  "quest.5AC1205779494828.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The iron shapes with \"},{\"text\":\"Ferricore Ingots\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"justdirethings:ferricore_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": they mine like iron, last 500 uses against iron's 250 and dig a little faster. The extended tooltip of each one lists the upgrades it takes; the hoe tills Primogel Soil.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3C94D3074187F71D.title": "Ferricore armor",
  "quest.3C94D3074187F71D.quest_desc": [
    "Iron's protection and durability in four pieces that learn tricks: each slot has its own list, from Mind Fog on the helmet to Step Assist on the boots, and every trick it learns here still fits the tiers above."
  ],
  "quest.70326800B28E4D69.title": "Blank Upgrade",
  "quest.70326800B28E4D69.quest_subtitle": "Every trick starts blank.",
  "quest.70326800B28E4D69.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four \"},{\"text\":\"Ferricore Ingots\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"justdirethings:ferricore_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make an \"},{\"text\":\"Upgrade: Blank\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"justdirethings:upgrade_blank\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", the base of every upgrade. Put the tool or armor piece and a finished upgrade in a \"},{\"text\":\"Smithing Table\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:smithing_table\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" with the template slot empty, and it learns the ability for good.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Each piece takes each upgrade once, and only those its tier allows: the extended tooltip lists them."
  ],
  "quest.278068AD8E06B9E6.title": "Two keys and a click",
  "quest.278068AD8E06B9E6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"justdirethings.key.toggle_tool\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" switches every ability of the held tool on or off; \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"justdirethings.key.toolUI\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\", or \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.sneak\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" and right-click, opens its settings. There a click toggles one ability and a right-click binds it to a key or a mouse button.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "The same screen reaches the armor you wear: click a worn piece to edit its abilities. A passive ability's key toggles it; an active one's key fires it."
  ],
  "quest.06DDA5E67EC2D5B0.title": "One pile",
  "quest.06DDA5E67EC2D5B0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"When an ability breaks many blocks at once, like the Hammer, the Ore Miner or the Tree Feller, everything they drop lands in one pile on the block you struck, experience included.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3448417EAD242327.title": "Broken, not lost",
  "quest.3448417EAD242327.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"When a Ferricore or Blazegold piece breaks, its installed upgrades fall back out as items. Celestigem and Eclipse Alloy gear runs on FE instead of durability and never breaks.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.232FF7A8F80DDE99.title": "Mind Fog",
  "quest.232FF7A8F80DDE99.quest_subtitle": "You were never here.",
  "quest.232FF7A8F80DDE99.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two \"},{\"text\":\"Fermented Spider Eyes\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:fermented_spider_eye\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and two \"},{\"text\":\"Lapis Lazuli\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:lapis_lazuli\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" around a blank make \"},{\"text\":\"Mind Fog\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"justdirethings:upgrade_mindfog\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for any helmet. Mobs only notice you within half their follow range: a third on Blazegold, a quarter on Celestigem, a fifth on Eclipse Alloy.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.21AE589E7437CF89.title": "Invulnerability",
  "quest.21AE589E7437CF89.quest_subtitle": "Ten seconds of nope.",
  "quest.21AE589E7437CF89.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two \"},{\"text\":\"Diamond Chestplates\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:diamond_chestplate\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and two \"},{\"text\":\"Shields\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:shield\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" around a blank. It needs a key of its own: press it for 10 seconds immune to all damage, then wait a minute to use it again, 30 seconds on Celestigem and 20 on Eclipse Alloy.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.19EAA5D1EA0A822A.title": "Walk and run",
  "quest.19EAA5D1EA0A822A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Sugar\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:sugar\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" with \"},{\"text\":\"Carrots\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:carrot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" makes \"},{\"text\":\"Walk Speed\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"justdirethings:upgrade_walkspeed\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; with \"},{\"text\":\"Potatoes\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:potato\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", \"},{\"text\":\"Run Speed\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"justdirethings:upgrade_runspeed\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Both go on leggings, and a slider sets the push: up to 1 on Ferricore, 2 on Blazegold, 3 on Celestigem and 5 on Eclipse Alloy.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.26ACF76C1CE96B9B.title": "Jump Boost",
  "quest.26ACF76C1CE96B9B.quest_subtitle": "Knees sold separately.",
  "quest.26ACF76C1CE96B9B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Piston\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:piston\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on each side of a blank. The boots jump higher, one level on Ferricore and up to five on Eclipse Alloy, and each level takes a block off every fall.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2FE7DB2A2CED2781.title": "Step Assist",
  "quest.2FE7DB2A2CED2781.quest_subtitle": "Stairs are optional now.",
  "quest.2FE7DB2A2CED2781.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four \"},{\"text\":\"Ladders\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:ladder\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" around a blank: any tier of boots walks up full blocks without jumping, one extra block of step height.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0181526B9AAF8491.title": "Ore Miner",
  "quest.0181526B9AAF8491.quest_subtitle": "Vein, vidi, vici.",
  "quest.0181526B9AAF8491.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An \"},{\"text\":\"Iron Pickaxe\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:iron_pickaxe\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on each side of a blank. Mining one ore takes the whole connected vein with it: up to 64 blocks on Ferricore, 128 on Blazegold, 192 on Celestigem and 256 on Eclipse Alloy.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.35768B7609460C7B.title": "Ore Scanner",
  "quest.35768B7609460C7B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two \"},{\"text\":\"Amethyst Shards\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:amethyst_shard\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and two \"},{\"text\":\"Redstone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:redstone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" around a blank. Activate it on the pickaxe and nearby ores light up through the stone as particles, every kind looking the same.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0EFC535653FBDDA8.title": "Tree Feller",
  "quest.0EFC535653FBDDA8.quest_subtitle": "Timber, in one swing.",
  "quest.0EFC535653FBDDA8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Diamond Axe\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:diamond_axe\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on each side of a blank. Cut one log and every connected log of the same wood falls with it, within the same per-tier cap as the Ore Miner.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3BA78629E99A40D4.title": "Leaf Breaker",
  "quest.3BA78629E99A40D4.quest_subtitle": "For packs without fast leaf decay.",
  "quest.3BA78629E99A40D4.quest_desc": [
    "Any two leaves around a blank. Right-click a leaf block with the axe and every connected leaf comes down too, dropping where you clicked."
  ],
  "quest.17245CE2BA543FEE.title": "Lawnmower",
  "quest.17245CE2BA543FEE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Short Grass\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:short_grass\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on each side of a blank, for the shovel. Activate it and the grass, ferns, flowers and berry bushes within five blocks are cut, up to 64 at a time.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5321067AD2EC7B0B.title": "Sky Sweeper",
  "quest.5321067AD2EC7B0B.quest_subtitle": "Oww, my head, no more.",
  "quest.5321067AD2EC7B0B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two \"},{\"text\":\"Gravel\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:gravel\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and two \"},{\"text\":\"Sand\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:sand\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" around a blank, for the shovel. Break one gravel or sand block and the matching column above it comes down with it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1FA7601E5D3D5DF3.title": "Mob Scanner",
  "quest.1FA7601E5D3D5DF3.quest_subtitle": "What's making THAT noise?",
  "quest.1FA7601E5D3D5DF3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two \"},{\"text\":\"Spider Eyes\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:spider_eye\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and two \"},{\"text\":\"Amethyst Shards\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:amethyst_shard\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" around a blank, for swords from Ferricore to Celestigem. Activate it and nearby mobs show through the walls as particles.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.319D1497FA3A8C5F.title": "Primogel Soil",
  "quest.319D1497FA3A8C5F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A switched-on Ferricore Hoe tills \"},{\"text\":\"Primogel Soil\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"justdirethings:goosoil_tier1\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" instead of farmland: it can't be trampled, and every random tick while watered it ages the crop above by one stage. It also grows cactus, sugar cane, bamboo and nether wart.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.36448DFFEDE4B6BD.title": "Ferricore Bow",
  "quest.36448DFFEDE4B6BD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three \"},{\"text\":\"String\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:string\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and three Ferricore make a bow with 250 uses and one Potion Canister slot in its settings. The tiers above draw faster: 17 ticks on Blazegold, 14 on Celestigem, 10 on Eclipse Alloy, against the usual 20.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.478F3C01E963F2AE.title": "Potion Arrows",
  "quest.478F3C01E963F2AE.quest_subtitle": "Like tipped arrows, without the crafting.",
  "quest.478F3C01E963F2AE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Potion Canister\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"justdirethings:potion_canister\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (four Ferricore round a \"},{\"text\":\"Glass Bottle\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:glass_bottle\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\") holds 1,000 mB, 250 per potion. Slot it in the bow's settings, install \"},{\"text\":\"Potion Arrow\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"justdirethings:upgrade_potionarrow\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (nether wart, bottles) and every arrow carries the effect.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1153F5D0877F380F.title": "Blazebloom and Blazegold",
  "quest.1153F5D0877F380F.quest_subtitle": "The goo went to the Nether and came back spicy.",
  "quest.1153F5D0877F380F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four \"},{\"text\":\"Blaze Powder\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:blaze_powder\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", two \"},{\"text\":\"Nether Wart\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:nether_wart\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and two \"},{\"text\":\"Redstone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:redstone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" around a Primogel Goo make \"},{\"text\":\"Blazebloom Goo\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"justdirethings:gooblock_tier2\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", fed with blaze powder or nether wart. It turns a \"},{\"text\":\"Block of Gold\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:gold_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" into Raw Blazegold Ore in a minute.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.00FB4EAA9055EF34.title": "Blazegold tools",
  "quest.00FB4EAA9055EF34.quest_desc": [
    "Diamond-tier mining at 12 speed, faster than diamond's 8, with 1,440 uses. Craft them fresh or carry your Ferricore ones up with a template; the hoe tills Blazebloom Soil."
  ],
  "quest.56DC82006B7F66EF.title": "Blazegold armor",
  "quest.56DC82006B7F66EF.quest_desc": [
    "Iron-level protection that lasts much longer, fire-resistant as items and enchantable like gold. It repairs itself in lava and opens a second round of armor upgrades."
  ],
  "quest.456AD35C5C20C680.title": "Templates",
  "quest.456AD35C5C20C680.quest_subtitle": "Your upgrades move up with you.",
  "quest.456AD35C5C20C680.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Five Blazegold round a Blank Upgrade make \"},{\"text\":\"Template: Blazegold\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"justdirethings:template_blazegold\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". In a Smithing Table it turns a Ferricore piece plus one ingot into its Blazegold version, every upgrade kept; the Celestigem and Eclipse Alloy templates work the same.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "A template plus two ingots of its material makes two templates."
  ],
  "quest.4AE15EE21BE7D161.title": "Skip the Ferricore template",
  "quest.4AE15EE21BE7D161.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The Ferricore template can be crafted, but no recipe in this version uses it: Ferricore gear is made straight from ingots. Save the blank.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7AE0844544E9FB73.title": "Repair it in lava",
  "quest.7AE0844544E9FB73.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Blazegold tools, armor, bows and the Blazejet Wand have Lava Repair: drop one into a lava source block and it comes back fully repaired.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7F6D3511430AEDEF.title": "Totem of Death Recall",
  "quest.7F6D3511430AEDEF.quest_subtitle": "Your stuff is where you left it. You too.",
  "quest.7F6D3511430AEDEF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four Blazegold, two \"},{\"text\":\"Diamonds\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:diamond\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", two \"},{\"text\":\"Lapis Lazuli\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:lapis_lazuli\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and an \"},{\"text\":\"Ender Pearl\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:ender_pearl\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Carry it when you die: it is spent, and you respawn holding a new one bound to that spot. Hold right-click on it for a second to go back.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2949245C7275A6AA.title": "Stupefy",
  "quest.2949245C7275A6AA.quest_subtitle": "Obliviate, but for zombies.",
  "quest.2949245C7275A6AA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four \"},{\"text\":\"Eyes of Ender\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:ender_eye\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", two \"},{\"text\":\"Fermented Spider Eyes\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:fermented_spider_eye\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and two \"},{\"text\":\"Poisonous Potatoes\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:poisonous_potato\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" round a blank, for helmets from Blazegold up. Look at a mob up to 32 blocks away and press its key: it forgets you and can't target you for five seconds.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.10B94E904A008D1B.title": "Extinguish",
  "quest.10B94E904A008D1B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two \"},{\"text\":\"Water Buckets\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:water_bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", two \"},{\"text\":\"Blaze Rods\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:blaze_rod\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and four \"},{\"text\":\"Magma Cream\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:magma_cream\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" round a blank. When you catch fire it puts you out, then rests 10 seconds; 5 on Celestigem, 2 on Eclipse Alloy.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.29C467A45753ECE5.title": "Swim Speed",
  "quest.29C467A45753ECE5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two \"},{\"text\":\"Sugar\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:sugar\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and two \"},{\"text\":\"Kelp\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:kelp\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" round a blank, for leggings from Blazegold up. It pushes you forward underwater, with a slider up to 2, 3 or 5 by tier.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.19BB643A2B5D326A.title": "Ground Stomp",
  "quest.19BB643A2B5D326A.quest_subtitle": "Personal space, enforced.",
  "quest.19BB643A2B5D326A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two \"},{\"text\":\"Pistons\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:piston\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and two \"},{\"text\":\"Slime Blocks\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:slime_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" round a blank, for boots from Blazegold up. Press its key and every mob within three blocks is thrown back; it rests 10 seconds.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3C26844C7C94A086.title": "Hammer",
  "quest.3C26844C7C94A086.quest_subtitle": "Mining, but in bulk.",
  "quest.3C26844C7C94A086.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Diamond Pickaxe\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:diamond_pickaxe\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on each side of a blank, for pickaxes, shovels and hoes from Blazegold up. They break, dig or till 3×3; Celestigem cycles up to 5×5 and Eclipse Alloy to 7×7.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4CD0A4674E4DF54F.title": "Smelter",
  "quest.4CD0A4674E4DF54F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two \"},{\"text\":\"Blast Furnaces\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:blast_furnace\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and two \"},{\"text\":\"Blaze Rods\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:blaze_rod\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" round a blank, for pickaxes, axes and shovels from Blazegold up. Whatever you break drops already smelted, for a little durability or FE.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7482ABB5E11AC833.title": "Cauterize Wounds",
  "quest.7482ABB5E11AC833.quest_subtitle": "Feel the burn.",
  "quest.7482ABB5E11AC833.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two \"},{\"text\":\"Golden Apples\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:golden_apple\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and two \"},{\"text\":\"Magma Cream\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:magma_cream\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" round a blank, for swords from Blazegold up. Activate it while hurt and you heal three hearts at once; it rests a minute.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7DD32C806B4D2BBE.title": "Smoker",
  "quest.7DD32C806B4D2BBE.quest_subtitle": "Dinner is served. Aggressively.",
  "quest.7DD32C806B4D2BBE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two \"},{\"text\":\"Smokers\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:smoker\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and two \"},{\"text\":\"Blaze Rods\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:blaze_rod\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" round a blank, for swords from Blazegold up. What you kill drops cooked: beef comes out as steak.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3D8EC13FAB4BAE24.title": "Blazebloom Soil",
  "quest.3D8EC13FAB4BAE24.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Blazegold Hoe tills \"},{\"text\":\"Blazebloom Soil\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"justdirethings:goosoil_tier2\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": two growth stages per random tick, and ripe crops harvest themselves and replant. The drops vanish after two seconds, so park an Item Collector nearby.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7CDFC8D8216E5B67.title": "Blazegold Bow",
  "quest.7CDFC8D8216E5B67.quest_desc": [
    "Three String and three Blazegold: 450 uses, a 17-tick draw, two Potion Canister slots and Lava Repair."
  ],
  "quest.289FDD347F853E82.title": "Splash",
  "quest.289FDD347F853E82.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four \"},{\"text\":\"Gunpowder\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:gunpowder\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and two \"},{\"text\":\"Glass Bottles\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:glass_bottle\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" round a blank, for bows from Blazegold up. Potion arrows burst on impact and splash their effect around.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1B71DFF60EA69B17.title": "Blazejet Wand",
  "quest.1B71DFF60EA69B17.quest_subtitle": "Safer than fireworks. Probably.",
  "quest.1B71DFF60EA69B17.quest_desc": [
    "One Blazegold on two Ferricore. Its built-in Air Burst throws you where you look, and while you hold it you take no fall damage at all; the slider sets the push."
  ],
  "quest.4BD7F2283783BCA5.title": "Wand in the off hand",
  "quest.4BD7F2283783BCA5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The no-fall-damage perk works from the off hand too, and on the Voidshift and Eclipsegate wands. Keep one there and dig down without a care.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6171EB6B3198E3EA.title": "Fire it from the inventory",
  "quest.6171EB6B3198E3EA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"In an ability's settings, switch «Activate if Equipped» to «Activate from Inventory»: its key then fires even with the tool tucked in your inventory, like an Air Burst with a sword in hand.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3C3DDECD763F0D21.title": "VoidShimmer and Celestigem",
  "quest.3C3DDECD763F0D21.quest_subtitle": "Diamonds, but they learned to hold a charge.",
  "quest.3C3DDECD763F0D21.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four \"},{\"text\":\"Ender Pearls\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:ender_pearl\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", two \"},{\"text\":\"End Stone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:end_stone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and two \"},{\"text\":\"Dragon's Breath\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:dragon_breath\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" around a Blazebloom Goo make \"},{\"text\":\"VoidShimmer Goo\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"justdirethings:gooblock_tier3\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", fed with chorus fruit or ender pearls. It turns a \"},{\"text\":\"Block of Diamond\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:diamond_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" into Raw Celestigem Ore in 48 seconds.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.531C8848E642FA27.title": "Celestigem tools",
  "quest.531C8848E642FA27.quest_subtitle": "Batteries included, charger sold separately.",
  "quest.531C8848E642FA27.quest_desc": [
    "Diamond-tier tools that run on FE instead of durability: 10,000 FE each, 50 per block. Craft them or carry your Blazegold ones up with a Celestigem template; the hoe tills VoidShimmer Soil."
  ],
  "quest.6A768D0F2EE4B495.title": "Celestigem armor",
  "quest.6A768D0F2EE4B495.quest_desc": [
    "Diamond protection and toughness, powered by 10,000 FE per piece: each point of damage it soaks costs 100 FE. Keep a Pocket Generator on you."
  ],
  "quest.10FB1DD541D51B51.title": "Celestigem Paxel",
  "quest.10FB1DD541D51B51.quest_subtitle": "Three tools walk into a smithing table.",
  "quest.10FB1DD541D51B51.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"In a Smithing Table, a Celestigem Pickaxe as the template, the Axe as the base and the Shovel as the addition make one \"},{\"text\":\"Celestigem Paxel\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"justdirethings:celestigem_paxel\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It keeps every upgrade and enchantment of the three.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.58C445EC82D97FF7.title": "Pocket Generator",
  "quest.58C445EC82D97FF7.quest_subtitle": "A furnace in your pocket, for the gear.",
  "quest.58C445EC82D97FF7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four Ferricore, a \"},{\"text\":\"Furnace\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:furnace\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", two \"},{\"text\":\"Coal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:coal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and two \"},{\"text\":\"Blocks of Redstone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:redstone_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Switched on, it burns fuel from its slot and charges every FE item you carry, Curios slots included, up to 5,000 FE/t each; the JDT coals burn hotter in it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.12A8373CF8A5E561.title": "Mind the charge",
  "quest.12A8373CF8A5E561.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"FE tools never break, but below 50 FE they lose their attack bonuses. Unbreaking still works on them: each level cuts the FE they spend by 10%.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.34C8323A852A7C44.title": "Night Vision",
  "quest.34C8323A852A7C44.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two \"},{\"text\":\"Eyes of Ender\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:ender_eye\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and two \"},{\"text\":\"Golden Carrots\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:golden_carrot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" round a blank, for helmets from Celestigem up: permanent night vision, paid in FE.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.531C53F21016155C.title": "Water Breathing",
  "quest.531C53F21016155C.quest_subtitle": "Just keep swimming.",
  "quest.531C53F21016155C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two \"},{\"text\":\"Prismarine Shards\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:prismarine_shard\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", two \"},{\"text\":\"Pufferfish\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:pufferfish\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", two Kelp and two Blazegold round a blank. Underwater, whenever your air drops below half, it refills it for 500 FE.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0F1BD1DEA21384C7.title": "Elytra",
  "quest.0F1BD1DEA21384C7.quest_subtitle": "Wings, now in chestplate.",
  "quest.0F1BD1DEA21384C7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An \"},{\"text\":\"Elytra\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:elytra\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a blank, shapeless: chestplates from Celestigem up glide like elytra without taking the slot, and crashing into walls stops hurting.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0441ADC9B761D44D.title": "Decoy",
  "quest.0441ADC9B761D44D.quest_subtitle": "Look, a distraction!",
  "quest.0441ADC9B761D44D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two \"},{\"text\":\"Wither Skeleton Skulls\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:wither_skeleton_skull\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", two \"},{\"text\":\"Armor Stands\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:armor_stand\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and four \"},{\"text\":\"Phantom Membranes\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:phantom_membrane\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" round a blank, for leggings from Celestigem up. Its key drops a decoy of you that every nearby mob attacks for 10 seconds.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2F3542F9BC9886C9.title": "Negate Fall Damage",
  "quest.2F3542F9BC9886C9.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two \"},{\"text\":\"Leather\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:leather\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and two wool round a blank, for boots from Celestigem up. Falls do no damage; each block fallen costs 50 FE, so a long drop on Celestigem boots can empty them.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.38862720C332B434.title": "Look at your decoy",
  "quest.20EFC3647C5AE4AF.title": "Handsome devil",
  "quest.20EFC3647C5AE4AF.quest_subtitle": "It has your good side.",
  "quest.20EFC3647C5AE4AF.quest_desc": [
    "You stared at your own decoy while the mobs took turns punching it. It lasts ten seconds and shares your name."
  ],
  "reward.570FF2F983382484.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.4338EA9F6D6BC84B.title": "Bottomless",
  "quest.4338EA9F6D6BC84B.quest_subtitle": "The ground was mostly a suggestion.",
  "quest.4338EA9F6D6BC84B.quest_desc": [
    "You fell from the top of the world to the bottom and walked away. Negate Fall Damage or a wand in hand turn it into a stroll."
  ],
  "reward.395C4758ADA913EF.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.2D97C4CA5B0F6C52.title": "Drops Teleport",
  "quest.2D97C4CA5B0F6C52.quest_subtitle": "My inventory is a mess. Not anymore.",
  "quest.2D97C4CA5B0F6C52.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two \"},{\"text\":\"Ender Chests\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:ender_chest\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", two \"},{\"text\":\"Amethyst Shards\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:amethyst_shard\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and four Ender Pearls round a blank, for Celestigem and Eclipse Alloy tools. \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.sneak\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" and right-click a chest with the tool to bind it: ore and mob drops go straight there.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0CB8633259DBC9F4.title": "VoidShimmer Soil",
  "quest.0CB8633259DBC9F4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Celestigem Hoe tills \"},{\"text\":\"VoidShimmer Soil\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"justdirethings:goosoil_tier3\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": three growth stages per random tick and self-harvesting. Till it with a hoe bound by Drops Teleport and the harvest goes to that chest.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7D2F9A08DC41242B.title": "Voidshift Wand",
  "quest.7D2F9A08DC41242B.quest_subtitle": "Walls are just suggestions.",
  "quest.7D2F9A08DC41242B.quest_desc": [
    "A Celestigem and a Blazegold on a Blazejet Wand. It keeps Air Burst and adds Void Shift: teleport to the spot you look at, up to 15 blocks away, 50 FE per block traveled."
  ],
  "quest.4D88D678B62F684E.title": "Celestigem Bow",
  "quest.4D88D678B62F684E.quest_desc": [
    "Three String and three Celestigem: a 14-tick draw, three Potion Canister slots and FE instead of durability."
  ],
  "quest.35EF6C378D81E1E7.title": "Homing Arrow",
  "quest.35EF6C378D81E1E7.quest_subtitle": "Aim is overrated.",
  "quest.35EF6C378D81E1E7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four \"},{\"text\":\"Eyes of Ender\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:ender_eye\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and two \"},{\"text\":\"Targets\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:target\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" round a blank, for bows from Celestigem up. Arrows curve toward the nearest target; 2,000 FE a shot.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6EDAE4DB85639ED7.title": "Lingering",
  "quest.6EDAE4DB85639ED7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four \"},{\"text\":\"Dragon's Breath\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:dragon_breath\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and two Glass Bottles round a blank, for bows from Celestigem up. Potion arrows leave a lingering cloud where they land.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.698AA53BB5EF5936.title": "Called shot",
  "quest.698AA53BB5EF5936.quest_subtitle": "The arrow did most of the work.",
  "quest.698AA53BB5EF5936.quest_desc": [
    "A skeleton down from fifty meters. With homing arrows the hard part was seeing it."
  ],
  "reward.1157F5CC666E8E3C.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.3C0722B85E6E4444.title": "Shadowpulse and Eclipse Alloy",
  "quest.3C0722B85E6E4444.quest_subtitle": "Bring back something from the Deep Dark. Quietly.",
  "quest.3C0722B85E6E4444.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four \"},{\"text\":\"Sculk\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:sculk\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", two \"},{\"text\":\"Sculk Shriekers\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:sculk_shrieker\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and two \"},{\"text\":\"Echo Shards\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:echo_shard\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" around a VoidShimmer Goo make \"},{\"text\":\"Shadowpulse Goo\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"justdirethings:gooblock_tier4\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", fed with sculk or a sculk catalyst. It turns a \"},{\"text\":\"Block of Netherite\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:netherite_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" into Raw Eclipse Alloy Ore in 24 seconds.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5E7A12CC4FDD903D.title": "Eclipse Alloy tools",
  "quest.5E7A12CC4FDD903D.quest_desc": [
    "Netherite-tier mining at speed 16, the best damage in the mod and 500,000 FE per tool. The hammer reaches 7×7 here, and the hoe tills Shadowpulse Soil."
  ],
  "quest.21AC425DC3842B2D.title": "Eclipse Alloy armor",
  "quest.21AC425DC3842B2D.quest_desc": [
    "Netherite's toughness and knockback resistance with 500,000 FE per piece. The chestplate alone takes seven upgrades, flight among them."
  ],
  "quest.25F9DEB6CF8AFCFD.title": "Debuff Remover",
  "quest.25F9DEB6CF8AFCFD.quest_subtitle": "Milk not included. Well, four are.",
  "quest.25F9DEB6CF8AFCFD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four \"},{\"text\":\"Milk Buckets\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:milk_bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", two \"},{\"text\":\"Golden Apples\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:golden_apple\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and two \"},{\"text\":\"Honey Bottles\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:honey_bottle\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" round a blank, for the Eclipse Alloy helmet. Its key clears every harmful effect, 50,000 FE each; it rests 20 seconds.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.68A4C7346E58EA6D.title": "Mental Obliteration",
  "quest.68A4C7346E58EA6D.quest_subtitle": "Nearby mobs completely stop. Forever.",
  "quest.68A4C7346E58EA6D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two Time Crystals, two \"},{\"text\":\"End Rods\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:end_rod\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and four \"},{\"text\":\"Calibrated Sculk Sensors\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:calibrated_sculk_sensor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" round a blank, for the Eclipse Alloy helmet. Its key freezes the brain of every mob within five blocks, for good: 100,000 FE each, two minutes of rest.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.02B266D76265D323.title": "Lava Immunity",
  "quest.02B266D76265D323.quest_subtitle": "Fancy a swim?",
  "quest.02B266D76265D323.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four \"},{\"text\":\"Netherite Scrap\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:netherite_scrap\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", two \"},{\"text\":\"Lava Buckets\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:lava_bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and two Magma Cream round a blank, for the Eclipse Alloy chestplate. Lava and fire stop hurting you; each hit it blocks costs 1,000 FE.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.052A177EC36C86E8.title": "Death Protection",
  "quest.052A177EC36C86E8.quest_subtitle": "Undo, but for dying.",
  "quest.052A177EC36C86E8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two \"},{\"text\":\"Totems of Undying\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:totem_of_undying\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", two Emeralds and four Time Crystals round a blank, for the Eclipse Alloy chestplate. A fatal blow leaves you at five hearts instead, once every five minutes, for 450,000 of its 500,000 FE.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.45DD06319979E41D.title": "Time Protection",
  "quest.45DD06319979E41D.quest_subtitle": "Wibbly wobbly, but not on you.",
  "quest.45DD06319979E41D.quest_desc": [
    "Two Time Crystals and two Shields round a blank, for the Eclipse Alloy chestplate. Time Crystals in your inventory now and then give you five seconds of Slowness VI or Speed VI; this upgrade blocks it for 5,000 FE."
  ],
  "quest.08FFBA668B6B01AB.title": "Flight",
  "quest.08FFBA668B6B01AB.quest_subtitle": "The sky's the limit, and the battery.",
  "quest.08FFBA668B6B01AB.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Here the recipe swaps an \"},{\"text\":\"End Crystal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:end_crystal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for a \"},{\"text\":\"Horizon Chart\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:horizon_chart\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (act IV), next to four Phantom Membranes, two Feathers and a blank. On the Eclipse Alloy chestplate you fly like in creative for 100 FE a tick, and mine at full speed in the air.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2917BF0EEF9294B4.title": "Phase",
  "quest.2917BF0EEF9294B4.quest_subtitle": "Doors are for other people.",
  "quest.2917BF0EEF9294B4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four \"},{\"text\":\"Shulker Shells\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:shulker_shell\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", two Phantom Membranes and two Dragon's Breath round a blank. On Eclipse Alloy leggings you walk through walls, never through the floor, bedrock or portals; on the Eclipse Alloy bow, arrows fly through blocks.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.17AA6EB84BFAC5CA.title": "Earthquake",
  "quest.17AA6EB84BFAC5CA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four \"},{\"text\":\"Soul Sand\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:soul_sand\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", two \"},{\"text\":\"Sticky Pistons\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:sticky_piston\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and two Fermented Spider Eyes round a blank, for Eclipse Alloy boots. Its key gives every grounded mob within five blocks Slowness IV for ten seconds; not the Wither, the Warden or the dragon.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7C0E824803234797.title": "Instant Break",
  "quest.7C0E824803234797.quest_subtitle": "Mining at the speed of now.",
  "quest.7C0E824803234797.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two \"},{\"text\":\"Netherite Pickaxes\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:netherite_pickaxe\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", two \"},{\"text\":\"Nether Stars\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:nether_star\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and four Time Crystals round a blank, for Eclipse Alloy tools. Blocks break at once, at 250 FE per point of hardness, so obsidian costs 12,500; Efficiency discounts 10% per level.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3403887BDF1C9BE8.title": "Ore X-Ray",
  "quest.3403887BDF1C9BE8.quest_subtitle": "That's overpowered. Yes.",
  "quest.3403887BDF1C9BE8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four Eyes of Ender, two \"},{\"text\":\"Sculk Shriekers\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:sculk_shrieker\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and two Calibrated Sculk Sensors round a blank, for the Eclipse Alloy pickaxe and paxel. It replaces the Ore Scanner: ores show through the stone as themselves, for 5,000 FE.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4806F29BF2B1D0DD.title": "Mob X-Ray",
  "quest.4806F29BF2B1D0DD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two Sculk Shriekers, four \"},{\"text\":\"End Rods\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:end_rod\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and two Calibrated Sculk Sensors round a blank, for the Eclipse Alloy sword. It replaces the Mob Scanner: every mob within 20 blocks glows for 10 seconds.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.06F04B58EE60930D.title": "Shadowpulse Soil",
  "quest.06F04B58EE60930D.quest_subtitle": "Farming, fast-forwarded.",
  "quest.06F04B58EE60930D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Eclipse Alloy Hoe tills \"},{\"text\":\"Shadowpulse Soil\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"justdirethings:goosoil_tier4\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": four growth stages per random tick, self-harvest and the same chest binding as VoidShimmer. Most crops ripen in two random ticks.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6AC7CA0C4296D78D.title": "Eclipse Alloy Bow",
  "quest.6AC7CA0C4296D78D.quest_desc": [
    "Three String and three Eclipse Alloy: a 10-tick draw, four Potion Canister slots and 500,000 FE. It is the only bow that takes the Yondu Arrow and Phase."
  ],
  "quest.37ED8D173997BF42.title": "Yondu Arrow",
  "quest.37ED8D173997BF42.quest_subtitle": "Whistle optional.",
  "quest.37ED8D173997BF42.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two \"},{\"text\":\"Nether Stars\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:nether_star\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", four Eyes of Ender and two Phantom Membranes round a blank. Its key arms the next arrow, which chains from mob to mob up to ten times; 100,000 FE and two minutes of rest.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.151D3284AC08AEA6.title": "Eclipsegate Wand",
  "quest.151D3284AC08AEA6.quest_subtitle": "The portable hole, on a timer.",
  "quest.151D3284AC08AEA6.quest_desc": [
    "An Eclipse Alloy and a Celestigem on a Voidshift Wand, with 100,000 FE. Right-click a wall and a 3×3 tunnel up to 20 blocks deep opens for five seconds, then the blocks come back; chests and machines stay put."
  ],
  "quest.182D2ECF5D2DE057.title": "Eclipse Alloy Paxel",
  "quest.182D2ECF5D2DE057.quest_subtitle": "One tool to break them all.",
  "quest.182D2ECF5D2DE057.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Upgrade a Celestigem Paxel with an Eclipse Alloy template, or fuse the three Eclipse Alloy tools in a Smithing Table. Either way the \"},{\"text\":\"Eclipse Alloy Paxel\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"justdirethings:eclipsealloy_paxel\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" keeps every upgrade: 7×7 hammer, Ore Miner, X-Ray, Instant Break, all on 500,000 FE.\"}]"
  ],
  "image.44C387679656D035.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Ferricore armor\",\"color\":\"#7BEA4F\"}]",
  "image.7C286551B9CBCC04.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Ferricore tools\",\"color\":\"#7BEA4F\"}]",
  "image.666A9509FF7BEECE.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Blazegold armor\",\"color\":\"#7BEA4F\"}]",
  "image.5B9BBD79C0A7333B.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Blazegold tools\",\"color\":\"#7BEA4F\"}]",
  "image.51A43F71F410D479.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Celestigem armor\",\"color\":\"#7BEA4F\"}]",
  "image.4AE9EFA8C4D0119D.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Celestigem tools\",\"color\":\"#7BEA4F\"}]",
  "image.5E1A2CEBF1C2E2B8.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eclipse Alloy armor\",\"color\":\"#7BEA4F\"}]",
  "image.69002398E77EEA4F.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eclipse Alloy tools\",\"color\":\"#7BEA4F\"}]",
  "image.3FC38116D057D9C6.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Just Dire Things\\nGoo and Gear\",\"color\":\"#EFFFE8\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.08AF0470ACB8B8CD.title": "Back to the Sun of Heliodor",
  "image.1D01B3F96E59DC38.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"feed it  wait  mine it\",\"color\":\"#9FE88A\",\"font\":\"minecraft:alt\"}]",
  "image.5466D8A7B06CAEFF.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» Machines and Time\",\"color\":\"#7BEA4F\"}]",
  "image.29DBD69C9013F9A7.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Primogel · Ferricore\",\"color\":\"#9F98B7\"}]",
  "image.4F070C3E41E0AA7F.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Blazebloom · Blazegold\",\"color\":\"#FA7400\"}]",
  "image.1B85F197809F801D.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"VoidShimmer · Celestigem\",\"color\":\"#1AC9AA\"}]",
  "image.6494D90FD60B7D76.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Shadowpulse · Eclipse Alloy\",\"color\":\"#0A7F8C\"}]",
  "chapter.5E2C299D592BBA4B.title": "Mekanism · Energy and reactors",
  "chapter.5E2C299D592BBA4B.chapter_subtitle": [
    "From a heat generator to antimatter: generators and storage, steam, fission, fusion and the SPS."
  ],
  "quest.770AF573AE4A1192.title": "Heat Generator",
  "quest.770AF573AE4A1192.quest_subtitle": "Warm hands, warm machines.",
  "quest.770AF573AE4A1192.quest_desc": [
    "Iron, osmium, copper, planks and a furnace. It burns lava or any furnace fuel for 200 J/t, and every side touching lava adds 30 J/t even with nothing to burn.",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Sunk in a lava pool it runs on the lava around it alone. In the Nether it gets 100 J/t more.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.04FC79C3C770E256.title": "Joules and FE",
  "quest.04FC79C3C770E256.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Mekanism counts in joules: 2.5 J make 1 FE. Its cables take and give FE to any mod, so the grid can mix generators from the whole pack.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.01BB17F4F1378EE0.title": "Reactors in this pack",
  "quest.01BB17F4F1378EE0.quest_desc": [
    "Generators, cables, cubes and the matrix are native. Three reactor parts wait on the Atlas: the fission port on a Containment Seal (act IV), the fusion controller on an Ark Connection Bus and the SPS port on a Renewal Engine (act V)."
  ],
  "quest.48EF67E0E00158F4.title": "Solar Generator",
  "quest.48EF67E0E00158F4.quest_subtitle": "Free, as long as the sky is.",
  "quest.48EF67E0E00158F4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three \"},{\"text\":\"Solar Panels\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanismgenerators:solar_panel\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on an energy tablet frame: up to 50 J/t at noon under open sky, nothing at night or under a roof. Cheap enough to line a whole roof with them.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6079E07B7D0A7527.title": "Advanced Solar Generator",
  "quest.6079E07B7D0A7527.quest_desc": [
    "Four solar generators, infused alloy and iron: up to 300 J/t, where the four apart peak at 200. It stands on a pole and takes three blocks of space above."
  ],
  "quest.2753A7DD48C438D3.title": "Wind Generator",
  "quest.2753A7DD48C438D3.quest_desc": [
    "From 60 J/t at height 24 up to 480 J/t at the top of the world, as long as the block four above its base sees the sky. Build tall, build on mountains."
  ],
  "quest.59101B3B1D85DE6B.title": "Bio-Generator",
  "quest.59101B3B1D85DE6B.quest_subtitle": "Compost with ambition.",
  "quest.59101B3B1D85DE6B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"It burns \"},{\"text\":\"Bio Fuel\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:bio_fuel\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for 350 J/t. A farm feeding a Crusher feeding this is power that grows back.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1AD59FD5A21F356B.title": "Gas-Burning Generator",
  "quest.1AD59FD5A21F356B.quest_desc": [
    "Osmium, infused alloy and an electrolytic core. It burns hydrogen, or far better, ethene. A separator on water plus this generator is the first power plant that fits in a closet."
  ],
  "quest.29C60AD95FEFC8B8.title": "Ethene",
  "quest.29C60AD95FEFC8B8.quest_subtitle": "Plastic-scented power.",
  "quest.29C60AD95FEFC8B8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"In the Pressurized Reaction Chamber two bio fuel, 10 water and 100 hydrogen become 100 ethene and a \"},{\"text\":\"Substrate\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:substrate\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Pipe the ethene to the generator; keep the substrate for plastic.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.22353FA19215A62E.title": "Large generators",
  "quest.22353FA19215A62E.quest_desc": [
    "MoreMachine's large gas-burning, heat and wind generators do the work of a row of small ones in one block. Every recipe has a Robit at its heart and steel blocks around it."
  ],
  "quest.483066BA7A7BDFE7.title": "Cables and cubes",
  "quest.483066BA7A7BDFE7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Steel and redstone make eight \"},{\"text\":\"Universal Cables\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:basic_universal_cable\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; an energy tablet in a steel casing makes a \"},{\"text\":\"Basic Energy Cube\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:basic_energy_cube\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" that holds 4 MJ. A cube beside each group of generators evens out day and night.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6D138669D05AF98C.title": "Which side is which",
  "quest.6D138669D05AF98C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A cube takes power on its input faces and pushes it out of the output face, like any machine. The slots on its left and right charge and drain items: park your jetpack and tools there.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0ADD31D31834E3C1.title": "Cables share, they do not store",
  "quest.0ADD31D31834E3C1.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Connected cables form one network that splits power between everything plugged in. A basic cable moves 8,000 J/t; when it caps out, upgrade the cable, not the generators.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7C48931B58F60FDB.title": "Thicker cables",
  "quest.7C48931B58F60FDB.quest_desc": [
    "Advanced, elite and ultimate cables carry 128,000, 1,024,000 and 8,192,000 J/t. Right-click a laid cable with the next alloy and it upgrades in place; Extras adds four tiers more."
  ],
  "quest.7A4342586EC6A4FC.title": "Ultimate Energy Cube",
  "quest.7A4342586EC6A4FC.quest_desc": [
    "Each tier wraps the last cube in its alloy: 16, 64 and 256 MJ, pushing out up to 256,000 J/t at the top. Past that, the Induction Matrix is cheaper per joule."
  ],
  "quest.7AE4606A98611357.title": "Cubes past Ultimate",
  "quest.7AE4606A98611357.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Mekanism Extras keeps wrapping: an \"},{\"text\":\"Absolute Energy Cube\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism_extras:absolute_energy_cube\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" is an ultimate cube in radiance alloy and emeralds, and Supreme, Cosmic and Infinite follow with the Extras alloys.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.19DD91D523871AD1.title": "Energized Induction Matrix",
  "quest.19DD91D523871AD1.quest_subtitle": "A battery the size of a room.",
  "quest.19DD91D523871AD1.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A hollow box, 3 to 18 blocks a side, of \"},{\"text\":\"Induction Casing\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:induction_casing\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and glass with \"},{\"text\":\"Induction Ports\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:induction_port\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Cells inside add capacity, providers add throughput. The ports want elite circuits.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.108225E99DB836AD.title": "Plan it in EMI first",
  "quest.108225E99DB836AD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Just Enough Mekanism Multiblocks lists every Mekanism structure in EMI: pick one, set its size and read the block count, the layout and the numbers before you place a block. A turbine the wrong shape will not form at all.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1A9CAB71A2C7FBFE.title": "Ports go both ways",
  "quest.1A9CAB71A2C7FBFE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"An induction port starts as input. Shift-right-click it with a Configurator and it switches to output; one of each makes the matrix a pass-through battery.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0BF84588B194D041.title": "Cells and providers",
  "quest.0BF84588B194D041.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A basic cube wrapped in lithium dust and energy tablets makes a \"},{\"text\":\"Basic Induction Cell\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:basic_induction_cell\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", 8 GJ; with circuits instead, a \"},{\"text\":\"Basic Induction Provider\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:basic_induction_provider\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Lithium comes from the evaporation tower.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.60AE550BDB340688.title": "Ultimate Induction Cell",
  "quest.60AE550BDB340688.quest_desc": [
    "Cells climb from 8 GJ to 64, 512 and 4,000 GJ; providers from 256,000 J/t to 131 million. One ultimate cell outholds a room of ultimate cubes."
  ],
  "quest.23923C1ED9CF0CE8.title": "A heavier matrix",
  "quest.23923C1ED9CF0CE8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Extras adds \"},{\"text\":\"Reinforced Induction Casing\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism_extras:reinforced_induction_casing\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" with its own ports, and cells and providers from Absolute to Infinite for when four terajoules start to feel small.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.71C9A91A53A8BE35.title": "Structural Glass",
  "quest.71C9A91A53A8BE35.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Structural Glass\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:structural_glass\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" works in the walls of any Mekanism multiblock that accepts glass, drops itself when broken, and lets you watch the tank inside fill up.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.65572E26D08B01C0.title": "Yellow cake for the common store",
  "quest.65572E26D08B01C0.quest_subtitle": "Look, do not eat.",
  "quest.65572E26D08B01C0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Sixteen \"},{\"text\":\"Yellow Cake Uranium\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:yellow_cake_uranium\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for the common store, once a day. Run uranium through the ore ladder first and it comes cheap.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5DEAF9CD61FFA814.title": "Resistive Heater",
  "quest.5DEAF9CD61FFA814.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Resistive Heater\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:resistive_heater\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" turns energy into heat at a rate you set in its screen. Heat is a resource in Mekanism: it boils water, warms the evaporation tower and moves through conductors.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0E30AEE8954C4BE0.title": "Fuelwood Heater",
  "quest.0E30AEE8954C4BE0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Heat without power: the \"},{\"text\":\"Fuelwood Heater\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:fuelwood_heater\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" burns any furnace fuel into heat. Next to the evaporation tower it gets a salt works going before you own a generator.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7B4BB59BBB4574CA.title": "Thermodynamic Conductor",
  "quest.7B4BB59BBB4574CA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Copper between steel: eight \"},{\"text\":\"Thermodynamic Conductors\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:basic_thermodynamic_conductor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" that carry heat from a heater to whatever needs it. Keep them away from anything that burns.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.23D65931AD41ED7F.title": "Thermoelectric Boiler",
  "quest.23D65931AD41ED7F.quest_subtitle": "A kettle the size of a house.",
  "quest.23D65931AD41ED7F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A hollow box of \"},{\"text\":\"Boiler Casing\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:boiler_casing\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and glass, up to 18 a side, with \"},{\"text\":\"Boiler Valves\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:boiler_valve\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for water in and steam out. Heat comes from superheating elements inside or from hot coolant.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.17CD7565B955CCAE.title": "Superheating Element",
  "quest.17CD7565B955CCAE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Placed inside the boiler's lower half and fed power through a valve, \"},{\"text\":\"Superheating Elements\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:superheating_element\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" boil the water directly. More elements, more steam, more power spent.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1BD33479F347F167.title": "Boiling with sodium",
  "quest.1BD33479F347F167.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A sodium-cooled fission reactor sends out \"},{\"text\":\"Superheated Sodium\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:superheated_sodium_bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; piped into the boiler, it boils the water and comes back as sodium. No elements needed.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4E20B3005A4F18E0.title": "Water below, steam above",
  "quest.4E20B3005A4F18E0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A full, gapless layer of Pressure Dispersers splits the boiler: water and heat below it, steam above. Leave room above for steam, or the boiler stalls with its tank full.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.34046E842925E770.title": "Pressure Disperser",
  "quest.34046E842925E770.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Steel, iron bars and infused alloy. The boiler and the turbine both need a full horizontal layer of \"},{\"text\":\"Pressure Dispersers\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:pressure_disperser\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" to steer the steam, so make a stack.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.29569F80D701AD3D.title": "Industrial Turbine",
  "quest.29569F80D701AD3D.quest_subtitle": "Steam in, lightning out.",
  "quest.29569F80D701AD3D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A box of \"},{\"text\":\"Turbine Casing\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanismgenerators:turbine_casing\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" from 5×3×5 up to 17×18×17, odd width and length, with valves for steam and power and \"},{\"text\":\"Turbine Vents\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanismgenerators:turbine_vent\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" at or above the rotor top. Boilers, fission and fusion all feed it steam.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.426B8D1FC37ED254.title": "The rotor",
  "quest.426B8D1FC37ED254.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A column of \"},{\"text\":\"Turbine Rotors\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanismgenerators:turbine_rotor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" up the middle, two \"},{\"text\":\"Blades\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanismgenerators:turbine_blade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" each, a \"},{\"text\":\"Rotational Complex\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanismgenerators:rotational_complex\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on top and \"},{\"text\":\"Electromagnetic Coils\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanismgenerators:electromagnetic_coil\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" touching it. Each coil carries four blades.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.082B24614DBD6C00.title": "Saturating Condenser",
  "quest.082B24614DBD6C00.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Saturating Condensers\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanismgenerators:saturating_condenser\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" above the rotational complex turn spent steam back into water for the boiler or the reactor. Without them, the turbine throws its water away.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3D9500F5BC2862AB.title": "Sizing a turbine",
  "quest.3D9500F5BC2862AB.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A turbine holds at most 28 blades, and every coil carries four, so a full rotor wants seven coils. Vents limit how fast steam gets in: when the steam tank fills, add vents before rotor.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.01F7BFEAFE162B95.title": "Yellow cake",
  "quest.01F7BFEAFE162B95.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A uranium ingot in the Enrichment Chamber makes two \"},{\"text\":\"Yellow Cake Uranium\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:yellow_cake_uranium\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; the Chemical Oxidizer turns each into 250 uranium oxide. Uranium ore is common and harmless until you refine it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.416CD1969C65C35A.title": "Hydrofluoric acid",
  "quest.416CD1969C65C35A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Fluorite\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:fluorite_gem\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" gem dissolved in sulfuric acid makes 1000 hydrofluoric acid. The Chemical Infuser joins it with uranium oxide into uranium hexafluoride, two for each pair.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6463C8145E0DE9C6.title": "Isotopic Centrifuge",
  "quest.6463C8145E0DE9C6.quest_desc": [
    "Lead, ultimate circuits and a chemical tank. It spins uranium hexafluoride into fissile fuel one to one. Later it also pulls plutonium out of nuclear waste, ten to one."
  ],
  "quest.2C96C2EAAF41B7E4.title": "Fission Reactor",
  "quest.2C96C2EAAF41B7E4.quest_subtitle": "Mostly safe!",
  "quest.2C96C2EAAF41B7E4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A hollow box of \"},{\"text\":\"Fission Reactor Casing\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanismgenerators:fission_reactor_casing\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and \"},{\"text\":\"Reactor Glass\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanismgenerators:reactor_glass\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", lead around steel, with towers of fuel assemblies inside. Fissile fuel in, heat into water or sodium out, nuclear waste to handle.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.44D5F6B2A82B0029.title": "Fission Reactor Port",
  "quest.44D5F6B2A82B0029.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"In this pack the \"},{\"text\":\"Fission Reactor Port\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanismgenerators:fission_reactor_port\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" has a \"},{\"text\":\"Containment Seal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:containment_seal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" at its heart: act IV. A Configurator sets each port to fuel in, coolant or waste out.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.01F230EB33555CA5.title": "Fuel towers",
  "quest.01F230EB33555CA5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Stack \"},{\"text\":\"Fission Fuel Assemblies\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanismgenerators:fission_fuel_assembly\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" into towers inside the reactor and cap each one with a \"},{\"text\":\"Control Rod Assembly\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanismgenerators:control_rod_assembly\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Every assembly adds 1 mB/t of maximum burn and 8000 mB of fuel space.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4D88D541E8192C7A.title": "Reactor Glass",
  "quest.4D88D541E8192C7A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Lead and enriched iron around glass: four \"},{\"text\":\"Reactor Glass\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanismgenerators:reactor_glass\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It goes in the walls of both reactors, and a window lets you see the fuel glow.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.086DE4D66647E1BA.title": "Fission Logic Adapter",
  "quest.086DE4D66647E1BA.quest_subtitle": "The big red button, automated.",
  "quest.086DE4D66647E1BA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Set the \"},{\"text\":\"Logic Adapter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanismgenerators:fission_reactor_logic_adapter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" to fire on high damage, high temperature or too much waste, and wire it to the activation side: the reactor shuts itself off before you have to.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.79FEDEB8FA6CF012.title": "Start low",
  "quest.79FEDEB8FA6CF012.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The reactor starts at 0.1 mB/t. Raise the burn rate a little at a time and watch damage: \"},{\"text\":\"past 100% it can melt down\",\"color\":\"#FF8C7A\"},{\"text\":\", and a meltdown leaves a crater and a radiation cloud. SCRAM is in its screen.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1087BE32E8ABE8C8.title": "Coolant first",
  "quest.1087BE32E8ABE8C8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Every mB of fissile fuel is 1 MJ of heat, and all of it must leave through the coolant. If the water or sodium runs out, the temperature climbs and so does the damage.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4B8323EF4B5D05E5.title": "Sodium coolant",
  "quest.4B8323EF4B5D05E5.quest_desc": [
    "Brine through the separator leaves sodium beside the chlorine. Pumped into a fission reactor as coolant, it comes out superheated and boils water in a boiler far better than water cooling does in the reactor."
  ],
  "quest.19E055E7E92C386F.title": "Water-cooled fission",
  "quest.19E055E7E92C386F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"With water as coolant the reactor boils it into steam itself. Pipe the steam to a turbine and its condensers send the water back: the simplest nuclear plant.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3D74EAF1AE047FEA.title": "Radioactive Waste Barrel",
  "quest.3D74EAF1AE047FEA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Pipe nuclear waste out of the reactor into a \"},{\"text\":\"Radioactive Waste Barrel\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:radioactive_waste_barrel\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": 512,000 mB that decay slowly on their own. Breaking a full barrel releases what is inside.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7D7970FC3C9C3E3E.title": "Fuel from waste",
  "quest.7D7970FC3C9C3E3E.quest_subtitle": "Recycling, the dangerous kind.",
  "quest.7D7970FC3C9C3E3E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A plutonium pellet with hydrogen chloride in the Injection Chamber makes four \"},{\"text\":\"Reprocessed Fissile Fragments\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:reprocessed_fissile_fragment\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; oxidized, each one is 2000 mB of fissile fuel.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.5B5710152CF67792.title": "Wear the full hazmat suit",
  "quest.36794BFC7D025A6D.title": "Hazmat Suit",
  "quest.36794BFC7D025A6D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Lead and orange dye make the \"},{\"text\":\"Hazmat Mask\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:hazmat_mask\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", gown, pants and boots. The full set keeps radiation out while you work near reactors, waste and spills.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.7E07100B4A3DBD65.title": "Use a Geiger Counter",
  "quest.2ACE0612C6394779.title": "Geiger Counter",
  "quest.2ACE0612C6394779.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Lead around a basic circuit. The \"},{\"text\":\"Geiger Counter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:geiger_counter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" reads the radiation around you; radiation spreads from leaks and fades over time.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.5002BE0317897996.title": "Use a Dosimeter",
  "quest.5312F92AC79A1CCC.title": "Dosimeter",
  "quest.5312F92AC79A1CCC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Dosimeter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:dosimeter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" reads the dose your body already took. Above a small threshold radiation starts to hurt, and it takes time to fall again.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.20F72A343D3A46C0.title": "Tastes like metal",
  "quest.20F72A343D3A46C0.quest_subtitle": "Does this taste like metal to you?",
  "quest.20F72A343D3A46C0.quest_desc": [
    "Radiation poisoning hurt you. Next time, the hazmat suit goes on before the barrel comes off."
  ],
  "reward.20C1E55727BA4023.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.4FA881875379C776.title": "Not great, not terrible",
  "quest.4FA881875379C776.quest_subtitle": "Three point six. Roentgen.",
  "quest.4FA881875379C776.quest_desc": [
    "Radiation poisoning killed you. The reactor, for the record, is fine."
  ],
  "reward.7459492A26B99762.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.13542F3D308446CB.title": "Bigger waste barrels",
  "quest.13542F3D308446CB.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Extras wraps a waste barrel in lead blocks and radiance alloy: the \"},{\"text\":\"Absolute Radioactive Waste Barrel\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism_extras:absolute_radioactive_waste_barrel\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", with Supreme, Cosmic and Infinite after it for reactors that never stop.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5EAB37617F376017.title": "Plutonium",
  "quest.5EAB37617F376017.quest_subtitle": "Plutonium, not polonium.",
  "quest.5EAB37617F376017.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Isotopic Centrifuge pulls one plutonium from ten nuclear waste. In the reaction chamber, 1000 of it with water and a fluorite dust make a \"},{\"text\":\"Plutonium Pellet\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:pellet_plutonium\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and 1000 spent waste.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4796BA493CB12C72.title": "Polonium",
  "quest.4796BA493CB12C72.quest_subtitle": "Polonium, not plutonium.",
  "quest.4796BA493CB12C72.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Solar Neutron Activator turns ten nuclear waste into one polonium. The same reaction as plutonium makes a \"},{\"text\":\"Polonium Pellet\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:pellet_polonium\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": fusion frames, the SPS and the MekaSuit all want them.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5DBB61A56876C197.title": "Solar Neutron Activator",
  "quest.5DBB61A56876C197.quest_desc": [
    "It needs to see the sun. It turns nuclear waste into polonium and lithium into tritium, faster at noon, slower in rain. Built from bronze, HDPE and elite parts."
  ],
  "quest.7680F7D2EE7883E6.title": "Activators like it cold",
  "quest.7680F7D2EE7883E6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Biome matters: hot biomes cut the activator's rate and cold ones raise it; where it rains, a storm cuts it to a fifth. A snowy peak with a clear sky is the best seat.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2B87016BAEC29307.title": "Large Solar Neutron Activator",
  "quest.2B87016BAEC29307.quest_desc": [
    "MoreMachine's big activator: an advanced solar generator and a laser around a Robit, many activators' worth of polonium in one block."
  ],
  "quest.2FEBB698F3A23BAD.title": "Supercritical Phase Shifter",
  "quest.2FEBB698F3A23BAD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"SPS Casing\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:sps_casing\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" is HDPE around plutonium and polonium pellets. Built into a 7×7×7 shifter with glass and ports, it pushes polonium past what matter should do.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.25CCCFDED78B1354.title": "SPS Port",
  "quest.25CCCFDED78B1354.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"In this pack the \"},{\"text\":\"SPS Port\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:sps_port\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" has a \"},{\"text\":\"Renewal Engine\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:renewal_engine\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" at its heart: act V. Ports take polonium and power in and let antimatter out.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.70BD68037A2199CD.title": "Supercharged Coil",
  "quest.70BD68037A2199CD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Copper, ultimate circuits and polonium around a laser. Each \"},{\"text\":\"Supercharged Coil\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:supercharged_coil\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" sits on an SPS port and feeds the shifter its enormous power.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.733E726F0EF5F9CF.title": "What antimatter costs",
  "quest.733E726F0EF5F9CF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"One mB of antimatter takes 1000 mB of polonium and a gigajoule of power. A pellet is 1000 mB: plan the fission plant and the power plant before the shifter.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5ED9780E29AA80B3.title": "Supercharged creeper",
  "quest.5ED9780E29AA80B3.quest_subtitle": "Science has gone too far.",
  "quest.5ED9780E29AA80B3.quest_desc": [
    "A creeper wandered into a running SPS and came out charged. Please do not do that again, and please do not do it near the base."
  ],
  "reward.2BAE5ED1373F9A71.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.02ACB717EAAAD56B.title": "A villain origin story",
  "quest.02ACB717EAAAD56B.quest_subtitle": "He had a good job at the library.",
  "quest.02ACB717EAAAD56B.quest_desc": [
    "A villager went through the SPS and came out something else. Every villain needs a start."
  ],
  "reward.66D303FB96AD0C9F.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.3E2D8928ADA59A5E.title": "Pig intelligence",
  "quest.3E2D8928ADA59A5E.quest_desc": [
    "You tried to make a pig smarter by walking it through a running SPS. It came out angrier, and now it has a sword."
  ],
  "reward.1AA9636C42C907B8.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.5F5A7F10DB9F3BFC.title": "Mooshroom recoloring",
  "quest.5F5A7F10DB9F3BFC.quest_subtitle": "Red or brown? Yes.",
  "quest.5F5A7F10DB9F3BFC.quest_desc": [
    "A mooshroom went through the SPS and came out the other color. The only safe use of antimatter physics so far."
  ],
  "reward.0570DB439985503B.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.433F2224AF985485.title": "Impossible material",
  "quest.433F2224AF985485.quest_subtitle": "Matter that should not exist here.",
  "quest.433F2224AF985485.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A thousand mB of antimatter from the SPS, crystallized: an \"},{\"text\":\"Antimatter Pellet\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:pellet_antimatter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It feeds the Nucleosynthesizer, the gravitational unit of the MekaSuit, the supermassive QIO drive and the creative tanks.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.03771164C730F823.title": "Antiprotonic Nucleosynthesizer",
  "quest.03771164C730F823.quest_desc": [
    "A few mB of antimatter and a lot of power transmute things: coal into a diamond, a diamond into an emerald, an egg into a dragon egg, a skeleton skull into a wither skeleton skull."
  ],
  "quest.126C5840D859F397.title": "Pellets travel",
  "quest.126C5840D859F397.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Store antimatter as pellets, not gas: the Chemical Oxidizer turns a pellet back into 1000 mB wherever you need it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.22A593034A787258.title": "Large Nucleosynthesizer",
  "quest.22A593034A787258.quest_desc": [
    "MoreMachine's big transmuter: antimatter pellets and a Robit at the core. It runs several transmutations at once from one antimatter tank."
  ],
  "quest.5F03ED0BD459380A.title": "Heavy water",
  "quest.5F03ED0BD459380A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An \"},{\"text\":\"Electric Pump\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:electric_pump\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" with a \"},{\"text\":\"Filter Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:upgrade_filter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", infused alloy and glass around tin dust, pulls 10 mB of \"},{\"text\":\"Heavy Water\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:heavy_water_bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" from every water block. The Electrolytic Separator splits it into deuterium and oxygen at twice the power.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4E357EB1FE93FFB0.title": "Advanced Electric Pump",
  "quest.4E357EB1FE93FFB0.quest_subtitle": "Ten times heavier.",
  "quest.4E357EB1FE93FFB0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Mekanism Extras' \"},{\"text\":\"Advanced Electric Pump\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism_extras:advanced_electric_pump\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" pulls 100 mB of heavy water per block with a Filter Upgrade, ten times the basic pump.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6687258309F2892C.title": "Lithium",
  "quest.6687258309F2892C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The evaporation tower turns ten brine into one lithium; the Chemical Crystallizer makes \"},{\"text\":\"Lithium Dust\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:dust_lithium\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" from 100 of it. Induction cells eat the dust, and the activator turns the gas into tritium.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4045B081AF1B0EEC.title": "Hohlraum",
  "quest.4045B081AF1B0EEC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four gold dust and 10 carbon in the infuser make a \"},{\"text\":\"Hohlraum\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanismgenerators:hohlraum\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Fill it with D-T fuel, deuterium and tritium joined in the Chemical Infuser, and it becomes the reactor's ignition charge.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0BD32FFF3ED3CA05.title": "Laser",
  "quest.0BD32FFF3ED3CA05.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Reinforced alloy, an energy tablet and a diamond in a steel casing: a \"},{\"text\":\"Laser\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:laser\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Fed power, it fires a beam up to 64 blocks that breaks blocks and hurts whatever stands in it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.20DBC68D3543C6E6.title": "Laser Amplifier",
  "quest.20DBC68D3543C6E6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Laser Amplifier\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:laser_amplifier\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" stores the beams of several lasers and fires them together, on redstone or when full. Aim it at the fusion reactor's laser focus matrix.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.677C96650C39AD0D.title": "Fusion Reactor Frame",
  "quest.677C96650C39AD0D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Atomic alloy and polonium pellets around a steel casing: four \"},{\"text\":\"Fusion Reactor Frames\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanismgenerators:fusion_reactor_frame\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". The fusion reactor is a 5×5×5 shape of frames, glass, ports and one controller.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.00FC1E2FC7343444.title": "Fusion Reactor Controller",
  "quest.00FC1E2FC7343444.quest_subtitle": "A small sun in a box.",
  "quest.00FC1E2FC7343444.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"In this pack the \"},{\"text\":\"Fusion Reactor Controller\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanismgenerators:fusion_reactor_controller\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" has an \"},{\"text\":\"Ark Connection Bus\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:ark_bus\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in place of a frame: act V. It sits on top of the reactor and holds the hohlraum.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.13FF3C190B4B26C3.title": "Fusion Reactor Ports",
  "quest.13FF3C190B4B26C3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Fusion Reactor Ports\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanismgenerators:fusion_reactor_port\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" take deuterium, tritium and water in and send power and steam out. Once burning, the reactor mixes its own D-T fuel from the two gases.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3CA9C31B0DCE2615.title": "Ignition",
  "quest.3CA9C31B0DCE2615.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Set a \"},{\"text\":\"Laser Focus Matrix\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanismgenerators:laser_focus_matrix\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in the reactor wall, put a full hohlraum in the controller and fire charged amplifiers into the matrix. When the plasma is hot enough the hohlraum burns and the reactor runs on its ports.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7B76EA62B5154097.title": "Fusion Logic Adapter",
  "quest.7B76EA62B5154097.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The fusion \"},{\"text\":\"Logic Adapter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanismgenerators:fusion_reactor_logic_adapter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" signals when the reactor is ready to ignite, too hot or out of fuel. Wire \\\"ready\\\" to the amplifier and ignition fires itself.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.74CB90540FFD6727.title": "Air or water",
  "quest.74CB90540FFD6727.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"An air-cooled fusion reactor turns heat straight into power. Pipe water in and it makes steam for a turbine instead, but it needs a higher temperature to ignite.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2EB2459E6FA8C586.title": "Fusion into a turbine",
  "quest.2EB2459E6FA8C586.quest_desc": [
    "Water-cooled fusion sends out so much steam that it wants the biggest turbine you can form. Add rotors and coils until the steam tank stops filling."
  ],
  "quest.5E9F060C3BC14C16.title": "Lead-coated focus matrix",
  "quest.5E9F060C3BC14C16.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Extras infuses a laser focus matrix with 40 lead: the \"},{\"text\":\"Lead Coated Laser Focus Matrix\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism_extras:lead_coated_laser_focus_matrix\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", the same window that also blocks radiation.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5DDBB2330BF01EE2.title": "Naquadah Reactor Casing",
  "quest.5DDBB2330BF01EE2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Nucleosynthesizer turns a lead block and one mB of antimatter into \"},{\"text\":\"Naquadah Reactor Casing\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism_extras:naquadah_reactor_casing\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", radiation-proof framing for the Extras reactor.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.697731EB08867DF6.title": "Naquadah Reactor",
  "quest.697731EB08867DF6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Its \"},{\"text\":\"controller\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism_extras:naquadah_reactor_controller\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" wants cosmic circuits and an absolute chemical tank, and its ports come four to a casing cross. Plan it in EMI before you commit the antimatter.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.38E8C7A7EE6B155D.title": "Naquadah fuel",
  "quest.38E8C7A7EE6B155D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Naquadah ingots dissolved in hydrofluoric acid give naquadah hexafluoride; infused with uranium hexafluoride it becomes \"},{\"text\":\"fluorinated naquadah uranium fuel\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism_extras:fluorinated_naquadah_uranium_fuel_bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", finished with osmium in the reaction chamber.\"}]"
  ],
  "image.54D1CF7CBDDFC33A.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Radiation\",\"color\":\"#7FD4F0\"}]",
  "image.16482BB9A00D5988.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Naquadah reactor\",\"color\":\"#7FD4F0\"}]",
  "image.3A49A9AD207ED930.title": "Back to Mekanism · Basics",
  "image.7687018B25CB4FCC.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Mekanism · Energy and reactors\",\"color\":\"#7FD4F0\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.62C11CEF9EE81780.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» Logistics and gear\",\"color\":\"#7FD4F0\"}]",
  "image.505AADC320AC9BA6.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"split fuse annihilate\",\"color\":\"#9FB8C8\",\"font\":\"minecraft:alt\"}]",
  "image.0567B1C8AFEF81D1.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Fission\",\"color\":\"#E0B84A\"}]",
  "image.271D8F7237AD4252.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Fusion\",\"color\":\"#E0B84A\"}]",
  "image.3B520A19A5DC4BF4.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Heat and steam\",\"color\":\"#E0B84A\"}]",
  "image.1F64101705A86B9A.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Generators\",\"color\":\"#7FD4F0\"}]",
  "image.33AD6D34FD5AE451.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Storage\",\"color\":\"#7FD4F0\"}]",
  "chapter.5A3F228A4F726C4A.title": "Mekanism · Logistics and gear",
  "chapter.5A3F228A4F726C4A.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Transmitters, storage, quantum machines and mining, and the gear that ends in the MekaSuit."
  ],
  "quest.35CFDD95EF0BEBE4.title": "Logistical Transporter",
  "quest.35CFDD95EF0BEBE4.quest_subtitle": "Conveyor belts are so last era.",
  "quest.35CFDD95EF0BEBE4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A basic circuit between two steel ingots makes eight \"},{\"text\":\"Logistical Transporters\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:basic_logistical_transporter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". They pull from a side set to pull and deliver to the nearest inventory that accepts. A Configurator on a connection cycles it through normal, push, pull and none.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.09371232462FDC98.title": "Upgrade a laid transmitter with an alloy",
  "quest.780288C388B8D535.title": "Upgrade in place",
  "quest.780288C388B8D535.quest_desc": [
    "Right-click a laid transmitter with the next alloy and it upgrades without breaking the line. Ultimate transporters pull a whole stack at a time and move items ten times as fast as basic ones."
  ],
  "quest.628288DF90D37CC6.title": "Past ultimate",
  "quest.628288DF90D37CC6.quest_subtitle": "Numbers go up.",
  "quest.628288DF90D37CC6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Mekanism Extras adds four tiers above ultimate to every transmitter. Eight ultimate transporters around a radiance alloy make eight \"},{\"text\":\"Absolute Logistical Transporters\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism_extras:absolute_logistical_transporter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; thermonuclear, shining and spectrum alloys climb on to Supreme, Cosmic and Infinite.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.02B9BA078BA74ED4.title": "Diversion and restriction",
  "quest.02B9BA078BA74ED4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Diversion Transporter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:diversion_transporter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" opens or closes with redstone, side by side with a Configurator. A \"},{\"text\":\"Restrictive Transporter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:restrictive_transporter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" is only used when no other path is left.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.58A15B3DB96171D5.title": "Logistical Sorter",
  "quest.58A15B3DB96171D5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Against an inventory, the \"},{\"text\":\"Logistical Sorter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:logistical_sorter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" pulls what matches its filters (item, tag or mod) into the transporter behind it, each filter with its own color. With auto-eject on, unfiltered items go out too.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.33085F4FBA3F1C38.title": "Paint the paths",
  "quest.33085F4FBA3F1C38.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A Configurator can color a transporter: colored items only ride matching or uncolored paths. A sorter per loot chest, each with its color, keeps a base tidy without digital storage.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.30F0A34B1A356CFF.title": "Oredictionificator",
  "quest.30F0A34B1A356CFF.quest_subtitle": "Yes, that is its real name.",
  "quest.30F0A34B1A356CFF.quest_desc": [
    "It turns items into the same-tag item of your choice, say one mod's ingot into another's. Almost Unified already unifies what recipes make; this one cleans up drops and old chests."
  ],
  "quest.7AD100EF8FCD9412.title": "Network Reader",
  "quest.7AD100EF8FCD9412.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Right-click a transmitter with the \"},{\"text\":\"Network Reader\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:network_reader\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": it counts the network's transmitters and acceptors and reports its buffer, capacity and throughput. The bottleneck shows up fast.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4E2B40690CB7E4C8.title": "Security Desk",
  "quest.4E2B40690CB7E4C8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Mekanism machines can be public, private or trusted. A network reader in a steel casing makes the \"},{\"text\":\"Security Desk\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:security_desk\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", which manages all of yours from one screen, including who counts as trusted.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0D7CDFC225E69930.title": "Bins",
  "quest.0D7CDFC225E69930.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Basic Bin\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:basic_bin\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" holds 4,096 of a single item and keeps them when broken. Transporters feed it and pull from it like any inventory.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3C75BCD391959DC9.title": "Ultimate Bin",
  "quest.3C75BCD391959DC9.quest_desc": [
    "Each tier wraps the last bin in its alloy and circuit: 8,192, 32,768 and 262,144 items. Extras keeps going from Absolute to Infinite; the Creative Bin has no recipe."
  ],
  "quest.3A0DF20C5DCFA229.title": "Personal storage",
  "quest.3A0DF20C5DCFA229.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Personal Chest\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:personal_chest\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a \"},{\"text\":\"Personal Barrel\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:personal_barrel\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" hold 54 slots each, open straight from your hand and can be locked to you. The Robit, the QIO array and the tractor beam each eat one.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0F53517556A943BE.title": "Transporters for the common store",
  "quest.0F53517556A943BE.quest_subtitle": "Every base needs one more line.",
  "quest.0F53517556A943BE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Thirty-two \"},{\"text\":\"Logistical Transporters\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:basic_logistical_transporter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for the common store, once a day.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.56242D5853E1D788.title": "Mechanical Pipes",
  "quest.56242D5853E1D788.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A bucket between two steel ingots makes eight \"},{\"text\":\"Mechanical Pipes\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:basic_mechanical_pipe\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". They carry fluids only: chemicals take pressurized tubes, and the two never share a line.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4670629995AFA392.title": "Fluid Tank",
  "quest.4670629995AFA392.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Basic Fluid Tank\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:basic_fluid_tank\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" carries 32 buckets and keeps them when broken. In bucket mode it picks up and places fluid in the world.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.25EA21F990D588C7.title": "Dynamic Tank",
  "quest.25EA21F990D588C7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A hollow box of \"},{\"text\":\"Dynamic Tank\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:dynamic_tank\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" blocks, glass and \"},{\"text\":\"Dynamic Valves\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:dynamic_valve\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", 3 to 18 blocks a side. It holds one fluid or one chemical: 350 buckets of fluid or 16,000 of a chemical per block of its size, walls included.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2B5CA7ED2918A593.title": "Electric Pump",
  "quest.2B5CA7ED2918A593.quest_subtitle": "Slurp.",
  "quest.2B5CA7ED2918A593.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Electric Pump\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:electric_pump\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" drains source blocks up to 80 blocks away, following the connected fluid. With a Filter Upgrade it pulls heavy water out of water instead, 10 mB per block.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.237E67AEC662E059.title": "Fluidic Plenisher",
  "quest.237E67AEC662E059.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The pump, backwards: the \"},{\"text\":\"Fluidic Plenisher\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:fluidic_plenisher\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" places fluid into the world, up to 4,000 blocks per run. Fill a ravine, drown a quarry, build a lake.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6BA1E6858BF91DC3.title": "Chemical tanks",
  "quest.6BA1E6858BF91DC3.quest_desc": [
    "Chemical tanks climb from 64 to 8,192 buckets at Ultimate and keep their contents when broken. MoreMachine's mid and max tanks wrap chemical tanks in dynamic tank blocks for more."
  ],
  "quest.31ADB01522DC9347.title": "Chemicals in AE2",
  "quest.31ADB01522DC9347.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Applied Mekanistics adds chemical cells: a \"},{\"text\":\"1k ME Chemical Storage Cell\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"appmek:chemical_storage_cell_1k\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" stores Mekanism chemicals in an AE2 network, and import and export buses move them like items.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4980D71C2A1CDF30.title": "Chemical P2P and QIO",
  "quest.4980D71C2A1CDF30.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Chemical P2P Tunnel\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"appmek:chemical_p2p_tunnel\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" carries chemicals through a single AE2 channel. And an ME Storage Bus facing a QIO Dashboard reads that QIO frequency into AE2.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.3A4D5F12F512D6CF.title": "Put a chemical disk in a disk drive",
  "quest.4C1E738B853DD5DB.title": "Chemicals in Refined Storage",
  "quest.4C1E738B853DD5DB.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Refined Storage bridge adds chemical disks from 64 to 8,192 buckets: a \"},{\"text\":\"64B Chemical Storage Disk\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage_mekanism_integration:64b_chemical_storage_disk\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in a disk drive stores Mekanism gases with the rest of the network.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.72FDB9137F8338F4.title": "Covers",
  "quest.72FDB9137F8338F4.quest_subtitle": "Pipes? What pipes?",
  "quest.72FDB9137F8338F4.quest_desc": [
    "Osmium nuggets, sawdust and glass make four Empty Covers; craft one with any block for a cover of it. Use it on a transmitter and the line hides behind your wall while it keeps working.",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Hold a Configurator in wrench mode to see and click the transmitter under a cover.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.69FAA53443B0B9B7.title": "Mekanistic Routers",
  "quest.69FAA53443B0B9B7.quest_desc": [
    "Chemical modules for Modular Routers: Mk1 moves chemicals to or from the block in front, Mk2 reaches any nearby block, and the Refill Module tops up jetpacks in your inventory wirelessly. The router needs a chemical container in its buffer."
  ],
  "quest.61D4474E5EBB99EE.title": "Recycler",
  "quest.61D4474E5EBB99EE.quest_subtitle": "A trash can with benefits.",
  "quest.61D4474E5EBB99EE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A crusher wrapped in infused alloy, advanced circuits and osmium makes MoreMachine's \"},{\"text\":\"Recycler\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekmm:recycler\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It eats stone, dirt and substrate: one in six comes out as \"},{\"text\":\"Scrap\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekmm:scrap\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", three in seven for substrate, and the rest is gone. The Osmium Compressor packs 64 scrap into a \"},{\"text\":\"Scrap Box\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekmm:scrap_box\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2968AFB27FA72DE3.title": "Ambient Gas Collector",
  "quest.2968AFB27FA72DE3.quest_subtitle": "Bottled nothing.",
  "quest.2968AFB27FA72DE3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two atomic alloys, an ultimate pressurized tube, two ultimate chemical tanks, a steel casing and three osmium blocks make the \"},{\"text\":\"Ambient Gas Collector\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekmm:ambient_gas_collector\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". With open air right above it, it draws Unstable Dimensional Gas out of nothing, slowly: about a millibucket a second, faster with speed upgrades.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1E88B5E18B0792BA.title": "Empty Crystal",
  "quest.1E88B5E18B0792BA.quest_subtitle": "Patience, crystallised.",
  "quest.1E88B5E18B0792BA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Pressurized Reaction Chamber turns 64 Scrap Boxes, 10,000 mB of Unstable Dimensional Gas and 10,000 mB of liquid D-T fuel into one \"},{\"text\":\"Empty Crystal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekmm:empty_crystal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and 1,000 mB of nuclear waste. Sixty-four crystals and antimatter in the Antiprotonic Nucleosynthesizer make one UU Matter.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "ENTRELUMEN switches MoreMachine's replicators off, so UU Matter only buys two decorative dolls. The crystal is the trophy; the rest is bragging."
  ],
  "quest.55BD3683FBEA0D6D.title": "Teleportation Core",
  "quest.55BD3683FBEA0D6D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Ender pearls, atomic alloy, gold and a diamond. The \"},{\"text\":\"Teleportation Core\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:teleportation_core\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" is the heart of every quantum machine: teleporters, the entangloporter, QIO and the Digital Miner.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2A86E8FD470FDDCC.title": "Teleporter Frame",
  "quest.2A86E8FD470FDDCC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Refined obsidian around refined glowstone: nine \"},{\"text\":\"Teleporter Frame\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:teleporter_frame\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" blocks. Build them into a doorway around an empty space, with the teleporter block as part of the frame.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.521C874127FD9BA6.title": "Build a teleporter and go through it",
  "quest.2F8F385F077C7A3E.title": "Teleporter",
  "quest.2F8F385F077C7A3E.quest_subtitle": "Now you see me.",
  "quest.2F8F385F077C7A3E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"In this pack the \"},{\"text\":\"Teleporter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:teleporter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" has a \"},{\"text\":\"Routing Matrix\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:routing_matrix\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" above its core: act III. Pick a destination on its frequency and walk through: 1,000 J, plus 10 per block, plus 10,000 across dimensions.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.71CA15B14166184F.title": "Portable Teleporter",
  "quest.71CA15B14166184F.quest_subtitle": "Beam me up.",
  "quest.71CA15B14166184F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A core between energy tablets and basic circuits. The \"},{\"text\":\"Portable Teleporter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:portable_teleporter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" jumps you to any teleporter on its frequency, from wherever you stand, as long as it is charged.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7734F3CA01E08282.title": "Quantum Entangloporter",
  "quest.7734F3CA01E08282.quest_subtitle": "Spooky action at a distance.",
  "quest.7734F3CA01E08282.quest_desc": [
    "Entangloporters on one frequency share items, fluids, chemicals, energy and heat at once, at any distance and across dimensions. Set their sides like a machine: power in here, ore out there."
  ],
  "quest.3F26FE59AD7D310A.title": "Wireless Transmission Station",
  "quest.3F26FE59AD7D310A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An entangloporter, a Robit and a supercharged coil go into MoreMachine's \"},{\"text\":\"Wireless Transmission Station\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekmm:wireless_transmission_station\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It sends energy, fluids, chemicals and more to blocks linked with its Connector, no transmitters in between, within one dimension.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.66C520DFF400128D.title": "QIO Drive Array",
  "quest.66C520DFF400128D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Quantum Item Orchestration: the \"},{\"text\":\"QIO Drive Array\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:qio_drive_array\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" holds the drives and everything else reaches it by frequency, no cables. In this pack an \"},{\"text\":\"Inventory Sensor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:inventory_sensor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" takes the glass's place: act III.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1979979E1A2C4484.title": "QIO or AE2?",
  "quest.1979979E1A2C4484.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"QIO has no channels and no cables, but its first drive already wants four ultimate circuits. AE2 starts cheaper and autocrafts deeper. Pick one main system; the bridges let the others feed it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.47C4442B0614B5A0.title": "QIO Drive",
  "quest.47C4442B0614B5A0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four ultimate circuits around an ender pearl, lead in the corners: a \"},{\"text\":\"QIO Drive\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:qio_drive_base\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" holds 16,000 items of up to 128 kinds. An array takes twelve.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.12E90346DFB48D27.title": "Denser drives",
  "quest.12E90346DFB48D27.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four drives, plutonium and a teleportation core make a Hyper-Dense one (128,000 items). Four of those with plutonium and polonium make a Time-Dilating one (1,048,000); four of those with polonium and antimatter, the \"},{\"text\":\"Supermassive QIO Drive\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:qio_drive_supermassive\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": sixteen billion.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7C607770F2B53FC1.title": "Drives from Extras",
  "quest.7C607770F2B53FC1.quest_subtitle": "Event horizon storage.",
  "quest.7C607770F2B53FC1.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Mekanism Extras keeps stacking: four supermassive drives, lead and an antimatter pellet make a \"},{\"text\":\"Collapse QIO Drive\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism_extras:qio_drive_collapse\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", and the same recipe climbs to Gamma, Black Hole and the \"},{\"text\":\"Singularity QIO Drive\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism_extras:qio_drive_singularity\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0B9671877CD95815.title": "QIO Dashboard",
  "quest.0B9671877CD95815.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Lead, ender pearls and a teleportation core: the \"},{\"text\":\"QIO Dashboard\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:qio_dashboard\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" shows the whole frequency, searches it and has crafting windows that pull straight from storage.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.27D4F630282E2F33.title": "Portable QIO Dashboard",
  "quest.27D4F630282E2F33.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A dashboard ringed with polonium, a teleportation core below: the \"},{\"text\":\"Portable QIO Dashboard\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:portable_qio_dashboard\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" is the whole base in your pocket.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4D91D5E9A9036EE6.title": "Importer and exporter",
  "quest.4D91D5E9A9036EE6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Place a \"},{\"text\":\"QIO Importer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:qio_importer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on a chest and its contents move into the frequency; a \"},{\"text\":\"QIO Exporter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:qio_exporter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" pushes filtered items out into a block. Machines fed straight from storage.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6D87EB6875CDE3DB.title": "QIO Redstone Adapter",
  "quest.6D87EB6875CDE3DB.quest_subtitle": "Redstone, now with quantum.",
  "quest.6D87EB6875CDE3DB.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"QIO Redstone Adapter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:qio_redstone_adapter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" watches one item in the frequency and gives a signal past a count: switch a farm off when the store is full.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.4154EE7A50A4FAC8.title": "Place a Robit on a Chargepad",
  "quest.2B9C871772346B23.title": "Robit",
  "quest.2B9C871772346B23.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Steel, atomic alloy, refined obsidian and two energy tablets around a personal chest. Placed on a \"},{\"text\":\"Chargepad\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:chargepad\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", the \"},{\"text\":\"Robit\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:robit\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" follows you, picks up drops, crafts, smelts and repairs, and goes home to charge when it runs dry.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.364ECDE9349AD343.title": "A new coat of paint",
  "quest.364ECDE9349AD343.quest_subtitle": "Fashion before function.",
  "quest.364ECDE9349AD343.quest_desc": [
    "You changed your Robit's skin. It did not ask, but it looks happier."
  ],
  "reward.0287D52F3566A9AA.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.03BFBDEE2B611179.title": "Wireless Charging Station",
  "quest.03BFBDEE2B611179.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Robit, an ultimate energy cube and a teleportation core go into MoreMachine's \"},{\"text\":\"Wireless Charging Station\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekmm:wireless_charging_station\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It charges what you carry and wear nearby, Curios included.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.679EE6710CBD36EA.title": "Digital Miner",
  "quest.679EE6710CBD36EA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Robit, two sorters and two teleportation cores make a \"},{\"text\":\"Digital Miner\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:digital_miner\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; in this pack a \"},{\"text\":\"Spectral Lens\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:spectral_lens\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" takes the circuit's place, so it is act IV. It mines whatever its filters name, up to 32 blocks out.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.49C447AD2B59E38E.title": "Filters and upgrades",
  "quest.49C447AD2B59E38E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Tag filters for ores catch every mod's ore at once. The miner takes 80 ticks a block before upgrades, and silk touch costs twelve times the energy: speed and energy upgrades pay off here.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.44EB1E0FBFC15996.title": "Stone Generator Upgrade",
  "quest.44EB1E0FBFC15996.quest_subtitle": "Filling holes since forever.",
  "quest.44EB1E0FBFC15996.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Water, lava and infused alloy make a \"},{\"text\":\"Stone Generator Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:upgrade_stone_generator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". In the Digital Miner, filters that replace mined blocks with stone or cobblestone stop using up items: no holes under the base, for free.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.6EDA72F27463FB1C.title": "Craft a Dimensional Stabilizer and an Anchor Upgrade",
  "quest.021E60BA01115D24.title": "Keeping it loaded",
  "quest.021E60BA01115D24.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Machines only run in loaded chunks. An \"},{\"text\":\"Anchor Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:upgrade_anchor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" keeps its own machine's chunk loaded; the \"},{\"text\":\"Dimensional Stabilizer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:dimensional_stabilizer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" loads the chunks you pick around it. Load only what must run alone.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.6A2066374F002EBD.title": "Build a Seismic Vibrator and Reader and read the ground",
  "quest.1CB8EC04D9B64321.title": "Seismic survey",
  "quest.1CB8EC04D9B64321.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A powered \"},{\"text\":\"Seismic Vibrator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:seismic_vibrator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" shakes the ground; a \"},{\"text\":\"Seismic Reader\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:seismic_reader\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" used beside it lists every layer down to bedrock. Pick the miner's spot before you pay for it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7BC44D289E1C6E3C.title": "Laser Tractor Beam",
  "quest.7BC44D289E1C6E3C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A laser amplifier with a personal chest on top: the \"},{\"text\":\"Laser Tractor Beam\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:laser_tractor_beam\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" merges and redirects beams and keeps the drops of what they break. A laser quarry, no miner needed.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7E392FDE02536764.title": "Get out of my spectrum",
  "quest.7E392FDE02536764.quest_subtitle": "Shields up.",
  "quest.7E392FDE02536764.quest_desc": [
    "You blocked a laser with a shield. Not the intended use of a shield, not the intended use of a laser."
  ],
  "reward.6DEF77EA7F49997F.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.535746100461D7D7.title": "Crispy",
  "quest.535746100461D7D7.quest_subtitle": "Well done. Very well done.",
  "quest.535746100461D7D7.quest_desc": [
    "A laser killed you. The beam reaches 64 blocks; stand farther than that next time."
  ],
  "reward.140D99DCF52F9767.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.22BECC4BB3890D57.title": "Paxel",
  "quest.22BECC4BB3890D57.quest_subtitle": "Pickaxe, axe, shovel. One slot.",
  "quest.22BECC4BB3890D57.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An axe, a pickaxe and a shovel of the same material on two sticks: a paxel. Mekanism Tools makes one for every vanilla material and its own osmium, bronze, steel, lapis and refined metals. The \"},{\"text\":\"Osmium Paxel\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanismtools:osmium_paxel\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" is a fine start.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.63410A90CB09B063.title": "Craft any Mekanism Tools armor piece",
  "quest.6A64E9D3DE5163E4.title": "More armor types",
  "quest.6A64E9D3DE5163E4.quest_desc": [
    "Mekanism Tools armor comes in osmium, bronze, steel, lapis, refined glowstone and refined obsidian, with tools and a shield for each. Bronze and steel sit between iron and diamond."
  ],
  "task.2386E7F26311C284.title": "Wear a piece of refined obsidian armor",
  "quest.75B83911CB666CA7.title": "Better than netherite",
  "quest.75B83911CB666CA7.quest_desc": [
    "Refined obsidian armor is the toughest set Mekanism Tools makes, above netherite. Refined obsidian comes from the Osmium Compressor."
  ],
  "quest.60405B00C5DADA2B.title": "Loved by piglins",
  "quest.60405B00C5DADA2B.quest_subtitle": "Brighter than gold, and they know it.",
  "quest.60405B00C5DADA2B.quest_desc": [
    "You wore refined glowstone armor. It glows brighter than gold, and piglins are very impressed."
  ],
  "reward.1CAD7D74CFD179DF.title": "Secret found",
  "task.51B45AF4ACC2F588.title": "Craft any Mekanism Tools shield",
  "quest.5CB5EBB88BD36F2B.title": "Not enough shielding",
  "quest.5CB5EBB88BD36F2B.quest_desc": [
    "A vanilla shield wrapped in ingots of a Mekanism Tools metal: a tougher shield that still takes banners."
  ],
  "quest.279A270193972EF0.title": "Atomic Disassembler",
  "quest.279A270193972EF0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Atomic and infused alloy, refined obsidian and an energy tablet: a powered tool for every block, and a weapon too. \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.mekanism.mode\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" switches its digging between normal, slow, fast and off. The Meka-Tool starts from one.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5806AB6DDADBB8C8.title": "Jetpack",
  "quest.5806AB6DDADBB8C8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"In this pack the \"},{\"text\":\"Jetpack\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:jetpack\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" has a \"},{\"text\":\"Power Regulator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:power_regulator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in its nozzle (act III) and burns 2.5 mB of hydrogen per tick instead of 1, like every jetpack here: its 24,000 mB last eight minutes of thrust.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.mekanism.chest_mode\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" cycles regular, hover and off.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4F745D11A483BCB2.title": "Armored Jetpack",
  "quest.4F745D11A483BCB2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Bronze, a steel block and diamond dust on a jetpack: the \"},{\"text\":\"Armored Jetpack\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:jetpack_armored\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" flies the same, burns the same, and protects like a chestplate.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1C956AD8E29B52C3.title": "HDPE Reinforced Elytra",
  "quest.1C956AD8E29B52C3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An elytra with HDPE sheets and atomic alloy: the \"},{\"text\":\"HDPE Reinforced Elytra\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:hdpe_elytra\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" glides like the original. With polonium and antimatter it becomes the MekaSuit's Elytra Unit.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.6ACBD1D5C4C28017.title": "Craft a Scuba Mask and Tank",
  "quest.105257561073EEA6.title": "Scuba gear",
  "quest.105257561073EEA6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Scuba Mask\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:scuba_mask\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a \"},{\"text\":\"Scuba Tank\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:scuba_tank\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" of oxygen let you breathe underwater. With your air full, effects that milk would clear wear off ten times as fast, good ones too. \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.mekanism.chest_mode\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" opens the valve.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.77C0D89C097DA818.title": "Craft a Flamethrower",
  "quest.2ECEE5427C87F580.title": "Flamethrower",
  "quest.2ECEE5427C87F580.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Flamethrower\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:flamethrower\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" burns hydrogen. In heat mode it smelts what it hits: sand turns to glass where it lies, and raw ore left on the floor comes back as ingots. Other modes just burn dropped items.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.001B133EFC0CB720.title": "Craft Free Runners",
  "quest.2B8D6B858A96EABA.title": "Free Runners",
  "quest.2B8D6B858A96EABA.quest_subtitle": "Free falling, minus the falling.",
  "quest.2B8D6B858A96EABA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Charged \"},{\"text\":\"Free Runners\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:free_runners\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" absorb all fall damage at 50 J per point and step up half a block more. Armored ones add a steel block, bronze and diamond dust.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0DCAD9D923C5CDCC.title": "Electric Bow",
  "quest.0DCAD9D923C5CDCC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"String, infused alloy and an energy tablet: the \"},{\"text\":\"Electric Bow\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:electric_bow\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" draws on its charge instead of wearing out, 120 J a shot, ten times that in flame mode for burning arrows.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.31B91F6DC3C0DCC5.title": "Liquid lunch",
  "quest.31B91F6DC3C0DCC5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Nutritional Liquifier\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:nutritional_liquifier\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" turns any food into nutritional paste, 50 mB per hunger point; a \"},{\"text\":\"Canteen\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:canteen\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" carries it and feeds you from your belt.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.221194AE890F34AD.title": "Tasty paste",
  "quest.221194AE890F34AD.quest_subtitle": "Chef's kiss. Probably.",
  "quest.221194AE890F34AD.quest_desc": [
    "You filled a Canteen to the brim with nutritional paste. Nobody said it tasted good."
  ],
  "reward.51287D1418FA3026.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.2AA764325E9BCC16.title": "Modification Station",
  "quest.2AA764325E9BCC16.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"HDPE, ultimate circuits, polonium and a chest on a steel casing. The \"},{\"text\":\"Modification Station\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:modification_station\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" installs and removes modules on the MekaSuit and the Meka-Tool.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.315075D52E32C2A3.title": "Suit controls",
  "quest.315075D52E32C2A3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.mekanism.module_tweaker\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" opens the module tweaker to toggle modules on the fly. \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.mekanism.head_mode\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\", \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.mekanism.chest_mode\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\", \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.mekanism.legs_mode\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" and \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.mekanism.feet_mode\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" cycle each piece's mode.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.38DEB312C5BB3ED8.title": "Meka-Tool",
  "quest.38DEB312C5BB3ED8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An atomic disassembler with a configurator, HDPE, ultimate circuits, polonium and an induction cell: the \"},{\"text\":\"Meka-Tool\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:meka_tool\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Modules make it dig faster, vein mine, take silk touch or fortune, and teleport.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3B4B14B5E1EC074D.title": "MekaSuit",
  "quest.3B4B14B5E1EC074D.quest_subtitle": "Netherite, but make it electric.",
  "quest.3B4B14B5E1EC074D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Each piece is a netherite piece in HDPE with polonium and an induction cell; in this pack an \"},{\"text\":\"Engineering Luminosity\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:luminosity_engineering\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" takes the circuit's place, so the suit is act VI. It runs on power and absorbs damage with it.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.2F1AD0A8D6D9AC55.title": "Wear the MekaSuit and hold a Meka-Tool",
  "quest.3DAD731E19FA8CED.title": "Mekanist",
  "quest.3DAD731E19FA8CED.quest_subtitle": "Everything you built, worn at once.",
  "quest.3DAD731E19FA8CED.quest_desc": [
    "The whole MekaSuit on and a Meka-Tool in hand. Every chapter of Mekanism went into it: alloys, reactors, polonium, and antimatter for the Gravitational Modulating Unit."
  ],
  "quest.635123388EFF19BD.title": "True dedication",
  "quest.635123388EFF19BD.quest_subtitle": "Every slot, every module.",
  "quest.635123388EFF19BD.quest_desc": [
    "You installed the maximum of every module in the MekaSuit and the Meka-Tool. There is nothing left to add, and it shows."
  ],
  "reward.722CE16547CA06B0.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.69E5BBA8648BAE2A.title": "Module Base",
  "quest.69E5BBA8648BAE2A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Bronze nuggets, tin and an HDPE sheet make two \"},{\"text\":\"Module Bases\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:module_base\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Every module starts from one plus its own parts; the suit or the tool, whichever comes first, is enough to begin.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.49C3B132C7143FCC.title": "Movement modules",
  "quest.49C3B132C7143FCC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Jetpack Unit\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:module_jetpack_unit\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" eats a whole jetpack and flies on hydrogen (2.5 to 10 mB/t in this pack). \"},{\"text\":\"Locomotive Boosting\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:module_locomotive_boosting_unit\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" speeds up sprinting and \"},{\"text\":\"Hydraulic Propulsion\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:module_hydraulic_propulsion_unit\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" jumps higher.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.40A9FE85A7C68752.title": "Mining modules",
  "quest.40A9FE85A7C68752.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Excavation Escalation\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:module_excavation_escalation_unit\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" digs faster, up to four stacked; \"},{\"text\":\"Vein Mining\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:module_vein_mining_unit\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" takes whole veins and trees; the \"},{\"text\":\"Ore Refinement Unit\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:module_fortune_unit\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" is fortune up to III and cannot share the tool with silk touch.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0B83F2430051E646.title": "Survival modules",
  "quest.0B83F2430051E646.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Radiation Shielding\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:module_radiation_shielding_unit\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on every piece keeps a meltdown survivable, \"},{\"text\":\"Inhalation Purification\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:module_inhalation_purification_unit\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" blocks the potion effects you pick and \"},{\"text\":\"Nutritional Injection\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:module_nutritional_injection_unit\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" feeds you paste.\"}]"
  ],
  "image.425759D5CA3C3276.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Items\",\"color\":\"#7FD4F0\"}]",
  "image.3B5217EEB3072D69.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Fluids\",\"color\":\"#7FD4F0\"}]",
  "image.2AD930F6F2F46E72.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Chemicals, bridges and matter\",\"color\":\"#7FD4F0\"}]",
  "image.48A8CEEF35B72A56.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Teleportation\",\"color\":\"#7FD4F0\"}]",
  "image.0103A4486F68003A.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Quantum Item Orchestration\",\"color\":\"#7FD4F0\"}]",
  "image.224BD95C64D2080E.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Robit and mining\",\"color\":\"#7FD4F0\"}]",
  "image.029EE49DDABBD410.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Laser quarry\",\"color\":\"#7FD4F0\"}]",
  "image.188788918999A518.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Mekanism Tools\",\"color\":\"#7FD4F0\"}]",
  "image.52D6DBD986B8EB96.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Gear\",\"color\":\"#7FD4F0\"}]",
  "image.5E85D712763A7441.title": "Back to Mekanism · Basics",
  "image.3A133C3EE0C3B01D.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Mekanism · Logistics and gear\",\"color\":\"#7FD4F0\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.15FF3E29D083C953.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» Energy and reactors\",\"color\":\"#7FD4F0\"}]",
  "image.629B429769590414.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"items fluids chemicals and you\",\"color\":\"#9FB8C8\",\"font\":\"minecraft:alt\"}]",
  "chapter.0F14CDFA7E1FF965.title": "Modern Industrialization · Electricity",
  "chapter.0F14CDFA7E1FF965.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Rubber, cables and circuits, the turbine and the assembler, the electric blast furnace and a refinery that ends in diesel."
  ],
  "quest.347E05CC70B27244.title": "Rubber",
  "quest.347E05CC70B27244.quest_subtitle": "Every machine asks for it. Every one.",
  "quest.347E05CC70B27244.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Coke dust and 100 mB of water in the Mixer make 200 mB of raw synthetic oil; the Steam Blast Furnace cooks it into synthetic oil, and paper with 100 mB of it makes two \"},{\"text\":\"Rubber Sheets\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modern_industrialization:rubber_sheet\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". The Mixer makes two paper from wood pulp and water.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Automate it early: cables, circuits, conveyors and the first hull all want rubber.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5B0213FF43FB35E9.title": "Cables",
  "quest.5B0213FF43FB35E9.quest_desc": [
    "The wiremill turns a plate into two wires. Three wires between six rubber sheets make three cables, by hand or in the Packer. Copper, tin and silver are LV: 32 EU per tick of tier, up to 256 EU/t into one network."
  ],
  "quest.718F567E0B439E0F.title": "R, L and C",
  "quest.718F567E0B439E0F.quest_subtitle": "The C in RLC.",
  "quest.718F567E0B439E0F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Resistors\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modern_industrialization:resistor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": copper fine wire, coal dust and paper. \"},{\"text\":\"Capacitors\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modern_industrialization:capacitor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": gold plates, copper wire and rubber. \"},{\"text\":\"Inductors\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modern_industrialization:inductor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": eight copper wires around a steel rod. Every analog circuit takes all three.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.24986923801E5674.title": "Analog Circuit",
  "quest.24986923801E5674.quest_subtitle": "RLC, the whole alphabet.",
  "quest.24986923801E5674.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An inductor, two resistors, two capacitors and three copper wires on an \"},{\"text\":\"Analog Circuit Board\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modern_industrialization:analog_circuit_board\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", which is a copper plate between two rubber sheets. The Electric Age runs on these.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6CAFC4E978B2318D.title": "Redstone Battery",
  "quest.6CAFC4E978B2318D.quest_desc": [
    "Lead and antimony dust mix into battery alloy; its plates and curved plates, redstone and two tin cables make the battery. Antimony is MI's own ore, below height 64."
  ],
  "quest.7DA382F1EC03A522.title": "Basic Machine Hull",
  "quest.7DA382F1EC03A522.quest_desc": [
    "An analog circuit, three tin cables and two redstone batteries on a steel machine casing. Every LV machine is built around one, and its hull decides which cables it accepts."
  ],
  "quest.5066D5824BDC4EF5.title": "Motors",
  "quest.5066D5824BDC4EF5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A magnetic steel rod, two steel rods, two tin cables and four copper wires. The magnetic rod takes eight redstone around a steel rod by hand; the \"},{\"text\":\"Polarizer\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"4690DCF1D93992F4\"}},{\"text\":\" makes it from the rod alone.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.06A9F570B460CEDF.title": "LV Steam Turbine",
  "quest.06A9F570B460CEDF.quest_subtitle": "Better than solar panels.",
  "quest.06A9F570B460CEDF.quest_desc": [
    "An analog circuit, two motors, a hull, two fluid pipes, two tin rotors and a tin cable. It turns 1 mB of steam into 1 EU, up to 32 per tick, and hands it only to cables on its output side. One EU is worth 10 FE in this pack."
  ],
  "quest.459B5981597ADD6D.title": "Pistons, pumps, belts, arms",
  "quest.459B5981597ADD6D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four parts built on motors: the \"},{\"text\":\"Piston\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modern_industrialization:piston\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" adds steel plates and a gear, the \"},{\"text\":\"Pump\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modern_industrialization:pump\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" tin rotors and fluid pipes, the \"},{\"text\":\"Conveyor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modern_industrialization:conveyor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" six rubber sheets, and the \"},{\"text\":\"Robot Arm\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modern_industrialization:robot_arm\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" a piston and a circuit.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.48D47667F4C39134.title": "Assembler",
  "quest.48D47667F4C39134.quest_subtitle": "Avengers, assemble.",
  "quest.48D47667F4C39134.quest_desc": [
    "Four robot arms, two analog circuits, two conveyors and a hull. It automates almost every crafting recipe of the mod, often at a better yield, and holds up to three recipes at once with locked slots. Put hulls, circuits, motors, pistons, robot arms and conveyors on assemblers first."
  ],
  "quest.4690DCF1D93992F4.title": "Polarizer",
  "quest.4690DCF1D93992F4.quest_subtitle": "One recipe (+2) to rule them all.",
  "quest.4690DCF1D93992F4.quest_desc": [
    "Tin wires, two inductors, two tin cables and a hull. It magnetizes steel rods without the eight redstone, and it is the only source of magnetic cupronickel wire, which the blast furnace, the electric furnace and the electrolyzer need."
  ],
  "quest.4CEEEC831ADE613B.title": "Coils and heatproof casings",
  "quest.4CEEEC831ADE613B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Copper and nickel dust mix into cupronickel; eight of its cables ring into a \"},{\"text\":\"Cupronickel Coil\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modern_industrialization:cupronickel_coil\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Invar plates around an invar gear make a \"},{\"text\":\"Heatproof Machine Casing\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modern_industrialization:heatproof_machine_casing\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3E3A5EE58B8536B4.title": "Electric Blast Furnace",
  "quest.3E3A5EE58B8536B4.quest_subtitle": "Electric best friend.",
  "quest.3E3A5EE58B8536B4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Seven magnetic cupronickel wires, a hull and a blast furnace. A heatproof layer, two hollow layers of coils and another heatproof layer; controller and hatches on the top or bottom layer, and an \"},{\"text\":\"Energy Input Hatch\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modern_industrialization:lv_energy_input_hatch\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" to feed it. Cupronickel coils allow recipes up to 32 EU/t.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.05200862F8FA217A.title": "Aluminum",
  "quest.05200862F8FA217A.quest_desc": [
    "Bauxite dust in the blast furnace gives an aluminum nugget every 10 seconds at 32 EU/t; a block of bauxite gives an ingot. Bauxite is MI's own ore, below height 32. Almost Unified hands out Immersive Engineering's ingot."
  ],
  "quest.7B18F51947A578AF.title": "Silicon",
  "quest.7B18F51947A578AF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Quartz dust and coke dust in the blast furnace make silicon dust at 32 EU/t. Smelt it into ingots and press them into \"},{\"text\":\"Silicon Plates\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modern_industrialization:silicon_plate\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for diodes and transistors.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5AAC305B1302996A.title": "Diodes and transistors",
  "quest.5AAC305B1302996A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Both are steel plates, silicon and electrum fine wire: a \"},{\"text\":\"Diode\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modern_industrialization:diode\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" adds glass and gives one, three steel over three silicon plates give two \"},{\"text\":\"Transistors\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modern_industrialization:transistor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Electrum wire comes from the wiremill like copper.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.096E7B421A9F292A.title": "Electronic Circuit",
  "quest.096E7B421A9F292A.quest_subtitle": "The power of silicon.",
  "quest.096E7B421A9F292A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four analog circuits, two diodes and two transistors on an \"},{\"text\":\"Electronic Circuit Board\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modern_industrialization:electronic_circuit_board\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": aluminum plates, electrum cables, an analog board and a redstone battery. The centrifuge, the chemical reactor, the distillery and the electrolyzer all need them.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.18D7085B81FCC178.title": "Large motor and pump",
  "quest.18D7085B81FCC178.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Six motors, two aluminum rods and an electronic circuit make a \"},{\"text\":\"Large Motor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modern_industrialization:large_motor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; three pumps, three aluminum rotors, a large motor and two circuits make a \"},{\"text\":\"Large Pump\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modern_industrialization:large_pump\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Every aluminum-age machine takes one.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1E9963A7B9C3EA10.title": "Distillery",
  "quest.1E9963A7B9C3EA10.quest_subtitle": "Al Capone approves.",
  "quest.1E9963A7B9C3EA10.quest_desc": [
    "Glass, a fluid pipe, two large pumps, a hull, two electronic circuits and an electrum cable. It splits a fluid into one lighter part per recipe: a bucket of crude oil gives 500 mB of sulfuric light fuel, 200 of sulfuric heavy fuel or 300 of sulfuric naphtha."
  ],
  "quest.151D921ED00F5879.title": "Advanced Machine Hull",
  "quest.151D921ED00F5879.quest_desc": [
    "An electronic circuit, two silicon batteries and three electrum cables on an advanced machine casing, aluminum plates around a basic hull. Right-click a machine with it and the machine turns MV: it then connects to MV cables only."
  ],
  "quest.1E682E77776C3BD2.title": "Oil Drilling Rig",
  "quest.1E682E77776C3BD2.quest_subtitle": "Freedom, by the barrel.",
  "quest.1E682E77776C3BD2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four steel large plates, an electronic circuit, two large pumps, an advanced hull and a pipe. Walled in steel casings, steel pipe casings and chains, it eats \"},{\"text\":\"Aluminum Drills\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modern_industrialization:aluminum_drill\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" under bedrock: 500 mB of crude oil every 10 seconds at 8 EU/t.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.475D64A24D3E1891.title": "Sweeten the fuel",
  "quest.475D64A24D3E1891.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Electrolyzer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modern_industrialization:electrolyzer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" splits 3,000 mB of water into 2,000 of hydrogen and 1,000 of oxygen. The \"},{\"text\":\"Chemical Reactor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modern_industrialization:chemical_reactor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" spends 2,000 mB of hydrogen to clean 12,000 of a sulfuric fuel, and gives back sulfuric acid.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.17E89ABAAF3DE720.title": "Diesel",
  "quest.17E89ABAAF3DE720.quest_subtitle": "Black gold, refined.",
  "quest.17E89ABAAF3DE720.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A thousand mB of heavy fuel and 5,000 of light fuel mix into 6,000 of diesel, 400 EU per mB. The \"},{\"text\":\"MV Diesel Generator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modern_industrialization:mv_diesel_generator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" burns it only when something draws power, up to 256 EU/t, and connects to MV cables only.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A fully heated \"},{\"text\":\"Large Steam Boiler\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"5AB3105DF0C1755B\"}},{\"text\":\" gets about twice the energy from the same fuel, if it never idles.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4216F075F5BC7246.title": "MV cables",
  "quest.4216F075F5BC7246.quest_desc": [
    "Electrum and cupronickel cables are MV: up to 1,024 EU/t into a network, four times LV. Single-block LV machines won't connect to them; transformers or an advanced hull bridge the tiers."
  ],
  "quest.78CF4610D3A41AA2.title": "LV to MV Transformer",
  "quest.78CF4610D3A41AA2.quest_desc": [
    "A basic hull, four tin cables and an electrum cable. Five faces take LV in and one gives MV out; its twin, MV to LV, does the reverse."
  ],
  "quest.7927054B7722F1B9.title": "LV Storage Unit",
  "quest.7927054B7722F1B9.quest_desc": [
    "Six redstone batteries, two battery alloy plates and a basic hull. It holds 3.2 million EU and buffers a turbine against machines that all start at once."
  ],
  "quest.1527A2BF0F988F4D.title": "Portable Storage Unit",
  "quest.1527A2BF0F988F4D.quest_desc": [
    "Battery alloy plates, tin cables and an analog circuit. It stores nothing until you load batteries into it; right-click a storage unit to charge it or drain it, and carry the energy wherever you go."
  ],
  "quest.0D7382B6FA622437.title": "LV Diesel Generator",
  "quest.0D7382B6FA622437.quest_desc": [
    "A hull, two pumps, two tin gears, three tin cables and an analog circuit. It burns any fluid fuel up to 64 EU/t: creosote from the coke oven already gives 160 EU per mB."
  ],
  "quest.65B117C8372168A4.title": "MV Steam Turbine",
  "quest.65B117C8372168A4.quest_subtitle": "Better than windmills.",
  "quest.65B117C8372168A4.quest_desc": [
    "An advanced hull, an electronic circuit, two aluminum rotors, two large motors and an electrum cable. The same steam, 128 EU/t, on MV cables."
  ],
  "quest.734C765B94E5D3AE.title": "Electric workshop",
  "quest.734C765B94E5D3AE.quest_desc": [
    "Electric versions of the steam machines, on hulls and motors; the macerator spins an invar rotary blade. They work like the steam ones but overclock their recipes up to 32 EU/t, faster the longer they run."
  ],
  "quest.2A12201D1CB5E042.title": "Configurable Chest",
  "quest.2A12201D1CB5E042.quest_desc": [
    "A steel casing, two motors, two hoppers and four analog circuits make four. Twenty-seven slots you can lock and cap, with auto-eject: the buffer between a line and its storage."
  ],
  "quest.390997195BA43BB0.title": "Configurable Tank",
  "quest.390997195BA43BB0.quest_desc": [
    "Aluminum tanks, pumps, analog circuits and a steel casing make four. Nine slots of 16 buckets each with auto-eject, for lines that juggle several fluids."
  ],
  "quest.17F903BAFABAECE5.title": "Redstone Control Module",
  "quest.17F903BAFABAECE5.quest_desc": [
    "Redstone, a torch, a capacitor, two resistors, two inductors and an analog board. Set it in your hand, then slot it into a machine or a multiblock controller: redstone decides when it runs."
  ],
  "quest.7B98A313BAEA05F1.title": "Basic Upgrade",
  "quest.7B98A313BAEA05F1.quest_subtitle": "Machine speedup.",
  "quest.7B98A313BAEA05F1.quest_desc": [
    "Only the assembler makes them: two conveyors, four motors, two robot arms and an analog board give four. Each one in a machine's upgrade slot raises its overclock cap by 2 EU/t; a stack counts whole."
  ],
  "quest.372085A3966DC0B6.title": "Pipe Config Card",
  "quest.372085A3966DC0B6.quest_desc": [
    "Glass panes, a capacitor, two resistors, two inductors and an analog board. Sneak-use it on an item pipe to copy its filter, use it on another to paste; held in the offhand it configures every item pipe you place."
  ],
  "quest.75246B8BC04859E1.title": "Lubricant",
  "quest.75246B8BC04859E1.quest_subtitle": "Grease is the word.",
  "quest.75246B8BC04859E1.quest_desc": [
    "Redstone and 500 mB of creosote mix into 500 mB of lubricant. Right-click an electric machine with a container of it: each 25 mB is one tick of overclock efficiency, and the cutting machine sips 1 mB per cut."
  ],
  "quest.21B97F891578A2BD.title": "Soldering Alloy",
  "quest.21B97F891578A2BD.quest_desc": [
    "Tin and lead dust mix into soldering alloy; any blast furnace melts a dust into 90 mB at 4 EU/t. The assembler uses it for better parts: two gears from four plates and a ring, a rotor from four blades and a ring, no bolts."
  ],
  "quest.5AB3105DF0C1755B.title": "Large Steam Boiler",
  "quest.5AB3105DF0C1755B.quest_subtitle": "Kiss your fuel goodbye.",
  "quest.5AB3105DF0C1755B.quest_desc": [
    "Bronze plated bricks, two analog circuits, a bronze boiler and curved plates. One heatproof layer, then three of bronze plated bricks with two bronze pipe casings in the middle; controller on the second layer, hatches on the bottom. Fully heated it makes 256 mB of steam per tick."
  ],
  "quest.480D294DD7BEBE4E.title": "Advanced Large Steam Boiler",
  "quest.480D294DD7BEBE4E.quest_desc": [
    "A large steam boiler with four pumps, two large pumps and two electronic circuits. Bigger, and up to 1,024 mB of steam per tick."
  ],
  "quest.48BB2E658CF26A65.title": "Large Tank",
  "quest.48BB2E658CF26A65.quest_desc": [
    "Steel tanks, pumps, tin rotors and a steel casing. Its size is chosen in the controller, and it stores 64 buckets per block of the structure, sides included. Break the controller and the fluid is gone."
  ],
  "quest.53BF48993AB2C569.title": "Electric Quarry",
  "quest.53BF48993AB2C569.quest_subtitle": "Resources go brrr.",
  "quest.53BF48993AB2C569.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Steam Quarry's shape with power instead of steam. In this pack two \"},{\"text\":\"Ironwood Ingots\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:ironwood_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" from the Twilight Forest replace two of its large motors, next to a robot arm, electronic circuits, a steam quarry and an advanced hull: act IV.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5AA0D688CBDB6575.title": "Steel and gold drills",
  "quest.5AA0D688CBDB6575.quest_desc": [
    "Two motors, iron gears, item pipes, a tin cable and an analog circuit around a drill head make four. In the Electric Quarry a steel drill brings bauxite, antimony, lead, nickel, salt and gems; a gold drill digs up the Nether, ancient debris included."
  ],
  "quest.40C6B59575168D85.title": "Centrifuge",
  "quest.40C6B59575168D85.quest_subtitle": "Actually, it's centripetal.",
  "quest.40C6B59575168D85.quest_desc": [
    "Four large motors, a large pump, electrum cables, a hull and a circuit. It spins coal dust into carbon dust: in the blast furnace four iron dusts and a carbon dust give five steel, and two quartz dusts and one carbon two silicon."
  ],
  "quest.7E917E0D3F56C2BD.title": "Diesel Jetpack",
  "quest.7E917E0D3F56C2BD.quest_subtitle": "Ely... we meant jetpack.",
  "quest.7E917E0D3F56C2BD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Pumps, motors, aluminum rotors, an aluminum tank and a circuit; in this pack a Mekanism \"},{\"text\":\"Reinforced Alloy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:alloy_reinforced\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" too, act III. It burns any fluid fuel, faster with stronger fuel, and turns on with \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.modern_industrialization.toggle_flight\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\".\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"This pack makes every jetpack pay 2.5 times its fuel: 2.5 mB per tick in the air and 5 while climbing, so a bucket lasts 20 seconds aloft. Stronger fuel flies faster for the same millibuckets.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5A013FE12BFC14B3.title": "Rubber helmet and boots",
  "quest.5A013FE12BFC14B3.quest_desc": [
    "Five and four rubber sheets. The boots take fall damage and the helmet takes hits from flying into walls, both paid in their own durability: made for the jetpack."
  ],
  "quest.6815B901AAEE21B7.title": "Diesel Mining Drill",
  "quest.6815B901AAEE21B7.quest_subtitle": "Through the walls of Ba Sing Se.",
  "quest.6815B901AAEE21B7.quest_desc": [
    "An aluminum drill head, invar rotary blades, motors, a pump, an aluminum tank and analog circuits. Fill it with any fluid fuel, which also sets its speed; sneak-use swaps Silk Touch and Fortune III."
  ],
  "quest.6A9E672D5673C8DD.title": "Run lines nonstop",
  "quest.6A9E672D5673C8DD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Electric machines speed up the longer they work and lose it when they stop. Run lines all the time into buffers and let storage pull from the buffers; MI's own guide advises against driving it on demand from AE2 or Refined Storage.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.637EECE644D817CC.title": "One-way power",
  "quest.637EECE644D817CC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"MI cables feed blocks of any mod but only draw from MI machines, and only MI cables power MI machines. At 10 FE per EU, MI power can run the rest of your base; the rest of your base cannot run MI.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6874DD30A1018358.title": "Grey tooltip, better yield",
  "quest.6874DD30A1018358.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Parts whose tooltip says 'Has an Assembler recipe with better yield' pay to automate: the assembler makes 12 resistors where the grid makes 3, and 4 capacitors or inductors where it makes 1.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.371BA2A6C08605FD.title": "Big boilers hate idling",
  "quest.371BA2A6C08605FD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The Large Steam Boiler burns fuel eight times faster than a furnace, and 80% of the heat it doesn't turn into steam is lost. Size it to run at full output, with a large tank as buffer, or it wastes most of its fuel.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6F5C8C6C82BBC09E.title": "EU per millibucket",
  "quest.6F5C8C6C82BBC09E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Crude oil gives 16 EU per mB, naphtha 80, creosote and light fuel 160, heavy fuel 240, biodiesel 250, diesel 400 and boosted diesel 800. Refining always pays.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.69874F86EFF1BAE5.title": "Which recipe, machine?",
  "quest.69874F86EFF1BAE5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"When the same inputs fit two recipes, lock an output slot to the product you want: the machine then only runs the recipe that makes it. It is also how one assembler keeps three recipes apart.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3A64172454C92C6F.title": "More than meets the eye",
  "quest.3A64172454C92C6F.quest_subtitle": "Transformers, roll out.",
  "quest.3A64172454C92C6F.quest_desc": [
    "You put an LV to MV transformer in a crafting grid and it came out the other way around: MV to LV."
  ],
  "reward.6E8F26075DD79CB9.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.47D52622D301F2E9.title": "Timber",
  "quest.47D52622D301F2E9.quest_subtitle": "A texas-sized lumberjack.",
  "quest.47D52622D301F2E9.quest_desc": [
    "You built the Diesel Chainsaw: rubber, invar rotary blades, motors and an aluminum tank, for felling trees in style."
  ],
  "reward.13B5CD3F47D647A7.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.3836309868494294.title": "Rubber for the common store",
  "quest.3836309868494294.quest_subtitle": "Nobody ever has enough.",
  "quest.3836309868494294.quest_desc": [
    "Sixty-four rubber sheets. Every cable, circuit board and conveyor on the server starts with them."
  ],
  "image.31955F5396CF4BED.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Cables and power\",\"color\":\"#FFA552\"}]",
  "image.4C2599386E8EA3A0.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Workshop\",\"color\":\"#FFA552\"}]",
  "image.6B73A784610A628A.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Multiblocks\",\"color\":\"#FFA552\"}]",
  "image.74F57EB16A929816.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"MV and diesel gear\",\"color\":\"#FFA552\"}]",
  "image.00C5028979F56EE0.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Modern Industrialization\\nElectricity\",\"color\":\"#FFF1DE\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.32C45D74CB05CBDB.title": "Back to the Sun of Heliodor",
  "image.6A9C188C5F39900F.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» Steam\",\"color\":\"#FFA552\"}]",
  "image.4D5D3CD02169B6B6.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» Digital\",\"color\":\"#FFA552\"}]",
  "image.57B8C59E6BB44272.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» Endgame\",\"color\":\"#FFA552\"}]",
  "image.107B0E185100D1C1.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"wire  wind  step up\",\"color\":\"#BFA58A\",\"font\":\"minecraft:alt\"}]",
  "image.29A3D45608D2C0F0.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"LV  32 EU/t\",\"color\":\"#C87533\"}]",
  "image.35A903C7228FF15E.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"MV  128 EU/t\",\"color\":\"#E3C75A\"}]",
  "chapter.5A47F14BD415B982.title": "Modern Industrialization · Steam",
  "chapter.5A47F14BD415B982.chapter_subtitle": [
    "From the Forge Hammer to the Steam Quarry: bronze, boilers, the coke oven and the first steel."
  ],
  "quest.0DA5E26857F9CA09.title": "Forge Hammer",
  "quest.0DA5E26857F9CA09.quest_subtitle": "Your first machine has no motor.",
  "quest.0DA5E26857F9CA09.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three heavy weighted pressure plates over four iron ingots. It works by hand: an iron ore block gives 2 raw iron, 3 with a \"},{\"text\":\"Hammer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modern_industrialization:iron_hammer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in its tool slot, and ingots become plates, rods, rings and bolts.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Copper ore gives 5 raw copper in it, 8 with the Hammer: hammer copper before you smelt it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.469475EF9C03C3A6.title": "Bronze",
  "quest.469475EF9C03C3A6.quest_subtitle": "Nine tiny dusts make one. Always.",
  "quest.469475EF9C03C3A6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Hammer copper and tin ingots into dust. Three copper dusts and a tin dust make three bronze dust in the grid; the \"},{\"text\":\"Mixer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modern_industrialization:bronze_mixer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" makes four from the same. Smelt the dust into ingots.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Almost Unified keeps one bronze for the whole pack: Mekanism's ingot is the one you get, and every MI recipe takes it."
  ],
  "quest.5EB016BD740A0784.title": "Casing and pipes",
  "quest.5EB016BD740A0784.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Every steam machine stands on a \"},{\"text\":\"Bronze Machine Casing\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modern_industrialization:bronze_machine_casing\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", eight bronze plates around a bronze gear, and most take three \"},{\"text\":\"Fluid Pipes\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modern_industrialization:fluid_pipe\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Six bronze curved plates, two copper rotors and a glass pane make sixteen pipes.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6F0A2292EED3B328.title": "Bronze Compressor",
  "quest.6F0A2292EED3B328.quest_subtitle": "Plates at half price.",
  "quest.6F0A2292EED3B328.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Forge Hammer spends two bronze ingots per plate unless it holds a Hammer; the compressor spends one, and presses a double ingot into two. Build it before the boiler, which alone takes twelve plates, and feed it a \"},{\"text\":\"Steam Bucket\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modern_industrialization:steam_bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": a water bucket smelted in a furnace.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.341EE5658553F72A.title": "Fire Clay Bricks",
  "quest.341EE5658553F72A.quest_subtitle": "Almost steam.",
  "quest.341EE5658553F72A.quest_desc": [
    "Brick dust comes from hammering or macerating bricks. Two of it and two clay balls make three fire clay dust, four in the Mixer; smelt it and put four bricks together. The boiler stands on three of these blocks."
  ],
  "quest.47D69210583ECE20.title": "Bronze Boiler",
  "quest.47D69210583ECE20.quest_subtitle": "Coal in, pressure out.",
  "quest.47D69210583ECE20.quest_desc": [
    "Four bronze plates, a bronze tank, a furnace and three fire clay brick blocks. It burns furnace fuel, heats up, then pushes up to 8 mB of steam per tick into the machines touching it. Bronze machines run recipes of up to 2 EU/t and 1 mB of steam is 1 EU: a hot boiler feeds four."
  ],
  "quest.69C4ED8DF233A0BE.title": "Bronze Macerator",
  "quest.69C4ED8DF233A0BE.quest_subtitle": "Ore hemiquadrupling.",
  "quest.69C4ED8DF233A0BE.quest_desc": [
    "Two diamonds, three copper gears, a casing and three pipes. An ore block gives three raw ores, and each raw ore a dust plus half a dust on average: 4.5 dusts per ore, so mine with Silk Touch. It also grinds scrap, gears and plates back into dust."
  ],
  "quest.0A3FA1CA253AD72E.title": "Bronze Mixer",
  "quest.0A3FA1CA253AD72E.quest_subtitle": "Better ratios, same dust.",
  "quest.0A3FA1CA253AD72E.quest_desc": [
    "Two glass blocks, a copper gear, two copper rotors, a casing and three pipes. It beats the grid: four bronze dust instead of three, four fire clay dust instead of three, nine uncooked steel dust instead of seven. With water it also turns sand into clay."
  ],
  "quest.057F22F8C91B1B17.title": "Coke Oven",
  "quest.057F22F8C91B1B17.quest_subtitle": "Coal, but more so.",
  "quest.057F22F8C91B1B17.quest_desc": [
    "Eight bricks around a furnace make the controller; 21 brick blocks and three hatches finish the oven: items in, items out and steam in. A coal becomes coke in 30 seconds, and coke burns four times longer than coal.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Hold a \"},{\"text\":\"Wrench\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modern_industrialization:wrench\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" near a controller to see which blocks are missing, or a hatch to see where it may go.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.730EDB392EA3EADA.title": "Uncooked Steel",
  "quest.730EDB392EA3EADA.quest_subtitle": "Steel, just add fire.",
  "quest.730EDB392EA3EADA.quest_desc": [
    "Macerate coke into coke dust; an oven fed coal dust gives coke dust directly. Seven iron dusts and two coke dusts make seven uncooked steel dust in the grid, nine in the Mixer."
  ],
  "quest.399A36874AA12E01.title": "Steam Blast Furnace",
  "quest.399A36874AA12E01.quest_desc": [
    "Eight fire clay brick blocks around a blast furnace make the controller. The shape is the coke oven's in fire clay bricks with one more hollow layer on top: 29 fire clay brick blocks and the same three hatches."
  ],
  "quest.045F585D14FC7B1D.title": "Steel",
  "quest.045F585D14FC7B1D.quest_subtitle": "Cooked uncooked steel.",
  "quest.045F585D14FC7B1D.quest_desc": [
    "The Steam Blast Furnace cooks one uncooked steel dust into one ingot every 30 seconds at 2 EU/t. Almost Unified hands out Immersive Engineering's ingot: one steel for the whole pack.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Gunpowder doubles that speed for two minutes: see \"},{\"text\":\"the gunpowder trick\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"7E5BB3388091A6E1\"}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.405B31B11FA83E58.title": "Steel Machine Casing",
  "quest.405B31B11FA83E58.quest_desc": [
    "Eight steel plates around a steel gear. Steel hatches, the packer, the wiremill, the steel upgrade and the Steam Quarry are all built on it."
  ],
  "quest.453C24EF98900FEF.title": "Steel Upgrade",
  "quest.453C24EF98900FEF.quest_subtitle": "Twice the speed, same machine.",
  "quest.453C24EF98900FEF.quest_desc": [
    "A steel casing, a bronze rotor, bronze gears and rods, pipes and a fire clay brick block make two. Sneak and right-click a bronze machine with one: it becomes the steel version, twice as fast up to 4 EU/t, with new recipes. An Unpacker takes the upgrade back out."
  ],
  "quest.34A66340B507C85E.title": "Invar Rotary Blade",
  "quest.34A66340B507C85E.quest_desc": [
    "Two iron dusts and a nickel dust make three invar dust in the Mixer. An invar gear ringed by four diamond dusts makes the blade the Steam Quarry spins, and later the electric macerator."
  ],
  "quest.7DD95D066787D269.title": "Bronze Drills",
  "quest.7DD95D066787D269.quest_desc": [
    "A bronze drill head, two iron gears, an item pipe and a fluid pipe make four. The quarry wears them down: each dig has a 4% chance to eat one."
  ],
  "quest.65B2AF2AA4A5C977.title": "Steam Quarry",
  "quest.65B2AF2AA4A5C977.quest_subtitle": "From Minecraft to Craft.",
  "quest.65B2AF2AA4A5C977.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four steel large plates, an item pipe, two steel gears, the invar blade and a steel casing. Walled in steel casings, with at least one \"},{\"text\":\"steel hatch\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"4DB84A002843BF2E\"}},{\"text\":\", it spends 4 EU/t and now and then a bronze drill to dig below bedrock: iron, coal, lignite, copper, tin, gold, redstone, zinc and osmium ores, every 30 seconds.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A copper drill digs cobblestone, stone variants, dirt and gravel instead: building filler that never runs out.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3CEB894C6180C21D.title": "Steel Wiremill",
  "quest.3CEB894C6180C21D.quest_subtitle": "Neither a wire nor a mill.",
  "quest.3CEB894C6180C21D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Bronze gears and rotors and two fluid pipes around a steel casing. A copper plate becomes two copper wires and a wire four fine wires: every cable starts here, and with cables the \"},{\"text\":\"Electric Age\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"0F14CDFA7E1FF965\"}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4B837C5C7F07818A.title": "Water Pump",
  "quest.4B837C5C7F07818A.quest_desc": [
    "Two copper rotors, two copper gears, a bronze tank, a casing and pipes. Ring it with water source blocks: each gives an eighth of a bucket every 5 seconds, a bucket at most, pushed out of its output side for 1 EU/t of steam. The steel pump doubles it."
  ],
  "quest.48C495AE88C96DFB.title": "Bronze Furnace",
  "quest.48C495AE88C96DFB.quest_subtitle": "Ten times less fuel.",
  "quest.48C495AE88C96DFB.quest_desc": [
    "Five bronze plates over a furnace and three fire clay brick blocks. It smelts at vanilla speed, but the steam behind it costs a tenth of the fuel a furnace would burn."
  ],
  "quest.2C393DAE76BB4BCF.title": "Cutting Machine",
  "quest.2C393DAE76BB4BCF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Glass, a diamond, two copper gears, a casing and pipes. For 1 mB of lubricant per cut, mixed from \"},{\"text\":\"creosote\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"1B9EDC3834394AC5\"}},{\"text\":\", it makes two rods per ingot, four per double ingot, two bolts per rod, and six planks per log.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.578FF1A850AD031A.title": "Steel Boiler",
  "quest.578FF1A850AD031A.quest_desc": [
    "A bronze boiler and a steel upgrade, shapeless. It makes up to 16 mB of steam per tick, twice the bronze one."
  ],
  "quest.063D8459D78ADA82.title": "Packer and Unpacker",
  "quest.063D8459D78ADA82.quest_subtitle": "To pack or not to pack.",
  "quest.063D8459D78ADA82.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Steel-only machines. The \"},{\"text\":\"Packer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modern_industrialization:steel_packer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" does simple crafts by itself: double ingots with a template it never uses up, large plates, blocks, blades and cables. The \"},{\"text\":\"Unpacker\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modern_industrialization:steel_unpacker\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" does the reverse.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4DB84A002843BF2E.title": "Steel Hatches",
  "quest.4DB84A002843BF2E.quest_desc": [
    "A hopper or a steel tank on a steel casing. One steel hatch lifts a steam multiblock to steel tier: recipes up to 4 EU/t, twice as fast below that. The quarry asks for exactly 4.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"An input hatch crafts into the matching output hatch and back, one for one.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3DA37A4FD2C99709.title": "The guidebook",
  "quest.3DA37A4FD2C99709.quest_subtitle": "Technology for newbies.",
  "quest.3DA37A4FD2C99709.quest_desc": [
    "A book ringed by eight copper nuggets. Nobody hands it out here, so craft one: every machine has a page, and each multiblock an interactive view of its shape."
  ],
  "quest.4549DBBCC7B881C1.title": "Iron Hammer",
  "quest.4549DBBCC7B881C1.quest_desc": [
    "Five iron large plates and two sticks. In the Forge Hammer's tool slot it raises yields and unlocks recipes, paying in durability: an ore block becomes 3 raw ores or 4 dusts, three raw ores become 4 dusts."
  ],
  "quest.1739A4C6983DDA8A.title": "Steam Mining Drill",
  "quest.1739A4C6983DDA8A.quest_subtitle": "Getting that 3×3 going.",
  "quest.1739A4C6983DDA8A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three diamonds, two furnaces, two iron large plates, a bucket and a copper drill head. Right-click water to fill it and slip it solid fuel; \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.modern_industrialization.toggle_3x3\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" toggles 3×3 and sneak-use Silk Touch.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0036D02B5773F56F.title": "Wrench",
  "quest.0036D02B5773F56F.quest_desc": [
    "Six bronze plates. Right-click turns a machine, sneak-right-click moves its output side; on a pipe it changes the connection, and sneaking pops the pipe off. Break machines with a pickaxe: the wrench won't drop them."
  ],
  "quest.3E83EEDD9694BCA6.title": "Lignite Coal",
  "quest.3E83EEDD9694BCA6.quest_desc": [
    "MI's own coal ore, common from bedrock up to height 256. It burns like coal, 1,600 ticks, but a block of nine burns 16,000: packing it earns a free piece."
  ],
  "quest.1B9EDC3834394AC5.title": "Creosote",
  "quest.1B9EDC3834394AC5.quest_desc": [
    "Add a bronze fluid output hatch to the coke oven: half its batches leave 500 mB of creosote, lost when there is no room. It burns at 160 EU per mB, and redstone mixes it into lubricant."
  ],
  "quest.295CC424254D2956.title": "Item Pipes",
  "quest.295CC424254D2956.quest_subtitle": "Whitelist by default. Yes, really.",
  "quest.295CC424254D2956.quest_desc": [
    "Six bronze curved plates and two steel gears make sixteen. They reach inventories only when told, and both ends start as an empty whitelist: nothing moves until you add the item or switch to blacklist. They carry 16 items every 3 seconds; a motor inside adds more."
  ],
  "quest.70048ADDD1887B1D.title": "Tanks and barrels",
  "quest.70048ADDD1887B1D.quest_desc": [
    "Eight bronze plates around glass make a tank of 4 buckets; around a wooden barrel, a barrel of 32 stacks, one fluid or item each. Both keep their contents when broken and stack when the contents match; the steel tank holds 16 buckets."
  ],
  "quest.6C1CCD02DF65160F.title": "Automatic Trash Can",
  "quest.6C1CCD02DF65160F.quest_subtitle": "Where overflow goes to die.",
  "quest.6C1CCD02DF65160F.quest_desc": [
    "Eight steel plates around a lava bucket. It deletes every item and fluid piped into it, and clicking a machine's fluid slot with it empties the slot."
  ],
  "quest.6161797455ACD079.title": "Locks, caps and eject",
  "quest.6161797455ACD079.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Steam machines take inputs from any side. Click a slot's lock to reserve it for one item or fluid, scroll over a slot to cap it, and switch on auto-eject to push outputs out of the output side.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3250F4E861F3B865.title": "Hammer or macerator?",
  "quest.3250F4E861F3B865.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Per ore block, the Forge Hammer gives 2 raw ores, 3 with a Hammer, or 4 dusts straight; the Macerator gives 3 raw ores that grind into 4.5 dusts. Keep ores whole with Silk Touch and let the machines break them.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7E5BB3388091A6E1.title": "The gunpowder trick",
  "quest.7E5BB3388091A6E1.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Right-click a steam machine, or a steam multiblock's controller, with gunpowder: it runs twice as fast for two minutes. Best spent on the coke oven and the blast furnace, whose recipes take 30 seconds.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.06B3DBBB8FFE4755.title": "The Industrialist",
  "quest.06B3DBBB8FFE4755.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A Forge Hammer is a job site: a villager without a trade near one becomes an Industrialist. He buys lignite and sulfur dust, and sells tin, bronze, steel, rubber sheets, motors, analog circuits, a steel hammer and bronze drills.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.50F652753CF9CFD7.title": "Upgrade like a boss",
  "quest.50F652753CF9CFD7.quest_subtitle": "No crafting table was harmed.",
  "quest.50F652753CF9CFD7.quest_desc": [
    "You upgraded a bronze machine where it stands, without breaking it or opening a crafting grid."
  ],
  "reward.171936D07D6DE26E.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.1FA6DF09BDBDA535.title": "Overkill",
  "quest.1FA6DF09BDBDA535.quest_subtitle": "Every problem looks like a plate.",
  "quest.1FA6DF09BDBDA535.quest_desc": [
    "A diamond hammer, a netherite ingot and an upgrade template, to flatten bronze. It does the iron hammer's job with 2,031 durability instead of 250."
  ],
  "reward.512C2439E2C60611.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.5F1F04498F760B8C.title": "Plates for the common store",
  "quest.5F1F04498F760B8C.quest_subtitle": "Someone always needs twelve more.",
  "quest.5F1F04498F760B8C.quest_desc": [
    "Thirty-two bronze plates: machines, tanks, boilers and wrenches all start with them."
  ],
  "image.7CE375DE39CC160F.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Steam machines\",\"color\":\"#FFA552\"}]",
  "image.3591F79F482634D6.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Steel tier\",\"color\":\"#FFA552\"}]",
  "image.063C1106BF099EEB.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Tools and storage\",\"color\":\"#FFA552\"}]",
  "image.5A97337952417C9D.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Fuel\",\"color\":\"#FFA552\"}]",
  "image.1A94395BEB71D61D.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Item pipes\",\"color\":\"#FFA552\"}]",
  "image.4DB25342F77C9AA1.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Modern Industrialization\\nSteam\",\"color\":\"#FFF1DE\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.0B2DF98A4CD954A0.title": "Back to the Sun of Heliodor",
  "image.144C000F9C55574E.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» Electricity\",\"color\":\"#FFA552\"}]",
  "image.64FEDE8F2BFB9007.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» Digital\",\"color\":\"#FFA552\"}]",
  "image.1E9EB5F5712D241F.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» Endgame\",\"color\":\"#FFA552\"}]",
  "image.3F6CBAA47C7AC356.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"hammer  mix  cook  quarry\",\"color\":\"#BFA58A\",\"font\":\"minecraft:alt\"}]",
  "image.1D837511CD3C70B6.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"firebox\",\"color\":\"#FFB347\"}]",
  "image.46C8C9E6FF26999A.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"smokebox\",\"color\":\"#C98A4B\"}]",
  "image.5D3E46C40FD721CC.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» wires lead on\",\"color\":\"#FFA552\"}]",
  "chapter.131B1C3AE984A6AC.title": "Oritech",
  "chapter.131B1C3AE984A6AC.chapter_subtitle": [
    "From nickel to prometheum: machines on cores and addons, generators, pipes and poles, the Enderic Laser and the Atomic Forge, bedrock mining, exo suits and jetpacks. The reactor and the accelerator are in Core and Particles."
  ],
  "quest.21C03EBF4DEA19C6.title": "Nickel",
  "quest.21C03EBF4DEA19C6.quest_subtitle": "Pocket change for a factory.",
  "quest.21C03EBF4DEA19C6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Nickel ore runs from Y -65 up to 40. On the surface, boulders of deepslate and ore mark richer ground: under each one, at bedrock, sits a resource node of the same metal. Smelted, nickel comes out as \"},{\"text\":\"Nickel Ingots\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:ingot_nickel\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in this pack.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Note where you see an amethyst geode: it becomes your fluxite mine.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.146591CC41F80C54.title": "Coils and Motors",
  "quest.146591CC41F80C54.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Six nickel and three steel make four \"},{\"text\":\"Magnetic Coils\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:magnetic_coil\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; a nickel, four steel and two coils make a \"},{\"text\":\"Motor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:motor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Motors go into almost every Oritech machine, so keep a stack. Steel from any mod works.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The Assembler makes six coils from one steel, two nickel and a copper ingot, and two motors per craft. Build it before mass-producing either.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6D3692B4895FD225.title": "Basic Generator",
  "quest.6D3692B4895FD225.quest_subtitle": "Coal goes in, RF comes out.",
  "quest.6D3692B4895FD225.quest_desc": [
    "Five nickel, a copper ingot, two coils and a furnace. It burns anything a furnace does for 32 RF/t, takes no addons and needs no cores: build two or three rather than wait for a better one.",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The first thing worth plugging in is a \"},{\"text\":\"Powered Furnace\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:powered_furnace_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": twice a furnace's speed for 32 RF/t, on one core.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.04932A1C97664069.title": "Pulverizer",
  "quest.04932A1C97664069.quest_subtitle": "Coarse in, fine out.",
  "quest.04932A1C97664069.quest_desc": [
    "Five iron, a nickel, two motors and a copper block; no cores. It grinds a raw ore into a dust and three small dusts, a third more metal than the furnace gives, and nine small dusts craft back into one.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Each ender pearl comes out as eight \"},{\"text\":\"Enderic Compound\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:enderic_compound\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", and seeds, saplings and crops as \"},{\"text\":\"Biomass\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:biomass\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.13FF438B9DAC8414.title": "Foundry",
  "quest.13FF438B9DAC8414.quest_subtitle": "Alloys at wholesale.",
  "quest.13FF438B9DAC8414.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Five copper, a motor, two electrum and a cauldron, standing on three machine cores. Right-click it to see where they go, or click it holding a core to place the next. \"},{\"text\":\"Primitive Machine Cores\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:machine_core_1\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" are planks around a crafting table.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"It alloys at half the grid's price: iron and coal dust make steel, nickel and a diamond make \"},{\"text\":\"Adamant\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:adamant_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", gold and redstone make electrum. The grid wants two of each ingredient per ingot.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.17BFEFFD52B91A0C.title": "Assembler",
  "quest.17BFEFFD52B91A0C.quest_desc": [
    "Three copper, two crafters, an adamant ingot, two motors and a blast furnace, on three cores. A 2×2 grid that crafts by itself at 128 RF/t and pays better than your hands: two motors or six coils per craft, and parts the grid can't make at all.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Ingredients go in any order, and an AE2 pattern provider feeds it as it is.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1B28C442DA9F58D8.title": "Centrifuge",
  "quest.1B28C442DA9F58D8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The cheap recipe takes two motors, two copper, two iron blocks and three glass bottles, on one core. It spins coal dust into \"},{\"text\":\"Carbon Fibre Strands\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:carbon_fibre_strands\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", the thread half the later parts are woven from, and ore clumps into gems.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"For fluids, attach a \"},{\"text\":\"Fluid Addon\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:machine_fluid_addon\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and pipe into the centrifuge itself, not the addon. If a fluid recipe won't start, open the machine once so it notices the addon.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.484443330BE723E2.title": "Processing Units",
  "quest.484443330BE723E2.quest_subtitle": "The brains of the operation.",
  "quest.484443330BE723E2.quest_desc": [
    "Plastic, a carbon fibre strand, electrum and redstone, in the Assembler only. The Target Designator, item filters, chargers and the reactor controller all run on them.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Plastic starts on the farm: packed wheat and water in the centrifuge give raw biopolymer, and a second spin with water gives a sheet. Here Oritech's sheets come out as \"},{\"text\":\"Duroplast Sheets\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"immersiveengineering:plate_duroplast\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", and any plastic plate works.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1738C06D92591D44.title": "Enderic Laser",
  "quest.1738C06D92591D44.quest_subtitle": "Point, click, vaporise.",
  "quest.1738C06D92591D44.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two carbon fibre, an \"},{\"text\":\"Enderic Lens\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:enderic_lens\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", two motors, electrum and three plating, on one core. Right-click a block with the \"},{\"text\":\"Target Designator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:target_designator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", then sneak (\"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.sneak\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\") and right-click the laser: it fires that way, up to 128 blocks.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "It mines everything on that line but passes through glass; drops that don't fit its inventory are destroyed, so pipe them out. Aimed at a machine, it charges it past the machine's own input limit.",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The lens comes from the Assembler: adamant, a carbon fibre strand and two enderic compound.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4E8B29DF95E47ED3.title": "Fluxite",
  "quest.4E8B29DF95E47ED3.quest_subtitle": "Crystal harvest, no pickaxe.",
  "quest.4E8B29DF95E47ED3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Aim the laser at the amethyst clusters of a geode. Every cluster it breaks drops \"},{\"text\":\"Fluxite\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:fluxite\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", and a \"},{\"text\":\"Budding Amethyst\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:budding_amethyst\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" under the beam isn't broken: it grows new clusters much faster instead.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Platinum clumps in the centrifuge shed a fluxite each, too.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3AC5B3B5FEAD6ABC.title": "Flux Gates",
  "quest.3AC5B3B5FEAD6ABC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A processing unit, two fluxite and a platinum ingot in the Assembler make a \"},{\"text\":\"Flux Gate\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:flux_gate\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; nickel and fluxite in the Foundry make \"},{\"text\":\"Energite\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:energite_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Batteries, solar panels, the forge and the fragment forge all wait on these two.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Platinum ore lies between Y -60 and -20 and is common in the End; nickel clumps in the centrifuge also shed small platinum dust.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3BE889B5BCB922B9.title": "Atomic Forge",
  "quest.3BE889B5BCB922B9.quest_subtitle": "No cables. Lasers only.",
  "quest.3BE889B5BCB922B9.quest_desc": [
    "Two flux gates, a duratium ingot, two plastic, enderic compound and three plating, on eight cores. Pipes can't feed it: aim Enderic Lasers at it. A recipe finishes once the forge is charged, so more lasers mean faster work.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The first \"},{\"text\":\"Duratium Ingot\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:duratium_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" comes from the Foundry: platinum and a netherite ingot. From then on the forge makes its own out of platinum and two reinforced carbon sheets.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.69E22F2896124E90.title": "Advanced Computing Engine",
  "quest.69E22F2896124E90.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"In the forge, a carbon fibre strand and two silicon become a \"},{\"text\":\"Silicon Wafer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:silicon_wafer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", and a processing unit with two wafers becomes an \"},{\"text\":\"Advanced Computing Engine\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:advanced_computing_engine\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Any silicon works, AE2's included.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Elite machine cores are eight adamant around one engine.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.19A9E13BBBEC2073.title": "Duratium",
  "quest.19A9E13BBBEC2073.quest_subtitle": "Heavier than it looks.",
  "quest.19A9E13BBBEC2073.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The forge fuses a platinum ingot with two \"},{\"text\":\"Reinforced Carbon Sheets\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:reinforced_carbon_sheet\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; the Refinery bakes each sheet from carbon fibre and 500 mB of naphtha. The accelerator, the Bedrock Extractor and the reactor's neutron reflectors are all built on duratium.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5A316D5F7D0529F3.title": "Superconductors",
  "quest.5A316D5F7D0529F3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A flux gate, electrum, a \"},{\"text\":\"Dubious Container\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:dubios_container\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and energite in the Assembler make four. As cable they carry 4,194,304 RF/t and won't join ordinary energy pipes; as parts they build the accelerator ring and the drone port.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The container is hand-made: plastic, four enderic compound and two adamant.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2827575517D6305B.title": "Heisenberg Compensator",
  "quest.2827575517D6305B.quest_subtitle": "Certainty, sold separately.",
  "quest.2827575517D6305B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"In the forge, a duratium ingot and two computing engines make a \"},{\"text\":\"Super AI Chip\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:super_ai_chip\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; the chip and two adamant make the \"},{\"text\":\"Heisenberg Compensator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:heisenberg_compensator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Prometheum, the Bedrock Extractor and the tachyon absorbers are built on it.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"An \"},{\"text\":\"Unholy Intelligence\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:unholy_intelligence\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" can stand in for the chip here, in the drone port and in the arcane catalyst.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4AA9D4ADA3ED7E7A.title": "Overcharged Crystal",
  "quest.4AA9D4ADA3ED7E7A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An amethyst block, four superconductors and two advanced batteries craft one. Once the accelerator runs, fluxite colliding with \"},{\"text\":\"Energite Dust\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:energite_dust\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" at 5,000 J makes them too.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"An advanced battery is two energite ingots, electrum and four steel; a centrifuge with sulfuric acid turns one Dubious Container into eight.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.723F7BF64568EA59.title": "Prometheum",
  "quest.723F7BF64568EA59.quest_subtitle": "Fire, borrowed from the gods.",
  "quest.723F7BF64568EA59.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Heisenberg Compensator and two overcharged crystals in a charged forge: Oritech's last material. It makes the \"},{\"text\":\"Prometheum Pickaxe\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:promethium_pickaxe\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and \"},{\"text\":\"Prometheum Battleaxe\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:promethium_axe\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", which never break, and the top machine core.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Each tool takes three ingots and two Block Destroyers as a handle. Sneak (\"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.sneak\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\") and right-click to switch the pickaxe between a 3×3 area and silk touch; the axe fells a whole tree while you sneak.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1A3370FE9D311FE3.title": "Ultimate Machine Core",
  "quest.1A3370FE9D311FE3.quest_subtitle": "Seven out of seven.",
  "quest.1A3370FE9D311FE3.quest_desc": [
    "Eight prometheum ingots around a superconductor. A machine's quality is the average of its cores, 1 for primitive up to 7 for ultimate: on these a Big Solar Panel makes seven times its base power, and a machine takes the most addon extenders it ever can."
  ],
  "quest.2E2BEDE6BEB55268.title": "Push, Never Pull",
  "quest.2E2BEDE6BEB55268.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Generators and batteries push their energy; \"},{\"text\":\"Energy Pipes\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:energy_pipe\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" carry 10,000 RF/t and never pull on their own. A \"},{\"text\":\"Pipe Wrench\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:wrench\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on the end of a pipe turns that connection off or on.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.52A0F427BA59383D.title": "Lava and Bio Generators",
  "quest.52A0F427BA59383D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Both make 64 RF/t on one core and take two addons. The \"},{\"text\":\"Lava Generator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:lava_generator_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" burns 100 mB of lava in 120 ticks, and the Refinery's Sheol fire in 800; the \"},{\"text\":\"Bio Generator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:bio_generator_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" eats biomass, packed wheat and solid biofuel.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A pump over a lava lake keeps the first one fed for a long time.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6716AE690B964746.title": "Energy Storage",
  "quest.6716AE690B964746.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Portable Energy Storage\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:small_storage_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" holds 1,000,000 RF and keeps it when broken. The \"},{\"text\":\"Large Energy Storage\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:large_storage_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" holds 20,000,000 on three cores, with eight addon slots. Both push power out of the red port alone.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Later, \"},{\"text\":\"Schrödinger's Safe\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:unstable_container\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" locks TNT or a nuke inside and stores more the more dangerous its prisoner; Enderic Lasers aimed at it raise the ceiling while they fire.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3D6A7A0D44BFB7EB.title": "Fuel Generator",
  "quest.3D6A7A0D44BFB7EB.quest_subtitle": "Dinosaur juice, refined.",
  "quest.3D6A7A0D44BFB7EB.quest_desc": [
    "Five steel, an enderic lens, two plating and a Basic Generator, on seventeen cores: 256 RF/t, sent out only through the two yellow ports on its front. 100 mB of crude oil lasts 20 ticks; the same of turbofuel, 320."
  ],
  "quest.38B1C2B14AF2303D.title": "Steam Engine",
  "quest.38B1C2B14AF2303D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Steam Boiler Addon\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:steam_boiler_addon\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" turns any generator but the basic one into a boiler: pipe water into the addon and it makes two steam for every RF it would have produced. The \"},{\"text\":\"Steam Engine\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:steam_engine_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", on three cores, turns that steam back into up to 50,000 RF/t.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "The fuller its steam tank, the faster it spins, up to ten times; efficiency peaks near 700 %, where each unit of steam gives about 1.4 times its base RF. Up to ten engines in a row share the first one's pipes.",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"It stops when its own water tank fills: send that water back to the boilers and the loop runs by itself.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.04978122063C0015.title": "Big Solar Panel",
  "quest.04978122063C0015.quest_desc": [
    "Five fluxite, an advanced battery, two flux gates and a Basic Generator, on fifteen cores. It makes 32 RF/t times the average tier of those cores: 32 on primitive ones, 224 on ultimate. It folds away at night and whenever sky light falls below 12."
  ],
  "quest.257FB597393ED681.title": "Speed and Efficiency",
  "quest.257FB597393ED681.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Addons sit on a machine's marked spots and turn from pink to blue once connected. Each \"},{\"text\":\"Speed Addon\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:machine_speed_addon\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" adds 50 % speed and 20 % energy per tick; each \"},{\"text\":\"Efficiency Addon\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:machine_efficiency_addon\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" takes 20 % off. They add up rather than multiply.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.35DBF6C8F461BD7E.title": "Cores Set the Ceiling",
  "quest.35DBF6C8F461BD7E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A better core never speeds a machine up. Quality is the average tier of a machine's cores, and it only limits how many addon extenders fit. With no addons planned, primitive cores are enough.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7E3F0EDF9999B0FA.title": "Addon Extenders",
  "quest.7E3F0EDF9999B0FA.quest_desc": [
    "An extender goes on an addon spot and offers new spots of its own, and a machine takes as many extenders as its quality. Each is a duratium ingot and four plating ringed by four basic machine cores."
  ],
  "quest.243FEDFDD8D38564.title": "Capacitor and Acceptor",
  "quest.243FEDFDD8D38564.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Capacitor Addon\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:machine_capacitor_addon\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" adds 2,000,000 RF of buffer and 2,000 RF/t of intake; an \"},{\"text\":\"Acceptor Addon\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:machine_acceptor_addon\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" adds 500,000 RF and 5,000 RF/t and takes power through its own faces, for machines with no side free.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A capacitor crafted onto an extender makes a Power Bank Extender: an extender that also adds 2,500,000 RF.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.433F381D89E12DBC.title": "Burst and Parallel",
  "quest.433F381D89E12DBC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Burst Addon\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:machine_burst_addon\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" runs a machine eight times faster for 240 ticks per addon, then throttles it to 80 % speed at 20 % more energy until it cools. An \"},{\"text\":\"Auxiliary Processing Chamber\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:machine_processing_addon\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" runs one more recipe at a time for 50 % more energy.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Bursts suit machines that work in spurts; for long recipes the chamber wins.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.52C5065D5FC2C2F2.title": "Synergy and the Heart",
  "quest.52C5065D5FC2C2F2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Synergy Matrix Addon\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:machine_ultimate_addon\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" gives 75 % speed for only 10 % more energy. The \"},{\"text\":\"Addon Splicer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:shrinker_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", on four cores, then fuses a machine's stat addons into a single Heart of the Machine, which works only as the machine's one and only addon.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Each splice needs its 50,000,000 RF buffer full and eats the addons for good. Steam boilers, control units, inventory proxies and hunter addons can't be spliced."
  ],
  "quest.4BC1353A1C9DC387.title": "Inventory Proxy",
  "quest.4BC1353A1C9DC387.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Five carbon fibre, a processing unit, two chests and a motor. An \"},{\"text\":\"Inventory Proxy Addon\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:machine_inventory_proxy_addon\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" stands for one slot of its machine, picked in its screen: a pipe on it fills or empties that slot and no other.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2816B723034A03FC.title": "Fragment Forge",
  "quest.2816B723034A03FC.quest_desc": [
    "Five plastic, a flux gate, two motors and plating, on seven cores with five addon slots. An ore block breaks into two raw ores plus one of a sister metal; a raw ore breaks into a clump, three small clumps and a few small clumps of that sister.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Feed it silk-touched ore: an iron ore block gives two raw iron and a raw nickel, and nickel's sister is platinum. One \"},{\"text\":\"Yield Addon\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:machine_yield_addon\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" doubles the side products.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.36F3568E2D4CC001.title": "One Ore, Six Ingots",
  "quest.36F3568E2D4CC001.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Centrifuge spins a clump into one gem dry, two with a bucket of water, three with a bucket of sulfuric acid, which also leaves 250 mB of mineral slurry. The Foundry melts two \"},{\"text\":\"Iron Gems\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:iron_gem\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" into three ingots.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"One raw ore, a third more in clumps, four gems, six ingots: the acid route turns a vein into six times the metal.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4BC093374936443B.title": "Oil and the Refinery",
  "quest.4BC093374936443B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Oil springs gush from the surface, about three times as often in deserts. A \"},{\"text\":\"Pump\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:pump_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" drains a lake of up to 100,000 blocks at 512 RF each. The \"},{\"text\":\"Refinery\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:refinery_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", on nine cores, splits a bucket of crude into heavy oil, naphtha and sulfuric acid.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Up to two chamber modules stacked on top open its second and third outputs; without them the first output doubles. \"},{\"text\":\"Clay Catalyst Beads\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:clay_catalyst_beads\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" turn the same bucket into 500 mB each of diesel, naphtha and acid.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.32312B712CCCD68F.title": "Turbofuel",
  "quest.32312B712CCCD68F.quest_subtitle": "Jetpack juice.",
  "quest.32312B712CCCD68F.quest_desc": [
    "A bucket of diesel and one fluxite in a centrifuge with a Fluid Addon make a bucket of turbofuel. It lasts sixteen times as long as crude oil in the Fuel Generator, and jetpacks fly faster on it than on RF.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Industrial Foregoing's biofuel and PneumaticCraft's oil also become turbofuel with fluxite in the centrifuge.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.15E03921D190A5B6.title": "Pipes",
  "quest.15E03921D190A5B6.quest_desc": [
    "Item pipes hold nothing: right-click the section touching an inventory to make it extract, 8 items every 5 ticks, into the nearest inventory down the line. Fluid pipes pull half a bucket every 3 ticks the same way.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"An extracting pipe takes from the first filled slot, and one item with nowhere to go blocks it. Right-click it with a \"},{\"text\":\"Motor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:motor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" to make it reach every slot; a \"},{\"text\":\"Pipe Booster\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:pipe_booster_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" against it moves a stack per tick.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1E63BE9D339F76C6.title": "Power Poles",
  "quest.1E63BE9D339F76C6.quest_subtitle": "The scenic route for energy.",
  "quest.1E63BE9D339F76C6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Link two \"},{\"text\":\"Energy Transmission Poles\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:power_pole_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" 50 to 1,000 blocks apart by sneak-clicking both with the Target Designator. Every linked pole shares one network of up to 1,000,000 RF/t: energy goes in at a green port and out at a red one.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Right-click the cable with a \"},{\"text\":\"Pipe Wrench\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:wrench\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" to zipline along it for free.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2A7D24510E3F1ED6.title": "Portable Tank",
  "quest.2A7D24510E3F1ED6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Six copper, two fluid pipes and a glass block. A \"},{\"text\":\"Portable Tank\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:small_tank_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" holds 256 buckets and keeps them when broken; stacked tanks pour down into the one below, and a comparator reads how full it is.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.724D2807FFBD0083.title": "Item Filter",
  "quest.724D2807FFBD0083.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Seven planks around a processing unit, on plating. Place the \"},{\"text\":\"Item Filter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:item_filter_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" against the inventory it should fill: it accepts only what its list allows, from pipes on any side, and passes it straight in. It holds one item at a time and never pulls on its own.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"This pack has FTB Filter System, so a \"},{\"text\":\"Smart Filter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ftbfiltersystem:smart_filter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in the list matches whole tags, mods or anything its expression can say.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3A196D95174295A5.title": "Hunter Addon",
  "quest.3A196D95174295A5.quest_subtitle": "Pest control, industrial grade.",
  "quest.3A196D95174295A5.quest_desc": [
    "On the laser's addon spot it turns the beam on mobs: it tracks them along its line and stores their loot, though they drop no experience. Sneak-click the laser with the designator to cycle targets: every non-player, hostile and neutral, or hostile only.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Speed addons raise its damage; a crop filter spares baby animals.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.53A62468ABABA920.title": "Plutonium",
  "quest.53A62468ABABA920.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A laser breaking a \"},{\"text\":\"Uranite Crystal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:uranium_crystal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in a uranium vein gets plutonium dust instead of raw uranium, and crystals never grow back. Pressed like uranium, \"},{\"text\":\"Plutonium Pellets\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:plutonium_pellet\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" burn ten times longer in a reactor.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Uranium dust colliding with fluxite at 2,500 J makes plutonium too, and the Fragment Forge leaves a pinch of it in every raw uranium.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2C294F1441BCF3BB.title": "Exo Suit",
  "quest.2C294F1441BCF3BB.quest_subtitle": "Armour that does chores.",
  "quest.2C294F1441BCF3BB.quest_desc": [
    "Machine plating and one part per piece: a lens gives the helmet night vision, an advanced battery lets the chestplate charge the powered tools you carry, a motor makes the legs run faster and silicon lets the boots ignore fall damage."
  ],
  "quest.376F76253F21BBB1.title": "Drill, Saw and Charger",
  "quest.376F76253F21BBB1.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Hand Drill\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:hand_drill\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" works as pickaxe and shovel for 10 RF times each block's hardness; the \"},{\"text\":\"Chainsaw\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:chainsaw\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" fells a whole tree when you sneak. Neither ever breaks: empty, they just crawl. The \"},{\"text\":\"Equipment Charger\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:charger_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" refills them.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Unbreaking on these tools cuts their energy use instead.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.099ED8E4C8962D59.title": "Jetpack",
  "quest.099ED8E4C8962D59.quest_subtitle": "Up is a direction now.",
  "quest.099ED8E4C8962D59.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Leather, two steel, two gunpowder, an advanced battery and, in this pack, a \"},{\"text\":\"Reinforced Alloy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:alloy_reinforced\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (act III). Hold jump to climb; there's no hover. Here it burns 320 RF/t or 25 mB/t of turbofuel, two and a half times the mod's own cost.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Turbofuel only goes in through the Equipment Charger, and it flies faster than RF.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1212F4953B1769ED.title": "Exo Jetpack",
  "quest.1212F4953B1769ED.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Exo Chestplate, the Jetpack, four \"},{\"text\":\"Ion Thrusters\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:ion_thruster\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", two portable tanks and, in this pack, a \"},{\"text\":\"Zanite Gemstone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:zanite_gemstone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (act IV). It holds 5,000,000 RF or 32 buckets, flies at speed 1.5 against the jetpack's 0.4 and charges your tools like the chestplate.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Here it burns 640 RF/t or 38 mB/t of turbofuel. Ion thrusters come from the Assembler: two reinforced carbon sheets, an advanced battery and a flux gate make two."
  ],
  "quest.4921456F4BFBE6C3.title": "Boosted Elytra",
  "quest.4921456F4BFBE6C3.quest_desc": [
    "Elytra, the Jetpack, two processing units and five gunpowder. It thrusts only while you glide, so it replaces fireworks instead of climbing on its own; same tank and cost as the jetpack, speed 0.6. The exo version, at 1.4, is built on the Exo Jetpack."
  ],
  "quest.5C88B4FC3C16FBAD.title": "A Geode at Home",
  "quest.5C88B4FC3C16FBAD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Assembler grows a \"},{\"text\":\"Budding Amethyst\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:budding_amethyst\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" from two amethyst shards, enderic compound and an overcharged crystal. Set it beside your laser and the fluxite mine moves home.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.30477B91CE1CF47F.title": "Stand on a resource node",
  "quest.0B0DC87266DB1928.title": "Resource Node",
  "quest.0B0DC87266DB1928.quest_desc": [
    "Dig straight down under an ore boulder: at bedrock waits a node of the same ore, unbreakable and endless. The rarest boulders hide diamond, emerald, uranium and platinum nodes."
  ],
  "quest.4365678511B2C10F.title": "Bedrock Extractor",
  "quest.4365678511B2C10F.quest_subtitle": "The bottom of the world has a tap.",
  "quest.4365678511B2C10F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Twenty-six cores over a node, powered only by Enderic Lasers. It scans three blocks down in the 3×3 under it, picks one node each cycle and spends 20 steps of 1,024 RF per ore; nodes never run dry. Here it also takes an \"},{\"text\":\"Ironwood Ingot\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:ironwood_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (act IV).\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.21C2D98A51480A18.title": "Bottled Spirit",
  "quest.21C2D98A51480A18.quest_subtitle": "It was only a little allay.",
  "quest.21C2D98A51480A18.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Dubious Container given to an allay, or pressed on a vex, now holds an \"},{\"text\":\"Unholy Intelligence\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:unholy_intelligence\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It replaces a Super AI Chip in the compensator, the drone port and the catalyst, and burns for 60,000 ticks in a Bio Generator.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.123FD1A705CF3C46.title": "Secret found",
  "task.7D75DC6E701E3134.title": "Get a gold gem",
  "quest.0A8B403396666261.title": "Alchemist's Margin",
  "quest.0A8B403396666261.quest_subtitle": "Gold in, more gold out.",
  "quest.0A8B403396666261.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Gold Gem\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:gold_gem\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", spun from a gold clump the same way as iron. Two of them melt into three gold ingots in the Foundry: the only alchemy Oritech needs is a centrifuge.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.1567754323A96031.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.3967AAB382DDAD96.title": "Motors for the Common Store",
  "quest.3967AAB382DDAD96.quest_subtitle": "Everyone's machine wants two.",
  "quest.3967AAB382DDAD96.quest_desc": [
    "Sixteen motors, from the grid or the Assembler. Nearly every Oritech machine on the server starts with a pair of them."
  ],
  "quest.792CA8B0AABC4121.title": "Oritech in This Pack",
  "quest.792CA8B0AABC4121.quest_desc": [
    "Seven Oritech pieces wait on the Atlas: the Jetpack on a reinforced alloy (act III); the Exo Jetpack on zanite; the Bedrock Extractor, the Spawner Controller and both nukes on ironwood (act IV); the accelerator controller on an atomic alloy (act V).",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "The Nether Star collision is gone, and the Foundry and Atomic Forge make no Mekanism alloys or circuits. Almost Unified hands out Immersive Engineering's nickel, steel and electrum and turns Oritech plastic into duroplast. The Oracle Index manual isn't installed: use the recipe viewer."
  ],
  "image.13F2483F786A7D03.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Pipes, poles and tanks\",\"color\":\"#F0A24A\"}]",
  "image.0B61A544BAAD4FC6.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Generators\",\"color\":\"#F0A24A\"}]",
  "image.25629F95A2B32C22.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Ore processing\",\"color\":\"#F0A24A\"}]",
  "image.02814C139FDC484B.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Addons\",\"color\":\"#F0A24A\"}]",
  "image.0085F4F6EA8454C4.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Laser work\",\"color\":\"#F0A24A\"}]",
  "image.2A22C0968D2D7CEF.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Exo suit and jetpacks\",\"color\":\"#F0A24A\"}]",
  "image.7B0CE1DFDAD3EB2F.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Mining the bedrock\",\"color\":\"#F0A24A\"}]",
  "image.0452DF7B62FE17DB.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Oritech\",\"color\":\"#FFF1DC\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.3AEFB4E070D858BB.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"particle accelerator\",\"color\":\"#3A2A18\"}]",
  "image.1B4891375312F96F.title": "Back to the Sun of Heliodor",
  "image.1AE1096D082CAC7F.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"grind · alloy · lase · collide\",\"color\":\"#C9A77A\",\"font\":\"minecraft:alt\"}]",
  "image.4EB33C0182EAE6D5.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» Core and particles\",\"color\":\"#F0A24A\"}]",
  "image.6344716DB15690D3.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"0 m/s\",\"color\":\"#A9C7CE\"}]",
  "image.6A97BF7B828CA073.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"10\",\"color\":\"#A9C7CE\"}]",
  "image.4D84EEB0F781BF17.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"100\",\"color\":\"#A9C7CE\"}]",
  "image.3BE64E15BFAE971B.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"250\",\"color\":\"#A9C7CE\"}]",
  "image.7C5B72F835EAD56D.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"500\",\"color\":\"#A9C7CE\"}]",
  "image.5E5478AAFB308D90.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"1,000\",\"color\":\"#A9C7CE\"}]",
  "image.1A1489911BF4B78A.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"2,500\",\"color\":\"#A9C7CE\"}]",
  "image.270A6711D956052C.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"5,000\",\"color\":\"#A9C7CE\"}]",
  "image.00D2F74E09C90E49.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"10,000\",\"color\":\"#A9C7CE\"}]",
  "chapter.724FCB653EBDEDDF.title": "PneumaticCraft · Drones and armor",
  "chapter.724FCB653EBDEDDF.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Drones and their programs, logistics frames, pneumatic armor from helmet to jet boots, and elevators."
  ],
  "quest.6C988EF917A96E05.title": "Harvesting Drone",
  "quest.6C988EF917A96E05.quest_subtitle": "Farmhand, no wages.",
  "quest.6C988EF917A96E05.quest_desc": [
    "Four turbine rotors around any crop. Charge it and place it: it harvests every grown crop and tree in a 17×17×17 cube. Deploy it sneaking against a chest that holds only a hoe and it replants too.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"It leaves the harvest on the ground. A Collector Drone next to a chest picks it up.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.21C6CF393CAF57AB.title": "Collector Drone",
  "quest.21C6CF393CAF57AB.quest_desc": [
    "Four rotors around a hopper. Deployed against a chest, it gathers items within its 17-block cube into that chest, only the kinds already inside; placed on the ground beside the chest, it takes everything. Up to 16 Range Upgrades widen the cube."
  ],
  "quest.04F0ED32A093AB35.title": "Guard Drone",
  "quest.04F0ED32A093AB35.quest_subtitle": "Bring your own sword.",
  "quest.04F0ED32A093AB35.quest_desc": [
    "Four rotors around an iron sword. Deploy it on a chest holding a weapon: it takes one and attacks hostile mobs around that spot. When the weapon breaks and none is left, it fights bare-handed, badly."
  ],
  "quest.0E94A6D7B8872266.title": "Pressurized Spawner",
  "quest.0E94A6D7B8872266.quest_desc": [
    "A Spawner Core holds mob essence: fill a crafted one with a Vacuum Trap under vacuum, or rip one out of a dungeon spawner with a Spawner Extractor. The Pressurized Spawner runs it at 10 bar or more, whatever the light or distance to a player."
  ],
  "task.01A125D5F94E655A.title": "Craft a Minigun",
  "quest.49E5A98BAD2810C9.title": "Minigun",
  "quest.49E5A98BAD2810C9.quest_desc": [
    "Air canister, cannon barrel, chest, lever and a little metal. Hold right-click to spin it up; it fires from ammo loaded into its own magazine, never from your pockets. A Minigun Upgrade gives the same gun to a Guard Drone."
  ],
  "quest.517D2F26FD2063C2.title": "Special rounds",
  "quest.517D2F26FD2063C2.quest_desc": [
    "Plain ammo is gunpowder, compressed iron and copper: 2,000 rounds. Wrapped in compressed iron with a pair of extras it specialises: blaze rods set fire, ice freezes, diamonds pierce armor, gold and obsidian hit hard at short range, TNT explodes."
  ],
  "quest.35CB08179E3A4947.title": "Sentry Turret",
  "quest.35CB08179E3A4947.quest_subtitle": "Guards the door. No lunch breaks.",
  "quest.35CB08179E3A4947.quest_desc": [
    "A minigun on plastic and compressed iron legs. It needs no air, only ammo, shoots anything its entity filter matches within 16 blocks, 32 with Range Upgrades, and starts out aimed at mobs only."
  ],
  "quest.7D5B0F96F00FAE14.title": "Drones come home to charge",
  "quest.7D5B0F96F00FAE14.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Low on air, any drone drops its job and flies to a Charging Station within 80 blocks that has a Dispenser Upgrade and at least 1 bar, then goes back to work. Out of air, it falls, and drones take fall damage.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.42B18B892CEA1957.title": "Rotors for the common store",
  "quest.42B18B892CEA1957.quest_subtitle": "Somebody always crashes one.",
  "quest.42B18B892CEA1957.quest_desc": [
    "Eight turbine rotors, blades pressed from gold and redstone. Every drone on the server flies on four of them."
  ],
  "quest.14CC555DEE6D9EF0.title": "Logistics Frames",
  "quest.14CC555DEE6D9EF0.quest_subtitle": "Factorio, in your chests.",
  "quest.14CC555DEE6D9EF0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Seven sticks, a dye and a \"},{\"text\":\"Logistics Core\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:logistics_core\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make eight frames. Stick them on chests and tanks: a Passive Provider offers what it holds, a Requester keeps the amounts you set in stock, and something with air moves the goods.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.386454CA91BFE0C8.title": "Deploy a Logistics Drone",
  "quest.5BD58D3051790F97.title": "Logistics Drone",
  "quest.5BD58D3051790F97.quest_desc": [
    "Four rotors around a logistics core. Deployed, it serves every framed inventory and tank in a wide cube around that spot, no tubes needed; Speed and Inventory Upgrades make each trip faster and fuller."
  ],
  "quest.52C982F2BBAC381B.title": "Logistics Configurator",
  "quest.52C982F2BBAC381B.quest_desc": [
    "Compressed iron, an air canister, a lever and red dye. Right-click a placed frame to set its filters, minimum order size or invisibility; sneak-right-click to take the frame off, or a Heat Frame, Transfer Gadget or Crop Support."
  ],
  "quest.2779D5516BA4E596.title": "Three more frames",
  "quest.2779D5516BA4E596.quest_desc": [
    "An Active Provider pushes its contents out to storage and requesters. Storage Frames take what active providers send, Default Storage too but only when no Storage Frame has room, and both feed requesters."
  ],
  "quest.044E8E2FCFD932D2.title": "Logistics Module",
  "quest.044E8E2FCFD932D2.quest_desc": [
    "A logistics core, four redstone and two tubes. Fixed on a tube facing a framed inventory, it joins every module on the same tube network; from 3 bar they move items and fluids, and the receiving end pays more air for bigger loads and longer runs. Dyes pick one of 16 channels."
  ],
  "quest.02AB7C7C49AF3CDC.title": "Tag Filter",
  "quest.02AB7C7C49AF3CDC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A book and quill on a display table make the \"},{\"text\":\"Tag Workbench\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:tag_workbench\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Put in an item, pick its tags and add paper: out comes a Tag Filter that frames and drone filters read as every item with those tags, every log for instance.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.79FD69E27466B6CB.title": "Drone",
  "quest.79FD69E27466B6CB.quest_subtitle": "Does anything. Once told.",
  "quest.79FD69E27466B6CB.quest_desc": [
    "Four turbine rotors around a PCB. A blank drone does nothing until a Programmer writes a program onto it; then it digs, builds, farms, fetches or fights wherever you point it.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A drone crafted with a dye, or right-clicked with one, changes colour. Nothing else changes, but twelve drones become easy to tell apart.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3BD9D308F28F4E96.title": "Drone upgrades",
  "quest.3BD9D308F28F4E96.quest_subtitle": "Pockets, patience and a swimsuit.",
  "quest.3BD9D308F28F4E96.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Drones take upgrades in the Charging Station: each \"},{\"text\":\"Inventory Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:inventory_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" adds a slot and 16,000 mB of tank, each Speed Upgrade 10%, and a \"},{\"text\":\"Standby Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:standby_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" parks it when idle to save air. A Security Upgrade lets it work in water.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.34E8B4DE6BC8751D.title": "Chunkloader Upgrade",
  "quest.34E8B4DE6BC8751D.quest_desc": [
    "Two PCBs, two eyes of ender and four lapis. In a drone, one upgrade keeps its own chunk loaded, two load a cross of five chunks and three a 3×3 square. It won't let a drone fly into chunks that are unloaded."
  ],
  "quest.2FE8CD0776A4B59E.title": "Programmer",
  "quest.2FE8CD0776A4B59E.quest_subtitle": "No keyboard required.",
  "quest.2FE8CD0776A4B59E.quest_desc": [
    "Two turbine rotors, a PCB, plastic, red dye and a black glass pane. Drag puzzle-piece widgets into a chain, put a drone in its slot and press the arrow to write the program. The Programmer itself runs without air."
  ],
  "quest.030C439820CFB2EC.title": "Puzzle Pieces",
  "quest.030C439820CFB2EC.quest_desc": [
    "Eight plastic around a PCB make eight. Writing a program spends one piece per widget, from your inventory or a chest touching the Programmer; overwrite the drone with a shorter program and the spare pieces come back."
  ],
  "quest.5B4003F96D7A044A.title": "GPS Tools",
  "quest.5B4003F96D7A044A.quest_subtitle": "You are here. Also there.",
  "quest.5B4003F96D7A044A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"GPS Tool\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:gps_tool\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" remembers the block you right-click. Two crafted together make a \"},{\"text\":\"GPS Area Tool\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:gps_area_tool\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": right-click marks one corner, left-click the other. Click either onto an Area widget in the Programmer to copy it.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.14264C46AB908F04.title": "Program a Drone",
  "quest.50E94211F67F595A.title": "First program",
  "quest.50E94211F67F595A.quest_subtitle": "Hello, world. Now dig.",
  "quest.50E94211F67F595A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Start\",\"color\":\"#E3A93F\"},{\"text\":\", then \"},{\"text\":\"Import From Inventory\",\"color\":\"#E3A93F\"},{\"text\":\" with an Area on the chest and an Item Filter for a shovel, then \"},{\"text\":\"Dig\",\"color\":\"#E3A93F\"},{\"text\":\" with an Area of dirt. Six pieces, no red borders, a charged drone in the slot: write it, place the drone, watch.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.70A24EAFCEE356EE.title": "Program storage",
  "quest.70A24EAFCEE356EE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Plastic, dye and a chest make both. A \"},{\"text\":\"Network API\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:network_api\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" holds a program built from real puzzle pieces and can run in a Programmable Controller; a \"},{\"text\":\"Network Data Storage\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:network_data_storage\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" only keeps it, free, for a library or a trade.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.61AFBDBE7222527E.title": "Remote and Universal Sensor",
  "quest.61AFBDBE7222527E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Sneak-right-click the \"},{\"text\":\"Remote\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:remote\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" to draw your own buttons and checkboxes; each one sets a global variable. A \"},{\"text\":\"Universal Sensor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:universal_sensor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" with a Dispenser Upgrade can read that variable and emit redstone, and drone programs read it too.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.431E1C94CF878EF7.title": "Right means yes, left means no",
  "quest.431E1C94CF878EF7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"An Area or filter widget snapped to the right of another widget is a whitelist; snapped to its left, a blacklist. Dig this box but not that corner is one Dig widget with an Area on each side.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5EE478D8E925B48F.title": "Programs travel well",
  "quest.5EE478D8E925B48F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Convert to Relative rewrites every area around one base coordinate, so a farm program works in anyone's world after changing a single widget. The Pastebin button exports and imports programs, or copies them to the clipboard.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.747148527B77FFE1.title": "Programmable Controller",
  "quest.747148527B77FFE1.quest_subtitle": "A drone that stays home.",
  "quest.747148527B77FFE1.quest_desc": [
    "A remote, a drone, a PCB, a network registry and an advanced tube. It runs a drone's or a Network API's program with a minidrone that is not an entity: no pathfinding, straight through walls, kinder to the server, for 10 mL of air per tick against a drone's 1.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"It skips the widgets that need a body: Entity Attack, Entity Import and Export, Teleport, Standby, Suicide and Computer Control. Big digs and big builds are its job.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.68025A2B624C85EA.title": "Debugging a drone",
  "quest.68025A2B624C85EA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A Pneumatic Helmet with Entity Tracker and Dispenser Upgrades debugs drones: look at one, press the helmet's drone-debugging key, then open the armor options and pick the Drone Debugger page to watch its program run, errors included.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "A Security Upgrade in the helmet hacks a stuck drone: it pauses and flies to you, and a second hack resumes it. Right-clicking a drone with a GPS Tool sends it to the stored block."
  ],
  "quest.771CB4D8CC04DD8B.title": "Drones don't travel alone",
  "quest.771CB4D8CC04DD8B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A drone won't go through a portal unless its program holds a Condition: Dimension widget, and each branch of that condition needs its own coordinates, since the far side's blocks sit elsewhere.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6A0E8877EC6D4946.title": "Compressed Iron Armor",
  "quest.6A0E8877EC6D4946.quest_desc": [
    "Each piece is its leather version wrapped in compressed iron: a little tougher than iron, with some knockback resistance, repaired with compressed iron at an anvil. The pneumatic suit is built on top of it."
  ],
  "task.70319D437878F9C5.title": "Wear the full Pneumatic Armor",
  "quest.21F5D15D3C5C324C.title": "Pneumatic Armor",
  "quest.21F5D15D3C5C324C.quest_subtitle": "Suit up. Charge first.",
  "quest.21F5D15D3C5C324C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Each compressed iron piece plus a PCB and air canisters: four boards and twenty-two canisters for the set. Plain, it is barely better than iron; charged and upgraded in the Charging Station, it tracks, flies and mends itself. Tune it all from the \"},{\"text\":\"armor options key\",\"color\":\"#D8C8FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_text\",\"contents\":\"Controls, PneumaticCraft: Pneumatic Armor General Options\"}},{\"text\":\".\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "{image:pneumaticcraft:textures/patchouli/pneumatic_armor.png width:96 height:96 align:center}"
  ],
  "quest.73ED07FEAFA9A651.title": "Armor and Item Life",
  "quest.73ED07FEAFA9A651.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A compressed iron ingot ringed with diamonds and lapis makes an \"},{\"text\":\"Armor Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:armor_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": two per piece match diamond, four beat it. A clock and apples make an \"},{\"text\":\"Item Life Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:item_life_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", which repairs the piece with air, up to five per piece.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.53F1A72ADA8B1B2F.title": "Radiation Shielding",
  "quest.53F1A72ADA8B1B2F.quest_desc": [
    "Mekanism's Radiation Shielding Unit surrounded by compressed iron and lapis. With one in every piece, the suit keeps out Mekanism radiation like the MekaSuit module does; fewer pieces, partial cover."
  ],
  "quest.7CFA74F4DE00C89A.title": "Trackers",
  "quest.7CFA74F4DE00C89A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An \"},{\"text\":\"Entity Tracker\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:entity_tracker_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" marks living things within 16 blocks, even behind walls, and warns when a mob targets you. A \"},{\"text\":\"Block Tracker\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:block_tracker_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" marks inventories, spawners, silverfish blocks, TNT and more within 30, and hovering shows their contents.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.498BE84A18C87DC9.title": "Item Search Upgrade",
  "quest.498BE84A18C87DC9.quest_subtitle": "Where did I put that?",
  "quest.498BE84A18C87DC9.quest_desc": [
    "A golden carrot ringed with eyes of ender. Pick an item in the helmet's screen and every stack of it within 16 blocks glows green: in chests with the Block Tracker, on the ground with the Entity Tracker."
  ],
  "quest.6A97BCB7BD78C429.title": "Coordinate Tracker",
  "quest.6A97BCB7BD78C429.quest_desc": [
    "A GPS Tool ringed with redstone and lapis. It paths you to a chosen block, and its Navigate to surface option finds the way out of any cave."
  ],
  "quest.63328EDBEFD556B9.title": "Night Vision, SCUBA, Ender Visor",
  "quest.63328EDBEFD556B9.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three helmet comforts. \"},{\"text\":\"Night Vision\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:night_vision_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" costs a trickle of air; \"},{\"text\":\"SCUBA\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:scuba_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" breathes underwater from the helmet's tank and clears your view; the \"},{\"text\":\"Ender Visor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:ender_visor_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" lets you look endermen in the eye.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4F2CA991F1066B28.title": "Magnet Upgrade",
  "quest.4F2CA991F1066B28.quest_desc": [
    "Plastic ringed with compressed iron and lapis. In the chestplate it draws nearby items and experience orbs to you for a little air each; more upgrades, more range. It leaves Immersive Engineering conveyor belts alone."
  ],
  "quest.54D3ABB18810ED9B.title": "Charging Upgrade",
  "quest.54D3ABB18810ED9B.quest_desc": [
    "A Charging Module, itself four charging stations around a tube, ringed with tubes and lapis. In the chestplate it charges every other pneumatic item you wear or carry, up to its own pressure; up to six speed it up."
  ],
  "quest.34274EFA664F57F3.title": "Security Upgrade",
  "quest.34274EFA664F57F3.quest_subtitle": "Stop, drop and vent.",
  "quest.34274EFA664F57F3.quest_desc": [
    "A safety module ringed with obsidian and lapis. In the chestplate it dumps air to put out fire and cool you when you are about to burn, slowly turning nearby lava to stone, and it absorbs shocks from bare Immersive Engineering wires."
  ],
  "quest.04D1525DEEE4550A.title": "Speed Upgrades in the leggings",
  "quest.04D1525DEEE4550A.quest_desc": [
    "Speed Upgrades in the leggings make you run faster for a little air, up to four; the armor screen can dial the boost down on the fly. In the other pieces they only shorten the boot-up."
  ],
  "quest.6839C2750CDE0566.title": "Jumping Upgrades I and II",
  "quest.6839C2750CDE0566.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Tier I is a cylinder, two vortex cannons, a tube, a piston and lapis; tier II adds slime blocks and pistons around it. Each tier jumps higher for more air, and holding \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.sneak\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" as you jump drops back to a tier-I hop.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4C8C4D72035599CE.title": "Jumping Upgrades III and IV",
  "quest.4C8C4D72035599CE.quest_desc": [
    "Three potions of Leaping around the previous tier, with pistons and a cylinder, make tier III; Leaping II potions make tier IV, the highest jump in the mod."
  ],
  "quest.61713EDE7C93C53C.title": "Vortex Cannon",
  "quest.61713EDE7C93C53C.quest_subtitle": "Also works as a ride.",
  "quest.61713EDE7C93C53C.quest_desc": [
    "Compressed iron, an air canister, a lever and yellow dye. It fires spinning air that pushes mobs back, knocks down leaves and plants and shears sheep; catch your own vortex for a fast trip, with no fall protection. Jumping and Jet Boots Upgrades are built around it."
  ],
  "task.12090DC22C4797F1.title": "Fly with Jet Boots",
  "quest.71A07B3ECDEE2E66.title": "Jet Boots",
  "quest.71A07B3ECDEE2E66.quest_subtitle": "Watch the gauge, not the ground.",
  "quest.71A07B3ECDEE2E66.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An Advanced Air Compressor, two advanced tubes, two vortex cannons and lapis make \"},{\"text\":\"Jet Boots Upgrade: Tier I\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:jet_boots_upgrade_1\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Hold the Jet Boots thrust key to fly where you look. \"},{\"text\":\"In this pack every tier adds 30 mL of air per tick of thrust, 2.5 times the mod's 12.\",\"color\":\"#FF8C7A\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Give the boots and chestplate Volume Upgrades, a Charging Upgrade in the chestplate, and an Aerial Interface at home to refill on the move.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6B853541C30214CB.title": "Jet Boots II and III",
  "quest.6B853541C30214CB.quest_desc": [
    "Tier II adds feathers and cylinders around the first; tier III, ghast tears and blaze rods. Each flies faster and thirstier, and from tier III the armor screen offers Builder Mode: slower, creative-style flight with quick digging in the air."
  ],
  "quest.13D89BDD280848AC.title": "Jet Boots IV and V",
  "quest.13D89BDD280848AC.quest_desc": [
    "Tier IV takes a nether star, phantom membranes and slow falling potions and adds Flight Stabilizers, which stop you dead when you let go of thrust. Tier V takes an elytra, end rods and dragon's breath: the fastest flight here, and the thirstiest."
  ],
  "quest.3BCE5AB14670A27E.title": "Kick and Stomp",
  "quest.3BCE5AB14670A27E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Up to four Dispenser Upgrades in the boots add a pneumatic kick with heavy knockback, on the boots' kick key. A \"},{\"text\":\"Stomp Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pneumaticcraft:stomp_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", TNT ringed with pistons, hurts mobs around you when you land hard enough to take damage.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1942F806BE1A86B5.title": "What the boots do for free",
  "quest.1942F806BE1A86B5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Even without upgrades the Pneumatic Boots cancel fall damage for a little air, and give a free one-block step assist you can switch off in the armor screen.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6910A2EE33386404.title": "Plausible deniability",
  "quest.6910A2EE33386404.quest_subtitle": "It opened itself. Honest.",
  "quest.6910A2EE33386404.quest_desc": [
    "You hacked a block with the helmet: a Security Upgrade and the Block Tracker let you flip levers, open doors and switch off spawners from a distance, with the helmet's hacking key."
  ],
  "reward.00FC980AB9397655.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.3302CBE3E23DA022.title": "They never saw it coming",
  "quest.3302CBE3E23DA022.quest_subtitle": "Reprogrammed, not harmed.",
  "quest.3302CBE3E23DA022.quest_desc": [
    "You hacked a living thing with the helmet. Each creature has its own trick: endermen stop teleporting, villagers reshuffle their trades, sheep change colour, and some animals just become yours."
  ],
  "reward.55D7E26C17245169.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.3DBCC563FDD3BBAB.title": "Who put that there?",
  "quest.3DBCC563FDD3BBAB.quest_subtitle": "Kinetic energy, meet stone.",
  "quest.3DBCC563FDD3BBAB.quest_desc": [
    "You flew into a wall fast enough to hurt. Tier IV stabilizers stop you when you let go of thrust, and Builder Mode flies slower."
  ],
  "reward.66EEC44FCF44841C.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.62E1FA669B0AB790.title": "Security Station",
  "quest.62E1FA669B0AB790.quest_desc": [
    "A PCB, two turbine rotors, plastic and glass. Build a network of Diagnostic Subroutine, IO Port, Registry and Nodes in it, and nobody untrusted can open, place or break anything nearby, up to 16 blocks out with Range Upgrades, until they hack it with a helmet."
  ],
  "quest.6C618483B1F7AE4B.title": "Pneumatic Jackhammer",
  "quest.6C618483B1F7AE4B.quest_desc": [
    "It mines anything at one speed, on air, once a drill bit goes in its screen: iron, compressed iron, diamond or netherite, each better and with more dig modes. Bits are pressed in the processing plant with lubricant; diamond digs 3×3. A Silk Touch or Fortune book goes in its book slot.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A Diamond Drill Bit is a block of diamond in 8,000 mB of lubricant at 7.5 bar and 500 °C: plan the heat before the diamonds.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.376CB63F6E0EB6BA.title": "Elevator",
  "quest.376CB63F6E0EB6BA.quest_subtitle": "Going up. Going down is free.",
  "quest.376CB63F6E0EB6BA.quest_desc": [
    "Bases of plastic and pneumatic cylinders at the bottom, frames of compressed iron stacked above: it rises as high as the frames, up to six blocks per base. It lifts any entity, with air, and a redstone signal on a base sets the height.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "{image:pneumaticcraft:textures/patchouli/elevator.png width:96 height:96 align:center}"
  ],
  "quest.3776239283570D33.title": "Elevator Callers",
  "quest.3776239283570D33.quest_desc": [
    "Stone buttons, plastic and stone. Placed beside the frames, each caller becomes a floor with buttons for every other floor; name the floors in the base's screen. A caller emits redstone while the car is there, and a pulse calls it."
  ],
  "quest.6431528A4A06CED9.title": "Elevators that pay you back",
  "quest.6431528A4A06CED9.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Up to four Charging Upgrades in an Elevator Base reclaim air on the way down: with four, 60% of the climb's cost comes back and the descent runs 40% slower. Bases side by side at the same height act as one wide car.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.102CEF252799D43A.title": "Pneumatic Door",
  "quest.102CEF252799D43A.quest_subtitle": "It saw you coming.",
  "quest.102CEF252799D43A.quest_desc": [
    "The door is six compressed iron; its base, a cylinder, a tube and more compressed iron, set level with the door's upper half. With air it opens for a nearby player, a looking player or like a wooden door, and a Security Station keeps it shut to strangers."
  ],
  "quest.13E6C2640FF1CD4A.title": "Air Cannon",
  "quest.13E6C2640FF1CD4A.quest_desc": [
    "A cannon barrel on a stone base, a tube and reinforced slabs. Aim it with a GPS Tool and a redstone pulse throws its items there; with an Entity Tracker Upgrade it throws the nearest entity instead, you included."
  ],
  "quest.0E52573060604097.title": "Aerial Interface",
  "quest.0E52573060604097.quest_subtitle": "Your pockets, from anywhere.",
  "quest.0E52573060604097.quest_desc": [
    "A nether star, ender pearls and an omnidirectional hopper between chamber walls: your inventory as a block, in any dimension. A Requester Frame on it keeps you stocked, a Charging Module on its armor side charges your suit, and a Dispenser Upgrade feeds you when you're hungry.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"With air it also lets you breathe underwater for 80 mL per tick, and it charges any FE item you carry from a 100,000 FE buffer.\"}]"
  ],
  "image.79EFB0DF53E6DEDC.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Drones that need no program\",\"color\":\"#E3A93F\"}]",
  "image.5B5BE0CA4A2AC575.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Firepower\",\"color\":\"#E3A93F\"}]",
  "image.622E974C349D9267.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Frames and tubes\",\"color\":\"#E3A93F\"}]",
  "image.02C5F5E019AF7FB4.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Upgrades\",\"color\":\"#E3A93F\"}]",
  "image.72343042BAFACE71.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Programming kit\",\"color\":\"#E3A93F\"}]",
  "image.7028F5D27731456F.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Programs, stored\",\"color\":\"#E3A93F\"}]",
  "image.6B604750A396E24C.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Blacklist\",\"color\":\"#E3A93F\"}]",
  "image.7F42C20845A5F177.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"In hand\",\"color\":\"#E3A93F\"}]",
  "image.6A9E41F93EBB9BDB.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Helmet\",\"color\":\"#E3A93F\"}]",
  "image.7C603EAF62D69633.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Chestplate\",\"color\":\"#E3A93F\"}]",
  "image.69AC2D66D79D0AE3.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Leggings\",\"color\":\"#E3A93F\"}]",
  "image.06A8B49DA8F2E866.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Boots\",\"color\":\"#E3A93F\"}]",
  "image.0F3B7A5C44B7621F.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Around the base\",\"color\":\"#E3A93F\"}]",
  "image.066D4027705C26BC.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"PneumaticCraft\\nDrones and armor\",\"color\":\"#FFF3D6\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.7503AE1FC3653FF8.title": "Back to the Sun of Heliodor",
  "image.120B79E347960237.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» Pressure\",\"color\":\"#E3A93F\"}]",
  "image.7907C6D6AFB16260.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"start · go to · dig · repeat\",\"color\":\"#B9A27A\",\"font\":\"minecraft:alt\"}]",
  "image.07D8CE70554DA59C.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Start\",\"color\":\"#F2F2F2\"}]",
  "image.3EA00E386A1D56A6.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Logistics\",\"color\":\"#F2F2F2\"}]",
  "image.17985A018B02427E.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Go To\",\"color\":\"#F2F2F2\"}]",
  "image.3DB176EF394B1A5C.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Import\",\"color\":\"#F2F2F2\"}]",
  "image.2A9BB6BA6E697A8B.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Dig\",\"color\":\"#F2F2F2\"}]",
  "image.37E945171C90FE8E.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"External\\nProgram\",\"color\":\"#F2F2F2\"}]",
  "image.7F061E005831C429.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"head\",\"color\":\"#B9A27A\"}]",
  "image.43D5A3991285CA6E.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"chest\",\"color\":\"#B9A27A\"}]",
  "image.7E3CFA685D18A507.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"legs\",\"color\":\"#B9A27A\"}]",
  "image.710FA3BF3A4D9A38.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"feet\",\"color\":\"#B9A27A\"}]",
  "chapter.4303D6A6B06E5331.title": "RFTools and XNet",
  "chapter.4303D6A6B06E5331.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Machine frames and shards, power, the Builder and its cards, screens and logic, teleporters, and XNet's channel networks."
  ],
  "quest.58B31E223A20F0D6.title": "Machine Frame",
  "quest.58B31E223A20F0D6.quest_subtitle": "The chassis of a whole mod family.",
  "quest.58B31E223A20F0D6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four \"},{\"text\":\"Iron Ingots\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:iron_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", two \"},{\"text\":\"Blue Dye\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:blue_dye\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and two \"},{\"text\":\"Gold Nuggets\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:gold_nugget\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make a \"},{\"text\":\"Machine Frame\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsbase:machine_frame\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Generators, crafters, teleporters, the Builder and the XNet Controller are all built around one, so keep a stack at hand.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.782A76788891D895.title": "Smart Wrench",
  "quest.782A76788891D895.quest_subtitle": "Blue in, yellow out.",
  "quest.782A76788891D895.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An \"},{\"text\":\"Iron Ingot\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:iron_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and two \"},{\"text\":\"Blue Dye\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:blue_dye\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make the \"},{\"text\":\"Smart Wrench\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsbase:smartwrench\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Right-click turns a machine and \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.sneak\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" + right-click picks it up; right-click the air for Select mode, which ties blocks to a master block, like shield sections to their projector.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.05304B06AF7BC363.title": "Technology Guide",
  "quest.05304B06AF7BC363.quest_subtitle": "One book, five mods.",
  "quest.05304B06AF7BC363.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Book\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:book\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and three \"},{\"text\":\"Iron Nuggets\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:iron_nugget\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make the \"},{\"text\":\"Technology Guide\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsbase:manual\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", one manual for Base, Power, Utility, Builder and XNet. While an RFTools item's tooltip is on screen, \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.openManual\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" opens its page.\"}]",
    "",
    "RFTools Storage and RFTools Dimensions are left out on purpose: AE2 keeps the items, and the pack already has its worlds."
  ],
  "quest.27604CCE0CDE6DFC.title": "Dimensional Shards",
  "quest.27604CCE0CDE6DFC.quest_subtitle": "Fortune says yes.",
  "quest.27604CCE0CDE6DFC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Dimensional Shard Ore\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsbase:dimensionalshard_overworld\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" hides between y -15 and 40 in the Overworld, and in the Nether and the End too. Mine it with an iron pickaxe or better for four or five \"},{\"text\":\"Dimensional Shards\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsbase:dimensionalshard\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" per block, more with Fortune.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"No ore nearby? A diamond, an emerald, gold, iron, redstone, glowstone dust, quartz, a prismarine shard and glass craft a single shard. It works; it isn't cheap.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.29E9AAEA105FD7E2.title": "Machine Infuser",
  "quest.29E9AAEA105FD7E2.quest_subtitle": "Feed your machines rocks. They like it.",
  "quest.29E9AAEA105FD7E2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four shards, two \"},{\"text\":\"Diamonds\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:diamond\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and two redstone around a \"},{\"text\":\"Machine Frame\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsbase:machine_frame\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make the \"},{\"text\":\"Machine Infuser\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsbase:machine_infuser\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Put a machine and \"},{\"text\":\"Dimensional Shards\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsbase:dimensionalshard\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in, give it 600 FE/t, and every shard stays in the machine for good, up to 256.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Most machines spend less FE when infused, and some gain more: the Coal Generator burns longer and hotter, the Builder quarries faster, the Screen Controller reaches farther, Dimensional Cells lose less over distance. Infusing the Infuser makes it cheaper to run.",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Infuse what runs all day first. A fully infused Builder quarries 28 blocks a tick instead of 8.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7FB35717721685F6.title": "Infused gems",
  "quest.7FB35717721685F6.quest_subtitle": "Diamonds, now with an extra dimension.",
  "quest.7FB35717721685F6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight \"},{\"text\":\"Dimensional Shards\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsbase:dimensionalshard\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" around a \"},{\"text\":\"Diamond\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:diamond\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make an \"},{\"text\":\"Infused Diamond\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsbase:infused_diamond\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; around an \"},{\"text\":\"Ender Pearl\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:ender_pearl\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", an \"},{\"text\":\"Infused Ender Pearl\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsbase:infused_enderpearl\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". The top recipes ask for them: advanced cells, module templates, the blazing and endergenic generators, the Scanner.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.62856E4D18F31118.title": "Look at Dimensional Shard Ore in end stone",
  "quest.11E68B6573C63E11.title": "Shards in the End",
  "quest.11E68B6573C63E11.quest_subtitle": "The void has sparkles too.",
  "quest.11E68B6573C63E11.quest_desc": [
    "The End grows its own shard veins in end stone: eight tries per chunk between y 2 and 80, against two in the Overworld, and twice the size. Bring a Fortune pickaxe and a way home."
  ],
  "reward.21F2EC995469BACF.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.513F15E4F2902951.title": "Shards for the common store",
  "quest.513F15E4F2902951.quest_subtitle": "Infusers are always hungry.",
  "quest.513F15E4F2902951.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Thirty-two \"},{\"text\":\"Dimensional Shards\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsbase:dimensionalshard\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for the common store, once a day. A Fortune III pickaxe averages six per ore.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7C066FE9FC7FCF26.title": "Coal Generator",
  "quest.7C066FE9FC7FCF26.quest_subtitle": "Old-school FE.",
  "quest.7C066FE9FC7FCF26.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Six coal or charcoal and two \"},{\"text\":\"Redstone Torches\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:redstone_torch\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" around a \"},{\"text\":\"Machine Frame\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsbase:machine_frame\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make a \"},{\"text\":\"Coal Generator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolspower:coalgenerator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": 60 FE/t for 600 ticks per coal, nine times as long per \"},{\"text\":\"Block of Coal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:coal_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It pushes FE into its neighbours and charges an item in its slot.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Fully infused it doubles its output and makes each coal last half again as long: three times the FE per lump.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.190FED7518F4144F.title": "Powercell",
  "quest.190FED7518F4144F.quest_subtitle": "Stackable, like good ideas.",
  "quest.190FED7518F4144F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Diamond\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:diamond\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a redstone block and three redstone make a \"},{\"text\":\"Power Core (Low)\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolspower:power_core1\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; four cores, four redstone and a frame, a \"},{\"text\":\"Powercell (Low)\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolspower:cell1\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": 500,000 FE, 250 FE/t per face. With no screen, the \"},{\"text\":\"Smart Wrench\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsbase:smartwrench\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" sets each face: blue in, yellow out, blank off.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Cells of any tier merge into one bank, up to 729 blocks, and each extra cell adds a quarter of the base rate to every face: five cells move twice as fast.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.51CEF74EF94D6644.title": "Medium and High Powercells",
  "quest.51CEF74EF94D6644.quest_subtitle": "Four million, then twenty.",
  "quest.51CEF74EF94D6644.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four \"},{\"text\":\"Power Cores (Medium)\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolspower:power_core2\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (shards, an emerald and redstone) and four redstone around a Low cell make a \"},{\"text\":\"Powercell (Medium)\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolspower:cell2\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": 4,000,000 FE, 1,000 FE/t per face. \"},{\"text\":\"High cores\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolspower:power_core3\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" around that give a \"},{\"text\":\"Powercell (High)\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolspower:cell3\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": 20,000,000 FE, 4,000 FE/t.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.45510A06967F9601.title": "Dimensional Cell",
  "quest.45510A06967F9601.quest_subtitle": "Power without wires or borders.",
  "quest.45510A06967F9601.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Cells linked by a \"},{\"text\":\"Powercell Card\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolspower:powercell_card\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" share one bank, anywhere and in any dimension: put an unlinked card in a cell, then use it on the others. A \"},{\"text\":\"Dimensional Cell\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolspower:dimensionalcell\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" holds 1,000,000 FE and moves 5,000 FE/t; drawing from far away costs up to a tenth extra.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Pack change: the Dimensional Cell takes two \"},{\"text\":\"Reinforced Alloy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:alloy_reinforced\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (act III) in its bottom corners, and the \"},{\"text\":\"Simple\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolspower:dimensionalcell_simple\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" one, with a quarter of the capacity and rate, takes one. Infusing a cell cuts the distance cost and raises its rate.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7F1312A254419439.title": "Advanced Dimensional Cell",
  "quest.7F1312A254419439.quest_subtitle": "Four times the everything.",
  "quest.7F1312A254419439.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four \"},{\"text\":\"Infused Diamonds\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsbase:infused_diamond\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and four \"},{\"text\":\"Blocks of Redstone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:redstone_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" around a Dimensional Cell make the \"},{\"text\":\"Advanced\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolspower:dimensionalcell_advanced\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" one: 4,000,000 FE and 20,000 FE/t. Link it with the same card and it joins the bank like any other.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.217A9A026B9C255E.title": "Reading the charge",
  "quest.217A9A026B9C255E.quest_subtitle": "Is it full yet?",
  "quest.217A9A026B9C255E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An \"},{\"text\":\"Information Screen\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsbase:information_screen\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" placed on a cell shows its charge, and the wrench changes what it displays. On a Machine Base, a \"},{\"text\":\"Power Level\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolspower:power_level\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" shows a digit from 0 to 9 and emits it as redstone, and a \"},{\"text\":\"Power Monitor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolspower:power_monitor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" emits only between the percentages you set.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.751BEB9127DC888E.title": "Blazing Agitator",
  "quest.751BEB9127DC888E.quest_subtitle": "Shaken, not stirred.",
  "quest.751BEB9127DC888E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three \"},{\"text\":\"Blaze Rods\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:blaze_rod\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", glass, iron and a frame make the \"},{\"text\":\"Blazing Agitator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolspower:blazing_agitator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", which spends 10 FE/t turning blaze rods into \"},{\"text\":\"Blazing Rods\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolspower:blazing_rod\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Good rods in its grid make their neighbours finish faster and better, and the lock buttons keep your best ones in place as boosters.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.708E3B66B75618DD.title": "Blazing Generator",
  "quest.708E3B66B75618DD.quest_subtitle": "Warm-up included.",
  "quest.708E3B66B75618DD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four blaze rods, two \"},{\"text\":\"Infused Diamonds\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsbase:infused_diamond\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", two redstone blocks and a frame make the \"},{\"text\":\"Blazing Generator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolspower:blazing_generator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It burns up to four Blazing Rods at once, each with its own power and duration, and needs to warm up before it gives its all, so keep it running.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Blazing Infuser\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolspower:blazing_infuser\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" improves finished rods: redstone adds power, quartz and glowstone add duration, shards add both. An infused rod no longer boosts others in the Agitator, so infuse only fuel.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.23ACEAB7303FB1B9.title": "Endergenic Generator",
  "quest.23ACEAB7303FB1B9.quest_subtitle": "Juggling pearls for a living.",
  "quest.23ACEAB7303FB1B9.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two \"},{\"text\":\"Endergenic Generators\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolspower:endergenic\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" pass an ender pearl back and forth, and every well-timed catch pays FE. A \"},{\"text\":\"Pearl Injector\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolspower:pearl_injector\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" loads the first on a redstone pulse; pair the two with the wrench, which reports the pearl's flight time in ticks.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Pulse the catcher into Charging so the pearl lands on tick 10 of its 15-tick cycle, then fire it on at once: a held pearl costs 500 FE/t and can slip away. \"},{\"text\":\"Ender Monitors\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolspower:ender_monitor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" watch the generator's state and handle the timing.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.58DECA7D319F0107.title": "Builder",
  "quest.58DECA7D319F0107.quest_subtitle": "Brick by brick, 500 FE apiece.",
  "quest.58DECA7D319F0107.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four \"},{\"text\":\"Bricks\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:bricks\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", an ender pearl, redstone and a \"},{\"text\":\"Machine Frame\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsbase:machine_frame\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make the \"},{\"text\":\"Builder\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsbuilder:builder\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; the pack sets a \"},{\"text\":\"Handling Core\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:handling_core\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (act III) in its foot. With a card and FE it builds, quarries, pumps, clears, and copies or moves whole rooms.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "It takes blocks from a chest on top of it or under it and puts what it digs into the same chests. Building costs 500 FE a block.",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.sneak\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" + right-click the Builder with a Shape Card to mark an area: two corner clicks set its size and offset.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5A681A52123D7131.title": "Shape Card",
  "quest.5A681A52123D7131.quest_subtitle": "Box, sphere, torus... and a heart.",
  "quest.5A681A52123D7131.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four \"},{\"text\":\"Paper\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:paper\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", two bricks, redstone and iron make a \"},{\"text\":\"Shape Card\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsbuilder:shape_card_def\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Right-click it to choose a shape (box, domes, sphere, cylinder, prism, torus, cone, even a heart), its size, offset and whether it is solid or hollow. In the Builder, it builds that shape from your blocks.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6BCC84C1A724B3A7.title": "Quarry Card",
  "quest.6BCC84C1A724B3A7.quest_subtitle": "Eight blocks a tick, before breakfast.",
  "quest.6BCC84C1A724B3A7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Shape Card, a \"},{\"text\":\"Diamond Pickaxe\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:diamond_pickaxe\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a \"},{\"text\":\"Diamond Shovel\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:diamond_shovel\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", iron and redstone make the \"},{\"text\":\"Quarry Card\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsbuilder:shape_card_quarry\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; the pack adds two \"},{\"text\":\"Ironwood Ingots\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:ironwood_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (act IV) in the top corners. The Builder mines the whole shape, 8 blocks a tick, from 300 FE a block.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "The card keeps the shape, size and offset of the Shape Card it came from, and hands them on to every card crafted from it."
  ],
  "quest.095CEC2B71BC1EB2.title": "Where to dig",
  "quest.095CEC2B71BC1EB2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Park the Builder in \"},{\"text\":\"the mining dimension\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"706A01ED65FEE247\"}},{\"text\":\", not under your base: a normal Quarry Card refills every hole with dirt, a Clearing one leaves air. The Builder's chunk must stay loaded; the quarry loads the chunk it is digging, one at a time.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6CFAD0EF97557697.title": "Fortune Quarry Card",
  "quest.6CFAD0EF97557697.quest_subtitle": "More ore, same hole.",
  "quest.6CFAD0EF97557697.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four shards, a \"},{\"text\":\"Ghast Tear\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:ghast_tear\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", an \"},{\"text\":\"Emerald\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:emerald\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a \"},{\"text\":\"Diamond\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:diamond\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a redstone around a Quarry Card make the \"},{\"text\":\"Fortune\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsbuilder:shape_card_quarry_fortune\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" version: ores drop as if mined with Fortune, for twice the FE per block.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.47450443504B71B2.title": "Silk Touch Quarry Card",
  "quest.47450443504B71B2.quest_subtitle": "Ores stay ores.",
  "quest.47450443504B71B2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Nether Star\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:nether_star\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", three \"},{\"text\":\"Diamonds\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:diamond\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and four shards around a Quarry Card make the \"},{\"text\":\"Silk Touch\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsbuilder:shape_card_quarry_silk\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" version. Blocks come out whole, for three times the FE: ore blocks for a processing line that multiplies them.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.29B6F92F9CE9BAA0.title": "Nothing but air",
  "quest.29B6F92F9CE9BAA0.quest_subtitle": "Leave not even the dirt behind.",
  "quest.29B6F92F9CE9BAA0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight \"},{\"text\":\"Glass\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:glass\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" around a Fortune Quarry Card make the \"},{\"text\":\"Clearing Fortune\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsbuilder:shape_card_quarry_clear_fortune\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" one: the hole stays empty. Fully infused, the Builder takes 28 blocks a tick; feed it from a linked Dimensional Cell and send the haul home over XNet.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2F760D81906579A3.title": "Void, Pump and Liquid Cards",
  "quest.2F760D81906579A3.quest_subtitle": "Delete, drain, pour.",
  "quest.2F760D81906579A3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Obsidian and black dye around a Shape Card make a \"},{\"text\":\"Void Card\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsbuilder:shape_card_void\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": the Builder deletes the shape without drops, at half the FE. Buckets and redstone make the \"},{\"text\":\"Pump Card\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsbuilder:shape_card_pump\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", which drains fluids into a tank by the Builder, and the \"},{\"text\":\"Liquid Card\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsbuilder:shape_card_liquid\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", which pours them out.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7AEEB06B2B144946.title": "Space Chambers",
  "quest.7AEEB06B2B144946.quest_subtitle": "Copy-paste, but for rooms.",
  "quest.7AEEB06B2B144946.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Put seven \"},{\"text\":\"Space Chambers\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsbuilder:space_chamber\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a \"},{\"text\":\"Controller\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsbuilder:space_chamber_controller\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on the corners of a box up to 128 blocks a side, and \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.sneak\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" + right-click the Controller with a \"},{\"text\":\"Space Card\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsbuilder:space_chamber_card\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". In the Builder, that card copies, moves or swaps the room.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Right-click the card in the air to list what the room holds. Moving it costs 500 FE a block, five times that into another dimension, and Collect mode gathers the items and XP inside instead."
  ],
  "quest.079EADD02C8453CE.title": "Scanner and Composer",
  "quest.079EADD02C8453CE.quest_subtitle": "Photocopy a castle.",
  "quest.079EADD02C8453CE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Scanner\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsbuilder:scanner\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" reads the area one Shape Card describes and writes it into another as a Scan shape, which the Builder rebuilds elsewhere from your blocks. The \"},{\"text\":\"Composer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsbuilder:composer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" adds, subtracts or intersects shapes into one card, and the \"},{\"text\":\"Projector\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsbuilder:projector\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" previews any card in the air.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.273D0DFA045CFC50.title": "Shield Projector",
  "quest.273D0DFA045CFC50.quest_subtitle": "A wall of light and FE.",
  "quest.273D0DFA045CFC50.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Template blocks of one colour touching a \"},{\"text\":\"Shield Projector\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsbuilder:shield_block1\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" become a force field, or a Shape Card gives it a form. Filters decide who passes, who is blocked and who takes damage, and the look goes from invisible to solid or mimicking a block. Tier 1 covers 256 blocks.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Each tier wraps the last: 1,024 blocks with redstone blocks and obsidian, 4,096 with shards, 32,768 with Nether Stars. Eight \"},{\"text\":\"Shield Templates\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsbuilder:red_shield_template_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" come from wool, dye and glass.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.0F3C37666D49219E.title": "Look at a shield you raised",
  "quest.26D5680DAE4CFF91.title": "Force field",
  "quest.26D5680DAE4CFF91.quest_subtitle": "Nobody gets through. Probably.",
  "quest.26D5680DAE4CFF91.quest_desc": [
    "A damage filter strikes for 5 per hit at 1,000 FE. Switch it to player damage (2,000 FE) and mobs drop loot and XP as if you had swung; with shards in the projector, each hit spends two of them for Looting III."
  ],
  "reward.66D6C24FF40B6D5F.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.7E9C9385B150C8F3.title": "Movers",
  "quest.7E9C9385B150C8F3.quest_subtitle": "A railway without rails.",
  "quest.7E9C9385B150C8F3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two \"},{\"text\":\"Movers\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsbuilder:mover\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in a straight line, up to 128 blocks apart, are stops on a track, and a \"},{\"text\":\"Mover Controller\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsbuilder:mover_controller\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" placed against one finds every Mover linked to it. Each trip costs the controller 1,000 FE.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3BFE2836A84398FF.title": "Vehicles",
  "quest.3BFE2836A84398FF.quest_subtitle": "Your base, but it drives.",
  "quest.3BFE2836A84398FF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Build the vehicle inside a Space Chamber; the \"},{\"text\":\"Vehicle Builder\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsbuilder:vehicle_builder\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" packs it into a \"},{\"text\":\"Vehicle Card\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsbuilder:vehicle_card\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", and the card in a Mover sets it down there. A \"},{\"text\":\"Mover Control\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsbuilder:mover_control\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" block inside steers it, and \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.unmountVehicle\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" gets you off.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"From outside, a \"},{\"text\":\"Vehicle Control Module\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsbuilder:vehicle_control_module\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on a Screen, bound to the Mover Controller, sends it to any stop.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.181E685FFBFE7E7E.title": "Matter Transmitter and Receiver",
  "quest.181E685FFBFE7E7E.quest_subtitle": "Beam me home.",
  "quest.181E685FFBFE7E7E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Step into the beam of a \"},{\"text\":\"Matter Transmitter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsutility:matter_transmitter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" dialed to a \"},{\"text\":\"Matter Receiver\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsutility:matter_receiver\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and you arrive there, even in another dimension. Both are ender pearls, iron and redstone around a frame; the pack sets a \"},{\"text\":\"Reinforced Alloy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:alloy_reinforced\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (act III) in the Receiver.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Charge the Receiver before anyone uses it: every arrival draws 5,000 FE from it, and landing on one that can't pay hurts."
  ],
  "quest.76F8456772C49F54.title": "Dialing Device",
  "quest.76F8456772C49F54.quest_subtitle": "Pick a number.",
  "quest.76F8456772C49F54.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Six redstone and two torches around a frame make the \"},{\"text\":\"Dialing Device\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsutility:dialing_device\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It finds transmitters within 10 blocks around it and 5 up or down, lists every receiver in reach and dials; Dial Once hangs up after the first trip.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Simple Dialer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsutility:simple_dialer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" dials on a redstone signal: \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.sneak\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" + right-click it on a transmitter or a dialed receiver to set the route.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.224660F38550102F.title": "Analyzer and Booster",
  "quest.224660F38550102F.quest_subtitle": "Look before you leap.",
  "quest.224660F38550102F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Destination Analyzer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsutility:destination_analyzer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" next to the transmitter colours it by its destination: green is safe, yellow unknown, red bad. A \"},{\"text\":\"Matter Booster\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsutility:matter_booster\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" next to it spends 20,000 FE to land you even when the receiver has run dry.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.38A860709D10EF92.title": "Charged Porters",
  "quest.38A860709D10EF92.quest_subtitle": "A teleporter that fits in a pocket.",
  "quest.38A860709D10EF92.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.sneak\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" + right-click a Receiver with a \"},{\"text\":\"Charged Porter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsutility:charged_porter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" to store it, then right-click to go; it pays half again what a transmitter would. The \"},{\"text\":\"Advanced\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsutility:advanced_charged_porter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" one holds eight targets and 1,000,000 FE, and teleports four times faster.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.prevDestination\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" and \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.nextDestination\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" step through its targets.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4F1056C9A0388EA8.title": "The teleport bill",
  "quest.4F1056C9A0388EA8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A local trip costs the transmitter 5,000 FE plus 10 per block, never more than 100,000, and any trip to another dimension costs the full 100,000, plus 500 FE/t while the beam charges. The transmitter holds 200,000: fill it before the long jumps.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.425583372E07221F.title": "Machine Base",
  "quest.425583372E07221F.quest_subtitle": "A quarter block of brains.",
  "quest.425583372E07221F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three \"},{\"text\":\"Gold Nuggets\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:gold_nugget\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" over three stone make a \"},{\"text\":\"Machine Base\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsbase:machine_base\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", the foot of every screen and logic block. Logic blocks sit a quarter block high on floors, walls or ceilings and face the edge your cursor is nearest when you place them.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.612F9FC41120325A.title": "Screens",
  "quest.612F9FC41120325A.quest_subtitle": "A dashboard for your base.",
  "quest.612F9FC41120325A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Five glass and three iron on a Machine Base make a \"},{\"text\":\"Screen\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsutility:screen\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It shows nothing until you add modules and runs only near a \"},{\"text\":\"Screen Controller\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsutility:screen_controller\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": press Scan in the controller to power every screen in a 32x32x32 area.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The wrench resizes a screen and toggles its transparency; each module's settings have a full-bright switch.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.56F2460D6599157A.title": "Screen modules",
  "quest.56F2460D6599157A.quest_subtitle": "What's on tonight?",
  "quest.56F2460D6599157A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Modules are the screen's channels: the \"},{\"text\":\"Text Module\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsutility:text_module\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" is free, the \"},{\"text\":\"Energy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsutility:energy_module\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and \"},{\"text\":\"Inventory\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsutility:inventory_module\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" ones cost 4 FE/t each. \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.sneak\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" + right-click a module on a machine to aim it, then put it in the screen.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"There are also clock, counter, fluid, redstone, button and machine-information modules. Plain ones read targets up to 64 blocks away on each axis, in the same dimension; the Plus versions, like the \"},{\"text\":\"Energy Plus Screen Module\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsutility:energyplus_module\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", read any distance and any dimension.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.21BD0826D9586A7F.title": "Tablet",
  "quest.21BD0826D9586A7F.quest_subtitle": "The whole base, in your pocket.",
  "quest.21BD0826D9586A7F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Fit a \"},{\"text\":\"Screen Link\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsutility:screen_link\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (\"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.sneak\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" + right-click it on a Screen) or a \"},{\"text\":\"Redstone Module\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsutility:redstone_information\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (right-click a transmitter or receiver to add its channel) in a \"},{\"text\":\"Tablet\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsbase:tablet\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": right-click then opens it wherever the target's chunk is loaded.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.sneak\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" + right-click the tablet to fit up to six; \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.prevDestination\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" and \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.nextDestination\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" switch between them.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.42ED65A4D4594D90.title": "Wireless redstone",
  "quest.42ED65A4D4594D90.quest_subtitle": "Pull a lever three rooms away.",
  "quest.42ED65A4D4594D90.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Redstone Transmitter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsutility:redstone_transmitter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" opens a channel when placed; right-click it with a \"},{\"text\":\"Redstone Receiver\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsutility:redstone_receiver\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in hand to tune the receiver in, and switch the receiver to analog to keep the strength. A \"},{\"text\":\"Button Module\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsutility:button_module\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on a screen sends on a channel too.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.57E52BD2048A1FBC.title": "Logic blocks",
  "quest.57E52BD2048A1FBC.quest_subtitle": "Redstone with a degree.",
  "quest.57E52BD2048A1FBC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"On Machine Bases: a \"},{\"text\":\"Timer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsutility:timer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" pulses at any delay and restarts on every input, a \"},{\"text\":\"Counter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsutility:counter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" fires every N pulses, a \"},{\"text\":\"Sequencer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsutility:sequencer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" plays 64 steps in seven modes, and a \"},{\"text\":\"Logic\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsutility:logic\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" block maps three inputs to any truth table.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A Timer fed by a working process never fires: wire a machine's output pulses into it and it raises the alarm only when the machine stalls.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.57552BCF69FD6EBB.title": "Analog, Digit and Wire",
  "quest.57552BCF69FD6EBB.quest_subtitle": "Small parts, fewer headaches.",
  "quest.57552BCF69FD6EBB.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An \"},{\"text\":\"Analog\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsutility:analog\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" multiplies and offsets a signal depending on how its A and B sides compare, a \"},{\"text\":\"Digit\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsutility:digit\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" shows a strength from 0 to F, and a \"},{\"text\":\"Wire\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsutility:wire\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" carries a signal in a straight line without the lag of redstone dust.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.290BC456094F281E.title": "Sensor and Inventory Checker",
  "quest.290BC456094F281E.quest_subtitle": "Eyes on the farm.",
  "quest.290BC456094F281E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Sensor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsutility:sensor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" looks 1, 3 or 5 blocks ahead for blocks, fluids, crop growth, mobs or players and emits redstone. An \"},{\"text\":\"Inventory Checker\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsutility:invchecker\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" emits when a slot of the inventory behind it holds more than a set number of an item or tag. Slots count from zero.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.36B12A0BD6F53671.title": "Crafter",
  "quest.36B12A0BD6F53671.quest_subtitle": "It crafts while you mine.",
  "quest.36B12A0BD6F53671.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two crafting tables and two redstone torches around a frame make a \"},{\"text\":\"Crafter Tier 1\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsutility:crafter1\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Lay a recipe in its grid and apply it; ingredients go in 26 slots, results come out of 4, and each craft costs 100 FE. Tier 1 remembers two recipes.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"R remembers what sits in a slot so only that item goes there; F forgets. In Int mode a result stays inside to feed the next recipe. The Crafting Card from the manual has no reader in this pack: the Crafter keeps its recipes itself.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.50CABE0EA36EF81B.title": "Crafter Tiers 2 and 3",
  "quest.50CABE0EA36EF81B.quest_subtitle": "Two, four, eight.",
  "quest.50CABE0EA36EF81B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two more crafting tables and torches around a Crafter make the next tier, recipes and contents included: \"},{\"text\":\"Tier 2\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsutility:crafter2\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" remembers four recipes and \"},{\"text\":\"Tier 3\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsutility:crafter3\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" eight. Fast mode runs five crafts at a time, and infusion cuts the FE.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1C4C957B5C85CA8F.title": "Environmental Controller",
  "quest.1C4C957B5C85CA8F.quest_subtitle": "Buffs by the cubic metre.",
  "quest.1C4C957B5C85CA8F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Diamond, emerald, gold and iron blocks and ender pearls around a frame make the \"},{\"text\":\"Environmental Controller\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsutility:environmental_controller\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; the pack swaps one pearl for a \"},{\"text\":\"Reinforced Alloy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:alloy_reinforced\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (act III). Up to seven modules act on everyone inside its radius and height band, and each costs FE per block covered.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Every module starts as a \"},{\"text\":\"Module Template\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsutility:module_template\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": four shards and four iron around an Infused Diamond. The filter picks who is affected (everyone, listed players, passive or hostile mobs), and mobs cost double.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.424D4DCD81CCFBEE.title": "Syringe",
  "quest.424D4DCD81CCFBEE.quest_subtitle": "This might sting a little.",
  "quest.424D4DCD81CCFBEE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two \"},{\"text\":\"Iron Ingots\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:iron_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a \"},{\"text\":\"Glass Bottle\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:glass_bottle\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make a \"},{\"text\":\"Syringe\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsutility:syringe\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Hit a mob with it ten times, always the same kind, and it holds that mob's essence: effect modules and the Spawner both start from a full one.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.625D93D2ED91DBFA.title": "Effect modules",
  "quest.625D93D2ED91DBFA.quest_subtitle": "Coffee for the whole room.",
  "quest.625D93D2ED91DBFA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A full syringe, a Module Template and seven matching items make a module: wolf and \"},{\"text\":\"Powered Rails\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:powered_rail\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for \"},{\"text\":\"Speed\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsutility:speed_module\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", pillager and redstone for \"},{\"text\":\"Haste\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsutility:haste_module\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", zombie and rotten flesh for \"},{\"text\":\"Saturation\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsutility:saturation_module\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Each costs 0.001 FE/t per block covered.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Plus versions (Speed, Haste, Regeneration and Saturation III) add a Plus template and infused gems and cost three times as much. Blindness, Poison, Slowness and Weakness only touch mobs here, and No-Teleport pins endermen and shulkers in place."
  ],
  "quest.50CFB8CC0A0BC881.title": "Peaceful Module",
  "quest.50CFB8CC0A0BC881.quest_subtitle": "No monsters, no drama.",
  "quest.50CFB8CC0A0BC881.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An iron golem's syringe, a \"},{\"text\":\"ModulePlus Template\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsutility:moduleplus_template\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", four \"},{\"text\":\"Blocks of Iron\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:iron_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and three \"},{\"text\":\"Infused Ender Pearls\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsbase:infused_enderpearl\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make the \"},{\"text\":\"Peaceful Module\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsutility:peaceful_module\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": no hostile mob spawns inside the controller's range, for 0.001 FE/t per block.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.083D065001E084EC.title": "Flight Module",
  "quest.083D065001E084EC.quest_subtitle": "Creative mode, rented by the block.",
  "quest.083D065001E084EC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A ghast's syringe, a ModulePlus Template, six \"},{\"text\":\"Ghast Tears\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:ghast_tear\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and an \"},{\"text\":\"Infused Ender Pearl\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsbase:infused_enderpearl\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make the \"},{\"text\":\"Flight Module\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsutility:flight_module\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": creative flight for anyone in range, at 0.004 FE/t per block, four times a basic module.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5A1F529EBFEAF725.title": "Spawner",
  "quest.5A1F529EBFEAF725.quest_subtitle": "Mobs to order.",
  "quest.5A1F529EBFEAF725.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A full syringe in the \"},{\"text\":\"Spawner\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsutility:spawner\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" picks the mob. \"},{\"text\":\"Matter Beamers\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsutility:matter_beamer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", linked with the wrench and given a redstone signal, feed it the three materials that mob's recipe lists, and FE does the rest: 800 FE for a zombie, 1,000 for a blaze.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Pack change: the Spawner takes an \"},{\"text\":\"Ironwood Ingot\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:ironwood_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (act IV) in a bottom corner.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Infuse the beamers: they send more per pulse for less FE. Materials the mob doesn't need are ignored.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.0F34816A42DE1D71.title": "A syringe full of Wither",
  "quest.3E97C0EDD20723C8.title": "A sample from the Wither",
  "quest.3E97C0EDD20723C8.quest_subtitle": "Ten jabs. It noticed.",
  "quest.3E97C0EDD20723C8.quest_desc": [
    "The syringe takes bosses like any other mob: ten hits and it's full. In this pack the Spawner has no Wither recipe, though: a Wither for a tenth of a star would have printed stars."
  ],
  "reward.723B044FC0431D62.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.06141C8077AB2510.title": "XNet Controller",
  "quest.06141C8077AB2510.quest_subtitle": "Eight channels, one brain.",
  "quest.06141C8077AB2510.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two repeaters, a comparator, redstone, iron and a frame make the \"},{\"text\":\"Controller\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"xnet:controller\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; the pack puts a \"},{\"text\":\"Reinforced Alloy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:alloy_reinforced\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (act III) where its gold went. It runs up to eight channels (items, fluids, energy or logic) for every connector on its cable network.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "It draws 1 FE/t per active channel and 2 FE per operation from a 100,000 FE buffer, so wire it to power first."
  ],
  "quest.57B2140EFD756F01.title": "Cables and connectors",
  "quest.57B2140EFD756F01.quest_subtitle": "Red never talks to blue.",
  "quest.57B2140EFD756F01.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"String, redstone, a gold nugget and a dye make sixteen \"},{\"text\":\"Network Cables\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"xnet:netcable_red\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; red, green, blue and yellow never join, so four networks can share a wall. A \"},{\"text\":\"Connector\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"xnet:connector_red\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (a chest, gold, redstone and dye) goes on the cable beside each block the network should reach.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Name a connector in its screen and the Controller lists it by that name. Any cable or connector can be re-dyed in the crafting grid."
  ],
  "quest.70EA46A774BBF977.title": "Item channels",
  "quest.70EA46A774BBF977.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"An item channel shares by priority or round robin, and each connector inserts or extracts. Extractors take from the first slot, a random one or in order; one item, a stack or a set count; every 10 ticks at best, 5 on an advanced connector.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0B100AF4DA0987E5.title": "Fluid channels",
  "quest.0B100AF4DA0987E5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A fluid connector moves up to 1,000 mB per operation, 5,000 when advanced. Its minimum and maximum pause it when the tank on the other side gets too empty or too full.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.766AEE98414EBF0E.title": "Energy channels",
  "quest.766AEE98414EBF0E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Energy connectors carry up to 10,000 FE/t, advanced ones 100,000. Give the machines that must never starve a higher priority and let the rest share what is left.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7CF9EF22817C4CDF.title": "Logic channels",
  "quest.7CF9EF22817C4CDF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A logic connector in Sensor mode reads the items, fluid, energy or redstone of its block and lights a colour when a comparison holds; one in Output mode turns that colour into redstone. Feed a generator's fuel only while its buffer is low.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1ED624C1C43D1356.title": "Filter Module",
  "quest.1ED624C1C43D1356.quest_subtitle": "Only the good stuff.",
  "quest.1ED624C1C43D1356.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A hopper, iron, redstone and paper make a \"},{\"text\":\"Filter Module\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsbase:filter_module\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": items, blocks and tags as a whitelist or blacklist, matching NBT and damage if you want. \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.sneak\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" + right-click a chest to copy what it holds. The Controller holds four for its item connectors; Crafters and Builders take one.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.72F958976F6C18DD.title": "Tank",
  "quest.72F958976F6C18DD.quest_subtitle": "Thirty-two buckets, one flavour.",
  "quest.72F958976F6C18DD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Glass, buckets, iron and a frame make an RFTools \"},{\"text\":\"Tank\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"rftoolsutility:tank\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for 32,000 mB. A filled bucket in its filter slot locks it to that fluid, so a fluid channel can't mix things up.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.655F01B97DD53BD2.title": "Advanced connectors",
  "quest.655F01B97DD53BD2.quest_subtitle": "Same wire, more lanes.",
  "quest.655F01B97DD53BD2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Paper, a \"},{\"text\":\"Diamond\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:diamond\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", an ender pearl and redstone make a \"},{\"text\":\"Connector Upgrade Kit\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"xnet:connector_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.sneak\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" + right-click a placed connector to make it advanced. It moves items every 5 ticks, 100,000 FE/t and 5,000 mB, and reaches any side of the block it touches.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.39F2B06F5B6C0B59.title": "Redstone Proxy",
  "quest.39F2B06F5B6C0B59.quest_subtitle": "A stand-in for your redstone.",
  "quest.39F2B06F5B6C0B59.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight redstone around a frame make a \"},{\"text\":\"Redstone Proxy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"xnet:redstone_proxy\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a plain block a logic connector can read or drive when the real contraption has no good face. Craft it with a torch for the \"},{\"text\":\"update\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"xnet:redstone_proxy_upd\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" version, which also wakes up its neighbours.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.64E9E38C94BBDB98.title": "Facades",
  "quest.64E9E38C94BBDB98.quest_subtitle": "Cables? What cables?",
  "quest.64E9E38C94BBDB98.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Paper, wool and glass make sixteen \"},{\"text\":\"Facades\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"xnet:facade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Right-click a block to copy its look, then right-click a cable or connector to hide it inside; break the facade and the cable is back.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4B7327FBE1FDB730.title": "Router",
  "quest.4B7327FBE1FDB730.quest_subtitle": "Networks, meet networks.",
  "quest.4B7327FBE1FDB730.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Routing cables (black dye) and routing connectors (redstone and gold around any connector) join a \"},{\"text\":\"Router\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"xnet:router\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" to several controllers. In it, one network publishes a channel under a name and another consumes it: up to 32 published channels per routing network.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.66117F0122FEB0E2.title": "Wireless Router",
  "quest.66117F0122FEB0E2.quest_subtitle": "Look, no cables.",
  "quest.66117F0122FEB0E2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Wireless Router\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"xnet:wireless_router\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" needs an \"},{\"text\":\"Antenna Base\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"xnet:antenna_base\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on top and an \"},{\"text\":\"Antenna\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"xnet:antenna\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on that: 100 blocks of range, 500 with a second antenna above. Two routers link when each sits within the other's range, in the same dimension; each published channel costs 20 or 50 FE/t.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.02619F5F1BD9855B.title": "Antenna Dish",
  "quest.02619F5F1BD9855B.quest_subtitle": "Anywhere, any world.",
  "quest.02619F5F1BD9855B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An \"},{\"text\":\"Antenna Dish\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"xnet:antenna_dish\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on the Antenna Base, instead of antennas, gives unlimited range, and two routers with dishes link even across dimensions. Each channel they publish costs 200 FE/t.\"}]"
  ],
  "image.1951DEF90E777B81.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Infusion\",\"color\":\"#7FE3DD\"}]",
  "image.5B21CF069E60A25D.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Power\",\"color\":\"#7FE3DD\"}]",
  "image.5453752DE8AB28DE.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Cards and quarries\",\"color\":\"#7FE3DD\"}]",
  "image.2DAF7B281A049DC4.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Scan, move and shield\",\"color\":\"#7FE3DD\"}]",
  "image.7CF639A1591A833E.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Teleportation\",\"color\":\"#7FE3DD\"}]",
  "image.3B668BC1BFC4B714.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Screens and logic\",\"color\":\"#7FE3DD\"}]",
  "image.5B34AB64D8D735D6.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Environment and spawning\",\"color\":\"#7FE3DD\"}]",
  "image.140F67A6CC69B2FA.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Items\",\"color\":\"#7FE3DD\"}]",
  "image.78B6BC2EB17D6AB1.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Fluids\",\"color\":\"#7FE3DD\"}]",
  "image.5613B848BDD8BB2E.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Energy\",\"color\":\"#7FE3DD\"}]",
  "image.0A98342320671571.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Logic\",\"color\":\"#7FE3DD\"}]",
  "image.450D26BFF37AFED6.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Routing\",\"color\":\"#7FE3DD\"}]",
  "image.0C1630A376B5408F.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"RFTools and XNet\",\"color\":\"#EAFBFA\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.60E032750E759347.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"one frame, many machines\",\"color\":\"#9FEDE7\",\"font\":\"minecraft:uniform\"}]",
  "image.5CBE8BE0C3C92460.title": "Back to the Sun of Heliodor",
  "chapter.09DFA10FF144C082.title": "Refined Storage",
  "chapter.09DFA10FF144C082.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Disks, grids and autocrafting on one network: no channels, devices just touch."
  ],
  "quest.092BCE5A62415FEB.title": "Quartz Enriched Iron",
  "quest.092BCE5A62415FEB.quest_subtitle": "Iron that picked up a quartz habit.",
  "quest.092BCE5A62415FEB.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three \"},{\"text\":\"Iron Ingots\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:iron_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a \"},{\"text\":\"Nether Quartz\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:quartz\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in a 2×2 grid make four \"},{\"text\":\"Quartz Enriched Iron\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:quartz_enriched_iron\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Casings, disks and almost every device start here.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.54732CCEAF78597A.title": "AE2 or Refined Storage?",
  "quest.54732CCEAF78597A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Here both controllers take a Routing Matrix. Refined Storage has no channels: devices only need to touch the network, and disks count items, not types. AE2 makes you plan channels and brings more addons. Pick one main storage; the other road is \"},{\"text\":\"AE2 · Network\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"1E24729503A1C81A\"}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.025E856BE0A514AA.title": "Enriched by the stack",
  "quest.025E856BE0A514AA.quest_subtitle": "The network pays in metal.",
  "quest.025E856BE0A514AA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Sixty-four \"},{\"text\":\"Quartz Enriched Iron\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:quartz_enriched_iron\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for the common store, once a day. Write it into a crafting pattern and it keeps coming as long as iron and quartz do.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.768B95CEAB6E83BD.title": "Into the furnace",
  "quest.768B95CEAB6E83BD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Smelt \"},{\"text\":\"Nether Quartz\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:quartz\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" into \"},{\"text\":\"Silicon\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:silicon\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Each raw processor takes one, each 1k storage part four, and the controller two.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4FB7A47C14F171A1.title": "Quartz on tap",
  "quest.4FB7A47C14F171A1.quest_subtitle": "The Nether is optional. Diorite isn't.",
  "quest.4FB7A47C14F171A1.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Refined Storage runs on \"},{\"text\":\"Nether Quartz\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:quartz\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": a quarter of each Quartz Enriched Iron, all its silicon, every destruction core. No Nether trip yet? Create's \"},{\"text\":\"Crushing Wheels\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:crushing_wheel\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" get quartz out of \"},{\"text\":\"Diorite\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:diorite\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" one time in four.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.33943ED8452F5D57.title": "Sticky business",
  "quest.33943ED8452F5D57.quest_subtitle": "Slime holds the whole network together.",
  "quest.33943ED8452F5D57.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Slimeball\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:slime_ball\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" between two \"},{\"text\":\"String\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:string\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" makes eight \"},{\"text\":\"Processor Binding\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:processor_binding\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", one for each raw processor.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.05ADD56B9952F082.title": "Three processors",
  "quest.05ADD56B9952F082.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Binding, silicon and redstone plus iron, gold or a diamond make a raw processor, and the furnace finishes it: \"},{\"text\":\"Basic\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:basic_processor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", \"},{\"text\":\"Improved\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:improved_processor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" or \"},{\"text\":\"Advanced Processor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:advanced_processor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Save diamonds: the controller and the drive want the last one.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.306E7CEC236531EB.title": "Build and break",
  "quest.306E7CEC236531EB.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Basic Processor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:basic_processor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" with glowstone dust is a \"},{\"text\":\"Construction Core\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:construction_core\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; with Nether Quartz, a \"},{\"text\":\"Destruction Core\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:destruction_core\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Devices that put things somewhere take the first, those that take things away the second, and grids take both.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.35C49D84762C46F4.title": "The shell",
  "quest.35C49D84762C46F4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight \"},{\"text\":\"Quartz Enriched Iron\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:quartz_enriched_iron\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" around a block of stone make a \"},{\"text\":\"Machine Casing\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:machine_casing\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": the body of the controller, the drive, the grid and most blocks after them.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.00C3E7E3AAEE0179.title": "Turn and take apart",
  "quest.00C3E7E3AAEE0179.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Quartz Enriched Iron and a \"},{\"text\":\"Basic Processor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:basic_processor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make the \"},{\"text\":\"Wrench\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:wrench\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": use it to rotate a Refined Storage block, and sneak-use it to dismantle one. Carry On won't lift them in this pack.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.10FAA64D2E954C57.title": "Copper, then cable",
  "quest.10FAA64D2E954C57.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three copper and a quartz make four \"},{\"text\":\"Quartz Enriched Copper\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:quartz_enriched_copper\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; six of it around glass and redstone give twelve \"},{\"text\":\"Cable\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:cable\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Devices also connect just by touching each other.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.427B8236C0805010.title": "A matrix for the heart",
  "quest.427B8236C0805010.quest_subtitle": "Same part, other network.",
  "quest.427B8236C0805010.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Here the \"},{\"text\":\"Controller\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:controller\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" takes a \"},{\"text\":\"Routing Matrix\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:routing_matrix\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" where one silicon used to go: two \"},{\"text\":\"Logic Processors\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:logic_processor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a PneumaticCraft circuit board, two Palis crystals and a calibration frame. The first one belongs to \"},{\"text\":\"A Shared Language\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"17BBD680007901AB\"}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2A2F996E127DE9DE.title": "Colour-coded",
  "quest.2A2F996E127DE9DE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Craft any device or cable with a dye to recolour it. A coloured cable joins only its own colour or plain grey; full blocks join every colour. Two cable colours let two networks run side by side without merging.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.32B9B66B927733C8.title": "Energy budget",
  "quest.32B9B66B927733C8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A controller holds 1,000 FE and every device draws its share each tick: a grid 10, a drive 10 plus 4 per disk, a network transmitter 32. Several controllers can power the same network.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.22CE2389278194D6.title": "Look at a Controller with no power",
  "quest.76979388CABCC684.title": "Lights out",
  "quest.76979388CABCC684.quest_subtitle": "Have you tried plugging it in?",
  "quest.76979388CABCC684.quest_desc": [
    "You met a dark controller: below 1% of its buffer it switches the whole network off. Grids go blank, disks stop answering, and everything comes back the moment FE flows in again."
  ],
  "reward.19408EEE50475B40.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.0C90134B43428CA3.title": "Power to the network",
  "quest.0C90134B43428CA3.quest_subtitle": "The heart, battery included.",
  "quest.0C90134B43428CA3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Quartz Enriched Iron, an \"},{\"text\":\"Advanced Processor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:advanced_processor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", two silicon, a casing and the matrix make the \"},{\"text\":\"Controller\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:controller\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Feed it FE: every device on the network draws from its buffer, and with the buffer empty nothing works.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5382BA302E8991CE.title": "Eight slots",
  "quest.5382BA302E8991CE.quest_subtitle": "Plug in, fill up.",
  "quest.5382BA302E8991CE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A chest, a casing, an \"},{\"text\":\"Advanced Processor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:advanced_processor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and Quartz Enriched Iron make the \"},{\"text\":\"Disk Drive\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:disk_drive\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It holds eight storage disks and lists them all as one storage.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "{image:refinedstorage:textures/block/disk_drive/front.png width:48 height:48 align:center}",
    "",
    "Each disk shows a light on the drive's face. A disk counts items, not types: fill one with a single block or a thousand kinds, it's the same space."
  ],
  "quest.7C60EA6BFACC4923.title": "1k, then 4k",
  "quest.7C60EA6BFACC4923.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A 1k storage part wrapped in glass, redstone and Quartz Enriched Iron is a \"},{\"text\":\"1k Storage Disk\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:1k_storage_disk\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": \"},{\"text\":\"1,024 items\",\"color\":\"#D8C8FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_text\",\"contents\":\"Here 1k means 1,024, not 1,000.\"}},{\"text\":\". Three 1k parts and four Basic Processors make a 4k part, and a disk crafted with a bigger part upgrades, contents and all.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5A83D25E27AC434A.title": "Improved tier",
  "quest.5A83D25E27AC434A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four \"},{\"text\":\"Improved Processors\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:improved_processor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and three parts of the tier below make each next part: a \"},{\"text\":\"16k Storage Disk\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:16k_storage_disk\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" holds 16,384 items, a \"},{\"text\":\"1024B Fluid Storage Disk\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:1024b_fluid_storage_disk\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" 1,024 buckets.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2CC45B74F48DD2DA.title": "Advanced tier",
  "quest.2CC45B74F48DD2DA.quest_subtitle": "Diamonds, well spent.",
  "quest.2CC45B74F48DD2DA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Advanced Processors\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:advanced_processor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" top the ladder: a \"},{\"text\":\"64k Storage Disk\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:64k_storage_disk\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" holds 65,536 items and a \"},{\"text\":\"4096B Fluid Storage Disk\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:4096b_fluid_storage_disk\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" 4,096 buckets. A drive full of 64k disks passes half a million items.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1390F2BE736126B0.title": "Disks without a drive",
  "quest.1390F2BE736126B0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Any storage part in a casing becomes a storage block that joins the network by itself, no drive needed, like a \"},{\"text\":\"1k Storage Block\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:1k_storage_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" or a \"},{\"text\":\"64B Fluid Storage Block\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:64b_fluid_storage_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Broken, it keeps what it holds.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.487B8630E765B3F8.title": "Nothing is wasted",
  "quest.487B8630E765B3F8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Use an empty disk while holding it and you get its storage part back; an empty storage block returns its part and its Machine Casing. Rebuilding a bigger setup costs \"},{\"text\":\"nothing\",\"color\":\"#9BE08A\"},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5F24C8E4C696A42A.title": "Chests join the network",
  "quest.5F24C8E4C696A42A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An \"},{\"text\":\"External Storage\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:external_storage\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on a chest, barrel, drawer or tank lists what's inside on the network and stores into it.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Aim it at a Functional Storage \"},{\"text\":\"Storage Controller\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"functionalstorage:storage_controller\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and every linked drawer joins at once.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3E51495A62D760CB.title": "Storage pecking order",
  "quest.3E51495A62D760CB.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Drives, storage blocks and External Storage each have a priority: resources go into the highest first and leave from it first. An allowlist filter ties items to one storage, and void excess deletes what no longer fits there.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.245716722C1DD09D.title": "Spare shells",
  "quest.245716722C1DD09D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Glass, redstone and Quartz Enriched Iron make a \"},{\"text\":\"Storage Housing\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:storage_housing\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Any storage part plus a housing is a finished disk, so a few spare housings turn loose parts into disks in one step.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1741C58E7AABC190.title": "Buckets on disk",
  "quest.1741C58E7AABC190.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Swap redstone for a bucket and the parts hold fluids: a \"},{\"text\":\"64B Fluid Storage Disk\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:64b_fluid_storage_disk\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" holds 64 buckets. Grids list fluids beside items, and a side button shows one kind only.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.25865080017091A2.title": "Chemicals too",
  "quest.25865080017091A2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The Mekanism bridge adds chemicals as a third resource: importers, exporters, External Storage, grids, storage monitors and autocrafters handle them like fluids. The chemical disks are in \"},{\"text\":\"Chemicals in Refined Storage\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"4C1E738B853DD5DB\"}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2DF0680282D23B52.title": "One search box",
  "quest.2DF0680282D23B52.quest_subtitle": "Every chest you own, in one window.",
  "quest.2DF0680282D23B52.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two Improved Processors, both cores, glass and a casing make the \"},{\"text\":\"Grid\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:grid\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": every disk, storage block and External Storage in one window, searched as you type.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.119CE532DF85C65F.title": "Search like a librarian",
  "quest.119CE532DF85C65F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"In a grid, \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.refinedstorage.focus_search_bar\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" jumps to the search box. Start with @ for a mod, # for a tag or $ for tooltip text. Side buttons sort by count, name or last change, and can show only what autocrafting can make.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.02300D001A32355C.title": "A bench on the network",
  "quest.02300D001A32355C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Grid, an Advanced Processor and a crafting table make the \"},{\"text\":\"Crafting Grid\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:crafting_grid\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": craft straight out of storage, and its 3×3 refills from the network after every craft. \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.refinedstorage.clear_crafting_grid_matrix_to_network\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" sends what's left on it back to the network.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.13DD9E12275A5772.title": "Blank patterns",
  "quest.13DD9E12275A5772.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Glass, redstone and Quartz Enriched Iron make a \"},{\"text\":\"Pattern\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:pattern\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". A written pattern is a recipe the network can repeat; sneak-use it to wipe it clean for reuse.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4DBF19D35FE33780.title": "A window on one item",
  "quest.4DBF19D35FE33780.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Storage Monitor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:storage_monitor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" shows one resource and its count. Left-click takes a stack out, right-click stores what you hold, and quick right-clicks store every one you carry.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3BF8277D84F5415B.title": "EMI does the typing",
  "quest.3BF8277D84F5415B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"In EMI, the + on a recipe fills the Crafting Grid from the network, or writes the recipe into the Pattern Grid. A grid's synchronization button can also mirror its search box into EMI's filter, one way or both.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2B7F4D2A5A49DB38.title": "Four kinds of pattern",
  "quest.2B7F4D2A5A49DB38.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The Pattern Grid writes crafting, processing, stonecutter and smithing table patterns. Fuzzy mode lets a crafting pattern take alternatives, like any planks, and processing slots accept the tags you allow.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1369D14F7AADABE3.title": "Storage to go",
  "quest.1369D14F7AADABE3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two grids and a controller in Quartz Enriched Iron make the \"},{\"text\":\"Portable Grid\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:portable_grid\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": one disk, its own 1,000 FE battery and no network at all. Open it from your inventory or sneak-place it as a block; \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.refinedstorage.open_portable_grid\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" opens it once you give that key a binding.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.51C3C2B8607DF302.title": "Look at a placed Portable Grid",
  "quest.6BDA3DB195DEC9F3.title": "Portable, but parked",
  "quest.6BDA3DB195DEC9F3.quest_subtitle": "All that portability, to leave it on the floor.",
  "quest.6BDA3DB195DEC9F3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"You set the \"},{\"text\":\"Portable Grid\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:portable_grid\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" down as a block. It still reads its one disk, and now any FE cable can charge it like a machine. Break it and it comes along again, disk and charge included.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.6A747B3F6219AE62.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.209B0A1ED546BE7E.title": "Pull it in",
  "quest.209B0A1ED546BE7E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Cable, a \"},{\"text\":\"Destruction Core\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:destruction_core\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and an Improved Processor make an \"},{\"text\":\"Importer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:importer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": it pulls from the inventory it faces into the network, filtered by an allow or block list.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4AF54AD3486EC50E.title": "Push it out",
  "quest.4AF54AD3486EC50E.quest_subtitle": "The furnace never waits for you again.",
  "quest.4AF54AD3486EC50E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Swap the destruction core for a \"},{\"text\":\"Construction Core\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:construction_core\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and you get an \"},{\"text\":\"Exporter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:exporter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": it pushes only what its filter names into the inventory it faces. An exporter over a furnace and an importer under it make a smelter that feeds itself, fuel aside.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.748DCAC5DEF7B093.title": "A counter for pipes",
  "quest.748DCAC5DEF7B093.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An Importer, an Exporter, a casing and redstone make the \"},{\"text\":\"Interface\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:interface\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": it keeps nine slots stocked with what you set, for pipes and machines to pull from, and whatever they push into it goes to the network.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7EE5A91CD3F6715E.title": "Pour a disk out",
  "quest.7EE5A91CD3F6715E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Disk Interface\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:disk_interface\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" takes six disks and moves their contents into the network, or fills them from it. Use it to empty an old disk, or to pack a chosen stock into one and carry it off.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4FFB37E757DD93E4.title": "Blank upgrades",
  "quest.4FFB37E757DD93E4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An Improved Processor in glass and Quartz Enriched Iron is a blank \"},{\"text\":\"Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Every speed, stack, regulator, range and autocrafting upgrade starts as one, and so do the enchanted ones.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7F55EF6672E13CAC.title": "Sugar rush",
  "quest.7F55EF6672E13CAC.quest_subtitle": "Four is the limit. Your dentist agrees.",
  "quest.7F55EF6672E13CAC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three sugar and Quartz Enriched Iron around an \"},{\"text\":\"Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make a \"},{\"text\":\"Speed Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:speed_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Importers, exporters, constructors, destructors, disk interfaces and autocrafters take up to four, each adding 4 FE per tick.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.539EE3BACFC773DC.title": "By the stack",
  "quest.539EE3BACFC773DC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four \"},{\"text\":\"Speed Upgrades\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:speed_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and five sugar make a \"},{\"text\":\"Stack Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:stack_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". One fits per importer, exporter, constructor or disk interface, and it moves 64 at a time instead of one.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7BAFF1A1552163BB.title": "Keep it at N",
  "quest.7BAFF1A1552163BB.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A comparator and redstone on an Upgrade make the \"},{\"text\":\"Regulator Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:regulator_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; use it to set an amount. An Exporter then only exports while the target holds less than that, an Importer only imports while it holds more.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2AD215C33B684DDF.title": "Same settings, next device",
  "quest.2AD215C33B684DDF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Sneak-use a \"},{\"text\":\"Configuration Card\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:configuration_card\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on a device to copy its settings and upgrades, then sneak-use it on another of the same kind to paste them. Sneak-use it in the air to clear it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.330E2F5809DE66F8.title": "Break into storage",
  "quest.330E2F5809DE66F8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Destructor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:destructor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" breaks the block in front of it and stores the drops, filtered by an allow or block list. In pickup mode it gathers the items lying in front of it instead.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.355D5EE6B779EF6B.title": "Place from storage",
  "quest.355D5EE6B779EF6B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Constructor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:constructor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" places the blocks its filter names, from the network into the spot in front of it. In drop mode it throws items instead, and with an autocrafting upgrade it first crafts whatever is missing.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6FF80467B51C056D.title": "Redstone by the count",
  "quest.6FF80467B51C056D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Detector\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:detector\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" watches one resource and gives a redstone signal when the network holds less than, exactly or more than the amount you set. Wire it to a farm and the farm stops once the stock is full.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.51229A032B9EDC78.title": "Gentle hands",
  "quest.51229A032B9EDC78.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An Upgrade, a Silk Touch \"},{\"text\":\"Enchanted Book\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:enchanted_book\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", two bookshelves and five Quartz Enriched Iron make the \"},{\"text\":\"Silk Touch Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:silk_touch_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". In a Destructor it breaks blocks whole, like the enchanted pickaxe.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0ECAC65D50BCCE67.title": "Lucky breaks",
  "quest.0ECAC65D50BCCE67.quest_subtitle": "Luck is just maths with a book.",
  "quest.0ECAC65D50BCCE67.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The same recipe with a Fortune book gives the upgrade of that level; the \"},{\"text\":\"Fortune III Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:fortune_3_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" needs a Fortune III book. In a Destructor it multiplies ore drops like the pickaxe enchantment.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.11CF3CA51536FEDB.title": "Endless cobble",
  "quest.11CF3CA51536FEDB.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Face a Destructor at a cobblestone generator and cobble flows in on its own. Set its redstone mode and a Detector next to it can cut it off at, say, ten thousand.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.39B92FEDAE94E47B.title": "Write it down",
  "quest.39B92FEDAE94E47B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Grid, an Advanced Processor and a Pattern make the \"},{\"text\":\"Pattern Grid\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:pattern_grid\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Lay out a recipe, press create, and a blank pattern comes out written.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1486B24C529A5BCF.title": "Hands for the crafter",
  "quest.1486B24C529A5BCF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Autocrafter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:autocrafter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" takes a \"},{\"text\":\"Handling Core\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:handling_core\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" where its casing used to go: two blank router modules, a \"},{\"text\":\"Precision Mechanism\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:precision_mechanism\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a power regulator. The first one belongs to \"},{\"text\":\"Small Hands, Large Workshops\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"6C696AA48D00D512\"}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.693470EAA0DF5046.title": "It crafts while you don't",
  "quest.693470EAA0DF5046.quest_subtitle": "Nine recipes per box.",
  "quest.693470EAA0DF5046.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Both cores, two Advanced Processors and the handling core make the \"},{\"text\":\"Autocrafter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:autocrafter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", with room for nine patterns. Crafting patterns run inside it; processing patterns go to the machine it faces. Click anything autocraftable in a grid and the network makes it, parts first.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.64046813EA62830E.title": "On demand",
  "quest.64046813EA62830E.quest_subtitle": "The chest that refills itself.",
  "quest.64046813EA62830E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A construction core and two crafting tables on an Upgrade make the \"},{\"text\":\"Autocrafting Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:autocrafting_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". In an Exporter, Interface or Constructor it crafts whatever is missing: with a Regulator Upgrade beside it, an exporter keeps any chest at the amount you set.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.199EE20D52999C18.title": "Every pattern, one screen",
  "quest.199EE20D52999C18.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two Autocrafters, two Advanced Processors and a casing make the \"},{\"text\":\"Autocrafter Manager\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:autocrafter_manager\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": every autocrafter on the network and its patterns in one screen, searchable by name, input or output.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6EEE74B2A7DA9CA6.title": "Jobs in progress",
  "quest.6EEE74B2A7DA9CA6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An \"},{\"text\":\"Autocrafting Monitor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:autocrafting_monitor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" follows every running job step by step, and tells you why one is stuck: no machine found, machine won't take it, autocrafter locked. Cancel one job or all of them from there.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.42632901D609BA0A.title": "Machines on patterns",
  "quest.42632901D609BA0A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A processing pattern lists what goes into the machine and what must come back to the network; an Importer or the machine's own output brings it home. Lock modes stop the autocrafter from flooding a slow machine.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7D94078B4C91C6D8.title": "Chained crafters",
  "quest.7D94078B4C91C6D8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"An Autocrafter facing another one joins its chain: up to eight of them feed their patterns through the head into a single machine. Speed Upgrades, up to four, make each one faster.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.27DBD6F23A8605F2.title": "Look before you craft",
  "quest.27DBD6F23A8605F2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Every request opens a preview: what's in stock, what gets crafted and what's missing, as a list or a tree. Max fills in the most you can make right now, and Notify pings you when the job is done.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2CD3875062B75B90.title": "Off the cable",
  "quest.2CD3875062B75B90.quest_subtitle": "Freedom, 16 blocks at a time.",
  "quest.2CD3875062B75B90.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An ender pearl, an Advanced Processor and a casing make the \"},{\"text\":\"Wireless Transmitter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:wireless_transmitter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": wireless items reach the network within 16 blocks of it. Several transmitters cover a wider area.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.513F06F955BF43C6.title": "A grid you carry",
  "quest.513F06F955BF43C6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Grid, an ender pearl and an Advanced Processor make the \"},{\"text\":\"Wireless Grid\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:wireless_grid\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Use it on any network device to bind it; \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.refinedstorage.open_wireless_grid\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" opens it from your inventory once you give that key a binding in Controls.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1E20DF61CA0A91F3.title": "Longer reach",
  "quest.1E20DF61CA0A91F3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three ender pearls and Quartz Enriched Iron on an Upgrade make a \"},{\"text\":\"Range Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:range_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": each adds 8 blocks, up to four per transmitter, so one covers \"},{\"text\":\"48\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\". Each also costs 8 FE per tick.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4825012E9BEB5EF9.title": "Jobs in your pocket",
  "quest.4825012E9BEB5EF9.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An Autocrafting Monitor, an ender pearl and an Advanced Processor make the \"},{\"text\":\"Wireless Autocrafting Monitor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:wireless_autocrafting_monitor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": watch and cancel jobs anywhere a transmitter reaches. \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.refinedstorage.open_wireless_autocrafting_monitor\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" opens it too, once bound.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4E12666A1E451997.title": "Creative, and still local",
  "quest.4E12666A1E451997.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"translate\":\"item.refinedstorage.creative_range_upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\"},{\"text\":\" and the other creative parts have no recipe here. Even infinite range stays in its own dimension: other worlds need a Network Transmitter.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7EA9A6C7CCDDCB81.title": "Mind the battery",
  "quest.7EA9A6C7CCDDCB81.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The Wireless Grid, the Portable Grid and the wireless monitor carry 1,000 FE each, and every open, insert or extract costs 5. Charge them like any powered tool, for example in a Mekanism Energy Cube's charge slot.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.51C6629012600BCD.title": "A card with an address",
  "quest.51C6629012600BCD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Paper, an Advanced Processor and Quartz Enriched Iron make a \"},{\"text\":\"Network Card\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:network_card\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Sneak-use it on a Network Receiver and it remembers that spot, dimension included.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.530809CCD5A0308F.title": "Look at a transmitting Network Transmitter",
  "quest.1110515AD1564BE5.title": "A network at a distance",
  "quest.1110515AD1564BE5.quest_subtitle": "Long-distance relationship, zero cables.",
  "quest.1110515AD1564BE5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Network Transmitter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:network_transmitter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" with the bound card sends the whole network to its \"},{\"text\":\"Network Receiver\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:network_receiver\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", at any distance, even in another dimension. Each end costs a netherite ingot, and the transmitter draws 32 FE per tick.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0CE58F48F1576CBE.title": "Switch a branch",
  "quest.0CE58F48F1576CBE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A casing, cable, an Advanced Processor and a redstone torch make a \"},{\"text\":\"Relay\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:relay\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": it joins two parts of a network and cuts the link on redstone. Turn pass-through off to choose what crosses: energy, storage, security or autocrafting.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.061C65230878587F.title": "Hold a Security Manager and a Security Card",
  "quest.74FB21C976711467.title": "House rules",
  "quest.74FB21C976711467.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Security Manager\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:security_manager\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" with \"},{\"text\":\"Security Cards\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:security_card\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" sets, player by player, who may open, insert, extract, build, autocraft or change security. \"},{\"text\":\"Once active it denies everything to everyone\",\"color\":\"#FF8C7A\"},{\"text\":\", so bind a card to yourself first.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.613AC5907B05185D.title": "Look at a Network Transmitter in error",
  "quest.271839B3FEE3B3FC.title": "Is anybody out there?",
  "quest.271839B3FEE3B3FC.quest_subtitle": "The far side stopped answering.",
  "quest.271839B3FEE3B3FC.quest_desc": [
    "You found a red Network Transmitter. Either its card is missing or the receiver can't be reached: broken, rebound or sitting in an unloaded chunk. Fix the far side and it goes back to transmitting on its own."
  ],
  "reward.77247A1CB3EC591A.title": "Secret found",
  "task.68EEDCE22AB5F88D.title": "Enter the Nether",
  "task.729A8175D4611BB0.title": "Look at a live Network Receiver",
  "quest.6FE81D1978F22822.title": "A branch office in the Nether",
  "quest.6FE81D1978F22822.quest_subtitle": "The commute is instant. The rent is netherite.",
  "quest.6FE81D1978F22822.quest_desc": [
    "Put a Network Receiver in the Nether, bind the card to it there and slot the card into a transmitter at home. Once the receiver lights up, grids, importers and exporters beside it run on your home network: a quartz mine that ships itself."
  ],
  "quest.2089B6F053D095EA.title": "Keep the far side loaded",
  "quest.2089B6F053D095EA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The link holds only while the receiver's chunk is loaded. Claim it with FTB Chunks and force-load it: it stays up while someone on your team is online. If it unloads, the transmitter turns red until it's back.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2184DCB320F1FED3.title": "A full drive",
  "quest.2184DCB320F1FED3.quest_subtitle": "Half a million items, one search box.",
  "quest.2184DCB320F1FED3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight \"},{\"text\":\"64k Storage Disks\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"refinedstorage:64k_storage_disk\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" fill a drive: \"},{\"text\":\"524,288 items\",\"color\":\"#56CAFF\"},{\"text\":\" behind one search box, crafted on demand and reachable from other worlds.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "{image:refinedstorage:textures/block/storage_block/64k_storage_block.png width:48 height:48 align:center}",
    "",
    "Full, the drive draws 42 FE per tick: 10 for itself and 4 per disk. The next one is a single block away."
  ],
  "quest.44949B83830DDE36.title": "Label on a drive",
  "quest.44949B83830DDE36.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Every item in Heliodor had an address: we could find one screw across three districts. Nobody thought to index the people. —T.\",\"italic\":true}]"
  ],
  "image.1C9D00EBCE46B649.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Parts and power\",\"color\":\"#56CAFF\"}]",
  "image.5EC8C300CBD5F0F2.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Disks and storage\",\"color\":\"#56CAFF\"}]",
  "image.1C753E262B2389C2.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"In and out\",\"color\":\"#56CAFF\"}]",
  "image.3A5707BA311FDE0A.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Grids\",\"color\":\"#56CAFF\"}]",
  "image.2ADAF5A4D6F79C16.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Into the world\",\"color\":\"#56CAFF\"}]",
  "image.419A56D4CF8FFAE6.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Autocrafting\",\"color\":\"#56CAFF\"}]",
  "image.34B20F7D48ADAA2F.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Wireless\",\"color\":\"#56CAFF\"}]",
  "image.7EE36FA5109DAAEC.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Across worlds\",\"color\":\"#56CAFF\"}]",
  "image.0CF6BF10954AEF10.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Refined Storage\",\"color\":\"#EAF6FF\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.5B18FA29BB30925F.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"no channels · one search box\",\"color\":\"#8FDFFF\",\"font\":\"minecraft:uniform\"}]",
  "image.701C6007754B7270.title": "Back to the Sun of Heliodor",
  "image.3D1666A731662146.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Nether\",\"color\":\"#C79BFF\"}]",
  "chapter.0209063232CEE2AE.title": "AE2 · Addons",
  "chapter.0209063232CEE2AE.chapter_subtitle": [
    "ExtendedAE, Advanced AE and MEGA Cells make the network bigger, faster and smarter; the ME Requester and the wireless terminals take it with you."
  ],
  "task.03FBF109636C6779.title": "Look at a grown Entro Cluster",
  "quest.5C68DAF813931E9C.title": "Plant a seed in fluix",
  "quest.5C68DAF813931E9C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Sand, ender dust, redstone, glowstone and sky stone dust make two \"},{\"text\":\"Entro Seeds\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"extendedae:entro_seed\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Right-click a Fluix Block with one: it becomes budding entroized fluix, which grows entro clusters the way certus does.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0F6307C6C7CC3424.title": "Crystals that wear out",
  "quest.0F6307C6C7CC3424.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Grown clusters drop \"},{\"text\":\"Entro Crystals\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"extendedae:entro_crystal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; young buds drop shards, eight to a crystal. Unlike flawless certus, every entroized block wears down to plain quartz, about ten crystals from a fully entroized one.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.55B1293957CF36D1.title": "Gold for backbone",
  "quest.55B1293957CF36D1.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Entro dust, a gold ingot and a lapis thrown in water fuse into an \"},{\"text\":\"Entro Infused Ingot\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"extendedae:entro_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". The AE2 inscriber grinds crystals into the dust.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.41A3155BDBAF9F5E.title": "The ExtendedAE frame",
  "quest.41A3155BDBAF9F5E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four entro ingots, copper, iron and quartz glass: an \"},{\"text\":\"Extended Machine Frame\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"extendedae:machine_frame\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Nearly every ExtendedAE block starts as one.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.090ED9DBA874A5D9.title": "Silicon by the stack",
  "quest.090ED9DBA874A5D9.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"One quartz dust, two coal and six sand make six \"},{\"text\":\"Quartz Blend\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"extendedae:quartz_blend\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Each smelts into four silicon, or six in an enrichment chamber: up to 36 silicon from a single dust.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.31EE3A93EA52F51E.title": "Second chances",
  "quest.31EE3A93EA52F51E.quest_subtitle": "One in twenty is a miracle.",
  "quest.31EE3A93EA52F51E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Crystal Fixer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"extendedae:crystal_fixer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" fed charged certus upgrades the budding block in front of it: damaged to chipped and chipped to flawed four times in five, flawed to \"},{\"text\":\"flawless\",\"color\":\"#9BE08A\"},{\"text\":\" one time in twenty. Every crystal is one try.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7A39924BE358AEF1.title": "Too complex for a table",
  "quest.7A39924BE358AEF1.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A frame, a crafting terminal, two logic processors and a sky stone tank: the \"},{\"text\":\"Crystal Assembler\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"extendedae:crystal_assembler\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It builds ExtendedAE's devices and runs in-world reactions, fluix included, without throwing anything in water. Its screen face takes no cable.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.62F496551155C154.title": "A fourth processor",
  "quest.62F496551155C154.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three eyes of ender, four entro crystals and a Silicon Press become an \"},{\"text\":\"Inscriber Concurrent Press\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"extendedae:concurrent_processor_press\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in the crystal assembler. Print entro with it and press as usual: \"},{\"text\":\"Concurrent Processors\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"extendedae:concurrent_processor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The recipe eats the Silicon Press: copy one first.\",\"color\":\"#FF8C7A\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1D9A38C2746E325D.title": "Thirty-six patterns",
  "quest.1D9A38C2746E325D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A pattern provider, three capacity cards, three crafting tables, a concurrent processor and six cables: the \"},{\"text\":\"ME Extended Pattern Provider\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"extendedae:ex_pattern_provider\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", with \"},{\"text\":\"36 pattern slots\",\"color\":\"#E2A3E3\"},{\"text\":\" instead of 9. A Pattern Provider Upgrade converts one already placed, patterns and all.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.17FD3A8C96B919F9.title": "Double drives",
  "quest.17FD3A8C96B919F9.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"ME Extended Drive\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"extendedae:ex_drive\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" holds 20 cells instead of 10, and the \"},{\"text\":\"ME Extended IO Port\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"extendedae:ex_io_port\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" moves cells eight times faster. Each starts from its AE2 original plus upgrades in the crystal assembler.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.74C48BE5415074BD.title": "Bottomless",
  "quest.74C48BE5415074BD.quest_desc": [
    "ExtendedAE's infinity cells hand out endless water or cobblestone and swallow as much as you send: a 16k component, quartz glass, diamonds and the buckets. Each costs 8 AE/t just sitting in a drive."
  ],
  "quest.15A5FC4FA4204A96.title": "A pocket condenser",
  "quest.15A5FC4FA4204A96.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two overflow destruction cards, a matter condenser, a 16k component, quartz glass and amethyst make the \"},{\"text\":\"ME Void Cell\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"extendedae:void_cell\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Partition it in a cell workbench: whatever matches is deleted, or pressed into matter balls and singularities as a condenser would.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2AE78D1C2D9B981F.title": "Fill it, drain it",
  "quest.2AE78D1C2D9B981F.quest_subtitle": "A bottling plant in one block.",
  "quest.2AE78D1C2D9B981F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A frame, an \"},{\"text\":\"ME Ingredient Buffer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"extendedae:ingredient_buffer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and both cores make the \"},{\"text\":\"ME Canner\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"extendedae:caner\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in the crystal assembler. It fills containers with fluids, and here with Mekanism chemicals too, through Applied Mekanistics; in empty mode it drains them. 80 AE a go.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Its pattern lists only the filling and the container. Power and cable go in through the top or the bottom.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.085841E46AF8285F.title": "Any ExtendedAE device upgrade",
  "quest.5A8D8FE5BE630608.title": "Upgrade in place",
  "quest.5A8D8FE5BE630608.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An extended device crafted with any ingot turns into an upgrade: \"},{\"text\":\"Pattern Provider Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"extendedae:pattern_provider_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", or the ones for interfaces, buses, drives, the access terminal and the wireless connector. Sneak and use it on the plain device: it turns extended, settings and contents kept.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.41E408BFD860DD24.title": "Bigger pockets",
  "quest.41E408BFD860DD24.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"ME Extended Interface\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"extendedae:ex_interface\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" has more stocking slots. The \"},{\"text\":\"ME Oversize Interface\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"extendedae:oversize_interface\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" holds sixteen stacks' worth in each slot, 1024 items, for providers that push huge batches.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.57076F7961A3C5A8.title": "Eight at once",
  "quest.57076F7961A3C5A8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four molecular assemblers and four \"},{\"text\":\"concurrent processors\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"62F496551155C154\"}},{\"text\":\" make an \"},{\"text\":\"Extended Molecular Assembler\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"extendedae:ex_molecular_assembler\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": eight jobs at a time with enough co-processors, twice as fast, but only from a pattern provider.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2532A52AED357D7E.title": "The assembler hall",
  "quest.2532A52AED357D7E.quest_subtitle": "A factory that fits in a room.",
  "quest.2532A52AED357D7E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A solid box: \"},{\"text\":\"Assembler Matrix Frame\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"extendedae:assembler_matrix_frame\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on the edges, walls or glass on the faces, cores filling the inside. Each pattern core holds 36 patterns, each craft core runs 8 jobs, and five speed cores reach full speed.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"It needs a pattern core and a craft core inside, so the smallest working hall is 4×3×3.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.639042130B45E06B.title": "Eight times the traffic",
  "quest.639042130B45E06B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"ME Extended Import Bus\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"extendedae:ex_import_bus_part\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and its export twin move eight times what AE2's buses do and take more cards. A bus upgrade swaps one already placed without losing its filter.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.269292DAF4B3FC91.title": "Picky buses",
  "quest.269292DAF4B3FC91.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"ME Tag Storage Bus\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"extendedae:tag_storage_bus\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" filters by tags like c:ingots/*, a mod bus by mod ID. A \"},{\"text\":\"ME Precise Export Bus\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"extendedae:precise_export_bus\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" sends exact amounts, and only if they fit; a threshold bus exports only above or below a set stock.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7CBA4584BFF8E45D.title": "Export by the family",
  "quest.7CBA4584BFF8E45D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"ME Tag Export Bus\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"extendedae:tag_export_bus\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" sends out whatever matches a tag rule, written as for the tag storage bus, and the \"},{\"text\":\"ME Mod Export Bus\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"extendedae:mod_export_bus\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" everything from the mods you list. One bus set to c:raw_materials/* feeds a smelter every raw ore there is.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.79FA1DBAE939DB1C.title": "Planes without a subnet",
  "quest.79FA1DBAE939DB1C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"ME Active Formation Plane\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"extendedae:active_formation_plane\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" places or drops what you filter, like an export bus that builds. The \"},{\"text\":\"ME Smart Annihilation Plane\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"extendedae:smart_annihilation_plane\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" breaks or picks up only what it's set to, like an import bus. Neither needs a subnet.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Each is its AE2 plane with three pistons, two cores and an extended bus, in the crystal assembler."
  ],
  "quest.12A0AD8F2A6E1F25.title": "Only this many",
  "quest.12A0AD8F2A6E1F25.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"ME Precise Storage Bus\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"extendedae:precise_storage_bus\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" takes a limit and inserts only up to it, so the chest in front of a machine never holds more than you meant. Two calculation processors around a storage bus make one.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1998F42030E0C28F.title": "A latch, not a light",
  "quest.1998F42030E0C28F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"ME Threshold Level Emitter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"extendedae:threshold_level_emitter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" has two numbers: it switches on above the upper one and stays on until the stock falls below the lower one. A farm driven by it runs in long batches instead of flickering on and off.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3F64799000F9B704.title": "Four at a time",
  "quest.3F64799000F9B704.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Extended Inscriber\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"extendedae:ex_inscriber\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" runs four inscribing jobs at once and the \"},{\"text\":\"Extended Charger\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"extendedae:ex_charger\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" charges four items. When a provider feeds the inscriber, set its stack size to one.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.756DECB49F3EE53A.title": "Slice, don't press",
  "quest.756DECB49F3EE53A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Circuit Slicer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"extendedae:circuit_cutter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" cuts storage blocks straight into prints: gold into nine logic prints, diamond into nine engineering, silicon into nine printed silicon, a certus block into four calculation.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Building it uses up a full set of presses: copy them first.\",\"color\":\"#FF8C7A\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.677182A1070AC6A2.title": "Big fish",
  "quest.677182A1070AC6A2.quest_subtitle": "Nobody asked. Here it is anyway.",
  "quest.677182A1070AC6A2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight pufferfish around nothing make a \"},{\"text\":\"Fishbig\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"extendedae:fishbig\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It does nothing. The circuit slicer turns it back into fish, if you have the heart.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.47827EC6F3BB0EBD.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.5B253F2B8A78DFF5.title": "Find the stuck one",
  "quest.5B253F2B8A78DFF5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"ExtendedAE's \"},{\"text\":\"ME Extended Pattern Access Terminal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"extendedae:ex_pattern_access_part\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" searches patterns by what goes in or comes out and highlights the provider in the world: the fastest way to find the one holding up a big job.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5A0D1C65D84B3717.title": "Tools for tidy people",
  "quest.5A0D1C65D84B3717.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Pattern Modifier\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"extendedae:pattern_modifier\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" multiplies, divides, swaps ingredients in or clones a whole stack of patterns. \"},{\"text\":\"ME Packing Tape\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"extendedae:me_packing_tape\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" boxes up a provider, interface or drive with its settings and contents for moving day.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2B6DDA03A6260F64.title": "Bulk edits",
  "quest.2B6DDA03A6260F64.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A blank pattern, an engineering processor and two blue dyes make a \"},{\"text\":\"Config Modifier\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"extendedae:config_modifier\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Click it on an interface or any device with set amounts to add, multiply, max out or clear every amount at once.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.401FD97051B632E6.title": "Quantum computer",
  "quest.401FD97051B632E6.quest_subtitle": "Every order, at once.",
  "quest.401FD97051B632E6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Quantum Computer Core\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"advanced_ae:quantum_core\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" is a crafting computer on its own: 256M of storage and 8 co-processor threads, running as many jobs at once as its storage holds. Its recipe swallows an accelerator, a unit and a 256M storage.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0E1BDAE616808553.title": "Pick the side",
  "quest.0E1BDAE616808553.quest_subtitle": "For machines with opinions about sides.",
  "quest.0E1BDAE616808553.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An \"},{\"text\":\"Advanced Pattern Provider\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"advanced_ae:small_adv_pattern_provider\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" can push each ingredient to a chosen face. Run a processing pattern through the \"},{\"text\":\"Advanced Pattern Encoder\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"advanced_ae:adv_pattern_encoder\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", pick a face per ingredient, and one block feeds a fussy machine with no pipes.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.49A196E8774DD984.title": "Pressure cooker",
  "quest.49A196E8774DD984.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Reaction Chamber\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"advanced_ae:reaction_chamber\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" runs AE2's in-world reactions in a tank, on a lot of power: 64 certus charge at once, 16 sets of fluix ingredients give 64 crystals, and 64 matter balls with lava make a singularity.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.68782DEC239C573B.title": "Break the unbreakable",
  "quest.68782DEC239C573B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"In the chamber, a singularity with two ender dust, two sky stone dust and a little lava shatters into two \"},{\"text\":\"Shattered Singularities\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"advanced_ae:shattered_singularity\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Pressed in the inscriber, they become quantum dust.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3CBEB2AA4E0485F4.title": "Quantum alloy",
  "quest.3CBEB2AA4E0485F4.quest_subtitle": "Singularities, sold by the four.",
  "quest.3CBEB2AA4E0485F4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Quantum dust in four buckets of water becomes a bucket of quantum infusion. Four copper, four shattered singularities, four singularities and that bucket make one \"},{\"text\":\"Quantum Alloy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"advanced_ae:quantum_alloy\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Every quantum part starts here.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5F5D3066B1F29FED.title": "The quantum chip",
  "quest.5F5D3066B1F29FED.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Logic press below, Engineering press above and a shattered singularity between: the inscriber makes an \"},{\"text\":\"Inscriber Quantum Press\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"advanced_ae:quantum_processor_press\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Print alloy with it, press with redstone and printed silicon: a \"},{\"text\":\"Quantum Processor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"advanced_ae:quantum_processor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"That press eats both presses: copy them first.\",\"color\":\"#FF8C7A\"}]"
  ],
  "task.00C84D362741C698.title": "Either advanced provider upgrade",
  "quest.0A09FF77F7135589.title": "Keep the patterns",
  "quest.0A09FF77F7135589.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Used on a placed AE2 or ExtendedAE provider, an \"},{\"text\":\"Advanced Pattern Provider Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"advanced_ae:adv_pattern_provider_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" makes it advanced with the same slot count. The capacity upgrade jumps a plain provider straight to 36 slots. Patterns and cards stay where they are.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5398D0A990BF8702.title": "How fast is it filling?",
  "quest.5398D0A990BF8702.quest_subtitle": "A speedometer for storage.",
  "quest.5398D0A990BF8702.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A storage monitor and a calculation processor make an \"},{\"text\":\"ME Throughput Monitor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"advanced_ae:throughput_monitor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": one item's count and how fast it changes, no channel needed. The \"},{\"text\":\"Throughput Monitor Configurator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"advanced_ae:throughput_monitor_configurator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" switches it between per tick, per second and per minute.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.16D14DB5ABBF8B2D.title": "One bus for the chest",
  "quest.16D14DB5ABBF8B2D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"ME Import Export Bus\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"advanced_ae:import_export_bus_part\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" exports what's in its filter and imports the rest; the stock export bus keeps an exact amount in the target. Fuse both with quantum processors: the \"},{\"text\":\"ME Advanced IO Bus\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"advanced_ae:advanced_io_bus_part\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", eight times faster.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.79AE6322C80A6B72.title": "Wear the network",
  "quest.79AE6322C80A6B72.quest_subtitle": "Netherite, but it has a network.",
  "quest.79AE6322C80A6B72.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Here each quantum armor piece takes a netherite piece, quantum processors, alloy plates, a quantum storage component and a \"},{\"text\":\"Logistics Luminosity\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:luminosity_logistics\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" from Solsticio, in act VI. Link it in an access point; \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.advanced_ae.quantum_armor_config\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" opens its upgrades.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.237AED38FD83E75C.title": "Build it bigger",
  "quest.237AED38FD83E75C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Wrap the core in \"},{\"text\":\"Quantum Computer Structural Glass\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"advanced_ae:quantum_structure\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", up to 7×7×7, and fill the inside: accelerators add 8 threads each, storages add memory, one data entangler multiplies storage by 4 and one multi-threader multiplies threads by 4. Plug any gap with quantum units.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5CED5C9952E61C07.title": "Craft forever",
  "quest.5CED5C9952E61C07.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Quantum Crafter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"advanced_ae:quantum_crafter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" runs crafting patterns nonstop, no order needed, keeping each ingredient above a floor and the product under a cap. It handles recipes that feed themselves, and acceleration cards reach 64 crafts a tick per pattern.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.06C849A60F4675D5.title": "Wings from the network",
  "quest.06C849A60F4675D5.quest_subtitle": "An elytra, folded into a card.",
  "quest.06C849A60F4675D5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"You made a \"},{\"text\":\"Flight Card\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"advanced_ae:flight_card\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Installed in the quantum armor it grants creative flight, speed on a slider; a drift card decides how fast you stop.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.574DED7C837D000E.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.1662C1571EF019DD.title": "One mega",
  "quest.1662C1571EF019DD.quest_subtitle": "A thousand k, give or take.",
  "quest.1662C1571EF019DD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three 256k components, an accumulation processor, sky stone dust and vibrant quartz glass make a 1M component; in a sky steel housing it becomes a \"},{\"text\":\"1M MEGA Item Storage Cell\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"megacells:item_storage_cell_1m\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". The tiers climb to 256M.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.28D2C20801AE4DD9.title": "Small MEGA things",
  "quest.28D2C20801AE4DD9.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"ME Cell Dock\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"megacells:cell_dock\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" is a flat part that holds one cell, several to a cable: a buffer for a tight subnet. The \"},{\"text\":\"Portable Cell Workbench\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"megacells:portable_cell_workbench\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" partitions cells from your hand. MEGA portable cells accept only greater energy cards.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1DF60856B095D66C.title": "Steel from the sky",
  "quest.1DF60856B095D66C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Drop a charged certus crystal, an iron ingot and a sky stone block into lava: two \"},{\"text\":\"Sky Steel Ingots\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"megacells:sky_steel_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Copper instead of iron gives sky bronze, for MEGA fluid cells.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.39DDD1DB462F3B21.title": "The MEGA processor",
  "quest.39DDD1DB462F3B21.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Engineering press below, Calculation press above and a singularity between make the \"},{\"text\":\"Inscriber Accumulation Press\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"megacells:accumulation_processor_press\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Print sky steel with it, then press with fluix dust and printed silicon: \"},{\"text\":\"Accumulation Processors\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"megacells:accumulation_processor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"That press eats both presses: copy them first.\",\"color\":\"#FF8C7A\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.406FE4042F663117.title": "Superdense",
  "quest.406FE4042F663117.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight dense energy cells around an accumulation processor: a \"},{\"text\":\"Superdense Energy Cell\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"megacells:mega_energy_cell\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", 12.8M AE. With an advanced card it becomes a \"},{\"text\":\"Greater Energy Card\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"megacells:greater_energy_card\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", the only battery MEGA portable cells take.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2DDD50A125F7AC5A.title": "Double capacity",
  "quest.2DDD50A125F7AC5A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An accumulation processor doubles a provider or an interface. The \"},{\"text\":\"MEGA Pattern Provider\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"megacells:mega_pattern_provider\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" holds 18 patterns, processing ones only, so it can't drive molecular assemblers; the MEGA Interface has twice the slots and throughput.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.14B3509B39589C97.title": "A darker, bigger CPU",
  "quest.14B3509B39589C97.quest_desc": [
    "MEGA crafting units take 1M to 256M crafting storage, and each MEGA co-processor counts as four. They look sleek in black, which is half the point."
  ],
  "quest.64563A581542B04F.title": "Up the M ladder",
  "quest.64563A581542B04F.quest_desc": [
    "Each MEGA component holds four times the last and takes three of it plus an accumulation processor: 4M, 16M, 64M, 256M. The top cell holds over a thousand times what a 256k does."
  ],
  "task.2D7A6782933F15C4.title": "Any MEGA chemical cell",
  "quest.4EE0BCE741AA3671.title": "Chemicals by the million",
  "quest.4EE0BCE741AA3671.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Charged certus, an osmium ingot and sky stone dropped in lava give sky osmium, the metal of the MEGA chemical housing. Add an M component and it becomes a \"},{\"text\":\"1M MEGA Chemical Storage Cell\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"megacells:chemical_storage_cell_1m\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for Mekanism chemicals, up to 256M.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3A360B8D8614C956.title": "Hot storage",
  "quest.3A360B8D8614C956.quest_subtitle": "Handle with tongs.",
  "quest.3A360B8D8614C956.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Chemical cells refuse anything radioactive. The \"},{\"text\":\"MEGA Radioactive Chemical Storage Cell\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"megacells:radioactive_chemical_cell\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" holds one such chemical, partitioned, up to 2048 buckets: polonium, plutonium or nuclear waste, but not spent waste. It draws 250 AE/t in a drive.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Its component takes radioactive waste barrels and a 256k component; the cell adds reactor glass, HDPE and a \"},{\"text\":\"Polonium Pellet\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:pellet_polonium\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.77B57C740D36701E.title": "One item, no limit",
  "quest.77B57C740D36701E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"MEGA Bulk Item Storage Cell\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"megacells:bulk_item_cell\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" stores a single item type in practically endless amounts, once partitioned to it. A \"},{\"text\":\"Compression Card\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"megacells:compression_card\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" folds its nuggets, ingots and blocks into one count.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.494F6D0C06B062B0.title": "Unpack on demand",
  "quest.494F6D0C06B062B0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A compressed bulk cell may show only a few ingots. A \"},{\"text\":\"MEGA Decompression Module\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"megacells:decompression_module\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" anywhere on the network writes hidden patterns that turn blocks back into ingots and nuggets, so autocrafting sees all of it.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.1D90F21A4D952705.title": "Any MEGA Source cell",
  "quest.4E68C28949FA17B6.title": "Source by the million",
  "quest.4E68C28949FA17B6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"On the enchanting apparatus, an Ars Énergistique source cell housing with three manipulation essences, two source gem blocks, three sky steel ingots and 2000 Source becomes the MEGA one. With an M component: a \"},{\"text\":\"1M MEGA Source Storage Cell\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"megacells:source_storage_cell_1m\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4A6BD678C9C562E0.title": "Every cell lit",
  "quest.4A6BD678C9C562E0.quest_subtitle": "The drive is full and humming.",
  "quest.4A6BD678C9C562E0.quest_desc": [
    "Four extended pattern providers and four 1M MEGA cells on the network a quantum computer runs: 144 pattern slots, room for millions of items and every order at once.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "{image:ae2:textures/block/drive/drive_front.png width:48 height:48 align:center}",
    "",
    "ExtendedAE gives the network hands, Advanced AE a mind, MEGA a memory. Requesters and wireless terminals keep you out of the base while the base keeps working."
  ],
  "quest.4CF3951459326881.title": "Every order, one list",
  "quest.4CF3951459326881.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"ME Requester Terminal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"merequester:requester_terminal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" edits every requester on the network from one screen; rename them in an anvil to group them. The wireless version works from the field, \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.ae2.wireless_requester_terminal\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" included.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1EE79393C2041D02.title": "Standing orders",
  "quest.1EE79393C2041D02.quest_subtitle": "The pantry that restocks itself.",
  "quest.1EE79393C2041D02.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An \"},{\"text\":\"ME Requester\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"merequester:requester\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" watches a list of items and fluids: when stock drops below your amount, it orders a batch from autocrafting. Each row has its amount and batch size, and a status bar that says what it's waiting for.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7170B24DC402C8AD.title": "See the channels",
  "quest.7170B24DC402C8AD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Click any part of a network with the \"},{\"text\":\"ME Network Analyzer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2netanalyser:network_analyser\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": every device and link shows up in the world, coloured by capacity, with the channel count on each link. Offline devices stand out in red.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.286E35060397F0CB.title": "One terminal, every screen",
  "quest.286E35060397F0CB.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An engineering processor turns the wireless crafting terminal into a pattern encoding one. Combine AE2WTLib terminals in a crafting grid: the \"},{\"text\":\"Wireless Universal Terminal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2wtlib:wireless_universal_terminal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" cycles between them with one button and pools their batteries.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4D342AA969825067.title": "Signal everywhere",
  "quest.4D342AA969825067.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four quantum rings, a link chamber and an advanced card: the \"},{\"text\":\"Quantum Bridge Card\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2wtlib:quantum_bridge_card\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". With one entangled singularity inside, the terminal reaches the bridge holding its twin from any distance or dimension, as long as \"},{\"text\":\"that network stays loaded\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"53D836F6AAEBB9D0\"}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5509EDD87153177B.title": "Hoover",
  "quest.5509EDD87153177B.quest_subtitle": "Tidy by attraction.",
  "quest.5509EDD87153177B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Magnet Card\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2wtlib:magnet_card\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in the wireless crafting terminal picks up items from 16 blocks away and, if you like, sends them straight to the network. Pickup and insert filters are separate; \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.ae2.ae2wtlib_magnet\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" toggles it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3088BE356FF8F068.title": "Inventory on autopilot",
  "quest.3088BE356FF8F068.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"In a wireless terminal, an \"},{\"text\":\"Import Card\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2importexportcard:import_card\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" sends the inventory slots you tick to the network, and an \"},{\"text\":\"Export Card\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2importexportcard:export_card\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" keeps chosen slots filled from it. Fuzzy, acceleration and crafting cards tune them.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3E117BE8A918172A.title": "Patterns on the go",
  "quest.3E117BE8A918172A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A receiver, a pattern access terminal and a dense energy cell make the \"},{\"text\":\"Wireless Pattern Access Terminal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2wtlib:wireless_pattern_access_terminal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": every provider's patterns from anywhere in range. ExtendedAE builds a wireless version of its extended access terminal the same way.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1CCD5D611FDDE16C.title": "Wireless, the short way",
  "quest.1CCD5D611FDDE16C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two \"},{\"text\":\"ME Wireless Connectors\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"extendedae:wireless_connect\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" paired with the setup kit join two networks like a quantum bridge, no entangled pair needed, up to 1000 blocks apart in one dimension. A hub links eight; energy cards trim the power bill.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3C2A76AB6C29324A.title": "Addon chips",
  "quest.3C2A76AB6C29324A.quest_subtitle": "Eight and eight, every day.",
  "quest.3C2A76AB6C29324A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight \"},{\"text\":\"Concurrent Processors\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"extendedae:concurrent_processor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and eight \"},{\"text\":\"Accumulation Processors\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"megacells:accumulation_processor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for the common store, once a day. The circuit slicer cuts an entro block into four concurrent prints and a sky steel block into nine accumulation prints.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.338317E643750F94.title": "Nothing thrown away",
  "quest.338317E643750F94.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Heliodor never threw anything away; we built bigger cells. When the light went out the drives were still full and humming, keeping a city nobody came back for. —T.\",\"italic\":true}]"
  ],
  "image.0C595DF14E1FEEEC.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"ExtendedAE · entro\",\"color\":\"#E2A3E3\"}]",
  "image.3054341CB587A4FF.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"ExtendedAE · devices\",\"color\":\"#E2A3E3\"}]",
  "image.3E82B6F2A8E9749E.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"ExtendedAE · buses and planes\",\"color\":\"#E2A3E3\"}]",
  "image.22628C186BFCF1E9.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"ExtendedAE · assembly\",\"color\":\"#E2A3E3\"}]",
  "image.29EBD313657EB527.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Advanced AE · quantum line\",\"color\":\"#E2A3E3\"}]",
  "image.30E304F121A35BEB.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Advanced AE · computer\",\"color\":\"#E2A3E3\"}]",
  "image.3BC1610DB32B031A.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"MEGA Cells · processor\",\"color\":\"#E2A3E3\"}]",
  "image.2219E23C2143FA05.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"MEGA Cells · cells\",\"color\":\"#E2A3E3\"}]",
  "image.713AE863650655F4.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Requests and analysis\",\"color\":\"#E2A3E3\"}]",
  "image.27EF918B4DFA327A.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Wireless terminals\",\"color\":\"#E2A3E3\"}]",
  "image.6E33298DB7399DEA.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"AE2 · Addons\",\"color\":\"#F6EEFF\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.5C9361FF59A5BA90.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"ten cells, one drive\",\"color\":\"#E2A3E3\",\"font\":\"minecraft:uniform\"}]",
  "image.62BD4F8EE6FA6366.title": "Back to AE2 · Automation",
  "chapter.0808DAF1804471FC.title": "Draconic Evolution · Draconium and Wyvern",
  "chapter.0808DAF1804471FC.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Draconium, fusion crafting, dislocators and wireless energy; then the wyvern tier, its modular gear and the Energy Core."
  ],
  "quest.4EB8C042E050A063.title": "Draconium",
  "quest.4EB8C042E050A063.quest_subtitle": "Deep, purple and worth the dig.",
  "quest.4EB8C042E050A063.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Draconium Ore\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"draconicevolution:overworld_draconium_ore\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" hides between Y -64 and -48, in about one chunk of ten. The Nether has rarer, bigger veins at Y 4 to 16; the End, three small veins per chunk in end stone. Each ore drops 2 to 4 \"},{\"text\":\"Draconium Dust\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"draconicevolution:draconium_dust\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", more with Fortune.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Skip Silk Touch: a smelted ore block gives one ingot, while its 2 to 4 dust smelt into 2 to 4.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.299B603EE41120B4.title": "Draconium Ingots",
  "quest.299B603EE41120B4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Dust or ore smelts into \"},{\"text\":\"Draconium Ingots\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"draconicevolution:draconium_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in any furnace, one per item. Nine ingots pack into a \"},{\"text\":\"Draconium Block\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"draconicevolution:draconium_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", and nine nuggets into an ingot.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6FAF1D5F3B08ABED.title": "Draconium Core",
  "quest.6FAF1D5F3B08ABED.quest_subtitle": "Every machine's purple heart.",
  "quest.6FAF1D5F3B08ABED.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four draconium ingots at the corners, four gold ingots at the sides and a diamond in the middle. Nearly every block of the mod has one inside, from the \"},{\"text\":\"Fusion Crafting Core\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"draconicevolution:crafting_core\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" to the Generator, so make several.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.41FBB0214C9BD641.title": "Fusion Crafting Core",
  "quest.41FBB0214C9BD641.quest_subtitle": "A crafting table that needs a runway.",
  "quest.41FBB0214C9BD641.quest_desc": [
    "Four lapis blocks, four diamonds and a draconium core. The catalyst goes in the core; every other ingredient sits in its own injector, facing the core from 2 to 16 blocks away. When the screen reads Ready to craft, press Craft: it charges, then fuses.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Every fusion recipe has a tier and an energy cost; the core's screen and the recipe viewer show both."
  ],
  "quest.6278042A667B5A83.title": "Fusion injectors",
  "quest.6278042A667B5A83.quest_desc": [
    "Two diamonds, a draconium core, an iron block and five stone. One injector holds one ingredient, so a recipe with eight ingredients needs eight injectors, all facing the core."
  ],
  "quest.38319050D58B029A.title": "Draconium Chest",
  "quest.38319050D58B029A.quest_subtitle": "260 slots and a furnace that never sleeps.",
  "quest.38319050D58B029A.quest_desc": [
    "The first fusion: a chest as catalyst, then five furnaces, two crafting tables, two draconium cores and a draconium block, for 2,000,000 OP. You get 260 slots, a crafting grid, a capacitor slot and a five-slot furnace that runs on OP.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "The furnace can smelt everything smeltable, only what it is already smelting, or keep one item so that filter sticks. Shulker boxes, bags, pouches and strongboxes are refused."
  ],
  "quest.360F22819A833356.title": "Wyvern Energy Controller",
  "quest.360F22819A833356.quest_desc": [
    "Four draconium ingots, four redstone blocks and a draconium core. Despite the name it needs no Wyvern Core: energy crystals, the Mob Grinder and every wyvern tool start here, and the Energy Core takes two."
  ],
  "quest.7C622A55EE0714E6.title": "Wyvern Core",
  "quest.7C622A55EE0714E6.quest_subtitle": "A nether star in a purple coat.",
  "quest.7C622A55EE0714E6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four draconium ingots, three draconium cores, a nether star and, in this pack, an \"},{\"text\":\"Atomic Alloy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:alloy_atomic\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" from act V in place of the fourth core. Wyvern injectors, the Energy Core and the Celestial Manipulator each need one.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3908A85F2275DB46.title": "Wyvern injectors",
  "quest.3908A85F2275DB46.quest_desc": [
    "Fuse a draconium injector with a Wyvern Core, two draconium cores, four diamonds and a draconium block, for 32,000 OP. Wyvern recipes want an injector of that tier or better under every ingredient: six for a tool, seven to awaken draconium."
  ],
  "quest.1D1B95FB6A450FED.title": "Slowest injector sets the pace",
  "quest.1D1B95FB6A450FED.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Charging and fusing take 300, 220, 140 or 60 ticks with draconium, wyvern, draconic or chaotic injectors, and the lowest tier in use decides. For automation, switch injectors to single-item mode.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3739ACC5156DB6D2.title": "Power goes to the injectors",
  "quest.3739ACC5156DB6D2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The core itself takes no energy: a craft's cost is split evenly across the injectors in use, and each needs its share piped or beamed in. A 2,000,000 OP recipe with ten ingredients asks 200,000 of each injector.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5D1F8676AE15787F.title": "Energy Core",
  "quest.5D1F8676AE15787F.quest_subtitle": "A battery you build around.",
  "quest.5D1F8676AE15787F.quest_desc": [
    "Six draconium ingots, two wyvern energy controllers and a Wyvern Core. Alone it holds 45.5 million OP; shells of draconium and redstone blocks around it raise the tier, up to 2.14 trillion OP at tier 7. It will not wake up without stabilizers."
  ],
  "quest.1C6E350905F716BD.title": "Core stabilizers",
  "quest.1C6E350905F716BD.quest_desc": [
    "Four diamonds around a particle generator. Set four in a cross around the core, all in one plane and in line with it, no more than 16 blocks out; the core's screen checks the layout before it activates."
  ],
  "quest.369C5D3CB91ACA41.title": "Energy Pylons",
  "quest.369C5D3CB91ACA41.quest_subtitle": "Glass hat, big job.",
  "quest.369C5D3CB91ACA41.quest_desc": [
    "A pylon moves OP in and out of an active core within 18 blocks. Put any glass block on its top or bottom: it turns into the pylon's sphere, and stained glass tints it. Click the sphere to switch between input and output.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Sneak-click the pylon to pick another core in range; a comparator beside it reads how full the core is.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.045F40DC45EBA538.title": "Tier 2 core",
  "quest.045F40DC45EBA538.quest_desc": [
    "Six draconium blocks, one on each face of the core: 273 million OP. Raise the tier on the core's screen first; its build guide shows where every block goes."
  ],
  "quest.690B141F0BB53B9B.title": "Tier 3 core",
  "quest.690B141F0BB53B9B.quest_subtitle": "Cubism, but load-bearing.",
  "quest.690B141F0BB53B9B.quest_desc": [
    "A full shell of 26 draconium blocks closes the core in a 3×3×3 cube: 1.64 billion OP."
  ],
  "quest.457378AE7DFE01DB.title": "Tier 4 core",
  "quest.457378AE7DFE01DB.quest_desc": [
    "Redstone moves inside: 26 redstone blocks around the core, wrapped in 54 draconium blocks. 9.88 billion OP."
  ],
  "quest.152F15AA4CDA3A77.title": "Tier 5 core",
  "quest.152F15AA4CDA3A77.quest_desc": [
    "90 draconium and 80 redstone blocks hold 59.3 billion OP. From this tier on each of the four stabilizers becomes an advanced one: a flat 3×3 square of nine, facing the core."
  ],
  "quest.347BC91FA72703B0.title": "Tier 6 core",
  "quest.347BC91FA72703B0.quest_desc": [
    "150 draconium and 178 redstone blocks: 356 billion OP."
  ],
  "quest.4CEE7970AB4B5311.title": "Tier 7 core",
  "quest.4CEE7970AB4B5311.quest_subtitle": "Two trillion. Don't spend it all at once.",
  "quest.4CEE7970AB4B5311.quest_desc": [
    "210 draconium and 328 redstone blocks: 2.14 trillion OP, the largest core that still has a number on it. Tier 8 wants awakened draconium."
  ],
  "quest.36695713834AC30E.title": "Let the core build itself",
  "quest.36695713834AC30E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"With the blocks in your inventory, Assemble Core on the core's screen places the whole structure for you. Toggle Build Guide draws it in the world first.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2F8D25D890467F1F.title": "Wireless Energy Link",
  "quest.2F8D25D890467F1F.quest_desc": [
    "A module that feeds your gear straight from an active Energy Core: sneak-click the core with it to link them. Switching it on costs 4 million OP and staying on 51 to 512 OP/t; it moves up to 2,048 OP/t, only within the core's dimension."
  ],
  "quest.368A87DE8F18AFCB.title": "Draconic in this pack",
  "quest.368A87DE8F18AFCB.quest_desc": [
    "Draconium, fusion crafting and the draconium-tier machines are native. Three recipes wait on the Atlas: the Dislocator takes a reinforced alloy (act III), the Wyvern and Draconic Cores an atomic alloy (act V). The Creative Capacitor is made with Luminosities in act VI."
  ],
  "quest.4E43ABD196122DD3.title": "Draconium from a farm",
  "quest.4E43ABD196122DD3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Mystical Agriculture grows draconium too: its tier 5 draconium seeds give essence, and eight essences craft one ingot. See \"},{\"text\":\"Platinum, iridium and draconium\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"2833DB15EE38A8A5\"}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6277BB1EA49AD09F.title": "Draconium Blocks",
  "quest.6277BB1EA49AD09F.quest_desc": [
    "Keep a stack of these: the Draconium Chest and every wyvern injector take one, four of them are the catalyst that awakens draconium, and Energy Core shells eat them by the hundred."
  ],
  "quest.4452A916DD598AAF.title": "Draconium for the common store",
  "quest.4452A916DD598AAF.quest_subtitle": "Purple is the new iron.",
  "quest.4452A916DD598AAF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Thirty-two \"},{\"text\":\"Draconium Ingots\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"draconicevolution:draconium_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for the common store, once a day. Drop the dust in a Draconium Chest and its furnace smelts it on OP while you mine.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.5B1AFA613B32BD88.title": "Look at a placed item",
  "quest.46B71AD9BFA1C0F3.title": "Put it down",
  "quest.46B71AD9BFA1C0F3.quest_subtitle": "Museum of things you were holding.",
  "quest.46B71AD9BFA1C0F3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"You set an item on the ground with \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.draconicevolution.place_item\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\". It stays there as a display block, a trophy shelf with no shelf.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.07B92ECCD0565020.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.624AC266DD69B3EF.title": "Dislocator",
  "quest.624AC266DD69B3EF.quest_subtitle": "Home is a sneak-click away.",
  "quest.624AC266DD69B3EF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Blaze powder, draconium dust, an ender eye and, in this pack, a \"},{\"text\":\"Reinforced Alloy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:alloy_reinforced\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" from act III. Sneak-click to store your position, facing and dimension; click to jump back. Hit a mob with it to send the mob there instead.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Each jump wears it down, and its tooltip counts the uses left."
  ],
  "quest.3C4C06D81A2A0DE4.title": "Bound Dislocators",
  "quest.3C4C06D81A2A0DE4.quest_desc": [
    "Two dislocators, a draconium core and a ghast tear make an unbound pair: right click to split it into two linked dislocators. Each takes you to wherever its twin is, even in another player's inventory."
  ],
  "quest.5CDBF87B8A53F84F.title": "Player Dislocator",
  "quest.5CDBF87B8A53F84F.quest_desc": [
    "One dislocator, a draconium core and a ghast tear. Right click to bind it to yourself and hand it to a teammate: using it brings them to you, as long as you are online."
  ],
  "quest.60A22B2D626E2F40.title": "Item Dislocator",
  "quest.60A22B2D626E2F40.quest_subtitle": "A magnet with a doctorate.",
  "quest.60A22B2D626E2F40.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Built around a dislocator with redstone, draconium and iron, it pulls drops within 8 blocks to you. \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.draconicevolution.toggle_magnet\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" switches it on and off.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.54FC5A43AEF102F7.title": "Normalization Field Projector",
  "quest.54FC5A43AEF102F7.quest_desc": [
    "Six iron ingots, two iron bars and an item dislocator. Items dropped within 5 blocks of it ignore item dislocators: set one beside farms and machines that spit their output onto the floor."
  ],
  "quest.2B0EBB5CB8D7C41A.title": "Dislocator portals",
  "quest.2B0EBB5CB8D7C41A.quest_desc": [
    "Put one half of a bound pair in a Dislocator Receptacle set in a frame of Draconium Infused Obsidian, then give it a redstone signal: the frame fills with a portal to the other half. A frame can span up to 256 by 256.",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Click the receptacle with infused obsidian to hide it in the frame.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.22820E1A1808C706.title": "Dislocator Pedestal",
  "quest.22820E1A1808C706.quest_subtitle": "Next stop: wherever you saved.",
  "quest.22820E1A1808C706.quest_desc": [
    "A pressure plate, stone, two slabs and blaze powder. Set a dislocator on it and anyone who clicks the pedestal goes where it points: a bus stop for the whole team."
  ],
  "quest.6ECBE13B33353C78.title": "Advanced Dislocator",
  "quest.6ECBE13B33353C78.quest_subtitle": "Teleport, blink, repeat.",
  "quest.6ECBE13B33353C78.quest_desc": [
    "The dislocator fused with ender pearls, draconium and a Wyvern Core. It keeps a named list of places and burns ender pearls as fuel, up to 1,024: one pearl is one teleport or four blinks of up to 32 blocks where you look.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"It has its own keys: \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.draconicevolution.dislocator_teleport\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" teleports, \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.draconicevolution.dislocator_blink\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" blinks, and \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.draconicevolution.dislocator_up\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" and \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.draconicevolution.dislocator_down\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" move through the list.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.410E749CBE021D8F.title": "Mob Grinder",
  "quest.410E749CBE021D8F.quest_subtitle": "Customer service, with swords.",
  "quest.410E749CBE021D8F.quest_desc": [
    "Iron, draconium, two diamond swords, a skull and a wyvern energy controller. It kills mobs in an adjustable area for 80 OP per point of health, can gather their drops into a neighbouring inventory, stores their experience and swings a weapon you give it."
  ],
  "quest.52FF4E101C5D8D6A.title": "Disenchanter",
  "quest.52FF4E101C5D8D6A.quest_desc": [
    "Emeralds, enchanted books, bookshelves, an enchanting table and a draconium core. It lifts one enchantment off an item onto a book, for the level cost shown on its screen."
  ],
  "quest.4148B15B912B7F05.title": "Detectors and sensors",
  "quest.4148B15B912B7F05.quest_desc": [
    "An Entity Detector puts out redstone by how many mobs it sees, up to 16 blocks away, as a steady signal or a pulse per scan; the advanced one reaches 64 blocks and filters what it counts. The Rain Sensor turns on when it rains."
  ],
  "quest.76A2210E3079BEAE.title": "Stabilized Mob Spawner",
  "quest.76A2210E3079BEAE.quest_subtitle": "Adopt a spawner.",
  "quest.76A2210E3079BEAE.quest_desc": [
    "Click a dungeon spawner with a draconium core and it pops out as a Stabilized Mob Spawner for that mob. It spawns 4 at a time with a player near; a wyvern, draconic or chaotic core clicked on it raises the tier.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Wyvern tier spawns 6 and needs no player, draconic 8 and ignores light, chaotic 12 every 25 to 100 ticks. A mob soul or spawn egg changes the mob, and redstone switches it off."
  ],
  "quest.3A406FA50C7C7ADF.title": "Celestial Manipulator",
  "quest.3A406FA50C7C7ADF.quest_subtitle": "Weather, on request.",
  "quest.3A406FA50C7C7ADF.quest_desc": [
    "A Wyvern Core, a dragon egg, a clock, redstone blocks, draconium and iron. For OP it skips to sunrise, noon, sunset, moonrise or midnight, and starts rain or storms or clears the sky. The dragon drops a new egg every time here."
  ],
  "quest.10106938A37E49D1.title": "Particle Generator",
  "quest.10106938A37E49D1.quest_desc": [
    "Redstone blocks, blaze rods and a draconium core. It is a crafting part, not a machine: every core stabilizer and wyvern shield controller takes one, and every wireless crystal two."
  ],
  "quest.3BB338A92B22481C.title": "Generator",
  "quest.3BB338A92B22481C.quest_subtitle": "Five gears, one furnace.",
  "quest.3BB338A92B22481C.quest_desc": [
    "Nether bricks, iron, a furnace and a draconium core make a furnace-fuel generator with five modes: Eco Plus gives 5 OP/t, Eco 20, Normal 40, Performance 80 and Overdrive 300. The slower modes squeeze more out of each piece of fuel."
  ],
  "quest.76C66BEE122035C1.title": "One in a thousand",
  "quest.76C66BEE122035C1.quest_subtitle": "It was looking at you.",
  "quest.76C66BEE122035C1.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A mob dropped its \"},{\"text\":\"Soul\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"draconicevolution:mob_soul\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". With the Reaper enchantment every kill has a one-in-a-thousand chance, better at higher levels and for animals; a soul sets a stabilized spawner to its mob.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.1FC4EF9F5249AB42.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.44330FBEB7C072BC.title": "Energy crystals",
  "quest.44330FBEB7C072BC.quest_subtitle": "Cables are so last act.",
  "quest.44330FBEB7C072BC.quest_desc": [
    "Four diamonds around a wyvern energy controller make four relay crystals, and a relay splits into two I/O crystals. I/O crystals take OP from the block they sit on or give it to it; relays pass it along, up to 8 links each within 32 blocks.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"With the Crystal Binder, sneak-click the first device, then click the second. Links never cross dimensions.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.11A1B95C4B288E81.title": "Wireless crystals",
  "quest.11A1B95C4B288E81.quest_desc": [
    "A relay crystal with ender pearls, ender eyes and two particle generators. It feeds up to 16 machines at 32,000 OP/t each with no crystal on them: sneak-click it with the binder, then click each machine."
  ],
  "quest.115C28EEF4E18E04.title": "Wyvern crystals",
  "quest.115C28EEF4E18E04.quest_desc": [
    "Four basic relays, four wyvern energy controllers and a draconium core make four wyvern relays. Wyvern crystals reach 64 blocks and buffer 16 million OP; relays take 16 links and wireless ones feed 32 machines at 128,000 OP/t."
  ],
  "quest.5D8D55BE51520F91.title": "Energy Transfuser",
  "quest.5D8D55BE51520F91.quest_desc": [
    "Draconium, three draconium cores, a core stabilizer and an enchanting table. Its four slots each charge an item, drain one or buffer, and it balances input between them or fills them left to right."
  ],
  "quest.1812E6F0EAE3F887.title": "Flux and Fluid Gates",
  "quest.1812E6F0EAE3F887.quest_desc": [
    "A potentiometer, a comparator, iron and a draconium core, with redstone blocks for energy or buckets for fluids. Each gate lets through a flow set between two values, picked by the redstone signal it gets."
  ],
  "quest.6469CE9F02D289C5.title": "OP is FE, just bigger",
  "quest.6469CE9F02D289C5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Draconic counts Operational Potential, OP, and every OP storage is also an FE storage: cables and generators from any mod plug straight in. OP only lets the numbers grow past two billion.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6FC734E34DCB6224.title": "Wyvern tools",
  "quest.6FC734E34DCB6224.quest_subtitle": "Modular means empty on day one.",
  "quest.6FC734E34DCB6224.quest_desc": [
    "Fuse a diamond tool with a draconium core, two draconium ingots, two basic relay crystals and a wyvern energy controller, for 8 million OP. They dig at speed 15 but store no energy of their own: fill their 4×4 module grid first.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Enchant the diamond tool before the fusion: enchantments carry over, and so do modules and charge at every later upgrade.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3FAC5D94A9389FDE.title": "Wyvern weapons",
  "quest.3FAC5D94A9389FDE.quest_desc": [
    "The sword and bow fuse like the tools, from a diamond sword and a plain bow. Each sword hit costs 1,024 OP per point of damage and its Attack Radius sweeps a 100-degree arc; each shot costs 1,024 OP per point of its damage, and the bow still uses arrows."
  ],
  "quest.4B4841985E8F8C47.title": "Projectile modules",
  "quest.4B4841985E8F8C47.quest_desc": [
    "Velocity, accuracy, damage, penetration and gravity compensation each start from a module core, two draconium cores and arrows. The Auto Fire module looses the arrow the moment the bow is fully drawn."
  ],
  "quest.596EBD6A3A451C55.title": "Wyvern Chestpiece",
  "quest.596EBD6A3A451C55.quest_subtitle": "Armor with a spreadsheet inside.",
  "quest.596EBD6A3A451C55.quest_desc": [
    "Fused from a diamond chestplate like the tools. Its 6×5 grid takes the armor modules: shields, flight, undying, speed, jump and more. Like every modular item, it needs energy modules to work."
  ],
  "quest.56592C9F369893F4.title": "Wyvern Capacitor",
  "quest.56592C9F369893F4.quest_subtitle": "The battery pack you forget you carry.",
  "quest.56592C9F369893F4.quest_desc": [
    "A Wyvern Core as catalyst with four wyvern energy controllers and four draconium ingots, 8 million OP. It charges your armor, held items, hotbar, inventory and curios, each switchable, from the energy modules in its 4×4 grid."
  ],
  "quest.25EAC6BC8B22C4D5.title": "Two keys for modular gear",
  "quest.25EAC6BC8B22C4D5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.draconicevolution.tool_modules\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" opens the module grid of what you hold or wear; \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.draconicevolution.tool_config\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" opens its settings: dig speed, area, shield, flight and every other property.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7E68D268279ACFB7.title": "AOE Safe Mode",
  "quest.7E68D268279ACFB7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Area tools have an AOE Safe Mode: switched on, a swing that would reach a block entity breaks nothing at all. Leave it on around your base.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.36CE8B537891F02B.title": "Curios slots",
  "quest.36CE8B537891F02B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Modular chestpieces fit the Curios body slot, which leaves your chestplate slot free; capacitors, item dislocators and the advanced dislocator fit curio slots.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0B9157E507C9C4F2.title": "Module Core",
  "quest.0B9157E507C9C4F2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four iron, two gold, two redstone and a draconium ingot. Every draconium and wyvern module starts from one. A module fits any modular item of its tier or above, in the grid \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.draconicevolution.tool_modules\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" opens.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.247DF2B44D50E82D.title": "Draconium modules",
  "quest.247DF2B44D50E82D.quest_desc": [
    "The basic set: energy (1 million OP), speed (+10%), damage (+2), area (3×3), jump (+25%) and auto feed (40 hunger points). Iron, gold, redstone, glowstone and potions do most of the work."
  ],
  "quest.00A8EDA141CBB5FA.title": "Wyvern modules",
  "quest.00A8EDA141CBB5FA.quest_desc": [
    "Each folds one or two draconium modules of the same kind into more: 4 million OP, +25% speed, +4 damage, a 5×5 area, +75% jump and 150 hunger points. The area module also wants a Wyvern Core."
  ],
  "quest.1188EA7F609D3521.title": "Selective Incineration",
  "quest.1188EA7F609D3521.quest_subtitle": "Cobblestone goes to a better place.",
  "quest.1188EA7F609D3521.quest_desc": [
    "A lava bucket and redstone in a module. Set its filter slots, by item or by tag like c:stone, and the tool destroys matching drops before they reach your inventory."
  ],
  "quest.597D96ABF4987CEE.title": "Ender Collection",
  "quest.597D96ABF4987CEE.quest_desc": [
    "Drops from your tool go straight to your ender chest instead of your inventory, for 32 OP an item. Sneak-click an Ender Storage chest with the module to send them there instead."
  ],
  "quest.69BD16A1BDC592B5.title": "Tree Harvester",
  "quest.69BD16A1BDC592B5.quest_subtitle": "Lumberjacking, the lazy way.",
  "quest.69BD16A1BDC592B5.quest_desc": [
    "Two diamond axes, two draconium cores and a module core. Hold right click on a tree to fell it whole, with 16 blocks of reach at 5 blocks per second; hold it in the middle of a grove to clear the area."
  ],
  "quest.45F134B49E15D9E3.title": "Presets on a key",
  "quest.45F134B49E15D9E3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"In the equipment config screen you can group properties into presets and bind each to a key, even one that works with the screen closed.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0583F603465CFA25.title": "Wyvern flight",
  "quest.0583F603465CFA25.quest_subtitle": "Elytra without the rockets.",
  "quest.0583F603465CFA25.quest_desc": [
    "An elytra, a firework rocket, two draconium cores and a module core. At wyvern tier it grants elytra flight only, at 1,024 OP per tick; hold Forward and Sprint in the air for a boost. Creative flight waits for the draconic tier."
  ],
  "quest.4620906548036F36.title": "Shields",
  "quest.4620906548036F36.quest_subtitle": "Health points, but purple.",
  "quest.4620906548036F36.quest_desc": [
    "The shield controller runs the shield, and it takes a Dragon Heart. Capacity modules add 25 points each, recovery modules speed up the recharge, and the controller sets the cooldown: 20 seconds at wyvern tier.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "A shield draws its points squared times 0.0005 OP per tick just to stay up, and 8,192 OP for each point it recharges."
  ],
  "quest.08058AF486EA64DE.title": "Undying",
  "quest.08058AF486EA64DE.quest_subtitle": "A totem that reloads.",
  "quest.08058AF486EA64DE.quest_desc": [
    "A totem of undying in a module. When a hit would kill you it heals 6 health, adds 25 shield points for 15 seconds and grants a moment of invulnerability, then recharges over 2 minutes with 5 million OP."
  ],
  "quest.48E4BDD4C3F0053F.title": "Mining anywhere",
  "quest.48E4BDD4C3F0053F.quest_desc": [
    "Two chestpiece modules against the vanilla slowdowns: the Mining Stabilizer digs at full speed while you fly or float, Aqua Adept at full speed underwater. Sneak to switch Aqua Adept off for a moment."
  ],
  "quest.0CA0C19F37F1945C.title": "Night vision and hill step",
  "quest.0CA0C19F37F1945C.quest_desc": [
    "Night Vision turns on below a light level you choose and drains 20 OP per tick while active. Hill Step walks you up full blocks; hold sneak to turn it off for a moment."
  ],
  "quest.3E099A4E1C49A182.title": "The shield HUD",
  "quest.3E099A4E1C49A182.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The shield HUD shows your shield, energy and undying charge on screen; its settings pick armor energy, capacitor energy or both, as numbers, at any scale.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.4B69597ACA16A3DB.title": "Defeat the Ender Dragon",
  "quest.1530700DF8E3E846.title": "The dragon's heart",
  "quest.1530700DF8E3E846.quest_subtitle": "Organ donor, reluctantly.",
  "quest.1530700DF8E3E846.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Every time the Ender Dragon dies, a \"},{\"text\":\"Dragon Heart\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"draconicevolution:dragon_heart\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" floats above the exit portal and never despawns, and the dragon also drops 57 to 70 draconium dust. Here a new egg appears after every kill, not only the first.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Respawn the dragon with four end crystals on the portal whenever you need another heart."
  ],
  "quest.06697A24187FAC62.title": "More than one job for a heart",
  "quest.06697A24187FAC62.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A heart awakens four draconium blocks, sits in every wyvern shield controller, and two go into the Creative Capacitor. Count them before you stop respawning the dragon.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.16774DB33CC0D7FB.title": "Egg, again",
  "quest.16774DB33CC0D7FB.quest_subtitle": "The dragon has a very full nest.",
  "quest.16774DB33CC0D7FB.quest_desc": [
    "Two dragon eggs in one inventory. Draconic makes the egg return after every kill, and the Celestial Manipulator and the chaotic injectors are glad of it."
  ],
  "reward.4B5B450657B6C22E.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.41B48E165E08F982.title": "Awakened Draconium",
  "quest.41B48E165E08F982.quest_subtitle": "Fifty million OP to wake up a block.",
  "quest.41B48E165E08F982.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four draconium blocks as catalyst, six draconium cores and the Dragon Heart on wyvern injectors: 50 million OP for four \"},{\"text\":\"Awakened Draconium Blocks\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"draconicevolution:awakened_draconium_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Everything draconic starts with them.\"}]"
  ],
  "image.5C6F98132FB2CC15.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Dislocators\",\"color\":\"#FF9D3B\"}]",
  "image.73A6C8E61439CFDA.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Machines\",\"color\":\"#FF9D3B\"}]",
  "image.4FBCE85C4FD5E8B8.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Wireless energy\",\"color\":\"#FF9D3B\"}]",
  "image.56A810938B41EB61.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Modules\",\"color\":\"#FF9D3B\"}]",
  "image.11029942F789F163.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Chestpiece modules\",\"color\":\"#FF9D3B\"}]",
  "image.10E415185E06929A.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Draconic Evolution\\nDraconium and Wyvern\",\"color\":\"#FFF1DC\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.6BF3191C66F26A16.title": "Back to the Sun of Heliodor",
  "image.5A674D028264792F.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» Draconic and Chaotic\",\"color\":\"#FF9D3B\"}]",
  "image.112C5AB09CD47F24.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"mine  fuse  store  fly\",\"color\":\"#B9A7E0\",\"font\":\"minecraft:alt\"}]",
  "image.2AA071B9DB08389A.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"45.5M\",\"color\":\"#FF9D3B\"}]",
  "image.7AE1961798CC2560.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"fusion\",\"color\":\"#C9B8F0\"}]",
  "image.2F902F7145EDA123.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"273M\",\"color\":\"#C9B8F0\"}]",
  "image.3D48041A7ECC0B9C.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"1.64B\",\"color\":\"#C9B8F0\"}]",
  "image.67C064D704720BB6.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"9.88B\",\"color\":\"#C9B8F0\"}]",
  "image.5938E7F60FB990BB.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"59.3B\",\"color\":\"#C9B8F0\"}]",
  "image.509266FC641EA4A6.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"356B\",\"color\":\"#C9B8F0\"}]",
  "image.60881D6AA70AC9CB.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"2.14T\",\"color\":\"#C9B8F0\"}]",
  "chapter.47DB1CC102DAD5C0.title": "Just Dire Things · Machines and Time",
  "chapter.47DB1CC102DAD5C0.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Breakers, placers and clickers in two tiers, coal and fuel generators, portals, and the time crystals that feed the Time Wand and the Paradox Machine."
  ],
  "quest.6A34D999CCB88294.title": "Simple Block Breaker",
  "quest.6A34D999CCB88294.quest_subtitle": "Mining, minus the miner.",
  "quest.6A34D999CCB88294.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four Ferricore, a \"},{\"text\":\"Diamond\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:diamond\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", two Lapis, an \"},{\"text\":\"Observer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:observer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a Redstone. It needs no power: give it a pickaxe or shovel and it breaks the block it faces with it, wearing the tool as you would. Speed and redstone mode are in its screen.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.72C672CE8CFD9554.title": "Simple Block Placer",
  "quest.72C672CE8CFD9554.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The breaker's recipe with a \"},{\"text\":\"Dispenser\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:dispenser\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in the middle. It places the block in its slot into the space in front; the direction button sets which way it faces, handy for torches.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6E2F7442D8632D66.title": "Simple Clicker",
  "quest.6E2F7442D8632D66.quest_subtitle": "The bot that presses buttons for you.",
  "quest.6E2F7442D8632D66.quest_desc": [
    "An Eye of Ender and a Dispenser in the breaker's frame. It clicks with the item in its slot: right, left or held for a set number of ticks, sneaking or not, at blocks, air, hostile or passive mobs, adults, children or players."
  ],
  "quest.360C206EE7C6A0D5.title": "Simple Sensor",
  "quest.360C206EE7C6A0D5.quest_desc": [
    "An Eye of Ender and an Observer in the frame. It sends a strong or weak redstone signal when what's in front matches its filter: a block, air, a kind of mob, a player, or items lying on the ground."
  ],
  "quest.55DD4FF09383E307.title": "Simple Dropper",
  "quest.55DD4FF09383E307.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two Redstone and a \"},{\"text\":\"Dropper\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:dropper\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in the frame. It drops its items in the direction you pick, from one at a time to a whole stack, with a pickup delay you set: zero means they can be grabbed at once.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7E4FCA08EF3A912A.title": "Simple Fluid Placer",
  "quest.7E4FCA08EF3A912A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Bucket\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a Dropper in the frame. Load it with buckets or a Fluid Canister; with 1,000 mB inside and nothing in front, it places a source block.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.30F89EB3F0378D63.title": "Simple Fluid Collector",
  "quest.30F89EB3F0378D63.quest_desc": [
    "A Bucket and a Dispenser in the frame. It picks up the fluid source in front into its tank, one fluid kind at a time, and fills buckets or canisters put in its slot."
  ],
  "quest.3168476F6DD668E2.title": "Simple Swapper",
  "quest.3168476F6DD668E2.quest_subtitle": "Teleport, but for scenery.",
  "quest.3168476F6DD668E2.quest_desc": [
    "Four Blazegold, an Eye of Ender, two Lapis, an Observer and a Redstone. Link two with the Ferricore Wrench and they trade the blocks in front of them, chests with contents included, or the entities there, even across dimensions."
  ],
  "quest.025801C5908EBD90.title": "Ferricore Wrench",
  "quest.025801C5908EBD90.quest_desc": [
    "Four Ferricore Ingots. It rotates blocks and links Swappers: right-click the first, then the second, and a message confirms the pair."
  ],
  "quest.70DD4EB190444582.title": "Machine Settings Copier",
  "quest.70DD4EB190444582.quest_subtitle": "Configure once, click everywhere.",
  "quest.70DD4EB190444582.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Primal Coal, a \"},{\"text\":\"Paper\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:paper\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a Ferricore. \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.sneak\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" and right-click a machine to copy its settings, right-click another to paste them; click the air to pick which ones travel: area, filters, offset, redstone.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4C5BFCC25ADFE7A9.title": "Item Collector",
  "quest.4C5BFCC25ADFE7A9.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Diamond, two \"},{\"text\":\"Hoppers\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:hopper\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", an Ender Pearl and three Ferricore. No power needed: it vacuums up the items lying in its area, up to five blocks each way, into the inventory it's placed against, filters included.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3D03BDCDC9D0108C.title": "Speed and pulses",
  "quest.3D03BDCDC9D0108C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A machine acts once every 20 ticks by default; the Speed button goes down to every tick, which costs server time. Redstone can be ignored, required low or high, or set to Pulse: one action per pulse.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.25E733A510A100BD.title": "Goo on autopilot",
  "quest.25E733A510A100BD.quest_subtitle": "Three machines and a blob.",
  "quest.25E733A510A100BD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Around a goo: a Block Placer feeds it iron blocks, a Block Breaker with a pickaxe mines the raw ore, and a Clicker holding its food right-clicks it awake whenever it dozes off.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.15B0A7051FEC41B4.title": "Just Dire Things in this pack",
  "quest.15B0A7051FEC41B4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Five recipes wait on the Atlas: both Portal Guns take a \"},{\"text\":\"Reinforced Alloy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:alloy_reinforced\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (act III), the Flight upgrade a \"},{\"text\":\"Horizon Chart\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:horizon_chart\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (act IV), the Time Wand and the Paradox Machine an \"},{\"text\":\"Atomic Alloy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:alloy_atomic\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (act V).\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Each act material takes the place of one ingredient, a Blazegold, an End Crystal or a Time Crystal. Everything else in the mod is untouched."
  ],
  "quest.534FBB18F0E57992.title": "Advanced Block Breaker",
  "quest.534FBB18F0E57992.quest_subtitle": "Now with an area of effect.",
  "quest.534FBB18F0E57992.quest_desc": [
    "Four Celestigem, three Eyes of Ender, a Redstone and the simple breaker make its advanced form: every block in an area up to 11×11×11, 500 FE each, with filters by block or by the item it drops. The direction button aims hammer tools."
  ],
  "quest.78C36B0045D04DB4.title": "Advanced Block Placer",
  "quest.78C36B0045D04DB4.quest_desc": [
    "Same upgrade recipe around the simple placer. It fills its area, 500 FE a block, and its filter says which blocks it may place on: filter stone with direction down and it only covers the tops of stone."
  ],
  "quest.73625A4D993CC913.title": "Advanced Clicker",
  "quest.73625A4D993CC913.quest_subtitle": "Your farmhand never sleeps.",
  "quest.73625A4D993CC913.quest_desc": [
    "It clicks every match in its area for 250 FE a click, with block and entity filters. Set to left-click hostiles with a sword it's a mob farm; right-clicking adults with wheat, a breeder."
  ],
  "quest.160D4A13E93FA5F7.title": "Advanced Sensor",
  "quest.160D4A13E93FA5F7.quest_desc": [
    "It counts matches in its area and compares them: greater than, less than or equal to a number you set. «Fewer than ten adult cows» can switch on a clicker that feeds them. It spends 2 FE per block it scans."
  ],
  "quest.426BAE3D9F3A6715.title": "Advanced Dropper",
  "quest.426BAE3D9F3A6715.quest_desc": [
    "It holds a 3×3 grid and drops in the order its filter lists, cobblestone then redstone, waiting if one runs out. It moves where it drops with an offset instead of a radius, for 25 FE a drop."
  ],
  "quest.245139A46259D8A5.title": "Advanced Fluid Placer",
  "quest.245139A46259D8A5.quest_desc": [
    "It places fluid across an area for 500 FE a block, and like the advanced placer its filter picks the blocks it may place on."
  ],
  "quest.18E80D13D66E25FA.title": "Advanced Fluid Collector",
  "quest.18E80D13D66E25FA.quest_subtitle": "Lakes are just big buckets.",
  "quest.18E80D13D66E25FA.quest_desc": [
    "It drinks every source in its area for 500 FE each; a filled bucket in a filter slot limits it to that fluid."
  ],
  "quest.79797CC222BC0242.title": "Advanced Swapper",
  "quest.79797CC222BC0242.quest_subtitle": "Moving day, in one tick.",
  "quest.79797CC222BC0242.quest_desc": [
    "Four Eclipse Alloy around the simple swapper. Linked pairs share one radius, so a whole house, contents and all, can trade places with an empty field; 50 FE a block. Entity filters narrow it down to, say, babies or blue sheep."
  ],
  "quest.30AD539C61D7C859.title": "Area and filters",
  "quest.30AD539C61D7C859.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Turn on Render Area before touching RAD and OFF: RAD grows the box up to five blocks each way, OFF moves its center up to nine. Filters take items, buckets, spawn eggs or a Creature Catcher, as an allow or a deny list, with NBT if you need a blue sheep.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0371F41FEBE1DD9F.title": "Read a block's state",
  "quest.0371F41FEBE1DD9F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Right-click a sensor's filter slot with a block in it to pick block states: detect whether a door is open, a lever is on or a crop is ripe.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2C3AB0D2EAD2E915.title": "Creature Catcher",
  "quest.2C3AB0D2EAD2E915.quest_subtitle": "Gotta catch 'em all. One at a time.",
  "quest.2C3AB0D2EAD2E915.quest_desc": [
    "Four Blazegold around an Ender Pearl. Throw it at a mob to catch it, throw it again to let it out. It holds any ordinary mob, not the Ender Dragon, and doubles as an entity filter in advanced machines."
  ],
  "quest.709AED657C035839.title": "Ghast in a jar",
  "quest.709AED657C035839.quest_subtitle": "It trusted you. Mostly.",
  "quest.709AED657C035839.quest_desc": [
    "You brought a ghast home to the Overworld and then betrayed it. A Creature Catcher makes the trip a lot less stressful, for you."
  ],
  "reward.0782B61A0C0DD615.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.6DA306F2EF01A023.title": "Primal Coal",
  "quest.6DA306F2EF01A023.quest_subtitle": "Coal, but it did the reading.",
  "quest.6DA306F2EF01A023.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Block of Coal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:coal_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" or a charcoal block next to an awake Primogel Goo turns into Raw Primal Coal in two minutes; mined, it drops three or four \"},{\"text\":\"Primal Coal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"justdirethings:coal_t1\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Each burns 4,800 ticks, three times a coal.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.30B3BB63E89B266B.title": "Charcoal Block",
  "quest.30B3BB63E89B266B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Nine \"},{\"text\":\"Charcoal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:charcoal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make a charcoal block; in this pack Almost Unified hands out Mekanism's \"},{\"text\":\"Block of Charcoal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:block_charcoal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". The Primogel Goo takes any block tagged as charcoal, so a tree farm becomes a Primal Coal farm.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7538A530292C2C5C.title": "Blaze Ember",
  "quest.7538A530292C2C5C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A block of Primal Coal next to a Blazebloom Goo becomes Raw Blaze Ember in a minute, three or four \"},{\"text\":\"Blaze Ember\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"justdirethings:coal_t2\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" mined. Each burns 14,400 ticks.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.031F2B6A7D076539.title": "Voidflame Coal",
  "quest.031F2B6A7D076539.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A block of Blaze Ember next to a VoidShimmer Goo becomes Raw Voidflame Coal in 48 seconds. Each \"},{\"text\":\"Voidflame Coal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"justdirethings:coal_t3\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" burns 43,200 ticks.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7276769D1634170C.title": "Eclipse Ember",
  "quest.7276769D1634170C.quest_subtitle": "Eighty-one coals in one.",
  "quest.7276769D1634170C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A block of Voidflame Coal next to a Shadowpulse Goo becomes Raw Eclipse Ember in 24 seconds. \"},{\"text\":\"Eclipse Ember\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"justdirethings:coal_t4\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" burns 129,600 ticks, the densest fuel in the mod.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2491EF53E6ED64AE.title": "Simple Coal Generator",
  "quest.2491EF53E6ED64AE.quest_subtitle": "The first watt is the hardest.",
  "quest.2491EF53E6ED64AE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four Ferricore, two Redstone, two Coal and a \"},{\"text\":\"Blast Furnace\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:blast_furnace\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It burns any furnace fuel at 60 FE/t, pushes power into the blocks around it and holds 1,000,000 FE; the JDT coals burn two to sixteen times faster in it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1EFBEC9555478138.title": "Hotter, not longer",
  "quest.1EFBEC9555478138.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"In the Coal Generator, Primal Coal gives 120 FE/t, Blaze Ember 240, Voidflame 480 and Eclipse Ember 960. Each tier triples the energy per piece, but the goo only returns three or four for nine: climb the ladder for power per tick, not for total energy.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1A198DFAC0298714.title": "Fuel Canister",
  "quest.1A198DFAC0298714.quest_subtitle": "A fuel tank that never wastes a lump.",
  "quest.1A198DFAC0298714.quest_desc": [
    "Four Ferricore around a Coal. Load fuel through its screen and it stores the burn time, up to 10,000,000 ticks, averaging the JDT coal multipliers; no lava and no way to take it back. In a furnace it spends only 200 ticks per item, so one ore no longer eats a whole coal."
  ],
  "quest.286E9DD3A04004DF.title": "Energy Transmitter",
  "quest.286E9DD3A04004DF.quest_subtitle": "Wireless, with a toll.",
  "quest.286E9DD3A04004DF.quest_desc": [
    "A Celestigem, two Redstone, an Ender Pearl and three Blazegold. Wired to a generator, it beams up to 1,000 FE/t to every machine in its area, losing 1% per block of distance; transmitters in range of each other balance for free."
  ],
  "quest.749010CCF4F9F3BC.title": "Primal Coal for the common store",
  "quest.749010CCF4F9F3BC.quest_subtitle": "Keep the home fires burning.",
  "quest.749010CCF4F9F3BC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Thirty-two \"},{\"text\":\"Primal Coal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"justdirethings:coal_t1\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" a day. Furnaces, generators and pocket generators on the server all run hotter on it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5CA0446ED94B38A0.title": "Polymorphic Fluid",
  "quest.5CA0446ED94B38A0.quest_subtitle": "Water, but open-minded.",
  "quest.5CA0446ED94B38A0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Blazegold Ingot and a Nether Wart, shapeless, make four \"},{\"text\":\"Polymorphic Catalysts\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"justdirethings:polymorphic_catalyst\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Toss one into a water source and it becomes \"},{\"text\":\"Polymorphic Fluid\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"justdirethings:polymorphic_fluid_bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", the base of every other JDT fluid.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7ADC2732447495A1.title": "Blaze Ember Fuel",
  "quest.7ADC2732447495A1.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Drop a Blaze Ember into Polymorphic Fluid for Unrefined Blaze Ember Fuel, then leave it next to a Blazebloom Goo or higher: a minute later it is \"},{\"text\":\"Blaze Ember Fuel\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"justdirethings:refined_t2_fluid_bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", worth 450,000 FE a bucket in the Fuel Generator.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.693848977EF93CED.title": "Voidflame Fuel",
  "quest.693848977EF93CED.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Voidflame Coal dropped into refined Blaze Ember Fuel makes the unrefined kind; a VoidShimmer Goo or higher refines it into \"},{\"text\":\"Voidflame Fuel\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"justdirethings:refined_t3_fluid_bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", 1,300 FE per mB.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.122D345169F0AA5E.title": "Eclipse Ember Fuel",
  "quest.122D345169F0AA5E.quest_subtitle": "The top shelf.",
  "quest.122D345169F0AA5E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eclipse Ember into refined Voidflame Fuel, then a Shadowpulse Goo: \"},{\"text\":\"Eclipse Ember Fuel\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"justdirethings:refined_t4_fluid_bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" runs the generator at 4,000 FE/t, four million FE a bucket.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5E691CBFC66B1E73.title": "Simple Fuel Generator",
  "quest.5E691CBFC66B1E73.quest_desc": [
    "Four Blazegold, two Redstone, two Buckets and a Blast Furnace. It drinks 1 mB of refined fuel a tick and turns it into its FE per mB, 450, 1,300 or 4,000 a tick, into a 5,000,000 FE buffer."
  ],
  "quest.1DC2CDB95D4733A4.title": "Refine before you burn",
  "quest.1DC2CDB95D4733A4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A Blaze Ember burns for 216,000 FE in the Coal Generator; dropped into Polymorphic Fluid and refined, the same ember is a bucket worth 450,000 FE. The first refinery pays for itself.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7DE44328939DA928.title": "Fluid Canister",
  "quest.7DE44328939DA928.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four Ferricore around a \"},{\"text\":\"Glass\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:glass\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" block: a bucket that holds 8,000 mB. \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.sneak\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" and right-click to set its auto-fill: off, Just Dire Things items only, or every fluid holder you carry.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4C55646122C1DEC9.title": "Polymorphic Wand",
  "quest.4C55646122C1DEC9.quest_subtitle": "Pig in, surprise out.",
  "quest.4C55646122C1DEC9.quest_desc": [
    "A Fluid Canister, a Polymorphic Catalyst and a Blazegold. Fill it from a Polymorphic Fluid source, then use it on a mob within four blocks: for 100 mB a hostile turns into another random hostile, a passive one into another passive."
  ],
  "quest.37236326D0F7C0C7.title": "Advanced Polymorphic Wand",
  "quest.37236326D0F7C0C7.quest_subtitle": "Sheep in, sheep out. By choice.",
  "quest.37236326D0F7C0C7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An Eclipse Alloy and a Celestigem on the wand. \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.sneak\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" and right-click a mob to save its kind, then Targeted Polymorph turns any mob into it for 250 mB and 50,000 FE; not the Wither, the Warden or the dragon.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.75C696C42634E1FD.title": "Experience Holder",
  "quest.75C696C42634E1FD.quest_subtitle": "A piggy bank for enchanters.",
  "quest.75C696C42634E1FD.quest_desc": [
    "An Emerald, two Books, an Ender Pearl and three Blazegold. Bank your levels with its buttons, let it soak up orbs in its area, and it keeps everything when broken. It is a tank too: 20 mB of XP Fluid per experience point."
  ],
  "quest.7D8E3C5F2388EA70.title": "XP Fluid",
  "quest.7D8E3C5F2388EA70.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Take a bucket of \"},{\"text\":\"XP Fluid\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"justdirethings:xp_fluid_bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" out of the holder. This pack registers it with Create: Enchantment Industry at the same 20 mB per point, so it feeds \"},{\"text\":\"its machines\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"50EABAD3AA74115B\"}},{\"text\":\" too.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7043B03FABC435F6.title": "Always level 30",
  "quest.7043B03FABC435F6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Set the holder's target level to 30 and its redstone to always: each time you enchant nearby, it tops you back up to exactly 30. Owner Only keeps it from feeding anyone else.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.057E6F65BF4275B0.title": "Inventory Holder",
  "quest.057E6F65BF4275B0.quest_subtitle": "Outfit change, one click.",
  "quest.057E6F65BF4275B0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four Blazegold around an \"},{\"text\":\"Armor Stand\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:armor_stand\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": a stand with a full player inventory, armor and off hand included. Save per-slot filters, then Swap Items trades your whole inventory with its layout in one click.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2357289316AED1EB.title": "Player Accessor",
  "quest.2357289316AED1EB.quest_subtitle": "Your pockets, now with plumbing.",
  "quest.2357289316AED1EB.quest_desc": [
    "Four Blazegold, an Eye of Ender, two Ender Pearls, a Dispenser and a Lapis. It hands your inventory to pipes and hoppers while you're online, wherever you are; each face can reach the main slots, the armor or the off hand."
  ],
  "quest.7C8D885F7153DA80.title": "Portal Gun",
  "quest.7C8D885F7153DA80.quest_subtitle": "Now you're thinking with portals.",
  "quest.7C8D885F7153DA80.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"In this pack it takes a \"},{\"text\":\"Reinforced Alloy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:alloy_reinforced\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (act III), three Blazegold and an Eye of Ender. Left-click fires a blue portal, right-click an orange one; players and items walk through. 1,000 FE a shot; \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.sneak\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" and right-click closes yours.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.19FBEBBB581E102B.title": "Portal Fluid Catalyst",
  "quest.19FBEBBB581E102B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four \"},{\"text\":\"Chorus Fruit\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:chorus_fruit\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" around a Lapis. Toss it into Polymorphic Fluid in the End and you get Unstable Portal Fluid; anywhere else it boils away the moment it forms.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.74F85D1A10809975.title": "Portal Fluid",
  "quest.74F85D1A10809975.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Put a VoidShimmer Goo or higher next to the unstable fluid, still in the End: in 24 seconds it settles into \"},{\"text\":\"Portal Fluid\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"justdirethings:portal_fluid_bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", which keeps anywhere.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.66173EC9CFA5816A.title": "Advanced Portal Gun",
  "quest.66173EC9CFA5816A.quest_subtitle": "Home is one click away.",
  "quest.66173EC9CFA5816A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Celestigem, a Reinforced Alloy (act III), the catalyst, a Fluid Canister and three Blazegold. Save up to twelve spots in its favorites wheel, opened with \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"justdirethings.key.toggle_tool\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\", then fire: a portal pair opens between you and the chosen spot.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7C5BEAF96133402D.title": "Five seconds",
  "quest.7C5BEAF96133402D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Advanced portals close after five seconds, so step through. Fill the gun from a Portal Fluid source; a jump costs a quarter mB per block, 100 mB at most, and 100 mB to another dimension. Fire while sneaking to go back to where you last fired from.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6E093861D1A4B0FE.title": "Handle with care",
  "quest.6E093861D1A4B0FE.quest_subtitle": "Do not shake.",
  "quest.6E093861D1A4B0FE.quest_desc": [
    "You scooped a bucket of Unstable Portal Fluid. Pour it anywhere outside the End and it's gone in a puff of dragon's breath."
  ],
  "reward.6C366AE5E8985596.title": "Secret found",
  "task.28B207F32EE93F81.title": "Overworld charge (blue)",
  "task.65A8877273E3BCEE.title": "Nether charge (orange)",
  "task.4BC0DE024273CCB6.title": "End charge (green)",
  "quest.730E2B8E451FDB7C.title": "Budding Time Crystal",
  "quest.730E2B8E451FDB7C.quest_subtitle": "It needs a holiday in three dimensions.",
  "quest.730E2B8E451FDB7C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Put a Shadowpulse Goo against a \"},{\"text\":\"Budding Amethyst\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:budding_amethyst\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in its geode: 24 seconds later it's a \"},{\"text\":\"Budding Time Crystal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"justdirethings:time_crystal_budding_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It must soak up time in the Overworld, then the Nether, then the End, changing color at each step. Look at it after each one.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3E6D0D1E871BA257.title": "Move it, don't mine it",
  "quest.3E6D0D1E871BA257.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The budding block shatters when mined, Silk Touch or not. Swap it through dimensions with a pair of linked Swappers, and once buds grow, use an Advanced Swapper with a radius so they travel with it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.730A505CE9A6F44A.title": "Time Crystals",
  "quest.730A505CE9A6F44A.quest_subtitle": "Patience, crystallized.",
  "quest.730A505CE9A6F44A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Fully charged, the block grows buds on its faces: small, medium, large, cluster. Only the full cluster drops a \"},{\"text\":\"Time Crystal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"justdirethings:time_crystal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; break a bud early and you get nothing. Each growth has a 5% chance of draining the block back to the start.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3CA0D818C52D7C74.title": "A clock in a rock",
  "quest.3CA0D818C52D7C74.quest_subtitle": "Time well wasted.",
  "quest.3CA0D818C52D7C74.quest_desc": [
    "You took a whole Time Crystal Cluster with Silk Touch. It makes a fine clock for a shelf, and it still gives its one crystal if you break it the normal way later."
  ],
  "reward.017993208A336FB4.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.183BA8E6B5BCCD80.title": "Time Crystal Block",
  "quest.183BA8E6B5BCCD80.quest_desc": [
    "Nine Time Crystals make a block. A Shadowpulse Goo turns it into a fresh Budding Time Crystal, so you never need another amethyst geode; the Paradox Machine takes one too."
  ],
  "quest.7E3C72D8F8E556FE.title": "Timey wimey",
  "quest.7E3C72D8F8E556FE.quest_desc": [
    "Carrying Time Crystals now and then gives you five seconds of Slowness VI or Speed VI, at random. The Time Protection upgrade on an Eclipse Alloy chestplate stops it."
  ],
  "quest.2718EF320FB935A1.title": "Time Fluid",
  "quest.2718EF320FB935A1.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Toss a Time Crystal into a \"},{\"text\":\"Polymorphic Fluid\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"5CA0446ED94B38A0\"}},{\"text\":\" source and it becomes \"},{\"text\":\"Time Fluid\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"justdirethings:time_fluid_bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", nearly transparent. Every time-bending tool and machine runs on it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7E14F225C1D98074.title": "Time Wand",
  "quest.7E14F225C1D98074.quest_subtitle": "Fast-forward for furnaces.",
  "quest.7E14F225C1D98074.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Here it takes an \"},{\"text\":\"Atomic Alloy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:alloy_atomic\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (act V), a Time Crystal, two Ferricore and a Blazegold. Fill it from a Time Fluid source, then right-click any ticking block: twice as fast for 30 seconds, doubling each click up to 256×, for 100 FE and half a mB per unit of speed.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6B7FBBEA308106C7.title": "Hand the wand to a clicker",
  "quest.6B7FBBEA308106C7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Fake players may use the Time Wand here, and advanced machines charge the FE items in their slots. An Advanced Clicker right-clicking a furnace with the wand keeps it sped up; just keep the Time Fluid topped up.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7A52BC6A10427B4A.title": "Paradox Machine",
  "quest.7A52BC6A10427B4A.quest_subtitle": "Undo, for a price.",
  "quest.7A52BC6A10427B4A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four Eclipse Alloy, an \"},{\"text\":\"Atomic Alloy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:alloy_atomic\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (act V), two Time Crystals, a Time Crystal Block and a Time Fluid bucket. Snapshot an area up to 11×11×11: its ore blocks and mobs. Mine or kill them, then run it, and it pulls them back from a parallel timeline.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Each restored block or mob costs 250,000 FE and 50 mB of Time Fluid; it holds 10,000,000 FE and 16,000 mB. Its screen tracks the Paradox Energy each run adds."
  ],
  "quest.79DE68D4DD0FD17C.title": "The Paradox",
  "quest.79DE68D4DD0FD17C.quest_desc": [
    "Every restoration adds a quarter point of Paradox Energy; at 100, four hundred restorations, a Paradox opens. It grows a block of radius a minute up to 12, faster as it feeds, and swallows blocks, items and mobs for good.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Toss a Time Crystal into its center\",\"color\":\"#FF8C7A\"},{\"text\":\" and it collapses. Bedrock, unbreakable blocks and players are safe; your base is not.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2170597F696D55A4.title": "Ore insurance",
  "quest.2170597F696D55A4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The goo's raw ore blocks count as ores to the machine. Snapshot a Raw Eclipse Alloy Ore, mine it, restore it, repeat: an ore farm paid in FE and Time Fluid.\"}]"
  ],
  "image.2F9BCC4CCD64E9A9.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Simple machines · no power\",\"color\":\"#7BEA4F\"}]",
  "image.46A064602009EE91.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Advanced machines · FE\",\"color\":\"#7BEA4F\"}]",
  "image.164C6481D0C77F21.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Coal and power\",\"color\":\"#7BEA4F\"}]",
  "image.05A01EC769AE2697.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Polymorphic fluid and fuel\",\"color\":\"#7BEA4F\"}]",
  "image.5EE4876158022FED.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Experience and inventories\",\"color\":\"#7BEA4F\"}]",
  "image.1596BA8ABE969D7F.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Portals\",\"color\":\"#7BEA4F\"}]",
  "image.6A39825C2E8D9AD2.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Time\",\"color\":\"#7BEA4F\"}]",
  "image.6C57E8986980F211.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Just Dire Things\\nMachines and Time\",\"color\":\"#EFFFE8\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.288B4877C20BA7C0.title": "Back to the Sun of Heliodor",
  "image.0165E5C02CB96A47.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"snapshot  undo  regret\",\"color\":\"#9FE88A\",\"font\":\"minecraft:alt\"}]",
  "image.4BB7B42628F71A85.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"« Goo and Gear\",\"color\":\"#7BEA4F\"}]",
  "chapter.39AA416007D5AA46.title": "Modern Industrialization · Digital",
  "chapter.39AA416007D5AA46.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Stainless steel, titanium and plastics, digital circuits and the processing unit, high pressure steam, and flight."
  ],
  "quest.351FCB2858456867.title": "Vacuum Freezer",
  "quest.351FCB2858456867.quest_subtitle": "Enslaved winter.",
  "quest.351FCB2858456867.quest_desc": [
    "Three large pumps, three electronic circuits, an advanced hull and two aluminum large plates. It cools the hot ingots the blast furnace starts to make from here on, and with an air intake inside, never used up, it turns air into liquid air."
  ],
  "quest.1DF240EEB7B6E217.title": "Chromium",
  "quest.1DF240EEB7B6E217.quest_desc": [
    "Ten redstone in the centrifuge give a ruby dust; six ruby dusts give a chromium crushed dust. It dissolves in 9,000 mB of hydrochloric acid, and each bucket of that solution electrolyzes into three chromium tiny dusts, giving back hydrogen and chlorine."
  ],
  "quest.7F2DB374F68A2C30.title": "Manganese",
  "quest.7F2DB374F68A2C30.quest_desc": [
    "Six raw iron in the centrifuge give eight iron dusts and a manganese crushed dust. Sulfuric acid dissolves it into 9,000 mB of solution; each bucket electrolyzes into three manganese tiny dusts and 900 mB of the acid back."
  ],
  "quest.611AB3FB81F103D7.title": "Stainless Steel",
  "quest.611AB3FB81F103D7.quest_subtitle": "Invar with slot locking.",
  "quest.611AB3FB81F103D7.quest_desc": [
    "Six iron dusts, a chromium, a nickel and a manganese dust make nine stainless steel dust in the Mixer. The blast furnace turns each into a hot ingot at 32 EU/t, and the Vacuum Freezer cools it in 12.5 seconds.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Iron and nickel also match invar in the Mixer: lock an output slot to stainless steel dust.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.061D077F052293CD.title": "Kanthal Coils",
  "quest.061D077F052293CD.quest_subtitle": "Electric better furnace.",
  "quest.061D077F052293CD.quest_desc": [
    "Stainless steel, chromium and aluminum dust mix into kanthal; its cables ring into coils like cupronickel. Swap the blast furnace's sixteen coils for these and it takes recipes up to 128 EU/t: titanium, platinum and annealed copper need it."
  ],
  "quest.185D3CB6FB138BEF.title": "Monazite",
  "quest.185D3CB6FB138BEF.quest_subtitle": "Rare earths, rarely.",
  "quest.185D3CB6FB138BEF.quest_desc": [
    "MI's rarest ore: two small veins per chunk below height 24. Nine of its dusts in the centrifuge give three neodymium, three yttrium and three cadmium dusts, and half the time 300 mB of helium. Neodymium makes advanced motors, cadmium batteries and control rods."
  ],
  "quest.54FB0BAF3FD3D1EC.title": "Annealed Copper",
  "quest.54FB0BAF3FD3D1EC.quest_desc": [
    "Copper dust and 250 mB of oxygen in the blast furnace make a hot ingot at 64 EU/t, cooled like the rest. Its wires go into advanced motors, and its cables are EV: 65,536 EU/t into a network."
  ],
  "quest.7ED3D0E666CBB516.title": "Polyethylene",
  "quest.7ED3D0E666CBB516.quest_desc": [
    "Steam-crack light fuel or naphtha in the chemical reactor, distill it for ethylene, then polymerize: 500 mB of ethylene with four lead tiny dusts give 300 mB of polyethylene, with one chromium tiny dust 700."
  ],
  "quest.36836A1982A8D841.title": "Digital Circuit Board",
  "quest.36836A1982A8D841.quest_desc": [
    "Only the assembler makes it: six aluminum cables, a silicon battery, an electronic board, four stainless steel plates and 750 mB of polyethylene. Aluminum cables are HV, 8,192 EU/t into a network."
  ],
  "quest.5EDEE7569637D27D.title": "Logic gates",
  "quest.5EDEE7569637D27D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An \"},{\"text\":\"Op Amp\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modern_industrialization:op_amp\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" is four resistors, four transistors and a diode. With aluminum wire it becomes an AND gate with resistors, an OR gate with a diode and a second op amp, and a NOT gate with one resistor.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.71323E5DE10F7F15.title": "Digital Circuit",
  "quest.71323E5DE10F7F15.quest_subtitle": "No need for Sodium anymore.",
  "quest.71323E5DE10F7F15.quest_desc": [
    "Four electronic circuits, an AND gate, an OR gate and two NOT gates on a digital board. The turbo hull, the distillation tower, the pressurizer and every HV machine start here."
  ],
  "quest.27378F0D2B36AE9B.title": "Turbo Machine Hull",
  "quest.27378F0D2B36AE9B.quest_desc": [
    "A digital circuit, two sodium batteries and three aluminum cables on a turbo casing: eight stainless steel plates around an advanced hull. Sodium comes from electrolyzing salt, MI's own ore, which also gives chlorine."
  ],
  "quest.1F654CF0CC18BCC0.title": "Advanced motor and pump",
  "quest.1F654CF0CC18BCC0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Polarizer magnetizes a stainless steel rod with a neodymium dust; with two stainless rods, two aluminum cables and four annealed copper wires it makes an \"},{\"text\":\"Advanced Motor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modern_industrialization:advanced_motor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Stainless rotors and pipes around one make an \"},{\"text\":\"Advanced Pump\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modern_industrialization:advanced_pump\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.30D8772C1600CA50.title": "Titanium",
  "quest.30D8772C1600CA50.quest_subtitle": "Steel, but pink.",
  "quest.30D8772C1600CA50.quest_desc": [
    "Nothing generates titanium ore: bauxite electrolysis leaves titanium tiny dust, and the Electric Quarry digs the ore with stainless drills. Three raw titanium and 3,000 mB of manganese solution give four hot ingots at 128 EU/t, with 2,500 mB of the solution back."
  ],
  "quest.68DD9957F287E0FE.title": "Pressurizer",
  "quest.68DD9957F287E0FE.quest_subtitle": "Under pressure.",
  "quest.68DD9957F287E0FE.quest_desc": [
    "Four advanced pumps, a digital circuit, a turbo hull, an aluminum cable and two titanium pipe casings. It squeezes 1,000 mB of water or steam into 125 of high pressure at 64 EU/t, lets it back down for 2, and with an air intake makes liquid air cheaper than the freezer."
  ],
  "quest.7BE181EF3C63334C.title": "Liquid air",
  "quest.7BE181EF3C63334C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Aluminum and stainless plates around a stainless rotor make an \"},{\"text\":\"Air Intake\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modern_industrialization:air_intake\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Its liquid air splits in the centrifuge: 3,000 mB give 650 of oxygen, 2,315 of nitrogen and 35 of argon, the rare one.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0515B48700D32CDF.title": "Blastproof Alloy",
  "quest.0515B48700D32CDF.quest_subtitle": "Creeper nightmare.",
  "quest.0515B48700D32CDF.quest_desc": [
    "A tungsten, a titanium and a stainless steel ingot in the Packer make a mixed ingot; the compressor squeezes two into one plate at 32 EU/t. Tungsten is MI's own ore, deep below height 20."
  ],
  "quest.045A4467B5C095EB.title": "Implosion Compressor",
  "quest.045A4467B5C095EB.quest_subtitle": "Automated creeper.",
  "quest.045A4467B5C095EB.quest_desc": [
    "Four blastproof large plates, two advanced motors, two titanium large plates and a turbo hull. With one Industrial TNT per job it crushes what nothing else can: a mixed blastproof ingot into three blastproof ingots, a mixed iridium ingot into a plate."
  ],
  "quest.1FE570F659ECF04E.title": "Industrial TNT",
  "quest.1FE570F659ECF04E.quest_subtitle": "Not that kind of explosive.",
  "quest.1FE570F659ECF04E.quest_desc": [
    "Four sand, three flint, 250 mB of toluene and 1,000 mB of nitrogen make four in the Mixer. Place one and it just sits there: it never goes off, it only feeds the implosion compressor."
  ],
  "quest.2A369259B3A151A7.title": "Platinum",
  "quest.2A369259B3A151A7.quest_desc": [
    "Raw platinum dissolves in 9,000 mB of sulfuric acid; the centrifuge purifies the solution, with a 5% chance of an iridium tiny dust per bucket, and the electrolyzer gives three platinum tiny dusts per bucket. The hot ingot takes 128 EU/t."
  ],
  "quest.071C9E85BFE13EAD.title": "Monocrystalline Silicon",
  "quest.071C9E85BFE13EAD.quest_subtitle": "Grown, not crafted.",
  "quest.071C9E85BFE13EAD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Thirty-two silicon dust, an iridium tiny dust and 1,250 mB of argon grow a silicon crystal in the blast furnace at 64 EU/t, on kanthal coils. The cutting machine slices it into 32 \"},{\"text\":\"Silicon Wafers\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modern_industrialization:silicon_wafer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" with 500 mB of lubricant: RAM takes one, the memory management unit two.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Titanium drills dig iridium ore but need a processing unit, and that needs wafers. Bootstrap with platinum refining's tiny dust, one bucket in twenty, or with an \"},{\"text\":\"Ore Laser Base\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"industrialforegoing:ore_laser_base\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a white lens, best in the End.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1229B240D7D4D719.title": "PVC and synthetic rubber",
  "quest.1229B240D7D4D719.quest_desc": [
    "Acetylene and hydrochloric acid make vinyl chloride, styrene and butadiene make styrene-butadiene; lead or chromium polymerizes each like ethylene. PVC goes into boards and upgrades, the rubber into RAM, and 200 mB of it freeze into 64 rubber sheets."
  ],
  "quest.726026B86C55218F.title": "Processing Unit",
  "quest.726026B86C55218F.quest_subtitle": "Bitcoin miner.",
  "quest.726026B86C55218F.quest_desc": [
    "Four digital circuits, two RAM, a memory management unit and an arithmetic logic unit on a processing unit board. The board alone asks for annealed copper cables, cadmium batteries, platinum plates and 1,500 mB of PVC. Nuclear power and quantum parts begin here."
  ],
  "quest.177CFD9E5A8B9232.title": "Highly Advanced Upgrade",
  "quest.177CFD9E5A8B9232.quest_subtitle": "I'm speed.",
  "quest.177CFD9E5A8B9232.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight large advanced motors, four large advanced pumps, four \"},{\"text\":\"turbo upgrades\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"022564284418A1AF\"}},{\"text\":\" and a processing unit board, with 2,500 mB of PVC, make four. Each raises a machine's overclock cap by 512 EU/t.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5D02BD2E83CF3500.title": "Cooling cells",
  "quest.5D02BD2E83CF3500.quest_desc": [
    "Three fluid pipes, two small heat exchangers, six tin plates and 1,000 mB of cryofluid. Cryofluid is 140 mB of argon and 60 of helium in the Vacuum Freezer, a 256 EU/t recipe: give the freezer +128 of upgrades first."
  ],
  "quest.3AC8328C545DAD97.title": "Superconductor",
  "quest.3AC8328C545DAD97.quest_subtitle": "Unlimited power (transfer).",
  "quest.3AC8328C545DAD97.quest_desc": [
    "An iridium dust, three annealed copper, three yttrium and two neodymium dusts mix into nine superconductor dust; its hot ingot takes 128 EU/t. Three wires, two cooling cells and 1,000 mB of PVC make six cables, and eight cables ring into a coil."
  ],
  "quest.3611FAE403FF9A1C.title": "Gravichestplate",
  "quest.3611FAE403FF9A1C.quest_subtitle": "Creative flight, survival paperwork.",
  "quest.3611FAE403FF9A1C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four superconductor plates, a highly advanced upgrade, a superconductor coil and two cooling cells; in this pack a \"},{\"text\":\"Horizon Chart\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:horizon_chart\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" from the Atlas too, act IV. It flies like creative, cancels fall damage and nothing else, and runs on EU: charge it on a storage unit or transformer.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"It shares the jetpack's \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.modern_industrialization.toggle_flight\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" toggle.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.135380011E79C8C9.title": "Advanced Upgrade",
  "quest.135380011E79C8C9.quest_subtitle": "Machine speedup-speedup.",
  "quest.135380011E79C8C9.quest_desc": [
    "Four basic upgrades, two large motors, a large pump and an electronic board, with 1,000 mB of polyethylene, make four. Each adds 16 EU/t to a machine's overclock cap."
  ],
  "quest.022564284418A1AF.title": "Turbo Upgrade",
  "quest.022564284418A1AF.quest_subtitle": "Gotta go fast.",
  "quest.022564284418A1AF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Sixteen \"},{\"text\":\"advanced motors\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"1F654CF0CC18BCC0\"}},{\"text\":\", two advanced pumps, four advanced upgrades and a digital board, with 1,000 mB of PVC, make four. Each adds 64 EU/t.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.45E64BEF467243CD.title": "Overdrive Module",
  "quest.45E64BEF467243CD.quest_desc": [
    "Electrum fine wire, two diodes, two transistors and an electronic board. In a machine it keeps the efficiency from dropping when the work stops, by burning the same EU/t with nothing to do; the recipe stays locked until you remove it or power runs out."
  ],
  "quest.550454BF1A7F3057.title": "Deep drills",
  "quest.550454BF1A7F3057.quest_desc": [
    "In the Electric Quarry a stainless steel drill brings titanium, tungsten, monazite and platinum ores; a titanium drill, which needs a processing unit, brings uranium, fluorite and 5% iridium ore."
  ],
  "quest.0DFFBA122223C041.title": "High Pressure Boiler",
  "quest.0DFFBA122223C041.quest_desc": [
    "An advanced large steam boiler with four advanced pumps, two digital circuits and two clean stainless casings. Fed high pressure water it makes high pressure steam: each mB is worth 8 of regular steam, 8 EU."
  ],
  "quest.5DD7E6CCBA56976B.title": "HV Steam Turbine",
  "quest.5DD7E6CCBA56976B.quest_subtitle": "Better than a water wheel.",
  "quest.5DD7E6CCBA56976B.quest_desc": [
    "A digital circuit, two advanced motors, a turbo hull, two stainless rotors, pipes and an aluminum cable. Regular steam only, up to 512 EU/t."
  ],
  "quest.79A712ACEBDAAC90.title": "Large Steam Turbine",
  "quest.79A712ACEBDAAC90.quest_subtitle": "Enslaved hurricane.",
  "quest.79A712ACEBDAAC90.quest_desc": [
    "Four HV steam turbines, two advanced pumps, two stainless rotors and a turbo hull. It takes regular and high pressure steam, up to 16,384 EU/t, and gives no water back."
  ],
  "quest.332F7CBC4692CD4B.title": "Heat Exchanger",
  "quest.332F7CBC4692CD4B.quest_subtitle": "Lava power, but balanced.",
  "quest.332F7CBC4692CD4B.quest_desc": [
    "Small heat exchangers, a turbo hull, stainless pipe casings, frostproof and heatproof casings. It trades 2,000 mB of high pressure steam and 1,000 of water for 125 of high pressure water and 16,000 of regular steam: the expensive water goes around again."
  ],
  "quest.31BBAFEFC706F63A.title": "HV Diesel Generator",
  "quest.31BBAFEFC706F63A.quest_subtitle": "Fast and Furious 2.",
  "quest.31BBAFEFC706F63A.quest_desc": [
    "A turbo hull, two advanced pumps, stainless gears, aluminum cables and a digital circuit. Any fluid fuel, up to 1,024 EU/t, still only when something asks."
  ],
  "quest.429062C1AA630702.title": "Large Diesel Generator",
  "quest.429062C1AA630702.quest_subtitle": "Fast and Furious 42.",
  "quest.429062C1AA630702.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An HV diesel generator at the core, with large advanced pumps and motors, titanium gears, a \"},{\"text\":\"processing unit\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"726026B86C55218F\"}},{\"text\":\" and a highly advanced hull. Up to 16,384 EU/t from fuel.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.617F994D3B1A960E.title": "MV and HV storage",
  "quest.617F994D3B1A960E.quest_desc": [
    "Six silicon batteries on an advanced hull, or six sodium batteries on a turbo hull. They hold 12.8 and 102.4 million EU, and buffer a generator that sleeps between demands."
  ],
  "quest.2AE30BD79021E9BE.title": "Distillation Tower",
  "quest.2AE30BD79021E9BE.quest_subtitle": "Total distillation.",
  "quest.2AE30BD79021E9BE.quest_desc": [
    "Two distilleries, four advanced pumps, two digital circuits and a turbo hull. Where a distillery gives one product per recipe, the tower gives one per layer: crude oil splits into all three fuels at once."
  ],
  "quest.60E87308277CC3F9.title": "Steam cracking",
  "quest.60E87308277CC3F9.quest_desc": [
    "Fuel plus 100 mB of steam in the chemical reactor cracks it; distilled, cracked naphtha gives methane, acetylene, ethylene, propene, butadiene, benzene, toluene and ethylbenzene. Toluene makes Industrial TNT, acetylene PVC, ethylene polyethylene, butadiene and ethylbenzene rubber."
  ],
  "quest.26D8BD3C0E3ADBB2.title": "Boosted Diesel",
  "quest.26D8BD3C0E3ADBB2.quest_desc": [
    "Ethanol and a splash of acrylic acid make diethyl ether; 250 mB of it and 1,000 of diesel mix into 1,200 of boosted diesel, 800 EU per mB instead of 400."
  ],
  "quest.7BC0785B2E2B7BB8.title": "Biodiesel",
  "quest.7BC0785B2E2B7BB8.quest_desc": [
    "The centrifuge squeezes plant oil out of compostable items. With ethanol and sodium hydroxide it becomes raw biodiesel, and with steam biodiesel: 250 EU per mB, from a farm instead of a well."
  ],
  "quest.323FB06AF7B81911.title": "Upgrade arithmetic",
  "quest.323FB06AF7B81911.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Single-block machines overclock to 32 EU/t, multiblocks to 128. Upgrades add to that cap: basic +2, advanced +16, turbo +64, highly advanced +512, and a stack in the slot counts whole.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.212031F00512B970.title": "Which coils?",
  "quest.212031F00512B970.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The coils decide the blast furnace's ceiling: cupronickel up to 32 EU/t, kanthal up to 128. Titanium, platinum, superconductor and every nuclear metal need kanthal.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.41F26F7BFFBD23DF.title": "Thousands of mB per tick",
  "quest.41F26F7BFFBD23DF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Every fluid pipe holds one bucket and connected pipes share it: 25 pipes move up to 25,000 mB per tick. A steel tank joined with an I/O connection adds its 16 buckets to the network.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.44165F5F7DDFE958.title": "Cool it with cryofluid",
  "quest.44165F5F7DDFE958.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A Heat Exchanger also cools hot ingots, 20 mB of cryofluid each, and hands back 13 mB of argon and 5 of helium: the cryofluid almost pays for itself.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4C69A597982064B8.title": "Chemistry that copies",
  "quest.4C69A597982064B8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"In the chemical reactor a slime ball that stays put plus 25 mB of acrylic glue gives a new slime ball, and a string plus 20 mB of nylon a new string.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5ED22E99B4A9FB12.title": "Diamond 2.0",
  "quest.5ED22E99B4A9FB12.quest_subtitle": "Electric boogaloo.",
  "quest.5ED22E99B4A9FB12.quest_desc": [
    "You held a piece of raw iridium, worth more than any diamond here: a titanium drill brings up the ore once every twenty digs, and a pickaxe on the placed ore gives the raw piece."
  ],
  "reward.631942742AC8DCE3.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.1A629C77425FE43C.title": "Moonshine",
  "quest.1A629C77425FE43C.quest_subtitle": "The still always wins.",
  "quest.1A629C77425FE43C.quest_desc": [
    "A full bucket of ethanol. Eight sugar and a bucket of water make a bucket of sugar solution, and the distillery gets 10 mB of ethanol out of it: someone was patient, or knew ethylene is quicker."
  ],
  "reward.5828D272E786FD61.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.6C6AB1D2C841C966.title": "Stainless for the common store",
  "quest.6C6AB1D2C841C966.quest_subtitle": "Shiny, and it stays shiny.",
  "quest.6C6AB1D2C841C966.quest_desc": [
    "Thirty-two stainless steel ingots: turbo casings, advanced motors and the digital circuit board all start with them."
  ],
  "image.2EB9C285F5694286.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Upgrades\",\"color\":\"#FFA552\"}]",
  "image.46CF37C7F812415C.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Power plant\",\"color\":\"#FFA552\"}]",
  "image.6567B8D71A753667.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Refinery\",\"color\":\"#FFA552\"}]",
  "image.1F4D6373BE28CCE2.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Modern Industrialization\\nDigital\",\"color\":\"#FFF1DE\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.1CA40CDAB1F3B4FA.title": "Back to the Sun of Heliodor",
  "image.24E9B0AFE862BC68.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» Steam\",\"color\":\"#FFA552\"}]",
  "image.5FFCEAB0C46AF964.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» Electricity\",\"color\":\"#FFA552\"}]",
  "image.12C01551721DC2AE.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» Endgame\",\"color\":\"#FFA552\"}]",
  "image.5F41CB39D92AB85E.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"etch  solder  compute\",\"color\":\"#BFA58A\",\"font\":\"minecraft:alt\"}]",
  "image.447A14F3F4D03138.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"U1\",\"color\":\"#E6EFE6\"}]",
  "image.1260B3B205E9316F.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"MI-PU  2.5.6\",\"color\":\"#9AA3AD\"}]",
  "image.4E3C52E5D4243CD7.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"ENTRELUMEN  REV B\",\"color\":\"#E6EFE6\"}]",
  "chapter.6ABB1358FF6D448A.title": "Draconic Evolution · Draconic and Chaotic",
  "chapter.6ABB1358FF6D448A.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Awakened draconium and the draconic tier, the Chaos Guardian and the chaotic tier, and the Draconic Reactor between them."
  ],
  "quest.698802A16527E485.title": "Awakened Draconium",
  "quest.698802A16527E485.quest_subtitle": "Wide awake, and slightly orange.",
  "quest.698802A16527E485.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"One awakened block splits into nine \"},{\"text\":\"Awakened Draconium Ingots\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"draconicevolution:awakened_draconium_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", and nine nuggets make an ingot. They go into everything draconic: controllers, cores, rotors and the reactor's own fuel.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.73AFDC7DD2D99015.title": "Draconic Core",
  "quest.73AFDC7DD2D99015.quest_subtitle": "Four wyverns walk into a fusion core.",
  "quest.73AFDC7DD2D99015.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A nether star as catalyst, then four Wyvern Cores, three awakened ingots and, in this pack, an \"},{\"text\":\"Atomic Alloy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:alloy_atomic\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", on wyvern injectors: 1,000,000 OP. The draconic capacitor and staff build on it, and four of them make a Chaotic Core.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5701AC99EB5D7F3C.title": "Draconic Energy Controller",
  "quest.5701AC99EB5D7F3C.quest_desc": [
    "Four awakened ingots, four wyvern energy controllers and a Wyvern Core. Each draconic tool, bow and chestpiece takes one, and the capacitor three."
  ],
  "quest.768E865FF9DD8FE2.title": "Draconic injectors",
  "quest.768E865FF9DD8FE2.quest_desc": [
    "A wyvern injector as catalyst, two Wyvern Cores, four diamonds and an awakened draconium block, for 256,000 OP. Draconic recipes need one per ingredient: eight for a draconic tool."
  ],
  "quest.4338BEEF620CA369.title": "Draconic tools",
  "quest.4338BEEF620CA369.quest_subtitle": "Netherite goes in. Orange comes out.",
  "quest.4338BEEF620CA369.quest_desc": [
    "Fuse each wyvern tool with four netherite ingots, two awakened ingots, a Wyvern Core and a draconic energy controller: 32 million OP apiece. They dig at speed 25 in a 6×5 grid, and modules, enchantments and charge carry over."
  ],
  "quest.1AF5529C2E6667ED.title": "Draconic Chestpiece",
  "quest.1AF5529C2E6667ED.quest_subtitle": "Now with actual flying.",
  "quest.1AF5529C2E6667ED.quest_desc": [
    "The same fusion, from the wyvern chestpiece. Its 8×6 grid takes draconic modules, and the draconic flight module finally adds creative flight on top of the elytra."
  ],
  "quest.21C7B2E3854277D3.title": "Count your nether stars",
  "quest.21C7B2E3854277D3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Every Wyvern Core eats a nether star, so a Draconic Core costs five with its catalyst, and a Chaotic Core twenty. Keep a Wither farm running.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1BDD73107F477142.title": "Awakened Item Dislocator",
  "quest.1BDD73107F477142.quest_desc": [
    "Two awakened ingots, draconium and redstone around the item dislocator stretch its pull from 8 to 32 blocks. It keeps the same toggle key and fits a curio slot."
  ],
  "quest.1DB7070BA01CBCFD.title": "Draconic modules",
  "quest.1DB7070BA01CBCFD.quest_desc": [
    "The same six, one tier up: 16 million OP, +50% speed, +8 damage, a 7×7 area, +125% jump and 400 hunger points. Awakened nuggets turn wyvern modules into these; damage also wants dragon's breath and the area module a Draconic Core."
  ],
  "quest.2168C7C5481E24A4.title": "Awakened draconium for the store",
  "quest.2168C7C5481E24A4.quest_subtitle": "The dragon pays in installments.",
  "quest.2168C7C5481E24A4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Nine \"},{\"text\":\"Awakened Draconium Ingots\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"draconicevolution:awakened_draconium_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for the common store, once a day. One Dragon Heart awakens four blocks, thirty-six ingots.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.054E5E3645D53554.title": "Defeat the Ender Dragon ten times",
  "quest.4CD241050470D0F0.title": "Serial dragon slayer",
  "quest.4CD241050470D0F0.quest_subtitle": "The End's longest-running show.",
  "quest.4CD241050470D0F0.quest_desc": [
    "Ten dragons, ten hearts, ten eggs. The exit portal must be tired of the fireworks by now."
  ],
  "reward.54BC4C2F41E69EBA.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.73A64B923A0020EA.title": "Draconic Capacitor",
  "quest.73A64B923A0020EA.quest_desc": [
    "The wyvern capacitor as catalyst, a Draconic Core, three draconic energy controllers and four awakened ingots: 32 million OP. Its grid grows to 5×5, room for draconic energy modules of 16 million OP each."
  ],
  "quest.2F7A27B782F6FA7A.title": "Draconic crystals",
  "quest.2F7A27B782F6FA7A.quest_desc": [
    "Four wyvern relays fuse into four draconic ones with wyvern energy controllers, diamonds and a Wyvern Core. Draconic crystals reach 127 blocks and buffer 64 million OP; relays take 32 links, wireless ones feed 64 machines at 512,000 OP/t."
  ],
  "quest.7E833D59C93BCBB0.title": "Draconic weapons",
  "quest.7E833D59C93BCBB0.quest_desc": [
    "The sword and bow fuse from the wyvern ones like the tools, 32 million OP each. Draconic damage modules add 8 each, and the sword's Attack Radius still sweeps a 100-degree arc."
  ],
  "quest.1941728FF791EE5F.title": "Draconic projectile modules",
  "quest.1941728FF791EE5F.quest_desc": [
    "Awakened nuggets and a Wyvern Core fold two wyvern projectile modules into each draconic one: velocity, accuracy, damage, penetration and gravity compensation."
  ],
  "quest.2D8FE4BDB7ADAE81.title": "Projectile Immunity Cancellation",
  "quest.2D8FE4BDB7ADAE81.quest_subtitle": "Endermen hate this one trick.",
  "quest.2D8FE4BDB7ADAE81.quest_desc": [
    "A wither skeleton skull, an ender pearl and two Wyvern Cores in a module. Its arrows ignore the arrow immunity of endermen, withers, the Ender Dragon, Guardian Withers and shulkers."
  ],
  "quest.03875AA4C6C690F5.title": "Draconic Staff of Power",
  "quest.03875AA4C6C690F5.quest_subtitle": "Three tools, one pocket.",
  "quest.03875AA4C6C690F5.quest_desc": [
    "A Draconic Core as catalyst, the draconic pickaxe, sword and shovel, six awakened ingots and a draconic energy controller: 256 million OP. One tool that digs like all three and hits like an axe, with an 8×6 grid."
  ],
  "quest.75E4A59AE1C488FD.title": "Filterable Ender Collection",
  "quest.75E4A59AE1C488FD.quest_desc": [
    "Two comparators, a chest and awakened nuggets turn the wyvern module into a filtered one: choose by item or by tag, like c:ores, which drops go to the ender chest."
  ],
  "quest.42652613F714362E.title": "Forest Reduction Assistant",
  "quest.42652613F714362E.quest_subtitle": "It assists. The forest reduces.",
  "quest.42652613F714362E.quest_desc": [
    "The draconic tree harvester: 48 blocks of reach at 15 blocks per second, from the wyvern module with netherite, awakened ingots and a Wyvern Core."
  ],
  "quest.1B95ECB5DCFE8862.title": "It mines anything",
  "quest.1B95ECB5DCFE8862.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Draconic and chaotic tools skip the tool-tier tags: they mine any block that can be mined, while wyvern tools stop at the netherite tier.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.480EA392BB172842.title": "Creative flight",
  "quest.480EA392BB172842.quest_subtitle": "Finally, no rockets.",
  "quest.480EA392BB172842.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two Wyvern Cores, awakened ingots, a slow falling potion and a firework rocket around the wyvern module. It adds creative flight to the elytra, drawing 4,096 OP per tick while you fly; \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.draconicevolution.toggle_flight\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" switches it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.32EE81388B4A3DFA.title": "Draconic shields",
  "quest.32EE81388B4A3DFA.quest_desc": [
    "Capacity modules hold 50 points each and the large one 250; recovery modules recharge faster. The draconic controller, built from two Draconic Cores, emeralds and netherite, cuts the cooldown to 10 seconds."
  ],
  "quest.1DCC6E5F82119C12.title": "Draconic Undying",
  "quest.1DCC6E5F82119C12.quest_desc": [
    "When a hit would kill you it heals 12 health and adds 50 shield points for 30 seconds, then recharges in 60 seconds with 10 million OP. A strong healing potion and a draconic shield module go into it."
  ],
  "quest.4C9A4F18EFE9C986.title": "Spawners, one tier up",
  "quest.4C9A4F18EFE9C986.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Click a stabilized spawner with a Draconic Core and it spawns 8 mobs at a time, ignoring light; with a Chaotic Core, 12 every 25 to 100 ticks.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.133B1AC7E9466F8F.title": "Look at a Chaos Crystal",
  "quest.2664683DD65474A2.title": "Chaos Islands",
  "quest.2664683DD65474A2.quest_subtitle": "Ten thousand blocks of nothing, then this.",
  "quest.2664683DD65474A2.quest_desc": [
    "Chaos Islands sit on a grid 10,000 blocks apart in the End, each around a Chaos Crystal at Y 80. Walking up to one wakes it: pillars rise with Guardian Crystals, then the Chaos Guardian arrives."
  ],
  "task.6966FAC3B88CD936.title": "Look at a Guardian Crystal",
  "quest.4E665D9DCF8F50B1.title": "Guardian Crystals",
  "quest.4E665D9DCF8F50B1.quest_subtitle": "Friendly fire, weaponized.",
  "quest.4E665D9DCF8F50B1.quest_desc": [
    "Each crystal carries a 512-point shield. The Guardian's own attacks leave it unstable for 10 seconds: stand near a crystal, let the Guardian's fire hit it, then break it before it settles."
  ],
  "task.46E92EDB2C8304DA.title": "Defeat the Chaos Guardian",
  "quest.31E115F8C09BE03F.title": "The Chaos Guardian",
  "quest.31E115F8C09BE03F.quest_subtitle": "It has a frickin laser beam.",
  "quest.31E115F8C09BE03F.quest_desc": [
    "With the crystals down its 16,000-point shield comes next, and only then its 1,000 health. It charges, bombards, fires lasers and sends shockwaves; when it lands it calls Guardian Withers. It drops 57 to 70 draconium dust."
  ],
  "quest.5791246A44136D6D.title": "Chaos Shards",
  "quest.5791246A44136D6D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Break the Chaos Crystal after the fight for five \"},{\"text\":\"Chaos Shards\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"draconicevolution:chaos_shard\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Until a reactor runs, they are the only chaos you get, so spend them on Chaotic Cores first.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.5D21515ABE27BB41.title": "Defeat a Guardian Wither",
  "quest.07067B00110036C1.title": "Wither on the side",
  "quest.07067B00110036C1.quest_subtitle": "Bring a friend, it said.",
  "quest.07067B00110036C1.quest_desc": [
    "You beat one of the withers the Guardian calls when it lands. It had backup. It always has backup."
  ],
  "reward.18F00A7F870D0FF0.title": "Secret found",
  "task.4B78BF19DDB11798.title": "Defeat two Chaos Guardians",
  "quest.6D8EC12CA997A6CA.title": "Island hopper",
  "quest.6D8EC12CA997A6CA.quest_subtitle": "Frequent flyer miles: earned.",
  "quest.6D8EC12CA997A6CA.quest_desc": [
    "A second Chaos Guardian means a second island, at least 10,000 blocks from the first. Nobody said the End was small."
  ],
  "reward.11E793673C78C660.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.21723AE1748B2106.title": "Pack a way home",
  "quest.21723AE1748B2106.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Store your base in an Advanced Dislocator before you sail for an island: islands sit 10,000 blocks apart, and the End has few landmarks.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5599B9637FC46B07.title": "Farming guardians",
  "quest.5599B9637FC46B07.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A chaotic weapon destabilizes Guardian Crystal shields by itself, no Guardian needed, which makes every later island fight much quicker.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.34BFF089141ABF9E.title": "Bows melt shields",
  "quest.34BFF089141ABF9E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The Guardian's shield has no limit on how fast it takes hits: a strong bow firing quickly strips its 16,000 points far sooner than a sword.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0E32A88DBE8E87AA.title": "Chaos fragments",
  "quest.0E32A88DBE8E87AA.quest_desc": [
    "A shard crafts into nine Large Chaos Fragments, each of those into nine Small ones, and each Small into nine Tiny ones; nine of a size craft back up. Recipes ask for large and small fragments, so split only what you need."
  ],
  "quest.3124B2C57CD54099.title": "Count your fragments",
  "quest.3124B2C57CD54099.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"One shard is nine large fragments. A Chaotic Core takes five of them, a chaotic injector four, the reactor core two and each reactor stabilizer one.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3D5FC627AD89EF21.title": "Chaotic Core",
  "quest.3D5FC627AD89EF21.quest_subtitle": "Twenty nether stars, one very angry marble.",
  "quest.3D5FC627AD89EF21.quest_desc": [
    "A large chaos fragment as catalyst; four Draconic Cores, four awakened ingots and four more large fragments around it, on draconic injectors: 100 million OP. Every chaotic tool, each reactor stabilizer and the chaotic capacitor take one."
  ],
  "quest.0706045D6A4F3D73.title": "Chaotic injectors",
  "quest.0706045D6A4F3D73.quest_subtitle": "One dragon egg each. Yes, each.",
  "quest.0706045D6A4F3D73.quest_desc": [
    "A draconic injector as catalyst, four diamonds, four large chaos fragments and a dragon egg, for 8,000,000 OP. Chaotic recipes need one per ingredient, eight for a tool, so start collecting eggs."
  ],
  "quest.645AFAAF981ECED2.title": "Chaotic Energy Controller",
  "quest.645AFAAF981ECED2.quest_desc": [
    "Four small chaos fragments, four draconic energy controllers and a Draconic Core. Each chaotic tool takes one, the capacitor three and the Staff of Power up to three."
  ],
  "quest.2747470770A8C4BD.title": "Chaotic tools",
  "quest.2747470770A8C4BD.quest_subtitle": "Speed 50. Blinking not recommended.",
  "quest.2747470770A8C4BD.quest_desc": [
    "Fuse each draconic tool with a Chaotic Core, six awakened ingots and a chaotic energy controller, on chaotic injectors: 128 million OP apiece. They dig at speed 50 and carry an 8×6 grid."
  ],
  "quest.118F626BC2BDFBC0.title": "Chaotic Chestpiece",
  "quest.118F626BC2BDFBC0.quest_desc": [
    "The same fusion from the draconic chestpiece. Its 10×8 grid is the largest armor grid in the mod: room for chaotic shields, undying and the fastest flight."
  ],
  "quest.39C47D3CF0A89A62.title": "Chaotic weapons",
  "quest.39C47D3CF0A89A62.quest_desc": [
    "The chaotic sword and bow, fused from the draconic ones for 128 million OP each. Chaotic damage modules add 16 each, and with one of these the crystal shields on a Chaos Island stop waiting for the Guardian."
  ],
  "quest.03614DC52E5FA259.title": "Chaotic projectile modules",
  "quest.03614DC52E5FA259.quest_desc": [
    "Six small chaos fragments and a Draconic Core fold two draconic projectile modules into each chaotic one: velocity, accuracy, damage, penetration and gravity compensation, each at its best."
  ],
  "quest.16263537DE3E3C87.title": "Chaotic Deforestation Module",
  "quest.16263537DE3E3C87.quest_subtitle": "Pack a sapling or two.",
  "quest.16263537DE3E3C87.quest_desc": [
    "144 blocks of reach at 45 blocks per second: the forest reduction module with large chaos fragments, netherite and a Draconic Core."
  ],
  "quest.5C98E32C32C173B3.title": "Chaotic modules",
  "quest.5C98E32C32C173B3.quest_desc": [
    "64 million OP, +150% speed, +16 damage, an 11×11 area and +400% jump. Small chaos fragments and a Draconic Core fold two draconic modules into each; the area module takes a Chaotic Core instead."
  ],
  "quest.2A4AD39AB148560F.title": "Chaotic flight",
  "quest.2A4AD39AB148560F.quest_desc": [
    "Strong swiftness potions, large chaos fragments and two Draconic Cores around the draconic flight module. The same creative and elytra flight, with the strongest elytra boost in the mod."
  ],
  "quest.4644EC069DBFDB12.title": "Chaotic shields",
  "quest.4644EC069DBFDB12.quest_desc": [
    "100 points per capacity module, 500 for the large one, and a controller with a 5-second cooldown that takes two Chaotic Cores and four nether stars. The chaotic capacity module also goes into the chaotic undying module."
  ],
  "quest.449E2D2B5E71AD83.title": "Chaotic Undying",
  "quest.449E2D2B5E71AD83.quest_desc": [
    "Heals 20, adds 100 shield points for 2 minutes and recharges in 45 seconds with 20 million OP. An enchanted golden apple and chaos fragments go into it."
  ],
  "quest.32D5BD08230CCACC.title": "Chaotic Capacitor",
  "quest.32D5BD08230CCACC.quest_desc": [
    "The draconic capacitor as catalyst, a Chaotic Core, three chaotic energy controllers and four awakened ingots: 128 million OP. Its 8×6 grid holds chaotic energy modules of 64 million OP each."
  ],
  "quest.10A0BE617423F4C2.title": "Creative Capacitor",
  "quest.10A0BE617423F4C2.quest_subtitle": "Infinite, if you ask the light nicely.",
  "quest.10A0BE617423F4C2.quest_desc": [
    "In this pack it has a recipe: a chaotic capacitor, two Dragon Hearts, two awakened ingots and four Luminosities, two of Exploration and two of the Arcane, from act VI. It holds more OP than you will ever spend."
  ],
  "quest.69AB3AE30A4CEF6B.title": "Rotor assembly",
  "quest.69AB3AE30A4CEF6B.quest_desc": [
    "Inner rotors take three awakened ingots, outer rotors three diamonds, each with a draconium core and two draconium ingots. Two of each, two more draconium ingots and a Wyvern Core make a rotor assembly."
  ],
  "quest.64BBF9F67B55698D.title": "Focus ring and frame",
  "quest.64BBF9F67B55698D.quest_desc": [
    "The focus ring is four gold ingots, three diamonds and two Wyvern Cores; the frame, six iron ingots around a Wyvern Core and an awakened ingot. Each reactor stabilizer takes one of each."
  ],
  "quest.3EBE9506A494CA69.title": "Reactor Stabilizers",
  "quest.3EBE9506A494CA69.quest_desc": [
    "Fuse the frame with a rotor assembly, a focus ring, a draconic energy controller, a Chaotic Core, three awakened ingots and a large chaos fragment: 16 million OP each, on chaotic injectors. The reactor needs four."
  ],
  "quest.134DE10F4A3F8B2D.title": "Reactor Energy Injector",
  "quest.134DE10F4A3F8B2D.quest_desc": [
    "A Wyvern Core as catalyst with four inner rotors, four draconium ingots and two iron ingots, 16 million OP. It feeds the containment field; the stabilizers take the power out."
  ],
  "quest.38D5FD5FBCE2625C.title": "Draconic Reactor",
  "quest.38D5FD5FBCE2625C.quest_subtitle": "Handle with oven mitts.",
  "quest.38D5FD5FBCE2625C.quest_desc": [
    "A Chaos Shard as catalyst, four awakened and three draconium ingots and two large chaos fragments: 64 million OP. Build it with four stabilizers in a cross, 4 to 7 blocks from the core and facing it, and the injector on one of the two free sides."
  ],
  "quest.501EAFA581A696FF.title": "Fuel",
  "quest.501EAFA581A696FF.quest_desc": [
    "The core holds up to eight awakened draconium blocks of fuel, and ingots and nuggets count too. As it burns, spent fuel turns to chaos and comes back out of the same screen as chaos fragments."
  ],
  "quest.223852AB4F08EC17.title": "Two flux gates",
  "quest.223852AB4F08EC17.quest_desc": [
    "Run the stabilizers' output through one flux gate and feed the injector through another. Set by redstone, they hold the field input steady while the surplus goes to your Energy Core."
  ],
  "quest.4C459D50DA1779A4.title": "Charge, then activate",
  "quest.4C459D50DA1779A4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Fuel it, press Charge and feed the injector. Activate unlocks once the core reaches 2,000°C with its field and saturation at least half full.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4C284AC4C8715B0D.title": "Watch the field",
  "quest.4C284AC4C8715B0D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Field Input Rate is the exact OP/t that holds the containment field where it is, and it grows exponentially as the field gets stronger. An empty field means an overload nothing can stop.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.522EA902EA4030CB.title": "Let SAS shut it down",
  "quest.522EA902EA4030CB.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"With SAS on, the reactor shuts itself down once the temperature drops below 2,500°C at 99% saturation: the right moment to refuel, or a safety net when something breaks.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2AE7DBDA8E6972DA.title": "Reactors speak redstone",
  "quest.2AE7DBDA8E6972DA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Every stabilizer and injector can drive a comparator: set it on the part's screen to temperature, field, saturation or fuel conversion, or their inverses.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7D2BA62A345567C4.title": "Mind the blast radius",
  "quest.7D2BA62A345567C4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The full-size reactor explosion is on in this pack.\",\"color\":\"#FF8C7A\"},{\"text\":\" Build the reactor far from anything you love and keep an eye on it while it runs.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6CBCCB13367E49CC.title": "Tier 8 core",
  "quest.6CBCCB13367E49CC.quest_subtitle": "The number stops being a number.",
  "quest.6CBCCB13367E49CC.quest_desc": [
    "The last shell trades redstone for awakened draconium: 786 draconium blocks and 378 awakened ones. Tier 8 has no practical ceiling; you will run out of power plants before it fills."
  ],
  "quest.4DA714D09E8C37B2.title": "Hearts for tier 8",
  "quest.4DA714D09E8C37B2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"378 awakened blocks at four per heart is 95 Dragon Hearts. The egg returns with every kill, so respawn the dragon on a schedule.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2BFD14ABA9927DE9.title": "Quantum Energy Tunnel",
  "quest.2BFD14ABA9927DE9.quest_desc": [
    "The draconic energy link: an end crystal, two wyvern wireless crystals, awakened ingots and a Draconic Core around the wyvern link. It crosses dimensions and moves 16,000 OP/t; switching it on costs 16 million OP."
  ],
  "quest.457B61FDD30C5F01.title": "Chaos-Entangled Quantum Energy Tunnel",
  "quest.457B61FDD30C5F01.quest_desc": [
    "The top link: 128,000 OP/t across dimensions, 64 million OP to switch on and up to 8,192 OP/t to keep open. Two draconic wireless crystals, netherite, an end crystal and a Chaotic Core wrap the draconic tunnel."
  ],
  "quest.4A10A9877F78B94B.title": "Chaotic Staff of Power",
  "quest.4A10A9877F78B94B.quest_subtitle": "A billion OP, give or take nothing.",
  "quest.4A10A9877F78B94B.quest_desc": [
    "A Chaotic Core as catalyst; the chaotic pickaxe, sword and shovel, six small chaos fragments and a chaotic energy controller around it: 1,024,000,000 OP in one fusion. It digs, mines and fights as one tool with a 10×8 grid.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "A draconic staff can be the catalyst instead, fused with three chaotic energy controllers, two Draconic Cores, a Chaotic Core and chaos fragments."
  ],
  "image.6FA47F591CEC56AD.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Draconic weapons and tools\",\"color\":\"#FF9D3B\"}]",
  "image.44AD153F32B70064.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Draconic armor\",\"color\":\"#FF9D3B\"}]",
  "image.27954CB7078F697B.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Chaotic weapons and tools\",\"color\":\"#FF9D3B\"}]",
  "image.3B455EA1E2F5A5B0.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Chaotic armor\",\"color\":\"#FF9D3B\"}]",
  "image.0FD1974CB3AEC67D.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Energy beyond wyvern\",\"color\":\"#FF9D3B\"}]",
  "image.7ECB3AA53A311FC0.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Draconic Evolution\\nDraconic and Chaotic\",\"color\":\"#FFF1DC\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.3BD90A08BF1AD03F.title": "Back to the Sun of Heliodor",
  "image.7DF66F68BF76B55C.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» Draconium and Wyvern\",\"color\":\"#FF9D3B\"}]",
  "image.7022CBB198B95F20.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"wake  break  burn  contain\",\"color\":\"#B9A7E0\",\"font\":\"minecraft:alt\"}]",
  "image.799B0D5DA81558D4.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"chaos island\",\"color\":\"#E0473A\"}]",
  "image.31C9FF24EFC1B600.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"reactor\",\"color\":\"#FF9D3B\"}]",
  "chapter.03D298843B4E907C.title": "Modern Industrialization · Endgame",
  "chapter.03D298843B4E907C.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Fission that cannot melt down, fusion that breeds its own fuel, and a pocket black hole for the quantum tier."
  ],
  "quest.50B0F1DC62355C80.title": "Nuclear Alloy",
  "quest.50B0F1DC62355C80.quest_subtitle": "Three metals, one controlled explosion.",
  "quest.50B0F1DC62355C80.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A blastproof alloy plate, a beryllium plate and a cadmium plate pack into one mixed plate; the implosion compressor turns it into three \"},{\"text\":\"Nuclear Alloy Plates\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modern_industrialization:nuclear_alloy_plate\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Beryllium ingots also come out of that compressor, from electrolyzed emerald dust.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.40D3A83B326757F2.title": "Casings and hatches",
  "quest.40D3A83B326757F2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight nuclear alloy plates around a turbo hull make a \"},{\"text\":\"Nuclear Alloy Casing\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modern_industrialization:nuclear_casing\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; around a highly advanced input hatch, a \"},{\"text\":\"Nuclear Item Hatch\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modern_industrialization:nuclear_item_hatch\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" or \"},{\"text\":\"Nuclear Fluid Hatch\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modern_industrialization:nuclear_fluid_hatch\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Each hatch has one input and two outputs, and their inputs form the grid in the reactor's screen.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4A6B01F3A0DA0A56.title": "Uranium fuel rods",
  "quest.4A6B01F3A0DA0A56.quest_desc": [
    "Eighteen uranium rods, two blastproof curved plates, a large motor and two robot arms, with 500 mB of soldering alloy and 100 of helium, make one rod in the assembler. Two rods and a nuclear alloy plate pack into a double, two doubles and two plates into a quad."
  ],
  "quest.3D2155E3D6873087.title": "Cadmium control rods",
  "quest.3D2155E3D6873087.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The same frame around eighteen cadmium rods makes a \"},{\"text\":\"Cadmium Control Rod\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modern_industrialization:cadmium_control_rod\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": it soaks up neutrons instead of making them. The reactor's controller takes two.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3D484AC9377B043F.title": "Nuclear Reactor",
  "quest.3D484AC9377B043F.quest_subtitle": "3.6 roentgen. Not great, not terrible.",
  "quest.3D484AC9377B043F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four nuclear alloy large plates, two control rods, a highly advanced hull and a processing unit; in this pack an \"},{\"text\":\"Ark Connection Bus\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:ark_bus\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" too, act V. It comes in several sizes: nuclear casings for walls, hatches on top, and water in a fluid hatch boils into steam.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.51944A0A4F67E1A8.title": "Deuterium and tritium",
  "quest.51944A0A4F67E1A8.quest_desc": [
    "Neutrons turn a little of the water in a fluid hatch into deuterium, and heavy water into tritium. The electrolyzer also splits heavy water into deuterium, and the centrifuge gets 20 mB of deuterium and 1 of tritium from a bucket of hydrogen."
  ],
  "quest.358BDFF782F85724.title": "Plutonium",
  "quest.358BDFF782F85724.quest_desc": [
    "Spent fuel isn't waste: in five minutes the centrifuge splits a depleted uranium rod into 53 uranium-238 and 27 plutonium tiny dusts, often with a uranium-235 one. Plutonium melts into ingots at 128 EU/t, for MOX fuel, nukes and batteries."
  ],
  "quest.778354EA50D91E74.title": "MOX fuel",
  "quest.778354EA50D91E74.quest_desc": [
    "Eight uranium-238 dusts and a plutonium dust mix into LE MOX, six and three into HE MOX: new fuel rods from your spent ones. A depleted LE MOX rod still centrifuges into 30 plutonium tiny dusts."
  ],
  "quest.40DE7DB4FA96B619.title": "Enriched uranium",
  "quest.40DE7DB4FA96B619.quest_desc": [
    "Nine uranium dusts in the centrifuge give a uranium-235 tiny dust and eighty uranium-238 ones. Eight U-238 and one U-235 dust make LE uranium, six and three HE uranium: richer fuel for the same rod frame."
  ],
  "quest.6D147773F1EC0EE0.title": "Qubits",
  "quest.6D147773F1EC0EE0.quest_desc": [
    "Two arithmetic logic units, two carbon plates, two glass panes and six superconductor wires, with 250 mB of cryofluid and 50 of tritium, in the assembler."
  ],
  "quest.6F61A86BE1F99619.title": "Quantum Circuit Board",
  "quest.6F61A86BE1F99619.quest_desc": [
    "Twelve superconductor cables, two plutonium batteries, a processing unit board, six iridium plates and 50 mB of helium-3, at 64 EU/t: the assembler needs +32 of upgrades. The centrifuge gets 5 mB of helium-3 from each bucket of helium."
  ],
  "quest.587D363313351442.title": "Quantum Circuit",
  "quest.587D363313351442.quest_subtitle": "Möbius strip eigenvalues.",
  "quest.587D363313351442.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four processing units, two qubits, a cooling cell and a quantum board; in this pack a Mekanism \"},{\"text\":\"Atomic Alloy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:alloy_atomic\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" too, act V, and the assembler version is gone. Fusion, the plasma turbine and every quantum item start here.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6BD19C3987AF82FC.title": "Quantum Machine Hull",
  "quest.6BD19C3987AF82FC.quest_desc": [
    "A quantum circuit, two plutonium batteries and three superconductor cables on a quantum casing: eight iridium plates around a highly advanced hull."
  ],
  "quest.0B96AFD2B5BF217D.title": "Fusion chambers",
  "quest.0B96AFD2B5BF217D.quest_desc": [
    "Four superconductor coils, two large heat exchangers and two nuclear alloy large plates around a plasma-handling iridium casing. The fusion reactor's controller takes six."
  ],
  "quest.624F68BE1B3A1661.title": "Fusion Reactor",
  "quest.624F68BE1B3A1661.quest_subtitle": "A star core, on a leash.",
  "quest.624F68BE1B3A1661.quest_desc": [
    "Six fusion chambers, two quantum circuits and a quantum hull. It fuses deuterium, tritium or helium-3 into helium plasma, 16,000 EU/t per reaction: deuterium and tritium give a bucket of plasma in 45 seconds, helium-3 and tritium in 15."
  ],
  "quest.43475F84B3C8A758.title": "Plasma Turbine",
  "quest.43475F84B3C8A758.quest_subtitle": "Better than fission.",
  "quest.43475F84B3C8A758.quest_desc": [
    "Four superconductor coils, two quantum circuits, two titanium rotors and a quantum hull, walled in plasma-handling iridium casings. Helium plasma is worth 100,000 EU per mB, and the turbine turns out about a million EU per tick."
  ],
  "quest.6F553EC59E91D4F4.title": "Superconductor grid",
  "quest.6F553EC59E91D4F4.quest_subtitle": "Unlimited power, transferred.",
  "quest.6F553EC59E91D4F4.quest_desc": [
    "Six plutonium batteries on a quantum hull store 12.8 trillion EU. An EV to SV transformer joins annealed copper cables to superconductor ones, which carry up to 1,024,000,000 EU/t."
  ],
  "quest.07DDBCC0B2B60995.title": "Ultradense Metal Ball",
  "quest.07DDBCC0B2B60995.quest_subtitle": "Heavier than it looks. It looks heavy.",
  "quest.07DDBCC0B2B60995.quest_desc": [
    "Four tungsten large plates, four lead plates and an iridium plate: the only thing hard enough to hold a black hole together."
  ],
  "quest.65D901EA3E3872A0.title": "Singularity",
  "quest.65D901EA3E3872A0.quest_subtitle": "A pocket black hole.",
  "quest.65D901EA3E3872A0.quest_desc": [
    "An ultradense metal ball and sixty-four nukes in the implosion compressor. The assembler makes two nukes per run from six Industrial TNT, four plutonium ingots, two processing units, four nuclear alloy plates, tritium and deuterium."
  ],
  "quest.6007318C5A71DCB1.title": "Quantum Upgrade",
  "quest.6007318C5A71DCB1.quest_subtitle": "Time dilation.",
  "quest.6007318C5A71DCB1.quest_desc": [
    "Thirty-two highly advanced upgrades, eight quantum circuits, a singularity, a quantum board and 50 mB of UU matter. The UU matter drips from a second singularity left in an electrolyzer, never used up: 1 mB every 125 seconds at 40 EU/t. It lifts a machine's cap by 999,999,999 EU/t."
  ],
  "quest.64430FB2641C2CC2.title": "Quantum barrel and tank",
  "quest.64430FB2641C2CC2.quest_subtitle": "Two billion, give or take.",
  "quest.64430FB2641C2CC2.quest_desc": [
    "A quantum hull, a singularity, two quantum circuits, sixteen iridium plates and eight large advanced motors, or pumps for the tank, around a titanium barrel or tank: 2,147,483,647 stacks of one item, or buckets of one fluid."
  ],
  "quest.0557FB3BF06083E3.title": "Quantum armor",
  "quest.0557FB3BF06083E3.quest_subtitle": "Quantum immortality.",
  "quest.0557FB3BF06083E3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Packer fuses a netherite piece with a quantum upgrade at 1,000,000 EU/t, so it needs a quantum upgrade of its own; in this pack each piece also takes a \"},{\"text\":\"Habitation Luminosity\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:luminosity_habitation\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" from Solsticio, act VI. Each piece gives a 25% chance to ignore any damage: the full set, immunity and creative flight.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6EDE6FEA6AE1F57E.title": "Nothing melts down",
  "quest.6EDE6FEA6AE1F57E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The reactor cannot explode, emit radiation or harm the map. When a hatch runs too hot it only destroys what sits in it, so experiment freely: MI's guide suggests trying designs in creative first.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.375EA2771D12EC4F.title": "Fast and thermal",
  "quest.375EA2771D12EC4F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Fuel emits fast neutrons, which carry the energy; scattered, some slow into thermal neutrons, which fuel absorbs far better. Past a temperature threshold a fuel emits fewer neutrons, so a reactor settles by itself. The recipe viewer lists each component's odds.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.36C503EF459A5C6F.title": "Read the grid",
  "quest.36C503EF459A5C6F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The reactor's screen switches between temperature, neutron flux, absorption, generation and fuel views. Watch where heat piles up and where neutrons escape before moving a single rod.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1F7F2D2A6474BFA5.title": "Breed your own tritium",
  "quest.1F7F2D2A6474BFA5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Deuterium with deuterium gives half a bucket of plasma and half a bucket of tritium: a fusion reactor can breed the tritium its faster reactions want.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0BE0CA8DF9D8CF09.title": "What the pack changed",
  "quest.0BE0CA8DF9D8CF09.quest_desc": [
    "Five MI pieces wait on the Atlas: the diesel jetpack (act III), the Electric Quarry and the Gravichestplate (IV), the nuclear reactor and quantum circuits (V), and no assembler recipe skips the gate; each quantum armor piece waits for act VI.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "The Replicator can't be crafted, and the implosion compressor makes no Nether Stars: the Wither stays their only source. Almost Unified gives MI the lowest metal priority, so shared metals come out as another mod's item."
  ],
  "quest.170767E6736997F1.title": "Destroyer of worlds",
  "quest.170767E6736997F1.quest_subtitle": "It doesn't even go off.",
  "quest.170767E6736997F1.quest_desc": [
    "You built a Nuke. Place it and nothing happens: it is a plain block, and sixty-four of them are only the price of a singularity."
  ],
  "reward.14DBBF91D550CFF2.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.53B68F03D8CA6913.title": "Annihilation operator",
  "quest.53B68F03D8CA6913.quest_subtitle": "The wandering trader's llamas have been warned.",
  "quest.53B68F03D8CA6913.quest_desc": [
    "A netherite sword and a quantum upgrade, fused in a packer running 1,000,000 EU/t: a blade with infinite damage."
  ],
  "reward.37B967D86EBF0D06.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.4E4D6A6620138701.title": "Alloy for the common store",
  "quest.4E4D6A6620138701.quest_subtitle": "Handle with tongs.",
  "quest.4E4D6A6620138701.quest_desc": [
    "Sixteen nuclear alloy plates: casings, hatches, fuel rod packs and nukes all start with them."
  ],
  "image.5C9895B7EE4B6114.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Fuel cycle\",\"color\":\"#FFA552\"}]",
  "image.0D14301A84FC02A5.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Quantum tier\",\"color\":\"#FFA552\"}]",
  "image.3F1347CBBA544805.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Modern Industrialization\\nEndgame\",\"color\":\"#FFF1DE\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.5E820409ADF24EBF.title": "Back to the Sun of Heliodor",
  "image.6F923053F79B8444.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» Steam\",\"color\":\"#FFA552\"}]",
  "image.155AA9D124B8A111.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» Electricity\",\"color\":\"#FFA552\"}]",
  "image.7191C8026370F900.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» Digital\",\"color\":\"#FFA552\"}]",
  "image.35C7F231F979627A.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"split  fuse  fold\",\"color\":\"#BFA58A\",\"font\":\"minecraft:alt\"}]",
  "image.3F1B4ECF25FF3FCA.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"fission\",\"color\":\"#7FB069\"}]",
  "image.5BDFD96957A79190.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"fusion\",\"color\":\"#E07BFF\"}]",
  "chapter.1169BE958A7CDC3C.title": "Oritech · Core and Particles",
  "chapter.1169BE958A7CDC3C.chapter_subtitle": [
    "From a uranium pellet to plutonium bred in the ring: the reactor piece by piece, nuclear explosives, the particle accelerator and its collisions, cybernetic augments, arcane machines, frame heads, drones and building blocks."
  ],
  "quest.08B9DDBC899D2CE0.title": "Uranium Pellets",
  "quest.08B9DDBC899D2CE0.quest_subtitle": "Glows a little. That's normal.",
  "quest.08B9DDBC899D2CE0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Uranium veins cling to cave walls and floors between Y -64 and -24. The forge turns copper dust and two raw uranium into a \"},{\"text\":\"Uranium Gem\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:uranium_gem\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; the Assembler presses two gems and plastic with nickel, adamant or duratium into two, three or four \"},{\"text\":\"Uranium Pellets\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:uranium_pellet\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Test a new design on small pellets: they burn a tenth as long, so an overheating reactor goes quiet sooner.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.59937063F0B18650.title": "Nuclear Reactor",
  "quest.59937063F0B18650.quest_subtitle": "Safety first. Or second.",
  "quest.59937063F0B18650.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Reactor Walls\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:reactor_wall\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" frame a box up to 64 per side, with the controller and energy ports set in the walls and a fuel port on the roof above each rod column. Design one layer: a taller reactor repeats it, and its power and fuel use grow with the height.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Each \"},{\"text\":\"Reactor Energy Port\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:reactor_energy_port\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" sends out up to 25,000 RF/t, so a big reactor needs several with superconductors behind them. A rod kept above 2,000 °C for 30 seconds melts down, and sirens sound well before that.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.33DA03D4BC3B6768.title": "Single Rods",
  "quest.33DA03D4BC3B6768.quest_subtitle": "One pulse at a time.",
  "quest.33DA03D4BC3B6768.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Plastic over two energite ingots makes a \"},{\"text\":\"Single Reactor Rod\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:reactor_rod\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Each column of rods needs a \"},{\"text\":\"Reactor Fuel Port\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:reactor_fuel_port\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on the roof above it, and pellets go in there. Alone, a rod pulses once: 64 RF/t per layer and 4 heat a tick.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Every rod burns one unit of fuel per layer each tick. A uranium pellet holds 4,000, a small one 400 and a plutonium pellet 40,000, so a single rod one layer tall runs 200 seconds on one uranium pellet."
  ],
  "quest.3E8F8C5E43AE8117.title": "Heat Pipes and Vents",
  "quest.3E8F8C5E43AE8117.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Reactor Heat Pipe\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:reactor_heat_pipe\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" pulls heat from each hotter neighbour, a quarter of the difference plus 10 a tick. A \"},{\"text\":\"Reactor Heat Vent\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:reactor_vent\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" throws 4 plus a hundredth of its hottest neighbour's heat out of the reactor. Pipes spread a rod's heat; vents get rid of it.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Four gold around an electrum ingot make a pipe; four carbon fibre around a motor, a vent. Vents like it hot: one sheds 14 heat a tick from a part at 1,000 °C and only 5 from one at 100 °C."
  ],
  "quest.61198D825DFF7E02.title": "Quad Rods",
  "quest.61198D825DFF7E02.quest_subtitle": "Twelve pulses, zero chill.",
  "quest.61198D825DFF7E02.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two single rods and a \"},{\"text\":\"Reactor Neutron Reflector\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:reactor_reflector\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make a double; two doubles and another reflector, a \"},{\"text\":\"Reactor Quad Rod\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:reactor_quad_rod\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". On its own it pulses 12 times: 768 RF/t per layer for 76 heat a tick, so it wants cooling on every side.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "It burns four units of fuel per layer each tick, yet gets three times as much RF out of every pellet as a single rod. Neighbouring rods and reflectors push it further: a quad hemmed in by four reflectors reaches 28 pulses and 396 heat."
  ],
  "quest.26A7F7A273919745.title": "Particle Accelerator",
  "quest.26A7F7A273919745.quest_subtitle": "Round and round, faster and faster.",
  "quest.26A7F7A273919745.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Guide rings lay the track, and right-clicking one bends it 45°. Each pass through a powered linear motor adds 1 m/s and costs the particle's speed times 10 RF. The controller shoots any item into a straight ring set right behind it; here it needs an \"},{\"text\":\"Atomic Alloy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:alloy_atomic\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (act V).\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Faster particles turn wider: the last full turn must sit at least the square root of the speed over 2.5 blocks back, and guides can stand up to the square root over 2 apart, 2 to 10. A \"},{\"text\":\"Sensor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:accelerator_sensor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a comparator read the speed; a powered bend becomes a switch.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3C968D4017F06584.title": "Plutonium Breeder",
  "quest.3C968D4017F06584.quest_subtitle": "The ring feeds the core, the core feeds the ring.",
  "quest.3C968D4017F06584.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Uranium dust and fluxite colliding at 2,500 J make \"},{\"text\":\"Plutonium Dust\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:plutonium_dust\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Two dusts, plastic and nickel, adamant or duratium press into two, three or four \"},{\"text\":\"Plutonium Pellets\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:plutonium_pellet\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", and each burns ten times as long as uranium.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A Pulverizer grinds a raw uranium into two uranium dust; the Fragment Forge adds a pinch of plutonium on top.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7AD6481EEC866CF2.title": "Double Rods",
  "quest.7AD6481EEC866CF2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Reactor Double Rod\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:reactor_double_rod\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" pulses four times alone, 256 RF/t per layer for 12 heat, on two units of fuel a tick: twice the RF per pellet of a single rod. Set two side by side and each hits the other with two more pulses.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7F892B66552A6091.title": "Neutron Reflectors",
  "quest.7F892B66552A6091.quest_desc": [
    "Four adamant, four reactor walls and a duratium ingot. Beside a rod, a reflector sends back as many pulses as that rod holds: one for a single, two for a double, four for a quad. It makes no heat itself, but the rod heats up with every extra pulse."
  ],
  "quest.399B196402E6D8D6.title": "Heat Absorbers",
  "quest.399B196402E6D8D6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Reactor Heat Absorber\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:reactor_condenser\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" takes 16 heat a tick from every warm neighbour, 64 when all four sides are hot. It needs a \"},{\"text\":\"Reactor Coolant Absorber Port\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:reactor_absorber_port\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on the roof above its column, fed with ice, and does nothing once the ice runs out.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Ice, packed ice and blue ice count the same: 1,000 units of coolant each, and a working absorber burns one unit per layer every tick. Steel, two ice and four glass make an absorber; the port is a wall, two ice, a hopper and three item pipes."
  ],
  "quest.19ACD06EE59DE4FF.title": "Industrial Chiller",
  "quest.19ACD06EE59DE4FF.quest_subtitle": "Ice, on tap.",
  "quest.19ACD06EE59DE4FF.quest_desc": [
    "Five iron, a motor, a cauldron and two ice, on one core. It freezes a bucket of water into three ice every 200 ticks for 32 RF/t, twice as fast and on half the energy in a cold biome. Pipe the ice straight into the coolant ports.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "A bucket of lava comes out as two obsidian, and a bucket of steam as three snow blocks."
  ],
  "quest.7EA1F6D855C44877.title": "Redstone Port",
  "quest.7EA1F6D855C44877.quest_desc": [
    "A repeater, three processing units, two redstone torches and a wall, set into the reactor's walls. A signal stops the rods from loading new pellets, though what is burning finishes. A comparator reads it: right-click to cycle between hottest part, fuelled rods and stored energy."
  ],
  "quest.54C18F9DB6D1080C.title": "Count the Pulses",
  "quest.54C18F9DB6D1080C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A single rod pulses once, a double four times, a quad twelve; each neighbouring rod or neutron reflector adds more. Every pulse makes 64 RF/t per layer, but heat grows with the square: a lone quad rod gives 768 RF/t and 76 heat.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3DF6FFDA6F86BDD8.title": "Tall, Not Hot",
  "quest.3DF6FFDA6F86BDD8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Height multiplies a reactor's RF, fuel and coolant use, but never its heat, which is counted per column. A layout that stays cool one block tall stays as cool ten blocks tall, with ten times the power. A meltdown still grows with burning rods times height.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.660DAF7C6FE8F21B.title": "Mind the Siren",
  "quest.660DAF7C6FE8F21B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The controller's Warning slider sets when the sirens start: 1,600 °C out of the box. Past 2,000 °C with any rod burning, a 30-second countdown runs; cool the hot part or let the rods burn out before it ends, or the reactor explodes.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1BF611CE9E2A9592.title": "Low-Yield Nuke",
  "quest.1BF611CE9E2A9592.quest_subtitle": "The quiet one of the family.",
  "quest.1BF611CE9E2A9592.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four uranium pellets, three Dubious Containers, TNT and, in this pack, an \"},{\"text\":\"Ironwood Ingot\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:ironwood_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (act IV). Redstone, flint and steel, a fire charge, a burning arrow or another blast sets the \"},{\"text\":\"Low-Yield Nuclear Explosion Device\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:low_yield_nuke\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" off at once: no fuse.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "It blows out a sphere some 21 blocks in radius, then about ten shock waves carve on past it; around the rim, sand turns to glass and logs to basalt."
  ],
  "quest.3BAE5B4AE3AF4BDF.title": "Manhattan Module",
  "quest.3BAE5B4AE3AF4BDF.quest_subtitle": "Measure twice. Detonate never.",
  "quest.3BAE5B4AE3AF4BDF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The same frame with four plutonium pellets and three Heisenberg Compensators, plus the ironwood. The \"},{\"text\":\"Manhattan Module\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:nuke\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" blows out a sphere some 27 blocks in radius and sends thirteen shock waves on from there. It goes off like the small one.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1BCB2D8EADF2C78A.title": "Schrödinger's Safe",
  "quest.1BCB2D8EADF2C78A.quest_subtitle": "Is the nuke in there? Better not check.",
  "quest.1BCB2D8EADF2C78A.quest_desc": [
    "Two Super AI Chips, a flux gate, two duratium, a Large Energy Storage and three fluxite. Right-click it on a dangerous block and that block becomes its core: TNT or a fluxite block hold 6 million RF, a nuke or a dragon egg 20 million, a black hole 100 million.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Enderic Lasers aimed at it don't charge it: while they fire, they stretch its capacity up to 5,000 times. RF leaves from the top and bottom and goes in anywhere else, and it needs clear space around the block to set itself up."
  ],
  "quest.03089564AC1BF337.title": "Pellets for the Common Store",
  "quest.03089564AC1BF337.quest_subtitle": "Some reactor is always hungry.",
  "quest.03089564AC1BF337.quest_desc": [
    "Eight uranium pellets, pressed in the Assembler from gems the forge made. Somebody's reactor on the server is always one pellet short."
  ],
  "quest.5FAF5E3419270BD0.title": "One Fast, One Still",
  "quest.5FAF5E3419270BD0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Collision energy is the sum of both speeds, whatever the items. Bring one particle up to speed, then drop a still one into the same ring: 5,000 m/s against 0 is 5,000 J, and only one of them cost you power.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.52A22D06CBE96EAF.title": "Small Collisions",
  "quest.52A22D06CBE96EAF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"At 500 J two coal dusts fuse into a diamond and two gold dusts into platinum dust; at 1,000 J an ender pearl and an amethyst shard give an \"},{\"text\":\"Echo Shard\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:echo_shard\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; at 2,500 J adamant dust and netherrack give \"},{\"text\":\"Netherite Scrap\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:netherite_scrap\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5F6A465C36624315.title": "Fluxite from the Ring",
  "quest.5F6A465C36624315.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"At 1,000 J electrum dust and redstone fuse into \"},{\"text\":\"Fluxite\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:fluxite\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", no geode or laser needed. At 500 J redstone and rotten flesh make \"},{\"text\":\"Enderic Compound\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:enderic_compound\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", which finally gives every zombie's leftovers a job.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.345798BBD94D033C.title": "Big Collisions",
  "quest.345798BBD94D033C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"At 8,000 J reinforced deepslate, which the forge makes from deepslate and two duratium, meets duratium dust and becomes a \"},{\"text\":\"Heavy Core\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:heavy_core\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". At 10,000 J a feather and a saddle become \"},{\"text\":\"Elytra\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:elytra\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The heavy core becomes the head of an \"},{\"text\":\"Electric Mace\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:electric_mace\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.665121A2D71519A3.title": "Electric Mace",
  "quest.665121A2D71519A3.quest_subtitle": "Thor called. He wants a word.",
  "quest.665121A2D71519A3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Heavy Core\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:heavy_core\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", three adamant, carbon fibre and two advanced batteries. It swings like a mace with 3 more blocks of reach, and a hit calls six lightning bolts down on the target over two and a half seconds, for 16,384 RF, once every 2 seconds.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "It holds 500,000 RF and never breaks. In hand it also lets you fall 10 extra blocks unhurt: climb, jump, strike."
  ],
  "quest.759B10C9F5497A15.title": "Tachyon Absorber",
  "quest.759B10C9F5497A15.quest_desc": [
    "Fast collisions throw tachyons out in random directions, more and farther the harder the hit. Absorbers around the impact turn them back into energy, up to four times what the acceleration cost; each one holds 1,000,000 RF.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Set absorbers farther back to spread the load: past about 10,000 J even distant ones overflow.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.540A49F0F6D548EE.title": "Enderic Railgun",
  "quest.540A49F0F6D548EE.quest_desc": [
    "An Enderic Laser, a linear motor, three adamant and two advanced batteries: a handheld laser holding 5,000,000 RF. Mining mode breaks blocks up to 128 away; combat mode only hits mobs, blasts for 100,000 RF a shot and turns creepers charged.",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Combat mode explodes\",\"color\":\"#FF8C7A\"},{\"text\":\": keep it away from your own walls.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5D43F7D63BCE3C94.title": "Release at Speed",
  "quest.5D43F7D63BCE3C94.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Particle Accelerator Sensor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:accelerator_sensor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" gives a comparator 1 up to 10 m/s, rising in steps to 15 past 15,000. Wire that into a bent guide ring: powered, the bend runs straight, and the particle leaves the loop at the speed you chose.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "A particle that misses a bend flies straight out for about 0.9 times the square root of its speed in blocks, hurting mobs and breaking blocks until its speed is spent. Keep that line clear."
  ],
  "quest.097A60690C3AE668.title": "Portals on Demand",
  "quest.097A60690C3AE668.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Two fire charges colliding above 5,000 J raise a Nether portal on the spot, with netherrack and fire splashed around it. Two ender pearls above 10,000 J open an End portal ringed with end stone and chorus. Both land on whatever stood there.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.111742A794190747.title": "Look into a black hole",
  "quest.58103E5EAD266366.title": "Event Horizon",
  "quest.58103E5EAD266366.quest_subtitle": "Don't feed it the base.",
  "quest.58103E5EAD266366.quest_desc": [
    "A particle faster than 15,000 m/s hit a portal and tore a hole in the world. It swallows blocks up to 16 away, one by one, and throws 50,000 RF of tachyons at an absorber in line for each: a generator that eats the scenery.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A black hole is also the best prisoner for \"},{\"text\":\"Schrödinger's Safe\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"1BCB2D8EADF2C78A\"}},{\"text\":\": five times the storage a nuke gives.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.5B59A377503BC4C0.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.3254C4AE398025A8.title": "Cybernetic Augmentation",
  "quest.3254C4AE398025A8.quest_subtitle": "Flesh is optional.",
  "quest.3254C4AE398025A8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Cybernetic Augmentation Center\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:augment_application_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" sits on ten cores, and each of its up to three research stations needs three more. Walk into the center to research and install permanent upgrades: health, reach, speed, night vision and, from the arcane station, flight.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Hold \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.oritech.augment_screen\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" to switch installed augments on and off.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3CF872C0C453F40D.title": "Cybernetic Research Station",
  "quest.3CF872C0C453F40D.quest_desc": [
    "Five electrum, a redstone block, a brewing stand and two plating, on three cores in one of the center's station spots. It researches the body basics: health, armor, a steel fist, speed, step assist, reach, mining speed, a magnet, an auto-feeder, water breathing, and shrinking or growing.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Research spends RF from the center's own 500,000,000 RF store and items from its five slots or your pockets, then runs 20 seconds to 3 minutes on a free station of the right kind. What you research stays with that center."
  ],
  "quest.18DF62024D48C77F.title": "Quantum Research Station",
  "quest.18DF62024D48C77F.quest_desc": [
    "Five duratium, a flux gate, a Centrifuge and two plating. It takes the body further: two +10 health upgrades, the Aegis System's 8 armor, Flash Steps, Hyper Mining Speed, Far Reach, Weapon Reach and Night Vision."
  ],
  "quest.730F3C6A6C7D4F37.title": "Arcane Research Station",
  "quest.730F3C6A6C7D4F37.quest_desc": [
    "Five overcharged crystals, an enderic lens, an eye of ender and two plating. It holds the strange ones: Flight, Reduced Gravity, a Portal home, Cloak, Ore Vision, Luck and Psionic Strikes."
  ],
  "quest.0EEC0FAABCF17CA8.title": "Biosteel",
  "quest.0EEC0FAABCF17CA8.quest_subtitle": "Grown, not mined.",
  "quest.0EEC0FAABCF17CA8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Raw biopolymer and an iron ingot in the Foundry make a \"},{\"text\":\"Biosteel Ingot\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:biosteel_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Four augments ask for it by name: Steel-Infused Frame, Carbon-Reinforced Lungs, Synthetic Muscles and Water Breathing. Here it stays its own metal instead of turning into steel.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Raw biopolymer comes from a centrifuge with a Fluid Addon: packed wheat and a quarter bucket of water.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5724CB0305FC591C.title": "Body Work",
  "quest.5724CB0305FC591C.quest_subtitle": "Dents out, hearts in.",
  "quest.5724CB0305FC591C.quest_desc": [
    "Health climbs through Steel-Infused Frame (+6), Carbon-Reinforced Lungs (+4), Hyper-Redundancy Matrix (+10) and Living Fortress (+10): fifteen extra hearts. Armor adds 4, 6 and 8. The Matrix, the Aegis System and the Fortress want Nether Stars, and this pack's accelerator doesn't make them."
  ],
  "quest.51A807F75F0BC982.title": "Moving Parts",
  "quest.51A807F75F0BC982.quest_desc": [
    "Synthetic Muscles add 25% speed and Flash Steps far more; Step Assist walks up 0.6 blocks; Mining Speed doubles your digging and Hyper Mining Speed doubles it again. The Magnet, whose research eats two lodestones, pulls loose items from 8 blocks away.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Block Reach adds 30% and Far Reach doubles whatever you have; Weapon Reach adds 30% to melee. The Auto-Feeder eats the best harmless food in your inventory whenever you're two points hungry."
  ],
  "quest.23F5595F01C12F68.title": "Second Sight",
  "quest.23F5595F01C12F68.quest_desc": [
    "Night Vision, from the quantum station, keeps the dark lit for good. Ore Vision, from the arcane one, outlines every ore within 16 blocks through the rock; its research eats a spyglass, a sculk sensor and a prometheum ingot. Cloak makes you invisible."
  ],
  "quest.3CFC165EEB1E3B04.title": "Flight",
  "quest.3CFC165EEB1E3B04.quest_subtitle": "Creative mode, paid in full.",
  "quest.3CFC165EEB1E3B04.quest_desc": [
    "Free flight from the arcane station, once Reactive Plating and Portal are researched. The research takes 64 ion thrusters, 16 wind charges, 16 prometheum, 32 plutonium pellets and 500 million RF; installing it, four more thrusters.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Reduced Gravity follows and halves your weight. Portal, installed at the center, opens a door back to it wherever you switch it on."
  ],
  "quest.168FFC0A8124663A.title": "Catalyst and Enchanter",
  "quest.168FFC0A8124663A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Arcane Catalyst\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:enchantment_catalyst_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" stores the souls of mobs dying within 23 blocks: 50 at most, one more for every 20 RF/t a laser feeds it. The \"},{\"text\":\"Stabilized Enchanter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:enchanter_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" spends souls and power to apply exactly the enchantment you pick, one level at a time.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"It needs soul-holding catalysts within 16 blocks, as many as the enchantment's cost plus the level it aims for. \"},{\"text\":\"A catalyst holding more souls than it can take explodes after three seconds\",\"color\":\"#FF8C7A\"},{\"text\":\", so keep its laser running. A max-level book placed in one pushes an item past the vanilla cap, at an exponential soul bill.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4C36F0D342D15AD3.title": "Spawner Controller",
  "quest.4C36F0D342D15AD3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The first mob to walk over the controller sets its type for good, bosses aside here; build the cage it highlights underneath. Each spawn costs souls, the square root of the mob's health. Here the controller takes an \"},{\"text\":\"Ironwood Ingot\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:ironwood_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (act IV).\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Soul Flowers\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"0FEBBC0EEBC59A59\"}},{\"text\":\" give it souls without killing anything.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0FEBBC0EEBC59A59.title": "Soul Flowers",
  "quest.0FEBBC0EEBC59A59.quest_subtitle": "Nobody died for these.",
  "quest.0FEBBC0EEBC59A59.quest_desc": [
    "Three wither roses and two flowers make one. Plant it on soul soil in light 9 or brighter; broken by hand once fully grown, it lets out a soul for a nearby catalyst or spawner controller. Bone meal speeds it up."
  ],
  "quest.4CF9F7061C7E44ED.title": "Past the Cap",
  "quest.4CF9F7061C7E44ED.quest_subtitle": "Ten is just a number.",
  "quest.4CF9F7061C7E44ED.quest_desc": [
    "An item with an enchantment at level ten. The catalyst's hyper enchanting goes further still, and every extra level costs exponentially more souls."
  ],
  "reward.22F187CE0E28B0F2.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.6FD6C7FAEFE40674.title": "Taint a Refinery",
  "quest.6FD6C7FAEFE40674.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Blow up a Refinery while an Arcane Catalyst holding at least one soul sits within 6 blocks: the catalyst goes off too, and a Tainted Refinery stands where the refinery was. It can't be crafted, and breaking it gives back a plain refinery.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "In its line of sight within 16 blocks, sculk, spawners and cages multiply its yield up to three times, and bookshelves, amethyst and soul lights make each RF count up to nine times. Sixteen blocks of four kinds max out either."
  ],
  "task.07387C432BDB1F86.title": "Look at a Tainted Refinery",
  "quest.7FFA2A7B5EBBC2F2.title": "Happy Accident",
  "quest.7FFA2A7B5EBBC2F2.quest_subtitle": "It was like that when I got here.",
  "quest.7FFA2A7B5EBBC2F2.quest_desc": [
    "A Refinery blew up next to a charged Arcane Catalyst and came back tainted. It swallows all the power you feed it, runs faster with arcane blocks in sight, yields more with sculk around, and keeps a single output."
  ],
  "reward.0288F455E7F79756.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.2749BEE5AECFECFB.title": "Machine Frames",
  "quest.2749BEE5AECFECFB.quest_desc": [
    "Nickel and iron bars make sixteen. Lay them as a hollow rectangle up to 64 long: gantry machines clamp onto any edge, even a corner, and work the layer below the frame. Several machines can share one frame."
  ],
  "quest.5F6088ECCC71303A.title": "Block Destroyer",
  "quest.5F6088ECCC71303A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An Enderic Laser, a Pulverizer, four motors and plating. On a frame it breaks the layer below; each \"},{\"text\":\"Quarry Addon\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:quarry_addon\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" multiplies its depth by eight: 8, 64, then 512 blocks. On a laser the same addon widens the beam by one.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1B9F4BAE282690A5.title": "Farms on a Frame",
  "quest.1B9F4BAE282690A5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Placer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:placer_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" plants seeds and saplings only where they can grow; the \"},{\"text\":\"Fertilizer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:fertilizer_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" hydrates the farmland and boosts growth for a quarter bucket per block, far stronger on mineral slurry. A crop filter on the Destroyer leaves unripe crops alone.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Tree Cutter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:treefeller_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" needs no frame: it fells whole trees in front of it, up to 8,000 blocks each, and keeps the saplings and fruit.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4586998E1BEFA974.title": "Heads with Manners",
  "quest.4586998E1BEFA974.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"On a Block Destroyer or an Enderic Laser, a \"},{\"text\":\"Silk Touch Addon\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:machine_silk_touch_addon\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" keeps blocks whole, each \"},{\"text\":\"Yield Addon\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:machine_yield_addon\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" adds a level of Fortune up to three, and a \"},{\"text\":\"Crop Filter Addon\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:crop_filter_addon\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" leaves unripe crops standing. Silk touch wins over yield.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"On a laser with a Hunter Addon, yield turns into Looting instead.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.386CE7DAA46B48F5.title": "Drone Port",
  "quest.386CE7DAA46B48F5.quest_desc": [
    "Two ports on eleven cores each, at least 50 blocks apart and linked with the designator, fly items between bases in a fixed time; with a Fluid Addon on both, fluids too. The energy grows with the square root of the distance, and both ends must be loaded.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A port sends to one place but receives from many; a busy sender can clog a receiver for the rest.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3BF719F96BE57EE6.title": "Control Unit",
  "quest.3BF719F96BE57EE6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Five redstone, a comparator, two repeaters and plating. On any machine, a \"},{\"text\":\"Control Unit Addon\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:machine_redstone_addon\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" either stops it while it gets a signal or feeds a comparator its energy, one slot, its progress or whether it's working. Right-click the addon to choose.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "On a Drone Port, working means a drone in the air, so one comparator tells you when a shipment left or landed."
  ],
  "task.41E3E22CD025D166.title": "Any 16 plating blocks",
  "quest.18F4435B93B9BE5F.title": "Reinforced Plating",
  "quest.18F4435B93B9BE5F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four stone, four steel and copper, iron or nickel make two \"},{\"text\":\"Copper Reinforced Plating\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:machine_plating_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" or its iron and nickel twins; a reinforced carbon sheet makes the carbon one. Every recipe that asks for plating takes any of the four, and each has a slab, stairs and a pressure plate.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.617F754A77AF1BD7.title": "Glass, Beams and Lights",
  "quest.617F754A77AF1BD7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four glass, four steel and plating make four \"},{\"text\":\"Industrial Glass\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:industrial_glass_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", far tougher than glass. Steel and carbon fibre make six \"},{\"text\":\"Industrial Support Beams\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:metal_beam_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" or six girders, and a machine frame joins onto a beam above or below it.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Six steel and three glowstone dust make six \"},{\"text\":\"Industrial Lights\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:ceiling_light\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", always on; hang one from a chain for a high ceiling.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.19A932A06F6C851A.title": "Doors and Buttons",
  "quest.19A932A06F6C851A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Six steel make an \"},{\"text\":\"Industrial Door\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:tech_door\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; seven steel and two motors, an \"},{\"text\":\"Industrial Hangar Door\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:hangar_door\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", 1×3 and moved by redstone alone. Hangar doors that touch open together on one signal, and an \"},{\"text\":\"Industrial Button\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"oritech:tech_button\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" holds its pulse for four seconds.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.402ED6204D3F294F.title": "Any 4 machine paints",
  "quest.0FF93D869BAC6E34.title": "Machine Paints",
  "quest.0FF93D869BAC6E34.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Each of the nine paints is two plastic plates, a pair of colourants and one core item, for four. Sneak (\"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.sneak\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\") and right-click a machine or any of its cores to repaint the whole multiblock for one paint; the netherite one really takes two netherite ingots.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.59E765E8AAEF364F.title": "Any 4 pipe ducts",
  "task.1C39577724FE9F4D.title": "Any 8 framed pipes",
  "quest.0A3C4C6A1C969C8F.title": "Pipes in the Walls",
  "quest.0A3C4C6A1C969C8F.quest_desc": [
    "Four pipes, four stone and plating make four ducts: full blocks that carry what their pipe carries and join pipes and other ducts, never a machine. Eight pipes around plating make eight framed pipes, and eight item pipes around glass turn see-through."
  ],
  "image.75A1EDEF6A0C38D0.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Nuclear explosives\",\"color\":\"#F0A24A\"}]",
  "image.3F187718F602C8F2.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Cybernetic augments\",\"color\":\"#F0A24A\"}]",
  "image.790ACC0303C721DF.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Arcane machines\",\"color\":\"#F0A24A\"}]",
  "image.1F73ECDCA09DC630.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Frame heads\",\"color\":\"#F0A24A\"}]",
  "image.3BA65CE01C309F43.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Drones\",\"color\":\"#F0A24A\"}]",
  "image.4BDEB965DB169FD9.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Building blocks\",\"color\":\"#F0A24A\"}]",
  "image.488D3F4E287A452D.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Oritech\",\"color\":\"#FFF1DC\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.184240CC8D627D86.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"core and particles\",\"color\":\"#3A2A18\"}]",
  "image.7B6B6C2F60F54676.title": "Back to Oritech",
  "image.5C5E989B63AD457E.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"burn · cool · accelerate · collide\",\"color\":\"#C9A77A\",\"font\":\"minecraft:alt\"}]",
  "image.219439E288CA42D2.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Nuclear reactor\",\"color\":\"#F0A24A\"}]",
  "image.4B41EE74FB1FF568.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Particle\\naccelerator\",\"color\":\"#A9C7CE\"}]",
  "chapter.23EBFFCF7DB0326C.title": "Magic in ENTRELUMEN",
  "chapter.23EBFFCF7DB0326C.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Which schools open in each act, and the Atlas components that tie them together."
  ],
  "quest.64B2A5E5963EA9CE.title": "Many schools, no walls",
  "quest.64B2A5E5963EA9CE.quest_desc": [
    "You can play the whole story leaning on a few schools. What ties them together are the Atlas components, story items made from magic materials: every team touches Ars Nouveau, Occultism, Malum, EvilCraft and Nature's Aura at least once.",
    "",
    "Heliodor ran on light. You'll run on whatever works."
  ],
  "quest.37C01E0CCF31B45B.title": "Which school for what",
  "quest.37C01E0CCF31B45B.quest_desc": [
    "Fights: Iron's Spells. Utility and automation: Ars Nouveau. Working spirits: Occultism. Alchemical ores: Theurgy. Growing the world: Nature's Aura. Souls: Malum. Dark forging: Forbidden and Arcanus. Blood and brooms: EvilCraft. Relics: Reliquary. Programmed spells: Psi. Blood circles: Mahou Tsukai. Gear: Apotheosis.",
    "",
    "Master one or two; taste the rest."
  ],
  "quest.3F94947246CE6851.title": "Act I: the first sparks",
  "quest.3F94947246CE6851.quest_desc": [
    "No magic required yet, but doors are open: bookshelves take the table toward 30, Apotheosis starts at Haven, EvilCraft's dark ore shows up around redstone depth, and Artifacts turn up in chests.",
    "",
    "Stock up on books, lapis and gold."
  ],
  "quest.2C0E497095FC1CAA.title": "Act II: the magic act",
  "quest.2C0E497095FC1CAA.quest_desc": [
    "Most schools open: Ars, Occultism, Nature's Aura, Iron's Spells, Forbidden and Arcanus, Theurgy, the first relics and EvilCraft's blood. The table reaches 45. The story asks for Ars: the Living Matrix, delivered to «Living Workshop»."
  ],
  "quest.4051B723D469D474.title": "A Matrix for the Atlas",
  "quest.4051B723D469D474.quest_desc": [
    "Two magebloom fibers and two Source Gems in a cross around a Calibration Frame. Beyond the Act II delivery, Matrices go into the Propagation Core (Act III) and the Ecosystem Capsule (Act IV): a steady Ars workshop pays off for a long time."
  ],
  "quest.16714199FE6F628C.title": "Act III: deeper magic",
  "quest.16714199FE6F628C.quest_desc": [
    "Psi and Mahou Tsukai arrive. Put Occultism's spirits to work and start Malum's soul research: Act IV needs both. The table reaches 60, the first spawner augments appear, and the World Tier rises to Frontier, invaders included.",
    "",
    "Salvage the affix gear you don't use."
  ],
  "quest.3164104B39F3F774.title": "Act IV: voices and seals",
  "quest.3164104B39F3F774.quest_desc": [
    "Magic supplies two key components: the Spectral Lens and the Containment Seal. They unlock Theurgy's transmutation, the Eternal Stella, shelves up to 90, the Act IV augments and, with a Horizon Chart, the Rending Gale. World Tier: Ascent."
  ],
  "quest.157613639B482C59.title": "The Spectral Lens",
  "quest.157613639B482C59.quest_desc": [
    "An Occultism attuned crystal, two Malum arcane spirits, a Create precision mechanism and a Calibration Frame. Deliver one to «Voices in the Glass» and keep making them: the Seal, reinforced machines, shelves and the Arcane Module use it.",
    "",
    "Glass that hears what isn't said."
  ],
  "quest.51EE903C0C24FFF6.title": "Seal of the dark schools",
  "quest.51EE903C0C24FFF6.quest_desc": [
    "Two EvilCraft dark gems, two Malum Soulstained Steel and a Spectral Lens. Delivered to «A Vessel for Restless Memory», it gives your team an Altar of Time. It also gates the Eternal Stella, Theurgy's emitter, the fission reactor, the Burning augment and the Atlas Library."
  ],
  "quest.0690F6AE03FF5F8F.title": "Act V: the Ark",
  "quest.0690F6AE03FF5F8F.quest_desc": [
    "Two Ark pieces are magical: the Renewal Engine (Nature's Aura, farming and bees) and the Arcane Module (every dark school). The table reaches 100, the Atlas Library opens up, and at Summit tier Mythic loot and Godforged Pearls start to drop."
  ],
  "quest.523AB48D42660EA3.title": "An engine that grows gardens",
  "quest.523AB48D42660EA3.quest_desc": [
    "Two Ingots of the Skies, two imperium essences, two Ecosystem Capsules and two Propagation Cores. Deliver one to «Renewable Horizons»; more go into the Nature Module, Mekanism's SPS, the Mega pots and Act V augments.",
    "",
    "The gardens come back, one engine at a time."
  ],
  "quest.112D4E9BD5A29894.title": "The Arcane Module",
  "quest.112D4E9BD5A29894.quest_desc": [
    "Two Spectral Lenses, two Containment Seals, an iesnium ingot and the Wither's nether star. In a complete Ark it resets an item's anvil penalty for books and XP, keeping enchantments, affixes and sockets. Iesnium needs Occultism's infused pickaxe: plan ahead."
  ],
  "quest.318923AC1CC86BDE.title": "Act VI: light made solid",
  "quest.318923AC1CC86BDE.quest_desc": [
    "Solsticio's villagers sell six Luminosities, one per discipline; violet Arcane is magic's. They make the Luminous ingot and the creative items: the Source Jar for Ars, the Blood Drop for EvilCraft, the bookshelf for Create: Enchantment Industry. World Tier: Pinnacle."
  ],
  "quest.2E7C7D0C1E3A8844.title": "Where the magic keys went",
  "quest.2E7C7D0C1E3A8844.quest_desc": [
    "Ars radial: F6. Iron's wheel: the key left of 1, cast: Alt+Q. Psi: Alt+F. Mahou Tsukai's circle: Alt+M. Occultism's satchel: Insert, ender bag: O. Apotheosis: Ctrl+T World Tiers, Ctrl+O radial mining, Shift+T link item. All changeable under Controls."
  ],
  "quest.450143F1ED9D1D09.title": "Shortcuts the pack closed",
  "quest.450143F1ED9D1D09.quest_desc": [
    "Reliquary's Alkahestry Tome (item duplication) and its spawn-egg crafting, Apotheosis's spawner runes (copper augments replace them) and portable spawners. Everything else keeps its native recipe unless its chapter says otherwise.",
    "",
    "Every school keeps its place in line."
  ],
  "quest.5A233C6A570EB457.title": "Every school has a book",
  "quest.5A233C6A570EB457.quest_desc": [
    "Most guides craft from a book: Tattered Tome (Ars), Dictionary of Spirits (Occultism), Encyclopedia Arcana (Malum), Book of Natural Aura, Chronicle of Shadows (Apotheosis), Knowledge Compendium (Mahou Tsukai). EvilCraft's is chest loot, Psi's is cast onto a book, Reliquary uses EMI."
  ],
  "quest.60B4CFB438EA8E87.title": "Magic that belongs to the story",
  "quest.60B4CFB438EA8E87.quest_desc": [
    "Living Matrices from your Ars workshop, lenses and seals from the dark schools, a Renewal Engine that grows the world back and an Arcane Module that listens. Magic is half of what the Atlas asks for, and which half is yours to pick.",
    "",
    "The light came back. Part of it was yours."
  ],
  "chapter.6C4A35CBE27ABDD9.title": "Ars Nouveau",
  "chapter.6C4A35CBE27ABDD9.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Four schools on one circle: spellcraft, Source, rituals and the creatures that do the chores."
  ],
  "quest.15546909CB740D3E.title": "Four tools for one book",
  "quest.15546909CB740D3E.quest_subtitle": "The blacksmith weeps. The scholar shrugs.",
  "quest.15546909CB740D3E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A book plus an iron shovel, pickaxe, axe and sword, all consumed: the \"},{\"text\":\"Novice Spell Book\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:novice_spell_book\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It casts tier 1 glyphs and keeps every glyph you learn through each upgrade.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2C02AB120B59CEC5.title": "The Tattered Tome",
  "quest.2C02AB120B59CEC5.quest_subtitle": "It never says 'I told you so'.",
  "quest.2C02AB120B59CEC5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A book and a lapis: the \"},{\"text\":\"Tattered Tome\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:worn_notebook\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", Ars's own manual. Every glyph, ritual, machine and creature, with its recipe. Nobody hands it to you here: craft it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0C1577A49BF96193.title": "Write, then cast",
  "quest.0C1577A49BF96193.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"With the book in your hotbar, \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.ars_nouveau.open_book\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" opens spellcrafting: click glyphs into the bottom row, name the spell, save it to a slot, right-click to cast. First spell: Projectile, Break. Aim away from the house.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.379561AE02FBE13A.title": "Archwood",
  "quest.379561AE02FBE13A.quest_desc": [
    "Some Overworld forests are Archwood Forests, with trees in four colours; lone ones grow, rarely, in any biome. Planks and slabs build the scribe's table and the jars; each log colour goes into a ritual tablet.",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Plant the saplings at home. A grove by the door beats an expedition a week.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4F4C641A8B25C1DF.title": "A stick that finds geodes",
  "quest.4F4C641A8B25C1DF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Archwood planks and a gold ingot make a \"},{\"text\":\"Dowsing Rod\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:dowsing_rod\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Each use briefly shows budding amethyst and magic creatures nearby. Geodes are the easy early amethyst for Source Gems.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.432DA860F1086112.title": "To die for",
  "quest.432DA860F1086112.quest_subtitle": "Technically, a fruit.",
  "quest.432DA860F1086112.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"You ate a \"},{\"text\":\"Bombegranate\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:bombegranate_pod\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". The name was a warning, and you read it as a menu.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.2C3EE13CDDDCF2AC.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.259634AEB1E1C72A.title": "The Scribe's Table",
  "quest.259634AEB1E1C72A.quest_subtitle": "It eats whatever you drop. Don't drop dinner.",
  "quest.259634AEB1E1C72A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Use your book on a \"},{\"text\":\"Scribe's Table\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:scribes_table\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", pick a glyph, drop in the items it lists and pay the experience. The glyph item teaches it. It also pulls from inventories next to it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.73E32446AA1C3E4F.title": "Grammar with consequences",
  "quest.73E32446AA1C3E4F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"One Form first (Projectile flies, Touch hits close, Self hits you), then Effects. An augment only changes the glyph to its left. The book's tier caps the glyph tier: novice 1, mage 2, archmage 3.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5C48B88C95EB53EF.title": "Amplify eats a diamond pick",
  "quest.5C48B88C95EB53EF.quest_subtitle": "The pick dies so the spell can dig.",
  "quest.5C48B88C95EB53EF.quest_desc": [
    "The table consumes a diamond pickaxe for Amplify. After Break it raises the harvest tier; after Harm, the damage. It stacks, and so does the mana cost."
  ],
  "quest.2EBEB756212DF370.title": "Every glyph pays rent",
  "quest.2EBEB756212DF370.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A spell costs the sum of its glyphs. Every glyph you learn also raises your maximum mana, even the ones you never cast; book tiers, robes and trinkets add more.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.487A0352D4FD90EA.title": "Projectile",
  "quest.487A0352D4FD90EA.quest_subtitle": "Point, click, no regrets.",
  "quest.487A0352D4FD90EA.quest_desc": [
    "You know it from the first page. The bolt flies until it hits something and runs the rest of the spell there, for 10 mana. Accelerate and Decelerate set its speed, each Split adds a bolt, Pierce goes through one more target and Sensitive makes it hit grass and flowers."
  ],
  "quest.71B6DB10E0AA2FFE.title": "Touch",
  "quest.71B6DB10E0AA2FFE.quest_subtitle": "Magic at arm's length.",
  "quest.71B6DB10E0AA2FFE.quest_desc": [
    "Also known from the start. It works on the block or creature you use the book on, for 5 mana, and fizzles in empty air. Touch, Break is a pickaxe that never wears out; Sensitive lets it reach air and fluids too."
  ],
  "quest.14319B4522649B40.title": "Self",
  "quest.14319B4522649B40.quest_subtitle": "Self-care, arcane edition.",
  "quest.14319B4522649B40.quest_desc": [
    "The third form you start with. The spell lands on you, for 10 mana, and takes no augments: Self, Leap throws you where you look; Self, Heal mends you for a little hunger; Self, Conjure Magelight gives night vision."
  ],
  "quest.350AF559923FE36B.title": "Underfoot",
  "quest.350AF559923FE36B.quest_subtitle": "Dig straight down. Carefully.",
  "quest.350AF559923FE36B.quest_desc": [
    "Iron boots and a wooden pressure plate teach it at the table: a tier 1 form, 5 mana, that hits the block you stand on. Underfoot, Break digs straight down; add AOE and the floor opens three by three."
  ],
  "quest.1F038A78334231A5.title": "Pantomime",
  "quest.1F038A78334231A5.quest_subtitle": "Mime a wall until there is one.",
  "quest.1F038A78334231A5.quest_desc": [
    "Eight glass blocks teach it at the table: a tier 1 form, 5 mana, that hits the spot two blocks past your eyes, air or not, three when you look down. Amplify pushes it a block out, Dampen pulls it in; Pantomime, Conjure Mageblock builds on nothing."
  ],
  "quest.1B497A4C308EA5AD.title": "Magelight, not torches",
  "quest.1B497A4C308EA5AD.quest_desc": [
    "A lantern and a torch teach Conjure Magelight. On a block it leaves a permanent light; on yourself, night vision. Projectile plus Magelight lights a cave from across the room."
  ],
  "quest.2413D4FAA7DEC70D.title": "No loot in lava",
  "quest.2413D4FAA7DEC70D.quest_desc": [
    "Two hoppers teach Item Pickup: it pulls in the drops where the spell lands. After Break, the ore comes to you instead of taking a lava bath."
  ],
  "quest.5CA2AB5806697427.title": "A spell that digs",
  "quest.5CA2AB5806697427.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Projectile, Break, Amplify, AOE, Item Pickup: a 3×3 face at range, drops collected. For ores add Extract or Luck after Break, never both. Three good slots beat ten half-written ones.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4D872E563C2A08FE.title": "The Mage's Spell Book",
  "quest.4D872E563C2A08FE.quest_subtitle": "Blaze rods mean the Nether. Pack a lunch.",
  "quest.4D872E563C2A08FE.quest_desc": [
    "Your novice book plus obsidian, diamonds, quartz blocks and blaze rods; every glyph carries over. It unlocks tier 2 glyphs and more mana."
  ],
  "quest.4A5CA3AB42662843.title": "Think in squares",
  "quest.4A5CA3AB42662843.quest_desc": [
    "A firework star teaches AOE, tier 2. Each AOE after an effect widens it around the target: one on Break mines 3×3. It widens Pickup, Smelt and others too."
  ],
  "quest.43D4ABD3B4D1EAA2.title": "Extract or Luck",
  "quest.43D4ABD3B4D1EAA2.quest_desc": [
    "An emerald teaches Extract: Break acts with silk touch. Luck, from a rabbit's foot, adds drops instead. Both are tier 2 and refuse to share a spell."
  ],
  "quest.46E0D864D0E37AEE.title": "Imbuement Chamber",
  "quest.46E0D864D0E37AEE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An item inside an \"},{\"text\":\"Imbuement Chamber\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:imbuement_chamber\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" soaks up Source until it changes. Alone it gathers a trickle; jars within two blocks make it fast. Side items sit on pedestals and are not consumed.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.620B3140D18DC266.title": "Source Gems",
  "quest.620B3140D18DC266.quest_subtitle": "Purple is the colour of 'not enough yet'.",
  "quest.620B3140D18DC266.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Imbue an amethyst shard or a lapis for 500 Source: one \"},{\"text\":\"Source Gem\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:source_gem\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Almost every Ars recipe wants them. A budding amethyst geode is the renewable supply.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7985E5BBF62B2095.title": "A piggy bank that glows",
  "quest.7985E5BBF62B2095.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Archwood slabs top and bottom, glass on the sides: a \"},{\"text\":\"Source Jar\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:source_jar\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Machines, rituals and creatures drink from jars nearby; a comparator reads the level, and a broken jar keeps its Source.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.63936B61C6CCE928.title": "Making Source",
  "quest.63936B61C6CCE928.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An \"},{\"text\":\"Agronomic Sourcelink\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:agronomic_sourcelink\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" turns crops and trees growing nearby into \"},{\"text\":\"Source\",\"color\":\"#D8C8FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_text\",\"contents\":\"Ars's power: jars store it, relays move it, the apparatus and some rituals spend it.\"}},{\"text\":\" for jars within five blocks; magic plants count extra, bonemeal doesn't. Its siblings eat food, deaths, fuel or potions.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0E9DF5090BA3B399.title": "The volcanic link melts floors",
  "quest.0E9DF5090BA3B399.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The Volcanic Sourcelink burns fuel and pays best for archwood. Its heat turns nearby stone into magma, then lava: build it on a floor you can lose, away from wood.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.009AAD8E3CEA0FAE.title": "Berries for two links",
  "quest.009AAD8E3CEA0FAE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Sourceberries\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:sourceberry_bush\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" count as magic plants for an agronomic link, and berries and pie beat plain food in a mycelial one. Eating them restores mana.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.748221FDB6430A60.title": "Source tithe",
  "quest.748221FDB6430A60.quest_subtitle": "The circle keeps a ledger.",
  "quest.748221FDB6430A60.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Sixteen \"},{\"text\":\"Source Gems\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:source_gem\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for the common store, once a day. A geode, a golem and a chamber make it painless.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6203913FCF726BDD.title": "Sourcestone and pedestals",
  "quest.6203913FCF726BDD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight stone around a Source Gem give eight \"},{\"text\":\"Sourcestone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:sourcestone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; with gold nuggets and a gem it becomes an \"},{\"text\":\"Arcane Pedestal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:arcane_pedestal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Make four for side ingredients.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3D5F2958796F6901.title": "Elemental essences",
  "quest.3D5F2958796F6901.quest_desc": [
    "A Source Gem in the chamber plus three items on pedestals, 2000 Source: an essence. Earth takes an iron ingot, seeds and dirt. Only the gem is spent, so leave the pedestals set."
  ],
  "quest.47F1C61D11319558.title": "Arcane Core",
  "quest.47F1C61D11319558.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Sourcestone around two gold ingots and a Source Gem. The apparatus only works with an \"},{\"text\":\"Arcane Core\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:arcane_core\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" right below it: build them as one piece, with room for pedestals around.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.70166A508E203421.title": "Enchanting Apparatus",
  "quest.70166A508E203421.quest_desc": [
    "It sits on the core. Side ingredients go on pedestals within three blocks, then you use the central item on it; Source comes from jars nearby. Charms, armour, rings and magebloom seeds are born here."
  ],
  "quest.28007D969FECC081.title": "Enchanting without dice",
  "quest.28007D969FECC081.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The apparatus applies vanilla enchantments one level at a time: tool in the centre, items on pedestals, each level after the previous one. From 2000 Source for level I up to 9000. Exact, no dice.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.40ABFF9AE882714A.title": "Thinking with prisms",
  "quest.40ABFF9AE882714A.quest_subtitle": "The spell went round the houses.",
  "quest.40ABFF9AE882714A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"One spell redirected by four \"},{\"text\":\"Spell Prisms\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:spell_prism\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Nobody asked the spell whether it wanted the scenic route.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.4C4A5190A402C7E1.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.4A9AE22AE00B592E.title": "Cable management, magic edition",
  "quest.4A9AE22AE00B592E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A stick with two Source Gems and a gold ingot in the apparatus: the \"},{\"text\":\"Dominion Wand\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:dominion_wand\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Use it on a source, then on a target: jar to relay, creature to chest. Sneak-use clears a relay's links.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.65604676A34768EC.title": "Source on the move",
  "quest.65604676A34768EC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Wand-link jar, \"},{\"text\":\"Source Relay\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:relay\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", distant jar: up to 30 blocks a hop; redstone stops it. Upgraded relays collect from or fill every jar nearby.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.61BC93666A3CB4A1.title": "Magebloom",
  "quest.61BC93666A3CB4A1.quest_subtitle": "A flower that pays for itself.",
  "quest.61BC93666A3CB4A1.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Any seeds ringed by four Source Gems in the apparatus give a \"},{\"text\":\"Magebloom Seed\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:magebloom_crop\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; \"},{\"text\":\"next to an agronomic link it adds Source while it grows\",\"color\":\"#9BE08A\"},{\"text\":\". Each bloom crafts into four \"},{\"text\":\"Magebloom Fiber\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:magebloom_fiber\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", Ars's cloth.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.539A03F5CDA2B0CF.title": "Robes over plate",
  "quest.539A03F5CDA2B0CF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A golden chestplate and four fiber in the apparatus: \"},{\"text\":\"Sorcerer's Wrap\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:sorcerer_robes\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", with mana regen and thread slots. Blank thread becomes a perk thread in the apparatus; the alteration table sews it in.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3F84D749D6ADB214.title": "The Living Matrix",
  "quest.3F84D749D6ADB214.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A cross: \"},{\"text\":\"Source Gems\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:source_gem\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" above and below, \"},{\"text\":\"Magebloom Fiber\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:magebloom_fiber\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" at the sides and a \"},{\"text\":\"Calibration Frame\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:calibration_frame\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in the middle. It moves the story only when delivered to \"},{\"text\":\"Living Workshop\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"7A2C3D602817EC20\"}},{\"text\":\" in the Atlas, and later acts ask for more.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2F3E42797FDBC5DD.title": "Ritual Brazier",
  "quest.2F3E42797FDBC5DD.quest_subtitle": "Spells too big for a book.",
  "quest.2F3E42797FDBC5DD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An arcane pedestal, a Source Gem block and three gold ingots: the \"},{\"text\":\"Ritual Brazier\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:ritual_brazier\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It casts rituals from tablets, and many drink Source from jars within six blocks. Redstone pauses the one running.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.350D28FB512A0937.title": "Tablet, augments, empty hand",
  "quest.350D28FB512A0937.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Use the tablet on the brazier, throw augment items on top, then start it with an empty hand; the tablet is spent. Log colour hints the theme: green grows, red burns, blue is water and sky, purple binds.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.68D703CB2F0A1672.title": "Sunrise, on demand",
  "quest.68D703CB2F0A1672.quest_subtitle": "For once, the sun comes up when you say.",
  "quest.68D703CB2F0A1672.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A red archwood log, three dandelions and a clock make the \"},{\"text\":\"Sunrise\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:ritual_sunrise\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" tablet: it makes it day. Cheap and instant, the best way to learn the brazier.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.617FC8B4C2F0CBFD.title": "More tablets worth a log",
  "quest.617FC8B4C2F0CBFD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Cloudshaping sets the weather. Fertility breeds animals. Disintegration kills monsters for experience, no drops. Burrowing digs to bedrock. Forestation and Flowering reshape the land.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.671E9DA04BF8532A.title": "A quiet base",
  "quest.671E9DA04BF8532A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"While \"},{\"text\":\"Sanctuary\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:ritual_sanctuary\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" runs, no hostile mob spawns naturally within 32 blocks; rotten flesh thrown in before starting widens it. It only charges Source when it actually blocks a spawn.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6906CC2C09BAA8A8.title": "See through stone",
  "quest.6906CC2C09BAA8A8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Throw in one block of what you're after before starting \"},{\"text\":\"Scrying\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:ritual_scrying\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": for a while you see it through everything, white near, green middling, blue far.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.652BE291CD20CB8F.title": "Den of the Wilden",
  "quest.652BE291CD20CB8F.quest_subtitle": "Wipe your feet.",
  "quest.652BE291CD20CB8F.quest_desc": [
    "You walked into a Wilden den. Horns, spikes and wings, and the owners, all in one forest clearing."
  ],
  "reward.5ABEF5A1E1482975.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.3E586171800E29F1.title": "Crops, no hands",
  "quest.3E586171800E29F1.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Harvest\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:ritual_harvest\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" reaps ripe crops around the brazier for a bit of Source each, into an inventory next to it if there is one.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.225F391735441554.title": "Cheap cures",
  "quest.225F391735441554.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Restoration\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:ritual_restoration\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" heals the living nearby and hurts the undead. Zombie villagers are cured at once, and cured villagers trade at a discount.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.718037DFEA5B61ED.title": "Mobs in jars",
  "quest.718037DFEA5B61ED.quest_subtitle": "A farm that fits on a shelf.",
  "quest.718037DFEA5B61ED.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Empty \"},{\"text\":\"Containment Jars\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:mob_jar\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a creature within three blocks of the brazier: in it goes. Jarred mobs keep living, so eggs, wool, milk and trades keep coming.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.75F78A67ECF0E466.title": "What a jar can do",
  "quest.75F78A67ECF0E466.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A jarred villager trades and restocks; a piglin barters thrown gold; an allay stores items into an inventory next to it; a drygmy counts jars as creatures.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.506DBB17A2827156.title": "Time in a bottle",
  "quest.506DBB17A2827156.quest_subtitle": "If words could make wishes come true.",
  "quest.506DBB17A2827156.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A clock in a \"},{\"text\":\"Containment Jar\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:mob_jar\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It's still ticking. It's just ticking somewhere smaller.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.428B9AD817D7A594.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.7FF171DC9AFB1F3D.title": "Your first familiar",
  "quest.7FF171DC9AFB1F3D.quest_subtitle": "Friendship, with paperwork.",
  "quest.7FF171DC9AFB1F3D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Run \"},{\"text\":\"Binding\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:ritual_binding\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" next to a creature, a starbuncle to start: it becomes a bound script that teaches you the familiar. Summon it from the book's familiar tab.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.44481184CD68D732.title": "Bookwyrm, the tidy one",
  "quest.44481184CD68D732.quest_desc": [
    "Bind a bookwyrm and, as a familiar, it pulls items and experience within five blocks, but not what you throw. Take it mining; take the starbuncle for speed on the surface."
  ],
  "quest.7143B2456F90D31D.title": "Who does what",
  "quest.7143B2456F90D31D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Starbuncle: speed. Bookwyrm: item magnet. Drygmy: earth spells and looting. Whirlisprig: cheaper earth glyphs. Wixie: longer potions. A familiar reserves part of your mana while it's out.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.2FE29D5739879663.title": "Defeat the Wilden Chimera",
  "quest.50BF33B63B7ECACF.title": "The Wilden Chimera",
  "quest.50BF33B63B7ECACF.quest_subtitle": "Not in the garden.",
  "quest.50BF33B63B7ECACF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A purple archwood log, three Wilden drops and a lapis block make the Summon Wilden tablet. Throw a \"},{\"text\":\"horn\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:wilden_horn\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a \"},{\"text\":\"spike\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:wilden_spike\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a \"},{\"text\":\"wing\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:wilden_wing\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on the brazier before lighting it. The Chimera drops a \"},{\"text\":\"Wilden Tribute\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:wilden_tribute\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "task.28B2A0E9BE07F7E4.title": "Watch your starbuncle at work",
  "quest.095EDA334AA7BB45.title": "Starbuncle Charm",
  "quest.095EDA334AA7BB45.quest_subtitle": "The only employee paid in advance.",
  "quest.095EDA334AA7BB45.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Starbuncles flee from players unless you hold a gold nugget: let one take it and it leaves a \"},{\"text\":\"Starbuncle Token\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:starbuncle_shards\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Token and four gold ingots in the apparatus make the \"},{\"text\":\"Starbuncle Charm\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:starbuncle_charm\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]",
    "",
    "Use the charm on the ground and it picks up items nearby. Dispel or death returns the charm."
  ],
  "quest.47DCEDEE953B0EDB.title": "Starbuncle routes",
  "quest.47DCEDEE953B0EDB.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Wand the starbuncle, then a chest: it delivers there. Chest first, then starbuncle: it takes from there. One can serve many chests; a charm used on a starbuncle stacks them into one.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1022D6A130C47354.title": "Thinking with portals",
  "quest.1022D6A130C47354.quest_subtitle": "Wrong game, right idea.",
  "quest.1022D6A130C47354.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Warp Scroll\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:warp_scroll\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" records a spot and takes you there once. Thrown into a sourcestone frame with a full jar nearby, it opens a permanent one-way portal.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4BE4DD0664E13443.title": "Filters on paper",
  "quest.4BE4DD0664E13443.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Write items into an \"},{\"text\":\"Allow scroll\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:allow_scroll\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" at the scribe's table; a starbuncle holding it moves only those. Deny does the opposite. A scroll in an item frame on a chest filters every starbuncle using it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.786B44F172D40CA9.title": "Beds and shades",
  "quest.786B44F172D40CA9.quest_subtitle": "Sunglasses: the uniform of focus.",
  "quest.786B44F172D40CA9.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A wand-bound \"},{\"text\":\"Magebloom Bed\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:orange_sbed\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" gives idle starbuncles a place to rest; redstone on it sends them all to sleep. Starbuncle shades stop them picking things up off the ground.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.62CD69998B3B9F95.title": "Drops without killing",
  "quest.62CD69998B3B9F95.quest_subtitle": "A farm where nobody dies.",
  "quest.62CD69998B3B9F95.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Throw a Wilden horn near a wild drygmy for its token; the \"},{\"text\":\"Drygmy Charm\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:drygmy_charm\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on mossy cobblestone makes a henge. It yields drops and experience from creatures nearby, unharmed. Jars count.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.737CF509DB564035.title": "Honey, I shrunk the starbuncle",
  "quest.737CF509DB564035.quest_subtitle": "It seems fine. Probably.",
  "quest.737CF509DB564035.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A starbuncle in a \"},{\"text\":\"Containment Jar\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:mob_jar\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It's still working. It's just working very small.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.2BF6AF8A9B5EBA07.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.701527690A16BF87.title": "A garden that pays",
  "quest.701527690A16BF87.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Grow a tree next to a wild whirlisprig for its token; the \"},{\"text\":\"Whirlisprig Charm\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:whirlisprig_charm\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" goes on a flower with a chest beside it. It produces what grows nearby, but only when it's happy with the variety.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5F0C2EE9E724C72B.title": "A rock with feelings",
  "quest.5F0C2EE9E724C72B.quest_subtitle": "Source Gems forever.",
  "quest.5F0C2EE9E724C72B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Wand the \"},{\"text\":\"Amethyst Golem\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:amethyst_golem_charm\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", then a block, to set its home. It turns amethyst blocks into budding ones, speeds growth, harvests clusters and stores the shards.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6D214A6A8D2A3D24.title": "A witch, reformed",
  "quest.6D214A6A8D2A3D24.quest_subtitle": "Now in middle management.",
  "quest.6D214A6A8D2A3D24.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Dispel a witch at half health or less for the token; the \"},{\"text\":\"Wixie Charm\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:wixie_charm\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on a cauldron makes a Wixie Cauldron. Show it an item and it crafts it from inventories nearby, for a little Source.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6E9B8E04BACF9D1C.title": "Potions by the jar",
  "quest.6E9B8E04BACF9D1C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An empty \"},{\"text\":\"Potion Jar\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:potion_jar\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" by the cauldron, an awkward potion used on it, nether wart nearby: the wixie brews three doses per craft and brings the water.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1AF787950B270CE0.title": "Spells on paper",
  "quest.1AF787950B270CE0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Blank parchment on the scribe's table, pick a spell slot as if to cast, sneak-use the book on the table. The \"},{\"text\":\"Spell Parchment\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:spell_parchment\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" holds that spell and programs turrets.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.01C5F3CD9478E555.title": "Spell turrets",
  "quest.01C5F3CD9478E555.quest_subtitle": "One-block farms, polite mob disposal.",
  "quest.01C5F3CD9478E555.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Load a written parchment into a \"},{\"text\":\"Basic Spell Turret\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:basic_spell_turret\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": on redstone it casts, like a dispenser, paid from nearby jars. With an inventory next to it, Pickup and Place Block work.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3B21E8052927B4E1.title": "A turret with a clock",
  "quest.3B21E8052927B4E1.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Timer Spell Turret\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:timer_spell_turret\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" fires on its own, every second by default: right-click adds time, punching removes it. Forms and Sensitive are free; only effects cost Source.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.496BD651BCA3D872.title": "Storage Lectern",
  "quest.496BD651BCA3D872.quest_subtitle": "A library where the librarians fly.",
  "quest.496BD651BCA3D872.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A lectern ringed by four chests in the apparatus. Wand-link inventories up to 30 blocks away to the \"},{\"text\":\"Storage Lectern\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:storage_lectern\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", then view, sort and craft from all of them on one screen.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4138621CF1D1D61C.title": "Archmage",
  "quest.4138621CF1D1D61C.quest_subtitle": "Four schools, one book.",
  "quest.4138621CF1D1D61C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Your mage's book, ender pearls, emeralds, a Totem of Undying, a Nether Star and a Wilden Tribute: the \"},{\"text\":\"Archmage Spell Book\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:archmage_spell_book\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Tier 3 opens: Blink, Burst, Wall, Lightning.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Nether Star only comes from the Wither here.\",\"color\":\"#FF8C7A\"},{\"text\":\" Plan that fight.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "{image:entrelumen:textures/gui/quests/diagram_glyphs.png width:96 height:48 align:center}",
    "",
    "A good benchmark: one slot to dig, one to light, one to move, one to fight, and one you invented.",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Its spine reads \"},{\"text\":\"ars longa\",\"color\":\"#B98CFF\",\"font\":\"minecraft:alt\"},{\"text\":\". Nobody can read it, but it looks important.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.73F873CF3B844D0C.title": "Blink, and you're there",
  "quest.73F873CF3B844D0C.quest_subtitle": "Legs, the magic edition.",
  "quest.73F873CF3B844D0C.quest_desc": [
    "Self and Blink throw you forward; Projectile and Blink take you where the bolt lands. With a written warp scroll in the other hand, Blink sends a creature to the scroll's spot."
  ],
  "quest.581AD0E934387194.title": "One diamond pick per team",
  "quest.581AD0E934387194.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An \"},{\"text\":\"Annotated Codex\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:annotated_codex\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" records every glyph you know, for experience per glyph; another player uses it to learn them all. In co-op, one scribes the pricey glyphs and the rest copy.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.23F0756ADB690ACD.title": "The tailor's bench",
  "quest.23F0756ADB690ACD.quest_subtitle": "Measure twice, enchant once.",
  "quest.23F0756ADB690ACD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Scribe's Table\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:scribes_table\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" with four \"},{\"text\":\"Magebloom Fiber\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:magebloom_fiber\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" around it: the \"},{\"text\":\"Alteration Table\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:alteration_table\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Magical armor goes on its stand; threads go on its tablet.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.71405CA068B8E5DF.title": "Blank threads",
  "quest.71405CA068B8E5DF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Six \"},{\"text\":\"Magebloom Fiber\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:magebloom_fiber\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" around a row of three gold nuggets: a \"},{\"text\":\"Blank Thread\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:blank_thread\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". The enchanting apparatus turns it into a perk; a bigger armor slot makes the same perk stronger.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.15A4E219C99F91A3.title": "Threads for casters",
  "quest.15A4E219C99F91A3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Spell Power\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:thread_spellpower\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" adds spell damage per level; \"},{\"text\":\"Magic Capacity\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:thread_magic_capacity\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" adds 10% maximum mana per level. The first takes seven essences and a magebloom, the second sourceberries and magebloom.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.034005479D041AB1.title": "Threads that keep you going",
  "quest.034005479D041AB1.quest_subtitle": "A totem that recharges in bed.",
  "quest.034005479D041AB1.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Repairing\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:thread_repairing\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" mends every magical armor and enchanter's item you carry, paid in mana. \"},{\"text\":\"Undying\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:thread_undying\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" needs a tier 3 slot and cancels one death per sleep, like a totem.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.014664D114061E9D.title": "Threads for the road",
  "quest.014664D114061E9D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"High Step\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:thread_high_step\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" raises your step by a block per level; \"},{\"text\":\"Feather\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:thread_feather\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" cuts fall damage. Heights jumps higher, and Gliding flies like an elytra from a level 3 slot.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0B32EE7DA07573F6.title": "Three cuts of robe",
  "quest.0B32EE7DA07573F6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Sorcerer robes have the best thread slots and the least armor. Four fibers on an iron chestplate give \"},{\"text\":\"Arcanist's Robes\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:arcanist_robes\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; on a diamond one, the \"},{\"text\":\"Battlemage's Gambeson\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:battlemage_robes\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": more armor, smaller slots.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.406670C2DC5C14DF.title": "Tier by tier",
  "quest.406670C2DC5C14DF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Two blaze rods and 2500 Source at the apparatus take armor to tier 2; two ender pearls, a chorus fruit and 5000 Source, to tier 3. Each tier adds mana regeneration and bigger slots.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0E868C267D665E13.title": "Rings and amulets",
  "quest.0E868C267D665E13.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight iron nuggets around a Source Gem make a \"},{\"text\":\"Ring of Potential\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:ring_of_potential\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; four, a \"},{\"text\":\"Dull Trinket\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:dull_trinket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". The apparatus turns them into a \"},{\"text\":\"Ring of Lesser Discount\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:ring_of_lesser_discount\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and an \"},{\"text\":\"Amulet of Mana Regen\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:amulet_of_mana_regen\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.75E5FBC8E128F902.title": "Up, without stairs",
  "quest.75E5FBC8E128F902.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Leather and a Source Gem make a \"},{\"text\":\"Mundane Belt\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:mundane_belt\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; gold, feathers and air essence turn it into a \"},{\"text\":\"Belt of Levitation\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:belt_of_levitation\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": sneak mid-air to rise. Three Wilden Wings on a Ring of Potential give the \"},{\"text\":\"Ring of Jumping\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:jump_ring\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.28B30FE07DECA2B8.title": "Two jars for the pocket",
  "quest.28B30FE07DECA2B8.quest_subtitle": "One glows, one eats.",
  "quest.28B30FE07DECA2B8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Jar of Light\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:jar_of_light\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" calls a light that follows you. The \"},{\"text\":\"Jar of Voiding\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:void_jar\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" destroys the items you set as you pick them up and pays a little mana back; sneak-use to switch it on or off.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3AC7B08133F9EAF0.title": "Past the ten-glyph limit",
  "quest.3AC7B08133F9EAF0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An archwood log, four Source Gems, two gold, air and manipulation essence: an \"},{\"text\":\"Enchanter's Wand\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:wand\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It always fires Projectile → Accelerate; inscribe a spell with no form, just Break for instance, and it can outgrow the ten-glyph limit.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7803E74ED7481617.title": "A spell on every hit",
  "quest.7803E74ED7481617.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A diamond sword, a diamond, two gold blocks and two Source blocks: the \"},{\"text\":\"Enchanter's Sword\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:enchanters_sword\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It casts its spell as Touch before each hit, and all your spells gain Spell Damage. Inscribe it without a form: Ignite → Extend Time.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.07EF60D5B3E6A8E9.title": "Blocking pays",
  "quest.07EF60D5B3E6A8E9.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Blocking with the \"},{\"text\":\"Enchanter's Shield\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:enchanters_shield\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" grants a short burst of Mana Regeneration and Spell Damage, and the shield mends itself with your mana. A plain shield, two gold blocks and two Source blocks.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0E326CBB26344ADC.title": "Buffs at a discount",
  "quest.0E326CBB26344ADC.quest_subtitle": "Vanity, but useful.",
  "quest.0E326CBB26344ADC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Enchanter's Mirror\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:enchanters_mirror\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" casts its spell on you, cheaper and longer. Inscribe it with no form, like Heal → Amplify. A Source block, glass, gold, archwood and manipulation essence at the apparatus.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.690C490506EB8DF4.title": "Arrows that cast",
  "quest.690C490506EB8DF4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"With mana, the \"},{\"text\":\"Enchanter's Bow\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:spell_bow\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" turns arrows into spell arrows; with none, it fires a harmless one. Imbue arrows with a Source Gem, air essence and a diamond for \"},{\"text\":\"Amplify arrows\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:amplify_arrow\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.27576A9B1958183B.title": "A fist that mines",
  "quest.27576A9B1958183B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Leather, a diamond, two gold blocks and two Source blocks: the \"},{\"text\":\"Enchanter's Gauntlet\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:enchanters_gauntlet\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a spell multitool that breaks blocks up to diamond hardness. It starts with Touch, takes one formless spell and casts it at a discount.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.738C3D981148DA76.title": "Fishing, with intent",
  "quest.738C3D981148DA76.quest_subtitle": "The one that got away got Ignited.",
  "quest.738C3D981148DA76.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Enchanter's Fishing Rod\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:enchanters_fishing_rod\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" fishes like any rod, but a hooked creature keeps taking its spell until the line breaks. A rod, two gold blocks and two Source blocks.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4F85AB62309DC3E5.title": "Throwing the scenery",
  "quest.4F85AB62309DC3E5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Focus of Block Shaping\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:shapers_focus\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" makes blocks you move hurt what they hit, and copies the rest of your spell onto blocks you create or move. Try Conjure Mageblock → Launch → Delay → Knockback.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1A16226D87118401.title": "Someone else's spell",
  "quest.1A16226D87118401.quest_subtitle": "Previous owner unknown.",
  "quest.1A16226D87118401.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"You found a \"},{\"text\":\"Caster Tome\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:caster_tome\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in the loot. It casts a mage's finished spell for half its cost, or your whole mana bar, whichever is smaller.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.5AD2C7FD0BDA8C69.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.1134B871CB70A5CB.title": "Eight sips per flask",
  "quest.1134B871CB70A5CB.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A bottle, two abjuration essences, a Source block and a gold block: a \"},{\"text\":\"Potion Flask\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:potion_flask\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" with eight doses of one potion. Fill it at a Potion Jar or craft it with the potion; sneak-use it on a jar to empty it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3C4CDD018D260A4A.title": "Longer or stronger",
  "quest.3C4CDD018D260A4A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight manipulation essences turn a flask into \"},{\"text\":\"Extend Time\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:potion_flask_extend_time\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": effects last 50% longer. Eight abjuration essences make \"},{\"text\":\"Amplify\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:potion_flask_amplify\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": one level more, half the time.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7C97D0F232283559.title": "Potion Melder",
  "quest.7C97D0F232283559.quest_subtitle": "Two potions walk into a cauldron.",
  "quest.7C97D0F232283559.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Potion Melder\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:potion_melder\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" takes three doses from each of two linked Potion Jars and fills a third with one potion carrying both effects. Link every jar with the dominion wand; chain melders for longer recipes.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2E840D9EA0A8BFD4.title": "A potion for the whole room",
  "quest.2E840D9EA0A8BFD4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Bind a Potion Jar to a \"},{\"text\":\"Potion Diffuser\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:potion_diffuser\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": every 10 minutes it drinks one potion and keeps applying it to everyone nearby. A campfire, gold and archwood planks.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5AD6CFBD0F6F7CA1.title": "Flask cannon",
  "quest.5AD6CFBD0F6F7CA1.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A dispenser, gold, blaze rods and gunpowder: the \"},{\"text\":\"Splash Flask Cannon\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:splash_flask_cannon\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" throws the flask or potion you pick in its radial menu as a splash. Dragon's breath and two air essences make the lingering one.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.24DCC5AD0088520F.title": "A window anywhere",
  "quest.24DCC5AD0088520F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An eye of ender and a Source Gem: a \"},{\"text\":\"Scry Crystal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:scryers_crystal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Right-click to look through it; blank parchment on it makes a \"},{\"text\":\"Scryer's Scroll\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:scryer_scroll\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" that remembers the spot.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.59D53C3170DFF6EC.title": "The control room",
  "quest.59D53C3170DFF6EC.quest_subtitle": "Security cameras, arcane edition.",
  "quest.59D53C3170DFF6EC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Put Scryer's Scrolls on pedestals around a \"},{\"text\":\"Scryer's Oculus\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:scryers_oculus\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and choose which crystal to watch. The crystals must be chunk-loaded.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.419FFFFE2574E421.title": "Casting by remote",
  "quest.419FFFFE2574E421.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Use an \"},{\"text\":\"Enchanter's Eye\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:enchanters_eye\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on a Scry Crystal to bind it: its inscribed spell is then cast from the crystal, like a turret you aim from home. Blaze powder and ender pearls on a Scry Crystal at the apparatus.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6A4ECF55168AC758.title": "Wilden parts",
  "quest.6A4ECF55168AC758.quest_subtitle": "Horns, wings and spikes, some assembly required.",
  "quest.6A4ECF55168AC758.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Hunters drop \"},{\"text\":\"horns\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:wilden_horn\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", Stalkers \"},{\"text\":\"wings\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:wilden_wing\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", Defenders \"},{\"text\":\"spikes\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:wilden_spike\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Hunter and Stalker dens hide in any forest; Defenders keep to cold biomes.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.13C8EA9106499916.title": "A tablet that calls the pack",
  "quest.13C8EA9106499916.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Purple archwood, three Wilden drops and a lapis block: the \"},{\"text\":\"Summon Wilden\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:ritual_wilden_summon\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" tablet. Lit bare, it calls a Wilden pack for a while: the farm for wings and spikes. With a horn, a wing and a spike thrown in first, the Chimera.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3560C93C587C0594.title": "Dive-bombed",
  "quest.3560C93C587C0594.quest_subtitle": "Turns out they fly.",
  "quest.3560C93C587C0594.quest_desc": [
    "A Stalker climbed, dove and exploded at your feet. They commit to the bit."
  ],
  "reward.2C837CE528C8524A.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.1607A6491A418849.title": "Wings for the whole base",
  "quest.1607A6491A418849.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Purple archwood, three Wilden Wings, two diamonds and an ender pearl: \"},{\"text\":\"Flight\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:ritual_flight\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Near the brazier, a jump grants creative flight for a while, paid in Source from nearby jars.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4C917EB19C67E227.title": "Grounded",
  "quest.4C917EB19C67E227.quest_subtitle": "Flight's evil twin.",
  "quest.4C917EB19C67E227.quest_desc": [
    "A Gravity ritual caught you: no flying and a heavy fall for a while. Somebody in your team has a sense of humor."
  ],
  "reward.75FE27B3DE916336.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.08AEC6B9FC9B87BE.title": "The trees get up",
  "quest.08AEC6B9FC9B87BE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Archwood, four archwood saplings and four Source Gems: \"},{\"text\":\"Awakening\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:ritual_awakening\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It turns nearby archwood trees into Weald Walkers that guard a spot, and budding amethyst into Amethyst Golems. Book and quills in the brazier give Bookwyrm charms.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.395B1D0782E5F18E.title": "Landscaping by ritual",
  "quest.395B1D0782E5F18E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Forestation\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:ritual_forestation\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" plants grown oaks and birches; \"},{\"text\":\"Flowering\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:ritual_flowering\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" fills the ground with flowers and grass. Each Source Gem in the brazier widens them by a block. The Conjure Island tablets raise a round island of grass or sand.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.21F0ABD5BEF8915C.title": "Weather on request",
  "quest.21F0ABD5BEF8915C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Cloudshaping\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:ritual_cloudshaping\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" clears the sky; gunpowder in the brazier makes rain, a lapis block a storm. \"},{\"text\":\"Moonfall\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:ritual_moonfall\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" turns the day to night, for when Sunrise overdid it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3F3603B858A3C2FE.title": "The ranch and the grinder",
  "quest.3F3603B858A3C2FE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Fertility\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:ritual_fertility\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" keeps nearby animals breeding, up to twenty of them. \"},{\"text\":\"Disintegration\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:ritual_disintegration\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" turns monsters into Experience Gems worth double, with no item drops. Both run on Source.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0479D6A76E4CE375.title": "Focus of Summoning",
  "quest.0479D6A76E4CE375.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Source block with a horn, a spike, a wing, the \"},{\"text\":\"Wilden Tribute\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:wilden_tribute\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and gold: the \"},{\"text\":\"Focus of Summoning\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:summon_focus\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Summons last longer and hit harder, and Self spells copy onto them.\"}]"
  ],
  "image.607ACE330E8C390B.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Ars Nouveau\",\"color\":\"#C7A0F5\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.0AE03DEBB0C987AC.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"four schools one circle\",\"color\":\"#C7A0F5\",\"font\":\"minecraft:alt\"}]",
  "image.2866B7F5AD186E56.title": "Back to the Sun of Heliodor",
  "image.11B0181CB03BB281.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Spellcraft\",\"color\":\"#C7A0F5\"}]",
  "image.694A5CD0A0E55F1D.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Source\",\"color\":\"#C7A0F5\"}]",
  "image.0D1A7C926165B739.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Rituals and familiars\",\"color\":\"#C7A0F5\"}]",
  "image.73F7B6E352483579.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Creatures at work\",\"color\":\"#C7A0F5\"}]",
  "image.62D1E38A31BA869D.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Armor and threads\",\"color\":\"#C7A0F5\"}]",
  "image.5BAD0C42AE18B3FA.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Tools of the trade\",\"color\":\"#C7A0F5\"}]",
  "image.2045BDFF9EAD8055.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Potions and scrying\",\"color\":\"#C7A0F5\"}]",
  "image.13B6D14D1DF2BA54.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The wild and the Wilden\",\"color\":\"#C7A0F5\"}]",
  "chapter.48BC3B6935A4143B.title": "Apotheosis · Adventure",
  "chapter.48BC3B6935A4143B.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Affix loot from Common to Mythic, gems, salvaging, reforging and Invaders, up the World Tier mountain that the story climbs for you."
  ],
  "task.1B6CB2AF28738493.title": "Any Apotheosis gem",
  "quest.7904F35EDB118489.title": "Loot with opinions",
  "quest.7904F35EDB118489.quest_subtitle": "The sword you find may beat the one you made.",
  "quest.7904F35EDB118489.quest_desc": [
    "Gear now drops with affixes, extra stats named on the item and coloured by rarity, and gems drop beside it. A quarter of vanilla chests hold a gem, and monsters you kill yourself drop one about 4% of the time."
  ],
  "quest.1AC33FE41F2CF11A.title": "Drop an anvil on it",
  "quest.1AC33FE41F2CF11A.quest_subtitle": "Crude, loud, effective.",
  "quest.1AC33FE41F2CF11A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The first gems get crushed the old way: an anvil falling on a gem lying on the ground turns it into \"},{\"text\":\"Gem Dust\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apotheosis:gem_dust\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Dust builds the Salvaging Table, and one among eight deepslate makes eight \"},{\"text\":\"Gem-Fused Slate\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apotheosis:gem_fused_slate\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for every sigil.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.01CA501717FC9BB8.title": "Salvage everything",
  "quest.01CA501717FC9BB8.quest_subtitle": "One adventurer's junk is another's pearl.",
  "quest.01CA501717FC9BB8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three copper ingots, an iron pickaxe and axe, a smithing table, two Gem Dust and a lava bucket make the \"},{\"text\":\"Salvaging Table\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apotheosis:salvaging_table\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It breaks affix items into one to four rarity materials, gems into dust and plain vanilla gear back into ingots or diamonds.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3B2622C422A7A223.title": "Read the colour",
  "quest.3B2622C422A7A223.quest_subtitle": "Gray: the colour of humble beginnings.",
  "quest.3B2622C422A7A223.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Gray Common items carry one stat, sometimes two, and salvage into \"},{\"text\":\"Mysterious Scrap Metal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apotheosis:mysterious_scrap_metal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". In Haven six drops in ten are Common, most of them stone tools, leather or chainmail.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2239D43E4DF40534.title": "Uncommon green",
  "quest.2239D43E4DF40534.quest_subtitle": "Not a single tear in it, somehow.",
  "quest.2239D43E4DF40534.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Green Uncommon items get two stats, may add an effect and a socket, and salvage into \"},{\"text\":\"Timeworn Fabric\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apotheosis:timeworn_fabric\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". They are over a third of what drops in Haven, and six in ten at Frontier.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.6E5D6CED96A21A2D.title": "Your team completes Act II",
  "quest.7A5070A642F45370.title": "Frontier",
  "quest.7A5070A642F45370.quest_subtitle": "The story sets your tier.",
  "quest.7A5070A642F45370.quest_desc": [
    "When your team's campaign completes Act II, everyone rises to Frontier, and it never goes back down. Monsters get +4 armor and Invaders start to arrive; you get 35% more experience and the enchanting ceiling goes up to 75."
  ],
  "quest.6A1ED011EE674073.title": "Rare blue",
  "quest.6A1ED011EE674073.quest_subtitle": "A shard of the brightest crystal ever. Allegedly.",
  "quest.6A1ED011EE674073.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Blue Rare items add a real effect to their stats, up to two sockets and 10 to 25% more durability, and salvage into \"},{\"text\":\"Luminous Crystal Shards\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apotheosis:luminous_crystal_shard\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". One drop in ten at Frontier, half of them at Ascent.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.6DD1891503C81DE9.title": "Your team completes Act III",
  "quest.5FCB8953E204F939.title": "Ascent",
  "quest.5FCB8953E204F939.quest_subtitle": "The expedition act gets the good loot.",
  "quest.5FCB8953E204F939.quest_desc": [
    "Act III complete: Ascent. Monsters get +8 armor and 5 armor pierce, you get 55% more experience and the table reaches 90. Diamond gear starts dropping with affixes, one item in ten is Epic and most gems come Flawed."
  ],
  "quest.3DF87C5F1EF35450.title": "Epic purple",
  "quest.3DF87C5F1EF35450.quest_subtitle": "Sand from a realm where magic warps everything.",
  "quest.3DF87C5F1EF35450.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Purple Epic items carry three stats, an effect, an ability, one to three sockets and 25 to 55% more durability. They salvage into \"},{\"text\":\"Arcane Sands\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apotheosis:arcane_sands\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", which the Reforging Table needs.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.4F41B361AB6E48F3.title": "Your team completes Act IV",
  "quest.16D7038A67BD9180.title": "Summit",
  "quest.16D7038A67BD9180.quest_subtitle": "The top, but not the end.",
  "quest.16D7038A67BD9180.quest_desc": [
    "Act IV complete, and the Ark begins: Summit. Monsters get +12 armor, 10 toughness and more pierce; you get 75% more experience and the full 100 at the table. Epic becomes the usual drop, Mythic appears, and a gem can come Perfect."
  ],
  "quest.3724B9462B19033C.title": "Mythic orange",
  "quest.3724B9462B19033C.quest_subtitle": "Volatile. Handle with gauntlets.",
  "quest.3724B9462B19033C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Orange Mythic items carry four stats, two effects, an ability and up to three sockets. Only salvaging them yields \"},{\"text\":\"Godforged Pearls\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apotheosis:godforged_pearl\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": the Augmenting Table, its sigils and, in act VI, the \"},{\"text\":\"Luminous Ingot\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:luminous_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" want them.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.37BE31EFF565EE5A.title": "Your team activates the Ark",
  "quest.28DFFCD308929D12.title": "Pinnacle",
  "quest.28DFFCD308929D12.quest_subtitle": "Where the lightning lives.",
  "quest.28DFFCD308929D12.quest_desc": [
    "Activating the Ark opens Act VI and Pinnacle: monsters get +16 armor, 20 toughness and 25 armor pierce, and you get 125% more experience. A quarter of drops are Mythic and one gem in ten is Perfect."
  ],
  "task.5C3E987406523E63.title": "A Perfect gem",
  "quest.67A024413D93A15C.title": "Perfect",
  "quest.67A024413D93A15C.quest_subtitle": "It can't be improved. It doesn't need to be.",
  "quest.67A024413D93A15C.quest_desc": [
    "A Perfect gem tops the purity ladder. From Flawless it costs nine Gem Dust, 27 Luminous Crystal Shards, nine Arcane Sands, three Godforged Pearls and a second Flawless gem of the same kind; at Pinnacle, one gem in ten drops Perfect."
  ],
  "quest.4A5FBC9E2F7A3860.title": "Gems and sockets",
  "quest.4A5FBC9E2F7A3860.quest_subtitle": "Some assembly required.",
  "quest.4A5FBC9E2F7A3860.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A gem goes into a socket at a Smithing Table, and each gem lists the items it fits. Four Gem Dust, three slate, gunpowder and an amethyst shard make three \"},{\"text\":\"Sigils of Socketing\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apotheosis:sigil_of_socketing\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": each adds a socket, but only up to two.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.21CE9709A73B86DB.title": "Take them back",
  "quest.21CE9709A73B86DB.quest_subtitle": "Gems are forever. Sockets aren't.",
  "quest.21CE9709A73B86DB.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four slate, a blaze rod, two ender pearls, a lava bucket and Gem Dust make four \"},{\"text\":\"Sigils of Withdrawal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apotheosis:sigil_of_withdrawal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". At a Smithing Table one gives back the item and every gem in it, so moving to better gear costs nothing.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2B16672990E6A285.title": "Cutting gems",
  "quest.2B16672990E6A285.quest_subtitle": "Two gems in, one better gem out.",
  "quest.2B16672990E6A285.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two smooth stone, shears, four planks and Gem Dust make the \"},{\"text\":\"Gem Cutting Table\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apotheosis:gem_cutting_table\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Two gems of the same kind and purity, dust and rarity materials raise the purity one step, Cracked to Perfect; a Cracked gem only needs a dust, three scrap and a fabric.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5268C4373B1B787E.title": "The Gem Case",
  "quest.5268C4373B1B787E.quest_subtitle": "For the dragon in all of us.",
  "quest.5268C4373B1B787E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three glass, four basalt, a Gem Cutting Table and an ender chest. The \"},{\"text\":\"Gem Case\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apotheosis:gem_case\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" holds 32,000 of each gem and purity, filters by name or by what fits an item, and cuts gems itself from six side slots.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Infused at exactly 100 Eterna, 100 Quanta and 45 to 50 Arcana, it becomes the \"},{\"text\":\"Gem Case of House Fabergé\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apotheosis:ender_gem_case\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": two billion of each, contents included.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.6D35A04D42620126.title": "A Flawless gem",
  "quest.2EC669D201EA9C1F.title": "Flawless",
  "quest.2EC669D201EA9C1F.quest_subtitle": "Almost there.",
  "quest.2EC669D201EA9C1F.quest_desc": [
    "Flawless gems start dropping at Ascent, one in a hundred, and turn common only at Pinnacle. Cutting one from Normal costs seven Gem Dust, 27 Timeworn Fabric, nine shards, three sands and a Godforged Pearl."
  ],
  "task.568AC4035BD68B1C.title": "Gem of the Frozen Queen",
  "quest.0A917B487A123513.title": "A frozen queen's gem",
  "quest.0A917B487A123513.quest_subtitle": "Cold hands, warm heart.",
  "quest.0A917B487A123513.quest_desc": [
    "The Gem of the Frozen Queen drops only in the Twilight Forest, from Summit on, like the Gem of the Twilight Forest. Nether gems wait for Ascent, End gems for Summit."
  ],
  "reward.7384D057765473D3.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.540189E6AF8A9257.title": "Reforging",
  "quest.540189E6AF8A9257.quest_subtitle": "Three choices, no guarantees.",
  "quest.540189E6AF8A9257.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An iron ingot, two Gem Dust, an enchanting table and three smooth stone make the \"},{\"text\":\"Simple Reforging Table\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apotheosis:simple_reforging_table\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": it rerolls any item's affixes up to Rare. Rarity materials and \"},{\"text\":\"Sigils of Rebirth\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apotheosis:sigil_of_rebirth\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" pay, and the second and third choice cost double and triple.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.79B807A275A900F7.title": "Keep the affixes, upgrade the base",
  "quest.79B807A275A900F7.quest_subtitle": "Stone to diamond, one template at a time.",
  "quest.79B807A275A900F7.quest_desc": [
    "Two slate, four stone and a rarity material make two templates: scrap takes stone or chain to iron, fabric iron to gold, a crystal shard gold to diamond. At a Smithing Table, with four ingots or diamonds, the item upgrades and keeps every affix."
  ],
  "quest.4AB8D5D286618E49.title": "Just call it a sword",
  "quest.4AB8D5D286618E49.quest_subtitle": "Of the Earthbreaker, of the Butcher, of the... no.",
  "quest.4AB8D5D286618E49.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Six slate and three flint make six \"},{\"text\":\"Sigils of Unnaming\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apotheosis:sigil_of_unnaming\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". At a Smithing Table one strips the long affix name and keeps every affix; an anvil can name it whatever you like afterwards.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4B5334A4F9F09A92.title": "Epic and beyond",
  "quest.4B5334A4F9F09A92.quest_subtitle": "Netherite, but make it rerollable.",
  "quest.4B5334A4F9F09A92.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A netherite ingot, two Arcane Sands and three nether bricks upgrade the simple table into the \"},{\"text\":\"Reforging Table\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apotheosis:reforging_table\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", which also reforges Epic and Mythic items. A Mythic reroll costs 50 levels, three Godforged Pearls and five sigils.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.321CB17CC82D127F.title": "Scrap for the common store",
  "quest.321CB17CC82D127F.quest_subtitle": "Somebody's junk drawer.",
  "quest.321CB17CC82D127F.quest_desc": [
    "Thirty-two Mysterious Scrap Metal and sixteen Timeworn Fabric, once a day. Salvage what you won't wear: it is the cheapest way to keep a team's gems climbing."
  ],
  "quest.008DCF98C026BD08.title": "Potion charms",
  "quest.008DCF98C026BD08.quest_subtitle": "The potion that never runs dry.",
  "quest.008DCF98C026BD08.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three potions of one kind between six blaze powder make a \"},{\"text\":\"Potion Charm\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apotheosis:potion_charm\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" that outlasts all three. Right-click to switch it on: from your inventory or a Curios charm slot it applies the effect a few seconds at a time, spending durability.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Infused at exactly 100 Eterna, 8.5 to 13.5 Quanta and 32.5 to 37.5 Arcana, a charm becomes Unbreakable."
  ],
  "task.79E0FA9721B1DCCA.title": "Potion of Ancient Knowledge",
  "quest.7F604552BBE6113B.title": "Ancient knowledge",
  "quest.7F604552BBE6113B.quest_subtitle": "Study hard, hunt harder.",
  "quest.7F604552BBE6113B.quest_desc": [
    "An Awkward Potion and a Bottle o' Enchanting brew Ancient Knowledge: +400% experience from what you kill and break, +800% at level II. In a charm it keeps the table's levels coming."
  ],
  "task.2E2EE4EB43D5F615.title": "Potion of Flying",
  "quest.158B11A1DFC87818.title": "Potion of Flying",
  "quest.158B11A1DFC87818.quest_subtitle": "Creative mode, eight minutes at a time.",
  "quest.158B11A1DFC87818.quest_desc": [
    "A Potion of Slow Falling and a fermented spider eye brew Apothic Levitation; popped chorus fruit turns that into Flying: creative-style flight for eight minutes, longer with redstone. In a charm, it lasts as long as the charm does."
  ],
  "reward.36928F77AF7F21AF.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.2BBA8EFEA68AF991.title": "Caged Invaders",
  "quest.2BBA8EFEA68AF991.quest_subtitle": "Please do not feed the invader.",
  "quest.2BBA8EFEA68AF991.quest_desc": [
    "Hidden rooms deep in the caves each hold a Caged Invader and a few chests. Come within eight blocks and it breaks free, in any tier; in Haven it is the only invader you will meet. Its rarity follows your tier, and it drops the usual trophy."
  ],
  "task.7963D4A37B1258EA.title": "Find a tome tower in a forest, plains or hills",
  "quest.6FC97DEE593B0195.title": "Tome towers",
  "quest.6FC97DEE593B0195.quest_subtitle": "A library, with a trap.",
  "quest.6FC97DEE593B0195.quest_desc": [
    "Stone towers full of bookshelves rise in forests, plains and mountains, with versions for deserts, jungles and taigas. Four item frames hold gems, and the chest is trapped: enchanted books, gems and affix gear."
  ],
  "quest.6573B89ED7F30C13.title": "The trader got better",
  "quest.6573B89ED7F30C13.quest_desc": [
    "Apotheosis restocks the Wandering Trader: beacons, totems, enchanted golden apples, diamonds and skulls for the table. From Summit it also sells named diamond gear for the matching piece and 45 to 64 emeralds, and it can show up underground."
  ],
  "quest.45FAFFA50C505D1C.title": "Rogue spawners",
  "quest.45FAFFA50C505D1C.quest_desc": [
    "Some caves hide a lone spawner over a chest. Brutal ones send fireproof zombies or pillagers with half again their health every 10 to 20 seconds; swarm ones pour out sped-up spiders, silverfish or baby zombies. About one chest in nine is the valuable kind."
  ],
  "quest.71BCDEB56D856B4E.title": "Invaders from the sky",
  "quest.71BCDEB56D856B4E.quest_desc": [
    "From Frontier on, an Apothic Invader can land nearby with a noise, a chat message and a beacon beam, in full enchanted gear. It always drops one affix item of its rarity, named after it. Here at most one comes every ten minutes, two to three times as often in the Twilight Forest."
  ],
  "quest.5AB22608149A92E7.title": "Touched by Malice",
  "quest.5AB22608149A92E7.quest_subtitle": "Power has a price: another affix.",
  "quest.5AB22608149A92E7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Invaders often drop a \"},{\"text\":\"Sigil of Malice\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apotheosis:sigil_of_malice\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". At a Smithing Table, on an item with two or more affixes, it makes one 50% stronger and destroys another, at random. Once per item.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Its cousin, the Sigil of Supremacy, only comes from Gateways to Eternity, which this pack does not include."
  ],
  "quest.612CD8086FE74C5B.title": "Size up an invader",
  "quest.612CD8086FE74C5B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Look at an invader and Jade names its rarity and lists its boss modifiers. Name and outline wear that rarity's colour, Uncommon to Mythic, and it shows: a Mythic zombie carries 110 to 180 extra health, an Uncommon one 20 to 60.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7AF5662234017803.title": "Elites",
  "quest.7AF5662234017803.quest_subtitle": "They don't ring the doorbell.",
  "quest.7AF5662234017803.quest_desc": [
    "From Frontier on, a monster may spawn named and empowered, without warning: a Honeyed Archer riding an angry bee, an Undead Knight on a skeleton horse, or in the Nether a Withering Archer trailing a cloud of wither. Some carry an affix item.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "At Pinnacle, one goat in two hundred is Craig the Eternal: four times the size, 4,096 extra health and a sheep called jeb_ at its side."
  ],
  "task.27F610E8727DFFDA.title": "One of the three invader discs",
  "quest.55B825A10C4018FB.title": "Boss music",
  "quest.55B825A10C4018FB.quest_subtitle": "Every fight deserves a soundtrack.",
  "quest.55B825A10C4018FB.quest_desc": [
    "Twelve kinds of invader, wolves and evokers among them, roll a richer bonus: a gem, a Sigil of Malice or, one time in twenty, a music disc. Renren's Flash, Caner Crebes' Glimmer or Chamberlain Kaifry's Shimmer."
  ],
  "reward.5841683478ADD8C4.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.21221E9000F809E7.title": "Invaders abroad",
  "quest.21221E9000F809E7.quest_desc": [
    "The Nether has six invaders of its own, blazes and piglin brutes among them, and they can land anywhere under its roof. The End's five come down only on the outer islands. The Twilight Forest has eight, kobolds and goblin knights among them, two to three times as often as the Overworld."
  ],
  "task.2A5F4A7F6022EF00.title": "Defeat the Wither",
  "quest.1C881E982AEC5E3A.title": "A star for the table",
  "quest.1C881E982AEC5E3A.quest_subtitle": "Three skulls, one bad afternoon.",
  "quest.1C881E982AEC5E3A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Augmenting Table is built around a \"},{\"text\":\"Nether Star\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:nether_star\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", so the Wither comes first. Fight it far from anything you want to keep.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Wither, step by step.\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"617F3D63E49031FA\"}}]"
  ],
  "quest.30179152BFACCA2A.title": "The Augmenting Table",
  "quest.30179152BFACCA2A.quest_subtitle": "Fine-tuning a legend.",
  "quest.30179152BFACCA2A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Nether Star, two Godforged Pearls, an enchanting table and three polished blackstone. The \"},{\"text\":\"Augmenting Table\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apotheosis:augmenting_table\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" edits one affix and leaves the rest alone: an upgrade makes it 25% stronger for two sigils and 225 levels, a reroll swaps it for another of its type for one sigil and 175 levels.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.029CF3492455ABAA.title": "Sigils of Enhancement",
  "quest.029CF3492455ABAA.quest_subtitle": "One pearl, four sigils.",
  "quest.029CF3492455ABAA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four Gem Dust, four slate and a Godforged Pearl make four \"},{\"text\":\"Sigils of Enhancement\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apotheosis:sigil_of_enhancement\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Augmenting is meant for Mythic items, maybe Epic ones: every sigil is a pearl you did not spend elsewhere.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.17B029BBFF83450F.title": "God-fused",
  "quest.17B029BBFF83450F.quest_subtitle": "A pearl, only more so.",
  "quest.17B029BBFF83450F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Godforged Pearl infused at exactly 100 Eterna, about 10 Quanta and 59 Arcana becomes a \"},{\"text\":\"God-Fused Pearl\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apotheosis:god_fused_pearl\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Two of them build \"},{\"text\":\"the Raven's table\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"60EC9EDD56376A7D\"}},{\"text\":\", where you set the stats by hand.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.6936553DF77B4F9D.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.2426B53E96944C95.title": "Two Apotheosis keys",
  "quest.2426B53E96944C95.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.apotheosis.toggle_radial_mining\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" switches radial mining on tools with the Radial affix, and \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.apotheosis.link_item_to_chat\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" links the item under your cursor to chat. Its own comparison is off: Equipment Compare already shows it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.07BD64834D15827D.title": "Salvage the plain stuff too",
  "quest.07BD64834D15827D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Old iron armor salvages into one to three ingots, diamond gear into one to three diamonds and netherite gear into up to two netherite scrap. Keep a Salvaging Table by the trash can.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6CBF0EEB024203B7.title": "Where your stats live",
  "quest.6CBF0EEB024203B7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The Show Attributes button in your inventory lists every attribute you have, from crit chance to life steal and dodge. Hold \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.keyboard.left.shift\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" over one to see where each modifier comes from.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.19A3C2824330197A.title": "The tier screen",
  "quest.19A3C2824330197A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.apotheosis.open_world_tier_select\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" opens the World Tier screen: Detailed Info shows each tier's buffs and the odds of every rarity and gem purity. Its Activate button stays off here, since the story moves the tier.\"}]"
  ],
  "image.6D75CC8E961F33E7.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Gems\",\"color\":\"#FF8A3D\"}]",
  "image.41B5271FECBC0DE1.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Salvaging and reforging\",\"color\":\"#FF8A3D\"}]",
  "image.187BE24AC917A938.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Charms and potions\",\"color\":\"#FF8A3D\"}]",
  "image.7E7A34EDC21F52CB.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Out in the world\",\"color\":\"#FF8A3D\"}]",
  "image.6A0E55BE3590CF84.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Invaders and elites\",\"color\":\"#FF8A3D\"}]",
  "image.5B79D02E64EAE201.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Augmenting\",\"color\":\"#FF8A3D\"}]",
  "image.0BEDBE1B5F52F861.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Apotheosis\",\"color\":\"#F3EEFF\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.6A855199250708CB.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Adventure\",\"color\":\"#F2B27A\"}]",
  "image.4402640A87BE061B.title": "Back to the Sun of Heliodor",
  "image.1E6E7877BF2D38D1.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» Enchanting\",\"color\":\"#F2B27A\"}]",
  "image.7DA6D349CF022A03.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» Spawners\",\"color\":\"#F2B27A\"}]",
  "image.6103E9F36D6023AB.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Haven\",\"color\":\"#F3EEFF\"}]",
  "image.41082A9171BA6DE8.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Frontier\",\"color\":\"#F3EEFF\"}]",
  "image.10AEA7F0CA7D0459.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Ascent\",\"color\":\"#F3EEFF\"}]",
  "image.739B41019383E3B7.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Summit\",\"color\":\"#F3EEFF\"}]",
  "image.525EFBA1B88A7C43.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Pinnacle\",\"color\":\"#F3EEFF\"}]",
  "chapter.78409D0F30264A4E.title": "Apotheosis · Enchanting",
  "chapter.78409D0F30264A4E.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Eterna, Quanta and Arcana: the table climbs with your World Tier, shelf by shelf, from 45 to 100, and the Atlas Library writes what it reaches."
  ],
  "task.0F05332E5318A580.title": "Enchant at level 100",
  "quest.28822DE1AC98F8F1.title": "Level 100",
  "quest.28822DE1AC98F8F1.quest_subtitle": "Fifteen bookshelves were the tutorial.",
  "quest.28822DE1AC98F8F1.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Summit lifts the last ceiling as act V opens, so shelves worth 100 Eterna count: a \"},{\"text\":\"Draconic Endshelf\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apothic_enchanting:draconic_endshelf\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on top of 90, or a ring of \"},{\"text\":\"Horizon Shelves\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:horizon_shelf\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Enchant anything in the top slot.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7E61A14FE07F9DB9.title": "The table, rewritten",
  "quest.7E61A14FE07F9DB9.quest_subtitle": "Same obsidian, new math.",
  "quest.7E61A14FE07F9DB9.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Apothic Enchanting takes over every \"},{\"text\":\"Enchanting Table\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:enchanting_table\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": under the three offers it shows Eterna, Quanta and Arcana, and past level 30 it needs better shelves than plain bookshelves.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.2DE8F61AE455E37D.title": "Enchant at level 30",
  "quest.2D9BB1DF1EF19BDD.title": "Level 30",
  "quest.2D9BB1DF1EF19BDD.quest_subtitle": "Where vanilla tops out.",
  "quest.2D9BB1DF1EF19BDD.quest_desc": [
    "Eterna is the top offer's level, so fifteen bookshelves reach 30. Better shelves go further, up to what your World Tier allows: Haven stops at 45, and the story raises it."
  ],
  "quest.3D47F1C2F57025F4.title": "The question mark",
  "quest.3D47F1C2F57025F4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Put an item in the table and click the question mark at the top right: the info screen lists every enchantment each slot can roll, its level, its odds and what it excludes. A slider tries other power levels.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.6E801477F0E31E70.title": "Enchant with 10 of each stat",
  "quest.025856A8FAADDE9F.title": "Eterna, Quanta, Arcana",
  "quest.025856A8FAADDE9F.quest_subtitle": "Three bars, three moods.",
  "quest.025856A8FAADDE9F.quest_desc": [
    "Eterna sets the level. Quanta, 15% from the table alone, swings the power of each roll up or down. Arcana tilts the pick toward rare enchantments: at 25% you always get two, at 75% three. A candle adds 1.25 Arcana, a skull 5 Quanta."
  ],
  "task.5627CF9193095A48.title": "Enchant at level 60",
  "quest.1FD96FD6D15D2278.title": "Level 60",
  "quest.1FD96FD6D15D2278.quest_subtitle": "Hell and sea, mastered.",
  "quest.1FD96FD6D15D2278.quest_desc": [
    "Infused shelves climb past Haven's 45: each adds 5 Eterna up to 60, and Frontier's ceiling of 75 lets all of it through. The Patina Shelf and the upgraded hell and sea shelves count as well."
  ],
  "quest.296483B1183E3B16.title": "The tier sets the ceiling",
  "quest.296483B1183E3B16.quest_desc": [
    "However many shelves you stack, the table only uses the Eterna your World Tier allows: Haven 45, Frontier 75, Ascent 90, Summit and Pinnacle 100. In this pack each ceiling is what that act's shelves reach, and the table says when it is holding you back.",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The whole climb: \"},{\"text\":\"Apotheosis · Adventure\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"48BC3B6935A4143B\"}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "task.7DB3EA814F3167C4.title": "Enchant at level 80",
  "quest.5F941E4000CA0D65.title": "Level 80",
  "quest.5F941E4000CA0D65.quest_subtitle": "Enchantments from the depths.",
  "quest.5F941E4000CA0D65.quest_desc": [
    "Sculkshelves and Lumen Shelves hold up to 80 Eterna, and Ascent, the act IV tier, lets the table use all of it. At 80, dragon's breath can be infused."
  ],
  "task.31CFE0AC3FB1A1C4.title": "The Chronicle of Shadows",
  "quest.071023362CD7F66D.title": "The Chronicle of Shadows",
  "quest.071023362CD7F66D.quest_subtitle": "Written by someone called Shadows. Of course.",
  "quest.071023362CD7F66D.quest_desc": [
    "A book and a gold ingot: Apotheosis's own guide to enchanting, affixes, gems, spawners and charms. It describes the mod without the pack's changes: here World Tiers rise by themselves, spawners stay put and spawner runes are gone."
  ],
  "quest.35FE1B0A8FA6BB5C.title": "Fifteen bookshelves",
  "quest.35FE1B0A8FA6BB5C.quest_subtitle": "The classic ring.",
  "quest.35FE1B0A8FA6BB5C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Each \"},{\"text\":\"Bookshelf\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:bookshelf\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" adds 2 Eterna, up to 30, when it stands two blocks from the table with air in between. Fifteen fill it; the ring has 32 spots over two layers, so there is room left for candles and skulls.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.43344AD478B35363.title": "The Cartographer's Shelf",
  "quest.43344AD478B35363.quest_subtitle": "Made from what a mapmaker keeps on the desk.",
  "quest.43344AD478B35363.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Act II: four planks, two empty maps, two bookshelves and a \"},{\"text\":\"Calibration Frame\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:calibration_frame\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" give two. Each adds 3 Eterna up to 40, past what a bookshelf reaches, and Haven's ceiling of 45 already lets it count.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1D8AB1AA11FFFBC3.title": "Hellshelves",
  "quest.1D8AB1AA11FFFBC3.quest_subtitle": "Books with a Nether tan.",
  "quest.1D8AB1AA11FFFBC3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Six nether bricks, a blaze rod, a bookshelf and a Potion of Regeneration make a \"},{\"text\":\"Hellshelf\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apothic_enchanting:hellshelf\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": +3 Eterna up to 45 and +3 Quanta. Five lift a table from 30 to 45, the Haven ceiling.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.26250DBD6915A9BB.title": "Seashelves",
  "quest.26250DBD6915A9BB.quest_subtitle": "Salt water, now in book form.",
  "quest.26250DBD6915A9BB.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Six prismarine bricks, a Water Bottle, a bookshelf and a pufferfish make a \"},{\"text\":\"Seashelf\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apothic_enchanting:seashelf\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": +3 Eterna up to 45 and +3 Arcana. Lumen and filtering shelves are built on them later.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"No pufferfish? Four bamboo around any fish craft a “Pufferfish”, quotes included, and the seashelf takes it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.22E1C3ED5D785AC2.title": "Infusion",
  "quest.22E1C3ED5D785AC2.quest_subtitle": "Crafting, but the table does the mixing.",
  "quest.22E1C3ED5D785AC2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Put one item in the table: if Eterna, Quanta and Arcana fall inside a recipe's range, the third slot lights up. A Hellshelf at 45 Eterna and 30 Quanta becomes an \"},{\"text\":\"Infused Hellshelf\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apothic_enchanting:infused_hellshelf\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": +5 Eterna up to 60 and +5 Quanta.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Haven's 45 already allows it; the shelf's Eterna past 45 counts once Frontier lifts the ceiling. EMI lists every infusion with its ranges, maximums included."
  ],
  "quest.424C145C052E00D4.title": "The sea, infused",
  "quest.424C145C052E00D4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Seashelf \"},{\"text\":\"infused\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"22E1C3ED5D785AC2\"}},{\"text\":\" at 45 Eterna, 15 Quanta and 10 Arcana: +5 Eterna up to 60 and +5 Arcana. Four of them and a Spectral Lens make four Lumen Shelves, two go into a filtering shelf.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.46AB8401847D2569.title": "The Patina Shelf",
  "quest.46AB8401847D2569.quest_subtitle": "Copper gone green, the colour of old Heliodor.",
  "quest.46AB8401847D2569.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Act III: four Oxidized Copper, four Hellshelves and a \"},{\"text\":\"Power Regulator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:power_regulator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" give four. Each adds 4 Eterna up to 60 and 12 Quanta: the high Quanta that many infusions ask for.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.4219A659908EE63F.title": "Make a Glowing or Blazing Hellshelf",
  "quest.73A6E9074281833F.title": "Glow or blaze",
  "quest.73A6E9074281833F.quest_subtitle": "Pick your flavour of fire.",
  "quest.73A6E9074281833F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three glowstone around an Infused Hellshelf make a \"},{\"text\":\"Glowing Hellshelf\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apothic_enchanting:glowing_hellshelf\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": +5 Eterna up to 60, +5 Quanta, +3.3 Arcana. Fire charges and blaze powder make a \"},{\"text\":\"Blazing Hellshelf\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apothic_enchanting:blazing_hellshelf\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": +10 Eterna up to 65 and +10 Quanta, one clue less.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.5626479DC1373FD6.title": "Make a Crystalline or Heart-Forged Seashelf",
  "quest.039874DC81814737.title": "Crystal or heart",
  "quest.039874DC81814737.quest_subtitle": "A Heart of the Sea, finally with a job.",
  "quest.039874DC81814737.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three prismarine crystals around an Infused Seashelf make a \"},{\"text\":\"Crystalline Seashelf\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apothic_enchanting:crystal_seashelf\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": +5 Eterna up to 60, +3 Quanta, +5 Arcana. A Heart of the Sea and five prismarine shards make a \"},{\"text\":\"Heart-Forged Seashelf\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apothic_enchanting:heart_seashelf\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": +15 Eterna up to 60 and +20 Arcana.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0710D4AB14BD5B44.title": "The Lumen Shelf",
  "quest.0710D4AB14BD5B44.quest_subtitle": "Light, bottled for the bookcase.",
  "quest.0710D4AB14BD5B44.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Act IV: four glowstone, four Infused Seashelves and a \"},{\"text\":\"Spectral Lens\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:spectral_lens\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" give four. Each adds 7.5 Eterna up to 80, 15 Arcana and a clue: the way to 80 that skips the Warden.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.36A49169676E2BCE.title": "Deepshelves",
  "quest.36A49169676E2BCE.quest_subtitle": "It was only sleeping.",
  "quest.36A49169676E2BCE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Infuse a Dormant Deepshelf at 60 Eterna, 40 Quanta and 40 Arcana: the \"},{\"text\":\"Deepshelf\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apothic_enchanting:deepshelf\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" adds 5 of each, Eterna up to 70. Frontier, with its ceiling of 75, is what lets it show.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.63CA3533F15E5F08.title": "Echoes and souls",
  "quest.63CA3533F15E5F08.quest_subtitle": "Two ways down, both dark.",
  "quest.63CA3533F15E5F08.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Deepshelf under an echo shard, on three candles, turns \"},{\"text\":\"Echoing\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apothic_enchanting:echoing_deepshelf\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": +15 Arcana. Under a soul lantern, on three sculk, it turns \"},{\"text\":\"Soul-Touched\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apothic_enchanting:soul_touched_deepshelf\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": +15 Quanta. Both add 5 Eterna up to 75, exactly the Frontier ceiling.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5671C0EC336AA93E.title": "Sculkshelves",
  "quest.5671C0EC336AA93E.quest_subtitle": "The Warden doesn't lend. You take.",
  "quest.5671C0EC336AA93E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Warden Tendril\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apothic_enchanting:warden_tendril\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", four sculk, a sculk catalyst and, in this pack, two \"},{\"text\":\"Zanite Gemstones\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:zanite_gemstone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" from act IV turn each kind of deepshelf into its sculk version: +10 Eterna up to 80, more Quanta and Arcana, and a clue.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.68EE07395D9794CA.title": "Endshelves",
  "quest.68EE07395D9794CA.quest_subtitle": "The bookshelf, End edition.",
  "quest.68EE07395D9794CA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Five end stone bricks, Infused Dragon's Breath, an ender pearl, a bookshelf and, here, a \"},{\"text\":\"Zanite Gemstone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:zanite_gemstone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make an \"},{\"text\":\"Endshelf\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apothic_enchanting:endshelf\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": +5 of each stat, Eterna up to 90, exactly Ascent's ceiling.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4311A266E2FDCD0F.title": "The Horizon Shelf",
  "quest.4311A266E2FDCD0F.quest_subtitle": "The last rung, and the view is worth it.",
  "quest.4311A266E2FDCD0F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Act V: four Deepshelves, two \"},{\"text\":\"Horizon Charts\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:horizon_chart\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", two Lumen Shelves and an \"},{\"text\":\"Ingot of the Skies\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:sky_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" give four. Each adds 12.5 Eterna up to 100 plus 10 Quanta and 10 Arcana: a way to 100 without the dragon.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.68B11C6DB747F182.title": "The Draconic Endshelf",
  "quest.68B11C6DB747F182.quest_subtitle": "One shelf, ten levels. Show-off.",
  "quest.68B11C6DB747F182.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An Endshelf under a dragon head, with five ender pearls and, here, two \"},{\"text\":\"Ingots of the Skies\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:sky_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It adds 20 Eterna up to 100 and nothing else: set on top of 90, it lifts the table to 100 on its own.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0B13EE78E580F4D8.title": "A shelf that sleeps",
  "quest.0B13EE78E580F4D8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Six Cracked Deepslate Tiles and three books make a \"},{\"text\":\"Dormant Deepshelf\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apothic_enchanting:dormant_deepshelf\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It is barely a bookshelf, 2 Eterna, until you infuse it. Deepslate tiles crack in a furnace.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.43E2479B7B06CBCB.title": "Same offers, same seed",
  "quest.43E2479B7B06CBCB.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The three offers only change when you enchant something. Don't like them? Enchant a book in the cheapest slot and look again.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.217DEEC16EE60BA9.title": "Tomes aim the roll",
  "quest.217DEEC16EE60BA9.quest_subtitle": "Books with opinions.",
  "quest.217DEEC16EE60BA9.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A tome enchants like a book but only takes its own type's enchantments, then turns into an enchanted book. Two books and blaze powder make two \"},{\"text\":\"Tomes of Weaponry\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apothic_enchanting:weapon_tome\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; armor, bow, fishing, pickaxe and other tomes use a blaze rod.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.25E5EC66F1123329.title": "Defeat a Warden",
  "quest.4A84B7DC9A68671B.title": "The Warden's tendril",
  "quest.4A84B7DC9A68671B.quest_subtitle": "It can't see you. It can hear you.",
  "quest.4A84B7DC9A68671B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Every Warden drops a \"},{\"text\":\"Warden Tendril\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apothic_enchanting:warden_tendril\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", and a second one 10% of the time, plus 10% per level of Looting. Each Sculkshelf needs one.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Where Wardens wake up.\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"2A5ED82F67EC1780\"}}]"
  ],
  "quest.49E3A6F7A66F5832.title": "Echo shards, multiplied",
  "quest.49E3A6F7A66F5832.quest_subtitle": "One whisper in, four out.",
  "quest.49E3A6F7A66F5832.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"At 70 Eterna with 50 Quanta and 50 Arcana, one \"},{\"text\":\"Echo Shard\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:echo_shard\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" infuses into four. Every Echoing Deepshelf eats one, so keep a shard back for the next batch.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0F690D98121B7951.title": "Dragon's breath, infused",
  "quest.0F690D98121B7951.quest_subtitle": "Bottled at the scene.",
  "quest.0F690D98121B7951.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"At 80 Eterna, 15 to 30 Quanta and 60 Arcana, a bottle of Dragon's Breath becomes three \"},{\"text\":\"Infused Dragon's Breath\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apothic_enchanting:infused_breath\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Each Endshelf takes one.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Filling the bottles.\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"58072A51FC29378C\"}}]"
  ],
  "quest.1313480229A3AF9E.title": "Pearlescent",
  "quest.1313480229A3AF9E.quest_subtitle": "Same ceiling, twice the push.",
  "quest.1313480229A3AF9E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four end rods and two ender pearls around an Endshelf make a \"},{\"text\":\"Pearlescent Endshelf\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apothic_enchanting:pearl_endshelf\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": +10 Eterna up to 90, +7.5 Quanta and +7.5 Arcana.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3FB019C3B6898FB5.title": "Honey into experience",
  "quest.3FB019C3B6898FB5.quest_subtitle": "Sweet, sticky, educational.",
  "quest.3FB019C3B6898FB5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Infuse a \"},{\"text\":\"Honey Bottle\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:honey_bottle\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" at 25 Quanta and 25 Arcana: at 20 Eterna it gives one \"},{\"text\":\"Bottle o' Enchanting\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:experience_bottle\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", at 60 eight, at 100 thirty-two. Bees turn into a bank of levels.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4CA5531B98A34F3E.title": "Exactly twenty",
  "quest.4CA5531B98A34F3E.quest_subtitle": "Less table, better carrot.",
  "quest.4CA5531B98A34F3E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A carrot infuses into a \"},{\"text\":\"Golden Carrot\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:golden_carrot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" only at exactly 20 Eterna, with 10 to 30 Quanta. Some infusions have a maximum as well as a minimum, and a strong table overshoots them.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6F74EB43DCED5D4A.title": "A trident without the drowned",
  "quest.6F74EB43DCED5D4A.quest_subtitle": "No drowned were harmed.",
  "quest.6F74EB43DCED5D4A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three nautilus shells, a Heart of the Sea and an iron ingot make an \"},{\"text\":\"Inert Trident\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apothic_enchanting:inert_trident\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Infused at 40 Eterna, 20 to 50 Quanta and 35 Arcana, it wakes into a real \"},{\"text\":\"Trident\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:trident\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.37AB5C60C43B9ACA.title": "A leash for anything",
  "quest.37AB5C60C43B9ACA.quest_subtitle": "Villager relocation services.",
  "quest.37AB5C60C43B9ACA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An ender pearl, a lead and a gold ingot make a Flimsy Ender Lead: animals only, eight uses. Infused at 45 Eterna, 25 Quanta and 40 Arcana it becomes an \"},{\"text\":\"Ender Lead\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apothic_enchanting:ender_lead\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": right-click almost any mob to carry it, 64 uses.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Its occult version \"},{\"text\":\"rewrites spawners\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"1E54FD607A2D4D56\"}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5C27C776CCE57ABA.title": "Firel, remastered",
  "quest.5C27C776CCE57ABA.quest_subtitle": "A creeper's disc, re-recorded.",
  "quest.5C27C776CCE57ABA.quest_desc": [
    "Any music disc a creeper drops, infused at 40 Eterna, turns into \"Eterna\" by Firel; 40 Quanta or 40 Arcana give the other two. The table has its own soundtrack."
  ],
  "reward.1E1803E53A10AD31.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.20E2542625AE6112.title": "Shelves that subtract",
  "quest.20E2542625AE6112.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"To land under a maximum, take shelves away or add negative ones: a \"},{\"text\":\"Melonshelf\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apothic_enchanting:melonshelf\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" takes 10 Quanta, a \"},{\"text\":\"Stoneshelf\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apothic_enchanting:stoneshelf\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" 7.5 Arcana. A \"},{\"text\":\"Beeshelf\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apothic_enchanting:beeshelf\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" does the opposite: +100 Quanta for 30 Eterna.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4F4583C7325315E7.title": "Aquatic filtration",
  "quest.4F4583C7325315E7.quest_subtitle": "A bouncer for enchantments.",
  "quest.4F4583C7325315E7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four prismarine bricks, two Infused Seashelves and three prismarine brick slabs make a \"},{\"text\":\"Seashelf of Aquatic Filtration\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apothic_enchanting:filtering_shelf\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Slot up to six single-enchantment books into it: those enchantments stop showing up, and the shelf gains Eterna and Arcana per book.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.24BD915B1B581562.title": "Enchant at 50% Quanta",
  "quest.560FEF2141847370.title": "Half chaos",
  "quest.560FEF2141847370.quest_subtitle": "Introduction to Chaos.",
  "quest.560FEF2141847370.quest_desc": [
    "At 50% Quanta the top offer's power can land anywhere from half the level to one and a half times it: bigger surprises, both ways. Patina, Soul-Touched and Blazing shelves and skulls push it."
  ],
  "quest.2BC7F48DD260BD7E.title": "Hellshelf of Sight",
  "quest.2BC7F48DD260BD7E.quest_subtitle": "A spyglass for the soul.",
  "quest.2BC7F48DD260BD7E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four gold blocks, two Infused Hellshelves, a Potion of Night Vision, an eye of ender and a spyglass make a \"},{\"text\":\"Hellshelf of Sight\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apothic_enchanting:sightshelf\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It adds a clue: one more enchantment shown in the preview before you pay.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.762F1B60A21D3B11.title": "Masterful sight",
  "quest.762F1B60A21D3B11.quest_subtitle": "The Runes Reveal All.",
  "quest.762F1B60A21D3B11.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Hellshelf of Sight with two netherite ingots, four emerald blocks and two long night vision potions becomes a \"},{\"text\":\"Hellshelf of Masterful Sight\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apothic_enchanting:sightshelf_t2\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": two clues. When every possible enchantment is visible, the preview says so.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.2A555E5E3609E571.title": "Enchant at 50% Arcana",
  "quest.56299E05BCF4C248.title": "Half arcane",
  "quest.56299E05BCF4C248.quest_subtitle": "Magical energy.",
  "quest.56299E05BCF4C248.quest_desc": [
    "Each 10% of Arcana shifts the rarity weights, Common 10, Uncommon 5, Rare 3, Very Rare 1, toward the reverse, and from 25% you always get two enchantments. Heart-Forged, Echoing and Lumen shelves carry the most."
  ],
  "quest.7E383D0B364AC07C.title": "Green, purple, red",
  "quest.7E383D0B364AC07C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Coloured names mark Apothic's enchantment types. Green Masterwork ones, like Scavenger or Chainsaw, need power 55 or more; purple Twisted ones come with a downside, from 45; red Corrupted ones cost health and count as curses.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.60EC9EDD56376A7D.title": "The Raven's table",
  "quest.60EC9EDD56376A7D.quest_subtitle": "Nevermore guessing.",
  "quest.60EC9EDD56376A7D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Perfect Gem of the Royal Family, two \"},{\"text\":\"God-Fused Pearls\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apotheosis:god_fused_pearl\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", an Apothic Enchanting Table and three obsidian make the \"},{\"text\":\"Enchanting Table of the Raven\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apothic_enchanting:raven_enchanting_table\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". On it you set Eterna, Quanta and Arcana by hand, within what your tier allows.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7A159D0EFA087EF4.title": "Quantic stability",
  "quest.7A159D0EFA087EF4.quest_subtitle": "Chaos, but only the good kind.",
  "quest.7A159D0EFA087EF4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Infuse a Block of Amethyst at 60 Eterna, 30 to 50 Quanta and 50 Arcana into \"},{\"text\":\"Budding Amethyst\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:budding_amethyst\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", then wrap it in calcite around a bookshelf. The \"},{\"text\":\"Bookshelf of Stability\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apothic_enchanting:geode_shelf\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" removes negative Quanta rolls: power only swings up.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4A34DCD37D74AAF6.title": "Arcane treasures",
  "quest.4A34DCD37D74AAF6.quest_subtitle": "Mending at the table. Curses too.",
  "quest.4A34DCD37D74AAF6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two Deepshelves, four gold blocks, two diamonds and an emerald block make a \"},{\"text\":\"Deepshelf of Arcane Treasures\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apothic_enchanting:treasure_shelf\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". In the ring, it lets treasure enchantments like Mending appear at the table, and most curses with them. +10 Eterna up to 70, −15 Quanta, −15 Arcana.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.24B7048C15F2E891.title": "Enchant at 100% Quanta",
  "quest.3C06D16AFDE59D64.title": "Rolling the dice",
  "quest.3C06D16AFDE59D64.quest_subtitle": "Bees: nature's random number generator.",
  "quest.3C06D16AFDE59D64.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Beeshelf\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apothic_enchanting:beeshelf\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", from four honeycomb, two beehives, two honey blocks and a bookshelf, adds 100 Quanta and takes 30 Eterna. You enchanted at 100% Quanta: power anywhere from zero to double.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.0EB31B6C735311FC.title": "Secret found",
  "task.4A060E9058C3DDBC.title": "Enchant at 0% Quanta",
  "quest.3E696F0DCECDD933.title": "Begone, flux",
  "quest.3E696F0DCECDD933.quest_subtitle": "Melons: the enemies of chaos.",
  "quest.3E696F0DCECDD933.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The table starts at 15 Quanta and two \"},{\"text\":\"Melonshelves\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apothic_enchanting:melonshelf\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" cancel it. You enchanted at 0% Quanta, where every roll lands exactly on the level you paid.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.019ADCCEBF7FC9BD.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.213870BB6F9F47F2.title": "No more Too Expensive",
  "quest.213870BB6F9F47F2.quest_subtitle": "The anvil stopped haggling.",
  "quest.213870BB6F9F47F2.quest_desc": [
    "Apothic removes the anvil's 40-level cap: every repair and combination goes through. It charges those levels' experience counted from zero, not your top levels, and each use still doubles the item's prior-work penalty."
  ],
  "quest.4D2D8B889ED9DAAC.title": "Tome of Scrapping",
  "quest.4D2D8B889ED9DAAC.quest_subtitle": "Recycling, the violent way.",
  "quest.4D2D8B889ED9DAAC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight books around an anvil make eight. In an anvil with an enchanted item, one \"},{\"text\":\"Tome of Scrapping\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apothic_enchanting:scrap_tome\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" destroys the item and returns a book with half its enchantments, rounded up; your enchanting seed picks which.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5EA5741561913A04.title": "Superior scrapping",
  "quest.5EA5741561913A04.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Infused\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"22E1C3ED5D785AC2\"}},{\"text\":\" at 45 Eterna, 25 to 50 Quanta and 35 Arcana, a Tome of Scrapping becomes four \"},{\"text\":\"Tomes of Superior Scrapping\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apothic_enchanting:improved_scrap_tome\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": every enchantment comes off, and the item still goes.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.66FF9CFD8BD2FD12.title": "Tome of Extraction",
  "quest.66FF9CFD8BD2FD12.quest_subtitle": "Keep the sword, take the magic.",
  "quest.66FF9CFD8BD2FD12.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"At 60 Eterna, 25 to 75 Quanta and 45 Arcana, a Superior tome infuses into four \"},{\"text\":\"Tomes of Extraction\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apothic_enchanting:extraction_tome\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Each pulls every enchantment into a book and leaves the item whole.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.60760C62C872171D.title": "Vanilla rules, bent",
  "quest.60760C62C872171D.quest_desc": [
    "Apothic lets Protection share an item with one specialized protection, and Sharpness with Smite or Bane of Arthropods. Enchantments also go well past vanilla's maximum levels; the question mark shows how far each one reaches."
  ],
  "quest.696C7F2B1A1F260E.title": "Prismatic Cobweb",
  "quest.696C7F2B1A1F260E.quest_subtitle": "A cobweb that catches curses.",
  "quest.696C7F2B1A1F260E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four prismarine shards around a cobweb; eight string and a honeycomb make the cobweb. In an anvil with a cursed item, the \"},{\"text\":\"Prismatic Cobweb\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apothic_enchanting:prismatic_web\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" strips every curse and keeps the rest.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6AEA9192E19F1112.title": "Lapis and books for the common table",
  "quest.6AEA9192E19F1112.quest_subtitle": "Somebody has to keep the shelves stocked.",
  "quest.6AEA9192E19F1112.quest_desc": [
    "Sixty-four Lapis Lazuli and sixteen books for the common store, once a day. Lapis pays for every offer the table makes; books become shelves, tomes and more books."
  ],
  "quest.758E6575C6681CC7.title": "The Enchantment Library",
  "quest.758E6575C6681CC7.quest_subtitle": "A bank that only takes books.",
  "quest.758E6575C6681CC7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four ender chests, four infused shelves and an enchanting table. Deposit enchanted books and the \"},{\"text\":\"Enchantment Library\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apothic_enchanting:library\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" keeps each enchantment as points; a click pulls one level onto a book. It holds up to XVI, never above the highest level you put in.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4F9972B26966FF7A.title": "Library of Alexandria",
  "quest.4F9972B26966FF7A.quest_subtitle": "No fire this time.",
  "quest.4F9972B26966FF7A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Infuse the library at exactly 100 Eterna, 45 to 50 Quanta and 100 Arcana: it becomes the \"},{\"text\":\"Library of Alexandria\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apothic_enchanting:ender_library\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", points included, and holds up to XXXI. A 100-Eterna infusion waits for Summit.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.034159BC81B6BB34.title": "The Atlas Library",
  "quest.034159BC81B6BB34.quest_subtitle": "It writes what it never read.",
  "quest.034159BC81B6BB34.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Library of Alexandria, two Horizon Shelves, two \"},{\"text\":\"Containment Seals\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:containment_seal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and four Ingots of the Skies make the \"},{\"text\":\"Atlas Library\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:atlas_library\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It writes any eligible enchantment, even one never deposited, up to XL: the Eterna of its own ring sets the cap, one level per 2.5.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Books pay into a pool of lumen: a deposit is worth at most half what the same level costs, and each level up doubles the price. Curses are refused. Its cap reads the shelves, not your World Tier."
  ],
  "quest.11BF9193B86B4311.title": "The Atlas Library, by the numbers",
  "quest.11BF9193B86B4311.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A Sharpness V book deposits 8 lumen and Sharpness X costs 512; Mending costs 10 and gives back 2. Hoppers and ME buses can feed it books, breaking it keeps the pool, and Quick Charge and Lure stop at V.\"}]"
  ],
  "image.2E687D60B894658B.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Crafting with the table\",\"color\":\"#FF8A3D\"}]",
  "image.36AF3E002D23DC68.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Shaping the roll\",\"color\":\"#FF8A3D\"}]",
  "image.0C811A12361BB5BA.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Tomes and the anvil\",\"color\":\"#FF8A3D\"}]",
  "image.0C93E5E5E3EF049A.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Libraries\",\"color\":\"#FF8A3D\"}]",
  "image.7072FFEAE59F3D24.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Apotheosis\",\"color\":\"#F3EEFF\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.0DD972323F58B6D5.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Enchanting\",\"color\":\"#F2B27A\"}]",
  "image.371B4B51E6EFF3DD.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"eterna\",\"color\":\"#4EE94E\",\"font\":\"minecraft:alt\"}]",
  "image.4F1277F6A7DE7C96.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"quanta\",\"color\":\"#E94E4E\",\"font\":\"minecraft:alt\"}]",
  "image.6C6B61B5C19FC109.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"arcana\",\"color\":\"#C13BC1\",\"font\":\"minecraft:alt\"}]",
  "image.7CC0D90FC4838600.title": "Back to the Sun of Heliodor",
  "image.6634FD4036BB8E76.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» Adventure\",\"color\":\"#F2B27A\"}]",
  "image.749D8CF04EBC7065.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» Spawners\",\"color\":\"#F2B27A\"}]",
  "image.1EF6B3F584835FFF.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"30\",\"color\":\"#4EE94E\"}]",
  "image.38C71766A36FF44B.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"45\",\"color\":\"#4EE94E\"}]",
  "image.60826BB32DBF8347.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"60\",\"color\":\"#4EE94E\"}]",
  "image.55C1EC09ABDEDF81.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"60\",\"color\":\"#4EE94E\"}]",
  "image.722ECF1723C9D805.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"65\",\"color\":\"#4EE94E\"}]",
  "image.408D39DB3AF7E00F.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"70\",\"color\":\"#4EE94E\"}]",
  "image.1FC3C0C8F0A99F85.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"75\",\"color\":\"#4EE94E\"}]",
  "image.41ABCC5353DE09C1.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"80\",\"color\":\"#4EE94E\"}]",
  "image.0A8AAA8B29AAB0C3.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"90\",\"color\":\"#4EE94E\"}]",
  "image.4BC0A4AEC22AB878.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"100\",\"color\":\"#4EE94E\"}]",
  "image.7C91713C921DEF77.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"100\",\"color\":\"#4EE94E\"}]",
  "image.5B8964C4CBA27A18.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"80\",\"color\":\"#4EE94E\"}]",
  "image.33BCC0EFC2197D4E.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"60\",\"color\":\"#4EE94E\"}]",
  "image.796E9A146D15C7A6.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"60\",\"color\":\"#4EE94E\"}]",
  "image.43C977DC01B62656.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"45\",\"color\":\"#4EE94E\"}]",
  "image.08E88DC184A2F19C.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"40\",\"color\":\"#4EE94E\"}]",
  "chapter.764474727FAF4C24.title": "EvilCraft: Blood Magic",
  "chapter.764474727FAF4C24.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Dark gems, blood extraction, the Blood Infuser, brooms and vengeance spirits."
  ],
  "quest.6FB6533026337171.title": "Blood, with machines",
  "quest.6FB6533026337171.quest_desc": [
    "Mine dark gems, collect blood from the fallen and feed it to machines that infuse items, repair tools, lift curses, fly brooms and trap spirits. It all works early; the story needs two dark gems for the Act IV Containment Seal.",
    "",
    "Squeamish? Try Nature's Aura."
  ],
  "quest.385FA6C934E3365F.title": "Origins of Darkness",
  "quest.385FA6C934E3365F.quest_desc": [
    "Loot, not a recipe: about one chest in five in villages, dungeons, mineshafts, temples, igloos, fortresses and ancient cities carries it. A diary in two ages, with clickable recipes.",
    "",
    "Someone else's diary. Read it anyway."
  ],
  "quest.7043B42051E1F0E1.title": "Dark gems",
  "quest.7043B42051E1F0E1.quest_desc": [
    "Dark Ore sits mostly around redstone depth and needs an iron pickaxe; Fortune adds Crushed Dark Gem. Keep a stack: gems build spikes, tanks and bricks, and two go into the Containment Seal.",
    "",
    "The darkest thing you'll mine on purpose."
  ],
  "quest.063626A177E886C8.title": "Blood Extractor",
  "quest.063626A177E886C8.quest_desc": [
    "In your inventory it fills when you kill certain creatures; sneak-use it on Blood Stains, left where things fell to their death. Right-click pours a bucket. Combine extractors, or add Dark Tanks, in a grid for capacity."
  ],
  "quest.439881AF0DC88B9D.title": "Dark Tank",
  "quest.439881AF0DC88B9D.quest_desc": [
    "About sixteen buckets, carried in your inventory; tanks merged in a grid grow without spilling. Right-click a placed tank to open a drain below it; sneak-use in the air to top up what you hold."
  ],
  "quest.7CDFDBE98EC4294D.title": "Dark Power Gems",
  "quest.7CDFDBE98EC4294D.quest_desc": [
    "Toss a dark gem into a blood pool of at least five source blocks: it becomes a Dark Power Gem. Once by hand; later the Infuser does it cheaper. Hardened blood shards around a power gem make the Blood Infusion Core.",
    "",
    "A pool party nobody wants to attend."
  ],
  "quest.76FA8595F2D5755E.title": "Blood Infuser",
  "quest.76FA8595F2D5755E.quest_desc": [
    "It fills blood containers and infuses items: cheaper Dark Power Gems, Blooks (books with blood), undead saplings and more; redstone pauses it. Promises of Tenacity, Velocity and Productivity upgrade capacity, speed and blood cost."
  ],
  "quest.7E2465162DFCD0F3.title": "Blood Chest",
  "quest.7E2465162DFCD0F3.quest_desc": [
    "It slowly repairs tools inside, using blood. The catch: now and then a tool picks up a bad effect, like Curse of Breaking, which the Purifier removes.",
    "",
    "Free repairs, fine print included."
  ],
  "quest.6D0085AFA7386179.title": "Purifier",
  "quest.6D0085AFA7386179.quest_desc": [
    "With a bucket of blood it strips bad effects from a tool. Full, with a Blook, it moves a random enchantment from an item onto the book, for three buckets. One of several ways to move enchantments, with Apothic's extraction tome."
  ],
  "quest.3235317897092347.title": "Pedestals and spiked plates",
  "quest.3235317897092347.quest_desc": [
    "A Sanguinary Pedestal pulls blood from nearby stains into adjacent tanks; a Spiked Plate on top adds the blood of whatever it kills. Mobs dropped onto plates over pedestals: the classic blood farm.",
    "",
    "Grim, efficient, and quiet."
  ],
  "quest.351C2326640B6B1B.title": "Dark Temples and weather",
  "quest.351C2326640B6B1B.quest_desc": [
    "A Weather Container thrown into a Dark Temple's core absorbs the weather; throw it again to release it. The temple's Environmental Accumulators empower items with lightning, but slowly wear down its biome. The Sanguinary Accumulator does it at home, on blood."
  ],
  "quest.0DE1D4B13C0A2DA2.title": "Vengeance spirits",
  "quest.0DE1D4B13C0A2DA2.quest_desc": [
    "Kills leave a fading aura. A Vengeance Ring shows it and taps its power, but angers the spirits, who chase you. A Vengeance Focus freezes them for a Box of Eternal Closure; the piercing one kills them for loot.",
    "",
    "They remember you. Specifically you."
  ],
  "quest.09F4B8C1E0773233.title": "Spirit Furnace",
  "quest.09F4B8C1E0773233.quest_desc": [
    "A cube of blood-infused Dark Bricks around a hollow sized for the mob, one Spirit Furnace in the wall. Load a Box of Eternal Closure with a spirit: the furnace revives and cooks it for drops, at a steep blood cost. A zombie needs a 3x4 shell."
  ],
  "quest.06763A6655A282B2.title": "Spirits into spawn eggs",
  "quest.06763A6655A282B2.quest_desc": [
    "The Spirit Reanimator pours a captured spirit and a lot of blood into an egg: a spawn egg. The spirit is spent; some mobs refuse. Reliquary's spawn-egg crafting is removed here, but this route is native. Spawners can't be moved with Silk Touch."
  ],
  "quest.711D75049FB2E851.title": "The Broom",
  "quest.711D75049FB2E851.quest_desc": [
    "Three parts combined in a grid: Rod, Brush and Cap. A material on each part (bone, blaze rod, feathers, diamonds, skulls) changes base stats, and modifiers like speed, levitation or flame are added for good. Keep it full of blood or it crawls.",
    "",
    "Witch-grade transport, blood-grade fuel."
  ],
  "quest.27FFB9FB26490BDB.title": "The broom flies first",
  "quest.27FFB9FB26490BDB.quest_desc": [
    "The broom isn't staged: real flight for blood and dark gems. The rest is: basic jetpacks wait for the Act III Power Regulator, and the Rending Gale, Exo Jetpack, Gravichestplate and Just Dire Things' flight upgrade for the Act IV Horizon Chart."
  ],
  "quest.0E305F7EF8D735F8.title": "Blood-powered tools",
  "quest.0E305F7EF8D735F8.quest_desc": [
    "The Blood Pearl of Teleportation is a reusable ender pearl paid in blood; the Mace of Distortion knocks back everything around you; the Necromancer Staff raises zombies against your target. Maces and staff need Empowered Inverted Potentia, charged by lightning."
  ],
  "quest.2B529AB6EBE14361.title": "Full moon over the village",
  "quest.2B529AB6EBE14361.quest_desc": [
    "Some villages hide a werewolf: a villager oddly keen on dark gems who turns into a tall wolf on full-moon nights. A tough fight that drops Werewolf Fur, bones and flesh.",
    "",
    "The quiet neighbor was never that quiet."
  ],
  "quest.56A5B35F99624D2A.title": "The Containment Seal",
  "quest.56A5B35F99624D2A.quest_desc": [
    "Two dark gems, two Soulstained Steel and a Spectral Lens, for «A Vessel for Restless Memory» in Act IV. It gates Theurgy's sulfuric emitter, the Eternal Stella, the fission reactor, burning augments and the Atlas Library.",
    "",
    "What the dark schools make, together."
  ],
  "quest.4AD07AAD58C2D981.title": "A blood engine",
  "quest.4AD07AAD58C2D981.quest_desc": [
    "Spiked plates feeding pedestals and tanks, an infuser with promises, a purifier cleaning tools, a broom overhead and a spirit furnace humming. Malum, Occultism and EvilCraft: the dark schools behind Act IV.",
    "",
    "Every fight is fuel now."
  ],
  "chapter.618DE437ED55A7C4.title": "Iron's Spells 'n Spellbooks",
  "chapter.618DE437ED55A7C4.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Nine schools around one table: scrolls, spell books, ink, the forge, the cauldron and the robes that carry your mana."
  ],
  "quest.5300AB8C0C6E4322.title": "The Inscription Table",
  "quest.5300AB8C0C6E4322.quest_subtitle": "A desk for spells, not homework.",
  "quest.5300AB8C0C6E4322.quest_desc": [
    "A book on three wooden slabs and two fences. Set a spell book and a scroll on it and the spell moves into the book; take the scroll back out later and the spell leaves the book, the scroll whole again."
  ],
  "quest.310C86E24A1949F0.title": "Don't read that scroll",
  "quest.310C86E24A1949F0.quest_subtitle": "The urge is strong. Resist.",
  "quest.310C86E24A1949F0.quest_desc": [
    "Spellcasters drop scrolls and magic chests hide them, each holding one spell at a fixed level. Reading one casts it once, with no mana or cooldown, and burns the page. Inscribed into a book, it casts for good."
  ],
  "quest.5874FEF7661D32F2.title": "Common Ink",
  "quest.5874FEF7661D32F2.quest_subtitle": "Cheap, plentiful and very sticky.",
  "quest.5874FEF7661D32F2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Spellcasters drop it, magic chests keep it and the \"},{\"translate\":\"entity.minecraft.wandering_trader\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\"},{\"text\":\" sells it. Ink sets a scroll's rarity: common writes a spell's lowest levels, legendary its highest.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.1891A0DBA205CAC7.title": "Wear it in the Spell Book slot",
  "quest.5B5796E05B4E5718.title": "A book to write in",
  "quest.5B5796E05B4E5718.quest_subtitle": "Flimsy by name, flimsy by nature.",
  "quest.5B5796E05B4E5718.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two copper ingots, a string and six paper: the \"},{\"text\":\"Flimsy Journal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"irons_spellbooks:copper_spell_book\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", five spell slots. It goes in the Spell Book slot of your curios; worn there, its spells fill the spell wheel.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0F2BD1F9BD1B43E6.title": "The wheel, then cast",
  "quest.0F2BD1F9BD1B43E6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Hold \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.irons_spellbooks.spell_wheel\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" and pick a spell, then press \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.irons_spellbooks.spellbook_cast\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" to cast it. Fifteen quick-cast slots come unbound under Controls: give your favourite spells a key each.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.010419F8C02E30ED.title": "A mana bar of its own",
  "quest.010419F8C02E30ED.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Iron's mana is its own bar, 100 to start and apart from Ars's. Robes, rings and books raise it, and the Ark's \"},{\"text\":\"Arcane Module\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"4BCEABDD4D9E618C\"}},{\"text\":\" adds half again to every magic that shows mana, this one included.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2DA843F392A3C84D.title": "Arcane Essence",
  "quest.2DA843F392A3C84D.quest_subtitle": "Magic dust, sold by the pinch.",
  "quest.2DA843F392A3C84D.quest_desc": [
    "Magic chests and spellcasters drop it, and the Dead King by the fistful. It sews robes, forges ingots, fills jars and tips staffs: keep a stack on you."
  ],
  "quest.6630614DD62181BF.title": "Arcane Cloth",
  "quest.6630614DD62181BF.quest_subtitle": "Wool that went to wizard school.",
  "quest.6630614DD62181BF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight \"},{\"text\":\"Arcane Essence\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"irons_spellbooks:arcane_essence\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" around any wool. Every robe from here on is cut from it, and the better spell books bind it into their covers.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.241F2B077C534AE0.title": "Blank Runestone",
  "quest.241F2B077C534AE0.quest_subtitle": "A rock with potential.",
  "quest.241F2B077C534AE0.quest_desc": [
    "Magic chests, vaults and catacomb walls hide them. Eight of a school's focus around one make that school's rune, and a rune turns a plain wizard piece into school armour.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Each piece of school armour is the matching wizard piece, the rune and one \"},{\"text\":\"Arcane Essence\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"irons_spellbooks:arcane_essence\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", at a crafting table or at a smithing table with the rune as template. Every piece gives 125 max mana, 10% power in its school and 5% spell power.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.3BEF209EA9D4C48E.title": "Iron's Guidebook",
  "quest.1588F3F9DFC9186D.title": "The mod's own manual",
  "quest.1588F3F9DFC9186D.quest_subtitle": "Read the instructions. They have pictures.",
  "quest.1588F3F9DFC9186D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A book and one \"},{\"text\":\"Arcane Essence\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"irons_spellbooks:arcane_essence\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make Iron's Guidebook: early, mid and late game, the nine schools, ink and every craftable book, recipes included.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.373EA23A6D7071EA.title": "The Ironbound Tome",
  "quest.373EA23A6D7071EA.quest_subtitle": "Chains included. Mercifully.",
  "quest.373EA23A6D7071EA.quest_desc": [
    "Three chains, four leather and two paper: six slots to the journal's five. To move house, pull each scroll out of the old book at the Inscription Table and write it into the new one."
  ],
  "quest.121B4A64A0030D29.title": "Hogskin",
  "quest.121B4A64A0030D29.quest_subtitle": "The hoglin disagreed.",
  "quest.121B4A64A0030D29.quest_desc": [
    "Hoglins drop it in the Crimson Forest. Both better books ask for it, and the Lesser Spell Slot Improvement eats six later. Four spare hides craft back into four leather."
  ],
  "quest.597CF7E4B465F18F.title": "The Apprentice's Spell Book",
  "quest.597CF7E4B465F18F.quest_subtitle": "Gold trim for a promising student.",
  "quest.597CF7E4B465F18F.quest_desc": [
    "Three gold ingots, four Arcane Essence and two Hogskin: eight slots, +50 max mana and 15% shorter cast times. The first book with bonuses of its own."
  ],
  "quest.4E40FFE6E511D3CC.title": "Read the book, not the cover",
  "quest.4E40FFE6E511D3CC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Found books carry fixed bonuses, and not all of them are gifts: the \"},{\"text\":\"Rotten Spell Book\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"irons_spellbooks:rotten_spell_book\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" adds 100 mana but takes 15% spell resistance. Hover a book before you swap: the tooltip lists slots, mana and every bonus.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3C1E081D38A18B38.title": "The Enchanted Spell Book",
  "quest.3C1E081D38A18B38.quest_subtitle": "Ten slots and a cover that hums.",
  "quest.3C1E081D38A18B38.quest_desc": [
    "Two diamonds, four Hogskin, two Arcane Cloth and an enchanted book: ten slots and +100 max mana. Fill it at the Inscription Table with scrolls you forged yourself.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "A good first page: one spell that hits hard, one that moves you, one that saves you, one that heals, and one from a school you haven't tried yet.",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Its spine reads \"},{\"text\":\"scribo ergo sum\",\"color\":\"#B98CFF\",\"font\":\"minecraft:alt\"},{\"text\":\". The book agrees.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.63517637E8CE5A1E.title": "The Scroll Forge",
  "quest.63517637E8CE5A1E.quest_subtitle": "Goodbye, loot lottery.",
  "quest.63517637E8CE5A1E.quest_desc": [
    "Three polished deepslate over four crying obsidian. Feed it ink, paper and a school's focus, then pick the spell: the ink sets the rarity, the focus the school. You write what you want instead of hoping for it."
  ],
  "quest.2D9931B075D2E8A5.title": "The trader deals in magic",
  "quest.2D9931B075D2E8A5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Here the \"},{\"translate\":\"entity.minecraft.wandering_trader\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\"},{\"text\":\" sells scrolls, ink and bundles of mystery scrolls, buys spare ink for emeralds or essence, and now and then carries a ring or an amulet. Check every one that wanders by.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.76D632E831E810D8.title": "Defeat an Ancient Knight",
  "quest.0F5261E364129735.title": "Cinder Essence",
  "quest.0F5261E364129735.quest_subtitle": "Knights in rusty armour.",
  "quest.0F5261E364129735.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Break an Armor Pile in the Nether's citadels and battlegrounds, or in a Pyromancer Tower, and an Ancient Knight climbs out. Killed by a player it always drops one \"},{\"text\":\"Cinder Essence\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"irons_spellbooks:cinder_essence\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", and one time in eight a netherite scrap.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.685ED6CB1E5B9681.title": "The Alchemist Cauldron",
  "quest.685ED6CB1E5B9681.quest_subtitle": "Double, double, ink and trouble.",
  "quest.685ED6CB1E5B9681.quest_desc": [
    "Four iron ingots around a cauldron, two Arcane Essence and one Cinder Essence. It brews ink up the ladder, elixirs from potions and blood from mobs; bottles fill it and empty it, 250 mB at a time.",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A swamp Mangrove Hut has one standing inside, and mining it drops the cauldron whole.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0A8DC93283501E75.title": "Scrolls you don't want",
  "quest.0A8DC93283501E75.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Drop an unwanted scroll into an Alchemist Cauldron holding water: half the time it dissolves into a bottle's worth of ink of its rarity. Duplicate loot becomes forge fuel.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.673162D9FF069DE3.title": "Three elixirs",
  "quest.673162D9FF069DE3.quest_subtitle": "Tastes like a fight you already won.",
  "quest.673162D9FF069DE3.quest_desc": [
    "All brewed from potions in the cauldron: Oakskin from Strong Healing and an oak log, Evasion from Mana III and an ender pearl, Invisibility from long Invisibility and a Shriving Stone. Amethyst or dragon's breath brews the greater ones."
  ],
  "quest.05BD517A1BB294A7.title": "Uncommon Ink",
  "quest.05BD517A1BB294A7.quest_subtitle": "Four bottles in, one bottle out.",
  "quest.05BD517A1BB294A7.quest_desc": [
    "In the Alchemist Cauldron, 1000 mB of Common Ink (four bottles) and a copper ingot brew one bottle of Uncommon. Every step up the ladder costs four of the ink below."
  ],
  "quest.2AFCDCE41D624416.title": "Rare Ink",
  "quest.2AFCDCE41D624416.quest_subtitle": "Rare, in theory.",
  "quest.2AFCDCE41D624416.quest_desc": [
    "Four bottles of Uncommon and an iron ingot. Wizards and magic chests hand it out often enough that brewing it is rarely the fast way."
  ],
  "quest.2D00795A42C7A800.title": "Epic Ink",
  "quest.2D00795A42C7A800.quest_subtitle": "Sixty-four commons walk into a cauldron.",
  "quest.2D00795A42C7A800.quest_desc": [
    "Four bottles of Rare and a gold ingot, or loot: boss vaults pay in rare to legendary ink, and an Icebreaker captain keeps a bottle. Brewed from the bottom, each costs 64 Common Ink."
  ],
  "task.2CDF850A88EC6027.title": "Brew a Potion of Mana",
  "quest.28B4C01DBB923BB8.title": "Liquid patience",
  "quest.28B4C01DBB923BB8.quest_subtitle": "Tastes like blue.",
  "quest.28B4C01DBB923BB8.quest_desc": [
    "An Awkward Potion and one Arcane Essence brew a Potion of Mana in a plain brewing stand; glowstone dust, then an amethyst shard, then a cluster take it up to IV. Each level refills 25 mana plus 5% of your maximum."
  ],
  "quest.4C06C356143F7FEC.title": "The Wandering Magician",
  "quest.4C06C356143F7FEC.quest_subtitle": "Leather, but make it mystical.",
  "quest.4C06C356143F7FEC.quest_desc": [
    "Each piece of leather armour plus one Arcane Essence, shapeless. 25 max mana per piece: small, but it's the first mana you can wear."
  ],
  "quest.237C28464BF31110.title": "The Scarecrow",
  "quest.237C28464BF31110.quest_subtitle": "Crows hate it. Zombies don't care.",
  "quest.237C28464BF31110.quest_desc": [
    "Arcane Cloth sewn onto hay bales, leather and a carved pumpkin over a leather cap. 75 max mana per piece, three times the Wandering Magician's."
  ],
  "quest.4C06564A76AECE57.title": "Wizard robes",
  "quest.4C06564A76AECE57.quest_subtitle": "The pointy hat is optional. Mostly.",
  "quest.4C06564A76AECE57.quest_desc": [
    "Pure Arcane Cloth: robes, leggings, boots and a hood or a pointy hat. Each piece adds 125 max mana and 5% spell power, and each is the blank that a rune turns into school armour."
  ],
  "quest.73227953D2C9A615.title": "Essence for the archive",
  "quest.73227953D2C9A615.quest_subtitle": "Every library runs on donations.",
  "quest.73227953D2C9A615.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Thirty-two \"},{\"text\":\"Arcane Essence\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"irons_spellbooks:arcane_essence\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for the common store, once a day. One Dead King covers it with change to spare.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0672E75E2444ABC8.title": "The Graybeard Staff",
  "quest.0672E75E2444ABC8.quest_subtitle": "The beard is optional.",
  "quest.0672E75E2444ABC8.quest_desc": [
    "A wooden shovel, an iron ingot and one Arcane Essence. Right-click casts your selected spell straight from the staff, and holding it adds 10% spell power and 25% mana regeneration."
  ],
  "quest.74FF66CA0E7C2F2B.title": "The Artificer's Cane",
  "quest.74FF66CA0E7C2F2B.quest_subtitle": "Wizardry, but make it dapper.",
  "quest.74FF66CA0E7C2F2B.quest_desc": [
    "Three crimson planks, two gold ingots and an amethyst shard. It trades the staff's mana regeneration for 10% shorter cast times and 10% shorter cooldowns, on top of 10% spell power."
  ],
  "quest.0B4F37178C16F430.title": "School of Fire",
  "quest.0B4F37178C16F430.quest_subtitle": "Hot takes only.",
  "quest.0B4F37178C16F430.quest_desc": [
    "Damage now and burning after. Its focus is the Blaze Rod: one in the forge writes a fire scroll, eight around a Blank Runestone make the Fire Rune. The Pyromancer sells fire scrolls in his tower."
  ],
  "quest.5D9708BE379038AC.title": "School of Lightning",
  "quest.5D9708BE379038AC.quest_subtitle": "Bottled at the source.",
  "quest.5D9708BE379038AC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Concentrated damage that jumps between targets. Its focus, the \"},{\"text\":\"Bottle o' Lightning\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"irons_spellbooks:lightning_bottle\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", is an empty bottle used on a charged creeper: wait for a storm and bring a trident with Channeling.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Here lightning heals a creeper and makes it fireproof, so the charged one survives to be bottled.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.149AD2EC3FEA6650.title": "School of Ender",
  "quest.149AD2EC3FEA6650.quest_subtitle": "Arcane, mystic, occasionally rude.",
  "quest.149AD2EC3FEA6650.quest_desc": [
    "Damage, utility and movement in one school: Magic Missile, Teleport, Counterspell, Portal and a Black Hole. Its focus is the Ender Pearl, the easiest focus to farm."
  ],
  "quest.549DE42C4E2EA1AF.title": "School of Evocation",
  "quest.549DE42C4E2EA1AF.quest_subtitle": "Illager tricks, legally obtained.",
  "quest.549DE42C4E2EA1AF.quest_desc": [
    "Trickery and conjuring: fangs, vexes, a spectral steed, shields and invisibility, the widest spread of any school. Its focus is the Emerald, and an Archevoker drops its rune half the time."
  ],
  "quest.16AAAB0D7E1898FC.title": "School of Holy",
  "quest.16AAAB0D7E1898FC.quest_subtitle": "Heals, buffs, smites. Mostly heals.",
  "quest.16AAAB0D7E1898FC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Support first: healing, buffs for allies and a little smiting. Its focus, the \"},{\"text\":\"Divine Pearl\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"irons_spellbooks:divine_pearl\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", is one gold ingot and one amethyst shard, shapeless.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3B82220E97B79356.title": "The Eldritch school",
  "quest.3B82220E97B79356.quest_subtitle": "Forgotten for a reason.",
  "quest.3B82220E97B79356.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Nobody starts with it. Eight \"},{\"text\":\"Ancient Knowledge Fragments\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"irons_spellbooks:ancient_knowledge_fragment\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" around an echo shard restore a manuscript; using it teaches one Eldritch spell, and from then on the echo shard is the school's focus.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Fragments turn up in Ancient Cities, End cities, stronghold libraries and boss vaults.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.38E649B2924F1E95.title": "School of Blood",
  "quest.38E649B2924F1E95.quest_subtitle": "It's not a phase.",
  "quest.38E649B2924F1E95.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Necromancy, wither and life-stealing damage. Its focus, the \"},{\"text\":\"Blood Vial\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"irons_spellbooks:blood_vial\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", comes from a cauldron over a lit campfire: mobs standing in it cook into blood you can bottle.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.50F2031A01160D47.title": "School of Nature",
  "quest.50F2031A01160D47.quest_subtitle": "Grown locally, poisonous globally.",
  "quest.50F2031A01160D47.quest_desc": [
    "Debuffs first, then damage to finish: poison, roots, acid, a stomp. Its focus is the Poisonous Potato, and eight plain potatoes around one make four."
  ],
  "quest.4796CEA3BD858B10.title": "School of Ice",
  "quest.4796CEA3BD858B10.quest_subtitle": "Chill. Literally.",
  "quest.4796CEA3BD858B10.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Damage and crowd control: freezing rays, ice tombs, a polar bear. Its focus is the \"},{\"text\":\"Frozen Bone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"irons_spellbooks:frozen_bone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", dropped by a \"},{\"translate\":\"entity.minecraft.stray\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\"},{\"text\":\" in the snow; the Cryomancer in his mountain tower sells ice scrolls.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.115FD59DCE962219.title": "Pyromancer robes",
  "quest.115FD59DCE962219.quest_subtitle": "Dress for the job you want.",
  "quest.115FD59DCE962219.quest_desc": [
    "Eight Blaze Rods around a Blank Runestone make the Fire Rune, and each wizard piece it touches becomes Pyromancer: +10% fire power apiece. Keep the robe; late on it becomes the Infernal Sorcerer's chestplate."
  ],
  "quest.3C5E14957C2B2FD4.title": "Electromancer robes",
  "quest.3C5E14957C2B2FD4.quest_subtitle": "The hairdo is included. Upright.",
  "quest.3C5E14957C2B2FD4.quest_desc": [
    "Eight Bottles o' Lightning make the Lightning Rune, and each Electromancer piece adds 10% lightning power. Eight bottles means eight charged creepers: collect them in one long thunderstorm."
  ],
  "quest.67357F1DEA4D674E.title": "Shadow-Walker armour",
  "quest.67357F1DEA4D674E.quest_subtitle": "Lurking is a lifestyle.",
  "quest.67357F1DEA4D674E.quest_desc": [
    "Eight Ender Pearls make the Ender Rune, and each Shadow-Walker piece adds 10% ender power. The Dragonskin Spell Book adds another 10 on top, if you ever meet a dragon."
  ],
  "quest.1A3FE40267096C8E.title": "Archevoker coat",
  "quest.1A3FE40267096C8E.quest_subtitle": "Stolen fashion is still fashion.",
  "quest.1A3FE40267096C8E.quest_desc": [
    "Eight Emeralds make the Evocation Rune, unless an Archevoker drops one first. Each piece adds 10% evocation power, and the boots are the base of the Boots of Speed."
  ],
  "quest.58A0A148F65AEB00.title": "Priest robes",
  "quest.58A0A148F65AEB00.quest_subtitle": "Vows optional.",
  "quest.58A0A148F65AEB00.quest_desc": [
    "Eight Divine Pearls make the Holy Rune. Each Priest piece adds 10% holy power, and the robes are the base of the Lightbringer Chestplate later on."
  ],
  "quest.0CB62D92B5694C3F.title": "Cultist armour",
  "quest.0CB62D92B5694C3F.quest_subtitle": "Membership has its privileges.",
  "quest.0CB62D92B5694C3F.quest_desc": [
    "Eight Blood Vials make the Blood Rune: park a cauldron over a campfire next to a mob farm. Each Cultist piece adds 10% blood power."
  ],
  "quest.35B78B120361E1C1.title": "Plagued armour",
  "quest.35B78B120361E1C1.quest_subtitle": "Smells like victory. And rot.",
  "quest.35B78B120361E1C1.quest_desc": [
    "Eight Poisonous Potatoes make the Nature Rune, and one rune with a Mithril Scrap later makes a Poisonward Ring. Each Plagued piece adds 10% nature power."
  ],
  "quest.1584DCF89D376C8B.title": "Cryomancer coat",
  "quest.1584DCF89D376C8B.quest_subtitle": "Cold shoulders, warm heart.",
  "quest.1584DCF89D376C8B.quest_desc": [
    "Eight Frozen Bones make the Ice Rune, and each Cryomancer piece adds 10% ice power. The Frostbranded Book adds another 10 once you've met the Ice Spider."
  ],
  "quest.5E4295CD5E030CFF.title": "Mind the wizard's chests",
  "quest.5E4295CD5E030CFF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Nearly every Iron's structure keeps an Inscription Table, and wizards guard the chests and barrels around them. Open one while its owner is there and the trader becomes a fight: shop first, loot later.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.24BBF85D0C5C8CF1.title": "Find a Pyromancer Tower",
  "task.54695E94C12BE681.title": "Meet the Pyromancer",
  "quest.3789FDF73666994F.title": "The Pyromancer Tower",
  "quest.3789FDF73666994F.quest_subtitle": "Knock. He's armed.",
  "quest.3789FDF73666994F.quest_desc": [
    "A stone tower in hills, forests, plains and swamps. The Pyromancer inside sells fire scrolls and buys ink; his casks keep Fire Ale, which grants Fire Resistance and Haste for 45 seconds and a bit of nausea."
  ],
  "task.10FF0027F4DDCAAB.title": "Find a Mountain Tower",
  "task.1F232EA3C6B84624.title": "Meet the Cryomancer",
  "quest.4500547D8732D2BC.title": "The Mountain Tower",
  "quest.4500547D8732D2BC.quest_subtitle": "Great view. Terrible heating.",
  "quest.4500547D8732D2BC.quest_desc": [
    "A lone tower on mountains and snowy plains, home of the Cryomancer, who sells ice scrolls and buys ink. His ice barrel sometimes hides a Frostward Ring or an Affinity Ring."
  ],
  "task.73D5DB32A48B01E2.title": "Find a Mangrove Hut",
  "task.426BA08A99B38EBD.title": "Meet the Apothecarist",
  "quest.7802410ECA5C97C5.title": "The Mangrove Hut",
  "quest.7802410ECA5C97C5.quest_subtitle": "Potions, no questions.",
  "quest.7802410ECA5C97C5.quest_desc": [
    "A stilt hut in the swamp where the Apothecarist sells nature scrolls and elixirs. A hidden shelf keeps Netherward Tinctures: used on a hoglin or piglin, one stops it zombifying in the Overworld."
  ],
  "quest.6B13D17F2D534BDA.title": "Hogskin at home",
  "quest.6B13D17F2D534BDA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Put a Netherward Tincture on two hoglins, bring them to the Overworld and breed them: their piglets inherit the immunity, and the pen becomes a Hogskin farm far from the Crimson Forest.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.012981119CA525A7.title": "Meet a village Priest",
  "quest.51CDF302EADF274D.title": "The village Priest",
  "quest.51CDF302EADF274D.quest_subtitle": "Tithes accepted in emeralds.",
  "quest.51CDF302EADF274D.quest_desc": [
    "Some villages grow a chapel with a Priest in holy robes, counted as an ally by their golems. He sells healing potions, and his chests keep Divine Pearls."
  ],
  "task.4BBA7BD650AD27EC.title": "Find an Evoker Fort",
  "task.45A62D995848628C.title": "Defeat the Archevoker",
  "quest.4F4D13E31901C04A.title": "The Evoker Fort",
  "quest.4F4D13E31901C04A.quest_subtitle": "Illager HQ. Bring friends.",
  "quest.4F4D13E31901C04A.quest_desc": [
    "A walled camp in hills, forests, deserts and plains, held by illagers, Magehunter Vindicators and an Archevoker. He drops an evocation scroll, ink and, half the time, an Evocation Rune; his logbooks explain what he came for."
  ],
  "quest.7C4C3A9A3D74E7D4.title": "Evidence for the Priest",
  "quest.7C4C3A9A3D74E7D4.quest_subtitle": "Confession is good for the loot.",
  "quest.7C4C3A9A3D74E7D4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Bring a Priest the Archevoker's translated logbook from an Evoker Fort and he trades you a \"},{\"text\":\"Villager Bible\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"irons_spellbooks:villager_spell_book\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": ten slots, 10% holy power, 10% shorter casts and 200 mana.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.6CBDA6AD1AA699F7.title": "Find the Impaled Icebreaker",
  "quest.621FB7ED1FD9EBF0.title": "The Impaled Icebreaker",
  "quest.621FB7ED1FD9EBF0.quest_subtitle": "It did not break the ice.",
  "quest.621FB7ED1FD9EBF0.quest_desc": [
    "A ship run aground in frozen oceans, ice spikes and frozen peaks. Its captain's quarters always hold a Permafrost Shard, a spyglass, a bottle of Epic Ink and a bundle of emeralds."
  ],
  "quest.348AD9A4EC2BD728.title": "Furled Maps",
  "quest.348AD9A4EC2BD728.quest_subtitle": "X marks the tower.",
  "quest.348AD9A4EC2BD728.quest_desc": [
    "Found in chests, sold by traders or crafted, each points to one kind of structure: Evoker Fort battle plans, an Arctic Expedition Route, a Legion Outpost. Opened, it marks the nearest one nobody has explored yet."
  ],
  "task.7D0124B322D0E739.title": "Anger a wizard",
  "quest.1B76343F3F74B4E0.title": "A Fool's Folly",
  "quest.1B76343F3F74B4E0.quest_subtitle": "The chest was in plain sight. So were you.",
  "quest.1B76343F3F74B4E0.quest_desc": [
    "You opened a chest right under a wizard's nose. He noticed."
  ],
  "reward.7C0199482B9F448D.title": "Secret found",
  "task.3A316F4B3CAF4405.title": "Find a Rotten Spell Book",
  "quest.0AE8AE8DBF5A0B43.title": "How long's this been here?",
  "quest.0AE8AE8DBF5A0B43.quest_subtitle": "Smells like a library basement.",
  "quest.0AE8AE8DBF5A0B43.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Rotten Spell Book\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"irons_spellbooks:rotten_spell_book\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": eight slots and 100 mana, minus 15% spell resistance. Catacomb coffins and old dungeon chests leave them lying around.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.1B09C8170022F2EF.title": "Secret found",
  "task.7D567C0D8937CB56.title": "Craft a Druidic Tome",
  "quest.1EF102ED5F947ACE.title": "One with Nature",
  "quest.1EF102ED5F947ACE.quest_subtitle": "Compost, but make it literature.",
  "quest.1EF102ED5F947ACE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The rot came off: a Rotten Spell Book, a spore blossom, an amethyst cluster, honey, glow ink and two Arcane Cloth make a \"},{\"text\":\"Druidic Tome\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"irons_spellbooks:druidic_spell_book\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", ten slots and 10% nature power.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.41C3C929EC20CBEB.title": "Secret found",
  "task.537FC6DB271D6B42.title": "Loot a Blaze Instruction Manual",
  "quest.79C72E8A5ADE77EC.title": "Defunct Machinery",
  "quest.79C72E8A5ADE77EC.quest_subtitle": "Warranty void if ignited.",
  "quest.79C72E8A5ADE77EC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"One blaze in a hundred carries a \"},{\"text\":\"Blaze Instruction Manual\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"irons_spellbooks:blaze_spell_book\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", and yours didn't burn: ten slots, 10% fire power and 200 mana.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.0F9231220C86439B.title": "Secret found",
  "task.6E125D3D54D54E04.title": "Loot a Grimoire of Evokation",
  "quest.5134789FE92AE19B.title": "Grimoire of Evokation",
  "quest.5134789FE92AE19B.quest_subtitle": "Some assembly required. Fangs included.",
  "quest.5134789FE92AE19B.quest_desc": [
    "An Evoker or Archevoker let go of its book: Fang Strike, Fang Ward and Summon Vex locked inside, 10% evocation power and 200 mana. About one kill in a hundred."
  ],
  "reward.27B5CB8B3C8FB4BA.title": "Secret found",
  "image.67160097DD163264.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Books and staves\",\"color\":\"#8EC8FF\"}]",
  "image.13AE6AF4BF9F23F3.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Scrolls to order\",\"color\":\"#8EC8FF\"}]",
  "image.1B14F107B7473D08.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Alchemy\",\"color\":\"#8EC8FF\"}]",
  "image.0C5544D701D25C27.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Robes and mana\",\"color\":\"#8EC8FF\"}]",
  "image.3C37F67F40E420DF.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Mage towers\",\"color\":\"#8EC8FF\"}]",
  "image.4D15D6BFB84C8D4E.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Iron's Spells 'n Spellbooks\",\"color\":\"#8EC8FF\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.7FE01C4309B18198.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"ink scroll book spell\",\"color\":\"#C9D6FF\",\"font\":\"minecraft:alt\"}]",
  "image.37EAD02131776D12.title": "Back to the Sun of Heliodor",
  "image.4EB19D21CC30AE84.title": "On to Iron's Spells · The Arcane Anvil",
  "image.1DED3B9ADAAA0C71.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"fire\",\"color\":\"#AFC0FF\"}]",
  "image.42AB33CBB4A56887.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"lightning\",\"color\":\"#AFC0FF\"}]",
  "image.20179B023449D03B.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"ender\",\"color\":\"#AFC0FF\"}]",
  "image.53F8407A0D073CBF.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"evocation\",\"color\":\"#AFC0FF\"}]",
  "image.750C67949B653926.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"holy\",\"color\":\"#AFC0FF\"}]",
  "image.20FD44A2405DB76B.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"eldritch\",\"color\":\"#AFC0FF\"}]",
  "image.060253D667C0D5C1.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"blood\",\"color\":\"#AFC0FF\"}]",
  "image.1DB69F605601A19E.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"nature\",\"color\":\"#AFC0FF\"}]",
  "image.21537DEC944F48D5.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"ice\",\"color\":\"#AFC0FF\"}]",
  "chapter.2AE77651E66CB572.title": "Nature's Aura",
  "chapter.2AE77651E66CB572.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Gold leaf, a ring of stands and an altar at the heart: take aura from the ground, spend it well, give it back."
  ],
  "quest.23D456E8D1488BBE.title": "The Ritual of the Forest",
  "quest.23D456E8D1488BBE.quest_subtitle": "A tree gives its life for your recipe.",
  "quest.23D456E8D1488BBE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Gold Leaf\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:gold_leaf\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" over any log makes a \"},{\"text\":\"Wooden Stand\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:wood_stand\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", and one leaf crushes into two \"},{\"text\":\"Gold Powder\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:gold_powder\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Lay sixteen powder in a ring around a sapling as the book shows, put the ingredients on stands around it and let the sapling grow.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "When the tree grows, by time or bone meal, the ritual eats it and the result drops in the middle. Only the stands that hold an ingredient need to be there."
  ],
  "quest.1ABA937F5A5951D2.title": "The Environmental Eye",
  "quest.1ABA937F5A5951D2.quest_subtitle": "Never garden blind.",
  "quest.1ABA937F5A5951D2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A ritual of a \"},{\"text\":\"Spider Eye\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:spider_eye\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a \"},{\"text\":\"Gold Ingot\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:gold_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and two \"},{\"text\":\"Gold Leaf\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:gold_leaf\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" makes the \"},{\"text\":\"Environmental Eye\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:eye\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". In your hotbar it shows a bar at the top left: the aura around you, half full when the ground is untouched.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Look at an aura block, such as the altar, and a second bar shows what it holds."
  ],
  "quest.0E8C5FBA5BEA7FEB.title": "Bottled air",
  "quest.0E8C5FBA5BEA7FEB.quest_subtitle": "The only souvenir that is literally air.",
  "quest.0E8C5FBA5BEA7FEB.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Glass Bottle\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:glass_bottle\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and any planks make a \"},{\"text\":\"Bottle and Cork\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:bottle_two_the_rebottling\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Use it on the air where the aura is plentiful: it takes 20,000 from the richest spot nearby and holds sunlight in the Overworld, ghosts in the Nether and darkness in the End.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.10FCA52E96462BEC.title": "A Token of Joy",
  "quest.10FCA52E96462BEC.quest_subtitle": "Carved happiness, two per tree.",
  "quest.10FCA52E96462BEC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Tokens are wooden figurines of an emotion, and nearly every device takes one. \"},{\"text\":\"Joy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:token_joy\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" is a ritual of Bottled Sunlight, a \"},{\"text\":\"Gold Leaf\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:gold_leaf\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a small flower, an \"},{\"text\":\"Apple\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:apple\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a \"},{\"text\":\"Torch\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:torch\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and an \"},{\"text\":\"Iron Ingot\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:iron_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", and each ritual carves two.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.45D368FDE6DD8769.title": "The Natural Altar",
  "quest.45D368FDE6DD8769.quest_subtitle": "Pillars, gold and a little patience.",
  "quest.45D368FDE6DD8769.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A ritual of three \"},{\"text\":\"Stone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:stone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a \"},{\"text\":\"Gold Leaf\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:gold_leaf\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a \"},{\"text\":\"Gold Ingot\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:gold_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a \"},{\"text\":\"Token of Joy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:token_joy\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" makes the \"},{\"text\":\"Natural Altar\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:nature_altar\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Build its structure as the book shows: four pillars and a floor, with eight \"},{\"text\":\"Golden Stone Bricks\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:gold_brick\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (stone bricks and one Brilliant Fiber each).\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Complete, it draws up to 300 aura a tick from within 20 blocks and stores 500,000. It stops when the area runs empty, so on its own it never drives the ground below zero.",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"It collects Overworld and Nether aura, not the End's. In the Nether, build it with nether bricks and Golden Nether Bricks.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4992211AD7666DB4.title": "What the altar makes",
  "quest.4992211AD7666DB4.quest_subtitle": "Iron with a green thumb.",
  "quest.4992211AD7666DB4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Set one item on the altar and wait. An \"},{\"text\":\"Iron Ingot\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:iron_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" becomes \"},{\"text\":\"Infused Iron\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:infused_iron\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for 15,000 aura in four seconds; a \"},{\"text\":\"Gold Ingot\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:gold_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" becomes \"},{\"text\":\"Tainted Gold\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:tainted_gold\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for 3,000 in fifteen; \"},{\"text\":\"Stone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:stone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" becomes \"},{\"text\":\"Infused Rock\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:infused_stone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Blocks work too.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The altar holds one item at a time and only lets finished ones out, so a hopper above it and one below make a production line.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5177A56C364EFD6A.title": "Bottled ghosts",
  "quest.5177A56C364EFD6A.quest_subtitle": "Spooky, scary, and it corks.",
  "quest.5177A56C364EFD6A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Take a \"},{\"text\":\"Bottle and Cork\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:bottle_two_the_rebottling\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" to the Nether and use it on the air: the aura there comes out as ghosts. Ghosts go into the Tokens of Fear and Anger and the Spirit of Calling, and the Natural Altar works in the Nether too.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.54A733D4D80AF58D.title": "Fear and Sorrow",
  "quest.54A733D4D80AF58D.quest_subtitle": "Two moods the gods respect.",
  "quest.54A733D4D80AF58D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Fear\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:token_fear\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" carves from Bottled Ghosts, a \"},{\"text\":\"Gold Leaf\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:gold_leaf\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", \"},{\"text\":\"Rotten Flesh\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:rotten_flesh\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a \"},{\"text\":\"Feather\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:feather\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a \"},{\"text\":\"Bone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:bone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and \"},{\"text\":\"Soul Sand\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:soul_sand\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". \"},{\"text\":\"Sorrow\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:token_sorrow\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" from Bottled Sunlight, a leaf, a \"},{\"text\":\"Ghast Tear\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:ghast_tear\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", raw meat, glass and a fish.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6544882E3E98EE62.title": "The Offering Table",
  "quest.6544882E3E98EE62.quest_subtitle": "Flowers for the gods, in two rings.",
  "quest.6544882E3E98EE62.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three stone, \"},{\"text\":\"Infused Iron\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:infused_iron\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a \"},{\"text\":\"Token of Fear\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:token_fear\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a \"},{\"text\":\"Token of Sorrow\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:token_sorrow\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and three logs make the \"},{\"text\":\"Offering Table\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:offering_table\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Plant two rings of small flowers around it as the book shows; any small flower counts.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.61D7D048F05DA8C6.title": "Gold that grows on trees",
  "quest.61D7D048F05DA8C6.quest_subtitle": "Money does grow on trees. You just have to ask.",
  "quest.61D7D048F05DA8C6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four leaves, four \"},{\"text\":\"Gold Nuggets\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:gold_nugget\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and one \"},{\"text\":\"Short Grass\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:short_grass\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make four \"},{\"text\":\"Brilliant Fiber\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:gold_fiber\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Use one on the leaves of any tree: the gold spreads through the crown, and fully golden leaves drop \"},{\"text\":\"Gold Leaf\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:gold_leaf\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.441C4201C1880A9C.title": "The Book of Natural Aura",
  "quest.441C4201C1880A9C.quest_subtitle": "A manual that grows with you.",
  "quest.441C4201C1880A9C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two \"},{\"text\":\"Paper\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:paper\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a \"},{\"text\":\"Leather\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:leather\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and any sapling, shapeless. Its chapters open as you earn the mod's advancements: a red mark is a new chapter, an orange one your next research step, and the front page links to the advancement tab.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.154F3AA4AAD11341.title": "Pick them ripe",
  "quest.154F3AA4AAD11341.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Golden leaves ripen through four stages and, from the third, gild a neighbouring leaf now and then. Break them only when fully gold: each then drops a \"},{\"text\":\"Gold Leaf\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:gold_leaf\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" three times in four; earlier, nothing.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.47441405B6AAB511.title": "Plants that hum",
  "quest.47441405B6AAB511.quest_subtitle": "Pressed flowers for a magical botanist.",
  "quest.47441405B6AAB511.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Aura Blooms\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:aura_bloom\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" grow on grass all over the Overworld, \"},{\"text\":\"Aura Cacti\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:aura_cactus\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in sandy biomes, and \"},{\"text\":\"Crimson\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:crimson_aura_mushroom\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and \"},{\"text\":\"Warped Aura Fungi\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:warped_aura_mushroom\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in the Nether. Every one the world generates leaves 150,000 extra aura in the ground around it.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"That makes their patches the gentlest place to fill your first bottles. The purple \"},{\"text\":\"Aura Mushroom\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:aura_mushroom\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" grows only on mushroom islands, and all of them fit in a flower pot.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.55EDA79C71E709D6.title": "The sapling decides",
  "quest.55EDA79C71E709D6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Each ritual names its sapling: almost all take an \"},{\"text\":\"Oak Sapling\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:oak_sapling\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", but the Transmutation Catalyst and the Powder of Fertility want a \"},{\"text\":\"Jungle Sapling\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:jungle_sapling\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". After the tree grows, a ritual takes ten to thirty seconds.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5C0DDAD164835AD4.title": "Wear it, don't hold it",
  "quest.5C0DDAD164835AD4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Curios slots take the mod's trinkets: the Environmental Eye and Ocular a charm, the Aura Cache and Trove a belt, the Amulet of Wrath a necklace and the Ring of Last Chance a ring. Every one of them works from there.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.09484EBB494EFD55.title": "The world is a battery",
  "quest.09484EBB494EFD55.quest_desc": [
    "Aura is not stored in nodes: it lies in the ground everywhere, a million units wherever nothing has touched it. Drains pull from the richest spot nearby and generators fill the poorest, so a drained area heals first when you add a generator.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Left alone, aura drifts to even itself out. Pushed more than 150 blocks from where it was made, it slowly fizzles away."
  ],
  "quest.244FA97B79277C8B.title": "A bottle of nothing",
  "quest.244FA97B79277C8B.quest_subtitle": "Contents: absolutely nothing. Handle with care.",
  "quest.244FA97B79277C8B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Where devices have dragged the aura far below empty, past what the Environmental Eye can show, a \"},{\"text\":\"Bottle and Cork\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:bottle_two_the_rebottling\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" catches a \"},{\"text\":\"Bottled Vacuum\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:vacuum_bottle\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" instead of aura. It is the heart of the Aura Imbalance Ward.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.24CFD6B0622822C3.title": "The Aura Imbalance Ward",
  "quest.24CFD6B0622822C3.quest_subtitle": "A seatbelt for your machines.",
  "quest.24CFD6B0622822C3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four \"},{\"text\":\"Infused Rock\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:infused_stone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", the four stronger tokens and a \"},{\"text\":\"Bottled Vacuum\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:vacuum_bottle\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make the \"},{\"text\":\"Aura Imbalance Ward\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:lower_limiter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Place it against a device that spends aura: the device only runs while the area stays above zero after its cost. The ward itself costs nothing.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.116B803C6C4E8D37.title": "Too little, too much",
  "quest.116B803C6C4E8D37.quest_desc": [
    "Below an empty bar, grass and leaves decay, netherrack rots into soul soil, breathing hurts and endermen and zombified piglins lose their temper; far below, the surface explodes. From three quarters of the bar up, crops grow in spurts, Aura Caches refill and netherrack grows grass.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Only the Overworld and the Nether suffer decay. The book's Aura Imbalance chapter lists every effect, and the Environmental Ocular shows the active ones."
  ],
  "quest.461C04169FA78A2B.title": "The Aura Detector",
  "quest.461C04169FA78A2B.quest_subtitle": "A thermometer with a redstone tongue.",
  "quest.461C04169FA78A2B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An \"},{\"text\":\"Environmental Eye\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:eye\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" ringed by \"},{\"text\":\"Infused Rock\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:infused_stone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and redstone makes the \"},{\"text\":\"Aura Detector\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:aura_detector\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". A \"},{\"text\":\"Redstone Comparator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:comparator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" against it reads the aura within 25 blocks: 15 is a full bar, half that is untouched ground. Use it to switch generators off before they overflow.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1F0C745EFAEBBCD8.title": "The Redstone Aura Vaporizer",
  "quest.1F0C745EFAEBBCD8.quest_subtitle": "Tick, tock, sunlight.",
  "quest.1F0C745EFAEBBCD8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Bottled aura in the \"},{\"text\":\"Redstone Aura Vaporizer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:aura_timer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" evaporates at a fixed pace and emits a pulse each time: sunlight lasts a second, ghosts a minute and darkness an hour, and more bottles add up. A redstone signal resets it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.544CC0113B575494.title": "Deadly Day",
  "quest.544CC0113B575494.quest_subtitle": "Congratulations, you broke the grass.",
  "quest.544CC0113B575494.quest_desc": [
    "The aura around you hit zero. Plant Ancient Trees to refill the ground and put an Aura Imbalance Ward beside anything that drains on its own."
  ],
  "reward.26C75992DD9A76D8.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.61D6F861B8C8FD80.title": "Effect Powder",
  "quest.61D6F861B8C8FD80.quest_subtitle": "Magic, by the pinch.",
  "quest.61D6F861B8C8FD80.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Rituals make powders that switch an imbalance effect off, or on for the ones that need them. Drop a stack on the ground: its range in blocks equals the stack size; hit it to pick it up. \"},{\"text\":\"Powder of Steady Growth\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:effect_powder\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" stops the crop spurts.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Powder Manipulator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:powder_placer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" lays powder from a chest beside it on a redstone pulse and picks it back up on the next.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.194BC2B18DD77BED.title": "Increase of Fertility",
  "quest.194BC2B18DD77BED.quest_subtitle": "Romance is in the air. Literally.",
  "quest.194BC2B18DD77BED.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A jungle-sapling ritual of two Gold Powder, an \"},{\"text\":\"Ingot of the Skies\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:sky_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and an \"},{\"text\":\"Egg\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:egg\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" makes eight \"},{\"text\":\"Powder of Fertility\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:effect_powder\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Near it, above three quarters of the bar, animals breed on their own and dropped eggs hatch, until 200 animals crowd the area.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.09A048CBBB5316C5.title": "Mineral Amassing",
  "quest.09A048CBBB5316C5.quest_subtitle": "The ground grows ores. Nobody asks how.",
  "quest.09A048CBBB5316C5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two Gold Powder, a \"},{\"text\":\"Diamond Ore\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:diamond_ore\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a \"},{\"text\":\"Redstone Ore\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:redstone_ore\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make four \"},{\"text\":\"Powder of the Bountiful Core\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:effect_powder\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". With the aura past the top of the Environmental Eye's bar, which takes a Creational Catalyst, ores appear in the stone around it; it drinks a lot of aura doing it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5B7EE54AECCA4453.title": "Bottled darkness",
  "quest.5B7EE54AECCA4453.quest_subtitle": "The End: now available to go.",
  "quest.5B7EE54AECCA4453.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"In the End, a \"},{\"text\":\"Bottle and Cork\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:bottle_two_the_rebottling\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" fills with darkness. Darkness goes into the World Eye, the Lamp of Sanctuary, the Ender Crate, the Eye of the Shulker and the Aura Attraction Cart; the altar turns it into \"},{\"text\":\"Dragon's Breath\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:dragon_breath\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" with a Transmutation Catalyst.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3D990502C6760FA3.title": "The World Eye",
  "quest.3D990502C6760FA3.quest_subtitle": "Someone has to keep watching.",
  "quest.3D990502C6760FA3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"World Eye\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:chunk_loader\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" keeps an area loaded for a little aura. A redstone signal sets its radius, up to about 30 blocks at full strength, and the loaded area can come out slightly bigger. Be kind to shared servers.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.41D803B6CBC77922.title": "Ender Crate and Ocular",
  "quest.41D803B6CBC77922.quest_subtitle": "Same box, any dimension.",
  "quest.41D803B6CBC77922.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Crates that share an Ender Name share one inventory, across dimensions. Name one on an anvil with an \"},{\"text\":\"Eye of Ender\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:ender_eye\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; the \"},{\"text\":\"Ender Ocular\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:ender_access\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" opens the same storage from your hand, paid from an Aura Cache.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A Token of Terror inside a crate locks its name, so nobody else can claim it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.16F95EDC5F597890.title": "The Aura Attraction Cart",
  "quest.16F95EDC5F597890.quest_subtitle": "Aura, now shipped by rail.",
  "quest.16F95EDC5F597890.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Aura Attraction Cart\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:mover_cart\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" carries aura along rails. A powered activator rail makes it grab the excess aura around it; an unpowered one makes it let go. Some aura is lost on the way.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.62807C86526F1FA4.title": "The Lamp of Sanctuary",
  "quest.62807C86526F1FA4.quest_subtitle": "Monsters: not on my lawn.",
  "quest.62807C86526F1FA4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"With a redstone signal, the \"},{\"text\":\"Lamp of Sanctuary\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:spawn_lamp\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" stops monsters from spawning within up to about 48 blocks, whatever the light. The signal's strength sets the range, and each spawn it prevents costs a little aura.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.18050EDDAEA8B54E.title": "Rails of the Worlds",
  "quest.18050EDDAEA8B54E.quest_subtitle": "Mind the gap between dimensions.",
  "quest.18050EDDAEA8B54E.quest_desc": [
    "A minecart rolling over one of these rails lands in that rail's dimension: Overworld and Nether trade places at one eighth of the distance, the End sends you to its obsidian platform and back to world spawn. Carts with living passengers stay put."
  ],
  "quest.02B79EE4FDE7D058.title": "Eyes that fly home",
  "quest.02B79EE4FDE7D058.quest_subtitle": "Like an Eye of Ender, with better taste.",
  "quest.02B79EE4FDE7D058.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Thrown, each eye flies toward its structure like an Eye of Ender: the \"},{\"text\":\"Eye of the Blaze\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:fortress_finder\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" to a Nether fortress, the \"},{\"text\":\"Eye of the Shulker\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:end_city_finder\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" to an End city and the \"},{\"text\":\"Eye of the Pillager\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:outpost_finder\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" to a pillager outpost. Each takes two bottles of its dimension's aura.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.465F5DC640F8DB06.title": "Aura from the End",
  "quest.465F5DC640F8DB06.quest_subtitle": "The dragon leaves flowers behind.",
  "quest.465F5DC640F8DB06.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Once the Ender Dragon dies, \"},{\"text\":\"Roses of Oblivion\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:end_flower\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" sprout on the End island. Drop an \"},{\"text\":\"Eye of Ender\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:ender_eye\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" beside one, in any dimension: it swallows the eye and releases 500,000 aura, no catalyst needed.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Reaper of Ender Heights\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:chorus_generator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" harvests a whole chorus plant growing within two blocks on a redstone signal; the taller and wider the plant, the more aura.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.52DF6B1354B40B19.title": "The Environmental Ocular",
  "quest.52DF6B1354B40B19.quest_subtitle": "Suddenly I see a lot better.",
  "quest.52DF6B1354B40B19.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A ritual of the \"},{\"text\":\"Environmental Eye\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:eye\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", two \"},{\"text\":\"Ingots of the Skies\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:sky_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a \"},{\"text\":\"Rose of Oblivion\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:end_flower\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and two Gold Leaf makes the \"},{\"text\":\"Environmental Ocular\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:eye_improved\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Its bar reaches twice as far, it works from anywhere in the inventory and it shows an icon for each imbalance effect where you stand.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7F4D00FE009AE647.title": "Infused iron for the common store",
  "quest.7F4D00FE009AE647.quest_subtitle": "The workshop always wants more.",
  "quest.7F4D00FE009AE647.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight \"},{\"text\":\"Infused Iron\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:infused_iron\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for the common store. The Aura Cache, the Offering Table, the Spirit of Calling and most devices each take some.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6099370A6BFA9DFE.title": "Hoppers with manners",
  "quest.6099370A6BFA9DFE.quest_subtitle": "Items, sorted with a green thumb.",
  "quest.6099370A6BFA9DFE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Hopper Enhancement\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:hopper_upgrade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on top of a hopper pulls items from about seven blocks away, a little aura each. The \"},{\"text\":\"Adept Hopper\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:grated_chute\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" is a faster hopper that only passes items shown in item frames on its sides; use it to invert the filter.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Item Distributor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:item_distributor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" takes from a container above and deals items evenly into the containers at its sides.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3FEBFE2C75518997.title": "The Imperceptible Builder",
  "quest.3FEBFE2C75518997.quest_subtitle": "Plop, plop, placement.",
  "quest.3FEBFE2C75518997.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Imperceptible Builder\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:placer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" places blocks from a container on top of it onto matching blocks within about five: cobblestone in an item frame on it and planks in the chest lay planks on every cobblestone. A \"},{\"text\":\"Farming Stencil\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:farming_stencil\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in the frame targets farmland. Redstone pauses it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.77BD2EF5398C4F34.title": "Invisible fences",
  "quest.77BD2EF5398C4F34.quest_subtitle": "Stay. Good cow.",
  "quest.77BD2EF5398C4F34.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Corporeal Eye\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:animal_container\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" keeps animals from leaving its area without a single fence; the \"},{\"text\":\"Item Grounder\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:pickup_stopper\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" lets dropped items be picked up only by someone sneaking, up to eight blocks away. On both, the redstone signal sets the range.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3A31B8FDDFF83B8B.title": "The Crumbling Catalyst",
  "quest.3A31B8FDDFF83B8B.quest_subtitle": "Your altar, now with a mortar and pestle.",
  "quest.3A31B8FDDFF83B8B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Anger\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:token_anger\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" carves from Bottled Ghosts, a leaf, a \"},{\"text\":\"Magma Block\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:magma_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", \"},{\"text\":\"Blaze Powder\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:blaze_powder\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", \"},{\"text\":\"Gunpowder\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:gunpowder\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and an \"},{\"text\":\"Ender Pearl\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:ender_pearl\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Add a golden brick, Infused Rock, a piston and flint for the \"},{\"text\":\"Crumbling Catalyst\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:crushing_catalyst\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Set it on one of the altar's four lower golden bricks and the altar crushes: a bone into six bone meal, a Gold Leaf into four Gold Powder, a blaze rod into four powder, cobblestone into sand. The first three are twice what a crafting grid gives."
  ],
  "quest.7DF9910955D1C05F.title": "The Extraneous Firestarter",
  "quest.7DF9910955D1C05F.quest_subtitle": "Cozy warmth, charged to the planet.",
  "quest.7DF9910955D1C05F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A ritual of two \"},{\"text\":\"Infused Rock\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:infused_stone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", \"},{\"text\":\"Tainted Gold\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:tainted_gold\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", \"},{\"text\":\"Infused Iron\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:infused_iron\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a \"},{\"text\":\"Fire Charge\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:fire_charge\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", flint, a magma block and a \"},{\"text\":\"Token of Fear\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:token_fear\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" makes the \"},{\"text\":\"Extraneous Firestarter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:furnace_heater\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Against any side of a furnace, it heats and speeds it with aura.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"It keeps drinking even past empty, so the ground can go negative.\",\"color\":\"#FF8C7A\"},{\"text\":\" An Aura Imbalance Ward beside it stops that.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.29894D4BE81A76E9.title": "Armorer's Aid",
  "quest.29894D4BE81A76E9.quest_subtitle": "Two ingots for the price of one, sometimes.",
  "quest.29894D4BE81A76E9.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An \"},{\"text\":\"Extraneous Firestarter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:furnace_heater\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a \"},{\"text\":\"Blast Furnace\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:blast_furnace\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", two Tokens of Terror, Infused Iron and cobblestone make \"},{\"text\":\"Armorer's Aid\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:blast_furnace_booster\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". On top of a blast furnace it gives each ore a chance at two ingots, and hoppers can feed it from any side.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0DC0D0332C4F6397.title": "The Aura Cache",
  "quest.0DC0D0332C4F6397.quest_subtitle": "Ca-ching.",
  "quest.0DC0D0332C4F6397.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four \"},{\"text\":\"Infused Rock\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:infused_stone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", four \"},{\"text\":\"Infused Iron\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:infused_iron\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a \"},{\"text\":\"Bucket\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make the \"},{\"text\":\"Aura Cache\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:aura_cache\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": 400,000 aura to carry. Set it on the altar to fill it. The mod's staffs and trinkets draw from it, and while you sneak it repairs the mod's tools in hand and its armor, 300 aura a point.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The book still has Nature's Mend pages, but 41.9 registers no such enchantment:\",\"color\":\"#FF8C7A\"},{\"text\":\" only Nature's Aura gear repairs from aura.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4057018AB5A21247.title": "Botanist's gear",
  "quest.4057018AB5A21247.quest_subtitle": "Tools with a green thumb.",
  "quest.4057018AB5A21247.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Infused Iron with Ancient Wood Rods for handles, so grow an Ancient Tree first. The \"},{\"text\":\"Botanist's Pickaxe\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:infused_iron_pickaxe\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" turns blocks mossy on right-click and the \"},{\"text\":\"Blade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:infused_iron_sword\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" slows what it hits; the axe clears leaves fast, the shovel spreads grass and the hoe finds seeds.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "The full Botanist's armor gives attackers a short Wither, and makes the Amulet of Wrath's shockwave wither them too."
  ],
  "quest.42D035F965D782A4.title": "Skyseeker's gear",
  "quest.42D035F965D782A4.quest_subtitle": "Diamonds never fall into lava again.",
  "quest.42D035F965D782A4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Ingots of the Skies on Ancient Wood Rods. The \"},{\"text\":\"Skyseeker's Pickaxe\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:sky_pickaxe\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" sends what it mines straight to your inventory, and the \"},{\"text\":\"Handaxe\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:sky_axe\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", switched on by sneak-using it, fells small trees at once. The shovel swaps blocks for the one in your off-hand and the hoe tills wide.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "The full Skyseeker's armor, or the set with an Elytra, makes you faster and lets you step up full blocks. The blade makes its targets float."
  ],
  "quest.25DD37FFB2ED5D5E.title": "Soulstrider's gear",
  "quest.25DD37FFB2ED5D5E.quest_subtitle": "Sky, earth and the depths in one bar.",
  "quest.25DD37FFB2ED5D5E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two \"},{\"text\":\"Ingots of the Skies\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:sky_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", two Tainted Gold and a \"},{\"text\":\"Netherite Scrap\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:netherite_scrap\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make an \"},{\"text\":\"Ingot of the Depths\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:depth_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Sneak-use the \"},{\"text\":\"Soulstrider's Pickaxe\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:depth_pickaxe\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" to mine whole ore veins; the handaxe fells any tree, however big.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "The shovel greens a wide area of dirt, the hoe clears leaves far around and the blade sweeps a crowd. The full armor freezes nearby enemies in place when you are struck."
  ],
  "quest.08614DCFBD78E746.title": "Striding in Style",
  "quest.08614DCFBD78E746.quest_subtitle": "Nine pieces. No regrets.",
  "quest.08614DCFBD78E746.quest_desc": [
    "Every Soulstrider's tool and armor piece, at once: thirty-five Ingots of the Depths, seventy sky ingots from the offering bowl."
  ],
  "reward.38BAD0EF2CA98ECB.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.4A49A9E8732DD39F.title": "The Aura Trove",
  "quest.4A49A9E8732DD39F.quest_subtitle": "Three caches in a trenchcoat.",
  "quest.4A49A9E8732DD39F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An \"},{\"text\":\"Aura Cache\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:aura_cache\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" with four \"},{\"text\":\"Ingots of the Skies\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:sky_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and four Infused Rock becomes the \"},{\"text\":\"Aura Trove\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:aura_trove\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": 1,200,000 aura, three times the cache.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0D6AB7E547FC1356.title": "The Mystical Magnifier",
  "quest.0D6AB7E547FC1356.quest_subtitle": "I spy with my little eye.",
  "quest.0D6AB7E547FC1356.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Hold the \"},{\"text\":\"Mystical Magnifier\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:range_visualizer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and use it on a device to see its working range drawn around it; use it again to hide it. On a Rail of the Worlds it marks the destination, even through walls.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3BFA3A15B7DDEF56.title": "Staffs that find",
  "quest.3BFA3A15B7DDEF56.quest_subtitle": "Treasure hunting, sponsored by aura.",
  "quest.3BFA3A15B7DDEF56.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Swung with an Aura Cache on you: the \"},{\"text\":\"Staff of Riches\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:loot_finder\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" lights up containers within about 64 blocks for a minute, the \"},{\"text\":\"Staff of Shadows\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:cave_finder\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" shows dark spots where monsters can spawn for half a minute, and the \"},{\"text\":\"Staff of Ancient Knowledge\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:netherite_finder\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" marks Ancient Debris through stone.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3A63930AA6A005BC.title": "Wrath and light",
  "quest.3A63930AA6A005BC.quest_subtitle": "Stomp first, ask questions later.",
  "quest.3A63930AA6A005BC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"With the \"},{\"text\":\"Amulet of Wrath\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:shockwave_creator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" anywhere on you, sneak and jump in place to stomp a shockwave that hurts everything close. The \"},{\"text\":\"Staff of Baldur\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:light_staff\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" fires a ray that lights up where it lands, as if glowstone were there, and sets creatures on fire. Both run on a cache.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.688C721A5A7E5C04.title": "Against loss",
  "quest.688C721A5A7E5C04.quest_subtitle": "Death, delayed. Paperwork pending.",
  "quest.688C721A5A7E5C04.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Ring of Last Chance\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:death_ring\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" saves you from death once, like a totem, and is used up. The \"},{\"text\":\"Token of Undying Friendship\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:pet_reviver\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", given to a tamed pet, sends it home instead of letting it die. \"},{\"text\":\"Eir's Token\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:break_prevention\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on an anvil makes a tool stop working at zero durability instead of breaking.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1EFEEF9BC6A10011.title": "The Bucket of Infinite Color",
  "quest.1EFEEF9BC6A10011.quest_subtitle": "Three dyes, every color.",
  "quest.1EFEEF9BC6A10011.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Sneak-use the \"},{\"text\":\"Bucket of Infinite Color\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:color_changer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on any dyed block to take its color, then use it to paint. Sneak-use it in the air for fill mode, which repaints every touching block of the same color. The paint is aura from a cache.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5C7810C168AFECD6.title": "Crimson Meal",
  "quest.5C7810C168AFECD6.quest_subtitle": "Bone meal, but make it Nether.",
  "quest.5C7810C168AFECD6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight \"},{\"text\":\"Bone Meal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:bone_meal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" around Bottled Ghosts make eight \"},{\"text\":\"Crimson Meal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:crimson_meal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Each use on \"},{\"text\":\"Nether Wart\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:nether_wart\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" has a one-in-five chance to grow it; used on bare soul sand, it can plant warts around.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.258DC1B17D1B42E8.title": "A wart the size of a tree",
  "quest.258DC1B17D1B42E8.quest_subtitle": "Some mushrooms just want to be trees.",
  "quest.258DC1B17D1B42E8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Crimson Meal on fully grown Nether Wart can raise a whole \"},{\"text\":\"Nether Wart Mushroom\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:nether_wart_mushroom\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", and Silk Touch keeps a block of it. Without it, each block drops one or two warts.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.1A23571A03ABB8A7.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.7D4CCA7580D5B1D1.title": "Ancient Trees",
  "quest.7D4CCA7580D5B1D1.quest_subtitle": "They give until they're bare.",
  "quest.7D4CCA7580D5B1D1.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A ritual of an \"},{\"text\":\"Oak Sapling\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:oak_sapling\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a \"},{\"text\":\"Dandelion\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:dandelion\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a \"},{\"text\":\"Poppy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:poppy\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", \"},{\"text\":\"Wheat Seeds\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:wheat_seeds\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", \"},{\"text\":\"Sugar Cane\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:sugar_cane\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a \"},{\"text\":\"Gold Leaf\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:gold_leaf\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" makes two \"},{\"text\":\"Ancient Saplings\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:ancient_sapling\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Grown, their leaves feed drained ground within 25 blocks back toward normal, and wilt as they give.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "They only work in the Overworld. Their logs make Ancient Wood Rods, the handle of every Nature's Aura tool and staff."
  ],
  "quest.7447D8C94CD8B600.title": "The Herbivorous Absorber",
  "quest.7447D8C94CD8B600.quest_subtitle": "A picky eater with a sweet tooth.",
  "quest.7447D8C94CD8B600.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Infused Iron\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:infused_iron\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a \"},{\"text\":\"Token of Joy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:token_joy\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a \"},{\"text\":\"Peony\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:peony\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and planks make the \"},{\"text\":\"Herbivorous Absorber\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:flower_generator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Every half second it eats a small flower within three blocks for up to 25,000 aura, in the Overworld only.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "The same kind again is worth 500 less each time, and eating other kinds lets it recover, so plant about six kinds and it stays at full value."
  ],
  "quest.1D0F0FEE089CC36B.title": "Red sparks mean full",
  "quest.1D0F0FEE089CC36B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Generators stop adding aura once the area within 35 blocks would pass the top of the Environmental Eye's bar, and red sparks fly from them. An Aura Detector can switch them off before that; a Creational Catalyst underneath lifts the limit.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7FF688D0F84EBBD4.title": "Aura from the garden",
  "quest.7FF688D0F84EBBD4.quest_subtitle": "Tidy trees, clean stones, happy planet.",
  "quest.7FF688D0F84EBBD4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Canopy Diminisher\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:oak_generator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" makes oaks within ten blocks grow small, and each big oak it prevents becomes 100,000 aura: a tree farm's best friend. The \"},{\"text\":\"Swamp Homi\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:moss_generator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" scrubs the moss off mossy blocks around it, a little aura per block. The Diminisher only works in the Overworld.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3CD669119305D757.title": "The Ritual of the Brewer",
  "quest.3CD669119305D757.quest_subtitle": "Brewed for the planet, not for you.",
  "quest.3CD669119305D757.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Build the \"},{\"text\":\"Lingering Absorber\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:potion_generator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"'s structure as the book shows, then throw a positive lingering potion beside it: the effect turns into aura, more for longer and stronger effects. One potion at a time, or the others go to waste.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3963C0259CD52088.title": "Aura from creatures",
  "quest.3963C0259CD52088.quest_subtitle": "Grim, but efficient.",
  "quest.3963C0259CD52088.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Passive animals killed near the \"},{\"text\":\"Disentangler of Mortals\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:animal_generator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" free their soul as aura, far more after about an hour and a half of life, and drop nothing. The \"},{\"text\":\"Offshoot Observer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:slime_split_generator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" turns each slime or magma cube that splits nearby into aura, more for bigger and rarer ones.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4AB62CCA8BFAC29B.title": "Aura on target",
  "quest.4AB62CCA8BFAC29B.quest_subtitle": "Aim for the north side. Always the north side.",
  "quest.4AB62CCA8BFAC29B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Shoot the \"},{\"text\":\"Shooting Mark\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:projectile_generator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"'s four sides in order, starting with north: each hit on the active side becomes aura, an ender pearl worth far more than a snowball. The \"},{\"text\":\"Firecracker Gaze\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:firework_generator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" launches fireworks dropped near it and turns the explosions into aura, more for fancier rockets.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6E3C0FEEC0276B33.title": "The Creational Catalyst",
  "quest.6E3C0FEEC0276B33.quest_subtitle": "No ceiling, only fizzle.",
  "quest.6E3C0FEEC0276B33.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four \"},{\"text\":\"Infused Rock\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:infused_stone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", the four stronger tokens and \"},{\"text\":\"Tainted Gold\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:tainted_gold\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make the \"},{\"text\":\"Creational Catalyst\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:generator_limit_remover\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Directly under a generator, it lets it keep adding aura past the top of the Environmental Eye's bar.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.20D5AAF1E3A44A3B.title": "The Spirit of Calling",
  "quest.20D5AAF1E3A44A3B.quest_subtitle": "Knocking on heaven's door, in triplicate.",
  "quest.20D5AAF1E3A44A3B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Bottled Sunlight on top, Bottled Ghosts below, \"},{\"text\":\"Infused Iron\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:infused_iron\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and \"},{\"text\":\"Tainted Gold\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:tainted_gold\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" at the sides and a \"},{\"text\":\"Diamond\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:diamond\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in the middle make three \"},{\"text\":\"Spirits of Calling\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:calling_spirit\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", the item that summons the gods' attention.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.14A224DDD4B25015.title": "One spirit, one bowl",
  "quest.14A224DDD4B25015.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"One spirit converts the whole bowl, up to sixteen items, so always fill it. Throw exactly one spirit within a block of the table: a dropped stack of them is ignored.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The gifts fall from the top of the world onto the table, so leave the sky above it open. A \"},{\"text\":\"Wither Rose\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:wither_rose\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in the rings makes the gods throw some \"},{\"text\":\"Black Dye\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:black_dye\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in with them.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.08001C294EFA9C63.title": "Ingots of the Skies",
  "quest.08001C294EFA9C63.quest_subtitle": "When the gods pay, they pay in metal.",
  "quest.08001C294EFA9C63.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Fill the table's bowl with \"},{\"text\":\"Infused Iron\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:infused_iron\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and throw one \"},{\"text\":\"Spirit of Calling\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:calling_spirit\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" beside it: a harmless bolt strikes and each ingot comes back as an \"},{\"text\":\"Ingot of the Skies\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:sky_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". \"},{\"text\":\"Tainted Gold\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:tainted_gold\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" gives two apiece.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "In this pack sky ingots are an act V material: the Powah spirited capacitor, the Draconic Endshelf, the horizon shelves, the Renewal Engine and act VI's Luminous Ingot all take them."
  ],
  "quest.5C61FC7DC4A15D47.title": "The Renewal Engine",
  "quest.5C61FC7DC4A15D47.quest_subtitle": "Keep the table busy.",
  "quest.5C61FC7DC4A15D47.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two \"},{\"text\":\"Ingots of the Skies\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:sky_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", two imperium essences, two Ecosystem Capsules and two Propagation Cores make the \"},{\"text\":\"Renewal Engine\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:renewal_engine\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", delivered for «Renewable Horizons» in act V. Mekanism's SPS port and the Mega pot upgrade take one each too.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0A7328CE39A59CC0.title": "A balanced grove",
  "quest.0A7328CE39A59CC0.quest_subtitle": "Leave it greener than you found it.",
  "quest.0A7328CE39A59CC0.quest_desc": [
    "Stand where the aura reaches three quarters of the Environmental Eye's bar, checked every ten seconds within 25 blocks of you. Ancient Trees, absorbers and generators have to out-produce everything the altar and your devices drain.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "At that level crops grow in spurts and Aura Caches refill on their own. Heliodor's gardens kept growing after everyone vanished; this one grows because of you."
  ],
  "quest.2F031A06427A0781.title": "Stronger feelings",
  "quest.2F031A06427A0781.quest_subtitle": "Upgrade your emotional range.",
  "quest.2F031A06427A0781.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Offer a token instead of iron: Joy comes back as \"},{\"text\":\"Euphoria\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:token_euphoria\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", Fear as \"},{\"text\":\"Terror\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:token_terror\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", Anger as \"},{\"text\":\"Rage\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:token_rage\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and Sorrow as \"},{\"text\":\"Grief\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:token_grief\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". The late devices and trinkets are built from these.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1E0BA88629F4B13E.title": "The Transmutation Catalyst",
  "quest.1E0BA88629F4B13E.quest_subtitle": "Not-so-equivalent exchange.",
  "quest.1E0BA88629F4B13E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A jungle-sapling ritual of a golden brick, \"},{\"text\":\"Infused Rock\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:infused_stone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a \"},{\"text\":\"Brewing Stand\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:brewing_stand\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", an \"},{\"text\":\"Ingot of the Skies\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:sky_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a Gold Leaf and \"},{\"text\":\"Glowstone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:glowstone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" makes the \"},{\"text\":\"Transmutation Catalyst\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:conversion_catalyst\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". On a lower golden brick of the altar, it turns one thing into another.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Soul soil into \"},{\"text\":\"Ghast Tears\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:ghast_tear\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", amethyst shards into \"},{\"text\":\"Ender Pearls\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:ender_pearl\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", charcoal into coal, rotten flesh into leather, a water bucket into milk, Bottled Darkness into \"},{\"text\":\"Dragon's Breath\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:dragon_breath\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.382146CD7C5728B1.title": "The Energetic Aura Forge",
  "quest.382146CD7C5728B1.quest_subtitle": "Nature, now in Forge Energy.",
  "quest.382146CD7C5728B1.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Transmutation Catalyst, two \"},{\"text\":\"Ingots of the Skies\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:sky_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", Tokens of Fear and Anger and four redstone blocks make the \"},{\"text\":\"Energetic Aura Forge\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:rf_converter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Built into its structure, it turns only the aura above normal within 45 blocks into Forge Energy, faster the more there is.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7D39D1A7D746D316.title": "The Everlasting Spring",
  "quest.7D39D1A7D746D316.quest_subtitle": "Water that never runs out, lava that learns manners.",
  "quest.7D39D1A7D746D316.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four \"},{\"text\":\"Water Buckets\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:water_bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", stone bricks and a \"},{\"text\":\"Token of Euphoria\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:token_euphoria\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make the \"},{\"text\":\"Everlasting Spring\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:spring\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It fills buckets and the cauldron above it, feeds pipes, wets sponges and waters farmland five blocks around, even in the Nether.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Lava one block away sideways turns into cobblestone, one block above or below into stone, and lava touching it into obsidian. Each costs aura."
  ],
  "quest.27BD68763485F01C.title": "Weather on order",
  "quest.27BD68763485F01C.quest_subtitle": "Tired of rain? File a complaint with the sky.",
  "quest.27BD68763485F01C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Throw items beside the \"},{\"text\":\"Cloudshifter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:weather_changer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": \"},{\"text\":\"Sunflowers\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:sunflower\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" clear the sky, \"},{\"text\":\"Dark Prismarine\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:dark_prismarine\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" brings rain and \"},{\"text\":\"Fire Charges\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:fire_charge\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" a thunderstorm; more items, longer weather. With a redstone signal, \"},{\"text\":\"Winter's Calling\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:snow_creator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" snows over an area, freezes water and sometimes builds snow golems.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.004CC4AE5EA71071.title": "The Shifting Sundial",
  "quest.004CC4AE5EA71071.quest_subtitle": "Skip the night. Or the whole week.",
  "quest.004CC4AE5EA71071.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Offer a \"},{\"text\":\"Nether Star\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:nether_star\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" to get the \"},{\"text\":\"Hand of Time\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:clock_hand\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", and hang it in an item frame on the \"},{\"text\":\"Shifting Sundial\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:time_changer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": its rotation picks the hour, straight up is midnight. Drop a \"},{\"text\":\"Clock\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:clock\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" next to it to jump there; the further, the more aura.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6E458C97F79C1565.title": "The Aura Field Creator",
  "quest.6E458C97F79C1565.quest_subtitle": "A quarry made of weather.",
  "quest.6E458C97F79C1565.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The recipe makes two \"},{\"text\":\"Aura Field Creators\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:field_creator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Sneak-use one and use the other to link them, up to 24 blocks apart, then give one a redstone signal: after a short charge, every block placed between them breaks and drops.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Shears or an enchanted tool in an item frame on either creator make the field break blocks as that tool would."
  ],
  "quest.1A36F0053CEB9C10.title": "The Automatic Constructor",
  "quest.1A36F0053CEB9C10.quest_subtitle": "A crafting table that works nights.",
  "quest.1A36F0053CEB9C10.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Build the \"},{\"text\":\"Automatic Constructor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:auto_crafter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"'s ring of Ancient Logs as the book shows, with its arrow pointing to the top row of the recipe. Drop the ingredients on the logs in their crafting positions: a few seconds later the result falls out of the bottom.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1DE6FC8C2CF9808A.title": "The Altar of Birthing",
  "quest.1DE6FC8C2CF9808A.quest_subtitle": "Some assembly required. Also a shulker shell.",
  "quest.1DE6FC8C2CF9808A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Breed two animals where the aura is a little above normal and the baby may come with \"},{\"text\":\"Spirits of Birthing\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:birth_spirit\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Throw a spirit and a creature's ingredients beside the \"},{\"text\":\"Altar of Birthing\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturesaura:animal_spawner\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", built into its structure, and the creature appears.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "A Shulker Shell makes a shulker for 150,000 aura; a bone and obsidian, a wither skeleton; beef and leather, a cow. The book lists every creature it knows."
  ],
  "image.468B5EDA1F877DE0.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Below empty\",\"color\":\"#F0CC52\"}]",
  "image.4BEFE805D4AE9ED6.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Imbalance\",\"color\":\"#F0CC52\"}]",
  "image.267D8F71693ADF8B.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Instruments\",\"color\":\"#F0CC52\"}]",
  "image.78BAD6F5FE5DD985.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Powders that create\",\"color\":\"#F0CC52\"}]",
  "image.59562E29A361B3D8.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The End\",\"color\":\"#F0CC52\"}]",
  "image.0DCDC7AFB86B0371.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Sanctuary and rails\",\"color\":\"#F0CC52\"}]",
  "image.4BC74D7599386FAC.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Aura at work\",\"color\":\"#F0CC52\"}]",
  "image.4253021624B31204.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Furnaces\",\"color\":\"#F0CC52\"}]",
  "image.5D5CBDE2C6C9A7F6.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three tiers of tools\",\"color\":\"#F0CC52\"}]",
  "image.5ACC38B1E8272F04.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Staffs\",\"color\":\"#F0CC52\"}]",
  "image.2E6E0ABF5BB1AC57.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Keepsakes\",\"color\":\"#F0CC52\"}]",
  "image.134FA7AFB6B83AD7.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Nether\",\"color\":\"#F0CC52\"}]",
  "image.097752A465C8D65C.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Garden and brew\",\"color\":\"#F0CC52\"}]",
  "image.7A1C767EEA221CEE.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Creatures and targets\",\"color\":\"#F0CC52\"}]",
  "image.14C1CE56ABC972ED.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Water, weather, time\",\"color\":\"#F0CC52\"}]",
  "image.6573B8F073410F1D.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Fields, crafts, births\",\"color\":\"#F0CC52\"}]",
  "image.7B08CB25ADB373BB.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Nature's Aura\",\"color\":\"#FFF2C0\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.5E2B85588759B5FC.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"what you take give back\",\"color\":\"#C9E88F\",\"font\":\"minecraft:alt\"}]",
  "image.76F8C69696BFE48C.title": "Back to the Sun of Heliodor",
  "chapter.5AB53528D9DFD2D3.title": "Occultism · Rituals",
  "chapter.5AB53528D9DFD2D3.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Chalk, bowls and true names: from a Foliot in a circle to spirits that forge on request."
  ],
  "quest.55F0051E7C82041E.title": "Demon's Dream",
  "quest.55F0051E7C82041E.quest_subtitle": "Grandma's garden, if grandma summoned demons.",
  "quest.55F0051E7C82041E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Break short or tall grass until \"},{\"text\":\"Demon's Dream Seeds\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:datura_seeds\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" drop: one try in fifty, and never with shears. Plant them on farmland. Everything in Occultism starts with the fruit.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4EF837799172E91F.title": "The Third Eye",
  "quest.4EF837799172E91F.quest_subtitle": "Side effects include enlightenment.",
  "quest.4EF837799172E91F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eat a \"},{\"text\":\"Demon's Dream Fruit\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:datura\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": with luck you get the Third Eye and see where the Otherworld overlaps ours. While it lasts you can also harvest those Otherworld blocks by hand, which even the goggles won't let you do.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Nine fruits or seeds press into a \"},{\"text\":\"Demon's Dream Essence\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:demons_dream_essence\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": the Third Eye for sure and for longer, plus a grab bag of other effects. Spiritfire purifies it into \"},{\"text\":\"Otherworld Essence\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:otherworld_essence\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", which keeps the good ones.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7823312EBC3C6871.title": "The Dictionary of Spirits",
  "quest.7823312EBC3C6871.quest_desc": [
    "Demon's Dream Seeds and a book: manual and tool in one. Each ritual page shows its pentacle; the eye icon previews it in the world, and a right-click with the book anchors the preview where you'll draw."
  ],
  "quest.0E09EEC04A2E0A79.title": "Spiritfire",
  "quest.0E09EEC04A2E0A79.quest_subtitle": "A bonfire with a customs office.",
  "quest.0E09EEC04A2E0A79.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Drop a \"},{\"text\":\"Demon's Dream Fruit\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:datura\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and light it with \"},{\"text\":\"Flint and Steel\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:flint_and_steel\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". \"},{\"text\":\"Spiritfire\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:spirit_fire\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" spares the living and converts what you throw in: \"},{\"text\":\"Andesite\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:andesite\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" into \"},{\"text\":\"Otherstone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:otherstone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a \"},{\"text\":\"Diamond\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:diamond\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" into a \"},{\"text\":\"Spirit Attuned Gem\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:spirit_attuned_gem\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A sacrificial bowl set above spiritfire converts whatever you put in it at once.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.20100A494B9AB672.title": "Trees from the other side",
  "quest.20100A494B9AB672.quest_subtitle": "Looks like oak. Isn't.",
  "quest.20100A494B9AB672.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An \"},{\"text\":\"Oak Sapling\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:oak_sapling\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in spiritfire turns into an \"},{\"text\":\"Unstable Otherworld Sapling\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:otherworld_sapling_natural\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Its tree looks like plain oak; eat Demon's Dream before you chop and the \"},{\"text\":\"Otherworld Logs\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:otherworld_log\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" come off as what they are.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Otherworld Groves grow wild underground: lush caves with these trees and walls of Otherstone. A divination rod attuned to their logs or leaves finds one; in the Overworld, look down.",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Otherworld saplings drop only from leaves you break by hand.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4B35F393DC92C7AA.title": "White chalk",
  "quest.4B35F393DC92C7AA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Smelt \"},{\"text\":\"Otherstone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:otherstone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" twice for \"},{\"text\":\"Burnt Otherstone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:burnt_otherstone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and burn Otherworld Logs in spiritfire for \"},{\"text\":\"Otherworld Ashes\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:otherworld_ashes\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Three of each make \"},{\"text\":\"Impure White Chalk\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:chalk_white_impure\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; spiritfire purifies it.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Right-click a block to draw a glyph. Only color and position count: clicking again just changes the doodle."
  ],
  "quest.1C3EF3482F1256F9.title": "Bowls for the offerings",
  "quest.1C3EF3482F1256F9.quest_subtitle": "Fine dining for spirits.",
  "quest.1C3EF3482F1256F9.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Five \"},{\"text\":\"Otherstone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:otherstone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" shape a \"},{\"text\":\"Sacrificial Bowl\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:sacrificial_bowl\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; eight gold ingots around one make the \"},{\"text\":\"Golden Ritual Bowl\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:golden_sacrificial_bowl\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". The golden one sits at the pentacle's center and starts the ritual. Plain bowls hold the ingredients anywhere within 8 blocks horizontally.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1C93C34CD1BCA38E.title": "Candles and tallow",
  "quest.1C93C34CD1BCA38E.quest_subtitle": "Ambience is a technical requirement.",
  "quest.1C93C34CD1BCA38E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Nearly every pentacle wants candles, and any candle counts, vanilla ones too. A \"},{\"text\":\"Butcher Knife\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:butcher_knife\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" takes \"},{\"text\":\"Tallow\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:tallow\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" from pigs, cows and sheep; string over tallow makes a \"},{\"text\":\"Large Candle\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:large_candle\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6517C4129FA2CD9B.title": "A book with a name in it",
  "quest.6517C4129FA2CD9B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Spiritfire makes the parts: black dye into \"},{\"text\":\"Purified Ink\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:purified_ink\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a feather into an \"},{\"text\":\"Awakened Feather\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:awakened_feather\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a book into a \"},{\"text\":\"Taboo Book\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:taboo_book\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". With blue dye they make a \"},{\"text\":\"Book of Binding: Foliot\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:book_of_binding_foliot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; craft it with the Dictionary to write a name in.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "The dye sets the tier: blue Foliot, purple Djinni, yellow Afrit, green Marid. Which name you get is decoration; only the tier counts.",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Six at once: fill a \"},{\"text\":\"Chiseled Bookshelf\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:chiseled_bookshelf\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" with books and sneak-use the Dictionary on it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.195DB7C39D08F1A7.title": "Divination Rod",
  "quest.195DB7C39D08F1A7.quest_subtitle": "Dowsing, with better eyesight.",
  "quest.195DB7C39D08F1A7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Spirit Attuned Gem\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:spirit_attuned_gem\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" set in gold and glass. Sneak-use it on andesite, oak wood, oak leaves or netherrack to attune it to their Otherworld twin, then hold right-click.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Theurgy is in this pack, so the rod answers with a trail of particles toward the find instead of an outline.",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The rod's crystals tell distance: white is nothing found, and the more purple, the closer.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.36C42226788C6281.title": "The Spirit Attuned Crystal",
  "quest.36C42226788C6281.quest_subtitle": "Four diamonds' worth of patience.",
  "quest.36C42226788C6281.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four Spirit Attuned Gems in a square. Crystals steady unstable pentacles, and from the Afrit tier on most pentacles want four or eight. It is also Occultism's share of the act IV \"},{\"text\":\"Spectral Lens\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:spectral_lens\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Short on diamonds? \"},{\"text\":\"Ars Ocultas\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"6644EE1A37239BF7\"}},{\"text\":\" imbues the gems from Source Gems.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5CB156A16604FA31.title": "Chalk wears out",
  "quest.5CB156A16604FA31.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Every glyph spends chalk. A Djinni repairs any chalk on Strigeor's Higher Binding for three Otherworld Essence and a Spirit Attuned Gem, and Malum's Repair Pylon mends white, yellow, purple and red with eight arcane spirits: the pack ships those four recipes fixed.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.053EFFA5CEA3E9E0.title": "Demon's Dream for the common store",
  "quest.053EFFA5CEA3E9E0.quest_subtitle": "The spirits eat first.",
  "quest.053EFFA5CEA3E9E0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Thirty-two \"},{\"text\":\"Demon's Dream Fruits\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:datura\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for the common store, once a day. Spiritfire, healing spirits and the dimensional battlefield's fuel all run on it.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.3380AF2584E7B8C6.title": "Summon a Foliot Crusher",
  "quest.1CA9462AE1EC919A.title": "Aviar's Circle",
  "quest.1CA9462AE1EC919A.quest_subtitle": "Ore doubling, with a pulse.",
  "quest.1CA9462AE1EC919A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Set the golden bowl down, draw \"},{\"text\":\"Aviar's Circle\",\"italic\":true},{\"text\":\" around it in white chalk with four candles, and put an iron, a gold, a copper and a silver ingot in the bowls. Right-click the golden bowl with the bound Foliot book: purple particles mean it took.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "The Foliot Crusher picks up ores dropped near it and turns each into two dusts. Djinni, Afrit and Marid crushers make three, four and six."
  ],
  "quest.0F3A72F66AD6AC52.title": "Any silver will do",
  "quest.0F3A72F66AD6AC52.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Rituals ask for tags, not mods: any silver ingot fills the crusher's bowl. Almost Unified merges duplicate metals, so recipes that make silver hand out Immersive Engineering's.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.63C6B6180B77CA54.title": "Yellow chalk",
  "quest.63C6B6180B77CA54.quest_subtitle": "Spirits, now with bodies.",
  "quest.63C6B6180B77CA54.quest_desc": [
    "Impure white chalk, glowstone dust and two gold dusts, purified in spiritfire; the crusher makes the dust, and so do Immersive Engineering and Mekanism. Yellow glyphs turn a summoning into a possession: the spirit takes a body instead of its own shape."
  ],
  "quest.0A1B2A6A83AAAF8F.title": "Grey smoke: it's waiting",
  "quest.0A1B2A6A83AAAF8F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Grey particles over the golden bowl and nothing consumed: the ritual wants an item used within 16 blocks, or a sacrifice killed by a player within 8. Kills by machines don't count.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.33500511937AA794.title": "Kill a Possessed Endermite",
  "quest.4E9DB6E8CEC581C6.title": "End stone without the End",
  "quest.4E9DB6E8CEC581C6.quest_subtitle": "It visits the End so you don't have to.",
  "quest.4E9DB6E8CEC581C6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Draw \"},{\"text\":\"Hedyrin's Lure\",\"italic\":true},{\"text\":\" (colorless and yellow glyphs, four candles), put dirt and stone twice in the bowls and start it with the Foliot book. When the smoke turns grey, throw an \"},{\"text\":\"Egg\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:egg\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". The Possessed Endermite drops one or two \"},{\"text\":\"End Stone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:end_stone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", every time.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5ECD62C10AC28D2B.title": "Purple chalk",
  "quest.5ECD62C10AC28D2B.quest_subtitle": "Put a Foliot in it. It'll work harder.",
  "quest.5ECD62C10AC28D2B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Impure white chalk, crushed end stone and two obsidian dusts, then spiritfire. Purple is the infusion color: the ritual binds a spirit into an object instead of calling it out. \"},{\"text\":\"Eziveus' Spectral Compulsion\",\"italic\":true},{\"text\":\", the Foliot infusion, wants purple, colorless glyphs and eight candles.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.360C63CD62EEDB62.title": "Otherworld Goggles",
  "quest.360C63CD62EEDB62.quest_subtitle": "Enlightenment, now with a prescription.",
  "quest.360C63CD62EEDB62.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Glass panes around a Spirit Attuned Gem make \"},{\"text\":\"Glass Lenses\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:lenses\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; a Foliot infusion with two silver and a gold ingot turns them into \"},{\"text\":\"Infused Lenses\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:infused_lenses\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Add a \"},{\"text\":\"Lens Frame\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:lens_frame\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and leather: a permanent Third Eye that even shows iesnium ore.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "They show, they don't harvest. Breaking an Otherworld block for its true drop still takes Demon's Dream or an Infused or Iesnium Pickaxe."
  ],
  "quest.2F116E61C2089619.title": "Research Fragment Dust",
  "quest.2F116E61C2089619.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Emerald dust and two \"},{\"text\":\"Bottles o' Enchanting\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:experience_bottle\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on the Foliot infusion: the spirit grinds experience into \"},{\"text\":\"dust\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:research_fragment_dust\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Lime chalk needs it, and later the iesnium bowl and the knowledge tablet.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2FDA25063F13E2DD.title": "Light gray and lime",
  "quest.2FDA25063F13E2DD.quest_subtitle": "Second tier. The spirits read the fine print.",
  "quest.2FDA25063F13E2DD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Light gray is impure white chalk with silver, iron and calcite dusts: a stronger foundation that stands in for white almost everywhere. Lime adds research dust, emerald dust and a slime ball, and lures Djinni. Their pentacles also want \"},{\"text\":\"skeleton skulls\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"41C2DC9AECD6B6D0\"}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.11E684A9434F73CD.title": "Read the table",
  "quest.11E684A9434F73CD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The Dictionary's Pentacles tab is a table: each row a ritual type, each column a spirit tier. Draw a pentacle once and every tier up is an upgrade of the same drawing; four 19-block squares hold them all.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.41C2DC9AECD6B6D0.title": "Skulls on demand",
  "quest.41C2DC9AECD6B6D0.quest_subtitle": "A bone to pick.",
  "quest.41C2DC9AECD6B6D0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Hedyrin's Lure with four bones and a chicken as the sacrifice: a Foliot raises a skeleton and possesses it. The Possessed Skeleton ignores daylight and always drops a \"},{\"text\":\"Skeleton Skull\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:skeleton_skull\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Djinni summonings want four skulls; Djinni infusions, eight.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.558FF11EBCA45173.title": "Possess a witch",
  "task.1064AB9DF4323337.title": "Possess a phantom",
  "quest.4C39CBA3E1BA49CD.title": "Hedyrin's other catches",
  "quest.4C39CBA3E1BA49CD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The lure calls more than endermites. A glass bottle, redstone and two mushrooms with a chicken give a Possessed Witch, whose drops include Bottles o' Enchanting. Leather and feathers with a bat, bee, parrot or allay give a Possessed Phantom and one to four \"},{\"text\":\"Phantom Membranes\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:phantom_membrane\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.57D4D0D6C014C7D4.title": "The Apprentice Ritual Satchel",
  "quest.57D4D0D6C014C7D4.quest_subtitle": "Pentacles to go.",
  "quest.57D4D0D6C014C7D4.quest_desc": [
    "A Foliot infusion of a hopper, a dispenser, wool, leather, string and silver. Fill it with chalk, candles and skulls, anchor a Dictionary preview, and right-click the preview with the satchel: it sets the pentacle block by block."
  ],
  "quest.4DD282FC85BCA251.title": "A pickaxe with a Djinni inside",
  "quest.4DD282FC85BCA251.quest_subtitle": "The Djinni did not sign up for this.",
  "quest.4DD282FC85BCA251.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three Spirit Attuned Gems make a \"},{\"text\":\"Spirit Attuned Pickaxe Head\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:spirit_attuned_pickaxe_head\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". With two sticks and two silver ingots, infuse it on \"},{\"text\":\"Strigeor's Higher Binding\",\"italic\":true},{\"text\":\", \"},{\"text\":\"eight skulls\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"41C2DC9AECD6B6D0\"}},{\"text\":\" and all, with a Book of Binding dyed purple. It mines iesnium ore, but it's brittle: get your first iesnium and make a real pick.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3E8773D95C626DDC.title": "Iesnium",
  "quest.3E8773D95C626DDC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"In the Nether it passes for netherrack. The goggles show it, a rod attuned to netherrack points at it, and only an Infused or Iesnium Pickaxe breaks it for \"},{\"text\":\"Raw Iesnium\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:raw_iesnium\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", which smelts into ingots. Fortune works; Silk Touch gives a stable ore any pickaxe can mine.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0DACD7FB4D755D9F.title": "Iesnium Pickaxe",
  "quest.0DACD7FB4D755D9F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three \"},{\"text\":\"Iesnium Ingots\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:iesnium_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and two sticks: a lasting pick for Otherworld ores. Keep a few on hand; every miner spirit's ritual eats one.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.0B39EF39FB3E5311.title": "Possess an enderman",
  "task.07F6E6B01A776037.title": "Possess a ghast",
  "task.0D04BE0FD1CFD69A.title": "Possess a blaze",
  "quest.43ECC510994B503E.title": "Ihagan's Enthrallment",
  "quest.43ECC510994B503E.quest_subtitle": "Nether and End drops, by appointment.",
  "quest.43ECC510994B503E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Djinni possession pentacle farms the Nether and the End from home. A Possessed Enderman (a pig) always drops an \"},{\"text\":\"Ender Pearl\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:ender_pearl\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; a Possessed Ghast (a cow) a \"},{\"text\":\"Ghast Tear\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:ghast_tear\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; a Possessed Blaze (a chicken) two to six \"},{\"text\":\"Blaze Rods\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:blaze_rod\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "task.1FA1397DB9988EED.title": "Call a villager",
  "quest.0A5441852CB56BEA.title": "A villager, to order",
  "quest.0A5441852CB56BEA.quest_subtitle": "Human resources.",
  "quest.0A5441852CB56BEA.quest_desc": [
    "Ihagan's Enthrallment with a bed, a campfire and a pie, then a Bottle o' Enchanting used when the smoke turns grey: a spirit takes a villager's shape. Several later rituals want a human sacrifice, and a villager counts as one."
  ],
  "quest.5F4B6EB6C68DE635.title": "Gray chalk",
  "quest.5F4B6EB6C68DE635.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Gunpowder, a clay ball, a Phantom Membrane and gray dye on Strigeor's Higher Binding give \"},{\"text\":\"Gray Paste\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:gray_paste\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; with impure white chalk it makes gray chalk, the third foundation. Afrit pentacles need gray or black wherever they show dark glyphs.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Gray Paste also crafts some dusts back into their minerals: emerald, lapis, obsidian, amethyst, echo shards.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6FABB369F5895D94.title": "Orange chalk",
  "quest.6FABB369F5895D94.quest_subtitle": "Honey, but make it haunted.",
  "quest.6FABB369F5895D94.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Ihagan's Enthrallment with honeycomb, a honey block, a honey bottle and a honeycomb block, plus a chicken: a Djinni possesses a bee that keeps its stinger and calls friends when hit. It is the only source of \"},{\"text\":\"Cursed Honey\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:cursed_honey\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; with glow berries and blaze powder, the honey makes orange chalk.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.6104BDB308593B64.title": "Kill the Unbound Afrit",
  "quest.2C1E92621CCD380C.title": "Kandar's Open Conjure",
  "quest.2C1E92621CCD380C.quest_subtitle": "You called it. It's your problem now.",
  "quest.2C1E92621CCD380C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An Afrit called on purpose with nothing to hold it: netherrack, an iesnium ingot, \"},{\"text\":\"Flint and Steel\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:flint_and_steel\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and gunpowder, a Book of Binding dyed yellow and a cow as the sacrifice. The pentacle has no red chalk. Kill the Afrit for \"},{\"text\":\"Afrit Essence\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:afrit_essence\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; nothing else drops it.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Unbound spirits attack everything near them.\",\"color\":\"#FF8C7A\"},{\"text\":\" Call it far from home, in good armor, with potions ready.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.63072CA991C42FDB.title": "Red chalk",
  "quest.63072CA991C42FDB.quest_subtitle": "Third tier. The contracts get serious.",
  "quest.63072CA991C42FDB.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Impure white chalk, Afrit Essence, a \"},{\"text\":\"Torchflower\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:torchflower\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and redstone dust, purified in spiritfire. Red glyphs hold an Afrit to your will: \"},{\"text\":\"Abras' Conjure\",\"italic\":true},{\"text\":\" summons one, \"},{\"text\":\"Posuc's Convocation\",\"italic\":true},{\"text\":\" makes one possess, \"},{\"text\":\"Sevira's Permanent Confinement\",\"italic\":true},{\"text\":\" binds one into objects.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.407A60E2360F572F.title": "The Artisanal Ritual Satchel",
  "quest.407A60E2360F572F.quest_desc": [
    "An Afrit takes over the satchel: upgrade the apprentice one with Afrit Essence and four ender pearls on Sevira's circle, contents kept. It sets a whole previewed pentacle in one click, and used on the golden bowl it packs an intact pentacle back up."
  ],
  "quest.6D7E55F1FBFCD366.title": "The Iesnium Ritual Bowl",
  "quest.6D7E55F1FBFCD366.quest_subtitle": "For summoners with somewhere to be.",
  "quest.6D7E55F1FBFCD366.quest_desc": [
    "Sevira's Permanent Confinement with a golden bowl, research dust, a Spirit Attuned Crystal, a block of iesnium and Afrit Essence. It takes the golden bowl's place at the center of any pentacle and runs every ritual in a quarter of the time.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Hang a sacrificial bowl upside down above the central bowl, up to three blocks up, and crafted results land in it instead of popping out.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.1DAF164C0D2872C0.title": "Possess a hoglin",
  "task.1AEB3789E20195F3.title": "Possess a shulker",
  "quest.0C49A13D32C096C4.title": "Posuc's Convocation",
  "quest.0C49A13D32C096C4.quest_subtitle": "Templates without the bastion.",
  "quest.0C49A13D32C096C4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Afrit possession, crystals included. A Possessed Hoglin (netherite scrap, porkchops, a crystal and a pig) can drop a \"},{\"text\":\"Netherite Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:netherite_upgrade_smithing_template\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" or give the scrap back; a Possessed Shulker (dragon's breath, purple glazed terracotta, end stone and a slime) drops one or two \"},{\"text\":\"Shulker Shells\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:shulker_shell\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Outside the Nether a hoglin turns zoglin after a while: kill it first.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.3EB8BE4F402CB1C4.title": "Possess a warden",
  "quest.044C780D22936829.title": "A warden on a leash",
  "quest.044C780D22936829.quest_subtitle": "Six sculk and a cow. Worth it.",
  "quest.044C780D22936829.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Posuc's Convocation with six sculk and a cow as the sacrifice: an Afrit wears a Warden. It always drops six to nine \"},{\"text\":\"Echo Shards\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:echo_shard\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", the raw stuff of cyan chalk, and sometimes a disc fragment or a trim. Run, and it digs back down like any warden.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.635B924428B70C33.title": "Pink chalk",
  "quest.635B924428B70C33.quest_subtitle": "Pork, fire and a questionable contract.",
  "quest.635B924428B70C33.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Odus' Open Convocation\",\"italic\":true},{\"text\":\" makes an Afrit possess a zombified piglin without red chalk: gilded blackstone, warped and crimson fungus and quartz, the Afrit book and a pig. The Possessed Zombified Piglin is the only source of \"},{\"text\":\"Demonic Meat\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:demonic_meat\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; three pieces make pink chalk.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1EFC2C35364A3693.title": "Green chalk",
  "quest.1EFC2C35364A3693.quest_subtitle": "Pesto for spirits.",
  "quest.1EFC2C35364A3693.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three each of leaves, saplings and seeds on the Foliot infusion: the spirit squeezes them into \"},{\"text\":\"Nature Paste\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:nature_paste\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". With impure white chalk it makes green chalk, the glyph wild spirits can't ignore.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Nature Paste and cobblestone craft mossy cobblestone.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.284793BE6235E376.title": "Light blue chalk",
  "quest.284793BE6235E376.quest_subtitle": "It never melts. Don't ask how.",
  "quest.284793BE6235E376.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Impure white chalk with crushed ice, crushed packed ice and crushed blue ice. A Foliot Crusher melts ice, so this takes a \"},{\"text\":\"Djinni Crusher\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"3E436D1792543A16\"}},{\"text\":\" or better. The glyphs are inert and steady the wild pentacles.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.0C7F8C1C847F834F.title": "Call the Wild Hunt",
  "quest.11A513C5F99884D1.title": "The Wild Hunt",
  "quest.11A513C5F99884D1.quest_subtitle": "They hunt. You provide the venue.",
  "quest.11A513C5F99884D1.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Osorin's Unbound Calling\",\"italic\":true},{\"text\":\" is pink, green and light blue glyphs and nothing else: no candles, no protection, an open door for wild spirits. A \"},{\"text\":\"Skeleton Skull\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:skeleton_skull\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" starts it, with copper, silver and gold blocks, a diamond, netherrack and soul sand in the bowls, and a human sacrifice.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Hunt answers: Greater Spirits shaped like wither skeletons, nearly untouchable until their skeleton minions fall. They drop \"},{\"text\":\"Wither Skeleton Skulls\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:wither_skeleton_skull\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; Marid pentacles take four.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A villager counts as a human sacrifice. So does a player. Bring the villager.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.77A12E53BD753221.title": "Forge a Budding Amethyst",
  "task.420FE0C6518E30F1.title": "Forge Reinforced Deepslate",
  "quest.305BA499CA315EE5.title": "Forged by wild spirits",
  "quest.305BA499CA315EE5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Some wild rituals bind nothing: the spirits forge an item and leave. An amethyst block, six amethyst dusts and a pig make \"},{\"text\":\"Budding Amethyst\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:budding_amethyst\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; deepslate, iron bars, obsidian and an iesnium ingot, paid with a warden, make \"},{\"text\":\"Reinforced Deepslate\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:reinforced_deepslate\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Possessed mobs count as their plain kind for sacrifices: a Possessed Warden pays for the deepslate.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.413B9ED44FD2B926.title": "Call a Wild Weak Breeze",
  "task.49C6DA72C97202FD.title": "Call a Wild Breeze",
  "task.0A9B56959D165173.title": "Call a Wild Strong Breeze",
  "quest.224E1F69351C3783.title": "Trial by breeze",
  "quest.224E1F69351C3783.quest_subtitle": "Three keys, no chamber.",
  "quest.224E1F69351C3783.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A honeycomb with four copper blocks and four tuff bricks calls a Wild Weak Breeze that drops a \"},{\"text\":\"Trial Key\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:trial_key\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". That key starts the next ritual, whose breeze drops an \"},{\"text\":\"Ominous Trial Key\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:ominous_trial_key\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; that one calls the Wild Strong Breeze and its \"},{\"text\":\"Heavy Core\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:heavy_core\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Each costs a villager.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.5474C8BBA2E93CAC.title": "Call a husk horde",
  "task.694920EAEDAFDA08.title": "Call a drowned horde",
  "task.30DD8832DDE2449F.title": "Call a silverfish horde",
  "quest.189C192C7E1E8EF6.title": "Hordes for sherds",
  "quest.189C192C7E1E8EF6.quest_subtitle": "Archaeology, minus the brushing.",
  "quest.189C192C7E1E8EF6.quest_desc": [
    "Osorin's circle also calls wild hordes, five at a time. Husks drop desert sherds and the dune trim; drowned drop ocean sherds, turtle and sniffer eggs and tridents; silverfish drop trail-ruin sherds, four trims and the relic disc."
  ],
  "task.4AFE931C4459760A.title": "Call a Wild Illager Invasion",
  "quest.5994EC33E05AD7DF.title": "An invasion you ordered",
  "quest.5994EC33E05AD7DF.quest_subtitle": "Totems, delivered by hand. Theirs.",
  "quest.5994EC33E05AD7DF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A golden apple, three dark oak logs and three emerald dusts, plus a human sacrifice, call a Wild Evoker and his crew. The evoker drops \"},{\"text\":\"Totems of Undying\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:totem_of_undying\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and the vex and sentry trims; the Afrit stabilizer and the Marid miner both eat totems.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.19405AED60C7208C.title": "Call a creeper horde",
  "quest.57A93FE444150288.title": "Mixtape from beyond",
  "quest.57A93FE444150288.quest_subtitle": "Five creepers, all charged, all opinions.",
  "quest.57A93FE444150288.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"You called a Wild Horde of Creepers with \"},{\"text\":\"Flint and Steel\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:flint_and_steel\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on Osorin's circle. They come charged, five at a time, and each drops one to three music discs, the ones a skeleton's arrow usually has to earn.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.39864DB8F5A4029D.title": "Secret found",
  "task.6C9F164E1B176627.title": "Forge a Bell",
  "quest.1B1BFCC1E67DAA02.title": "For whom the bell was forged",
  "quest.1B1BFCC1E67DAA02.quest_subtitle": "Ask not.",
  "quest.1B1BFCC1E67DAA02.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"You had wild spirits forge a \"},{\"text\":\"Bell\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:bell\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" from a gold block, gold nuggets, a chain, stone and a log, and a goat paid for it. Every village without one can finally stop pretending.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.47D4EC2194956E23.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.59B8673D231F55EE.title": "Black chalk",
  "quest.59B8673D231F55EE.quest_subtitle": "Fourth foundation, forged from the Wither's share.",
  "quest.59B8673D231F55EE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Sevira's Permanent Confinement with netherite dust, a \"},{\"text\":\"Wither Skeleton Skull\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:wither_skeleton_skull\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", crushed blackstone and a \"},{\"text\":\"Wither Rose\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:wither_rose\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" gives three \"},{\"text\":\"Witherite Dust\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:witherite_dust\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": one black chalk. Black is the strongest foundation and replaces every colorless glyph.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3DE2FD1DF100C63B.title": "A conduit, by possession",
  "quest.3DE2FD1DF100C63B.quest_subtitle": "Heart of the sea, on appointment.",
  "quest.3DE2FD1DF100C63B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Posuc's Convocation with prismarine bricks, dark prismarine, a sea lantern, a water bucket and an emerald, and any fish: an Afrit possesses an Elder Guardian. It drops two to four \"},{\"text\":\"Nautilus Shells\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:nautilus_shell\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and, 40% of the time, a \"},{\"text\":\"Heart of the Sea\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:heart_of_the_sea\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". The Marid wants a \"},{\"text\":\"Conduit\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:conduit\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "task.545E35A4AE1B5C9E.title": "Kill the Unbound Marid",
  "quest.52E803E1AC79FF90.title": "Tibira's Attraction",
  "quest.52E803E1AC79FF90.quest_subtitle": "Legendary, if you survive it.",
  "quest.52E803E1AC79FF90.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Black chalk opens \"},{\"text\":\"Tibira's Attraction\",\"italic\":true},{\"text\":\", an Afrit-sized pentacle that calls a Marid and binds nothing. A Conduit, prismarine crystals, a prismarine shard and a ghast tear go in the bowls, a Book of Binding dyed green starts it, and at the grey smoke you use a \"},{\"text\":\"Trident\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:trident\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Kill it for \"},{\"text\":\"Marid Essence\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:marid_essence\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4337313ECB14CF3D.title": "Blue chalk",
  "quest.4337313ECB14CF3D.quest_subtitle": "Fourth tier. Read everything twice.",
  "quest.4337313ECB14CF3D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Impure white chalk, Marid Essence, lapis dust and a tube coral. Blue glyphs overpower a Marid: \"},{\"text\":\"Fatma's Incentivized Attraction\",\"italic\":true},{\"text\":\" summons one, \"},{\"text\":\"Xeovrenth Adjure\",\"italic\":true},{\"text\":\" makes one possess, \"},{\"text\":\"Uphyxes Inverted Tower\",\"italic\":true},{\"text\":\" binds one into objects. Every Marid pentacle is 21 blocks across.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2DD8C1C18855F572.title": "The True Sight Staff",
  "quest.2DD8C1C18855F572.quest_subtitle": "Seeing is harvesting.",
  "quest.2DD8C1C18855F572.quest_desc": [
    "A Marid infusion of a netherite ingot, an Iesnium Pickaxe, Otherworld Goggles, a Divination Rod, Otherworld Essence and Marid Essence. In the off-hand or a curio slot it lets you harvest Otherworld blocks by hand, and your divination rods can search for any block."
  ],
  "quest.14454992886C61FD.title": "Brown chalk",
  "quest.14454992886C61FD.quest_subtitle": "An alignment test with one wrong answer.",
  "quest.14454992886C61FD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Xeovrenth Adjure calls the Goat of Mercy: pointed dripstone, rabbit feet, armadillo scutes and wool in the bowls, the Marid book and a human sacrifice. Kill the goat for \"},{\"text\":\"Cruelty Essence\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:cruelty_essence\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", its only source; with cocoa beans and a brown mushroom it makes brown chalk.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.10BB6D93F4A64E5B.title": "Cyan chalk",
  "quest.10BB6D93F4A64E5B.quest_subtitle": "The oldest color on record.",
  "quest.10BB6D93F4A64E5B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Impure white chalk, iesnium dust, \"},{\"text\":\"Echo Dust\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:echo_dust\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a \"},{\"text\":\"Glow Ink Sac\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:glow_ink_sac\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Only a \"},{\"text\":\"Marid Crusher\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"26FEE7CF2C363E14\"}},{\"text\":\" grinds an echo shard without ruining it; a \"},{\"text\":\"possessed warden\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"044C780D22936829\"}},{\"text\":\" keeps you in shards.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2B039873C1090434.title": "Magenta chalk",
  "quest.2B039873C1090434.quest_subtitle": "Dragon's breath, bottled and ground.",
  "quest.2B039873C1090434.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Uphyxes Inverted Tower\",\"italic\":true},{\"text\":\" with two amethyst dusts, crushed end stone, four \"},{\"text\":\"End Crystals\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:end_crystal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and three \"},{\"text\":\"Dragon's Breath\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:dragon_breath\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" makes one \"},{\"text\":\"Dragonyst Dust\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:dragonyst_dust\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". With amethyst dust and chorus fruit it becomes magenta chalk.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2544F516F6A9D36A.title": "The Celestial Chalice",
  "quest.2544F516F6A9D36A.quest_subtitle": "Rituals at the speed of thought.",
  "quest.2544F516F6A9D36A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Ronaza's Contact\",\"italic\":true},{\"text\":\" reaches the Eldritch spirits, and their service is instant. Twelve blocks (a heavy core, reinforced deepslate, a netherite block, a respawn anchor, a sculk catalyst among them), a ravager, and the iesnium bowl as the key: the chalice runs any ritual at once.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Built from the dark iesnium bowl instead, it comes out as the Eldritch Chalice, same power.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.21E542A0FB078F6A.title": "Every color in one stick",
  "quest.21E542A0FB078F6A.quest_subtitle": "Sixteen colors, one pocket.",
  "quest.21E542A0FB078F6A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Ronaza's Contact is a 21-block pentacle of cyan, magenta, brown and the three wild colors, set with a beacon, an enchanting table, a lodestone and five other oddities. Twelve colored chalks, a \"},{\"text\":\"Chalk Brush\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:brush\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a sheep buy its best service: the \"},{\"text\":\"Rainbow Chalk\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:chalk_rainbow\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "It draws any glyph. Hold a dye in the other hand to pick the color, and sneak-use it on a glyph to erase it.",
    "",
    "The circle is drawn. Every spirit in the Dictionary answers to it now."
  ],
  "task.11836A140C04C24B.title": "Draw with the Void Chalk",
  "quest.2457FF8BC9A7EFF5.title": "Silence, in chalk",
  "quest.2457FF8BC9A7EFF5.quest_subtitle": "...",
  "quest.2457FF8BC9A7EFF5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"You drew with the \"},{\"text\":\"Void Chalk\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:chalk_void\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": white, light gray, gray and black forged into one, paid with a human sacrifice. It stands in for any glyph and flickers between white and black. The Eldritch spirits declined to elaborate.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.2790999FB4AA2833.title": "Secret found",
  "image.66BF49D42325B4E5.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Foliot possessions\",\"color\":\"#CE8BFF\"}]",
  "image.797FDC24E31CFC3C.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Djinni possessions\",\"color\":\"#CE8BFF\"}]",
  "image.5BA25408377AE290.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Afrit possessions\",\"color\":\"#CE8BFF\"}]",
  "image.12709BD83F0FF733.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Wild rituals\",\"color\":\"#CE8BFF\"}]",
  "image.0E5DF840A7DA82E0.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Occultism\",\"color\":\"#F3EEDF\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.2C2940EA5B8D2CCF.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Rituals\",\"color\":\"#CE8BFF\"}]",
  "image.0BDD8A6E741176C5.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"chalk bowl true name\",\"color\":\"#B9A7E0\",\"font\":\"minecraft:alt\"}]",
  "image.08E5331C103EA473.title": "Back to the Sun of Heliodor",
  "image.1439E014414B2607.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» Spirits and storage\",\"color\":\"#CE8BFF\"}]",
  "image.0352DFDD7170A3F5.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Foliot\",\"color\":\"#E8E1CF\"}]",
  "image.66F89331E76554C9.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Djinni\",\"color\":\"#E8E1CF\"}]",
  "image.5E55A843ABFC2B0A.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Afrit\",\"color\":\"#E8E1CF\"}]",
  "image.749AC8DD89988F1F.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Wild\",\"color\":\"#E8E1CF\"}]",
  "image.7D70C51F0F561E04.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Marid\",\"color\":\"#E8E1CF\"}]",
  "chapter.3B13A4C4EA11278B.title": "Reliquary: Monster Relics",
  "chapter.3B13A4C4EA11278B.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Mob drops, the Void Tear, pedestals, the handgun, charms and the Rending Gale."
  ],
  "quest.131C52EB72D74003.title": "Relics from monsters",
  "quest.131C52EB72D74003.quest_desc": [
    "Rare monster parts become relics: a bottomless Void Tear, a magnet coin, an XP medallion, a handgun, charms that make one mob ignore you, pedestals that run items. No book: EMI's info tab is the manual.",
    "",
    "Every monster carries a souvenir."
  ],
  "quest.4046BADD160B83AA.title": "One trophy per monster",
  "quest.4046BADD160B83AA.quest_desc": [
    "Each monster has its part: Zombie Heart, Rib Bone, Chelicerae (spider), Catalyzing Gland (creeper), Nebulous Heart (enderman), Witch Hat, Eye of the Storm (charged creeper) and more. Player kills only, about 2% base; Looting raises it."
  ],
  "quest.75974F7E0E2DE9B1.title": "Severing and the Magicbane",
  "quest.75974F7E0E2DE9B1.quest_desc": [
    "Severing, a rare sword enchantment up to V, rolls its own much better chance for these drops, separate from Looting: two tries per kill. The Magicbane is a fragile athame with better odds, and its enchantments add damage."
  ],
  "quest.67E629F9FB07CC3A.title": "Spare parts, recycled",
  "quest.67E629F9FB07CC3A.quest_desc": [
    "Mob drops uncraft into vanilla items: a Rib Bone gives five bones, a Nebulous Heart three ender pearls, and so on. Nothing goes to waste. The only one removed here: spawn eggs from charm fragments."
  ],
  "quest.1602FCCE67071632.title": "The Void Tear",
  "quest.1602FCCE67071632.quest_desc": [
    "It swallows the item you carry most of, in near-unlimited amounts. Sneak-right-click to vacuum that item; right-click a chest to give or take; sneak-scroll changes how much it leaves you. It's also the heart of many relics.",
    "",
    "A pocket with no bottom. Finally."
  ],
  "quest.3F66B42978A29BEB.title": "Coin of Fortune",
  "quest.3F66B42978A29BEB.quest_desc": [
    "It pulls items and XP orbs from about five blocks around; sneak-right-click toggles it, and holding right-click roughly triples the range. On a pedestal it collects into adjacent containers.",
    "",
    "Heads you win. Tails you also win."
  ],
  "quest.6B7CA145EEF35E33.title": "A bank for your XP",
  "quest.6B7CA145EEF35E33.quest_desc": [
    "The Hero's Medallion stores your XP while active and returns it level by level on right-click. On a pedestal it repairs Mending items nearby. The Infernal Tear burns one item type from your inventory into XP.",
    "",
    "A savings account that levels up."
  ],
  "quest.0D1D01C3A723C11C.title": "Pain for hunger",
  "quest.0D1D01C3A723C11C.quest_desc": [
    "The Emperor's Chalice is an endless water bucket; aimed at nothing, you drink and trade health for hunger. The Infernal Chalice carries lava and turns fire damage into hunger, as the Kraken Shell does with drowning.",
    "",
    "Everything costs a sandwich."
  ],
  "quest.3D7F21C902B6A1AC.title": "Feathers that cheat death",
  "quest.3D7F21C902B6A1AC.quest_desc": [
    "The Angelic Feather turns fall damage into hunger. An Angelheart Vial shatters just before you'd die and saves you. Three vials and a feather make the Phoenix Down: full-health revival, then back to being a feather.",
    "",
    "Death, postponed."
  ],
  "quest.704767047C143491.title": "Ender Staff and Wraith Node",
  "quest.704767047C143491.quest_desc": [
    "Charge it with ender pearls; it throws pearls that don't hurt you, far and straight in long-cast mode. Bound to a Wraith Node, holding right-click takes you back there for pearls, same dimension only."
  ],
  "quest.47B3F1FBA7A0719F.title": "Harvest Rod and lily pads",
  "quest.47B3F1FBA7A0719F.quest_desc": [
    "The Harvest Rod stores bone meal and seeds, with three modes: fertilize, plant or unbreakable hoe, over an area while you hold right-click. The Lilypad of Fertility speeds nearby crops, and several stack.",
    "",
    "Farming, in bulk."
  ],
  "quest.1F2BD5D642D742F3.title": "Never place a torch again",
  "quest.1F2BD5D642D742F3.quest_desc": [
    "The Sojourner's Staff holds 1,500 torches and places them up to 30 blocks away. The Lantern of Paranoia places torches by itself wherever monsters could spawn. The Interdiction Torch pushes creatures away.",
    "",
    "Paranoid, and right."
  ],
  "quest.399F5E31880D8EC7.title": "The Hunter's Handgun",
  "quest.399F5E31880D8EC7.quest_desc": [
    "Barrel, grip and hammer assemblies. Right-click fires; hold to reload from magazines. Bullets range from neutral to exorcism, ender (piercing, seeking), buster (TNT-sized) and storm. Recoil, reload and fire rate improve with your XP level, up to 20.",
    "",
    "Magic, with a trigger."
  ],
  "quest.5211737DB3C3FFAB.title": "Peace treaties with mobs",
  "quest.5211737DB3C3FFAB.quest_desc": [
    "Six Charm Fragments of a mob, with leather and string, make a Charm: that mob ignores you even if you hit it. Killing it wears the charm down; its drops repair it. The Charm Belt holds them all.",
    "",
    "Diplomacy, one species at a time."
  ],
  "quest.2DF1BCA7D91D6E9F.title": "Pedestals that work",
  "quest.2DF1BCA7D91D6E9F.quest_desc": [
    "It runs the item on top: the coin collects, the medallion repairs, a sword attacks mobs in range (not bosses, pets or babies), a bucket milks, shears shear, a rod fishes. Switch it on by hand, with redstone, or from another pedestal."
  ],
  "quest.42624A1953E3F0E1.title": "Altar of Light",
  "quest.42624A1953E3F0E1.quest_desc": [
    "Feed it redstone until it activates, and after a while a glowstone block appears on top; it needs direct sunlight. Its partner, the Alkahestry Tome, is removed here, but the altar works alone.",
    "",
    "Photosynthesis for rocks."
  ],
  "quest.4CB4E091ADE69433.title": "Witherless Rose",
  "quest.4CB4E091ADE69433.quest_desc": [
    "Four nether stars, four fertile essences and a rose bush: while it's in your inventory, wither can't touch you. Stars only come from the Wither here, so it's a late, deliberate buy.",
    "",
    "Kill four Withers to stop fearing the fifth."
  ],
  "quest.3AE6FEA5D618D686.title": "The Rending Gale",
  "quest.3AE6FEA5D618D686.quest_desc": [
    "It flies you where you point, pushes or pulls creatures and calls lightning in storms; charge it with feathers. No fall protection, but pointing down and holding cancels the fall. Here its recipe takes an Act IV zanite gemstone.",
    "",
    "Your own private storm."
  ],
  "quest.09A09F5AB3BF9AE8.title": "What the pack took away",
  "quest.09A09F5AB3BF9AE8.quest_desc": [
    "The Alkahestry Tome and its recipes are gone: charged with redstone, it duplicated iron, gold, diamonds and even nether stars. Spawn eggs from charm fragments are gone too, to keep mob farms staged.",
    "",
    "No free diamonds. Sorry."
  ],
  "quest.632F3641C05B1EF2.title": "A hall of relics",
  "quest.632F3641C05B1EF2.quest_desc": [
    "A Void Tear that never fills, a coin and a medallion working on pedestals, a charm belt keeping the dangerous ones polite and, from Act IV, the Rending Gale overhead. Every drop has a use; hunting pays.",
    "",
    "The monsters funded your museum."
  ],
  "chapter.1B43556F7B974465.title": "Apotheosis · Spawners",
  "chapter.1B43556F7B974465.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Sixteen copper augments tune a spawner where it stands, one set per act from III to V: ENTRELUMEN's version of Apothic Spawners, with no runes."
  ],
  "task.76E7B6B79FF3082D.title": "Look at a Monster Spawner",
  "quest.46B4B2355B6D1190.title": "Spawners you tune in place",
  "quest.46B4B2355B6D1190.quest_subtitle": "You don't move the spawner. You move in.",
  "quest.46B4B2355B6D1190.quest_desc": [
    "Every Monster Spawner has stats: how long it waits, how many mobs it makes, how far it reaches. Here you change them where the spawner stands, with sixteen copper augments, one set per act from III to V."
  ],
  "quest.2FA66A984D5CBF5F.title": "What a spawner knows",
  "quest.2FA66A984D5CBF5F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A dungeon spawner waits 200 to 800 ticks, tries 4 mobs at once, stops at 6 nearby, runs with a player within 16 blocks and spawns within 4. Look at one with Jade and hold \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.keyboard.left.control\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" to read its current stats.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3604CB1267C1BCF1.title": "Spawners stay put",
  "quest.3604CB1267C1BCF1.quest_desc": [
    "Silk Touch cannot lift spawners in this pack: portable spawners would bring mob farms ahead of their acts. Build around the spawner you found, and scout a few before you sink augments into one."
  ],
  "quest.4A3E617E34F69B7F.title": "No runes here",
  "quest.4A3E617E34F69B7F.quest_desc": [
    "Apotheosis 8.7 moved spawner modifiers onto runes. The pack removes the runes and puts every modifier on the copper augments instead, so there is one route. Spawner chains still drop from blown-up spawners but craft nothing."
  ],
  "quest.1130D1DBD5D17857.title": "Copper medallions",
  "quest.1130D1DBD5D17857.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Every augment is the same small medallion: the classic core for its stat in the middle, like sugar for speed or a clock for delay, an act component on top and three copper sheets around. EMI lists each one with its step and cap.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.497457C6B927DEDB.title": "Enter a Nether fortress",
  "quest.482C3406948169E0.title": "Where spawners hide",
  "quest.482C3406948169E0.quest_subtitle": "Blazes by appointment.",
  "quest.482C3406948169E0.quest_desc": [
    "Dungeons hold zombie, skeleton and spider spawners, mineshafts cave spiders, and Nether fortresses blazes: blaze rods feed hellshelves, tomes and sigils. Apotheosis adds rogue spawners in caves, each over a chest."
  ],
  "task.2FB15D1A02FFAF30.title": "Apply an augment to a spawner",
  "quest.323AF494EF14AD45.title": "Applying an augment",
  "quest.323AF494EF14AD45.quest_subtitle": "Right-click, and the cage listens.",
  "quest.323AF494EF14AD45.quest_desc": [
    "Right-click the spawner holding an augment: it's spent and the stat moves one fixed step, up to its cap. Changed your mind? The same augment with Nether Quartz in the other hand undoes one step, and the quartz stays."
  ],
  "quest.1CEB5CEB62360BE4.title": "Act III: faster",
  "quest.1CEB5CEB62360BE4.quest_subtitle": "Sugar and a clock. Coffee not included.",
  "quest.1CEB5CEB62360BE4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"On a \"},{\"text\":\"Power Regulator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:power_regulator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": the \"},{\"text\":\"Quickening Augment\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:augment_min_delay\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" takes 10 ticks off the minimum delay and the \"},{\"text\":\"Hastening Augment\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:augment_max_delay\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" 20 off the maximum, both down to 20. If the maximum drops below the minimum, the minimum wins, so lower both.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.527B9F06CC766C21.title": "Act III: quiet and small",
  "quest.527B9F06CC766C21.quest_subtitle": "Peace and quiet, and tiny zombies.",
  "quest.527B9F06CC766C21.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Silent Augment\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:augment_silent\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", on a \"},{\"text\":\"Handling Core\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:handling_core\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", mutes whatever the spawner makes. The \"},{\"text\":\"Youthful Augment\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:augment_youthful\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", on a \"},{\"text\":\"Propagation Core\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:propagation_core\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", spawns babies whenever the mob has them. Both are switches: one of each does it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1250D901BD5952CE.title": "Act III: wider",
  "quest.1250D901BD5952CE.quest_subtitle": "More room, and you can stand further back.",
  "quest.1250D901BD5952CE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Spread Augment\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:augment_spawn_range\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", on a \"},{\"text\":\"Routing Matrix\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:routing_matrix\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", adds 2 to the spawn range, up to 32. The \"},{\"text\":\"Reach Augment\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:augment_player_range\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", on an \"},{\"text\":\"Inventory Sensor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:inventory_sensor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", adds 4 to the activation range, up to 48.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2F85F12146928AC0.title": "Act IV: more",
  "quest.2F85F12146928AC0.quest_subtitle": "A crowd needs room.",
  "quest.2F85F12146928AC0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Both sit on an \"},{\"text\":\"Ecosystem Capsule\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:ecosystem_capsule\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". The \"},{\"text\":\"Multitude Augment\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:augment_spawn_count\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" adds 2 mobs to each spawn, up to 16; the \"},{\"text\":\"Crowd Augment\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:augment_max_nearby\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" lets 2 more stay nearby, up to 32. Raise them together, or the spawner stops as soon as the room fills.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.26192F6158ECA5B3.title": "Act IV: weaker, hotter",
  "quest.26192F6158ECA5B3.quest_subtitle": "Pre-cooked mobs.",
  "quest.26192F6158ECA5B3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Debilitating Augment\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:augment_initial_health\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", on a \"},{\"text\":\"Spectral Lens\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:spectral_lens\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", spawns mobs with 5% less health per use, down to 20%. The \"},{\"text\":\"Burning Augment\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:augment_burning\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", on a \"},{\"text\":\"Containment Seal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:containment_seal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", sets them on fire as they appear.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.23901202F94D30E8.title": "Act V: echoes",
  "quest.23901202F94D30E8.quest_subtitle": "Loot, with an echo.",
  "quest.23901202F94D30E8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Echoing Augment\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:augment_echoing\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", on a \"},{\"text\":\"Renewal Engine\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:renewal_engine\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", makes spawned mobs drop extra loot: one more level per use, up to three. Three augments, three levels.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.496B759DBBF1D298.title": "Make a spawner ignore spawn conditions",
  "quest.382784377D7A7F60.title": "Act V: anywhere, any light",
  "quest.382784377D7A7F60.quest_subtitle": "Mobs, now also in daylight.",
  "quest.382784377D7A7F60.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Defiant Augment\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:augment_ignore_conditions\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", on a Renewal Engine, makes the spawner ignore the mob's own spawn rules, grass for animals and darkness for monsters. The \"},{\"text\":\"Twilight Augment\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:augment_ignore_light\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" only ignores light, so it does nothing once a spawner is Defiant.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.5E918C56A784CEBB.title": "Make a spawner work with nobody near",
  "task.7198FABE6E8F04E4.title": "Make a spawner spawn mobs without AI",
  "task.654FFD8BD35A5DF5.title": "Put a spawner under redstone control",
  "quest.1824D7301EBCE51D.title": "Act V: the farm runs itself",
  "quest.1824D7301EBCE51D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three augments sit on an \"},{\"text\":\"Ark Connection Bus\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:ark_bus\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": \"},{\"text\":\"Solitude\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:augment_ignore_players\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" runs the spawner with nobody near, \"},{\"text\":\"Stupor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:augment_no_ai\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" spawns mobs without AI and \"},{\"text\":\"Control\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:augment_redstone_control\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" makes it wait for a redstone signal. Apply all three.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.5ED54198BBBE1B02.title": "Build the Ultimate Spawner",
  "quest.161AAF92BC2C0056.title": "The ultimate spawner",
  "quest.161AAF92BC2C0056.quest_subtitle": "The dungeon works for you now.",
  "quest.161AAF92BC2C0056.quest_desc": [
    "Minimum and maximum delay at 20 ticks, redstone control, no AI, spawn rules ignored and no player needed: a machine built over three acts, some sixty augments in all."
  ],
  "quest.1D36BEF7A5EA2A67.title": "No AI, no lag",
  "quest.1D36BEF7A5EA2A67.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"For any big farm, use Stupor: mobs without AI hang in place doing nothing, which takes a lot of load off the server, and they can still be pushed into a killing chamber. Wire Control to a lever to switch it all off.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.67C43166A62B1243.title": "Count before you craft",
  "quest.67C43166A62B1243.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"From a dungeon spawner, 20 ticks takes 18 Quickening and 39 Hastening; Multitude needs 6 to reach 16, Crowd 13 to reach 32, Reach 8 and Spread 14. Every augment costs its act component, so automate them.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.3C93E2B31C8D75DD.title": "Bring a minimum delay down to 20",
  "quest.5806A46413A36138.title": "I am the fast",
  "quest.5806A46413A36138.quest_subtitle": "One spawn a second, if the maximum follows.",
  "quest.5806A46413A36138.quest_desc": [
    "Eighteen Quickening Augments take the minimum delay from 200 to 20 ticks. Every one costs a Power Regulator."
  ],
  "task.6974B031D3663DE8.title": "Raise a spawn count to 16",
  "quest.65349A6297B46B6F.title": "Look at the size of it",
  "quest.65349A6297B46B6F.quest_subtitle": "Sixteen at a time.",
  "quest.65349A6297B46B6F.quest_desc": [
    "Six Multitude Augments: sixteen mobs per spawn, the cap. The advancement's name is the mod's joke, not ours."
  ],
  "reward.769A862425965BC1.title": "Secret found",
  "task.63156D5E8345172F.title": "Raise max nearby entities to 32",
  "quest.610E9BE202898B4F.title": "Creating a horde",
  "quest.610E9BE202898B4F.quest_subtitle": "Thirty-two, and counting.",
  "quest.610E9BE202898B4F.quest_desc": [
    "Thirteen Crowd Augments let 32 mobs of that kind stay near the spawner before it pauses. Make sure the killing floor keeps up."
  ],
  "reward.4D48C0810BE2D8DB.title": "Secret found",
  "task.1992720CAB9FBB71.title": "Raise an activation range to 48",
  "quest.2F607943EAB276FE.title": "Far from the fight",
  "quest.2F607943EAB276FE.quest_subtitle": "Farming from the couch.",
  "quest.2F607943EAB276FE.quest_desc": [
    "Eight Reach Augments take the activation range from 16 blocks to its cap of 48: the spawner keeps working while you sort loot three chunks away."
  ],
  "task.334A8D5C0A6B1ED6.title": "Get a spawn egg with Capturing",
  "quest.7DFEB61C03844351.title": "Capturing and spawn eggs",
  "quest.7DFEB61C03844351.quest_subtitle": "Gotta catch... one, eventually.",
  "quest.7DFEB61C03844351.quest_desc": [
    "A spawn egg changes a spawner's mob. Capturing, a sword enchantment, gives each kill a 0.5% chance per level to drop the mob's egg: the Chronicle says 0.4%, the pack's config sets 0.5%."
  ],
  "quest.1E54FD607A2D4D56.title": "A leash that rewrites spawners",
  "quest.1E54FD607A2D4D56.quest_subtitle": "The witch is non-negotiable.",
  "quest.1E54FD607A2D4D56.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Catch a witch in an Ender Lead and infuse it at 80 Eterna, 85 Quanta and 60 to 85 Arcana: the \"},{\"text\":\"Occult Ender Lead\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"apothic_enchanting:occult_ender_lead\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" never breaks. Right-click a spawner while it holds a mob, and that mob becomes the spawner's new one.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "In this pack it takes 80 Eterna instead of 75, an Ascent table: rewriting spawners is a mob farm, and mob farms open in act IV."
  ],
  "quest.203B80FC2D8AAD20.title": "What the farm leaves behind",
  "quest.203B80FC2D8AAD20.quest_subtitle": "Bones for the garden, string for the looms.",
  "quest.203B80FC2D8AAD20.quest_desc": [
    "Sixty-four bones and sixty-four string for the common store, once a day: the usual harvest of a skeleton or spider spawner."
  ],
  "image.40AE1A455168D4A4.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eggs and leashes\",\"color\":\"#FF8A3D\"}]",
  "image.409E97275C2F490D.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Apotheosis\",\"color\":\"#F3EEFF\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.7863700F9B4697D1.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Spawners\",\"color\":\"#F2B27A\"}]",
  "image.7625E422669FC9A5.title": "Back to the Sun of Heliodor",
  "image.338E8DE148EF13C5.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» Enchanting\",\"color\":\"#F2B27A\"}]",
  "image.1D12028C369F1E21.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» Adventure\",\"color\":\"#F2B27A\"}]",
  "image.4117F3BEFDD5DCDF.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"III\",\"color\":\"#C2B6DC\"}]",
  "image.2B16AEE9B70782CF.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"IV\",\"color\":\"#C2B6DC\"}]",
  "image.747019D37B6F8275.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"V\",\"color\":\"#C2B6DC\"}]",
  "chapter.6299A6DE7C1CDB53.title": "Ars Nouveau · Addons",
  "chapter.6299A6DE7C1CDB53.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Nine addons around one mark: the elements, Create machines, AE2, fluids, spirits, charms, remote control and more glyphs."
  ],
  "quest.380894BB2C2418A4.title": "Mark of Mastery",
  "quest.380894BB2C2418A4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Wilden Tribute imbued with all eight essences gives five \"},{\"text\":\"Marks of Mastery\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_elemental:mark_of_mastery\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". A mark turns a lesser focus into a full one, or tier 3 Ars armour into elemental armour.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.3E81D67EA8414824.title": "Three elemental essences",
  "quest.4781668B662B5EB1.title": "Pick a school",
  "quest.4781668B662B5EB1.quest_subtitle": "Loyalty has perks.",
  "quest.4781668B662B5EB1.quest_desc": [
    "Three essences of your element, an amethyst shard and three gold make its lesser focus. With Ars Elemental most glyphs belong to a school, and gear attuned to one boosts it. Pick one focus: the other three close in this book, not in the game."
  ],
  "quest.2924750F480D52C9.title": "School of Fire",
  "quest.2924750F480D52C9.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An amethyst shard imbued with three \"},{\"text\":\"fire essences\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:fire_essence\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and three gold, 5000 Source: a \"},{\"text\":\"Lesser Focus of Fire\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_elemental:lesser_fire_focus\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". As a curio it boosts fire glyphs; Ignite adds Magic Burn.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6E26AB0785FDC99F.title": "School of Water",
  "quest.6E26AB0785FDC99F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The same recipe with water essences: a \"},{\"text\":\"Lesser Focus of Water\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_elemental:lesser_water_focus\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It boosts water glyphs and weakens the element across from it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3A6E58D645AAB6BE.title": "School of Earth",
  "quest.3A6E58D645AAB6BE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"With earth essences: a \"},{\"text\":\"Lesser Focus of Earth\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_elemental:lesser_earth_focus\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Diggers love it: earth glyphs get stronger and cheaper.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.02AEEEAC0E66F7ED.title": "School of Air",
  "quest.02AEEEAC0E66F7ED.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"With air essences: a \"},{\"text\":\"Lesser Focus of Air\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_elemental:lesser_air_focus\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Lightning, wind and falling slower, all a little better.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0EACFC65D758ED00.title": "Magic to shafts",
  "quest.0EACFC65D758ED00.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Imbue a Create precision mechanism with amethyst and Source Gems, then build the \"},{\"text\":\"Source Motor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_technica:source_motor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" with brass and cogs. It turns jar Source into rotation and stops when the jar runs dry: fuel, not free power.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.646DFC08E02887AB.title": "Create recipes, cast",
  "quest.646DFC08E02887AB.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Ars Technica glyphs run Create recipes on dropped items: Obliterate crushes, Press presses, Fuse mixes, Whirl washes or smelts by the next glyph. A timer turret over a hopper is a Create machine on Source.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.228526A103C7AB08.title": "A hamster wheel, rebranded",
  "quest.228526A103C7AB08.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A starbuncle charm and a water wheel make a \"},{\"text\":\"Starbuncle Wheel\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_creo:starbuncle_wheel\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": small rotation, more with a gold block in front. Ars blocks also work on moving contraptions.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6644EE1A37239BF7.title": "Spirits in jars",
  "quest.6644EE1A37239BF7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Catch an Occultism worker in a containment jar and it keeps working, never decaying, grabbing matching items around the jar. Ars Ocultas also imbues a \"},{\"text\":\"Spirit Attuned Gem\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:spirit_attuned_gem\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" from a Source Gem: no diamond burned.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4266D0AE6FBF7F11.title": "Source in AE2",
  "quest.4266D0AE6FBF7F11.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"With AE2, the \"},{\"text\":\"ME Source Converter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"arseng:source_acceptor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" turns Source from linked jars into AE energy. When the jars run dry, the network stops: a bridge, not a generator.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.67984B072FE95817.title": "Charms with charges",
  "quest.67984B072FE95817.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Ars Additions makes curios with charges around a bottle in the apparatus. The \"},{\"text\":\"Charm of Second Wind\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_additions:undying_charm\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" saves you from a fatal hit; others cover falls, fire, water and the void. Recharge them in the chamber.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2D79F650880F3F27.title": "Remote access",
  "quest.2D79F650880F3F27.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Warp Index\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_additions:warp_index\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" opens your storage lectern from anywhere in the dimension; the stabilised one crosses dimensions. Craft it on a mundane belt with an eye, a crystal and two charms.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.73D9F01382DCC7E0.title": "A lag alarm",
  "quest.73D9F01382DCC7E0.quest_subtitle": "On a shared server, a small act of love.",
  "quest.73D9F01382DCC7E0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Ars Controle's \"},{\"text\":\"Temporal Stability Sensor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_controle:temporal_stability_sensor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" raises its comparator signal as the world nears lag. Wire it to beds, turrets or braziers and your farms rest when the server struggles.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.45C9169153C229A0.title": "Major Focus of Fire",
  "quest.45C9169153C229A0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Mark of Mastery on your lesser focus at the apparatus, 5000 Source: the \"},{\"text\":\"Focus of Fire\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_elemental:fire_focus\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It keeps the school's boosts and adds Spell Damage II while you burn or swim in lava.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.614F9A50D2E3856A.title": "Major Focus of Water",
  "quest.614F9A50D2E3856A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Mark of Mastery on your lesser focus at the apparatus, 5000 Source: the \"},{\"text\":\"Focus of Water\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_elemental:water_focus\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It keeps the school's boosts and adds Mana Regen I while wet, II and Dolphin's Grace while swimming.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4B9BE3F1A0554C6F.title": "Major Focus of Earth",
  "quest.4B9BE3F1A0554C6F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Mark of Mastery on your lesser focus at the apparatus, 5000 Source: the \"},{\"text\":\"Focus of Earth\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_elemental:earth_focus\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It keeps the school's boosts and adds Mana Regen I below Y 0.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.60DDCF57404CF9D4.title": "Major Focus of Air",
  "quest.60DDCF57404CF9D4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Mark of Mastery on your lesser focus at the apparatus, 5000 Source: the \"},{\"text\":\"Focus of Air\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_elemental:air_focus\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It keeps the school's boosts and adds Mana Regen I high in the sky.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.7BBC20FD86AE97B9.title": "Any elemental armor piece",
  "quest.248939212EE20078.title": "Dressed for your element",
  "quest.248939212EE20078.quest_subtitle": "Fireproof, and stylish about it.",
  "quest.248939212EE20078.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Mark of Mastery\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_elemental:mark_of_mastery\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a netherite ingot and two essences at the apparatus turn tier 3 Ars armor into its elemental cut, 7000 Source, threads and enchantments kept. Each piece boosts and discounts its school and blunts that element's harm.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "A full set of one element turns the harm it blocks into mana and adds a trick: fire puts you out at once, water refills your air, earth feeds you when you starve underground, air all but cancels falls."
  ],
  "task.1D883BDA3CE7A196.title": "Any elemental turret",
  "quest.024694EFF95ED404.title": "Turrets with a school",
  "quest.024694EFF95ED404.quest_subtitle": "Sentries that went to school.",
  "quest.024694EFF95ED404.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Imbue an \"},{\"text\":\"Enchanted Spell Turret\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:spell_turret\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" with three essences and a major focus, 5000 Source: an \"},{\"text\":\"elemental turret\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_elemental:fire_turret\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", with the focus sealed inside. Its spells trigger that focus's combos and cost 65% less when they carry a glyph of its school.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Three manipulation essences and a Focus of Block Shaping make a Manipulation one, no mark needed."
  ],
  "quest.599AF2386989F5DA.title": "The fifth school",
  "quest.599AF2386989F5DA.quest_subtitle": "Your wolves come back. Angrier.",
  "quest.599AF2386989F5DA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two wither roses, a wither skeleton skull and anima essence on a Focus of Summoning: the \"},{\"text\":\"Focus of Necromancy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_elemental:necrotic_focus\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Summons that die rise once more, cast your homing spells and heal you when they kill.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4372B3A3FBF3073E.title": "Trinkets Pouch",
  "quest.4372B3A3FBF3073E.quest_subtitle": "For the jewelry you forgot you had.",
  "quest.4372B3A3FBF3073E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A chest wrapped in eight \"},{\"text\":\"Magebloom Fiber\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:magebloom_fiber\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": the \"},{\"text\":\"Trinkets Pouch\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_elemental:curio_bag\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a bag only for magical trinkets. Rings, amulets, charms and foci stop eating inventory slots.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.66064E8286CA9AB2.title": "Spellcaster Bag",
  "quest.66064E8286CA9AB2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two manipulation essences, blaze powder and two gold blocks turn the pouch into a \"},{\"text\":\"Spellcaster Bag\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_elemental:caster_bag\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": the same trinket storage, for the parchments, tomes and wands you carry.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3E086644DE69525E.title": "Enchanter's Bangle",
  "quest.3E086644DE69525E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An end crystal, two gold blocks and a Source block on a Ring of Potential: the \"},{\"text\":\"Enchanter's Bangle\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_elemental:base_bangle\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a chance to boost any spell. Attune it with a school's essences for a steady boost and that element's side effect.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.66D484D67EC210D9.title": "Any attuned bangle",
  "quest.64B762BA77F17761.title": "A bangle per school",
  "quest.64B762BA77F17761.quest_subtitle": "Accessorize, then incinerate.",
  "quest.64B762BA77F17761.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three essences and a catalyst attune the Enchanter's Bangle at the apparatus: fire charge, powder snow, cobweb or piston. A \"},{\"text\":\"Fire Bangle\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_elemental:fire_bangle\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and its kin boost their school's damage and mark your hits: fire burns, water freezes, earth snares, air knocks back.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Anima and summoning get theirs too: two anima essences, a ghast tear and a wither rose, or two conjuration essences, a bone and a Wilden horn."
  ],
  "quest.250FF80E57C9EF58.title": "Relays with an element",
  "quest.250FF80E57C9EF58.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two essences and two diamonds on a relay raise its capacity and speed. The warper version, the \"},{\"text\":\"Wind Warper Relay\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_elemental:air_relay\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", also stops losing Source over long jumps.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.3A65B3D53C59D881.title": "Any prism lens",
  "quest.54E58F67C38B3AE3.title": "Prisms with a lens",
  "quest.54E58F67C38B3AE3.quest_subtitle": "Aim once, bend forever.",
  "quest.54E58F67C38B3AE3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A spell prism ringed with quartz and four Source Gems: the \"},{\"text\":\"Advanced Spell Prism\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_elemental:advanced_prism\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Aim it at a block with the dominion wand and fit a lens to speed spells up, slow them down, arc them, make them home, pierce more or chain its own glyphs on.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Five lenses are quartz imbued with manipulation essence and the glyph they copy, 2000 Source; the chaining one is quartz with a Source Gem block and blank parchment at the apparatus, scribed like a spell. Piercing and chaining spend Source on every shot."
  ],
  "quest.0D09CAF0C2B68386.title": "Elevators by current",
  "quest.0D09CAF0C2B68386.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Soul sand, air and water essence and four prismarine shards: a \"},{\"text\":\"Bubble Current Elevator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_elemental:water_upstream\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It lifts anyone in water, even flowing water; stack them for height, sneak to go down.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4CEA23EB20EE1173.title": "Urn of Endless Waters",
  "quest.4CEA23EB20EE1173.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A flower pot with a Source Gem, two water essences and two prismarine shards: the \"},{\"text\":\"Urn of Endless Waters\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_elemental:everfull_urn\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Link a cauldron to it with the dominion wand and it stays full for a little Source.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.45DF8905C45955E4.title": "A siren of your own",
  "quest.45DF8905C45955E4.quest_subtitle": "Pays in pickles.",
  "quest.45DF8905C45955E4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Sirens swim near coral. Give one a sea pickle for shards, then add prismarine, fish and Source Gems at the apparatus: a \"},{\"text\":\"Siren Charm\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_elemental:siren_charm\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". On prismarine it becomes a shrine that fishes for you.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.392E849CBC22984F.title": "Two new ways to throw",
  "quest.392E849CBC22984F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Arc Projectile\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_elemental:glyph_arc_projectile\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" falls with gravity and bounces once per Pierce. \"},{\"text\":\"Homing Projectile\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_elemental:glyph_homing_projectile\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" chases the nearest creature; it costs a Nether Star at the scribe's table.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.69CFD7185398097F.title": "Calibrated Precision Mechanism",
  "quest.69CFD7185398097F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Create precision mechanism on the apparatus with four amethyst shards and four Source Gems, 500 Source: the \"},{\"text\":\"Calibrated Precision Mechanism\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_technica:calibrated_precision_mechanism\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Every Ars Technica machine starts from one.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1B21C821E7DB322C.title": "Arcane Wrench",
  "quest.1B21C821E7DB322C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Enchant a \"},{\"text\":\"Create wrench\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:wrench\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" at the apparatus with gold, a calibrated mechanism and manipulation essence, 500 Source: the \"},{\"text\":\"Arcane Wrench\",\"color\":\"#C7A0F5\"},{\"text\":\". Sneak-use picks up pedestals, turrets and containment jars; on a relay it makes a Precise Relay with a cooldown you set.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0133EA206A595221.title": "Focus of Transmutation",
  "quest.0133EA206A595221.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Brass, a rabbit's foot, a calibrated mechanism and an emerald on manipulation essence: the \"},{\"text\":\"Focus of Transmutation\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_technica:transmutation_focus\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Each glyph gets a free Luck, and Press, Polish and Whirl run twice as fast.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.11015A435B6A0D33.title": "Mark of Technomancy",
  "quest.11015A435B6A0D33.quest_subtitle": "Half wizard, half mechanic.",
  "quest.11015A435B6A0D33.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Wilden Tribute with both mechanisms, manipulation essence, iron, copper, zinc, and brass and gold plates, 10000 Source: the \"},{\"text\":\"Mark of Technomancy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_technica:mark_of_technomancy\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". With netherite and brass it turns Arcanist robes into Technomancer's.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.70D6A3CB2DEAC717.title": "Any technomancer armor piece",
  "quest.1FA8CDE6027E0DEC.title": "Robes with a toolbelt",
  "quest.1FA8CDE6027E0DEC.quest_subtitle": "Goggles included.",
  "quest.1FA8CDE6027E0DEC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Mark of Technomancy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_technica:mark_of_technomancy\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", netherite and two brass ingots turn tier 3 Ars armor into a technomancer cut, 7000 Source: Artificer from Sorcerer, Technomancer from Arcanist, Machinaguard from Battlemage. Each piece boosts manipulation glyphs and blunts saws and crushers.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "The hat shows what Create's engineer's goggles show, and a full set speeds up nearby schematicannons. A Mark of Mastery works in place of the Mark of Technomancy."
  ],
  "quest.3E56E680745C6F29.title": "Pocket Factory",
  "quest.3E56E680745C6F29.quest_subtitle": "The author's own soundtrack.",
  "quest.3E56E680745C6F29.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Burn any music disc blank with fire essence at the apparatus, then press it between two brass plates and two Source Gems: the \"},{\"text\":\"Music Disc\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_technica:pocket_factory\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" Pocket Factory, two and a half minutes by zeroregard, who also made Ars Technica.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3FFE6537FA814AB0.title": "A jar on the network",
  "quest.3FFE6537FA814AB0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Source Jar with manipulation essence and an ME Interface: the \"},{\"text\":\"ME Source Jar\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"arseng:me_source_jar\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Rituals, the apparatus and relays pull Source from it as if it were any jar, and it refills from your ME drives.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.338DF2041B8C05F8.title": "Source by the kilobyte",
  "quest.338DF2041B8C05F8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An item cell housing with manipulation essence, Source Gems and gold becomes an \"},{\"text\":\"ME Source Cell Housing\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"arseng:source_cell_housing\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; add a cell component for a \"},{\"text\":\"1k Source Storage Cell\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"arseng:source_storage_cell_1k\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Drives then hold Source like items.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.794EDB40FD230426.title": "Fluid Jar",
  "quest.794EDB40FD230426.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Gold, glass, a water essence and blue archwood: the \"},{\"text\":\"Fluid Jar\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"starbunclemania:fluid_jar\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", sixteen buckets of any fluid. A potion fluid inside feeds a Potion Jar placed on top.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.784895E98D1C389B.title": "New jobs for starbuncles",
  "quest.784895E98D1C389B.quest_subtitle": "Same pay, more paperwork.",
  "quest.784895E98D1C389B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Give a starbuncle a \"},{\"text\":\"Starbucket\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"starbunclemania:star_bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and it carries fluids; a \"},{\"text\":\"StarbAttery\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"starbunclemania:star_battery\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", and it carries FE. Sneak while giving it for looks only.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2557809358A7CDB4.title": "Source from fluids",
  "quest.2557809358A7CDB4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A bucket of liquid Source between gold and Source Gems: the \"},{\"text\":\"Fluid Sourcelink\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"starbunclemania:fluid_sourcelink\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It burns fluids for Source and drains tanks placed under it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5F27BA0E58089DE8.title": "Liquid Source",
  "quest.5F27BA0E58089DE8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Fluid Jar crafted with a relay: the \"},{\"text\":\"Source Condenser\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"starbunclemania:source_condenser\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It condenses Source from nearby jars into a fluid and pours it into tanks below; pipe it anywhere.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1C3ED9ADD74CF4A6.title": "Wixie workstations",
  "quest.1C3ED9ADD74CF4A6.quest_desc": [
    "Put a Wixie on a furnace, a crucible or a cooking pot and it works that station instead of the cauldron. On a fluid jar it mixes; on a stonecutter or cutting board it cuts."
  ],
  "quest.0F39DE69423A68E7.title": "Paperwork for fluids",
  "quest.0F39DE69423A68E7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Parchment with a water essence makes a \"},{\"text\":\"Fluid Scroll\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"starbunclemania:fluid_scroll_allow\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a filter for fluid starbuncles. Parchment and a compass, a \"},{\"text\":\"Direction Scroll\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"starbunclemania:direction_scroll\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": it picks which face of a block they use.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4E3289E49702193C.title": "Pie day",
  "quest.4E3289E49702193C.quest_subtitle": "The circle has a sweet tooth.",
  "quest.4E3289E49702193C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Sixteen \"},{\"text\":\"Source Berry Pies\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_nouveau:source_berry_pie\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for the common store: egg, sugar, magebloom and three sourceberries each. A Wixie on a cooking pot bakes them while you work.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.12F0F6FA1B7A48D7.title": "Sacrificial Altar",
  "quest.12F0F6FA1B7A48D7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Occultism's golden sacrificial bowl rebuilt at the apparatus with four silver ingots, a drygmy shard, sourcestone and a containment jar, 5000 Source: the \"},{\"text\":\"Sacrificial Altar\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_ocultas:altar\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". The same bridge also swaps gold and silver by imbuement.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3C249F478F112ADE.title": "One pool, many jars",
  "quest.3C249F478F112ADE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four ender pearls and four popped chorus fruits on a Source Jar: an \"},{\"text\":\"Ender Source Jar\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_additions:ender_source_jar\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Every one you place shares the same pool, so the base's Source reaches your outposts.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.70FAC3B7CEF3BB5C.title": "Handy Haversack",
  "quest.70FAC3B7CEF3BB5C.quest_subtitle": "Your chest, on your back.",
  "quest.70FAC3B7CEF3BB5C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Bind the \"},{\"text\":\"Handy Haversack\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_additions:handy_haversack\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" to a container, then use items on it to send them there from anywhere. When that container's chunk unloads, the haversack closes.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.47E41BC039657CAA.title": "Source Spawner",
  "quest.47E41BC039657CAA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Drygmy Charm with a Focus of Summoning and conjuration essence: the \"},{\"text\":\"Source Spawner\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_additions:source_spawner\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It spawns whatever sits in nearby Containment Jars and pays each mob in Source.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.602AEF84C9C21258.title": "Finding places",
  "quest.602AEF84C9C21258.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Gold around an amethyst shard makes a \"},{\"text\":\"Wayfinder\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_additions:wayfinder\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". With a compass, a Source Gem and purple archwood it becomes the \"},{\"text\":\"Locate Structure\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_additions:ritual_locate_structure\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" tablet: the augments pick what to find.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.19D4E6F1A92B57F7.title": "Arcane Permanence",
  "quest.19D4E6F1A92B57F7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Blue archwood, a Nether Star, a Source Gem and earth essence: \"},{\"text\":\"Arcane Permanence\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_additions:ritual_chunk_loading\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". While fed a steady stream of Source, it keeps the chunks around the brazier loaded.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.68D6813C3F8AA9AA.title": "Nexus Tower",
  "quest.68D6813C3F8AA9AA.quest_subtitle": "Built on a leyline, no rent due.",
  "quest.68D6813C3F8AA9AA.quest_desc": [
    "You found a Nexus Tower. Its Warp Nexus holds nine warp scrolls and, sitting on a leyline, teleports for free; moved anywhere else it costs 1000 Source per jump."
  ],
  "reward.2CDFECF3F1D39AD6.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.080357400D80C563.title": "A portal that still hums",
  "quest.080357400D80C563.quest_subtitle": "Mind the gap.",
  "quest.080357400D80C563.quest_desc": [
    "You found a ruined warp portal. Throw an Explorer's Warp Scroll into its frame and it drops you near a structure: which one, the scroll decides."
  ],
  "reward.5246C6E13ED93DCB.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.35F4412064FDADCF.title": "Pages from a lost codex",
  "quest.35F4412064FDADCF.quest_subtitle": "Homework from a vanished school.",
  "quest.35F4412064FDADCF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Chests in nexus towers, arcane libraries and ruined warp portals hold one to four \"},{\"text\":\"Codex Entries\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_additions:codex_entry\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", and dungeon, temple and stronghold chests sometimes one. Use an entry to learn a random tier 1 glyph you don't know yet, plus a little experience.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"No chest in this pack holds the Lost or Ancient entries, for tiers 2 and 3.\",\"color\":\"#FF8C7A\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4A5C9EDE9F43BA3B.title": "The dominion wand, from afar",
  "quest.4A5C9EDE9F43BA3B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A dominion wand with four ender pearls and four popped chorus fruits: the \"},{\"text\":\"Remote\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_controle:remote\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Select a block or creature once, then configure it from anywhere, like the wand at arm's length.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5B48725CCBD7B82A.title": "Scryer's Linkage",
  "quest.5B48725CCBD7B82A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Ender pearls and popped chorus on a Scry Crystal: the \"},{\"text\":\"Scryer's Linkage\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_controle:scryers_linkage\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Link it to a distant block with the dominion wand and machines at the linkage reach that block's items, fluids, energy and redstone.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6AF3C7F4F372CABF.title": "Warping Spell Prism",
  "quest.6AF3C7F4F372CABF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A spell prism with ender pearls and popped chorus: the \"},{\"text\":\"Warping Spell Prism\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_controle:warping_spell_prism\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". A projectile that hits it comes out wherever you bound it, even in another dimension.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.77CE704DBFDF9098.title": "A ritual in your pocket",
  "quest.77CE704DBFDF9098.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A brazier relay with a Nether Star, the Wilden Tribute, pearls, chorus and manipulation essence: the \"},{\"text\":\"Portable Brazier Relay\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ars_controle:portable_brazier_relay\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". You carry the ritual's effect, as long as its brazier stays loaded and fed.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.074836C0F4099E3B.title": "Spells with conditions",
  "quest.074836C0F4099E3B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Ars Controle's filter glyphs stop a spell unless a condition holds: Above, Below, Level, Not, Or, Xor, Random. Precise Delay waits an exact number of ticks. Filters make turrets pick their targets.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0D51ECA3FC9B3BE5.title": "Spell Binder",
  "quest.0D51ECA3FC9B3BE5.quest_subtitle": "A book of books.",
  "quest.0D51ECA3FC9B3BE5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Novice Spell Book wrapped in eight leather: the \"},{\"text\":\"Spell Binder\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"not_enough_glyphs:spell_binder\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It casts from the spell parchments and caster tomes you keep inside, ten of them on the radial menu.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.13547694FFCC308E.title": "Covers for the binder",
  "quest.13547694FFCC308E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Alteration Table fits two covers on a binder, like threads. \"},{\"text\":\"Lucky Cover\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"not_enough_glyphs:thread_scritchance\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" raises spell critical chance; \"},{\"text\":\"Keen Cover\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"not_enough_glyphs:thread_scritdamage\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", critical damage.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.10D1426A397B6EA7.title": "Spells on standby",
  "quest.10D1426A397B6EA7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Contingency glyphs hold the rest of the spell until something happens: \"},{\"text\":\"health drops\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"not_enough_glyphs:glyph_contingency_health\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" below 20%, or a \"},{\"text\":\"long fall\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"not_enough_glyphs:glyph_contingency_fall\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" starts. Heal or Slowfall behind them is insurance you cast in advance.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.73412E8EA4D0BDDB.title": "Farm and flatten",
  "quest.73412E8EA4D0BDDB.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Plow\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"not_enough_glyphs:glyph_plow\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" tills like a hoe. \"},{\"text\":\"Propagate Plane\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"not_enough_glyphs:glyph_propagate_plane\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" spreads the rest of the spell over a flat area from the block hit; AOE and Pierce size it, Sensitive makes it round.\"}]"
  ],
  "image.2529D426726ECB16.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Ars Nouveau · Addons\",\"color\":\"#C7A0F5\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.6A929B21B0921F03.title": "Back to Ars Nouveau",
  "image.53099A69CE519DD9.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Ars Elemental: schools\",\"color\":\"#C7A0F5\"}]",
  "image.50A5DA5E0ADD626E.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Ars Elemental: gear\",\"color\":\"#C7A0F5\"}]",
  "image.716D049135973A94.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Ars Technica\",\"color\":\"#C7A0F5\"}]",
  "image.6B5A920877314954.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Ars Énergistique\",\"color\":\"#C7A0F5\"}]",
  "image.4815AD2DEB50FAE7.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Starbunclemania\",\"color\":\"#C7A0F5\"}]",
  "image.4171D67886EC111B.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Ars Ocultas and Ars Creo\",\"color\":\"#C7A0F5\"}]",
  "image.64F4E5722FABD4F4.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Ars Additions\",\"color\":\"#C7A0F5\"}]",
  "image.6A6D50FEFFC8ECA3.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Ars Controle\",\"color\":\"#C7A0F5\"}]",
  "image.465866C6B057A9AB.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Not Enough Glyphs\",\"color\":\"#C7A0F5\"}]",
  "chapter.77684ABAA0372D83.title": "Forbidden and Arcanus",
  "chapter.77684ABAA0372D83.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Darkstone, deorum and dark rituals: the Clibano, the Hephaestus Forge from tier 1 to 5, modifiers and the Eternal Stella."
  ],
  "quest.4FC309242490B654.title": "Arcane Crystal",
  "quest.4FC309242490B654.quest_subtitle": "It hums. That's normal.",
  "quest.4FC309242490B654.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Its ore sits between Y -40 and 14, thickest around -13, in stone and deepslate. Each ore drops one \"},{\"text\":\"Arcane Crystal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"forbidden_arcanus:arcane_crystal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", more with Fortune.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Keep whole crystals: the first two forge upgrades eat eight.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.72FC0572C7252A6E.title": "Crystal for the common store",
  "quest.72FC0572C7252A6E.quest_subtitle": "Somebody always needs dust.",
  "quest.72FC0572C7252A6E.quest_desc": [
    "Sixteen arcane crystals for the common store, once a day. Dust, Mundabitur, Deorum and the first forge upgrades all start from them."
  ],
  "quest.58C0337B2A6CA678.title": "Arcane Crystal Dust",
  "quest.58C0337B2A6CA678.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Smelt or blast a crystal into \"},{\"text\":\"Arcane Crystal Dust\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"forbidden_arcanus:arcane_crystal_dust\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Mundabitur, Deorum, Aureal Bottles, Arcane Bone Meal and Corrupti Dust all take it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.338375EA7163146B.title": "Darkstone",
  "quest.338375EA7163146B.quest_subtitle": "The basement, sold by the ton.",
  "quest.338375EA7163146B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"It fills the floor of the world, from bedrock up to about Y -51, in veins of up to twenty blocks. Four \"},{\"text\":\"Darkstone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"forbidden_arcanus:darkstone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" polish into four Polished Darkstone, and the forge floor alone wants 48.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5693E18BB2B40839.title": "Mundabitur Dust",
  "quest.5693E18BB2B40839.quest_subtitle": "Wake-up powder for sleeping stone.",
  "quest.5693E18BB2B40839.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Arcane crystal dust, redstone, blaze powder, bone meal, a phantom membrane and gunpowder make four \"},{\"text\":\"Mundabitur Dust\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"forbidden_arcanus:mundabitur_dust\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Used on a finished structure it wakes it up: the Clibano, the forge and the crystal obelisks all start with a pinch.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3C32648DA7CFCF15.title": "Deorum",
  "quest.3C32648DA7CFCF15.quest_subtitle": "Gold that went to finishing school.",
  "quest.3C32648DA7CFCF15.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A gold ingot in the middle, two Mundabitur Dust and two arcane crystal dust beside it, charcoal in the corners. \"},{\"text\":\"Deorum Ingots\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"forbidden_arcanus:deorum_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" gild the forge floor, make its arcane blocks and pay the tier 3 upgrade.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5D48E2CFBF8D6733.title": "The forge floor",
  "quest.5D48E2CFBF8D6733.quest_subtitle": "Sixty-one blocks, no pressure.",
  "quest.5D48E2CFBF8D6733.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Nine by nine with the corners cut: 48 \"},{\"text\":\"Polished Darkstone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"forbidden_arcanus:polished_darkstone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", 9 \"},{\"text\":\"Gilded Chiseled Polished Darkstone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"forbidden_arcanus:gilded_chiseled_polished_darkstone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and 4 \"},{\"text\":\"Chiseled Arcane Polished Darkstone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"forbidden_arcanus:chiseled_arcane_polished_darkstone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in a cross around the centre.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "One Deorum Nugget gilds a chiseled block. The arcane ones start as eight Polished Darkstone around a Deorum Ingot, then slabs, then two slabs stacked. The gilded blocks sit under the centre and the eight pedestal spots."
  ],
  "quest.0DEEAA8CD231572A.title": "Darkstone Pedestals",
  "quest.0DEEAA8CD231572A.quest_subtitle": "Eight seats at the table.",
  "quest.0DEEAA8CD231572A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three arcane polished darkstone slabs on top, a pillar, three Polished Darkstone at the foot. Eight \"},{\"text\":\"Darkstone Pedestals\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"forbidden_arcanus:darkstone_pedestal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" stand on the outer gilded blocks, and each holds one ritual ingredient.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.358A3821475C5EDC.title": "Watch it built",
  "quest.358A3821475C5EDC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Hover a Darkstone Pedestal or the forge and hold \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.ponder.ponder\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\": Ponder lays the floor block by block. Its label says 45 Polished Darkstone; the pattern the forge checks wants 48.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.00D0B2C1D5AE335F.title": "Hands off the pedestals",
  "quest.00D0B2C1D5AE335F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Rituals never fail by chance. Swap a pedestal item while the circle turns and it fails with a bang, spitting out the main ingredient; wait, and the result lands in the main slot.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0E80A8EFE984002E.title": "Magical Farmland",
  "quest.0E80A8EFE984002E.quest_subtitle": "Double harvest, same seeds.",
  "quest.0E80A8EFE984002E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four bone meal around arcane crystal dust make four \"},{\"text\":\"Arcane Bone Meal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"forbidden_arcanus:arcane_bone_meal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; use one on farmland to make it magical. Fully grown crops on it drop twice, seeds of wheat, beetroot, melon and pumpkin excepted.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4E7A15C1D48FC57D.title": "Storm in a pinch",
  "quest.4E7A15C1D48FC57D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Mundabitur Dust on a creeper charges it, no thunderstorm needed. The mobs a charged creeper blows up can drop their heads.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0C5E009946DCB505.title": "Aurum, orchids and fungyss",
  "quest.0C5E009946DCB505.quest_subtitle": "The flower forest's secret shelf.",
  "quest.0C5E009946DCB505.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Aurum trees and Yellow Orchids grow in flower forests, and a few aurum leaves drop gold nuggets. Wandering Traders sell \"},{\"text\":\"Aurum Saplings\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"forbidden_arcanus:aurum_sapling\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", Yellow Orchids and Fungyss; bone meal grows a Fungyss into a giant mushroom.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.01CECD15EB6D9432.title": "What the mobs leave",
  "quest.01CECD15EB6D9432.quest_subtitle": "Bats, squid and endermen, all donors.",
  "quest.01CECD15EB6D9432.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Bats drop Bat Wings now and then, squid Tentacles, endermen up to two \"},{\"text\":\"Ender Pearl Fragments\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"forbidden_arcanus:ender_pearl_fragment\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; four fragments rebuild a pearl. A wing, a mushroom, nether wart and a bowl make Bat Soup, with twelve seconds of Night Vision.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.75FD269D6078BCB0.title": "Building in the dark",
  "quest.75FD269D6078BCB0.quest_subtitle": "The forge floor, but for your house.",
  "quest.75FD269D6078BCB0.quest_desc": [
    "Darkstone comes in bricks, tiles, pillars, walls and chiseled blocks. Deorum gives glass, doors, chains and lanterns, a Rune in eight glass makes Runic Glass, and Soulless Sand has a sandstone set of its own."
  ],
  "task.6E6D0FC41FCD90EF.title": "Look at your forge",
  "quest.253FE16B6D4A2791.title": "The Hephaestus Forge",
  "quest.253FE16B6D4A2791.quest_subtitle": "Stand back. It's a lightning thing.",
  "quest.253FE16B6D4A2791.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Put a \"},{\"text\":\"Smithing Table\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:smithing_table\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on the central gilded block, keep the air above the floor clear and use Mundabitur Dust on the table. A crimson bolt strikes, harmless, and the table is now a tier 1 forge.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Its menu holds the main ingredient in the middle, an input slot for each essence and the enhancer slots: one at tier 1 and one more per tier, up to four. Broken, the forge drops itself with its tier."
  ],
  "quest.25867C799AFFEEC8.title": "The first ritual",
  "quest.25867C799AFFEEC8.quest_subtitle": "Strike once. Then touch nothing.",
  "quest.25867C799AFFEEC8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Lodestone in the main slot; on the pedestals two clay balls, two Wax, two slime balls and an iron ingot. With 100 \"},{\"text\":\"aureal\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"20379F2B379281E0\"}},{\"text\":\", 1,250 \"},{\"text\":\"blood\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"43964D75733C9493\"}},{\"text\":\" and 2 \"},{\"text\":\"souls\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"13CC10E9C5C72D52\"}},{\"text\":\" in the forge, right-click it with a gavel: out comes \"},{\"text\":\"Ferrognetic Mixture\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"forbidden_arcanus:ferrognetic_mixture\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Every ritual works like this: the main ingredient in the forge, exactly one item per pedestal, the essences in the tanks, a gavel strike. Wax is a honey bottle and a slime ball."
  ],
  "task.1959157B41C5D9CE.title": "Look at a tier 2 forge",
  "quest.6488F327A9FE403D.title": "Tier 2",
  "quest.6488F327A9FE403D.quest_subtitle": "The forge grows by eating.",
  "quest.6488F327A9FE403D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Edelwood Planks\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"63CB6C45914A7709\"}},{\"text\":\" in the main slot, four arcane crystals and four \"},{\"text\":\"Spawner Scrap\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"689CD59FDC4C6701\"}},{\"text\":\" on the pedestals, then 500 aureal, 6,000 blood and 10 souls. Tier 2 holds 3,000 aureal, 50 souls, 15,000 blood and 1,350 experience, with two enhancer slots.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Each upgrade needs exactly the tier before it and every soul that tier can hold: 10, 50, 100, then 500.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6CA12743B44C426C.title": "Apply Modifier",
  "quest.6CA12743B44C426C.quest_subtitle": "Tools that cheat, one trick each.",
  "quest.6CA12743B44C426C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight darkstone around a Netherite Upgrade make the \"},{\"text\":\"Smithing Template\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"forbidden_arcanus:apply_modifier_smithing_template\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for modifiers. At a Smithing Table it joins a tool or an armor piece with a modifier item forged in the Hephaestus Forge.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.5066B1A110B63AF9.title": "Look at a tier 3 forge",
  "quest.4BCB6540F2A03C41.title": "Tier 3",
  "quest.4BCB6540F2A03C41.quest_subtitle": "Gold makes everything better. Deorum, twice.",
  "quest.4BCB6540F2A03C41.quest_desc": [
    "Chiseled Polished Darkstone in the main slot, four arcane crystals and four Deorum Ingots on the pedestals, then 1,000 aureal, 9,000 blood and 50 souls. Tier 3 holds 5,000 aureal, 100 souls, 30,000 blood and 2,500 experience, with three enhancer slots.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "It opens the Eternal Stella, the Quantum Injector and the Sea and Whirlwind Prisms."
  ],
  "quest.312349D84B6E290C.title": "Eternal Stella",
  "quest.312349D84B6E290C.quest_subtitle": "Forever has a price. It's in Act IV.",
  "quest.312349D84B6E290C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A tier 3 ritual: a diamond in the main slot; three Xpetrified Orbs, a \"},{\"text\":\"Stellarite Piece\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"52CF7E2611C2A687\"}},{\"text\":\" and, in this pack, a \"},{\"text\":\"Containment Seal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:containment_seal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on the pedestals; 82 aureal, 1,000 blood and 1 soul.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"At the Smithing Table the \"},{\"text\":\"Eternal Stella\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"forbidden_arcanus:eternal_stella\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" makes a tool or armor piece Eternal: its durability is gone for good. Elytra refuse it.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.4ED2727F9F418F91.title": "Look at a tier 4 forge",
  "quest.093B7EBC34AED82F.title": "Tier 4",
  "quest.093B7EBC34AED82F.quest_subtitle": "A hundred souls, all accounted for.",
  "quest.093B7EBC34AED82F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Chiseled Polished Darkstone again, four \"},{\"text\":\"Stellarite Pieces\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"52CF7E2611C2A687\"}},{\"text\":\" and four \"},{\"text\":\"Runes\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"1EF883D9A7A41ECA\"}},{\"text\":\" on the pedestals, then 2,000 aureal, 12,000 blood and 100 souls. Tier 4 holds 10,000 aureal, 500 souls, 50,000 blood and 5,000 experience, and all four enhancer slots open.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4D22C5E3A84C7B6F.title": "The last offering",
  "quest.4D22C5E3A84C7B6F.quest_subtitle": "Everything the forge asked for, at once.",
  "quest.4D22C5E3A84C7B6F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Tier 5 takes a \"},{\"text\":\"Stellarite Block\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"forbidden_arcanus:stellarite_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in the main slot and, on the pedestals, four Sculk Catalysts, two \"},{\"text\":\"Dark Nether Stars\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"5FA7700B4E305788\"}},{\"text\":\" and two Dragon Scales, with 5,000 aureal, 20,000 blood and 500 souls.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Crimson Stone\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"21FD8E9DDE9B1674\"}},{\"text\":\" halves those 500 souls.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.27D687CF2B3FA780.title": "Look at a tier 5 forge",
  "quest.5CA11C0E042C3532.title": "Master of the forge",
  "quest.5CA11C0E042C3532.quest_subtitle": "Five tiers, one circle of gold.",
  "quest.5CA11C0E042C3532.quest_desc": [
    "The last upgrade draws a circle of its own, ringed in gold instead of white. A tier 5 forge holds 20,000 aureal, 1,000 souls, 100,000 blood and 7,500 experience: room for any ritual twice over.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Every tier is still in the stone: darkstone, deorum, stellarite and a dragon's scales. The smithing table remembers what it was."
  ],
  "quest.1B60A5EE34117ECD.title": "Blacksmith Gavel",
  "quest.1B60A5EE34117ECD.quest_subtitle": "A hammer that thinks it's a judge.",
  "quest.1B60A5EE34117ECD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Six clay balls shape a \"},{\"text\":\"Blacksmith Gavel Head\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"forbidden_arcanus:blacksmith_gavel_head\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; four ingots and two sticks around it finish the gavel. It mines like a pickaxe of its material, and every ritual it starts costs 50 durability.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2A2194624B5B9D37.title": "Netherite Gavel",
  "quest.2A2194624B5B9D37.quest_subtitle": "Order in the forge, for longer.",
  "quest.2A2194624B5B9D37.quest_desc": [
    "A Diamond Blacksmith Gavel, a Netherite Upgrade and a netherite ingot at the Smithing Table. It shrugs off fire and lava like any netherite tool and starts about forty rituals before it needs mending."
  ],
  "quest.36C3D50459FB3977.title": "The gavel's other job",
  "quest.36C3D50459FB3977.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Any gavel is also a pickaxe, and ores mined with one drop double 30% of the time. Silk Touch turns that off.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.20379F2B379281E0.title": "Aureal",
  "quest.20379F2B379281E0.quest_subtitle": "Bottled light, arcane blend.",
  "quest.20379F2B379281E0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight arcane crystal dust around a Potion of Regeneration II make an \"},{\"text\":\"Aureal Bottle\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"forbidden_arcanus:aureal_bottle\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": 35 aureal in the forge's aureal slot. Dungeon chests hold one or two a fifth of the time.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Drink one instead and its 35 go to your own aureal, which holds 100. Brewed with gunpowder it becomes a Splash Aureal Bottle: 30 aureal for every player within four blocks."
  ],
  "quest.13CC10E9C5C72D52.title": "Souls",
  "quest.13CC10E9C5C72D52.quest_subtitle": "Ten fill a tier 1 forge.",
  "quest.13CC10E9C5C72D52.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Lost Souls wander the Overworld and drop a \"},{\"text\":\"Soul\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"forbidden_arcanus:soul\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" when killed, and a Soul Extractor pulls one out of every soul sand block. A Soul is 1 in the forge's soul slot; tier 1 holds 10.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.43964D75733C9493.title": "Blood",
  "quest.43964D75733C9493.quest_subtitle": "The forge takes it fresh.",
  "quest.43964D75733C9493.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Anything hurt within five blocks of the forge adds 20 blood per point of health it loses. To carry it, hold a \"},{\"text\":\"Test Tube\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"forbidden_arcanus:test_tube\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (a glass bottle and a Rune) in your off hand while you fight: it fills up to 3,000.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.331BF33031809BFF.title": "Look at an obelisk",
  "quest.51BC45132861AF2D.title": "Arcane Crystal Obelisk",
  "quest.51BC45132861AF2D.quest_subtitle": "Aureal on a drip.",
  "quest.51BC45132861AF2D.quest_desc": [
    "Stack two Arcane Crystal Blocks on an Arcane Polished Darkstone and use Mundabitur on them. The obelisk gives 1 aureal every five seconds to the nearest forge within four blocks."
  ],
  "task.73D1F97B97ACF0A9.title": "Kill 3 Lost Souls",
  "quest.7AEAAC0E31EFF00A.title": "Soul Looting",
  "quest.7AEAAC0E31EFF00A.quest_subtitle": "Everybody has a little ghost in them.",
  "quest.7AEAAC0E31EFF00A.quest_desc": [
    "Soul Looting on a sword gives each kill a 5, 10 or 15% chance to free a Lost Soul. Players, villagers and traders release plain ones; zombies, skeletons, witches, illagers and piglins, corrupt ones that drop Corrupt Souls.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"One freed soul in 25 comes out enchanted, and its Enchanted Soul is worth 10 in the forge. Corrupt Souls grow \"},{\"text\":\"Edelwood\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"63CB6C45914A7709\"}},{\"text\":\".\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Splash Aureal Bottle\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"20379F2B379281E0\"}},{\"text\":\" turns a Corrupt Lost Soul into a plain one, and a plain one into an enchanted one.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.24A3592008C81356.title": "Experience",
  "quest.24A3592008C81356.quest_subtitle": "Melt the old gear. Sentiment not included.",
  "quest.24A3592008C81356.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Bottle o' Enchanting\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:experience_bottle\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" is worth 15 in the forge's experience slot. Enchanted gear and books melt there too: their enchantments turn into experience and books come back blank, but curses stay put.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.40C2A1FCDBC69DD4.title": "Soul Extractor",
  "quest.40C2A1FCDBC69DD4.quest_subtitle": "Soul sand, now with less soul.",
  "quest.40C2A1FCDBC69DD4.quest_desc": [
    "An Utrem Jar, nether bricks, quartz and a quartz block. Hold use on soul sand for a moment: it turns into Soulless Sand and drops a Soul. 128 uses per extractor.",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Soulless Sand still lifts bubble columns, and a Soul used on it turns it back into soul sand.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.66FA3B10ABA7E628.title": "A soul with a glint",
  "quest.66FA3B10ABA7E628.quest_subtitle": "One in twenty-five. You were the one.",
  "quest.66FA3B10ABA7E628.quest_desc": [
    "You took down an Enchanted Lost Soul. Its Enchanted Soul feeds the forge 10 souls at once, or burns in the Clibano as enchanted fire, two and a half times faster."
  ],
  "reward.311CE0DAD9836FD8.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.1754343F2BDF9563.title": "Essence in a jar",
  "quest.1754343F2BDF9563.quest_subtitle": "A pantry for the forge.",
  "quest.1754343F2BDF9563.quest_desc": [
    "Seven colorless glass and an Edelwood Plank make an Utrem Jar. Place it and use any essence item on it (a bottle, a soul, a filled test tube) and it becomes a jar of that essence, up to 10,000; broken, it keeps what it holds."
  ],
  "quest.0C9814B908DFD505.title": "Quantum Injector",
  "quest.0C9814B908DFD505.quest_subtitle": "Plumbing, but for souls.",
  "quest.0C9814B908DFD505.quest_desc": [
    "Set it within four blocks of a forge and right-click it on: it pipes essence from jars within eight blocks, 20 a second of each kind the forge lacks. Another right-click switches it off.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "A tier 3 ritual: Mundabitur Dust in the main slot and four Quantum Cores, for 5,000 aureal, 3,000 blood, 1,060 experience and 50 souls."
  ],
  "task.5159267783BDD88D.title": "Look at a Magnetized Pedestal",
  "quest.0F1D6797D3FB32B6.title": "Magnetized",
  "quest.0F1D6797D3FB32B6.quest_subtitle": "It's attractive, and it knows it.",
  "quest.0F1D6797D3FB32B6.quest_desc": [
    "Ferrognetic Mixture on a Darkstone Pedestal magnetizes it: when empty it grabs one item dropped on top, so a dropper can load it. On boots at the Smithing Table the mixture is the Magnetized modifier, which pulls nearby items to you."
  ],
  "quest.63CB6C45914A7709.title": "Edelwood",
  "quest.63CB6C45914A7709.quest_subtitle": "A tree that grows from a bad mood.",
  "quest.63CB6C45914A7709.quest_desc": [
    "Use a Corrupt Soul on an oak sapling or a dead bush and it becomes Growing Edelwood; Wandering Traders sell one for 6 emeralds. It grows in bright light, faster with bone meal, into a hollow tree whose branches drop Edelwood Sticks.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Its planks are the tier 2 main ingredient. Smelt a log into Dark Matter; now and then a log turns oily, and a glass bottle collects \"},{\"text\":\"Edelwood Oil\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"forbidden_arcanus:edelwood_oil\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", which crafts into black dye.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.689CD59FDC4C6701.title": "Spawner Scrap",
  "quest.689CD59FDC4C6701.quest_subtitle": "Recycling, but angrier.",
  "quest.689CD59FDC4C6701.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Break a spawner without Silk Touch and it drops \"},{\"text\":\"Spawner Scrap\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"forbidden_arcanus:spawner_scrap\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". In this pack Silk Touch never lifts a spawner, so it only costs you the scrap. Four go into the tier 2 upgrade, four into a Quantum Catcher.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.374121FB0483D5B9.title": "Edelwood Bucket",
  "quest.374121FB0483D5B9.quest_subtitle": "A wooden bucket with ambitions.",
  "quest.374121FB0483D5B9.quest_desc": [
    "Five Edelwood Planks make a bucket that carries four buckets of water or milk, or three of lava or powder snow. Edelwood Ladders are worth one look too: you climb them faster.",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A Botany Pot takes a full Edelwood Water Bucket as a water soil.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5AF7DFE420AA7A06.title": "Magic Wand",
  "quest.5AF7DFE420AA7A06.quest_subtitle": "Point the dangerous end away from friends.",
  "quest.5AF7DFE420AA7A06.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An arcane crystal, a Deorum Ingot and an Edelwood Stick from an Edelwood branch. Hold use for a second and a half and the \"},{\"text\":\"Magic Wand\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"forbidden_arcanus:magic_wand\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" fires an aureal missile, 5 of your own aureal a shot.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4D06EC892DA23352.title": "Quantum Catcher",
  "quest.4D06EC892DA23352.quest_subtitle": "A moving van for villagers.",
  "quest.4D06EC892DA23352.quest_desc": [
    "A tier 1 ritual: a Quantum Core (Rune, flint, Mundabitur) in the main slot and four Spawner Scrap, with 200 aureal, 1,200 blood, 155 experience and 5 souls. Right-click a creature to store it and a block to let it out.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "The catch costs your own aureal: half a passive creature's health, or its health plus a tenth for a hostile one. Your meter holds 100, and bosses don't fit."
  ],
  "quest.49DE53235C00DEB6.title": "Boss Catcher",
  "quest.49DE53235C00DEB6.quest_subtitle": "The fine print is in aureal.",
  "quest.49DE53235C00DEB6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A tier 4 ritual turns a Quantum Catcher into a \"},{\"text\":\"Boss Catcher\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"forbidden_arcanus:boss_catcher\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" with a Nether Star and three Stellarite Pieces, for 500 aureal, 7,500 blood, 1,200 experience and 10 souls.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"It lifts the boss ban, not the price: with 100 aureal at most, a hostile catch tops out at 90 health.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6653C2EF87A62B16.title": "Elementarium",
  "quest.6653C2EF87A62B16.quest_subtitle": "The prisms won't answer without it.",
  "quest.6653C2EF87A62B16.quest_desc": [
    "Jungle temples, desert pyramids and ocean ruins hide one about a fifth of the time. It does nothing by itself: every prism ritual wants it in one of the forge's enhancer slots."
  ],
  "quest.4963D4735CDC9490.title": "One trick per tool",
  "quest.4963D4735CDC9490.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"An item takes a single modifier, and only if it carries none of the enchantments that modifier refuses: Silk Touch blocks Fiery, Unbreaking and Mending block Eternal.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.07F9AD9AAA721431.title": "Fiery",
  "quest.07F9AD9AAA721431.quest_subtitle": "Cooks the ore before it lands.",
  "quest.07F9AD9AAA721431.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Tier 1: an Arcane Crystal Block in the middle, two coal and four blaze powder around it, 200 aureal, 1,250 blood and 4 souls. The \"},{\"text\":\"Smelter Prism\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"forbidden_arcanus:smelter_prism\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" makes a digging tool Fiery: whatever it breaks drops already smelted.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4EE724303EDEEC12.title": "Demolishing",
  "quest.4EE724303EDEEC12.quest_subtitle": "Three by three, no questions asked.",
  "quest.4EE724303EDEEC12.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Tier 2: a Diamond Block, two flint, two dripstone blocks and two pointed dripstone, 300 aureal, 1,500 blood and 9 souls. The \"},{\"text\":\"Terrastomp Prism\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"forbidden_arcanus:terrastomp_prism\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" makes a digging tool Demolishing: it breaks the 3×3 face around the block you mine.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2C296EDA7EF8439A.title": "Aquatic",
  "quest.2C296EDA7EF8439A.quest_subtitle": "Gills sold separately. Healing included.",
  "quest.2C296EDA7EF8439A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Tier 3: a Heart of the Sea, two prismarine shards, two turtle scutes and two lapis, 1,000 aureal, 2,000 blood and 8 souls. The \"},{\"text\":\"Sea Prism\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"forbidden_arcanus:sea_prism\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" makes a helmet Aquatic: head underwater, you mine at full speed and heal a heart every five seconds.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0314F0A0C8F9511D.title": "Whirlwind Prism",
  "quest.0314F0A0C8F9511D.quest_subtitle": "An elevator with no floors.",
  "quest.0314F0A0C8F9511D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Tier 3: white wool, a bat wing, two feathers and three phantom membranes, 1,000 aureal, 2,250 blood and 3 souls. Use the \"},{\"text\":\"Whirlwind Prism\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"forbidden_arcanus:whirlwind_prism\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on the ground: a ten-block updraft lifts you and leaves you a few seconds of Slow Falling.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.52CF7E2611C2A687.title": "Stellarite",
  "quest.52CF7E2611C2A687.quest_subtitle": "The ore that fights back.",
  "quest.52CF7E2611C2A687.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Stella Arcanum ore sits between Y -44 and 42 in small clusters. Mined without Silk Touch it explodes, radius 3, breaking the blocks around it; the \"},{\"text\":\"Stellarite Piece\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"forbidden_arcanus:stellarite_piece\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" it leaves survives the blast.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Four pay the tier 4 upgrade, nine make the Stellarite Block tier 5 wants, and the Eternal Stella and the Boss Catcher take one and three."
  ],
  "quest.2368838F0CC9051D.title": "Defused",
  "quest.2368838F0CC9051D.quest_subtitle": "You carried a bomb home in your pocket.",
  "quest.2368838F0CC9051D.quest_desc": [
    "You lifted a Stella Arcanum with Silk Touch: no blast, and no stellarite either. Place it and mine it again without Silk Touch and it goes off just the same."
  ],
  "reward.100C2ECCAE7A0CE1.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.7A8E426591B7C77C.title": "A black hole",
  "quest.7A8E426591B7C77C.quest_subtitle": "Handle with tongs.",
  "quest.7A8E426591B7C77C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Toss a Dark Matter (a smelted Edelwood Log) and a \"},{\"text\":\"Corrupti Dust\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"forbidden_arcanus:corrupti_dust\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" so they touch in open air and they collapse into a Black Hole. Within five blocks it pulls in items, experience orbs and arrows, and \"},{\"text\":\"loose items are destroyed\",\"color\":\"#FF8C7A\"},{\"text\":\".\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Every 60 experience it swallows comes back as an Xpetrified Orb, thrown at the nearest player within six blocks. Nether stars, stellarite and obsidian are spared. Broken, it drops nothing: choose its spot first."
  ],
  "quest.74A847173675E8AB.title": "Xpetrified Orbs",
  "quest.74A847173675E8AB.quest_subtitle": "Experience, set in stone.",
  "quest.74A847173675E8AB.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Each \"},{\"text\":\"Xpetrified Orb\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"forbidden_arcanus:xpetrified_orb\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" holds 91 experience for the forge, a shade over six Bottles o' Enchanting. The Eternal Stella takes three.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A Stellarite Bee's combs give one 30% of the time in a centrifuge: see \"},{\"text\":\"Productive Bees\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"7ACCFA699A46A465\"}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5DCED9F986C02FD7.title": "Leave the Mending off",
  "quest.5DCED9F986C02FD7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Eternal won't go onto an item that already carries Unbreaking or Mending, and it won't need them afterwards. Every other enchantment stays.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.21FD8E9DDE9B1674.title": "Crimson Stone",
  "quest.21FD8E9DDE9B1674.quest_subtitle": "Half the souls, same miracle.",
  "quest.21FD8E9DDE9B1674.quest_desc": [
    "Pillager outpost chests hide one 18% of the time. In the forge it halves the souls every ritual costs, and the last upgrades want 100 and 500; in the Clibano a soul burns 30% longer."
  ],
  "quest.5FA7700B4E305788.title": "Dark Nether Star",
  "quest.5FA7700B4E305788.quest_subtitle": "A Wither trophy, repainted.",
  "quest.5FA7700B4E305788.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four \"},{\"text\":\"Obsidiansteel Ingots\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"4A09E43F3C8A02F5\"}},{\"text\":\" around a Nether Star. The tier 5 upgrade takes two, and like stellarite the \"},{\"text\":\"Dark Nether Star\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"forbidden_arcanus:dark_nether_star\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" shrugs off explosions and black holes.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.556990A438665B44.title": "Relics with no job",
  "quest.556990A438665B44.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The Maledictus Pact turns up in bastion treasure, but no ritual in this version asks for it. The Divine Pact, Crescent Moon and Soul Crimson Stone have no source, so neither the Soul Binding Crystal nor its Soulbound modifier can be made.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1D876A40378DA0A7.title": "Spectral Eye Amulet",
  "quest.1D876A40378DA0A7.quest_subtitle": "Everyone glows. Nobody asked.",
  "quest.1D876A40378DA0A7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three string, a Nether Star, two Deorum Ingots and an Eye of Ender. Right-click it on: while the \"},{\"text\":\"Spectral Eye Amulet\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"forbidden_arcanus:spectral_eye_amulet\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" rides in your inventory you have Spectral Vision, and every creature nearby glows through walls.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4C5843A9AF1223C3.title": "Ghosts in the catalog",
  "quest.4C5843A9AF1223C3.quest_desc": [
    "EMI shows items this version never hands out: Mortem armor, the Draco Arcanus tools, scepter and staff, the Aureal Tank and Aureal Wardstone, Eternal and Aurealic Obsidian Skulls, the Mortar, the Arcane Crystal Dust Speck and the corrupted arcane crystal set. Nothing gives you the first one."
  ],
  "quest.14F67361629CE0D0.title": "Dragon Scales",
  "quest.14F67361629CE0D0.quest_subtitle": "Shed, not stolen. Mostly.",
  "quest.14F67361629CE0D0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Every Ender Dragon kill drops one to three \"},{\"text\":\"Dragon Scales\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"forbidden_arcanus:dragon_scale\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", more with Looting, and End City treasure chests hold one or two a bit over half the time. The End is Act V ground.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A respawned dragon drops them too.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.44D5BD1787A15336.title": "Draco Arcanus",
  "quest.44D5BD1787A15336.quest_subtitle": "Dress like the thing you killed.",
  "quest.44D5BD1787A15336.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Tier 2 rituals turn each netherite armor piece into Draco Arcanus with Dragon Scales and \"},{\"text\":\"Obsidiansteel\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"4A09E43F3C8A02F5\"}},{\"text\":\", eleven of each for the set. The ritual keeps everything on the netherite piece, enchantments included.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "The full set refills your own aureal by 5 every five seconds."
  ],
  "quest.75C83BB63C6B3C8F.title": "Golden and aquatic scales",
  "quest.75C83BB63C6B3C8F.quest_subtitle": "Same dragon, better tailoring.",
  "quest.75C83BB63C6B3C8F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four Deorum Ingots around a Dragon Scale make a \"},{\"text\":\"Golden Dragon Scale\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"forbidden_arcanus:golden_dragon_scale\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; a scale, a prismarine shard, prismarine crystals and arcane crystal dust make an \"},{\"text\":\"Aquatic Dragon Scale\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"forbidden_arcanus:aquatic_dragon_scale\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Tyr wants fifteen aquatic and ten golden.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2C177CE6AB67CEA0.title": "Tyr",
  "quest.2C177CE6AB67CEA0.quest_subtitle": "The god of war wants his armor back.",
  "quest.2C177CE6AB67CEA0.quest_desc": [
    "Tier 4 rituals raise each Draco Arcanus piece into Tyr with aquatic and golden scales; the chestplate alone costs 6,300 aureal, 8,080 blood, 3,420 experience and 60 souls. Enchantments carry over again.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "The full set refills your own aureal by 10 every five seconds."
  ],
  "quest.5E2C197D4D14E92F.title": "Arrows with opinions",
  "quest.5E2C197D4D14E92F.quest_subtitle": "One goes boom, one breathes.",
  "quest.5E2C197D4D14E92F.quest_desc": [
    "Four arrows around TNT make four Boom Arrows, which explode where they land without breaking blocks. Four around a bottle of Dragon's Breath make one Draco Arcanus Arrow: a hit leaves a cloud of harming breath, like the dragon's own."
  ],
  "quest.1B0AE141F13BB7A6.title": "An egg worth more than the dragon",
  "quest.1B0AE141F13BB7A6.quest_subtitle": "Six golden scales for a paperweight.",
  "quest.1B0AE141F13BB7A6.quest_desc": [
    "You wrapped the Dragon Egg in six Golden Dragon Scales, twenty-four Deorum Ingots of gilding. The Arcane Dragon Egg does nothing but fall like sand and look expensive."
  ],
  "reward.2E8788169AB790F1.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.2591D00C81AFB14D.title": "The Clibano",
  "quest.2591D00C81AFB14D.quest_subtitle": "Three by three, hollow, and hot.",
  "quest.2591D00C81AFB14D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight darkstone around a Blast Furnace make the \"},{\"text\":\"Clibano Core\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"forbidden_arcanus:clibano_core\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Build a 3×3×3 cube of Polished Darkstone Bricks with Polished Darkstone corners, leave the middle hollow, set the core in the centre of one face and dust it with \"},{\"text\":\"Mundabitur\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"5693E18BB2B40839\"}},{\"text\":\".\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "It cooks only its own recipes (ores, raw metals, arcane crystal, runic stone), two at a time. Blast furnace fuel works; Souls in their own slot make the fire faster."
  ],
  "quest.1EF883D9A7A41ECA.title": "Runes",
  "quest.1EF883D9A7A41ECA.quest_subtitle": "Stone with something to say.",
  "quest.1EF883D9A7A41ECA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Runic stone forms below Y 2, and inside darkstone it turns into runic darkstone. Mining it drops a \"},{\"text\":\"Rune\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"forbidden_arcanus:rune\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", Fortune helps, and a furnace, a blast furnace or the Clibano turns silk-touched stone into one too.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Runes make Test Tubes, Quantum Cores and Runic Glass, and four pay the tier 4 upgrade."
  ],
  "quest.16950761F7920B65.title": "Nine residues, one block",
  "quest.16950761F7920B65.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Clibano recipes can leave a residue: a third of the time for iron, copper, coal and arcane crystal, a fifth for gold and lapis, a tenth for diamond, emerald and runes, one in twenty for ancient debris. Nine of a kind make a block, and nine netherite residues a Block of Netherite.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3B69EC6CAD40801E.title": "Soul fire",
  "quest.3B69EC6CAD40801E.quest_subtitle": "Faster, and it only costs a soul.",
  "quest.3B69EC6CAD40801E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Soul\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"forbidden_arcanus:soul\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" or a Corrupt Soul in the soul slot turns the flames blue and cooks 1.5 times faster for 135 seconds; an Enchanted Soul makes enchanted fire, 2.5 times. \"},{\"text\":\"Souls\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"13CC10E9C5C72D52\"}},{\"text\":\" come from soul sand and Lost Souls.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4DEE5DD3B7F31445.title": "Artisan Relic",
  "quest.4DEE5DD3B7F31445.quest_subtitle": "Borrowed from the village smith. Indefinitely.",
  "quest.4DEE5DD3B7F31445.quest_desc": [
    "Armorer, toolsmith and weaponsmith chests in villages hold one 28% of the time, and Wandering Traders sometimes sell it for 18 emeralds. In the Clibano's enhancer slot it unlocks alloys; in the forge it cuts experience costs by a quarter."
  ],
  "quest.4A09E43F3C8A02F5.title": "Obsidiansteel",
  "quest.4A09E43F3C8A02F5.quest_subtitle": "Iron that learned patience.",
  "quest.4A09E43F3C8A02F5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"With the Artisan Relic in the enhancer slot, raw iron in one input and obsidian in the other come out as an \"},{\"text\":\"Obsidiansteel Ingot\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"forbidden_arcanus:obsidiansteel_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Draco Arcanus armor, Dark Nether Stars, Corrupti Dust and Obsidian Skulls all take it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1441F80228D80C07.title": "Obsidian Skull",
  "quest.1441F80228D80C07.quest_subtitle": "Fireproof, with an expiry date.",
  "quest.1441F80228D80C07.quest_desc": [
    "Eight Obsidiansteel Ingots around a skeleton skull. Worn on your head it grants Fire Resistance, but every 8 to 13 seconds you spend burning it cracks a stage: cracked, fragmented, fading, then a plain skeleton skull.",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Two Obsidiansteel Ingots mend it one stage.\"}]"
  ],
  "image.59C83714226331F8.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The forge floor\",\"color\":\"#A99BFF\"}]",
  "image.4261731A66AFE3B0.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Field notes\",\"color\":\"#A99BFF\"}]",
  "image.1C3D4D16ADFB83D1.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four essences\",\"color\":\"#A99BFF\"}]",
  "image.011E754964CB59C7.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Edelwood and scrap\",\"color\":\"#A99BFF\"}]",
  "image.5AB7D266F399332E.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Prisms and modifiers\",\"color\":\"#A99BFF\"}]",
  "image.3BBB8782FF7E9B09.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Toward eternity\",\"color\":\"#A99BFF\"}]",
  "image.3904C95DE4DA69E2.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Relics\",\"color\":\"#A99BFF\"}]",
  "image.3B9937958608DBCD.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Dragon scales\",\"color\":\"#A99BFF\"}]",
  "image.589DD03BDF284958.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Forbidden and Arcanus\",\"color\":\"#F3EEDF\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.1B21913D5E560F7C.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"forge pedestal ritual\",\"color\":\"#C9BEFF\",\"font\":\"minecraft:alt\"}]",
  "image.7CDC0DD8304F18B9.title": "Back to the Sun of Heliodor",
  "image.1B5DCF82A624AB58.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Clibano\",\"color\":\"#A99BFF\"}]",
  "chapter.7A8CF776A4A9F342.title": "Mahou Tsukai",
  "chapter.7A8CF776A4A9F342.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Blood circles, powdered catalysts, scrolls, the Fae and Caliburn."
  ],
  "quest.0FA522C681794545.title": "Circles drawn in blood",
  "quest.0FA522C681794545.quest_desc": [
    "Draw circles in your own blood, grind gems and metals into catalysts and put three on a circle to make a spell: one that stays on the floor, or a scroll. No machines, no tiers; mana grows with use.",
    "",
    "Bring bandages."
  ],
  "quest.595636BCD5A9064E.title": "Knowledge Compendium",
  "quest.595636BCD5A9064E.quest_desc": [
    "Red dye, paper and leather. It lists every spell by category, with its cost and whether it needs a cloth. EMI shows each spell's circle and scroll recipe: search the spell's name to see its three catalysts."
  ],
  "quest.0859CF3B84289FA9.title": "First blood",
  "quest.0859CF3B84289FA9.quest_desc": [
    "Take some damage and right away press Draw Mahoujin (Alt+M here): a blood circle appears and a mana bar shows on screen. Rather not jump off things? The Dagger hurts you on purpose.",
    "",
    "The first cut is the deepest. The first voluntary one."
  ],
  "quest.5CDFF2165D9D638C.title": "Mana is a muscle",
  "quest.5CDFF2165D9D638C.quest_desc": [
    "Max mana grows as you spend it. It regenerates slowly, faster on a full stomach, and sleep restores a big chunk: sleep often. Standing near a leyline or leypoint speeds regen further.",
    "",
    "The only gym where naps count as training."
  ],
  "quest.44720A1D5EEEF884.title": "Powdered catalysts",
  "quest.44720A1D5EEEF884.quest_desc": [
    "A Hammer crushes one powder per catalyst; a Mortar and Pestle, two. One per school: iron (Boundaries), ender pearl (Displacement), diamond (Projection), emerald (Exchange), gold (Mystic), quartz (Intelligence), eye of ender (Mystic Eyes)."
  ],
  "quest.4C1CB94C2C87E21C.title": "The mortar pays for itself",
  "quest.4C1CB94C2C87E21C.quest_desc": [
    "Four diamonds, and from then on every catalyst you crush gives double, diamonds and emeralds included. If you'll cast more than a handful of spells, build it early.",
    "",
    "The best investment advice you'll get in this pack."
  ],
  "quest.6592F31DF7E45E78.title": "Circle or scroll",
  "quest.6592F31DF7E45E78.quest_desc": [
    "A spell takes mana, a blood circle and three powders right-clicked onto it. Lay a Spell Cloth first and draw on top, and it comes out as a portable scroll; without the cloth, it stays as a circle on the floor. The book says which spells need cloth."
  ],
  "quest.1A487DE58D0BAD17.title": "Projection and Strengthening",
  "quest.1A487DE58D0BAD17.quest_desc": [
    "Projection copies the tool or weapon you look at, with limited durability. Strengthening makes your first hotbar item briefly unbreakable, stronger and faster. Strengthened items unlock several legendary weapons.",
    "",
    "A sword out of thin air. Literally."
  ],
  "quest.2980EF2C6FEB6D5B.title": "Boundaries",
  "quest.2980EF2C6FEB6D5B.quest_desc": [
    "Circles that act on the area around them and drain mana at a fixed rate: Alarm, Gravity, Drain Life and more. Right-click toggles them, redstone inverts them, and a comparator reads their state (the Alarm gives 15 when it detects something)."
  ],
  "quest.555113334FA34893.title": "Attuned gems",
  "quest.555113334FA34893.quest_desc": [
    "An Attuner (gold and lapis) plus a diamond or an emerald makes an Attuned Gem. Right-click with it in hand to store mana; spells draw from any attuned gem you carry. A spare tank for long casts, before you have circuits."
  ],
  "quest.6E69EB7DC94BE8E5.title": "Leylines and the Fae",
  "quest.6E69EB7DC94BE8E5.quest_desc": [
    "Fay Sight reveals leylines and the Fae. Leylines raise mana regen and even boost an elytra flying along them. The Fae drop Fae Essence, which places circles anyone can use: ideal for automating scrolls.",
    "",
    "The world has veins. Now you can see them."
  ],
  "quest.6713F22CD30C7F75.title": "Mana Circuits",
  "quest.6713F22CD30C7F75.quest_desc": [
    "A Mana Circuit stores mana you can draw on nearby. The first to right-click owns it: right-click deposits, sneak toggles, Fae Essence shares it. The Magitech version skips the Fae. Kodoku worms and written works can feed circuits."
  ],
  "quest.52951C5E08145F8D.title": "The Mystic Code",
  "quest.52951C5E08145F8D.quest_desc": [
    "It holds three stacks of scrolls: sneak-right-click opens it, its key switches scrolls, right-click casts. The First Sorcery variant wears out but reuses scrolls instead of burning them.",
    "",
    "A wizard's holster."
  ],
  "quest.42CD70A6B27D9F8B.title": "Swaps, scrying, familiars",
  "quest.42CD70A6B27D9F8B.quest_desc": [
    "Equivalent Displacement circles pair up anywhere, even across dimensions, and swap only when both have something on top. Summon Familiar sends a scout that reports players, mobs and blocks and keeps its area loaded; hand it a block to hunt just that."
  ],
  "quest.6CBDD65A4899ED9C.title": "Kodoku worms",
  "quest.6CBDD65A4899ED9C.quest_desc": [
    "It feeds on conflict: each time a monster kills something, its value grows by one plus the victim's. Put a hungry worm on a strong specimen, kill it, pick the worm back up. Burned near circuits it makes mana; carried, it shields you from sympathetic magic.",
    "",
    "The food chain, bottled."
  ],
  "quest.609BD579C2FEF1AF.title": "A sword from the lake",
  "quest.609BD579C2FEF1AF.quest_desc": [
    "The Power Consolidation circle grows a lake, mana per step. Once full, throw in an enchanted sword to receive Caliburn: its damage plus a bonus for enchantments, holier ones counting more. Undead flee it; a lance becomes Rhongomyniad.",
    "",
    "The lady of the lake takes swords, not requests."
  ],
  "quest.17D803A7819F2A32.title": "Weapons you earn",
  "quest.17D803A7819F2A32.quest_desc": [
    "Some weapons are feats, not recipes. Nobu appears when a strengthened bow hits an enemy 200 blocks away; Replica wants a block with a strengthened shield under stacked defensive spells. EMI shows each condition as a special recipe.",
    "",
    "Morgan's is cruel on purpose."
  ],
  "quest.60C225AB0B544AE1.title": "Big spells, big bills",
  "quest.60C225AB0B544AE1.quest_desc": [
    "Treasury Projection throws weapons from your inventory, bags and ender chest; Rho Aias bounces mobs and deletes projectiles. Late spells like these charge per use or per weapon: carry attuned gems or stay near circuits.",
    "",
    "No casting on credit."
  ],
  "quest.68924C9E1161B371.title": "Mahou keys",
  "quest.68924C9E1161B371.quest_desc": [
    "Draw Mahoujin is Alt+M here (plain M is a JourneyMap waypoint; Ctrl+M and Shift+M toggle magnets) and Selective Displacement is Ctrl+H. The Mystic Code, Nobu and settings keys keep their defaults. Nothing in Mahou Tsukai needs an Atlas component."
  ],
  "quest.5DE51A3BBD3C868B.title": "A true mahoutsukai",
  "quest.5DE51A3BBD3C868B.quest_desc": [
    "Mana trained by use, a mortar full of powders, circuits fed by the Fae, Caliburn in hand and a Mystic Code loaded. Keep experimenting and chase the book's secret hints.",
    "",
    "No tiers, no ceiling. Just you and a lot of blood."
  ],
  "chapter.1E6CA53296A6FFE4.title": "Malum",
  "chapter.1E6CA53296A6FFE4.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Scythes, spirit altars and totems: from a crude scythe to the Weeping Well."
  ],
  "quest.581C01A7948EB423.title": "Soulstone",
  "quest.581C01A7948EB423.quest_subtitle": "Boring rock, interesting afterlife.",
  "quest.581C01A7948EB423.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Its ore turns up all over the Overworld, from the bottom of the deepslate up to height 100. Each \"},{\"text\":\"Raw Soulstone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:raw_soulstone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" smelts into two \"},{\"text\":\"Refined Soulstone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:refined_soulstone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": the scythe, the altar, the Encyclopedia and every Soulstained Steel ingot start here.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0699DB3FC29CDC66.title": "The Crude Scythe",
  "quest.0699DB3FC29CDC66.quest_subtitle": "The harvest is not wheat.",
  "quest.0699DB3FC29CDC66.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three iron ingots, a \"},{\"text\":\"Refined Soulstone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:refined_soulstone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and two sticks. Whatever you kill with it shatters into spirit crystals that fly to you. It hits softer than a sword but sweeps wide, and its soulstone core is what reaches the soul.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.639E0711137A795A.title": "The primary arcana",
  "quest.639E0711137A795A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Every mob carries its own mix. \"},{\"text\":\"Sacred\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:sacred_spirit\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" comes from peaceful animals, \"},{\"text\":\"Wicked\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:wicked_spirit\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" from zombies, pillagers and other hostiles, \"},{\"text\":\"Arcane\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:arcane_spirit\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" from witches and skeletons. One witch alone drops two Wicked and two Arcane.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Iron's Spellbooks damage counts as soul damage here: a spell kill drops spirits the same as a scythe kill.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.26F8A7D4DA540396.title": "Runewood",
  "quest.26F8A7D4DA540396.quest_subtitle": "Orange leaves, loud magic.",
  "quest.26F8A7D4DA540396.quest_desc": [
    "Look for orange-yellow leaves in plains, hills and mountains; they are rarer in forests. Snowy biomes grow an azure variant that drops the same logs. Sixteen logs is a fair first haul: the altar, its pedestals and the first totem all eat runewood."
  ],
  "quest.5B96C1F2F831C4BE.title": "The Spirit Altar",
  "quest.5B96C1F2F831C4BE.quest_subtitle": "Slow on purpose. The soul doesn't rush.",
  "quest.5B96C1F2F831C4BE.quest_desc": [
    "Runewood planks, two gold ingots and a Refined Soulstone. Put the item to infuse on the altar together with its spirits; extra ingredients go on Runewood pedestals or stands within four blocks, and the altar pulls them in one by one while the spirits flow."
  ],
  "quest.0F75CFDAF88DDB4D.title": "First infusion: Hex Ash",
  "quest.0F75CFDAF88DDB4D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Gunpowder on the altar with one Arcane Spirit. \"},{\"text\":\"Hex Ash\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:hex_ash\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" turns up everywhere later: totem bases, the crucible, the impetus, the scythe upgrade. Make a stack while you learn the altar's pace.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6B389E759EB3AD28.title": "Hallowed Gold",
  "quest.6B389E759EB3AD28.quest_subtitle": "Gold, but with better manners.",
  "quest.6B389E759EB3AD28.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A gold ingot with two Sacred and one Arcane, plus four quartz on the pedestals. Nether quartz works, and so does \"},{\"text\":\"Natural Quartz\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:natural_quartz\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" from Malum's deep geodes. Arcana glide through the metal, which is why jars, obelisks and trinkets are built on it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5168CEF9792AB068.title": "Soulstained Steel",
  "quest.5168CEF9792AB068.quest_subtitle": "Steel that hits the soul, not the armor.",
  "quest.5168CEF9792AB068.quest_desc": [
    "An iron ingot with three Wicked, one Earthen and one Arcane, and four Refined Soulstone on the pedestals. Whatever you forge from it strikes the soul directly, so every Soulstained tool and weapon reaps spirits.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"One zombie and one witch drop enough spirits for one ingot. The act IV \"},{\"text\":\"containment seal\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"429BA86EC20C7A84\"}},{\"text\":\" takes two.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.59C7038E69692155.title": "The elemental arcana",
  "quest.59C7038E69692155.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Earthen\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:earthen_spirit\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" comes from zombies, cows and iron golems; \"},{\"text\":\"Infernal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:infernal_spirit\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" from creepers, blazes and most of the Nether; \"},{\"text\":\"Aerial\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:aerial_spirit\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" from spiders, bats and anything fast; \"},{\"text\":\"Aqueous\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:aqueous_spirit\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" from drowned, squid and fish. The crucible, the calx and every totem want them.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.029C950DD37077D3.title": "Tainted and Twisted Rock",
  "quest.029C950DD37077D3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Sixteen cobblestone with one Sacred and one Arcane: sixteen \"},{\"text\":\"Tainted Rock\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:tainted_rock\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", which dissipates nearby magic. Swap the Sacred for a Wicked and you get \"},{\"text\":\"Twisted Rock\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:twisted_rock\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", which pushes magic away. The crucible takes eight of each.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.450D7029194842F9.title": "Calx and flesh",
  "quest.450D7029194842F9.quest_subtitle": "Unfit for human consumption. Keep it anyway.",
  "quest.450D7029194842F9.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four clay balls with two Arcane, two Earthen and two Aqueous give four \"},{\"text\":\"Alchemical Calx\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:alchemical_calx\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", the base of every impetus and crucible augment. Four rotten flesh with two Sacred and two Wicked give \"},{\"text\":\"Living Flesh\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:living_flesh\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for the healing trinkets.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.79FCE5C4DDFC5420.title": "The Alchemical Impetus",
  "quest.79FCE5C4DDFC5420.quest_desc": [
    "Four calx with four Refined Soulstone and two Hex Ash, fed four Arcane and four Earthen. It is the crucible's substrate: every focusing cycle costs it durability, and at zero it fractures."
  ],
  "quest.3A6925EFDA62BD58.title": "The Spirit Crucible",
  "quest.3A6925EFDA62BD58.quest_subtitle": "Slow, but it beats mining.",
  "quest.3A6925EFDA62BD58.quest_desc": [
    "A furnace on the altar with two Hex Ash, eight of each rock, eight Infernal and eight Aqueous. Load an impetus and spirits and it focuses them into matter, a little at a time.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"One Arcane gives eight redstone, one Infernal eight glowstone dust, one Earthen eight gunpowder. Two Arcane with two Earthen, Aerial or Aqueous give four quartz, amethyst shards or prismarine shards; with two Infernal, four \"},{\"text\":\"Blazing Quartz\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:blazing_quartz\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7DB3153950957ACD.title": "Ether",
  "quest.7DB3153950957ACD.quest_subtitle": "A flame that never asks for fuel.",
  "quest.7DB3153950957ACD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Blazing Quartz\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:blazing_quartz\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" comes from Nether ore or from the crucible. Four glowstone dust and one Blazing Quartz, with two Infernal and one Arcane, give two \"},{\"text\":\"Ether\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:ether\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": a cold flame you can dye. It crafts torches and braziers, goes into the catalyzer and lights the Soulbinding Brazier.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Ether with a prismarine crystal, Arcane Charcoal and two Aqueous becomes \"},{\"text\":\"Iridescent Ether\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:iridescent_ether\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", which takes a second colour. Its first colour is then locked.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1E17E6CE323B2651.title": "The Eldritch spirit",
  "quest.1E17E6CE323B2651.quest_subtitle": "The last principle, found in the strangest mobs.",
  "quest.1E17E6CE323B2651.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Endermen drop three \"},{\"text\":\"Eldritch\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:eldritch_spirit\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" each; evokers, ravagers, shulkers and elder guardians carry some too. It is the pair of raw arcana, the impulse of endings, and every totem base and every greater rite needs it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0292DE93381C1030.title": "The Totem Base",
  "quest.0292DE93381C1030.quest_subtitle": "Carve, stack, wait.",
  "quest.0292DE93381C1030.quest_desc": [
    "Four Runewood logs, six planks and two Hex Ash, with two each of Aerial, Aqueous, Earthen, Infernal and Eldritch, make four bases. Stack engraved logs on one in the right order and the totem performs a spirit rite on what surrounds it."
  ],
  "task.676A998FE5A5CA62.title": "Look at an engraved Runewood pole",
  "quest.450BE31FCA508D09.title": "The first rite",
  "quest.450BE31FCA508D09.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Use a spirit on a Runewood Log placed in the world to engrave it; an axe scrapes a wrong rune back off. Arcane right on the base, then two Sacred above it: the \"},{\"text\":\"Rite of Healing\",\"color\":\"#E07BFF\"},{\"text\":\" mends two hearts on every creature nearby.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.33FC81BAF7B5B870.title": "Soulwood",
  "quest.33FC81BAF7B5B870.quest_subtitle": "It starts as one tree. It never ends as one tree.",
  "quest.33FC81BAF7B5B870.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Five Arcane runes on a Runewood base run the Undirected Rite: it scars the totem into Soulwood and turns the ground around it into blight. Run it far from anything you care about, then break the base for a \"},{\"text\":\"Soulwood Totem Base\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:soulwood_totem_base\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.34EA22986567F0EE.title": "Cthonic Gold",
  "quest.34EA22986567F0EE.quest_subtitle": "Pyrite's rich cousin.",
  "quest.34EA22986567F0EE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A rare ore deep in the deepslate, between heights -48 and 0, rooted in gold veins. Each ore drops three or four fragments, and eight fragments make one \"},{\"text\":\"Cthonic Gold\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:cthonic_gold\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Metal impetuses, the Soulbinding Brazier and the Belt of the Prospector need it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3542C9C7C35584B7.title": "The Soulbinding Brazier",
  "quest.3542C9C7C35584B7.quest_subtitle": "Power for a price, signed in blood.",
  "quest.3542C9C7C35584B7.quest_desc": [
    "Hallowed Gold, Cthonic Gold, Runewood planks and Tainted Rock. Load a geas's central item, extras and spirits into it, light it with Ether, then use it to offer your blood: the oath binds to your soul. A soul holds two geasa at most.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "The Pact of the Reaper takes twelve Refined Soulstone, four Grim Talc and four Hex Ash, with sixteen Wicked, Aerial and Infernal: your scythe strikes sometimes follow up with extra cuts, while weapons you forswore deal a tenth of their damage and wear out."
  ],
  "task.76E043F6A9492B93.title": "Find the Weeping Well",
  "quest.2EE87396150D02FA.title": "The Weeping Well",
  "quest.2EE87396150D02FA.quest_subtitle": "Somebody walled this in on purpose.",
  "quest.2EE87396150D02FA.quest_desc": [
    "An old structure buried under the Overworld: Tainted Rock walls around a pool that is neither liquid nor solid. Arcane materials tug at your pockets near it. Throw them in and the Well spits each one back out, changed."
  ],
  "quest.7A8A6543C926E779.title": "What the Well gives back",
  "quest.7A8A6543C926E779.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Refined Soulstone comes back as \"},{\"text\":\"Null Slate\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:null_slate\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", Hex Ash as \"},{\"text\":\"Void Salts\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:void_salts\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", Brilliance as \"},{\"text\":\"Mnemonic Fragments\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:mnemonic_fragment\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and blaze powder as \"},{\"text\":\"Auric Embers\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:auric_embers\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Most raw ores come back as Raw Soulstone.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Everything the Well rejects flies out due south. Stand on the north side, or build your catcher to the south.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.293935903406C9F7.title": "A black crystal",
  "quest.293935903406C9F7.quest_subtitle": "Ethics committee: still pending.",
  "quest.293935903406C9F7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Step into the Well yourself. It throws you back out for two hearts of damage, and the first time a black spirit crystal comes out with you: \"},{\"text\":\"Umbral\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:umbral_spirit\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", the absence of arcana. Until you do, Malum keeps the void's items out of JEI and the creative tabs.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4B5FE76D7A2B1A33.title": "The Complete Design",
  "quest.4B5FE76D7A2B1A33.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Throw a block of iron into the Well for an \"},{\"text\":\"Anomalous Design\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:anomalous_design\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". On the altar with four of each of the eight spirits, it becomes the \"},{\"text\":\"Complete Design\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:complete_design\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2D93ECBE7A5490E5.title": "Fused Consciousness",
  "quest.2D93ECBE7A5490E5.quest_subtitle": "The blueprint of everything, pocket-sized.",
  "quest.2D93ECBE7A5490E5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Give the Complete Design back to the Well. What returns is a \"},{\"text\":\"Fused Consciousness\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:fused_consciousness\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": the eight arcana and the void in one thought. The Belt of the Limitless, the Sundering Anchor, Unwinding Chaos and the Stellar Mechanism are built on it.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "The altar, the crucible, the totems and the Well have all answered you. What remains of Malum is built from this thought."
  ],
  "quest.2CB3D5EEC792BEB2.title": "Encyclopedia Arcana",
  "quest.2CB3D5EEC792BEB2.quest_desc": [
    "A book and a Refined Soulstone. Malum's guide reads like a researcher's notebook, and every entry shows its infusion with the spirits and extra items it needs.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"With Malum's default settings, one of the first undead you kill drops a copy anyway.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.20A10730D14A955F.title": "Arcane spirits for the common store",
  "quest.20A10730D14A955F.quest_subtitle": "Every lens wants two.",
  "quest.20A10730D14A955F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Sixteen \"},{\"text\":\"Arcane Spirits\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:arcane_spirit\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for the common store, once a day. Each act IV spectral lens takes two, and Hex Ash, rocks and rites burn through the rest.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3BCF26E098F0AE8C.title": "What runewood gives",
  "quest.3BCF26E098F0AE8C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Some runewood logs ooze sap: strip one with an axe and use a glass bottle on it for \"},{\"text\":\"Runic Sap\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:runic_sap\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a healing drink that also crafts into sapballs, which stand in for slimeballs in most recipes. Smelted runewood gives \"},{\"text\":\"Arcane Charcoal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:arcane_charcoal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", which burns longer than charcoal.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.44280DA3558E5C39.title": "Esoteric reaping",
  "quest.44280DA3558E5C39.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A soul shattered by the scythe changes what the body drops. Zombies leave \"},{\"text\":\"Rotting Essence\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:rotting_essence\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", skeletons \"},{\"text\":\"Grim Talc\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:grim_talc\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", phantoms and ghasts \"},{\"text\":\"Astral Weave\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:astral_weave\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", endermen \"},{\"text\":\"Warp Flux\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:warp_flux\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", and a breeze leaves a Wind Nucleus.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Grim Talc crafts into six bone meal, and eight bones around one make a skeleton skull.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.78C17A1C11002516.title": "Enchant the scythe",
  "quest.78C17A1C11002516.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Spirit Plunder reaps extra spirits at the cost of some durability. Rebound lets you throw the scythe, Ascension launches you upward in a cutting gust, and the two don't mix. Haunted adds magic damage and Animated attack speed.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1B30DDEA4B287B48.title": "Recipes the pack repaired",
  "quest.1B30DDEA4B287B48.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Create's millstone grinds Grim Talc into six bone meal, with a chance of yellow dye and of four more bone meal; the pack fixed that recipe so it loads. Malum's repairs for The Undergarden's gear stay off: they name their spirits in a format this version rejects.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6C9C6969DFA3029C.title": "Soulwoven Silk",
  "quest.6C9C6969DFA3029C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two wool and two string with three Aerial and three Earthen weave four \"},{\"text\":\"Soulwoven Silk\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:soulwoven_silk\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". The cloth insulates against arcana, so pouches, banners, Soulhunter robes and the Runic Workbench are made of it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4FB4904FC059FA41.title": "Pouches for the harvest",
  "quest.4FB4904FC059FA41.quest_subtitle": "It bites. Only what you told it to.",
  "quest.4FB4904FC059FA41.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"String over Soulwoven Silk sews a \"},{\"text\":\"Soulwoven Pouch\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:soulwoven_pouch\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" that snaps up every spirit you collect. On the altar with twelve Rotting Essence and eight Grim Talc it grows teeth: the \"},{\"text\":\"Ravenous Pouch\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:ravenous_pouch\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" grabs any item that matches what it already holds.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5DB4B6324C23E1DD.title": "Obelisks",
  "quest.5DB4B6324C23E1DD.quest_subtitle": "Bookshelves, but occult.",
  "quest.5DB4B6324C23E1DD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two Runewood planks and two Hallowed Gold, with sixteen Aerial and eight Sacred: each \"},{\"text\":\"Runewood Obelisk\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:runewood_obelisk\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" near the altar adds a quarter to its speed, up to four. Socket Raw Brilliance instead and the \"},{\"text\":\"Brilliant Obelisk\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:brilliant_obelisk\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" counts as five bookshelves.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Raw Brilliance comes from small pockets of Brilliant Stone below height 40. Smelted, it becomes refined Brilliance, solid experience you can bottle."
  ],
  "quest.28681B052594E15E.title": "Spirit Jars",
  "quest.28681B052594E15E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Hallowed Gold over a glass block. Each \"},{\"text\":\"Spirit Jar\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:spirit_jar\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" holds a near-infinite amount of one spirit type, so a row of eight by the altar ends the inventory juggling.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6BA85AC9B81751C1.title": "The Soulstained Scythe",
  "quest.6BA85AC9B81751C1.quest_desc": [
    "Put the Crude Scythe on the altar with four Soulstained Steel, two Hex Ash and four Refined Soulstone, fed sixteen Earthen, eight Wicked and eight Arcane. Same wide sweep, far more bite."
  ],
  "quest.1DD9966736E00C7B.title": "Ring of Esoteric Spoils",
  "quest.1DD9966736E00C7B.quest_subtitle": "Where the extra comes from, nobody asks.",
  "quest.1DD9966736E00C7B.quest_desc": [
    "An Ornate Ring, Soulstained Steel on leather, goes on the altar with eight Refined Soulstone and eight each of Wicked, Arcane and Eldritch. Every soul you shatter then gives up one extra spirit."
  ],
  "quest.476C27099A46B315.title": "Necklace of the Narrow Edge",
  "quest.476C27099A46B315.quest_desc": [
    "An Ornate Necklace with a block and two ingots of iron, fed sixteen Wicked, sixteen Earthen and eight Eldritch. It trades the scythe's sweep for a strong single-target hit. Wind Nuclei and wind charges make the rings that reshape Rebound and Ascension."
  ],
  "quest.0DC886308A399ADF.title": "Soulstained armor",
  "quest.0DC886308A399ADF.quest_desc": [
    "Each piece is its iron counterpart on the altar with six Soulstained Plating, four Refined Soulstone and eight Twisted Rock. The set carries Soul Ward, a recharging barrier: while it holds, magic damage drops by nine tenths and physical damage by three tenths.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The Ring of Manaweaving, a Gilded Ring with six plating and four Refined Soulstone, speeds Soul Ward's recovery every time you collect a spirit.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.71D3D1E7DA80F940.title": "Soulhunter armor",
  "quest.71D3D1E7DA80F940.quest_subtitle": "Leather with opinions about magic.",
  "quest.71D3D1E7DA80F940.quest_desc": [
    "Leather armor on the altar with Soulwoven Silk, Refined Soulstone and more leather, fed Aerial and Earthen. It guards about as well as leather but amplifies your arcane power, and with Iron's Spellbooks installed it adds spell power too."
  ],
  "quest.5E5D469EB7EAF98D.title": "Rings of the harvest",
  "quest.5E5D469EB7EAF98D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Gilded Ring\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:gilded_ring\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" is Hallowed Gold on leather. On the altar with four Living Flesh, four calx and a ghast tear, fed Sacred and Arcane, it becomes the \"},{\"text\":\"Ring of Curative Talent\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:ring_of_curative_talent\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": every spirit you pick up heals you a little.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Before any effect, Hallowed Gold trinkets add armor and Soulstained Steel ones add toughness.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7CE451A92CFB8144.title": "The Runic Workbench",
  "quest.7CE451A92CFB8144.quest_desc": [
    "A Runewood pedestal on the altar with four Runewood planks, four Soulwoven Silk and two Hallowed Gold, fed sixteen Sacred, Arcane and Aqueous. It carves runes from four base blocks and sixteen or thirty-two spirits."
  ],
  "quest.7B32469A75343012.title": "Brooches and runes",
  "quest.7B32469A75343012.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Runes need slots that only brooches open. The \"},{\"text\":\"Runic Brooch\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:runic_brooch\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" trades ring space for two rune slots, one per palm. Four Tainted Rock and sixteen Arcane carve the \"},{\"text\":\"Rune of Reinforcement\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:rune_of_reinforcement\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", which strengthens Soul Ward.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "You wear one brooch at a time: the Glass Brooch opens its two rune slots with max health instead of ring space. Wooden runes, carved from planks with thirty-two spirits, carry a totem rite's aura at half strength."
  ],
  "quest.3CB2F87E38786E69.title": "The Repair Pylon",
  "quest.3CB2F87E38786E69.quest_desc": [
    "A Tainted Rock pedestal with eight of each rock, fed sixteen Sacred, Aerial, Aqueous and Infernal. Load it with spirits and repair material and it mends a damaged item on a nearby pedestal, stand or crucible without experience: about half its durability, three quarters for spirit gear.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "The pack fixed Malum's four chalk repairs for Occultism: white, yellow, purple and red chalk come back to full for eight Arcane and, in that order, burnt otherstone, gold dust, two obsidian dust or Afrit essence."
  ],
  "quest.40C549A72E38B844.title": "Fractured, not finished",
  "quest.40C549A72E38B844.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A fractured impetus goes back to full on the Repair Pylon: two calx, four Arcane and four Earthen for the alchemical one; two Cthonic Gold fragments, eight Aqueous and eight Infernal for a metal one.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.548DF607820F8C9B.title": "Metal nodes",
  "quest.548DF607820F8C9B.quest_subtitle": "Mining, but make it alchemy.",
  "quest.548DF607820F8C9B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An impetus with four gunpowder, one Cthonic Gold and six iron ingots, fed eight Earthen, Infernal and Aqueous, becomes an \"},{\"text\":\"Iron Impetus\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:iron_impetus\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Each crucible cycle then gives three \"},{\"text\":\"Iron Nodes\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:iron_node\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", and each node smelts into six nuggets.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "The same recipe works for gold, copper, lead, silver, tin, nickel, zinc, osmium, uranium and aluminum, the metals this pack has ingots for. Cobalt's impetus does not load here."
  ],
  "quest.7D1F27E89D571CA2.title": "Tuning the crucible",
  "quest.7D1F27E89D571CA2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Augments go in a catalyzer, or up to four in the crucible itself. The \"},{\"text\":\"Accelerating Inlay\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:accelerating_inlay\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (calx, Astral Weave and soulstone) speeds focusing with no drawback. A \"},{\"text\":\"Tuning Fork\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:tuning_fork\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" shows every attribute and lets you raise one at the cost of the others.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "The Prismatic Focus Lens lowers instability, the Mending Diffuser may mend the impetus after each cycle, and the Shielding Apparatus can absorb the damage outright, at the cost of some speed."
  ],
  "quest.7967FDD815A59827.title": "The Spirit Catalyzer",
  "quest.7967FDD815A59827.quest_desc": [
    "A Twisted Rock pedestal with four of each rock and one Ether, fed eight Infernal and eight Aerial. Each fueled catalyzer near a crucible speeds focusing, up to eight of them, but instability grows with each one and can wear the impetus faster."
  ],
  "quest.5C9C0AC8B5BF7B90.title": "Reading a totem",
  "quest.5C9C0AC8B5BF7B90.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Runes count upward from the base. A lesser rite is Arcane plus two of one spirit; a greater rite puts Eldritch first, then Arcane, then two of the spirit. A Soulwood base turns every rite into a different one.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"On Runewood, the lesser and greater rites are: Sacred, \"},{\"text\":\"Healing\",\"color\":\"#E07BFF\"},{\"text\":\" and \"},{\"text\":\"Nurturing\",\"color\":\"#E07BFF\"},{\"text\":\"; Wicked, \"},{\"text\":\"Harming\",\"color\":\"#E07BFF\"},{\"text\":\" and \"},{\"text\":\"Culling\",\"color\":\"#E07BFF\"},{\"text\":\"; Earthen, \"},{\"text\":\"Stone Ward\",\"color\":\"#E07BFF\"},{\"text\":\" and \"},{\"text\":\"Creation\",\"color\":\"#E07BFF\"},{\"text\":\"; Infernal, \"},{\"text\":\"Burning Fervor\",\"color\":\"#E07BFF\"},{\"text\":\" and \"},{\"text\":\"Smelting\",\"color\":\"#E07BFF\"},{\"text\":\"; Aerial, \"},{\"text\":\"Howling Gale\",\"color\":\"#E07BFF\"},{\"text\":\" and \"},{\"text\":\"Gravity\",\"color\":\"#E07BFF\"},{\"text\":\"; Aqueous, \"},{\"text\":\"Flowing Grasp\",\"color\":\"#E07BFF\"},{\"text\":\" and \"},{\"text\":\"Soaking\",\"color\":\"#E07BFF\"},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.102A3EB7D226F91E.title": "The Totemic Staff",
  "quest.102A3EB7D226F91E.quest_desc": [
    "A Runewood plank on top of two sticks. Holding it shows the area each totem affects, and using it on an engraved rune lights the rune up without starting a rite."
  ],
  "quest.4B7AAE82103542F0.title": "The Arcana Pylon",
  "quest.4B7AAE82103542F0.quest_desc": [
    "A Runewood Obelisk with eight Refined Soulstone, four Hex Ash and two Soulwood planks, fed eight Aerial, Aqueous, Earthen and Infernal. Fed Arcane, each pylon speeds a nearby altar by half, up to four; fed an elemental spirit, it strengthens matching rite and rune auras."
  ],
  "quest.2FE7E7D4223AABFC.title": "Rite Anchors",
  "quest.2FE7E7D4223AABFC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Greater rites send out a bound locus that wanders at four blocks per second. A \"},{\"text\":\"Rite Anchor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:rite_anchor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" socketed with a spirit steers any locus that passes: Arcane turns it, Aerial doubles its speed, Infernal its distance, Earthen its impact and Aqueous its potency.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Anchors stop working while powered by redstone, and a locus crossing Tainted Rock does nothing and does not age."
  ],
  "quest.1E9A894EF7F3BD45.title": "Waveform totems",
  "quest.1E9A894EF7F3BD45.quest_desc": [
    "Copper blocks, redstone, Runewood and Ether make four Waveform Totem Bases. They hold the rite's energy until a redstone pulse fires it; only the pulse's rising edge counts, and an observer shows when the rite is ready.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "The same copper and Ether make four spirit diodes that bend redstone signals, one per element, and the Artificer's Claw tunes their delays."
  ],
  "quest.1E5BF251F3080AFD.title": "Blight: keep it fenced",
  "quest.1E5BF251F3080AFD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Blight is random matter the rite left behind, not a poison. It never spreads alone, but spirits or bone meal make it echo outward. Break blighted earth without silk touch for \"},{\"text\":\"Blighted Gunk\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:blighted_gunk\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Blightroot and Blightpearl grow on it with no light or water. They are useless, and they grow anyway."
  ],
  "quest.0BEEFC25FD2F172A.title": "The Unchained Rite",
  "quest.0BEEFC25FD2F172A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Five Arcane runes on a Soulwood base run the Unchained Rite: its locus travels through blight and transmutes the block sitting on top. Runewood becomes Soulwood, so a Runewood Sapling set on blight comes back as a \"},{\"text\":\"Soulwood Sapling\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:soulwood_sapling\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Stone steps down to cobblestone, gravel, sand and finally blight; dirt goes to rooted dirt, grass and moss. \"},{\"text\":\"Every step ends in more blight\",\"color\":\"#FF8C7A\"},{\"text\":\", but the locus dies where the blight ends, so its edge is also the rite's fence.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.51FCBE11068D6261.title": "A plant made of crystal",
  "quest.51FCBE11068D6261.quest_subtitle": "Pretty. Useless. Grows anyway.",
  "quest.51FCBE11068D6261.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"You broke a \"},{\"text\":\"Strange Crystal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:strange_crystal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" off Scarstone with silk touch. About one blight spread in ten carves a Scarstone deposit, and the crystal grows on it like a plant. The Encyclopedia still hasn't found a use for it.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.41D35F556FDC14CA.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.175F98B754DE7A98.title": "Cursed Sap",
  "quest.175F98B754DE7A98.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Soulwood logs ooze sap far more often than Runewood ones. Bottled the same way, \"},{\"text\":\"Cursed Sap\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:cursed_sap\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" doesn't heal: it raises your attack strength and adds damage resistance.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7AC60A64A2A2953C.title": "Soulwood rites",
  "quest.7AC60A64A2A2953C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"On a Soulwood base the same runes do something else: Healing becomes \"},{\"text\":\"Nourishment\",\"color\":\"#E07BFF\"},{\"text\":\", Stone Ward becomes \"},{\"text\":\"Oaken Might\",\"color\":\"#E07BFF\"},{\"text\":\", Burning Fervor becomes \"},{\"text\":\"Fiery Embrace\",\"color\":\"#E07BFF\"},{\"text\":\", Smelting becomes \"},{\"text\":\"Quickening\",\"color\":\"#E07BFF\"},{\"text\":\" for furnaces, and Nurturing becomes \"},{\"text\":\"Lust\",\"color\":\"#E07BFF\"},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.787F9BFBCEB05F1F.title": "Belt of the Prospector",
  "quest.787F9BFBCEB05F1F.quest_subtitle": "Greed, with a fortune enchantment.",
  "quest.787F9BFBCEB05F1F.quest_desc": [
    "A Gilded Belt with one Cthonic Gold and four each of raw gold, iron and copper, fed thirty-two Earthen and Infernal and sixteen Arcane. Mining precious ore grants Avarice, a chance at an extra Fortune level, and your explosions dig with Fortune III."
  ],
  "quest.5D52A7B8BD1F1247.title": "Paracausal Flame",
  "quest.5D52A7B8BD1F1247.quest_desc": [
    "Ether on the altar with eight Hex Ash, four Warp Flux and two crying obsidian, fed eight Arcane and eight Eldritch. Light the brazier with it instead of Ether and the geas you assemble burns away instead of binding."
  ],
  "quest.32059C1B4AFDCD51.title": "Tyrving",
  "quest.32059C1B4AFDCD51.quest_subtitle": "No sweep, all grudge.",
  "quest.32059C1B4AFDCD51.quest_desc": [
    "A Soulstained sword with sixteen Twisted Rock, eight Soulwood planks and a Paracausal Flame. Each hit adds magic damage that grows with the target's soul and snaps back a moment later. It cannot sweep, and it repairs with obsidian."
  ],
  "quest.1B5120631CA9DFB2.title": "The Ritual Plinth",
  "quest.1B5120631CA9DFB2.quest_desc": [
    "Malum 1.8.2 registers a Ritual Plinth but gives it no recipe and no rituals; its Encyclopedia page only says the future holds secrets. Bound, lasting magic lives in the Soulbinding Brazier."
  ],
  "quest.17A359645F8F7874.title": "Encyclopedia Esoterica",
  "quest.17A359645F8F7874.quest_desc": [
    "Throw your Encyclopedia Arcana into the Well. It comes back as the Esoterica, the notebook of the void: material studies, the black crystal and everything made from them."
  ],
  "quest.281FF55A316F6646.title": "Checkerboard, recharged",
  "quest.281FF55A316F6646.quest_subtitle": "Works even while bent.",
  "quest.281FF55A316F6646.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"You crafted The Device, a checkerboard of Twisted and Tainted Rock, and fed it to the Well. It came back as \"},{\"text\":\"The Vessel\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:the_vessel\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". The Encyclopedia's only comment on the matter is a joke.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.2A475781F517DA10.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.3FFCA6FAF2719604.title": "Dressed for the void",
  "quest.3FFCA6FAF2719604.quest_subtitle": "Formal wear for an informal abyss.",
  "quest.3FFCA6FAF2719604.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"You threw black wool into the Weeping Well and it came back as a \"},{\"text\":\"Tophat\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:tophat\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Nothing in either Encyclopedia explains why. Wear it anyway.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.01F35DBE91DAFF72.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.09C7B1D66513E14F.title": "Voidish runes",
  "quest.09C7B1D66513E14F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Carve runes on Null Slate instead of Tainted Rock and they come out warped: four slate and sixteen of a spirit each. Sacred gives the \"},{\"text\":\"Rune of Bolstering\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:rune_of_bolstering\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", extra health past full; Arcane gives Spell Mastery, staves charging twice as fast.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.069350E465C17D20.title": "The Mnemonic Hex Staff",
  "quest.069350E465C17D20.quest_desc": [
    "A Totemic Staff with eight Mnemonic Fragments, four Soulstained Steel and two Soulwood planks, fed sixteen Wicked, Aerial, Aqueous and Eldritch. Using it throws balls of liquid Wicked; the charge refills from your soul and is shared by all your staves.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Two Malignant Pewter and eight Void Salts turn it into the Erosion Scepter, whose bolts strip a tenth of the target's magic with every hit."
  ],
  "quest.0506EE5F0EA759DE.title": "Overclocked rings",
  "quest.0506EE5F0EA759DE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Sixteen Null Slate and eight Void Salts push the Ring of Curative Talent into the \"},{\"text\":\"Ring of Growing Flesh\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:ring_of_growing_flesh\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": every spirit you collect now grants extra health instead of healing. Null Slate with Mnemonic Fragments does the same for Manaweaving and Esoteric Spoils.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.172A9B6588AB9477.title": "Malignant Pewter",
  "quest.172A9B6588AB9477.quest_subtitle": "The alloy that unwinds progress.",
  "quest.172A9B6588AB9477.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Cthonic Gold thrown into the Well comes back as \"},{\"text\":\"Malignant Lead\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:malignant_lead\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Four iron ingots on the altar with the lead, eight Null Slate and two netherite scrap, fed sixteen Earthen and sixteen Eldritch, make a \"},{\"text\":\"Malignant Pewter Ingot\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:malignant_pewter_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": a metal that magic cannot form around.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2DFAA6209F4758A9.title": "Malignant Stronghold armor",
  "quest.2DFAA6209F4758A9.quest_desc": [
    "Each Soulstained piece takes eight Soulwoven Silk and three Malignant Pewter Plating. With the full set only half of any harm reaches your soul, and the magic it intercepts feeds Malignant Aegis, a barrier that can nullify most incoming harm."
  ],
  "quest.0EE19A191A8A2592.title": "Weight and Edge",
  "quest.0EE19A191A8A2592.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two Malignant Pewter turn a Soulstained axe into the \"},{\"text\":\"Weight of Worlds\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:weight_of_worlds\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": a kill stores a doubled blow for your next swing. The same pair turns the Soulstained scythe into the \"},{\"text\":\"Edge of Deliverance\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"malum:edge_of_deliverance\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", which alternates killing strength after each taste of blood.\"}]"
  ],
  "image.1AA23F24FAAF7216.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The harvest\",\"color\":\"#E07BFF\"}]",
  "image.033402037719177F.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Around the altar\",\"color\":\"#E07BFF\"}]",
  "image.643B9E9BD992A145.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Soulstained gear\",\"color\":\"#E07BFF\"}]",
  "image.4B7632005A98CF65.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Trinkets and runes\",\"color\":\"#E07BFF\"}]",
  "image.7BB4E88439BF7321.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Focusing\",\"color\":\"#E07BFF\"}]",
  "image.3F045EDCF85A0A1D.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Totem magic\",\"color\":\"#E07BFF\"}]",
  "image.03A53DE2647F8581.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Soulwood and blight\",\"color\":\"#E07BFF\"}]",
  "image.1C26E96C9E42CAF9.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Oaths\",\"color\":\"#E07BFF\"}]",
  "image.5F7F8D6ECD19780E.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Weeping Well\",\"color\":\"#E07BFF\"}]",
  "image.392DBEE7632D4B86.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Malignant Pewter\",\"color\":\"#E07BFF\"}]",
  "image.6DA8CC3A4CF61D1A.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Malum\",\"color\":\"#F3EEDF\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.5BDCD031C6981A07.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"scythe altar well\",\"color\":\"#D9B8F0\",\"font\":\"minecraft:alt\"}]",
  "image.6E498F64292DFA09.title": "Back to the Sun of Heliodor",
  "chapter.433D202F0AB8B336.title": "Occultism · Spirits and storage",
  "chapter.433D202F0AB8B336.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Workers, miners, familiars and a dimension for your things: every job has its spirit, and every spirit its tier."
  ],
  "quest.353FC9B6E478C883.title": "The Foliot Transporter",
  "quest.353FC9B6E478C883.quest_subtitle": "A hopper line without the hoppers.",
  "quest.353FC9B6E478C883.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Aviar's Circle with a minecart, a chest, a dispenser and a hopper calls a Transporter, and the ritual drops its \"},{\"text\":\"Book of Calling\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:book_of_calling_foliot_transport_items\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Sneak-use the book on the source inventory, then on the target: it hauls between them, machines and other spirits included.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5D6A2910F50F7AD3.title": "The Foliot Janitor",
  "quest.5D6A2910F50F7AD3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A brush, a chest, a dispenser and a hopper on Aviar's Circle. The Janitor picks up items dropped in its area and delivers them to the inventory you sneak-used its \"},{\"text\":\"Book of Calling\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:book_of_calling_foliot_cleaner\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on. Transporter in, Janitor out, a crusher in between: the classic ore loop.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.25BD7367034ED0C8.title": "It starts on allow",
  "quest.25BD7367034ED0C8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A new Janitor or Transporter moves nothing: both start with an empty allow list. Sneak-use the spirit to open its filter, then list items or a tag, or flip it to a block list.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.7A1A571CD29A25E7.title": "Summon a Foliot Smelter",
  "task.2CE2CA84DA337880.title": "Summon a Foliot Crystallizer",
  "quest.340A9A1A5DB500E2.title": "Smelter and crystallizer",
  "quest.340A9A1A5DB500E2.quest_desc": [
    "Coal, a furnace and a campfire call a Foliot Smelter: furnace, blast furnace, smoker and campfire recipes at furnace speed, no fuel. A Spirit Attuned Crystal with amethyst, lapis and emerald dusts calls a Foliot Crystallizer, which slowly turns gem dusts back into gems and multiplies gem ores."
  ],
  "quest.15EA42219BD31C44.title": "The Foliot Farmer",
  "quest.15EA42219BD31C44.quest_subtitle": "Farm work, outsourced to the afterlife.",
  "quest.15EA42219BD31C44.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Demon's Dream Fruit, wheat, a carrot, a potato and a hoe: a Farmer that harvests and replants the crops in its work area and, with a deposit set in its \"},{\"text\":\"Book of Calling\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:book_of_calling_foliot_farmer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", carries the harvest to a chest.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"It rests a few minutes after clearing the area. Setting the work area again wakes it.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.4612A935AB6117BF.title": "Summon an Otherstone Trader",
  "task.36BC525E28CCBE32.title": "Summon a Sapling Trader",
  "quest.0E2BA12F8E939E80.title": "Trade spirits",
  "quest.0E2BA12F8E939E80.quest_subtitle": "Brief, but fair.",
  "quest.0E2BA12F8E939E80.quest_desc": [
    "Stone, granite, diorite and andesite call an Otherstone Trader; four vanilla saplings, a Sapling Trader. Drop the offer beside one and it throws the trade back: stone for Otherstone, unstable Otherworld saplings for stable ones anyone can harvest. Traders fade fast."
  ],
  "quest.4DF7EE2F9042D90F.title": "The Foliot Lumberjack",
  "quest.4DF7EE2F9042D90F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A stable \"},{\"text\":\"Otherworld Sapling\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:otherworld_sapling\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" from the Sapling Trader, oak, birch and spruce saplings and an axe. The Lumberjack fells the trees in its work area and, with a deposit set in its \"},{\"text\":\"Book of Calling\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:book_of_calling_foliot_lumberjack\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", stores the wood and replants.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2113321E34D6AB18.title": "Books of Calling and lamps",
  "quest.2113321E34D6AB18.quest_subtitle": "The worker goes where you go.",
  "quest.2113321E34D6AB18.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Book of Calling runs its worker: right-click the air to configure, sneak-use a block to apply, sneak-use the spirit to capture it. Lost one? Craft it again from a bound book and sneak-use it on the spirit. A \"},{\"text\":\"Magic Lamp\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:magic_lamp_empty\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" carries a worker safe from decay.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.24E3EE5F590F43EF.title": "Summon a Djinni Crusher",
  "task.3B110190CE00533F.title": "Summon a Djinni Smelter",
  "task.034C69768679F790.title": "Summon a Djinni Crystallizer",
  "quest.3E436D1792543A16.title": "Djinni at work",
  "quest.3E436D1792543A16.quest_subtitle": "Faster hands, sharper teeth.",
  "quest.3E436D1792543A16.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Ophyx' Calling\",\"italic\":true},{\"text\":\", with lime chalk and four skulls. A Djinni Crusher turns one ore into three dusts and crushes ice without melting it; a Djinni Smelter works twice as fast; a Djinni Crystallizer is faster, yields more from gem ores and breaks amethyst and quartz blocks back down.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.73CE60572DDE5C99.title": "Make it day",
  "task.73140217EC678081.title": "Make it night",
  "quest.4A60EF2567A10FC6.title": "A Djinni with a watch",
  "quest.4A60EF2567A10FC6.quest_desc": [
    "A torch, a sapling, wheat and yellow dye call a Djinni that makes it day; gunpowder, rotten flesh, a bone and black dye, one that makes it night. Each changes the time once and leaves: cheaper than waiting when a ritual or a hunt wants a certain hour."
  ],
  "task.3B70805F2DDAA330.title": "Summon the Wondering Trader",
  "quest.32889FF2E657980A.title": "The Wondering Trader",
  "quest.32889FF2E657980A.quest_subtitle": "Not a typo. He wonders.",
  "quest.32889FF2E657980A.quest_desc": [
    "Two Otherworld Essence and two emeralds on Ophyx' Calling. To plain eyes he's a wandering trader; with the Third Eye or the goggles you see what he really is. The first time you talk to him, he only shows the mundane stock."
  ],
  "task.32EAB44D9D51232A.title": "Summon the Gem Gambler",
  "quest.2AF30E54DE53E590.title": "The house always wins",
  "quest.2AF30E54DE53E590.quest_subtitle": "Especially when the house is a Djinni.",
  "quest.2AF30E54DE53E590.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"You summoned the Gem Gambler with an emerald, a diamond block, gold and a silver block. Bet a gem and get a random gem or nugget back, the rare \"},{\"text\":\"Iesnium Nugget\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:iesnium_nugget\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" included. Grab your winnings fast: it keeps betting whatever it finds on the floor.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.7988E3E417E69ED4.title": "Secret found",
  "task.4BF89B3CE5730D0A.title": "Summon an Afrit Crusher",
  "task.6224FE790BA47933.title": "Summon an Afrit Smelter",
  "task.0E0A7A957C41F5C2.title": "Summon an Afrit Crystallizer",
  "quest.171288938B89FB4E.title": "Afrit at work",
  "quest.171288938B89FB4E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Abras' Conjure\",\"italic\":true},{\"text\":\", red chalk and four crystals. An Afrit Crusher makes four dusts per ore, an Afrit Smelter works in a tenth of the time, and an Afrit Crystallizer also rebuilds crushed blocks.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.29A446C21E266C33.title": "Call the rain",
  "task.17623287DE105865.title": "Call a thunderstorm",
  "quest.47651405BEFD17E0.title": "Weather on demand",
  "quest.47651405BEFD17E0.quest_desc": [
    "Sand, dried kelp, a cactus and a dead bush with a cow bring rain; bones, gunpowder and a ghast tear with a cow bring a thunderstorm. A Djinni with beetroot, carrot, potato and wheat clears the sky. Weather spirits change it once, then vanish."
  ],
  "task.5CDFA8409363DE17.title": "Summon a Marid Crusher",
  "task.1D8A8579B5203D09.title": "Summon a Marid Smelter",
  "task.3761871741A16F35.title": "Summon a Marid Crystallizer",
  "quest.26FEE7CF2C363E14.title": "Marid at work",
  "quest.26FEE7CF2C363E14.quest_subtitle": "Overkill, by design.",
  "quest.26FEE7CF2C363E14.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Fatma's Incentivized Attraction\",\"italic\":true},{\"text\":\", blue chalk and eight crystals. A Marid Crusher makes six dusts per ore and grinds echo shards whole; a Marid Smelter needs a hundredth of the time; a Marid Crystallizer turns amethyst clusters into budding amethyst and obsidian into crying obsidian.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.07EE66B014AB00A6.title": "A tablet full of levels",
  "quest.07EE66B014AB00A6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An Otherworldly Tablet, research dust, a Spirit Attuned Gem and an ender pearl on the Foliot infusion: a spirit that holds experience. Right-click stores all your levels in the \"},{\"text\":\"Knowledge Tablet\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:knowledge_tablet\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; sneak-right-click takes them back, or hand it to a friend.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7DC606A8388E92A2.title": "The Spirit Grindstone",
  "quest.7DC606A8388E92A2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Djinni infusion of a grindstone, glass, a Spirit Attuned Crystal and prismarine crystals. The \"},{\"text\":\"Spirit Grindstone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:spirit_grindstone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" strips only curses, keeps every other enchantment, refunds all of the curses' experience and repairs better when you combine two items.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.29686E1D7D47A842.title": "An iesnium edge",
  "quest.29686E1D7D47A842.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Sevira's circle upgrades the butcher knife with two iesnium ingots, Afrit Essence and netherite dust. The \"},{\"text\":\"Iesnium Butcher Knife\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:iesnium_butcher_knife\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" hits harder, still takes tallow, deals triple damage to spirits and sometimes takes heads: a skeleton loses its skull one time in four.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.177EAD9F1FA367B4.title": "The Iesnium Anvil",
  "quest.177EAD9F1FA367B4.quest_subtitle": "Past the maximum, at half price.",
  "quest.177EAD9F1FA367B4.quest_desc": [
    "Uphyxes Inverted Tower with an anvil, three blocks of iesnium and Marid Essence. It never breaks, takes an enchantment one level past its maximum, pays half the shown cost itself, slows the prior-work penalty and raises the too-expensive cap."
  ],
  "quest.125BACA6BF18264C.title": "The Dimensional Mineshaft",
  "quest.125BACA6BF18264C.quest_subtitle": "Mining without the commute.",
  "quest.125BACA6BF18264C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Strigeor's Higher Binding with Otherstone, a gold ingot, a block of iesnium and a Spirit Attuned Crystal; in this pack it also takes an \"},{\"text\":\"Ironwood Ingot\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:ironwood_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", the act IV material. A Djinni holds open a portal too small for you, and miner spirits go through it for ore.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Lamp in the top, ores out the bottom, every slot from the sides. It destroys what it can't store, so drain it with a hopper, a pipe or a Transporter. A redstone signal pauses it; a comparator reads fill and lamp wear, and at 10 it's time to stop."
  ],
  "quest.2CDF4CFA614E7F02.title": "Miner Foliot",
  "quest.2CDF4CFA614E7F02.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An empty Magic Lamp, an Iesnium Pickaxe, an iron ingot and gravel on the Foliot infusion. The \"},{\"text\":\"Miner Foliot\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:miner_foliot_unspecialized\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" digs slowly and brings back whatever it finds, stone included; its lamp wears slowly, and when it breaks the spirit goes home.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.70071D10FE1B5D24.title": "Ore Miner Djinni",
  "quest.70071D10FE1B5D24.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Foliot's lamp, another Iesnium Pickaxe, gold, lapis and a crystal on Strigeor's circle. The \"},{\"text\":\"Ore Miner Djinni\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:miner_djinni_ores\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" skips stone and brings only ores, faster, but it wears its lamp quickly.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.04F1FE3356E5ED23.title": "Deep Ore Miner Afrit",
  "quest.04F1FE3356E5ED23.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Djinni's lamp, a third Iesnium Pickaxe, a crystal, Afrit Essence, an echo shard and crying obsidian on Sevira's circle. The \"},{\"text\":\"Afrit\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:miner_afrit_deeps\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" adds deepslate ores and is faster and gentler on its lamp.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Sevira's circle also repairs a worn lamp for three Otherworld Essence and a gem, enchantments kept; the same Afrit ritual fixes tools and armor.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.303A749BB761A870.title": "Master Miner Marid",
  "quest.303A749BB761A870.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Afrit's lamp with an Iesnium Pickaxe, a crystal, a netherite pickaxe, dragon's breath, a Totem of Undying, a Nether Star and Marid Essence. The \"},{\"text\":\"Marid\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:miner_marid_master\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" is the fastest, the kindest to its lamp, and the only miner that finds ancient debris and iesnium ore.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1E82438707E4EBB5.title": "Enchant your miners",
  "quest.1E82438707E4EBB5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Miners take enchantments: Efficiency speeds them up, Fortune adds results, Silk Touch multiplies them, Unbreaking and Mending spare the lamp. They draw from ore tags, and Create: New Age's thorium has none in this pack, so it still needs real mining.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5DB6E183D1C6408E.title": "The Dimensional Extractor",
  "quest.5DB6E183D1C6408E.quest_desc": [
    "A pedestal, a hopper, a block of iesnium, a crystal and two gold ingots on Strigeor's circle. Set mineshafts, battlefields or worker spirits on top and a chest below: a Djinni moves the results down, fast. When the chest is full, the extra is thrown away."
  ],
  "quest.54C1268D341BB5CA.title": "The Eldritch Ancient Miner",
  "quest.54C1268D341BB5CA.quest_subtitle": "It stares back.",
  "quest.54C1268D341BB5CA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight Master Miner Marids pressed into one on Ronaza's Contact, started with a \"},{\"text\":\"Mining Dimension Core Piece\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:mining_dim_core\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and paid with a human sacrifice. It skips stone and ore alike and hauls whole storage blocks: raw ore, diamond and more. Core pieces turn up, very rarely, in a Marid's haul.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5606D86189A9DD0B.title": "Iesnium for the common store",
  "quest.5606D86189A9DD0B.quest_subtitle": "Everyone needs a pickaxe eventually.",
  "quest.5606D86189A9DD0B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight \"},{\"text\":\"Iesnium Ingots\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:iesnium_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for the common store, once a day. Every miner's ritual eats a pickaxe made of it, and a Master Miner Marid digs the ore for you.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.212D8FE4CBAB4DA8.title": "The Dimensional Storage Actuator",
  "quest.212D8FE4CBAB4DA8.quest_subtitle": "One chest, a dimension deep.",
  "quest.212D8FE4CBAB4DA8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Djinni binds three quartz blocks and an ender pearl into a \"},{\"text\":\"Dimensional Crystal Matrix\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:dimensional_matrix\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; a Foliot binds a pedestal, two copper and a gold ingot into a \"},{\"text\":\"Storage Actuator Base\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:storage_controller_base\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Matrix over base crafts the actuator: 128 item types, 256,000 items.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Break it and everything stays inside, like a shulker box. Damaged or enchanted variants take one type each. To other mods it's just a very large chest."
  ],
  "quest.4AAF6194A6D896F8.title": "Stabilizer, tier 1",
  "quest.4AAF6194A6D896F8.quest_subtitle": "Room to breathe.",
  "quest.4AAF6194A6D896F8.quest_desc": [
    "A pedestal crafts into a stabilizer base; a Foliot infusion with a copper block, blaze powder and a gem makes tier 1, for 64 more types and 512,000 more items. Aim it at the matrix, one block above the actuator, from up to five blocks away in a straight line."
  ],
  "quest.08A131AC6CE8A3DD.title": "Stabilizer, tier 2",
  "quest.08A131AC6CE8A3DD.quest_subtitle": "Room for the hoard.",
  "quest.08A131AC6CE8A3DD.quest_desc": [
    "Tier 1, a silver block, a ghast tear and two gems on Strigeor's circle: 128 more types and 1,024,000 more items.",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Breaking a stabilizer to upgrade it loses nothing; new items just wait until there's room again.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3BEE431FEB920864.title": "Stabilizer, tier 3",
  "quest.3BEE431FEB920864.quest_subtitle": "Room for your regrets.",
  "quest.3BEE431FEB920864.quest_desc": [
    "Tier 2, a gold block, a Totem of Undying, a crystal and Afrit Essence on Sevira's circle: 256 more types and 2,048,000 more items."
  ],
  "quest.1205B49603EF0C40.title": "Stabilizer, tier 4",
  "quest.1205B49603EF0C40.quest_subtitle": "Room for everything else.",
  "quest.1205B49603EF0C40.quest_desc": [
    "Tier 3, a block of iesnium, a beacon, two crystals and Marid Essence on Uphyxes Inverted Tower: 512 more types and 4,096,000 more items."
  ],
  "quest.2CB1AAE292F36D40.title": "A second door",
  "quest.2CB1AAE292F36D40.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An Otherstone frame, an ender pearl, two quartz and two gold ingots on the Foliot infusion make a \"},{\"text\":\"Stable Wormhole\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:stable_wormhole\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Sneak-use it on the actuator, then place it anywhere: another access point to the same storage, as long as the actuator's chunk stays loaded.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4EF9BE143EF7E3EF.title": "The Storage Accessor",
  "quest.4EF9BE143EF7E3EF.quest_subtitle": "The whole vault, one keypress away.",
  "quest.4EF9BE143EF7E3EF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An inert accessor (iesnium nuggets, silver, a gem and an Otherworldly Tablet) with two ender pearls and quartz on Strigeor's circle. Sneak-use it on the actuator; then \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.occultism.storage_remote\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" opens your storage from anywhere, other dimensions included.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3FA223CC01603AE4.title": "The Djinni Machine Operator",
  "quest.3FA223CC01603AE4.quest_subtitle": "On-demand crafting, with attitude.",
  "quest.3FA223CC01603AE4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A coal block, gold, iron and a furnace on Ophyx' Calling. Link its \"},{\"text\":\"Book of Calling\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:book_of_calling_djinni_manage_machine\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" to the actuator and a machine: it feeds the machine what you order from the actuator's screen and returns the results to storage. It can also empty a chest into the actuator.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3E8D875D9D616EAE.title": "Bigger on the inside",
  "quest.3E8D875D9D616EAE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A chest, two leather, string and silver on the Foliot infusion: the spirit bends the \"},{\"text\":\"Surprisingly Substantial Satchel\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:satchel\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" so it holds more than its size suggests. \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.occultism.backpack\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" opens it without taking it out, from your belt slot or your inventory.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7E54EA93E09A8A97.title": "The Ender Satchel",
  "quest.7E54EA93E09A8A97.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An ender chest, leather, string, silver and gold on Strigeor's circle: your ender chest, carried. \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.occultism.ender_bag\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" opens it; sneak-right-click binds it to you, so a friend holding it reaches your ender chest.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.59DC9600D63225DB.title": "Pull with spirits, not pipes",
  "quest.59DC9600D63225DB.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Pushing items into the actuator is cheap at any rate. Pulling is what costs: a filtered pipe searches the whole storage item by item. A Transporter spirit, even one that drops into a chest right beside it, is far lighter, and so is Theurgy's extractor with a list filter.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.042DE88B7A10B52B.title": "Summon a familiar",
  "quest.43B08A1E3138F0D9.title": "Familiars",
  "quest.43B08A1E3138F0D9.quest_subtitle": "A pet with a résumé.",
  "quest.43B08A1E3138F0D9.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Possession pentacles can also call a spirit into an animal body that follows you and helps. Start the ritual by hand, since a hopper-fed ritual brings familiars out untamed, and heal them with \"},{\"text\":\"Demon's Dream Fruit\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:datura\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Two cheap first picks on Hedyrin's Lure: a Greedy Familiar (a chest, an iron block, a dispenser, a hopper and a zombie) picks up items for you; a Deer Familiar (sticks, string and a cow) gives speed, jump boost and step assist."
  ],
  "task.6473F6B7B71FDC48.title": "Summon a Blacksmith Familiar",
  "task.203CC1D20734EA2E.title": "Summon a Beaver Familiar",
  "quest.4A0440E2A68B91C9.title": "The blacksmith and the beaver",
  "quest.4A0440E2A68B91C9.quest_desc": [
    "Iron tools, an anvil and stone with a zombie: the Blacksmith Familiar mends your gear a little whenever you pick up stone and, fed iron, upgrades your other familiars. Logs and a pig give a Beaver Familiar, which fells the small trees that grow near it."
  ],
  "task.4A7335EC8BEAD1AE.title": "Summon a Bat Familiar",
  "task.2489EA46485ECC38.title": "Summon a Drikwing",
  "task.0BB8D6EBAB92869B.title": "Summon a Devil Familiar",
  "quest.1C8520A590AF5DEF.title": "Djinni companions",
  "quest.1C8520A590AF5DEF.quest_desc": [
    "Ihagan's Enthrallment gives stronger familiars. A Bat (a bat as the sacrifice) grants night vision; a Drikwing (a parrot) multi-jump, jump boost and slow falling; a Devil (a horse) fire resistance, and it breathes fire at your enemies."
  ],
  "task.0446177A4F9E246A.title": "Summon a Fairy Familiar",
  "task.3FED09DF6A225976.title": "Summon a Mummy Familiar",
  "task.4C3441C52A55FEFA.title": "Summon a Beholder Familiar",
  "quest.37F92F1083517311.title": "Guards, lasers and a fairy",
  "quest.37F92F1083517311.quest_desc": [
    "A Fairy (golden apples, a ghast tear, gunpowder and milk, and a horse) keeps your other familiars from dying and drains enemies. A Mummy (slime, paper and wool, and a llama) fights and grants Dodge. A Beholder (spider eyes and glowstone, and a spider) outlines nearby mobs and fires lasers."
  ],
  "task.69F3EFB58967D6FB.title": "Summon a Chimera Familiar",
  "task.15CE8D4AAD925E47.title": "Split the goat off",
  "task.6C0E0A2B66FF9A79.title": "Call Shub Niggurath",
  "quest.26A5FBDCDCD9460C.title": "The goat that got away",
  "quest.26A5FBDCDCD9460C.quest_subtitle": "Some assembly required. And disassembly.",
  "quest.26A5FBDCDCD9460C.quest_desc": [
    "A Chimera Familiar (leather, string, feathers, wool, a bone and four raw meats, and a sheep) grows as you feed it meat until you can ride it. A golden apple splits its goat off; take the goat to a forest and use black dye, flint and an eye of ender on it."
  ],
  "quest.14809600791FA54B.title": "Soul gems",
  "quest.14809600791FA54B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Foliot binds an egg, an iron ingot and glass into a Fragile Soul Gem that carries one creature, then breaks. A Djinni binds a diamond, copper, silver and gold, the fragile gem and soul sand into a \"},{\"text\":\"Soul Gem\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:soul_gem\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" that lasts. Right-click to capture, again to release; bosses refuse.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7D62DC89A1D57289.title": "The Familiar Ring",
  "quest.7D62DC89A1D57289.quest_subtitle": "Pocket-sized loyalty.",
  "quest.7D62DC89A1D57289.quest_desc": [
    "A Soul Gem, two gold and two silver on Strigeor's circle. Right-click your tamed familiar with the ring to capture it, then wear the ring as a curio: the effect stays, the animal doesn't tag along. Whoever releases it becomes its master, so familiars can change hands.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Each familiar's ring effect has its own on-off key, \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.occultism.familiar.greedy_familiar\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" for the Greedy one. They come unbound: set the ones you use in Controls, under Occultism.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5CEE9965BE070ED8.title": "The Dimensional Battlefield",
  "quest.5CEE9965BE070ED8.quest_subtitle": "A mob farm with no mobs in your yard.",
  "quest.5CEE9965BE070ED8.quest_desc": [
    "Sevira's circle with Otherstone, a netherite ingot, a block of iesnium, a crystal and Afrit Essence. Load a creature in a soul gem, a weapon for the Afrit and spiritual fuel such as Demon's Dream: it clones the creature and kills it for loot, as long as the fuel is worth the creature's health.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Looting adds drops; Sharpness, or better Smite and its kin where they apply, speeds it up. A \"},{\"text\":\"Trinity Gem\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:trinity_gem\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", forged by Eldritch spirits, even takes possessed mobs and bosses, and triples ordinary loot.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.6F06B2637D3D7A1F.title": "Summon a Guardian Familiar",
  "quest.7FBCCDC83270F980.title": "The Guardian Familiar",
  "quest.7FBCCDC83270F980.quest_subtitle": "Every limb a second chance.",
  "quest.7FBCCDC83270F980.quest_desc": [
    "Posuc's Convocation with four diamonds, two golden apples and a human sacrifice. Each time you are about to die, the Guardian gives up a limb instead, until it has none left. It arrives with a random number of limbs; a Blacksmith upgrade grows one back."
  ],
  "task.5E295305574DE562.title": "Call an Iesnium Golem",
  "quest.74E0184C21382D21.title": "The Iesnium Golem",
  "quest.74E0184C21382D21.quest_subtitle": "Unbreakable, unbribable.",
  "quest.74E0184C21382D21.quest_desc": [
    "Xeovrenth Adjure with three blocks of iesnium, Marid Essence, a crystal, a Nether Star and a Soul Gem, and an iron golem as the sacrifice. The result is a far stronger golem that can't be hurt; only a player who sneaks and hits it dismisses it, back into a Fragile Soul Gem."
  ],
  "task.298E6EB7112BFEBD.title": "Resurrect a familiar",
  "quest.1733BF26B7326E96.title": "Susje's Simple Circle",
  "quest.1733BF26B7326E96.quest_subtitle": "Death is more of a setback.",
  "quest.1733BF26B7326E96.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A familiar that dies leaves a \"},{\"text\":\"Soul Shard\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:soul_shard\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Draw Susje's Simple Circle, sixteen colorless glyphs and nothing else, put four Otherworld Essence in the bowls and use the shard on the golden bowl: the familiar builds itself a new body.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4BB1C919B907C365.title": "The Entity Wormhole",
  "quest.4BB1C919B907C365.quest_subtitle": "Step in here, step out there.",
  "quest.4BB1C919B907C365.quest_desc": [
    "An Otherstone frame, an ender pearl, crying obsidian and an iesnium ingot on Strigeor's circle. Right-click a compass into it to set the exit: a plain one leads to world spawn, a lodestone compass to its lodestone, a recovery compass to your last death.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A compass renamed HOME leads to your own spawn point, one renamed RTP somewhere random. A \"},{\"text\":\"Vitality Compass\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:vitality_compass\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" bound to a creature leads to it, and a fishing rod cast into the portal reels the creature in.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.158EAF9001B5A2F9.title": "Watch your deer familiar",
  "quest.7F213A8DE4D95C01.title": "Demonic fertilizer",
  "quest.7F213A8DE4D95C01.quest_subtitle": "Fertilizer with a pedigree.",
  "quest.7F213A8DE4D95C01.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Your Deer Familiar pooped out a \"},{\"text\":\"Demon's Dream Seed\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:datura_seeds\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Free seeds are free seeds; nobody needs to know where they came from.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.0083B6B1F7541FFD.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.73A4E27CDA77DEB2.title": "Till death, and past it",
  "quest.73A4E27CDA77DEB2.quest_subtitle": "A contract with a very long term.",
  "quest.73A4E27CDA77DEB2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"You married a demon, and your gift of Cursed Honey came back as a \"},{\"text\":\"Sweet-Honey-Heart\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"occultism:sweet_honey_heart\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". The Demonic Partner fights beside you, cooks raw food on a right-click and makes potions last much longer. The bond is permanent: spirits take contracts seriously.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.003AB4C491F4D566.title": "Secret found",
  "task.770E45317E604381.title": "Purify a vex",
  "quest.71C12374CBE5A56E.title": "Redeemed",
  "quest.71C12374CBE5A56E.quest_subtitle": "Vex no more.",
  "quest.71C12374CBE5A56E.quest_desc": [
    "Susje's circle, a sugar used as the key, redstone, glowstone, silver and gold dusts in the bowls and a Vex as the sacrifice: you purified a Vex into an Allay. Its true name turned out nicer than its manners."
  ],
  "reward.517263F50D9AA598.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.7983A45463227146.title": "Space, folded",
  "quest.7983A45463227146.quest_subtitle": "The stabilizers went somewhere. Don't ask where.",
  "quest.7983A45463227146.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Ronaza's Contact forges tier 5 stabilizers, 1,024 types and 8,192,000 items each. Six of them, your actuator, two echo dusts and a \"},{\"text\":\"Calibrated Sculk Sensor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:calibrated_sculk_sensor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", paid with a shulker, fold every stabilizer into the block: the equal of eight tier 5s, contents kept.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "External stabilizers add nothing to it anymore. The house is full of spirits, and every one of them has a job."
  ],
  "image.752CE90576C8D666.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Workers\",\"color\":\"#CE8BFF\"}]",
  "image.642EE8F5D4498DE4.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Miners\",\"color\":\"#CE8BFF\"}]",
  "image.7D1AC96254377E33.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Storage\",\"color\":\"#CE8BFF\"}]",
  "image.57C71683807720FA.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Familiars\",\"color\":\"#CE8BFF\"}]",
  "image.7B4A6D9C331310BB.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Tools\",\"color\":\"#CE8BFF\"}]",
  "image.7F1474AF404B4404.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Occultism\",\"color\":\"#F3EEDF\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.217D6A71FA258AF4.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Spirits and storage\",\"color\":\"#CE8BFF\"}]",
  "image.44A7A22A40C0C1C9.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"every job a spirit\",\"color\":\"#B9A7E0\",\"font\":\"minecraft:alt\"}]",
  "image.475153F040C7A9D1.title": "Back to Occultism · Rituals",
  "image.3D9CD6FF17173C9E.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Foliot\",\"color\":\"#E8E1CF\"}]",
  "image.3770F0594A4E2F25.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Djinni\",\"color\":\"#E8E1CF\"}]",
  "image.12BC3519576E6438.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Afrit\",\"color\":\"#E8E1CF\"}]",
  "image.6333B820B4210930.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Marid\",\"color\":\"#E8E1CF\"}]",
  "chapter.330F418E7969E977.title": "Psi: Programmable Spells",
  "chapter.330F418E7969E977.chapter_subtitle": [
    "The CAD, the Spell Programmer, bullets, psimetal and the Exosuit."
  ],
  "quest.31660A2849BD9384.title": "Spells you program",
  "quest.31660A2849BD9384.quest_desc": [
    "Build a Casting Assistant Device (CAD), write spells on a 9x9 grid of small pieces, copy them into Spell Bullets and cast. All of Psi is Act III here: the CAD Assembler needs a Power Regulator.",
    "",
    "Terra's kind of magic: a machine you teach to think."
  ],
  "quest.7D362F3E6640B2DF.title": "CAD Assembler",
  "quest.7D362F3E6640B2DF.quest_desc": [
    "Iron, a piston and a Power Regulator (Act III). It builds a CAD from its components and loads Spell Bullets into it, and into Psimetal tools and armor. No Assembler, no CAD, no spell: this is where Psi really starts."
  ],
  "quest.24BA6CEFF3600962.title": "A bare CAD makes Psidust",
  "quest.24BA6CEFF3600962.quest_desc": [
    "An Iron CAD Assembly alone in the Assembler is a bare CAD. It can't cast spells, but drop redstone dust, point the empty CAD at it and right-click: the redstone becomes Psidust, the base of every early part.",
    "",
    "Step one of magic: redstone, but spicier."
  ],
  "quest.377B938ABA847AB6.title": "Core, Socket and Bullets",
  "quest.377B938ABA847AB6.quest_desc": [
    "A casting CAD needs an Assembly, a Core and a Socket, all from iron and psidust; bullets too. A bare CAD in a crafting grid gives the Assembly back. A Battery is worth it; a Colorizer only changes colors."
  ],
  "quest.336C46A2C862033C.title": "The Spell Programmer",
  "quest.336C46A2C862033C.quest_desc": [
    "Right-click a cell and type to search pieces; left-click a piece to point its inputs at neighbors. When the corner X turns into a check, the spell compiles. The book's tutorials teach the whole system in order.",
    "",
    "First program: «hello, world». Second: «hello, crater»."
  ],
  "quest.349FE8F901DFB239.title": "Load and fire",
  "quest.349FE8F901DFB239.quest_desc": [
    "Use a bullet on the Programmer to copy the spell, then load it into the CAD at the Assembler. Hold the Psi key (Alt+F here) to pick it on the radial and right-click. Sneak-use the CAD on the Programmer to refresh the loaded bullet."
  ],
  "quest.1A449BEF14F33074.title": "Five numbers to respect",
  "quest.1A449BEF14F33074.quest_desc": [
    "The Core caps Complexity and Projection, the Assembly Potency, the Socket spell size. Cost comes from your Psi energy; overdraw and the rest comes out of your health, and the CAD shuts down until you refill. Tricks reach 32 blocks at most.",
    "",
    "A Battery is cheaper than a funeral."
  ],
  "quest.49C120F578144C3E.title": "One CAD per mage",
  "quest.49C120F578144C3E.quest_desc": [
    "Carry a single CAD. Two or more in your inventory interfere and every spell shorts out; the book calls it cast jamming. Spares go in a chest.",
    "",
    "Two radios on the same frequency. Same result."
  ],
  "quest.66787E7A0B61BE71.title": "Psimetal",
  "quest.66787E7A0B61BE71.quest_desc": [
    "Cast Trick: Infusion near gold ingots on the ground and they become Psimetal: better cores, sockets and batteries, the Psimetal Assembly, drives, tools and armor. It also upgrades a Gold CAD Assembly lying there.",
    "",
    "Alchemy, compiled."
  ],
  "quest.1E8264AB0191DD07.title": "Bullet types",
  "quest.1E8264AB0191DD07.quest_desc": [
    "One extra ingredient sets the bullet type: arrow Projectile, string Loopcast (four times a second while held), snowball Circle, gunpowder Grenade, redstone Charge (waits for a Detonator), button Mine. Each type multiplies the cost and moves the focal point."
  ],
  "quest.2BAA9AA5501D9B58.title": "Better cores and sockets",
  "quest.2BAA9AA5501D9B58.quest_desc": [
    "Psimetal shell, and the dust inside picks the model. Redstone: Overclocked Core (double Complexity) and Signaling Socket (six bullets). Glowstone: Conductive Core (four tricks at once) and Large Socket (eight bullets). The Psimetal Assembly adds Potency."
  ],
  "quest.6089239E241C601C.title": "Psigems",
  "quest.6089239E241C601C.quest_desc": [
    "With a Psimetal Assembly, cast Trick: Greater Infusion near diamonds on the ground: they become Psigems, for the top cores and sockets, Psimetal tools and the Exosuit.",
    "",
    "Diamonds, but with opinions."
  ],
  "quest.7E7538E140C58749.title": "Psigem cores need a Matrix",
  "quest.7E7538E140C58749.quest_desc": [
    "The Hyperclocked Core (double a Conductive's Complexity) and the Radiative Core (seven tricks at once) keep their native recipes, psimetal and psigems: the CAD Assembler already makes Psi an Act III mod."
  ],
  "quest.4E1D12B86BB751F6.title": "Ebony and Ivory",
  "quest.4E1D12B86BB751F6.quest_desc": [
    "In the End only: cast Trick: Ebony and Ivory (Psimetal Assembly needed) near coal and nether quartz on the ground. Coat psimetal with the results for the top Assemblies: Ebony takes more Potency, Ivory is more efficient.",
    "",
    "In perfect harmony, far from home."
  ],
  "quest.51AA960E129CC4FD.title": "Tools that cast",
  "quest.51AA960E129CC4FD.quest_desc": [
    "About diamond grade. They cast their selected spell every time they break a block (the sword on every hit), hold three bullets and repair with spare Psi. A pickaxe that also breaks the blocks around the one you mined is a classic."
  ],
  "quest.52A72E20AF458775.title": "The Psimetal Exosuit",
  "quest.52A72E20AF458775.quest_desc": [
    "Each piece holds three bullets and fires on its own trigger: the Helmet on its Sensor (light, heat, water…), the Chestplate when you're hit, the Leggings every tick, the Boots when you jump. A bit better than iron, self-repairing.",
    "",
    "Armor with reflexes."
  ],
  "quest.4621F69AC863F5AC.title": "A spell library",
  "quest.4621F69AC863F5AC.quest_desc": [
    "A Spell Drive stores one spell: sneak-use it on the Programmer to save, again to load. A Vector Ruler stores a position or offset your spells can read.",
    "",
    "Version control, the magical kind."
  ],
  "quest.1F1890606B8EECB9.title": "Alt+F and the missing book",
  "quest.1F1890606B8EECB9.quest_desc": [
    "Psi's master key moves from C to Alt+F here: C saves hotbars and opens the Ars book even with Alt held. With no CAD in hand it opens the Encyclopaedia Psionica. Psi's book as an item: drop a plain book and cast at it with a CAD."
  ],
  "quest.7B2642782F246FD0.title": "A spellslinger",
  "quest.7B2642782F246FD0.quest_desc": [
    "A psigem-core CAD, an Exosuit that reacts by itself, tools that cast as they work and a drive full of spells you wrote. The only ceiling is your ingenuity: compress, chain tricks, share spells with friends.",
    "",
    "The grid is small. What fits in it is not."
  ],
  "chapter.706C1D99E8A3B84A.title": "Theurgy",
  "chapter.706C1D99E8A3B84A.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Salt, sulfur and mercury: take matter apart, put it back together three times over, then turn iron into gold."
  ],
  "quest.45B1C0CCAB3365E4.title": "Pyromantic Brazier",
  "quest.45B1C0CCAB3365E4.quest_subtitle": "Alchemy starts with a good fire.",
  "quest.45B1C0CCAB3365E4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Five copper ingots and four stone make a \"},{\"text\":\"Pyromantic Brazier\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:pyromantic_brazier\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Every heated apparatus sits on one: the oven, the cauldron, the distiller and the incubator. It burns furnace fuel, by hand or from a hopper.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four braziers cover the whole refinery. Later a \"},{\"text\":\"Caloric Flux Emitter\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"2362DF329027AE22\"}},{\"text\":\" heats from a distance and the coal can stay in the chest.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.083771EBDC43B500.title": "Hands, hoppers and buckets",
  "quest.083771EBDC43B500.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Every apparatus takes the same clicks. Empty hand: the output first, then the input. An item in hand goes in. A full bucket pours in, an empty one fills; \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.sneak\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" and right-click drains every fluid. Hoppers and pipes load them too.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0485429A4ED9F39F.title": "Stone means stone",
  "quest.0485429A4ED9F39F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Theurgy's recipes ask for the stone tag: stone, andesite, diorite, granite, deepslate and tuff all count, cobblestone doesn't. Smelt a stack before the braziers, the distiller and the vessels.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.73C3DD49C2314F5A.title": "The Hermetica",
  "quest.73C3DD49C2314F5A.quest_subtitle": "It insists it's science. Humor it.",
  "quest.73C3DD49C2314F5A.quest_desc": [
    "A book and two sand of any kind. The Hermetica runs its experiments in order, and most entries open as you read the ones before: raw iron into three ingots, lapis into quartz, quartz into iron, iron into gold. Every apparatus page shows its recipe and the clicks it takes."
  ],
  "quest.5E1BACB0C941F280.title": "Salt: the body",
  "quest.5E1BACB0C941F280.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four iron ingots around a block of copper make the \"},{\"text\":\"Calcination Oven\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:calcination_oven\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". On a brazier it calcines minerals: an ore block gives three \"},{\"text\":\"Mineral Salt\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:alchemical_salt_mineral\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", an ingot or a gem two, a raw metal one. Each ingot or gem the incubator makes eats one.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7038E75724D0B7B7.title": "Sal Ammoniac: the solvent",
  "quest.7038E75724D0B7B7.quest_subtitle": "It evaporates water until the water gives up.",
  "quest.7038E75724D0B7B7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Set the \"},{\"text\":\"Sal Ammoniac Accumulator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:sal_ammoniac_accumulator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on its \"},{\"text\":\"Tank\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:sal_ammoniac_tank\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and pour in up to ten water buckets. Every bucket of water leaves a tenth of a bucket of solvent; an empty bucket on the tank draws a \"},{\"text\":\"Sal Ammoniac Bucket\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:sal_ammoniac_bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Sal Ammoniac Crystal\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"229F97FB2222BE89\"}},{\"text\":\" dissolved in the accumulator turns each bucket of water into a whole bucket of solvent.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.00239A02D0B8CA69.title": "Sulfur: the soul",
  "quest.00239A02D0B8CA69.quest_subtitle": "The soul of an ingot, in a jar.",
  "quest.00239A02D0B8CA69.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Five copper ingots, a cauldron and three stone make the \"},{\"text\":\"Liquefaction Cauldron\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:liquefaction_cauldron\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". On a brazier and filled with sal ammoniac it dissolves what you feed it and keeps the sulfur: one \"},{\"text\":\"Raw Iron\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:raw_iron\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" gives three \"},{\"text\":\"Iron Sulfur\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:alchemical_sulfur_iron\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". That's where the multiplying happens.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3A0E5E4FB37C3C75.title": "Mercury: the spirit",
  "quest.3A0E5E4FB37C3C75.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three iron ingots, a block of copper and three stone make the \"},{\"text\":\"Mercury Distiller\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:distiller\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". On a brazier it boils almost anything down to \"},{\"text\":\"Mercury Shards\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:mercury_shard\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": ten cobblestone give one, a raw iron one, an iron ore block five. Mercury is the incubator's third ingredient and Theurgy's fuel.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7E37B0C668398893.title": "Three ingots from one",
  "quest.7E37B0C668398893.quest_subtitle": "Body, soul and spirit, back together.",
  "quest.7E37B0C668398893.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Set the \"},{\"text\":\"Incubator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:incubator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on a brazier with its salt, sulfur and mercury vessels beside it, one of each. An Iron Sulfur, a Mineral Salt and a Mercury Shard incubate into an \"},{\"text\":\"Iron Ingot\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:iron_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": three for every raw iron.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Three gold ingots, copper, stone and planks make the incubator; each vessel is four copper and three stone around the principle it holds.",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Hoppers fill the vessels, so one chest per principle keeps the line running.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.229F97FB2222BE89.title": "Sal Ammoniac Crystals",
  "quest.229F97FB2222BE89.quest_subtitle": "Ten times the acid, same water.",
  "quest.229F97FB2222BE89.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Sal Ammoniac Ore\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:sal_ammoniac_ore\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" runs through the Overworld's stone and deepslate, up to twenty veins a chunk, and Fortune works on it. One \"},{\"text\":\"crystal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:sal_ammoniac_crystal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in the accumulator turns a bucket of water into a whole bucket of solvent instead of a tenth.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "A Sal Ammoniac Bucket crafted alone gives the crystal back, and the bucket."
  ],
  "quest.256C856A88C80CFD.title": "Silk Touch, then acid",
  "quest.256C856A88C80CFD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The cauldron pays more for whole ores: an iron, gold or copper ore block gives five sulfur where the raw metal gives three, a diamond ore four, a lapis ore twelve. Mine with Silk Touch and dissolve the blocks.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.19BDB6F62D99F6FE.title": "A bucket, a hundred jobs",
  "quest.19BDB6F62D99F6FE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A liquefaction drinks only 10 mB of sal ammoniac, so one bucket in the cauldron dissolves a hundred raw ores: three hundred sulfurs. The accumulator never has to hurry.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1344D8BC7C0811D2.title": "Every metal in the pack",
  "quest.1344D8BC7C0811D2.quest_subtitle": "Mekanism's ores at alchemy's prices.",
  "quest.1344D8BC7C0811D2.quest_desc": [
    "The recipes read the common metal tags, so the cauldron also takes the pack's other raw metals: osmium, tin, lead, silver, nickel, zinc, aluminum, uranium and platinum, three sulfurs each. The incubator hands back the ingot Almost Unified picks."
  ],
  "quest.22AECFBCC6A23EE3.title": "Fermentation Vat",
  "quest.22AECFBCC6A23EE3.quest_subtitle": "A brewery with a doctorate.",
  "quest.22AECFBCC6A23EE3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Six copper ingots, a copper block, a barrel and any sulfur make the \"},{\"text\":\"Fermentation Vat\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:fermentation_vat\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It needs no fire: load a sulfur, sugar or a crop and water, then close it with \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.sneak\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" and an empty-handed right-click. It opens again when the \"},{\"text\":\"niter\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"30885D7DF78DB6DA\"}},{\"text\":\" is ready.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.30885D7DF78DB6DA.title": "Niter: the idea of a thing",
  "quest.30885D7DF78DB6DA.quest_subtitle": "Philosophy you can smelt.",
  "quest.30885D7DF78DB6DA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Sulfur is stubborn and won't turn into anything else. Fermented, it becomes niter, the idea of a material: \"},{\"text\":\"Common Metals Niter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:alchemical_niter_metals_common\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" instead of iron. Each iron sulfur, a sugar or a crop and 250 mB of water give one.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.21451CC7D8C2C18D.title": "Fermentation Starter",
  "quest.21451CC7D8C2C18D.quest_subtitle": "Sourdough for alchemists.",
  "quest.21451CC7D8C2C18D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A crop, a sugar and 100 mB of sal ammoniac ferment into twenty \"},{\"text\":\"Fermentation Starters\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:fermentation_starter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Each one stands in for the sugar or the crop of a niter fermentation: twenty niters for one sugar.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6EA24A0AF88E0747.title": "Vats that close themselves",
  "quest.6EA24A0AF88E0747.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A redstone signal closes a vat as soon as a valid recipe is inside, and a vat gives off a signal while its output holds something. A redstone torch between the two runs the loop: fill, close, finish, open, empty.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1EF21A76A090EE96.title": "Mercury Catalyst",
  "quest.1EF21A76A090EE96.quest_subtitle": "Shards in, energy out.",
  "quest.1EF21A76A090EE96.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Iron, gold, a block of quartz and a mercury shard make the \"},{\"text\":\"Mercury Catalyst\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:mercury_catalyst\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Feed it shards and it turns each into 800 mercury flux, 20 a tick; its sides go blue as it fills. An emitter set on it spends that flux.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2CAB85EC62D1FA63.title": "Mercury Crystal",
  "quest.2CAB85EC62D1FA63.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four shards pack into a \"},{\"text\":\"Mercury Crystal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:mercury_crystal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and unpack again. The catalyst gets 3,200 flux out of one, four shards' worth. The catalyst, the mercury vessel and the caloric emitter take either in their recipes; incubation and the logistics parts want shards.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6993A430469BB97D.title": "What's worth distilling",
  "quest.6993A430469BB97D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The distiller pays by value: ten stone, fifteen sand or three crops for a shard; five for an iron or copper ore block, twenty-five for a gold ore, fifty for a diamond or emerald ore or a block of Ancient Debris.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2362DF329027AE22.title": "Heat without fire",
  "quest.2362DF329027AE22.quest_subtitle": "Coal is for barbarians.",
  "quest.2362DF329027AE22.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Gold, stone, a mercury shard and a campfire or a lava bucket make the \"},{\"text\":\"Caloric Flux Emitter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:caloric_flux_emitter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.sneak\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" and right-click the apparatus to heat, then set the emitter on a catalyst: it keeps its target hot from up to eight blocks away, with no fuel and no brazier.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.16A48A9D4E0F7868.title": "Redstone on the flux",
  "quest.16A48A9D4E0F7868.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A redstone signal switches the caloric emitter off. A powered catalyst keeps converting shards but holds the flux, so one lever on the catalyst pauses whatever sits on it and nothing is lost.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2970F8DD054660BA.title": "Mercurial logistics",
  "quest.2970F8DD054660BA.quest_subtitle": "Items over copper wire.",
  "quest.2970F8DD054660BA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Copper over a mercury shard makes a \"},{\"text\":\"Mercurial Item Extractor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:logistics_item_extractor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; the shard over copper, an \"},{\"text\":\"Inserter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:logistics_item_inserter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Click them onto inventories, join them with \"},{\"text\":\"Mercurial Copper Wire\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:copper_wire\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", and items flow from every extractor to the inserters of that network.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"An extractor with a list filter is also the lightest way to pull items out of \"},{\"text\":\"Occultism's storage\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"59DC9600D63225DB\"}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.65BBC794F76CDB98.title": "Mercurial Wand",
  "quest.65BBC794F76CDB98.quest_subtitle": "A wrench with a philosophy degree.",
  "quest.65BBC794F76CDB98.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three sticks, copper and a shard. \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.sneak\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" and scroll to change modes: pick which side of its block an extractor pulls from, switch a node on or off, or set a frequency so only nodes with the same number talk to each other.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6461E2F56CB30B1E.title": "Connection Node",
  "quest.6461E2F56CB30B1E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A shard, an iron ingot and three bricks make three \"},{\"text\":\"Mercurial Connection Nodes\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:logistics_connector_node\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Stick them on any block to carry wire round corners and across distance: everything wired to them is one network, and extractors deal their items out in turns.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4988FE6DD038EA06.title": "Filters",
  "quest.4988FE6DD038EA06.quest_subtitle": "Paper, a shard and opinions.",
  "quest.4988FE6DD038EA06.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight paper around a shard make nine \"},{\"text\":\"List Filters\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:list_filter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; trade one paper for a feather and you get \"},{\"text\":\"Attribute Filters\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:attribute_filter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Right-click the air to set one up, then right-click an extractor or inserter to fit it. Buckets in a list filter filter fluids.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.033A1AD8988EFD53.title": "Fluids on the wire",
  "quest.033A1AD8988EFD53.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Blue dye on top of the extractor or inserter recipe makes the \"},{\"text\":\"Fluid Extractor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:logistics_fluid_extractor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and the \"},{\"text\":\"Fluid Inserter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:logistics_fluid_inserter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Draw from the sal ammoniac tank, feed the cauldrons and vats, and nobody carries buckets again.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.46E441D26E993D4C.title": "Wrong way round",
  "quest.46E441D26E993D4C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Made an extractor where you wanted an inserter? Put it alone in the crafting grid and it flips to the other one, and back.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.080F63B7A6A18AC7.title": "Mercury for the common store",
  "quest.080F63B7A6A18AC7.quest_subtitle": "Every apparatus drinks it.",
  "quest.080F63B7A6A18AC7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Thirty-two \"},{\"text\":\"Mercury Shards\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:mercury_shard\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for the common store, once a day. Incubators, catalysts and wires all run on them, and a quarry's leftover stone distills into plenty.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.19EF84624B37F27C.title": "Salt from dirt",
  "quest.19EF84624B37F27C.quest_subtitle": "Renewable, unlike your ores.",
  "quest.19EF84624B37F27C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Dirt, cobblestone, sand, gravel and clay carry traces of minerals: the oven turns each into \"},{\"text\":\"Strata Salt\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:alchemical_salt_strata\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", and five strata salts calcine into one Mineral Salt. Keep the ores for sulfur.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3C3EA38712290D0C.title": "Salt for living things",
  "quest.3C3EA38712290D0C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Logs, saplings, crops and leaves calcine into \"},{\"text\":\"Plant Salt\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:alchemical_salt_plant\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", and two plant salts into one \"},{\"text\":\"Creature Salt\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:alchemical_salt_creature\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Meat, bones and mob drops give creature salt straight away.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1AE994324DF11D20.title": "Water in your pocket",
  "quest.1AE994324DF11D20.quest_subtitle": "Lava you can pocket. What could go wrong?",
  "quest.1AE994324DF11D20.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Any alchemical salt crafted with a water or lava bucket crystallizes it: \"},{\"text\":\"Crystallized Water\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:crystallized_water\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and \"},{\"text\":\"Crystallized Lava\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:crystallized_lava\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" travel as items and craft back into a bucket. In the accumulator each melts into a full bucket; calcined, the lava gives eight strata salts.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4EF9978192D47174.title": "The right salt",
  "quest.4EF9978192D47174.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The salt has to match the sulfur: ores, gems, coal and redstone want Mineral Salt; logs and crops, Plant Salt; animal and mob drops, Creature Salt; earth and stone, Strata Salt. A blaze rod is incubated with creature salt, never with a diamond's.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.09B46C72FEF179E8.title": "A rod for ordinary ores",
  "quest.09B46C72FEF179E8.quest_subtitle": "Dowsing, except it works.",
  "quest.09B46C72FEF179E8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two glass and three sticks. \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.sneak\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" and right-click a block to attune the \"},{\"text\":\"Glass Divination Rod\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:divination_rod_t1\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", then hold right-click: it points to the nearest match. Iron, coal and the other common ores are in its reach; gold and diamonds need a better rod.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.55F5487F803EA5AE.title": "Rod habits",
  "quest.55F5487F803EA5AE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A rod that found something turns purple. A right-click without holding points to the last find again and costs no durability; hold it to search anew.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.59C862440444FF26.title": "Amethyst Divination Rod",
  "quest.59C862440444FF26.quest_subtitle": "The rod that finds rods.",
  "quest.59C862440444FF26.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Glass, sticks and purple dye: no amethyst needed. The \"},{\"text\":\"Amethyst Divination Rod\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:amethyst_divination_rod\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" comes attuned to \"},{\"text\":\"Budding Amethyst\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:budding_amethyst\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", and every better rod asks for an \"},{\"text\":\"Amethyst Shard\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:amethyst_shard\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7D3637F5F5FD6808.title": "Iron Divination Rod",
  "quest.7D3637F5F5FD6808.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Glass, a gold nugget, an amethyst shard and a stick. The \"},{\"text\":\"Iron Divination Rod\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:divination_rod_t2\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" lasts longer and reaches the rarer ores, gold among them, and obsidian too.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5FD84443AFEE1716.title": "Diamond Divination Rod",
  "quest.5FD84443AFEE1716.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Glass, a diamond, nether quartz and an amethyst shard. The \"},{\"text\":\"Diamond Divination Rod\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:divination_rod_t3\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" finds the high-tier ores, diamonds included, and wears much slower.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2564C149CC2D0F22.title": "Netherite Divination Rod",
  "quest.2564C149CC2D0F22.quest_subtitle": "It wants the ore, not the scrap.",
  "quest.2564C149CC2D0F22.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Glass, a blaze rod, an amethyst shard and a whole block of \"},{\"text\":\"Ancient Debris\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:ancient_debris\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". The \"},{\"text\":\"Netherite Divination Rod\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:divination_rod_t4\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" finds ores of any tier and barely wears.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.16600D4AB59B2501.title": "Rods that already know",
  "quest.16600D4AB59B2501.quest_subtitle": "Pre-attuned, no second opinions.",
  "quest.16600D4AB59B2501.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Craft a rod with a sulfur in place of a stick and it comes attuned to that sulfur's ore: \"},{\"text\":\"Iron Sulfur\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:alchemical_sulfur_iron\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" makes a \"},{\"text\":\"Divination Rod: Common Materials\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:sulfur_attuned_divination_rod_common\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" that finds iron. It can't be re-attuned, but it lasts far longer. Copper or coal sulfur makes the abundant one.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.34410AA11D616C6F.title": "Pre-attuned: rare",
  "quest.34410AA11D616C6F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A rare sulfur, glass, a stick and an amethyst shard: \"},{\"text\":\"Gold Sulfur\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:alchemical_sulfur_gold\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" makes a \"},{\"text\":\"Divination Rod: Rare Materials\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:sulfur_attuned_divination_rod_rare\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" locked on gold. Any rare sulfur works the same way.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.229CF914EE735453.title": "Pre-attuned: precious",
  "quest.229CF914EE735453.quest_subtitle": "A diamond to find diamonds.",
  "quest.229CF914EE735453.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A precious sulfur, glass, a diamond and an amethyst shard: \"},{\"text\":\"Diamond Sulfur\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:alchemical_sulfur_diamond\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" makes a \"},{\"text\":\"Divination Rod: Precious Materials\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:sulfur_attuned_divination_rod_precious\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", the toughest of the pre-attuned rods, locked on diamonds.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7AFB72ECB64931DE.title": "Sulfuric Flux Emitter",
  "quest.7AFB72ECB64931DE.quest_subtitle": "The soul, sent by wire.",
  "quest.7AFB72ECB64931DE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Gold, stone, any sulfur, a sal ammoniac crystal and, in this pack, a \"},{\"text\":\"Containment Seal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:containment_seal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (act IV) in the bottom row. Right-click the reformation pedestals with the \"},{\"text\":\"emitter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:sulfuric_flux_emitter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and set it on a catalyst, within eight blocks of them.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Right-click the placed emitter to check its links. If a pedestal is missing, break the emitter, link it again and put it back."
  ],
  "quest.6104E3D2E6C0C579.title": "Why transmutation waits",
  "quest.6104E3D2E6C0C579.quest_desc": [
    "Reformation, transmutation and exaltation together copy nearly any material, diamonds and netherite included, so the pack ties the emitter to the Containment Seal like its other replication tools. Refining ores stays free from the start."
  ],
  "quest.60577799DFED02A7.title": "The Reformation Array",
  "quest.60577799DFED02A7.quest_subtitle": "Alchemy that needs the furniture just so.",
  "quest.60577799DFED02A7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"No fixed shape: a \"},{\"text\":\"Target Pedestal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:reformation_target_pedestal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" holds the sulfur you want more of and is never used up, \"},{\"text\":\"Source Pedestals\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:reformation_source_pedestal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" hold what gets consumed, and one \"},{\"text\":\"Result Pedestal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:reformation_result_pedestal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" collects the copies. Keep them within a few blocks of each other.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "All three are built on blackstone, so the Nether comes first."
  ],
  "quest.2064E0CCFA2BFEA8.title": "Room for eight",
  "quest.2064E0CCFA2BFEA8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Build more source pedestals than you think you need: the expensive recipes spread their sources over up to eight pedestals, sometimes with several sulfurs on each. The recipe viewer shows exactly how many.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3EC4794CDE267F83.title": "The flux budget",
  "quest.3EC4794CDE267F83.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A reformation costs 50 mercury flux for abundant sulfurs, 100 for common ones, 150 for rare and 200 for precious. At 800 flux a shard, one shard pays for four diamonds.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.594FA098977EB3EF.title": "Lapis into quartz",
  "quest.594FA098977EB3EF.quest_subtitle": "Same type, same tier, new face.",
  "quest.594FA098977EB3EF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Reformation swaps sulfurs of the same type and tier. Put a \"},{\"text\":\"Quartz Sulfur\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:alchemical_sulfur_quartz\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on the target and \"},{\"text\":\"Lapis Sulfur\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:alchemical_sulfur_lapis\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on the sources: each lapis becomes one more quartz for 100 flux. Certus quartz sits in the same tier, if AE2 is calling.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4975298B6C4B378C.title": "Emeralds into diamonds",
  "quest.4975298B6C4B378C.quest_subtitle": "The villagers never saw it coming.",
  "quest.4975298B6C4B378C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Diamond and emerald share the precious gem tier. With a \"},{\"text\":\"Diamond Sulfur\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:alchemical_sulfur_diamond\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on the target, every emerald sulfur on the sources turns into another for 200 flux: the villagers pay in emeralds and you cash in diamonds.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.60135ED4B0E2DC66.title": "Blaze rods from slime",
  "quest.60135ED4B0E2DC66.quest_subtitle": "Zombie leftovers, now with ambition.",
  "quest.60135ED4B0E2DC66.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Mob drops have tiers too. Ender pearls, blaze rods, slimeballs, phantom membranes and magma cream are all common: with a \"},{\"text\":\"Blaze Rod Sulfur\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:alchemical_sulfur_blaze_rod\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on the target, slime sulfur turns into blaze rods. Rotten flesh, string, bone and gunpowder swap among themselves the same way.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Animal drops follow the same rule: a rabbit's foot and a turtle scute share the rare tier, so rabbits pay for turtle helmets. Everything from a creature comes back out of the incubator with Creature Salt."
  ],
  "quest.045C5ED3C0D5D418.title": "Any wood from oak",
  "quest.045C5ED3C0D5D418.quest_subtitle": "A lumberjack who never leaves the lab.",
  "quest.045C5ED3C0D5D418.quest_desc": [
    "Logs and crops are abundant tiers of their own and reform for 50 flux. With a birch, cherry or mangrove sulfur on the target, oak sulfur turns into that wood; with a coffee bean sulfur there, wheat does the same. Plant Salt brings them back out of the incubator."
  ],
  "quest.686FBC454CFADC18.title": "Quartz into iron",
  "quest.686FBC454CFADC18.quest_subtitle": "Two metals for every gem.",
  "quest.686FBC454CFADC18.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Transmutation changes the type. Ferment quartz sulfur into \"},{\"text\":\"Common Gems Niter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:alchemical_niter_gems_common\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and reform it against a Common Metals Niter target, two metal niters per gem niter; then reform those against an Iron Sulfur target. Two metals are worth one gem, and two other minerals one metal.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3DB00AF14446AD73.title": "Gold that grows on trees",
  "quest.3DB00AF14446AD73.quest_subtitle": "The goose had a point after all.",
  "quest.3DB00AF14446AD73.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Charcoal counts as a mineral: its \"},{\"text\":\"Coal Sulfur\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:alchemical_sulfur_coals\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" ferments into \"},{\"text\":\"Abundant Other Minerals Niter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:alchemical_niter_other_minerals_abundant\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Transmute and exalt from there and a tree farm feeds gold, or diamonds, forever. Slowly.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.06D05CB9F8D2BA6F.title": "Digestion Vat",
  "quest.06D05CB9F8D2BA6F.quest_subtitle": "Slow food for niter.",
  "quest.06D05CB9F8D2BA6F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A sal ammoniac crystal, two gold ingots, a decorated pot and three sandstone make the \"},{\"text\":\"Digestion Vat\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:digestion_vat\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Like the fermentation vat it works closed and loads open. It moves niter between tiers: up with a catalyst, down for free.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2D97536F8A6F5FA6.title": "Purified Gold",
  "quest.2D97536F8A6F5FA6.quest_subtitle": "Salt scrubs gold. Don't ask.",
  "quest.2D97536F8A6F5FA6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"One \"},{\"text\":\"Gold Ingot\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:gold_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", any alchemical salt and a water bucket digest into twenty \"},{\"text\":\"Purified Gold\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:purified_gold\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": the salt draws the impurities out. Every upward digestion burns one.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0F41A90BDD204B8C.title": "Four into one",
  "quest.0F41A90BDD204B8C.quest_subtitle": "Iron, promoted.",
  "quest.0F41A90BDD204B8C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Exaltation climbs tiers. Four Common Metals Niter, a Purified Gold and 15 mB of sal ammoniac digest into one \"},{\"text\":\"Rare Metals Niter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:alchemical_niter_metals_rare\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in twenty seconds. Load the vat in bulk and it repeats until something runs out.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.710AF1C214920C73.title": "Past gold",
  "quest.710AF1C214920C73.quest_subtitle": "Netherite, the long way round.",
  "quest.710AF1C214920C73.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four Rare Metals Niter digest into one \"},{\"text\":\"Precious Metals Niter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:alchemical_niter_metals_precious\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", and precious is netherite's tier. Sixteen niters of iron, a Netherite Sulfur on the target, and the incubator hands you a \"},{\"text\":\"Netherite Ingot\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:netherite_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "task.2CA3C823CBC92C53.title": "Look at your Sulfuric Flux Emitter",
  "quest.4297D7DC09942CDB.title": "The Great Work",
  "quest.4297D7DC09942CDB.quest_subtitle": "Base metal in, sun out.",
  "quest.4297D7DC09942CDB.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Put a \"},{\"text\":\"Gold Sulfur\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"theurgy:alchemical_sulfur_gold\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on the target and Rare Metals Niter on the sources, and let the emitter work: every niter becomes gold sulfur, and the incubator makes it gold. Iron in, gold out: the oldest promise in alchemy, kept.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1F234AE79532CF15.title": "A doctorate in dirt",
  "quest.1F234AE79532CF15.quest_subtitle": "Somebody had to try.",
  "quest.1F234AE79532CF15.quest_desc": [
    "You fermented dirt. Sixteen of these reform into one Abundant Gems Niter, and three digestions later that's a precious gem: a diamond is 1,024 dirt niters away."
  ],
  "reward.69F74C2B1B425B06.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.6549045E0C681D42.title": "Scrambled",
  "quest.6549045E0C681D42.quest_subtitle": "The only egg in the world, in acid.",
  "quest.6549045E0C681D42.quest_desc": [
    "You dissolved the Dragon Egg, and in this pack there's no way back: the incubator no longer rebuilds eggs or Nether Stars from their sulfur. Another egg means another Ender Dragon."
  ],
  "reward.3C67DA3703B42AD8.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.0D77AC225CBA9BD9.title": "Acid in acid",
  "quest.0D77AC225CBA9BD9.quest_subtitle": "Somebody had to.",
  "quest.0D77AC225CBA9BD9.quest_desc": [
    "You dissolved sal ammoniac in sal ammoniac. It works: a crystal gives one sulfur, an ore block six, and the result counts as an abundant gem. The acid is not amused."
  ],
  "reward.13416D66221AFE7A.title": "Secret found",
  "image.048F5B76CA12AD21.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Divination\",\"color\":\"#EBCB4F\"}]",
  "image.558F2E8215CE1C96.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Salts\",\"color\":\"#EBCB4F\"}]",
  "image.487056F7C6C05DE3.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Mercurial logistics\",\"color\":\"#EBCB4F\"}]",
  "image.161798EB71045D16.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Same tier, new face\",\"color\":\"#EBCB4F\"}]",
  "image.2BC52EEFD7282976.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Heat by flux\",\"color\":\"#EBCB4F\"}]",
  "image.026F7010E06B8DF0.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Theurgy\",\"color\":\"#F3EEDF\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.698F951F9810A0BD.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"solve et coagula\",\"color\":\"#A7B7C6\",\"font\":\"minecraft:alt\"}]",
  "image.35A37F5D0F282340.title": "Back to the Sun of Heliodor",
  "image.0F2BE617FDF32064.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Sulfur · soul\",\"color\":\"#EBCB4F\"}]",
  "image.56A9A1BA0F009B85.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Salt · body\",\"color\":\"#F3EEDF\"}]",
  "image.39D3DD454B0B55E6.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Mercury · spirit\",\"color\":\"#A7B7C6\"}]",
  "chapter.7FD8A9B267B7C9D3.title": "Iron's Spells · The Arcane Anvil",
  "chapter.7FD8A9B267B7C9D3.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Eight runes around one orb: mithril, three bosses, the ancient books, battlemage gear, rings and Iron's Gems 'n Jewelry."
  ],
  "quest.49A652D6796F6545.title": "The Arcane Anvil",
  "quest.49A652D6796F6545.quest_subtitle": "Heavy, purple and worth every block.",
  "quest.49A652D6796F6545.quest_desc": [
    "Three amethyst blocks over a diamond, an anvil and two polished deepslate. It levels scrolls with ink, locks spells into weapons, fits upgrade orbs into armour and books, and attunes rings."
  ],
  "quest.226BC5F8AF53B7AC.title": "One level at a time",
  "quest.226BC5F8AF53B7AC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A scroll plus one bottle of the ink its next level needs gives the same scroll a level higher. A unique book plus a higher scroll of one of its locked spells raises that spell instead.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6F6D8FBB1ADF111A.title": "A spell on a sword",
  "quest.6F6D8FBB1ADF111A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A weapon plus a scroll imbues it with that spell, cast from the weapon itself. Imbued weapons still spend mana, on half the usual cooldown, and a Shriving Stone at the anvil takes the spell back off.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0F20910E4E8C2CC8.title": "Arcane Ingot",
  "quest.0F20910E4E8C2CC8.quest_subtitle": "Metal with a mind of its own.",
  "quest.0F20910E4E8C2CC8.quest_desc": [
    "Eight Arcane Essence around an iron, copper or gold ingot. Upgrade orbs, rings of mana, weapon parts and portal frames all start here."
  ],
  "quest.4843FD54806C56BA.title": "The Empty Upgrade Orb",
  "quest.4843FD54806C56BA.quest_subtitle": "A blank waiting for a rune.",
  "quest.4843FD54806C56BA.quest_desc": [
    "Four Arcane Ingots, four Cinder Essence and a Mithril Ingot. Ring it with eight runes of one kind and it becomes that orb; at the anvil an orb adds its bonus to armour or a spell book, three upgrades per item at most."
  ],
  "quest.6ABD80D961145D42.title": "Orbs for any school",
  "quest.6ABD80D961145D42.quest_subtitle": "One size fits all.",
  "quest.6ABD80D961145D42.quest_desc": [
    "Eight Arcane Runes (essence) make the Mana orb, +50 max mana; eight Recovery Runes (phantom membrane) the Cooldown orb, 5% shorter cooldowns; eight Protective Runes (pufferfish) the Protection orb, 5% spell resistance. School orbs add 5% to their school."
  ],
  "quest.32107FDAB27722D9.title": "Room for one more",
  "quest.32107FDAB27722D9.quest_subtitle": "Books, now with an extension.",
  "quest.32107FDAB27722D9.quest_desc": [
    "Six Hogskin and three Arcane Cloth make a Lesser Spell Slot Improvement. At the anvil it adds a slot to a spell book, up to 12."
  ],
  "quest.4354A593903826B0.title": "Shriving Stone",
  "quest.4354A593903826B0.quest_subtitle": "Undo, in rock form.",
  "quest.4354A593903826B0.quest_desc": [
    "Raw iron and an amethyst shard, shapeless. At the anvil it strips an item's imbued spell and upgrades; in a crafting grid it wipes an inscribed rune back to a Blank Runestone."
  ],
  "quest.53C0612C3F0710ED.title": "Legendary Ink",
  "quest.53C0612C3F0710ED.quest_subtitle": "Premium, and priced like it.",
  "quest.53C0612C3F0710ED.quest_desc": [
    "Four bottles of Epic Ink and an amethyst shard in the cauldron, or a boss vault. Only legendary ink writes a spell's top levels, and some spells have several legendary levels that only the anvil reaches."
  ],
  "quest.1A797F17F13CB152.title": "Ingots for the forge-house",
  "quest.1A797F17F13CB152.quest_subtitle": "Heavy donations welcome.",
  "quest.1A797F17F13CB152.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight \"},{\"text\":\"Arcane Ingots\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"irons_spellbooks:arcane_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for the common store, once a day: sixty-four essence and eight plain ingots of work.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2C5C02FD1DB072D3.title": "Mithril",
  "quest.2C5C02FD1DB072D3.quest_subtitle": "Deep, dark and fussy.",
  "quest.2C5C02FD1DB072D3.quest_desc": [
    "Mithril ore hides between Y -63 and -38, never touching air, and only a netherite pickaxe mines it. Blast the Raw Mithril into scrap for 40 experience each; four scrap make an ingot."
  ],
  "quest.535AE19EBA0DBC90.title": "Mithril Weave",
  "quest.535AE19EBA0DBC90.quest_subtitle": "Chainmail's fancy cousin.",
  "quest.535AE19EBA0DBC90.quest_desc": [
    "Five mithril ingots checkered with four chains. The late chestplates and the Boots of Speed are woven from it."
  ],
  "quest.3AA7FEA28E043C1A.title": "Weapon Parts",
  "quest.3AA7FEA28E043C1A.quest_subtitle": "Some assembly required.",
  "quest.3AA7FEA28E043C1A.quest_desc": [
    "Three mithril and two Arcane Ingots make Weapon Parts, the hilt of every mage blade. Two mithril and two diamonds on them make the Spellbreaker; amethyst and chains, the Amethyst Rapier."
  ],
  "quest.4220639AB1AC0339.title": "Portal Frames",
  "quest.4220639AB1AC0339.quest_subtitle": "Two doors, no hallway.",
  "quest.4220639AB1AC0339.quest_desc": [
    "Two mithril ingots, four Arcane Ingots and an ender pearl make two frames. Place both and link them with the Portal spell: a two-way gate that stays."
  ],
  "quest.0FC4D20ED2316AA2.title": "Seven forbidden spells",
  "quest.0FC4D20ED2316AA2.quest_subtitle": "Choose wisely. Or at least choose.",
  "quest.0FC4D20ED2316AA2.quest_desc": [
    "Using an Eldritch Manuscript opens a circle of seven spells: Abyssal Shroud, Eldritch Blast, Planar Sight, Pocket Dimension, Sculk Tentacles, Sonic Boom and Telekinesis. Press and hold one to learn it; each costs a manuscript, and only a learned one can be forged or cast."
  ],
  "task.3D098023340F86F2.title": "Enter your pocket dimension",
  "task.5AABCBE3D6C595ED.title": "Look at the frame that leads back",
  "quest.63CA28457AF2DC41.title": "A room off the map",
  "quest.63CA28457AF2DC41.quest_subtitle": "No rent, no neighbours, no windows.",
  "quest.63CA28457AF2DC41.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Pocket Dimension is a Legendary Eldritch spell: forge its scroll with \"},{\"text\":\"Legendary Ink\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"irons_spellbooks:legendary_ink\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and an echo shard, or find one. Cast it out of combat, 300 mana and two seconds of charge, and you step into a room that is yours alone; the frame inside walks you back to where you cast.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.63834E893D842A05.title": "Seven by seven",
  "quest.63834E893D842A05.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The room is a seven-by-seven voidstone floor under a shaft 27 blocks high, walled in barrier: build up, not out. It is the same room every time, so whatever you leave there stays.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2961D2D1C2B5820A.title": "House rules",
  "quest.2961D2D1C2B5820A.quest_subtitle": "Tidy, dark and pearl-proof.",
  "quest.2961D2D1C2B5820A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Inside, ender pearls and chorus fruit fail and the spell won't cast again. Beds, respawn anchors, waystones, warp plates, spatial pylons and portal frames refuse to be placed: the frame is the way out.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1F175D1AB007C933.title": "The Wayward Compass",
  "quest.1F175D1AB007C933.quest_subtitle": "The soul inside wants to go home.",
  "quest.1F175D1AB007C933.quest_desc": [
    "Four Arcane Essence, four iron ingots and a soul lantern. The trapped soul points to the nearest Catacombs; if none is loaded yet, use it to search."
  ],
  "task.004EABF345719E90.title": "Enter the Catacombs",
  "quest.4F473C051C7DE50A.title": "The Catacombs",
  "quest.4F473C051C7DE50A.quest_subtitle": "Mind the zombies. And the stairs.",
  "quest.4F473C051C7DE50A.quest_desc": [
    "Buried under hills, forests, taigas and jungles: halls of Catacombs Zombies, cursed armour stands and a Necromancer. In the deepest one lies a skeleton that isn't finished with you."
  ],
  "task.18C62E708195E1D7.title": "Defeat the Dead King",
  "quest.122E552959C3FE9C.title": "The Dead King",
  "quest.122E552959C3FE9C.quest_subtitle": "Long live the king. Unfortunately.",
  "quest.122E552959C3FE9C.quest_desc": [
    "Hit or touch the skeleton in the deepest hall and the Dead King rises, calling the dead around him. He drops 28 to 45 Arcane Essence and, half the time, the Blood Staff or the Necronomicon; every player who fought gets a Bone Key."
  ],
  "quest.6DD225004EEEF7BC.title": "Bone Vault and Phylactery",
  "quest.6DD225004EEEF7BC.quest_subtitle": "Keys, shards and a rematch.",
  "quest.6DD225004EEEF7BC.quest_desc": [
    "A Bone Key opens the catacombs' Bone Vault once per player: rare ink, blood, a scroll and one to three Phylactery Shards. Eight shards around a soul lantern make the Phylactery; used on the King's soul, he rises again."
  ],
  "task.3C46EB8CB979B269.title": "Take the Necronomicon",
  "quest.3201610D632C8592.title": "Necronomicon",
  "quest.3201610D632C8592.quest_subtitle": "Do not read aloud.",
  "quest.3201610D632C8592.quest_desc": [
    "The Dead King's own tome: Blood Slash, Blood Step, Ray of Siphoning and Blaze Storm locked at level 5, six slots, 200 mana and two extra levels to Raise Dead."
  ],
  "reward.1F34F1284E3F8E9C.title": "Secret found",
  "task.66A6B15B795A7559.title": "Take the Blood Staff",
  "quest.5BD141F9B2023AF3.title": "Staff of Blood",
  "quest.5BD141F9B2023AF3.quest_subtitle": "Pried from bony fingers.",
  "quest.5BD141F9B2023AF3.quest_desc": [
    "The Dead King's scepter: +15% blood power, +10% summon damage and 5% spell power, and it casts your selected spell like any staff."
  ],
  "reward.5B733CC232A53B81.title": "Secret found",
  "task.18D95A7AC8C1A021.title": "Find the Citadel",
  "quest.52FDDD1B3A854FDE.title": "The Citadel",
  "quest.52FDDD1B3A854FDE.quest_subtitle": "Nether real estate, poorly maintained.",
  "quest.52FDDD1B3A854FDE.quest_desc": [
    "A ruined fortress in the Nether's bastion biomes, kept by Ancient Knights and cursed armour. Five paper, two Ancient Knowledge Fragments and two Cinder Essence make a Furled Map that leads there."
  ],
  "quest.4DE9435551F7A808.title": "The Cinderous Soulcaller",
  "quest.4DE9435551F7A808.quest_subtitle": "Ring twice for Tyros.",
  "quest.4DE9435551F7A808.quest_desc": [
    "Six Cinder Essence, two netherite scraps and an echo shard. Rung near the Citadel's Cinderous Soul Rune, it calls up what's left of Tyros; anywhere else, nothing echoes back."
  ],
  "task.0D04066AB5ECE331.title": "Defeat the Echo of Tyros",
  "quest.04CB9B7F34B0FA10.title": "Echo of Tyros",
  "quest.04CB9B7F34B0FA10.quest_subtitle": "The first flamebearer still burns.",
  "quest.04CB9B7F34B0FA10.quest_desc": [
    "The echo of the First Flamebearer fights with walls of fire, magma and swarms of fiery daggers. It drops a Divine Soulshard, 8 to 16 Cinder Essence, two piles of Arcane Essence and, half the time, the Decrepit Scythe or the Signet of the Betrayer."
  ],
  "quest.1886A3EFD833D5C4.title": "The Cinderous Vault",
  "quest.1886A3EFD833D5C4.quest_subtitle": "Keys, fire and a pyrium surprise.",
  "quest.1886A3EFD833D5C4.quest_desc": [
    "Every player who fought Tyros gets a Decrepit Key for the Citadel's vault: always a Pyrium Ingot, plus rare ink, scrolls, runes and mithril or netherite scrap.",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A Pyrium Ingot in a blast furnace comes out as five Ancient Debris.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.67CB46EF1DB1D0FE.title": "The Pyrium Staff",
  "quest.67CB46EF1DB1D0FE.quest_subtitle": "Hot to the touch. On purpose.",
  "quest.67CB46EF1DB1D0FE.quest_desc": [
    "Two Pyrium Ingots, an Arcane Cloth and a netherite ingot: +15% fire power, 10% shorter casts and 5% spell power, and it casts your selected spell."
  ],
  "quest.5426009F4BB82AC4.title": "Timeless Slurry",
  "quest.5426009F4BB82AC4.quest_subtitle": "Rust remover, industrial strength.",
  "quest.5426009F4BB82AC4.quest_desc": [
    "A Mundane Potion and an echo shard brew Timeless Slurry in the cauldron. At a smithing table it restores relics with a Pyrium Ingot: the Decrepit Scythe becomes the Hellrazor, a Decrepit Flamberge the Legionnaire Flamberge."
  ],
  "task.564579CE49A08640.title": "Find an Ice Spider Den",
  "quest.6E25AEDA2CC2E9DD.title": "The Infested Ruin",
  "quest.6E25AEDA2CC2E9DD.quest_subtitle": "Webs, snow and a very large egg.",
  "quest.6E25AEDA2CC2E9DD.quest_desc": [
    "Ice Spider dens hide in snowy and icy biomes away from mountains and oceans; two Frozen Bones, four cobwebs and an Arcane Cloth make a Furled Map to one. Break an egg inside and its mother comes to see who did it."
  ],
  "task.08FCBF0019513A5D.title": "Defeat the Ice Spider",
  "quest.4CB0382E9F2BD114.title": "The Ice Spider",
  "quest.4CB0382E9F2BD114.quest_subtitle": "Eight legs, zero chill.",
  "quest.4CB0382E9F2BD114.quest_desc": [
    "A giant spider that pounces, grapples and leaps back out of reach. It drops 4 to 16 Arcane Essence, string and, four times in ten, an Icy Fang. When it snows, one may come hunting you on its own."
  ],
  "quest.29849C349E293C7F.title": "The Frostbranded Book",
  "quest.29849C349E293C7F.quest_subtitle": "Cold to the touch, as advertised.",
  "quest.29849C349E293C7F.quest_desc": [
    "An Icy Fang in cauldron water brews Ice Venom; three vials, two mithril scraps, a Ruined Book and three Arcane Cloth make the book. Twelve slots, 10% ice power and 200 mana."
  ],
  "quest.5407D7E066F81FA6.title": "The Ice Staff",
  "quest.5407D7E066F81FA6.quest_subtitle": "Mournful, but effective.",
  "quest.5407D7E066F81FA6.quest_desc": [
    "Four Frozen Bones and three Arcane Ingots make the Frosted Helve; add the Permafrost Shard from the Icebreaker. +15% ice power, 25% mana regeneration and 5% spell power."
  ],
  "quest.134503AEA3A84F8C.title": "Breakfast of champions",
  "quest.134503AEA3A84F8C.quest_subtitle": "Tastes like revenge.",
  "quest.134503AEA3A84F8C.quest_desc": [
    "Silk Touch on an egg that hadn't frosted over, then honey, sweet berries and a bowl, cooked on a campfire. Nobody asked, and you did it anyway."
  ],
  "reward.2FFAD0EBA1DD4979.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.3C51E9A3764B335F.title": "The Ruined Book",
  "quest.3C51E9A3764B335F.quest_subtitle": "Water damage from before the Warden.",
  "quest.3C51E9A3764B335F.quest_desc": [
    "Found in Ancient Cities, and now and then on a Citadel bookshelf. Every late spell book starts from one: the Ancient Codex, the Dragonskin, the Vampiric and the Frostbranded."
  ],
  "quest.2D520DA7AC1E66AF.title": "The Dragonskin Spell Book",
  "quest.2D520DA7AC1E66AF.quest_subtitle": "Ethically sourced. Probably.",
  "quest.2D520DA7AC1E66AF.quest_desc": [
    "Six Dragonskin, two obsidian and a Ruined Book: twelve slots, 10% ender power and 200 mana. Each Ender Dragon kill drops six to ten skins."
  ],
  "quest.40F8300A2D30AD7E.title": "The Vampiric Spell Book",
  "quest.40F8300A2D30AD7E.quest_subtitle": "A piece of yourself, bound in leather.",
  "quest.40F8300A2D30AD7E.quest_desc": [
    "Soak Hogskin in a cauldron of blood for Bloody Vellum; four of it, two Arcane Ingots and a Ruined Book make the book. Ten slots, 10% blood power, 10% spell resistance and 200 mana."
  ],
  "quest.6095C571C61BE84F.title": "The Ancient Codex",
  "quest.6095C571C61BE84F.quest_subtitle": "Restored, not rewritten.",
  "quest.6095C571C61BE84F.quest_desc": [
    "A netherite ingot, a Ruined Book, four Arcane Cloth, two Blood Vials and a Bottle o' Lightning restore the Ancient Codex: twelve slots, 200 mana and 20% shorter cooldowns, the best book two hands can make.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "A battle mage's kit: the Codex with three orbs in it, school armour with three each, a Ring of Mana and a Ring of Recovery, and a staff for quick casts.",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The last page is blank, and signed \"},{\"text\":\"iron\",\"color\":\"#B98CFF\",\"font\":\"minecraft:alt\"},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6DCA9D2256EC5E7E.title": "Netherite Battlemage",
  "quest.6DCA9D2256EC5E7E.quest_subtitle": "Robes that stop a sword.",
  "quest.6DCA9D2256EC5E7E.quest_desc": [
    "A netherite upgrade template and a netherite ingot on each wizard piece, at the smithing table. The same 125 mana and 5% spell power per piece, with far more armour than cloth."
  ],
  "quest.12AE111657AC7782.title": "The Infernal Sorcerer",
  "quest.12AE111657AC7782.quest_subtitle": "Three stacks and it goes boom.",
  "quest.12AE111657AC7782.quest_desc": [
    "A Pyromancer robe, the Divine Soulshard from Tyros, two Mithril Weave and two Pyrium Ingots: +150 mana and 10% spell power. Fire spells stack Immolation on their target, and at three stacks it explodes and spreads."
  ],
  "quest.0F049277E5D4B154.title": "The Lightbringer",
  "quest.0F049277E5D4B154.quest_subtitle": "Shine responsibly.",
  "quest.0F049277E5D4B154.quest_desc": [
    "A Priest robe, a Divine Soulshard, three Mithril Weave and four gold ingots make the Lightbringer Chestplate: +150 mana and 10% spell power for the holy school's front line."
  ],
  "quest.6A48B3ADC1F0474F.title": "Boots of Speed",
  "quest.6A48B3ADC1F0474F.quest_subtitle": "Cast and run. Mostly run.",
  "quest.6A48B3ADC1F0474F.quest_desc": [
    "Archevoker boots, a Mithril Weave, two feathers and a Divine Soulshard: +150 mana, 10% spell power, 25% movement speed and 60% more speed while casting."
  ],
  "task.5437C0039DA7EADB.title": "Make a Rod o' Lightning",
  "quest.6ADFA6C54B457EEA.title": "Shocking Discovery",
  "quest.6ADFA6C54B457EEA.quest_subtitle": "Hopefully you survived.",
  "quest.6ADFA6C54B457EEA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight Bottles o' Lightning around a copper block make an Energized Core; used on a lightning rod in a thunderstorm, the sky answers and the rod becomes a \"},{\"text\":\"Rod o' Lightning\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"irons_spellbooks:lightning_rod\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", +15% lightning power and 10% shorter cooldowns.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.23E691495FC90F5F.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.17C6528A2DBACDC7.title": "Ring of Mana",
  "quest.17C6528A2DBACDC7.quest_subtitle": "A hundred reasons to wear it.",
  "quest.17C6528A2DBACDC7.quest_desc": [
    "Four Arcane Ingots and a diamond: +100 max mana in a ring slot. Loot and the Wandering Trader also turn up Silver Rings, worth 25."
  ],
  "quest.758939CDF2092C17.title": "Rings of the trade",
  "quest.758939CDF2092C17.quest_subtitle": "Faster, then faster again.",
  "quest.758939CDF2092C17.quest_desc": [
    "A Mithril Scrap ringed by four copper ingots makes the Ring of Recovery, 15% shorter cooldowns; an amethyst shard beside a scrap makes the Ring of Expediency, 15% shorter casts."
  ],
  "quest.2DC8D08D5613ECB6.title": "Wards",
  "quest.2DC8D08D5613ECB6.quest_subtitle": "Immunity, one ring at a time.",
  "quest.2DC8D08D5613ECB6.quest_desc": [
    "Each on a Mithril Scrap: four Cinder Essence make the Fireward Ring, a Permafrost Shard the Frostward, a Nature Rune the Poisonward. Fire, freezing and poison stop hurting."
  ],
  "quest.08748D559A2AEDD8.title": "An unattuned ring",
  "quest.08748D559A2AEDD8.quest_subtitle": "Bring your own spell.",
  "quest.08748D559A2AEDD8.quest_desc": [
    "A bucket and a Mithril Scrap make an unattuned Ring of Affinity. At the Arcane Anvil a scroll attunes it to that spell, which then casts one level higher."
  ],
  "quest.09FD5F6876EBD90E.title": "The Conjurer's Talisman",
  "quest.09FD5F6876EBD90E.quest_subtitle": "For people with a lot of friends.",
  "quest.09FD5F6876EBD90E.quest_desc": [
    "A skeleton skull, three string and a Mithril Scrap: +15% summon damage. Four Bloody Vellum and an Arcane Rune make it Greater, and summons that time out stop going on cooldown."
  ],
  "quest.6AD961EF77B52800.title": "The Jewelcrafting Station",
  "quest.6AD961EF77B52800.quest_subtitle": "Bling, with stats.",
  "quest.6AD961EF77B52800.quest_desc": [
    "Two copper ingots over four planks; a book and one more copper make its guide, «Jewelcrafting and You». Pick a pattern, lay a material in each part, and the station makes the ring or amulet."
  ],
  "quest.483693B0BA94F259.title": "A ring and a chain",
  "quest.483693B0BA94F259.quest_subtitle": "Start simple. Stay shiny.",
  "quest.483693B0BA94F259.quest_desc": [
    "Four patterns come unlocked: Simple Ring, Gemset Ring, Simple Chain and Simple Amulet. Every material brings its own bonus: iron and diamond add armour, copper attack speed, gold mining speed, ruby health."
  ],
  "quest.7BB1F830FFEAE450.title": "The primary part",
  "quest.7BB1F830FFEAE450.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"One part of each pattern is its primary part, and that material's quality scales every bonus on the piece: copper 0.5, iron 0.75, gold 1.5, diamond and the gems 2. Some patterns, like Tearstone or Haggling, multiply quality again.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2DCA6BC6C8B7FF81.title": "Seven new gems",
  "quest.2DCA6BC6C8B7FF81.quest_subtitle": "Collect them all. Or just the pretty ones.",
  "quest.2DCA6BC6C8B7FF81.quest_desc": [
    "Ruby, sapphire, topaz, moonstone, peridot, onyx and garnet turn up in dungeon, temple and treasure chests. Each has its own trick when its bonus fires: ruby sets things alight, sapphire freezes them, onyx heals you."
  ],
  "quest.1068D9D37D579C0A.title": "Artisan Scrolls",
  "quest.1068D9D37D579C0A.quest_subtitle": "Patterns, sold separately.",
  "quest.1068D9D37D579C0A.quest_desc": [
    "Locked patterns come on Artisan Scrolls from dungeon, library and Nether chests, from Jewelers and from the Wandering Trader. Use one to learn its pattern for good; Iron's own Rune Inscribed Ring is among them."
  ],
  "quest.5581113C7A4BCF60.title": "Ask the Jeweler",
  "quest.5581113C7A4BCF60.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A villager who claims a Jewelcrafting Station becomes a Jeweler, selling rings, amulets and patterns. Only Jewelers deal in the Ring of Haggling, which takes items off villager prices; the Piglin Signet pattern comes from Nether chests and makes piglins leave you alone.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4742E138AC0E5B46.title": "Mage metals",
  "quest.4742E138AC0E5B46.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Iron's materials work at the station too: mithril has quality 3 and adds 5% spell power, pyrium quality 3 and 5% shorter casts, an Arcane Ingot 50 mana, and each rune adds power in its own school.\"}]"
  ],
  "image.26CDA27E983D81D8.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The anvil and the orb\",\"color\":\"#8EC8FF\"}]",
  "image.0BDA48FEC078E57E.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Mithril\",\"color\":\"#8EC8FF\"}]",
  "image.37759B7DF67D1BB5.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Dead King\",\"color\":\"#8EC8FF\"}]",
  "image.13D3FE71F4921983.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Echo of Tyros\",\"color\":\"#8EC8FF\"}]",
  "image.01AF2ABDA469572D.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Ice Spider\",\"color\":\"#8EC8FF\"}]",
  "image.6873C6B0DB9C4628.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Ancient books\",\"color\":\"#8EC8FF\"}]",
  "image.5A0AFE505760B900.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Battlemage gear\",\"color\":\"#8EC8FF\"}]",
  "image.104942FF07BBBCA6.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Rings and charms\",\"color\":\"#8EC8FF\"}]",
  "image.3791F0DC3C3CDE85.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Iron's Gems 'n Jewelry\",\"color\":\"#8EC8FF\"}]",
  "image.1279747487425BE2.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Pocket Dimension\",\"color\":\"#8EC8FF\"}]",
  "image.44FA71549E05E254.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Iron's Spells\\nThe Arcane Anvil\",\"color\":\"#8EC8FF\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.4AD1EC51C982BC22.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"rune rune rune rune orb rune\",\"color\":\"#C9D6FF\",\"font\":\"minecraft:alt\"}]",
  "image.76D101C384342E3A.title": "Back to Iron's Spells 'n Spellbooks",
  "chapter.5EEA4B45009E12E6.title": "Explore without getting lost",
  "chapter.5EEA4B45009E12E6.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Compass, Atlas, maps, locators and waystones: which one to reach for."
  ],
  "quest.2B106DDD74F05ABD.title": "Always know the next step",
  "quest.2B106DDD74F05ABD.quest_desc": [
    "Three layers keep you oriented: the Heliodor Compass says where the story goes next, the Living Atlas says what to deliver, and maps, locators and waystones get you there and back.",
    "",
    "The story never asks you to walk thousands of blocks or fly a jetpack."
  ],
  "quest.3963A066C717E409.title": "The Heliodor Compass",
  "quest.3963A066C717E409.quest_desc": [
    "Take it from the pedestal in your start ruin, one per player and world, and carry it a moment to attune it. It points to whatever the story needs next and turns on its own when your team gets there.",
    "",
    "Colors, states and route: The Heliodor Compass chapter."
  ],
  "quest.561896BFDF3BEFF6.title": "Reading the needle",
  "quest.561896BFDF3BEFF6.quest_desc": [
    "The needle's color names the target's world. Grey means there is nothing to point at: nothing within 1,500 blocks, a goal from a later act, or nothing left. Hover it and the tooltip spells out the state.",
    "",
    "The full legend is in The Heliodor Compass chapter."
  ],
  "quest.28F6CDF826378F45.title": "The compass follows the team",
  "quest.28F6CDF826378F45.quest_desc": [
    "It works per FTB team: everyone sees the same objective, and whatever any member completes counts for all. Places found by any team are remembered by the world.",
    "",
    "More in The Heliodor Compass chapter."
  ],
  "quest.2DF6858601AF0E06.title": "Do not lose it",
  "quest.2DF6858601AF0E06.quest_desc": [
    "The pedestal gives one compass per player and no recipe makes another. A Soulbound rune from Tombstone's Book of Soulbound keeps it on you when you die.",
    "",
    "Or leave it at home once you know the way. It will not sulk."
  ],
  "quest.7BF4FFF84427DFBB.title": "The Living Atlas",
  "quest.7BF4FFF84427DFBB.quest_desc": [
    "A book and a copper ingot. It takes each act's deliveries, keeps the lore fragments and the compass page, and never delivers anything by accident: delivering is always a button.",
    "",
    "How it works: The Living Atlas chapter."
  ],
  "quest.1F9F7B401D29563A.title": "The Survey Station",
  "quest.1F9F7B401D29563A.quest_desc": [
    "A movable bookmark: use a plain compass on it and the compass points to the station, like a lodestone; with an empty hand it opens the Atlas.",
    "",
    "Put one at your base and carry the bound compass on expeditions: an arrow home that does not need a map."
  ],
  "quest.3015B662CC892ACD.title": "Your map: JourneyMap",
  "quest.3015B662CC892ACD.quest_desc": [
    "It remembers everything you have seen and marks where you die; &eJ&r opens the full map and &eM&r drops a waypoint where you stand. Mark every ruin and portal you want to find again.",
    "",
    "Views, keys and death points: the Travel chapter."
  ],
  "quest.09CC6C35446FD380.title": "Waystones as anchors",
  "quest.09CC6C35446FD380.quest_desc": [
    "Every waystone you activate becomes a destination and, by default, a JourneyMap waypoint. Plant one next to everything that matters: your base, each Heliodor ruin, each portal.",
    "",
    "Costs, scrolls and building your own: the Travel chapter."
  ],
  "quest.0B70E5F10FB1C6D9.title": "Explorer's Compass",
  "quest.0B70E5F10FB1C6D9.quest_desc": [
    "A compass ringed by cobwebs and cracked stone bricks. Right-click to pick any structure, vanilla or modded; it finds the nearest, points at it and shows the distance.",
    "",
    "Made for side trips. The story never needs it."
  ],
  "quest.1595C7F7FF1FE7A5.title": "Nature's Compass",
  "quest.1595C7F7FF1FE7A5.quest_desc": [
    "A compass ringed by saplings and logs finds the nearest biome you choose, with its climate: a Solsticio native's biome, a mushroom island, the Aether's cloud biomes.",
    "",
    "Both locator compasses are repaired by crafting them with a plain compass."
  ],
  "quest.5D02424D936F2EF9.title": "Maps that lead somewhere",
  "quest.5D02424D936F2EF9.quest_desc": [
    "Cartographers sell ocean, woodland and trial maps (ocean maps also find YUNG's monuments), Repurposed Structures adds maps to some trades, Dungeons and Taverns taverns sell maps to their dungeons, and the Twilight Forest has magic, maze and ore maps.",
    "",
    "The maps you fill yourself look great framed on a wall."
  ],
  "quest.52E2B71D1CE5C3B2.title": "The Ark's chart room",
  "quest.52E2B71D1CE5C3B2.quest_desc": [
    "From act V, the Ark's Exploration Module merges maps: hold a filled map, use the module, and it absorbs the explored detail of your other maps of the same area, even one already framed on a wall. Nothing is consumed.",
    "",
    "Five field maps in, one overview out."
  ],
  "quest.7766CF40B9EB3115.title": "Special locators",
  "quest.7766CF40B9EB3115.quest_desc": [
    "Eyes of Ender find the stronghold (YUNG's version), Cataclysm's eyes one boss arena each, and Eternal Starlight's Seeking Eyes aim with a locator item in the other hand. Twilight magic maps chart the forest, the recovery compass points to your last death, and a lodestone or a Survey Station anchors any compass."
  ],
  "quest.0C32CBED1669E8DF.title": "Solsticio's cartographer",
  "quest.0C32CBED1669E8DF.quest_desc": [
    "In act VI, Rumbo sells survey maps that chart the nearest monument, trial chamber, jungle temple, swamp hut, buried treasure, mansion or ancient city under the Overworld sky, plus locator compasses, a spyglass and a lodestone.",
    "",
    "Memoria, the curator, sells Heliodor lore books and every pottery sherd."
  ],
  "quest.383C1B79AE356FE3.title": "A routine that never fails",
  "quest.383C1B79AE356FE3.quest_desc": [
    "Before each trip: check the compass and the Atlas, mark your base waystone, pack a Return Scroll, a bound compass and a sleeping bag. On arrival, place a waystone and a waypoint. If you die, follow the Death waypoint to your grave.",
    "",
    "Boring? Yes. Dying far from home is worse."
  ],
  "quest.47008CA35EB7072E.title": "Map, compass, way home",
  "quest.47008CA35EB7072E.quest_desc": [
    "A compass for the story, an Atlas for the why, a map for the where and a waystone for the way back.",
    "",
    "Heliodor lost its way once. You do not have to."
  ],
  "chapter.6701A0A9BE8B444F.title": "The Otherside and the mining worlds",
  "chapter.6701A0A9BE8B444F.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Deeper and Darker's sculk dimension below the ancient cities, and JAMD's disposable mining dimensions."
  ],
  "quest.1D8476E08D24EE0A.title": "Worlds below",
  "quest.1D8476E08D24EE0A.quest_desc": [
    "Two more dimensions live under your feet: the Otherside, Deeper and Darker's dark sculk world beyond the ancient cities, with the Warden's best gear; and JAMD's flat, ore-rich mining worlds, opened with act components, so you can dig without scarring home.",
    "",
    "Neither is part of the story. Both make the rest easier."
  ],
  "quest.268BE62D8492E76E.title": "A Metropolis of Restless Souls",
  "quest.268BE62D8492E76E.quest_desc": [
    "Find an ancient city in the Deep Dark. Sculk sensors and shriekers call the Warden: sneak, avoid stepping on sculk, and muffle your steps with wool.",
    "",
    "Deeper and Darker adds Warden Carapaces and the Warden upgrade template to their loot. Worth the whispering."
  ],
  "quest.766213489C04EA8E.title": "The Heart of the Deep",
  "quest.766213489C04EA8E.quest_desc": [
    "Slay the Warden and take its heart (Phantom Thief): with Deeper and Darker it drops a Heart of the Deep and Warden Carapaces. It is the hardest vanilla creature, so bring a plan (ranged damage, strong armor, potions) or come back later.",
    "",
    "The heart opens the way to the Otherside."
  ],
  "quest.064BBB48B3503996.title": "Below the Bedrock",
  "quest.064BBB48B3503996.quest_desc": [
    "Use the Heart of the Deep on an ancient city's portal frame to open the way to the Otherside: dark, hostile and full of sculk creatures. Bring light, food and a way back.",
    "",
    "Exploring every Otherside biome is Echolocation; killing one of each sculk monster, Sculk Slayer."
  ],
  "quest.0139E5BED18C0C11.title": "Abyssal Descent",
  "quest.0139E5BED18C0C11.quest_desc": [
    "Ancient temples hide deep in the Otherside with its rarest loot, including the Sonorous Staff (Noise Complaint), which fires sonic blasts like the Warden's; Reverberation and Volume enchantments improve it.",
    "",
    "Finally, a weapon that is also a noise complaint."
  ],
  "quest.0C808CA553F23E84.title": "Cover Me with Sculk",
  "quest.0C808CA553F23E84.quest_desc": [
    "Two upgrade paths: Resonarium plates turn iron gear into Resonarium, and Reinforced Echo Shards (Sculk Engineer) plus the Warden template turn netherite gear into Warden gear. A full Warden set earns Cover Me with Sculk.",
    "",
    "Sculk Smite adds damage against sculk mobs and the Warden."
  ],
  "quest.322768E7F9B343C6.title": "Sculk gadgets",
  "quest.322768E7F9B343C6.quest_desc": [
    "The Sculk Transmitter (Remote Storage) links to a container and opens it from far away. Soul Elytra have a boost on a cooldown.",
    "",
    "Their keys moved here to &eAlt+B&r (boost) and &eAlt+N&r (transmitter), off the backpack and Ultimine keys."
  ],
  "quest.706A01ED65FEE247.title": "A mining portal (act II)",
  "quest.706A01ED65FEE247.quest_desc": [
    "JAMD's Mining Portal leads to a separate mining dimension, so your home world stays intact. Here it takes seven obsidian, a diamond pickaxe and a Calibration Frame, the act II component.",
    "",
    "Place it, step in, and come back through the portal on the other side."
  ],
  "quest.5C93958CD8D9B795.title": "To Infinity and Underground",
  "quest.5C93958CD8D9B795.quest_desc": [
    "Enter the Mining dimension and dig freely: it exists to be dug up. Bring torches, and mark your portal on JourneyMap before wandering off.",
    "",
    "Its ores feed your processing lines, and Ultimine and the pack's mining gadgets are right at home here."
  ],
  "quest.39444A8C452B5290.title": "Nether and End portals (act IV)",
  "quest.39444A8C452B5290.quest_desc": [
    "The Nether Mining Portal takes seven Nether bricks, a netherite pickaxe and a Containment Seal; the End one seven End stone, a diamond pickaxe and a Horizon Chart, both act IV components.",
    "",
    "Nether and End blocks and ores, minus the parts of those dimensions that want you dead."
  ],
  "quest.290EE2DE0AFF78E4.title": "Nether Mining",
  "quest.290EE2DE0AFF78E4.quest_desc": [
    "Visit the Nether Mining dimension through its portal. Pack as you would for the real Nether: fire resistance and a way home.",
    "",
    "Safer than the original. Not safe."
  ],
  "quest.08D53AB973F79599.title": "How these fit in ENTRELUMEN",
  "quest.08D53AB973F79599.quest_desc": [
    "The Otherside is optional and native, with the Warden's heart as its key. JAMD portals are staged with act components (Calibration Frame in II, Containment Seal and Horizon Chart in IV); the rest of their recipes is the mod's own.",
    "",
    "The Undergarden, the other underground dimension, has its own chapter."
  ],
  "quest.5F16E45ACDCAF7F7.title": "End Mining",
  "quest.5F16E45ACDCAF7F7.quest_desc": [
    "End stone and End materials without endermen breathing down your neck.",
    "",
    "A good stop before building an End base."
  ],
  "quest.0C70A64FFF7EB727.title": "Echoes to spare",
  "quest.0C70A64FFF7EB727.quest_desc": [
    "Echo shards from ancient cities become Reinforced Echo Shards, the core of Warden gear.",
    "",
    "They are also a luxury trade: Solsticio's rarities dealer sells them from act III."
  ],
  "quest.0A744E5120330A73.title": "Deeper than deep",
  "quest.0A744E5120330A73.quest_desc": [
    "You stole the Warden's heart, crossed below the bedrock and opened portals to worlds made for digging.",
    "",
    "The deep is no longer a place to fear. Only a place to mine."
  ],
  "chapter.6EDF48A8FC48C541.title": "Weapons and armor by act",
  "chapter.6EDF48A8FC48C541.chapter_subtitle": [
    "What to wear and wield in each act, and where it comes from."
  ],
  "quest.068B39AFC641D9DE.title": "Gear follows the story",
  "quest.068B39AFC641D9DE.quest_desc": [
    "For each act, the gear worth having and where it drops. The world gets tougher as the story advances, and the best set in the pack, Luminous, only appears in act VI.",
    "",
    "None of it is mandatory. Dress for your own style."
  ],
  "quest.3FDA107F53BB433C.title": "The story sets the difficulty",
  "quest.3FDA107F53BB433C.quest_desc": [
    "Apotheosis World Tiers rise when your team completes an act and never drop: Haven for acts I and II, then Frontier, Ascent, Summit and Pinnacle. Higher tiers mean tougher monsters and better loot.",
    "",
    "The whole ladder, invaders included: the World Tiers chapter."
  ],
  "quest.23CAAA5BB61ABC15.title": "Affix loot: colors and salvage",
  "quest.23CAAA5BB61ABC15.quest_desc": [
    "Apotheosis gear drops with a rarity color, Common to Mythic, and random affixes; hover to read them. Break what you will not wear at a &eSalvaging Table&r for rarity materials, which upgrade gems at the Gem Cutting Table and pay the Augmenting Table.",
    "",
    "Smithing keeps affixes: an Epic diamond sword stays Epic as netherite, and as Luminous."
  ],
  "quest.6D553D7AA84D7933.title": "Test your damage",
  "quest.6D553D7AA84D7933.quest_desc": [
    "Before a boss, compare weapons on a &eTarget Dummy&r: it shows each hit's damage and never dies. Equipment Compare sets what you hold beside what you wear, Overloaded Armor Bar keeps armor above 20 readable, and AttributeFix lifts the vanilla armor cap.",
    "",
    "The dummy does not judge. Much."
  ],
  "quest.7B66E584AE08E8C5.title": "Act I: iron and a shield",
  "quest.7B66E584AE08E8C5.quest_desc": [
    "A full iron set, a shield (it stops creeper blasts and arrows) and a bow. Watch for the camouflaged biome creepers and wildlife that bites; dungeon loot can already beat crafted iron.",
    "",
    "The tier is Haven: no invaders yet. Enjoy it while it lasts."
  ],
  "quest.5DCF5003DE90D8A8.title": "Act II: diamond and a big axe",
  "quest.5DCF5003DE90D8A8.quest_desc": [
    "Enchanted diamond gear, from the table or Apotheosis shelves, carries you through act II. The best early prize is optional: Mowzie's Ferrous Wroughtnaut guards the Axe of a Thousand Metals and the Wrought Helm, both unbreakable.",
    "",
    "He is slow. He is not gentle."
  ],
  "quest.77D4B4D620982CB6.title": "Act III: Twilight and Undergarden",
  "quest.77D4B4D620982CB6.quest_desc": [
    "Two armories open.\n- Twilight: Naga armor, Ironwood, Steeleaf, Knightmetal (bonus against armor), Fiery gear (auto-smelting pickaxe, burning armor) and Phantom armor, never lost on death.\n- Undergarden: Cloggrum, then Froststeel (slows), Utherium (1.5× against Rotspawn) and Forgotten tools.",
    "",
    "The tier rises to Frontier, and invaders appear."
  ],
  "quest.224722532A1DBC7C.title": "Netherite: the base of it all",
  "quest.224722532A1DBC7C.quest_desc": [
    "Ancient debris, netherite scrap and an upgrade template from a bastion turn diamond into netherite. Keep those pieces: Cataclysm's Ignitium and Cursium upgrades and ENTRELUMEN's Luminous gear are all smithed on top of netherite.",
    "",
    "In Solsticio, the smith sells the upgrade template from act IV on."
  ],
  "quest.66BCFEB62531D362.title": "Act IV: sky gear and boss loot",
  "quest.66BCFEB62531D362.quest_desc": [
    "- Aether: Gravitite (high jump, no fall damage), Valkyrie (short flight), Phoenix and Obsidian armor; Deep Aether adds Skyjade and Stratus.\n- Cataclysm: Ignitium (from Ignis) and Cursium (from Maledictus) upgrade netherite, plus unique weapons.\n- Eternal Starlight: Unrealium and boss weapons.",
    "",
    "Aether set bonuses need the matching gloves. The tier rises to Ascent."
  ],
  "quest.646ACD59C4D7C3BE.title": "Act V: space suits",
  "quest.646ACD59C4D7C3BE.quest_desc": [
    "Venus and Mercury need Ad Astra's Netherite Space Suit (fire resistance, oxygen), and the Jet Suit adds flight. Tech mods bring their own top armor, like the MekaSuit and Modern Industrialization's quantum suit.",
    "",
    "The tier rises to Summit, where Mythic loot appears: salvaging it is the only source of the Godforged Pearl."
  ],
  "quest.31F1025C6342BEC4.title": "Act VI: Luminous gear",
  "quest.31F1025C6342BEC4.quest_desc": [
    "The best set in the pack: netherite pieces upgraded with a Luminous Ingot and a nether star. It never breaks, repairs itself in light, and the full set flies.",
    "",
    "Recipe, stats and tricks: the Luminosities and Luminous Gear chapter."
  ],
  "quest.5B6C3F10776C0B4F.title": "Ranged options along the way",
  "quest.5B6C3F10776C0B4F.quest_desc": [
    "A well-enchanted bow ages well, and each dimension adds its own: the Aether's dart shooters (darts ignore gravity) and Phoenix Bow, Twilight's Triple and Seeker bows from the Snow Queen, the Undergarden Slingshot, Cataclysm's Cursed Bow and Astrape, Eternal Starlight's crystal crossbow and Moonring Bow, and Mowzie's blowgun with poison darts."
  ],
  "quest.1420E6D2867191CA.title": "Staying alive",
  "quest.1420E6D2867191CA.quest_desc": [
    "Run-savers: the Totem of Undying (evokers), Friends and Foes' Totems of Freezing and Illusion (below half health), Twilight's Charms of Life and Keeping, the Cursium chestplate (one revive), Aether Life Shards (up to 10 extra hearts) and, in this pack, buffs for varied food and leftover saturation.",
    "",
    "Dying is optional. Mostly."
  ],
  "quest.5361C7F7A2A980B5.title": "Keep your look",
  "quest.5361C7F7A2A980B5.quest_desc": [
    "Cosmetic Armor Reworked adds cosmetic slots: wear the protection you need and show the armor you like. Armor trims work on any armor with the vanilla tags, and Solsticio's smith sells all eighteen templates.",
    "",
    "Saving the world is no excuse to dress badly."
  ],
  "quest.37575A687460FCA9.title": "Dressed in light",
  "quest.37575A687460FCA9.quest_desc": [
    "From iron to Luminous, every dimension left something on your belt.",
    "",
    "The last set is not about numbers: it is Heliodor's light, forged with respect this time."
  ],
  "chapter.6CB674C10F6F716D.title": "Accessories and artifacts",
  "chapter.6CB674C10F6F716D.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Curios slots, the Artifacts you find while exploring and the Aether's own accessory menu."
  ],
  "quest.44730CF39368B534.title": "Extra slots, extra powers",
  "quest.44730CF39368B534.quest_desc": [
    "Most mods hang accessories on Curios slots (head, necklace, belt, hands, feet, back and more), the Aether keeps its own menu, and Eternal Starlight's are fused into your gear. The richest source is the Artifacts mod: uncraftable trinkets found while exploring.",
    "",
    "Armor keeps you alive; trinkets make it interesting."
  ],
  "quest.56867C76555F0B5F.title": "Open the Curios inventory",
  "quest.56867C76555F0B5F.quest_desc": [
    "&eG&r, or the Curios button in your inventory, opens the slots. Each slot can hide its item visually, and Artifacts adds cosmetic slots to show one trinket while wearing another.",
    "",
    "If something does not fit, it belongs to another slot: hover the slot to read its name."
  ],
  "quest.6AFD3B81196BB353.title": "Find an Artifact",
  "quest.6AFD3B81196BB353.quest_desc": [
    "Artifacts are never crafted. They hide in the loot of mineshafts, dungeons, temples, strongholds, fortresses, bastions, End and ancient cities, shipwrecks, buried treasure, outposts, igloos, ruined portals and village chests, plus suspicious sand and gravel; YUNG's rebuilt structures count too.",
    "",
    "Your first one earns Amateur Archaeologist."
  ],
  "quest.6C0D53F0E5B344E2.title": "Campsites and Mimics",
  "quest.6C0D53F0E5B344E2.quest_desc": [
    "Artifacts adds small underground campsites with supply barrels and a tool chest. Some of those chests are Mimics that jump and bite when opened; kill one for Chest Slayer, since every Mimic drops an artifact. Lootr keeps structure loot per player, so each teammate rolls their own.",
    "",
    "If the chest has teeth, it has loot."
  ],
  "quest.10DCD6E41BA4EB13.title": "Artifacts for moving",
  "quest.10DCD6E41BA4EB13.quest_desc": [
    "Cloud in a Bottle double-jumps, Bunny Hoppers jump higher and land softer, Running Shoes sprint faster and step higher, Aqua-Dashers run across fluids, Flippers swim much faster, Snowshoes walk on powder snow, Steadfast Spikes shrug off knockback and ice, and the Helium Flamingo \"swims\" through the air for a while."
  ],
  "quest.5D491DCB10C0BB73.title": "Artifacts for mining and looting",
  "quest.5D491DCB10C0BB73.quest_desc": [
    "Digging Claws mine faster and at a higher base tier, even bare-handed; the Pickaxe Heater smelts ores as you mine; the Lucky Scarf adds Fortune and the Superstitious Hat Looting; the Universal Attractor pulls nearby items; Night Vision Goggles see in the dark; the Onion Ring gives Haste after eating; the Golden Hook adds creature experience."
  ],
  "quest.6AC851742C49051F.title": "Artifacts for fighting",
  "quest.6AC851742C49051F.quest_desc": [
    "The Power Glove adds damage, Feral Claws attack speed and the Pocket Piston knockback. The Vampiric Glove heals on melee hits, the Fire Gauntlet burns and the Withered Bracelet may inflict Wither. The Crystal Heart adds max health, the Cross Necklace longer invincibility, the Panic Necklace speed when hurt, and Thorn, Flame and Shock Pendants hit back."
  ],
  "quest.75F48F47F46DCE94.title": "Artifacts that save you",
  "quest.75F48F47F46DCE94.quest_desc": [
    "The Chorus Totem may teleport you away from a fatal hit (with a cooldown), the Obsidian Skull grants fire resistance after a burn, Strider Shoes ignore hot floors, the Antidote Vessel shortens bad effects, the Snorkel and the Charm of Sinking handle water, Kitty Slippers keep creepers and phantoms away, and the Umbrella slows falls and blocks like a shield."
  ],
  "quest.0DF1D75734FC4CE0.title": "Everyday artifacts",
  "quest.0DF1D75734FC4CE0.quest_desc": [
    "Villager Hat: better trades, handy before Solsticio. Angler's Hat: more Luck of the Sea and Lure. Cowboy Hat: faster mounts. Drinking hats: eat and drink faster. Rooted Boots: hunger refills on grass. Warp Drive: ender pearls cost hunger instead of pearls. Charm of Shrinking: go tiny. Scarf of Invisibility: go unseen."
  ],
  "quest.0CF6BCA100209E87.title": "Adventurous Eater",
  "quest.0CF6BCA100209E87.quest_desc": [
    "The Everlasting Beef and the Eternal Steak are food that never runs out, each with a cooldown. Eat one for Adventurous Eater.",
    "",
    "This pack rewards variety: an endless steak is a safety net, not a diet."
  ],
  "quest.1F729E92C66954CF.title": "Toggles and keys",
  "quest.1F729E92C66954CF.quest_desc": [
    "The Universal Attractor, Night Vision Goggles, Scarf of Invisibility, Charms of Shrinking and Sinking and the Helium Flamingo's flight can be switched on and off; their keys are in Controls, under Artifacts.",
    "",
    "Turn the attractor off at home, unless you enjoy collecting every dropped seed."
  ],
  "quest.6ED869120880E115.title": "The Aether accessory menu",
  "quest.6ED869120880E115.quest_desc": [
    "The Aether has its own screen (&eI&r, or its inventory button) for rings, a pendant, gloves, a cape, a shield and more. Highlights: Zanite rings and pendants (faster mining for a while) and Ice ones (walk on water and lava), the Regeneration Stone, the Iron Bubble, the Invisibility Cloak, and Deep Aether's Cloud Cape (double jump) and Aercloud Necklace."
  ],
  "quest.4E0B57BF283905C8.title": "Terra's Arm",
  "quest.4E0B57BF283905C8.quest_desc": [
    "ENTRELUMEN's own accessory: Terra's cyborg arm, worn in a Curios hands slot for extra block reach. The Atlas gives it when act II closes, and the sunken workshop ruin keeps one in a chest.",
    "",
    "Everything else: the Terra's Arm chapter."
  ],
  "quest.434AD099488E169B.title": "Starlight goes inside your gear",
  "quest.434AD099488E169B.quest_desc": [
    "Eternal Starlight's accessories are not worn: each one combines into a specific kind of equipment, like items into a bundle, and the gear gains its effect. How many fit depends on the gear's accessory slots.",
    "",
    "The Glimmering Tablet says how to get each one."
  ],
  "quest.0A8B8F620E1A4BED.title": "Accessories in this pack",
  "quest.0A8B8F620E1A4BED.quest_desc": [
    "Curios and the Aether's Accessories run side by side. Artifacts registers its slots and cosmetic slots in Curios, and Cataclysm, Occultism, Industrial Foregoing and Sophisticated Backpacks use Curios slots too (a backpack goes on your back).",
    "",
    "Iron's Gems and Jewelry makes rings and amulets at a jeweller's bench; it has its own chapter."
  ],
  "quest.68A75072CA987105.title": "A full set of trinkets",
  "quest.68A75072CA987105.quest_desc": [
    "Every slot filled with something that suits you: a jump, a heal, a magnet, a lucky scarf.",
    "",
    "That is how two players in the same armor end up playing completely different games."
  ],
  "chapter.7B3D8EAE5467125E.title": "Creatures of the world",
  "chapter.7B3D8EAE5467125E.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Friends and Foes, Naturalist, Creeper Overhaul and Enderman Overhaul: who helps, who bites."
  ],
  "quest.1428DDF847B60627.title": "A livelier world",
  "quest.1428DDF847B60627.quest_desc": [
    "From the first night: Friends and Foes brings vanilla-style mobs and golems, Naturalist fills biomes with real-world wildlife, and Creeper Overhaul and Enderman Overhaul give creepers and endermen a variant per biome. None is gated.",
    "",
    "Some help, some bite, and a few do both depending on your manners."
  ],
  "quest.5B073D11A6FC1137.title": "A copper golem",
  "quest.5B073D11A6FC1137.quest_desc": [
    "A block of copper, a carved pumpkin and a lightning rod on top build a Copper Golem (Off you go); any oxidation stage works, waxed or not. It wanders looking for copper buttons and presses them.",
    "",
    "A small, living redstone clock. Heliodor would approve of the copper."
  ],
  "quest.57FA2F4D749C9AB2.title": "A Glare in the dark",
  "quest.57FA2F4D749C9AB2.quest_desc": [
    "Glares are small, grumpy moss creatures from lush caves. Tame one with glow berries (Grumpy and Cute) and it leads you to dark spots where monsters could spawn.",
    "",
    "A torch-placement consultant that works for berries."
  ],
  "quest.51525F2225F81724.title": "Crab claw: longer reach",
  "quest.51525F2225F81724.quest_desc": [
    "Beach crabs drop Crab Claws, which brew the Potion of Reaching: longer range for placing and breaking blocks, great for building.",
    "",
    "Moobloom cows grow buttercups on their backs; shear one for MooBoom!"
  ],
  "quest.473AD09B7CEAB75C.title": "Hide and seek with a Rascal",
  "quest.473AD09B7CEAB75C.quest_desc": [
    "Rascals are shy creatures hiding in mineshafts. Find one and it runs to hide again; find it three times (Hide and Seek) and it rewards you, sometimes with ores or a pickaxe.",
    "",
    "The most harmless thing in any mineshaft."
  ],
  "quest.2769E179BE1CCD4C.title": "The illager magicians",
  "quest.2769E179BE1CCD4C.quest_desc": [
    "The Iceologer throws ice from its cabin; the Illusioner, in shacks and training grounds, copies himself. Kill both plus an Evoker for The Magicians.",
    "",
    "Each drops a totem that triggers below half health: the Totem of Freezing and the Totem of Illusion."
  ],
  "quest.715470BADBA985D5.title": "The Wildfire",
  "quest.715470BADBA985D5.quest_desc": [
    "The Nether's Citadel (A fortress? No, a citadel!) is guarded by the Wildfire, a blaze-like boss, and its barrels hold diamond gear.",
    "",
    "The Wildfire drops Crown Fragments; enough of them make the Wildfire Crown (Who's da New King of Nether?)."
  ],
  "quest.58D1BA3AF7E9C073.title": "Friends and Foes, the rest",
  "quest.58D1BA3AF7E9C073.quest_desc": [
    "The Tuff Golem (tuff, wool, a carved pumpkin) holds an item for you. The Mauler is a biting ambush predator (It Bites). The Beekeeper is a villager profession, with beehives for every wood (Be Keeper). Zombie horse traps are the skeleton trap with zombie riders (Riders On The Storm)."
  ],
  "quest.11386129FAD7C940.title": "Naturalist: wildlife",
  "quest.11386129FAD7C940.quest_desc": [
    "Real-world animals in fitting biomes: bears, deer, boars, lions, zebras, giraffes, elephants, rhinos, hippos, alligators, komodo dragons, snakes, scorpions, sharks, whales, birds, butterflies, fireflies and more.",
    "",
    "Honeycomb for a Bear, melon for a Hippo, a map read on a Giraffe: three advancements."
  ],
  "quest.25F90752659FC778.title": "The Capture Net",
  "quest.25F90752659FC778.quest_desc": [
    "Bamboo and string. It catches small creatures (butterflies, caterpillars, snails and the like) as items to release elsewhere: decorate, breed, fill a greenhouse.",
    "",
    "Fish and small water creatures still go in buckets."
  ],
  "quest.5E9E708CBED4A95A.title": "What wildlife gives",
  "quest.5E9E708CBED4A95A.quest_desc": [
    "Hide smelts into leather and makes a Knapsack; Glow Goop, from glow berries, turns arrows spectral; duck eggs work in cakes and pumpkin pie; and new meats and fish cook the usual way. Naturalist also brews Antivenom and Forest Dasher potions: EMI shows how.",
    "",
    "More variety for a pack that rewards eating well."
  ],
  "quest.66132E311AD3BBD4.title": "Wildlife that bites back",
  "quest.66132E311AD3BBD4.quest_desc": [
    "Early on, respect alligators in swamps and rivers, sharks and piranhas in water, desert and jungle scorpions, snakes, and big cats like lions and tigers. Rhinos charge and break some blocks.",
    "",
    "Keep your distance from anything large until you have armor. Especially the rhino."
  ],
  "quest.3F178A29219B7BE0.title": "Creepers in camouflage",
  "quest.3F178A29219B7BE0.quest_desc": [
    "Creeper Overhaul gives most biomes their own creeper, textured to blend in: jungle, bamboo, desert, badlands, hills, savanna, mushroom, swamp, dripstone, cave, dark oak, spruce, beach, snowy, ocean and birch.",
    "",
    "The hiss is your best warning. In caves and forests, listen before you look."
  ],
  "quest.56E3082B5DAADD68.title": "Endermen for every biome",
  "quest.56E3082B5DAADD68.quest_desc": [
    "Enderman Overhaul adds an enderman for badlands, caves, coral, crimson, dark oak, desert, End, End islands, flower fields, ice spikes, mushroom, Nether wastes, savanna, snow, soul sand valley, swamp, warped and windswept hills. Some hit harder than vanilla; cave ones can drop ores and emeralds.",
    "",
    "Their drops are worth the hunt."
  ],
  "quest.46128FFEEEFDAAD4.title": "A hood against stares",
  "quest.46128FFEEEFDAAD4.quest_desc": [
    "Badlands, savanna and snowy endermen can drop hoods. Wear one and you can look endermen in the eye without angering them.",
    "",
    "A carved pumpkin, minus the pumpkin on your face."
  ],
  "quest.3252F91E012FD964.title": "Special pearls",
  "quest.3252F91E012FD964.quest_desc": [
    "Each biome enderman drops its own pearl: Bubble (coral) flies straight, Icy (ice spikes, snow) freezes, Crimson and Warped grant Strength II and Resistance II on teleport, Soul (soul sand valley) moves a bound creature, Summoner (swamp, windswept hills) teleports nearby targets, Corrupted (End) sends targets anywhere and Ancient (End islands) summons an allied enderman."
  ],
  "quest.6B546E821D9A722C.title": "Corrupted gear",
  "quest.6B546E821D9A722C.quest_desc": [
    "End endermen drop Corrupted Pearls and Enderman Teeth. Two teeth on a stick make the Corrupted Blade, which teleports what it hits; the Corrupted Shield teleports whoever hits you.",
    "",
    "Any special pearl crafts back into a plain ender pearl if you need one."
  ],
  "quest.3267C60676392C44.title": "How these fit in ENTRELUMEN",
  "quest.3267C60676392C44.quest_desc": [
    "All four mods are native, with no recipe changes, and live in the world from act I. Their meats, fish and berries add food variety, which the pack rewards. Carry On can lift some animals but never bosses or protected entities, and Friends and Foes structures keep per-player loot through Lootr."
  ],
  "quest.65D3528A8F5F856A.title": "Naturalist's notebook",
  "quest.65D3528A8F5F856A.quest_desc": [
    "Working golems, a Glare that finds dark corners, a crab claw for reach, totems from illager magicians, a hood against endermen and a pocketful of odd pearls.",
    "",
    "The living world is on your side now. Mostly."
  ],
  "chapter.66656B710E644D7B.title": "Death without stress: Tombstone",
  "chapter.66656B710E644D7B.chapter_subtitle": [
    "What happens when you die, how to get your things back and how to die less."
  ],
  "quest.5B2E78124626820D.title": "Death is a detour",
  "quest.5B2E78124626820D.quest_desc": [
    "Tombstone is the pack's only death-recovery mod, on purpose. When you die, your items go into a grave on the spot and you respawn with a Grave Key and a brief Ghostly Shape that keeps creatures off you. With default settings, nothing is lost.",
    "",
    "A grave with your things, no stress. Death here is paperwork."
  ],
  "quest.00B31EEBD396DE86.title": "The Grave Key",
  "quest.00B31EEBD396DE86.quest_desc": [
    "In the same dimension, the key shows your grave from a distance. Walk back and right-click the grave, or sneak over it, to get everything back.",
    "",
    "Items lying a few blocks from your death go into the grave too, and dying again before you recover it adds to the same grave instead of making another."
  ],
  "quest.313E939E0182E31D.title": "Find it on the map",
  "quest.313E939E0182E31D.quest_desc": [
    "JourneyMap drops a Death waypoint where you fall: follow its beam, and let a Return Scroll or a nearby waystone save most of the walk.",
    "",
    "In the Aether, falling off an island drops you into the Overworld instead of killing you; your grave, if any, stays where you actually died."
  ],
  "quest.3882431F9809F0FC.title": "A key that teleports",
  "quest.3882431F9809F0FC.quest_desc": [
    "An enchanted Grave Key lets you hold right-click to teleport straight to your grave. Enchant it by crafting it with an ender pearl, or with a soul haunting a decorative grave; sometimes it comes enchanted already.",
    "",
    "The trip caps Ghostly Shape at 10 seconds, so land ready to fight."
  ],
  "quest.104A12BF2CCE58CC.title": "Grave Dust",
  "quest.104A12BF2CCE58CC.quest_desc": [
    "Undead drop it, and cats sometimes bring it as a morning gift. It is the base of almost everything Tombstone crafts: marble, decorative graves, scrolls, tablets, books and the Ankh.",
    "",
    "Keep a stack. Your cat is doing its best."
  ],
  "quest.7C5F2A452A57289E.title": "Soulbound: keep it on death",
  "quest.7C5F2A452A57289E.quest_desc": [
    "A Book of Soulbound (book, diamond, lapis and grave dust) puts a Soulbound rune on a non-stackable item, which then stays in your inventory when you die. Use it on a soul-haunted decorative grave, book in the offhand and item in the main hand.",
    "",
    "Start with your pickaxe and your Heliodor Compass."
  ],
  "quest.30CFA1170E3DD6BA.title": "Decorative graves and souls",
  "quest.30CFA1170E3DD6BA.quest_desc": [
    "Marble (stone and grave dust, tinted with lapis, emerald, red sand or bone meal) crafts decorative graves. At night they smoke, and sometimes a soul haunts one: that soul powers Tombstone's magic.",
    "",
    "Do not overuse one grave: too much corruption makes it a Screaming Grave that throws bones and refuses rituals until it calms down. Relatable."
  ],
  "quest.691F4A212F9F9496.title": "Tablets: home and recall",
  "quest.691F4A212F9F9496.quest_desc": [
    "From a Strange Tablet (marble and grave dust) come travel tablets, charged on a soul-haunted grave: Home takes you to your respawn point, Recall to a memorized place, Assistance toward another player. Ancient versions bring nearby creatures along.",
    "",
    "Lost Tablets found in the world lead somewhere far away."
  ],
  "quest.34A8C9D3EA1C3B96.title": "Scrolls and books",
  "quest.34A8C9D3EA1C3B96.quest_desc": [
    "Strange Scrolls become magic scrolls with one extra ingredient: Knowledge (stores your experience, with a loss), Feather Fall, Aquatic Life, Frost and Lightning Resistance, Reach, True Sight, Preservation and more.",
    "",
    "Tombstone's books repair, disenchant, recycle or move enchantments. EMI has every recipe."
  ],
  "quest.766C9D99AAF5C9E3.title": "The Ankh of Prayer",
  "quest.766C9D99AAF5C9E3.quest_desc": [
    "The Ankh (gold, a stick and grave dust) lets you pray at decorative graves, with a cooldown, for Knowledge of Death. Knowledge buys perks: Memento Mori cuts experience lost on death by 20% per level, up to 100%, and Jailer raises the chance of a pre-enchanted Grave Key by 20% per level.",
    "",
    "Pray a little. Die a lot less."
  ],
  "quest.133E7F3115F3B234.title": "Other ways to keep your things",
  "quest.133E7F3115F3B234.quest_desc": [
    "Twilight's Charms of Keeping save armor, hotbar or everything, and Phantom armor is never lost. Charms of Life, the Totem of Undying and Friends and Foes' totems stop the death itself, Cataclysm's Cursium chestplate revives you once, and Tombstone's Receptacle of Soul and Voodoo Poppet can prevent one too."
  ],
  "quest.69A50A20C65D42DD.title": "For the server owner",
  "quest.69A50A20C65D42DD.quest_desc": [
    "Operators have /tbshowlastgrave (where a player's last grave is), /tbteleport death (your last death spot) and /tbrecovery (save and restore player backups).",
    "",
    "The pack keeps Tombstone's defaults: no random item loss, graves fill up instead of multiplying, and a grave from player-versus-player death stays unlocked."
  ],
  "quest.20F71F03CB9DD338.title": "Knowledge of Death",
  "quest.20F71F03CB9DD338.quest_desc": [
    "A key that teleports, soulbound tools, tablets home and a few perks from the Ankh: death is now an inconvenience, not a disaster.",
    "",
    "Go take the risks the story asks for."
  ],
  "quest.4F8FE857899146D4.title": "A Voodoo Poppet",
  "quest.4F8FE857899146D4.quest_desc": [
    "Leather, string, a clay ball, a dead bush and grave dust. Enchant it on a soul-haunted grave and it saves you from your next death (Not Today, Grim Reaper); the Witch Doctor perk may let you keep it afterwards.",
    "",
    "One active poppet is cheap insurance before a boss."
  ],
  "quest.6175649F4EB8ECBF.title": "Bring your pet back",
  "quest.6175649F4EB8ECBF.quest_desc": [
    "A Receptacle of Familiar (iron, a ghast tear and an impregnated diamond) captures a pet's soul when it dies, with what it carried. Carry it while the soul slowly recovers on some of your vital essence, then use it on a soul-haunted grave to revive your familiar (Bound Forever).",
    "",
    "Nobody gets left behind. Not even the parrot."
  ],
  "chapter.478633D3CFCF8540.title": "Farm · Crops and Trees",
  "chapter.478633D3CFCF8540.chapter_subtitle": [
    "A fenced field in rows, an orchard of three trees and a market: every crop the pack grows, from the first knife to a chorus flower."
  ],
  "quest.45F807AF9E04E1B8.title": "Flint and a stick",
  "quest.45F807AF9E04E1B8.quest_subtitle": "Sharper than it looks.",
  "quest.45F807AF9E04E1B8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Flint on a stick makes a \"},{\"text\":\"Flint Knife\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"farmersdelight:flint_knife\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Cut tall grass, wheat or rice with it for \"},{\"text\":\"Straw\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"farmersdelight:straw\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; kill a pig with it and you get ham. Every knife also works the cutting board.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6906134AB6E3A95F.title": "Straw work",
  "quest.6906134AB6E3A95F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two straw stacked make four \"},{\"text\":\"Rope\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"farmersdelight:rope\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; four in a square make \"},{\"text\":\"Canvas\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"farmersdelight:canvas\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; nine make a bale, and a bale breaks back into nine. Rope is what tomatoes climb, canvas what baskets and signs are made of.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.725A3EF33D10C15D.title": "Crops of the wild",
  "quest.725A3EF33D10C15D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four crops grow wild: cabbage and sea beet on beaches, tomatoes in hot dry lands, onions in most mild ones, rice where it is wet. Break the plant for \"},{\"text\":\"Cabbage Seeds\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"farmersdelight:cabbage_seeds\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", \"},{\"text\":\"Tomato Seeds\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"farmersdelight:tomato_seeds\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", an \"},{\"text\":\"Onion\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"farmersdelight:onion\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" or \"},{\"text\":\"Rice\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"farmersdelight:rice\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3D8D11D6E1700397.title": "Good dirt",
  "quest.3D8D11D6E1700397.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Dirt, straw, bone meal and four \"},{\"text\":\"Tree Bark\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"farmersdelight:tree_bark\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", or two rotten flesh instead, make \"},{\"text\":\"Organic Compost\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"farmersdelight:organic_compost\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Placed, it slowly turns into rich soil; sunlight, water and nearby mushrooms, mycelium or podzol hurry it.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Tree bark comes off a log stripped on the cutting board with an axe.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5A06C33CE079E461.title": "Black gold",
  "quest.5A06C33CE079E461.quest_subtitle": "The good stuff.",
  "quest.5A06C33CE079E461.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Compost left in place becomes \"},{\"text\":\"Rich Soil\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"farmersdelight:rich_soil\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Crops planted on it get a free bone meal boost one time in five, and a hoe turns it into \"},{\"text\":\"Rich Soil Farmland\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"farmersdelight:rich_soil_farmland\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Mushrooms planted on it grow into colonies.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2040926786BCD44E.title": "A crop of mushrooms",
  "quest.2040926786BCD44E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A mushroom planted on rich soil grows into a \"},{\"text\":\"Mushroom Colony\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"farmersdelight:brown_mushroom_colony\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Break it for more mushrooms the older it is; shear a grown one to take it whole. Mushroom fields grow them wild.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2D4352FFE039FDEA.title": "Nine to a crate",
  "quest.2D4352FFE039FDEA.quest_desc": [
    "Nine crops pack into a crate: tomatoes, cabbages, onions, carrots, potatoes and beetroots each have one, rice goes in a bag and panicles in a bale. A crate is a block, so a cellar full of them doubles as decoration."
  ],
  "quest.62E524285F7B767A.title": "Knee-deep",
  "quest.62E524285F7B767A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Rice only takes root in shallow water, one block deep. When it tops out, the \"},{\"text\":\"Rice Panicle\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"farmersdelight:rice_panicle\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on top is the harvest; a knife on the board splits it into rice and straw.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2AD55E38B2F1A7E7.title": "Tomato skyscraper",
  "quest.2AD55E38B2F1A7E7.quest_subtitle": "Gardening's cheapest skyscraper.",
  "quest.2AD55E38B2F1A7E7.quest_desc": [
    "Hang rope above a tomato plant and the vine keeps climbing it, fruiting as it goes. Pick the tomatoes by hand; the vine stays."
  ],
  "quest.790231F32D54816F.title": "Tough crowd",
  "quest.790231F32D54816F.quest_subtitle": "Boo.",
  "quest.790231F32D54816F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Rotten Tomato\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"farmersdelight:rotten_tomato\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" can be thrown. One in a pillager's face is the review the raid deserved.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.0D8C5DB17D3DF6EA.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.7804B242B4084A02.title": "One tomato, not four",
  "quest.7804B242B4084A02.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Almost Unified merges 69 crops that several mods share: a tomato is the same item whatever plant it came from, and EMI hides the copies. Farmer's Delight wins ties, then Croptopia, Pam's and Herbs and Harvest.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6C13A603F08403DE.title": "A whole field at once",
  "quest.6C13A603F08403DE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Right-click a ripe crop to harvest it and leave it planted. With a \"},{\"text\":\"Vein Resonator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:vein_resonator_1\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in a charm slot, hold \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.ftbultimine\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" to till or harvest many blocks at once.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.49C3B2317618601A.title": "Hundreds of crops",
  "quest.49C3B2317618601A.quest_desc": [
    "Croptopia scatters wild crops across every biome; break one and its seeds come with it. One crop crafts back into one seed, and the Market sells almost all of them for an emerald."
  ],
  "task.7833B66B04DF035C.title": "Plains",
  "task.03572428CFD39385.title": "Forests",
  "task.346C3318F046330E.title": "Savannas",
  "task.2B119C90BB648161.title": "Jungles",
  "task.6C9E568040005332.title": "Swamps",
  "task.26A22505581B7525.title": "Desert",
  "quest.3A62E3A4B22FB168.title": "A seed for every climate",
  "quest.3A62E3A4B22FB168.quest_desc": [
    "Croptopia's seeds follow the weather: fifteen in the plains, fifteen in forests, ten in savannas, thirteen in jungles, four in swamps and the saguaro in the desert. Carry them all and you hold every seed the mod has."
  ],
  "quest.0952B02711D30945.title": "Salt of the river",
  "quest.0952B02711D30945.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Patches of \"},{\"text\":\"Salt Ore\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"croptopia:salt_ore\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" lie on river beds. No river nearby? Smelt one of Croptopia's water bottles, sixteen from a water bucket and three glass, and the water boils off into \"},{\"text\":\"Salt\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"croptopia:salt\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2877E523261DFA89.title": "The Croptopedia",
  "quest.2877E523261DFA89.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Three crops and a book make the \"},{\"text\":\"Croptopedia\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"croptopia:guide\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", the mod's own guide.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7CDBF34580A2B0FB.title": "Spices from seed",
  "quest.7CDBF34580A2B0FB.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Croptopia grows its own spice rack: \"},{\"text\":\"Vanilla\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"croptopia:vanilla\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", \"},{\"text\":\"Pepper\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"croptopia:pepper\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", \"},{\"text\":\"Mustard\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"croptopia:mustard\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and \"},{\"text\":\"Chile Pepper\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"croptopia:chile_pepper\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" come from seeds like any crop, and the mortar and pestle grinds paprika.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.336AD770D8371E44.title": "The sea harvest",
  "quest.336AD770D8371E44.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Croptopia adds tuna, anchovy, shrimp, crab, clams and oysters to what a rod brings up. Cod, salmon and tropical fish drop \"},{\"text\":\"Roe\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"croptopia:roe\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; squid drop \"},{\"text\":\"Calamari\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"croptopia:calamari\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", and glow squid a glowing one.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.43DCA7C7C8099BBC.title": "A garden for the sushi bar",
  "quest.43DCA7C7C8099BBC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Grass also drops Sushi Go Crafting's seeds: rice that grows underwater on dirt, cucumber, soy, sesame and \"},{\"text\":\"Wasabi Root\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sushigocrafting:wasabi_root\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Its avocado trees grow mostly in plains; right-click the grown leaves for the fruit.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.67E9E631C3EF212F.title": "Mountain salt, found at sea",
  "quest.67E9E631C3EF212F.quest_subtitle": "Ask the captain.",
  "quest.67E9E631C3EF212F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Shipwreck treasure chests sometimes hold \"},{\"text\":\"Mountain Salt\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"croptopia:mountain_salt\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Nobody explains how it got there. It is also one of six ingredients of something enormous.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.50C1989AAA97642F.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.004A8D21394AD997.title": "Wild gardens",
  "quest.004A8D21394AD997.quest_desc": [
    "Pam's crops hide in wild gardens, bushes of mixed plants: arid in dry lands, frost in conifer forests, shaded in forests, soggy in swamps, tropical by jungles and the sea, windy in plains and savannas. Each one you break gives a crop of its climate."
  ],
  "task.2AD38669F3494F2B.title": "Arid",
  "task.15E5C50796809D44.title": "Frost",
  "task.22F1A679ADC46AE2.title": "Shaded",
  "task.2646D82C9ABF455D.title": "Soggy",
  "task.15645A39A8C2A141.title": "Tropical",
  "task.6061E0E8946B720A.title": "Windy",
  "quest.566D490748F58B28.title": "Six climates",
  "quest.566D490748F58B28.quest_desc": [
    "One crop from each kind of garden: agave, cloudberry, tea leaf, lotus, coffee bean and sunchoke. Any crop crafts into its seed, and the Market sells all 96 of Pam's seeds for an emerald each."
  ],
  "quest.2A0112E749CFE888.title": "Not everything is food",
  "quest.2A0112E749CFE888.quest_subtitle": "A bucket of water from a cactus. Sure.",
  "quest.2A0112E749CFE888.quest_desc": [
    "Three aloe make a slime ball, a barrel cactus fills a bucket with water, two calabashes make two glass bottles and two cattails four sticks. Any two fibers, cotton, jute, sisal, flax or kenaf, twist into string."
  ],
  "quest.4DFA0085B387B0A3.title": "Bread from any grain",
  "quest.4DFA0085B387B0A3.quest_desc": [
    "Three of any grain craft a loaf of bread: rye, millet, quinoa, sorghum, barley and oats all count, not only wheat. Pam's grinder turns the same grains into flour."
  ],
  "quest.38B894278804E073.title": "Coffee and tea",
  "quest.38B894278804E073.quest_subtitle": "Breakfast for the night shift.",
  "quest.38B894278804E073.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Smelt coffee beans for \"},{\"text\":\"Hot Coffee\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pamhc2crops:hotcoffeeitem\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and tea leaves for \"},{\"text\":\"Hot Tea\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pamhc2crops:hotteaitem\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; nettles make a hot tea of their own. No kettle, no filter: the furnace does it all.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.676505AA50EF425D.title": "No pig required",
  "quest.676505AA50EF425D.quest_subtitle": "Oink not included.",
  "quest.676505AA50EF425D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Shaded gardens in the forests sometimes hide a \"},{\"text\":\"Truffle\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pamhc2crops:truffleitem\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Plant its seed and it grows like any crop: the priciest mushroom in the world, in a row.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.7F5705E02F338121.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.2BFBCA7D7CD7B083.title": "An herb garden",
  "quest.2BFBCA7D7CD7B083.quest_desc": [
    "Mama's Herbs and Harvest brings 32 crops, 14 herbs, grapes and eight fruit trees. Its seeds turn up in village farms and chests across the Overworld; herbs want farmland and water like any crop, and one crop crafts into one seed."
  ],
  "quest.6B122A4CA97A6168.title": "Parsley, sage, rosemary and thyme",
  "quest.6B122A4CA97A6168.quest_desc": [
    "Four fresh herbs from the garden. Each one chops into four on the board with a knife, or in the crafting grid, and the chopped herbs season soups, pans and sandwiches. Picked herbs also sit on grass or in a flower pot as decoration."
  ],
  "quest.7A63004E8D6F4EB3.title": "The spice rack",
  "quest.7A63004E8D6F4EB3.quest_desc": [
    "Peppercorn, ginger and turmeric also grow on farmland. Peppercorn grinds into pepper, ginger and turmeric into powders, and a spice jar keeps a stack of any seasoning, labeled by what is inside."
  ],
  "quest.00539AD577BA67F5.title": "A flower for cheese",
  "quest.00539AD577BA67F5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Thistle\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"herbsandharvest:thistle\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" grows wild in nearly every Overworld biome, two blocks tall with purple flowers, and bone meal spreads it like any tall flower. A water bucket, a glass bottle and a thistle make rennet for \"},{\"text\":\"cheese\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"31C11EDE6863ECBA\"}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.704E05D6E5A3C28D.title": "Two blocks tall",
  "quest.704E05D6E5A3C28D.quest_desc": [
    "Corn, eggplant, peas and tomatoes from Herbs and Harvest grow two blocks tall from a single seed. Breaking either half harvests the whole plant, seeds included, so replant after every harvest."
  ],
  "quest.7949F20E085F81AC.title": "The produce basket",
  "quest.7949F20E085F81AC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four bamboo make a \"},{\"text\":\"Produce Basket\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"herbsandharvest:crop_basket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" that holds eight stacks of fruit and vegetables, one of each shown on top. Right-click it with an empty hand to take the latest back.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2E39D96D48C4BBB6.title": "A salt pan",
  "quest.2E39D96D48C4BBB6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Right-click sand with a shovel to dig a salt basin. Fill it with a water bucket or let the rain do it; when it dries, \"},{\"text\":\"Salt\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"herbsandharvest:salt\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" is left behind. A hopper underneath collects it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.693F292BBFAA480B.title": "Plant an orchard",
  "quest.693F292BBFAA480B.quest_desc": [
    "Croptopia's fruit trees grow wild in plains, forests, dark forests and jungles. Two fruits and any sapling craft a new sapling of that fruit, so a single find starts an orchard."
  ],
  "task.6C627140CED710F8.title": "Plains",
  "task.045091F2504847C2.title": "Forests",
  "task.45859B73E0B32E07.title": "Dark forests",
  "task.64F59C744F69AB14.title": "Jungles",
  "quest.0AF3ED5FEB62B928.title": "Every tree in the book",
  "quest.0AF3ED5FEB62B928.quest_desc": [
    "Three saplings from the plains, eleven from forests, four nut trees from dark forests and ten from jungles: every tree Croptopia grows. The Market sells all of them for an emerald each."
  ],
  "quest.0BD708EB0E901A5B.title": "Bark you can eat",
  "quest.0BD708EB0E901A5B.quest_subtitle": "Like a regular log, only tastier.",
  "quest.0BD708EB0E901A5B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Cinnamon grows in the trunk: strip one of Croptopia's jungle cinnamon logs with an axe and \"},{\"text\":\"Cinnamon\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"croptopia:cinnamon\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" falls out.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7A653F67B29F59B1.title": "A handful of nuts",
  "quest.7A653F67B29F59B1.quest_desc": [
    "Almonds, cashews, pecans and walnuts grow on dark forest trees. They go into almond brittle, trail mix, pecan pie and nutty cookies."
  ],
  "quest.6EE73BCEA08C042C.title": "Five from the jungle",
  "quest.6EE73BCEA08C042C.quest_desc": [
    "Banana, mango, coconut, dragon fruit and fig: five jungle trees, five new foods, and every one of them counts as fruit for Pam's punch and salads."
  ],
  "quest.2FAE04CEC54E369D.title": "Pam's orchard",
  "quest.2FAE04CEC54E369D.quest_desc": [
    "Pam's trees hang their fruit as blocks under the leaves. Right-click ripe fruit with an empty hand: it drops and grows back. Eight fruits and any sapling craft a sapling of that tree."
  ],
  "quest.56CDDD1356FA1787.title": "Only in Pam's orchard",
  "quest.56CDDD1356FA1787.quest_desc": [
    "Pomegranate, lychee, papaya, guava and passion fruit: five fruits no other mod here grows. Pam's Trees has 49 fruit trees in all, from acorns to tamarind."
  ],
  "quest.32DA6F16D4DDBBF6.title": "Trees that grow supplies",
  "quest.32DA6F16D4DDBBF6.quest_subtitle": "Paper grows on trees. Finally literal.",
  "quest.32DA6F16D4DDBBF6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Maple trees grow \"},{\"text\":\"Maple Syrup\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pamhc2trees:maplesyrupitem\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on the trunk, paperbark trees grow paper and spiderweb trees grow string. Eight paper or eight string and a sapling craft the last two.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.451F078A12EB81B7.title": "Nine trees at the Market",
  "quest.451F078A12EB81B7.quest_desc": [
    "Nine of Pam's trees repeated Herbs and Harvest ones: avocado, cherry, cinnamon, lemon, lime, orange, peach, pear and plum. Their Pam's versions no longer grow wild; the Market sells those saplings for an emerald each."
  ],
  "quest.5BFC6D8A0B6DBD11.title": "Round trees, endless fruit",
  "quest.5BFC6D8A0B6DBD11.quest_desc": [
    "Herbs and Harvest's eight fruit trees are round and dark green, and grow in almost every Overworld biome. Their leaves keep growing fruit, bone meal hurries it, and the saplings turn up in chests and fit in a flower pot."
  ],
  "quest.45C20B371BF45A31.title": "The cinnamon tree",
  "quest.45C20B371BF45A31.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Herbs and Harvest's cinnamon tree is two blocks tall, and its bark keeps growing back. Strip it with an axe when the bark is mature for \"},{\"text\":\"Cinnamon\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"herbsandharvest:cinnamon\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; saplings grow in tropical biomes.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3608E1E0D8C9FD21.title": "Vines that grow down",
  "quest.3608E1E0D8C9FD21.quest_desc": [
    "Grape vines hang from the underside of a block and grow downward like glow berries, and bone meal speeds them up. Some villages keep a trellis of them; chests hold the rest."
  ],
  "quest.50A6912B6169501B.title": "A merchant comes to town",
  "quest.50A6912B6169501B.quest_subtitle": "He brings his own parachute.",
  "quest.50A6912B6169501B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Planks, logs and red wool make a \"},{\"text\":\"Market\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"farmingforblockheads:market\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Place it and a merchant arrives: down from the sky if the spot is open, up through the floor if not. Emeralds buy seeds and saplings of Croptopia, Pam's, Farmer's Delight and vanilla, and bone meal.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.26389A080A510E7A.title": "Three fertilizers",
  "quest.26389A080A510E7A.quest_desc": [
    "Seeds, gold and a dye make each fertilizer. Used on farmland, red makes crops grow faster, green adds extra crops and yellow keeps the soil from being trampled. Fertilized farmland never wears off."
  ],
  "quest.3D23A751FF1AE437.title": "Nest egg",
  "quest.3D23A751FF1AE437.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Planks and a hay bale make a \"},{\"text\":\"Chicken Nest\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"farmingforblockheads:chicken_nest\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" that picks up every egg laid within eight blocks. No more egg hunts around the coop.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3B1C954C178CDA25.title": "Feeding time",
  "quest.3B1C954C178CDA25.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Planks, hay and a golden carrot make a \"},{\"text\":\"Feeding Trough\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"farmingforblockheads:feeding_trough\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Fill it with the right food and it feeds animals ready to breed within eight blocks, up to 24 of each kind.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Search an animal in EMI: Just Enough Breeding lists what it eats to breed.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3FA285E3389B23B2.title": "Harvest tithe",
  "quest.3FA285E3389B23B2.quest_subtitle": "The pantry is always hungry.",
  "quest.3FA285E3389B23B2.quest_desc": [
    "Two crates of tomatoes and two of cabbages for the common store, once a day. Eighteen of each, packed nine to a crate."
  ],
  "quest.471462F642DDE401.title": "Trade the surplus",
  "quest.471462F642DDE401.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Novice and apprentice farmer villagers may buy Farmer's Delight crops, and the Wandering Trader may sell its seeds.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5EDB0491D1D23CD9.title": "A farm in a pot",
  "quest.5EDB0491D1D23CD9.quest_subtitle": "Farming, apartment edition.",
  "quest.5EDB0491D1D23CD9.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Botany Pot\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"botanypots:terracotta_botany_pot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" grows a crop or a sapling without a field: soil and seed in, harvest out, and its tooltip shows the time and yield. A \"},{\"text\":\"Hopper Botany Pot\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"botanypots:terracotta_hopper_botany_pot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" drops the harvest into the container below.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.74566BCAF79C084B.title": "Pot tiers by act",
  "quest.74566BCAF79C084B.quest_desc": [
    "Better pots cost the act's component, once per tier: the Elite upgrade takes a Propagation Core (III), Ultra an Ecosystem Capsule (IV), Mega a Renewal Engine (V). An upgrade applied to a placed pot of the tier below keeps what is in it."
  ],
  "quest.27B01F863308CB58.title": "Soil that forgets",
  "quest.27B01F863308CB58.quest_subtitle": "Named after the river of oblivion.",
  "quest.27B01F863308CB58.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Soul sand or soil, bone meal, Nether roots or straw and rotten flesh make \"},{\"text\":\"Leteos Compost\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mynethersdelight:letios_compost\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Only in the Nether does it forget itself into \"},{\"text\":\"Resurgent Soil\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mynethersdelight:resurgent_soil\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", faster beside lava or flames: the Nether's rich soil.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2EF8C94237256F52.title": "Nether colonies",
  "quest.2EF8C94237256F52.quest_desc": [
    "Crimson and warped fungi planted on resurgent soil grow into colonies, just as mushrooms do on rich soil. Resurgent soil also spreads the plants around it."
  ],
  "quest.7DD271F093405060.title": "Handle with care",
  "quest.7DD271F093405060.quest_subtitle": "Spicy is an understatement.",
  "quest.7DD271F093405060.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Powdery Cane grows wild in crimson forests, and its berries burst on contact. Cut the stem instead and plant the \"},{\"text\":\"Powdery Cannon\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mynethersdelight:powder_cannon\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; when it fruits it drops \"},{\"text\":\"Bullet Peppers\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mynethersdelight:bullet_pepper\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", which a knife grinds into pepper powder.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.110D03529EA5EBD4.title": "A garden in the sky",
  "quest.110D03529EA5EBD4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Skyroot meadows and forests in the Aether grow wild ginger, parsnip and leek, and \"},{\"text\":\"Peppermint\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aethersdelight:peppermint_leaf\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" bushes. Unification hands you the same ginger, parsnip and leek your fields grow; the peppermint is the Aether's own.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7B42DF34C070F496.title": "What grows in the Twilight",
  "quest.7B42DF34C070F496.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Twilight Forest's plants go into the pot: \"},{\"text\":\"Torchberries\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:torchberries\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" fill pies and fuel the Maze Stove, and \"},{\"text\":\"Liveroot\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:liveroot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" with fiddleheads, fallen leaves, root strands and vines makes a Thousand Plant Stew.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.625B0E890F82013D.title": "A garden at the end",
  "quest.625B0E890F82013D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Chorus Succulent\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ends_delight:chorus_succulent\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" grows in the End Highlands, and a knife on the board splits a chorus fruit into four \"},{\"text\":\"Chorus Fruit Grains\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ends_delight:chorus_fruit_grain\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Both go into End's Delight's feasts.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3F6E3C8B11246C62.title": "Crop rotation",
  "quest.3F6E3C8B11246C62.quest_subtitle": "From the riverbank to the End.",
  "quest.3F6E3C8B11246C62.quest_desc": [
    "Plant every food plant Farmer's Delight counts, nineteen in all: wheat, carrots, potatoes, beetroots, melons, pumpkins, sugar cane, sweet berries, cocoa, kelp, glow berries, both mushrooms, cabbage, onions, tomatoes, rice, nether wart and a chorus flower."
  ],
  "image.5AFF742DD682103F.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Farmer's Delight\",\"color\":\"#E6C766\"}]",
  "image.3CA45C5BACD032E9.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Croptopia and the coast\",\"color\":\"#E6C766\"}]",
  "image.37907D6C41A01930.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Pam's gardens\",\"color\":\"#E6C766\"}]",
  "image.4E27B90839D7A0F1.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Herbs and Harvest\",\"color\":\"#E6C766\"}]",
  "image.25D069F810983504.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Market\",\"color\":\"#E6C766\"}]",
  "image.21D4CBD6D4BD71BF.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Beyond the fence\",\"color\":\"#E6C766\"}]",
  "image.3736F81498DCC77C.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Croptopia\",\"color\":\"#E6C766\"}]",
  "image.65865AE5D6A413FF.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Pam's Trees\",\"color\":\"#E6C766\"}]",
  "image.6FC306FF98580687.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Herbs and Harvest\",\"color\":\"#E6C766\"}]",
  "image.2E88CE6E972731E4.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Farm · Crops and Trees\",\"color\":\"#E6C766\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.798ED1A899A2503E.title": "Back to the Sun of Heliodor",
  "chapter.71AA5DE361B1FD32.title": "Structures and loot",
  "chapter.71AA5DE361B1FD32.chapter_subtitle": [
    "What each structure mod adds, what is worth looting and why every player gets their own chest."
  ],
  "quest.745231331921FF54.title": "A world full of places",
  "quest.745231331921FF54.quest_desc": [
    "One answer per role: YUNG's mods replace vanilla dungeons, mineshafts, temples, witch huts, monuments, fortresses, strongholds and the End island instead of adding a second set, and Repurposed Structures, Dungeons and Taverns, Towns and Towers, Explorify and Hellish Trials fill in around them.",
    "",
    "Structures only appear in newly generated chunks."
  ],
  "quest.74D96402A467B05B.title": "Lootr: a chest for each player",
  "quest.74D96402A467B05B.quest_desc": [
    "Structure chests, barrels, shulkers, minecarts, item frames, decorated pots and even suspicious sand and gravel become Lootr containers: each player opens their own copy. Arriving second is never a waste.",
    "",
    "Breaking one takes sneaking and removes it for everyone. Your first one earns 'X' Marks the Spot."
  ],
  "quest.296E4C9B99FD4B9E.title": "Loot collector",
  "quest.296E4C9B99FD4B9E.quest_desc": [
    "Lootr counts what you open: 10, 25, 50 and 100 containers each earn an advancement, and there is a Centennial Trophy for the most dedicated. Brushing every kind of Lootr suspicious block is Brush It Off.",
    "",
    "Carry On cannot lift Lootr containers, spawners, trial spawners or vaults in this pack."
  ],
  "quest.3F33812A507EFF11.title": "YUNG's: dungeons, mines and huts",
  "quest.3F33812A507EFF11.quest_desc": [
    "Better Dungeons gives skeleton, spider and zombie dungeons real layouts; Better Mineshafts styles them by biome, a good early source of ore and rails; Better Witch Huts adds swamp and cave huts; YUNG's Extras scatters wells and ruins.",
    "",
    "They keep vanilla chest tables, so Artifacts and other mods still add their loot."
  ],
  "quest.6033524BE932FAA1.title": "YUNG's: temples with puzzles",
  "quest.6033524BE932FAA1.quest_desc": [
    "Better Desert Temples are puzzle temples that apply Mining Fatigue while you are inside, so digging around the rooms is not the answer. Better Jungle Temples are trapped and many-roomed.",
    "",
    "Bring a brush: desert structures and trail ruins hide suspicious sand, and the pack's archaeology viewer shows what each one can give."
  ],
  "quest.38DDCCC783CF1767.title": "YUNG's: the big ones",
  "quest.38DDCCC783CF1767.quest_desc": [
    "Better Ocean Monuments, Nether Fortresses, Strongholds and End Island rebuild the big vanilla structures under new IDs: locate them as betteroceanmonuments:ocean_monument, betterfortresses:fortress or betterstrongholds:stronghold. Eyes of Ender and ocean explorer maps still find them.",
    "",
    "The Heliodor Compass uses these same structures in acts III and V."
  ],
  "quest.29F5F44DF6356939.title": "Repurposed Structures",
  "quest.29F5F44DF6356939.quest_desc": [
    "Vanilla structures re-imagined for other biomes and dimensions: mansions in seven styles, biome mineshafts, outposts, pyramids, igloos, ruins, shipwrecks and witch huts, Nether and End strongholds, crimson, warped, mushroom and ocean villages, and ancient cities in the End, the Nether and the ocean.",
    "",
    "Each group has its own advancement."
  ],
  "quest.4D4B19A26212780C.title": "Repurposed: the unusual ones",
  "quest.4D4B19A26212780C.quest_desc": [
    "Some have no vanilla twin: the Jungle Fortress, the Underground Bastion, the Overworld City in the sky, the Nether City and the End-themed Ruined Portal. Dangerous and well stocked.",
    "",
    "Its villager maps say \"Locating... (Do not buy this map until finished)\" while they search. Believe them."
  ],
  "quest.77AC4F74AE0AED43.title": "Find a tavern",
  "quest.77AC4F74AE0AED43.quest_desc": [
    "Dungeons and Taverns builds taverns in many wood styles across the Overworld: a safe place to rest, trade and hear about adventures (Safe Haven), and its cartographer sells maps to the mod's dungeons.",
    "",
    "Two hidden DnT advancements do not load in 1.21.1 and are disabled, so the quest trader has one trade fewer than upstream."
  ],
  "quest.6CD7B0207C292C8D.title": "Dungeons and Taverns mini-bosses",
  "quest.6CD7B0207C292C8D.quest_desc": [
    "Several DnT structures hide a boss room behind keys found inside: the Lone Citadel (a frozen breeze), the Toxic Lair (the Spider Queen), the underwater Trident Trial Monument (an Ancient Guardian) and the End Castle (a haunting phantom). Beating each once is Dungeon Master.",
    "",
    "Shrines are combat trials in five tiers."
  ],
  "quest.324E7D8B1ED78009.title": "Illagers and witches",
  "quest.324E7D8B1ED78009.quest_desc": [
    "DnT adds a whole illager and witch network: manors, hideouts and camps, witch villas, swamp villages, the Badlands Miner Outpost and more; visiting them all is The Ill Manored.",
    "",
    "Its loot hides treasure-only enchantments: Traveler (faster sprint, step-up), Outreach (longer block reach), Photosynthesis (repairs in sunlight) and Illager's Bane."
  ],
  "quest.7949A648A9538C15.title": "Towns and Towers",
  "quest.7949A648A9538C15.quest_desc": [
    "Villages and pillager outposts get a style for almost every biome, plus rare exclusives (Iberian, Mediterranean, Nilotic, Rustic, Swedish and Tudor), a Piglin village and a wandering trader camp.",
    "",
    "More villages, more trades, more spots for a waystone."
  ],
  "quest.41C40BD2B08166F8.title": "Explorify: small stops",
  "quest.41C40BD2B08166F8.quest_desc": [
    "Small vanilla-style places everywhere: campsites, farmsteads, watchtowers, guide posts, supply caches for each forest type, desert shrines, a badlands pyramid, a mausoleum, dark forest settlements, mangrove huts, ruins and even an End shipwreck.",
    "",
    "Open the supply caches in your first days."
  ],
  "quest.7D9A441741BA22FB.title": "Hellish Trials",
  "quest.7D9A441741BA22FB.quest_desc": [
    "Trial chambers in the Nether, with trial spawners and vaults like the Overworld ones.",
    "",
    "Bring fire resistance and a way back. Especially the way back."
  ],
  "quest.283F099B40C6AFCA.title": "Trial chambers and vaults",
  "quest.283F099B40C6AFCA.quest_desc": [
    "Trial chambers are an act I stop: the compass leads you to one until your team reaches First Signal. Beat the trial spawners, collect trial keys and open the vaults (Under Lock and Key).",
    "",
    "Vaults, like Lootr containers, reward each player separately."
  ],
  "quest.7DB4E463C1F1E87E.title": "How to find them",
  "quest.7DB4E463C1F1E87E.quest_desc": [
    "From cheapest to most specific: explore (most are common near villages and rivers), the Explorer's Compass, villager and tavern maps, special locators (Cataclysm eyes, Eternal Starlight Seeking Eyes, Twilight magic maps) and, in act VI, Solsticio's cartographer.",
    "",
    "The tools themselves: the Explore Without Getting Lost chapter."
  ],
  "quest.1C01894D54875656.title": "Worldgen and performance",
  "quest.1C01894D54875656.quest_desc": [
    "Measured on a dedicated server, new Overworld chunks generate noticeably slower than vanilla, mostly because of the whole batch (ores, crops, fauna) rather than one structure mod. Existing chunks are unaffected.",
    "",
    "On a modest PC, explore at a steady pace instead of flying over new land at full speed, and let the world catch up."
  ],
  "quest.698FE5ED4BE18AB2.title": "Cartographer of ruins",
  "quest.698FE5ED4BE18AB2.quest_desc": [
    "Temples solved, fortresses cleared, taverns visited and a hundred Lootr chests opened.",
    "",
    "Somewhere among them Heliodor left its own ruins, and the compass knows which ones matter."
  ],
  "chapter.0D797BF58DA82A00.title": "Travel: waystones, maps and vehicles",
  "chapter.0D797BF58DA82A00.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Get anywhere and back: JourneyMap, the Waystones network, beds on the road and aircraft."
  ],
  "quest.5ED3EEFF545DFC0B.title": "Walking it twice is optional",
  "quest.5ED3EEFF545DFC0B.quest_desc": [
    "The toolkit: JourneyMap for maps and waypoints, Waystones for fast travel between places you have visited, Comforts for sleeping away from home and, from act III, aircraft and late-game teleports.",
    "",
    "The compass says where. This is about getting there, and back in time for dinner."
  ],
  "quest.14793195884A6FFF.title": "JourneyMap: open the map",
  "quest.14793195884A6FFF.quest_desc": [
    "It draws the world as you explore: a minimap in the corner and a full map on &eJ&r, with day, night, topography, biome and cave views; underground it switches to caves on its own.",
    "",
    "FTB Chunks' minimap is off so the two do not overlap; FTB Chunks stays for claims (&eK&r)."
  ],
  "quest.214D3B0E22D5020A.title": "Waypoints and death points",
  "quest.214D3B0E22D5020A.quest_desc": [
    "&eM&r makes a waypoint where you stand; &eB&r on the full map makes one at the cursor (both moved off the backpack key). Waypoints show a beam in the world and can be shared.",
    "",
    "A Death waypoint marks where you fell and leads straight back to your Tombstone grave."
  ],
  "quest.11D3557EB07DBDD1.title": "Find a waystone",
  "quest.11D3557EB07DBDD1.quest_desc": [
    "Waystones spawn in the wild, roughly every 25 chunks in the biome's style, and in some villages. Right-click one to activate it for yourself: from then on it is in your destination list and, by default, on your JourneyMap.",
    "",
    "A glowing stone in the middle of nowhere is always worth the detour."
  ],
  "quest.48B1F5AEFE7478C8.title": "A Warp Stone",
  "quest.48B1F5AEFE7478C8.quest_desc": [
    "An ender pearl, amethyst shards and an emerald. Hold right-click to open your list of activated waystones from anywhere; each use costs durability.",
    "",
    "It is also the heart of every waystone you build."
  ],
  "quest.3B12191E4646294F.title": "Your own waystone",
  "quest.3B12191E4646294F.quest_desc": [
    "Stone bricks, obsidian and a Warp Stone, in mossy, sandy, deepslate, blackstone, Nether, End, purpur, prismarine and mud brick styles. Put one at your base, at each camp and at every structure you will revisit.",
    "",
    "Only the owner can edit a placed waystone, and Carry On cannot move it."
  ],
  "quest.6AC8F125761802DA.title": "What a warp costs",
  "quest.6AC8F125761802DA.quest_desc": [
    "Warps cost experience: within a dimension the cost grows with distance, between dimensions it is flat and higher, capped either way. Warps to global waystones and from warp plates are free.",
    "",
    "Leashed animals come along; pets stay home. Keep some levels in reserve before a long trip."
  ],
  "quest.243D9C659D4F16E0.title": "Scrolls: one-way tickets",
  "quest.243D9C659D4F16E0.quest_desc": [
    "Single use: the &eReturn Scroll&r takes you to your nearest activated waystone, the &eWarp Scroll&r opens the destination list once, a &eBlank Scroll&r used on a waystone becomes a Bound Scroll to it (a gift for a friend who has never been there), and the &ePortal Scroll&r opens a temporary Warp Portal.",
    "",
    "Never leave home without a Return Scroll."
  ],
  "quest.51955BCEF229BF86.title": "Sharestones and warp plates",
  "quest.51955BCEF229BF86.quest_desc": [
    "Sharestones come in sixteen colors, each linking to every other of its color and shared by everyone: perfect for a team network. Warp Plates pair up with shards: step on one, appear on the other, for free.",
    "",
    "Portstones are waystones you can leave from but never arrive at. One-way doors."
  ],
  "quest.0BA11AB7D4F5E416.title": "Solsticio joins the network",
  "quest.0BA11AB7D4F5E416.quest_desc": [
    "When the Town Hall portal opens in act VI, a global Solsticio waystone appears there, so any waystone can reach the city.",
    "",
    "Until then, keep a waystone near your Ark: act V is the busiest act for travel."
  ],
  "quest.1176F66E03A9338E.title": "A bed for the road",
  "quest.1176F66E03A9338E.quest_desc": [
    "A &eSleeping Bag&r skips the night away from home without moving your respawn; crouch to place it. &eHammocks&r hang between two Rope and Nail blocks and let you sleep through the day.",
    "",
    "Your spawn stays at base while you camp at the edge of the map."
  ],
  "quest.39BDBAC06BA5F7D3.title": "Small travel fixes",
  "quest.39BDBAC06BA5F7D3.quest_desc": [
    "Jump Boat lets a boat hop onto the shore instead of getting stuck or breaking. Fireproof Boats adds crimson and warped boats that survive lava like their planks. Nether Portal Fix links return portals to the one you came from, so two bases never share a Nether exit by accident."
  ],
  "quest.487E9F0D517D781D.title": "Aircraft (act III)",
  "quest.487E9F0D517D781D.quest_desc": [
    "Immersive Aircraft builds airships, biplanes, quadrocopters and gyrodynes. Here the engine needs a Power Regulator and the gyrodyne a reinforced alloy, both act III; the rest is the mod's own, with no pack gates on fuel or repairs.",
    "",
    "Dismount moved to &eF12&r. Mind the landing."
  ],
  "quest.77A8A9F84C5EA7C9.title": "Late-game teleports",
  "quest.77A8A9F84C5EA7C9.quest_desc": [
    "Ender IO's Travel Anchor and Staff of Travelling take an act III reinforced alloy, and Tombstone's tablets take you home or to a memorized place.",
    "",
    "Pick one system for your base network and keep it simple. Three half-built networks add up to zero."
  ],
  "quest.18E4ED0DBED8F947.title": "Always a way back",
  "quest.18E4ED0DBED8F947.quest_desc": [
    "A map that remembers, a waypoint on every find, a waystone network, a scroll in your pocket and a bed on your back.",
    "",
    "Getting lost is now a choice."
  ],
  "chapter.3608810979379C92.title": "Farm · Kitchen",
  "chapter.3608810979379C92.chapter_subtitle": [
    "A table for every guest: the pot, the board and the skillet, four worlds of Delights, and a menu that pays in hearts."
  ],
  "quest.1B01756BFFD75E45.title": "A pot on the fire",
  "quest.1B01756BFFD75E45.quest_subtitle": "Grandma's first appliance.",
  "quest.1B01756BFFD75E45.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two bricks, five iron ingots, a wooden shovel and a water bucket make a \"},{\"text\":\"Cooking Pot\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"farmersdelight:cooking_pot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Set it over heat: fire, a campfire, lava, magma or a \"},{\"text\":\"Stove\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"farmersdelight:stove\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Up to six ingredients go in; bowl meals also want a bowl in its container slot.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.36BC5D4950D2E5E3.title": "Soup of the day",
  "quest.36BC5D4950D2E5E3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A carrot, a potato, a beetroot and a leafy green such as cabbage, with a bowl waiting in the pot: \"},{\"text\":\"Vegetable Soup\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"farmersdelight:vegetable_soup\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Two of them are half of the pack's first \"},{\"text\":\"Travel Rations\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:ration_bundle\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4695455C2AEC2B69.title": "Mind the board",
  "quest.4695455C2AEC2B69.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Planks and two sticks make a \"},{\"text\":\"Cutting Board\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"farmersdelight:cutting_board\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Put an item on it and use it with a tool: a knife slices food, an axe strips a log into \"},{\"text\":\"Tree Bark\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"farmersdelight:tree_bark\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Raw beef becomes \"},{\"text\":\"Minced Beef\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"farmersdelight:minced_beef\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", dough becomes \"},{\"text\":\"Raw Pasta\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"farmersdelight:raw_pasta\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Each Fortune level on the tool adds 10% to the odds of the rare results.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7E603A9650927253.title": "A stove of your own",
  "quest.7E603A9650927253.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three iron ingots over four brick blocks and a campfire: a \"},{\"text\":\"Stove\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"farmersdelight:stove\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It heats the pot above it and cooks up to six items on top with campfire recipes. It also counts as a passive heater under a Create boiler.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0A07CF5E464A415B.title": "Hot off the skillet",
  "quest.0A07CF5E464A415B.quest_subtitle": "Can double as a frying pan. It is one.",
  "quest.0A07CF5E464A415B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four iron ingots and a brick make a \"},{\"text\":\"Skillet\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"farmersdelight:skillet\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Hold food in your other hand and use it within a block of any heat, or while you are on fire: a campfire's thirty seconds become six. Sneak to set it down as a block.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Fire Aspect on the skillet shortens that to four seconds at level I and three at level II. It is also a fine blunt weapon.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2ACD7F355EDDAEF7.title": "A glorious feast",
  "quest.2ACD7F355EDDAEF7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Some meals are too big for one plate. Craft a \"},{\"text\":\"Roast Chicken\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"farmersdelight:roast_chicken_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" or cook a stuffed pumpkin, place it and serve it with a bowl, one portion at a time. Honey glazed ham, shepherd's pie and the gleaming salad serve the same way.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1B78187A9833F748.title": "Pies count too",
  "quest.1B78187A9833F748.quest_subtitle": "Dessert, but it counts as strategy.",
  "quest.1B78187A9833F748.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three wheat, three apples, two sugar and a \"},{\"text\":\"Pie Crust\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"farmersdelight:pie_crust\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": an \"},{\"text\":\"Apple Pie\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"farmersdelight:apple_pie\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Placed, it gives four bites by hand, or four slices with a knife. A bite eaten from a block also turns surplus into buffs, cakes and cheesecakes included.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3DD29430B6B744F4.title": "Nourished",
  "quest.3DD29430B6B744F4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Most pot meals give \"},{\"text\":\"Nourishment\",\"color\":\"#E6C766\"},{\"text\":\": while it lasts the hunger bar stops dropping, except when saturation is healing you. Vanilla soups and stews give it here too. A good stew before a long trip is the cheapest travel insurance in the pack.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.484404374247F7B6.title": "Master Chef",
  "quest.484404374247F7B6.quest_subtitle": "Twenty-seven plates. Nobody said at once.",
  "quest.484404374247F7B6.quest_desc": [
    "One course of every meal Farmer's Delight serves: twenty-seven dishes, from cooked rice to the stuffed pumpkin, eaten by you. Each new one also counts for Spice of Life.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Soups, stews, pastas, the grill and every feast on the table. The pot, the board and the skillet have all earned their place."
  ],
  "quest.6209169BDCFA8F8D.title": "Soup kitchen",
  "quest.6209169BDCFA8F8D.quest_subtitle": "Same time tomorrow?",
  "quest.6209169BDCFA8F8D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight \"},{\"text\":\"Vegetable Soups\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"farmersdelight:vegetable_soup\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for the common store, once a day. A pot keeps cooking while the bowls last.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7BE9272565596766.title": "Heat goes through",
  "quest.7BE9272565596766.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A hopper or a Create chute between the pot and the fire still passes the heat, and pulls the finished meals out. Ingredients go in from the top, bowls from the sides.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.494730E1B5502978.title": "One machine per recipe",
  "quest.494730E1B5502978.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Once Create turns, the \"},{\"text\":\"Slicer\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"28984D492046759D\"}},{\"text\":\" runs the cutting-board recipes. Central Kitchen's saw and deployer copies of them and Slice and Dice's basin cooking are off, so each recipe shows up in one machine only.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4F5B21376BE057BC.title": "Wild butcher",
  "quest.4F5B21376BE057BC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Kill a pig or a hoglin with a knife and it drops \"},{\"text\":\"Ham\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"farmersdelight:ham\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Smoke it for \"},{\"text\":\"Smoked Ham\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"farmersdelight:smoked_ham\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", the heart of the honey glazed feast, or take it to the board: two porkchops and a bone.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.407C269A4181174F.title": "If you can't take the heat",
  "quest.407C269A4181174F.quest_subtitle": "Or get out of the kitchen.",
  "quest.407C269A4181174F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Knives climb the usual ladder: flint, iron, gold, diamond, and a whole netherite ingot at the smithing table for the \"},{\"text\":\"Netherite Knife\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"farmersdelight:netherite_knife\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". A better knife lasts longer; Fortune on it pays on the board.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4F75C73313B9BA5C.title": "Staff meals",
  "quest.4F75C73313B9BA5C.quest_subtitle": "The dog eats better than you did in act I.",
  "quest.4F75C73313B9BA5C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Rotten flesh, bone meal, raw meat and rice in the pot make \"},{\"text\":\"Dog Food\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"farmersdelight:dog_food\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; hay or a rice bale, two apples and a golden carrot make \"},{\"text\":\"Horse Feed\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"farmersdelight:horse_feed\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Their tooltips list what they do for a tamed wolf or a mount.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5A61644E1853D20B.title": "A second set of utensils",
  "quest.5A61644E1853D20B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Croptopia cooks in the crafting grid with its own tools: a \"},{\"text\":\"Frying Pan\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"croptopia:frying_pan\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for over fifty recipes, a \"},{\"text\":\"Cooking Pot\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"croptopia:cooking_pot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for jams and ice cream, a \"},{\"text\":\"Food Press\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"croptopia:food_press\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for juices and oils, a \"},{\"text\":\"Mortar and Pestle\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"croptopia:mortar_and_pestle\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a \"},{\"text\":\"Knife\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"croptopia:knife\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4ECCD65911905F15.title": "Press, pour, drink",
  "quest.4ECCD65911905F15.quest_subtitle": "Hydration with extra steps.",
  "quest.4ECCD65911905F15.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A glass bottle and the press turn grapes into \"},{\"text\":\"Grape Juice\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"croptopia:grape_juice\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", lemons into lemonade and soybeans into soy milk; two grapes make \"},{\"text\":\"Wine\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"croptopia:wine\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", hops and barley make beer. Twenty-two drinks in all.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2FF7F7B153C02B02.title": "Dinner around the world",
  "quest.2FF7F7B153C02B02.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Croptopia cooks by country: a \"},{\"text\":\"Burrito\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"croptopia:burrito\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" of tortilla, rice, black beans and tomato; \"},{\"text\":\"Fish and Chips\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"croptopia:fish_and_chips\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a \"},{\"text\":\"Croque Monsieur\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"croptopia:croque_monsieur\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" from the frying pan; \"},{\"text\":\"Sushi\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"croptopia:sushi\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" of seagrass, fish and rice.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2E5B0F2EDA032D7D.title": "A breakfast beyond reason",
  "quest.2E5B0F2EDA032D7D.quest_subtitle": "The most important meal of the campaign.",
  "quest.2E5B0F2EDA032D7D.quest_desc": [
    "A tuna sandwich from a dungeon chest, mountain salt from a shipwreck, cooked ravager meat, a cake crowned with a nether star, an omelette of the dragon egg itself and the big breakfast. Six plates, one very long morning."
  ],
  "reward.50AA44274A637CE5.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.0819A2C4F788D8CE.title": "Pam's utensil drawer",
  "quest.0819A2C4F788D8CE.quest_desc": [
    "Pam's Food Core cooks in the crafting grid with nine tools that are never used up. Copper makes the pot, skillet, saucepan and cutting board; terracotta the juicer and bakeware; planks the mixing bowl, andesite the grinder and a log the roller. About 180 dishes follow, most from ingredients you already have."
  ],
  "quest.34509DE6AFBF7254.title": "Stock the pantry",
  "quest.34509DE6AFBF7254.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A water bucket makes eight \"},{\"text\":\"Fresh Water\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pamhc2foodcore:freshwateritem\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a milk bucket eight fresh milk. The pot turns water into \"},{\"text\":\"Salt\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pamhc2foodcore:saltitem\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and milk into \"},{\"text\":\"Butter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pamhc2foodcore:butteritem\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", or into \"},{\"text\":\"Cheese\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pamhc2foodcore:cheeseitem\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" with salt. The grinder makes \"},{\"text\":\"Flour\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pamhc2foodcore:flouritem\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" from wheat or other grains.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0BEBA194BF209D26.title": "Sunday chicken",
  "quest.0BEBA194BF209D26.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Pot, flour, raw chicken and cooking oil: \"},{\"text\":\"Fried Chicken\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pamhc2foodcore:friedchickenitem\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Mixing bowl, baked potato, butter and salt: \"},{\"text\":\"Mashed Potatoes\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pamhc2foodcore:mashedpotatoesitem\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Both on the cutting board with a vegetable: a \"},{\"text\":\"Chicken Dinner\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pamhc2foodcore:chickendinneritem\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", one of the routes to \"},{\"text\":\"Travel Rations\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"2FEA6E9F24C83087\"}},{\"text\":\".\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The roller presses cooking oil out of canola, nuts or vegetables.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.441A807E8AF62C26.title": "Any fruit will do",
  "quest.441A807E8AF62C26.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Pam's recipes ask for fruit by kind, not by mod: three of any fruit in the juicer make \"},{\"text\":\"Fruit Punch\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pamhc2foodcore:fruitpunchitem\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", two on the cutting board a \"},{\"text\":\"Fruit Salad\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"pamhc2foodcore:fruitsaladitem\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Every orchard in the pack feeds them.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.57AED951CA2AC124.title": "Epic bacon",
  "quest.57AED951CA2AC124.quest_subtitle": "Seven colors, one strip.",
  "quest.57AED951CA2AC124.quest_desc": [
    "Bakeware, cooked pork and seven dyes: red, orange, yellow, green, blue, purple and pink. Nobody asked for rainbow bacon. Pam made it anyway."
  ],
  "reward.6EBAB0F7B73C063E.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.31C11EDE6863ECBA.title": "Say cheese",
  "quest.31C11EDE6863ECBA.quest_subtitle": "Curds, whey and patience.",
  "quest.31C11EDE6863ECBA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Heat a cauldron from below and pour in milk, then add \"},{\"text\":\"Rennet\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"herbsandharvest:rennet\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" at once, or the milk turns to cream. Wait for curds and whey, add \"},{\"text\":\"Salt\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"herbsandharvest:salt\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", and out comes a wheel. Cow's milk gives \"},{\"text\":\"Raw Cheddar\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"herbsandharvest:raw_cheddar\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Rennet is a water bucket, a glass bottle and a \"},{\"text\":\"Thistle\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"00539AD577BA67F5\"}},{\"text\":\"; salt comes from a \"},{\"text\":\"salt basin\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"2E39D96D48C4BBB6\"}},{\"text\":\". A dispenser can add both.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.44C544953C3BC486.title": "Not only cows",
  "quest.44C544953C3BC486.quest_subtitle": "The camel is not amused.",
  "quest.44C544953C3BC486.quest_desc": [
    "A bucket on a goat or a sheep milks it; sneak and use it on a camel. Each milk makes other cheeses: goat for chèvre, sheep for gouda, camel for caravane, and mixes for parmesan, swiss, feta and ricotta."
  ],
  "quest.4A040B502207961E.title": "Time does the rest",
  "quest.4A040B502207961E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Hard cheeses age on a \"},{\"text\":\"Cheese Aging Shelf\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"herbsandharvest:cheese_shelf\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", two wheels at a time; hoppers load it and empty it. An \"},{\"text\":\"Aged Cheddar\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"herbsandharvest:aged_cheddar\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" set down gives four wedges, or four on the cutting board. A placed wheel never comes back up.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.13F59C97FF90F6C7.title": "Eight servings, one pan",
  "quest.13F59C97FF90F6C7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Fill an iron \"},{\"text\":\"Baking Pan\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"herbsandharvest:pan\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" with the ingredients, bake it in a furnace and set the \"},{\"text\":\"Pan of Lasagna\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"herbsandharvest:lasagna_pan\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on the table. Each \"},{\"text\":\"Dinner Plate\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"herbsandharvest:dinner_plate\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" takes one of its eight servings.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.24AFEBEE9D973F10.title": "The field sandwich",
  "quest.24AFEBEE9D973F10.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Cooked beef, two bread slices, cheddar, lettuce, mayonnaise and tomato: a \"},{\"text\":\"Beef and Cheddar Sandwich\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"herbsandharvest:beef_cheddar\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Two of them and two \"},{\"text\":\"Fish Stews\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"farmersdelight:fish_stew\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" are another way to pack \"},{\"text\":\"Travel Rations\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"2FEA6E9F24C83087\"}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.418EF78F1339E392.title": "A kitchen that reads recipes",
  "quest.418EF78F1339E392.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Smelt a book into \"},{\"text\":\"Cooking for Blockheads I\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"cookingforblockheads:recipe_book\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": it lists what you can cook right now. Two diamonds and two crafting tables turn it into \"},{\"text\":\"Cooking for Blockheads II\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"cookingforblockheads:crafting_book\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", which cooks from your inventory. Built into a \"},{\"text\":\"Cooking Table\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"cookingforblockheads:cooking_table\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", it cooks from the whole kitchen.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0291675EEB56ED5D.title": "Everything within reach",
  "quest.0291675EEB56ED5D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A chest and an iron door make a \"},{\"text\":\"Fridge\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"cookingforblockheads:white_fridge\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; a \"},{\"text\":\"Kitchen Counter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"cookingforblockheads:counter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and cabinets store more. Joined to the cooking table, whatever they hold counts as an ingredient. Kitchen floor and connectors link blocks across a gap or around a corner.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.261EFAA27C928268.title": "Water and milk on tap",
  "quest.261EFAA27C928268.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Sink\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"cookingforblockheads:sink\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" gives the kitchen endless water, and a \"},{\"text\":\"Milk Jar\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"cookingforblockheads:milk_jar\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" keeps milk for its recipes.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A cow nearby and something heavy could keep that jar full forever.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.261A8D385121A7A3.title": "The oven",
  "quest.261A8D385121A7A3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A furnace dressed in iron and black glass: an \"},{\"text\":\"Oven\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"cookingforblockheads:white_oven\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" that cooks for the whole kitchen, with its own fuel and slots. A \"},{\"text\":\"Heating Unit\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"cookingforblockheads:heating_unit\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" lets it run on energy instead of fuel.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3938174A2187F7D8.title": "Cow in a jar",
  "quest.3938174A2187F7D8.quest_subtitle": "Ethically questionable dairy.",
  "quest.3938174A2187F7D8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Lure a cow onto a \"},{\"text\":\"Milk Jar\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"cookingforblockheads:milk_jar\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and drop an anvil on it. What is left, a \"},{\"text\":\"Cow in a Jar\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"cookingforblockheads:cow_jar\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", makes milk forever and asks no questions.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.617459E01B90D644.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.27D38F5307E82FBD.title": "Rice, the right way",
  "quest.27D38F5307E82FBD.quest_subtitle": "Not too wet, not too dry.",
  "quest.27D38F5307E82FBD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Sushi Go Crafting's seeds come from breaking grass, and its rice grows underwater on dirt. A \"},{\"text\":\"Rice Cooker\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sushigocrafting:rice_cooker\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" of iron, a furnace, redstone and a light pressure plate turns rice, water and fuel into \"},{\"text\":\"Cooked Rice\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sushigocrafting:cooked_rice\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7016ED64739DFD99.title": "Cleaver and board",
  "quest.7016ED64739DFD99.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Put fish or produce on the sushi \"},{\"text\":\"Cutting Board\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sushigocrafting:cutting_board\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and use the \"},{\"text\":\"Cleaver Knife\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sushigocrafting:cleaver_knife\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on it: salmon and tuna turn into fillets, avocado and cucumber into slices, cod into imitation crab. Sneak and use the board to take things back.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.349CB0D0BC4F2090.title": "Pressed seaweed",
  "quest.349CB0D0BC4F2090.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Drop a dried kelp block between a piston and an iron block, and the piston squeezes it into \"},{\"text\":\"Nori Sheets\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sushigocrafting:nori_sheets\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Kelp grows in any ocean.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3592D742DC428127.title": "Tuna and shrimp",
  "quest.3592D742DC428127.quest_subtitle": "Sashimi grade.",
  "quest.3592D742DC428127.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Tuna and shrimp swim in the oceans and drop \"},{\"text\":\"Raw Tuna\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sushigocrafting:raw_tuna\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and \"},{\"text\":\"Shrimp\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sushigocrafting:shrimp\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; a bucket brings them home alive. Killing fish also drops \"},{\"text\":\"Tobiko\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sushigocrafting:tobiko\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5E52DEB7BB3ECF42.title": "The perfect roll",
  "quest.5E52DEB7BB3ECF42.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Bamboo and string make a \"},{\"text\":\"Roller\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sushigocrafting:roller\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Pick the sushi, place the ingredients, set how much of each, then click the roller until it rolls. The perfect weight makes a better \"},{\"text\":\"Salmon Maki\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"sushigocrafting:salmon_maki\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", and the roller remembers every perfect weight you find.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3B4B147E249F11A5.title": "Omakase",
  "quest.3B4B147E249F11A5.quest_subtitle": "Chef's choice. The chef is you.",
  "quest.3B4B147E249F11A5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Nigiri, gunkan, temaki, california and onigiri: each style takes different ingredients, and ingredients carry effects. \"},{\"text\":\"Acquired Taste\",\"color\":\"#E6C766\"},{\"text\":\" adds food to what you eat, \"},{\"text\":\"Small Bites\",\"color\":\"#E6C766\"},{\"text\":\" sometimes spares the bite, \"},{\"text\":\"Steady Hands\",\"color\":\"#E6C766\"},{\"text\":\" adds weight on the board.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5F3E54942A4BE8EF.title": "Hearts for variety",
  "quest.5F3E54942A4BE8EF.quest_subtitle": "An apple a day is not enough.",
  "quest.5F3E54942A4BE8EF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Spice of Life counts every different food you eat and adds a heart at 10, 25, 45, 70 and 100 of them: five over the base ten, and death keeps them. A book and a carrot make the \"},{\"text\":\"Food Book\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"solcarrot:food_book\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" that shows your list.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A food must fill at least half a drumstick to count.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.61DA3B7739F1D466.title": "Two messages at once",
  "quest.61DA3B7739F1D466.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"When a new food both counts for Spice of Life and overflows, Spice of Life's line stays above the hotbar; the buff icons and sparkles still show what you got. AppleSkin previews a food's hunger and saturation: aim for the surplus.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.795AA46FEC18B774.title": "Nothing eaten is wasted",
  "quest.795AA46FEC18B774.quest_desc": [
    "Vanilla stops hunger at 20 and saturation at your hunger level; whatever a meal adds past that is lost. Here the surplus turns into short random buffs, more and longer the bigger it is. You only eat below 20 hunger, so most surplus is saturation: a rich meal when you are not that hungry."
  ],
  "quest.20A33F8FE7351249.title": "How many, how long",
  "quest.20A33F8FE7351249.quest_desc": [
    "Under 2 points of surplus, nothing. From 2, one buff, plus one every 10 points, up to three. Durations grow with the surplus and top out at 20 points; from 16, buffs that allow it come at level II. The action bar names what you got.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "No buffs in creative or spectator, nor for fake players such as Create deployers."
  ],
  "quest.632BB29C19DACBBF.title": "The buff pool",
  "quest.632BB29C19DACBBF.quest_desc": [
    "Drawn by weight, never twice in one meal: Haste, Speed, Absorption and Luck (up to II), Regeneration, Strength, Resistance, Water Breathing and Night Vision. A buff only adds or extends; it never replaces a stronger or endless effect.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Server owners: every number lives in data/entrelumen/satiety/overflow.json, and a datapack at that path replaces it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1D8BC6BE01CD5AD2.title": "Worked examples",
  "quest.1D8BC6BE01CD5AD2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"With no recent overeating: bread at 19 hunger and 15 saturation is 5 points, one buff. A \"},{\"text\":\"Plate of Roast Chicken\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"farmersdelight:roast_chicken\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" at 14 and 8 is 17 points: two buffs, level II where allowed. A cookie at 19 and 19 is 1 point: nothing.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1220B712D2C97C4B.title": "Glut",
  "quest.1220B712D2C97C4B.quest_subtitle": "Pace yourself.",
  "quest.1220B712D2C97C4B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"After a buff, ten seconds of nothing. Every surplus also feeds a hidden glut that halves every five minutes; the more glut you carry, the less new surplus is worth. Five \"},{\"text\":\"Honey Bottles\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:honey_bottle\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in a row buy one buff and a stomachache.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4054F7EA70F42E88.title": "Food that ignores a full bar",
  "quest.4054F7EA70F42E88.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Golden apples, chorus fruit, suspicious stew, honey bottles and some drinks go down at full hunger, so they are the only way to overflow hunger itself. Space them out: the glut remembers.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2FEA6E9F24C83087.title": "Rations for the road",
  "quest.2FEA6E9F24C83087.quest_subtitle": "Pack a lunch. The road is long.",
  "quest.2FEA6E9F24C83087.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three recipes share one drawing, bowls on the axis and dishes at the sides: two Vegetable Soups with two cooked Aquaculture fish fillets or two \"},{\"text\":\"Chicken Dinners\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"0BEBA194BF209D26\"}},{\"text\":\", or two Fish Stews with two \"},{\"text\":\"Beef and Cheddar Sandwiches\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"24AFEBEE9D973F10\"}},{\"text\":\". The bowls come back.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.408556EEDFCE671E.title": "The habitation charter",
  "quest.408556EEDFCE671E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"In act V the Ark needs a place worth coming back to: the \"},{\"text\":\"Habitation Charter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:habitation_contract\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" takes two Fish Stews, two Mixed Salads, an AE2 Calculation Processor and two Travel Rations. A kitchen that cooks by itself turns it into an errand.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.57235F2902A239A5.title": "A stove for the Nether",
  "quest.57235F2902A239A5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Nether bricks over polished blackstone bricks and a campfire: the \"},{\"text\":\"Nether Stove\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mynethersdelight:nether_bricks_stove\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", blue with a soul campfire. My Nether's Delight cooks hoglin loin, strider and ghast in the same pot and on the same board.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.76F38BDBF0F447AF.title": "The whole hoglin",
  "quest.76F38BDBF0F447AF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Hoglin hide, hams, loins and both fungus colonies make a \"},{\"text\":\"Raw Stuffed Hoglin\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mynethersdelight:raw_stuffed_hoglin\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Into the pot with a hot spice, a crimson fungus and two nether salads: a \"},{\"text\":\"Roast Stuffed Hoglin\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mynethersdelight:roast_stuffed_hoglin\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for the whole crew.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Hide comes off a hoglin killed with something lighter than a sword: a knife.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.04397981AE0EF92C.title": "A stove at the end of the world",
  "quest.04397981AE0EF92C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Popped chorus fruit, end stone bricks and a campfire: the \"},{\"text\":\"End Stove\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ends_delight:end_stove\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". End's Delight cuts shulker meat, dragon meat and chorus fruit on the same board, and makes knives of end stone and purpur.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.42D25BDE037AB337.title": "An egg worth a star",
  "quest.42D25BDE037AB337.quest_subtitle": "Omelette of legends.",
  "quest.42D25BDE037AB337.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four obsidian, four end crystals and a dragon tooth from the Ender Dragon make a \"},{\"text\":\"Non Hatchable Dragon Egg\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ends_delight:non_hatchable_dragon_egg\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Crack it on the cutting board with a nether star as the tool: liquid egg, and a shell to cook the feasts in.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6DC28439D3B85705.title": "Chewy, and it teleports",
  "quest.6DC28439D3B85705.quest_subtitle": "Chew responsibly.",
  "quest.6DC28439D3B85705.quest_desc": [
    "Enderman gristle does to you what it did to the enderman: one bite and you are somewhere else. The game even has a death message for landing badly."
  ],
  "reward.60974DC33B653987.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.2B2C389B01006E55.title": "Cooking above the clouds",
  "quest.2B2C389B01006E55.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Arkenium, a metal of the Aether that needs a zanite pickaxe, tops the \"},{\"text\":\"Holystone Stove\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aethersdelight:holystone_stove\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" over holystone bricks and a campfire. Aether's Delight adds moa roasts, knives of holystone, zanite and gravitite, and its own furnace and smoker.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1DC8387EA4042DAE.title": "Cookie cutters",
  "quest.1DC8387EA4042DAE.quest_subtitle": "Run, run, as fast as you can.",
  "quest.1DC8387EA4042DAE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Arkenium nuggets bend into cutters: a man, a star and a \"},{\"text\":\"Moa Cookie Cutter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aethersdelight:cookie_cutter_moa\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Egg, ginger spice, wheat and sugar make the dough; cut it on the board with a cutter as the tool and bake a \"},{\"text\":\"Gingerbread Moa\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aethersdelight:gingerbread_moa\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4C3A5C1111D60D0A.title": "A pot that brings its own fire",
  "quest.4C3A5C1111D60D0A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Mazestone bricks, fiery ingots, an ironwood shovel and a water bucket: the \"},{\"text\":\"Fiery Cooking Pot\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightdelight:fiery_cooking_pot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" heats itself and cooks Twilight meals faster. The \"},{\"text\":\"Maze Stove\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightdelight:maze_stove\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", of knightmetal and torchberries, speeds them up too.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3D4696261A8F3CD7.title": "Knives from the Twilight",
  "quest.3D4696261A8F3CD7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Ironwood, steeleaf and knightmetal each make a knife; the knightly one hits armored targets harder. The \"},{\"text\":\"Fiery Knife\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightdelight:fiery_knife\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" burns what it hits and cooks food as it cuts.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.04D32E12B66C0A34.title": "Experiment 113",
  "quest.04D32E12B66C0A34.quest_subtitle": "Do not ask what happened to 111 and 112.",
  "quest.04D32E12B66C0A34.quest_desc": [
    "Put the Ur-Ghast's trophy on a cutting board and use a knife on it: nine Experiment 113, four Experiment 115 and, one time in ten, an Experiment 110. Nobody knows what the numbers mean."
  ],
  "reward.0C0443FC3EF3C16D.title": "Secret found",
  "image.49A00E45C90ECB45.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Farmer's Delight\",\"color\":\"#E6C766\"}]",
  "image.33E72D4822F8141D.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Croptopia\",\"color\":\"#E6C766\"}]",
  "image.1E01BC71EE42CB21.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Pam's HarvestCraft\",\"color\":\"#E6C766\"}]",
  "image.281740E029F76B94.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Herbs and Harvest\",\"color\":\"#E6C766\"}]",
  "image.4A451BA4055EE88E.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Cooking for Blockheads\",\"color\":\"#E6C766\"}]",
  "image.67C1CB084C56CA2E.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Sushi Go Crafting\",\"color\":\"#E6C766\"}]",
  "image.31FF42BF14C129D2.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The menu: variety and surplus\",\"color\":\"#E6C766\"}]",
  "image.2874AD900DCA5AE5.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"For the road\",\"color\":\"#E6C766\"}]",
  "image.2CC184F121CAD5A6.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Nether and End\",\"color\":\"#E6C766\"}]",
  "image.08DB16A85AA25A06.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Aether and Twilight\",\"color\":\"#E6C766\"}]",
  "image.2DB9CD27223AEF3C.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Farm · Kitchen\",\"color\":\"#E6C766\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.5071092AC323EBF3.title": "Back to the Sun of Heliodor",
  "chapter.523A3AABA8EB23F1.title": "Mystical Agriculture · Essence",
  "chapter.523A3AABA8EB23F1.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Five furrows, one per tier: inferium in the first, diamonds in the last."
  ],
  "quest.252518C96A668BF4.title": "First essence",
  "quest.252518C96A668BF4.quest_subtitle": "Every mob pays a tithe, sometimes.",
  "quest.252518C96A668BF4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Most mobs drop an \"},{\"text\":\"Inferium Essence\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:inferium_essence\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" one kill in five, and \"},{\"text\":\"Inferium Ore\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:inferium_ore\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", between Y -32 and 64, breaks into two to four, more with Fortune. Collect eight: they buy your first seeds.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1E897EF672669A87.title": "The other half",
  "quest.1E897EF672669A87.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Prosperity Ore\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:prosperity_ore\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" sits deeper, from Y -60 to 24, and breaks into one to four \"},{\"text\":\"Prosperity Shards\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:prosperity_shard\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Shards turn plain things magical: seed bases, crystals, ingots and gems all start here.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.39DA614DB7567591.title": "Eight pedestals and a wand",
  "quest.39DA614DB7567591.quest_subtitle": "Seed crafting, now in 3D.",
  "quest.39DA614DB7567591.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Gold, red wool and stone make the \"},{\"text\":\"Infusion Altar\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:infusion_altar\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and its eight \"},{\"text\":\"Infusion Pedestals\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:infusion_pedestal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; placed, the altar shows where each one goes. Load the pedestals, set the centre item on the altar and tap it with a \"},{\"text\":\"Wand\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:wand\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "The pedestals stand three blocks out on each side and two out on each diagonal. The wand is an inferium essence, a stick and a stone."
  ],
  "quest.054EA259896B2E80.title": "The heart of every seed",
  "quest.054EA259896B2E80.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four \"},{\"text\":\"Prosperity Shards\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:prosperity_shard\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" around a wheat seed make a \"},{\"text\":\"Prosperity Seed Base\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:prosperity_seed_base\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", the altar's centre piece for every resource seed. The pedestals take four of the material and four essences of the seed's tier.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7FF967D445354074.title": "Ingots and gems of luck",
  "quest.7FF967D445354074.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four shards around an iron ingot make a \"},{\"text\":\"Prosperity Ingot\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:prosperity_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; around a diamond, a \"},{\"text\":\"Prosperity Gemstone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:prosperity_gemstone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Add two essences of a tier and they become that tier's ingot or gemstone: the metal of tools, upgrades and accelerators.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.375DF0A306B9F117.title": "Growth from below",
  "quest.375DF0A306B9F117.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four inferium, four stone and an \"},{\"text\":\"Inferium Gemstone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:inferium_gemstone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make three \"},{\"text\":\"Inferium Growth Accelerators\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:inferium_growth_accelerator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Stacked under the farmland, each one gives the first plant above it, up to nine blocks up, a growth tick every ten seconds.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Each tier reaches nine blocks further, up to 54 for awakened supremium, and tiers mix freely while the plant is in range."
  ],
  "quest.3964CD9DEA254664.title": "The manual in the box",
  "quest.3964CD9DEA254664.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A book and one Inferium Essence make Mystical Agriculture's own guide book: every block, machine and augment, each with its recipe.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.196AA88954C3825D.title": "A wand that never gets lost",
  "quest.196AA88954C3825D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A redstone pulse switches the altar on just like the wand, and it finishes the craft five seconds later. A button on a block beside it saves you hunting for the wand.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6C7A05FE816F93CF.title": "What this pack changes",
  "quest.6C7A05FE816F93CF.quest_desc": [
    "Nothing gates the seeds: every recipe here is the mod's own. The Altar of Growth speeds mystical crops but never multiplies their essence, and Mekanism More Machine's planting recipes for these seeds are removed."
  ],
  "quest.20BEA5C813745DD5.title": "Bees with essence",
  "quest.20BEA5C813745DD5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Productive Bees keeps essence bees too: an Inferium Bee's combs spin into two to four inferium essence in a centrifuge, and the higher tiers have bees of their own.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1C930EDE6CE6C782.title": "Essence, gift-wrapped",
  "quest.1C930EDE6CE6C782.quest_subtitle": "Some people open presents very carefully.",
  "quest.1C930EDE6CE6C782.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Silk Touch keeps \"},{\"text\":\"Inferium Ore\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:inferium_ore\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" whole. A furnace turns it into one essence; a pickaxe would have given two to four.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.68406D1347A52E09.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.54D72FA681247A52.title": "Seeds that grow essence",
  "quest.54D72FA681247A52.quest_subtitle": "Magic, in rows.",
  "quest.54D72FA681247A52.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight inferium around a wheat seed make \"},{\"text\":\"Inferium Seeds\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:inferium_seeds\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". On plain farmland each harvest gives one essence and the seed back. Bone meal vanishes into them without a sprout.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5411392CCA652CA0.title": "Seasoned soil",
  "quest.5411392CCA652CA0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Right-click farmland with \"},{\"text\":\"Inferium Essence\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:inferium_essence\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and it becomes \"},{\"text\":\"Inferium Farmland\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:inferium_farmland\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; a hoe, the essence and dirt in the grid do the same. Only essence farmland gives mystical crops a shot at a second seed.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.14D697C4BADC2CCB.title": "Twice lucky",
  "quest.14D697C4BADC2CCB.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"On any essence farmland a resource crop has a 10% chance of a second seed and, rolled apart, 10% of a second essence. On the farmland of its own tier both rise to 20%.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1C8DB440E19666FE.title": "Better dirt, bigger harvest",
  "quest.1C8DB440E19666FE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Inferium Seeds still roll for a second seed, but their essence grows with the soil: one on plain or inferium farmland, two on tertium, three on supremium, and a coin flip for one more on prudentium and imperium.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3F4B267760DE93D6.title": "Stone and deepslate",
  "quest.3F4B267760DE93D6.quest_subtitle": "Quarrying, but seasonal.",
  "quest.3F4B267760DE93D6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The first resource seeds cost only inferium: a \"},{\"text\":\"Prosperity Seed Base\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:prosperity_seed_base\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on the altar, four of the block and four inferium on the pedestals. Eight essences give back 24 cobblestone or 24 cobbled deepslate.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.305CDCF7849CE957.title": "Dirt, wood and ice",
  "quest.305CDCF7849CE957.quest_desc": [
    "Tier 1 as well: dirt, any log and ice. Eight dirt or ice essences give 24 of the block, and three wood essences give 16 logs: the shape you lay them in picks the tree.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Dirt with stone essence makes gravel, and ice essence alone also gives packed ice and snow blocks.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.50AF43A699D462B3.title": "Leftover magic",
  "quest.50AF43A699D462B3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Every resource crop harvest has a 10% chance to drop \"},{\"text\":\"Fertilized Essence\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:fertilized_essence\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; inferium never does. It works like bone meal that mystical crops accept, and four of it in the fertilizer recipe double the output.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1D2D61B587E78473.title": "Rain on demand",
  "quest.1D2D61B587E78473.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Bone meal, a bowl and iron make a \"},{\"text\":\"Watering Can\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:watering_can\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Fill it at a water source and hold use over crops: it waters a 3×3 patch, and about one pass in four gives every plant there an extra growth tick.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.23DF24ADBE2C616D.title": "Cans that water themselves",
  "quest.23DF24ADBE2C616D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four inferium ingots and four \"},{\"text\":\"Mystical Fertilizer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:mystical_fertilizer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" around the can make an \"},{\"text\":\"Inferium Watering Can\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:inferium_watering_can\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Hold \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.sneak\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" and press \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.use\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" at the sky to let it water on its own. Each tier above adds two blocks of reach and five points of chance, up to 13×13 at 50%.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.77B51CA6FFAB161D.title": "Reap, don't uproot",
  "quest.77B51CA6FFAB161D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Diamonds and sticks make a \"},{\"text\":\"Diamond Sickle\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:diamond_sickle\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", which clears plants in an area, and a \"},{\"text\":\"Diamond Scythe\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:diamond_scythe\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": use it on a field to harvest every ripe crop in reach and leave the plants standing.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Essence tiers widen both, and the scythe also hits everything around its target."
  ],
  "quest.674A789E0DCB9989.title": "Instant harvest",
  "quest.674A789E0DCB9989.quest_subtitle": "Bone meal with a doctorate.",
  "quest.674A789E0DCB9989.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Bone meal, inferium and a diamond make four \"},{\"text\":\"Mystical Fertilizer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:mystical_fertilizer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". One grows any crop or sapling to full at once, resource crops included, where plain bone meal is wasted.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5805DD7AA45FBD28.title": "A crystal that climbs",
  "quest.5805DD7AA45FBD28.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A diamond, four \"},{\"text\":\"Prosperity Shards\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:prosperity_shard\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and four inferium make the \"},{\"text\":\"Infusion Crystal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:infusion_crystal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Surround it with four essences of one tier to get one of the next; it survives a thousand crafts.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Going down is free: one essence of any tier breaks back into four of the tier below."
  ],
  "quest.1A7EAFC13E0A2D23.title": "Tier 2: prudentium",
  "quest.1A7EAFC13E0A2D23.quest_subtitle": "Every tier costs four of the last.",
  "quest.1A7EAFC13E0A2D23.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four inferium around the crystal make one \"},{\"text\":\"Prudentium Essence\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:prudentium_essence\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Right-click farmland with it for \"},{\"text\":\"Prudentium Farmland\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:prudentium_farmland\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", where tier-2 crops get their best odds. Tier-2 seeds need four prudentium on the pedestals.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3396B56D9BDA9984.title": "Tier 3: tertium",
  "quest.3396B56D9BDA9984.quest_subtitle": "Where iron starts to grow.",
  "quest.3396B56D9BDA9984.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four prudentium around the crystal make \"},{\"text\":\"Tertium Essence\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:tertium_essence\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", sixteen inferium deep. \"},{\"text\":\"Tertium Farmland\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:tertium_farmland\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" feeds tier-3 crops, and inferium planted on it yields two essences a harvest.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6C25629BBF18E209.title": "Tier 4: imperium",
  "quest.6C25629BBF18E209.quest_subtitle": "Sixty-four inferium in a trench coat.",
  "quest.6C25629BBF18E209.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four tertium make one \"},{\"text\":\"Imperium Essence\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:imperium_essence\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", 64 inferium all told. \"},{\"text\":\"Imperium Farmland\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:imperium_farmland\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" suits tier-4 crops: gold, lapis, the End and most of the mod alloys.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6FA2E55C53DD1300.title": "Tier 5: supremium",
  "quest.6FA2E55C53DD1300.quest_subtitle": "The top of the ladder. Almost.",
  "quest.6FA2E55C53DD1300.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four imperium make one \"},{\"text\":\"Supremium Essence\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:supremium_essence\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", 256 inferium in one orb. \"},{\"text\":\"Supremium Farmland\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:supremium_farmland\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" is the best soil there is: tier-5 crops grow on it, and inferium gives three essences a harvest.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.781B0C1FDB5C0F75.title": "The crystal that never cracks",
  "quest.781B0C1FDB5C0F75.quest_subtitle": "A thousand uses was never enough.",
  "quest.781B0C1FDB5C0F75.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four supremium, four prosperity shards and a \"},{\"text\":\"Supremium Gemstone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:supremium_gemstone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make the \"},{\"text\":\"Master Infusion Crystal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:master_infusion_crystal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": no durability, ever. It also fuses four essence blocks straight into one block of the next tier.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0A2BC146F40908F3.title": "Garden, dye and reef",
  "quest.0A2BC146F40908F3.quest_subtitle": "A greenhouse in a sack.",
  "quest.0A2BC146F40908F3.quest_desc": [
    "These four take an agglomeratio each, a 2×2 of the real thing: pumpkin, potato, cactus and cane for nature, four dyes, four coral blocks, or honey and comb. Back come 16 sugar cane from six nature essences, six dye from three, six honeycomb from three."
  ],
  "quest.55D57D23F84A2FCF.title": "Coal, amethyst and netherrack",
  "quest.55D57D23F84A2FCF.quest_desc": [
    "Coal and amethyst seeds take the plain item; the nether seed takes an agglomeratio of netherrack, soul sand, nether bricks and wart. Eight essences return 12 coal, 20 amethyst shards or 24 netherrack."
  ],
  "quest.1CE42D19ACC25D11.title": "Silicon, sulfur and aluminum",
  "quest.1CE42D19ACC25D11.quest_desc": [
    "Three staples of the tech mods, all tier 2. Silicon from AE2, Ender IO, Oritech or Refined Storage feeds the seed; three essences give 8 silicon or 8 sulfur dust, and eight give 8 aluminum ingots."
  ],
  "quest.2E629BB69DC4535F.title": "Limestone, menril and infinity",
  "quest.2E629BB69DC4535F.quest_subtitle": "Three mods, one furrow.",
  "quest.2E629BB69DC4535F.quest_desc": [
    "Tier-2 seeds for three mods' own materials: Create's limestone, Integrated Dynamics' menril berries and Ender IO's grains of infinity. Three menril essences give 16 menril logs; eight limestone essences, 16 limestone."
  ],
  "quest.63564B04087489E5.title": "Prudentium for the common store",
  "quest.63564B04087489E5.quest_subtitle": "The nursery always wants more.",
  "quest.63564B04087489E5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Sixteen \"},{\"text\":\"Prudentium Essence\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:prudentium_essence\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for the common store. A propagation core takes two, and every tier-2 seed takes four.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.726AFCFBD33EAACA.title": "Iron from the ground",
  "quest.726AFCFBD33EAACA.quest_subtitle": "Mining, but it grows back.",
  "quest.726AFCFBD33EAACA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four iron ingots and four tertium on the pedestals make \"},{\"text\":\"Iron Seeds\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:iron_seeds\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; copper works the same way. Eight essences in a ring give six ingots, and a crop never runs dry.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.01BFC7A793AEBFD3.title": "Redstone, glowstone and quartz",
  "quest.01BFC7A793AEBFD3.quest_desc": [
    "Tier-3 dusts and crystals for every machine you build. Eight essences return 12 redstone dust, 12 glowstone dust or 12 nether quartz; quartz essence around stone essence also makes andesite, diorite and granite."
  ],
  "quest.7F777AEFBEB66DBC.title": "Obsidian, prismarine and sculk",
  "quest.7F777AEFBEB66DBC.quest_desc": [
    "Blocks you'd rather not fetch by hand. The prismarine seed takes a prismarine agglomeratio; eight obsidian essences give 8 obsidian, three sculk essences 16 sculk and three prismarine essences 8 shards."
  ],
  "quest.60C032204CE10FE9.title": "Tin, lead and silver",
  "quest.60C032204CE10FE9.quest_desc": [
    "Tier-3 seeds that take any mod's ingot: Mekanism, Immersive Engineering, Modern Industrialization or Occultism, whichever you have. Eight essences give four ingots back."
  ],
  "quest.33912EC1AF8C46A9.title": "Zinc, brass and bronze",
  "quest.33912EC1AF8C46A9.quest_desc": [
    "Create's zinc and brass, plus bronze from Mekanism, Modern Industrialization or Silent Gear, all at tier 3. Eight essences give four ingots of any of them."
  ],
  "quest.4D89C1F862E1E19D.title": "Stones for Create",
  "quest.4D89C1F862E1E19D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Eight stone essences around one iron, zinc, copper or gold essence make 16 \"},{\"text\":\"Crimsite\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:crimsite\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", \"},{\"text\":\"Asurine\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:asurine\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", \"},{\"text\":\"Veridium\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:veridium\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" or \"},{\"text\":\"Ochrum\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"create:ochrum\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": Create's ore stones, for when a palette needs a whole wall.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.799AA5FC36204439.title": "Catalysts, homegrown",
  "quest.799AA5FC36204439.quest_subtitle": "No Warden was harmed.",
  "quest.799AA5FC36204439.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight sculk essences make three \"},{\"text\":\"Sculk Catalysts\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:sculk_catalyst\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", and seven make two sensors or two shriekers.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.0522AC6F7723E0DF.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.1D53066FBC32E1BD.title": "Gold, lapis and the End",
  "quest.1D53066FBC32E1BD.quest_desc": [
    "Eight gold essences give four ingots, eight lapis essences twelve lapis lazuli and eight End essences 24 end stone. The End seed takes an agglomeratio of end stone, purpur and chorus fruit."
  ],
  "quest.23AFCC2E2EC0BF19.title": "Steel, nickel and their alloys",
  "quest.23AFCC2E2EC0BF19.quest_desc": [
    "Five tier-4 metals of the machine mods. Steel returns three ingots for eight essences; nickel, invar, constantan and electrum return four. Imperium goes on four pedestals, the ingot of any mod on the other four."
  ],
  "quest.18C244C3B5666682.title": "The Mekanism shelf",
  "quest.18C244C3B5666682.quest_desc": [
    "Four tier-4 seeds that only exist with Mekanism. Eight essences give four osmium ingots, eight fluorite gems, three refined glowstone ingots or two refined obsidian ingots."
  ],
  "quest.3FFB26DED6FC94F7.title": "Twilight metals",
  "quest.3FFB26DED6FC94F7.quest_subtitle": "Beat it once, farm it forever.",
  "quest.3FFB26DED6FC94F7.quest_desc": [
    "Steeleaf and ironwood are tier 3, knightmetal and fiery ingots tier 4, and every seed wants four of the real thing. Eight essences give four steeleaf or ironwood, three knightmetal, two fiery ingots."
  ],
  "quest.2E9C52E0D72914F2.title": "Certus, fluix and sky stone",
  "quest.2E9C52E0D72914F2.quest_desc": [
    "Certus quartz and sky stone are tier 3, fluix tier 4. Eight essences give six certus or fluix crystals, or 16 blocks of sky stone."
  ],
  "quest.222AE9DFC27DD38A.title": "Presses without meteorites",
  "quest.222AE9DFC27DD38A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Eight certus essences around a certus crystal, gold ingot, diamond or silicon make the \"},{\"text\":\"Inscriber Calculation Press\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"ae2:calculation_processor_press\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", logic, engineering or silicon press. No crater hunt for \"},{\"text\":\"Applied Energistics 2\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"1E24729503A1C81A\"}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.62D3B1C1ABB53CCF.title": "Iron, improved",
  "quest.62D3B1C1ABB53CCF.quest_subtitle": "Explosions optional.",
  "quest.62D3B1C1ABB53CCF.quest_desc": [
    "Refined Storage's quartz enriched iron (tier 3) and PneumaticCraft's compressed iron (tier 4). Eight essences give eight quartz enriched iron or six compressed iron ingots, no blast required."
  ],
  "quest.4F51C7697F0647DE.title": "Ruby, sapphire and peridot",
  "quest.4F51C7697F0647DE.quest_desc": [
    "Iron's Gems 'n Jewelry supplies the ruby, sapphire and peridot these tier-4 seeds need. Eight essences give six gems back."
  ],
  "quest.349F4E899A63B028.title": "Uranium and HOP graphite",
  "quest.349F4E899A63B028.quest_desc": [
    "Two tier-4 seeds for the power plants: uranium from Mekanism, Immersive Engineering or Modern Industrialization, and Immersive Engineering's HOP graphite. Eight essences give two uranium or three graphite ingots."
  ],
  "quest.35BDC314D202A42C.title": "Diamond, emerald and netherite",
  "quest.35BDC314D202A42C.quest_subtitle": "The reason you came.",
  "quest.35BDC314D202A42C.quest_desc": [
    "Tier 5, and priced like it: four supremium and four of the gem or ingot per seed. Nine diamond or emerald essences make one gem; eight netherite essences, one netherite ingot."
  ],
  "quest.2833DB15EE38A8A5.title": "Platinum, iridium and draconium",
  "quest.2833DB15EE38A8A5.quest_desc": [
    "Platinum from Modern Industrialization or Oritech, Modern Industrialization's iridium and Draconic Evolution's draconium, all tier 5. Eight essences give two platinum or iridium ingots, or one of draconium."
  ],
  "quest.28AA8EDE378BDCA3.title": "Powah crystals",
  "quest.28AA8EDE378BDCA3.quest_desc": [
    "Energized steel and blazing crystal are tier 4; niotic crystal, spirited crystal and uraninite tier 5. Eight essences give three energized steel or blazing crystals, or two uraninite; nine give one niotic or spirited crystal."
  ],
  "quest.7087CEAC048D1FDD.title": "Ender IO's power alloys",
  "quest.7087CEAC048D1FDD.quest_desc": [
    "Ender IO's conduit alloys, tier by tier: redstone alloy and conductive alloy at 3, energetic at 4, vibrant at 5. Eight essences give five of the first two, three energetic, two vibrant."
  ],
  "quest.17C390EAF2E2DFA8.title": "Dark steel, soularium, end steel",
  "quest.17C390EAF2E2DFA8.quest_desc": [
    "The rest of Ender IO's metals: dark steel, soularium and pulsating alloy at tier 4, end steel at 5. Eight essences give four dark steel or soularium, three pulsating alloy, two end steel."
  ],
  "image.42BDDA874345A7A1.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Tier 1 · Inferium\",\"color\":\"#C4DE52\"}]",
  "image.533C4C76E53ABE41.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Tier 2 · Prudentium\",\"color\":\"#C4DE52\"}]",
  "image.22680A0EFF1DC43A.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Tier 3 · Tertium\",\"color\":\"#C4DE52\"}]",
  "image.4C9D23FEA6C06559.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Tier 4 · Imperium\",\"color\":\"#C4DE52\"}]",
  "image.20367BE794673C17.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Tier 5 · Supremium\",\"color\":\"#C4DE52\"}]",
  "image.3A08778835D537BF.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Mystical Agriculture\",\"color\":\"#F1F6D8\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.5690A53C2848EBC3.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Essence\",\"color\":\"#C4DE52\"}]",
  "image.3C27BA225BE4B2C5.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"five tiers one field\",\"color\":\"#B9D77A\",\"font\":\"minecraft:alt\"}]",
  "image.7CB6C048CF1689A4.title": "Back to the Sun of Heliodor",
  "image.4B442FCC0A2058D3.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» Souls and awakening\",\"color\":\"#C4DE52\"}]",
  "chapter.7FA7A2A4481A3E5F.title": "Productive Bees · The Apiary",
  "chapter.7FA7A2A4481A3E5F.chapter_subtitle": [
    "From a wild nest to a modular apiary: cages, hives, centrifuges, upgrades and genes."
  ],
  "quest.1B7F19111B288D0A.title": "A cage for the first bee",
  "quest.1B7F19111B288D0A.quest_subtitle": "Catch and release, beekeeper edition.",
  "quest.1B7F19111B288D0A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two planks around a \"},{\"text\":\"Honey Bottle\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:honey_bottle\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make a \"},{\"text\":\"Bee Cage\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"productivebees:bee_cage\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Right-click a bee to catch it and right-click the ground to let it out; a plain cage is spent on release.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Honey bottles come from a full vanilla nest with a campfire under it. Released on a flower, a bee adopts it; released on a hive while sneaking, it moves in."
  ],
  "quest.0730A6031314681F.title": "Bee in a box",
  "quest.0730A6031314681F.quest_desc": [
    "Any bee counts, vanilla ones included. Carry a few cages when you travel: the rare species live far from home, and a caged bee rides in your pocket."
  ],
  "quest.02AF0E7EC2CF26A4.title": "The advanced beehive",
  "quest.02AF0E7EC2CF26A4.quest_subtitle": "No campfire, no silk touch, no drama.",
  "quest.02AF0E7EC2CF26A4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Planks, two honeycombs, a vanilla beehive, a campfire and shears make an \"},{\"text\":\"Advanced Oak Beehive\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"productivebees:advanced_oak_beehive\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; every wood has its own. Its window shows who is home and keeps the combs they bring, and broken, it moves with its bees inside.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Resource bees only make their combs in an advanced hive. After each trip a bee rests inside for four minutes before flying out again."
  ],
  "quest.2AD4F6AB278F5444.title": "Room for five",
  "quest.2AD4F6AB278F5444.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight planks around a honeycomb make an \"},{\"text\":\"Oak Expansion Box\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"productivebees:expansion_box_oak\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Set it on top of the hive or beside it: five bees fit instead of three, and the hive starts taking upgrades. One box per hive.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6350E535E200243F.title": "The centrifuge",
  "quest.6350E535E200243F.quest_subtitle": "Spin cycle for honeycomb.",
  "quest.6350E535E200243F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Seven iron around a grindstone, or a grindstone on a cauldron, make a \"},{\"text\":\"Centrifuge\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"productivebees:centrifuge\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". A comb takes fifteen seconds: plain honeycomb gives one \"},{\"text\":\"Wax\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"productivebees:wax\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and 100 mB of honey, and resource combs give their resource.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "It holds ten buckets of honey and pushes it into any tank beside it."
  ],
  "quest.5A798BA757C433EB.title": "Plugged in",
  "quest.5A798BA757C433EB.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four redstone, two iron and two \"},{\"text\":\"Basic Control Circuits\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mekanism:basic_control_circuit\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" around a centrifuge make the \"},{\"text\":\"Powered Centrifuge\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"productivebees:powered_centrifuge\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": five seconds a comb, for 10 FE per tick.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.681D78624825336C.title": "The upgrade base",
  "quest.681D78624825336C.quest_subtitle": "Every upgrade starts as this one.",
  "quest.681D78624825336C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four sticks, three emeralds, a diamond and a \"},{\"text\":\"Honey Treat\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"productivebees:honey_treat\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make an upgrade base. Hives, centrifuges, catchers and incubators take the upgrades built on it; a hive, once it has its expansion box.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Upgrades go in through the machine's screen, or with a sneaking right-click on the block."
  ],
  "quest.1DE5554E846A0B84.title": "The modular beehive",
  "quest.1DE5554E846A0B84.quest_subtitle": "A hive the size of a room.",
  "quest.1DE5554E846A0B84.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Here the \"},{\"text\":\"Modular Beehive\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularbees:modular_beehive_core\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" core costs two ironwood ingots, an advanced hive, two scented planks, iron bars and the simulator and adult upgrades. It runs a 3×3×3 cube whose bees never leave: no breeding, no tricks in the world, only combs and honey.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Pack change:\",\"color\":\"#FF8C7A\"},{\"text\":\" the native recipe takes four scented planks; ENTRELUMEN swaps two of them for ironwood, from the Twilight Forest (act IV).\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7734EBCAB681625C.title": "Full throttle",
  "quest.7734EBCAB681625C.quest_subtitle": "Five times faster, four and a half times fuller.",
  "quest.7734EBCAB681625C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Netherite Electrode\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularbees:electrode_netherite\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" runs an overclocker at ×5 and a \"},{\"text\":\"Soul Treat\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularbees:soul_treat\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" feeds a treater at ×4.5, the best food on its list. Give both to one modular hive and watch the combs pile up.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "The electrode is a gold one taken to a smithing table with a netherite block. The treat takes two ender treats, a royal treat, two sculk, a sculk catalyst and a potion of regeneration."
  ],
  "quest.491FCA9D81A703AF.title": "Honey treats",
  "quest.491FCA9D81A703AF.quest_subtitle": "Bribery, but sweet.",
  "quest.491FCA9D81A703AF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A honeycomb and a \"},{\"text\":\"Honey Bottle\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:honey_bottle\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make a \"},{\"text\":\"Honey Treat\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"productivebees:honey_treat\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It calms an angry bee, grows a baby faster, wakes an empty nest and carries genes. A bottler makes one from a honeycomb and 250 mB of honey, too.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.3D8AA887BEC8001A.title": "Productive Bees' guide book",
  "quest.2A61897BEFAA9A59.title": "The beekeeper's manual",
  "quest.2A61897BEFAA9A59.quest_desc": [
    "A book and a bee cage make Productive Bees' own guide: every nest, bee and machine, with its recipe. A book and a sturdy cage work too."
  ],
  "quest.5D25EBF13FDA659C.title": "A cage that comes back",
  "quest.5D25EBF13FDA659C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Village chests hide a \"},{\"text\":\"Sturdy Bee Cage\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"productivebees:sturdy_bee_cage\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" one time in five. Unlike the plain one, it drops back into your inventory empty once the bee is out.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.728803E0BD272784.title": "A nest for a hat",
  "quest.728803E0BD272784.quest_subtitle": "Fashion that stings back.",
  "quest.728803E0BD272784.quest_desc": [
    "Press a bee nest onto a diamond helmet. While you wear it, bees leave you alone, and when something hurts you, there is a 30% chance a KamikazBee bursts out to sting it."
  ],
  "quest.6F292C163404D10D.title": "A bomb full of bees",
  "quest.6F292C163404D10D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A glass bottle, a bee cage and gunpowder make a \"},{\"text\":\"Bee Bomb\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"productivebees:bee_bomb\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Combine it with filled cages, up to ten bees, and throw it to let them all out at once. Crafted alone, it turns into the angry version.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.29D2FB583C6AC83A.title": "Steering a bumble bee",
  "quest.29D2FB583C6AC83A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A fishing rod and a honey treat make a \"},{\"text\":\"Treat on a Stick\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"productivebees:treat_on_a_stick\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Put a saddle on a Bumble Bee from a plains nest, climb on, and steer it the way you would steer a pig.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5B33089DEA569D5D.title": "Air cavalry",
  "quest.5B33089DEA569D5D.quest_subtitle": "Keep your arms inside the bee.",
  "quest.5B33089DEA569D5D.quest_desc": [
    "A saddled Bumble Bee carries its rider wherever the treat points. Nobody promised it would be fast."
  ],
  "reward.23EE0B0A75C0BF3E.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.7252ECDE61BB61AD.title": "Solitary homes",
  "quest.7252ECDE61BB61AD.quest_desc": [
    "Solitary bees live one to a nest, in logs, dirt, sand, gravel, stone, snow and reeds all over the Overworld. Break a nest and it comes home with its bee inside, no silk touch needed."
  ],
  "quest.7BC26A005AFBD40E.title": "Follow the buzz",
  "quest.7BC26A005AFBD40E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Gold nuggets, iron bars and a note block make a \"},{\"text\":\"Nest Locator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"productivebees:nest_locator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Sneak-right-click a nest, or the block it is made of, to tune it; then right-click and it points at the nearest one within 100 blocks.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.602C7789D41EB288.title": "Vacancy",
  "quest.602C7789D41EB288.quest_subtitle": "Now accepting tenants.",
  "quest.602C7789D41EB288.quest_desc": [
    "An empty nest takes a honey treat, and a day later a new bee moves in. Craft a nest on its own to evict its bee and its eggs."
  ],
  "quest.73780133DAD334E1.title": "Nests from a sword",
  "quest.73780133DAD334E1.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A sword and a block make that block's nest: a wooden sword for logs, dirt, grass, sand, gravel, snow, reeds, glowstone and soul sand; iron for stone, slime, nether bricks, quartz and end stone; diamond for obsidian and nether gold.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0EEA25FD10B24C23.title": "Bait for the Nether",
  "quest.0EEA25FD10B24C23.quest_desc": [
    "Nether and End nests are picky: each one is refilled with its own bait, used on the nest in its home dimension.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Quartz for Crystalline Bees, glowstone dust for Glowing, magma cream for Magmatic, a ghast tear for Ghostly, a gold ingot for Gold, popped chorus fruit for Ender and dragon's breath for Draconic."
  ],
  "quest.38EA45C6A062B1B5.title": "The feeding slab",
  "quest.38EA45C6A062B1B5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A smooth stone slab on a chest makes a \"},{\"text\":\"Feeding Slab\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"productivebees:feeder\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It holds three flower blocks, so one spot feeds several species, and Lumber and Quarry Bees feeding there work a random block from it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7A51E1B504D2809E.title": "The catcher",
  "quest.7A51E1B504D2809E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Iron, dirt and a dispenser make a \"},{\"text\":\"Catcher\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"productivebees:catcher\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Fill it with empty cages and it cages every bee that flies over; a flower or a feeding slab on top draws them in. Range, filter and BaBee upgrades widen it, pick the species or keep only babies.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3EDF78772A4BF619.title": "Anger management",
  "quest.3EDF78772A4BF619.quest_desc": [
    "A honey treat calms an angry bee on the spot. Feed a bee lots of treats and its temper improves for good."
  ],
  "quest.5314E233829D55E1.title": "A bee on the shelf",
  "quest.5314E233829D55E1.quest_subtitle": "Look, don't touch.",
  "quest.5314E233829D55E1.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Glass panes and an oak button make a \"},{\"text\":\"Bee Jar\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"productivebees:jar_oak\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Feed it a filled cage with a hopper or a pipe and it shows the bee off.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0EC40D1C07824671.title": "Hurry them out",
  "quest.0EC40D1C07824671.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Whack a hive or a nest with a stick and the bees inside come out now, losing their progress. It only works when it is safe for them to leave.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2DD2E73B86C8E00C.title": "Hot tub",
  "quest.2DD2E73B86C8E00C.quest_subtitle": "Regeneration, with sticky feet.",
  "quest.2DD2E73B86C8E00C.quest_desc": [
    "Honey poured over a feeding slab turns it into a spa: bees dipping their feet in it regenerate after a long day of work."
  ],
  "reward.479A286BF5B568D5.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.64F754223B0398C5.title": "The bottler",
  "quest.64F754223B0398C5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Iron, a smooth stone slab and glass make a \"},{\"text\":\"Bottler\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"productivebees:bottler\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Beside a centrifuge it fills itself: 250 mB of honey turn a glass bottle into a honey bottle, or a honeycomb into a honey treat.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.49976F6341A00B8C.title": "Honey jelly",
  "quest.49976F6341A00B8C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Spin a honey block in a centrifuge and one time in ten it leaves a \"},{\"text\":\"Honey Jelly\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularbees:honey_jelly\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Modular Bees needs it: two jellies, four wax and three planks make three scented planks.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.650669F370AD06EE.title": "Honey by the bucket",
  "quest.650669F370AD06EE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four honey bottles and a bucket, or a honey block and a bucket, make a \"},{\"text\":\"Honey Bucket\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"productivebees:honey_bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Honey is a fluid here: pipes move it and generators burn it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.759F7091BD83C1D1.title": "Bottled experience",
  "quest.759F7091BD83C1D1.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Experience Bee combs spin into 100 mB of liquid experience, and a bottler turns every 250 mB of it into a bottle o' enchanting.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7E8939A55C670067.title": "Sweet power",
  "quest.7E8939A55C670067.quest_subtitle": "Runs on breakfast.",
  "quest.7E8939A55C670067.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Iron, a furnace and a honey bucket make a \"},{\"text\":\"Honey Generator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"productivebees:honey_generator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": 60 FE per tick for 2 mB of honey, so one comb's honey lasts 50 ticks. A productivity upgrade stretches the honey and a speed upgrade burns it faster.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1C98317F4B988A71.title": "Wax, block by block",
  "quest.1C98317F4B988A71.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Nine \"},{\"text\":\"Wax\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"productivebees:wax\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make a \"},{\"text\":\"Wax Block\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"productivebees:wax_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and come back out of it. Two wax under a string make a candle, so no hive has to stay dark.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6FE11D2F3D0A7F8C.title": "Combs by the block",
  "quest.6FE11D2F3D0A7F8C.quest_desc": [
    "Four resource combs of one kind press into a comb block and come back out the same. The block upgrade makes a hive hand over whole blocks, and a heated centrifuge spins them without unpacking."
  ],
  "quest.2B7B20362E553A54.title": "Hands-free centrifuge",
  "quest.2B7B20362E553A54.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A centrifuge swallows combs thrown on top of it and passes its fluid to any tank beside it, other centrifuges included.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5DA08CF612789AC5.title": "Wax for the store",
  "quest.5DA08CF612789AC5.quest_subtitle": "Every workshop runs on wax.",
  "quest.5DA08CF612789AC5.quest_desc": [
    "Thirty-two wax for the common store. The Atlas asks for wax in more than one act, and a spare stack never hurts."
  ],
  "quest.5C0B60D74C785DC5.title": "Squashed bee",
  "quest.5C0B60D74C785DC5.quest_subtitle": "Science is messy.",
  "quest.5C0B60D74C785DC5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Put a bottler with empty bottles under a bee and a piston facing down above it, then pull a lever: out comes \"},{\"text\":\"Squashed Bee Material\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"productivebees:gene_bottle\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". A centrifuge splits it into the useful genes and the junk.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.29AFAB552FFECC07.title": "Tough love",
  "quest.29AFAB552FFECC07.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Leash a bee outside in the rain and it may learn to work in it. Leash a day bee at night and it may turn nocturnal; a night bee by day may start working around the clock. Each try can hurt it, so keep treats handy.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4637DE3532F4C65A.title": "Gene samples",
  "quest.4637DE3532F4C65A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Gene Sample\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"productivebees:gene\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" carries one trait at a purity: productivity, weather tolerance, working hours, endurance, temper, or the bee's type. A gene sampler upgrade pulls one from a bee in the hive now and then, no piston needed.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1A77F9F6046128DA.title": "The bee extractor",
  "quest.1A77F9F6046128DA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two redstone, a piston, two stone and a bottler make Modular Bees' \"},{\"text\":\"Bee Extractor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularbees:bee_extractor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": a bottler with the press built in. It bottles bee material in five seconds for 500 FE per tick.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.35CBCA2B0B6414D7.title": "Purer genes",
  "quest.35CBCA2B0B6414D7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Two samples of the same gene combine into a purer one, and more of it on the same treat raises the odds too. Type genes come out around 33% pure.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.176FB263A5C0E7EF.title": "The gene indexer",
  "quest.176FB263A5C0E7EF.quest_subtitle": "For when combining genes by hand gets old.",
  "quest.176FB263A5C0E7EF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Iron, a comparator and a crafting table make a \"},{\"text\":\"Gene Indexer\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"productivebees:gene_indexer\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Fill it with samples, give it a redstone signal, and it combines matching genes on its own.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3221DCBBBB0504C7.title": "The incubator",
  "quest.3221DCBBBB0504C7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Iron, hay and a daylight detector make an \"},{\"text\":\"Incubator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"productivebees:incubator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". A caged BaBee with 20 honey treats comes out grown in three minutes, at 10 FE per tick; an egg with a treat carrying a type gene comes out as that bee's spawn egg.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6C236EAE980A79A5.title": "A bee in an egg",
  "quest.6C236EAE980A79A5.quest_subtitle": "Portable, stackable, craftable.",
  "quest.6C236EAE980A79A5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Resource bee spawn eggs are more than a shortcut: other mods' machines turn them into new species. Ender IO's alloy smelter, Powah's energizing orb, the infusion altar and draconic fusion all take bee eggs, as the \"},{\"text\":\"breeding tree\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"3256FA24100D6B05\"}},{\"text\":\" shows.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.50C138F4A5FCFFA0.title": "The breeding chamber",
  "quest.50C138F4A5FCFFA0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Iron, a rose bush and a BaBee upgrade make a \"},{\"text\":\"Breeding Chamber\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"productivebees:breeding_chamber\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Give it two caged parents, their breeding items and an empty cage: five minutes and 50 FE per tick later, the baby comes out caged.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Installed in a hive, the same BaBee upgrade gives the bees inside a 5% chance per trip to breed on their own, as long as no more than ten bees crowd the hive."
  ],
  "quest.5C55ED13C4FD4785.title": "The heated centrifuge",
  "quest.5C55ED13C4FD4785.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A powered centrifuge, two speed upgrades, an inactive dragon egg, two copper blocks and three iron make the \"},{\"text\":\"Heated Centrifuge\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"productivebees:heated_centrifuge\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It takes whole comb blocks and spins three times faster than the powered one, for three times the power.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.435FB59D29EC8C07.title": "The productivity ladder",
  "quest.435FB59D29EC8C07.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Productivity upgrades multiply a hive's combs: alpha ×1.2, beta ×1.5, gamma ×2, omega ×2.6. Alpha costs draconic chunks; beta, nether stars; gamma, echo shards and a simulator; omega, hearts of the sea and a block upgrade.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.08C5B8333B6065FF.title": "Speed and stability",
  "quest.08C5B8333B6065FF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Each speed upgrade takes 15% off a bee's time inside the hive, or off a centrifuge's or an incubator's work. A stability upgrade adds 15% to every centrifuge output that is not guaranteed.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.652B40A0F3F2827F.title": "Bees that never leave",
  "quest.652B40A0F3F2827F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A simulator upgrade keeps the bees inside and simulates their trips, which spares the server. Their flower or a feeding slab goes at the foot of the hive, right below its front, and a slab lets three species share one simulated hive.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.3D0D36D235901D2C.title": "Book of Modular Bees",
  "quest.712A9CB877262241.title": "Modular Bees' manual",
  "quest.712A9CB877262241.quest_desc": [
    "A book and a scented plank make the Book of Modular Bees: every part, electrode and treat, with its numbers."
  ],
  "quest.03AE68BB3155CD0E.title": "Structure boxes",
  "quest.03AE68BB3155CD0E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight scented planks around iron bars make a \"},{\"text\":\"Beehive Structure Box\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularbees:modular_beehive_part\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". The core sits in the middle of one face of a 3×3×3 cube; the other 26 blocks are boxes or the parts that replace them.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6E5EA58C98832ACC.title": "The alveary",
  "quest.6E5EA58C98832ACC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An expansion box and a structure box make a \"},{\"text\":\"Modular Alveary\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularbees:modular_beehive_alveary\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". The core holds no bees and each alveary holds five: right-click it with filled cages to move them in or out. Babies and solitary bees stay out.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.10ED28C8254A96DB.title": "The modular feeder",
  "quest.10ED28C8254A96DB.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A feeding slab and a structure box make a \"},{\"text\":\"Modular Feeder\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularbees:modular_beehive_feeder\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". The bees inside look for flowers only here: nine kinds fit, and a bucket or a tank covers the ones that want a fluid.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4B43AF8BDA6B971E.title": "The export hatch",
  "quest.4B43AF8BDA6B971E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two pistons, a structure box and a hopper make a \"},{\"text\":\"Beehive Export Hatch\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularbees:modular_export\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": it pushes combs and honey into the chest or tank it faces. Fluix and an ME interface turn it into an ME hatch that feeds the network.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.034A3D3D10EF696F.title": "Overclocker and electrodes",
  "quest.034A3D3D10EF696F.quest_subtitle": "Totally safe. Probably.",
  "quest.034A3D3D10EF696F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Beehive Overclocker\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularbees:modular_beehive_overclocker\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" burns 100 FE per tick and an electrode: copper ×1.2, iron ×1.5, gold ×2.8, netherite ×5. Boosts from several overclockers add up, and electrodes wear faster the more bees work.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.42698CD48FBED99B.title": "The treater",
  "quest.42698CD48FBED99B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Beehive Treater\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularbees:modular_treater\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" feeds the bees for more combs: honey bottle ×1.03, treat ×1.06, honey block ×1.15, jelly ×1.4, \"},{\"text\":\"Royal Treat\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularbees:royal_treat\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" ×2, ender treat ×3, soul treat ×4.5. It eats only as each trip ends.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "A royal treat is a honey treat, three honey jellies and a potion of healing."
  ],
  "quest.478528318BE1AB6E.title": "The stacker",
  "quest.478528318BE1AB6E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two chests, a structure box, two leather and a block upgrade make a \"},{\"text\":\"Beehive Stacker\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularbees:modular_beehive_stacker\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Each one triples how much every output slot holds, and several add up.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4C0AD2BA1C8C3E11.title": "The modular dragon hive",
  "quest.4C0AD2BA1C8C3E11.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A dragon egg hive and a structure box make a \"},{\"text\":\"Modular Dragon Hive\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularbees:modular_dragon_hive\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Draconic Bees inside it gather liquid dragon's breath: a bottler bottles it, and a bucket holds four bottles' worth.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6B9776AD0CD29F1F.title": "The modular centrifuge",
  "quest.6B9776AD0CD29F1F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four netherite ingots, a filter upgrade, an inactive dragon egg, a centrifuge and two wax blocks make the \"},{\"text\":\"Modular Centrifuge\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularbees:modular_centrifuge_core\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" core. Its cube stands on four corner legs, and speed and productivity upgrades make it faster and run jobs in parallel.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Each of its 21 walls takes four iron bars, two obsidian shards, two wither skull chips and a cauldron: obsidian and withered bees pay for them."
  ],
  "quest.1BDD887B9E67DDD8.title": "Heater and gearbox",
  "quest.1BDD887B9E67DDD8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Centrifuge Heater\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularbees:modular_centrifuge_heater\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" lets the modular centrifuge take comb blocks at triple speed, one per machine and only while powered. A \"},{\"text\":\"Centrifuge Gearbox\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"modularbees:modular_centrifuge_gearbox\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" adds 1.5 parallel jobs for 40 wax a cycle.\"}]"
  ],
  "image.726EA8211C57BCA6.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Beekeeper's kit\",\"color\":\"#FFD84A\"}]",
  "image.0677BEFC7277A856.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Nests\",\"color\":\"#FFD84A\"}]",
  "image.42239C01B0D56DE0.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Life in the hive\",\"color\":\"#FFD84A\"}]",
  "image.429B42C76D1BE9D6.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Honey\",\"color\":\"#FFD84A\"}]",
  "image.3D4E2499D919AD99.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Wax and combs\",\"color\":\"#FFD84A\"}]",
  "image.1612F322AC9C892B.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Genes\",\"color\":\"#FFD84A\"}]",
  "image.6406A8914738A401.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Upgrades at work\",\"color\":\"#FFD84A\"}]",
  "image.497797BF6146DDB3.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Modular Bees\",\"color\":\"#FFD84A\"}]",
  "image.58F209FB0D779011.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Productive Bees\",\"color\":\"#FFD84A\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.75B34009A2A236CF.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Apiary\",\"color\":\"#EDE3C4\"}]",
  "image.379C23E3DDD152C5.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"cage hive comb wax\",\"color\":\"#C9B98E\",\"font\":\"minecraft:alt\"}]",
  "image.2066A53C1F10217B.title": "Back to the Sun of Heliodor",
  "image.4E28B2C68AB67078.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» The Breeding Tree\",\"color\":\"#FFD84A\"}]",
  "chapter.0ECAD0EA1E7A5124.title": "The Aether",
  "chapter.0ECAD0EA1E7A5124.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Islands in the sky, three dungeons and the Sun Spirit: the long way up."
  ],
  "quest.42F9D9395A6E191A.title": "A glowstone frame",
  "quest.42F9D9395A6E191A.quest_subtitle": "The only portal you fill with a bucket.",
  "quest.42F9D9395A6E191A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Stack \"},{\"text\":\"Glowstone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:glowstone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" into a frame shaped like a Nether portal, with an opening at least 2 wide and 3 tall, then pour a \"},{\"text\":\"Water Bucket\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:water_bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" inside. Corners are optional, so ten blocks do it.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Aim the water at the opening: a misclick is the classic way to break the frame you just built. The pack doesn't hand out a ready-made portal frame, so this is the way up.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2D510131BF5A8D84.title": "Hostile Paradise",
  "quest.2D510131BF5A8D84.quest_subtitle": "Lovely view. Mind the edges.",
  "quest.2D510131BF5A8D84.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Your first arrival brings a \"},{\"text\":\"Golden Parachute\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:golden_parachute\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a \"},{\"text\":\"Book of Lore\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:book_of_lore\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Days up here last three times as long as on the surface, and while the Sun Spirit lives, the sun doesn't set.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Beds work here; respawn anchors don't. Your team's first arrival also counts for \"},{\"text\":\"the Atlas\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"2D6ECC29EBA13A7E\"}},{\"text\":\", even before act IV.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4F2B4AEB1BDA3011.title": "Skyroot first",
  "quest.4F2B4AEB1BDA3011.quest_subtitle": "Wood, but make it double.",
  "quest.4F2B4AEB1BDA3011.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Tools from outside mine Aether blocks slower, on purpose, so start over with \"},{\"text\":\"Skyroot Planks\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:skyroot_planks\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Skyroot tools double what they break: the pickaxe Holystone and Ambrosium Ore, the axe logs, the shovel dirt and Quicksoil, the sword mob drops.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7B852EB9C8B39D21.title": "Holystone, with a bonus",
  "quest.7B852EB9C8B39D21.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Holystone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:holystone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" is the Aether's stone, and its tools are the stone tier: the pickaxe is what \"},{\"text\":\"Zanite Ore\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:zanite_ore\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and Icestone ask for. Every Holystone tool now and then drops an \"},{\"text\":\"Ambrosium Shard\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:ambrosium_shard\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" as you work.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6F240D5A235EA0B5.title": "Ambrosium, the sky's coal",
  "quest.6F240D5A235EA0B5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The most common Aether ore. Its shards fuel the Altar, top \"},{\"text\":\"Ambrosium Torches\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:ambrosium_torch\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and heal half a heart when eaten; a Skyroot pickaxe doubles them.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A shard also burns in a furnace as long as coal. Keep a stack in reserve: every enchantment and repair at the Altar eats them.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.18F6BB6F5F90C589.title": "Zanite gets better as it wears",
  "quest.18F6BB6F5F90C589.quest_subtitle": "The only gear that likes being used.",
  "quest.18F6BB6F5F90C589.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Mine Zanite Ore with a stone-tier pickaxe. \"},{\"text\":\"Zanite\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:zanite_gemstone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" is the Aether's iron: the armor protects like iron, and the tools get faster, the sword stronger, as they lose durability.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3B595FC78D380340.title": "The Altar",
  "quest.3B595FC78D380340.quest_subtitle": "Do you believe in magic?",
  "quest.3B595FC78D380340.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight \"},{\"text\":\"Holystone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:holystone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" around a \"},{\"text\":\"Zanite Gemstone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:zanite_gemstone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", burning Ambrosium. Its enchanting is a conversion: ore to Enchanted Gravitite, Holystone to a Healing Stone, a Cold Aercloud to a golden one. It also repairs gear, vanilla tools included.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Fuel with a \"},{\"text\":\"Block of Ambrosium\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:ambrosium_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for long jobs: it burns ten times as long as a shard, enough for ten repairs of a Zanite pickaxe.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.008596E65CFB1CEE.title": "Pink is the new blue",
  "quest.008596E65CFB1CEE.quest_subtitle": "Mining it is the easy part.",
  "quest.008596E65CFB1CEE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The rarest Aether ore asks for an iron-tier pickaxe, Zanite counts. The Altar enchants each \"},{\"text\":\"Gravitite Ore\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:gravitite_ore\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" into \"},{\"text\":\"Enchanted Gravitite\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:enchanted_gravitite\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in 750 ticks, three shards of fuel: the material of the Aether's best tools and armor.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.12B4C1E93AEDF30B.title": "The Bronze Dungeon",
  "quest.12B4C1E93AEDF30B.quest_desc": [
    "Carved Stone halls tucked inside a floating island, and the most common of the three dungeons. Sentries guard the rooms, some chests are Chest Mimics, and the Slider waits in the boss room."
  ],
  "task.098F086C84640158.title": "Defeat the Slider",
  "quest.0D4FDE9B09C3C886.title": "The Slider",
  "quest.0D4FDE9B09C3C886.quest_subtitle": "Bring a pickaxe to a boss fight.",
  "quest.0D4FDE9B09C3C886.quest_desc": [
    "A stone block that slides at you and crushes you against the walls. Only pickaxes hurt it; a sword does nothing, and the game points that out. Keep moving and never let it pin you to a wall.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"It drops the \"},{\"text\":\"Bronze Key\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:bronze_dungeon_key\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a few blocks of Carved Stone. The key opens the Treasure Chest in the treasure room and is used up doing it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.490CC829667C2072.title": "The Silver Dungeon",
  "quest.490CC829667C2072.quest_desc": [
    "A Valkyrie sanctuary of Angelic Stone, some of it trapped, and no breaking in: the walls stay unbreakable until the Queen falls. Silver and Gold dungeons share the same spots in the world, three silver for every gold."
  ],
  "quest.50470D5C8C86C94D.title": "Ten Victory Medals",
  "quest.50470D5C8C86C94D.quest_subtitle": "Proof of worth, in bulk.",
  "quest.50470D5C8C86C94D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Queen won't fight until you bring ten. Every lesser Valkyrie drops one \"},{\"text\":\"Victory Medal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:victory_medal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; they teleport and hit hard, so take them one at a time.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.328CE38388C8945C.title": "Defeat the Valkyrie Queen",
  "quest.48C59C6D4759C71F.title": "The Valkyrie Queen",
  "quest.48C59C6D4759C71F.quest_subtitle": "She's been expecting you. With medals.",
  "quest.48C59C6D4759C71F.quest_desc": [
    "Talk to her with the medals in your pack, and strike once she says she's ready. She glides, teleports and throws thunder crystals, so reach helps. On Peaceful she refuses to fight.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"She leaves the \"},{\"text\":\"Silver Key\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:silver_dungeon_key\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for the Treasure Chest, and a golden sword on the side.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4E3BA24DFAF6D86A.title": "The Gold Dungeon",
  "quest.4E3BA24DFAF6D86A.quest_desc": [
    "An island of its own, with a Hellfire Stone chamber buried inside it. Like the silver halls, the stone won't break until its boss is dead. It's the rarest of the three: follow the compass or keep exploring."
  ],
  "task.08DDD75ACB780B35.title": "Defeat the Sun Spirit",
  "quest.05E67C9013A9B189.title": "The Sun Spirit",
  "quest.05E67C9013A9B189.quest_desc": [
    "Normal hits don't reach it. It throws ice crystals among its fireballs: hit one back into it, and only while it's frozen can your weapons hurt it. It also calls Fire Minions, so bring fire protection.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"It always drops the \"},{\"text\":\"Gold Key\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:gold_dungeon_key\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and the \"},{\"text\":\"Sun Altar\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:sun_altar\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". What else it carried belongs to \"},{\"text\":\"the story\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"0E407D24B1E4BA07\"}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.15FAE0E455CA7991.title": "A well-earned rest",
  "quest.15FAE0E455CA7991.quest_subtitle": "Lights out, finally.",
  "quest.15FAE0E455CA7991.quest_desc": [
    "With the Sun Spirit gone, the endless day is over and the Aether turns like any other world, three times slower. Lie down in a bed up here and sleep through your first night in the sky.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "{image:aether:textures/item/miscellaneous/gold_dungeon_key.png width:32 height:32 align:center}",
    "",
    "Three keys turned, three chests opened. The sky is quieter now; the islands are yours to keep."
  ],
  "quest.55968319FACF3C73.title": "What pushes you off",
  "quest.55968319FACF3C73.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Up here, most deaths are falls, not fights: Zephyr snowballs knock you back, Quicksoil on island edges is slippery, Blue Aerclouds launch you, and deep shafts open anywhere. Fight with your back to the island, never to the edge.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.26C073711D7A6DF1.title": "No fire up here",
  "quest.26C073711D7A6DF1.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Aether biomes are ultracold: torches and lanterns won't place, flint and steel only lights blocks like netherrack, lit campfires and candles go out, and lava you pour hardens into \"},{\"text\":\"Aerogel\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:aerogel\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Light the base with \"},{\"text\":\"Ambrosium Torches\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:ambrosium_torch\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1B7D3535D683B41C.title": "House rules",
  "quest.1B7D3535D683B41C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Carry On can't lift Treasure Chests, Chest Mimics or the three bosses. In act IV the \"},{\"text\":\"Heliodor Compass\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"34DC677E5D339B3F\"}},{\"text\":\" walks you from the Aether to the Bronze, Silver and Gold dungeons, and its needle turns gold while its target is up here.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.65645ABECD7F3F68.title": "The Book of Lore",
  "quest.65645ABECD7F3F68.quest_subtitle": "An encyclopedia with a cloud problem.",
  "quest.65645ABECD7F3F68.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Open the \"},{\"text\":\"Book of Lore\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:book_of_lore\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and put any Aether item in its slot: it reads you that item's entry. A book and an \"},{\"text\":\"Ambrosium Shard\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:ambrosium_shard\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make another copy for the team.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7A01ECF775897E61.title": "Lore-ception",
  "quest.7A01ECF775897E61.quest_subtitle": "We need to go deeper.",
  "quest.7A01ECF775897E61.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"You put a \"},{\"text\":\"Book of Lore\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:book_of_lore\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" inside a Book of Lore. It has an entry about itself, and now you've read it.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.0A89FDE16D411513.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.184C5196748CB082.title": "A bed among the clouds",
  "quest.184C5196748CB082.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Wool over \"},{\"text\":\"Skyroot Planks\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:skyroot_planks\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" makes a \"},{\"text\":\"Skyroot Bed\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:skyroot_bed\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". By day it only sets your respawn, and while the Sun Spirit lives it's always day. Vanilla beds don't explode up here either.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6833E110D55B57C8.title": "Falling is not the end",
  "quest.6833E110D55B57C8.quest_subtitle": "More of a transfer, really.",
  "quest.6833E110D55B57C8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Drop below the Aether and you reappear at the top of the Overworld's sky, still falling. A parachute in your pack opens by itself once you fall fast: four \"},{\"text\":\"Cold Aerclouds\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:cold_aercloud\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make a \"},{\"text\":\"Cold Parachute\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:cold_parachute\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", good for one jump.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Hold \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.sneak\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" to keep it closed. Landing on a Cold Aercloud cancels the damage too.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.44FFB3CE7B4D782A.title": "Twenty soft landings",
  "quest.44FFB3CE7B4D782A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Golden Aerclouds\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:golden_aercloud\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" float in small patches, higher than the cold ones; four make a \"},{\"text\":\"Golden Parachute\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:golden_parachute\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" with 20 uses instead of one. None in sight? The Altar enchants a Cold Aercloud into a golden one.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.296788BEB5470DB2.title": "Bounce house",
  "quest.296788BEB5470DB2.quest_subtitle": "Up is also a direction.",
  "quest.296788BEB5470DB2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Step on a \"},{\"text\":\"Blue Aercloud\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:blue_aercloud\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and it launches you high, mobs included. They hang close to the ground; a Freezer turns a Cold Aercloud blue if you want a launch pad at home.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Near an edge, a bounce is a one-way ticket.\",\"color\":\"#FF8C7A\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0472AAE887E5E84D.title": "A wooden bucket",
  "quest.0472AAE887E5E84D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three planks make a \"},{\"text\":\"Skyroot Bucket\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:skyroot_bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It carries water, milk, powder snow and fish like an iron one, and it's the only bucket that milks an Aechor Plant for its poison.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.219A76A239711D10.title": "Tending the garden",
  "quest.219A76A239711D10.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Use an \"},{\"text\":\"Ambrosium Shard\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:ambrosium_shard\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on Aether grass and it becomes Enchanted: berry bushes on it drop twice as much. Plant a White or Purple Flower on it and Aechor Plants won't spawn there.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.59178A7BC0D51C7A.title": "Ambrosium for the common store",
  "quest.59178A7BC0D51C7A.quest_subtitle": "Fuel for everyone's Altar.",
  "quest.59178A7BC0D51C7A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Thirty-two \"},{\"text\":\"Ambrosium Shards\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:ambrosium_shard\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for the common store, once a day. A Skyroot pickaxe doubles every Ambrosium Ore you break.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.46D903B647338573.title": "Mine Icestone",
  "quest.71B9F0B85C252B0F.title": "The Freezer",
  "quest.71B9F0B85C252B0F.quest_subtitle": "Cold as ice, on demand.",
  "quest.71B9F0B85C252B0F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Icestone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:icestone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" is common ore for a stone-tier pickaxe, and the Freezer's fuel: Holystone, one Icestone and \"},{\"text\":\"Skyroot Planks\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:skyroot_planks\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" build it. Placed on its own, Icestone freezes the water and lava around it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.42F15E58283F1514.title": "Cool jewelry",
  "quest.42F15E58283F1514.quest_subtitle": "Walk on water. Also on lava.",
  "quest.42F15E58283F1514.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Freeze an \"},{\"text\":\"Iron Ring\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:iron_ring\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" or a Golden Pendant and it becomes ice jewelry: worn, it freezes the water and lava under your feet as you walk.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5592AE04171F10D2.title": "What the Freezer takes",
  "quest.5592AE04171F10D2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Besides jewelry: a lava bucket becomes a block of obsidian, a water bucket ice, ice packed ice, a Cold Aercloud a blue one and Skyroot leaves Crystal Leaves. One Icestone runs it for 400 ticks.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.45C09783B94CF760.title": "Wear it in",
  "quest.45C09783B94CF760.quest_subtitle": "Broken in, not broken.",
  "quest.45C09783B94CF760.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Zanite Pickaxe\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:zanite_pickaxe\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and the \"},{\"text\":\"Zanite Axe\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:zanite_axe\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" work faster the more worn they are, and the \"},{\"text\":\"Zanite Sword\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:zanite_sword\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" goes from iron damage up to double. The axe also gets Golden Amber out of Golden Oak.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Repairing resets the bonus, so repair late, right before it breaks.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.14968BF98158D2B0.title": "Gloves complete the set",
  "quest.14968BF98158D2B0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Aether armor has a fifth piece, and set bonuses need their gloves. \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.aether.open_accessories.desc\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" opens the accessory slots: gloves, rings, pendant, cape, shield and one for charms. There are gloves for vanilla armor too.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1EE1CC47AF283D04.title": "Rings for miners",
  "quest.1EE1CC47AF283D04.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four gems in a ring make a \"},{\"text\":\"Zanite Ring\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:zanite_ring\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; string and one gem, a \"},{\"text\":\"Zanite Pendant\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:zanite_pendant\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Worn, they speed up mining and wear down while doing it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1011BB4D93050756.title": "Zanite goes down, too",
  "quest.1011BB4D93050756.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"In this pack a \"},{\"text\":\"Zanite Gemstone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:zanite_gemstone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" is an act IV part in six recipes below the clouds: the Iron Jetpacks elite coil, Oritech's exo jetpack, Reliquary's Rending Gale and three Apotheosis shelves, the endshelf among them.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0401093AF6BC17B0.title": "What the Altar enchants",
  "quest.0401093AF6BC17B0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Holystone becomes a \"},{\"text\":\"Healing Stone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:healing_stone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", food that gives Regeneration; a Blue Berry an \"},{\"text\":\"Enchanted Berry\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:enchanted_berry\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" that fills far more hunger; Quicksoil, tinted \"},{\"text\":\"Quicksoil Glass\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:quicksoil_glass\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Quicksoil Glass only drops with Silk Touch: place it where it stays.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.424E6096D0EBB9B6.title": "Repair at the Altar",
  "quest.424E6096D0EBB9B6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Put a damaged tool or armor piece in the Altar and it comes out whole, no extra materials, only Ambrosium: a Gravitite sword takes 1500 ticks, six shards. It works on vanilla gear too, and on Zanite it resets the bonus.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.71867D70C098EA24.title": "Aether tune",
  "quest.71867D70C098EA24.quest_subtitle": "Same song, bluer.",
  "quest.71867D70C098EA24.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"You enchanted a plain music disc at the Altar and got a \"},{\"text\":\"Blue Music Disc\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:music_disc_aether_tune\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Ambrosium well spent, arguably.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.27F0C9E2760CAB1E.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.23AFBDB1414D53C2.title": "Ore that floats away",
  "quest.23AFBDB1414D53C2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Gravitite Ore floats up as soon as nothing is above it, so dig from underneath or cover it first. Enchanted Gravitite blocks do the same when powered by redstone: a cheap floating elevator.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.353183661978AEA7.title": "Tools that lift",
  "quest.353183661978AEA7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Right-click stone with a \"},{\"text\":\"Gravitite Pickaxe\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:gravitite_pickaxe\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and it levitates; the pickaxe also mines any ore. The \"},{\"text\":\"Gravitite Sword\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:gravitite_sword\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" flings whatever it hits into the air.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.34AAA2ACF2827249.title": "Defying gravity",
  "quest.34AAA2ACF2827249.quest_subtitle": "Parachutes are for other people.",
  "quest.34AAA2ACF2827249.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"All five Gravitite pieces, gloves included: \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.aether.gravitite_jump_ability.desc\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" jumps far higher, and you take no fall damage. The best insurance there is up here.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.296FD95599743C71.title": "Chests with teeth",
  "quest.296FD95599743C71.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"In Bronze and Silver dungeons some chests are Chest Mimics: open one and it bites. Killing it drops the chest plus a few darts, gems or tools, so it isn't a total loss.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6002D1E1406E0EDB.title": "The Bronze treasure",
  "quest.6002D1E1406E0EDB.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Each Bronze reward chest rolls one treasure: the Slider's music disc half the time, otherwise the \"},{\"text\":\"Valkyrie Lance\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:valkyrie_lance\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", long reach for Zephyrs and the Queen; the \"},{\"text\":\"Hammer of Kingbdogz\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:hammer_of_kingbdogz\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", which fires shockwaves, or \"},{\"text\":\"Sentry Boots\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:sentry_boots\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", no fall damage.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.51FC5C91B5544463.title": "Neptune armor",
  "quest.51FC5C91B5544463.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Every Bronze reward chest holds one Neptune piece, sometimes more. It swims faster, and the whole set with the \"},{\"text\":\"Neptune Gloves\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:neptune_gloves\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" beats Depth Strider. Pair it with an Iron Bubble for ocean monuments.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.304BE74AC7A80387.title": "Dungeon charms",
  "quest.304BE74AC7A80387.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three accessories worth a slot: the \"},{\"text\":\"Agility Cape\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:agility_cape\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" steps you up blocks, the \"},{\"text\":\"Shield of Repulsion\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:shield_of_repulsion\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" throws projectiles back, the \"},{\"text\":\"Iron Bubble\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:iron_bubble\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" lets you breathe underwater. The first two come from Bronze rewards, the bubble from Gold.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5F331382032266A3.title": "Ultimate ban hammer",
  "quest.5F331382032266A3.quest_subtitle": "Sweet, sweet revenge.",
  "quest.5F331382032266A3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"You took down a Zephyr with a shockwave from the \"},{\"text\":\"Hammer of Kingbdogz\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:hammer_of_kingbdogz\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". For every snowball it ever threw at you.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.4C863190FC1D5659.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.4F744B0263CA523A.title": "Earning your wings",
  "quest.4F744B0263CA523A.quest_desc": [
    "Silver rewards always hold Valkyrie gear, and the full armor set with its gloves lets you fly for a short while. The Valkyrie pickaxe, axe and shovel reach much farther than normal tools."
  ],
  "quest.27AF38BF4263F717.title": "Battle hardened",
  "quest.27AF38BF4263F717.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Regeneration Stone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:regeneration_stone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" is a Silver treasure: wear it in a charm slot and your wounds close on their own. Two stones stack.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.76F0500F487A5F6E.title": "Now you don't see me",
  "quest.76F0500F487A5F6E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Invisibility Cloak\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:invisibility_cloak\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" goes in the cape slot and makes you fully invisible, gear included: mobs that can't see you can't attack. \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.aether.invisibility_toggle.desc\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" switches it off without taking it off.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.020979BD8B89417C.title": "Plunderer's remorse",
  "quest.020979BD8B89417C.quest_subtitle": "Farming, from a safe distance.",
  "quest.020979BD8B89417C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"You beat the Valkyrie Queen and used your prize, the \"},{\"text\":\"Valkyrie Hoe\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:valkyrie_hoe\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", to till dirt. From very far away, at least.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.4F67F9C75E130A1F.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.3BB24EE38039A313.title": "Fireproof",
  "quest.3BB24EE38039A313.quest_desc": [
    "The Gold treasure rolls two to five times on Phoenix armor, with a rare Life Shard in the mix. The whole set with gloves makes you immune to fire and lets you swim in lava.",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Stand in water long enough and each piece turns into Obsidian armor, stronger than diamond. Choose before you swim.\",\"color\":\"#FF8C7A\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.73BDDA23774A264C.title": "Ice bucket armor",
  "quest.73BDDA23774A264C.quest_subtitle": "Worth the cold shower.",
  "quest.73BDDA23774A264C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A full set of \"},{\"text\":\"Obsidian armor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:obsidian_chestplate\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", gloves included. The only way to get it is to take a swim in Phoenix armor, and you went all the way.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.69BD7B8AFBB5469B.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.7D711A8074032A49.title": "A permanent heart",
  "quest.7D711A8074032A49.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Use a \"},{\"text\":\"Life Shard\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:life_shard\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and you gain an extra heart for good, up to ten shards per player. They're rare Gold treasure, so share them fairly: every player has their own cap.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3CCD844296921C32.title": "The sun on a dial",
  "quest.3CCD844296921C32.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Sun Altar\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:sun_altar\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" the Spirit dropped sets the time of day in the Aether, and only there. On a server anyone can use it, unless an operator turns on its whitelist.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.07164C544A900A0B.title": "A note above the clouds",
  "quest.07164C544A900A0B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The light up here doesn't come from the sun. I measured it for a month: not one dusk. Heliodor went up to ask the sky a question; I only wanted to know where the light was coming from. T.\",\"italic\":true}]"
  ],
  "quest.51645D0B8EF4C3A1.title": "Aechor Plants",
  "quest.51645D0B8EF4C3A1.quest_subtitle": "Pretty. Venomous. Delicious to Moas.",
  "quest.51645D0B8EF4C3A1.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Rooted plants that spit poison needles at you. Kill one for an \"},{\"text\":\"Aechor Petal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:aechor_petal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a Moa's favourite food, or use a \"},{\"text\":\"Skyroot Bucket\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:skyroot_bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on a living one to collect its poison.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.03FC782CF49140C2.title": "The cure grows on trees",
  "quest.03FC782CF49140C2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Aether poison causes Inebriation: damage over time and random stumbling, lovely near an edge. A \"},{\"text\":\"White Apple\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:white_apple\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" cures it; they grow on the Crystal Trees you find on small islands.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.64D72AAD47BF859A.title": "A remedy in a bucket",
  "quest.64D72AAD47BF859A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Enchant a \"},{\"text\":\"Skyroot Poison Bucket\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:skyroot_poison_bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" at the Altar and it becomes a \"},{\"text\":\"Skyroot Remedy Bucket\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:skyroot_remedy_bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Drink it for Remedy: it cures Inebriation and keeps you immune for a while.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0D80B878726AC7CE.title": "Poison on a dart",
  "quest.0D80B878726AC7CE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Golden Dart Shooter and an \"},{\"text\":\"Aechor Petal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:aechor_petal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make a \"},{\"text\":\"Poison Dart Shooter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:poison_dart_shooter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; eight Golden Darts around a Skyroot Poison Bucket make its ammo. Whatever it hits gets Inebriated.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.35217160B419E527.title": "Amber in the gold",
  "quest.35217160B419E527.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Golden Oak logs hold \"},{\"text\":\"Golden Amber\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:golden_amber\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", and only a Zanite, Gravitite or Valkyrie axe gets it out, by chopping the log or by stripping it. Any other axe gives plain Skyroot.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.202A02A46148CED5.title": "Darts that don't drop",
  "quest.202A02A46148CED5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two planks over a \"},{\"text\":\"Golden Amber\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:golden_amber\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make a \"},{\"text\":\"Golden Dart Shooter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:golden_dart_shooter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; a feather, a stick and amber make \"},{\"text\":\"Golden Darts\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:golden_dart\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Darts fly straight, with no gravity.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The Altar enchants both the shooter and the darts into their stronger Enchanted versions.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.184543A04B54654C.title": "A census of the sky",
  "quest.184543A04B54654C.quest_subtitle": "Everyone here has wings or a plan.",
  "quest.184543A04B54654C.quest_desc": [
    "Look at each of the Aether's six passive animals for a moment. Moas lay eggs, Phygs and Flying Cows take a saddle, Sheepuffs puff their wool and float, an Aerbunny rides on your head and slows your fall, and Aerwhales drift overhead."
  ],
  "quest.0956045C8803BDBE.title": "When Phygs fly",
  "quest.0956045C8803BDBE.quest_subtitle": "Finally, the saying makes sense.",
  "quest.0956045C8803BDBE.quest_desc": [
    "Put a saddle on a Phyg and ride it through the air. Blue Berries lure Phygs and Flying Cows alike, and a saddled Flying Cow flies too."
  ],
  "quest.41C87E88BE6D8C4E.title": "Swets",
  "quest.41C87E88BE6D8C4E.quest_subtitle": "Gooey, jumpy, occasionally hungry.",
  "quest.41C87E88BE6D8C4E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Jelly blobs that swallow you whole. Blue Swets drop \"},{\"text\":\"Swet Balls\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:swet_ball\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": a slimeball for leads, and they turn Aether dirt into grass. Golden Swets drop glowstone, handy for a second portal.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.41621867BB7705C7.title": "Defeat a Zephyr",
  "quest.4BB74AAC72630E56.title": "Clear skies",
  "quest.4BB74AAC72630E56.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Zephyrs float at a distance and fire snowballs that knock you back; they drop \"},{\"text\":\"Cold Aerclouds\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:cold_aercloud\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Arrows, darts or a long reach work better than chasing them over the void.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6A849092A4FDAF09.title": "Whirlwind etiquette",
  "quest.6A849092A4FDAF09.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Whirlwinds drift around and fling you. Now and then they spit out junk: sand, logs, flint, even a diamond. The Evil Whirlwinds sometimes spit out a creeper instead.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.157454C8A47D5E06.title": "Don't count your Moas",
  "quest.157454C8A47D5E06.quest_desc": [
    "A wild adult Moa lays an egg of its own color every five to ten minutes. Blue Moas are common and jump three times in the air, White ones four, Black ones eight; Silver dungeon chests hold Blue and White eggs too."
  ],
  "quest.7358AEF66888973E.title": "Until they hatch",
  "quest.7358AEF66888973E.quest_subtitle": "A bird in the hand.",
  "quest.7358AEF66888973E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Holystone around an \"},{\"text\":\"Ambrosium Torch\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:ambrosium_torch\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" makes an \"},{\"text\":\"Incubator\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:incubator\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; an egg and two torches of fuel hatch a chick. Feed it an \"},{\"text\":\"Aechor Petal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:aechor_petal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" each time it's hungry, three in all, and it grows up.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Only a Moa you raised takes a saddle. Riding it, jump again in mid-air: the jumps left show on screen and refill when you land."
  ],
  "quest.6F42F1516D71A75C.title": "Sit. Stay. Good bird.",
  "quest.6F42F1516D71A75C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Zanite Gemstone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:zanite_gemstone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on a stick makes a \"},{\"text\":\"Nature Staff\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:nature_staff\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Use it on a Moa you raised to make it sit or stand; sneak and use it to have the Moa follow you.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4CA47E44FA303713.title": "Eight jumps high",
  "quest.4CA47E44FA303713.quest_subtitle": "The best seat in the sky.",
  "quest.4CA47E44FA303713.quest_desc": [
    "Ride a Black Moa: eight jumps in the air, the best island-hopper there is. Black Moas are the rarest in the wild, so grab the egg one lays and raise it yourself; only raised Moas take a saddle."
  ],
  "image.0C43DD51158640DB.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"First steps\",\"color\":\"#F6D77A\"}]",
  "image.1D92FB250EBF26E6.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Aerclouds\",\"color\":\"#F6D77A\"}]",
  "image.4F9E976DCC754289.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Skyroot and Holystone\",\"color\":\"#F6D77A\"}]",
  "image.270BD944DEE5F66C.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Freezer\",\"color\":\"#F6D77A\"}]",
  "image.5C36594B19ED18C0.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Zanite\",\"color\":\"#F6D77A\"}]",
  "image.6898551BD7CFA50A.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Altar\",\"color\":\"#F6D77A\"}]",
  "image.5A624B9234152B1E.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Gravitite\",\"color\":\"#F6D77A\"}]",
  "image.5AFD6D7D63D39BCA.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Bronze treasure\",\"color\":\"#F6D77A\"}]",
  "image.69C969A08D8358BF.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Silver treasure\",\"color\":\"#F6D77A\"}]",
  "image.4FC6740D304A64E9.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Gold treasure\",\"color\":\"#F6D77A\"}]",
  "image.49AB3CE2456EF7C0.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Poison and remedy\",\"color\":\"#F6D77A\"}]",
  "image.03580C9C32989701.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Golden oak and darts\",\"color\":\"#F6D77A\"}]",
  "image.4D6515EEEC334016.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Sky fauna\",\"color\":\"#F6D77A\"}]",
  "image.20A6004E12AF54F9.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Moas\",\"color\":\"#F6D77A\"}]",
  "image.02DFCE3F166441C7.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Aether\",\"color\":\"#F6D77A\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.1C6C1C3EB23BAD20.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"the sun never sets here\",\"color\":\"#B8D8EE\",\"font\":\"minecraft:alt\"}]",
  "image.3BA5588365042EAE.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» Deep Aether\",\"color\":\"#F6D77A\"}]",
  "image.4496413A02CB4B32.title": "Back to the Sun of Heliodor",
  "chapter.2141D3453BBA64F0.title": "The Nether and the End",
  "chapter.2141D3453BBA64F0.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Two vanilla dimensions, rebuilt and crowded: what changes, what to look for and how to survive."
  ],
  "quest.03CC695E3623C8E5.title": "Familiar places, new rules",
  "quest.03CC695E3623C8E5.quest_desc": [
    "Both dimensions are far busier than vanilla: YUNG's rebuilds the big structures, Repurposed Structures, Dungeons and Taverns, Cataclysm, Friends and Foes and Hellish Trials add many more, and Enderman Overhaul fills them with biome endermen.",
    "",
    "The compass sends you to a Nether fortress in act III and to the End in act V."
  ],
  "quest.5A8E9C6BA67CBFA4.title": "We Need to Go Deeper",
  "quest.5A8E9C6BA67CBFA4.quest_desc": [
    "Build an obsidian frame and light it; Nether Portal Fix links the return portal to the one you came from.",
    "",
    "Pack fire resistance, one piece of gold armor (piglins leave you alone), blocks to bridge and something to put out fires. The Nether does not do second chances."
  ],
  "quest.653E3DFA0A5DA6FE.title": "A blaze rod from a fortress",
  "quest.653E3DFA0A5DA6FE.quest_desc": [
    "YUNG's Better Nether Fortresses makes them larger and themed. In act III the compass points to one and counts it done as soon as someone on your team carries a Blaze Rod.",
    "",
    "Blaze rods feed brewing, Powah and many mid-game recipes, and wither skeletons here drop the skulls for the Wither."
  ],
  "quest.6C2CB59EB7AB9359.title": "Crossing lava seas",
  "quest.6C2CB59EB7AB9359.quest_desc": [
    "Fireproof Boats adds crimson and warped boats that survive lava like their planks: cross lava oceans and scout the shores.",
    "",
    "Or go vanilla: saddle a strider and steer it with a warped fungus on a stick. Slower, but it has personality."
  ],
  "quest.0905D2D4B1D95BDF.title": "What else lives in the Nether",
  "quest.0905D2D4B1D95BDF.quest_desc": [
    "Dungeons and Taverns adds Nether Keeps (with their own key), ports, skeleton towers and camps, and piglin camps, hamlets and donjons. Repurposed Structures adds Nether cities, underground bastions, strongholds, pyramids, mineshafts, temples and crimson or warped villages. Add Hellish Trials' chambers, the Citadel of the Wildfire (Friends and Foes) and the Burning Arena and Soul Forge (Cataclysm)."
  ],
  "quest.76C7A1F4CEEEEE65.title": "Concrete Halls",
  "quest.76C7A1F4CEEEEE65.quest_desc": [
    "Find a Dungeons and Taverns Nether Keep for Concrete Halls. Keeps and ports are skeleton strongholds; exploring every skeleton camp, tower, port, fortress and keep is Skull Collector.",
    "",
    "Bathing in powder snow inside a keep is its own advancement, Cool Off. Somebody had a fun afternoon designing that."
  ],
  "quest.2A4135289353D989.title": "Bastions and piglins",
  "quest.2A4135289353D989.quest_desc": [
    "Bastion remnants hold gold and netherite upgrade templates, with ancient debris nearby. Wear gold, do not open chests in sight of piglins, and watch for Piglin Brutes, which ignore gold entirely.",
    "",
    "Dungeons and Taverns adds four more piglin places, for Hog Hunt."
  ],
  "quest.50763FDA378A360C.title": "Hidden in the Depths",
  "quest.50763FDA378A360C.quest_desc": [
    "Ancient debris hides low in the Nether and shrugs off explosions. Mine it with a diamond pickaxe, smelt it into scrap and combine with gold into netherite ingots.",
    "",
    "Keep your netherite gear: it is the base for Cataclysm's Ignitium and Cursium and for Luminous gear."
  ],
  "quest.4394BC17C2F2C3BE.title": "Nether endermen and food",
  "quest.4394BC17C2F2C3BE.quest_desc": [
    "Enderman Overhaul gives each Nether biome its own enderman: crimson ones drop pearls that grant Strength on teleport, warped ones Resistance, and soul sand valley ones a pearl that teleports a bound creature.",
    "",
    "My Nether's Delight adds Nether cooking to Farmer's Delight: more variety for the pack's food system."
  ],
  "quest.6F418FFE86CB3ACD.title": "The stronghold",
  "quest.6F418FFE86CB3ACD.quest_desc": [
    "Eyes of Ender lead to the stronghold, rebuilt by YUNG's Better Strongholds. In act V the compass counts it done when your team reaches the End.",
    "",
    "Bring spare eyes. They break at the worst moment."
  ],
  "quest.5DC959C522847AC4.title": "The End",
  "quest.5DC959C522847AC4.quest_desc": [
    "YUNG's Better End Island rebuilds the central island and the Dragon arena; the fight itself is in the bosses chapter. After the Dragon, throw an ender pearl into an End Gateway to reach the outer islands (Remote Getaway)."
  ],
  "quest.108AAEC672725EF9.title": "The City at the End of the Game",
  "quest.108AAEC672725EF9.quest_desc": [
    "End cities rise on the outer islands, guarded by Shulkers whose Levitation can kill you when it wears off: carry slow falling or a water bucket. Their ships hide Elytra, and their chests hold good enchanted gear.",
    "",
    "Look up before you look down."
  ],
  "quest.2DB3986BA317369E.title": "The busy outer End",
  "quest.2DB3986BA317369E.quest_desc": [
    "Dungeons and Taverns adds the End Castle (a haunting boss), the End Lighthouse and lone ships; Repurposed Structures, End outposts, mineshafts, shipwrecks, pyramids, strongholds and an ancient city; Explorify, a shipwreck; Cataclysm, the Ruined Citadel and its Ender Guardian. Enderman Overhaul's End endermen drop Corrupted and Ancient Pearls, and End's Delight cooks it all."
  ],
  "quest.09764E768DB75F4F.title": "The Light at the End of the Game",
  "quest.09764E768DB75F4F.quest_desc": [
    "Find a Dungeons and Taverns End Lighthouse: a fitting landmark for a pack about light, and a good spot for a waystone before exploring further.",
    "",
    "Even at the end of the world, someone left a light on."
  ],
  "quest.6771B1C3C9DED3B8.title": "Waystones in other dimensions",
  "quest.6771B1C3C9DED3B8.quest_desc": [
    "Build a Nether waystone (red Nether bricks) and an End one (End stone bricks) near each portal. Warping between dimensions costs a flat amount of experience and saves the portal walk every time.",
    "",
    "Wild waystones also generate in the Nether and the End."
  ],
  "quest.0A003066AB308EE3.title": "What ENTRELUMEN changes here",
  "quest.0A003066AB308EE3.quest_desc": [
    "The compass visits a YUNG's fortress in act III (carry a blaze rod) and, in act V, the ocean monument, the stronghold and the End (kill the Dragon). The Wither is the only nether star source.",
    "",
    "Dungeons and Taverns adds fortresses, ports and towers to the Nether, and the pack's measurements flag them as worth watching on a modest PC."
  ],
  "quest.5DEB6F3020339532.title": "Both ends of the world",
  "quest.5DEB6F3020339532.quest_desc": [
    "Fortresses, bastions and keeps below; cities, lighthouses and citadels beyond the void.",
    "",
    "You have seen both ends of the world. Heliodor is somewhere in between."
  ],
  "chapter.6E9693DC6106BEC9.title": "The Twilight Forest",
  "chapter.6E9693DC6106BEC9.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Eight bosses, nine locked biomes: each curse lifts when its keeper falls."
  ],
  "quest.0EA44BF18B7729BC.title": "A pool, flowers and a diamond",
  "quest.0EA44BF18B7729BC.quest_subtitle": "The lightning is part of the recipe.",
  "quest.0EA44BF18B7729BC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Dig a pool of water, up to 64 blocks, edged with grass or dirt and a plant on every edge block: flowers, ferns, saplings, crops. Throw a \"},{\"text\":\"Diamond\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:diamond\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in and lightning turns the water into a portal.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"It only forms in the Overworld, and the lightning \"},{\"text\":\"sets fires\",\"color\":\"#FF8C7A\"},{\"text\":\": keep it away from wood. The way back needs no diamond.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4955DC5E41BC9388.title": "The Naga Courtyard",
  "quest.4955DC5E41BC9388.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Nagastone walls, leafy hedges and serpent-head statues around a paved arena: the Naga's home. The compass points here in act III, and a \"},{\"text\":\"Magic Map\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"0C4CE938F64896BA\"}},{\"text\":\" marks it with the Naga's face.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.51586CD75D2DEDB2.title": "Defeat the Naga",
  "quest.7212AD2EC72A656F.title": "The Naga",
  "quest.7212AD2EC72A656F.quest_subtitle": "Long body, short temper.",
  "quest.7212AD2EC72A656F.quest_desc": [
    "A serpent that charges in straight lines and coils around its arena. Sidestep the charges; steer it into a wall and it stuns itself, and that's your window.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"It leaves 6 to 11 \"},{\"text\":\"Naga Scales\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:naga_scale\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and its \"},{\"text\":\"Naga Trophy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:naga_trophy\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in a chest where it appeared. Carrying a scale is what gets you through the Lich Tower's barrier.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.23F4B84C5B6538D2.title": "The Lich Tower",
  "quest.23F4B84C5B6538D2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A spire of stone and bridges, sealed to anyone who hasn't beaten the Naga: a \"},{\"text\":\"Naga Scale\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:naga_scale\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in your pack counts. Zombies, skeletons and Death Tomes fill the floors; the Lich waits at the top.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Death Tomes drop paper and books, and now and then a \"},{\"text\":\"Magic Map Focus\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:magic_map_focus\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "task.510851CE428B9332.title": "Defeat the Twilight Lich",
  "quest.4946C8BB9106BD4D.title": "The Twilight Lich",
  "quest.4946C8BB9106BD4D.quest_subtitle": "He brought friends. Several.",
  "quest.4946C8BB9106BD4D.quest_desc": [
    "Three rounds: shields and shadow clones (break the shields; the clones can't be hurt), then minions, then he closes in. His bolts make any minion they hit stronger and faster, so keep them out of his line of fire.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"He drops one of four scepters, \"},{\"text\":\"Exanimate Essence\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:exanimate_essence\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", enchanted gold gear and the \"},{\"text\":\"Twilight Lich Trophy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:lich_trophy\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". His fall opens the Swamp, the Dark Forest and the Snowy Forest, in any order.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.363D1E6BBE352CC4.title": "Ultimate Showdown",
  "quest.363D1E6BBE352CC4.quest_desc": [
    "Hydra, Ur-Ghast and Snow Queen down: the acid rain over the Highlands stops. Each of the three kept part of that storm alive."
  ],
  "quest.00871B769FF15A7D.title": "The Highlands",
  "quest.00871B769FF15A7D.quest_desc": [
    "Hills over deep troll caves, with clouds hanging above them. Locked, it rains acid on anyone inside; after the showdown the troll caves let you in."
  ],
  "quest.1983173282DF3813.title": "Beans to the clouds",
  "quest.1983173282DF3813.quest_subtitle": "Jack had it easy.",
  "quest.1983173282DF3813.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Troll garden chests always hold \"},{\"text\":\"Magic Beans\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:magic_beans\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", and trolls drop them now and then. Use one on the glowing \"},{\"text\":\"Uberous Soil\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:uberous_soil\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" below the clouds and a stalk climbs all the way up.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1279980AEFD3DB26.title": "Giants in the clouds",
  "quest.1279980AEFD3DB26.quest_subtitle": "Fee-fi-fo-mine.",
  "quest.1279980AEFD3DB26.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Giant Miners roam the clouds and drop a \"},{\"text\":\"Giant's Pickaxe\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:giant_pickaxe\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" when you kill them. It breaks the giant blocks that wall off the troll vaults; mine a 4×4×4 cube of one block and it comes out as a single giant one.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.305E00B5ADF67301.title": "The Lamp of Cinders",
  "quest.305E00B5ADF67301.quest_desc": [
    "It waits in a troll vault behind giant blocks. Use it and the thorns around the plateau burn away; burnt thorns crumble when you step on them."
  ],
  "quest.545788B47FC5D0BF.title": "The Final Plateau",
  "quest.545788B47FC5D0BF.quest_subtitle": "The map ends here. For now.",
  "quest.545788B47FC5D0BF.quest_desc": [
    "Past the burnt thorns, the plateau and its castle. Setting foot on the Final Plateau ends the mod's progression: the castle is still unfinished, and the game tells you so.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "{image:twilightforest:textures/item/filled_magic_map.png width:48 height:48 align:center}",
    "",
    "Nine curses lifted, eight trophies to hang. The forest is still dark, but now it's yours."
  ],
  "quest.28D1279FCE9BE606.title": "Trolls and Trollber",
  "quest.28D1279FCE9BE606.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Trolls guard the caves. Kill one next to Trollber and it ripens: each ripe one drops 4 to 8 \"},{\"text\":\"Torchberries\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:torchberries\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7BAACB5DDB46EED3.title": "A note under the canopy",
  "quest.7BAACB5DDB46EED3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Every curse here is kept alive by something that refuses to fall. Remove the keeper and the weather changes by morning. We called this forest a rehearsal. —J.\",\"italic\":true}]"
  ],
  "quest.4FD94E7FFA74C632.title": "The Twilight Swamp",
  "quest.4FD94E7FFA74C632.quest_desc": [
    "Until the Lich falls, the swamp piles Hunger on you every three seconds, worse the longer you stay. After him it's just a swamp: mangroves, mosquito swarms and the Minotaur Labyrinth underneath."
  ],
  "quest.7CAC3BCB9FBF1F4D.title": "The Minotaur Labyrinth",
  "quest.7CAC3BCB9FBF1F4D.quest_desc": [
    "Mazestone corridors under the swamp, full of Minotaurs, Maze Slimes and beetles. Dead ends hide chests, the Minoshroom keeps its own room, and a secret vault sits somewhere in the walls."
  ],
  "task.37984B578667CBAC.title": "Defeat the Minoshroom",
  "quest.531A3002A39E814B.title": "The Minoshroom",
  "quest.531A3002A39E814B.quest_subtitle": "Half bull, half mushroom, all attitude.",
  "quest.531A3002A39E814B.quest_desc": [
    "A mushroom-headed minotaur with an axe. It charges, and if you linger too close it slams the ground: circle it and hit it between charges.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"It drops 2 to 5 \"},{\"text\":\"Meef Stroganoff\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:meef_stroganoff\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a \"},{\"text\":\"Diamond Minotaur Axe\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:diamond_minotaur_axe\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and its \"},{\"text\":\"Minoshroom Trophy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:minoshroom_trophy\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1BC244DB1E06B5D7.title": "Stroganoff for the heat",
  "quest.1BC244DB1E06B5D7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eat a \"},{\"text\":\"Meef Stroganoff\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:meef_stroganoff\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and your body gets used to the Fire Swamp's heat: that's the key to its lock. Each player eats their own, so share the pot.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4AA1DE958E2309EB.title": "The Fire Swamp",
  "quest.4AA1DE958E2309EB.quest_subtitle": "Warm, with a chance of worse.",
  "quest.4AA1DE958E2309EB.quest_desc": [
    "Fire jets spit around the Hydra's lair. Without the stroganoff it sets you alight for eight seconds, every three; with it, only the scenery burns."
  ],
  "task.552796629E194D44.title": "Defeat the Hydra",
  "quest.282914EAB0C2CF9C.title": "The Hydra",
  "quest.282914EAB0C2CF9C.quest_subtitle": "More heads than patience.",
  "quest.282914EAB0C2CF9C.quest_desc": [
    "Its heads bite, breathe fire and lob mortars. Hit a head when it lunges; mortars can be knocked back. Fire resistance turns this from grim to fair.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"It leaves 5 to 35 \"},{\"text\":\"Hydra Chops\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:hydra_chop\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", 7 to 10 \"},{\"text\":\"Fiery Blood\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:fiery_blood\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and its \"},{\"text\":\"Hydra Trophy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:hydra_trophy\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.10AEECD6C7411D0C.title": "Heads up",
  "quest.10AEECD6C7411D0C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Each head you cut grows back as two, so the fight won't shrink. Afterwards, look up: every stalactite in the lair is ore, from coal to gold and redstone.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.755BA6E21400F24E.title": "Empty stomach, full chop",
  "quest.755BA6E21400F24E.quest_subtitle": "Chef's kiss.",
  "quest.755BA6E21400F24E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"You ate a \"},{\"text\":\"Hydra Chop\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:hydra_chop\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on an empty hunger bar. One chop fills it to the brim: the most efficient revenge on record.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.741748C9A34AAD13.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.7C2E55F2F5F32A25.title": "Fiery Ingot",
  "quest.7C2E55F2F5F32A25.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Fiery Blood\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:fiery_blood\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" or \"},{\"text\":\"Fiery Tears\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:fiery_tears\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" plus an iron ingot, shapeless. Fiery tools and armor are made of it, and they repair with more ingots.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7C71AB5384C5C545.title": "A pickaxe that smelts",
  "quest.7C71AB5384C5C545.quest_subtitle": "The furnace is jealous.",
  "quest.7C71AB5384C5C545.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Fiery Pickaxe\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:fiery_pickaxe\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" smelts what it breaks, so ore comes out as ingots. Three fiery ingots and two blaze rods, or an iron pickaxe with three Fiery Blood or Tears and two rods.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.359D4E0E0376586D.title": "Blood and tears",
  "quest.359D4E0E0376586D.quest_desc": [
    "Fiery armor burns whoever hits you; the Fiery Sword burns whatever you hit. Hold a fiery tool with a piece of fiery armor in your inventory and the set is complete, bragging rights included."
  ],
  "quest.00395A19070A1E8F.title": "Maze Map Focus",
  "quest.00395A19070A1E8F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Minotaurs drop one about once every forty kills, and Labyrinth and Knight Stronghold rooms keep them in chests. Eight crafting tables around one make an \"},{\"text\":\"Uncrafting Table\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"2F31C4287AA428C1\"}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6CEB860E54C43B0F.title": "A map of the maze",
  "quest.6CEB860E54C43B0F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The focus in the middle, paper around it: a \"},{\"text\":\"Blank Maze Map\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:maze_map\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Filled inside the Labyrinth, it draws the corridors on the level you stand on.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.17FA3D1126D19955.title": "Worth every block",
  "quest.17FA3D1126D19955.quest_subtitle": "Accountants hate this map.",
  "quest.17FA3D1126D19955.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Maze Map plus a block each of diamond, gold and iron: the \"},{\"text\":\"Blank Maze/Ore Map\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:ore_map\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", which marks ores too. You paid a diamond block for directions.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.48029B99038FF9A7.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.6A0411B8ED3687D9.title": "The secret vault",
  "quest.6A0411B8ED3687D9.quest_subtitle": "The walls were load-bearing. Were.",
  "quest.6A0411B8ED3687D9.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Sealed vaults in the Labyrinth's walls hold enchanted steeleaf gear. One holds the \"},{\"text\":\"Mazebreaker\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:mazebreaker_pickaxe\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", which cuts Mazestone 16 times faster and without the extra wear.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7540FCE64CAFFEBD.title": "The Dark Forest",
  "quest.7540FCE64CAFFEBD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Locked, it wraps you in \"},{\"text\":\"Darkness\",\"color\":\"#D8C8FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_text\",\"contents\":\"The vanilla effect that dims the screen in pulses, like the Warden's.\"}},{\"text\":\" every few seconds. With the Lich beaten it's only very dark: goblins, crabs in helmets and the ruins of the Knight Stronghold.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4698EBAFF4445D37.title": "A trophy on the pedestal",
  "quest.4698EBAFF4445D37.quest_subtitle": "Show and tell, knight edition.",
  "quest.4698EBAFF4445D37.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Deep in the stronghold ruins stands a \"},{\"text\":\"Trophy Pedestal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:trophy_pedestal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Set any boss trophy on it: the shield blocks around it break, everyone within 16 blocks who beat the Lich earns the title, and the stronghold's inner halls open.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A comparator by the pedestal reads the trophy: 5 for the Naga, up to 14 for the Snow Queen.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3F2B34D964E4C5A9.title": "The Knight Phantoms",
  "quest.3F2B34D964E4C5A9.quest_subtitle": "A whole order of grudges.",
  "quest.3F2B34D964E4C5A9.quest_desc": [
    "They come out together in the stronghold's tomb. The invisible ones take far less damage: always swing at the one you can see.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"They drop enchanted knightmetal tools and, now and then, Phantom armor that stays with you when you die. Beating the whole order leaves the \"},{\"text\":\"Knight Phantom Trophy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:knight_phantom_trophy\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2BCAAA1AB40D789D.title": "The Dark Tower",
  "quest.2BCAAA1AB40D789D.quest_desc": [
    "A towerwood spire in the Dark Forest's center, locked until the Knight Phantoms rest. Inside: vanishing and reappearing blocks, carminite golems, ghastlings, and borers hiding in infested planks."
  ],
  "quest.1921A9F593AFFAC9.title": "The Ghast Trap",
  "quest.1921A9F593AFFAC9.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"At the top, Carminite Ghastlings float around a \"},{\"text\":\"Ghast Trap\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:ghast_trap\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Kill them near it to charge it, then give it a redstone signal: it drags the Ur-Ghast down from the sky.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.1F2C75782C5A4791.title": "Defeat the Ur-Ghast",
  "quest.2DE150A68B058983.title": "The Ur-Ghast",
  "quest.2DE150A68B058983.quest_subtitle": "Cries fire, takes it personally.",
  "quest.2DE150A68B058983.quest_desc": [
    "Pulled into the trap's room, it floats and throws fireballs. A bow and fire resistance make it a fair fight.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"It drops \"},{\"text\":\"Carminite\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:carminite\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", \"},{\"text\":\"Fiery Tears\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:fiery_tears\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and its \"},{\"text\":\"Ur-Ghast Trophy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:ur_ghast_trophy\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.076AE29C59A9324D.title": "Knightmetal",
  "quest.076AE29C59A9324D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Goblin knights and helmet crabs drop \"},{\"text\":\"Armor Shards\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:armor_shard\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Nine make a cluster; smelt it for one \"},{\"text\":\"Knightmetal Ingot\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:knightmetal_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Stronghold caches sometimes hold whole ingots.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Knightmetal swords and pickaxes hit armored targets harder; the axe hits unarmored ones harder.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4D2685DFA1660B0B.title": "Block and Chain",
  "quest.4D2685DFA1660B0B.quest_subtitle": "Ball and chain's heavier cousin.",
  "quest.4D2685DFA1660B0B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A block of knightmetal, three ingots and a \"},{\"text\":\"Knightmetal Loop\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:knightmetal_ring\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": a flail you throw and reel back in. Enchant it with Destruction and it breaks blocks too.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3A217D75DCDDAB73.title": "Knightmetal Shield",
  "quest.3A217D75DCDDAB73.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Knightmetal, a loop and two \"},{\"text\":\"Towerwood Planks\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:towerwood\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" from the Dark Tower. It blocks like any shield, and a block timed right sends Twilight projectiles back at their owner.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4B472ABB4E1D0B01.title": "Carminite",
  "quest.4B472ABB4E1D0B01.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four \"},{\"text\":\"Borer Essence\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:borer_essence\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", four redstone and a ghast tear, shapeless. The Ur-Ghast drops it ready-made, and the tower's gadgets and the Traveller's Wings are built from it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.39AC9427B5AAAAB2.title": "Carminite Builder",
  "quest.39AC9427B5AAAAB2.quest_subtitle": "Instant bridge, no refunds.",
  "quest.39AC9427B5AAAAB2.quest_desc": [
    "A dispenser set in encased towerwood and carminite. Powered, it lays temporary blocks in the direction you look: a bridge that cleans up after itself.",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Reappearing Blocks\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:reappearing_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", from the same towerwood with carminite and redstone, vanish on a signal and come back: a door for your own tower.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.31639B75E9E89201.title": "Tower rules",
  "quest.31639B75E9E89201.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A chest in the Dark Tower holds the \"},{\"text\":\"Tower Key\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:tower_key\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": it opens the locked vanishing blocks and is never lost on death. Plain vanishing blocks disappear for good once triggered.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5390B36EAF0484B0.title": "Huge success",
  "quest.5390B36EAF0484B0.quest_subtitle": "Still hungry, still here.",
  "quest.5390B36EAF0484B0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"You sprinkled redstone on a whole \"},{\"text\":\"Experiment 115\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:experiment_115\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", and now it refills itself. Nobody asked what's in it, and nobody should.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.088DEA6A2B31A2B7.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.3FF5A6855AD8BBA9.title": "The Snowy Forest",
  "quest.3FF5A6855AD8BBA9.quest_desc": [
    "Locked, the blizzard gives you Frosted every few seconds, which slows you down. After the Lich it's just cold: yetis, winter wolves and the Yeti Caves."
  ],
  "task.2A161ECF4403011B.title": "Defeat the Alpha Yeti",
  "quest.40852BEC9F8AF9D4.title": "The Alpha Yeti",
  "quest.40852BEC9F8AF9D4.quest_subtitle": "Throws tantrums. And ice.",
  "quest.40852BEC9F8AF9D4.quest_desc": [
    "It hurls ice bombs, and its rampage shakes icicles loose from the cave roof: watch above you and keep moving. When the rampage ends it stops, tired, and that's when to hit it hard.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"It drops 6 \"},{\"text\":\"Alpha Yeti Fur\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:alpha_yeti_fur\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", 6 \"},{\"text\":\"Ice Bombs\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:ice_bomb\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and its \"},{\"text\":\"Alpha Yeti Trophy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:alpha_yeti_trophy\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Holding the fur is what the Glacier's lock asks for.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5F41C06E9CC8832D.title": "The Twilight Glacier",
  "quest.5F41C06E9CC8832D.quest_desc": [
    "The ice sheet at the heart of the snow. Locked, its frost bites one level harder; on top stands the Aurora Palace, and inside it, the Snow Queen."
  ],
  "task.600504641A0E9492.title": "Defeat the Snow Queen",
  "quest.5E27FBC034C96D9A.title": "The Snow Queen",
  "quest.5E27FBC034C96D9A.quest_subtitle": "Cold reception guaranteed.",
  "quest.5E27FBC034C96D9A.quest_desc": [
    "She fights on the palace roof, guarded by ice cores and Snow Guardians, and drops ice from above. Keep moving. The cores and guardians melt in hot biomes, a fact of no use up here.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"She drops a \"},{\"text\":\"Tri-Bow\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:triple_bow\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" or a \"},{\"text\":\"Seeker Bow\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:seeker_bow\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", packed ice, snowballs and her \"},{\"text\":\"Snow Queen Trophy\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:snow_queen_trophy\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.29D3048BF2590F2E.title": "In fashion",
  "quest.29D3048BF2590F2E.quest_subtitle": "Warm, and in any colour you like.",
  "quest.29D3048BF2590F2E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Yetis and winter wolves drop \"},{\"text\":\"Arctic Fur\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:arctic_fur\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for a full set of Arctic armor. Dye all four pieces. A block of the fur on the floor cuts fall damage by 90%.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.526279D1FFEFB514.title": "Yeti Boots",
  "quest.526279D1FFEFB514.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four \"},{\"text\":\"Alpha Yeti Fur\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:alpha_yeti_fur\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make boots that come with Feather Falling IV and Protection II. Yeti armor chills whoever hits you.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4636683B8480C66D.title": "Handle with care",
  "quest.4636683B8480C66D.quest_subtitle": "It was a very good hit.",
  "quest.4636683B8480C66D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"You broke a \"},{\"text\":\"Glass Sword\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:glass_sword\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" from the Aurora Palace. It shatters on the first hit, so that hit had better have mattered.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.407F58780F553D60.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.2343281F0BF397DB.title": "Naga armor",
  "quest.2343281F0BF397DB.quest_desc": [
    "Naga Scales make a tunic that comes with Fire Protection III and leggings with Protection III: a real step above iron for the early forest.",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Keep one scale in your pack: it's your pass into the Lich Tower.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4AB7CFD4E16E2DF1.title": "Conquered ground",
  "quest.4AB7CFD4E16E2DF1.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Beat a structure's boss and its monsters stop spawning there. Boss loot waits in a chest where the boss first appeared; the Knight Phantoms are the exception.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.039C50EEE3A8B7EC.title": "Eight trophies",
  "quest.039C50EEE3A8B7EC.quest_subtitle": "The wall of shame, theirs.",
  "quest.039C50EEE3A8B7EC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"One per boss. Right-click one, or power it with redstone, and it makes its boss's sound; you can also wear it as a hat. Any of them wakes the \"},{\"text\":\"Trophy Pedestal\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"4698EBAFF4445D37\"}},{\"text\":\".\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Crafting a trophy with paper makes a banner pattern, but it uses the trophy up.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3E8731CF585FE49B.title": "Unlocks are personal",
  "quest.3E8731CF585FE49B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Biome and tower locks check each player. Whoever missed a fight catches up by holding its trophy; a Naga Scale, a scepter or Alpha Yeti Fur also count, and each player eats their own stroganoff.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.74502BCE49B10400.title": "Nine locked biomes",
  "quest.74502BCE49B10400.quest_desc": [
    "Walk into a biome you haven't earned and a Biome Locked! warning pops up while its curse works on you. Locked landmarks can't be dug into, built on or fought in: try, and a shield box flashes up around them.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Swamp, Dark Forest, Snowy Forest: the Lich. Fire Swamp: the Minoshroom's stroganoff. Dark Forest Center: the Knight Phantoms. Glacier: the Alpha Yeti. Highlands: Hydra, Ur-Ghast and Snow Queen. Thornlands and Final Plateau: the Lamp of Cinders."
  ],
  "quest.7DB66B6FB9B0FC8E.title": "The explorer's notebook",
  "quest.7DB66B6FB9B0FC8E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Poke around a locked landmark and a Kobold turns up clutching an explorer's notebook. Kill it for the book: it hints at what feeds the curse.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6139B043AA702225.title": "By our powers combined",
  "quest.6139B043AA702225.quest_subtitle": "Collect them all. Somebody had to.",
  "quest.6139B043AA702225.quest_desc": [
    "All four scepters in one pack: Twilight, Life Draining, Zombie and Fortification. Each Lich drops one, so this took a few Liches."
  ],
  "reward.01AA80D8C43BC674.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.304944F7499F48EF.title": "Recharging scepters",
  "quest.304944F7499F48EF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Craft a spent scepter with its fuel: ender pearls for Twilight, fermented spider eyes for Life Draining, rotten flesh with a strength potion for Zombie, golden apples for Fortification. \"},{\"text\":\"Exanimate Essence\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:exanimate_essence\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" fills any scepter.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3E8DB96DD09A1F3A.title": "Mystic Crown",
  "quest.3E8DB96DD09A1F3A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight \"},{\"text\":\"Crown Splinters\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:crown_splinter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" from the Lich Tower's chests, in a ring. Worn, it strengthens your scepters a little; a book with Renewal, from the tower library, lets them refill themselves from your inventory.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2F0B1CBA95DC7814.title": "Potion flasks",
  "quest.2F0B1CBA95DC7814.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The tower's potion rooms stock \"},{\"text\":\"Brittle Potion Flasks\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:brittle_potion_flask\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": several doses of one potion in a single slot, until the glass gives out. The rare Greater Potion Flask never breaks.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7B4A5EA85E4210E0.title": "Full mettle",
  "quest.7B4A5EA85E4210E0.quest_subtitle": "Do not try this at home. Or anywhere.",
  "quest.7B4A5EA85E4210E0.quest_desc": [
    "Three doses of Harming II from a flask inside six seconds, and you're still standing. The flask has concerns about you."
  ],
  "reward.4BF9B586ADA6F4B0.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.043A26821E611B21.title": "Keepsake Casket",
  "quest.043A26821E611B21.quest_subtitle": "Pack light. Die heavy.",
  "quest.043A26821E611B21.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A room in the Lich Tower keeps one. Carry it and, when you die, it sets itself down holding everything you had. It wears out with use; the \"},{\"text\":\"Tombstone chapter\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"66656B710E644D7B\"}},{\"text\":\" covers the rest.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7FC4E052AE4B63B7.title": "Light in a jar",
  "quest.7FC4E052AE4B63B7.quest_subtitle": "Mood lighting, literally.",
  "quest.7FC4E052AE4B63B7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Glass and a Twilight Oak log make four \"},{\"text\":\"Mason Jars\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:mason_jar\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; a jar and a \"},{\"text\":\"Firefly\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:firefly\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make a living lamp. Fireflies cling to tree trunks, and in here it's always dusk.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Monsters here spawn at block light up to 7, not only in the dark: light your camp twice as densely. Beds work; respawn anchors don't.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5FF0EB53D58A8B39.title": "Moonworm Queen",
  "quest.5FF0EB53D58A8B39.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Found in large hollow hills and Lich Tower rooms, it shoots glowing moonworms that stick to walls as lights. \"},{\"text\":\"Torchberries\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:torchberries\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" repair it, 64 uses each.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1AA7DD193A8A3DE3.title": "Shh",
  "quest.1AA7DD193A8A3DE3.quest_subtitle": "Blessed silence.",
  "quest.1AA7DD193A8A3DE3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"You killed a \"},{\"text\":\"Cicada\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:cicada\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". The forest is quieter by exactly one insect.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.6FA7CA514A22BBC7.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.1B8963062DD20278.title": "The Hedge Maze",
  "quest.1B8963062DD20278.quest_desc": [
    "Walls of hedge, hedge spiders, swarm spiders and a few chests. Kill a spider in there; the chests carry string, food and, now and then, a diamond."
  ],
  "quest.24460174056CB15A.title": "The Questing Ram",
  "quest.24460174056CB15A.quest_subtitle": "Ewe complete me.",
  "quest.24460174056CB15A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A rainbow ram in a Quest Grove wants wool in the colours it's missing, and a dropper nearby holds a few. Complete its coat for a \"},{\"text\":\"Crumble Horn\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:crumble_horn\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", its trophy and a bundle of mineral blocks.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6C9DF6F4657630F5.title": "Magic saplings",
  "quest.6C9DF6F4657630F5.quest_desc": [
    "Hollow oak trees hide small rooms in their leaves, and those chests sometimes hold a magic sapling. Each grows a tree around a core: Time speeds up crops, Transformation turns the land into Enchanted Forest, the Miner's pulls ore up, Sorting sorts chests.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A core only works where its tree grew: break it and you get a plain log. Magic leaves drop no saplings, so each one counts.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.514F42EDF180AD10.title": "Dinner at eternal sundown",
  "quest.514F42EDF180AD10.quest_desc": [
    "One of everything the forest serves: venison, meef, Meef Stroganoff, a Hydra Chop, a Maze Wafer, Experiment 115, any jerky, berries, a slime drop, Berry Medley and Moss Soup. This pack rewards a varied diet."
  ],
  "quest.55D0B07C36817F68.title": "Hollow Hills",
  "quest.55D0B07C36817F68.quest_subtitle": "Not so hollow, as it turns out.",
  "quest.55D0B07C36817F68.quest_desc": [
    "Mounds in the forest are caves inside: stalactites of stone and ore, chests, and Redcaps that light TNT. Beat a Redcap inside a small one."
  ],
  "quest.31B921BAF6D1B5ED.title": "Bigger hills, better loot",
  "quest.31B921BAF6D1B5ED.quest_desc": [
    "Medium hills add Redcap Sappers; large ones add Wraiths, and diamond, emerald and lapis to the stalactites. Their chests can hold an Uncrafting Table, a Magic Map or a Moonworm Queen."
  ],
  "quest.6E6F66D22337899A.title": "Ore Magnet",
  "quest.6E6F66D22337899A.quest_desc": [
    "Aim it at rock and use it: it drags the nearest ore vein out to you. Hollow hill chests carry it, and it saves a lot of digging."
  ],
  "quest.4E7EC7E237F86655.title": "Ore Meter",
  "quest.4E7EC7E237F86655.quest_desc": [
    "Switched on, it lists every ore in range with counts and ratios; sneak-click a block to count only that one. It turns up in small hollow hills."
  ],
  "quest.4A3DFDF2F4D70AE2.title": "Transformation Powder",
  "quest.4A3DFDF2F4D70AE2.quest_desc": [
    "Sprinkle it on a creature to swap it for its Twilight cousin: cow to deer, pig to boar, bat to raven. Some work backwards too.",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A silverfish turns into a Towerwood Borer, which drops the essence for \"},{\"text\":\"Carminite\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"4B472ABB4E1D0B01\"}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4300F63962E5C022.title": "Steeleaf",
  "quest.4300F63962E5C022.quest_desc": [
    "It can't be crafted: hollow hills, the Labyrinth, the Knight Stronghold and the Dark Tower keep it in chests. Its tools come enchanted from the table, the pickaxe with Fortune II and the sword with Looting II.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The armor comes enchanted too: Projectile, Blast and Fire Protection II, and Feather Falling II on the boots.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.258FDDFEE1E8F9DE.title": "Charms of Life and Keeping",
  "quest.258FDDFEE1E8F9DE.quest_desc": [
    "A Charm of Life saves you from one fatal blow and is used up. A Charm of Keeping hands back part of your inventory after death; four of one tier make the next, up to Keeping III."
  ],
  "quest.53ED9695118C9F68.title": "Peacock Feather Fan",
  "quest.53ED9695118C9F68.quest_subtitle": "Stylish and aerodynamic.",
  "quest.53ED9695118C9F68.quest_desc": [
    "One wave pushes mobs away; wave it while jumping and you go up instead. It pairs well with an elytra, and it snuffs out candles."
  ],
  "quest.7A964152B947BDAF.title": "Ironwood",
  "quest.7A964152B947BDAF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Liveroot\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:liveroot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" grows among the roots under most trees. Craft it with raw iron and a gold nugget for two Raw Ironwood, then smelt: \"},{\"text\":\"Ironwood Ingots\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:ironwood_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"It's the pack's act IV material: over a dozen machines from other mods ask for it, and the Atlas asks for \"},{\"text\":\"two\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"63A78566481EFF47\"}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.138D86C2F19F6F21.title": "Ironwood armor",
  "quest.138D86C2F19F6F21.quest_desc": [
    "Ironwood gear comes enchanted from the table: Protection I on chest and legs, Aqua Affinity on the helmet, Feather Falling I on the boots. The tools too, like an Efficiency I pickaxe and a Fortune I axe."
  ],
  "quest.0D0572B4D28B6FDB.title": "Roots for the common store",
  "quest.0D0572B4D28B6FDB.quest_subtitle": "Dig deep, share deeper.",
  "quest.0D0572B4D28B6FDB.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Sixteen \"},{\"text\":\"Liveroot\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:liveroot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for the common store, once a day. A Fortune tool gets more out of each block.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6EFB8DDF44376135.title": "Torchberries",
  "quest.6EFB8DDF44376135.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"They hang glowing from cave ceilings and roots. One berry on a stick makes five torches, and it's a third of a \"},{\"text\":\"Magic Map Focus\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:magic_map_focus\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0C4CE938F64896BA.title": "The Magic Map",
  "quest.0C4CE938F64896BA.quest_subtitle": "You are here. So is everything else.",
  "quest.0C4CE938F64896BA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Raven Feather\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:raven_feather\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", \"},{\"text\":\"Torchberries\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:torchberries\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and glowstone dust make the focus; paper around it, a blank map. Use it in the forest and it charts biomes and landmarks, each boss's lair marked with its face.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"It only works in the Twilight Forest. Ravens drop the feathers, and Lich Tower chests keep a few.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2F31C4287AA428C1.title": "The Uncrafting Table",
  "quest.2F31C4287AA428C1.quest_subtitle": "Crafting, in reverse gear.",
  "quest.2F31C4287AA428C1.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"It turns crafted items back into ingredients for experience, repairs gear, recrafts items into others and moves enchantments between pieces. Eight crafting tables around a \"},{\"text\":\"Maze Map Focus\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"00395A19070A1E8F\"}},{\"text\":\", or find one in medium hollow hills and graveyards.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.15B64384FC64738C.title": "Uncrafting rules",
  "quest.15B64384FC64738C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Only shaped recipes come apart. It never hands back magic saplings or Transformation Powder: those parts are lost. It's also the only source of Wrought Iron Bars, from the wrought iron blocks you find.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1E0EF707C3D1B2DC.title": "A step too far",
  "quest.1E0EF707C3D1B2DC.quest_subtitle": "Recursion, table edition.",
  "quest.1E0EF707C3D1B2DC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"You uncrafted an \"},{\"text\":\"Uncrafting Table\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:uncrafting_table\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" with an Uncrafting Table. Eight crafting tables and a focus fall out, along with some doubts.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.7F91F09F91A11987.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.5BCE6765F2A6F7C5.title": "Tanned leather",
  "quest.5BCE6765F2A6F7C5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Tannin\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:tannin\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" is a water bottle, a Twilight Oak sapling, root strands and Twilight Oak leaves. With leather it makes \"},{\"text\":\"Treated Leather\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:treated_leather\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; hang that on a drying rack, three slabs in a row, for five minutes.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The rack also dries meat into jerky, kelp into dried kelp and mud back into clay.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.396813E5E068791C.title": "Traveller's gear",
  "quest.396813E5E068791C.quest_subtitle": "Dressed for the long way round.",
  "quest.396813E5E068791C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Tanned leather becomes goggles, a vest, a belt, boots and gloves; the wings also take gold, copper and \"},{\"text\":\"Carminite\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"4B472ABB4E1D0B01\"}},{\"text\":\". Each piece brings one built-in ability; the gloves are just for looks.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.345A569F27F5AD76.title": "Modifiers",
  "quest.345A569F27F5AD76.quest_desc": [
    "Up to three more abilities per piece, each crafted around it: moss and experience bottles give Auto-Repair; others add double jump, gliding, water walking, a dash or dodging projectiles."
  ],
  "quest.3033F575F02DE540.title": "Traveller's Wings",
  "quest.3033F575F02DE540.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Gold, copper, tanned leather and \"},{\"text\":\"Carminite\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"4B472ABB4E1D0B01\"}},{\"text\":\". They take the gliding, double-jump and dash modifiers, the closest the forest gets to flying.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7C5915F88661C5A1.title": "Two hotbars",
  "quest.7C5915F88661C5A1.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Traveller's Belt\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:travellers_belt\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" keeps a second hotbar: \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.twilightforest.swap_hotbar\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" swaps it with yours.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.77638E94F87539A7.title": "Poultry justice",
  "quest.77638E94F87539A7.quest_subtitle": "Nobody saw anything.",
  "quest.77638E94F87539A7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"You finished off a baby zombie riding a chicken while holding \"},{\"text\":\"Chicken Jerky\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"twilightforest:chicken_jerky\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". The chicken's view on the matter was not recorded.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.46656B0AE9A70D56.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.0D69862767E638BA.title": "House rules",
  "quest.0D69862767E638BA.quest_desc": [
    "Carry On won't lift Twilight bosses or their spawners. Bosses don't scale up for more players, so bringing the team makes a fight easier. The Heliodor Compass needle turns green when its target is in here."
  ],
  "image.392C18C1741F22C2.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Hollow Hills\",\"color\":\"#D6E77A\"}]",
  "image.2D710BEBBD8B05E1.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Around the forest\",\"color\":\"#D6E77A\"}]",
  "image.21D1CA1E6B445B44.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Night lights\",\"color\":\"#D6E77A\"}]",
  "image.0DF27D0A559089D5.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Uncrafting\",\"color\":\"#D6E77A\"}]",
  "image.5A593068A7861B9C.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Traveller's gear\",\"color\":\"#D6E77A\"}]",
  "image.4AEC8A9224EE6C98.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Lich Tower loot\",\"color\":\"#D6E77A\"}]",
  "image.011FE471A924BCEE.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Maze maps\",\"color\":\"#D6E77A\"}]",
  "image.32A265CB7AC078A0.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Fiery gear\",\"color\":\"#D6E77A\"}]",
  "image.277141666270765A.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Knightmetal\",\"color\":\"#D6E77A\"}]",
  "image.7719931313A47E4A.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Tower tech\",\"color\":\"#D6E77A\"}]",
  "image.29EDFDF52476FE32.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Furs\",\"color\":\"#D6E77A\"}]",
  "image.0802FFADF616EB1C.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Twilight Forest\",\"color\":\"#D6E77A\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.1F994CAA82BEA4E4.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"where the light never arrives\",\"color\":\"#D6E77A\",\"font\":\"minecraft:alt\"}]",
  "image.1B480A4C4B835E81.title": "Back to the Sun of Heliodor",
  "image.565825EF58AEE983.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Twilight Swamp\",\"color\":\"#D6E77A\"}]",
  "image.136EB4F730CF3DA6.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Snowy Forest\",\"color\":\"#D6E77A\"}]",
  "image.3DC690EB0730220F.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Highlands\",\"color\":\"#D6E77A\"}]",
  "chapter.414AD5669711F386.title": "The Undergarden",
  "chapter.414AD5669711F386.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Six metals, one Guardian and a plague, below a stone-brick portal."
  ],
  "quest.1BD7823BF183F956.title": "The Catalyst",
  "quest.1BD7823BF183F956.quest_subtitle": "A ticket that never gets punched.",
  "quest.1BD7823BF183F956.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four copper ingots in the corners, three stones on the sides and bottom, an ender pearl in the middle and, in this pack, a \"},{\"text\":\"Routing Matrix\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:routing_matrix\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" top center. The \"},{\"text\":\"Catalyst\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"undergarden:catalyst\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" lights a stone-brick portal and is never used up.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.56473A0DAA1097B3.title": "A door of stone bricks",
  "quest.56473A0DAA1097B3.quest_desc": [
    "Build a frame like a Nether portal's from stone bricks, deepslate bricks or tiles, polished deepslate or the Undergarden's own bricks, then use the Catalyst on the inside. It only lights in the Overworld and in the Undergarden.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "You arrive in the dark: no sky, always midnight, though beds still work. The portal home is built of stone bricks."
  ],
  "quest.1466A6848DB8FD1C.title": "Six bricks will do",
  "quest.1466A6848DB8FD1C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The opening can be as small as one block wide and two tall, and the corners are optional: six bricks make a working portal. The largest opening is 21 by 21.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6EA3A9A4DC2B60C3.title": "One block down, four up",
  "quest.6EA3A9A4DC2B60C3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Undergarden distances count four times over: walk 100 blocks down here and a portal home comes out about 400 blocks from where you left. With Create, trains cross this portal like a \"},{\"text\":\"Nether one\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"0E63E76DEBBC6A9C\"}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6D7F3B5108B92223.title": "House rules",
  "quest.6D7F3B5108B92223.quest_desc": [
    "The Catalyst takes a Routing Matrix, so the way down opens in act III, and no story step or Heliodor Compass target waits here. Malum's spirit repairs for Undergarden gear don't load in 1.21.1 and are switched off: mend it at an anvil."
  ],
  "quest.64BB6C9B5B694154.title": "Cloggrum, the local iron",
  "quest.64BB6C9B5B694154.quest_subtitle": "Brown, lumpy, reliable.",
  "quest.64BB6C9B5B694154.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Cloggrum ore turns up in Depthrock and Shiverstone all over the cavern, and a stone pickaxe is enough. Smelt the \"},{\"text\":\"Raw Cloggrum\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"undergarden:raw_cloggrum\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" into ingots: down here it does the job iron does up top.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.08116F2B51A7FD13.title": "Cloggrum tools",
  "quest.08116F2B51A7FD13.quest_subtitle": "Iron's tier, a little tougher.",
  "quest.08116F2B51A7FD13.quest_desc": [
    "Cloggrum tools mine like iron and last a bit longer, 286 uses to iron's 250, and the sword hits one point harder. Keep the pickaxe: the Forgotten upgrade turns it into the tool that breaks Dreadrock."
  ],
  "quest.40EB69CE87614288.title": "A full suit of Cloggrum",
  "quest.40EB69CE87614288.quest_subtitle": "Fashionably brown.",
  "quest.40EB69CE87614288.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The set gives 14 armor, one short of iron, but every piece adds a point of toughness. The \"},{\"text\":\"Cloggrum Boots\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"undergarden:cloggrum_boots\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" are the reason to wear it: Scintling goo stops slowing you down.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5AD8C4922B6EE917.title": "Depthrock is cobblestone",
  "quest.5AD8C4922B6EE917.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Depthrock and Shiverstone count as stone for stone tools and furnaces, so a broken pickaxe is never a problem. Nine Depthrock Pebbles make a block, and three Depthrock under an iron ingot make a stonecutter.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0244990CBBDEA01A.title": "Where the ores are",
  "quest.0244990CBBDEA01A.quest_desc": [
    "Cloggrum everywhere; Froststeel only in Shiverstone, in the cold biomes; Utherium from the bottom up to Y 32, often sealed inside the rock; Regalium between Y 0 and 12. The Dreadrock floor starts below Y 5, and Rogdorium waits under it, in the Depths."
  ],
  "quest.1E70F7E6847B82D3.title": "Bucket, shield and lantern",
  "quest.1E70F7E6847B82D3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Cloggrum Bucket\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"undergarden:cloggrum_bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" carries any fluid, powder snow or a fish, and empty ones stack to 16. The \"},{\"text\":\"Cloggrum Shield\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"undergarden:cloggrum_shield\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" blocks like any shield, and eight nuggets around a torch make a \"},{\"text\":\"Cloggrum Lantern\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"undergarden:cloggrum_lantern\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "task.2CBBF112058FEEB8.title": "Watch a Gloomper",
  "task.5F10F355170C0D85.title": "Watch a Dweller",
  "task.7096A5C8B82294E9.title": "Watch a Mog",
  "task.322E5D972C6C8AC5.title": "Watch a Brute",
  "task.3D4EFB9D5CFC6A8B.title": "Watch a Scintling",
  "quest.68C302C8CB5FA6FF.title": "A census of the cavern",
  "quest.68C302C8CB5FA6FF.quest_subtitle": "Most of them won't bite. Most.",
  "quest.68C302C8CB5FA6FF.quest_desc": [
    "Look at each of the calm locals for a moment. Gloompers eat gloomgourds and now and then let off a Virulence cloud when hit; Dwellers take a saddle; Mogs can be sheared; Brutes stand up for each other; Scintlings leave slime trails."
  ],
  "quest.68BCE53F9961E317.title": "Ride a Dweller",
  "quest.68BCE53F9961E317.quest_subtitle": "It jumps. You don't get hurt.",
  "quest.68BCE53F9961E317.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Saddle a Dweller and steer it with an \"},{\"text\":\"Underbean on a Stick\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"undergarden:underbean_on_a_stick\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", like a pig with a carrot. It clears blocks in a hop, and you take no fall damage while riding. Underbeans breed them.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3FE3B1A1A842FEA1.title": "A bed of stone and moss",
  "quest.3FE3B1A1A842FEA1.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Shear a Mog for \"},{\"text\":\"Mogmoss\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"undergarden:mogmoss\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; Depthrock Pebbles lure and breed them. Three moss over three Depthrock make a \"},{\"text\":\"Depthrock Bed\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"undergarden:depthrock_bed\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a respawn point that matches the decor.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4E45A4DCDED96ABA.title": "Weird fish",
  "quest.4E45A4DCDED96ABA.quest_desc": [
    "Gwiblings school in the Ancient and Icy Seas; a bucket brings one home. Their big cousins, the Gwibs, only bite while you're in the water, so fish from the shore."
  ],
  "quest.6710158F9F179E4B.title": "Terrible person",
  "quest.6710158F9F179E4B.quest_subtitle": "It had one heart. Literally.",
  "quest.6710158F9F179E4B.quest_desc": [
    "You killed a Scintling. It had one heart, left a slime trail and bothered nobody. The Goo Balls it dropped are slingshot ammo, if that helps."
  ],
  "reward.5FB09AAFF42BFAAB.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.77C84B8CF84BD02E.title": "Forgotten Vestiges",
  "quest.77C84B8CF84BD02E.quest_desc": [
    "Ruined Depthrock and Shiverstone houses, arches and aqueducts across the forests and the cold. Break the Depthrock Pots inside for pebbles, food, nuggets, Regalium and now and then a diamond, and hit any pot that wiggles."
  ],
  "task.780C177527379F52.title": "Catch a Mysterious Pot",
  "quest.0C20FF67A5EFFABC.title": "The pot with legs",
  "quest.0C20FF67A5EFFABC.quest_subtitle": "Plot twist: it runs.",
  "quest.0C20FF67A5EFFABC.quest_desc": [
    "You caught a Mysterious Pot. Hit one and it sprouts legs and bolts; swords, axes and pickaxes deal it double damage. It carried nuggets, Regalium and maybe a Mammoth or Relict disc."
  ],
  "reward.0ABD4FE71E1EDA46.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.6F9634CD107335CC.title": "Underbeans",
  "quest.6F9634CD107335CC.quest_subtitle": "Glorious beans, the game insists.",
  "quest.6F9634CD107335CC.quest_desc": [
    "Underbean bushes grow in the forests and fields. Eat the beans raw, fast, or roast them in a furnace or on a campfire for double the food; Dwellers and Greater Dwellers follow anyone holding them."
  ],
  "quest.267E273CAA53AD0E.title": "Gloomgourds",
  "quest.267E273CAA53AD0E.quest_subtitle": "Purple pumpkins, for once not a metaphor.",
  "quest.267E273CAA53AD0E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Plant the seeds like pumpkins; shears carve a gourd and hand back four seeds. A mushroom, a Gloomgourd and Glitterkelp bake a \"},{\"text\":\"Gloomgourd Pie\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"undergarden:gloomgourd_pie\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": 8 food and 30 seconds of Virulent Resistance.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7E90C8D6521EC5E2.title": "Not a pumpkin",
  "quest.7E90C8D6521EC5E2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A Carved Gloomgourd on your head does the opposite of a pumpkin: look at one enderman and every enderman within 64 blocks that can see you comes for you. Put it on a block of Forgotten metal instead.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.650A9BB0D5D5247B.title": "Gourd lord",
  "quest.650A9BB0D5D5247B.quest_subtitle": "All hail.",
  "quest.650A9BB0D5D5247B.quest_desc": [
    "Sixty-four Gloomgourds in one stack. Gloompers are lured and bred with them, so right now a whole herd would follow you anywhere."
  ],
  "reward.530790E08A8BDCA1.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.4D3E59665BB1AD64.title": "Four mushroom stews",
  "quest.4D3E59665BB1AD64.quest_desc": [
    "Three of one mushroom in a bowl, and every stew is a 30-second trade: Bloody gives Strength with Brittleness, Inky Resistance with Blindness, Indigo Night Vision with Slowness, Veiled Slow Falling with Featherweight."
  ],
  "quest.4B9D0CD2FB63AD8E.title": "Undergarden brews",
  "quest.4B9D0CD2FB63AD8E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Into an Awkward Potion: a \"},{\"text\":\"Blood Globule\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"undergarden:blood_globule\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" brews Brittleness, a Veiled Mushroom Featherweight, Droopfruit Glowing and a Gloomgourd Virulent Resistance. Redstone lengthens them; glowstone strengthens the first two.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Brittleness punishes armor: each hit adds the effect's level, plus two for every four armor points the target wears. Blood Globules burst from engorged Blood Mushroom caps.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.089B8B06663552DB.title": "Dyes from the dark",
  "quest.089B8B06663552DB.quest_desc": [
    "Seven local plants craft straight into dye: Ink Mushroom black, Indigo blue, Blood red, Veiled white, Amorous Bristle pink, Butterbunch yellow and Miserabell light blue.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The Ink Mushroom is the only plant in the pack that crafts into black dye, which is why the \"},{\"text\":\"Altar of Renewal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:renewal_altar\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" grows huge ones.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2BEF042651071A38.title": "Ditchbulb paste",
  "quest.2BEF042651071A38.quest_desc": [
    "Ditchbulbs grow in most biomes down here. Their paste lights fires, campfires and candles like flint and steel, one dab per use, and with a stick it makes two torches: light without coal."
  ],
  "quest.1EF964F39F27AEC6.title": "The Rotspawn",
  "quest.1EF964F39F27AEC6.quest_subtitle": "The locals nobody invited.",
  "quest.1EF964F39F27AEC6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Rotlings, Rotwalkers, Rotbelchers and Rotbeasts: the local plague, from 10 health to 80. Every hit they land feeds the \"},{\"text\":\"Utheric Infection\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"31925B8BBF81F6AE\"}},{\"text\":\", and they drop Utheric Shards when you finish them.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.31925B8BBF81F6AE.title": "Utheric Infection",
  "quest.31925B8BBF81F6AE.quest_subtitle": "The meter you don't want to fill.",
  "quest.31925B8BBF81F6AE.quest_desc": [
    "Rotspawn hits and the air of the Depths fill an infection meter up to 20. Below that it only warns you; at 20 it hurts every second, a little more each time. Away from the Depths it drains one point every 20 seconds.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Rotbeast adds almost two points per hit, and the Infected Depths fill the meter in under three minutes.\",\"color\":\"#FF8C7A\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7116837FE8E9BEAD.title": "All four kinds of rot",
  "quest.7116837FE8E9BEAD.quest_desc": [
    "Put down one of each. The Rotbelcher spits from range, so close in fast; the Rotbeast has 80 health and hits for 10, but a Shard Torch sends even it running."
  ],
  "quest.7A5577FC60DD8C3A.title": "Shard Torches",
  "quest.7A5577FC60DD8C3A.quest_subtitle": "Rot repellent, in stick form.",
  "quest.7A5577FC60DD8C3A.quest_desc": [
    "A Utheric Shard on a stick. Once a second it zaps every Rotspawn within four blocks for 4 damage and sends it running, and it never touches you. Ring your camp with them."
  ],
  "quest.1EBAD5995D345598.title": "Warped fungus by the door",
  "quest.1EBAD5995D345598.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Rotspawn flee what hoglins flee: warped fungus, potted or not, a respawn anchor or a Nether portal within 16 blocks. A potted warped fungus by the door is the cheapest guard you'll ever hire.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0E5B5DAF54406675.title": "Shards for the common store",
  "quest.0E5B5DAF54406675.quest_subtitle": "Every shard is one Rotspawn fewer.",
  "quest.0E5B5DAF54406675.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Sixteen \"},{\"text\":\"Utheric Shards\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"undergarden:utheric_shard\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for the common store, once a day. A Rotbeast drops up to eight, and Looting adds more.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.201A8D2DE391BF18.title": "Cold country",
  "quest.201A8D2DE391BF18.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Frostfields, the frosty Smogstem forests and the Icy Sea sit on Shiverstone, and only there does Froststeel ore grow. A \"},{\"text\":\"Nature's Compass\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"1595C7F7FF1FE7A5\"}},{\"text\":\" finds them.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2BCA276FF34515F9.title": "Froststeel",
  "quest.2BCA276FF34515F9.quest_subtitle": "Cold, and it shares.",
  "quest.2BCA276FF34515F9.quest_desc": [
    "Froststeel tools mine like iron, faster and with 575 uses. Whatever they hit turns Chilly for 30 seconds: 45% slower from a sword or axe, 30% slower from a pickaxe or shovel."
  ],
  "quest.7CBD631CC072C48F.title": "Froststeel armor",
  "quest.7CBD631CC072C48F.quest_subtitle": "Heavy on purpose.",
  "quest.7CBD631CC072C48F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"18 armor and 4 toughness per piece, more toughness than netherite, but each piece slows you by 5%. The \"},{\"text\":\"Froststeel Boots\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"undergarden:froststeel_boots\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" walk on powder snow.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0E7BEC7B420B7310.title": "Three woods and a twig",
  "quest.0E7BEC7B420B7310.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Smogstem, Wigglewood and Grongle each make a full wood set and a boat. Two Wigglewood planks make four \"},{\"text\":\"Twistytwigs\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"undergarden:twistytwig\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", the string of the Undergarden: slingshots, leads, scaffolding and bombs.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5243B599FDF23D62.title": "The Slingshot",
  "quest.5243B599FDF23D62.quest_subtitle": "Your new best friend, says the game.",
  "quest.5243B599FDF23D62.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Six sticks around a Twistytwig. It fires \"},{\"text\":\"Depthrock Pebbles\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"undergarden:depthrock_pebble\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", which Mogs, Stoneborn and Sploogies drop, and a pebble hits harder the longer it flies.\"}]",
    "",
    "It also takes Goo Balls, Rotten Blisterberries and Gronglets, each with its own trick."
  ],
  "quest.5318F48B18D03606.title": "Sticky situation",
  "quest.5318F48B18D03606.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Scintling Goo Ball\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"undergarden:goo_ball\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" does no damage: it leaves the target Gooey for five seconds, laying goo under its feet, and it heals Scintlings. Just the thing to slow a Rotwalker to a crawl.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0ED530FAA915175E.title": "Slingshot enchantments",
  "quest.0ED530FAA915175E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Longevity doubles, triples or quadruples its 192 uses. Ricochet bounces shots off walls, and Self Sling fires you instead, as long as you stand on the ground; those two can't share a slingshot.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6A0415C6389D8F84.title": "Sniping's a good job",
  "quest.6A0415C6389D8F84.quest_subtitle": "Mate.",
  "quest.6A0415C6389D8F84.quest_desc": [
    "One pebble, 20 damage. Pebbles hit harder the longer they fly, so a long, high arc turns a rock into artillery."
  ],
  "reward.733A8F89E2D211CF.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.3B1350351B3ED7FB.title": "Gronglets",
  "quest.3B1350351B3ED7FB.quest_subtitle": "Tiny, glowing, emphatically not food.",
  "quest.3B1350351B3ED7FB.quest_desc": [
    "Little glowing critters that cling to Grongle trunks in the Gronglegrowth. Placed, they shine at light level 12 on any surface, and they double as a hat.",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eating one gives you Wither X for a minute.\",\"color\":\"#FF8C7A\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0C4D82D0ADD9083C.title": "Ethically questionable",
  "quest.0C4D82D0ADD9083C.quest_subtitle": "It chirps when it lands. Probably fine.",
  "quest.0C4D82D0ADD9083C.quest_desc": [
    "You loaded a Gronglet into a slingshot and fired it. It sticks where it lands and keeps glowing, and on a friend without a helmet it lands on their head."
  ],
  "reward.3383E3FFC3F78B74.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.52B6019D84E9B5C4.title": "Blisterbombs",
  "quest.52B6019D84E9B5C4.quest_subtitle": "Handle with gloves.",
  "quest.52B6019D84E9B5C4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Twistytwig over six Rotten Blisterberries makes a \"},{\"text\":\"Blisterbomb\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"undergarden:blisterbomb\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a throwable that blasts nearly as hard as TNT and breaks blocks. The berry bushes of the Smog Spires prick whoever walks through them.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6BB399C3FF57D954.title": "Berries that go bang",
  "quest.6BB399C3FF57D954.quest_desc": [
    "A Rotten Blisterberry fired from the slingshot bursts in a small explosion where it lands, without breaking blocks. Keep your distance: the blast doesn't care who fired it."
  ],
  "quest.2B1021F37B868331.title": "Boomgourd",
  "quest.2B1021F37B868331.quest_subtitle": "Carved with a grin, lit with a fuse.",
  "quest.2B1021F37B868331.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight Blisterbombs around a Gloomgourd make a \"},{\"text\":\"Boomgourd\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"undergarden:boomgourd\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", the Undergarden's TNT: set it alight or catch it in a blast, and four seconds later it goes off as hard as TNT.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.6F84AE95B76CD316.title": "Defeat a Muncher",
  "task.63D0B3B819C914F0.title": "Defeat a Nargoyle",
  "task.3005F3CD0A2A2BE7.title": "Defeat a Sploogie",
  "quest.1FD53EE39E10EDE3.title": "What lives in the walls",
  "quest.1FD53EE39E10EDE3.quest_subtitle": "Something is chewing. It isn't you.",
  "quest.1FD53EE39E10EDE3.quest_desc": [
    "Below Y 24, in the dark, the caves grow their own hunters. Nargoyles leap at you, Sploogies spit from a distance, and Munchers chew straight through stone to reach you, healing with every bite. Munchers drop Cloggrum and Froststeel nuggets."
  ],
  "quest.5C513BE32F443B45.title": "One torch is enough",
  "quest.5C513BE32F443B45.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Rotspawn and the cave hunters only spawn in total darkness down here: any block light at all stops them. The Forgotten and the Denizens don't care about light.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.71CD26528152288B.title": "Clusters for later",
  "quest.71CD26528152288B.quest_subtitle": "Red, shiny and useless. For now.",
  "quest.71CD26528152288B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Utherium ore drops \"},{\"text\":\"Utheric Clusters\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"undergarden:utheric_cluster\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", not crystals, and smelting the ore gives a cluster too; nine Utheric Shards also make one. Hoard them: only the Infuser, far below, purifies a cluster into Utherium.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6F7AC76712295A12.title": "Regalium",
  "quest.6F7AC76712295A12.quest_subtitle": "The only thing down here with a price tag.",
  "quest.6F7AC76712295A12.quest_desc": [
    "A gold crystal from Depthrock and Shiverstone between Y 0 and 12, in small veins, for an iron or Cloggrum pickaxe. It crafts into nothing but its block: its worth is that the Stoneborn take it as money."
  ],
  "quest.3CD69E20DBB6D319.title": "Business with the Stoneborn",
  "quest.3CD69E20DBB6D319.quest_subtitle": "Interdimensional, apparently.",
  "quest.3CD69E20DBB6D319.quest_desc": [
    "Tall stone folk of the forests, neutral until hit. Each offers four of eleven deals in Regalium: they buy iron at 4 crystals, gold at only 2, a diamond at 12 and a Block of Utherium at 48, and sell seeds, Shard Torches, Blisterbombs and discs."
  ],
  "task.482059EEA6FE7070.title": "Gloomper Anthem",
  "task.5C4EAA72C0AAC01E.title": "Limax Maximus",
  "task.19D7EC6E8D58D35C.title": "Mammoth",
  "task.3C3487081D5B283A.title": "Relict",
  "quest.222F9463D97DB4EF.title": "Four records by Screem",
  "quest.222F9463D97DB4EF.quest_desc": [
    "Gloomper Anthem and Limax Maximus cost 32 Regalium each at a Stoneborn. Mammoth and Relict come from Mysterious Pots, and a Stoneborn pays 32 Regalium for either: a record collection that pays for itself."
  ],
  "quest.0BA532B38B8EB832.title": "Six metals for a beacon",
  "quest.0BA532B38B8EB832.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Cloggrum, Froststeel, Utherium, Regalium, Rogdorium and Forgotten metal all pay a beacon, and their blocks, all but Rogdorium's, build its base. Five of them also trim armor.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1D2937A709407866.title": "Stoneborn stay home",
  "quest.1D2937A709407866.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Take a Stoneborn out of the Undergarden and it gets dizzy, then chants and explodes after 15 seconds. They only trade down here anyway.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7F610543B4FC037F.title": "Play it for a Gloomper",
  "quest.7F610543B4FC037F.quest_subtitle": "It was their anthem. It was too much.",
  "quest.7F610543B4FC037F.quest_desc": [
    "You played the Gloomper Anthem at a Gloomper, in the most direct way possible, and it did not survive the honor. It left the secret disc behind."
  ],
  "reward.21FC1A8E1E85F0A0.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.2E81A1F973314EFF.title": "The Catacombs",
  "quest.2E81A1F973314EFF.quest_desc": [
    "Depthrock-brick halls in the forests, the fields and by the Ancient Sea, patrolled by the Forgotten. Their chests hold nuggets, Utheric Shards, Regalium and, in about one chest out of four, the Forgotten upgrade template."
  ],
  "quest.64592C426FE2BB43.title": "Cold dead hands",
  "quest.64592C426FE2BB43.quest_subtitle": "Finders keepers.",
  "quest.64592C426FE2BB43.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"One Forgotten in fifty spawns with a \"},{\"text\":\"Cloggrum Battleaxe\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"undergarden:cloggrum_battleaxe\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and Ancient armor, and that axe always drops. It hits harder and slower than a sword and knocks back hard.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.04CD836CE9BBF88F.title": "Defeat the Forgotten Guardian",
  "quest.43D1DB8A024E10C7.title": "The Forgotten Guardian",
  "quest.43D1DB8A024E10C7.quest_subtitle": "Decommissioned, eventually.",
  "quest.43D1DB8A024E10C7.quest_desc": [
    "It guards a tunnel of the Catacombs: 80 health, 10 armor and a shove that sends you flying. Arrows and other projectiles bounce off, potions don't take, and it smashes through walls to reach you. Bring a blade and fight it up close.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"It drops 4 to 16 \"},{\"text\":\"Forgotten Nuggets\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"undergarden:forgotten_nugget\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", only when a player lands the final blow. It counts as a boss, so Forgotten weapons get no bonus against it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1DEE3FE4EDEC5785.title": "A spare ticket",
  "quest.1DEE3FE4EDEC5785.quest_subtitle": "Single use. Read the fine print.",
  "quest.1DEE3FE4EDEC5785.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four Cloggrum ingots, four Depthrock and a Forgotten Nugget make a \"},{\"text\":\"Crumbling Catalyst\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"undergarden:crumbling_catalyst\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", no Routing Matrix needed. It lights one portal and falls apart: handy for a second base up top.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2E2ACB3604FB7157.title": "Forgotten metal",
  "quest.2E2ACB3604FB7157.quest_subtitle": "Nine nuggets of something older than you.",
  "quest.2E2ACB3604FB7157.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Nine Forgotten Nuggets make a \"},{\"text\":\"Forgotten Ingot\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"undergarden:forgotten_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", the metal of this dimension's best gear. The Guardian is the sure source; now and then a catacomb chest holds a single nugget.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A quarter of catacomb chests also hold a Forgotten Bee egg: with Productive Bees, its combs give a nugget now and then, for good.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.61947CE83E83349C.title": "The Forgotten template",
  "quest.61947CE83E83349C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Forgotten upgrade template\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"undergarden:forgotten_upgrade_smithing_template\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" turns up in catacomb chests. At a smithing table it joins a Cloggrum tool and a Forgotten Ingot into a Forgotten one.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.10395897F8C8BE4F.title": "Copy the template",
  "quest.10395897F8C8BE4F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Seven diamonds, a Depthrock block and the template make two templates, so one lucky chest covers every Cloggrum tool you own.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0E7DE09D7A18EDF9.title": "Build a sentry",
  "quest.0E7DE09D7A18EDF9.quest_subtitle": "Works for nuggets.",
  "quest.0E7DE09D7A18EDF9.quest_desc": [
    "A Carved Gloomgourd on a Block of Forgotten Metal wakes a Forgotten Minion. It shoots monsters, Rotspawn and cave hunters, never a Stoneborn, and each Forgotten Nugget you feed it mends 5 health."
  ],
  "quest.5EE9D31CF36D4673.title": "The Forgotten Pickaxe",
  "quest.5EE9D31CF36D4673.quest_subtitle": "The key to the basement.",
  "quest.5EE9D31CF36D4673.quest_desc": [
    "Template, Cloggrum Pickaxe and Forgotten Ingot at a smithing table. It mines anything, obsidian included, has 1,876 uses and breaks Dreadrock, the floor between you and the Depths, which diamond and netherite pickaxes can't touch."
  ],
  "quest.7A5E0F225A38D8BC.title": "Forgotten arsenal",
  "quest.7A5E0F225A38D8BC.quest_desc": [
    "All six Forgotten tools, battleaxe included. The pickaxe, axe, shovel and hoe work Undergarden blocks 50% faster; the sword, axe and battleaxe hit this dimension's creatures 50% harder, bosses excepted."
  ],
  "quest.1075165C09B99F54.title": "Into the Depths",
  "quest.1075165C09B99F54.quest_subtitle": "Mind the step. It's a big one.",
  "quest.1075165C09B99F54.quest_desc": [
    "Dig through the Dreadrock around Y 0 and you drop into the Depths: open caverns of Ancient Roots, puff mushrooms, Denizen camps and, in the Infected Depths, the plague at full strength. Down here the air itself infects you."
  ],
  "quest.7A23675E5A97B838.title": "Rogdorium",
  "quest.7A23675E5A97B838.quest_subtitle": "The cure grows in the poison's basement.",
  "quest.7A23675E5A97B838.quest_desc": [
    "Rogdorium ore is scattered through the Dreadrock of the Depths, and only a Forgotten tool mines it. Eat one while infected and the meter drops to zero; it also fuels the Infuser."
  ],
  "quest.7DB1066C527E1A9F.title": "The Infuser",
  "quest.7DB1066C527E1A9F.quest_subtitle": "I heart infusing, the game says.",
  "quest.7DB1066C527E1A9F.quest_desc": [
    "A Utheric Cluster, a Rogdorium and five Dreadrock. It burns two fuels: Rogdorium purifies, turning a cluster into a Utherium Crystal or an Ancient Root into a Mysterious Totem; a Utherium Crystal corrupts, turning a Gronglet Utheric.",
    "",
    "Each conversion takes 10 seconds and one fuel."
  ],
  "quest.076C572D488031D1.title": "Utherium, purified",
  "quest.076C572D488031D1.quest_subtitle": "Red, shiny and finally useful.",
  "quest.076C572D488031D1.quest_desc": [
    "Purify the clusters you've been hoarding, one Rogdorium each. Utherium makes diamond-tier gear, and its sword and axe hit Rotspawn 50% harder."
  ],
  "quest.2A574F05F7829F64.title": "Collector's edition",
  "quest.2A574F05F7829F64.quest_subtitle": "Six metals, one shelf.",
  "quest.2A574F05F7829F64.quest_desc": [
    "A block of each Undergarden metal: Cloggrum, Froststeel, Regalium, Utherium, Rogdorium and Forgotten metal. Nine ingots or crystals apiece, and the Forgotten block alone eats 81 nuggets, at 4 to 16 per Guardian.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "{image:undergarden:textures/item/catalyst.png width:32 height:32 align:center}",
    "",
    "Down past the Dreadrock and back up with every metal it hides. The ticket still works."
  ],
  "quest.5D70D35E8BE51092.title": "Meeting the locals",
  "quest.5D70D35E8BE51092.quest_desc": [
    "Denizens gather in camps around campfires and totem circles in the Depths. They stare you down from afar and attack once you come close, but they also hunt Rotspawn, so a camp is a safe place if you're welcome."
  ],
  "quest.04E5B17B3C7E2EFC.title": "One of us",
  "quest.04E5B17B3C7E2EFC.quest_subtitle": "The dress code is the password.",
  "quest.04E5B17B3C7E2EFC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Wear a \"},{\"text\":\"Mysterious Mask\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"undergarden:denizen_mask\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and Denizens leave you be, unless you start it. Masks sit in camp chests, and a Denizen drops one now and then when you finish it yourself.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.06DB0A7BE67FC613.title": "Party pooper",
  "quest.06DB0A7BE67FC613.quest_subtitle": "The mask doesn't cover this.",
  "quest.06DB0A7BE67FC613.quest_desc": [
    "You broke a campfire while Denizens were sitting around it. Every one of them within four blocks got up to discuss it with you."
  ],
  "reward.66DF4BC793E3772F.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.2B947E4249401201.title": "A Denizen spear",
  "quest.2B947E4249401201.quest_desc": [
    "Rogdorium on two sticks makes the spear the Denizens throw at you. Throw it like a trident for 8 damage, or keep it in hand for a 7-damage jab."
  ],
  "quest.1B7EA50370798865.title": "A Mysterious Totem",
  "quest.1B7EA50370798865.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Infuse an Ancient Root with Rogdorium, or take one from a camp. A placed \"},{\"text\":\"Mysterious Totem\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"undergarden:denizen_totem\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" gives Purity to everyone within five blocks, and Purity slowly drains the infection: a safe corner for a base.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.7C45CF16033436AD.title": "Watch a Greater Dweller",
  "quest.714002267E7EECCD.title": "Greater Dwellers",
  "quest.714002267E7EECCD.quest_subtitle": "Big, calm, and best kept that way.",
  "quest.714002267E7EECCD.quest_desc": [
    "The Depths' own grazers: 100 health, neutral, and they hit for 10 once angered. Underbeans lure and breed them, and one drops 4 to 8 Raw Dweller Meat."
  ],
  "quest.38DF9C345116BE28.title": "A much needed antidote",
  "quest.38DF9C345116BE28.quest_desc": [
    "Eat Rogdorium or a nugget, or stand in a totem's Purity, while infected. A Rogdorium clears the whole meter and a nugget only two points, but nine nuggets make a Rogdorium."
  ],
  "quest.4AAB6823A7B72E6E.title": "Rogdoric roots",
  "quest.4AAB6823A7B72E6E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Some Ancient Roots in the Depths grow veined with Rogdorium; a Forgotten tool breaks them for one or two \"},{\"text\":\"Rogdorium Nuggets\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"undergarden:rogdorium_nugget\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", more with Fortune. The Rogdorium Groves are thick with them.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2606E4FF6F680E78.title": "Gronglets, two ways",
  "quest.2606E4FF6F680E78.quest_desc": [
    "Purified with Rogdorium, a Gronglet turns Rogdoric; corrupted with Utherium, Utheric. Eat a Rogdoric one and your infection clears; eat a Utheric one and it maxes out. Both still give Wither X."
  ],
  "quest.0799EEF7CE271AE2.title": "Rogdorium-infused armor",
  "quest.0799EEF7CE271AE2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Any armor piece goes in the Infuser with Rogdorium: each one stores ten minutes of protection, up to an hour per piece, and with a full infused set infection builds five times slower. It burns up to six at once, so load only what the piece needs.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4B652855CDA8152C.title": "Utherium tools",
  "quest.4B652855CDA8152C.quest_desc": [
    "Diamond-tier and a hair faster than diamond, with 1,279 uses. Save the sword or axe for the Infected Depths: every hit on a Rotspawn deals 50% more and throws red sparks."
  ],
  "quest.0CBEE518C93EE95E.title": "Utherium armor",
  "quest.0CBEE518C93EE95E.quest_desc": [
    "20 armor, like diamond, with 3 toughness per piece, one more than diamond, and no speed penalty. Infuse it with Rogdorium before you go deep."
  ],
  "quest.5D6CCDF390CEC557.title": "The Infected Depths",
  "quest.5D6CCDF390CEC557.quest_subtitle": "Where the rot comes from.",
  "quest.5D6CCDF390CEC557.quest_desc": [
    "Nothing lives here but Rotspawn and Utherium growths, and the air alone fills your meter in under two and a half minutes. Go infused, with Rogdorium in your pockets and a Utherium blade."
  ],
  "quest.3763B5DEC13B1BC5.title": "Virulent Mix",
  "quest.3763B5DEC13B1BC5.quest_desc": [
    "The glowing sludge that pools at the bottom of Undergarden caves, just above the Dreadrock. A dip gives Virulence, 2 damage every 2.5 seconds that stops at one heart; Virulent Resistance, from a Gloomgourd Pie or a potion, shrugs it off."
  ],
  "quest.3F5CA95A85051F64.title": "Depleted Mines",
  "quest.3F5CA95A85051F64.quest_desc": [
    "Wooden walkways deep in the Depths, between Y -54 and -31, where Forgotten miners still work with Forgotten Pickaxes. The dirt mounds hide chests with raw metals, Regalium, Utheric Clusters and, sometimes, a worn Forgotten Pickaxe."
  ],
  "quest.5DD3FBB588B8A96D.title": "Subterranean cartographer",
  "quest.5DD3FBB588B8A96D.quest_desc": [
    "All twenty Undergarden biomes, the four of the Depths included. JourneyMap keeps mapping down here; a waypoint at every portal saves a lot of wandering."
  ],
  "image.7F464941B84F5B1E.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Life on the floor\",\"color\":\"#57E3B3\"}]",
  "image.51F208A1B80B994C.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Ruins\",\"color\":\"#57E3B3\"}]",
  "image.2ECF7EB5A70EA912.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The dark garden\",\"color\":\"#57E3B3\"}]",
  "image.65438C70BAE4C2B4.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Rot and remedy\",\"color\":\"#57E3B3\"}]",
  "image.0FB2FD37520E8BC2.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Cold country\",\"color\":\"#57E3B3\"}]",
  "image.59FE1BD62419895B.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Slings and bangs\",\"color\":\"#57E3B3\"}]",
  "image.1A76A77413D56910.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"In the walls\",\"color\":\"#57E3B3\"}]",
  "image.3A77CE32CB7EE0EA.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Regalium and trade\",\"color\":\"#57E3B3\"}]",
  "image.404B7DFFF98B828D.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Forgotten halls\",\"color\":\"#57E3B3\"}]",
  "image.7C2376E3E717E8CE.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Denizens\",\"color\":\"#57E3B3\"}]",
  "image.77B9903497D70625.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Rogdorium\",\"color\":\"#57E3B3\"}]",
  "image.48F7F9EC2ED67F22.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Utherium\",\"color\":\"#57E3B3\"}]",
  "image.12A43BD415AB8002.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Deeper still\",\"color\":\"#57E3B3\"}]",
  "image.7291F7C11F0C4714.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Undergarden\",\"color\":\"#EAF7F0\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.5C6D6131F825E85A.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"the forgotten land below\",\"color\":\"#A8D8C0\",\"font\":\"minecraft:alt\"}]",
  "image.40BB79BAAC4BFC7D.title": "Back to the Sun of Heliodor",
  "image.68AEDECD06597C0B.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Overworld\",\"color\":\"#9CC77A\"}]",
  "image.54E4A0D51D49408D.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The cavern\",\"color\":\"#A8D8C0\"}]",
  "image.40495462F6CA9FF0.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Dreadrock, Y 0 to 5\",\"color\":\"#A8D8C0\"}]",
  "image.4170BFD3C686DFCA.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Depths\",\"color\":\"#E08A7A\"}]",
  "chapter.7FFE55E39FF744F9.title": "Deep Aether",
  "chapter.7FFE55E39FF744F9.chapter_subtitle": [
    "New biomes, Skyjade, Stratus and a storm with a boss inside."
  ],
  "task.08FD750B1A058B45.title": "Enter an Aerglow, Aerlavender or Golden biome",
  "quest.09480F82FCA889E5.title": "More sky",
  "quest.09480F82FCA889E5.quest_subtitle": "Same portal, bigger map.",
  "quest.09480F82FCA889E5.quest_desc": [
    "Deep Aether adds biomes to the same dimension: Aerglow forests, the Yagroot Swamp, the Golden Heights and their grove, the Aerlavender Fields, the Sacred Lands and the rare Cloud biome. Walk into an Aerglow forest, the Aerlavender Fields or golden ground.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Nature's Compass\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"naturescompass:naturescompass\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" finds any of them by name.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1E7AA1B9A19FBDC5.title": "Aether explorer",
  "quest.1E7AA1B9A19FBDC5.quest_subtitle": "Ten biomes, one pair of boots.",
  "quest.1E7AA1B9A19FBDC5.quest_desc": [
    "Visit all ten biomes the advancement lists: the four Skyroot ones and six from Deep Aether. The Yagroot Swamp and the Golden Heights count; the Golden Grove, the Sacred Lands and the Cloud biome don't."
  ],
  "quest.183BB0D3AA9BC18F.title": "Five new woods",
  "quest.183BB0D3AA9BC18F.quest_subtitle": "Builders, rejoice.",
  "quest.183BB0D3AA9BC18F.quest_desc": [
    "Each biome brings its trees: Roseroot in the Aerglow forests, Yagroot and Cruderoot in the Yagroot Swamp, Sunroot and Conberry on the Golden Heights and Grove. Their planks work wherever Skyroot planks do, tools and sticks included."
  ],
  "quest.38DBA359037690C1.title": "Swamp rules",
  "quest.38DBA359037690C1.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The Yagroot Swamp has lakes of Poison instead of water, patches of Virulent Quicksand that pull you under, and Venomites that only fight when provoked. Carry an Antidote, or at least a White Apple, and watch every step.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.71775AFF5EE844C0.title": "Bio Crystals",
  "quest.71775AFF5EE844C0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Venomites buzz around the Yagroot Swamp and spit bubbles when angry: pop a bubble and it leaves a \"},{\"text\":\"Bio Crystal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"deep_aether:bio_crystal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It goes into Antidotes, and one over three Holystone makes a brewing stand, no blaze rod needed.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.78E2FDDEBE4738FF.title": "Purple magic",
  "quest.78E2FDDEBE4738FF.quest_subtitle": "Un-enchanting, the messy way.",
  "quest.78E2FDDEBE4738FF.quest_desc": [
    "Throw an item into Poison and it changes: Altar-made things lose their enchantment, so a Healing Stone goes back to Holystone, squashes turn purple and a potato turns poisonous. Mixed with water, Poison makes Aersmog, a venomous cloud block."
  ],
  "quest.65A38A2393BDB1FB.title": "Golden vines",
  "quest.65A38A2393BDB1FB.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"On the Golden Heights and in their grove, Golden Vines grow heavy with \"},{\"text\":\"Goldenleaf Berries\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"deep_aether:goldenleaf_berries\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". They're a snack, but the Freezer turns them into Frozen Goldenleaf Berries in 50 ticks, and that's what the Combiner wants.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.15B2CFFE81FDD257.title": "The Combiner",
  "quest.15B2CFFE81FDD257.quest_subtitle": "Three in, one out.",
  "quest.15B2CFFE81FDD257.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Skyroot planks, Holystone, three \"},{\"text\":\"Skyjade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"deep_aether:skyjade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and an Ambrosium Shard build it. Every recipe takes \"},{\"text\":\"Golden Amber\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:golden_amber\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", Frozen Goldenleaf Berries and a third item that decides the result, 100 ticks a batch.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.17547AFAED165CDB.title": "Antidote",
  "quest.17547AFAED165CDB.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Golden Amber, Frozen Goldenleaf Berries and a \"},{\"text\":\"Bio Crystal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"deep_aether:bio_crystal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" combine into an \"},{\"text\":\"Antidote\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"deep_aether:antidote\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": 15 seconds of Remedy. Enchant it at the Altar and the Remedy lasts twice as long.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.76EA1298D2F473D8.title": "Moa Fodder",
  "quest.76EA1298D2F473D8.quest_subtitle": "Snacks with side effects.",
  "quest.76EA1298D2F473D8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"With Golden Amber and Frozen Goldenleaf Berries, the third slot picks the effect: a \"},{\"text\":\"Quail Egg\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"deep_aether:quail_egg\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" gives a Moa bonus jumps, a Blue Berry Jump Boost, an Icestone Fire Resistance. Quails lay those eggs in the Aerglow forests, the Aerlavender Fields and on golden ground.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0CD74F73BE883B6B.title": "Skyjade",
  "quest.0CD74F73BE883B6B.quest_subtitle": "Strong now, weaker later.",
  "quest.0CD74F73BE883B6B.quest_desc": [
    "Skyjade Ore hides deep in Holystone, below height 60, and asks for an iron-tier pickaxe; the Sacred Lands hold far more of it. Its gear hits hard while new and fades as it wears: Zanite in reverse."
  ],
  "quest.0A0BCB2E5585E169.title": "Strong, then weaker",
  "quest.0A0BCB2E5585E169.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A fresh \"},{\"text\":\"Skyjade Pickaxe\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"deep_aether:skyjade_pickaxe\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" mines at twice its speed and slows as it wears; the \"},{\"text\":\"Skyjade Sword\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"deep_aether:skyjade_sword\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" starts at double damage and loses the bonus by a quarter worn. Keep them topped up at the Altar.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Skyjade gear takes no enchantments, from a table or from books.\",\"color\":\"#FF8C7A\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.591F277935D724D3.title": "Skyjade for the common store",
  "quest.591F277935D724D3.quest_subtitle": "Share the shine.",
  "quest.591F277935D724D3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight \"},{\"text\":\"Skyjade Gemstones\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"deep_aether:skyjade\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for the common store, once a day. The Sacred Lands are the richest place to dig.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.66F9BC95835E5C0D.title": "Silver clouds",
  "quest.66F9BC95835E5C0D.quest_subtitle": "Look, don't touch.",
  "quest.66F9BC95835E5C0D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Rare silver clouds drift between heights 200 and 255, and Silver or Gold dungeon rewards sometimes add one. Mine the \"},{\"text\":\"Sterling Aercloud\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"deep_aether:sterling_aercloud\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" from the side.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Step inside one and lightning strikes it: you're left with a plain Cold Aercloud and singed eyebrows.\",\"color\":\"#FF8C7A\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2E16BB026A9514DA.title": "Chromatic Aerclouds",
  "quest.2E16BB026A9514DA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Altar enchants a Sterling Aercloud into a \"},{\"text\":\"Chromatic Aercloud\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"deep_aether:chromatic_aercloud\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in 2000 ticks, eight shards of fuel each. A Stratus Ingot takes five.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Fuel it with Blocks of Ambrosium: one block covers a whole Chromatic Aercloud.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6E067188FF68A39A.title": "A Stratus Ingot",
  "quest.6E067188FF68A39A.quest_subtitle": "Five clouds and a pink metal.",
  "quest.6E067188FF68A39A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Five Chromatic Aerclouds, \"},{\"text\":\"Enchanted Gravitite\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"aether:enchanted_gravitite\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a Zanite Gemstone, an Ambrosium Shard and Skyjade make one \"},{\"text\":\"Stratus Ingot\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"deep_aether:stratus_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": the metal that upgrades Gravitite gear.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1AB627D19E68B650.title": "The Stratus template",
  "quest.1AB627D19E68B650.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Gold treasure always holds a \"},{\"text\":\"Stratus Smithing Template\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"deep_aether:stratus_smithing_template\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", and a Silver reward sometimes does. At a smithing table it upgrades any Gravitite piece with one Stratus Ingot.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Seven diamonds, or seven Enchanted Gravitite, around the template and a Holystone make two templates.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3E3294BAFC6127C5.title": "Cover me in sunshine",
  "quest.3E3294BAFC6127C5.quest_subtitle": "Above the storm, at last.",
  "quest.3E3294BAFC6127C5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Upgrade all four armor pieces to Stratus. With the Stratus gloves on as well, the set keeps Gravitite's high jump and adds a dash on \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.deep_aether.stratus_dash_ability.desc\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\"; Stratus tools shift gravity the way Gravitite ones do.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "{image:deep_aether:textures/item/stratus_ingot.png width:32 height:32 align:center}",
    "",
    "Past the storm and over the clouds. From here, the only way left is sideways."
  ],
  "quest.1664B126EBAA03D8.title": "Rings for jumpers",
  "quest.1664B126EBAA03D8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four Enchanted Gravitite in a ring make a \"},{\"text\":\"Gravitite Ring\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"deep_aether:gravitite_ring\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; the Stratus template and an ingot upgrade it into a \"},{\"text\":\"Stratus Ring\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"deep_aether:stratus_ring\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Worn, either one boosts the Gravitite jump and the Stratus dash.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6B0E8B6D303641A1.title": "Whale riding",
  "quest.6B0E8B6D303641A1.quest_subtitle": "The tallest mount in the sky.",
  "quest.6B0E8B6D303641A1.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three leather over two Stratus Ingots and a Sun Core make an \"},{\"text\":\"Aerwhale Saddle\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"deep_aether:aerwhale_saddle\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Put it on an Aerwhale and ride it through the clouds. The Sun Core is the hard part.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.432171EDEB694B08.title": "The Brass Dungeon",
  "quest.432171EDEB694B08.quest_desc": [
    "It only spawns in the rare Cloud biome, from about height 184 up, among huge masses of Aercloud. Getting there is half the fight: bring parachutes, a Moa or Gravitite armor. Nimbus Stone halls, a room with a Combiner, and a storm at the end."
  ],
  "task.450B8EEEEED45502.title": "Defeat the Eye of the Storm",
  "quest.12D8D2165B156844.title": "The Eye of the Storm",
  "quest.12D8D2165B156844.quest_subtitle": "Hit the wind. Seriously.",
  "quest.12D8D2165B156844.quest_desc": [
    "A living storm that hides inside a whirlwind and blows you around the arena. When the game suggests hitting the wind, do exactly that: the wind is the target.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"It drops the \"},{\"text\":\"Brass Key\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"deep_aether:brass_dungeon_key\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a handful of Cold Aerclouds. The key opens the Brass Treasure Chest.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3A4F665CCCBAB6E4.title": "Brass treasure",
  "quest.3A4F665CCCBAB6E4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Brass chest holds one or two of three prizes: the \"},{\"text\":\"Cloud Cape\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"deep_aether:cloud_cape\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a double jump; the \"},{\"text\":\"Aercloud Necklace\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"deep_aether:aercloud_necklace\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", to stand on Aerclouds and powder snow; or a book of Gloves Block Reach.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.78D224D8F415371D.title": "Stormforged",
  "quest.78D224D8F415371D.quest_subtitle": "Immovable object.",
  "quest.78D224D8F415371D.quest_desc": [
    "Every Brass reward chest guarantees a Stormforged piece, sometimes two. The full set with its gloves shrugs off most knockback and throws attackers back instead."
  ],
  "quest.48096BA3C2FC7634.title": "Flawless",
  "quest.48096BA3C2FC7634.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Beat an Aether boss without taking a single hit and it drops a bonus trophy: the Slider, the Valkyrie Queen, the Sun Spirit and the Eye of the Storm each have one. Bring reach, keep your distance and don't get greedy.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.16A70692C70A26CF.title": "Eye of the Slider",
  "quest.16A70692C70A26CF.quest_subtitle": "It saw everything. You dodged anyway.",
  "quest.16A70692C70A26CF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Not one hit from the Slider, and it gave up its eye. Wear the \"},{\"text\":\"Eye of the Slider\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"deep_aether:slider_eye\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and press \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.deep_aether.slider_eye_ability\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" two blocks or more above the ground to slam down on everything around you.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.731BE5C763953CD3.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.27C7543FC2F87C72.title": "Medal of Honor",
  "quest.27C7543FC2F87C72.quest_subtitle": "Flawless, and the Queen noticed.",
  "quest.27C7543FC2F87C72.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"You beat the Valkyrie Queen without a scratch. The \"},{\"text\":\"Medal of Honor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"deep_aether:medal_of_honor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" goes in the pendant slot and grants Valkyries' Grace: extra resistance against undead mobs.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.1B6BA75E00DDDF87.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.17372370DE6938BD.title": "Sun Core",
  "quest.17372370DE6938BD.quest_subtitle": "Warm to the touch. Very.",
  "quest.17372370DE6938BD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Sun Spirit fell without landing a single hit, and left its \"},{\"text\":\"Sun Core\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"deep_aether:sun_core\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Four obsidian around it make the Afterburner, a flamethrower that never breaks, it only runs out of charge.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.54967B2702145F3E.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.4814CD000DDC9ED3.title": "Floaty Scarf",
  "quest.4814CD000DDC9ED3.quest_subtitle": "The storm's kid follows you now.",
  "quest.4814CD000DDC9ED3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Not one hit from the Eye of the Storm, and a piece of it stayed behind: the \"},{\"text\":\"Floaty Scarf\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"deep_aether:floaty_scarf\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a little wind that wraps around your neck, helps you in fights and can be dyed.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.5C0B561BADD8E7E1.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.609F33918E4CE5DF.title": "Champion of the Aether",
  "quest.609F33918E4CE5DF.quest_subtitle": "Bragging rights, in cloud form.",
  "quest.609F33918E4CE5DF.quest_desc": [
    "Beat all four bosses without taking a hit: the Slider, the Valkyrie Queen, the Sun Spirit and the Eye of the Storm. Any order, as many tries as it takes; each flawless fight counts on its own."
  ],
  "image.4362C22E229F2FCA.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Biomes and woods\",\"color\":\"#F6D77A\"}]",
  "image.0CFE081581077D4C.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Yagroot Swamp\",\"color\":\"#F6D77A\"}]",
  "image.05F7F876C4B1F98F.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Combiner\",\"color\":\"#F6D77A\"}]",
  "image.327879C4F586D583.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Flawless\",\"color\":\"#F6D77A\"}]",
  "image.721C9CD219EFEED8.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Deep Aether\",\"color\":\"#F6D77A\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.0FB87B6838A7DDAE.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"above the storm\",\"color\":\"#B8D8EE\",\"font\":\"minecraft:alt\"}]",
  "image.2FB43A1B5C878663.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» The Aether\",\"color\":\"#F6D77A\"}]",
  "image.6D68053D9268A4F0.title": "Back to the Sun of Heliodor",
  "chapter.1EEAD2600F982F97.title": "Eternal Starlight · Eternal Night",
  "chapter.1EEAD2600F982F97.chapter_subtitle": [
    "The Gatekeeper, the Orb and the diamond portal; then twenty-two biomes under a sky that never gets light."
  ],
  "quest.57487D350C886A96.title": "The portal ruins",
  "quest.57487D350C886A96.quest_subtitle": "Someone left the door ajar.",
  "quest.57487D350C886A96.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A small diamond of eight \"},{\"text\":\"Chiseled Voidstone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:chiseled_voidstone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" stands in the Overworld with the Gatekeeper's spawner beside it. Plains and savannas, forests, deserts and badlands, jungles and cold biomes each have their own version, and each kind turns up about once every 36 chunks.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"An \"},{\"text\":\"Explorer's Compass\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"explorerscompass:explorerscompass\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" finds them: look for the five kinds of Portal Ruins.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.0EA7B3DC957A7501.title": "Pass the Gatekeeper's trial",
  "quest.2193C7A643FCA2F9.title": "The Gatekeeper's trial",
  "quest.2193C7A643FCA2F9.quest_subtitle": "He asks politely before he hits you.",
  "quest.2193C7A643FCA2F9.quest_desc": [
    "Talk to him and pick Challenge. He has 175 health and switches between sword, greatsword, hammer and bow, throws fireballs, dashes and teleports. He won't trade with anyone who hasn't beaten him or the Ender Dragon.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The first win drops the \"},{\"text\":\"Glimmering Tablet\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:book\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and, in this pack, four \"},{\"text\":\"Blue Starlight Crystal Shards\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:blue_starlight_crystal_shard\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" instead of the Orb, and teaches the Guidance of Stars crest. Every win drops a music disc, a handful of coal, gold, iron and \"},{\"text\":\"Seeking Eyes\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:seeking_eye\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and, more often than not, a Glistering weapon.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4F008F32A6C61611.title": "The Glimmering Tablet",
  "quest.4F008F32A6C61611.quest_desc": [
    "The dimension's own guide, and it grows with you: a page unlocks when you find, craft or beat what it describes, and a toast says so. Nobody starts with one. Lost it? The Gatekeeper sells another for five coins."
  ],
  "quest.09AFA411E26E9BD2.title": "The Orb of Prophecy",
  "quest.09AFA411E26E9BD2.quest_subtitle": "It knows all. It mostly opens doors.",
  "quest.09AFA411E26E9BD2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Right-click the ruin's diamond of \"},{\"text\":\"Chiseled Voidstone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:chiseled_voidstone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" with it to open the portal. The same Orb holds your crests and casts them, which comes later, at the \"},{\"text\":\"Golem Forge\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"21631D869DFFBC46\"}},{\"text\":\".\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"In this pack the Orb only comes from its recipe: four \"},{\"text\":\"Glass\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:glass\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", four \"},{\"text\":\"Blue Starlight Crystal Shards\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:blue_starlight_crystal_shard\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a \"},{\"text\":\"Horizon Chart\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"entrelumen:horizon_chart\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" (act IV). The Gatekeeper's first win pays the shards, and once you've beaten him, one coin buys four more.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.372541EA469042D0.title": "Look into a lit Starlight portal",
  "quest.089FAC8D0E185DDB.title": "Light the diamond",
  "quest.089FAC8D0E185DDB.quest_subtitle": "It's a diamond. Rectangles need not apply.",
  "quest.089FAC8D0E185DDB.quest_desc": [
    "The frame is a diamond around an empty plus-shaped hole: the ruin's eight blocks make the smallest one, and it can grow to 21 blocks tip to tip. Light it with the Orb and look into the portal."
  ],
  "quest.6857CE79DA16E994.title": "Under a sky that never ends",
  "quest.6857CE79DA16E994.quest_subtitle": "Sky of a million stars, clock of zero hours.",
  "quest.6857CE79DA16E994.quest_desc": [
    "The clock is stuck just after dusk and never moves, so it's always night and anything dark enough spawns monsters. Beds and respawn anchors still work here: one by the portal saves a long walk."
  ],
  "quest.146B68A60537D26F.title": "Every corner of the night",
  "quest.146B68A60537D26F.quest_subtitle": "The map is full. The sky is not.",
  "quest.146B68A60537D26F.quest_desc": [
    "Set foot in all twenty-two Starlight biomes: forests and plains, the cold north, the swamp and the desert, both rivers, the seas and shores, the Abyss and the two kinds of island.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "{image:eternal_starlight:textures/environment/dead_star.png width:48 height:48 align:center}",
    "",
    "Up there hangs a star that went out long ago. Down here, everything it shone on is on your map."
  ],
  "quest.59739A8BCE355AF0.title": "Starlight Silver Coins",
  "quest.59739A8BCE355AF0.quest_subtitle": "Exact change only.",
  "quest.59739A8BCE355AF0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Once you've proven yourself, the Gatekeeper trades. Two \"},{\"text\":\"Iron Ingots\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:iron_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" or an \"},{\"text\":\"Emerald\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:emerald\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" buy a coin; a coin buys five \"},{\"text\":\"Seeking Eyes\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:seeking_eye\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", eight \"},{\"text\":\"Chiseled Voidstone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:chiseled_voidstone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" or, in this pack, four \"},{\"text\":\"Blue Starlight Crystal Shards\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:blue_starlight_crystal_shard\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" instead of an Orb. Five coins buy the Keeper armor trim or a new Tablet.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6E6DABC6D9415D4F.title": "The Glistering arsenal",
  "quest.6E6DABC6D9415D4F.quest_subtitle": "Collect all four. He doesn't mind.",
  "quest.6E6DABC6D9415D4F.quest_desc": [
    "Each win against the Gatekeeper has about a three-in-four chance of one Glistering weapon, picked at random: a sword, a greatsword, a morning star that swings as a hammer, and a bow. All four take a few rematches."
  ],
  "quest.6704BFB20E652DD8.title": "Rematch rules",
  "quest.6704BFB20E652DD8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Every boss of this dimension comes back: its spawner returns 30 minutes after the fight, and each player who fought gets their own loot chest. Choose Leave this place and the Gatekeeper goes for good: no more duels, no more trades.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4B2D5F060CEA8A5A.title": "House rules",
  "quest.4B2D5F060CEA8A5A.quest_desc": [
    "The Orb's recipe takes a Horizon Chart here, but the Gatekeeper still hands out the first one. Nobody gets the Tablet on joining. Carry On can't lift the portal. In the pack's server tests this was the costliest dimension to generate: explore at a walking pace."
  ],
  "quest.01837D42903342EC.title": "A portal of your own",
  "quest.01837D42903342EC.quest_subtitle": "Some assembly required.",
  "quest.01837D42903342EC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Voidstone is the deep stone of Starlight, and a stonecutter turns it into \"},{\"text\":\"Chiseled Voidstone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:chiseled_voidstone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Build the diamond wherever suits you and light it with the Orb: in Starlight it leads to the Overworld, anywhere else it leads here. One coin buys exactly the eight blocks of the smallest frame.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1D265267129434E6.title": "Seeking Eyes",
  "quest.1D265267129434E6.quest_subtitle": "Guided by starlight, and a bit of redstone.",
  "quest.1D265267129434E6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight \"},{\"text\":\"Starlight Flowers\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:starlight_flower\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" around an \"},{\"text\":\"Ender Pearl\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:ender_pearl\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make 16. Thrown, an Eye flies toward the nearest boss ruin; hold a locator in your other hand to choose which: \"},{\"text\":\"Redstone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:redstone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" or Golem Steel for the Golem Forge, vines, cave moss or \"},{\"text\":\"Lunar Berries\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:lunar_berries\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for the Cursed Garden.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1854B10F8C564348.title": "Seven woods",
  "quest.1854B10F8C564348.quest_subtitle": "Plant a sky, one sapling at a time.",
  "quest.1854B10F8C564348.quest_desc": [
    "Lunar grows in the forests and scrubland, Northland in the cold north, Banyin in the swamp, Scarlet and Torreya in their own forests, Jinglestem in the lush shallow seas and Cradlewood on the floating Solaris Isles. Each wood has its full set of planks, doors, boats and signs."
  ],
  "quest.1E64401CFF4C70E1.title": "Meteors and auroras",
  "quest.1E64401CFF4C70E1.quest_desc": [
    "Starlight has its own weather. An aurora hangs in the sky for five to ten minutes; a meteor shower lasts one or two, and its big meteorites leave craters with ore. Each comes around every half hour to two and a half hours."
  ],
  "quest.596BBE1ABD7A94DE.title": "A bed by the portal",
  "quest.596BBE1ABD7A94DE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Sleeping won't end this night, but a bed still sets your spawn point here. Put one next to your portal before the first long trip.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6D6977F0503B7CAF.title": "The Abyss",
  "quest.6D6977F0503B7CAF.quest_subtitle": "The Mariana Trench, but it glows.",
  "quest.6D6977F0503B7CAF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The deepest sea, down to a floor of abysslate cut by geysers. Luminofish, Luminaris and the violet-eyed Twilight Gaze live here; the Gaze only fights back, and it always drops a \"},{\"text\":\"Seeking Eye\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:seeking_eye\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0E93F5E8BF6EE4BD.title": "Seas and shores",
  "quest.0E93F5E8BF6EE4BD.quest_desc": [
    "Four seas and two shores. Rookfish swim in the seas, the Lush Shallow Seas grow Jinglestem trees among the marimold, and the Spiral Kelp Forest grows the kelp that stands in for feathers in arrows."
  ],
  "quest.1FA8373E1C76D9AF.title": "Two kinds of island",
  "quest.1FA8373E1C76D9AF.quest_subtitle": "One glows, the other floats.",
  "quest.1FA8373E1C76D9AF.quest_desc": [
    "Lucent Mycelium Isles are covered in giant glowing and shining mushrooms. The Solaris Isles float in the sky with Cradlewood trees, golden grass, sacred starlight flowers and lanternvines."
  ],
  "quest.68A0B3B01E048039.title": "Two rivers",
  "quest.68A0B3B01E048039.quest_desc": [
    "Shimmer Rivers carry water, lacewings and rookfish. Ether Rivers carry Ether, which eats away at your armor while you stand in it, and Thioquartz geodes line their banks."
  ],
  "quest.094C595F3DC8EDD5.title": "The Dark Swamp",
  "quest.094C595F3DC8EDD5.quest_desc": [
    "Banyin trees on muddy roots, Pungency Fruit hanging from vines and the dimension's only Malarite ore. Stranghouls keep their dens here, and they don't much like silver."
  ],
  "quest.09D240CF2F5DB074.title": "Lunar forests",
  "quest.09D240CF2F5DB074.quest_subtitle": "Blue, cyan or purple, never green.",
  "quest.09D240CF2F5DB074.quest_desc": [
    "Lunar trees in three leaf colours; the biggest carry Starfire Bird nests and Lunar Berries on the trunk. Ents, Ratlins and Shadow Snails wander between giant glowing mushrooms. Shear a leafy Ent and it drops its leaves; bone meal grows them back."
  ],
  "quest.6B15D04AE5013392.title": "Plains and scrubland",
  "quest.6B15D04AE5013392.quest_desc": [
    "Open ground between the forests: scattered lunar and scarlet trees on the Umbral Plains, dwarf and giant lunar trees in the Glimmer Scrubland, and mossy monoliths on both."
  ],
  "quest.3CD435596A54E45A.title": "The Scarlet Forest",
  "quest.3CD435596A54E45A.quest_desc": [
    "Red-leaved Scarlet trees shed piles of leaves on the ground, and red, orange and purple buds grow underneath."
  ],
  "quest.6187265CC5470566.title": "The Torreya Forest",
  "quest.6187265CC5470566.quest_subtitle": "Sap now, amber later.",
  "quest.6187265CC5470566.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Torreya trees hang vines, and some hold Starfire Bird nests. Strip a Torreya log with an axe and Raw Amaramber falls out: the resin behind a whole set of self-mending gear in the \"},{\"text\":\"next chapter\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"5EC08F3914201E7C\"}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5EA9DF05D1E92176.title": "The cold north",
  "quest.5EA9DF05D1E92176.quest_subtitle": "Pack a scarf. Or a yeti.",
  "quest.5EA9DF05D1E92176.quest_desc": [
    "Northland pines on the taiga and the permafrost, Yetis rolling down the slopes and Aurora Deer on the snow. Under the Permafrost Forest and Peaks the ice caves hold Glacite, and below Y −5 you reach a layer of Ashen Snow."
  ],
  "quest.0A6E97F5DECA4E45.title": "The Crystallized Desert",
  "quest.0A6E97F5DECA4E45.quest_subtitle": "Castle of glass, sand of crystal.",
  "quest.0A6E97F5DECA4E45.quest_desc": [
    "Red and blue starlight crystals grow out of the sand, among Lunaris Cacti and dead lunar trees; Thirst Walkers, Gleeches and Crystallized Moths share the dunes. Blue shards go into Orbs, red ones into mana crystals."
  ],
  "quest.53BA439A530FB077.title": "Lights of the deep",
  "quest.53BA439A530FB077.quest_desc": [
    "Luminofish and Luminaris only swim, and only bite on a line, in the Abyss. Raw they barely feed you; cooked, each is worth 6 hunger."
  ],
  "quest.61A9FFC335A781FB.title": "Abyssal Romance",
  "quest.61A9FFC335A781FB.quest_subtitle": "Say it with flowers. Very deep flowers.",
  "quest.61A9FFC335A781FB.quest_desc": [
    "Red Velvetumoss carpets patches of the Abyss floor and now and then flowers. The flower crafts into red dye; a Velvetumoss Ball is a snack with a one-in-five chance of 20 seconds of Water Breathing."
  ],
  "task.5AA958226AC43DCD.title": "Watch an Abyssal Geyser",
  "quest.0E7BCD53E0A59AF3.title": "Smoke from the sea floor",
  "quest.0E7BCD53E0A59AF3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Abyssal Geysers erupt every so often, and whatever items float above one come out smoked. Three \"},{\"text\":\"Grimstone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:grimstone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" become two \"},{\"text\":\"Voidstone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:voidstone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", \"},{\"text\":\"White Dye\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:white_dye\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" turns black, and a \"},{\"text\":\"Skeleton Skull\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:skeleton_skull\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" turns into a \"},{\"text\":\"Wither Skeleton Skull\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:wither_skeleton_skull\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1AA8689B3FAF441E.title": "Nature Patty",
  "quest.1AA8689B3FAF441E.quest_subtitle": "Crunchy sapling, leafy bun.",
  "quest.1AA8689B3FAF441E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Cook a \"},{\"text\":\"Jinglestem Sapling\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:jinglestem_sapling\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" into a crisp in a smoker, furnace or campfire, then put it between two algaleaves: a \"},{\"text\":\"Jinglestem Sandwich\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:jinglestem_sandwich\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", 7 hunger.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.18C663476FFB1B65.title": "Rookfish",
  "quest.18C663476FFB1B65.quest_desc": [
    "The common fish of Starlight's seas and rivers: 7 hunger cooked, and three sticks turn one into three skewers. Its air sacs go into arrows, a diving mask and boots that swim almost as fast as they walk."
  ],
  "quest.57DCFA1F9F867EC1.title": "Nimble as a squirrel",
  "quest.57DCFA1F9F867EC1.quest_subtitle": "Walls are just floors standing up.",
  "quest.57DCFA1F9F867EC1.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Bouldershroom\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:bouldershroom\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a \"},{\"text\":\"Glowing Mushroom\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:glowing_mushroom\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a bowl: 6 hunger and, four times in five, two minutes of Sticky, which lets you climb any block at a slightly slower walk.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.48341A9A3CA8E40A.title": "Nocturnal Millet",
  "quest.48341A9A3CA8E40A.quest_desc": [
    "Its seeds hide inside Thioquartz on the Ether River banks. Sow them on dirt, farmland or Dusted Gravel: the stalk keeps growing panicles you pick by hand. Now and then a stalk withers and starts killing nearby crops; bone meal revives it."
  ],
  "quest.28DBA8100AAA1CA7.title": "Return to Oblivion",
  "quest.28DBA8100AAA1CA7.quest_subtitle": "Walls are more of a suggestion.",
  "quest.28DBA8100AAA1CA7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"On Dusted Gravel, bone meal turns a millet stalk forgotten: it steals life from nearby crops and grows \"},{\"text\":\"Forgotten Nocturnal Millet\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:forgotten_nocturnal_millet\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Roasted, it gives 15 seconds of Oblivion: you walk through walls, and sneaking sinks you through the floor.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5DDB824E5560A148.title": "Movie night",
  "quest.5DDB824E5560A148.quest_subtitle": "Every night is movie night here.",
  "quest.5DDB824E5560A148.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three \"},{\"text\":\"Nocturnal Millet\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:nocturnal_millet\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a \"},{\"text\":\"Starcore\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:starcore\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a \"},{\"text\":\"Bucket\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make a bucket of popped millet: 5 hunger, eaten fast, and you keep the bucket.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4AE0B3B14A0DD357.title": "Smells like hydrogen ions",
  "quest.4AE0B3B14A0DD357.quest_subtitle": "Your armor has notes.",
  "quest.4AE0B3B14A0DD357.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"You took a dip in Ether and your armor points started draining. Things thrown into it change too: any accessory comes out a \"},{\"text\":\"Butterfly Wings Amulet\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:butterfly_wings_amulet\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", and a music disc comes out as a different song.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.74276E0545A2D04B.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.4793DEA8A84AADBF.title": "Pungency Stew",
  "quest.4793DEA8A84AADBF.quest_subtitle": "Garlic, with notes of zombie.",
  "quest.4793DEA8A84AADBF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Pungency Fruit hangs from vines all over the swamp and tastes like garlic. With a piece of \"},{\"text\":\"Rotten Flesh\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:rotten_flesh\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in a bowl it becomes \"},{\"text\":\"Pungency Stew\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:pungency_stew\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", which rids you of Hunger and is the Stranghouls' favourite meal.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.17F178E61BD3E14C.title": "Anyone can cook",
  "quest.17F178E61BD3E14C.quest_desc": [
    "Hand a Stranghoul a bowl of Pungency Stew and it works for you for a day. It fights with whatever it carries, from stone tools to a Malarite spear or a Seeds Launcher."
  ],
  "quest.3A6A79BDE269CC98.title": "Payment in Malarite",
  "quest.3A6A79BDE269CC98.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Stranghouls trade in \"},{\"text\":\"Malarite\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:malarite\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": give them a piece and they pay you back 2 to 4 things. Only they deal the Pungency Fruit smithing template, the Battleaxe Pendant, the Drying Rack and the Seeds Launcher.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0BCE6B1A5BF03797.title": "A Stranghoul den",
  "quest.0BCE6B1A5BF03797.quest_desc": [
    "Their camps in the Dark Swamp. They farm, raise their young and dry rotten flesh on racks into leather for their armor. Bring silver: a Deepsilver sword, axe, pickaxe or sickle hurts them more than anything else."
  ],
  "quest.21692FB859B4345B.title": "Jerky, Stranghoul style",
  "quest.21692FB859B4345B.quest_subtitle": "Harder to chew, easier to love.",
  "quest.21692FB859B4345B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Drying Rack\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:drying_rack\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" over a campfire dries Rotten Flesh into jerky in 30 seconds (5 hunger), and also bakes clay into bricks, dries kelp and wrings out a wet sponge. Without a fire it slowly tans the flesh into \"},{\"text\":\"Leather\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:leather\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", two minutes a piece.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.225BD61A3469F49F.title": "Even death may die",
  "quest.225BD61A3469F49F.quest_subtitle": "Bon appétit, apparently.",
  "quest.225BD61A3469F49F.quest_desc": [
    "You watched a Stranghoul hunt. They scavenge, but they won't turn down anyone who's dying either, and they're scared stiff of silver."
  ],
  "reward.049C0BBBA1EB29DA.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.7AF8322DC49292D7.title": "Nurturing roots",
  "quest.7AF8322DC49292D7.quest_desc": [
    "Starfire Birds nest in the tallest Lunar and Torreya trees. Put seeds or Lunar Berries in a nest and they breed; the grown birds then fly to whoever fed them and drop a gift."
  ],
  "quest.0C333E07F3C4FED9.title": "Crystalline Blaze",
  "quest.0C333E07F3C4FED9.quest_subtitle": "A thank-you note that burns.",
  "quest.0C333E07F3C4FED9.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The birds' gifts are \"},{\"text\":\"Feathers\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:feather\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", \"},{\"text\":\"Starfire\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:starfire\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and Deepsilver Nuggets. Six planks and three Starfire build an Aviary, a nest you place yourself; the \"},{\"text\":\"next chapter\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"5EC08F3914201E7C\"}},{\"text\":\" turns Starfire into weapons and Flowglaze.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2467B330A9DEBAB9.title": "Berries for the store",
  "quest.2467B330A9DEBAB9.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Thirty-two \"},{\"text\":\"Lunar Berries\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:lunar_berries\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for the common store, once a day. They grow on the trunks of the giant Lunar trees and on berry vines, and Ents drop them.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7581361DB1F94183.title": "A blossom among the stars",
  "quest.7581361DB1F94183.quest_subtitle": "To a thinker!",
  "quest.7581361DB1F94183.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"One leaf block in forty thousand broken in Starlight hides a \"},{\"text\":\"Blossom of Stars\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:blossom_of_stars\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", and you just ate it: two minutes of Dream Catcher, extra armor and words of encouragement. Swinging in the boundless Milky Way, as the mod puts it.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.1BC8DF4C4A8DCF32.title": "Secret found",
  "task.1AE0DD154972AF29.title": "Defeat a Lonestar Skeleton",
  "quest.7D946FEA389E263B.title": "The night shift",
  "quest.7D946FEA389E263B.quest_subtitle": "Bony, lonely and armed.",
  "quest.7D946FEA389E263B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Lonestar Skeletons roam every dry biome and throw shattered blades at you from range. Each drops bones and up to two \"},{\"text\":\"Deepsilver Nuggets\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:deepsilver_nugget\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", so an evening of them adds up to ingots.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.6F6313C73A989071.title": "Defeat a Nightfall Spider",
  "quest.38049FFD405821C8.title": "Nightfall Spiders",
  "quest.38049FFD405821C8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"They drop string, and a \"},{\"text\":\"Nightfall Spider Eye\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:nightfall_spider_eye\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" only when a player lands the kill. Keep the eyes: with Soul Dew from the Cursed Garden they make the Soulit Spectator.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.38CA10E83E1A8310.title": "Defeat a Seeker",
  "quest.48127E2D72917716.title": "Seekers",
  "quest.48127E2D72917716.quest_subtitle": "It was looking for you, too.",
  "quest.48127E2D72917716.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Seekers drop one or two \"},{\"text\":\"Seeker Tentacles\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:seeker_tentacle\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and one or two Seeking Eyes. The tentacles are a quick snack, and three of them make the Tentacle Spike whip.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.36528D1EBFBDC6F8.title": "Shadow Snails",
  "quest.36528D1EBFBDC6F8.quest_subtitle": "Slow food.",
  "quest.36528D1EBFBDC6F8.quest_desc": [
    "Hit one and it hides in its shell; it drops the shell when it grows up, and again when it dies. One shell grinds into four Shell Powder: black dye, or the fertiliser that grows a sheared Ent's leaves back. They breed on leaves, berries and cave moss."
  ],
  "quest.25CD9ED020C41493.title": "Snail, two ways",
  "quest.25CD9ED020C41493.quest_desc": [
    "Cooked Shadow Snail Meat goes into a pie with Raw Amaramber and Crinoa (9 hunger) or into Shadow Escargot with a Velvetumoss Ball and a shell (10 hunger)."
  ],
  "quest.2C27209B6AB660E3.title": "Ratlins",
  "quest.2C27209B6AB660E3.quest_subtitle": "Rats, but make it dimension.",
  "quest.2C27209B6AB660E3.quest_desc": [
    "They nibble Glow Lichen, Cave Moss and Crinoa, which also breed them, and drop Leather, Cave Moss and meat (6 hunger cooked). The Zombified Ratlin is the one that bites."
  ],
  "quest.235622B466BBA3F4.title": "A whole palette of weeds",
  "quest.235622B466BBA3F4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Starlight's plants cover most of the dye chart: \"},{\"text\":\"Conebloom\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:conebloom\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" brown, \"},{\"text\":\"Swamp Rose\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:swamp_rose\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" green, \"},{\"text\":\"Starlight Flower\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:starlight_flower\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" blue, \"},{\"text\":\"Glintgrass\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:glintgrass\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" light blue, scarlet buds red, orange or purple, and \"},{\"text\":\"Shell Powder\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:shadow_snail_shell_powder\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" black.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5EAD049EE1591895.title": "Under the permafrost",
  "quest.5EAD049EE1591895.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Dig below Y −5 under the Permafrost Forest or Peaks and you reach the Ashen Snow. Its snowballs are the frozen bomb's fuse, and the ice caves above it are where \"},{\"text\":\"Glacite\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:glacite\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" grows.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.35987E4EF2C323AC.title": "Yeti fur",
  "quest.35987E4EF2C323AC.quest_subtitle": "Shear, wait, repeat.",
  "quest.35987E4EF2C323AC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Yetis roll down the slopes like giant snowballs. Shear one for \"},{\"text\":\"White Yeti Fur\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:white_yeti_fur\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", which grows back; any dye recolours it, and eight sticks around a fur make a \"},{\"text\":\"Starlit Painting\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:starlit_painting\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Lunar Berries, Cave Moss or Crinoa breed them.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.279A66DABF00BFAE.title": "Asking for trouble",
  "quest.279A66DABF00BFAE.quest_subtitle": "Olé.",
  "quest.279A66DABF00BFAE.quest_desc": [
    "Hit an Aurora Deer and it charges; sidestep so it rams stone and an antler snaps off. The antler works as a sickle. Lunar Berries, Abyssal Fruit or Crinoa breed them."
  ],
  "quest.3853C46138616ADF.title": "Dental surgery",
  "quest.3853C46138616ADF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Thirst Walkers are what the Gleeches left of an old people, drained and grown through with crystal. Most drop a \"},{\"text\":\"Tooth of Hunger\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:tooth_of_hunger\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" or more, and a bite caught on a shield sometimes knocks one loose; the tooth stores what it eats to grow sharper.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.69DBE913170E3106.title": "Crystal-desertification",
  "quest.69DBE913170E3106.quest_subtitle": "Terraforming, but greedy.",
  "quest.69DBE913170E3106.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four Teeth of Hunger, four \"},{\"text\":\"Cinder Bricks\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:cinder_brick\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a \"},{\"text\":\"Redstone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:redstone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make the Crystalborn Catalyst. Fed crystal shards and given a redstone signal, it infests the ground around it with crystal and gathers what that ground held.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1336335B680D87B1.title": "Lost in the echo",
  "quest.1336335B680D87B1.quest_desc": [
    "Crystallized Moths fight with sound waves. Feed one enough meat, raw or cooked fish, deer, ratlin, snail or jerky, and it fights for you. Wild ones drop starlight crystal shards and sometimes Shivering Gel."
  ],
  "quest.62B2DFB035D9CDA0.title": "A grain of crystal",
  "quest.62B2DFB035D9CDA0.quest_desc": [
    "Crinoa grows wild on the desert sand. Three make a Crinoa Porridge (8 hunger), two and a Lunar Berry a Crinoa Ball (6); the seeds feed Starfire Birds and load a Seeds Launcher."
  ],
  "quest.0E28649D9B810A7F.title": "A living display case",
  "quest.0E28649D9B810A7F.quest_desc": [
    "Shear a fruiting Lunaris Cactus to carve its fruit, like a pumpkin, and set it on a block of Grimstone Bricks: a Grimstone Golem wakes up. Hand it anything and it holds it up for show."
  ],
  "quest.1DE5C4BE8C3D5779.title": "Bloodletting therapy",
  "quest.1DE5C4BE8C3D5779.quest_subtitle": "Not a recommended treatment.",
  "quest.1DE5C4BE8C3D5779.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"You threw a \"},{\"text\":\"Gleech Egg\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:gleech_egg\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" at something and it hit. Gleeches drop them by the dozen, and they're the reason the Thirst Walkers are so thirsty.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.402139E0B85344D8.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.4977107652D0119D.title": "Quackstarvers",
  "quest.4977107652D0119D.quest_subtitle": "Interior design with a bite.",
  "quest.4977107652D0119D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"You tiled a floor with teeth: four Teeth of Hunger make four \"},{\"text\":\"Tooth of Hunger Tiles\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:tooth_of_hunger_tiles\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Bold choice.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.52F39269C35A8DD3.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.194B0FD9278B8820.title": "Lunaris Cactus",
  "quest.194B0FD9278B8820.quest_subtitle": "Don't hug it. Don't eat it either.",
  "quest.194B0FD9278B8820.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"It grows on the desert sand and now and then bears a fruit. Eaten, \"},{\"text\":\"Lunaris Cactus Fruit\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:lunaris_cactus_fruit\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" feeds 4 but usually makes you glow for half a minute and poisons you for ten seconds. Shears carve the fruit on the cactus, like a pumpkin.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.45DC24AA20247816.title": "Abyssal Fruit",
  "quest.45DC24AA20247816.quest_desc": [
    "It grows on the Abyss's kelp and you can eat it even when full. Now and then it lends 30 seconds of Glowing or 20 of Water Breathing, and Ents and Aurora Deer take it as feed."
  ],
  "task.4389639D621CD29D.title": "Defeat a Twilight Gaze",
  "quest.5C9128D226FA35EA.title": "Twilight Gaze",
  "quest.5C9128D226FA35EA.quest_subtitle": "Look it in the eye. Then take the eye.",
  "quest.5C9128D226FA35EA.quest_desc": [
    "The violet-eyed fish of the Abyss leaves you alone until you strike first, and it always drops a Seeking Eye: a cheap way to stock up without the Gatekeeper."
  ],
  "task.6652EA3AB004DE15.title": "Watch an Ent",
  "quest.627E21BA61F3D684.title": "Ents",
  "quest.627E21BA61F3D684.quest_subtitle": "Walking trees, very slow gossip.",
  "quest.627E21BA61F3D684.quest_desc": [
    "Peaceful walking trees, dressed in the leaves of their wood. Shears take the leaves off and bone meal or Shell Powder grows them back; Lunar Berries and Abyssal Fruit breed them, and they drop sticks and berries."
  ],
  "quest.703D79CE358D6088.title": "Moving the flock",
  "quest.703D79CE358D6088.quest_desc": [
    "Take eggs out of a wild nest with an empty hand, up to three per nest, and set them into your own Aviary. The birds hatch where you want the gifts."
  ],
  "task.2C93721BCBC7A712.title": "Watch a Shimmer Lacewing",
  "quest.6BF2090CAD8A601A.title": "Shimmer Lacewings",
  "quest.6BF2090CAD8A601A.quest_subtitle": "Useless. Beloved.",
  "quest.6BF2090CAD8A601A.quest_desc": [
    "Four pairs of glowing blue or purple wings over the Shimmer Rivers and the Dark Swamp. They threaten nothing and drop nothing: when the Starlighters were still around, their children loved them."
  ],
  "image.50BC333F5F5EE767.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Gatekeeper's stall\",\"color\":\"#ACFFFC\"}]",
  "image.2F35243B95097205.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Abyss\",\"color\":\"#ACFFFC\"}]",
  "image.1D32527C96EA3B25.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Seas\",\"color\":\"#ACFFFC\"}]",
  "image.1896673D37DB102E.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Islands\",\"color\":\"#ACFFFC\"}]",
  "image.55D4D9ACC79F8CC1.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Rivers\",\"color\":\"#ACFFFC\"}]",
  "image.78FFAA2D158D648C.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Dark Swamp\",\"color\":\"#ACFFFC\"}]",
  "image.5875BB1046B68950.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Lunar forests\",\"color\":\"#ACFFFC\"}]",
  "image.736AB9D147BCD1B3.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Plains\",\"color\":\"#ACFFFC\"}]",
  "image.6E3DE95E82392580.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Scarlet Forest\",\"color\":\"#ACFFFC\"}]",
  "image.3A1133C54B192E38.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The north\",\"color\":\"#ACFFFC\"}]",
  "image.0630C8283D2A47CE.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Crystallized Desert\",\"color\":\"#ACFFFC\"}]",
  "image.1EACF4B56E70ED3A.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eternal Starlight\\nEternal Night\",\"color\":\"#E8F7FF\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.18228249F326807B.title": "Back to the Sun of Heliodor",
  "image.57AB745842184AAB.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"the night that never ends\",\"color\":\"#B9B4F0\",\"font\":\"minecraft:alt\"}]",
  "image.6D740F7EDCE9E8BB.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» Ores and Arms\",\"color\":\"#ACFFFC\"}]",
  "image.7334E5798F43A023.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» Ruins and the Crest\",\"color\":\"#ACFFFC\"}]",
  "image.385010FA12DFFBE2.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"the Overworld\",\"color\":\"#B7A6B7\"}]",
  "chapter.5EC08F3914201E7C.title": "Eternal Starlight · Ores and Arms",
  "chapter.5EC08F3914201E7C.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Deepsilver, Thermal Springstone and Aethersent, four more metals, the smithing upgrades, the arrows and the accessories that live inside your gear."
  ],
  "quest.53B40E460A2787F6.title": "Deepsilver",
  "quest.53B40E460A2787F6.quest_subtitle": "Unstained in the mud.",
  "quest.53B40E460A2787F6.quest_desc": [
    "Deepsilver ore grows in grimstone, voidstone, both ices and the Dark Swamp's nightfall mud, all over the dimension. Smelt the raw ore or the ore itself; Lonestar Skeletons and Starfire Birds hand out nuggets too."
  ],
  "quest.28C9F7CAFE2BD34E.title": "Saltpeter",
  "quest.28C9F7CAFE2BD34E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Saltpeter ore is common in every stone of the dimension. The powder is the flux of the Alloy Furnace, and three of it between six strings make a \"},{\"text\":\"Saltpeter Matchbox\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:saltpeter_matchbox\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a pocket lighter that also melts Stellagmite and sets the Lunar Monstrosity alight.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Put the Matchbox in the crafting grid with a stick: four torches come out and the Matchbox only takes some wear.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1FDA4AF0FA2864DF.title": "Deepsilver tools",
  "quest.1FDA4AF0FA2864DF.quest_subtitle": "Quick as gold, three times as tough as iron.",
  "quest.1FDA4AF0FA2864DF.quest_desc": [
    "Iron-grade tools with 800 uses that dig as fast as gold. The sword, axe and pickaxe also count as silver: Stranghouls take extra damage from them."
  ],
  "quest.081780CA9258CB29.title": "Deepsilver armor",
  "quest.081780CA9258CB29.quest_subtitle": "Silver lining, literally.",
  "quest.081780CA9258CB29.quest_desc": [
    "Iron-grade protection, and every piece makes you a little faster, in your step and in your swing. With the full set, Poison, Wither, Nausea, Hunger, Slowness, Infested and Blindness wear off you on their own."
  ],
  "quest.67F000DC4E34B5CE.title": "A silver sickle",
  "quest.67F000DC4E34B5CE.quest_subtitle": "Shears with ambition.",
  "quest.67F000DC4E34B5CE.quest_desc": [
    "Every sickle works as shears on Starlight's plants: grasses, ferns, mosses and vines drop themselves instead of nothing, 63 blocks in all. This one also counts as silver against Stranghouls."
  ],
  "quest.4BB0F58B5B8E49C3.title": "I've become so numb",
  "quest.4BB0F58B5B8E49C3.quest_subtitle": "Pain, but on layaway.",
  "quest.4BB0F58B5B8E49C3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight Deepsilver Ingots around a Pungency Fruit make a \"},{\"text\":\"Silver Pungency Fruit\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:silver_pungency_fruit\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Eaten, it gives a minute of Numbness: three quarters of the damage you take is held back, then all of it hits you when the effect ends.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.579F015CCA685D31.title": "Double the silver",
  "quest.579F015CCA685D31.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Don't smelt your ore yet. The \"},{\"text\":\"Alloy Furnace\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"77AC77A3BF504933\"}},{\"text\":\" of the Golem Forge turns one Deepsilver ore and a pinch of Saltpeter into two ingots, and two raw Deepsilver into three.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.068EEE82EC15DB13.title": "Silver for the store",
  "quest.068EEE82EC15DB13.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Sixteen \"},{\"text\":\"Deepsilver Ingots\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:deepsilver_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for the common store, once a day. Every biome has the ore, in the stone and in the ice.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.364544B042F8D75F.title": "Wish upon a star",
  "quest.364544B042F8D75F.quest_subtitle": "Make it quick. It's coming down.",
  "quest.364544B042F8D75F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Every so often a meteor shower crosses the sky for a minute or two. Watch it from cover: the big meteors hit hard, and where they land they leave a crater with \"},{\"text\":\"Raw Aethersent\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:raw_aethersent\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and other ore.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.09A9D7E845A30DD2.title": "Gift from the sky",
  "quest.09A9D7E845A30DD2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Smelt Raw Aethersent into an \"},{\"text\":\"Aethersent Ingot\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:aethersent_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". The Rage of Stars forged from it is diamond-grade with 1750 uses, and anything made of Aethersent smelts back into nuggets.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.22D0BEBA9B60BA0D.title": "C'mon TARS!",
  "quest.22D0BEBA9B60BA0D.quest_subtitle": "It came with the meteor. It wants its rock back.",
  "quest.22D0BEBA9B60BA0D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Big meteors sometimes crawl: a Creteor climbs out of the crater, and Tiny Creteors fall during the shower. They drop Raw Aethersent and \"},{\"text\":\"Creteor Hide\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:creteor_hide\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", the leather of every Aethersent piece.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5DB9C02D42FF6A68.title": "Meteor armor",
  "quest.5DB9C02D42FF6A68.quest_subtitle": "Hit me. Go on. Look up first.",
  "quest.5DB9C02D42FF6A68.quest_desc": [
    "Hood, cape, bottoms and boots in Aethersent and Creteor Hide. Each piece is a one-in-four chance that whatever hurts you gets a meteor shower on its head; with all four, it always does."
  ],
  "quest.2A381FB51A51AEAD.title": "Rage of Stars",
  "quest.2A381FB51A51AEAD.quest_desc": [
    "Two Aethersent Ingots on a stick: a sword that calls meteors down on whatever it hits, and on what you swing at up to 20 blocks ahead."
  ],
  "quest.21B85E31924B55F0.title": "Starfall Longbow",
  "quest.21B85E31924B55F0.quest_subtitle": "Aim high. Higher.",
  "quest.21B85E31924B55F0.quest_desc": [
    "Aethersent, Creteor Hide and string. Its arrows bring a meteor shower down where they land."
  ],
  "quest.40C289B4CB285DF0.title": "Galactic Quiver",
  "quest.40C289B4CB285DF0.quest_desc": [
    "Three pieces of Creteor Hide sewn into a quiver that holds up to 512 arrows. Load and unload it like a bundle."
  ],
  "quest.403360FCE2E0DAD0.title": "Cosmic rainmaker",
  "quest.403360FCE2E0DAD0.quest_subtitle": "Weather on demand.",
  "quest.403360FCE2E0DAD0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Creteor Hide, a \"},{\"text\":\"Starcore\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:starcore\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and \"},{\"text\":\"Paper\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:paper\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make an \"},{\"text\":\"Aetherstrike Rocket\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:aetherstrike_rocket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": fire it and a meteor shower starts. More Aethersent, when you want it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.78644223C6DF9940.title": "Planetary protection policy",
  "quest.78644223C6DF9940.quest_subtitle": "Your roof thanks you.",
  "quest.78644223C6DF9940.quest_desc": [
    "A Carved Lunaris Cactus Fruit on a Block of Aethersent wakes an Aethersent Golem, and it guards your home against meteors. When it falls it drops Aethersent Ingots and raw ore."
  ],
  "reward.4C4042A1FAC6A879.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.4EA36D0509B195B4.title": "Watch out for hand burns",
  "quest.4EA36D0509B195B4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Hot springs dot most biomes: pools rimmed with Springstone, and about one rim block in eleven is \"},{\"text\":\"Thermal Springstone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:thermal_springstone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Smelt it into ingots.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2760C3E74F6C68B2.title": "Thermal Springstone tools",
  "quest.2760C3E74F6C68B2.quest_desc": [
    "Iron-grade, 400 uses, and every hit from these sets the target on fire for 10 seconds, which is exactly what the Lunar Monstrosity hates."
  ],
  "quest.4CEA3EAE69732BA9.title": "Hot-blooded",
  "quest.4CEA3EAE69732BA9.quest_subtitle": "Touch me and you'll get burned.",
  "quest.4CEA3EAE69732BA9.quest_desc": [
    "Thermal Springstone armor sets fire to whatever hurts you, and each piece softens fire damage a little."
  ],
  "quest.3DEF79310B472197.title": "The Hammer of Justice",
  "quest.3DEF79310B472197.quest_subtitle": "Jump. Swing. Apologise later.",
  "quest.3DEF79310B472197.quest_desc": [
    "Five ingots and two sticks make a Thermal Springstone Hammer. Land a jumping critical hit with the attack meter full and it slams the ground around the target."
  ],
  "quest.56207A3C2215F766.title": "CHAOS, CHAOS",
  "quest.56207A3C2215F766.quest_desc": [
    "Three ingots across two sticks: a scythe reaches further than a sword, sweeps everything in front of it, and still tills dirt like a hoe. Thermal Springstone and Glacite scythes can be upgraded later."
  ],
  "quest.36A55CF0D5551254.title": "Starfire template",
  "quest.36A55CF0D5551254.quest_desc": [
    "The Golem Forge and the Cursed Garden hide the first one in their chests. Copy it with seven Thermal Springstone Ingots and a Block of Starcore: two come out."
  ],
  "quest.0C2BCDC012F70360.title": "Starfire",
  "quest.0C2BCDC012F70360.quest_subtitle": "It spreads. That's the point.",
  "quest.0C2BCDC012F70360.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Upgrade Thermal Springstone gear with the template and a \"},{\"text\":\"Starfire\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:starfire\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": diamond-grade, 1000 uses. Every hit gives three seconds of Starfire, which makes the target hurt everything around it when struck and passes to its neighbours when it dies.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6B273C3013A04E29.title": "Starfire Crossbow",
  "quest.6B273C3013A04E29.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The same template on a plain \"},{\"text\":\"Crossbow\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:crossbow\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": its bolts burst into Starfire where they hit.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5980795F2675E7A5.title": "My December",
  "quest.5980795F2675E7A5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Glacite grows in the caves under the Permafrost Forest and Peaks, below Y 45. Break it for \"},{\"text\":\"Glacite Shards\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:glacite_shard\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", more with Fortune; Silk Touch keeps the crystal whole.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5632BEC940D2BF0B.title": "Glacite tools",
  "quest.5632BEC940D2BF0B.quest_subtitle": "Brain freeze, delivered.",
  "quest.5632BEC940D2BF0B.quest_desc": [
    "Iron-grade with 500 uses, and every hit freezes the target a little more, the way powder snow does. Six of them, scythe included."
  ],
  "quest.102D52E6E6159A98.title": "Glacite armor",
  "quest.102D52E6E6159A98.quest_desc": [
    "Freezes whatever hits you. Pair it with a Glacite weapon and the fight turns into a very slow dance."
  ],
  "quest.05698DF12CD75B4E.title": "Glacite Shield",
  "quest.05698DF12CD75B4E.quest_desc": [
    "A small shield of planks around one Glacite Shard. It's the base for the Flowglaze Shield."
  ],
  "quest.5D788B7F70A178FB.title": "Snow pea",
  "quest.5D788B7F70A178FB.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A Glacite Shard, a stick and a feather, or Spiral Kelp in its place, make four \"},{\"text\":\"Glacite Arrows\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:glacite_arrow\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". They freeze what they hit.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3DD8323489F7BA2F.title": "Under a sky of dust",
  "quest.3DD8323489F7BA2F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An Ashen Snowball, four Glacite Shards and a Starcore make twelve \"},{\"text\":\"Frozen Bombs\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:frozen_bomb\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", throwable ice for crowds.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1C7DA2DFAECF3767.title": "Liquid radiance",
  "quest.1C7DA2DFAECF3767.quest_subtitle": "Sand, meet fire. Fire, meet sand.",
  "quest.1C7DA2DFAECF3767.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Throw a \"},{\"text\":\"Starfire\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:starfire\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" at sand and it fuses into Raw Flowglaze. Smelted, it's \"},{\"text\":\"Flowglaze\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:flowglaze\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a glass of its own for panes and bricks, and the next upgrade.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1D7F8D4997F971B3.title": "Flowglaze template",
  "quest.1D7F8D4997F971B3.quest_desc": [
    "Also from the Golem Forge and Cursed Garden chests. Seven Glacite Shards and a block of Eternal Ice copy it: two out of one."
  ],
  "quest.47974BEE9054240D.title": "Flowglaze",
  "quest.47974BEE9054240D.quest_subtitle": "Keep hitting. It likes that.",
  "quest.47974BEE9054240D.quest_desc": [
    "Glacite gear, upgraded: diamond-grade, 1000 uses. Weapons hit harder with each consecutive blow on the same target, tools break a block outright once you've dug at it long enough, the bow's arrows hit harder the longer they fly, and the shield sends projectiles back."
  ],
  "quest.6AD9EF220B63C6AC.title": "Ooo! Shiny!",
  "quest.6AD9EF220B63C6AC.quest_desc": [
    "Starlit Diamond ore hides in grimstone, voidstone and both ices across the dimension. Smelt the ore block, or mine it for the gem."
  ],
  "quest.23B45E6AE7C73F2F.title": "Starlit armor",
  "quest.23B45E6AE7C73F2F.quest_subtitle": "Netherite, minus the Nether.",
  "quest.23B45E6AE7C73F2F.quest_desc": [
    "Crafted straight from the gem, no smithing: armor as sturdy as netherite, with the same toughness and knockback resistance, and diamond-grade tools with 2500 uses."
  ],
  "quest.07548770CFCBB2B4.title": "Poorly Ether-soluble",
  "quest.07548770CFCBB2B4.quest_desc": [
    "Thioquartz geodes line the Ether Rivers. The shards make arrows, the Alchemist's gear and the Etheric Eye, and some hold Nocturnal Millet seeds."
  ],
  "quest.5290A70355DD0004.title": "Final masquerade",
  "quest.5290A70355DD0004.quest_desc": [
    "Leather and Thioquartz: an Alchemist Mask and Robe. Each piece throws your potions a quarter further and makes Ether bite less."
  ],
  "quest.7AC8AD99B912F899.title": "Etheric Eye",
  "quest.7AC8AD99B912F899.quest_subtitle": "The emergency exit.",
  "quest.7AC8AD99B912F899.quest_desc": [
    "Four Thioquartz Shards around a Seeking Eye make four Etheric Eyes. Use one and it teleports you straight up to the surface."
  ],
  "quest.172B2BFAA9EAED49.title": "Fastidious!",
  "quest.172B2BFAA9EAED49.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Strip a Torreya log with an axe and a lump of \"},{\"text\":\"Raw Amaramber\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:raw_amaramber\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" falls off. It also lights the Torreya Campfire.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4466AD9D01B08A6C.title": "Amaramber Ingots",
  "quest.4466AD9D01B08A6C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Raw Amaramber and a block of \"},{\"text\":\"Deepslate\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:deepslate\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make two ingots, no furnace needed. Nuggets turn into arrows; ingots into candles, lanterns and gear.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4A83AB2890498C1C.title": "Gear that heals itself",
  "quest.4A83AB2890498C1C.quest_subtitle": "Resin remembers its shape.",
  "quest.4A83AB2890498C1C.quest_desc": [
    "Amaramber gear is weak, iron-grade with 250 uses, but it mends itself over time: a mask, a chestplate and every tool, sickle included."
  ],
  "quest.6E08DA530D3652E5.title": "Candlash",
  "quest.6E08DA530D3652E5.quest_desc": [
    "Three Amaramber Ingots on a stick: a whip. Whips hit from further away than any sword, and Swift Lash makes them faster; the Coldsnap and the Tentacle Spike are the other two."
  ],
  "quest.666D7C6020995ECD.title": "Malarite",
  "quest.666D7C6020995ECD.quest_subtitle": "Swamp money.",
  "quest.666D7C6020995ECD.quest_desc": [
    "The only Malarite ore of the dimension is in the Dark Swamp, in its grimstone, voidstone and mud. Stranghouls take it as payment and drop a piece now and then."
  ],
  "quest.541D8C3CE3B5B290.title": "Malarite weapons",
  "quest.541D8C3CE3B5B290.quest_desc": [
    "Iron-grade with 400 uses, and each hit poisons the target for three seconds. The spear throws like a trident once you hold it back and let go."
  ],
  "quest.25EB1260C7D41468.title": "Pungency weapons",
  "quest.25EB1260C7D41468.quest_subtitle": "They'll smell you coming.",
  "quest.25EB1260C7D41468.quest_desc": [
    "The Stranghouls' template plus a Pungency Fruit upgrades a Malarite axe or spear: Poison II and Nausea on every hit. Seven Malarite and Nightfall Mud Bricks copy the template."
  ],
  "quest.458641D86C21AD0F.title": "Whoever may cry",
  "quest.458641D86C21AD0F.quest_subtitle": "Onions have layers. So does this.",
  "quest.458641D86C21AD0F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"You lit a \"},{\"text\":\"Tear Bomb\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:tear_bomb\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": Pungency Fruit, gunpowder and a Malarite. Its gas blurs vision and makes mobs forget who they were chasing, until they get used to it. It also comes in a minecart that works like a TNT one.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.072B2A0BAB1D699E.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.5246BBF74C2B6819.title": "Weapon families",
  "quest.5246BBF74C2B6819.quest_desc": [
    "Starlight weapons come in families: greatswords that reach further than swords, hammers that slam on a critical, scythes that reach and sweep, spears to throw, whips that lash from afar, and sickles that double as shears."
  ],
  "quest.6D6AE7D888D9F568.title": "Accessories go inside your gear",
  "quest.6D6AE7D888D9F568.quest_desc": [
    "Starlight's accessories are never worn: each combines into one kind of equipment, like items into a bundle, and lives there while the gear lasts. Four go into chestplates, the Warhammer Pendant into hammers and the Battleaxe Pendant into axes.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"You can also combine them in the crafting grid. If the gear breaks, every accessory inside it is lost.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6718C7D78A679519.title": "Butterfly Wings Amulet",
  "quest.6718C7D78A679519.quest_desc": [
    "Throw any other accessory into Ether and it comes out as this one. In a chestplate, it uses Ether to wear down the armor of whatever you fight."
  ],
  "quest.58D87424EFD2ED2A.title": "Pearl Necklace",
  "quest.58D87424EFD2ED2A.quest_desc": [
    "A rare treasure when you fish above the Abyss. In a chestplate, your air refills the moment you leave the water."
  ],
  "quest.00E76B78B85B4ABF.title": "Battleaxe Pendant",
  "quest.00E76B78B85B4ABF.quest_desc": [
    "Only Stranghouls barter it away. In an axe, the axe wears down less when you fight with it, and it stops stripping logs by accident."
  ],
  "quest.7AEE236486007259.title": "Warhammer Pendant",
  "quest.7AEE236486007259.quest_desc": [
    "Found in Golem Forge and Cursed Garden chests. In a hammer, each hit grows stronger the faster you're moving: charge in."
  ],
  "quest.3D9FE8ADD30D3920.title": "Fungus Amulet",
  "quest.3D9FE8ADD30D3920.quest_subtitle": "Mushrooms, straight off the ground.",
  "quest.3D9FE8ADD30D3920.quest_desc": [
    "The same chests hold it. In a chestplate, you can eat Glowing and Shining Mushrooms, Bouldershrooms and Marimold raw, 6 hunger each with rich saturation."
  ],
  "quest.589745CEE3A1AB0E.title": "Seven arrows",
  "quest.589745CEE3A1AB0E.quest_subtitle": "Feathers optional. Kelp accepted.",
  "quest.589745CEE3A1AB0E.quest_desc": [
    "Every Starlight arrow comes four to a craft, and Spiral Kelp can stand in for the feather. Thioquartz, Aethersent, Glacite, Malarite, Amaramber, a Tooth of Hunger or a Rookfish air sac each give the arrow its own trick."
  ],
  "quest.7EC5A8EB7739C9DF.title": "Diving gear",
  "quest.7EC5A8EB7739C9DF.quest_desc": [
    "Four Rookfish air sacs make boots that swim almost as fast as they walk. The mask takes an Amaramber Mask, Jinglestem logs, a Velvetumoss Ball and two more sacs."
  ],
  "quest.619991D0B8B1DAAC.title": "Insatiable",
  "quest.619991D0B8B1DAAC.quest_subtitle": "Feed it, or it feeds on you.",
  "quest.619991D0B8B1DAAC.quest_desc": [
    "Two Teeth of Hunger on a stick make the Dagger of Hunger. It grows sharper as it feeds on what you hit, and keep it fed: a starving dagger turns on its owner."
  ],
  "quest.44FB15073422BA2C.title": "Lingering heat",
  "quest.44FB15073422BA2C.quest_desc": [
    "Stellagmite grows in caves across the dimension. Lava melts it, and so does any igniter: flint and steel, a fire charge, blaze powder, a Saltpeter Matchbox or a Thermal Springstone Ingot."
  ],
  "quest.43FDE53CA8101650.title": "Starcore and cinder",
  "quest.43FDE53CA8101650.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Starcore ore is common everywhere. A lava bucket, two Starcore and four gravel bake eight \"},{\"text\":\"Cinder Bricks\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:cinder_brick\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", the frame of the Crystalborn Catalyst and a cheaper Energy Transmitter.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4FE4955D4C5500E9.title": "Ancient tears",
  "quest.4FE4955D4C5500E9.quest_desc": [
    "Dusted Shards lie on the sea floor, and they tip the Air Sac Arrow along with a Rookfish air sac."
  ],
  "quest.19EA0450770436C8.title": "Three templates, three edges",
  "quest.19EA0450770436C8.quest_subtitle": "Fire, glass and garlic.",
  "quest.19EA0450770436C8.quest_desc": [
    "A Starfire Sword, a Flowglaze Sword and a Pungency Fruit Spear: every smithing upgrade of the dimension in one rack.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "{image:eternal_starlight:textures/particle/shine.png width:32 height:32 align:center}",
    "",
    "Every metal here fell or grew under the same dead sky. Now it's in your hands, sharpened."
  ],
  "quest.673F30CBE8582DFE.title": "Seeds Launcher",
  "quest.673F30CBE8582DFE.quest_subtitle": "Farming, but aggressive.",
  "quest.673F30CBE8582DFE.quest_desc": [
    "Only Stranghouls barter it away. It fires the seeds you carry, and each kind has its own damage, speed and cooldown: Crinoa, Pungency Fruit and Nocturnal Millet seeds, and wheat, beetroot, melon, pumpkin or torchflower from home."
  ],
  "quest.6AA856422C599EE3.title": "Millet makes the best ammo",
  "quest.6AA856422C599EE3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Load the Seeds Launcher with Nocturnal Millet seeds: half again the damage and speed of wheat seeds, on one of the shortest cooldowns. Overheat sets the seeds on fire, Glacial Sowing freezes, Fertile fires more of them.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7AE74324B60835C0.title": "Tentacle Spike",
  "quest.7AE74324B60835C0.quest_desc": [
    "Three Seeker Tentacles on a stick make a second whip. Seekers drop the tentacles all over the dimension, so it's the cheapest way to fight from a whip's distance."
  ],
  "quest.1E49E4B6C5A84401.title": "Starfire hammer and scythe",
  "quest.1E49E4B6C5A84401.quest_desc": [
    "The Thermal Springstone Hammer and Scythe take the Starfire upgrade too, and keep their critical slam and their sweep."
  ],
  "quest.2987DE45F7347E16.title": "Starlight's enchantments",
  "quest.2987DE45F7347E16.quest_desc": [
    "Thirteen of its own: Poisoning for armor, Fearless for blades, Swift Lash and Abyssal Touch for whips, Precision, Homing and Gathering for the boomerang, three for the Seeds Launcher, Tearing for the Pungency Spear and two for the Chain of Souls. Poisoning, Fearless and Soul Snatcher are treasure."
  ],
  "quest.1DC8AE679B5F7AD3.title": "Set up the next hit",
  "quest.1DC8AE679B5F7AD3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The Candlash and Amaramber Arrows leave a target Flammable, so fire hurts it more; the Coldsnap leaves it Brittle, so cold does. Follow up with Thermal Springstone or Glacite.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.055D08239E9E8864.title": "Stones of the night",
  "quest.055D08239E9E8864.quest_desc": [
    "Four building stones with a story: Nebulaite, pressed from two Raw Aethersent and two deepslate; Reinforced Ice, ice bound with Glacite; Radianite, quarried on the Solaris Isles; and Voidstone, which geysers smoke out of Grimstone."
  ],
  "quest.2653D122813F47D2.title": "Lights for the night",
  "quest.2653D122813F47D2.quest_subtitle": "The darkness here is picky.",
  "quest.2653D122813F47D2.quest_desc": [
    "Here monsters spawn wherever block light is 7 or less, not only in total darkness as in the Overworld, so light more densely. Crystal lanterns take four shards and a torch; the others, Eternal Ice, an Amaramber Candle or a carved cactus fruit."
  ],
  "image.6CF13075A42CCE91.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Deepsilver\",\"color\":\"#ACFFFC\"}]",
  "image.09EA1C1D2F09FFE9.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Aethersent\",\"color\":\"#ACFFFC\"}]",
  "image.7EDA692B988258BC.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Thermal Springstone\",\"color\":\"#ACFFFC\"}]",
  "image.53DA827CF1336673.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Glacite\",\"color\":\"#ACFFFC\"}]",
  "image.1AC85023CF601B51.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Malarite\",\"color\":\"#ACFFFC\"}]",
  "image.5A21229C5BC2D495.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Other metals\",\"color\":\"#ACFFFC\"}]",
  "image.6F297ACA15EEC68F.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Accessories\",\"color\":\"#ACFFFC\"}]",
  "image.4EAAD7CA7AA5F308.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Know your arsenal\",\"color\":\"#ACFFFC\"}]",
  "image.5B21AED2C359CA9F.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Builder's corner\",\"color\":\"#ACFFFC\"}]",
  "image.49AEACB41C88C2D1.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Ammunition and oddities\",\"color\":\"#ACFFFC\"}]",
  "image.383CD74B86FC65E1.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eternal Starlight\\nOres and Arms\",\"color\":\"#E8F7FF\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.3E8FD0C992BE1620.title": "Back to the Sun of Heliodor",
  "image.222E18EB27151AF9.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"what the sky drops, the forge keeps\",\"color\":\"#B9B4F0\",\"font\":\"minecraft:alt\"}]",
  "image.3F06BD36005AE5ED.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» Eternal Night\",\"color\":\"#ACFFFC\"}]",
  "image.5BC3789C0CC4A37E.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» Ruins and the Crest\",\"color\":\"#ACFFFC\"}]",
  "image.47D7BD16C15C446B.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"where they land\",\"color\":\"#B7A6B7\"}]",
  "chapter.766FAB83B63098E9.title": "L_Ender's Cataclysm · Arenas",
  "chapter.766FAB83B63098E9.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Eight bosses in three dimensions: find each arena, wake its keeper, bring it down."
  ],
  "quest.64975244823C07C4.title": "An eye for every arena",
  "quest.64975244823C07C4.quest_subtitle": "Unlike the vanilla ones, these come back.",
  "quest.64975244823C07C4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Each arena has its own eye, crafted around an \"},{\"text\":\"Eye of Ender\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:ender_eye\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Throw it and it flies toward the nearest arena of its kind, then fades out; the eye itself stays in your hand, ready again three seconds later.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Eight arenas, eight eyes, and ender eyes are the one ingredient they all share. Keep a few spare: five of the bosses come back when you feed their arena's eye to a \"},{\"text\":\"Boss Respawner\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"4420728015E09F1A\"}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4A129E62F8672B9D.title": "Eye of Desert",
  "quest.4A129E62F8672B9D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Gold, an emerald, two chiseled sandstone, a dead bush, a cactus, rotten flesh and a bone around an \"},{\"text\":\"Eye of Ender\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:ender_eye\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It finds the Cursed Pyramid, which only rises in deserts.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6E4573618DC54B72.title": "The Cursed Pyramid",
  "quest.6E4573618DC54B72.quest_subtitle": "Mind the sand. All of it.",
  "quest.6E4573618DC54B72.quest_desc": [
    "Falling sand, poison darts and fire traps line its halls, and Koboletons, Wadjets and Kobolediators keep watch. Its chests roll a desert temple's loot; the real prize is buried in the suspicious sand."
  ],
  "quest.059880952E2D4F02.title": "The Necklace of the Desert",
  "quest.059880952E2D4F02.quest_subtitle": "Some jewelry works as an alarm clock.",
  "quest.059880952E2D4F02.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Brush the suspicious sand inside the pyramid with a \"},{\"text\":\"Brush\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:brush\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": some patches always hold it, and the rest now and then. Its tooltip warns that it can wake something up, and it isn't bluffing.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.2872AE865EA27E21.title": "Defeat the Ancient Remnant",
  "quest.78546A4B9B108D1B.title": "The Ancient Remnant",
  "quest.78546A4B9B108D1B.quest_subtitle": "Death Finds a Way. So does a necklace.",
  "quest.78546A4B9B108D1B.quest_desc": [
    "It sleeps in the pyramid and takes no damage until you use the necklace on it, which spends the necklace. Arrows bounce off, except in the few seconds it stands winded after each charge; below half health it starts to regenerate.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"It drops \"},{\"text\":\"Sandstorm in a Bottle\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"cataclysm:sandstorm_in_a_bottle\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", the \"},{\"text\":\"Remnant's Skull\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"cataclysm:remnant_skull\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a \"},{\"text\":\"Block of Ancient Metal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"cataclysm:ancient_metal_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", and one kill in ten its music disc.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.1D5BAD15804B539B.title": "Defeat a Kobolediator",
  "quest.4FBB8B7C8634FA98.title": "The Kobolediator",
  "quest.4FBB8B7C8634FA98.quest_subtitle": "A skeleton with a gladiator license.",
  "quest.4FBB8B7C8634FA98.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The desert's heavyweight skeleton stands still until it spots you up close, then fights like a gladiator. It always drops its \"},{\"text\":\"Kobolediator Skull\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"cataclysm:kobolediator_skull\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", plus bones and ancient metal; the skull crowns a \"},{\"text\":\"Bone Reptile Helmet\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"261D3F4284075006\"}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.57E5FBEEF7AA974D.title": "The occupied village",
  "quest.57E5FBEEF7AA974D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Koboletons took over a desert village, and its villagers are still around. Its treasure chests hold diamonds, ancient metal and golden apples, and half of them a \"},{\"text\":\"Vitality Ankh\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"cataclysm:vitality_ankh\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" or an \"},{\"text\":\"Unbreakable Skull\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"cataclysm:unbreakable_skull\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6A9B27E36174951D.title": "Butterfingers",
  "quest.6A9B27E36174951D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Koboletons knock an item out of your hands on one hit in twenty, and they always try the offhand first. Something sticky there, like a slime ball, can't be pried loose and covers both hands; \"},{\"text\":\"Sticky Gloves\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"150CE9EEDBA459D9\"}},{\"text\":\" do the same from an accessory slot.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.34422029EB662AA1.title": "Eye of Curse",
  "quest.34422029EB662AA1.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four gold ingots, a bone, two phantom membranes and rotten flesh around an \"},{\"text\":\"Eye of Ender\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:ender_eye\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It points to the Frosted Prison, out on the snowy plains.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2EB85A616616FC85.title": "The Frosted Prison",
  "quest.2EB85A616616FC85.quest_subtitle": "Jail of Cold, and it shows.",
  "quest.2EB85A616616FC85.quest_desc": [
    "A frozen keep full of Draugr: plain ones with black steel blades, Royal Draugr behind shields, Elite Draugr with crossbows. Doors of Seal split its halls, and its treasure chests hold diamonds, black steel and enchanted gear."
  ],
  "quest.0B1BDB63B3B69138.title": "The Strange Key",
  "quest.0B1BDB63B3B69138.quest_subtitle": "The Aptrgangr won't hand it over nicely.",
  "quest.0B1BDB63B3B69138.quest_desc": [
    "Every Aptrgangr carries one, along with black steel: a hulking draugr that hurls axe blades. The key opens the Doors of Seal and isn't used up, so one key opens them all."
  ],
  "task.7822A5680DDDA51F.title": "Defeat Maledictus",
  "quest.52BC12CEDD020F1B.title": "Maledictus",
  "quest.52BC12CEDD020F1B.quest_subtitle": "Crusade Against Curse.",
  "quest.52BC12CEDD020F1B.quest_desc": [
    "The Cursed Tombstone needs a minute with the prison loaded to gather strength; until then it only says its power is still weak. Then right-click it: three seconds later Maledictus rises.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Every hit he lands adds a point of rage, up to five, and each point is 20% more damage; he loses one for every ten seconds without hitting you. He drops three or four \"},{\"text\":\"Cursium Ingots\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"cataclysm:cursium_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and, one kill in ten, his disc. The tombstone comes back for a rematch.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.26B0AE156618435B.title": "Draugr country",
  "quest.26B0AE156618435B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The snowy plains also hide an abandoned village, temple and spire, all Draugr ground. Their treasure chests can hold \"},{\"text\":\"Sturdy Boots\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"cataclysm:sturdy_boots\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", and every other one a \"},{\"text\":\"Ring of Grudged\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"cataclysm:ring_of_grudged\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" or a \"},{\"text\":\"Berserker Soul Amulet\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"cataclysm:berserker_soul_amulet\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Learn their rhythm here: shields in front, crossbows behind. Some of these faces turn up again, somewhere the light goes sour.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4AF37061F51F8062.title": "Heads will roll",
  "quest.4AF37061F51F8062.quest_subtitle": "Timing, lightning and a very specific creeper.",
  "quest.4AF37061F51F8062.quest_desc": [
    "A charged creeper's blast took a trophy off a Draugr and an Aptrgangr, same as off a zombie. Both heads also fit the head slot of your accessories."
  ],
  "reward.5B297AA6E05C0969.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.62AC70B058AB3A3A.title": "Eye of Abyss",
  "quest.62AC70B058AB3A3A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four crying obsidian and four obsidian around an \"},{\"text\":\"Eye of Ender\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:ender_eye\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It leads down to the Sunken City, on the floor of a deep ocean.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.218996A57FF6A475.title": "The Sunken City",
  "quest.218996A57FF6A475.quest_subtitle": "Sunken in the Sea. Bring air.",
  "quest.218996A57FF6A475.quest_desc": [
    "A drowned city full of Deeplings: brutes, anglers, priests and warlocks, with a few Coralssus among them. The Altar of Abyss sits in its lower city, and an Altar of Amethyst in one of its temples."
  ],
  "quest.2140289FCF36ACEA.title": "A lionfish on a leash",
  "quest.2140289FCF36ACEA.quest_subtitle": "Tastes like a bad idea. Breathes like a good one.",
  "quest.2140289FCF36ACEA.quest_desc": [
    "Every Deepling Angler walks one on a leash, like bait that bites. Eating it costs three seconds of Poison and Nausea and buys four minutes of Water Breathing."
  ],
  "quest.3E8F31B21F13008D.title": "An Athame",
  "quest.3E8F31B21F13008D.quest_desc": [
    "Deepling Priests and Warlocks always drop this ritual dagger, and the Abyssal Sacrifice needs one. After the Leviathan's first defeat, priests and warlocks also spawn in deep oceans on their own."
  ],
  "quest.682BF08A020029EB.title": "A chunk of Coralssus",
  "quest.682BF08A020029EB.quest_subtitle": "Rocks with legs, and a grudge.",
  "quest.682BF08A020029EB.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The city's coral giants drop a \"},{\"text\":\"Coral Chunk\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"cataclysm:coral_chunk\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", and your first sacrifice needs one. The other coral it takes comes from Coral Golems, and those only appear once the Leviathan has fallen.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.14A4E8511B1AF84B.title": "The Abyssal Sacrifice",
  "quest.14A4E8511B1AF84B.quest_subtitle": "Nine slots of very expensive bait.",
  "quest.14A4E8511B1AF84B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A nautilus shell, the Athame, the Coral Chunk, a \"},{\"text\":\"Heart of the Sea\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:heart_of_the_sea\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and blocks of diamond, emerald, iron, gold and amethyst, in any order. This is how you send for the Leviathan.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.6C374B97739CCFCE.title": "Defeat the Leviathan",
  "quest.769A2395F35EC1DB.title": "The Leviathan",
  "quest.769A2395F35EC1DB.quest_subtitle": "A Multidimensional Predator, with a big appetite.",
  "quest.769A2395F35EC1DB.quest_desc": [
    "Place the sacrifice on the Altar of Abyss and back off: six seconds later it breaks loose. It can't be hurt while its head is out of the water, so the fight is a swim, and at half health it melts down into a second phase.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"It drops the \"},{\"text\":\"Tidal Claws\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"cataclysm:tidal_claws\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", an \"},{\"text\":\"Abyssal Egg\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"cataclysm:abyssal_egg\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and, one kill in ten, its disc. The first kill changes the sea: Coral Golems, Deepling Priests and Warlocks start roaming deep oceans.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5878178D1E40155E.title": "Crystallized Coral",
  "quest.5878178D1E40155E.quest_subtitle": "The sea started keeping score.",
  "quest.5878178D1E40155E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"After the Leviathan's first defeat, Coral Golems walk the deep oceans; each drops a fragment, and four make \"},{\"text\":\"Crystallized Coral\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"cataclysm:crystallized_coral\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It stands in for the Coral Chunk in every sacrifice after that.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6D6298C224FD84B0.title": "The Amethyst Nest",
  "quest.6D6298C224FD84B0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A geode in the lush caves with barrels of supplies and an Amethyst Crab at home; crabs also wander lush caves on their own. Each drops four to ten \"},{\"text\":\"Amethyst Crab Meat\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"cataclysm:amethyst_crab_meat\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a few shells.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4CD300D0AC1CBA75.title": "Blessed crab",
  "quest.4CD300D0AC1CBA75.quest_subtitle": "Holy crab, literally.",
  "quest.4CD300D0AC1CBA75.quest_desc": [
    "Right-click the Altar of Amethyst with crab meat: it blesses one piece every three seconds. The blessing lasts a minute and a half and makes you immune to Darkness, Abyssal Fear and Abyssal Burn, the Leviathan's favorite tricks."
  ],
  "quest.4D983B340ADA5719.title": "Eye of Storm",
  "quest.4D983B340ADA5719.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Prismarine shards and crystals, two diamonds, a lightning rod and a water bucket around an \"},{\"text\":\"Eye of Ender\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:ender_eye\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It points to the Acropolis, over warm oceans.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2DC24D7A21183977.title": "The Acropolis",
  "quest.2DC24D7A21183977.quest_subtitle": "Why in the Sky? Because they kept building.",
  "quest.2DC24D7A21183977.quest_desc": [
    "A temple city stacked from a warm ocean up past the clouds. Urchinkins, Cindarias, Hippocamtus and Drowned Hosts with Symbioctos on their heads guard it, and its chests hold diamonds, golden apples and enchanted books."
  ],
  "quest.41636EC8574D88FD.title": "Lacrima",
  "quest.41636EC8574D88FD.quest_subtitle": "The sea's tears, sold by the handful.",
  "quest.41636EC8574D88FD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Acropolis's creatures cry it: a few from Cindarias and Hippocamtus, now and then from the rest, five to eight from a Clawdian and more from Scylla. It becomes \"},{\"text\":\"Astrape\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"4F6E7458F875AC15\"}},{\"text\":\", \"},{\"text\":\"Ceraunus\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"1233DD55F5B84B40\"}},{\"text\":\" and the \"},{\"text\":\"Azure Sea Shield\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"2A764E6E192E17D4\"}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.46455E53B5F0F705.title": "The Clawdian",
  "quest.46455E53B5F0F705.quest_subtitle": "Not so Shrimple Now.",
  "quest.46455E53B5F0F705.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three of these armored crustaceans guard the Acropolis, and they soak damage like a boss. Each drops a \"},{\"text\":\"Chitin Claw\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"cataclysm:chitin_claw\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and five to eight Lacrima.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.4CFCA9BA0BC08CF3.title": "Defeat Scylla",
  "quest.6B5403BBFAF47AC5.title": "Scylla, the Storm Empress",
  "quest.6B5403BBFAF47AC5.quest_subtitle": "The Calm after the Storm comes later.",
  "quest.6B5403BBFAF47AC5.quest_desc": [
    "She sleeps at the top of the Acropolis until you right-click her, and wakes at full health. Hits from the front teach her to parry, arrows twice as fast, until she blocks and strikes back: work her flanks.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"She throws spears and anchors, calls lightning and drags the weather along. She drops 8 to 16 Lacrima, three or four \"},{\"text\":\"Essence of the Storm\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"cataclysm:essence_of_the_storm\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and, one kill in ten, her disc.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0827B1B68C41A2C1.title": "Eye of Mech",
  "quest.0827B1B68C41A2C1.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four blocks of redstone and four iron ingots around an \"},{\"text\":\"Eye of Ender\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:ender_eye\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It points down to the Ancient Factory, buried under cave biomes.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4C7FF27418A7D8F5.title": "The Ancient Factory",
  "quest.4C7FF27418A7D8F5.quest_subtitle": "Out-of-Place, and out of the way.",
  "quest.4C7FF27418A7D8F5.quest_desc": [
    "It sits around height −30, and factories lie over a thousand blocks apart: the rarest arena of all. Watchers patrol it, a Prowler stands guard and the Harbinger sleeps at its core."
  ],
  "task.3FE941111B49CEFA.title": "Defeat the Prowler",
  "quest.44EFACD76D60A40A.title": "The Prowler",
  "quest.44EFACD76D60A40A.quest_desc": [
    "The factory's heavy sentry fires homing missiles and a death laser. It drops five to nine redstone and five to seven iron ingots: scrap, but honest scrap."
  ],
  "quest.78BC89117E23694E.title": "Pull the plug",
  "quest.78BC89117E23694E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The factory's EMP blocks fire once when redstone reaches them: a pulse that hurts everything within five blocks and stuns the Harbinger. They burn out afterwards and drop nothing, so lure it close before you flip the lever.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4210D02A340ABF99.title": "A star to wake it",
  "quest.4210D02A340ABF99.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Harbinger sleeps, heals and can't be hurt until you right-click it with a \"},{\"text\":\"Nether Star\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:nether_star\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", which it keeps. In this pack \"},{\"text\":\"the Wither\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"617F3D63E49031FA\"}},{\"text\":\" is the only source of stars.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.4F98E5D51660CECE.title": "Defeat the Harbinger",
  "quest.18D815D26CB453DD.title": "The Harbinger",
  "quest.18D815D26CB453DD.quest_subtitle": "The Thing of Ancient Civilization. Still under warranty.",
  "quest.18D815D26CB453DD.quest_desc": [
    "It swaps missiles for lasers every quarter minute or so and heals two health a second. Below half health arrows stop hurting it and its missiles come faster.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"It drops a \"},{\"text\":\"Block of Witherite\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"cataclysm:witherite_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", nine ingots of the metal behind the \"},{\"text\":\"Mechanical Fusion Anvil\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"486360E2B176D81D\"}},{\"text\":\", and one kill in ten its disc.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7B8B0ECBE23FD0ED.title": "Eye of Flame",
  "quest.7B8B0ECBE23FD0ED.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Three blaze powder, two netherite scrap and three soul sand around an \"},{\"text\":\"Eye of Ender\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:ender_eye\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Throw it in the Nether: it finds the Burning Arena in the Nether Wastes.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.75BDA8800F4E0BEF.title": "The Burning Arena",
  "quest.75BDA8800F4E0BEF.quest_subtitle": "A Massive Arena, with a volcano's manners.",
  "quest.75BDA8800F4E0BEF.quest_desc": [
    "A nether-brick colosseum ringed with basalt and obsidian, with the Altar of Fire at its heart and two Ignited Revenants on guard. No other monster spawns inside: what you see is the whole guest list."
  ],
  "quest.6A427F71D5F16597.title": "Burning Ashes",
  "quest.6A427F71D5F16597.quest_subtitle": "Imperfect thing, perfect fuel.",
  "quest.6A427F71D5F16597.quest_desc": [
    "Each Ignited Revenant drops one, and four Dying Embers from the Ignited Berserkers make another. The Altar of Fire takes nothing else."
  ],
  "task.30F3EC3DE8F3681B.title": "Defeat Ignis",
  "quest.412A7A62CD34F63A.title": "Ignis",
  "quest.412A7A62CD34F63A.quest_subtitle": "The Extinguished Fire. Eventually.",
  "quest.412A7A62CD34F63A.quest_desc": [
    "Place Burning Ashes on the Altar of Fire and step off it, since it burns: six seconds later Ignis lands. Hit his blue fireballs back at him; three of them crack his shield.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"He changes phase at two thirds and at one third of his health, and every hit that brands you heals him. He drops three \"},{\"text\":\"Ignitium Ingots\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"cataclysm:ignitium_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and, one kill in ten, his disc; the first kill wakes Ignited Berserkers in Nether fortresses.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.58C01F770A38D459.title": "Defeat an Ignited Berserker",
  "quest.723C8AF726227E79.title": "Ignited Berserkers",
  "quest.723C8AF726227E79.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"After Ignis's first defeat they spawn in Nether fortresses. Each drops up to two \"},{\"text\":\"Dying Embers\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"cataclysm:dying_ember\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", and four embers are a Burning Ashes: Ignis becomes renewable.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.34F6375650C91967.title": "Embers for the common store",
  "quest.34F6375650C91967.quest_subtitle": "Keep the fire going. Someone has to.",
  "quest.34F6375650C91967.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Sixteen \"},{\"text\":\"Dying Embers\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"cataclysm:dying_ember\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", once a day: four summons' worth of Burning Ashes, kept where the whole team can reach them.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3ACAA2A9CEEF8E98.title": "Eye of Monstrous",
  "quest.3ACAA2A9CEEF8E98.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four lava buckets, two netherite scrap and two blackstone around an \"},{\"text\":\"Eye of Ender\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:ender_eye\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Throw it in the Nether: it finds the Soul Forge in crimson and warped forests, soul sand valleys and the Nether Wastes.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.583916C2A54A3B6A.title": "The Soul Forge",
  "quest.583916C2A54A3B6A.quest_subtitle": "Where the Monstrous be Forged, grammar included.",
  "quest.583916C2A54A3B6A.quest_desc": [
    "A blackstone smithy built over lava, where the Netherite Monstrosity waits by its forge. A small Netherite Ministrosity lives there too, and it's worth keeping alive."
  ],
  "task.5AC30163576C4630.title": "Defeat the Netherite Monstrosity",
  "quest.507AEE61E72A81D7.title": "The Netherite Monstrosity",
  "quest.507AEE61E72A81D7.quest_subtitle": "The Broken Nether's Warmachine.",
  "quest.507AEE61E72A81D7.quest_desc": [
    "It stays still until it sees you within sixteen blocks, or until you hit it. Its head takes half again as much damage, and while it stands in lava it lobs lava bombs: pull it onto dry rock.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"At 40% health it goes berserk, untouchable while it changes. It drops the \"},{\"text\":\"Infernal Forge\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"cataclysm:infernal_forge\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a \"},{\"text\":\"Monstrous Horn\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"cataclysm:monstrous_horn\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", 16 to 24 \"},{\"text\":\"Lava Power Cells\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"cataclysm:lava_power_cell\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and, one kill in ten, its disc.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7DF64AF13742A998.title": "The Ministrosity",
  "quest.7DF64AF13742A998.quest_subtitle": "All the netherite, none of the attitude.",
  "quest.7DF64AF13742A998.quest_desc": [
    "Hand a Lava Power Cell to the Soul Forge's Ministrosity and it's yours: fifteen slots of storage on legs, healed with coal. Right-click it to open its pack, or with an empty bucket to carry it."
  ],
  "quest.6B0CA0DF6398CC81.title": "Eye of Void",
  "quest.6B0CA0DF6398CC81.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two purpur pillars, two shulker shells, two end stone bricks and two purpur blocks around an \"},{\"text\":\"Eye of Ender\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:ender_eye\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Throw it in the End: it finds the Ruined Citadel on the outer highlands and midlands.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3AD88921A7247356.title": "The Ruined Citadel",
  "quest.3AD88921A7247356.quest_subtitle": "Another Stronghold?! Another stronghold.",
  "quest.3AD88921A7247356.quest_desc": [
    "A broken fortress of end stone and obsidian bricks, guarded by shulker sentries, some of them silent, and three Ender Golems. Endermapteras crawl its halls, and the Altar of Void waits inside."
  ],
  "quest.488A3E1F13BE6683.title": "Ender Golems",
  "quest.488A3E1F13BE6683.quest_subtitle": "Palette Swap. Hits just as hard.",
  "quest.488A3E1F13BE6683.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Each drops a \"},{\"text\":\"Void Core\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"cataclysm:void_core\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": right-click it to raise Void Runes from the ground, every eight seconds. Cores also feed two fusions at the \"},{\"text\":\"Mechanical Fusion Anvil\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"486360E2B176D81D\"}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.44886E78B5DF1F1D.title": "Void Jaws",
  "quest.44886E78B5DF1F1D.quest_subtitle": "Bite-sized loot.",
  "quest.44886E78B5DF1F1D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Endermapteras spawn inside the Citadel, and each bite has a one-in-six chance to break their jaws; one killed with its jaws on drops one or two \"},{\"text\":\"Void Jaws\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"cataclysm:void_jaw\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". A jaw on a \"},{\"text\":\"Spectral Arrow\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:spectral_arrow\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" makes two \"},{\"text\":\"Void Scatter Arrows\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"cataclysm:void_scatter_arrow\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "task.33BB21AB8941F0E4.title": "Defeat the Ender Guardian",
  "quest.587DF57B0258B9AC.title": "The Ender Guardian",
  "quest.587DF57B0258B9AC.quest_subtitle": "Wasn't that a Shulker? It was never a shulker.",
  "quest.587DF57B0258B9AC.quest_desc": [
    "It shows up when you walk within six blocks of the Altar of Void, except on Peaceful. Arrows glance off its helmet; at half health the helmet breaks, it unleashes a mass destruction nothing interrupts, and from then on arrows land.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"It drops the \"},{\"text\":\"Gauntlet of Guard\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"cataclysm:gauntlet_of_guard\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and, one kill in ten, its disc.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0CDA886D408DA541.title": "Where the eyes look",
  "quest.0CDA886D408DA541.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"An arena eye searches the dimension you're standing in, up to 100 chunks away: throw the Flame and Monstrous eyes in the Nether and the Void eye in the End. If it never leaves your hand, nothing of its kind is in range.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.134981EE21C9111A.title": "They heal when you leave",
  "quest.134981EE21C9111A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"With nobody to fight, a boss heals 25 health a second, and after twenty seconds without a target, one that strayed snaps back home. Stepping back to eat is fine; leaving the arena means starting over.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.33B485075F4A3158.title": "No sniping, no one-shots",
  "quest.33B485075F4A3158.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A boss caps how much a single hit and a whole second of hits can take off, around 20 per hit, and past its reach your damage fades to nothing. Poison and Levitation don't stick either: close, steady pressure is what works.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7D3F711B7A5C58B5.title": "House rules",
  "quest.7D3F711B7A5C58B5.quest_desc": [
    "No act, Atlas delivery or compass stop needs Cataclysm. The Wither is the pack's only Nether Star source, arena chests are per player through Lootr, and Carry On won't lift bosses or their altars."
  ],
  "task.6A8C4F64B3877A55.title": "Look at a Boss Respawner",
  "quest.4420728015E09F1A.title": "Round two",
  "quest.4420728015E09F1A.quest_subtitle": "Some bosses leave a forwarding address.",
  "quest.4420728015E09F1A.quest_desc": [
    "The Remnant, Scylla, the Harbinger, the Monstrosity and the Ender Guardian leave a Boss Respawner where they fell. Feed it their arena's eye, which it keeps, stay within nine blocks, and the boss comes back.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Ignis and the Leviathan return through their altars, and Maledictus through the tombstone he leaves behind."
  ],
  "quest.701F40C4B578AFEB.title": "The whole soundtrack",
  "quest.701F40C4B578AFEB.quest_subtitle": "Encore. Eight times.",
  "quest.701F40C4B578AFEB.quest_desc": [
    "Every boss drops its music disc one kill in ten, and Looting doesn't help. Eight tracks by Yuri_O and Rotch Gwylt, from Light My Fire to Self-Destruction Sequence, and you went back for each one."
  ],
  "reward.4434919CEA712E14.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.2E15E4E5C60FFCDF.title": "The Cataclysmfarer",
  "quest.2E15E4E5C60FFCDF.quest_subtitle": "Eight for eight.",
  "quest.2E15E4E5C60FFCDF.quest_desc": [
    "All eight bosses down, and the advancement counts per player: one of you has to land every final blow. The game calls it the summit of Cataclysm and pays 500 experience on top."
  ],
  "image.62FF97676DF9A347.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Cursed Pyramid\",\"color\":\"#FF6040\"}]",
  "image.02A5D96A248F09DD.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Frosted Prison\",\"color\":\"#FF6040\"}]",
  "image.6AA33A86C65C2708.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Acropolis\",\"color\":\"#FF6040\"}]",
  "image.4A94E355018F2F0C.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Soul Forge\",\"color\":\"#FF6040\"}]",
  "image.1B5102778FAC1C2E.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Burning Arena\",\"color\":\"#FF6040\"}]",
  "image.2713C9EF2BE89E14.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Ancient Factory\",\"color\":\"#FF6040\"}]",
  "image.737CA71E5DE53269.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Sunken City\",\"color\":\"#FF6040\"}]",
  "image.053EE43ECF99690A.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Ruined Citadel\",\"color\":\"#FF6040\"}]",
  "image.51FCA2ADE66991CA.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Before you go\",\"color\":\"#FF6040\"}]",
  "image.1300C28157FE73D7.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"L_Ender's Cataclysm\\nArenas\",\"color\":\"#FFE9CC\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.205368E701D80AD1.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"eight eyes, eight keepers\",\"color\":\"#C9B8E8\",\"font\":\"minecraft:alt\"}]",
  "image.4FF12878EECE9343.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» Armory\",\"color\":\"#FF6040\"}]",
  "image.6DF443339B410BA1.title": "Back to the Sun of Heliodor",
  "image.5A5A17B9B901D3AF.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Overworld\",\"color\":\"#7CCB8A\"}]",
  "image.5108EECAA69D19F2.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Nether\",\"color\":\"#FF7043\"}]",
  "image.5D7524B5801F2255.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The End\",\"color\":\"#B58CFF\"}]",
  "chapter.672A13120F109441.title": "Mystical Agriculture · Souls and Awakening",
  "chapter.672A13120F109441.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Jars of souls for mob seeds, four workshops, and an altar that wakes supremium up."
  ],
  "quest.563D0C29FC49F2A6.title": "Grey veins",
  "quest.563D0C29FC49F2A6.quest_subtitle": "Five percent of the vein, all of the fun.",
  "quest.563D0C29FC49F2A6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Soulstone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:soulstone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" fills big veins in the Nether's netherrack, and one block in twenty of them is \"},{\"text\":\"Soulium Ore\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:soulium_ore\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Each one breaks into one to three \"},{\"text\":\"Soulium Dust\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:soulium_dust\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", more with Fortune.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3C087CEFDAC598BE.title": "Three trips through the furnace",
  "quest.3C087CEFDAC598BE.quest_subtitle": "Soul glass is patient glass.",
  "quest.3C087CEFDAC598BE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Mined soulstone drops cobbled: smelt it into soulstone, again into \"},{\"text\":\"Smooth Soulstone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:soulstone_smooth\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a third time into \"},{\"text\":\"Soul Dust\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:soul_dust\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Four soul dust around a glass block make \"},{\"text\":\"Soul Glass\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:soul_glass\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5A13565919E1219A.title": "An ingot with a pulse",
  "quest.5A13565919E1219A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Prosperity Ingot\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:prosperity_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and two soulium dust make a \"},{\"text\":\"Soulium Ingot\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:soulium_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; with a prosperity gemstone instead, a \"},{\"text\":\"Soulium Gemstone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:soulium_gemstone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Jars, daggers and most of the mod's machines are built from it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4D3E4A5F11849986.title": "Jars for souls",
  "quest.4D3E4A5F11849986.quest_subtitle": "Label them. Trust us.",
  "quest.4D3E4A5F11849986.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four soul glass and a soulium ingot make a \"},{\"text\":\"Soul Jar\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:soul_jar\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Each one holds the souls of a single mob, from 4 for a ghast to 12 for slimes, and mob seeds eat full jars: four per seed.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A jar alone in the crafting grid comes out empty, in case you filled it with the wrong mob.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.323C9F5E9BCF93B3.title": "The dagger that collects",
  "quest.323C9F5E9BCF93B3.quest_subtitle": "Every kill is a deposit.",
  "quest.323C9F5E9BCF93B3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A golden sword, two soulium ingots and two soulium dust make the \"},{\"text\":\"Soulium Dagger\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:soulium_dagger\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Each kill with it pours one soul into a jar you carry that holds that mob or nothing yet; ten zombies fill a zombie jar.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4B2E72150245EAAE.title": "A base for mob seeds",
  "quest.4B2E72150245EAAE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Prosperity Seed Base\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:prosperity_seed_base\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and two soulium dust make a \"},{\"text\":\"Soulium Seed Base\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:soulium_seed_base\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It takes the altar's centre for every mob seed, with four full jars and four essences of the mob's tier around it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0499CD9769672CBA.title": "Attuned daggers",
  "quest.0499CD9769672CBA.quest_desc": [
    "On the altar, a dagger with two soulium ingots, two soulium gemstones and four full jars attunes: pig, chicken, cow and sheep make it passive, zombie, skeleton, creeper and spider hostile. Attuned, it takes one and a half souls per kill of its kind."
  ],
  "quest.43C99D740412F605.title": "A thirstier dagger",
  "quest.43C99D740412F605.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The Enchanter puts Soul Siphoner on a dagger: eight soulium dust and 64 experience essence per level. Each level adds 10% to every soul the dagger collects.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.03E49E7C0F6AFD18.title": "Souls from leftovers",
  "quest.03E49E7C0F6AFD18.quest_subtitle": "Rotten flesh finally has a job.",
  "quest.03E49E7C0F6AFD18.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Iron, two soulium ingots, two daggers and a machine frame make the \"},{\"text\":\"Soul Extractor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:soul_extractor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Fed fuel and mob drops, it fills the jar inside: rotten flesh is half a zombie soul, a zombie head three.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.45299D3D5558A8EF.title": "Soulium, planted",
  "quest.45299D3D5558A8EF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Soulium Seeds\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:soulium_seeds\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" are a tier-4 resource crop: four soulium dust and four imperium on the pedestals. Eight essences give four dust, and the trips to the Nether can stop.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.77186F2E840A27EB.title": "Soulstone masonry",
  "quest.77186F2E840A27EB.quest_desc": [
    "Soulstone works like any stone: bricks, chiseled bricks, smooth, slabs, stairs and walls, most of them in one step at a stonecutter. It also goes into the awakening altar, its pedestals and its vessels."
  ],
  "quest.4CCBA490C2627426.title": "Soulium for the common store",
  "quest.4CCBA490C2627426.quest_subtitle": "Every jar starts with a pinch.",
  "quest.4CCBA490C2627426.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Sixteen \"},{\"text\":\"Soulium Dust\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:soulium_dust\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for the common store. Jars, daggers and mob seed bases all start with a pinch of it.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.7D588542D958FD79.title": "Look at Soulium Ore",
  "quest.1004167F6E745720.title": "Five percent",
  "quest.1004167F6E745720.quest_subtitle": "Found one. Staring is allowed.",
  "quest.1004167F6E745720.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"One soulstone block in twenty is \"},{\"text\":\"Soulium Ore\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:soulium_ore\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", and you found one. Fortune on the pickaxe raises its one to three dust.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.4155995101685E81.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.1BE9829A3104120B.title": "The barnyard",
  "quest.1BE9829A3104120B.quest_subtitle": "The whole farm, in seeds.",
  "quest.1BE9829A3104120B.quest_desc": [
    "Tier-2 mob seeds: a soulium base, four full jars and four prudentium each. Three pig or cow essences give six porkchops or six leather, three chicken essences eight eggs, eight sheep essences six white wool."
  ],
  "quest.526C8A3DF6CF5C83.title": "Things that swim",
  "quest.526C8A3DF6CF5C83.quest_desc": [
    "Tier 2 again, with six-soul jars. Three squid essences give six ink sacs, three fish essences six cod or salmon, eight turtle essences four scutes: turtle shells without babysitting eggs."
  ],
  "quest.1EF5BA76D43A805E.title": "Slime, rabbit and armadillo",
  "quest.1EF5BA76D43A805E.quest_desc": [
    "Slime and armadillo are tier 2, rabbit tier 3; a slime jar takes twelve souls. Three slime essences give eight slimeballs, three rabbit essences three rabbit's feet, eight armadillo essences four scutes for wolf armor."
  ],
  "quest.1F907047E1DF6C8C.title": "The night shift",
  "quest.1F907047E1DF6C8C.quest_subtitle": "They clock in at dusk.",
  "quest.1F907047E1DF6C8C.quest_desc": [
    "The classic mob farm, tier 3, with ten-soul jars. Three zombie essences give twelve rotten flesh, eight skeleton essences twelve bones, three creeper essences six gunpowder, three spider essences eight string."
  ],
  "quest.4ECA4B68CEA2AA4F.title": "Wings, wind and pearls",
  "quest.4ECA4B68CEA2AA4F.quest_desc": [
    "Phantom is tier 3, breeze and enderman tier 4, and their jars are small: six, four and eight souls. Eight essences give four phantom membranes, four breeze rods or four ender pearls."
  ],
  "quest.34E01B34A482BAA2.title": "Nether fire",
  "quest.34E01B34A482BAA2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Blaze and ghast are tier 4, wither skeleton tier 5. Eight essences give six blaze rods or two ghast tears; eight wither skeleton essences around a blank skull give a \"},{\"text\":\"Wither Skeleton Skull\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:wither_skeleton_skull\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.21E823E3994079D2.title": "Heads on order",
  "quest.21E823E3994079D2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A bone block and four soul dust make four \"},{\"text\":\"Blank Skulls\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:blank_skull\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Eight zombie, skeleton, creeper or wither skeleton essences around one turn it into that mob's head.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6C66E1691D1F0D96.title": "Records on request",
  "quest.6C66E1691D1F0D96.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four creeper and four skeleton essences around an iron ingot make a \"},{\"text\":\"Blank Record\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:blank_record\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". On the record, one creeper essence, one skeleton essence and a dye press most vanilla discs; the dye picks the song.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1DDA93C864ADF619.title": "Walls the Wither can't break",
  "quest.1DDA93C864ADF619.quest_subtitle": "Boss arena, some assembly required.",
  "quest.1DDA93C864ADF619.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four wither skeleton essences around soulstone make a \"},{\"text\":\"Witherproof Block\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:witherproof_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; around soul glass, \"},{\"text\":\"Witherproof Glass\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:witherproof_glass\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". The Wither can't break either one, and the Dragon can't damage them, though it flies straight through.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7429D142E01E50C5.title": "Pigstep, homegrown",
  "quest.7429D142E01E50C5.quest_subtitle": "Bastions hate this one trick.",
  "quest.7429D142E01E50C5.quest_desc": [
    "A blank record with one nether, one netherite and one gold essence presses Pigstep, the disc that otherwise only turns up in bastion chests."
  ],
  "reward.37028C0C1BD92C93.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.49C5D52870DE19E7.title": "A heart, grown to order",
  "quest.49C5D52870DE19E7.quest_subtitle": "No treasure map required.",
  "quest.49C5D52870DE19E7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Diamond, prismarine and squid essence around a nautilus shell make a \"},{\"text\":\"Heart of the Sea\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:heart_of_the_sea\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", and prismarine with fish essence makes the shell.\"}]"
  ],
  "reward.75708C4E692FB7A0.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.5023171132D78E9D.title": "One frame, five machines",
  "quest.5023171132D78E9D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Iron, redstone and stone make the \"},{\"text\":\"Machine Frame\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:machine_frame\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" inside the Furnace, Harvester, Seed Reprocessor, Soul Extractor and Soulium Spawner. All five burn solid fuel and keep a small power buffer.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4AF7DF1AD20071DC.title": "A farmhand that never sleeps",
  "quest.4AF7DF1AD20071DC.quest_subtitle": "Replants, too. Unlike some people.",
  "quest.4AF7DF1AD20071DC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two diamond scythes, two soulium ingots, iron and a frame make the \"},{\"text\":\"Harvester\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:harvester\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Facing a field, it picks ripe crops, replants them and keeps the harvest inside; machine upgrades widen its reach, and redstone pauses it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.619FAACEEAA5DACE.title": "Spare seeds into essence",
  "quest.619FAACEEAA5DACE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two soulium ingots, two iron hoes, iron and a frame make the \"},{\"text\":\"Seed Reprocessor\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:seed_reprocessor\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Every spare seed becomes two essences of its crop, so the second seeds from essence farmland finally have a use.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.77EBCA19F26ED39B.title": "A furnace that takes upgrades",
  "quest.77EBCA19F26ED39B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two furnaces, two prosperity ingots, iron and a frame make Mystical Agriculture's \"},{\"text\":\"Furnace\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:furnace\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It smelts like any other until a machine upgrade speeds it up.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4321C26C27515858.title": "Faster machines",
  "quest.4321C26C27515858.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Shards, prosperity ingots and a diamond make the \"},{\"text\":\"Machine Upgrade Base\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:upgrade_base\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; four essences and four ingots of a tier turn it into that tier's upgrade, inferium to supremium. Upgraded machines work and burn faster, and the Harvester reaches further.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3DDB2166F4ACF858.title": "Mobs from essence",
  "quest.3DDB2166F4ACF858.quest_subtitle": "Agriculture, in reverse.",
  "quest.3DDB2166F4ACF858.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two wither skeleton skulls, two soulium ingots, iron and a frame make the \"},{\"text\":\"Soulium Spawner\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:soulium_spawner\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It turns mob essence back into the mob, within three blocks: 16 zombie essences per zombie, 24 per blaze.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.59D4499CC9596240.title": "Enchantments without dice",
  "quest.59D4499CC9596240.quest_subtitle": "No lapis, no luck.",
  "quest.59D4499CC9596240.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"An enchanting table on a soulium ingot and three soulstone makes the \"},{\"text\":\"Enchanter\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:enchanter\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It puts the enchantment you pick on a tool or a book for experience essence and a themed item: 64 essence and 16 redstone for Efficiency, for example.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Each multiple of the recipe adds a level, up to the enchantment's cap, and a slot holds up to 512.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.27291BF52E3A7961.title": "Experience, bottled and planted",
  "quest.27291BF52E3A7961.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two soulium ingots and two soul glass make an \"},{\"text\":\"Experience Capsule\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:experience_capsule\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" that soaks up the orbs you collect, up to 1,200 points. Four full ones on the pedestals make tier-4 \"},{\"text\":\"Experience Seeds\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:experience_seeds\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight experience essences give eight \"},{\"text\":\"Experience Droplets\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:experience_droplet\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; each one and a glass bottle make a \"},{\"text\":\"Bottle o' Enchanting\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:experience_bottle\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". The Enchanter drinks the essence itself.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.39DCEA564325CFBA.title": "Mending, on request",
  "quest.39DCEA564325CFBA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The Enchanter also does Mending: three wither skeleton skulls and 256 experience essence. Silk Touch takes 32 slimeballs and 128 essence.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.77509E143AE258EE.title": "Room for one more ability",
  "quest.77509E143AE258EE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Stone and two soulium dust make the \"},{\"text\":\"Tinkering Table\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:tinkering_table\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; shards and iron make an \"},{\"text\":\"Unattuned Augment\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:unattuned_augment\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Infuse the augment on the altar, then socket it into essence gear at the table.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.60B77A10CE64CA72.title": "Inferium gear",
  "quest.60B77A10CE64CA72.quest_desc": [
    "Diamond gear plus two ingots and two gemstones of a tier becomes that tier's essence gear and keeps its enchantments. It lasts longer, digs faster and has one augment slot; an anvil repairs it with the tier's ingot."
  ],
  "quest.028575103C17E899.title": "Prudentium gear",
  "quest.028575103C17E899.quest_desc": [
    "Each tier upgrades the last one's piece, so the pickaxe you started with keeps climbing. Tier 2 opens the next shelf of augments: Speed I, Night Vision, Jump Boost I and Mining AOE I among them."
  ],
  "quest.012E9C2FB7D8302C.title": "Tertium gear",
  "quest.012E9C2FB7D8302C.quest_desc": [
    "Tertium gear takes the augments that change how you move: Step Assist, No Fall Damage, Slow Falling and Fire Resistance, plus Haste I and Strength I."
  ],
  "quest.47C8AA0B473443EC.title": "Imperium gear",
  "quest.47C8AA0B473443EC.quest_desc": [
    "Imperium gear carries the tier-4 augments: Haste II, Speed III, Strength II, Poison Resistance, Hunger Resistance and Mining AOE III."
  ],
  "quest.49FEC79F35F926CA.title": "Supremium gear",
  "quest.49FEC79F35F926CA.quest_desc": [
    "Supremium gear takes every augment, flight included, and its tools can be enchanted at a plain enchanting table. Supremium armor still wears out: the pack keeps that default."
  ],
  "quest.1CA1FB45E4B92545.title": "Creative flight, earned",
  "quest.1CA1FB45E4B92545.quest_subtitle": "Four nether stars. Worth every one.",
  "quest.1CA1FB45E4B92545.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four nether stars and four supremium essences infuse the \"},{\"text\":\"Flight Augment\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:flight_augment\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Socketed in a supremium chestplate, it grants creative flight while you wear it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.72DD20610A9F8208.title": "Bows, rods and shears",
  "quest.72DD20610A9F8208.quest_desc": [
    "The same upgrade works on bows, crossbows, fishing rods and shears. Essence bows and crossbows draw faster and hit harder with each tier: from 1.1 times the speed and +1 damage at inferium to 2.1 times and +4 awakened."
  ],
  "quest.22280B31AA115989.title": "Augments for digging",
  "quest.22280B31AA115989.quest_desc": [
    "Iron tools around an unattuned augment make the area augments: digging, tilling and paths in 3×3, up to 9×9 at their top tier. Haste goes on a chestplate and costs redstone."
  ],
  "quest.259A5D9E40C11F79.title": "Augments for the senses",
  "quest.259A5D9E40C11F79.quest_desc": [
    "Golden carrots for Night Vision and pufferfish for Water Breathing go on helmets; magma cream makes Fire Resistance, which fits any armor piece."
  ],
  "quest.2000F9DD845234F3.title": "Augments for the road",
  "quest.2000F9DD845234F3.quest_desc": [
    "Sugar for Speed, rabbit's feet for Jump Boost, stairs for Step Assist, diamonds and wool for No Fall Damage. Speed sits on leggings, Jump Boost and No Fall Damage on boots, Step Assist on either."
  ],
  "quest.23476146D562F567.title": "Augments for a fight",
  "quest.23476146D562F567.quest_desc": [
    "Strength and Attack AOE go on swords; Health Boost and Absorption on any armor, up to ten extra hearts or ten absorption hearts at their top tier. Health Boost costs wither skeleton skulls from its first level."
  ],
  "quest.295E42EA74678741.title": "Augments against bad luck",
  "quest.295E42EA74678741.quest_desc": [
    "Leather and milk stop Nausea, torches and glowstone Blindness, milk and imperium Poison. Wither Resistance is tier 5: two nether stars, two wither skeleton skulls and four supremium."
  ],
  "quest.48508F4ED026C786.title": "The second altar",
  "quest.48508F4ED026C786.quest_subtitle": "Orange wool this time. It matters.",
  "quest.48508F4ED026C786.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Gold, orange wool and soulstone make the \"},{\"text\":\"Awakening Altar\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:awakening_altar\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and four \"},{\"text\":\"Awakening Pedestals\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:awakening_pedestal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Placed, it shows the eight spots for pedestals and vessels, the same ring as the infusion altar; a redstone signal starts it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0E4DADD35126FC7B.title": "The four elements",
  "quest.0E4DADD35126FC7B.quest_subtitle": "Gravel, dirt and clay, four ways.",
  "quest.0E4DADD35126FC7B.quest_desc": [
    "Each element's agglomeratio is gravel, dirt and clay plus its own touch: a glass bottle for air, grass for earth, a water or lava bucket for the other two. On the altar with inferium they grow the essences the vessels hold.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Elemental crops count inferium farmland as their own tier: plant them there for the 20% odds.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1684E583E20FDEC9.title": "Four vessels",
  "quest.1684E583E20FDEC9.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Gold, glass and soulstone make an \"},{\"text\":\"Essence Vessel\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:essence_vessel\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Each one holds up to 40 of a single elemental essence, and the awakening altar drinks from all four at once.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0826D3348EC4A160.title": "The Wither",
  "quest.0826D3348EC4A160.quest_subtitle": "A donor with three heads.",
  "quest.0826D3348EC4A160.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Kill it with an essence weapon enchanted with Mystical Enlightenment and it drops \"},{\"text\":\"Cognizant Dust\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:cognizant_dust\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", four at level I and one more per level. Any essence weapon also shakes out one to three essences of its tier.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Mystical Enlightenment comes from the Enchanter: three supremium essences and 64 experience essences per level.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2F9D40EF186A4510.title": "The Ender Dragon",
  "quest.2F9D40EF186A4510.quest_subtitle": "Better odds, longer commute.",
  "quest.2F9D40EF186A4510.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Dragon pays more: four \"},{\"text\":\"Cognizant Dust\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:cognizant_dust\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" plus two per Mystical Enlightenment level, and two to four essences of your weapon's tier.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.407E45A9049C0435.title": "Dust that knows",
  "quest.407E45A9049C0435.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four \"},{\"text\":\"Cognizant Dust\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:cognizant_dust\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on the four pedestals, a supremium block on the altar and ten of each elemental essence in the vessels: that is one awakening.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.70D61774E3B61F65.title": "Awake",
  "quest.70D61774E3B61F65.quest_subtitle": "The block that got a promotion.",
  "quest.70D61774E3B61F65.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The altar turns a supremium block into an \"},{\"text\":\"Awakened Supremium Block\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:awakened_supremium_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", which breaks into nine \"},{\"text\":\"Awakened Supremium Essence\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"mysticalagriculture:awakened_supremium_essence\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Two per prosperity ingot or gemstone make the awakened metal.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.68E2164A9801BDE9.title": "Awakened gear",
  "quest.68E2164A9801BDE9.quest_desc": [
    "Supremium gear on the awakening altar, with awakened ingots and gemstones on the pedestals and 40 of each element in the vessels, wakes up with two augment slots. The awakened can waters 13×13 at even odds."
  ],
  "quest.3AB01992C621BB93.title": "A full awakened set",
  "quest.3AB01992C621BB93.quest_subtitle": "Walk through the field. It grows.",
  "quest.3AB01992C621BB93.quest_desc": [
    "Wear all four awakened armor pieces together for the set bonus: plants grow faster in an area around you. Each piece still keeps its own two augment slots."
  ],
  "quest.162E139D9D4F412F.title": "The last accelerator",
  "quest.162E139D9D4F412F.quest_desc": [
    "Four awakened essences, stone and an awakened gemstone make three accelerators that reach 54 blocks. On the awakening altar, 20 of each element turn a supremium upgrade into the top machine upgrade."
  ],
  "quest.3351251FE66D5565.title": "Forty to the brim",
  "quest.3351251FE66D5565.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Keep the vessels topped up: a block takes ten of each element, every awakened tool or armor piece forty, the top machine upgrade twenty.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3E66DC04BBCA6752.title": "Pick your boss",
  "quest.3E66DC04BBCA6752.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Level V of Mystical Enlightenment costs 15 supremium and 320 experience essence in the Enchanter. With it the Dragon drops 14 dust and the Wither eight.\"}]"
  ],
  "image.40B633AA3484965C.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Souls\",\"color\":\"#C4DE52\"}]",
  "image.5864F8B8B25E6A99.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Mob seeds\",\"color\":\"#C4DE52\"}]",
  "image.69245B4E1575B38D.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Machines\",\"color\":\"#C4DE52\"}]",
  "image.4910F4FFADE7F186.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Gear and augments\",\"color\":\"#C4DE52\"}]",
  "image.3466BF667EBEF08C.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Mystical Agriculture\",\"color\":\"#F1F6D8\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.25D36AD33D9D5F9A.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Souls and awakening\",\"color\":\"#C4DE52\"}]",
  "image.0406B34710B887DC.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"souls jars dust waking\",\"color\":\"#B9D77A\",\"font\":\"minecraft:alt\"}]",
  "image.63C0F7E52589C4B0.title": "Back to the Sun of Heliodor",
  "image.532712EC9231C353.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» Essence\",\"color\":\"#C4DE52\"}]",
  "chapter.3256FA24100D6B05.title": "Productive Bees · The Breeding Tree",
  "chapter.3256FA24100D6B05.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Wild bees at the roots, a family on every branch, mod bees in the crown: breed, mutate and spin combs into ore."
  ],
  "quest.3152454A3DAF1728.title": "The first cross",
  "quest.3152454A3DAF1728.quest_subtitle": "Two carpenters walk into a log.",
  "quest.3152454A3DAF1728.quest_desc": [
    "Give two different bees a flower each and their baby can be a new species. A Yellow Carpenter and a Green Carpenter, both from oak and birch nests, make a Lumber Bee: breed a Lumber, Rancher, Quarry or Farmer Bee.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "When a pair fits several recipes, one is picked at random each time. A pair with no recipe gives its own kind, if that species breeds with itself."
  ],
  "quest.631D1DB8B25062CC.title": "The Crystalline Bee",
  "quest.631D1DB8B25062CC.quest_subtitle": "Every metal starts in the Nether.",
  "quest.631D1DB8B25062CC.quest_desc": [
    "Crystalline Bees live in quartz nests in the Nether and work quartz ore and quartz blocks. Crossed with an Ashy Mining Bee they give iron, copper, tin or aluminum; with a Mason, gold; with a Neon Cuckoo, iridium or menril."
  ],
  "quest.0B7D5340E1851DD0.title": "The Iron Bee",
  "quest.0B7D5340E1851DD0.quest_subtitle": "Mining, outsourced.",
  "quest.0B7D5340E1851DD0.quest_desc": [
    "Breed an Iron Bee. It works iron ore and blocks, bars, cauldrons, hoppers and anvils, and its combs spin into raw iron two times in five. Half the metal branch has it for a parent.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "An Iron Bee working a chipped or damaged anvil mends it one step, seven times in ten."
  ],
  "task.753ED335A4B7F1C8.title": "Look at a CreeBee",
  "quest.05F05DFFB67B931B.title": "The first mutation",
  "quest.05F05DFFB67B931B.quest_subtitle": "Handle with care. Seriously.",
  "quest.05F05DFFB67B931B.quest_desc": [
    "Some species are not bred but fed: give a vanilla bee a block of TNT and it turns into a CreeBee. Its powdery combs spin into gunpowder half the time.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Feeding changes a bee on the spot; breeding only makes the next generation. The mutation branch collects the rest."
  ],
  "quest.66ED5066B2E23522.title": "The Diamond Bee",
  "quest.66ED5066B2E23522.quest_subtitle": "The gem line pays off.",
  "quest.66ED5066B2E23522.quest_desc": [
    "Glowing and Chocolate Mining make Redstone; Redstone and Blue Banded make Lapis; an Ender Bee and a Lapis Bee make a Diamond Bee. It works diamond ore and blocks, and its combs give a diamond one time in five."
  ],
  "quest.5A702645B25D0E1B.title": "Melittologist",
  "quest.5A702645B25D0E1B.quest_subtitle": "A diploma no university hands out.",
  "quest.5A702645B25D0E1B.quest_desc": [
    "Breed every vanilla-material bee at least once: iron, gold, coal, redstone, lapis, emerald, diamond, blazing, experience, frosty and obsidian, plus the Dye, Lumber, Rancher, Quarry and Farmer Bees.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Frosty Bees come from feeding, so breed two of them together; obsidian comes from Lava and Water."
  ],
  "task.1FEA89B4F5F86BBD.title": "Look at an Ashy Mining Bee",
  "task.12779D5E0102F85C.title": "Look at a Chocolate Mining Bee",
  "quest.072FAF991DFA455F.title": "Mining bees",
  "quest.072FAF991DFA455F.quest_desc": [
    "Ashy and Chocolate Mining Bees nest in coarse dirt, sand and gravel. The ashy ones parent the quartz-line metals and let Nomad Bees hatch from their nests; the chocolate ones parent redstone and the Quarry Bee."
  ],
  "task.581042C50FE45598.title": "Look at a Yellow Carpenter Bee",
  "task.1E838E6E43DC1725.title": "Look at a Green Carpenter Bee",
  "quest.4F4FB5A0D8756EEC.title": "Carpenter bees",
  "quest.4F4FB5A0D8756EEC.quest_desc": [
    "Yellow Carpenter Bees nest in oak, birch, dark oak, spruce and mangrove logs; Green ones in oak, birch, dark oak, jungle and mangrove. Crossed with each other they give the Lumber Bee."
  ],
  "task.328EED074D88DC83.title": "Look at a Mason Bee",
  "task.3981D216C525A064.title": "Look at a Digger Bee",
  "task.14F6B33E52227820.title": "Look at a Reed Bee",
  "quest.329BBA38F3701A2B.title": "Masons, diggers and reeds",
  "quest.329BBA38F3701A2B.quest_desc": [
    "Mason Bees nest in stone and reeds, Digger Bees in stone and gravel, Reed Bees in sugar cane. Masons parent gold and silver, Diggers the Quarry and Sculk Bees, Reeds silicon and silk."
  ],
  "task.7837F50DB6E1DABA.title": "Look at a Leafcutter Bee",
  "task.7EE61A54DB9D11D6.title": "Look at a Sweat Bee",
  "task.238948234B35FD10.title": "Look at a Resin Bee",
  "task.77A87A2D3A0D2D2E.title": "Look at a Bumble Bee",
  "quest.3C5AA91A9F8B746B.title": "Leaves, snow and pine",
  "quest.3C5AA91A9F8B746B.quest_desc": [
    "Leafcutter Bees nest in coarse dirt, Sweat Bees in snow, Resin Bees in spruce and Bumble Bees in plains grass. Sweat Bees parent nickel, zinc and frost; Resin Bees, plastic and silk."
  ],
  "task.7EA73BECD32A4346.title": "Look at a Blue Banded Bee",
  "task.6E3CAC8266D203FC.title": "Look at a Neon Cuckoo Bee",
  "task.0943B501AF3D1685.title": "Look at a Nomad Bee",
  "quest.5D465DDC3AE835E1.title": "Blue bands and cuckoos",
  "quest.5D465DDC3AE835E1.quest_subtitle": "Squatters, technically.",
  "quest.5D465DDC3AE835E1.quest_desc": [
    "Blue Banded Bees nest in acacia, cherry and dark oak. Each time one heads out after delivering nectar, a Neon Cuckoo Bee hatches from its nest one time in ten; Ashy Mining nests hatch Nomad Bees the same way, two per nest at most."
  ],
  "quest.344C5473C699E755.title": "What bees eat to breed",
  "quest.344C5473C699E755.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Most bees breed on any flower. A few want their own food: mushroom bees their mushroom, Royal Bees a royal jelly bottle, Draconic Bees two draconic dust. The breeding chamber takes the same items.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.11C2F8166C465BE5.title": "Glowing and magmatic",
  "quest.11C2F8166C465BE5.quest_desc": [
    "Glowing Bees nest in the Nether's glowstone and spin glowstone dust. Magmatic Bees nest in fortress bricks, leave magma cream, and turn nearby cobblestone into lava: build their pen out of anything else."
  ],
  "quest.352070B28F32FD7B.title": "Ghostly and gold",
  "quest.352070B28F32FD7B.quest_desc": [
    "Ghostly Bees nest in soul sand and hide a ghast tear in their combs one time in twenty. Gold Bees move into nether gold nests, crafted with a diamond sword, or hatch from crystalline and mason parents.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "At work, Ghostly Bees turn sand into soul sand and Gold Bees gild blackstone."
  ],
  "quest.20323500A2C1E49E.title": "The mushroom ring",
  "quest.20323500A2C1E49E.quest_subtitle": "Fun guys, the lot of them.",
  "quest.20323500A2C1E49E.quest_desc": [
    "Crimson and Warped Bees nest in the huge fungi of their Nether forests. Give any mushroom bee a red mushroom, a brown mushroom, a crimson fungus or a warped fungus and it becomes that kind."
  ],
  "quest.1176AE6DA3431D93.title": "Ender Bees",
  "quest.1176AE6DA3431D93.quest_subtitle": "They teleport. Plan the fence.",
  "quest.1176AE6DA3431D93.quest_desc": [
    "Ender Bees nest in end stone on the outer End islands and work chorus plants. Their combs give an ender pearl one time in five, plus liquid chorus; an anti-teleport upgrade keeps them from blinking out of the hive."
  ],
  "quest.359D104890F36751.title": "Draconic Bees",
  "quest.359D104890F36751.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Draconic Bees rarely nest in the obsidian pillars of the main End island; they breed on draconic dust and work dragon eggs. A dragon egg and a beehive make a \"},{\"text\":\"Dragon Egg Hive\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"productivebees:dragon_egg_hive\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", where they need no flowers while in the End.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.17E6B72F905E995C.title": "Draconic chunks",
  "quest.17E6B72F905E995C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Draconic combs give \"},{\"text\":\"Draconic Dust\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"productivebees:draconic_dust\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" three times in ten, and nine dust make a \"},{\"text\":\"Draconic Chunk\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"productivebees:draconic_chunk\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": the price of productivity upgrades, block upgrades and inactive dragon eggs.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.58D56C17350E1496.title": "Bees from the sea",
  "quest.58D56C17350E1496.quest_desc": [
    "Some bees bite the hook: fishing in rivers turns up a Water Bee one cast in twenty, and deep oceans hide Prismarine and Oily Bees, and Sponge Bees now and then. Prismarine combs give shards and crystals; oily ones, crude oil."
  ],
  "quest.66556FCFB5C112F5.title": "Something's buzzing",
  "quest.66556FCFB5C112F5.quest_subtitle": "Catch of the day: stings.",
  "quest.66556FCFB5C112F5.quest_desc": [
    "A bee on the end of a fishing line. Nobody at the docks will believe it."
  ],
  "reward.43CDDB2B5F6544B0.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.11F46650CD7BEE2C.title": "An egg of your own",
  "quest.11F46650CD7BEE2C.quest_subtitle": "Omelette postponed.",
  "quest.11F46650CD7BEE2C.quest_desc": [
    "Eight draconic chunks around an egg make an Inactive Dragon Egg, and a bottle of dragon's breath wakes it into a real dragon egg: one more Dragon Egg Hive, no second fight."
  ],
  "reward.55621CE45EE4476F.title": "Secret found",
  "task.6EB63EBCB6A7FCDE.title": "Look at a Lumber Bee",
  "task.4458B62E13CB8F50.title": "Look at a Rancher Bee",
  "task.6EA09974380ADFFB.title": "Look at a Farmer Bee",
  "task.052BBE1B5E9D4CFA.title": "Look at a Quarry Bee",
  "quest.1002A9D2E2DDB3ED.title": "Worker bees",
  "quest.1002A9D2E2DDB3ED.quest_desc": [
    "Lumber Bees nibble logs, Quarry Bees stone, sand and gravel. Rancher Bees (Lumber and Sweat) milk cows and shear sheep; Farmer Bees (Lumber and Rancher) harvest crops four blocks around their hive, more with range upgrades."
  ],
  "task.517050472CBE545B.title": "Look at a CuBee",
  "task.7570053B8E967F0A.title": "Look at a Dye Bee",
  "task.0052E5DD79EA56DE.title": "Look at a Collector Bee",
  "task.671BAFB59BF349F5.title": "Look at a Hoarder Bee",
  "quest.4FB3C3DF12B6EA53.title": "Helper bees",
  "quest.4FB3C3DF12B6EA53.quest_desc": [
    "The CuBee (Farmer and Rancher) makes nearby animals breed, five per trip. The Dye Bee (Lapis and Skeletal) makes the dye of the flower it visits. A vanilla bee fed a hopper becomes a Collector, and a Collector fed a shulker shell a Hoarder."
  ],
  "quest.14E1846A3EAF31E5.title": "Chips and milk",
  "quest.14E1846A3EAF31E5.quest_subtitle": "Chips off the old block.",
  "quest.14E1846A3EAF31E5.quest_desc": [
    "Lumber Bees bring wood chips and Quarry Bees stone chips of whatever they nibbled, and chips craft back into their block. Rancher Bees bring milky combs: a centrifuge makes milk, and a bottler, milk bottles."
  ],
  "quest.18C079CB4192C7D0.title": "Quartz-line metals",
  "quest.18C079CB4192C7D0.quest_subtitle": "One pair, four surprises.",
  "quest.18C079CB4192C7D0.quest_desc": [
    "A Crystalline Bee and an Ashy Mining Bee give iron, copper, tin or aluminum, picked at random each time. Each works blocks of its own metal, and its combs spin into that raw metal two times in five."
  ],
  "quest.5773FD5506713484.title": "Crystalline crosses",
  "quest.5773FD5506713484.quest_desc": [
    "Crystalline and Neon Cuckoo give iridium or menril; Crystalline and Iron, quartz-enriched iron for Refined Storage; Crystalline and Ender, the Spacial Bee, whose combs spin into certus quartz."
  ],
  "quest.723F59239EE71E5D.title": "Flowers made of metal",
  "quest.723F59239EE71E5D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A resource bee's flower is usually its own block: a Tin Bee needs a block of tin nearby, a Lapis Bee a lapis block. Put the block beside the hive, or in a feeding slab, before the bees move in.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.32840927B6BD1C4C.title": "Iron's children",
  "quest.32840927B6BD1C4C.quest_desc": [
    "An Iron Bee crossed with a Blue Banded gives lead; with a Mason, silver; with Sweat, nickel or zinc; with Neon Cuckoo, osmium. Every one of them spins into its raw metal two times in five."
  ],
  "quest.2E3F943FA8053DFF.title": "Alloys",
  "quest.2E3F943FA8053DFF.quest_subtitle": "Smelting, skipped.",
  "quest.2E3F943FA8053DFF.quest_desc": [
    "Iron and Coal give steel; Copper and Tin, bronze; Copper and Zinc, brass; Iron and Nickel, invar. Alloy combs skip the smelter and spin straight into nuggets, seven to twelve for steel."
  ],
  "quest.7A640DDA90390D53.title": "Fine alloys",
  "quest.7A640DDA90390D53.quest_desc": [
    "Copper and Nickel give constantan; Gold and Silver, electrum; Lead with Tin or with Silver, antimony. Mithril comes from Steel and Bronze, or from Iron and an Arcane Essence Bee."
  ],
  "quest.3A7240161A860E14.title": "Heavy metals",
  "quest.3A7240161A860E14.quest_desc": [
    "Diamond and Iron give titanium; Ender and Gold, platinum; Ender and Coal, tungsten. A CreeBee and an Iron Bee give either a Radioactive Bee, raw uranium one comb in five, or a Uraninite Bee for Powah."
  ],
  "quest.715A6D89AA3915D3.title": "Glowing in the dark",
  "quest.715A6D89AA3915D3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A Radioactive Bee killed by Mekanism's radiation has a 3% chance to shrug it off and come back as a Wasted Radioactive Bee, whose combs oxidize into nuclear waste.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.400E9A331C578EBD.title": "Iron combs for the store",
  "quest.400E9A331C578EBD.quest_subtitle": "Ore that never runs out.",
  "quest.400E9A331C578EBD.quest_desc": [
    "Sixteen Iron Bee combs for the common store: someone downstream always needs iron."
  ],
  "quest.07F5EBD97A63DA65.title": "Sweets and drinks",
  "quest.07F5EBD97A63DA65.quest_desc": [
    "Feed a Sugarbag Bee cocoa beans for chocolate, a Leafcutter a water bucket for tea, a vanilla bee salt for salt. Sugarbag and Neon Cuckoo give the Pepto-Bismol Bee, which buffs you as it flies by.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Sugarbag Bees hide in cocoa: breaking a ripe pod sets one free one time in fifty. Their honeycomb is a snack."
  ],
  "quest.6A02ED6CE0F1FA4B.title": "Silk, plastic and silicon",
  "quest.6A02ED6CE0F1FA4B.quest_desc": [
    "Reed and Resin give the Silky Bee, whose combs spin into string; Resin and Lumber, the Plastic Bee; Nomad and Reed, the Silicon Bee for your processors."
  ],
  "quest.77F9ADF013C71242.title": "Straight from the comb",
  "quest.77F9ADF013C71242.quest_subtitle": "Wax and all.",
  "quest.77F9ADF013C71242.quest_desc": [
    "Sugarbag honeycomb is meant to be eaten as it comes. Tastes like a sunny afternoon."
  ],
  "reward.6FFC57B725F62F4C.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.08D823AC231670E3.title": "The fire line",
  "quest.08D823AC231670E3.quest_desc": [
    "Magmatic and Nomad give Blazing, whose combs drop blaze powder; Magmatic and Leafcutter, Coal; Magmatic and Coal, Sulfur; Magmatic and Water, the Breeze Bee, which works a heavy core and leaves wind charges."
  ],
  "quest.46C1298421E3E2D5.title": "Lava and obsidian",
  "quest.46C1298421E3E2D5.quest_desc": [
    "A Magmatic Bee given a lava bucket becomes a Lava Bee, whose combs hold 100 mB of lava. Lava and Water give the Obsidian Bee: three to six obsidian shards a comb, nine shards to a block."
  ],
  "quest.62FC314F8F4B3673.title": "Bees that redecorate",
  "quest.62FC314F8F4B3673.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Some bees change blocks as they work: Frosty Bees freeze water, Sponge Bees drink it, Draconic Bees make obsidian cry. Sussy Bees, whose eggs sniffers dig up now and then, turn sand and gravel suspicious half the time: an archaeology farm.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6DA616955F068A6F.title": "The undead",
  "quest.6DA616955F068A6F.quest_subtitle": "Nobody invited them.",
  "quest.6DA616955F068A6F.quest_desc": [
    "Skeletal Bees and ZomBees move into an advanced hive left empty in the dark. Give a Skeletal Bee a wither rose and it withers; Ghostly with Skeletal or with a ZomBee gives the Grave Bee, for Tombstone."
  ],
  "quest.405D1B9A0B3808FE.title": "Skulls by the comb",
  "quest.405D1B9A0B3808FE.quest_subtitle": "A Wither farm that starts with a flower.",
  "quest.405D1B9A0B3808FE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Withered combs give a \"},{\"text\":\"Wither Skull Chip\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"productivebees:wither_skull_chip\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" three times in ten, and nine chips make a wither skeleton skull. No fortress required.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2166A0403077A91B.title": "Frost and slime",
  "quest.2166A0403077A91B.quest_desc": [
    "A Sweat Bee fed ice or snow turns Frosty, and its combs give snowballs and ice. Feed a Slimy Bee Industrial Foregoing's pink slime and it turns Pink Slimy; feed that one an ether gas bucket for the Ether Gas Bee."
  ],
  "quest.247E0E93F2AE0C8E.title": "Sculk and butcher",
  "quest.247E0E93F2AE0C8E.quest_subtitle": "Not every mutation works on the first try.",
  "quest.247E0E93F2AE0C8E.quest_desc": [
    "A Digger Bee fed sculk turns into a Sculk Bee three times in ten; its combs give echo shards three times in ten. A Bumble Bee fed raw meat turns Butcher only one time in thirty-three, and brings back meat."
  ],
  "quest.05594A3B95BAAF25.title": "Amber and petrified honey",
  "quest.05594A3B95BAAF25.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Brushing cold ocean ruins can turn up an Amber Bee egg. Amber Bees turn honey blocks into \"},{\"text\":\"Petrified Honey\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"productivebees:petrified_honey\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", which takes any dye, and seal mobs in amber.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6B9A6A282B60EF4A.title": "Mutations in the feeding slab",
  "quest.6B9A6A282B60EF4A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Some mutations happen to eggs, not bees: a Blazing Bee visiting a feeding slab with an Obsidian Bee egg turns it into an Infinity Bee egg, an Obsidian Bee turns a Redstone egg into Flux, and a Rancher Bee turns a cheese block into a Cheese Bee egg.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.1513A599645887EF.title": "A Ribbeet Bee spawn egg",
  "quest.2E76EFBE7A126F2C.title": "Ribbeet",
  "quest.2E76EFBE7A126F2C.quest_subtitle": "Circle of life, with a croak.",
  "quest.2E76EFBE7A126F2C.quest_desc": [
    "A frog that eats a bee leaves a Ribbeet Bee egg behind. Ribbeet Bees pollinate magma cubes and bring home froglights."
  ],
  "reward.17BAC5F9DA524B1B.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.3B94F90648E02063.title": "Redstone and lapis",
  "quest.3B94F90648E02063.quest_desc": [
    "Glowing and Chocolate Mining give the Redstone Bee, redstone dust half the time; Redstone and Blue Banded give the Lapis Bee, a lapis half the time. Both are halfway to diamond."
  ],
  "quest.086669867D4B9EDB.title": "Emerald and experience",
  "quest.086669867D4B9EDB.quest_desc": [
    "Diamond and Slimy give the Emerald Bee; Emerald and Lapis, the Experience Bee, which works bookshelves and fills its combs with liquid experience."
  ],
  "quest.0C4A291074C8F28D.title": "Diamond mutations",
  "quest.0C4A291074C8F28D.quest_subtitle": "Same bee, new jewelry.",
  "quest.0C4A291074C8F28D.quest_desc": [
    "A Diamond Bee fed an amethyst, fluorite or rose quartz block becomes that gem's bee. Fed a netherite block, it becomes the Ancient Bee, whose combs give netherite scrap one time in ten."
  ],
  "quest.5851DE193CB09D11.title": "Mekanism",
  "quest.5851DE193CB09D11.quest_desc": [
    "Osmium and Glowing give refined glowstone; Osmium and Obsidian, refined obsidian. A Water Bee given a bucket of Mekanism's lithium becomes a Lithium Bee, whose combs a chemical oxidizer turns into lithium."
  ],
  "quest.640C5DF154FA9D17.title": "Applied Energistics",
  "quest.640C5DF154FA9D17.quest_desc": [
    "A Spacial Bee given a fluix pearl turns Fluix. A Copper or Osmium egg thrown into lava with charged certus and sky stone becomes Sky Bronze or Sky Osmium; a Spacial egg with a sky steel block, Sky Steel; a Fluix egg in water with entro dust, Entro."
  ],
  "quest.53D054BA4285FB3F.title": "Ender IO alloys",
  "quest.53D054BA4285FB3F.quest_desc": [
    "The alloy smelter fuses bee eggs: Iron and Copper into Conductive Alloy, Redstone and Silicon into Redstone Alloy, Redstone, Gold and Glowing into Energetic, Energetic and Ender into Vibrant, Iron and Ender into Pulsating."
  ],
  "quest.4E092E2386391602.title": "Dark steel and soularium",
  "quest.4E092E2386391602.quest_desc": [
    "Iron and Obsidian eggs with coal dust smelt into Dark Steel; end stone with Dark Steel and Obsidian, End Steel; Ghostly and Gold, Soularium. Infinity comes from a feeding slab: a Blazing Bee visiting an Obsidian egg."
  ],
  "quest.5AF4FE731A11C4BF.title": "Powah",
  "quest.5AF4FE731A11C4BF.quest_subtitle": "Charge the bee, not the battery.",
  "quest.5AF4FE731A11C4BF.quest_desc": [
    "The energizing orb climbs Powah's ladder with bee eggs: two Iron and a Gold with energized steel blocks make Energized Steel, then Blazing, Niotic, Spirited and Nitro crystals, each fed the eggs below it. Nitro costs two billion FE."
  ],
  "quest.010EEE4C3B363FE6.title": "Workshop metals",
  "quest.010EEE4C3B363FE6.quest_desc": [
    "An Iron egg in a pressure chamber at 2 bar hatches Compressed Iron; IE's squeezer presses two Coal eggs into HOP Graphite; a Crystalline Bee fed a black quartz block, Black Quartz; a Diamond Bee fed an infused diamond, Dimensional Shard; Flux comes from the feeding slab."
  ],
  "quest.1F890FDE5BBFAB6F.title": "Crimson, azure and super XP",
  "quest.1F890FDE5BBFAB6F.quest_desc": [
    "Iron and Blazing give Silent Gear's crimson iron, and Crimson Iron with Ender, azure silver. An Experience Bee fed a super enchanting template becomes the Super Experience Bee of Create Enchantment Industry."
  ],
  "quest.5C21D12EC528C301.title": "Bees that won't pair up",
  "quest.5C21D12EC528C301.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Many mod bees cannot breed with their own kind: the upper Mystical Agriculture tiers, the sky metals, the fusion bees and several Oritech and Powah bees each take another egg. Park one in a hive and let the combs do the rest.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7EED2F978C4BDF06.title": "Oritech alloys",
  "quest.7EED2F978C4BDF06.quest_desc": [
    "Oritech's foundry fuses eggs: Diamond and Nickel into Adamant, raw biopolymer and Iron into Biosteel, Platinum and Netherite into Duratium, Nickel and Fluxite into Energite. The grinder turns a Platinum egg into Fluxite."
  ],
  "quest.382D6E1DB419F015.title": "Oritech's strange liquids",
  "quest.382D6E1DB419F015.quest_desc": [
    "A Lava Bee given an Oritech bucket may turn: sulfuric acid eight times in ten, sheol fire half the time, strange matter one time in five. A Radioactive Bee fed plutonium dust becomes Uranite Crystal."
  ],
  "quest.197E91F71A8237F4.title": "Draconic Evolution",
  "quest.197E91F71A8237F4.quest_subtitle": "Fusion, but make it buzz.",
  "quest.197E91F71A8237F4.quest_desc": [
    "Fusion crafting takes a Draconic Bee egg to Draconium at wyvern tier, Draconium to Awakened at draconic tier, and Awakened to Chaos at chaotic tier, for up to 64 million FE."
  ],
  "quest.104808A7F29733EF.title": "Modern Industrialization",
  "quest.104808A7F29733EF.quest_desc": [
    "MI's electrolyzer splits three Emerald eggs into a Beryllium egg, its centrifuge six Iron eggs into a Manganese egg, and a Sulfur Bee fed a monazite block becomes Monazite."
  ],
  "quest.1C397532F8FEF781.title": "Just Dire Things",
  "quest.1C397532F8FEF781.quest_desc": [
    "Feed a Goo block to the right bee: tier 1 turns an Iron Bee Ferricore, tier 2 a Gold Bee Blazegold, tier 3 a Diamond Bee Celestigem, tier 4 an Ancient Bee Eclipse Alloy."
  ],
  "quest.744A3A5DEBBE4EF1.title": "Bees for space",
  "quest.744A3A5DEBBE4EF1.quest_subtitle": "One small step for a bee.",
  "quest.744A3A5DEBBE4EF1.quest_desc": [
    "Ad Astra's metals are mutations in a row: a Steel Bee fed a desh block turns Desh, Desh fed ostrum turns Ostrum, Ostrum fed calorite turns Calorite. The Cheese Bee is a Rancher's work on a cheese block."
  ],
  "quest.07E7E98882856A70.title": "Mystical Agriculture",
  "quest.07E7E98882856A70.quest_subtitle": "Essence, by the comb.",
  "quest.07E7E98882856A70.quest_desc": [
    "The infusion altar climbs the tiers with bee eggs: a Prosperity egg with inferium blocks and essence becomes Inferium, Inferium becomes Prudentium, and so on to Supremium. Inferium combs give two to four essence each."
  ],
  "quest.791ED9D0AF6167E2.title": "Prosperity, soulium and awakening",
  "quest.791ED9D0AF6167E2.quest_desc": [
    "A Crystalline Bee fed a prosperity block turns Prosperity; a Ghostly Bee given a soulium dagger turns Soulium. The awakening altar wakes a Supremium egg with four awakened supremium blocks and 20 of each elemental essence."
  ],
  "quest.24F6391602BEB257.title": "Ars Nouveau",
  "quest.24F6391602BEB257.quest_desc": [
    "The enchanting apparatus turns an Amethyst egg ringed by eight source gems into an Arcane Bee, whose combs give source gems. An Arcane egg with the right eggs and items on the pedestals, for 10,000 source, becomes one of the four essence bees."
  ],
  "quest.50E49156C7CAB54A.title": "Nature's Aura",
  "quest.50E49156C7CAB54A.quest_desc": [
    "The natural altar infuses an Iron egg with 15,000 aura into Infused Iron and a Gold egg with 3,000 into Tainted Gold. The offering table raises those two, with a calling spirit, into Sky Ingot and Depth Ingot."
  ],
  "quest.7ACCFA699A46A465.title": "Forbidden and Arcanus",
  "quest.7ACCFA699A46A465.quest_desc": [
    "A Diamond Bee fed an arcane crystal block turns Arcane Crystal, and that one fed a rune block turns Rune. The clibano's soul fire bakes a bee egg into Deorum; the Hephaestus forge raises a Diamond egg into Stellarite."
  ],
  "quest.59AF8487A39F1F7F.title": "The Undergarden",
  "quest.59AF8487A39F1F7F.quest_desc": [
    "An Iron Bee fed a cloggrum block turns Cloggrum, and Cloggrum with Frosty gives Froststeel. A Gold Bee given the Gloomper Anthem disc turns Regalium. Utheric Bees hide in gloomgourds, and Forgotten eggs in catacomb chests."
  ],
  "quest.424D3EB266E2D6E5.title": "Dark arts",
  "quest.424D3EB266E2D6E5.quest_desc": [
    "A Diamond egg ringed by arcane essence crafts an Arcane Essence Bee for Iron's Spells. Occultism's spiritfire turns a Silver egg into Iesnium. Eight filled blood orbs around a Nomad egg make a Bloody Bee, and a Diamond Bee fed a dark gem block turns Dark Gem."
  ],
  "quest.47E71767822A75B7.title": "Far shores",
  "quest.47E71767822A75B7.quest_desc": [
    "Neptune's Bounty chests hide a Neptunium Bee egg one time in four. The Bee Queen trades a Royal Bee egg for a royal jelly bucket. Modular Bees' Imperial Bee is crafted from two Draconic eggs, two Wanna Bee eggs, a soul treat and four honey jellies."
  ],
  "image.1D70C84C39EC93E6.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Overworld nests\",\"color\":\"#FFD84A\"}]",
  "image.6FE321B2623E99E4.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Nether, End and sea\",\"color\":\"#FFD84A\"}]",
  "image.1AD6FB17C00C7289.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Workers\",\"color\":\"#FFD84A\"}]",
  "image.25C2307AA8A01B58.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The quartz line\",\"color\":\"#FFD84A\"}]",
  "image.7515F54F5C31D003.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Iron and alloys\",\"color\":\"#FFD84A\"}]",
  "image.7BE396AF54E7CD41.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Heavy metals\",\"color\":\"#FFD84A\"}]",
  "image.0732F1E0693720FC.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Sweets and threads\",\"color\":\"#FFD84A\"}]",
  "image.1FA110DD70D3BAB4.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Fire\",\"color\":\"#FFD84A\"}]",
  "image.6FC6F968F68A0F3C.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Undead\",\"color\":\"#FFD84A\"}]",
  "image.051D65812483A91E.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Mutations\",\"color\":\"#FFD84A\"}]",
  "image.5415AA4B8F9980F5.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Gems\",\"color\":\"#FFD84A\"}]",
  "image.593CEF8A70C3A65D.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Machines\",\"color\":\"#FFD84A\"}]",
  "image.21F3F019C360BB7E.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Industry\",\"color\":\"#FFD84A\"}]",
  "image.492469B2E70CAC3A.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Arcana and far corners\",\"color\":\"#FFD84A\"}]",
  "image.159C8522046C1A45.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Productive Bees\",\"color\":\"#FFD84A\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.26618A8F772A81B2.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Breeding Tree\",\"color\":\"#EDE3C4\"}]",
  "image.6FBF57EB2CE9E429.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"roots trunk branch crown\",\"color\":\"#C9B98E\",\"font\":\"minecraft:alt\"}]",
  "image.739DEA68D7B64AC6.title": "Back to the Sun of Heliodor",
  "image.232EAFE80D5F03B1.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"« The Apiary\",\"color\":\"#FFD84A\"}]",
  "chapter.09493272DEE9E76E.title": "The Bumblezone · The Hive",
  "chapter.09493272DEE9E76E.chapter_subtitle": [
    "A dimension inside a beehive: honey on tap, pollen everywhere and bees that remember."
  ],
  "quest.7F28E1B8F31E6ADD.title": "A pearl into a beehive",
  "quest.7F28E1B8F31E6ADD.quest_subtitle": "The door is a hive. The key is a pearl.",
  "quest.7F28E1B8F31E6ADD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Throw an \"},{\"text\":\"Ender Pearl\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:ender_pearl\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" at a \"},{\"text\":\"Bee Nest\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:bee_nest\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" or a \"},{\"text\":\"Beehive\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:beehive\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", in any dimension, and you land inside the Bumblezone. A piston that shoves you into a nest works too.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Your team's first arrival also counts for \"},{\"text\":\"the Atlas\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"5F8D676F685B8FCE\"}},{\"text\":\", even before act IV.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.79EA1C65B8B7325C.title": "A gift for the hive",
  "quest.79EA1C65B8B7325C.quest_subtitle": "The way to a bee's heart is through its stomach.",
  "quest.79EA1C65B8B7325C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Feed \"},{\"text\":\"Honey Bottles\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:honey_bottle\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" to bees or to a \"},{\"text\":\"Honeycomb Brood Block\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:honeycomb_brood_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" until Protection of the Hive kicks in. For 5 minutes bees stay calm around you, and the next thing that would anger them only costs you the effect.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3159CA3F1D7126D2.title": "Honey with permission",
  "quest.3159CA3F1D7126D2.quest_subtitle": "Ask first. Then take the honey.",
  "quest.3159CA3F1D7126D2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"With Protection of the Hive on, take honey from a \"},{\"text\":\"Filled Porous Honeycomb Block\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:filled_porous_honeycomb_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" with a \"},{\"text\":\"Glass Bottle\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:glass_bottle\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", or mine a \"},{\"text\":\"Honey Block\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:honey_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Without it, either one brings Wrath.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Mined, a filled block drops a \"},{\"text\":\"Porous Honeycomb Block\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:porous_honeycomb_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and some \"},{\"text\":\"Honeycomb\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:honeycomb\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; Fortune adds more, Silk Touch keeps it whole.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.44F6D70D92566D98.title": "Honey by the bucket",
  "quest.44F6D70D92566D98.quest_subtitle": "More honey. Always more honey.",
  "quest.44F6D70D92566D98.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Honey is a fluid here: scoop it with a \"},{\"text\":\"Bucket\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", or craft a \"},{\"text\":\"Honey Bucket\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:honey_bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" from four \"},{\"text\":\"Honey Bottles\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:honey_bottle\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" or a \"},{\"text\":\"Honey Block\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:honey_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a bucket. It flows slowly and slows anything wading in it.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Where honey touches water or any other fluid but lava, it hardens into \"},{\"text\":\"Glistering Honey Crystal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:glistering_honey_crystal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; poured in the Nether, it sets into that crystal at once.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.18245D35F255C67B.title": "Crystal shards",
  "quest.18245D35F255C67B.quest_subtitle": "Teeth-shattering snacks.",
  "quest.18245D35F255C67B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Break \"},{\"text\":\"Honey Crystal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:honey_crystal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in caves and underwater for \"},{\"text\":\"Honey Crystal Shards\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:honey_crystal_shards\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; Fortune drops more. The crystal never grows back, so dig with purpose: shards make the compass, a shield and a cannon.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3D2652F97EBFEB82.title": "The Honey Compass",
  "quest.3D2652F97EBFEB82.quest_subtitle": "Is this even still a compass?",
  "quest.3D2652F97EBFEB82.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Craft a \"},{\"text\":\"Compass\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:compass\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" with a \"},{\"text\":\"Honey Bucket\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:honey_bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a \"},{\"text\":\"Honey Crystal Shard\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:honey_crystal_shards\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a \"},{\"text\":\"Pollen Puff\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:pollen_puff\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; the bucket comes back. Right-click the air in the Bumblezone and it tracks down the nearest Cell Maze.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Right-click a beehive or bee nest instead and the needle locks onto that block: a way home through the comb.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.27F798B570A3551C.title": "Lost in the cells",
  "quest.27F798B570A3551C.quest_subtitle": "Every corridor looks like the last one.",
  "quest.27F798B570A3551C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Follow the compass to a Cell Maze: corridors of comb full of \"},{\"text\":\"Honey Cocoons\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:honey_cocoon\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" with loot. Walking in without protection brings Wrath, so wear \"},{\"text\":\"Flower Headwear\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"79131B8ED1898017\"}},{\"text\":\" or earn Protection first.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0A933485DD35E596.title": "Off to see the Queen",
  "quest.0A933485DD35E596.quest_subtitle": "The needle knows the way.",
  "quest.0A933485DD35E596.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Some \"},{\"text\":\"Honey Cocoons\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:honey_cocoon\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in Cell Mazes hide a Honey Compass locked onto a Throne Pillar. Open them until one turns up; the Battle Cubes and the Honitel can hold one too.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6EE9C40B61ECB519.title": "An audience with the Queen",
  "quest.6EE9C40B61ECB519.quest_subtitle": "Mind your manners. She is enormous.",
  "quest.6EE9C40B61ECB519.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Bee Queen lives in the Throne Pillar. Near her you mine with Mining Fatigue, so don't come to dig: come to trade. The court continues in \"},{\"text\":\"The Queen's Court\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"19A133576F44FD8C\"}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.387BFA41046866DE.title": "The way out",
  "quest.387BFA41046866DE.quest_subtitle": "Falling was never this safe.",
  "quest.387BFA41046866DE.quest_desc": [
    "Drop below the floor or fly above the ceiling of the Bumblezone: instead of dying, you teleport out, back to the world you came from.",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Floor and ceiling are \"},{\"text\":\"Beehive Beeswax\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:beehive_beeswax\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", quick to break with an axe: dig down and let yourself drop.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.595734D3947891CD.title": "A bed that stays in one piece",
  "quest.595734D3947891CD.quest_subtitle": "Sweeter dreams.",
  "quest.595734D3947891CD.quest_desc": [
    "Sleep in one to set your respawn point inside the Bumblezone. Unlike the Nether, nothing here explodes."
  ],
  "quest.236E007E57109832.title": "Pushed in",
  "quest.236E007E57109832.quest_subtitle": "Doors are overrated.",
  "quest.236E007E57109832.quest_desc": [
    "You entered the Bumblezone the rude way: shoved into a hive by a piston."
  ],
  "reward.21749C124DFE1155.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.47C889B23C8B0BAB.title": "Hive rules",
  "quest.47C889B23C8B0BAB.quest_desc": [
    "The act IV compass points here, and your team's first arrival is recorded for the Atlas. Nothing gates the entry. Wrath of the Hive only exists inside this dimension: the bees back home stay calm."
  ],
  "quest.425D89601FD767DC.title": "What angers the hive",
  "quest.425D89601FD767DC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Hitting a bee, taking honey from a filled porous comb, killing a brood larva, mining a Honey Block or walking into a Cell Maze unprotected all bring Wrath of the Hive: for 84 seconds, every bee within 64 blocks hunts you.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The angry bees get faster and hit harder. Burying yourself in a deep \"},{\"text\":\"Pile of Pollen\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:pile_of_pollen\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" makes the swarm lose your trail.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0FC2E13C796C22CC.title": "A peace offering",
  "quest.0FC2E13C796C22CC.quest_subtitle": "Bribery works on bees too.",
  "quest.0FC2E13C796C22CC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Wrath can be negotiated: give an angry bee a \"},{\"text\":\"Sugar Water Bottle\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:sugar_water_bottle\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" while the swarm chases you. Each one has a chance to lift the effect, if you last that long.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5089959642B7A161.title": "Bodyguards with wings",
  "quest.5089959642B7A161.quest_subtitle": "Behold, my bees.",
  "quest.5089959642B7A161.quest_desc": [
    "While you have Protection of the Hive, whoever hits you gets the nearby bees on their case. Let a zombie try it."
  ],
  "quest.79131B8ED1898017.title": "Dress as a flower",
  "quest.79131B8ED1898017.quest_subtitle": "Bees can't resist a good hat.",
  "quest.79131B8ED1898017.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight flowers around a \"},{\"text\":\"Leather Cap\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:leather_helmet\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make \"},{\"text\":\"Flower Headwear\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:flower_headwear\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Bees take you for a giant flower: Wrath wears off twice as fast, and walking into a Cell Maze no longer angers them.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"It dyes like leather armor, and with four or more bee wearables on, Wrath fades faster still.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7E7C71DD54A899AC.title": "Not the bees",
  "quest.7E7C71DD54A899AC.quest_subtitle": "It was not a good idea. It never is.",
  "quest.7E7C71DD54A899AC.quest_desc": [
    "You hit a bee while the hive was already angry. Bold, and very loud."
  ],
  "reward.7A47F7C507878526.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.617902D4046FCAA9.title": "A bucket of romance",
  "quest.617902D4046FCAA9.quest_subtitle": "Bees, but make it a date.",
  "quest.617902D4046FCAA9.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Use a \"},{\"text\":\"Honey Bucket\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:honey_bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on an adult bee: it and the bees around it fall in love at once. On any bee, it also heals it fully.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4892E3A3531DBDE3.title": "They grow up so fast",
  "quest.4892E3A3531DBDE3.quest_subtitle": "Yesterday it was a larva.",
  "quest.4892E3A3531DBDE3.quest_desc": [
    "On a baby bee, the same bucket has a chance to turn it into an adult on the spot.",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Dispensers use Honey Buckets too, so a hive can look after itself.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6CCCE459930D2729.title": "Brood blocks",
  "quest.6CCCE459930D2729.quest_subtitle": "A nursery you can mine. Please don't.",
  "quest.6CCCE459930D2729.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A larva lives inside every \"},{\"text\":\"Honeycomb Brood Block\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:honeycomb_brood_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", grows through four stages and then hatches a bee or a Honey Slime. Honey Buckets speed it up; so do Honey Bottles and Sugar Water.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A comparator reads the stage, 1 to 4. Bottling its honey, or mining it without Silk Touch, kills the larva and angers the bees.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7D3212C3DD35E4F0.title": "Refillable comb",
  "quest.7D3212C3DD35E4F0.quest_subtitle": "A honey battery.",
  "quest.7D3212C3DD35E4F0.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Empty \"},{\"text\":\"Porous Honeycomb Blocks\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:porous_honeycomb_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" store honey: fill them with bottles or buckets, or let pollinated bees fill them by touch. A comparator reads 1 once one is full.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.20A09B7AD661AF86.title": "Honey for the common store",
  "quest.20A09B7AD661AF86.quest_subtitle": "Sticky, but it pays.",
  "quest.20A09B7AD661AF86.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Sixteen \"},{\"text\":\"Honey Bottles\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:honey_bottle\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for the depot. With porous comb and Protection of the Hive, it's a quiet afternoon.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7DA78DED148D9FC4.title": "Honey Slimes",
  "quest.7DA78DED148D9FC4.quest_subtitle": "Who needs bees?",
  "quest.7DA78DED148D9FC4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Use a \"},{\"text\":\"Honey Bucket\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:honey_bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on a small or medium Slime and it becomes a Honey Slime. A \"},{\"text\":\"Glass Bottle\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:glass_bottle\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on an adult gives a \"},{\"text\":\"Honey Bottle\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:honey_bottle\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; \"},{\"text\":\"Sugar\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:sugar\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" lures and breeds them.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Kill one and the Honey Slimes nearby come for revenge.\",\"color\":\"#FF8C7A\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0B6356FA544BB1FF.title": "A crystal, intact",
  "quest.0B6356FA544BB1FF.quest_subtitle": "A delicate touch.",
  "quest.0B6356FA544BB1FF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Mine \"},{\"text\":\"Honey Crystal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:honey_crystal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" with Silk Touch to keep the block. It sticks to any face, even upside down, and water that floods it turns into Sugar Water.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6D2B8D19AE95DBAD.title": "Let there be light",
  "quest.6D2B8D19AE95DBAD.quest_subtitle": "Honey, but it glows.",
  "quest.6D2B8D19AE95DBAD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Glistering Honey Crystal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:glistering_honey_crystal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" grows in the Crystal Canyon, or craft it from four shards. It gives light, breaks into a heap of shards and turns neighboring water into Sugar Water.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.677C609A4A78B14F.title": "Pack Silk Touch",
  "quest.677C609A4A78B14F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Silk Touch keeps Honey Crystal, a filled porous comb still full, a brood block with its larva alive, a \"},{\"text\":\"Honey Cocoon\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:honey_cocoon\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" with its loot, and a full Pile of Pollen. Without it, all five break into bits or anger the hive.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.232A845F73AB4065.title": "Sticky residue",
  "quest.232A845F73AB4065.quest_subtitle": "Wall-climbing, by the gram.",
  "quest.232A845F73AB4065.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Smelt shards, \"},{\"text\":\"Honey Crystal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:honey_crystal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" or a \"},{\"text\":\"Honey Block\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:honey_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" into \"},{\"text\":\"Sticky Honey Residue\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:sticky_honey_residue\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". On walls it slows mobs and lets you climb; rinse it off with water or a wet sponge.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A Glistering Honey Crystal smelts into nine residue, a Honey Block into six.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.432D207D8CC55FB8.title": "Sticky redstone",
  "quest.432D207D8CC55FB8.quest_subtitle": "Thinking with honey.",
  "quest.432D207D8CC55FB8.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Residue plus \"},{\"text\":\"Redstone Dust\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:redstone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" makes \"},{\"text\":\"Sticky Honey Redstone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:sticky_honey_redstone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", which outputs a signal of 1 while a mob is stuck in it. Three residue in a column make \"},{\"text\":\"Honey Web\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:honey_web\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", and it has a redstone version too.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.69727C5872B89D4E.title": "A shield of shards",
  "quest.69727C5872B89D4E.quest_subtitle": "Starts fragile. Grows on you.",
  "quest.69727C5872B89D4E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Seven shards make a \"},{\"text\":\"Honey Crystal Shield\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:honey_crystal_shield\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It starts weak, and every repair with shards at an \"},{\"text\":\"Anvil\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:anvil\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" levels it up, to about twice a vanilla shield's durability at the top.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Explosions and fire always hit it hard\",\"color\":\"#FF8C7A\"},{\"text\":\", and it takes no Mending. Mobs that strike it are slowed for a moment.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4A5585129DECD4BB.title": "Play catch with a bee",
  "quest.4A5585129DECD4BB.quest_subtitle": "A beeball home run.",
  "quest.4A5585129DECD4BB.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Throw a \"},{\"text\":\"Pollen Puff\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:pollen_puff\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" at an unpollinated bee and it's pollinated on the spot. Where a puff lands it leaves a \"},{\"text\":\"Pile of Pollen\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:pile_of_pollen\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Mining a pile without Silk Touch gives puffs back, more with Fortune.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6936808FB6087741.title": "Flowers on demand",
  "quest.6936808FB6087741.quest_subtitle": "The crazy florist starts here.",
  "quest.6936808FB6087741.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A puff that lands on a flower may make it reproduce, tall flowers included. Free flowers for \"},{\"text\":\"Flower Headwear\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:flower_headwear\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5F3EC38272768C95.title": "Unbeelievably ineffective",
  "quest.5F3EC38272768C95.quest_subtitle": "You brought a puff to a fireball fight.",
  "quest.5F3EC38272768C95.quest_desc": [
    "You answered a Ghast's fireball with a ball of pollen. It did nothing, and it was glorious."
  ],
  "reward.3B18B161166BD123.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.7C068141AD48CD60.title": "Bath time for bees",
  "quest.7C068141AD48CD60.quest_subtitle": "Bee clean.",
  "quest.7C068141AD48CD60.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Right-click a pollinated bee with a \"},{\"text\":\"Wet Sponge\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:wet_sponge\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a water bottle or a water bucket and it drops its pollen as a \"},{\"text\":\"Pollen Puff\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:pollen_puff\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1BC4648BC38530BB.title": "Tactical pollen",
  "quest.1BC4648BC38530BB.quest_subtitle": "Stealth, but sneezier.",
  "quest.1BC4648BC38530BB.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Bury yourself fully in a deep \"},{\"text\":\"Pile of Pollen\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:pile_of_pollen\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" to become Hidden: hostile mobs notice you from closer, and an angry swarm loses your trail.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.249D969CB96426B5.title": "Trust fall",
  "quest.249D969CB96426B5.quest_subtitle": "Stuffy nose, intact knees.",
  "quest.249D969CB96426B5.quest_desc": [
    "You jumped from high up into thick pollen and walked away. The pile took the landing."
  ],
  "reward.702B29691BB95A8A.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.0C780854B8740FBB.title": "Pollen with a surprise",
  "quest.0C780854B8740FBB.quest_subtitle": "Archaeology, sneezier edition.",
  "quest.0C780854B8740FBB.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Suspicious Pile of Pollen\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:pile_of_pollen_suspicious\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" hides loot: work it with a \"},{\"text\":\"Brush\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:brush\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Banner patterns, enchanted bee armor and books of Hive Lifeline come out of these.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7C271D916A7B6D49.title": "Bless you, panda",
  "quest.7C271D916A7B6D49.quest_subtitle": "Seasonal allergies are real.",
  "quest.7C271D916A7B6D49.quest_desc": [
    "A Pollen Puff to the face made a panda sneeze."
  ],
  "reward.0DD35B9DFEAC215A.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.0E7EB1AFA51B6708.title": "Sugar water",
  "quest.0E7EB1AFA51B6708.quest_subtitle": "Water, but make it sweet.",
  "quest.0E7EB1AFA51B6708.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Water Bucket\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:water_bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and \"},{\"text\":\"Sugar\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:sugar\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" craft a \"},{\"text\":\"Sugar Water Bucket\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:sugar_water_bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; the dimension's floor is full of it too. It behaves like water: it hydrates farmland and keeps coral alive.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Sugar Water Bottle\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:sugar_water_bottle\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" gives a short burst of Haste when you drink it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1E3F67F5B01BF79F.title": "Cane at full speed",
  "quest.1E3F67F5B01BF79F.quest_subtitle": "Soon it'll all be sugar cane.",
  "quest.1E3F67F5B01BF79F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Sugar Water next to \"},{\"text\":\"Sugar Cane\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:sugar_cane\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" makes it grow much faster, and the bonus stacks up to four times.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5CC290CD63160CED.title": "Candied stone",
  "quest.5CC290CD63160CED.quest_subtitle": "Lava plus sugar water: dessert.",
  "quest.5CC290CD63160CED.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Where Sugar Water meets lava you get \"},{\"text\":\"Sugar Infused Stone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:sugar_infused_stone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" or \"},{\"text\":\"Sugar Infused Cobblestone\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:sugar_infused_cobblestone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Both sweeten the water they touch, smelt back to plain stone for a little XP, and build the \"},{\"text\":\"Bee Cannon\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"339BF316B129A6AA\"}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3A5FFFB9F6B7AF9B.title": "Bee Bread",
  "quest.3A5FFFB9F6B7AF9B.quest_subtitle": "Gross-looking, bee-approved.",
  "quest.3A5FFFB9F6B7AF9B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Pollen Puff\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:pollen_puff\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and a \"},{\"text\":\"Honey Bottle\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:honey_bottle\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make \"},{\"text\":\"Bee Bread\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:bee_bread\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; three puffs and a Honey Bucket make three. Bees fed with it get Beenergized and fly faster.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"You can eat it too, if a couple of seconds of dizziness don't scare you.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6845E805B6FA5BBC.title": "Speedy buzzy bees",
  "quest.6845E805B6FA5BBC.quest_subtitle": "Zoom.",
  "quest.6845E805B6FA5BBC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Keep feeding one bee \"},{\"text\":\"Bee Bread\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:bee_bread\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" until its Beenergized is maxed out. The same effect stretches the flight of a \"},{\"text\":\"Bumble Bee Chestplate\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:bumble_bee_chestplate_1\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.401DD941C6165B47.title": "Bee Soup",
  "quest.401DD941C6165B47.quest_subtitle": "It makes your toes curl.",
  "quest.401DD941C6165B47.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Bee Bread\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:bee_bread\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a \"},{\"text\":\"Bowl\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:bowl\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a beetroot, a potato, two honeycombs and a \"},{\"text\":\"Bee Stinger\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:bee_stinger\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make \"},{\"text\":\"Bee Soup\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:bee_soup\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": a long Beenergized II, and maybe Levitation, Slow Falling, Poison, Paralysis or Luck.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.464C8437DCEB6D38.title": "Hive brewing",
  "quest.464C8437DCEB6D38.quest_subtitle": "Three new ways to ruin a mob's day.",
  "quest.464C8437DCEB6D38.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"On an Awkward Potion in a \"},{\"text\":\"Brewing Stand\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:brewing_stand\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", \"},{\"text\":\"Glistering Honey Crystal\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:glistering_honey_crystal\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" brews Luck, a \"},{\"text\":\"Bee Stinger\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:bee_stinger\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" brews Long Poison and \"},{\"text\":\"Bee Soup\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:bee_soup\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" brews Neurotoxin. Redstone lengthens the Neurotoxin.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2B44C41E7187747D.title": "The whole gift box",
  "quest.2B44C41E7187747D.quest_subtitle": "A delicate touch.",
  "quest.2B44C41E7187747D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Silk Touch lifts a \"},{\"text\":\"Honey Cocoon\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:honey_cocoon\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" with its loot still inside. It works as storage too, but left underwater it slowly loses items.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4A40C5AE82E3B3E5.title": "Free real estate",
  "quest.4A40C5AE82E3B3E5.quest_subtitle": "For bees, anyway.",
  "quest.4A40C5AE82E3B3E5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight \"},{\"text\":\"Beehive Beeswax\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:beehive_beeswax\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" around a \"},{\"text\":\"Honeycomb\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:honeycomb\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" craft a \"},{\"text\":\"Bee Nest\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:bee_nest\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Floor and ceiling are beeswax, so the Queen's \"},{\"text\":\"housing order\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"16DF138C0B556301\"}},{\"text\":\" never runs short.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.037E8A896AFD00F5.title": "Comb Cutter",
  "quest.037E8A896AFD00F5.quest_subtitle": "Collecting more rent from bees.",
  "quest.037E8A896AFD00F5.quest_desc": [
    "Swords and shears take this enchantment, and the Enchanting Table offers it on swords. It cuts comb, hives, nests and wax fast, and doubles what a Bee Nest or Beehive drops."
  ],
  "quest.749B4E399EE43FA9.title": "Nine carvings",
  "quest.749B4E399EE43FA9.quest_subtitle": "Bold and brash.",
  "quest.749B4E399EE43FA9.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Nine \"},{\"text\":\"Honeycomb\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:honeycomb\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", or beeswax in a furnace, make \"},{\"text\":\"Carvable Wax\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:carvable_wax\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Right-click it with shears or a sword to cycle its nine patterns; a comparator reads which one is showing.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.153B31DF97326930.title": "Super Candles",
  "quest.153B31DF97326930.quest_subtitle": "Mood lighting, industrial scale.",
  "quest.153B31DF97326930.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"String\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:string\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" over two \"},{\"text\":\"Carvable Wax\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:carvable_wax\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" makes a \"},{\"text\":\"Super Candle\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:super_candle\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": plenty of light, and anything standing in the flame catches fire. On soul sand or soul soil the flame turns blue and scares Piglins away.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5E16050D8F0E84FD.title": "Bee-proof curtains",
  "quest.5E16050D8F0E84FD.quest_subtitle": "The late sixties strike back.",
  "quest.5E16050D8F0E84FD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Sticks, string, glass and a dye craft a \"},{\"text\":\"String Curtain\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:string_curtain_yellow\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Right-click it with string to extend it down; bees and other flying insects barely get through, and it muffles vibrations for sculk.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5D23AB3A8AD69B98.title": "A bee you can ride",
  "quest.5D23AB3A8AD69B98.quest_subtitle": "Bee Movie, but 300% larger.",
  "quest.5D23AB3A8AD69B98.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Beehemoths only follow you while you hold a \"},{\"text\":\"Honey Bucket\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:honey_bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; feed them honey until one is tamed, then put a \"},{\"text\":\"Saddle\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:saddle\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on it. They're most common in the Bumbling Beepartments biome.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Fly up with \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.the_bumblezone.beehemoth_up\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" and down with \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.the_bumblezone.beehemoth_down\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2D3A96C8E7956CB3.title": "Friends till the very end",
  "quest.2D3A96C8E7956CB3.quest_subtitle": "Regal, and fast.",
  "quest.2D3A96C8E7956CB3.quest_desc": [
    "Feeding and riding raise a Beehemoth's friendship up to 1000; at the top it becomes a Queen Beehemoth and flies at full speed. Damage lowers friendship, and at zero it goes wild again.",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Royal Jelly Bucket\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:royal_jelly_bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" turns a Beehemoth into a queen on the spot.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.790024EFEE529DFB.title": "A shiny bee",
  "quest.790024EFEE529DFB.quest_subtitle": "Same bee, better outfit.",
  "quest.790024EFEE529DFB.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"About one bee in twenty wears a different coat: sixteen variants, from Redtail to Rainbow. They behave like any bee; put a \"},{\"text\":\"Name Tag\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:name_tag\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on one to keep it around.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7AE313F6B1E7E8A9.title": "Rootmins",
  "quest.7AE313F6B1E7E8A9.quest_subtitle": "The grass is shooting at you.",
  "quest.7AE313F6B1E7E8A9.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"In the Floral Meadows, some grass blocks are Rootmins in disguise, and they pelt anyone without bee wearables with \"},{\"text\":\"Dirt Pellets\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:dirt_pellet\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". With bee armor on, right-click one with a flower to swap the one on its head; then throw a pellet back, for fairness.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.529F3341F5E5F853.title": "What does it mean?",
  "quest.529F3341F5E5F853.quest_subtitle": "Rainbow roots.",
  "quest.529F3341F5E5F853.quest_desc": [
    "A Rootmin named jeb_ goes rainbow, like the sheep. Some jokes are older than the pack."
  ],
  "reward.0B7793ACBFFCCA46.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.3A5A7E9B114449E1.title": "Sky smackdown",
  "quest.3A5A7E9B114449E1.quest_subtitle": "Dirt: the anti-air solution.",
  "quest.3A5A7E9B114449E1.quest_desc": [
    "You downed a Phantom with thrown Dirt Pellets, which hit flying mobs harder."
  ],
  "reward.6A3805C4CF11CB35.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.1F3224E60E1C6A3C.title": "Places inside the hive",
  "quest.1F3224E60E1C6A3C.quest_subtitle": "The puns are not ours.",
  "quest.1F3224E60E1C6A3C.quest_desc": [
    "Past the Cell Mazes: Hanging Gardens drop from the ceiling, Honey Fountains pour, and there's a Hive Temple, a pirate ship, a subway and the Battle Cubes. Their cocoons hold compasses that lead to more."
  ],
  "quest.532097AFB2E17182.title": "The Crystalline Flower",
  "quest.532097AFB2E17182.quest_subtitle": "An enchanting table that eats.",
  "quest.532097AFB2E17182.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Find a \"},{\"text\":\"Crystalline Flower\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:crystalline_flower\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in the Gazebuzz Clusters and plant it on Glistering Honey Crystal or amethyst. Feed it items and XP to raise its tier, then enchant books with it: higher tiers offer more enchantments, at higher levels.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "At the top tier it offers treasure enchantments too. It fits up to three on one book, and a mined flower keeps its tier."
  ],
  "quest.1CE853F8B1F3D338.title": "Twelve records",
  "quest.1CE853F8B1F3D338.quest_subtitle": "Gotta hive a dance.",
  "quest.1CE853F8B1F3D338.quest_desc": [
    "The Bumblezone has twelve music discs of its own, from Flight of the Bumblebee to the themes of the Sempiternal Sanctums. Wandering Traders, structure loot and the Queen all carry some."
  ],
  "quest.3DB66EAE519D8F62.title": "Every biome of the hive",
  "quest.3DB66EAE519D8F62.quest_subtitle": "Eight biomes, one very tired pair of wings.",
  "quest.3DB66EAE519D8F62.quest_desc": [
    "Walk the Hive Wall and the Hive Pillar, the Sugar Water Floor, the Pollinated Fields and Pillar, the Floral Meadows, the Crystal Canyon and the Bumbling Beepartments."
  ],
  "quest.46EFB746F8123443.title": "Something in the sugar water",
  "quest.46EFB746F8123443.quest_subtitle": "The fish here are unusual.",
  "quest.46EFB746F8123443.quest_desc": [
    "You fished rare loot out of the Bumblezone. Compasses, cannons, briefcases and even flowers bite here."
  ],
  "reward.2C288577FE210093.title": "Secret found",
  "image.760F22C2A097A244.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Wrath and protection\",\"color\":\"#FFC83D\"}]",
  "image.0F63CB8DF682184E.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"What honey does\",\"color\":\"#FFC83D\"}]",
  "image.7DDA7F2937387262.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Crystal and sticky honey\",\"color\":\"#FFC83D\"}]",
  "image.60729519A824A0FE.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Pollen\",\"color\":\"#FFC83D\"}]",
  "image.26EF1A6AE1B126F9.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Sugar and bread\",\"color\":\"#FFC83D\"}]",
  "image.64FD3E1E576C74E7.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Wax and candles\",\"color\":\"#FFC83D\"}]",
  "image.1E56D01F2FB5EC09.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Creatures of the hive\",\"color\":\"#FFC83D\"}]",
  "image.1CB081F6CA20752C.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Around the hive\",\"color\":\"#FFC83D\"}]",
  "image.5D88E9AEE82BA9C6.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Bumblezone\",\"color\":\"#FFC83D\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.1043B8285CE80D4B.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"the hive remembers\",\"color\":\"#F2DCA0\",\"font\":\"minecraft:alt\"}]",
  "image.66CA465AAB4C1FD3.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» The Queen's Court\",\"color\":\"#FFC83D\"}]",
  "image.4BC608FD0122FE81.title": "Back to the Sun of Heliodor",
  "chapter.19A133576F44FD8C.title": "The Bumblezone · The Queen's Court",
  "chapter.19A133576F44FD8C.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Trades, wishes and six sanctums: the end of the hive, with a crystal at its heart."
  ],
  "quest.1C5656CBC74B525B.title": "The Bee Queen",
  "quest.1C5656CBC74B525B.quest_subtitle": "She isn't angry. She's hungry for trades.",
  "quest.1C5656CBC74B525B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Hold an item out to the Queen, or drop it in front of her, and she pays for what she likes. The first trade opens the Queen's Desire: a line of wishes, each paid with a \"},{\"text\":\"Royal Jelly Bottle\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:royal_jelly_bottle\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Hurting her brings Wrath, same as any bee.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4DEF457217A387AF.title": "What she pays for",
  "quest.4DEF457217A387AF.quest_subtitle": "Palace prices.",
  "quest.4DEF457217A387AF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Her tiers follow value. Comb, beeswax, sugar, petals, logs or redstone buy \"},{\"text\":\"Bee Stingers\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:bee_stinger\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and sticks; honey bottles, filled comb, bee bread, flowers and amethyst buy shards, pollen and beeswax.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Diamonds, tall flowers, spore blossoms and redstone blocks buy compasses, spears, shields and cannons. Honey blocks, diamond blocks, bee nests, beehives and Bee Soup buy bee armor, the Buzzing Briefcase and music discs."
  ],
  "quest.00BEE638ED279EBC.title": "Placeable wind",
  "quest.00BEE638ED279EBC.quest_subtitle": "A jetstream in your pocket.",
  "quest.00BEE638ED279EBC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Trade her any bee armor piece, spear, cannon, shield, compass or briefcase and she gives back \"},{\"text\":\"Windy Air\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:windy_air\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": a block that pushes whatever enters it one way. Holding it reveals the Windy Air around you.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.390E042C383B00ED.title": "One hundred and twenty-eight",
  "quest.390E042C383B00ED.quest_subtitle": "The title is earned.",
  "quest.390E042C383B00ED.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Trade with the Queen 128 times; any trade counts, bonus or not. It's one of her wishes, and it pays a \"},{\"text\":\"Royal Jelly Bottle\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:royal_jelly_bottle\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0F1E33D10E3D2D79.title": "Her mood of the day",
  "quest.0F1E33D10E3D2D79.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"When she buzzes that she wants something for the next few minutes, that item pays triple for 20 minutes or until she has taken 24 of it. Other trades keep working meanwhile.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4C7C2172F7A0DA0B.title": "Swaps and second chances",
  "quest.4C7C2172F7A0DA0B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"She also recolors: give her dyed wool, glass, concrete, terracotta, beds, candles or shulker boxes and she returns a random color. Dead coral comes back alive, and an \"},{\"text\":\"Empty Honeycomb Brood Block\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:empty_honeycomb_brood_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" comes back with a larva.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.58568AEE06F06D6F.title": "Bread for the common store",
  "quest.58568AEE06F06D6F.quest_subtitle": "Bees eat first. Then the depot.",
  "quest.58568AEE06F06D6F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Twelve \"},{\"text\":\"Bee Bread\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:bee_bread\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for the depot. Three pollen puffs and a Honey Bucket make three at a time.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7FBE29070800138F.title": "Royal powers",
  "quest.7FBE29070800138F.quest_subtitle": "The breakfast of queens.",
  "quest.7FBE29070800138F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Each of the Queen's wishes pays a \"},{\"text\":\"Royal Jelly Bottle\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:royal_jelly_bottle\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Drinking one fills you up and gives Speed II, Jump Boost IV, Slow Falling and Beenergized II, and cures Poison, Weakness and Slowness.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3DB1DB3CB730C998.title": "A bucket of royalty",
  "quest.3DB1DB3CB730C998.quest_subtitle": "Masterful collector.",
  "quest.3DB1DB3CB730C998.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four bottles and a \"},{\"text\":\"Bucket\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" make a \"},{\"text\":\"Royal Jelly Bucket\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:royal_jelly_bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Fed to a bee it gives a huge dose of Beenergized; fed to a Beehemoth it makes it a queen on the spot.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6EF6666BE7044380.title": "Pull, don't push",
  "quest.6EF6666BE7044380.quest_subtitle": "Redstone with manners.",
  "quest.6EF6666BE7044380.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four bottles make a \"},{\"text\":\"Royal Jelly Block\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:royal_jelly_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It sticks like a Honey Block, but pistons can only pull it, never push it: set one by a \"},{\"text\":\"Sticky Piston\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:sticky_piston\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and think flying machines.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2B124593ED1DF779.title": "Jelly back to the throne",
  "quest.2B124593ED1DF779.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A bottle traded back can pay golden apples, a totem or even a beacon. A bucket or a block rolls a better list: enchanted golden apples, 24 End Crystals, two totems and, once in a very long while, a Dragon Egg. Nether Stars left both lists here: they come from the Wither.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.19E6B145BC221411.title": "Potion Candles",
  "quest.19E6B145BC221411.quest_subtitle": "Magic the Candling.",
  "quest.19E6B145BC221411.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"String over two Carvable Wax, plus a \"},{\"text\":\"Royal Jelly Bottle\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:royal_jelly_bottle\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and up to five potions, make a \"},{\"text\":\"Potion Candle\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:potion_candle\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Lit, it gives their blended effect to everything nearby until its power runs out.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.66003E1EDAC90BFD.title": "Trap card",
  "quest.66003E1EDAC90BFD.quest_subtitle": "You activated my trap candle.",
  "quest.66003E1EDAC90BFD.quest_desc": [
    "You lit a harmful instant-effect Potion Candle with a flaming arrow. Whoever stood next to it had a bad moment."
  ],
  "reward.4B4E1B64E7E5A8FF.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.16DF138C0B556301.title": "Housing for the hive",
  "quest.16DF138C0B556301.quest_subtitle": "The market is flooded. With nests.",
  "quest.16DF138C0B556301.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Craft six Bee Nests or Beehives. \"},{\"text\":\"Beehive Beeswax\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"4A40C5AE82E3B3E5\"}},{\"text\":\" makes nests cheap: eight blocks and a honeycomb each.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6A1948A4F5BD417C.title": "Eight bottles, bottoms up",
  "quest.6A1948A4F5BD417C.quest_subtitle": "Hydration, the sweet way.",
  "quest.6A1948A4F5BD417C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Drink eight \"},{\"text\":\"Honey Bottles\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:honey_bottle\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Each one also cures Poison, which the other wishes may make handy.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3E9ABD62042C5F88.title": "Hungry hungry bees",
  "quest.3E9ABD62042C5F88.quest_subtitle": "Feeding time at the hive.",
  "quest.3E9ABD62042C5F88.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Feed bees 24 times with \"},{\"text\":\"Sugar Water\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:sugar_water_bottle\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" or anything made of honey; the same bee or many, it all counts.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6A5DE128DC342A84.title": "Eight new bees",
  "quest.6A5DE128DC342A84.quest_subtitle": "The birds and the bees. Mostly bees.",
  "quest.6A5DE128DC342A84.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Breed bees until eight babies are born. Flowers work, and a \"},{\"text\":\"Honey Bucket\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:honey_bucket\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" sets a whole group in love at once.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7F34D230FB54D43D.title": "Stingers back on",
  "quest.7F34D230FB54D43D.quest_subtitle": "Doctor Bee is in.",
  "quest.7F34D230FB54D43D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A bee that stings loses its stinger and dies soon after. Right-click twelve stingerless bees with a \"},{\"text\":\"Bee Stinger\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:bee_stinger\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" to save them.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.02411962935F6CE2.title": "A snowball fight, with pollen",
  "quest.02411962935F6CE2.quest_subtitle": "Other players count. Warn them first.",
  "quest.02411962935F6CE2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Hit 24 creatures with thrown \"},{\"text\":\"Pollen Puffs\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:pollen_puff\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\"; teammates count too.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.459D7E3C531B073E.title": "Eight flowers from thin air",
  "quest.459D7E3C531B073E.quest_subtitle": "The crazy florist rides again.",
  "quest.459D7E3C531B073E.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Spawn eight flowers by hitting flowers with \"},{\"text\":\"Pollen Puffs\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:pollen_puff\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". A meadow and a stack of puffs make short work of it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.01B747751E2949F4.title": "Six new Honey Slimes",
  "quest.01B747751E2949F4.quest_subtitle": "They really love sugar.",
  "quest.01B747751E2949F4.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Breed Honey Slimes with \"},{\"text\":\"Sugar\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:sugar\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" until six new ones are born. None around? A \"},{\"text\":\"Honey Bucket on a small Slime\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"7DA78DED148D9FC4\"}},{\"text\":\" makes one.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.20AE5D0B7BE74935.title": "Stingers by the quiver",
  "quest.20AE5D0B7BE74935.quest_subtitle": "Arrows with a grudge.",
  "quest.20AE5D0B7BE74935.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Fire 32 \"},{\"text\":\"Bee Stingers\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:bee_stinger\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" from bows or crossbows. They hit softly, but they can poison, weaken, slow or paralyze what they strike.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.61603AD9E1B3C3BB.title": "Pest control",
  "quest.61603AD9E1B3C3BB.quest_subtitle": "The Queen has opinions about bugs.",
  "quest.61603AD9E1B3C3BB.quest_desc": [
    "Kill 32 spiders, 16 cave spiders, 8 silverfish and 4 endermites. Mineshaft spawners have the cave spiders, strongholds the silverfish, and a thrown ender pearl sometimes hatches an endermite."
  ],
  "quest.549876876BBA3B57.title": "The Wither, by spear",
  "quest.549876876BBA3B57.quest_subtitle": "The least efficient victory possible.",
  "quest.549876876BBA3B57.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Land the killing blow on the Wither with a \"},{\"text\":\"Stinger Spear\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"015B1C57907CDD73\"}},{\"text\":\". The undead shrug off its poison, so bring patience and spare spears.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6BD5BFE2C4795CD7.title": "Dragon slayer, bee edition",
  "quest.6BD5BFE2C4795CD7.quest_subtitle": "Legendary, and a little ridiculous.",
  "quest.6BD5BFE2C4795CD7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Kill the Ender Dragon with all four pieces of \"},{\"text\":\"bee armor\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"38A8AD749EA449E6\"}},{\"text\":\" on.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.054E6433C230BD7F.title": "Every wish granted",
  "quest.054E6433C230BD7F.quest_subtitle": "The grand finale of a very demanding queen.",
  "quest.054E6433C230BD7F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"With every wish done, right-click the Queen with an empty hand for her final reward: the \"},{\"text\":\"Essence of the Bees\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:essence_of_the_bees\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Later, another right-click resets her wishes, so the royal jelly keeps coming.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.50DFE8EE5E66D049.title": "One of the hive",
  "quest.50DFE8EE5E66D049.quest_subtitle": "Hope, love, dreams and bees.",
  "quest.50DFE8EE5E66D049.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Consume the \"},{\"text\":\"Essence of the Bees\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:essence_of_the_bees\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and the hive accepts you for good: no Wrath in Cell Mazes, no Mining Fatigue near the Queen, honey and hives are yours without angering anyone, and honey and royal jelly heal you as you swim.\"}]",
    "",
    "It also opens the Sempiternal Sanctums, and by default it lasts through death."
  ],
  "quest.56F766EC2A7BB911.title": "The Sempiternal Sanctums",
  "quest.56F766EC2A7BB911.quest_subtitle": "Six colors, six very long days.",
  "quest.56F766EC2A7BB911.quest_desc": [
    "Sanctum compasses turn up in cocoons all over the dimension, one color each. Inside, Ancient and Luminescent Wax slow, weaken and tire anyone without the essence; with it, the channels give you Speed, Resistance and Beenergized."
  ],
  "quest.08574DB8F1A430DC.title": "The Red Sanctum",
  "quest.08574DB8F1A430DC.quest_subtitle": "Waves of anger, and one rabbit.",
  "quest.08574DB8F1A430DC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Waves of mobs pour in, from husks and spiders to blazes, wither skeletons, hoglins and the Killer Bunny, topped by a Ravager or a Piglin Brute. Beat them before the timer runs out for the \"},{\"text\":\"Essence of Raging\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:essence_raging\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "In the offhand it marks nearby monsters; every marked kill in a row raises your Strength, up to seven, then the chain starts over. Drained, it needs 30 minutes to recharge."
  ],
  "quest.4B7174CC3C5D2971.title": "The Purple Sanctum",
  "quest.4B7174CC3C5D2971.quest_subtitle": "The floor has opinions.",
  "quest.4B7174CC3C5D2971.quest_desc": [
    "Purple spikes burst from the arena floor in patterns; keep moving. This trial is won by staying alive until the timer runs out, a little over four minutes.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"In the offhand, the \"},{\"text\":\"Essence of Knowing\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:essence_knowing\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" highlights mobs from far away, shows chests, spawners and suspicious blocks through walls, and names the structure you're standing in. 15 minutes to recharge.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1F06BFA146FD42E8.title": "The Blue Sanctum",
  "quest.1F06BFA146FD42E8.quest_subtitle": "Drowning in Despair is the song's name.",
  "quest.1F06BFA146FD42E8.quest_desc": [
    "The arena floods. Drowned and guardians close in, an Elder Guardian shows up at the end, and Dense Bubble Blocks are where you catch your breath. Clear it before the timer runs out.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"In the offhand, the \"},{\"text\":\"Essence of Calming\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:essence_calming\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" makes most mobs forget they were angry at you, until you attack or get hit. Sprinting drains it fast; 10 minutes to recharge.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3469847460ABC5B5.title": "The Green Sanctum",
  "quest.3469847460ABC5B5.quest_subtitle": "The grass fights back. Again.",
  "quest.3469847460ABC5B5.quest_desc": [
    "A single Rootmin, boosted with extra health and knockback resistance, holds the arena and changes its mood as the fight goes on. Bring it down before the timer runs out.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"In the offhand, the \"},{\"text\":\"Essence of Life\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:essence_life\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" grows nearby crops and plants and heals your allies and pets, curing their Wither and Poison. 10 minutes to recharge.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5D89181441024606.title": "The Yellow Sanctum",
  "quest.5D89181441024606.quest_subtitle": "Praise the sun.",
  "quest.5D89181441024606.quest_desc": [
    "Electric rings appear around the arena while Vexes harass you; every ring you fly through counts toward the win. Clear enough of them before the timer runs out.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"In the offhand, under open daytime sky, the \"},{\"text\":\"Essence of Radiance\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:essence_radiance\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" gives Regeneration, Speed, Saturation, Resistance II and Haste II, and slowly mends your armor. A light that heals: Heliodor would have approved.\"}]"
  ],
  "task.7C2E416C877C61E7.title": "Break the six Cosmic Crystals",
  "quest.46AFBBC2F7091E8A.title": "The Cosmic Crystal Entity",
  "quest.46AFBBC2F7091E8A.quest_subtitle": "Six crystals, one very bad day.",
  "quest.46AFBBC2F7091E8A.quest_desc": [
    "The White Sanctum's trial: six Cosmic Crystals orbit the arena, fire lasers, spin and ram you, and turn meaner as their number drops. Break all six before the timer runs out.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Each crystal has 60 health and no single hit takes more than 2: fast, steady hits beat one huge swing. Fire does nothing to them.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Winning gives the \"},{\"text\":\"Essence of Continuity\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:essence_continuity\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". In the offhand, a death sends you back to your respawn point instead, healed, with a book about what almost killed you. 40 minutes to recharge.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0141D5FD03C6F696.title": "Six essences",
  "quest.0141D5FD03C6F696.quest_subtitle": "The full set of bad days, survived.",
  "quest.0141D5FD03C6F696.quest_desc": [
    "Hold all six essences at once. Each one recharges only in the inventory of someone who has consumed the Essence of the Bees, and every trial can be run again for another."
  ],
  "quest.5D9195CF9044684B.title": "A clause in wax",
  "quest.5D9195CF9044684B.quest_desc": [
    "Every trade with the Queen is fair: she takes, and she pays back. Juan's one clause, to take nothing you cannot give back, is still kept here, one trade at a time."
  ],
  "quest.457EA779CA572145.title": "Trial rules",
  "quest.457EA779CA572145.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Walk into a sanctum's essence block to start its trial: a boss bar counts down, \"},{\"text\":\"leaving the arena mid-trial kills you\",\"color\":\"#FF8C7A\"},{\"text\":\", and the arena restores itself afterwards. Heavy Air pulls you down and switches off jetpacks.\"}]",
    "",
    "Every trial can be repeated, and each win pays 3000 experience."
  ],
  "quest.56FDAC358FAA0BC7.title": "Ancient wax",
  "quest.56FDAC358FAA0BC7.quest_subtitle": "Perfecting the design.",
  "quest.56FDAC358FAA0BC7.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Sanctum walls are built of \"},{\"text\":\"Ancient Wax Bricks\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:ancient_wax_bricks\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and their kin, nearly blast-proof. Shears or a sword cycle their patterns and turn \"},{\"text\":\"Luminescent Wax Channels\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:luminescent_wax_channel\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" to face new ways.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0473A434F1E7F840.title": "A guardian of your own",
  "quest.0473A434F1E7F840.quest_subtitle": "It won't charge at you. Probably.",
  "quest.0473A434F1E7F840.quest_desc": [
    "Four Ancient Wax around a Luminescent Wax channel, corner or node craft a Sentry Watcher Spawn Egg. The statue charges any non-bee in front of it, harder the faster it goes, but never its owner. Double right-click packs it back up."
  ],
  "quest.182D1E423A353EEA.title": "Sightseeing, bee style",
  "quest.182D1E423A353EEA.quest_subtitle": "Sightbee-er.",
  "quest.182D1E423A353EEA.quest_desc": [
    "Enter every structure the Bumblezone has: 32 of them, from the Honitel to the six sanctums and the Throne Pillar. The hive's longest tour pays 2500 experience."
  ],
  "quest.38A8AD749EA449E6.title": "The Bee Warrior",
  "quest.38A8AD749EA449E6.quest_subtitle": "The bee warrior rises.",
  "quest.38A8AD749EA449E6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Bee armor can't be crafted: it comes from the Queen's richest trades, from Throne Pillar and sanctum loot, and from Suspicious Piles of Pollen. Hold a helmet, chestplate, leggings, boots and a \"},{\"text\":\"Stinger Spear\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:stinger_spear\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" at once.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Each piece has its own trick, and every extra bee wearable makes the others stronger. They repair with honeycomb, leather, wool or rabbit hide."
  ],
  "quest.1596B2F834A90043.title": "Compound eyes",
  "quest.1596B2F834A90043.quest_subtitle": "Where's the bee? Everywhere.",
  "quest.1596B2F834A90043.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Crouch while wearing the \"},{\"text\":\"Stingless Bee Helmet\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:stingless_bee_helmet_1\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" and the bees and Beehemoths nearby glow through walls; light up fifty at once. Nausea also wears off twice as fast.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2DBD9E43BA8567C5.title": "It's a bird, it's a plane",
  "quest.2DBD9E43BA8567C5.quest_subtitle": "No, it's someone in a bee costume.",
  "quest.2DBD9E43BA8567C5.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"With the \"},{\"text\":\"Bumble Bee Chestplate\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:bumble_bee_chestplate_1\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" on, hold \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.jump\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" after a jump to fly for a while. Beenergized stretches the flight; buzz with three other bee pieces on to fly at your best.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5213C7EA31BCC9FA.title": "The bee's knees",
  "quest.5213C7EA31BCC9FA.quest_subtitle": "Pollen in the pockets.",
  "quest.5213C7EA31BCC9FA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Honey Bee Leggings\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:honey_bee_leggings_1\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" shrug off the slowness of sticky blocks and gather pollen as you walk through flowers. Crouch to drop a Pollen Puff when they're full; water or a wet sponge washes them clean.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6A1B3FEFCA75E9BF.title": "Carpenter's boots",
  "quest.6A1B3FEFCA75E9BF.quest_subtitle": "The floor is lava. The wall isn't.",
  "quest.6A1B3FEFCA75E9BF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Carpenter Bee Boots\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:carpenter_bee_boots_1\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" let you hang from and run along wood, planks, leaves and comb. Crouch while looking down at those blocks and the boots bore through them; chew through 64 to prove it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0657CAFE1377D6A2.title": "Hive Lifeline",
  "quest.0657CAFE1377D6A2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"A treasure enchantment for bee armor: it passes a hit you'd take to a nearby bee instead, then rests for a moment. Its books come from Suspicious Piles of Pollen and from a Crystalline Flower at its top tier.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.46D08C3DF83E8097.title": "Grand hive defender",
  "quest.46D08C3DF83E8097.quest_subtitle": "Ten levels of stubbornness.",
  "quest.46D08C3DF83E8097.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Keep repairing a \"},{\"text\":\"Honey Crystal Shield\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:honey_crystal_shield\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" with shards at an anvil until it reaches level 10, the strongest it gets.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0BDD187C050A39EA.title": "Unblockable",
  "quest.0BDD187C050A39EA.quest_subtitle": "Axes weren't the only problem.",
  "quest.0BDD187C050A39EA.quest_desc": [
    "You found a weakness of the Honey Crystal Shield besides axes: explosions and fire wear its patience thin."
  ],
  "reward.1FC30616389A82BB.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.015B1C57907CDD73.title": "The Stinger Spear",
  "quest.015B1C57907CDD73.quest_subtitle": "Two sticks and a grudge.",
  "quest.015B1C57907CDD73.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two sticks and a \"},{\"text\":\"Bee Stinger\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:bee_stinger\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" in a line craft a \"},{\"text\":\"Stinger Spear\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:stinger_spear\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Throw it like a trident; it always leaves a weak poison on anything that isn't undead. Repair it with flint or stingers.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0E9A834691ED0A9D.title": "Potent Poison, Neurotoxins",
  "quest.0E9A834691ED0A9D.quest_subtitle": "Being the bee.",
  "quest.0E9A834691ED0A9D.quest_desc": [
    "The Enchanting Table offers the spear two enchantments of its own: Potent Poison, a stronger and longer poison with each level, and Neurotoxins, a chance to paralyze that drops against mobs with lots of health."
  ],
  "quest.0EDED4F62864F587.title": "Favorable odds",
  "quest.0EDED4F62864F587.quest_subtitle": "Even giants stand still sometimes.",
  "quest.0EDED4F62864F587.quest_desc": [
    "Paralyze a mob with a lot of health using the spear. The odds are low, so throw often; a paralyzed mob stays frozen for up to 30 seconds."
  ],
  "quest.3DADF9C74A6968DC.title": "Endless stinging",
  "quest.3DADF9C74A6968DC.quest_subtitle": "Death by a thousand pricks.",
  "quest.3DADF9C74A6968DC.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Keep shooting \"},{\"text\":\"Bee Stingers\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:bee_stinger\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" from a bow or crossbow at one mob until the pile-up paralyzes it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2D6CFCEC163C2C07.title": "Olympic javelin",
  "quest.2D6CFCEC163C2C07.quest_subtitle": "Somewhere, a crowd cheers.",
  "quest.2D6CFCEC163C2C07.quest_desc": [
    "You killed a mob with a Stinger Spear thrown from very far away."
  ],
  "reward.745858AF654FA095.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.3900AEFE6B72B1A1.title": "The Buzzing Briefcase",
  "quest.3900AEFE6B72B1A1.quest_subtitle": "Bees to go.",
  "quest.3900AEFE6B72B1A1.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Right-click bees with a \"},{\"text\":\"Buzzing Briefcase\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:buzzing_briefcase\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" to carry up to 14. Hold \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.sneak\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" and right-click to heal, re-sting, pollinate or grow them; left-click a block to release one, or a mob to release them angry at it.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"It's a rare trade from the Queen, and it also bites on a fishing line in the Bumblezone.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.339BF316B129A6AA.title": "The Bee Cannon",
  "quest.339BF316B129A6AA.quest_subtitle": "You'd better behave now.",
  "quest.339BF316B129A6AA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Sugar Infused Stone, Sugar Infused Cobblestone and gunpowder craft a \"},{\"text\":\"Bee Cannon\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:bee_cannon\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Load up to three bees, hold use and let go: they chase whatever you were looking at. Sugar-infused stone repairs it.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1EBCAFF5CFE07865.title": "The Crystal Cannon",
  "quest.1EBCAFF5CFE07865.quest_subtitle": "Extreme crowd control.",
  "quest.1EBCAFF5CFE07865.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A \"},{\"text\":\"Bee Cannon\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:bee_cannon\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" between two shards, over a Honey Crystal, makes a \"},{\"text\":\"Crystal Cannon\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"the_bumblezone:crystal_cannon\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": three shards per load, heavy damage and heavy knockback.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.153FA7856FB0C757.title": "Bee collector",
  "quest.153FA7856FB0C757.quest_subtitle": "Gotta catch fourteen.",
  "quest.153FA7856FB0C757.quest_desc": [
    "Fill a briefcase with 14 variant bees; repeats are allowed."
  ],
  "image.0A61ED0C4A8ADD84.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Queen's trades\",\"color\":\"#FFC83D\"}]",
  "image.0C7CDC7596CA7877.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Royal jelly\",\"color\":\"#FFC83D\"}]",
  "image.01A9A2B2216D6304.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Bee armor\",\"color\":\"#FFC83D\"}]",
  "image.0E158427B326A72B.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Stingers and cannons\",\"color\":\"#FFC83D\"}]",
  "image.1A20CB1EB9AC2B20.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Inside the sanctums\",\"color\":\"#FFC83D\"}]",
  "image.204C2222D2E87BF8.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Bumblezone\",\"color\":\"#FFC83D\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.3AC24490B49D2A1A.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"every wish has a price\",\"color\":\"#F2DCA0\",\"font\":\"minecraft:alt\"}]",
  "image.37237F84554EB0B9.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"« The Hive\",\"color\":\"#FFC83D\"}]",
  "image.64EABAD8DEF93EC0.title": "Back to the Sun of Heliodor",
  "chapter.2B47486A10736E41.title": "Ad Astra: rockets and planets",
  "chapter.2B47486A10736E41.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Steel, oxygen and fuel: from the first launch to another solar system."
  ],
  "quest.4B444004D4ACED14.title": "Beyond the sky",
  "quest.4B444004D4ACED14.quest_desc": [
    "Rockets, space suits, oxygen machines and worlds: the Moon, Mars, Venus, Mercury, their orbits and Glacio in another solar system. Each rocket tier unlocks a planet whose metal builds the next rocket: steel, Desh, Ostrum, Calorite.",
    "",
    "Space opens in act V: the NASA Workbench needs an atomic alloy. Steel, energy, oil and oxygen can be ready before."
  ],
  "quest.6CD31724A52E8A85.title": "The Astrodux",
  "quest.6CD31724A52E8A85.quest_desc": [
    "Ad Astra's own guide: a book ringed by iron ingots and blue dye. Its chapters walk the same route with recipes and pictures.",
    "",
    "Nobody hands out books on join here, so craft it yourself."
  ],
  "quest.20AAB21A1B32374E.title": "Carbon Footprint",
  "quest.20AAB21A1B32374E.quest_desc": [
    "Ad Astra machines run on FE. Its Coal Generator burns wood or coal, and any other mod's FE generator works too; Solar Panels produce more, especially near the sun and in orbit.",
    "",
    "The Etrionic Capacitor is a portable battery for machines and your inventory."
  ],
  "quest.6126FC516BA3CEB6.title": "Plates and steel",
  "quest.6126FC516BA3CEB6.quest_desc": [
    "The Compressor presses ingots and blocks into plates, used almost everywhere (Under Pressure). The Etrionic Blast Furnace blasts four slots at once, and in alloying mode turns one iron plus one coal into a Steel Ingot (Smart Blasting).",
    "",
    "Steel builds the first rocket, the suit and the launch pad."
  ],
  "quest.4D9B26FD92C13E4D.title": "Ocean Cleanup",
  "quest.4D9B26FD92C13E4D.quest_desc": [
    "Oil wells spout over ocean biomes in the Overworld: fill buckets there. Oil does not renew, and a Moon round trip burns six buckets of fuel, so collect plenty.",
    "",
    "A powered Fuel Refinery turns oil into rocket fuel."
  ],
  "quest.6D6B547743F538B7.title": "Refined fuel",
  "quest.6D6B547743F538B7.quest_desc": [
    "Oil in the refinery's left slot, fuel out. Three buckets launch the rocket and three more bring you back, all stored in the rocket's own inventory.",
    "",
    "Mars has a better option waiting: Cryo Fuel."
  ],
  "quest.1D2D65C4B7DDAB39.title": "Astronaut",
  "quest.1D2D65C4B7DDAB39.quest_desc": [
    "The full suit (helmet, suit, pants, boots) takes steel plates, wool, a glass pane for the helmet, and a gas tank and oxygen gear for the suit. It stores oxygen; without it the Moon kills you fast.",
    "",
    "The pocket TI-69 shows local oxygen, temperature and gravity. Check it before taking your helmet off."
  ],
  "quest.15752BDB4F142178.title": "Oxygen from water",
  "quest.15752BDB4F142178.quest_desc": [
    "An Oxygen Loader turns water in its left tank into oxygen for your suit and Gas Tanks; holding right-click with a full tank shares it into your inventory, armor first.",
    "",
    "Bring more oxygen than you think. The first trip is always the one that goes wrong."
  ],
  "quest.4B7A356D731AFC7A.title": "The NASA Workbench",
  "quest.4B7A356D731AFC7A.quest_desc": [
    "Every rocket is assembled here (Rocket Science): nose cone, fins, tanks and engine. Its recipe carries an atomic alloy in the top middle slot, so space opens with act V; the rest is steel plates, iron rods, steel blocks, a crafting table and redstone torches."
  ],
  "quest.55E62F8CB61E0090.title": "Baby's First Rocket",
  "quest.55E62F8CB61E0090.quest_desc": [
    "Nose cone, six steel blocks, four fins, two steel tanks and a steel engine. Place it on a Launch Pad (steel plates and rods); a redstone-powered pad launches it once fueled.",
    "",
    "Shift-right-click the rocket to open its inventory and load fuel."
  ],
  "quest.3E1882A814C9C57A.title": "The pre-launch checklist",
  "quest.3E1882A814C9C57A.quest_desc": [
    "Forget one item and you may live on the Moon now. Before jumping in: 3 buckets of fuel in the tank slot, 3 more plus a Launch Pad in the rocket inventory for the return; a full, charged suit and spare Gas Tanks; food, weapons, tools; and soul torches or glowstone, since normal torches go out without oxygen."
  ],
  "quest.1C874811C4A21BF4.title": "One Small Step",
  "quest.1C874811C4A21BF4.quest_desc": [
    "The Moon has no oxygen and is freezing: water freezes, torches break, plants die. Desh, the next metal, waits underground.",
    "",
    "To go home, Shift-right-click the lander to take back rocket, fuel and pad, punch the lander away, set up the pad, place and fuel the rocket and jump."
  ],
  "quest.38C048D4BF0517BC.title": "Lunarians and their traders",
  "quest.38C048D4BF0517BC.quest_desc": [
    "Big underground villages on the Moon house Lunarians, alien villagers who need no oxygen and trade planet materials, suits and oxygen gear. Their wandering traders visit every moon and planet with launch pads, oxygen, fuel, soul torches and water, for emeralds from space structures.",
    "",
    "If a trip goes wrong, one of them is your ticket home."
  ],
  "quest.71161BAE92ED02FC.title": "A room with air",
  "quest.71161BAE92ED02FC.quest_desc": [
    "The Oxygen Distributor fills a sealed room (Take a Deep Breath): feed it water nonstop from a Water Pump on an infinite source, power both, and press \"show\" to see the covered area.",
    "",
    "Cables and pipes leak, so use their duct blocks; 3×3 Sliding Doors seal and make good airlocks. The Gravity Normalizer does the same for gravity, 0 to 2 g."
  ],
  "quest.4BA52976F8727EBB.title": "Space stations",
  "quest.4BA52976F8727EBB.quest_desc": [
    "From the planet screen, build a station in any moon or planet's orbit if you carry the listed materials; nobody else can build in the same spot. Orbit is where Solar Panels shine brightest.",
    "",
    "In zero gravity you float without friction; the Zip Gun burns oxygen to push you around (Unconventional Flight)."
  ],
  "quest.47E25D6FB6A4DA3D.title": "Desh and the Tier 2 Rocket",
  "quest.47E25D6FB6A4DA3D.quest_desc": [
    "Moon Desh makes advanced machines, cables faster than steel, station parts and the Tier 2 Rocket, built like the first with Desh instead of steel (The Next Step).",
    "",
    "Moon cheese is real here. It has its own advancement."
  ],
  "quest.4ECC630DC8A5BE32.title": "A rover",
  "quest.4ECC630DC8A5BE32.quest_desc": [
    "A fast land vehicle for rough terrain: two seats, 16 storage slots, fuel in its left slot, and it hurts what it runs over. Its built-in radio plays real internet stations; open it with &eAlt+R&r here.",
    "",
    "The standalone Radio block is craftable too (DJ)."
  ],
  "quest.290170B66C86597D.title": "The Martian",
  "quest.290170B66C86597D.quest_desc": [
    "The Tier 2 Rocket reaches Mars, home of Ostrum: stronger space armor, better machines and the heat-proof Tier 3 Rocket. The polar caps also hold Ice Shard ore, the base of Cryo Fuel.",
    "",
    "As always, keep a spare pad and fuel for the way back."
  ],
  "quest.7FFBC1246DFE1803.title": "Cryo Fuel",
  "quest.7FFBC1246DFE1803.quest_desc": [
    "The Cryo Freezer turns Ice Shards (ore on the Moon, Mars and Glacio) into 25 mB of Cryo Fuel each; ice, packed ice and blue ice work too. It is about three times as efficient: one bucket per launch, two for a round trip.",
    "",
    "Poured out, it hurts like lava and freezes water. Handle with gloves."
  ],
  "quest.6164BA6BB34CC619.title": "Doom Slayer",
  "quest.6164BA6BB34CC619.quest_desc": [
    "Venus and Mercury burn a normal suit's wearer in seconds. The Netherite Space Suit adds permanent fire resistance and more protection: craft the full set before the Tier 3 Rocket takes you there.",
    "",
    "Sunscreen, but metal."
  ],
  "quest.7866F9F2E4D6B118.title": "The hot planets",
  "quest.7866F9F2E4D6B118.quest_desc": [
    "With the Tier 3 Rocket and the netherite suit, visit Venus (Venusian) and Mercury (Quite the Sun Tan) for Calorite, the metal of the Tier 4 Rocket.",
    "",
    "Solar Panels on Mercury, so close to the sun, produce the most. Heliodor would have loved it there."
  ],
  "quest.647B411C0A583890.title": "Rocket Man",
  "quest.647B411C0A583890.quest_desc": [
    "The Jet Suit upgrades the netherite suit with more protection, more oxygen and flight: jump to rise, jump and sprint to boost like a rocket-powered elytra. It runs on energy, charged at an Energizer; in this pack flight costs 2.5 times as much.",
    "",
    "Toggle its flight with &eCtrl+F4&r in this pack."
  ],
  "quest.4C18B1FEA4AF14BB.title": "Interstellar",
  "quest.4C18B1FEA4AF14BB.quest_desc": [
    "Calorite builds the Tier 4 Rocket, the only one that leaves the solar system (To Infinity and Beyond). First stop in Proxima Centauri: Glacio, brutally cold but breathable, so the helmet can come off (Interstellar).",
    "",
    "The Astrodux says it plainly: Ad Astra's progression ends here, for now."
  ],
  "quest.7A8C4395D7991615.title": "What changes in space",
  "quest.7A8C4395D7991615.quest_desc": [
    "The NASA Workbench needs an atomic alloy, so rockets and planets open during act V; everything before it can be prepared earlier. Ad Astra's old-format compatibility recipes with Create, Mekanism and Immersive Engineering do not load in 1.21.1 and are disabled, and its metals join Almost Unified. Keys: radio &eAlt+R&r, suit flight &eCtrl+F4&r."
  ],
  "quest.1B63ACCAD2B87970.title": "Ad astra",
  "quest.1B63ACCAD2B87970.quest_desc": [
    "From a coal generator to another star: steel, Desh, Ostrum and Calorite, rooms full of air and stations in orbit.",
    "",
    "Heliodor looked at the sky through a telescope. You went."
  ],
  "chapter.7D2C7B91D8E8EE7B.title": "Bosses: vanilla and Mowzie's",
  "chapter.7D2C7B91D8E8EE7B.chapter_subtitle": [
    "The Wither, the Dragon and the Elder Guardian as materials, plus Mowzie's optional mini-bosses."
  ],
  "quest.435A3AA816CEBEC3.title": "Materials, not milestones",
  "quest.435A3AA816CEBEC3.quest_desc": [
    "The Wither, the Ender Dragon and the Elder Guardian matter for their drops: nether stars, dragon hearts and wet sponges feed Luminous gear and act VI's creative items. The compass passes their lairs in act V.",
    "",
    "Mowzie's Mobs adds optional mini-bosses with unique weapons for acts II to IV. None of them closes an act; all of them hit hard."
  ],
  "quest.528E49AE28EBD771.title": "Three wither skeleton skulls",
  "quest.528E49AE28EBD771.quest_desc": [
    "Wither skeletons live in Nether fortresses, rebuilt larger by YUNG's. Skulls are a rare drop, so Looting helps a lot.",
    "",
    "Four soul sand or soul soil blocks in a T, three skulls on top: that is the Wither. Do it far from home."
  ],
  "quest.617F3D63E49031FA.title": "The Wither",
  "quest.617F3D63E49031FA.quest_desc": [
    "Summon it far from your base: it breaks blocks and explodes on spawn. Bring healing, milk for the Wither effect and a strong bow or a Smite sword. It drops a nether star.",
    "",
    "Here it is the only star source: the pack removed Modern Industrialization's implosion, Oritech's particle collision and Reliquary's alkahestry recipes."
  ],
  "quest.1CC6054DE3D91DA9.title": "What a nether star is for",
  "quest.1CC6054DE3D91DA9.quest_desc": [
    "Each Luminous piece uses one as its smithing template (nine for a set), several creative items ask for one, and so do beacons, Cataclysm's Harbinger and many high-tier recipes: &eU&r on the star in EMI lists them all.",
    "",
    "Tired of farming? Train a Hostile Neural Networks Wither model and simulate stars; the Simulation Chamber is an act IV machine here."
  ],
  "quest.321C015FCBE1CF65.title": "The monument and the wet sponge",
  "quest.321C015FCBE1CF65.quest_desc": [
    "YUNG's rebuilds ocean monuments, still guarded by Elder Guardians and their Mining Fatigue. In act V the compass counts one done when someone carries a wet sponge, which also goes into the creative fluid tanks.",
    "",
    "Bring water breathing and Respiration or Depth Strider; the Aether's Neptune armor and Iron Bubble shine here."
  ],
  "quest.6D96F605B73EC48A.title": "Eye Spy: the stronghold",
  "quest.6D96F605B73EC48A.quest_desc": [
    "Eyes of Ender still lead to the stronghold, rebuilt larger by YUNG's Better Strongholds. Follow one for Eye Spy. It is an act V compass stop, done when your team reaches the End.",
    "",
    "Bring spare eyes: some break on the way, always the one you needed."
  ],
  "quest.1367C89E923AF6CB.title": "The End",
  "quest.1367C89E923AF6CB.quest_desc": [
    "YUNG's Better End Island rebuilds the central island and the Dragon's arena, with its own towers and spawn platform. Your team's first arrival is an act V milestone.",
    "",
    "Bring blocks, a bow, slow falling or a water bucket, and a pumpkin on your head if you would rather not argue with every enderman."
  ],
  "quest.7D5F1D9C8CD14406.title": "Free the End",
  "quest.7D5F1D9C8CD14406.quest_desc": [
    "Break the End Crystals on the towers first (arrows, or climb to the caged ones), then hit the Dragon when it perches. Killing it completes the act V compass stop.",
    "",
    "It drops a pile of experience, the Dragon Egg, the gateway to the outer islands and, with Draconic Evolution, a Dragon Heart for act VI's creative energy items."
  ],
  "quest.58072A51FC29378C.title": "Bottled dragon's breath",
  "quest.58072A51FC29378C.quest_desc": [
    "During the fight the Dragon breathes a purple cloud: catch it in empty bottles (You Need a Mint). It makes lingering potions and shows up in several mod recipes.",
    "",
    "Need more? Four End Crystals on the exit portal bring the Dragon back (The End... Again...)."
  ],
  "quest.20DDBA794FE6B671.title": "Wings from an End city",
  "quest.20DDBA794FE6B671.quest_desc": [
    "The exit gateway leads to the outer islands, where End city ships hide Elytra (Sky's the Limit), guarded by Shulkers whose shells make shulker boxes.",
    "",
    "Solsticio's rarities dealer also sells Elytra, but only from act VI."
  ],
  "quest.2A5ED82F67EC1780.title": "The Warden: avoid, do not farm",
  "quest.2A5ED82F67EC1780.quest_desc": [
    "Sculk Shriekers summon it from the Deep Dark. It is blind, tracks vibrations and smell, and hits harder than almost anything: sneak, muffle steps with wool, and distract it with snowballs or arrows (Sneak 100).",
    "",
    "Ancient cities hold echo shards and Swift Sneak books, and Deeper and Darker adds a way into the Otherside."
  ],
  "quest.243E8667C02EA066.title": "Mowzie's Mobs",
  "quest.243E8667C02EA066.quest_desc": [
    "A handful of detailed creatures and four headline mini-bosses in a natural difficulty chain: the Ferrous Wroughtnaut underground, the Frostmaw in the cold, Tongbi the Sculptor in the mountains and Umvuthi the Sunbird with its tribe.",
    "",
    "Optional, acts II to IV here, and their prizes never break. Worth the detour."
  ],
  "quest.1F8C4C21E5A2D724.title": "The Ferrous Wroughtnaut",
  "quest.1F8C4C21E5A2D724.quest_desc": [
    "An armored giant asleep in a Wrought Chamber, roughly between Y 20 and Y 50. Dodge its huge axe, wait for the swing to end and hit its exposed back (Just a Flesh Wound).",
    "",
    "Prize: the unbreakable Axe of a Thousand Metals (right-click sweeps an arc, sneak-right-click sends a shockwave) and the unbreakable Wrought Helm."
  ],
  "quest.6FA6B0CE78579892.title": "The Frostmaw",
  "quest.6FA6B0CE78579892.quest_desc": [
    "A huge ice ape asleep in cold biomes (Rude Awakening is killing it). It freezes you in place; fire damage breaks Frozen early.",
    "",
    "It carries an Ice Crystal that channels an icy whirlwind and recharges in your inventory. You can steal it instead of fighting (Big Brain Time). The ape will not be pleased."
  ],
  "quest.36297A349942A165.title": "Tongbi, the Sculptor",
  "quest.36297A349942A165.quest_desc": [
    "He waits in a mountain monastery. Give him a Bluff Rod, from a Bluff, to start his test: climb the course he raises and right-click him at the top in time, without placing or breaking blocks, teleporting or flying (You Must Believe).",
    "",
    "Passing earns the Earthrend Gauntlet: throw boulders, tunnel and ride pillars of earth. Geomancer robes and beads boost it."
  ],
  "quest.74055B78138FF495.title": "Umvuthi, the Sunbird",
  "quest.74055B78138FF495.quest_desc": [
    "Umvuthi rules a grove guarded by masked Umvuthana. Beat a Raptor for a mask (Masquerade), then fight the Sunbird (Praise the Sun).",
    "",
    "It drops the unbreakable Sol Visage: wear it and right-click another mask to summon followers. The six masks give Strength, Speed, Haste, Resistance, Jump Boost or Health Boost."
  ],
  "quest.3C3360B975FDD608.title": "Heliomancer",
  "quest.3C3360B975FDD608.quest_desc": [
    "Sneak into a grove wearing a mask (Birds of a Feather) and Umvuthi may grant the Sun's Blessing (Heliomancer). With an empty hand: Sunstrike, Solar Flare, Solar Beam and Supernova, paid in blessing time that only starts counting when you use one; the Sunbird refills it for free later.",
    "",
    "Sun magic in a pack about Heliodor's light. Of course."
  ],
  "quest.5F3E5D75317D70D9.title": "The Grottol",
  "quest.5F3E5D75317D70D9.quest_desc": [
    "Diamond-crusted cave critters that flee on sight. Kill one with a Fortune pickaxe for extra diamonds (Double Or Nothing!), or with Silk Touch to capture it whole (You're Coming With Me).",
    "",
    "It is a rock with legs and a diamond problem."
  ],
  "quest.2F3AD185B74C7469.title": "The flying Naga",
  "quest.2F3AD185B74C7469.quest_desc": [
    "Not the Twilight one: Mowzie's Naga is a winged sea serpent that spits poison (Wingin' It). Its Naga Fang brews Poison Resistance, makes the Naga Fang Dagger (poison, double damage from behind) and makes darts for the Blowgun."
  ],
  "quest.7C0A20130CB7B6F9.title": "Smaller creatures",
  "quest.7C0A20130CB7B6F9.quest_desc": [
    "Foliaaths are carnivorous plants; their seed grows a pet if you feed it meat for two days. Lanterns drift at night and drop Luminous Jelly (brief night vision). Elokosa Howlers drop moon paws that inflict Weakness, Slowness, Mining Fatigue, Fragility or Eclipse on nearby mobs."
  ],
  "quest.4D9BB6756E65D6DE.title": "What ENTRELUMEN changes",
  "quest.4D9BB6756E65D6DE.quest_desc": [
    "The Wither is the only nether star source, and Hostile Neural Networks can simulate it once trained. YUNG's replaces fortresses, monuments, strongholds and the End island, so their /locate IDs change (for example betterstrongholds:stronghold). Carry On refuses the Wither, the Elder Guardian, the Warden, the Dragon and Mowzie's bosses.",
    "",
    "Nice try, though."
  ],
  "quest.45C9342D1E83A92F.title": "Trophy wall",
  "quest.45C9342D1E83A92F.quest_desc": [
    "Nether star, wet sponge, dragon's breath and Elytra from the vanilla bosses; an axe, a helm, a crystal, a gauntlet and the blessing of the sun from Mowzie's.",
    "",
    "None of it was required. All of it makes the rest easier."
  ],
  "chapter.21631D869DFFBC46.title": "Eternal Starlight · Ruins and the Crest",
  "chapter.21631D869DFFBC46.chapter_subtitle": [
    "The Golem Forge and the Cursed Garden, their three bosses and their weapons, Unrealium, and the Orb's crests fed by six crystals."
  ],
  "quest.71928319D4A2D4B1.title": "Cradle of Legion",
  "quest.71928319D4A2D4B1.quest_subtitle": "Mind the draught.",
  "quest.71928319D4A2D4B1.quest_desc": [
    "Throw a Seeking Eye with Redstone or Golem Steel in your other hand and follow it. The Golem Forge is buried under the forests, plains and permafrost: frozen halls, an alloy works, a storage wing and two bosses."
  ],
  "task.092241E92674CBF5.title": "Defeat a Freeze",
  "quest.388EF836A310ED45.title": "The Freezes",
  "quest.388EF836A310ED45.quest_subtitle": "The oldest air conditioning in the game.",
  "quest.388EF836A310ED45.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Cooling machines the Starlighters made from the dimension's frost magic, now its guards. Mechanical spawners keep making them; each drops one to three \"},{\"text\":\"Frozen Tubes\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:frozen_tube\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7B9216667321879A.title": "Dress for the cold",
  "quest.7B9216667321879A.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Thermal Springstone or Glacite armor keeps you from freezing the way leather does, and the Freezes and the Permafrost live on freezing you. Wear one of the two down here.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5DD37C29D8FC3703.title": "Chill out, buddy!",
  "quest.5DD37C29D8FC3703.quest_desc": [
    "Throw a Frozen Tube at the Starlight Golem while it fights and it drops into its charging state sooner. That's when it can be beaten."
  ],
  "quest.60436BA93B4A2364.title": "Tubes for the store",
  "quest.60436BA93B4A2364.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Sixteen \"},{\"text\":\"Frozen Tubes\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:frozen_tube\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" for the common store, once a day. The Forge's spawners never run out of Freezes.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5979BBCB0B4D7794.title": "Spare parts",
  "quest.5979BBCB0B4D7794.quest_desc": [
    "Once you've beaten the Starlight Golem, every Freeze you kill also drops four to six Oxidized Golem Steel Nuggets: Golem Steel that grows back."
  ],
  "quest.43AD4AF12BEB7050.title": "The Backstabber",
  "quest.43AD4AF12BEB7050.quest_subtitle": "Unplug it. Then hit it.",
  "quest.43AD4AF12BEB7050.quest_desc": [
    "When the Golem stops attacking to draw power, its armor runs on the Energy Blocks around the hall. Shut every one of them down and the armor drops for a while."
  ],
  "task.26123EE3825C45B0.title": "Defeat the Starlight Golem",
  "quest.633C1F8E3CE415A8.title": "The Starlight Golem",
  "quest.633C1F8E3CE415A8.quest_subtitle": "Built for a war nobody remembers.",
  "quest.633C1F8E3CE415A8.quest_desc": [
    "200 health behind armor that shrugs off almost everything, and it never moves: lasers, smashes and energized flames. Fight it in its charging windows.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "It drops 8 to 10 Oxidized Golem Steel Ingots, an Oxidized Alloy Furnace, the Forge armor trim and, three times in four, the Energy Sword. It also teaches the Blazing Beam crest."
  ],
  "quest.03F61FA45FC10810.title": "Energy Sword",
  "quest.03F61FA45FC10810.quest_desc": [
    "The Golem's own blade, dropped three times in four. Every hit throws off Energy Sparks at the target."
  ],
  "task.5CE2E0F9CAB7FCC9.title": "Defeat the Starlight Golem three times",
  "quest.1E6BA59ACFF16988.title": "Blazing Beam III",
  "quest.1E6BA59ACFF16988.quest_subtitle": "Third time's the laser.",
  "quest.1E6BA59ACFF16988.quest_desc": [
    "Each win against the Golem raises its crest a level, up to III. It respawns 30 minutes after a fight, so a free evening is enough."
  ],
  "task.70DCFDC4ABDC15EA.title": "Defeat the Permafrost",
  "quest.29268E6B61BB234A.title": "The Permafrost",
  "quest.29268E6B61BB234A.quest_subtitle": "Absolute zero, absolute attitude.",
  "quest.29268E6B61BB234A.quest_desc": [
    "Several Freezes fused into one thermal regulator, still set to cool the world to absolute zero. 120 health, freezing spit and clouds of frost; it guards its own chamber of the Forge.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "It drops the Coldsnap, 12 to 18 Frozen Tubes and 5 to 12 Oxidized Golem Steel Nuggets."
  ],
  "quest.0129EC0692F2B732.title": "Coldsnap",
  "quest.0129EC0692F2B732.quest_desc": [
    "The Permafrost's whip. It lashes from a whip's distance, freezes, and leaves the target Brittle, so cold hurts it more."
  ],
  "quest.1B8F68A61468190C.title": "Redox reactions",
  "quest.1B8F68A61468190C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Smelt the Golem's Oxidized Golem Steel Ingots back into clean \"},{\"text\":\"Golem Steel\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:golem_steel_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Its blocks weather like copper; honeycomb or Raw Amaramber waxes them.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.77AC77A3BF504933.title": "The Alloy Furnace",
  "quest.77AC77A3BF504933.quest_subtitle": "Two ores walk in, three ingots walk out.",
  "quest.77AC77A3BF504933.quest_desc": [
    "The Golem drops one, and the Forge's alloy room is lined with more. With a pinch of Saltpeter it doubles Deepsilver and iron ore and gets three ingots from two copper or gold ores and a Starcore. It also makes Golem Steel, Unrealium, and netherite from four gold and only two scrap."
  ],
  "quest.292BE60386B78A86.title": "Keep it cool",
  "quest.292BE60386B78A86.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"After ten minutes of steady work the Alloy Furnace overheats and \"},{\"text\":\"blows up\",\"color\":\"#FF8C7A\"},{\"text\":\". Feed its cooling slot: snow and ice buy a little time, Packed and Blue Ice a lot, and Glacite cools best of all.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.0B317E8A6CBABEF1.title": "Stretching the steel",
  "quest.0B317E8A6CBABEF1.quest_desc": [
    "Three Deepsilver Ingots and two Golem Steel Nuggets in the Alloy Furnace make a new ingot. A few nuggets, plenty of silver, and the Golem never needs to die again."
  ],
  "quest.1CBB7FC132E67E76.title": "Golem Steel Crate",
  "quest.1CBB7FC132E67E76.quest_desc": [
    "The Forge's storage wing is stacked with them. Craft your own from a chest, six Deepsilver Ingots and two Oxidized Golem Steel Ingots."
  ],
  "quest.48E9C9FBA2A99D48.title": "Energy Transmitter",
  "quest.48E9C9FBA2A99D48.quest_subtitle": "Redstone, minus the wire.",
  "quest.48E9C9FBA2A99D48.quest_desc": [
    "Link an emitter to a receiver by clicking one, then the other: the signal jumps between them as a beam of light, as far as you like. Four come from a craft with Cinder Bricks, one with stone."
  ],
  "quest.3CA7D445E2A4C924.title": "Accumulator",
  "quest.3CA7D445E2A4C924.quest_desc": [
    "Takes a redstone signal through the face with the red dot and gives it out of the other five, turning from grey to blue as the signal grows."
  ],
  "quest.6E730488E56B68C3.title": "Golem Steel Greatsword",
  "quest.6E730488E56B68C3.quest_desc": [
    "Four ingots on a stick. Its special swing launches Ball Lightning."
  ],
  "quest.29658190E22BBEA1.title": "Mechanical Crossbow",
  "quest.29658190E22BBEA1.quest_desc": [
    "A crossbow on a Golem Steel frame. Its bolts release Energy Sparks that chase the target."
  ],
  "quest.59DD475ABB93A4BE.title": "Energy Boomerang",
  "quest.59DD475ABB93A4BE.quest_subtitle": "It always comes back. Mostly.",
  "quest.59DD475ABB93A4BE.quest_desc": [
    "Five ingots bent into a boomerang: throw it and it returns. Precision lets it crit, Homing sends it after enemies, Gathering picks up items on its way."
  ],
  "quest.630A6D8F27896C22.title": "Underminer",
  "quest.630A6D8F27896C22.quest_subtitle": "The deeper, the faster.",
  "quest.630A6D8F27896C22.quest_desc": [
    "A Golem Steel pickaxe that digs faster the deeper you are. Voidstone never felt so soft."
  ],
  "quest.1ED0B8F134E2C2FA.title": "Crystal weapons",
  "quest.1ED0B8F134E2C2FA.quest_desc": [
    "Golem Steel set with red and blue starlight crystals, plus a Shivering Gel for the greatsword. Both leave Crystal Infection: damage over time and less armor."
  ],
  "quest.44883F07419F3989.title": "A map of the Forge",
  "quest.44883F07419F3989.quest_desc": [
    "Its rooms hang off long corridors: frozen halls full of Freezes and their spawners, the Permafrost's chamber, a storage wing of crates and chests, an alloy works with nineteen furnaces, and the Golem's hall at the heart."
  ],
  "quest.26F3D1BFAE4A1981.title": "The Cursed Garden",
  "quest.26F3D1BFAE4A1981.quest_subtitle": "Keep to the path. There is no path.",
  "quest.26F3D1BFAE4A1981.quest_desc": [
    "A hedge maze where the Starlighters fed their prisoners' souls to a plant. A Seeking Eye with vines, cave moss or Lunar Berries in your other hand finds it, in the forests, plains and taiga."
  ],
  "task.23E0CFC2657DFE40.title": "Defeat a Tangled",
  "quest.4319475ECFF226CA.title": "The Tangled",
  "quest.4319475ECFF226CA.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"What's left of the prisoners, grown over with vines. They drop sticks, vines and one to three \"},{\"text\":\"Soul Dew\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:soul_dew\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", the rarest ingredient of Unrealium.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.72EFE6F56A558F56.title": "It's just friendly fire",
  "quest.72EFE6F56A558F56.quest_subtitle": "Two skulls, one blast.",
  "quest.72EFE6F56A558F56.quest_desc": [
    "You killed a Tangled Skull and its blast finished off another. The souls inside them were in no mood to stay."
  ],
  "reward.5E55550C7B426C30.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.24E082A428DB54D8.title": "Burn it to the ground",
  "quest.24E082A428DB54D8.quest_desc": [
    "The Lunar Monstrosity's skin cuts almost all damage unless it's burning or stunned. Right-click it with flint and steel, a Fire Charge, a Blaze Rod or Powder, a Saltpeter Matchbox or a Thermal Springstone Ingot."
  ],
  "task.74DDBD797947AE29.title": "Defeat the Lunar Monstrosity",
  "quest.5131C5A8261FB584.title": "The Lunar Monstrosity",
  "quest.5131C5A8261FB584.quest_subtitle": "It's a plant. It's hungry. It's personal.",
  "quest.5131C5A8261FB584.quest_desc": [
    "200 health, rooted at the heart of the maze. It spits spores, raises thorns and breathes poison, and when you run it burrows after you. Keep it burning.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "It drops the Moonring Bow, the Crescent Pendant, the Twining trim, 10 to 15 petals and vines, Soul Dew and Tangled Skulls, and usually the Crescent Spear and the Wand of Teleportation."
  ],
  "quest.45F18FF99C1B8626.title": "Keep it lit",
  "quest.45F18FF99C1B8626.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Thermal Springstone weapons set their target on fire with every hit, so each blow keeps the Monstrosity's skin open for the next.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6FD0466D1AF1FFE8.title": "Petals, vines and dew",
  "quest.6FD0466D1AF1FFE8.quest_desc": [
    "Tenacious Petals and Vines and Soul Dew build every Monstrosity weapon; four petals also press into twelve Lunar Mosaic blocks."
  ],
  "quest.6DD9945FC62C3F0A.title": "Moonring Bow",
  "quest.6DD9945FC62C3F0A.quest_desc": [
    "A guaranteed drop. Fully drawn, its shots raise Lunar Thorns from the ground."
  ],
  "quest.02B087E0182ADE2E.title": "Complete darkness",
  "quest.02B087E0182ADE2E.quest_desc": [
    "Three in four Monstrosities drop the Crescent Spear; if yours didn't, craft it from three Deepsilver Ingots, two Tenacious Petals and a vine. Charge it and let go to lunge."
  ],
  "quest.777C4F6BD02ABFB4.title": "Wand of Teleportation",
  "quest.777C4F6BD02ABFB4.quest_subtitle": "Blink. Thorns.",
  "quest.777C4F6BD02ABFB4.quest_desc": [
    "Dropped three times in four. It teleports you where you point and leaves a ring of thorns where you land."
  ],
  "quest.0025FFA87F636101.title": "Crescent Pendant",
  "quest.0025FFA87F636101.quest_subtitle": "No single hit can take more than three quarters.",
  "quest.0025FFA87F636101.quest_desc": [
    "A chestplate accessory, always dropped. No single hit can take more than three quarters of your health, and it slowly mends the Monstrosity's weapons."
  ],
  "quest.4A3C2140E2219516.title": "Moonring Greatsword",
  "quest.4A3C2140E2219516.quest_desc": [
    "Two petals, two vines and a Soul Dew. A greatsword of the Monstrosity's own thorns."
  ],
  "quest.1225265360100F44.title": "Petal Scythe",
  "quest.1225265360100F44.quest_desc": [
    "Four petals and two vines. Its swings release clouds of poison, and it's the one scythe that can't be upgraded: it doesn't need to be."
  ],
  "quest.7CB92D7CC9E34E85.title": "Chain of Souls",
  "quest.7CB92D7CC9E34E85.quest_desc": [
    "Petals, vines, a Soul Dew and a nugget. It throws a chain that drags souls out of what it hits and heals you; Soul Snatcher and Tracing enchant it."
  ],
  "quest.71215B504C334711.title": "Wilted Crossbow",
  "quest.71215B504C334711.quest_desc": [
    "Golem Steel, a Red Velvetumoss Flower from the Abyss and Tenacious Vines for the string: a crossbow whose bolts come out wilted."
  ],
  "quest.3A7DC324F7947C55.title": "Soulit Spectator",
  "quest.3A7DC324F7947C55.quest_subtitle": "Out-of-body experience, sold separately.",
  "quest.3A7DC324F7947C55.quest_desc": [
    "A Soul Dew and a Nightfall Spider Eye. Throw it and your view flies with it, loading the land it passes over."
  ],
  "quest.27EAE4515DD72CDA.title": "Tangled Skulls",
  "quest.27EAE4515DD72CDA.quest_desc": [
    "The Monstrosity drops five to eight, and a killed Tangled Skull drops one now and then. Use one and it flies off where you look."
  ],
  "quest.7A1A544BD8A5C58F.title": "Unrealium",
  "quest.7A1A544BD8A5C58F.quest_subtitle": "Hard to see, harder to break.",
  "quest.7A1A544BD8A5C58F.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"One Deepsilver Ingot, one Golem Steel Ingot, one Malarite and one Soul Dew in the Alloy Furnace make one \"},{\"text\":\"Unrealium Ingot\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"eternal_starlight:unrealium_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\": the Forge and the Garden in one bar.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.629FBB625F9FEDC3.title": "Unrealium tools",
  "quest.629FBB625F9FEDC3.quest_desc": [
    "Diamond-grade with 1200 uses, the fastest digging in the dimension and a heavy hand. The sickle harvests like shears."
  ],
  "quest.1BF10CC5B54CA899.title": "Unrealium Crossbow",
  "quest.1BF10CC5B54CA899.quest_desc": [
    "The Mechanical Crossbow's frame with Unrealium in the middle. Its bolts fly half again as fast, hit a little harder and pierce everything in their path."
  ],
  "quest.16FDCDD39224D764.title": "Stepping into the unseen",
  "quest.16FDCDD39224D764.quest_subtitle": "Quiet as a thought.",
  "quest.16FDCDD39224D764.quest_desc": [
    "The full set makes you faster, lighter on your feet and harder to track, steps you up whole blocks and lets you see through fog. The helmet ignores suffocation, the chestplate cramming, and every piece mutes a sound you make."
  ],
  "quest.26ECAD8E983D0235.title": "Red starlight crystals",
  "quest.26ECAD8E983D0235.quest_desc": [
    "Break the red crystal clusters of the Crystallized Desert and its caves, or take them from Crystallized Moths. The red shards power every crest; the blue ones make Orbs."
  ],
  "quest.02855BC68D65BDD1.title": "Six elements",
  "quest.02855BC68D65BDD1.quest_desc": [
    "Four red shards around an element make its crystal: dirt or Conebloom for Terra, a Wind Charge for Wind, ice or kelp for Water, an Eye of Ender or Lunar Berries for Lunar, Blaze Powder or Thermal Springstone for Blaze, a torchflower for Light. Each holds 300 charge.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Five red shards in a plus, with nothing in the corners, make the crystal of the day instead: the element changes each in-game day and cycles through all six.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.36CE3BCBCE24A0FC.title": "The Mana Crystal",
  "quest.36CE3BCBCE24A0FC.quest_subtitle": "One crystal to cast them all.",
  "quest.36CE3BCBCE24A0FC.quest_desc": [
    "All six element crystals, shapeless, make one Mana Crystal: it counts as any element and holds 1800 charge, six crystals' worth."
  ],
  "quest.4B62CC0E9DA6A94A.title": "Guidance of Stars",
  "quest.4B62CC0E9DA6A94A.quest_subtitle": "Your personal Seeking Eye.",
  "quest.4B62CC0E9DA6A94A.quest_desc": [
    "The Gatekeeper's crest, yours since your first win. With a Terra, Wind or Lunar crystal on you, use the Orb and it points out the ruins where the powerful creatures live, every ten seconds."
  ],
  "quest.30E146F8C10837AA.title": "Blazing Beam",
  "quest.30E146F8C10837AA.quest_subtitle": "Point. Hold. Apologise.",
  "quest.30E146F8C10837AA.quest_desc": [
    "The Golem's crest. With a Blaze or Light crystal on you, hold the Orb's use key: after a moment's charge it fires a laser for up to 20 seconds, then cools down for twelve and a half."
  ],
  "quest.23EDD3EF25B03E4C.title": "Switching crests",
  "quest.23EDD3EF25B03E4C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"With the Orb in hand, \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.eternal_starlight.switch_crest\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" switches which crest it casts. Casting drains a matching crystal from your inventory, so carry a spare.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.58FFE310BDC01120.title": "Four armor trims",
  "quest.58FFE310BDC01120.quest_desc": [
    "Keeper from the Gatekeeper's trades, Forge from the Golem, Twining from the Monstrosity, and Blooming by taking shears to a Twining template. Seven Deepsilver or Amaramber Ingots around a Grimstone or Voidstone copy them.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The dimension's metals and crystals also work as trim colours, from Deepsilver to Unrealium.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.518E3507FB573DF6.title": "Boss portraits",
  "quest.518E3507FB573DF6.quest_subtitle": "Frame the enemy.",
  "quest.518E3507FB573DF6.quest_desc": [
    "The Golem, the Permafrost and the Monstrosity each have an even chance of dropping a Starlit Painting of themselves. Drop one into Ether and it comes out in its special version."
  ],
  "quest.16487B8381CDC430.title": "Boss records",
  "quest.16487B8381CDC430.quest_subtitle": "Put on something with a boss fight in it.",
  "quest.16487B8381CDC430.quest_desc": [
    "You own all four boss discs: Optimized Option from the Gatekeeper, Mechanical Fossil from the Golem, Moonlight and Fake Light from the Monstrosity."
  ],
  "reward.594275F035E2915F.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.401F3C6F1B4BD6FE.title": "The Starlighters' heir",
  "quest.401F3C6F1B4BD6FE.quest_subtitle": "Their machines, your hands.",
  "quest.401F3C6F1B4BD6FE.quest_desc": [
    "The Starlight Golem, the Permafrost and the Lunar Monstrosity beaten, and a full set of Unrealium on your back.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "{image:eternal_starlight:textures/gui/screen/book/icon.png width:40 height:40 align:center}",
    "",
    "Another people built machines out of light and fed them what they shouldn't have. Heliodor was not the only one."
  ],
  "image.26665FFBEB983462.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Frozen halls\",\"color\":\"#ACFFFC\"}]",
  "image.18B594B5EE70D4DE.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Golem's hall\",\"color\":\"#ACFFFC\"}]",
  "image.00922F94018DA361.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Permafrost's chamber\",\"color\":\"#ACFFFC\"}]",
  "image.0A5C4AE3B2E8CF7E.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Alloy works\",\"color\":\"#ACFFFC\"}]",
  "image.29CB0F773E81E5BA.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Control room\",\"color\":\"#ACFFFC\"}]",
  "image.7FC1FA740F023CDA.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Workshop\",\"color\":\"#ACFFFC\"}]",
  "image.30459B8B6684C170.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The maze\",\"color\":\"#ACFFFC\"}]",
  "image.3E13026F460A1E57.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Monstrosity's hoard\",\"color\":\"#ACFFFC\"}]",
  "image.65E8AA9B7FB72CE0.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Unrealium\",\"color\":\"#ACFFFC\"}]",
  "image.468B842BEB38C58F.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Orb and its crests\",\"color\":\"#ACFFFC\"}]",
  "image.51B91BF553D57A72.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Trophies\",\"color\":\"#ACFFFC\"}]",
  "image.1B98032CA9D0453F.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eternal Starlight\\nRuins and the Crest\",\"color\":\"#E8F7FF\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.6EBC1B05AB7B3256.title": "Back to the Sun of Heliodor",
  "image.142A3430794950DB.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"their machines, your hands\",\"color\":\"#B9B4F0\",\"font\":\"minecraft:alt\"}]",
  "image.07B30894DB924641.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» Eternal Night\",\"color\":\"#ACFFFC\"}]",
  "image.389DE74FECA35B7D.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» Ores and Arms\",\"color\":\"#ACFFFC\"}]",
  "chapter.5250DE207516A8E8.title": "L_Ender's Cataclysm · Armory",
  "chapter.5250DE207516A8E8.chapter_subtitle": [
    "What each boss leaves behind, and the anvil that fuses it."
  ],
  "quest.74213012D48E9D77.title": "Witherite",
  "quest.74213012D48E9D77.quest_subtitle": "The Harbinger's leftovers, by the block.",
  "quest.74213012D48E9D77.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Harbinger's \"},{\"text\":\"Block of Witherite\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"cataclysm:witherite_block\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" breaks into nine ingots. Six go into the Mechanical Fusion Anvil; the rest start its weapons: the Laser Gatling, the Meat Shredder and the Wither Assault Shoulder Weapon.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.486360E2B176D81D.title": "The Mechanical Fusion Anvil",
  "quest.486360E2B176D81D.quest_subtitle": "Two weapons walk in. One walks out.",
  "quest.486360E2B176D81D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Six witherite ingots, two blocks of redstone and an \"},{\"text\":\"Anvil\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:anvil\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It fuses a base weapon with an addition, and the result keeps the base's enchantments, name and wear.\"}]",
    "",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Enchant the base before you fuse it: nothing is lost in the anvil.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1DE23753AC909D16.title": "Gauntlet of Bulwark",
  "quest.1DE23753AC909D16.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Fuse the Gauntlet of Guard with the \"},{\"text\":\"Bulwark of the Flame\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"cataclysm:bulwark_of_the_flame\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Hold right-click for a second to shove everything nearby and brand it, then let go to charge forward.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.354B499DD4CA8ACD.title": "Gauntlet of Maelstrom",
  "quest.354B499DD4CA8ACD.quest_subtitle": "Hoovers, but for enemies.",
  "quest.354B499DD4CA8ACD.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Fuse the Gauntlet of Guard with \"},{\"text\":\"Sandstorm in a Bottle\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"cataclysm:sandstorm_in_a_bottle\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Right-click opens a Void Vortex that drags enemies down into it and bursts after a few seconds.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6ED4552DE676B05D.title": "Wrath of the Desert",
  "quest.6ED4552DE676B05D.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Fuse the Cursed Bow with \"},{\"text\":\"Sandstorm in a Bottle\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"cataclysm:sandstorm_in_a_bottle\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" from the \"},{\"text\":\"Remnant\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"225D314C3716757C\"}},{\"text\":\". It looses three cursed sandstorms instead of arrows.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.73B1C28F74EAF19C.title": "The Immolator",
  "quest.73B1C28F74EAF19C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Fuse the Annihilator with an \"},{\"text\":\"Ignitium Ingot\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"cataclysm:ignitium_ingot\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Every hit on a branded target is a critical, and held in both hands a two-second charge calls down a flame strike.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1518EB0EA1C01FF3.title": "Void Forge",
  "quest.1518EB0EA1C01FF3.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Fuse the Infernal Forge with a \"},{\"text\":\"Void Core\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"cataclysm:void_core\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" from an \"},{\"text\":\"Ender Golem\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"488A3E1F13BE6683\"}},{\"text\":\". Right-clicking a block now raises a fan of Void Runes, and it's still a pickaxe.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.637051B648ED2539.title": "Brontes",
  "quest.637051B648ED2539.quest_subtitle": "Also, this is a pickaxe.",
  "quest.637051B648ED2539.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Fuse the Infernal Forge with \"},{\"text\":\"Astrape\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"cataclysm:astrape\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". The result is a pickaxe you can throw, and it brings a storm down where it lands.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.04688EE0F24AC116.title": "Void Assault Shoulder Weapon",
  "quest.04688EE0F24AC116.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Fuse the Wither Assault Shoulder Weapon with a \"},{\"text\":\"Void Core\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"cataclysm:void_core\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It trades missiles for Void Howitzers, one every eight seconds.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5BA28D1851ACF891.title": "Wings of ignitium",
  "quest.5BA28D1851ACF891.quest_subtitle": "Armor that flies. Flight that doesn't wear.",
  "quest.5BA28D1851ACF891.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Fuse an Ignitium Chestplate with an \"},{\"text\":\"Elytra\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:elytra\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". It keeps the chestplate's 11 armor and glides like an elytra, except that gliding never wears it down.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Metal from the Nether, wings from the End, an anvil from under the Overworld: three worlds in one chestplate."
  ],
  "quest.36306EDF44825FD8.title": "Laser Gatling",
  "quest.36306EDF44825FD8.quest_desc": [
    "Two witherite ingots, iron, redstone and a block of redstone. Hold right-click to fire a stream of lasers; when the bar runs dry, one redstone dust from your inventory reloads all of it."
  ],
  "quest.5DC4524B486E7C38.title": "Meat Shredder",
  "quest.5DC4524B486E7C38.quest_subtitle": "Exactly what the name says.",
  "quest.5DC4524B486E7C38.quest_desc": [
    "Two witherite ingots, redstone and a block of iron. Hold right-click and it grinds whatever stands in front of you, ignoring the usual pause between hits."
  ],
  "quest.3CBEE615B2F39884.title": "Wither Assault Shoulder Weapon",
  "quest.3CBEE615B2F39884.quest_desc": [
    "Two witherite ingots, four gunpowder and a block of redstone, carried on the shoulder. Right-click fires Wither Missiles every two seconds; sneaking, it lobs a Wither Howitzer every five."
  ],
  "quest.6236483B32AD0DAB.title": "Black Steel",
  "quest.6236483B32AD0DAB.quest_desc": [
    "Draugr drop nuggets and now and then an ingot, an Aptrgangr one or two, and Frosted Prison treasure chests five to nine. It goes into the cursium template and every cursium weapon."
  ],
  "quest.409458AEF1C97906.title": "Black Steel Targe",
  "quest.409458AEF1C97906.quest_desc": [
    "The shield Royal Draugr carry: black steel nuggets around an ingot, with planks. It repairs with black steel instead of wood."
  ],
  "quest.363E2382CD80512A.title": "Cursium",
  "quest.363E2382CD80512A.quest_subtitle": "Cursed, but in a useful way.",
  "quest.363E2382CD80512A.quest_desc": [
    "Maledictus drops three or four ingots a kill. The armor takes one per piece, and the bow, the halberd and the Annihilator two or three each."
  ],
  "quest.51966D906C1EFBDB.title": "The cursium upgrade",
  "quest.51966D906C1EFBDB.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Six gold ingots and two black steel around a \"},{\"text\":\"Netherite Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:netherite_upgrade_smithing_template\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". At the smithing table it turns a netherite piece into cursium, and it's spent each time.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.3B8B713EF44059EF.title": "Cursium armor",
  "quest.3B8B713EF44059EF.quest_subtitle": "Dying is optional. Once.",
  "quest.3B8B713EF44059EF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Ghost Vision\",\"color\":\"#9BE08A\"},{\"text\":\": \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.cataclysm.helmet_ability\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" makes everything within 24 blocks glow. \"},{\"text\":\"Undead Revive\",\"color\":\"#9BE08A\"},{\"text\":\": a killing blow leaves you at 5 health and untouchable for five seconds, then six minutes of Ghost Sickness. The leggings sometimes dodge, the boots soften falls and back-step on \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.cataclysm.boots_ability\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\".\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "28 armor across the set (5, 10, 8 and 5) and 4 toughness a piece, against netherite's 20 and 3. It repairs with cursium ingots."
  ],
  "quest.4FFBBAD309C3456A.title": "Cursed Bow",
  "quest.4FFBBAD309C3456A.quest_subtitle": "Three arrows, one pull.",
  "quest.4FFBBAD309C3456A.quest_desc": [
    "Two cursium ingots, a black steel ingot and three string. It looses three Phantom Arrows per shot, and special arrows fire twice."
  ],
  "quest.7C74EA4DC9109605.title": "Soul Render",
  "quest.7C74EA4DC9109605.quest_desc": [
    "Three cursium ingots and two black steel make a halberd that rushes forward. Used while sneaking, it raises Phantom Halberds in a spiral around you."
  ],
  "quest.1A32C2B84B6A1A65.title": "The Annihilator",
  "quest.1A32C2B84B6A1A65.quest_desc": [
    "Two cursium ingots and a black steel ingot. Its critical hits land harder, and held in both hands a two-second charge smashes everything around you."
  ],
  "quest.0172D1245027C58F.title": "Ignitium",
  "quest.0172D1245027C58F.quest_subtitle": "Still warm.",
  "quest.0172D1245027C58F.quest_desc": [
    "Ignis drops three ingots a kill. The armor takes one per piece, the Incinerator and the Bulwark two each, the Blazing Grips one: plan on a few fights."
  ],
  "quest.65ABE72BF4ED523B.title": "The ignitium upgrade",
  "quest.65ABE72BF4ED523B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Four blaze powder and four blocks of nether bricks around a \"},{\"text\":\"Netherite Upgrade\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:netherite_upgrade_smithing_template\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Like the cursium one, it's spent on every piece.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.054BFB74FABFC49C.title": "Ignitium armor",
  "quest.054BFB74FABFC49C.quest_subtitle": "Fireproof is an understatement.",
  "quest.054BFB74FABFC49C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Gaze of Heat\",\"color\":\"#9BE08A\"},{\"text\":\": \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.cataclysm.helmet_ability\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" brands every creature within 16 blocks, and blazes and magma cubes ignore you until you strike them. \"},{\"text\":\"Flame Reflex\",\"color\":\"#9BE08A\"},{\"text\":\": an attacker is often set alight and branded. \"},{\"text\":\"Lava Walker\",\"color\":\"#9BE08A\"},{\"text\":\": the boots walk on lava unless you sneak.\"}]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"32 armor across the set (6, 11, 9 and 6) and 4 toughness a piece. The chestplate also fuses with an elytra into the \"},{\"text\":\"Ignitium Elytra Chestplate\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"5BA28D1851ACF891\"}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5B2A94CF33E627C6.title": "Bulwark of the Flame",
  "quest.5B2A94CF33E627C6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two ignitium ingots, nether bricks and blaze rods around a \"},{\"text\":\"Shield\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:shield\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Release it while sneaking to charge, and a target slammed into a wall is stunned; raise it just before a hit to set the attacker alight.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.7EFF723181E4F2EF.title": "The Incinerator",
  "quest.7EFF723181E4F2EF.quest_subtitle": "Every twenty seconds, a small apocalypse.",
  "quest.7EFF723181E4F2EF.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Two ignitium ingots and four blaze rods on a \"},{\"text\":\"Netherite Sword\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:netherite_sword\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\". Hold right-click for three seconds and let go to send a flame strike ahead; items caught in the blast can burn.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.785BD78675283257.title": "Blazing Grips",
  "quest.785BD78675283257.quest_desc": [
    "Eight nether bricks around an ignitium ingot, worn in a hands slot. Each hit has a 15% chance to brand the target, 30% with a pair."
  ],
  "quest.0F473A074A0B20E9.title": "The Infernal Forge",
  "quest.0F473A074A0B20E9.quest_subtitle": "FYI, it's a pickaxe.",
  "quest.0F473A074A0B20E9.quest_desc": [
    "Swing it at blocks and it mines; right-click a block and it sends a shockwave through everything nearby, every four seconds. It's also the base of two fusions, and each kill drops only one."
  ],
  "quest.264E7CD82BEDEC5C.title": "The Monstrous Helm",
  "quest.264E7CD82BEDEC5C.quest_subtitle": "Horns included. Temper too.",
  "quest.264E7CD82BEDEC5C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Smith the Monstrous Horn onto a \"},{\"text\":\"Netherite Helmet\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:netherite_helmet\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" with a netherite upgrade. When you drop below half health it knocks back everyone around you and grants Monstrous: more armor, knockback resistance and regeneration.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.4928066870F1DF36.title": "Netherite Effigy",
  "quest.4928066870F1DF36.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A netherite ingot, a \"},{\"text\":\"Totem of Undying\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:totem_of_undying\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", a block of redstone, gold and nether bricks. Use it to summon a Netherite Ministrosity of your own, and tame it with a Lava Power Cell.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.225D314C3716757C.title": "Sandstorm in a Bottle",
  "quest.225D314C3716757C.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Right-click to raise two sandstorms that circle you, every fifteen seconds. It's also the addition for \"},{\"text\":\"Wrath of the Desert\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"6ED4552DE676B05D\"}},{\"text\":\" and the \"},{\"text\":\"Gauntlet of Maelstrom\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"354B499DD4CA8ACD\"}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.489C3E3EA3FF4490.title": "A Remnant of your own",
  "quest.489C3E3EA3FF4490.quest_subtitle": "Smaller. Friendlier. Still bitey.",
  "quest.489C3E3EA3FF4490.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Use the Remnant's Skull on the ground and a Modern Remnant appears; a \"},{\"text\":\"Sniffer Egg\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"minecraft:sniffer_egg\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" tames it and bones heal it. An empty bucket carries it around.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.30D280D674C0D268.title": "Ancient Metal",
  "quest.30D280D674C0D268.quest_desc": [
    "Wadjets drop two to four ingots, Kobolediators one to three, Koboletons nuggets and now and then an ingot; the Remnant's block holds nine. Smelting a khopesh or an ancient spear gives back a nugget."
  ],
  "quest.261D3F4284075006.title": "Bone Reptile armor",
  "quest.261D3F4284075006.quest_desc": [
    "Ancient metal and Koboleton Bones make a helmet and a chestplate; the helmet also takes a Kobolediator Skull. 17 armor between them, and the best knockback resistance of any Cataclysm armor."
  ],
  "quest.0250C0257276AD83.title": "Ancient Spear",
  "quest.0250C0257276AD83.quest_desc": [
    "Three ancient metal ingots. Left-click also fires a sandstorm down the line, so it hits at range as well as up close."
  ],
  "quest.18D5184642C302C6.title": "Bones for the common store",
  "quest.18D5184642C302C6.quest_subtitle": "Koboletons: renewable, if you ask them firmly.",
  "quest.18D5184642C302C6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Thirty-two \"},{\"text\":\"Koboleton Bones\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"cataclysm:koboleton_bone\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", once a day. Each one crafts into four bone meal, so the team's farms eat well.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.69F61568CED53CB2.title": "Tidal Claws",
  "quest.69F61568CED53CB2.quest_subtitle": "Get over here. Politely.",
  "quest.69F61568CED53CB2.quest_desc": [
    "Right-click fires a grappling hook that reels you in, with no fall damage from the swing; left-click lashes out with a tentacle that hurts whatever it hits."
  ],
  "quest.7B9DFC0D6180A3F9.title": "Coral arms",
  "quest.7B9DFC0D6180A3F9.quest_desc": [
    "Deeplings carry Coral Spears and brutes Coral Bardiches, and now and then one falls with its weapon. Both are thrown like a trident."
  ],
  "quest.116D74197C681342.title": "Bloom Stone Pauldrons",
  "quest.116D74197C681342.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Eight Amethyst Crab Shells make a chest piece with 9 armor. \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.cataclysm.chestplate_ability\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" fires a ring of amethyst clusters that hurts everything around you, every twelve seconds.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.2CADD06B09C4E802.title": "Leviathan to go",
  "quest.2CADD06B09C4E802.quest_subtitle": "Some assembly required. Mostly fish.",
  "quest.2CADD06B09C4E802.quest_desc": [
    "The Abyssal Egg hatched after three slow cracks, the Baby Leviathan took tropical fish until it trusted you, and now it fits in a water bucket. Any fish heals it."
  ],
  "reward.26571948D74B1D06.title": "Secret found",
  "quest.63C8676A43BD1A49.title": "Essence of the Storm",
  "quest.63C8676A43BD1A49.quest_desc": [
    "Scylla drops three or four. Two of them and three Lacrima make either of her weapons."
  ],
  "quest.4F6E7458F875AC15.title": "Astrape",
  "quest.4F6E7458F875AC15.quest_subtitle": "Point it at the problem.",
  "quest.4F6E7458F875AC15.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"A spear that answers with lightning: right-click throws a Lightning Spear, every three seconds. It's also the addition that turns the Infernal Forge into \"},{\"text\":\"Brontes\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"637051B648ED2539\"}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.1233DD55F5B84B40.title": "Ceraunus",
  "quest.1233DD55F5B84B40.quest_desc": [
    "An anchor on a chain that you can throw. Used while sneaking, it sends waves out in a fan, every seven and a half seconds."
  ],
  "quest.2A764E6E192E17D4.title": "Azure Sea Shield",
  "quest.2A764E6E192E17D4.quest_desc": [
    "Four Lacrima, four gold nuggets and a gold ingot, no Scylla required. Raise it just before a hit to parry: the shield takes no damage, you get two seconds of Strength II and the attacker slows down for six."
  ],
  "quest.01C1F162A041F61A.title": "Chitin Claw",
  "quest.01C1F162A041F61A.quest_subtitle": "For the shelf you can almost reach.",
  "quest.01C1F162A041F61A.quest_desc": [
    "Worn in a hands slot, the Clawdian's claw adds a block of reach for mining and building, and a quarter block for hitting."
  ],
  "quest.6C68444982A4EE79.title": "Gauntlet of Guard",
  "quest.6C68444982A4EE79.quest_subtitle": "Come here. No, closer.",
  "quest.6C68444982A4EE79.quest_desc": [
    "Hold right-click to pull creatures toward you, then punch what arrives. It's the base of two fusions, and the Ender Guardian drops only one per kill."
  ],
  "quest.2D0F0C5927CA824C.title": "Void Scatter Arrows",
  "quest.2D0F0C5927CA824C.quest_subtitle": "Close enough is good enough.",
  "quest.2D0F0C5927CA824C.quest_desc": [
    "A Void Jaw on a Spectral Arrow makes two. On impact each one bursts into a spray of void shards, so a near miss still counts."
  ],
  "quest.150CE9EEDBA459D9.title": "Sticky Gloves",
  "quest.150CE9EEDBA459D9.quest_desc": [
    "String, leather, a slime ball and rabbit hide, worn in a hands slot. Koboletons can't knock anything out of your hands while you have them on."
  ],
  "quest.0B2268DA0644B773.title": "Room for a talisman",
  "quest.0B2268DA0644B773.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The \"},{\"text\":\"Belt of Beginner\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"cataclysm:belt_of_beginner\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\", two leather and an iron ingot, opens two talisman slots, and nothing else in the pack does. The desert's \"},{\"text\":\"Unbreakable Skull\",\"color\":\"#8FD6C8\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_item\",\"contents\":{\"id\":\"cataclysm:unbreakable_skull\",\"count\":1}}},{\"text\":\" needs one: it shrugs off a stun once per cooldown.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.334D7767B50C8C3D.title": "Vitality Ankh",
  "quest.334D7767B50C8C3D.quest_desc": [
    "From desert treasure chests, worn as a necklace: the healing you get from a full food bar comes 20% stronger."
  ],
  "quest.4A05FF06C89F1668.title": "Sturdy Boots",
  "quest.4A05FF06C89F1668.quest_desc": [
    "Worn in the feet slot, they let you walk on powder snow and step up half a block higher, so full blocks work like stairs."
  ],
  "quest.681565B503A27891.title": "Ring of Grudged",
  "quest.681565B503A27891.quest_subtitle": "It remembers every slight.",
  "quest.681565B503A27891.quest_desc": [
    "Worn in a ring slot: critical hits deal 10% more. There are two ring slots, and two rings stack."
  ],
  "quest.7A81F8C6D719C1E2.title": "Berserker Soul Amulet",
  "quest.7A81F8C6D719C1E2.quest_desc": [
    "Worn as a necklace: 10% more attack damage for 25% less armor. A deal for people who don't plan on getting hit."
  ],
  "quest.17F5B257E8CD8437.title": "Armor keys",
  "quest.17F5B257E8CD8437.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Cataclysm armor has keys of its own: \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.cataclysm.helmet_ability\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" for the ignitium and cursium helmets, \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.cataclysm.chestplate_ability\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" for the Bloom Stone Pauldrons and \"},{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[\"},{\"keybind\":\"key.cataclysm.boots_ability\"},{\"text\":\"]\"}],\"color\":\"#F2D060\"},{\"text\":\" for the cursium back-step.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.6AA83643CCEA47BE.title": "A template per piece",
  "quest.6AA83643CCEA47BE.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The smithing table spends a template on every piece, so a full cursium or ignitium set takes four boss templates and four netherite upgrades behind them. Copy the upgrade early: seven diamonds and a block of netherrack make two.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.60959F6C97F3C3D6.title": "One base, two fusions",
  "quest.60959F6C97F3C3D6.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"The Infernal Forge is the base of both Brontes and the Void Forge, and the Gauntlet of Guard of both gauntlets, but each kill drops just one. Choose, or book a rematch through the \"},{\"text\":\"Boss Respawner\",\"color\":\"#9DC3FF\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"4420728015E09F1A\"}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5194D275D01D32E2.title": "Boss metal",
  "quest.5194D275D01D32E2.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\",{\"text\":\"» \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\"},{\"text\":\"Pro tip: \",\"color\":\"#E8B04A\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\"Witherite, ignitium, cursium and ancient metal ingots all work as armor trim materials. Ignitium and cursium armor repair with their own ingots at an anvil.\"}]"
  ],
  "quest.5E0FAD8BEFA3CA47.title": "Trophy shelf",
  "quest.5E0FAD8BEFA3CA47.quest_subtitle": "Taste over armor.",
  "quest.5E0FAD8BEFA3CA47.quest_desc": [
    "A block of every boss metal: witherite, ignitium, cursium and ancient metal. Thirty-six ingots that could have been gear, set out for display instead."
  ],
  "reward.41A9D891474941F5.title": "Secret found",
  "image.304956602637D201.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Harbinger\",\"color\":\"#FF6040\"}]",
  "image.6D53AFF4592F10E6.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Maledictus\",\"color\":\"#FF6040\"}]",
  "image.7A803A58C5DC071D.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Ignis\",\"color\":\"#FF6040\"}]",
  "image.2F3940C331404B09.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Netherite Monstrosity\",\"color\":\"#FF6040\"}]",
  "image.1BEE28F9A0931035.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Ancient Remnant\",\"color\":\"#FF6040\"}]",
  "image.53A6A27841E219C5.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"The Leviathan\",\"color\":\"#FF6040\"}]",
  "image.3D54EF176DBB89AD.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Scylla\",\"color\":\"#FF6040\"}]",
  "image.323A99BE4A483E24.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Ender Guardian\",\"color\":\"#FF6040\"}]",
  "image.7BA60E590E93D750.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"From the ruins' chests\",\"color\":\"#FF6040\"}]",
  "image.33AEFCF9C9350D34.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"Workshop notes\",\"color\":\"#FF6040\"}]",
  "image.29D06783941342CC.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"L_Ender's Cataclysm\\nArmory\",\"color\":\"#FFE9CC\",\"bold\":true}]",
  "image.7D1BCA2BB5E7C290.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"what the keepers leave behind\",\"color\":\"#C9B8E8\",\"font\":\"minecraft:alt\"}]",
  "image.72BF0329D36493EF.title": "[\"\",{\"text\":\"« Arenas\",\"color\":\"#FF6040\"}]",
  "image.097283882158DB29.title": "Back to the Sun of Heliodor",
  "chapter.0EF22D195361F538.title": "The Sun of Heliodor",
  "chapter.0EF22D195361F538.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Six acts under one sun."
  ],
  "image.5BF9817D06F941EF.title": "I · A Light Among Ruins",
  "image.2DE77102B1FC7F1D.title": "&#E8DCB5A Light Among Ruins",
